rting at step 2)\\n  recursion_without_base_case_EXAMPLE(...) SKIPPED     (takes 1 argument(s); supply concrete values via args_map/--args to analyze a specific call)\\n  float_equality_never_true_EXAMPLE() UNSUPPORTED (only int/bool constants are supported, got float)\\n  mutating_collection_while_iterating_EXAMPLE(...) SKIPPED     (takes 1 argument(s); supply concrete values via args_map/--args to analyze a specific call)\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"Analysis of /mnt/user-data/outputs/non_halting_examples.py:\\n  wrong_direction()            LOOPS       (proven, exact state repeats every 130 steps starting at step 2)\\n  inverted_condition()         LOOPS       (proven, exact state repeats every 104 steps starting at step 2)\\n  off_by_one_never_reached()   LOOPS       (proven, exact state repeats every 104 steps starting at step 2)\\n  mutual_oscillation()         LOOPS       (proven, exact state repeats every 38 steps starting at step 10)\\n  reset_before_exit_check()    LOOPS       (proven, exact state repeats every 58 steps starting at step 2)\\n  unconditional_infinite_loop() LOOPS       (proven, exact state repeats every 22 steps starting at step 2)\\n  recursion_without_base_case_EXAMPLE(...) SKIPPED     (takes 1 argument(s); supply concrete values via args_map/--args to analyze a specific call)\\n  float_equality_never_true_EXAMPLE() UNSUPPORTED (only int/bool constants are supported, got float)\\n  mutating_collection_while_iterating_EXAMPLE(...) SKIPPED     (takes 1 argument(s); supply concrete values via args_map/--args to analyze a specific call)\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:07:55.122195Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:07:55.927044Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "All six Group A patterns now come back correctly and honestly proven `LOOPS`, each with a real exact cycle length as evidence.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:07:55.927077Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:07:56.255483Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_0156fpRDnsPPqW4sq3phBULw", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/non_halting_examples.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/non_halting_examples.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:07:56.275427Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:07:56.275464Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_0156fpRDnsPPqW4sq3phBULw", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/non_halting_examples.py", "name": "non halting examples", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "The file cards appear at the end of your reply if it ends with text, otherwise under this step; say they are below only if you finish the reply with text."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:07:57.801378Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:08:01.469364Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Six real, common bug patterns (Group A), each mechanically proven to loop forever by `code_halt_search.py`, not just claimed:\n\n| Function | The actual mistake |\n|---|---|\n| `wrong_direction` | Parity mismatch \u2014 target value is structurally unreachable, not just slow to reach |\n| `inverted_condition` | Loop's continue-condition is backwards |\n| `off_by_one_never_reached` | Step size skips clean over the exact target |\n| `mutual_oscillation` | Two variables swap forever, canceling out any progress |\n| `reset_before_exit_check` | Progress-resetting line accidentally placed before the exit check instead of after the loop |\n| `unconditional_infinite_loop` | No exit condition at all \u2014 the classic missing `break` |\n\nPlus three Group B examples (recursion without a shrinking base case, float-equality drift, mutating a list while iterating it) \u2014 shown as realistic source for discussion, correctly flagged as outside what the tool can safely execute rather than run as-is.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-09-26T13:08:01.556050Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-26T13:08:01.556050Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0ddd3-5095-7658-b00b-77790ef79624"}, {"uuid": "01a0ddd5-656d-7eee-82dc-80b8973d3b17", "text": "fuzz incoming data after each max Configurations seen", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:07.590984Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:07.590984Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "fuzz incoming data after each max Configurations seen", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-09-26T13:09:07.591146Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-26T13:09:07.591146Z", "attachments": [{"file_name": "", "file_size": 26706, "file_type": "txt", "extracted_content": "import numpy as np\r\nimport argparse\r\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\r\n\r\n\r\n@dataclass\r\nclass Program:\r\n    name: str\r\n    halt_step: int | None\r\n\r\n    def instruction(self, step):\r\n        if self.halt_step is not None and step == self.halt_step:\r\n            return \"HALT\"\r\n        return \"CONTINUE\"\r\n\r\n\r\nclass PathOrderedFork:\r\n    def __init__(self, modes=4):\r\n        self.modes = modes\r\n        self.I = np.eye(modes, dtype=complex)\r\n\r\n        self.TL = self.rotation(0, 1, 0.37, 0.21)\r\n        self.TR = self.rotation(1, 2, 0.61, 1.17)\r\n        self.TH = self.halt_transform()\r\n\r\n    def rotation(self, a, b, theta, phase):\r\n        U = np.eye(self.modes, dtype=complex)\r\n\r\n        c = np.cos(theta)\r\n        s = np.sin(theta)\r\n\r\n        U[a, a] = c\r\n        U[b, b] = c\r\n\r\n        U[a, b] = -1j * np.exp(1j * phase) * s\r\n        U[b, a] = -1j * np.exp(-1j * phase) * s\r\n\r\n        return U\r\n\r\n    def halt_transform(self):\r\n        U = np.eye(self.modes, dtype=complex)\r\n\r\n        theta = 0.9\r\n        c = np.cos(theta)\r\n        s = np.sin(theta)\r\n\r\n        U[0, 0] = c\r\n        U[3, 3] = c\r\n\r\n        U[0, 3] = -1j * s\r\n        U[3, 0] = -1j * s\r\n\r\n        return U\r\n\r\n    def branch_transform(self, branch):\r\n        if branch == 0:\r\n            return self.TL\r\n        return self.TR\r\n\r\n    def branch_sequence(self, n):\r\n        return [\r\n            ((k * 1103515245 + 12345) >> 4) & 1\r\n            for k in range(n)\r\n        ]\r\n\r\n    def evolve(self, program, branches, steps):\r\n        state = np.zeros(self.modes, dtype=complex)\r\n        state[0] = 1.0\r\n\r\n        U = self.I.copy()\r\n\r\n        history = []\r\n\r\n        for step in range(steps):\r\n            branch = branches[step]\r\n\r\n            T = self.branch_transform(branch)\r\n\r\n            instruction = program.instruction(step)\r\n\r\n            if instruction == \"HALT\":\r\n                T = self.TH @ T\r\n\r\n            # Exact discrete path-ordered multiplication.\r\n            U = T @ U\r\n\r\n            state = T @ state\r\n\r\n            state_norm = np.linalg.norm(state)\r\n\r\n            if state_norm > 0:\r\n                state /= state_norm\r\n\r\n            trace = np.trace(U) / self.modes\r\n\r\n            halt_signal = abs(state[3]) ** 2\r\n\r\n            history.append({\r\n                \"step\": step,\r\n                \"branch\": branch,\r\n                \"instruction\": instruction,\r\n                \"state\": state.copy(),\r\n                \"U\": U.copy(),\r\n                \"halt_signal\": halt_signal,\r\n                \"trace\": trace,\r\n                \"trace_abs\": abs(trace),\r\n                \"trace_phase\": np.angle(trace)\r\n            })\r\n\r\n        return state, U, history\r\n\r\n    def observable(self, state, U):\r\n        W = np.trace(U) / self.modes\r\n\r\n        return {\r\n            \"halt_signal\": float(abs(state[3]) ** 2),\r\n            \"holonomy_magnitude\": float(abs(W)),\r\n            \"holonomy_phase\": float(np.angle(W)),\r\n            \"state_norm\": float(np.linalg.norm(state)),\r\n            \"trace_real\": float(W.real),\r\n            \"trace_imag\": float(W.imag)\r\n        }\r\n\r\n    def commutator(self):\r\n        return np.linalg.norm(\r\n            self.TR @ self.TL -\r\n            self.TL @ self.TR\r\n        )\r\n\r\n\r\ndef compare_at_time(fork, p1, p2, branches, steps):\r\n    state1, U1, history1 = fork.evolve(\r\n        p1,\r\n        branches,\r\n        steps\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    state2, U2, history2 = fork.evolve(\r\n        p2,\r\n        branches,\r\n        steps\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    obs1 = fork.observable(state1, U1)\r\n    obs2 = fork.observable(state2, U2)\r\n\r\n    state_difference = np.linalg.norm(\r\n        state1 - state2\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    matrix_difference = np.linalg.norm(\r\n        U1 - U2\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    observable_difference = {\r\n        key: abs(obs1[key] - obs2[key])\r\n        for key in obs1\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    return {\r\n        \"state1\": state1,\r\n        \"state2\": state2,\r\n        \"U1\": U1,\r\n        \"U2\": U2,\r\n        \"obs1\": obs1,\r\n        \"obs2\": obs2,\r\n        \"state_difference\": state_difference,\r\n        \"matrix_difference\": matrix_difference,\r\n        \"observable_difference\": observable_difference,\r\n        \"history1\": history1,\r\n        \"history2\": history2\r\n    }\r\n\r\n\r\ndef print_observable(name, obs):\r\n    print(name)\r\n    print(\r\n        f\"  HALT signal       = \"\r\n        f\"{obs['halt_signal']:.15f}\"\r\n    )\r\n    print(\r\n        f\"  |Tr(U)/d|        = \"\r\n        f\"{obs['holonomy_magnitude']:.15f}\"\r\n    )\r\n    print(\r\n        f\"  arg(Tr(U)/d)     = \"\r\n        f\"{obs['holonomy_phase']:.15f}\"\r\n    )\r\n    print(\r\n        f\"  Tr real          = \"\r\n        f\"{obs['trace_real']:.15f}\"\r\n    )\r\n    print(\r\n        f\"  Tr imaginary     = \"\r\n        f\"{obs['trace_imag']:.15f}\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n\r\ndef run_experiment(observation_steps=1000, late_halt=2000):\r\n    fork = PathOrderedFork()\r\n\r\n    branches = fork.branch_sequence(\r\n        max(observation_steps, late_halt + 1)\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    early = Program(\r\n        \"EARLY_HALT\",\r\n        observation_steps // 2\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    late = Program(\r\n        \"LATE_HALT\",\r\n        late_halt\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    never = Program(\r\n        \"NEVER_HALT\",\r\n        None\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\"=\" * 78)\r\n    print(\"PATH-ORDERED FORK / FINITE-TIME HALTING TEST\")\r\n    print(\"=\" * 78)\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\r\n        f\"Observation window : {observation_steps} steps\"\r\n    )\r\n    print(\r\n        f\"Late HALT          : step {late_halt}\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\"1. NONCOMMUTATIVITY\")\r\n    print(\"-\" * 78)\r\n\r\n    comm = fork.commutator()\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"||T_R T_L - T_L T_R|| = \"\r\n        f\"{comm:.15f}\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"Ordering is encoded.\"\r\n        if comm > 1e-12\r\n        else\r\n        \"Ordering is not encoded.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\"2. EARLY HALT VS NEVER HALT\")\r\n    print(\"-\" * 78)\r\n\r\n    result = compare_at_time(\r\n        fork,\r\n        early,\r\n        never,\r\n        branches,\r\n        observation_steps\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print_observable(\r\n        \"EARLY HALT\",\r\n        result[\"obs1\"]\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n\r\n    print_observable(\r\n        \"NEVER HALT\",\r\n        result[\"obs2\"]\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\r\n        f\"State difference = \"\r\n        f\"{result['state_difference']:.15e}\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        f\"Matrix difference = \"\r\n        f\"{result['matrix_difference']:.15e}\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\"These differ because EARLY_HALT has actually executed HALT.\")\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\"3. LATE HALT VS NEVER HALT\")\r\n    print(\"-\" * 78)\r\n\r\n    result = compare_at_time(\r\n        fork,\r\n        late,\r\n        never,\r\n        branches,\r\n        observation_steps\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print_observable(\r\n        \"LATE HALT\",\r\n        result[\"obs1\"]\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n\r\n    print_observable(\r\n        \"NEVER HALT\",\r\n        result[\"obs2\"]\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\r\n        f\"State difference = \"\r\n        f\"{result['state_difference']:.15e}\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        f\"Matrix difference = \"\r\n        f\"{result['matrix_difference']:.15e}\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\"OBSERVABLE DIFFERENCES\")\r\n    print(\"-\" * 78)\r\n\r\n    for key, value in result[\r\n        \"observable_difference\"\r\n    ].items():\r\n        print(\r\n            f\"{key:25s} = {value:.15e}\"\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\"4. MATHEMATICAL IDENTITY\")\r\n    print(\"-\" * 78)\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"For every step j <= observation time:\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"    T_j(LATE_HALT) = T_j(NEVER_HALT)\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"Therefore:\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"    U_N(LATE_HALT) = U_N(NEVER_HALT)\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"and consequently:\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"    W_N(LATE_HALT) = W_N(NEVER_HALT)\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\"5. PATH-ORDERED PRODUCT\")\r\n    print(\"-\" * 78)\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"U_N = T_N T_(N-1) ... T_2 T_1\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"The multiplication order is retained.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"But the finite product contains only the first N \"\r\n        \"instructions.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\"6. THE LIMIT THAT WOULD BE REQUIRED\")\r\n    print(\"-\" * 78)\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"A universal halting detector would require a finite-time \"\r\n        \"observable F satisfying:\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\r\n        \"F(P) = 1  if P eventually halts\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"F(P) = 0  if P never halts\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\r\n        \"The problem is that for every finite N one can construct:\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\r\n        \"P_late  = O1 O2 ... ON ... HALT\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"P_loop  = O1 O2 ... ON ... LOOP\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\r\n        \"Their complete physical histories through N are identical.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\r\n        \"Therefore every observable calculated solely from that \"\r\n        \"finite history is identical.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\"=\" * 78)\r\n    print(\"CONCLUSION\")\r\n    print(\"=\" * 78)\r\n\r\n    if result[\"matrix_difference\"] < 1e-12:\r\n        print(\r\n            \"The simulation verifies finite-time indistinguishability.\"\r\n        )\r\n    else:\r\n        print(\r\n            \"Unexpected difference detected.\"\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\r\n        \"The path-ordered construction successfully preserves \"\r\n        \"noncommutative computational ordering.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"It does not, by itself, provide information about \"\r\n        \"instructions that have not yet occurred.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print(\r\n        \"To obtain a genuine halting oracle, an additional physical \"\r\n        \"mechanism would have to encode the infinite future into a \"\r\n        \"finite measurable quantity.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n\r\n# =============================================================================\r\n# TOY HALTING PROBLEM -- ACTUALLY DECIDABLE, ACTUALLY SOLVED\r\n# =============================================================================\r\n#\r\n# The section above demonstrates *why* halting is undecidable in general:\r\n# a finite observation window cannot distinguish \"halts later\" from \"never\r\n# halts,\" because both programs can have identical histories up to that\r\n# window, for any window size you pick.\r\n#\r\n# That impossibility relies on one thing: an unbounded configuration space\r\n# (an infinite-tape, infinite-future machine). If instead the configuration\r\n# space is FINITE -- bounded registers, bounded tape, finitely many\r\n# instructions -- halting becomes decidable, with a real proof, not a\r\n# simulation trick:\r\n#\r\n#   1. Every configuration is a tuple (program_counter, register_values).\r\n#   2. The machine is deterministic, so each configuration has exactly one\r\n#      successor.\r\n#   3. There are only finitely many possible configurations.\r\n#   4. Run the machine and record every configuration visited.\r\n#      - If HALT is reached: the machine halts. Proven.\r\n#      - If a configuration repeats: the machine has entered a deterministic\r\n#        cycle, and since it is deterministic, it will repeat that cycle\r\n#        forever. It provably never halts. Proven.\r\n#   5. Since there are finitely many configurations, one of these two\r\n#      outcomes MUST occur within (number of configurations) steps. There is\r\n#      no third case and no need to guess or bound the search heuristically.\r\n#\r\n# This is the same logic used by real, sound tools such as model checkers\r\n# and finite-state verifiers. It works precisely because the state space is\r\n# finite -- the one assumption that fails for general Turing machines.\r\n\r\n\r\n@dataclass\r\nclass Instruction:\r\n    op: str          # \"INC\", \"DEC\", \"JZ\", \"JMP\", \"HALT\"\r\n    reg: int = 0      # register index, for INC/DEC/JZ\r\n    target: int = 0   # jump target, for JZ/JMP\r\n\r\n\r\nclass ToyMachine:\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    A tiny register machine:\r\n      - a fixed number of registers, each clamped to [0, max_value]\r\n      - INC r        : reg[r] += 1 (clamped)\r\n      - DEC r        : reg[r] -= 1 (clamped, floor 0)\r\n      - JZ  r target : jump to target if reg[r] == 0, else fall through\r\n      - JMP target   : unconditional jump\r\n      - HALT         : stop\r\n\r\n    Because every register is bounded and there are finitely many\r\n    instructions, the total configuration space is finite:\r\n        num_instructions * (max_value + 1) ** num_registers\r\n    which makes halting decidable for this machine, exactly.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, program, num_registers, max_value):\r\n        self.program = program\r\n        self.num_registers = num_registers\r\n        self.max_value = max_value\r\n\r\n    def initial_config(self):\r\n        return (0, tuple([0] * self.num_registers))\r\n\r\n    def step(self, config):\r\n        pc, regs = config\r\n        instr = self.program[pc]\r\n        regs = list(regs)\r\n\r\n        if instr.op == \"INC\":\r\n            regs[instr.reg] = min(self.max_value, regs[instr.reg] + 1)\r\n            next_pc = pc + 1\r\n        elif instr.op == \"DEC\":\r\n            regs[instr.reg] = max(0, regs[instr.reg] - 1)\r\n            next_pc = pc + 1\r\n        elif instr.op == \"JZ\":\r\n            next_pc = instr.target if regs[instr.reg] == 0 else pc + 1\r\n        elif instr.op == \"JMP\":\r\n            next_pc = instr.target\r\n        elif instr.op == \"HALT\":\r\n            next_pc = pc  # unreachable; step() isn't called after HALT\r\n        else:\r\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown opcode: {instr.op}\")\r\n\r\n        return (next_pc, tuple(regs))\r\n\r\n    def total_configurations(self):\r\n        return len(self.program) * (self.max_value + 1) ** self.num_registers\r\n\r\n\r\ndef decide_halting(machine, verbose=False):\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    A genuine, correct halting decider for ToyMachine programs.\r\n\r\n    Returns a dict with:\r\n        halts        : True, False (never guessed -- always proven)\r\n        steps        : number of steps taken to halt (if halts)\r\n        cycle_start  : step index where the repeated configuration first\r\n                        occurred (if it loops)\r\n        cycle_length : length of the proven infinite cycle (if it loops)\r\n        configs_seen : how many configurations were explored\r\n        state_space  : total size of the machine's configuration space\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    config = machine.initial_config()\r\n    seen = {config: 0}\r\n    trace = [config]\r\n\r\n    step_count = 0\r\n    limit = machine.total_configurations()\r\n\r\n    while True:\r\n        pc, regs = config\r\n\r\n        if machine.program[pc].op == \"HALT\":\r\n            return {\r\n                \"halts\": True,\r\n                \"steps\": step_count,\r\n                \"configs_seen\": len(seen),\r\n                \"state_space\": limit,\r\n                \"trace\": trace if verbose else None,\r\n            }\r\n\r\n        config = machine.step(config)\r\n        step_count += 1\r\n\r\n        if config in seen:\r\n            cycle_start = seen[config]\r\n            return {\r\n                \"halts\": False,\r\n                \"cycle_start\": cycle_start,\r\n                \"cycle_length\": step_count - cycle_start,\r\n                \"configs_seen\": len(seen),\r\n                \"state_space\": limit,\r\n                \"trace\": trace if verbose else None,\r\n            }\r\n\r\n        seen[config] = step_count\r\n        trace.append(config)\r\n\r\n        # Safety net only -- mathematically this can never trigger,\r\n        # since the state space is finite and we check every visited\r\n        # configuration above. Kept only to fail loudly on a bug.\r\n        assert step_count <= limit + 1, \"unreachable: proof above guarantees termination\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef print_decision(name, machine, result):\r\n    print(name)\r\n    print(f\"  Registers x range   : {machine.num_registers} x [0, {machine.max_value}]\")\r\n    print(f\"  Total state space   : {result['state_space']} configurations\")\r\n    print(f\"  Configurations seen : {result['configs_seen']}\")\r\n\r\n    if result[\"halts\"]:\r\n        print(f\"  DECISION            : HALTS  (in {result['steps']} steps)\")\r\n    else:\r\n        print(\r\n            f\"  DECISION            : NEVER HALTS  \"\r\n            f\"(proven -- enters a cycle of length {result['cycle_length']} \"\r\n            f\"starting at step {result['cycle_start']})\"\r\n        )\r\n\r\n\r\ndef run_toy_halting_demo():\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\"=\" * 78)\r\n    print(\"TOY HALTING PROBLEM -- FINITE-STATE, ACTUALLY DECIDABLE\")\r\n    print(\"=\" * 78)\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\r\n        \"Unlike a general Turing machine, this machine has boundedly many\\n\"\r\n        \"registers over a bounded range, so its configuration space is\\n\"\r\n        \"finite. Halting is therefore genuinely decidable: run it, and\\n\"\r\n        \"either HALT is reached or a configuration repeats (a proven\\n\"\r\n        \"infinite loop). One of the two always happens.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    # Program A: counts a register down from 3 to 0, then halts.\r\n    #   0: JZ  r0 -> 3   (if r0 == 0, jump to HALT)\r\n    #   1: DEC r0\r\n    #   2: JMP -> 0\r\n    #   3: HALT\r\n    halting_program = [\r\n        Instruction(\"JZ\", reg=0, target=3),\r\n        Instruction(\"DEC\", reg=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"JMP\", target=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"HALT\"),\r\n    ]\r\n\r\n    # To make it start at 3 instead of 0, we bump r0 up first:\r\n    #   0: INC r0\r\n    #   1: INC r0\r\n    #   2: INC r0\r\n    #   3: JZ  r0 -> 6\r\n    #   4: DEC r0\r\n    #   5: JMP -> 3\r\n    #   6: HALT\r\n    halting_program = [\r\n        Instruction(\"INC\", reg=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"INC\", reg=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"INC\", reg=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"JZ\", reg=0, target=6),\r\n        Instruction(\"DEC\", reg=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"JMP\", target=3),\r\n        Instruction(\"HALT\"),\r\n    ]\r\n\r\n    # Program B: an unconditional infinite loop. Never reaches HALT.\r\n    #   0: INC r0\r\n    #   1: JMP -> 0\r\n    looping_program = [\r\n        Instruction(\"INC\", reg=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"JMP\", target=0),\r\n    ]\r\n\r\n    # Program C: a \"disguised\" infinite loop -- it increments and decrements\r\n    # in a cycle that never zeroes out at the right place, oscillating\r\n    # forever between two register states without ever reaching HALT.\r\n    #   0: INC r0\r\n    #   1: INC r1\r\n    #   2: DEC r0\r\n    #   3: JZ  r0 -> 0     (r0 is back to 0 here every time -> loops forever)\r\n    oscillating_program = [\r\n        Instruction(\"INC\", reg=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"INC\", reg=1),\r\n        Instruction(\"DEC\", reg=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"JZ\", reg=0, target=0),\r\n    ]\r\n\r\n    machine_a = ToyMachine(halting_program, num_registers=1, max_value=7)\r\n    machine_b = ToyMachine(looping_program, num_registers=1, max_value=7)\r\n    machine_c = ToyMachine(oscillating_program, num_registers=2, max_value=7)\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print_decision(\"PROGRAM A (counts down then halts)\", machine_a, decide_halting(machine_a))\r\n    print()\r\n    print_decision(\"PROGRAM B (unconditional infinite loop)\", machine_b, decide_halting(machine_b))\r\n    print()\r\n    print_decision(\"PROGRAM C (oscillates forever, never hits HALT)\", machine_c, decide_halting(machine_c))\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\"-\" * 78)\r\n    print(\r\n        \"Each decision above is a proof, not a guess: either an explicit\\n\"\r\n        \"HALT instruction was reached, or a configuration was shown to\\n\"\r\n        \"repeat, which -- for a deterministic machine -- guarantees it\\n\"\r\n        \"repeats forever. This does not contradict Turing's result: it\\n\"\r\n        \"works only because the register values here are bounded, so the\\n\"\r\n        \"state space is finite. Remove that bound (unbounded registers,\\n\"\r\n        \"i.e. a real counter machine) and this exact technique breaks,\\n\"\r\n        \"because 'seen' can then grow forever without ever repeating --\\n\"\r\n        \"which is the general halting problem again.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n\r\n# =============================================================================\r\n# INTEGRATION -- feed a PROVEN toy result into the quantum simulation\r\n# =============================================================================\r\n#\r\n# This does NOT make the quantum simulation decide anything. The toy decider\r\n# above already proved, with certainty, whether each ToyMachine halts. We\r\n# take that proven ground truth and hand it to the quantum simulation as\r\n# input, to see it demonstrate -- on a real decided case rather than an\r\n# arbitrary hand-picked one -- that its finite-time observable still cannot\r\n# tell the two apart within the observation window. The proof of halting\r\n# vs. non-halting comes entirely from decide_halting(); the quantum section\r\n# contributes zero decision-making, exactly as before.\r\n\r\n\r\ndef toy_result_to_program(name, machine, result):\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    Convert a proven ToyMachine halting result into a Program for the\r\n    quantum simulation. The halt_step is only ever set when decide_halting\r\n    already proved a halt -- the quantum side never determines this itself.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    if result[\"halts\"]:\r\n        return Program(name, result[\"steps\"])\r\n    return Program(name, None)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef run_integrated_demo(observation_steps=50):\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\"=\" * 78)\r\n    print(\"INTEGRATION: PROVEN TOY RESULTS FED INTO THE QUANTUM SIMULATION\")\r\n    print(\"=\" * 78)\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\r\n        \"Ground truth below comes ONLY from decide_halting() (proven, \"\r\n        \"finite-state).\\nThe quantum section is not asked to decide \"\r\n        \"anything -- it is only asked whether\\nits finite-time observable \"\r\n        \"can tell the two proven cases apart within the window.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    # A machine proven to halt, but only after more steps than our\r\n    # observation window -- so within the window it looks, to any\r\n    # finite-time observable, just like a machine that never halts.\r\n    slow_halting_program = [\r\n        Instruction(\"INC\", reg=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"INC\", reg=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"INC\", reg=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"INC\", reg=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"INC\", reg=0),  # r0 = 5\r\n        Instruction(\"JZ\", reg=0, target=8),  # loop: while r0 != 0, decrement\r\n        Instruction(\"DEC\", reg=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"JMP\", target=5),\r\n        Instruction(\"HALT\"),\r\n    ]\r\n    machine_halts = ToyMachine(slow_halting_program, num_registers=1, max_value=7)\r\n    result_halts = decide_halting(machine_halts)\r\n\r\n    # A machine proven to never halt.\r\n    looping_program = [\r\n        Instruction(\"INC\", reg=0),\r\n        Instruction(\"JMP\", target=0),\r\n    ]\r\n    machine_loops = ToyMachine(looping_program, num_registers=1, max_value=7)\r\n    result_loops = decide_halting(machine_loops)\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print_decision(\"TOY MACHINE (will halt)\", machine_halts, result_halts)\r\n    print()\r\n    print_decision(\"TOY MACHINE (proven infinite loop)\", machine_loops, result_loops)\r\n\r\n    halts_when = result_halts[\"steps\"] if result_halts[\"halts\"] else None\r\n    print()\r\n    print(f\"Observation window for quantum stage : {observation_steps} steps\")\r\n    print(f\"Proven halt step of PROGRAM_HALTS    : {halts_when}\")\r\n    print(\r\n        \"PROGRAM_LOOPS proven to never halt (cycle length \"\r\n        f\"{result_loops['cycle_length']} from step {result_loops['cycle_start']})\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    if halts_when is None or halts_when <= observation_steps:\r\n        print(\r\n            \"\\nNote: the proven halt step falls inside the observation \"\r\n            \"window, so the\\nquantum stage WILL show a difference here -- \"\r\n            \"that is expected and consistent,\\nnot a contradiction. The \"\r\n            \"interesting case is when the halt step exceeds the window.\"\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    program_halts = toy_result_to_program(\"PROGRAM_HALTS\", machine_halts, result_halts)\r\n    program_loops = toy_result_to_program(\"PROGRAM_LOOPS\", machine_loops, result_loops)\r\n\r\n    fork = PathOrderedFork()\r\n    branches = fork.branch_sequence(observation_steps)\r\n\r\n    result = compare_at_time(\r\n        fork,\r\n        program_halts,\r\n        program_loops,\r\n        branches,\r\n        observation_steps\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print_observable(\"PROGRAM_HALTS (as seen by the quantum stage)\", result[\"obs1\"])\r\n    print()\r\n    print_observable(\"PROGRAM_LOOPS (as seen by the quantum stage)\", result[\"obs2\"])\r\n    print()\r\n    print(f\"Matrix difference within window = {result['matrix_difference']:.15e}\")\r\n\r\n    print()\r\n    print(\"-\" * 78)\r\n    if result[\"matrix_difference\"] < 1e-9:\r\n        print(\r\n            \"As predicted: within this window the quantum observable cannot\\n\"\r\n            \"tell PROGRAM_HALTS and PROGRAM_LOOPS apart, even though\\n\"\r\n            \"decide_halting() already proved -- with certainty, from the toy\\n\"\r\n            \"machine's finite configuration space -- that one halts and the\\n\"\r\n            \"other does not. The certainty comes entirely from the toy\\n\"\r\n            \"decider; the quantum stage supplies zero information about it.\"\r\n        )\r\n    else:\r\n        print(\r\n            \"The quantum observable differs within this window because the\\n\"\r\n            \"proven halt step of PROGRAM_HALTS falls at or before the\\n\"\r\n            \"observation window -- consistent with the identity in section 4,\\n\"\r\n            \"not a case where the quantum math itself detected anything about\\n\"\r\n            \"the future.\"\r\n        )\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main():\r\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\r\n        description=(\r\n            \"Simulate path-ordered computational evolution, test \"\r\n            \"finite-time halting distinguishability, and separately run \"\r\n            \"a genuine decidable toy halting-problem demo, then integrate \"\r\n            \"the two.\"\r\n        )\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    parser.add_argument(\r\n        \"--steps\",\r\n        type=int,\r\n        default=1000\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    parser.add_argument(\r\n        \"--late-halt\",\r\n        type=int,\r\n        default=2000\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    parser.add_argument(\r\n        \"--skip-quantum\",\r\n        action=\"store_true\",\r\n        help=\"Skip the quantum path-ordered simulation and only run the toy halting demo.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    parser.add_argument(\r\n        \"--skip-toy\",\r\n        action=\"store_true\",\r\n        help=\"Skip the toy halting-problem demo and only run the quantum simulation.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    parser.add_argument(\r\n        \"--skip-integration\",\r\n        action=\"store_true\",\r\n        help=\"Skip the integrated demo that feeds a proven toy result into the quantum stage.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    parser.add_argument(\r\n        \"--integration-window\",\r\n        type=int,\r\n        default=50,\r\n        help=\"Observation window (in steps) used by the integrated demo.\"\r\n    )\r\n\r\n    args = parser.parse_args()\r\n\r\n    if args.steps <= 0:\r\n        raise ValueError(\r\n            \"--steps must be greater than zero\"\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    if args.late_halt <= args.steps:\r\n        raise ValueError(\r\n            \"--late-halt must be greater than --steps\"\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    if not args.skip_quantum:\r\n        run_experiment(\r\n            observation_steps=args.steps,\r\n            late_halt=args.late_halt\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    if not args.skip_toy:\r\n        run_toy_halting_demo()\r\n\r\n    if not args.skip_integration:\r\n        run_integrated_demo(observation_steps=args.integration_window)\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\n"}], "files": [{"file_uuid": "3a13a51f-9714-43a0-8e25-389293f78906", "file_name": ""}], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0ddd3-5095-7a47-bc9e-7d4d815f4f95"}, {"uuid": "01a0ddd5-656d-7a33-b8f6-ba98b85646c1", "text": "Good, legitimate ask \u2014 a fuzzer that generates random toy-machine programs, runs the halting decider on each, and whenever a machine's `configs_seen` hits the full `state_space` (i.e. the decider explored every reachable configuration), immediately feeds it fresh random data and keeps going, checking correctness invariants along the way.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow wire in the CLI flags and dispatch:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow let's actually run it to verify it works and the invariants hold:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nLet's confirm the \"full exploration\" trigger actually fires \u2014 it requires visiting literally every configuration, so let's use smaller state spaces to demonstrate it:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nGood catch worth explaining: `total_configurations()` is an *upper bound* on the state space, not the count of states actually reachable from the initial configuration \u2014 most random programs never touch every syntactically possible state, so \"fully explored\" is rare by construction, not a bug. Let me verify that it *does* fire correctly on machines small enough to make full traversal likely, and add an honest note about this in the summary.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nConfirmed \u2014 the trigger works correctly on machines small enough for full traversal. Let's add a note to the fuzzer's summary explaining this so the `0` count above doesn't look like a bug, and lower the `max_value_cap` a bit to make it easier to actually witness in a fuzzing run:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow let's add CLI control for the fuzz size parameters and confirm end-to-end with settings tuned to actually trigger full exploration:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nVerified: zero invariant failures across every run, with different machine sizes and seeds.\n\nTo be precise about what \"fuzz incoming data after each max Configurations seen\" now does in the code:\n\n- **Every trial**, right after `decide_halting()` returns (its result includes the `configs_seen` count, same field printed by `print_decision`), the fuzzer immediately discards that machine and generates a brand-new random one \u2014 it never reuses or \"idles\" on a finished machine. That's the core loop, confirmed by the verbose output above (500 fresh machines run back-to-back).\n- **Additionally** (a stricter, secondary metric), it tracks the special case where `configs_seen` reaches the machine's full theoretical `state_space` \u2014 meaning literally every syntactically possible configuration was visited, not just the ones reachable from the start. That's rarer, since `total_configurations()` is an upper bound, not a reachability count \u2014 which is why the summary correctly reported `0` at first, and my added note now explains why that's expected rather than hiding it.\n- Every trial checks real invariants against the proof (`configs_seen` never exceeds `state_space`; every decision is a genuine HALT or a genuine proven cycle) and reports any violation loudly rather than silently passing.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n- `--fuzz N` \u2014 run N random toy-machine trials instead of the demos\n- `--fuzz-seed S` \u2014 reproducible run\n- `--fuzz-verbose` \u2014 print every trial's `configs_seen` / decision, not just the summary\n- `--fuzz-max-value V` / `--fuzz-max-registers R` \u2014 shrink the search space, which makes full-state-space traversal (\"fully explored\") much more likely to actually appear", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:07.450647Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:18.246866Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Untangling an ambiguous request about fuzzing configuration data."}, {"summary": "Designing a continuous fuzz-testing loop for the halting decider."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:18.246924Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:19.429178Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Good, legitimate ask \u2014 a fuzzer that generates random toy-machine programs, runs the halting decider on each, and whenever a machine's `configs_seen` hits the full `state_space` (i.e. the decider explored every reachable configuration), immediately feeds it fresh random data and keeps going, checking correctness invariants along the way.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:19.429235Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:19.952267Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_017UU88Ubg7qx3zwpWPD3YVv", "name": "view", "input": {"path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/halting_demo.py", "view_range": [1, 5]}, "message": "Viewing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:20.311540Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:20.311590Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_017UU88Ubg7qx3zwpWPD3YVv", "name": "view", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "     1\timport numpy as np\n     2\timport argparse\n     3\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n     4\t\n     5\t\n[909 lines total]"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"import numpy as np\\nimport argparse\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\n\\n\\n\", \"filename\": \"/mnt/user-data/outputs/halting_demo.py\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:22.622097Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:43.774801Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01GqSCNbFuH7HEyqxc6o5pCG", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/halting_demo.py", "old_str": "def main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=(\n            \"Simulate path-ordered computational evolution, test \"\n            \"finite-time halting distinguishability, and separately run \"\n            \"a genuine decidable toy halting-problem demo, then integrate \"\n            \"the two.\"\n        )\n    )", "new_str": "# =============================================================================\n# FUZZING -- generate random toy machines, decide each, and keep feeding\n# fresh random data every time a machine's configuration space is fully\n# explored\n# =============================================================================\n#\n# This tests decide_halting() itself, not general halting. Every ToyMachine\n# has a finite, computable state_space = num_instructions * (max_value+1)**\n# num_registers. decide_halting() is guaranteed (proven earlier) to reach a\n# decision -- HALT or a proven cycle -- within state_space + 1 steps, and\n# configs_seen can never exceed that bound. A fuzzer is a good fit here\n# because these are checkable, mechanical invariants: generate random\n# (but syntactically valid) programs, run the real decider on each, and\n# assert the guarantees the proof makes actually hold in code. Whenever a\n# run's configs_seen reaches its machine's full state_space -- i.e. the\n# decider has now seen every configuration that program could ever reach --\n# a brand-new random machine is generated immediately and fuzzing\n# continues, rather than stopping.\n\nimport random\n\n\ndef random_instruction(program_length, num_registers, rng):\n    op = rng.choice([\"INC\", \"DEC\", \"JZ\", \"JMP\", \"JMP\", \"HALT\"])\n    reg = rng.randrange(num_registers)\n    target = rng.randrange(program_length)\n    return Instruction(op, reg=reg, target=target)\n\n\ndef random_toy_machine(rng, max_program_length=8, max_registers=3, max_value_cap=6):\n    program_length = rng.randint(2, max_program_length)\n    num_registers = rng.randint(1, max_registers)\n    max_value = rng.randint(1, max_value_cap)\n\n    program = [\n        random_instruction(program_length, num_registers, rng)\n        for _ in range(program_length - 1)\n    ]\n    # Guarantee at least one HALT exists somewhere in the program so both\n    # outcomes (reachable or unreachable HALT) show up across many trials,\n    # without forcing every trial to actually reach it.\n    program.append(Instruction(\"HALT\"))\n\n    return ToyMachine(program, num_registers=num_registers, max_value=max_value)\n\n\ndef check_invariants(machine, result):\n    \"\"\"\n    Assert the guarantees decide_halting()'s proof makes are actually true\n    in practice. Any failure here would mean a real bug in the decider,\n    not a property of the fuzzed program.\n    \"\"\"\n    state_space = machine.total_configurations()\n\n    assert result[\"state_space\"] == state_space, (\n        \"reported state_space does not match the machine's actual \"\n        \"configuration count\"\n    )\n    assert result[\"configs_seen\"] <= state_space, (\n        f\"configs_seen ({result['configs_seen']}) exceeded the machine's \"\n        f\"total state space ({state_space}) -- this should be impossible\"\n    )\n\n    if result[\"halts\"]:\n        assert result[\"steps\"] >= 0\n    else:\n        assert result[\"cycle_length\"] >= 1\n        assert result[\"cycle_start\"] >= 0\n        assert result[\"cycle_start\"] + result[\"cycle_length\"] == result[\"steps\"] if \"steps\" in result else True\n\n\ndef fuzz_toy_machines(num_trials=200, seed=None, max_program_length=8, max_registers=3, max_value_cap=6, verbose=False):\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n\n    stats = {\n        \"trials\": 0,\n        \"halts\": 0,\n        \"loops\": 0,\n        \"fully_explored\": 0,  # configs_seen == state_space exactly\n        \"max_state_space_seen\": 0,\n        \"failures\": [],\n    }\n\n    print(\"=\" * 78)\n    print(\"FUZZING decide_halting() ON RANDOM TOY MACHINES\")\n    print(\"=\" * 78)\n    print(f\"Trials requested: {num_trials}\" + (f\"  (seed={seed})\" if seed is not None else \"  (random seed)\"))\n    print()\n\n    trial = 0\n    while trial < num_trials:\n        machine = random_toy_machine(\n            rng,\n            max_program_length=max_program_length,\n            max_registers=max_registers,\n            max_value_cap=max_value_cap,\n        )\n\n        try:\n            result = decide_halting(machine)\n            check_invariants(machine, result)\n        except Exception as e:\n            stats[\"failures\"].append({\"trial\": trial, \"error\": repr(e), \"machine\": machine})\n            print(f\"  [trial {trial}] FAILURE: {e!r}\")\n            trial += 1\n            continue\n\n        stats[\"trials\"] += 1\n        stats[\"max_state_space_seen\"] = max(stats[\"max_state_space_seen\"], result[\"state_space\"])\n\n        if result[\"halts\"]:\n            stats[\"halts\"] += 1\n        else:\n            stats[\"loops\"] += 1\n\n        fully_explored = result[\"configs_seen\"] == result[\"state_space\"]\n        if fully_explored:\n            stats[\"fully_explored\"] += 1\n\n        if verbose:\n            tag = \"HALTS\" if result[\"halts\"] else \"LOOPS\"\n            explored_note = \" [FULL STATE SPACE EXPLORED]\" if fully_explored else \"\"\n            print(\n                f\"  [trial {trial}] regs={machine.num_registers} \"\n                f\"max_value={machine.max_value} state_space={result['state_space']} \"\n                f\"configs_seen={result['configs_seen']} -> {tag}{explored_note}\"\n            )\n\n        if fully_explored:\n            # The decider has now seen every configuration this machine\n            # could ever reach -- there is nothing more this machine can\n            # teach the fuzzer. Immediately generate fresh random data and\n            # keep going, rather than idling on an exhausted machine.\n            if verbose:\n                print(\n                    f\"  [trial {trial}] configs_seen reached max \"\n                    f\"({result['configs_seen']}/{result['state_space']}) \"\n                    f\"-- feeding a new random machine\"\n                )\n\n        trial += 1\n\n    print()\n    print(\"-\" * 78)\n    print(\"FUZZING SUMMARY\")\n    print(\"-\" * 78)\n    print(f\"  Trials completed          : {stats['trials']}\")\n    print(f\"  HALTS                     : {stats['halts']}\")\n    print(f\"  LOOPS (proven)            : {stats['loops']}\")\n    print(f\"  Fully explored state space: {stats['fully_explored']}\")\n    print(f\"  Largest state space seen  : {stats['max_state_space_seen']}\")\n    print(f\"  Invariant failures        : {len(stats['failures'])}\")\n\n    if stats[\"failures\"]:\n        print()\n        print(\"FAILURES DETECTED -- decide_halting() violated its own proof:\")\n        for f in stats[\"failures\"]:\n            print(f\"  trial {f['trial']}: {f['error']}\")\n    else:\n        print()\n        print(\n            \"No invariant failures: every trial's result was consistent with\\n\"\n            \"the proof decide_halting() relies on (configs_seen never exceeded\\n\"\n            \"state_space, and every decision was either a HALT or a proven cycle).\"\n        )\n\n    return stats\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=(\n            \"Simulate path-ordered computational evolution, test \"\n            \"finite-time halting distinguishability, and separately run \"\n            \"a genuine decidable toy halting-problem demo, then integrate \"\n            \"the two.\"\n        )\n    )"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:44.022027Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:44.022086Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01GqSCNbFuH7HEyqxc6o5pCG", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/halting_demo.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/halting_demo.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:45.790360Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:46.080079Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now wire in the CLI flags and dispatch:", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:46.080115Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:49.299347Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_019DkDLoqdYov2Jw8esusE1q", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/halting_demo.py", "old_str": "    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--integration-window\",\n        type=int,\n        default=50,\n        help=\"Observation window (in steps) used by the integrated demo.\"\n    )\n\n    args = parser.parse_args()", "new_str": "    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--integration-window\",\n        type=int,\n        default=50,\n        help=\"Observation window (in steps) used by the integrated demo.\"\n    )\n\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--fuzz\",\n        type=int,\n        default=0,\n        metavar=\"N\",\n        help=\"Fuzz decide_halting() with N random toy machines instead of running the demos.\"\n    )\n\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--fuzz-seed\",\n        type=int,\n        default=None,\n        help=\"Optional seed for reproducible fuzzing runs.\"\n    )\n\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--fuzz-verbose\",\n        action=\"store_true\",\n        help=\"Print a line for every fuzz trial, not just the summary.\"\n    )\n\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    if args.fuzz > 0:\n        fuzz_toy_machines(\n            num_trials=args.fuzz,\n            seed=args.fuzz_seed,\n            verbose=args.fuzz_verbose,\n        )\n        return"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:49.558242Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:49.558287Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_019DkDLoqdYov2Jw8esusE1q", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/halting_demo.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/halting_demo.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:51.330968Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:51.694539Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now let's actually run it to verify it works and the invariants hold:", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:51.694573Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:52.600823Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Tz9UcvQed9LmbpVsJVVrZM", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/halting_demo.py --fuzz 500 --fuzz-seed 42", "description": "Run the fuzzer with a fixed seed for reproducibility and check for invariant failures"}, "message": "Run the fuzzer with a fixed seed for reproducibility and check for invariant failures", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/halting_demo.py --fuzz 500 --fuzz-seed 42\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:53.011226Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:53.011285Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Tz9UcvQed9LmbpVsJVVrZM", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"==============================================================================\\nFUZZING decide_halting() ON RANDOM TOY MACHINES\\n==============================================================================\\nTrials requested: 500  (seed=42)\\n\\n\\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nFUZZING SUMMARY\\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n  Trials completed          : 500\\n  HALTS                     : 346\\n  LOOPS (proven)            : 154\\n  Fully explored state space: 0\\n  Largest state space seen  : 2744\\n  Invariant failures        : 0\\n\\nNo invariant failures: every trial's result was consistent with\\nthe proof decide_halting() relies on (configs_seen never exceeded\\nstate_space, and every decision was either a HALT or a proven cycle).\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"==============================================================================\\nFUZZING decide_halting() ON RANDOM TOY MACHINES\\n==============================================================================\\nTrials requested: 500  (seed=42)\\n\\n\\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nFUZZING SUMMARY\\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n  Trials completed          : 500\\n  HALTS                     : 346\\n  LOOPS (proven)            : 154\\n  Fully explored state space: 0\\n  Largest state space seen  : 2744\\n  Invariant failures        : 0\\n\\nNo invariant failures: every trial's result was consistent with\\nthe proof decide_halting() relies on (configs_seen never exceeded\\nstate_space, and every decision was either a HALT or a proven cycle).\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:54.593495Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:56.825597Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Investigating why the fully-explored-state-space trigger never activates."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:56.825642Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:57.466385Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Let's confirm the \"full exploration\" trigger actually fires \u2014 it requires visiting literally every configuration, so let's use smaller state spaces to demonstrate it:", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:57.466416Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:58.494392Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_013SyZHma6367kzBeFJPSA3P", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/halting_demo.py --fuzz 30 --fuzz-seed 7 --fuzz-verbose 2>&1 | head -60", "description": "Run verbose fuzzing to see per-trial output and check whether full-exploration cases appear"}, "message": "Run verbose fuzzing to see per-trial output and check whether full-exploration cases appear", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/halting_demo.py --fuzz 30 --fuzz-seed 7 --fuzz-verbose 2>&1 | head -60\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:58.825260Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-26T13:09:58.825310Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_013SyZHma6367kzBeFJPSA3P", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"==============================================================================\\nFUZZING decide_halting() ON RANDOM TOY MACHINES\\n==============================================================================\\nTrials requested: 30  (seed=7)\\n\\n  [trial 0] regs=1 max_value=4 state_space=20 configs_seen=1 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 1] regs=1 max_value=4 state_space=10 configs_seen=1 -> LOOPS\\n  [trial 2] regs=3 max_value=4 state_space=250 configs_seen=2 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 3] regs=3 max_value=6 state_space=1029 configs_seen=2 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 4] regs=1 max_value=5 state_space=18 configs_seen=3 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 5] regs=3 max_value=6 state_space=1372 configs_seen=2 -> LOOPS\\n  [trial 6] regs=3 max_value=5 state_space=1080 configs_seen=2 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 7] regs=2 max_value=5 state_space=216 configs_seen=2 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 8] regs=3 max_value=1 state_space=16 configs_seen=2 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 9] regs=3 max_value=3 state_space=256 configs_seen=2 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 10] regs=3 max_value=6 state_space=686 configs_seen=2 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 11] regs=3 max_value=4 state_space=500 configs_seen=1 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 12] regs=1 max_value=3 state_space=8 configs_seen=2 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 13] regs=2 max_value=1 state_space=20 configs_seen=2 -> LOOPS\\n  [trial 14] regs=1 max_value=2 state_space=9 configs_seen=3 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 15] regs=3 max_value=2 state_space=216 configs_seen=1 -> LOOPS\\n  [trial 16] regs=1 max_value=1 state_space=4 configs_seen=2 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 17] regs=2 max_value=5 state_space=72 configs_seen=2 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 18] regs=1 max_value=5 state_space=36 configs_seen=10 -> LOOPS\\n  [trial 19] regs=1 max_value=4 state_space=10 configs_seen=2 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 20] regs=1 max_value=2 state_space=12 configs_seen=5 -> LOOPS\\n  [trial 21] regs=3 max_value=1 state_space=56 configs_seen=2 -> LOOPS\\n  [trial 22] regs=3 max_value=2 state_space=81 configs_seen=3 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 23] regs=2 max_value=6 state_space=245 configs_seen=2 -> LOOPS\\n  [trial 24] regs=1 max_value=1 state_space=4 configs_seen=2 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 25] regs=1 max_value=4 state_space=20 configs_seen=2 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 26] regs=3 max_value=2 state_space=216 configs_seen=3 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 27] regs=3 max_value=4 state_space=750 configs_seen=1 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 28] regs=1 max_value=2 state_space=24 configs_seen=5 -> HALTS\\n  [trial 29] regs=1 max_value=2 state_space=24 configs_seen=5 -> HALTS\\n\\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nFUZZING SUMMARY\\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n  Trials completed          : 30\\n  HALTS                     : 22\\n  LOOPS (proven)            : 8\\n  Fully explored state space: 0\\n  Largest state space seen  : 1372\\n  Invariant failures        : 0\\n\\nNo invariant failures: every trial's result was consistent with\\nthe proof decide_halting() re