"integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/neural_circuit_project.zip']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T04:59:13.337431Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T04:59:13.337461Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_0176V6udJJFtMZVVqWsZFj2c", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/neural_circuit_project.zip", "name": "neural circuit project", "mime_type": "application/zip", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "The file cards appear at the end of your reply if it ends with text, otherwise under this step; say they are below only if you finish the reply with text."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T04:59:14.709548Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T04:59:14.905527Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Updated zip with the full-resolution (24,408-node) 3D page included.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-09-27T04:59:14.928408Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T04:59:14.928408Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0e13b-2f16-7cfb-bbdd-38cdd9af1948"}, {"uuid": "01a0e13d-dc10-7bd1-9e9c-d27f88cb129d", "text": "good now do self electrical stimulation simulation", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:03.999649Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:03.999649Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "good now do self electrical stimulation simulation", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-09-27T05:02:03.999839Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T05:02:03.999839Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0e13b-2f16-7fcb-a07d-9b01b40415cf"}, {"uuid": "01a0e13d-dc10-7481-9342-c19cb544b75d", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nAdding a periodic self-stimulation mode to the existing propagation model \u2014 instead of one initial pulse at the seed (which is what we had), the seed node re-injects current into itself on a fixed schedule, like a repeatedly-pulsing stimulating electrode (the same idea behind deep-brain-stimulation modeling), and I'll compare that against the single-pulse baseline.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow let's add a comparison run + plot in `main`, alongside the existing pipeline.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow update the plot to include the comparison.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow let's run it and check the results.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThe two curves are identical \u2014 because the propagation model is already in a supercritical regime (any single pulse cascades to saturate the whole graph), so extra self-stimulation pulses get swamped and add nothing visible. Let me find a more meaningful regime: one where a single pulse dies out on its own, but self-stimulation sustains ongoing activity \u2014 which is the actual point of modeling stimulation.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nFound it: `decay=0.6, gain=0.4, threshold=0.55` \u2014 a single pulse dies out completely, but the periodic self-stimulation sustains a small persistent firing zone indefinitely. That's the actual scientifically meaningful contrast. Let's lock that in.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nIt stabilizes into a clean repeating oscillation (period matches the 6-step stimulation interval) \u2014 a genuinely self-sustaining local circuit driven purely by periodic self-stimulation. Let's update the script with these parameters and rerun.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nSince the single-pulse activity now dies out almost instantly, the 3D wavefront panel needs to color by the self-stimulation history instead (which is the one with something interesting to show).\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nAlso update the panel title reference for consistency.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow rerun the full script to check everything works together.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n`argmax` picked step 0 (the very first pulse) since that already exceeds half the oscillation's peak \u2014 not useful. Let me pick a snapshot from later in the steady-state oscillation instead.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nLet's view the final result.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nTwo problems: the y-axis scale gets crushed by the (now irrelevant) saturation-ceiling reference line, and the handful of self-stimulation active nodes are too sparse to show up in a random background subsample. Let's fix both.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow explicitly highlight the handful of actually-active nodes on top of the background cloud, since they're too sparse to be caught by a random subsample.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow let's rerun.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThis clearly shows the effect now. Let's copy final files to outputs and give you a bundle.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nAdded `simulate_self_stimulation()`: instead of one initial pulse, the seed node keeps re-injecting current into itself every 6 steps, like a repeatedly-pulsing stimulating electrode (the same concept behind computational deep-brain-stimulation models).\n\nTwo bugs came up while making the comparison mean something, both fixed:\n\n1. **No visible effect at first** \u2014 with the original propagation parameters, a single pulse already cascades to saturate the entire graph, so extra self-stimulation pulses got swamped and looked identical. Fixed by dropping into a subcritical parameter regime (`decay=0.6, gain=0.4, threshold=0.55`) where a single pulse genuinely dies out \u2014 so any activity that persists is attributable to the self-stimulation itself. The middle plot (right after the fix) shows exactly that: the blue single-pulse curve decays to zero, the orange self-stimulation curve settles into a stable repeating oscillation.\n2. **Active nodes invisible in the 3D panel** \u2014 the sustained circuit is tiny (4 nodes), so a random background subsample almost never included them. Now they're explicitly pulled out and drawn as large highlighted markers along the beam-searched path.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:03.994779Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:24.108897Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Interpreting a request about simulating electrical stimulation in neural models."}, {"summary": "Weighing benign versus concerning readings of the stimulation request."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:24.108977Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:24.933903Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_014S8LkvUgREFBSmoVJAwcev", "name": "view", "input": {"description": "Review current script before adding a stimulation model", "path": "/home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py", "view_range": [120, 150]}, "message": "Review current script before adding a stimulation model", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Review current script before adding a stimulation model"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:26.365922Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:26.365960Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_014S8LkvUgREFBSmoVJAwcev", "name": "view", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "   120\t\n   121\t\n   122\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   123\t# 3. Real-time activation propagation (leaky-integrate-and-fire-ish)\n   124\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   125\tdef simulate_realtime_activity(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60,\n   126\t                                decay=0.85, threshold=0.5, gain=1.3):\n   127\t    \"\"\"\n   128\t    Simple discrete-time propagation: nodes above `threshold` \"fire\" and\n   129\t    push weighted activation to neighbors each step, while all activation\n   130\t    leaks away by `decay`. This is a coarse stand-in for real-time neural\n   131\t    circuit dynamics, not a biophysical model.\n   132\t    \"\"\"\n   133\t    n = len(adjacency)\n   134\t    activity = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n   135\t    activity[seed_idx] = 1.0\n   136\t    history = [activity.copy()]\n   137\t\n   138\t    for _ in range(steps):\n   139\t        new_activity = activity * decay\n   140\t        firing = np.where(activity > threshold)[0]\n   141\t        for i in firing:\n   142\t            for j, w in adjacency[i]:\n   143\t                new_activity[j] += gain * w * activity[i]\n   144\t        activity = np.clip(new_activity, 0, 3)\n   145\t        history.append(activity.copy())\n   146\t\n   147\t    return np.array(history)\n   148\t\n   149\t\n   150\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[338 lines total]"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# 3. Real-time activation propagation (leaky-integrate-and-fire-ish)\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef simulate_realtime_activity(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60,\\n                                decay=0.85, threshold=0.5, gain=1.3):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Simple discrete-time propagation: nodes above `threshold` \\\"fire\\\" and\\n    push weighted activation to neighbors each step, while all activation\\n    leaks away by `decay`. This is a coarse stand-in for real-time neural\\n    circuit dynamics, not a biophysical model.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    n = len(adjacency)\\n    activity = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\\n    activity[seed_idx] = 1.0\\n    history = [activity.copy()]\\n\\n    for _ in range(steps):\\n        new_activity = activity * decay\\n        firing = np.where(activity > threshold)[0]\\n        for i in firing:\\n            for j, w in adjacency[i]:\\n                new_activity[j] += gain * w * activity[i]\\n        activity = np.clip(new_activity, 0, 3)\\n        history.append(activity.copy())\\n\\n    return np.array(history)\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\", \"filename\": \"/home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:28.113852Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:29.782207Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Modeling a neural network with periodic self-stimulation."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:29.782255Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:31.194076Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Adding a periodic self-stimulation mode to the existing propagation model \u2014 instead of one initial pulse at the seed (which is what we had), the seed node re-injects current into itself on a fixed schedule, like a repeatedly-pulsing stimulating electrode (the same idea behind deep-brain-stimulation modeling), and I'll compare that against the single-pulse baseline.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:31.194105Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:38.790432Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_019w8wquLzx8FzkxVXE81bD5", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"new_str": "def simulate_realtime_activity(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60,\n                                decay=0.85, threshold=0.5, gain=1.3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Simple discrete-time propagation: nodes above `threshold` \"fire\" and\n    push weighted activation to neighbors each step, while all activation\n    leaks away by `decay`. This is a coarse stand-in for real-time neural\n    circuit dynamics, not a biophysical model.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(adjacency)\n    activity = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n    activity[seed_idx] = 1.0\n    history = [activity.copy()]\n\n    for _ in range(steps):\n        new_activity = activity * decay\n        firing = np.where(activity > threshold)[0]\n        for i in firing:\n            for j, w in adjacency[i]:\n                new_activity[j] += gain * w * activity[i]\n        activity = np.clip(new_activity, 0, 3)\n        history.append(activity.copy())\n\n    return np.array(history)\n\n\ndef simulate_self_stimulation(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60,\n                               decay=0.85, threshold=0.5, gain=1.3,\n                               stim_interval=8, stim_amplitude=1.0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Same propagation model as `simulate_realtime_activity`, but instead of a\n    single initial pulse the seed node re-injects current into itself every\n    `stim_interval` steps -- a coarse model of a repeatedly-pulsing\n    stimulating electrode (the same idea used in deep-brain-stimulation\n    modeling), rather than a one-off triggering event.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(adjacency)\n    activity = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n    activity[seed_idx] = stim_amplitude\n    history = [activity.copy()]\n\n    for t in range(steps):\n        new_activity = activity * decay\n        firing = np.where(activity > threshold)[0]\n        for i in firing:\n            for j, w in adjacency[i]:\n                new_activity[j] += gain * w * activity[i]\n\n        # periodic self-stimulation pulse at the seed node\n        if (t + 1) % stim_interval == 0:\n            new_activity[seed_idx] += stim_amplitude\n\n        activity = np.clip(new_activity, 0, 3)\n        history.append(activity.copy())\n\n    return np.array(history)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------", "old_str": "def simulate_realtime_activity(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60,\n                                decay=0.85, threshold=0.5, gain=1.3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Simple discrete-time propagation: nodes above `threshold` \"fire\" and\n    push weighted activation to neighbors each step, while all activation\n    leaks away by `decay`. This is a coarse stand-in for real-time neural\n    circuit dynamics, not a biophysical model.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(adjacency)\n    activity = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n    activity[seed_idx] = 1.0\n    history = [activity.copy()]\n\n    for _ in range(steps):\n        new_activity = activity * decay\n        firing = np.where(activity > threshold)[0]\n        for i in firing:\n            for j, w in adjacency[i]:\n                new_activity[j] += gain * w * activity[i]\n        activity = np.clip(new_activity, 0, 3)\n        history.append(activity.copy())\n\n    return np.array(history)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------", "path": "/home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:39.119863Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:39.119904Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_019w8wquLzx8FzkxVXE81bD5", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:40.988228Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:41.451090Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now let's add a comparison run + plot in `main`, alongside the existing pipeline.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:41.451118Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:42.207789Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01WY8gvQZTyDEt4qFgHimmMJ", "name": "view", "input": {"description": "Find the main block's activity-simulation section to insert the comparison", "path": "/home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py", "view_range": [280, 300]}, "message": "Find the main block's activity-simulation section to insert the comparison", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Find the main block's activity-simulation section to insert the comparison"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:42.466631Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:42.466679Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01WY8gvQZTyDEt4qFgHimmMJ", "name": "view", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "   280\t\n   281\t    adjacency = load_adjacency_from_disk(EDGES_PATH, len(coords))\n   282\t\n   283\t    seed_idx, target_idx, comp_size = largest_component_endpoints(adjacency, coords)\n   284\t    print(f\"Largest connected component: {comp_size}/{len(coords)} nodes\")\n   285\t    print(f\"Seed node: {coords[seed_idx]}  Target node: {coords[target_idx]}\")\n   286\t\n   287\t    print(\"\\nRunning real-time activation propagation...\")\n   288\t    history = simulate_realtime_activity(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60)\n   289\t    total_activity = history.sum(axis=1)\n   290\t\n   291\t    # Manhattan distance in stride-units tells us the minimum hops needed,\n   292\t    # so the beam search is given enough budget to actually reach the target.\n   293\t    dz, dy, dx = (abs(a - b) for a, b in zip(coords[seed_idx], coords[target_idx]))\n   294\t    min_hops = (dz + dy + dx) // STRIDE\n   295\t\n   296\t    print(\"Running beam search for the strongest signal path...\")\n   297\t    # beam_width=200: on real anatomical data the graph is close to a plain\n   298\t    # 3D grid, so the true shortest path is thin and a narrow beam (60, the\n   299\t    # value that worked on the synthetic phantom) prunes it away before it\n   300\t    # can reach the target. 200 was the smallest width in testing that\n[370 lines total]"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"\\n    adjacency = load_adjacency_from_disk(EDGES_PATH, len(coords))\\n\\n    seed_idx, target_idx, comp_size = largest_component_endpoints(adjacency, coords)\\n    print(f\\\"Largest connected component: {comp_size}/{len(coords)} nodes\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Seed node: {coords[seed_idx]}  Target node: {coords[target_idx]}\\\")\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nRunning real-time activation propagation...\\\")\\n    history = simulate_realtime_activity(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60)\\n    total_activity = history.sum(axis=1)\\n\\n    # Manhattan distance in stride-units tells us the minimum hops needed,\\n    # so the beam search is given enough budget to actually reach the target.\\n    dz, dy, dx = (abs(a - b) for a, b in zip(coords[seed_idx], coords[target_idx]))\\n    min_hops = (dz + dy + dx) // STRIDE\\n\\n    print(\\\"Running beam search for the strongest signal path...\\\")\\n    # beam_width=200: on real anatomical data the graph is close to a plain\\n    # 3D grid, so the true shortest path is thin and a narrow beam (60, the\\n    # value that worked on the synthetic phantom) prunes it away before it\\n    # can reach the target. 200 was the smallest width in testing that\\n\", \"filename\": \"/home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:44.313727Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:46.332382Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_014uwH8i7ZLTkkzGNWdbHRHp", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"new_str": "    print(\"\\nRunning real-time activation propagation (single pulse)...\")\n    history = simulate_realtime_activity(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60)\n    total_activity = history.sum(axis=1)\n\n    print(\"Running self-stimulation propagation (periodic pulses at seed)...\")\n    stim_history = simulate_self_stimulation(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60, stim_interval=8)\n    stim_total_activity = stim_history.sum(axis=1)", "old_str": "    print(\"\\nRunning real-time activation propagation...\")\n    history = simulate_realtime_activity(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60)\n    total_activity = history.sum(axis=1)", "path": "/home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:46.615328Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:46.615365Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_014uwH8i7ZLTkkzGNWdbHRHp", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:48.493703Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:48.736020Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now update the plot to include the comparison.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:48.736053Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:49.446471Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01L5Z3MtqTiRVj9jcmSRcK3u", "name": "view", "input": {"description": "Find the plotting section", "path": "/home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py", "view_range": [310, 340]}, "message": "Find the plotting section", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Find the plotting section"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:49.674289Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:49.674338Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01L5Z3MtqTiRVj9jcmSRcK3u", "name": "view", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "   310\t    if path_idx:\n   311\t        print(f\"Found path in {hops} hops ({len(path_idx)} nodes).\")\n   312\t    else:\n   313\t        print(\"No path found within hop budget.\")\n   314\t\n   315\t    # --- visualize in true 3D (coords are already (z, y, x) triples; the\n   316\t    # graph, propagation and beam search were all 3D already -- only the\n   317\t    # old rendering flattened it onto one slice) ---\n   318\t    from mpl_toolkits.mplot3d import Axes3D  # noqa: F401 (registers 3d proj)\n   319\t\n   320\t    coords_arr = np.array(coords, dtype=float)\n   321\t    intensities = np.array([volume[tuple(c)] for c in coords])\n   322\t    # A threshold cascade like this one saturates almost the entire graph\n   323\t    # once it fully settles (final step: ~every node at max activation), so\n   324\t    # coloring by the *final* state is visually uninformative -- it's just\n   325\t    # one flat color. The propagating wavefront partway through is what\n   326\t    # actually shows the circuit \"lighting up\" in real time.\n   327\t    snapshot_step = int(np.argmax(total_activity > 0.5 * total_activity.max()))\n   328\t    snapshot_activity = history[snapshot_step]\n   329\t    print(f\"Coloring 3D activity snapshot at step {snapshot_step}/{len(history)-1} \"\n   330\t          f\"(wavefront, not the fully-settled end state).\")\n   331\t\n   332\t    # subsample the point cloud for a legible, fast-to-render scatter\n   333\t    rng = np.random.default_rng(0)\n   334\t    n_show = min(4000, len(coords))\n   335\t    sample = rng.choice(len(coords), size=n_show, replace=False)\n   336\t\n   337\t    fig = plt.figure(figsize=(15, 5.5))\n   338\t\n   339\t    # Panel 1: the 3D structural graph (node cloud), colored by MRI intensity\n   340\t    ax0 = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 1, projection=\"3d\")\n[374 lines total]"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"    if path_idx:\\n        print(f\\\"Found path in {hops} hops ({len(path_idx)} nodes).\\\")\\n    else:\\n        print(\\\"No path found within hop budget.\\\")\\n\\n    # --- visualize in true 3D (coords are already (z, y, x) triples; the\\n    # graph, propagation and beam search were all 3D already -- only the\\n    # old rendering flattened it onto one slice) ---\\n    from mpl_toolkits.mplot3d import Axes3D  # noqa: F401 (registers 3d proj)\\n\\n    coords_arr = np.array(coords, dtype=float)\\n    intensities = np.array([volume[tuple(c)] for c in coords])\\n    # A threshold cascade like this one saturates almost the entire graph\\n    # once it fully settles (final step: ~every node at max activation), so\\n    # coloring by the *final* state is visually uninformative -- it's just\\n    # one flat color. The propagating wavefront partway through is what\\n    # actually shows the circuit \\\"lighting up\\\" in real time.\\n    snapshot_step = int(np.argmax(total_activity > 0.5 * total_activity.max()))\\n    snapshot_activity = history[snapshot_step]\\n    print(f\\\"Coloring 3D activity snapshot at step {snapshot_step}/{len(history)-1} \\\"\\n          f\\\"(wavefront, not the fully-settled end state).\\\")\\n\\n    # subsample the point cloud for a legible, fast-to-render scatter\\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(0)\\n    n_show = min(4000, len(coords))\\n    sample = rng.choice(len(coords), size=n_show, replace=False)\\n\\n    fig = plt.figure(figsize=(15, 5.5))\\n\\n    # Panel 1: the 3D structural graph (node cloud), colored by MRI intensity\\n    ax0 = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 1, projection=\\\"3d\\\")\\n\", \"filename\": \"/home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:51.567837Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:54.277486Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01PdFN7BXLr2tuj7LotM1tin", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"new_str": "    ax1 = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 2)\n    ax1.plot(total_activity, label=\"single pulse\")\n    ax1.plot(stim_total_activity, label=\"self-stimulation (periodic pulses)\")\n    ax1.axhline(len(coords) * 3, color=\"gray\", linestyle=\":\", linewidth=1, label=\"all-nodes-saturated ceiling\")\n    ax1.set_title(\"Total network activity: single pulse vs. self-stimulation\")\n    ax1.set_xlabel(\"time step\")\n    ax1.set_ylabel(\"summed activation\")\n    ax1.legend(fontsize=8)", "old_str": "    ax1 = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 2)\n    ax1.plot(total_activity)\n    ax1.set_title(\"Total network activity over time\")\n    ax1.set_xlabel(\"time step\")\n    ax1.set_ylabel(\"summed activation\")", "path": "/home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:54.547745Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:54.547777Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01PdFN7BXLr2tuj7LotM1tin", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:56.199244Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:56.471962Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now let's run it and check the results.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:56.471998Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:02:57.005676Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Nv96KmSWZTaZWjxRRorYX3", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude && python3 neural_circuit_simulation.py", "description": "Run script with self-stimulation comparison added"}, "message": "Run script with self-stimulation comparison added", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude && python3 neural_circuit_simulation.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:00.981095Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:00.981138Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Nv96KmSWZTaZWjxRRorYX3", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"=== Neural Circuit Simulation on Real MRI Volume ===\\n\\nLoaded and downsampled real MRI to shape (60, 60, 39)\\nVolume shape: (60, 60, 39), active graph nodes: 24408\\nStreamed 139342 directed edges to disk (1632.9 KB)\\nLargest connected component: 24407/24408 nodes\\nSeed node: (13, 29, 12)  Target node: (45, 41, 23)\\n\\nRunning real-time activation propagation (single pulse)...\\nRunning self-stimulation propagation (periodic pulses at seed)...\\nRunning beam search for the strongest signal path...\\nFound path in 55 hops (56 nodes).\\nColoring 3D activity snapshot at step 35/60 (wavefront, not the fully-settled end state).\\n\\nSaved visualization to /mnt/user-data/outputs/neural_circuit_simulation.png\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"=== Neural Circuit Simulation on Real MRI Volume ===\\n\\nLoaded and downsampled real MRI to shape (60, 60, 39)\\nVolume shape: (60, 60, 39), active graph nodes: 24408\\nStreamed 139342 directed edges to disk (1632.9 KB)\\nLargest connected component: 24407/24408 nodes\\nSeed node: (13, 29, 12)  Target node: (45, 41, 23)\\n\\nRunning real-time activation propagation (single pulse)...\\nRunning self-stimulation propagation (periodic pulses at seed)...\\nRunning beam search for the strongest signal path...\\nFound path in 55 hops (56 nodes).\\nColoring 3D activity snapshot at step 35/60 (wavefront, not the fully-settled end state).\\n\\nSaved visualization to /mnt/user-data/outputs/neural_circuit_simulation.png\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:02.655665Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:03.285678Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Nx8bbd3VGmRxYegVxezkCP", "name": "view", "input": {"description": "Check the resulting plot with self-stimulation comparison", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/neural_circuit_simulation.png"}, "message": "Check the resulting plot with self-stimulation comparison", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Check the resulting plot with self-stimulation comparison"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:04.008193Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:04.008231Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Nx8bbd3VGmRxYegVxezkCP", "name": "view", "content": [{"type": "image", "file_uuid": "49f92f7a-9646-4ddb-a261-52556ee8b651"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:05.844202Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:12.776825Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Investigating why network activity saturates regardless of stimulation pattern."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:12.776873Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:14.458248Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "The two curves are identical \u2014 because the propagation model is already in a supercritical regime (any single pulse cascades to saturate the whole graph), so extra self-stimulation pulses get swamped and add nothing visible. Let me find a more meaningful regime: one where a single pulse dies out on its own, but self-stimulation sustains ongoing activity \u2014 which is the actual point of modeling stimulation.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:14.458328Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:18.664795Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_014HqSZg2b3DvcbQVPuUEGJV", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude && python3 -c \"\nimport neural_circuit_simulation as ncs\nimport numpy as np\n\nvolume = ncs.load_real_mri_volume()\ncoords = ncs.build_connectivity_nodes(volume)\nncs.write_connectivity_edges(volume, coords)\nadjacency = ncs.load_adjacency_from_disk(ncs.EDGES_PATH, len(coords))\nseed_idx, target_idx, comp = ncs.largest_component_endpoints(adjacency, coords)\n\nfor decay, gain, thr in [(0.6,0.35,0.6), (0.55,0.4,0.6), (0.5,0.45,0.55), (0.6,0.4,0.55)]:\n    single = ncs.simulate_realtime_activity(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60, decay=decay, gain=gain, threshold=thr)\n    stim = ncs.simulate_self_stimulation(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60, decay=decay, gain=gain, threshold=thr, stim_interval=6, stim_amplitude=1.0)\n    print(f'decay={decay} gain={gain} thr={thr} -> single_final_total={single.sum(axis=1)[-1]:.3f}  stim_final_total={stim.sum(axis=1)[-1]:.3f}  stim_max_reach={ (stim[-1]>0).sum() }/{len(coords)}')\n\"\n", "description": "Search for a subcritical regime where single pulse dies but self-stimulation sustains activity"}, "message": "Search for a subcritical regime where single pulse dies but self-stimulation sustains activity", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude && python3 -c \\\"\\nimport neural_circuit_simulation as ncs\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nvolume = ncs.load_real_mri_volume()\\ncoords = ncs.build_connectivity_nodes(volume)\\nncs.write_connectivity_edges(volume, coords)\\nadjacency = ncs.load_adjacency_from_disk(ncs.EDGES_PATH, len(coords))\\nseed_idx, target_idx, comp = ncs.largest_component_endpoints(adjacency, coords)\\n\\nfor decay, gain, thr in [(0.6,0.35,0.6), (0.55,0.4,0.6), (0.5,0.45,0.55), (0.6,0.4,0.55)]:\\n    single = ncs.simulate_realtime_activity(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60, decay=decay, gain=gain, threshold=thr)\\n    stim = ncs.simulate_self_stimulation(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60, decay=decay, gain=gain, threshold=thr, stim_interval=6, stim_amplitude=1.0)\\n    print(f'decay={decay} gain={gain} thr={thr} -> single_final_total={single.sum(axis=1)[-1]:.3f}  stim_final_total={stim.sum(axis=1)[-1]:.3f}  stim_max_reach={ (stim[-1]>0).sum() }/{len(coords)}')\\n\\\"\\n\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:19.727422Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:19.727452Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_014HqSZg2b3DvcbQVPuUEGJV", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"decay=0.6 gain=0.35 thr=0.6 -> single_final_total=0.000  stim_final_total=1.205  stim_max_reach=4/24408\\ndecay=0.55 gain=0.4 thr=0.6 -> single_final_total=0.000  stim_final_total=1.084  stim_max_reach=4/24408\\ndecay=0.5 gain=0.45 thr=0.55 -> single_final_total=0.000  stim_final_total=1.054  stim_max_reach=4/24408\\ndecay=0.6 gain=0.4 thr=0.55 -> single_final_total=0.000  stim_final_total=1.227  stim_max_reach=4/24408\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"decay=0.6 gain=0.35 thr=0.6 -> single_final_total=0.000  stim_final_total=1.205  stim_max_reach=4/24408\\ndecay=0.55 gain=0.4 thr=0.6 -> single_final_total=0.000  stim_final_total=1.084  stim_max_reach=4/24408\\ndecay=0.5 gain=0.45 thr=0.55 -> single_final_total=0.000  stim_final_total=1.054  stim_max_reach=4/24408\\ndecay=0.6 gain=0.4 thr=0.55 -> single_final_total=0.000  stim_final_total=1.227  stim_max_reach=4/24408\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:21.534561Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:24.229753Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Testing decay and gain parameters for signal persistence."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:24.229791Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:25.187057Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Found it: `decay=0.6, gain=0.4, threshold=0.55` \u2014 a single pulse dies out completely, but the periodic self-stimulation sustains a small persistent firing zone indefinitely. That's the actual scientifically meaningful contrast. Let's lock that in.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:25.187086Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:27.243437Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01FqafUx4r8nWvc6Ms8pbcxy", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude && python3 -c \"\nimport neural_circuit_simulation as ncs\nimport numpy as np\n\nvolume = ncs.load_real_mri_volume()\ncoords = ncs.build_connectivity_nodes(volume)\nncs.write_connectivity_edges(volume, coords)\nadjacency = ncs.load_adjacency_from_disk(ncs.EDGES_PATH, len(coords))\nseed_idx, target_idx, comp = ncs.largest_component_endpoints(adjacency, coords)\n\nstim = ncs.simulate_self_stimulation(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=120, decay=0.6, gain=0.4, threshold=0.55, stim_interval=6, stim_amplitude=1.0)\ntotals = stim.sum(axis=1)\nprint(totals[-20:])\n\"\n", "description": "Check whether the sustained activity is stable over a longer run"}, "message": "Check whether the sustained activity is stable over a longer run", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude && python3 -c \\\"\\nimport neural_circuit_simulation as ncs\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nvolume = ncs.load_real_mri_volume()\\ncoords = ncs.build_connectivity_nodes(volume)\\nncs.write_connectivity_edges(volume, coords)\\nadjacency = ncs.load_adjacency_from_disk(ncs.EDGES_PATH, len(coords))\\nseed_idx, target_idx, comp = ncs.largest_component_endpoints(adjacency, coords)\\n\\nstim = ncs.simulate_self_stimulation(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=120, decay=0.6, gain=0.4, threshold=0.55, stim_interval=6, stim_amplitude=1.0)\\ntotals = stim.sum(axis=1)\\nprint(totals[-20:])\\n\\\"\\n\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:28.280635Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:28.280677Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01FqafUx4r8nWvc6Ms8pbcxy", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"[0.3791252 1.227475  1.8309166 1.7552092 1.0531255 0.6318753 0.3791252\\n 1.227475  1.8309166 1.7552092 1.0531255 0.6318753 0.3791252 1.227475\\n 1.8309166 1.7552092 1.0531255 0.6318753 0.3791252 1.227475 ]\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"[0.3791252 1.227475  1.8309166 1.7552092 1.0531255 0.6318753 0.3791252\\n 1.227475  1.8309166 1.7552092 1.0531255 0.6318753 0.3791252 1.227475\\n 1.8309166 1.7552092 1.0531255 0.6318753 0.3791252 1.227475 ]\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:30.091236Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:31.037006Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "It stabilizes into a clean repeating oscillation (period matches the 6-step stimulation interval) \u2014 a genuinely self-sustaining local circuit driven purely by periodic self-stimulation. Let's update the script with these parameters and rerun.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:31.037034Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:36.168009Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01KMRwY65vi3PHEsxBSnCham", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"new_str": "    print(\"\\nRunning real-time activation propagation (single pulse)...\")\n    # Default params (decay=0.85, gain=1.3, threshold=0.5) sit in a\n    # supercritical regime where any pulse cascades to saturate the whole\n    # graph -- self-stimulation pulses would just get swamped and show no\n    # visible effect. These params sit in a subcritical regime instead: a\n    # single pulse dies out completely, so any sustained activity we see\n    # is attributable to the self-stimulation itself.\n    sim_params = dict(decay=0.6, gain=0.4, threshold=0.55)\n    history = simulate_realtime_activity(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60, **sim_params)\n    total_activity = history.sum(axis=1)\n\n    print(\"Running self-stimulation propagation (periodic pulses at seed)...\")\n    stim_history = simulate_self_stimulation(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60,\n                                              stim_interval=6, stim_amplitude=1.0, **sim_params)\n    stim_total_activity = stim_history.sum(axis=1)\n    print(f\"Single pulse dies out to {total_activity[-1]:.3f}; \"\n          f\"self-stimulation sustains a periodic {stim_total_activity[-1]:.3f}-level oscillation.\")", "old_str": "    print(\"\\nRunning real-time activation propagation (single pulse)...\")\n    history = simulate_realtime_activity(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60)\n    total_activity = history.sum(axis=1)\n\n    print(\"Running self-stimulation propagation (periodic pulses at seed)...\")\n    stim_history = simulate_self_stimulation(adjacency, seed_idx, steps=60, stim_interval=8)\n    stim_total_activity = stim_history.sum(axis=1)", "path": "/home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:36.410689Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:36.410726Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01KMRwY65vi3PHEsxBSnCham", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:38.314330Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:44.163061Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Handling edge cases where activity never crosses threshold."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:44.163101Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:44.620403Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Since the single-pulse activity now dies out almost instantly, the 3D wavefront panel needs to color by the self-stimulation history instead (which is the one with something interesting to show).", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:44.620437Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:47.380046Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01X9gAVvo9YqMM56AXBb74QR", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"new_str": "    # A single pulse in this subcritical regime dies out almost immediately,\n    # so there's nothing interesting to color by. The self-stimulation run\n    # sustains a real, ongoing local firing zone -- that's the wavefront\n    # worth visualizing here.\n    snapshot_step = int(np.argmax(stim_total_activity > 0.5 * stim_total_activity.max()))\n    snapshot_activity = stim_history[snapshot_step]\n    print(f\"Coloring 3D snapshot at step {snapshot_step}/{len(stim_history)-1} \"\n          f\"of the self-stimulated (not single-pulse) run.\")", "old_str": "    snapshot_step = int(np.argmax(total_activity > 0.5 * total_activity.max()))\n    snapshot_activity = history[snapshot_step]\n    print(f\"Coloring 3D activity snapshot at step {snapshot_step}/{len(history)-1} \"\n          f\"(wavefront, not the fully-settled end state).\")", "path": "/home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:47.647526Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:47.647566Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01X9gAVvo9YqMM56AXBb74QR", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:49.495778Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:49.724298Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Also update the panel title reference for consistency.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:49.724365Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:50.734065Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01QuHua7EKiuZrh3cCAniRpT", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"new_str": "        ax2.set_title(f\"3D circuit path + self-stimulation wavefront (step {snapshot_step})\")", "old_str": "        ax2.set_title(f\"3D circuit path + activity wavefront (step {snapshot_step})\")", "path": "/home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:50.960101Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:50.960139Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01QuHua7EKiuZrh3cCAniRpT", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:52.379406Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:52.714961Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now rerun the full script to check everything works together.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:52.714989Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:53.205250Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01XvZKziXHT9jSdbWgbHCmfD", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude && python3 neural_circuit_simulation.py", "description": "Run the updated script end-to-end"}, "message": "Run the updated script end-to-end", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude && python3 neural_circuit_simulation.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:54.926712Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:54.926744Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01XvZKziXHT9jSdbWgbHCmfD", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"=== Neural Circuit Simulation on Real MRI Volume ===\\n\\nLoaded and downsampled real MRI to shape (60, 60, 39)\\nVolume shape: (60, 60, 39), active graph nodes: 24408\\nStreamed 139342 directed edges to disk (1632.9 KB)\\nLargest connected component: 24407/24408 nodes\\nSeed node: (13, 29, 12)  Target node: (45, 41, 23)\\n\\nRunning real-time activation propagation (single pulse)...\\nRunning self-stimulation propagation (periodic pulses at seed)...\\nSingle pulse dies out to 0.000; self-stimulation sustains a periodic 1.227-level oscillation.\\nRunning beam search for the strongest signal path...\\nFound path in 55 hops (56 nodes).\\nColoring 3D snapshot at step 0/60 of the self-stimulated (not single-pulse) run.\\n\\nSaved visualization to /mnt/user-data/outputs/neural_circuit_simulation.png\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"=== Neural Circuit Simulation on Real MRI Volume ===\\n\\nLoaded and downsampled real MRI to shape (60, 60, 39)\\nVolume shape: (60, 60, 39), active graph nodes: 24408\\nStreamed 139342 directed edges to disk (1632.9 KB)\\nLargest connected component: 24407/24408 nodes\\nSeed node: (13, 29, 12)  Target node: (45, 41, 23)\\n\\nRunning real-time activation propagation (single pulse)...\\nRunning self-stimulation propagation (periodic pulses at seed)...\\nSingle pulse dies out to 0.000; self-stimulation sustains a periodic 1.227-level oscillation.\\nRunning beam search for the strongest signal path...\\nFound path in 55 hops (56 nodes).\\nColoring 3D snapshot at step 0/60 of the self-stimulated (not single-pulse) run.\\n\\nSaved visualization to /mnt/user-data/outputs/neural_circuit_simulation.png\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:03:56.649811Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:04:02.533353Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Locating when the simulated activity peaks."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:04:02.533399Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:04:03.533284Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "`argmax` picked step 0 (the very first pulse) since that already exceeds half the oscillation's peak \u2014 not useful. Let me pick a snapshot from later in the steady-state oscillation instead.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:04:03.533316Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:04:05.784053Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01VsnST2ZzWqbiwbSzMfgQws", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"new_str": "    # Pick the snapshot from the later, steady-state portion of the run\n    # (skip the first half, which is just the initial transient) so we\n    # capture a peak of the settled self-stimulation oscillation rather\n    # than the very first pulse.\n    later_half = stim_total_activity[len(stim_total_activity) // 2:]\n    snapshot_step = len(stim_total_activity) // 2 + int(np.argmax(later_half))\n    snapshot_activity = stim_history[snapshot_step]", "old_str": "    snapshot_step = int(np.argmax(stim_total_activity > 0.5 * stim_total_activity.max()))\n    snapshot_activity = stim_history[snapshot_step]", "path": "/home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:04:06.037768Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:04:06.037807Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01VsnST2ZzWqbiwbSzMfgQws", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/neural_circuit_simulation.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:04:08.133352Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T05:04:08.727889Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_019uz7D1uWh2ky1Rsne18WWE", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude && python3 neural_circuit_simulation.py", "description": "Re-run with a proper steady-state snapshot pick"}, "message": "Re-run with a proper steady-state snapshot pick", 