\nRunning beam search for the strongest signal path...\\nFound path in 198 hops (199 nodes).\\nColoring 3D snapshot at step 37/60 of the self-stimulated (not single-pulse) run.\\n\\nSaved visualization to neural_circuit_simulation.png\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:49:56.719189Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:01.968914Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Handling a large-scale connectivity dataset with millions of nodes."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:01.968998Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:02.579843Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_018nR2Wxw4MCn54LycJwiGqM", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/ncs && python3 generate_connectivity_npy.py 2>&1 | tail -20", "description": "Generate connectivity_points.npy from edges"}, "message": "Generate connectivity_points.npy from edges", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/ncs && python3 generate_connectivity_npy.py 2>&1 | tail -20\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:07.203913Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:07.203948Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_018nR2Wxw4MCn54LycJwiGqM", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"created connectivity_points.npy\\nnodes: 1560800\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"created connectivity_points.npy\\nnodes: 1560800\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:08.818581Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:22.102535Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Verifying the point count behind the full label rendering."}, {"summary": "Uncovering a mismatched file format behind the mesh triangles."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:22.102655Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:24.900616Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_018qELunGyirnh85JzUE7wX8", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/ncs && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport numpy as np\n\npoints = np.load('connectivity_points.npy').astype(np.float64)\nprint(\"points shape:\", points.shape)\n\nraw_edges = np.fromfile('connectivity_edges.bin', dtype=np.int32)\nprint(\"raw_edges size:\", raw_edges.size)\nnum_triangles = raw_edges.size // 3\nedges = raw_edges[:num_triangles*3].reshape((-1,3))\nprint(\"edges (as triangles) shape:\", edges.shape)\nprint(\"edges min/max:\", edges.min(), edges.max())\nprint(\"sample rows:\", edges[:5])\n\nmax_idx = len(points)-1\nvalid_mask = (\n    (edges[:,0]>=0) & (edges[:,0]<=max_idx) &\n    (edges[:,1]>=0) & (edges[:,1]<=max_idx) &\n    (edges[:,2]>=0) & (edges[:,2]<=max_idx)\n)\nprint(\"num valid triangles:\", valid_mask.sum(), \"/\", len(edges))\nEOF\n", "description": "Diagnose mesh parsing mismatch"}, "message": "Diagnose mesh parsing mismatch", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/ncs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\npoints = np.load('connectivity_points.npy').astype(np.float64)\\nprint(\\\"points shape:\\\", points.shape)\\n\\nraw_edges = np.fromfile('connectivity_edges.bin', dtype=np.int32)\\nprint(\\\"raw_edges size:\\\", raw_edges.size)\\nnum_triangles = raw_edges.size // 3\\nedges = raw_edges[:num_triangles*3].reshape((-1,3))\\nprint(\\\"edges (as triangles) shape:\\\", edges.shape)\\nprint(\\\"edges min/max:\\\", edges.min(), edges.max())\\nprint(\\\"sample rows:\\\", edges[:5])\\n\\nmax_idx = len(points)-1\\nvalid_mask = (\\n    (edges[:,0]>=0) & (edges[:,0]<=max_idx) &\\n    (edges[:,1]>=0) & (edges[:,1]<=max_idx) &\\n    (edges[:,2]>=0) & (edges[:,2]<=max_idx)\\n)\\nprint(\\\"num valid triangles:\\\", valid_mask.sum(), \\\"/\\\", len(edges))\\nEOF\\n\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:25.544798Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:25.544841Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_018qELunGyirnh85JzUE7wX8", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"points shape: (1560800, 3)\\nraw_edges size: 27732516\\nedges (as triangles) shape: (9244172, 3)\\nedges min/max: 0 1065353216\\nsample rows: [[         0         52 1061113108]\\n [        52          0 1061113108]\\n [         0          3 1058574278]\\n [         3          0 1058574278]\\n [         0          1 1065327042]]\\nnum valid triangles: 0 / 9244172\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"points shape: (1560800, 3)\\nraw_edges size: 27732516\\nedges (as triangles) shape: (9244172, 3)\\nedges min/max: 0 1065353216\\nsample rows: [[         0         52 1061113108]\\n [        52          0 1061113108]\\n [         0          3 1058574278]\\n [         3          0 1058574278]\\n [         0          1 1065327042]]\\nnum valid triangles: 0 / 9244172\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:27.584988Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:35.585003Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Found it \u2014 two separate bugs, and they'd cause exactly this \"nothing shows\" symptom even before the label change:\n\n**1. Mesh file format mismatch (the real blocker).** `connectivity_edges.bin` was written by `neural_circuit_simulation.py` as **graph edges**: `(src: int32, dst: int32, weight: float32)` triplets \u2014 a connectivity graph, not a triangle mesh. But `app.py`'s `show_cortical_overlay` reads that same file and treats every 3 int32s as a **mesh triangle** `(i, j, k)`. The third value in each record is actually a *weight* stored as a float, reinterpreted as raw int32 bits \u2014 so `k` comes out as huge nonsense numbers (e.g. `1061113108`). I checked directly: **0 out of 9,244,172 \"triangles\" pass the validity filter.** The brain surface mesh has literally zero faces to draw \u2014 it was never showing anything, with or without labels.\n\n**2. The point cloud is enormous \u2014 1,560,800 points.** That's every MRI voxel above the tissue threshold, not a surface mesh's vertex count. \"Label all of them\" tries to create 1.56 million `Scatter3d` text labels in one Plotly figure. Even if the mesh weren't broken, a browser tab cannot render that \u2014 it'll hang or silently fail to paint, which looks like \"nothing shown.\"\n\nSo really there are two independent fixes needed:\n\n- **Mesh:** `app.py` needs an actual triangulated brain surface (e.g. via `nilearn.datasets.fetch_surf_fsaverage` + `nilearn.surface`, or `skimage.measure.marching_cubes` on the MRI volume) \u2014 the graph edge file from the other script was never meant to be mesh triangles.\n- **Labels:** pick a realistic count \u2014 a few hundred labels max on a brain plot is already visually dense; 1.5 million is not renderable by any browser.\n\nWant me to fix the mesh loading (build a real surface via marching cubes on the MRI volume) and set labels to a sane but generous count, or would you rather keep the graph-node point cloud as-is and just fix labeling/sampling?", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-09-27T11:50:35.670217Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T11:50:35.670217Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0e2b2-8b44-7fbe-95af-c94ee35368c6"}, {"uuid": "01a0e2b4-1c29-7fa0-b15d-418451d82e0a", "text": "just the app", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:48.776982Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:48.776982Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "just the app", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-09-27T11:50:48.777275Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T11:50:48.777275Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0e2b2-8b44-76a5-9fb4-2ddef14bc72d"}, {"uuid": "01a0e2b4-1c29-7cc7-91ae-7ee7e7109f31", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow let's make the fix. I'll swap the broken mesh source for a real marching-cubes surface built straight from the MRI, cached to disk, and reused for both the mesh and the label/path points.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow update the mesh-loading/rendering section of `show_cortical_overlay`:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow the label-generation block \u2014 replacing \"sample and repeat a handful of names across the mesh\" with \"show every distinct scientific label the classifier can produce\":\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThis part is unaffected \u2014 good, it still works using `points` from the new real surface. Now let's verify the whole thing end-to-end (headless, replicating the app's logic without Tkinter):\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow let's re-run the test, importing the actual `app.py` module (headless via `Xvfb`-free logic import, just not calling `Tk()`):\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nAll 28 distinct labels found, all 58,690 triangles valid (100%, vs. 0 before), builds in a fraction of a second and caches instantly on repeat runs. Now let's confirm the full figure actually renders by generating the real HTML output through the complete method:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nConfirmed working end-to-end \u2014 real mesh (58,690 valid triangles, up from 0), all 28 possible region labels shown exactly once, circuit paths still draw fine, and the output HTML renders (~6.5 MB, reasonable). Let's get the fixed file to you.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nFixed `app.py` \u2014 only that file changed, `neural_circuit_simulation.py` and `generate_connectivity_npy.py` untouched.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **Mesh:** now built with `skimage.measure.marching_cubes` straight off `real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz`, cached to `brain_surface_verts.npy` / `brain_surface_faces.npy` so it only rebuilds once. This is a real anatomical surface (~29k verts, ~59k triangles, all valid) instead of misreading a graph-edge file as mesh triangles.\n- **Labels:** `_get_scientific_region_name` can only ever produce 28 distinct strings (2 hemispheres \u00d7 14 zones). Rather than stamping the same 28 words tens of thousands of times, it now shows all 28 \u2014 each once, at the vertex closest to that region's centroid.\n- Dropped the unused `nilearn` import (no longer needed).\n- No more `connectivity_points.npy` / `connectivity_edges.bin` dependency for the visualizer \u2014 first click just needs `real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz` present.\n\nYou'll need `scikit-image` installed (`pip install scikit-image`) alongside the existing `plotly`/`nibabel`.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:50:48.771438Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:08.203520Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Fixing the mesh and labels within app.py only."}, {"summary": "Rebuilding the brain surface with marching cubes instead."}, {"summary": "Weighing the fabricated coordinates behind the region labels."}, {"summary": "Aligning circuit points to the real anatomical coordinate space."}, {"summary": "Centering voxel coordinates to mimic anatomical positioning."}, {"summary": "Choosing a step size to balance detail and speed."}, {"summary": "Enumerating every distinct label the classifier can generate."}, {"summary": "Picking one representative point per label category."}, {"summary": "Rerouting circuit paths through the real surface coordinates."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:08.203599Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:10.834502Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_012pXvdyyWEqxPNMcnwt4xwv", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/ncs && pip install scikit-image --break-system-packages -q 2>&1 | tail -5\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport time, numpy as np, nibabel as nib\nfrom skimage import measure\n\nt0=time.time()\nimg = nib.load(\"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\")\ndata = img.get_fdata().astype(np.float32)\nprint(\"shape\", data.shape, \"load time\", time.time()-t0)\n\nrobust_max = np.percentile(data[data>0], 99)\nvol = np.clip(data/robust_max, 0, 1)\n\nfor step in [3,2]:\n    t0=time.time()\n    verts, faces, normals, values = measure.marching_cubes(vol, level=0.2, step_size=step)\n    print(f\"step_size={step}: verts={len(verts)} faces={len(faces)} time={time.time()-t0:.2f}s\")\nEOF\n", "description": "Test marching cubes surface extraction performance"}, "message": "Test marching cubes surface extraction performance", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/ncs && pip install scikit-image --break-system-packages -q 2>&1 | tail -5\\npython3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport time, numpy as np, nibabel as nib\\nfrom skimage import measure\\n\\nt0=time.time()\\nimg = nib.load(\\\"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\\\")\\ndata = img.get_fdata().astype(np.float32)\\nprint(\\\"shape\\\", data.shape, \\\"load time\\\", time.time()-t0)\\n\\nrobust_max = np.percentile(data[data>0], 99)\\nvol = np.clip(data/robust_max, 0, 1)\\n\\nfor step in [3,2]:\\n    t0=time.time()\\n    verts, faces, normals, values = measure.marching_cubes(vol, level=0.2, step_size=step)\\n    print(f\\\"step_size={step}: verts={len(verts)} faces={len(faces)} time={time.time()-t0:.2f}s\\\")\\nEOF\\n\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:14.362338Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:14.362365Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_012pXvdyyWEqxPNMcnwt4xwv", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"shape (240, 240, 155) load time 0.14671897888183594\\nstep_size=3: verts=12850 faces=25684 time=0.05s\\nstep_size=2: verts=29359 faces=58690 time=0.06s\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"shape (240, 240, 155) load time 0.14671897888183594\\nstep_size=3: verts=12850 faces=25684 time=0.05s\\nstep_size=2: verts=29359 faces=58690 time=0.06s\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:17.432607Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:19.701305Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01MPi1t6zPHPJF4dfU1DuR72", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/ncs && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport numpy as np, nibabel as nib\nfrom skimage import measure\n\nimg = nib.load(\"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\")\ndata = img.get_fdata().astype(np.float32)\nrobust_max = np.percentile(data[data>0], 99)\nvol = np.clip(data/robust_max, 0, 1)\nverts, faces, normals, values = measure.marching_cubes(vol, level=0.2, step_size=2)\nprint(\"shape\", data.shape)\nprint(\"verts range per axis:\", verts.min(axis=0), verts.max(axis=0))\n\n# center\nshape = np.array(data.shape)\ncentered = verts - shape/2.0\nprint(\"centered range:\", centered.min(axis=0), centered.max(axis=0))\nEOF\n", "description": "Check vertex coordinate ranges for centering"}, "message": "Check vertex coordinate ranges for centering", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/ncs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport numpy as np, nibabel as nib\\nfrom skimage import measure\\n\\nimg = nib.load(\\\"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\\\")\\ndata = img.get_fdata().astype(np.float32)\\nrobust_max = np.percentile(data[data>0], 99)\\nvol = np.clip(data/robust_max, 0, 1)\\nverts, faces, normals, values = measure.marching_cubes(vol, level=0.2, step_size=2)\\nprint(\\\"shape\\\", data.shape)\\nprint(\\\"verts range per axis:\\\", verts.min(axis=0), verts.max(axis=0))\\n\\n# center\\nshape = np.array(data.shape)\\ncentered = verts - shape/2.0\\nprint(\\\"centered range:\\\", centered.min(axis=0), centered.max(axis=0))\\nEOF\\n\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:20.294247Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:20.294278Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01MPi1t6zPHPJF4dfU1DuR72", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"shape (240, 240, 155)\\nverts range per axis: [48.61487  40.509743 14.387273] [189.52342 219.58035 141.15935]\\ncentered range: [-71.38513184 -79.49025726 -63.11272717] [69.52342224 99.58035278 63.65934753]\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"shape (240, 240, 155)\\nverts range per axis: [48.61487  40.509743 14.387273] [189.52342 219.58035 141.15935]\\ncentered range: [-71.38513184 -79.49025726 -63.11272717] [69.52342224 99.58035278 63.65934753]\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:21.685674Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:26.627850Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Calibrating scoring thresholds for the heuristic function."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:26.627943Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:27.322323Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01VP3cACCQjviDg1gffFiHRz", "name": "view", "input": {"description": "Re-view current app.py before larger edits", "path": "/home/claude/ncs/app.py", "view_range": [1, 45]}, "message": "Re-view current app.py before larger edits", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Re-view current app.py before larger edits"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:27.532948Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:27.533011Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01VP3cACCQjviDg1gffFiHRz", "name": "view", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "     1\timport heapq\n     2\timport threading\n     3\timport queue\n     4\timport time\n     5\timport os\n     6\timport tkinter as tk\n     7\tfrom tkinter import ttk, messagebox\n     8\timport numpy as np\n     9\t\n    10\ttry:\n    11\t    import nibabel as nib\n    12\t    from nilearn import plotting, datasets\n    13\t    import plotly.graph_objects as go\n    14\t    PLOTLY_AVAILABLE = True\n    15\texcept ImportError:\n    16\t    PLOTLY_AVAILABLE = False\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\tclass NeuralBeamSimulationApp:\n    20\t    def __init__(self, root):\n    21\t        self.root = root\n    22\t        self.root.title(\"Neural Beam Engine & Custom Connectivity Visualizer\")\n    23\t        self.root.geometry(\"800x650\")\n    24\t        self.root.minsize(700, 550)\n    25\t\n    26\t        self.data_path = \"weights.bin\"\n    27\t        self.points_path = \"connectivity_points.npy\"\n    28\t        self.edges_path = \"connectivity_edges.bin\"\n    29\t\n    30\t        self.is_running = False\n    31\t        self.result_queue = queue.Queue()\n    32\t        self.latest_results = []\n    33\t\n    34\t        self._ensure_data_files()\n    35\t        self._create_widgets()\n    36\t\n    37\t    def _ensure_data_files(self):\n    38\t        \"\"\"Creates default files if weights.bin doesn't exist.\"\"\"\n    39\t        if not os.path.exists(self.data_path):\n    40\t            raw_weights = np.array([1.5, 2.2, 3.8, 4.1, 5.0, 6.3, 1.1], dtype=np.float32)\n    41\t            raw_weights.tofile(self.data_path)\n    42\t\n    43\t    def _create_widgets(self):\n    44\t        main_frame = ttk.Frame(self.root, padding=15)\n    45\t        main_frame.pack(fill=tk.BOTH, expand=True)\n[412 lines total]"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"import heapq\\nimport threading\\nimport queue\\nimport time\\nimport os\\nimport tkinter as tk\\nfrom tkinter import ttk, messagebox\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\ntry:\\n    import nibabel as nib\\n    from nilearn import plotting, datasets\\n    import plotly.graph_objects as go\\n    PLOTLY_AVAILABLE = True\\nexcept ImportError:\\n    PLOTLY_AVAILABLE = False\\n\\n\\nclass NeuralBeamSimulationApp:\\n    def __init__(self, root):\\n        self.root = root\\n        self.root.title(\\\"Neural Beam Engine & Custom Connectivity Visualizer\\\")\\n        self.root.geometry(\\\"800x650\\\")\\n        self.root.minsize(700, 550)\\n\\n        self.data_path = \\\"weights.bin\\\"\\n        self.points_path = \\\"connectivity_points.npy\\\"\\n        self.edges_path = \\\"connectivity_edges.bin\\\"\\n\\n        self.is_running = False\\n        self.result_queue = queue.Queue()\\n        self.latest_results = []\\n\\n        self._ensure_data_files()\\n        self._create_widgets()\\n\\n    def _ensure_data_files(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Creates default files if weights.bin doesn't exist.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not os.path.exists(self.data_path):\\n            raw_weights = np.array([1.5, 2.2, 3.8, 4.1, 5.0, 6.3, 1.1], dtype=np.float32)\\n            raw_weights.tofile(self.data_path)\\n\\n    def _create_widgets(self):\\n        main_frame = ttk.Frame(self.root, padding=15)\\n        main_frame.pack(fill=tk.BOTH, expand=True)\\n\", \"filename\": \"/home/claude/ncs/app.py\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:28.948020Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:29.877868Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now let's make the fix. I'll swap the broken mesh source for a real marching-cubes surface built straight from the MRI, cached to disk, and reused for both the mesh and the label/path points.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:29.877904Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:31.339571Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_011fKTYWNeHm6DomcGFAT24e", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"path": "/home/claude/ncs/app.py", "old_str": "try:\n    import nibabel as nib\n    from nilearn import plotting, datasets\n    import plotly.graph_objects as go\n    PLOTLY_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    PLOTLY_AVAILABLE = False", "new_str": "try:\n    import nibabel as nib\n    from skimage import measure\n    import plotly.graph_objects as go\n    PLOTLY_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    PLOTLY_AVAILABLE = False"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:31.612054Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:31.612096Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_011fKTYWNeHm6DomcGFAT24e", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/ncs/app.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/ncs/app.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:34.478236Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:35.857892Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01EqQYGpxngnYCaAj26ZwVdg", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"path": "/home/claude/ncs/app.py", "old_str": "        self.data_path = \"weights.bin\"\n        self.points_path = \"connectivity_points.npy\"\n        self.edges_path = \"connectivity_edges.bin\"", "new_str": "        self.data_path = \"weights.bin\"\n        self.mri_path = \"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\"\n        self.surface_verts_path = \"brain_surface_verts.npy\"\n        self.surface_faces_path = \"brain_surface_faces.npy\""}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:36.028381Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:36.028415Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01EqQYGpxngnYCaAj26ZwVdg", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/ncs/app.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/ncs/app.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:37.472194Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:37.896081Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now update the mesh-loading/rendering section of `show_cortical_overlay`:", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:37.896111Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:50.461642Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01CWduAdDhkdAFcyay2GJWUF", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"path": "/home/claude/ncs/app.py", "old_str": "    def show_cortical_overlay(self):\n        \"\"\"Renders brain mesh, circuit paths, and scientific text labels without marker balls.\"\"\"\n        if not PLOTLY_AVAILABLE:\n            messagebox.showerror(\"Missing Dependency\", \"Plotly is required. Run: pip install plotly\")\n            return\n\n        if not os.path.exists(self.points_path) or not os.path.exists(self.edges_path):\n            messagebox.showerror(\n                \"Files Missing\", \n                f\"Could not find required surface files:\\n- {self.points_path}\\n- {self.edges_path}\"\n            )\n            return\n\n        if not self.latest_results:\n            messagebox.showinfo(\"Empty Results\", \"Please run the simulation first to generate paths.\")\n            return\n\n        self.status_var.set(\"Status: Loading brain surface, labels, and circuit paths...\")\n        self.root.update_idletasks()\n\n        try:\n            points = np.load(self.points_path).astype(np.float64)\n            raw_edges = np.fromfile(self.edges_path, dtype=np.int32)\n            \n            num_triangles = raw_edges.size // 3\n            if num_triangles == 0:\n                raise ValueError(\"connectivity_edges.bin contains no valid triangle data.\")\n            \n            edges = raw_edges[:num_triangles * 3].reshape((-1, 3))\n            \n            if edges.min() >= 1:\n                edges -= 1\n                \n        except Exception as e:\n            messagebox.showerror(\"File Parsing Error\", f\"Failed to load binary mesh files:\\n{e}\")\n            return\n\n        if np.max(np.abs(points)) < 5.0:\n            points *= 1000.0\n\n        max_idx = len(points) - 1\n        valid_mask = (\n            (edges[:, 0] >= 0) & (edges[:, 0] <= max_idx) &\n            (edges[:, 1] >= 0) & (edges[:, 1] <= max_idx) &\n            (edges[:, 2] >= 0) & (edges[:, 2] <= max_idx)\n        )\n        edges = edges[valid_mask]\n\n        traces = []", "new_str": "    def _build_or_load_brain_surface(self):\n        \"\"\"\n        Builds a real triangulated brain surface straight from the MRI volume\n        (via marching cubes) and caches it to disk. The previous version read\n        `connectivity_edges.bin`, but that file stores graph edges\n        (src:int32, dst:int32, weight:float32) written by the simulation\n        script -- not triangle indices -- so reinterpreting its bytes as\n        (i, j, k) mesh faces produced zero valid triangles. This builds an\n        actual surface instead.\n        \"\"\"\n        if os.path.exists(self.surface_verts_path) and os.path.exists(self.surface_faces_path):\n            verts = np.load(self.surface_verts_path)\n            faces = np.load(self.surface_faces_path)\n            return verts, faces\n\n        if not os.path.exists(self.mri_path):\n            raise FileNotFoundError(f\"MRI file not found at {self.mri_path}\")\n\n        img = nib.load(self.mri_path)\n        data = img.get_fdata().astype(np.float32)\n\n        robust_max = np.percentile(data[data > 0], 99)\n        volume = np.clip(data / robust_max, 0, 1)\n\n        # step_size=2 keeps the surface at ~30k vertices/60k faces: detailed\n        # enough to look like a brain, light enough to render smoothly.\n        verts, faces, _normals, _values = measure.marching_cubes(\n            volume, level=0.2, step_size=2\n        )\n\n        # Center on the volume's midpoint so coordinates run roughly\n        # -80..+100 per axis, matching the ranges _get_scientific_region_name\n        # expects (it was written assuming roughly MNI-centered coordinates).\n        verts = verts - np.array(data.shape) / 2.0\n\n        np.save(self.surface_verts_path, verts)\n        np.save(self.surface_faces_path, faces)\n        return verts, faces\n\n    def show_cortical_overlay(self):\n        \"\"\"Renders brain mesh, circuit paths, and scientific text labels without marker balls.\"\"\"\n        if not PLOTLY_AVAILABLE:\n            messagebox.showerror(\"Missing Dependency\", \"Plotly and scikit-image are required. Run: pip install plotly scikit-image\")\n            return\n\n        if not self.latest_results:\n            messagebox.showinfo(\"Empty Results\", \"Please run the simulation first to generate paths.\")\n            return\n\n        self.status_var.set(\"Status: Building brain surface from MRI (first run only)...\")\n        self.root.update_idletasks()\n\n        try:\n            points, edges = self._build_or_load_brain_surface()\n        except Exception as e:\n            messagebox.showerror(\"Surface Build Error\", f\"Failed to build brain surface:\\n{e}\")\n            return\n\n        self.status_var.set(\"Status: Loading labels and circuit paths...\")\n        self.root.update_idletasks()\n\n        traces = []"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:50.717854Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:50.717885Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01CWduAdDhkdAFcyay2GJWUF", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/ncs/app.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/ncs/app.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:52.169759Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:53.034667Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now the label-generation block \u2014 replacing \"sample and repeat a handful of names across the mesh\" with \"show every distinct scientific label the classifier can produce\":", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:53.034696Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:59.527782Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01S8cyPreaHN4bJcVxQJKR41", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"path": "/home/claude/ncs/app.py", "old_str": "        # 2. Add Scientific Region Labels (all points labeled, no sampling)\n        sampled_points = points\n        scientific_labels = [\n            self._get_scientific_region_name(pt[0], pt[1], pt[2]) for pt in sampled_points\n        ]\n\n        labels_trace = go.Scatter3d(\n            x=sampled_points[:, 0], y=sampled_points[:, 1], z=sampled_points[:, 2],\n            mode='text',\n            text=scientific_labels,\n            textfont=dict(color='Black', size=10, family='Arial Bold'),\n            name='Scientific Region Labels'\n        )\n        traces.append(labels_trace)", "new_str": "        # 2. Add Scientific Region Labels. _get_scientific_region_name only\n        # ever produces ~28 distinct strings (2 hemispheres x 14 named\n        # zones) -- with ~30k mesh vertices, labeling \"all of them\" would\n        # mean stamping the same ~28 words tens of thousands of times on\n        # top of each other and would also make the browser choke trying to\n        # render that many text objects. Instead this labels every one of\n        # those distinct regions exactly once, at a representative point\n        # (the vertex closest to that region's own centroid) -- so all the\n        # labels the app can produce are actually shown, just without\n        # thousands of redundant duplicates stacked on each other.\n        all_labels = np.array([\n            self._get_scientific_region_name(pt[0], pt[1], pt[2]) for pt in points\n        ])\n\n        label_points = []\n        label_text = []\n        for label in np.unique(all_labels):\n            group_idx = np.where(all_labels == label)[0]\n            group_pts = points[group_idx]\n            centroid = group_pts.mean(axis=0)\n            nearest = group_idx[np.argmin(np.linalg.norm(group_pts - centroid, axis=1))]\n            label_points.append(points[nearest])\n            label_text.append(label)\n        label_points = np.array(label_points)\n\n        labels_trace = go.Scatter3d(\n            x=label_points[:, 0], y=label_points[:, 1], z=label_points[:, 2],\n            mode='text',\n            text=label_text,\n            textfont=dict(color='Black', size=12, family='Arial Bold'),\n            name='Scientific Region Labels'\n        )\n        traces.append(labels_trace)"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:59.811720Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:52:59.811757Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01S8cyPreaHN4bJcVxQJKR41", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/ncs/app.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/ncs/app.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:53:02.447431Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:53:03.251698Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01HfdbbG5dkxvuwe7ic2wCrj", "name": "view", "input": {"description": "Review rest of show_cortical_overlay for consistency", "path": "/home/claude/ncs/app.py", "view_range": [340, 420]}, "message": "Review rest of show_cortical_overlay for consistency", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Review rest of show_cortical_overlay for consistency"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:53:03.433791Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:53:03.433886Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01HfdbbG5dkxvuwe7ic2wCrj", "name": "view", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "   340\t        )\n   341\t        traces.append(labels_trace)\n   342\t\n   343\t        def create_pipe_mesh(p1, p2, radius=4.5, n_segs=10):\n   344\t            p1, p2 = np.array(p1), np.array(p2)\n   345\t            v = p2 - p1\n   346\t            length = np.linalg.norm(v)\n   347\t            if length < 1e-6:\n   348\t                return np.empty((0, 3)), np.empty((0, 3), dtype=int)\n   349\t            v = v / length\n   350\t            \n   351\t            n1 = np.array([0, 1, 0]) if abs(v[0]) > 0.9 else np.array([1, 0, 0])\n   352\t            n1 = np.cross(v, n1)\n   353\t            n1 /= np.linalg.norm(n1)\n   354\t            n2 = np.cross(v, n1)\n   355\t            \n   356\t            theta = np.linspace(0, 2 * np.pi, n_segs, endpoint=False)\n   357\t            circle = [radius * (np.cos(th) * n1 + np.sin(th) * n2) for th in theta]\n   358\t            \n   359\t            verts = [p1 + pt for pt in circle] + [p2 + pt for pt in circle]\n   360\t            verts = np.array(verts)\n   361\t            \n   362\t            faces = []\n   363\t            for i in range(n_segs):\n   364\t                nxt = (i + 1) % n_segs\n   365\t                faces.append([i, nxt, i + n_segs])\n   366\t                faces.append([nxt, nxt + n_segs, i + n_segs])\n   367\t                \n   368\t            return verts, np.array(faces, dtype=int)\n   369\t\n   370\t        colorscales = ['Turbo', 'Viridis', 'Plasma', 'Inferno', 'Magma', 'Cividis']\n   371\t        num_points = len(points)\n   372\t\n   373\t        # 3. Render all optimal circuit paths\n   374\t        for rank_idx, res in enumerate(self.latest_results):\n   375\t            target_path = res[2]\n   376\t            if not target_path or len(target_path) < 2:\n   377\t                continue\n   378\t\n   379\t            circuit_coords = []\n   380\t            path_weights = []\n   381\t            for idx, weight in enumerate(target_path):\n   382\t                mapped_idx = (idx * 19 + rank_idx * 7) % num_points\n   383\t                circuit_coords.append(points[mapped_idx])\n   384\t                path_weights.append(float(weight))\n   385\t\n   386\t            all_verts = []\n   387\t            all_faces = []\n   388\t            all_intensities = []\n   389\t            vertex_offset = 0\n   390\t\n   391\t            for i in range(len(circuit_coords) - 1):\n   392\t                p1 = circuit_coords[i]\n   393\t                p2 = circuit_coords[i + 1]\n   394\t                seg_weight = (path_weights[i] + path_weights[i+1]) / 2.0\n   395\t                \n   396\t                v_mesh, f_mesh = create_pipe_mesh(p1, p2, radius=5.0 - (rank_idx * 0.2), n_segs=10)\n   397\t                if len(v_mesh) > 0:\n   398\t                    all_verts.append(v_mesh)\n   399\t                    all_faces.append(f_mesh + vertex_offset)\n   400\t                    all_intensities.extend([seg_weight] * len(v_mesh))\n   401\t                    vertex_offset += len(v_mesh)\n   402\t\n   403\t            if all_verts:\n   404\t                combined_verts = np.vstack(all_verts)\n   405\t                combined_faces = np.vstack(all_faces)\n   406\t                combined_intensities = np.array(all_intensities)\n   407\t\n   408\t                cscale = colorscales[rank_idx % len(colorscales)]\n   409\t                pipe_trace = go.Mesh3d(\n   410\t                    x=combined_verts[:, 0], y=combined_verts[:, 1], z=combined_verts[:, 2],\n   411\t                    i=combined_faces[:, 0], j=combined_faces[:, 1], k=combined_faces[:, 2],\n   412\t                    intensity=combined_intensities,\n   413\t                    colorscale=cscale,\n   414\t                    opacity=0.95,\n   415\t                    lighting=dict(ambient=0.5, diffuse=0.9, specular=0.6),\n   416\t                    name=f'Path Rank #{rank_idx+1}'\n   417\t                )\n   418\t                traces.append(pipe_trace)\n   419\t\n   420\t        fig = go.Figure(data=traces)\n[445 lines total]"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"        )\\n        traces.append(labels_trace)\\n\\n        def create_pipe_mesh(p1, p2, radius=4.5, n_segs=10):\\n            p1, p2 = np.array(p1), np.array(p2)\\n            v = p2 - p1\\n            length = np.linalg.norm(v)\\n            if length < 1e-6:\\n                return np.empty((0, 3)), np.empty((0, 3), dtype=int)\\n            v = v / length\\n            \\n            n1 = np.array([0, 1, 0]) if abs(v[0]) > 0.9 else np.array([1, 0, 0])\\n            n1 = np.cross(v, n1)\\n            n1 /= np.linalg.norm(n1)\\n            n2 = np.cross(v, n1)\\n            \\n            theta = np.linspace(0, 2 * np.pi, n_segs, endpoint=False)\\n            circle = [radius * (np.cos(th) * n1 + np.sin(th) * n2) for th in theta]\\n            \\n            verts = [p1 + pt for pt in circle] + [p2 + pt for pt in circle]\\n            verts = np.array(verts)\\n            \\n            faces = []\\n            for i in range(n_segs):\\n                nxt = (i + 1) % n_segs\\n                faces.append([i, nxt, i + n_segs])\\n                faces.append([nxt, nxt + n_segs, i + n_segs])\\n                \\n            return verts, np.array(faces, dtype=int)\\n\\n        colorscales = ['Turbo', 'Viridis', 'Plasma', 'Inferno', 'Magma', 'Cividis']\\n        num_points = len(points)\\n\\n        # 3. Render all optimal circuit paths\\n        for rank_idx, res in enumerate(self.latest_results):\\n            target_path = res[2]\\n            if not target_path or len(target_path) < 2:\\n                continue\\n\\n            circuit_coords = []\\n            path_weights = []\\n            for idx, weight in enumerate(target_path):\\n                mapped_idx = (idx * 19 + rank_idx * 7) % num_points\\n                circuit_coords.append(points[mapped_idx])\\n                path_weights.append(float(weight))\\n\\n            all_verts = []\\n            all_faces = []\\n            all_intensities = []\\n            vertex_offset = 0\\n\\n            for i in range(len(circuit_coords) - 1):\\n                p1 = circuit_coords[i]\\n                p2 = circuit_coords[i + 1]\\n                seg_weight = (path_weights[i] + path_weights[i+1]) / 2.0\\n                \\n                v_mesh, f_mesh = create_pipe_mesh(p1, p2, radius=5.0 - (rank_idx * 0.2), n_segs=10)\\n                if len(v_mesh) > 0:\\n                    all_verts.append(v_mesh)\\n                    all_faces.append(f_mesh + vertex_offset)\\n                    all_intensities.extend([seg_weight] * len(v_mesh))\\n                    vertex_offset += len(v_mesh)\\n\\n            if all_verts:\\n                combined_verts = np.vstack(all_verts)\\n                combined_faces = np.vstack(all_faces)\\n                combined_intensities = np.array(all_intensities)\\n\\n                cscale = colorscales[rank_idx % len(colorscales)]\\n                pipe_trace = go.Mesh3d(\\n                    x=combined_verts[:, 0], y=combined_verts[:, 1], z=combined_verts[:, 2],\\n                    i=combined_faces[:, 0], j=combined_faces[:, 1], k=combined_faces[:, 2],\\n                    intensity=combined_intensities,\\n                    colorscale=cscale,\\n                    opacity=0.95,\\n                    lighting=dict(ambient=0.5, diffuse=0.9, specular=0.6),\\n                    name=f'Path Rank #{rank_idx+1}'\\n                )\\n                traces.append(pipe_trace)\\n\\n        fig = go.Figure(data=traces)\\n\", \"filename\": \"/home/claude/ncs/app.py\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:53:04.845753Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:53:05.974722Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "This part is unaffected \u2014 good, it still works using `points` from the new real surface. Now let's verify the whole thing end-to-end (headless, replicating the app's logic without Tkinter):", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:53:05.974751Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T11:53:10.941989Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_015mxgviDUMWsm4iNRsTaEb8", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/ncs && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport numpy as np\nnp.random.seed(0)\n\nimport sys\nsys.path.insert(0, \".\")\nimport importlib\nimport app as app_module\n\n# Fake object using app.py's methods without tkinter\nclass Fake:\n    pass\n\nobj = Fake()\nobj.mri_path = \"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\"\nobj.surface_verts_path = \"brain_surface_verts.npy\"\nobj.surface_faces_path = \"brain_surface_faces.npy\"\nobj._build_or_load_brain_surface = app_module.NeuralBeamSimulationApp._build_or_load_brain_surface.__get__(obj)\nobj._get_scientific_region_name = app_module.NeuralBeamSimulationApp._get_scientific_region_name.__get__(obj)\n\nimport time\nt0=time.time()\npoints, edges = obj._build_or_load_brain_surface()\nprint(\"verts:\", points.shape, \"faces:\", edges.shape, \"time:\", time.time()-t0)\n\nall_labels = np.array([obj._get_scientific_region_name(pt[0], pt[1], pt[2]) for pt in points])\nuniq = np.unique(all_labels)\nprint(\"distinct labels:\", len(uniq))\nprint(uniq)\n\nmax_idx = len(points) - 1\nvalid_mask = (\n    (edges[:, 0] >= 0) & (edges[:, 0] <= max_idx) &\n    (edges[:, 1] >= 0) & (edges[:, 1] <= max_idx) &\n    (edges[:, 2] >= 0) & (edges[:, 2] <= max_idx)\n)\nprint(\"valid triangles:\", valid_mask.sum(), \"/\", len(edges))\nEOF\n", "description": "Test the new surface build and label enumeration logic end-to-end"}, "message": "Test the new surface build and label enumeration logic end-to-end", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/ncs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport numpy as np\\nnp.random.seed(0)\\n\\nimport sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\".\\\")\\nimport importlib\\nimport app as app_module\\n\\n# Fake object using app.py's methods without tkinter\\nclass Fake:\\n    pass\\n\\nobj = Fake()\\nobj.mri_path = \\\"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\\\"\\nobj.surface_verts_path = \\\"brain_surface_verts.npy\\\"\\nobj.surface_faces_path = \\\"brain_surface_faces.npy\\\"\\nobj._build_or_load_brain_surface = app_module.NeuralBeamSimulationApp._build_or_load_brain_surface.__get__(obj)\\nobj._get_scientific_region_name = app_module.NeuralBeamSimulationApp._get_scientific_region_name.__get__(obj)\\n\\nimport time\\nt0=time.time()\\npoints, edges = obj._build_or_load_brain_surface()\\nprint(\\\"verts:\\\", points.shape, \\\"faces:\\\", edges.shape, \\\"time:\\\", time.time()-t0)\\n\\nall_labels = np.array([obj._get_scientific_region_name(pt[0], pt[1], pt[2]) for pt in points])\\nuniq = np.unique(all_labels)\\nprint(\\\"distinct labels:\\\", len(uniq))\\nprint(uniq)\\n\\nmax_idx = len(points) - 1\\nvalid_mask = (\\n    (edges[:, 0] >= 0) & (edges[:, 0] <= max_idx) &\\n    (edges[:, 1] >= 0) & (edges[:, 1] <= max_idx) &\\n    (edges[:, 2] >= 0) & (edges[:, 2] <= max_idx)\\n)\\nprint(\\\"valid triangles:\\\", valid_mask.sum(), \\\"/\\\", len(edges))\\nEOF\\n\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_time