"approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:14:51.425198Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:14:51.425221Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_015zNGE45MLT7YZBm6S7JyGC", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/app.py", "name": "app", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "The file cards appear at the end of your reply if it ends with text, otherwise under this step; say they are below only if you finish the reply with text."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:14:53.742453Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:14:55.548169Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Fixed \u2014 the mesh color string had an alpha value baked in (`rgba(135, 206, 250, 0.2)`) *plus* a separate `opacity=0.25` stacked on top, compounding down to roughly 0.05 effective opacity. That's invisible against a white background even though the geometry itself was fine (which is why labels and pipes, which don't go through `color`, still showed). Switched to a plain solid color name with a single `opacity=0.35`, so it renders at an actually visible transparency now.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-09-27T12:14:55.628683Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T12:14:55.628683Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0e2c9-7451-7dd4-affb-58fc5a4cfce1"}, {"uuid": "01a0e2ca-69b2-7611-9c22-8beab4534c40", "text": "add inner labels, like in the inner of the brain", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:15:10.631425Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:15:10.631425Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "add inner labels, like in the inner of the brain", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-09-27T12:15:10.631662Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T12:15:10.631662Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0e2c9-7451-786d-92eb-3c1e94abff31"}, {"uuid": "01a0e2ca-69b2-7680-ab62-754ee30c0438", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow let's add an inner-structure heuristic and an interior-point builder, right after the existing surface-label heuristic:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow register the new cache path and wire the inner labels into the render:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow let's look at the render section to add the inner-labels trace right after the existing outer-label trace:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow insert the inner-labels build/render right after the outer labels trace:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow let's test end-to-end:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nMissing \"Cerebellum\" from the label set (edge-of-range heuristic bucket just didn't get hit in the random subsample) \u2014 let's bump the sample size a bit for better coverage:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nAll 14 distinct interior labels now present with reasonable coverage. Let's run the full end-to-end render once more to confirm everything still works together:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nRuns clean, fast (cached), and produces the expected output. Let's clean up and ship:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nAdded inner labels. Since the surface mesh only has vertices on the *outer* boundary of the head, there was nothing to anchor a deep-structure label to before \u2014 now it samples points from well inside the tissue (erodes the mask ~15 voxels in via `scipy.ndimage.binary_erosion`, then randomly samples 60k interior points) and labels those with a second heuristic function tuned for subcortical-style structures instead of outer cortex.\n\nYou'll now see, in dark red (vs. black for the outer labels) so they're visually distinct:\n- Thalamus, Brainstem, Corpus Callosum (Genu/Splenium) \u2014 midline\n- Left/Right Caudate Nucleus, Putamen, Amygdala, Hippocampus, Cerebellum \u2014 lateral\n\nSame caveat as the outer labels applies here too: it's a coordinate-bucket heuristic, not a real anatomical segmentation \u2014 same level of rigor as the rest of the app, just extended inward. All 14 distinct interior labels get placed (one per region, at the point closest to that region's own centroid), same approach as before so it doesn't reintroduce the \"millions of overlapping duplicates\" problem.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:15:10.626161Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:15:41.461717Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Adding labels for internal brain structures, not just surface."}, {"summary": "Designing coordinate-based heuristics for subcortical structure names."}, {"summary": "Sampling interior volume points to represent inner regions."}, {"summary": "Mapping coordinate zones to specific subcortical structure names."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:15:41.461816Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:15:43.961172Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_015D8Xz6fR1xcB1DsQX98eLi", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/ncs && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport time, numpy as np, nibabel as nib\nfrom scipy import ndimage\n\nt0=time.time()\nimg = nib.load(\"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\")\ndata = img.get_fdata().astype(np.float32)\nrobust_max = np.percentile(data[data > 0], 99)\nvolume = np.clip(data / robust_max, 0, 1)\nmask = volume > 0.2\nprint(\"mask voxels:\", mask.sum(), \"load+mask time\", time.time()-t0)\n\nfor iters in [10, 20, 30]:\n    t0=time.time()\n    eroded = ndimage.binary_erosion(mask, iterations=iters)\n    print(f\"iterations={iters}: remaining voxels={eroded.sum()}, time={time.time()-t0:.2f}s\")\nEOF\n", "description": "Test erosion performance and remaining interior voxel counts"}, "message": "Test erosion performance and remaining interior voxel counts", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/ncs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport time, numpy as np, nibabel as nib\\nfrom scipy import ndimage\\n\\nt0=time.time()\\nimg = nib.load(\\\"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\\\")\\ndata = img.get_fdata().astype(np.float32)\\nrobust_max = np.percentile(data[data > 0], 99)\\nvolume = np.clip(data / robust_max, 0, 1)\\nmask = volume > 0.2\\nprint(\\\"mask voxels:\\\", mask.sum(), \\\"load+mask time\\\", time.time()-t0)\\n\\nfor iters in [10, 20, 30]:\\n    t0=time.time()\\n    eroded = ndimage.binary_erosion(mask, iterations=iters)\\n    print(f\\\"iterations={iters}: remaining voxels={eroded.sum()}, time={time.time()-t0:.2f}s\\\")\\nEOF\\n\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:15:45.225832Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:15:45.225872Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_015D8Xz6fR1xcB1DsQX98eLi", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"mask voxels: 1560800 load+mask time 0.22513651847839355\\niterations=10: remaining voxels=975798, time=0.11s\\niterations=20: remaining voxels=552415, time=0.11s\\niterations=30: remaining voxels=259944, time=0.12s\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"mask voxels: 1560800 load+mask time 0.22513651847839355\\niterations=10: remaining voxels=975798, time=0.11s\\niterations=20: remaining voxels=552415, time=0.11s\\niterations=30: remaining voxels=259944, time=0.12s\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:15:49.095279Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:15:52.007773Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01KmkXy64oKWX5Zw9tT2649q", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/ncs && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport numpy as np, nibabel as nib\nfrom scipy import ndimage\n\nimg = nib.load(\"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\")\ndata = img.get_fdata().astype(np.float32)\nrobust_max = np.percentile(data[data > 0], 99)\nvolume = np.clip(data / robust_max, 0, 1)\nmask = volume > 0.2\neroded = ndimage.binary_erosion(mask, iterations=25)\ncoords = np.argwhere(eroded).astype(np.float64)\ncentered = coords - np.array(data.shape)/2.0\nprint(\"interior centered range:\", centered.min(axis=0), centered.max(axis=0))\nprint(\"count:\", len(centered))\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(0)\nsample = centered[rng.choice(len(centered), size=20000, replace=False)]\nprint(\"x range\", sample[:,0].min(), sample[:,0].max())\nprint(\"y range\", sample[:,1].min(), sample[:,1].max())\nprint(\"z range\", sample[:,2].min(), sample[:,2].max())\nEOF\n", "description": "Check coordinate ranges of interior sample points"}, "message": "Check coordinate ranges of interior sample points", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/ncs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport numpy as np, nibabel as nib\\nfrom scipy import ndimage\\n\\nimg = nib.load(\\\"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\\\")\\ndata = img.get_fdata().astype(np.float32)\\nrobust_max = np.percentile(data[data > 0], 99)\\nvolume = np.clip(data / robust_max, 0, 1)\\nmask = volume > 0.2\\neroded = ndimage.binary_erosion(mask, iterations=25)\\ncoords = np.argwhere(eroded).astype(np.float64)\\ncentered = coords - np.array(data.shape)/2.0\\nprint(\\\"interior centered range:\\\", centered.min(axis=0), centered.max(axis=0))\\nprint(\\\"count:\\\", len(centered))\\n\\nrng = np.random.default_rng(0)\\nsample = centered[rng.choice(len(centered), size=20000, replace=False)]\\nprint(\\\"x range\\\", sample[:,0].min(), sample[:,0].max())\\nprint(\\\"y range\\\", sample[:,1].min(), sample[:,1].max())\\nprint(\\\"z range\\\", sample[:,2].min(), sample[:,2].max())\\nEOF\\n\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:15:52.946239Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:15:52.946274Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01KmkXy64oKWX5Zw9tT2649q", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"interior centered range: [-44.  -53.  -37.5] [42.  74.  38.5]\\ncount: 390537\\nx range -43.0 42.0\\ny range -53.0 74.0\\nz range -37.5 38.5\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"interior centered range: [-44.  -53.  -37.5] [42.  74.  38.5]\\ncount: 390537\\nx range -43.0 42.0\\ny range -53.0 74.0\\nz range -37.5 38.5\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:15:54.601809Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:06.801253Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Working out the shape's interior bounding dimensions."}, {"summary": "Designing a heuristic to label inner brain structures."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:06.801436Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:07.569956Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01HUfGovDsY7KHETyenrbSaE", "name": "view", "input": {"description": "Locate the inner structure area to insert new method and path variable", "path": "/home/claude/ncs/app.py", "view_range": [195, 245]}, "message": "Locate the inner structure area to insert new method and path variable", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Locate the inner structure area to insert new method and path variable"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:07.781294Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:07.781436Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01HUfGovDsY7KHETyenrbSaE", "name": "view", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "   195\t\n   196\t    def _get_scientific_region_name(self, x: float, y: float, z: float) -> str:\n   197\t        \"\"\"Maps MNI coordinate space to standard neuroanatomical scientific names.\"\"\"\n   198\t        hemisphere = \"Right\" if x >= 0 else \"Left\"\n   199\t        ax, ay, az = abs(x), y, z\n   200\t\n   201\t        if ay > 30:\n   202\t            if az > 20:\n   203\t                return f\"{hemisphere} Sup. Frontal\"\n   204\t            elif az > 0:\n   205\t                return f\"{hemisphere} Mid. Frontal\"\n   206\t            else:\n   207\t                return f\"{hemisphere} Orbital Frontal\"\n   208\t        elif 0 <= ay <= 30:\n   209\t            if az > 35:\n   210\t                return f\"{hemisphere} Precentral / Motor\"\n   211\t            elif az > 10:\n   212\t                return f\"{hemisphere} Supp. Motor\"\n   213\t            elif az < -5:\n   214\t                return f\"{hemisphere} Insular\"\n   215\t            else:\n   216\t                return f\"{hemisphere} Ant. Cingulate\"\n   217\t        elif -50 <= ay < 0:\n   218\t            if az > 40:\n   219\t                return f\"{hemisphere} Postcentral\"\n   220\t            elif az > 20:\n   221\t                return f\"{hemisphere} Inf. Parietal\"\n   222\t            elif az < 0:\n   223\t                return f\"{hemisphere} Sup. Temporal\"\n   224\t            else:\n   225\t                return f\"{hemisphere} Post. Cingulate\"\n   226\t        else:\n   227\t            if az > 10:\n   228\t                return f\"{hemisphere} Precuneus\"\n   229\t            elif az < -10:\n   230\t                return f\"{hemisphere} Fusiform\"\n   231\t            else:\n   232\t                return f\"{hemisphere} Occipital Pole\"\n   233\t\n   234\t    def _build_or_load_brain_surface(self):\n   235\t        \"\"\"\n   236\t        Builds a real triangulated brain surface straight from the MRI volume\n   237\t        (via marching cubes) and caches it to disk. The previous version read\n   238\t        `connectivity_edges.bin`, but that file stores graph edges\n   239\t        (src:int32, dst:int32, weight:float32) written by the simulation\n   240\t        script -- not triangle indices -- so reinterpreting its bytes as\n   241\t        (i, j, k) mesh faces produced zero valid triangles. This builds an\n   242\t        actual surface instead.\n   243\t        \"\"\"\n   244\t        if os.path.exists(self.surface_verts_path) and os.path.exists(self.surface_faces_path):\n   245\t            verts = np.load(self.surface_verts_path)\n[498 lines total]"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"\\n    def _get_scientific_region_name(self, x: float, y: float, z: float) -> str:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Maps MNI coordinate space to standard neuroanatomical scientific names.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        hemisphere = \\\"Right\\\" if x >= 0 else \\\"Left\\\"\\n        ax, ay, az = abs(x), y, z\\n\\n        if ay > 30:\\n            if az > 20:\\n                return f\\\"{hemisphere} Sup. Frontal\\\"\\n            elif az > 0:\\n                return f\\\"{hemisphere} Mid. Frontal\\\"\\n            else:\\n                return f\\\"{hemisphere} Orbital Frontal\\\"\\n        elif 0 <= ay <= 30:\\n            if az > 35:\\n                return f\\\"{hemisphere} Precentral / Motor\\\"\\n            elif az > 10:\\n                return f\\\"{hemisphere} Supp. Motor\\\"\\n            elif az < -5:\\n                return f\\\"{hemisphere} Insular\\\"\\n            else:\\n                return f\\\"{hemisphere} Ant. Cingulate\\\"\\n        elif -50 <= ay < 0:\\n            if az > 40:\\n                return f\\\"{hemisphere} Postcentral\\\"\\n            elif az > 20:\\n                return f\\\"{hemisphere} Inf. Parietal\\\"\\n            elif az < 0:\\n                return f\\\"{hemisphere} Sup. Temporal\\\"\\n            else:\\n                return f\\\"{hemisphere} Post. Cingulate\\\"\\n        else:\\n            if az > 10:\\n                return f\\\"{hemisphere} Precuneus\\\"\\n            elif az < -10:\\n                return f\\\"{hemisphere} Fusiform\\\"\\n            else:\\n                return f\\\"{hemisphere} Occipital Pole\\\"\\n\\n    def _build_or_load_brain_surface(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Builds a real triangulated brain surface straight from the MRI volume\\n        (via marching cubes) and caches it to disk. The previous version read\\n        `connectivity_edges.bin`, but that file stores graph edges\\n        (src:int32, dst:int32, weight:float32) written by the simulation\\n        script -- not triangle indices -- so reinterpreting its bytes as\\n        (i, j, k) mesh faces produced zero valid triangles. This builds an\\n        actual surface instead.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if os.path.exists(self.surface_verts_path) and os.path.exists(self.surface_faces_path):\\n            verts = np.load(self.surface_verts_path)\\n\", \"filename\": \"/home/claude/ncs/app.py\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:09.529088Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:10.211069Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now let's add an inner-structure heuristic and an interior-point builder, right after the existing surface-label heuristic:", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:10.211166Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:19.647210Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01QZBdamKuF1DcpbZ6ganAhL", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"new_str": "        else:\n            if az > 10:\n                return f\"{hemisphere} Precuneus\"\n            elif az < -10:\n                return f\"{hemisphere} Fusiform\"\n            else:\n                return f\"{hemisphere} Occipital Pole\"\n\n    def _get_inner_structure_name(self, x: float, y: float, z: float) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Same kind of coordinate-bucket heuristic as _get_scientific_region_name,\n        just tuned for the deeper structures instead of outer cortex -- not a\n        real anatomical segmentation, just a plausible-looking label for a\n        given position relative to the brain's center.\n        \"\"\"\n        hemisphere = \"Right\" if x >= 0 else \"Left\"\n        ax, ay, az = abs(x), y, z\n\n        if ax < 10:  # near the midline\n            if ay > 15:\n                return \"Corpus Callosum (Genu)\"\n            elif ay > -5:\n                return \"Thalamus\"\n            elif ay > -25:\n                return \"Corpus Callosum (Splenium)\"\n            else:\n                return \"Brainstem\"\n        else:  # lateral structures, mirrored left/right\n            if az > 10:\n                if ay > 0:\n                    return f\"{hemisphere} Caudate Nucleus\"\n                else:\n                    return f\"{hemisphere} Putamen\"\n            elif az > -12:\n                if ay > -5:\n                    return f\"{hemisphere} Putamen\"\n                elif ay > -25:\n                    return f\"{hemisphere} Amygdala\"\n                else:\n                    return f\"{hemisphere} Hippocampus\"\n            else:\n                if ay < -35:\n                    return f\"{hemisphere} Cerebellum\"\n                else:\n                    return f\"{hemisphere} Hippocampus\"\n\n    def _build_or_load_inner_points(self):\n        \"\"\"\n        Samples points from well *inside* the tissue mask (not on its outer\n        boundary) so labels can be placed for interior/subcortical-style\n        structures, not just the outer surface. Erodes the same tissue mask\n        used for the surface by ~25 voxels so sampled points sit clearly\n        underneath the surface, then randomly subsamples for a manageable\n        point count.\n        \"\"\"\n        if os.path.exists(self.inner_points_path):\n            return np.load(self.inner_points_path)\n\n        if not os.path.exists(self.mri_path):\n            raise FileNotFoundError(f\"MRI file not found at {self.mri_path}\")\n\n        from scipy import ndimage\n\n        img = nib.load(self.mri_path)\n        data = img.get_fdata().astype(np.float32)\n        robust_max = np.percentile(data[data > 0], 99)\n        volume = np.clip(data / robust_max, 0, 1)\n\n        mask = volume > 0.2\n        interior_mask = ndimage.binary_erosion(mask, iterations=25)\n\n        coords = np.argwhere(interior_mask).astype(np.float64)\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(0)\n        n_sample = min(20000, len(coords))\n        sample = coords[rng.choice(len(coords), size=n_sample, replace=False)]\n\n        sample = sample - np.array(data.shape) / 2.0  # center, same as the surface\n\n        np.save(self.inner_points_path, sample)\n        return sample\n\n    def _build_or_load_brain_surface(self):", "old_str": "        else:\n            if az > 10:\n                return f\"{hemisphere} Precuneus\"\n            elif az < -10:\n                return f\"{hemisphere} Fusiform\"\n            else:\n                return f\"{hemisphere} Occipital Pole\"\n\n    def _build_or_load_brain_surface(self):", "path": "/home/claude/ncs/app.py"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:20.092219Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:20.092256Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01QZBdamKuF1DcpbZ6ganAhL", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/ncs/app.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/ncs/app.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:22.166413Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:22.626595Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now register the new cache path and wire the inner labels into the render:", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:22.626627Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:24.513898Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01PpRssYr1ufzXR3BRUpRCkb", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"new_str": "        self.data_path = \"weights.bin\"\n        self.mri_path = \"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\"\n        self.surface_verts_path = \"brain_surface_verts.npy\"\n        self.surface_faces_path = \"brain_surface_faces.npy\"\n        self.inner_points_path = \"brain_inner_points.npy\"", "old_str": "        self.data_path = \"weights.bin\"\n        self.mri_path = \"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\"\n        self.surface_verts_path = \"brain_surface_verts.npy\"\n        self.surface_faces_path = \"brain_surface_faces.npy\"", "path": "/home/claude/ncs/app.py"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:24.841369Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:24.841408Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01PpRssYr1ufzXR3BRUpRCkb", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/ncs/app.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/ncs/app.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:33.224119Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:33.595290Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now let's look at the render section to add the inner-labels trace right after the existing outer-label trace:", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:33.595330Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:34.401593Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01JcHtcWgKyUsM2veQ7kkPp8", "name": "view", "input": {"description": "View current show_cortical_overlay label section for insertion point", "path": "/home/claude/ncs/app.py", "view_range": [355, 405]}, "message": "View current show_cortical_overlay label section for insertion point", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "View current show_cortical_overlay label section for insertion point"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:34.663101Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:34.663157Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01JcHtcWgKyUsM2veQ7kkPp8", "name": "view", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "   355\t            return\n   356\t\n   357\t        self.status_var.set(\"Status: Building brain surface from MRI (first run only)...\")\n   358\t        self.root.update_idletasks()\n   359\t\n   360\t        try:\n   361\t            points, edges = self._build_or_load_brain_surface()\n   362\t        except Exception as e:\n   363\t            messagebox.showerror(\"Surface Build Error\", f\"Failed to build brain surface:\\n{e}\")\n   364\t            return\n   365\t\n   366\t        self.status_var.set(\"Status: Loading labels and circuit paths...\")\n   367\t        self.root.update_idletasks()\n   368\t\n   369\t        traces = []\n   370\t\n   371\t        # 1. Real Anatomical Brain Surface Mesh\n   372\t        # Note: the color string previously had alpha baked in\n   373\t        # ('rgba(...,0.2)') *and* a separate opacity=0.25 on top of it.\n   374\t        # Mesh3d doesn't reliably honor an alpha channel inside a solid\n   375\t        # `color` string, and stacking that with `opacity` compounded down\n   376\t        # to ~0.05 effective opacity -- invisible against a white\n   377\t        # background, even though the geometry itself was rendering fine\n   378\t        # (labels and pipes, which don't go through `color`, still showed).\n   379\t        # A solid color name plus a single opacity value fixes it.\n   380\t        brain_mesh = go.Mesh3d(\n   381\t            x=points[:, 0], y=points[:, 1], z=points[:, 2],\n   382\t            i=edges[:, 0], j=edges[:, 1], k=edges[:, 2],\n   383\t            color='lightskyblue',\n   384\t            opacity=0.35,\n   385\t            lighting=dict(ambient=0.7, diffuse=0.6, specular=0.2),\n   386\t            name='Anatomical Brain Mesh',\n   387\t            hoverinfo='skip'\n   388\t        )\n   389\t        traces.append(brain_mesh)\n   390\t\n   391\t        # 2. Add Scientific Region Labels. _get_scientific_region_name only\n   392\t        # ever produces ~28 distinct strings (2 hemispheres x 14 named\n   393\t        # zones) -- with ~30k mesh vertices, labeling \"all of them\" would\n   394\t        # mean stamping the same ~28 words tens of thousands of times on\n   395\t        # top of each other and would also make the browser choke trying to\n   396\t        # render that many text objects. Instead this labels every one of\n   397\t        # those distinct regions exactly once, at a representative point\n   398\t        # (the vertex closest to that region's own centroid).\n   399\t        all_labels = np.array([\n   400\t            self._get_scientific_region_name(pt[0], pt[1], pt[2]) for pt in points\n   401\t        ])\n   402\t\n   403\t        mesh_centroid = points.mean(axis=0)\n   404\t        label_points = []\n   405\t        label_text = []\n[572 lines total]"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"            return\\n\\n        self.status_var.set(\\\"Status: Building brain surface from MRI (first run only)...\\\")\\n        self.root.update_idletasks()\\n\\n        try:\\n            points, edges = self._build_or_load_brain_surface()\\n        except Exception as e:\\n            messagebox.showerror(\\\"Surface Build Error\\\", f\\\"Failed to build brain surface:\\\\n{e}\\\")\\n            return\\n\\n        self.status_var.set(\\\"Status: Loading labels and circuit paths...\\\")\\n        self.root.update_idletasks()\\n\\n        traces = []\\n\\n        # 1. Real Anatomical Brain Surface Mesh\\n        # Note: the color string previously had alpha baked in\\n        # ('rgba(...,0.2)') *and* a separate opacity=0.25 on top of it.\\n        # Mesh3d doesn't reliably honor an alpha channel inside a solid\\n        # `color` string, and stacking that with `opacity` compounded down\\n        # to ~0.05 effective opacity -- invisible against a white\\n        # background, even though the geometry itself was rendering fine\\n        # (labels and pipes, which don't go through `color`, still showed).\\n        # A solid color name plus a single opacity value fixes it.\\n        brain_mesh = go.Mesh3d(\\n            x=points[:, 0], y=points[:, 1], z=points[:, 2],\\n            i=edges[:, 0], j=edges[:, 1], k=edges[:, 2],\\n            color='lightskyblue',\\n            opacity=0.35,\\n            lighting=dict(ambient=0.7, diffuse=0.6, specular=0.2),\\n            name='Anatomical Brain Mesh',\\n            hoverinfo='skip'\\n        )\\n        traces.append(brain_mesh)\\n\\n        # 2. Add Scientific Region Labels. _get_scientific_region_name only\\n        # ever produces ~28 distinct strings (2 hemispheres x 14 named\\n        # zones) -- with ~30k mesh vertices, labeling \\\"all of them\\\" would\\n        # mean stamping the same ~28 words tens of thousands of times on\\n        # top of each other and would also make the browser choke trying to\\n        # render that many text objects. Instead this labels every one of\\n        # those distinct regions exactly once, at a representative point\\n        # (the vertex closest to that region's own centroid).\\n        all_labels = np.array([\\n            self._get_scientific_region_name(pt[0], pt[1], pt[2]) for pt in points\\n        ])\\n\\n        mesh_centroid = points.mean(axis=0)\\n        label_points = []\\n        label_text = []\\n\", \"filename\": \"/home/claude/ncs/app.py\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:36.599882Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:37.494811Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_015y6xPC4QvCgp8tqNk5GMC9", "name": "view", "input": {"description": "Continue viewing to find end of label trace block", "path": "/home/claude/ncs/app.py", "view_range": [405, 435]}, "message": "Continue viewing to find end of label trace block", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Continue viewing to find end of label trace block"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:37.735525Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:37.735578Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_015y6xPC4QvCgp8tqNk5GMC9", "name": "view", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "   405\t        label_text = []\n   406\t        for label in np.unique(all_labels):\n   407\t            group_idx = np.where(all_labels == label)[0]\n   408\t            group_pts = points[group_idx]\n   409\t            centroid = group_pts.mean(axis=0)\n   410\t            nearest = group_idx[np.argmin(np.linalg.norm(group_pts - centroid, axis=1))]\n   411\t            anchor = points[nearest]\n   412\t            # Push the label outward along the mesh's own radial direction so\n   413\t            # it floats just outside the surface instead of sitting exactly\n   414\t            # on it -- with 28 labels around one small object, text anchored\n   415\t            # right at the surface reads as one dense, overlapping cloud.\n   416\t            # Pushing radially outward spreads near neighbors further apart\n   417\t            # in screen space and stops the mesh from crowding the text.\n   418\t            direction = anchor - mesh_centroid\n   419\t            direction = direction / (np.linalg.norm(direction) + 1e-8)\n   420\t            label_points.append(anchor + direction * 18.0)\n   421\t            label_text.append(label)\n   422\t        label_points = np.array(label_points)\n   423\t\n   424\t        labels_trace = go.Scatter3d(\n   425\t            x=label_points[:, 0], y=label_points[:, 1], z=label_points[:, 2],\n   426\t            mode='text',\n   427\t            text=label_text,\n   428\t            textfont=dict(color='Black', size=10, family='Arial Bold'),\n   429\t            name='Scientific Region Labels'\n   430\t        )\n   431\t        traces.append(labels_trace)\n   432\t\n   433\t        def create_pipe_mesh(p1, p2, radius=4.5, n_segs=10):\n   434\t            p1, p2 = np.array(p1), np.array(p2)\n   435\t            v = p2 - p1\n[572 lines total]"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"        label_text = []\\n        for label in np.unique(all_labels):\\n            group_idx = np.where(all_labels == label)[0]\\n            group_pts = points[group_idx]\\n            centroid = group_pts.mean(axis=0)\\n            nearest = group_idx[np.argmin(np.linalg.norm(group_pts - centroid, axis=1))]\\n            anchor = points[nearest]\\n            # Push the label outward along the mesh's own radial direction so\\n            # it floats just outside the surface instead of sitting exactly\\n            # on it -- with 28 labels around one small object, text anchored\\n            # right at the surface reads as one dense, overlapping cloud.\\n            # Pushing radially outward spreads near neighbors further apart\\n            # in screen space and stops the mesh from crowding the text.\\n            direction = anchor - mesh_centroid\\n            direction = direction / (np.linalg.norm(direction) + 1e-8)\\n            label_points.append(anchor + direction * 18.0)\\n            label_text.append(label)\\n        label_points = np.array(label_points)\\n\\n        labels_trace = go.Scatter3d(\\n            x=label_points[:, 0], y=label_points[:, 1], z=label_points[:, 2],\\n            mode='text',\\n            text=label_text,\\n            textfont=dict(color='Black', size=10, family='Arial Bold'),\\n            name='Scientific Region Labels'\\n        )\\n        traces.append(labels_trace)\\n\\n        def create_pipe_mesh(p1, p2, radius=4.5, n_segs=10):\\n            p1, p2 = np.array(p1), np.array(p2)\\n            v = p2 - p1\\n\", \"filename\": \"/home/claude/ncs/app.py\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:39.495250Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:40.014314Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now insert the inner-labels build/render right after the outer labels trace:", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:40.014346Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:48.075808Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01TFsstocsW8MHVCDStErLp3", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"new_str": "        labels_trace = go.Scatter3d(\n            x=label_points[:, 0], y=label_points[:, 1], z=label_points[:, 2],\n            mode='text',\n            text=label_text,\n            textfont=dict(color='Black', size=10, family='Arial Bold'),\n            name='Scientific Region Labels'\n        )\n        traces.append(labels_trace)\n\n        # 2b. Inner/subcortical labels. The outer surface trace only has\n        # vertices ON the boundary of the head, so it can only ever label\n        # outer-cortex-style regions -- there was nothing to anchor a label\n        # like \"Thalamus\" or \"Hippocampus\" to, since those sit underneath\n        # the surface, not on it. This samples points from well inside the\n        # tissue mask instead (see _build_or_load_inner_points) and labels\n        # those the same \"one representative point per distinct name\" way,\n        # so labels for deep structures actually sit inside the brain\n        # rather than being pushed outward like the surface ones are.\n        try:\n            inner_points = self._build_or_load_inner_points()\n        except Exception as e:\n            inner_points = None\n            self.status_var.set(f\"Status: Inner labels skipped ({e})\")\n\n        if inner_points is not None and len(inner_points) > 0:\n            inner_all_labels = np.array([\n                self._get_inner_structure_name(pt[0], pt[1], pt[2]) for pt in inner_points\n            ])\n            inner_label_points = []\n            inner_label_text = []\n            for label in np.unique(inner_all_labels):\n                group_idx = np.where(inner_all_labels == label)[0]\n                group_pts = inner_points[group_idx]\n                centroid = group_pts.mean(axis=0)\n                nearest = group_idx[np.argmin(np.linalg.norm(group_pts - centroid, axis=1))]\n                inner_label_points.append(inner_points[nearest])\n                inner_label_text.append(label)\n            inner_label_points = np.array(inner_label_points)\n\n            inner_labels_trace = go.Scatter3d(\n                x=inner_label_points[:, 0], y=inner_label_points[:, 1], z=inner_label_points[:, 2],\n                mode='text',\n                text=inner_label_text,\n                textfont=dict(color='darkred', size=10, family='Arial Bold'),\n                name='Inner Structure Labels'\n            )\n            traces.append(inner_labels_trace)\n\n        def create_pipe_mesh(p1, p2, radius=4.5, n_segs=10):\n            p1, p2 = np.array(p1), np.array(p2)\n            v = p2 - p1", "old_str": "        labels_trace = go.Scatter3d(\n            x=label_points[:, 0], y=label_points[:, 1], z=label_points[:, 2],\n            mode='text',\n            text=label_text,\n            textfont=dict(color='Black', size=10, family='Arial Bold'),\n            name='Scientific Region Labels'\n        )\n        traces.append(labels_trace)\n\n        def create_pipe_mesh(p1, p2, radius=4.5, n_segs=10):\n            p1, p2 = np.array(p1), np.array(p2)\n            v = p2 - p1", "path": "/home/claude/ncs/app.py"}, "message": "Editing file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:48.647985Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:48.648024Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01TFsstocsW8MHVCDStErLp3", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/ncs/app.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /home/claude/ncs/app.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:50.528352Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:50.791422Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now let's test end-to-end:", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:50.791462Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:56.552021Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01QvCQinxy5hebDR2gdQqbsq", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/ncs && rm -f labeled_clean_brain.html brain_inner_points.npy && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport numpy as np, time\nimport app as app_module\n\nclass Fake: pass\nobj = Fake()\nobj.mri_path = \"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\"\nobj.surface_verts_path = \"brain_surface_verts.npy\"\nobj.surface_faces_path = \"brain_surface_faces.npy\"\nobj.inner_points_path = \"brain_inner_points.npy\"\nobj._build_or_load_brain_surface = app_module.NeuralBeamSimulationApp._build_or_load_brain_surface.__get__(obj)\nobj._build_or_load_inner_points = app_module.NeuralBeamSimulationApp._build_or_load_inner_points.__get__(obj)\nobj._get_scientific_region_name = app_module.NeuralBeamSimulationApp._get_scientific_region_name.__get__(obj)\nobj._get_inner_structure_name = app_module.NeuralBeamSimulationApp._get_inner_structure_name.__get__(obj)\n\nobj.latest_results = [\n    (0.1, 6.9, (1.5, 2.2, 3.8, -1.6, 5.0, 6.3, 1.1)),\n    (0.3, 7.3, (2.2, 5.0, 4.1)),\n]\nclass DummyStatus:\n    def set(self, *a, **k): pass\nclass DummyRoot:\n    def update_idletasks(self): pass\nobj.status_var = DummyStatus()\nobj.root = DummyRoot()\n\nt0=time.time()\nobj.show_cortical_overlay = app_module.NeuralBeamSimulationApp.show_cortical_overlay.__get__(obj)\nobj.show_cortical_overlay()\nprint(\"render time:\", round(time.time()-t0,2))\n\nimport os\nprint(\"HTML size KB:\", round(os.path.getsize(\"labeled_clean_brain.html\")/1024,1))\n\ninner = obj._build_or_load_inner_points()\nlabels = np.array([obj._get_inner_structure_name(p[0],p[1],p[2]) for p in inner])\nuniq = np.unique(labels)\nprint(\"distinct inner labels:\", len(uniq))\nfor u in uniq: print(\" -\", u)\nEOF\n", "description": "Full end-to-end test of inner labels feature"}, "message": "Full end-to-end test of inner labels feature", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/ncs && rm -f labeled_clean_brain.html brain_inner_points.npy && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport numpy as np, time\\nimport app as app_module\\n\\nclass Fake: pass\\nobj = Fake()\\nobj.mri_path = \\\"real_brain_mri_t1.nii.gz\\\"\\nobj.surface_verts_path = \\\"brain_surface_verts.npy\\\"\\nobj.surface_faces_path = \\\"brain_surface_faces.npy\\\"\\nobj.inner_points_path = \\\"brain_inner_points.npy\\\"\\nobj._build_or_load_brain_surface = app_module.NeuralBeamSimulationApp._build_or_load_brain_surface.__get__(obj)\\nobj._build_or_load_inner_points = app_module.NeuralBeamSimulationApp._build_or_load_inner_points.__get__(obj)\\nobj._get_scientific_region_name = app_module.NeuralBeamSimulationApp._get_scientific_region_name.__get__(obj)\\nobj._get_inner_structure_name = app_module.NeuralBeamSimulationApp._get_inner_structure_name.__get__(obj)\\n\\nobj.latest_results = [\\n    (0.1, 6.9, (1.5, 2.2, 3.8, -1.6, 5.0, 6.3, 1.1)),\\n    (0.3, 7.3, (2.2, 5.0, 4.1)),\\n]\\nclass DummyStatus:\\n    def set(self, *a, **k): pass\\nclass DummyRoot:\\n    def update_idletasks(self): pass\\nobj.status_var = DummyStatus()\\nobj.root = DummyRoot()\\n\\nt0=time.time()\\nobj.show_cortical_overlay = app_module.NeuralBeamSimulationApp.show_cortical_overlay.__get__(obj)\\nobj.show_cortical_overlay()\\nprint(\\\"render time:\\\", round(time.time()-t0,2))\\n\\nimport os\\nprint(\\\"HTML size KB:\\\", round(os.path.getsize(\\\"labeled_clean_brain.html\\\")/1024,1))\\n\\ninner = obj._build_or_load_inner_points()\\nlabels = np.array([obj._get_inner_structure_name(p[0],p[1],p[2]) for p in inner])\\nuniq = np.unique(labels)\\nprint(\\\"distinct inner labels:\\\", len(uniq))\\nfor u in uniq: print(\\\" -\\\", u)\\nEOF\\n\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T12:16:57