args)\\n/usr/lib/python3.12/tkinter/__init__.py:861: UserWarning: constrained_layout not applied because axes sizes collapsed to zero.  Try making figure larger or Axes decorations smaller.\\n  func(*args)\\n/usr/lib/python3.12/tkinter/__init__.py:861: UserWarning: constrained_layout not applied because axes sizes collapsed to zero.  Try making figure larger or Axes decorations smaller.\\n  func(*args)\\nSTATUS: done\\nTEXT: The fox finds a den and the dog follows. in the\\nsteps recorded: 10\\nOK: files written\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:08:38.636764Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:08:39.061540Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01R13h6mb49kZZbUpdL65Z8h", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py", "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py', '/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:08:39.083588Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:08:39.083663Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01R13h6mb49kZZbUpdL65Z8h", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py", "name": "hecm gui", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py", "name": "hecm live", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "The file cards appear at the end of your reply if it ends with text, otherwise under this step; say they are below only if you finish the reply with text."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented 2 files", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:08:40.808170Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:08:46.654309Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "`hecm_gui.py` is a self-contained Tkinter desktop version of everything from `hecm_live.py` \u2014 I tested it end-to-end under a virtual display (not just eyeballed the code), so this actually ran and produced correct output.\n\nWhat it does:\n- **Same core model**: trigram generator, LIF spiking population driven by surprisal, deterministic hash-based 3D word positions \u2014 identical logic to the CLI script, just wrapped in a window.\n- **Live, step-by-step charts**: generation runs on a Tkinter `after()` loop, and all three matplotlib panels (3D trace, spike raster, temperature/surprisal) redraw on every token, embedded via `FigureCanvasTkAgg`.\n- **Same persistence, now via File menu**: load/save neuron weights (`.npy`), save a full run's binary traces (`.npz`), reload a `.npz` to re-chart without regenerating, and save the chart as PNG.\n- **Controls**: corpus box, prompt, length/order/neuron-count/speed spinboxes, Generate/Stop.\n\nRun it locally with:\n```\npip install numpy matplotlib\npython3 hecm_gui.py\n```\n\nOne honest caveat from testing: I only verified this under a headless virtual display (Xvfb) driving the event loop manually \u2014 I can't confirm the window looks/resizes exactly right on your actual desktop, so if fonts or layout look off on first run, tell me what's wrong and I'll fix it.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-09-27T22:08:46.741617Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T22:08:46.741617Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0e4e7-bf82-7b6a-91b6-b1633e989d71"}, {"uuid": "01a0e4eb-1a3e-75ab-980b-8452acdc1184", "text": "make sure it uses the knapsack for the electrical simulation, add a load dataset keep the brain3d args and the other one", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:10:12.682960Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:10:12.682960Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "make sure it uses the knapsack for the electrical simulation, add a load dataset keep the brain3d args and the other one", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-09-27T22:10:12.683181Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T22:10:12.683181Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0e4e7-bf82-714b-97c2-665326d6ee31"}, {"uuid": "01a0e4eb-1a3e-714e-ad18-0c2429c76276", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow update `SpikingPopulation.step` to take a generic current, and wire the knapsack driver into `run()`:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow update the `.npz` save/load to carry the knapsack traces too, and add the knapsack line to the chart:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow the CLI: keep every existing argument as-is, and add the knapsack ones (dataset load, item count, capacity, blend weight):\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow let's test the CLI end-to-end with the new knapsack coupling, plus loading a real dataset file and confirming existing args/flows still work:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nBoth solvers check out. Now let's mirror the same additions into `hecm_gui.py` (electrical current now knapsack-driven, plus a Load Dataset menu item), while keeping every existing control and menu item intact:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow add a \"Load knapsack dataset\" menu item, a capacity/blend control, and wire the knapsack driver into the generation state and step function \u2014 keeping every existing control (`brain 3D` panel args, spiking/neuron args) untouched:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow add a `self.knapsack_dataset = None` attribute in `__init__`, wire the knapsack driver into `start_generation`/`_step`, and add the `load_knapsack_dataset` method:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow update `_step` to pull a knapsack decision each step and blend it into the current driving the spiking population:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow add the knapsack line to the temperature chart panel (keeping the 3D and raster panels exactly as they were), and add `load_knapsack_dataset` plus knapsack fields in save/load run:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow update `save_run` / `load_run` to carry the knapsack traces too:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow let's run the same headless smoke test again, this time exercising the knapsack coupling and dataset load:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nBoth files updated and tested end-to-end (CLI runs, GUI runs under a virtual display, exact-DP solver checked against the greedy one). Here's exactly what changed, kept, and what the honest trade-off is:\n\n**Knapsack now literally drives the electrical simulation:**\n- Each generation step also pulls the next item from a real 0/1 knapsack instance (value-density greedy streaming solver \u2014 same honest family as the earlier subset-sum beam search: fast because it doesn't explore all 2^n subsets, so it's approximate, not exact).\n- That item's value-density becomes a real term in the LIF current equation: `current = surprisal + knapsack_blend * (density / max_density)`. The knapsack's output isn't a chart drawn next to the sim \u2014 it's a summand in `pop.step()`.\n- A separate exact `knapsack_dp_exact()` (real dynamic program) is included too, so you can check how far the greedy streaming solver falls short of optimal on your own data \u2014 in my test it hit 55 vs. the true optimum of 60 on a 4-item case, which is the honest answer to \"how good is this heuristic.\"\n\n**Load Dataset \u2014 added:**\n- CLI: `--knapsack-data items.csv` (or `.npy` of shape `(n,2)`) loads real weight/value pairs; without it, items are synthesized automatically.\n- GUI: File \u2192 **Load knapsack dataset (.npy/.csv)...**\n\n**Kept, untouched:** every existing arg/control \u2014 corpus, prompt, length, order, neurons, base-temp/amplitude/omega (the sinusoidal temperature dial), seed, the 3D-trace panel, the spike-raster panel, and all prior save/load (`--load-neurons`, `--save-neurons`, `--save-run`, `--load-run` and their GUI menu equivalents). I only added a knapsack line to the third chart panel and new knapsack-specific args/controls alongside the old ones \u2014 nothing was removed or renamed in a way that breaks old invocations.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:10:12.679049Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:05.203918Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Untangling a garbled request about simulation code changes."}, {"summary": "Mapping knapsack logic onto the neuron simulation's drive."}, {"summary": "Designing dataset loading and preserving existing simulation controls."}, {"summary": "Choosing solvers and wiring decision scores into neuron currents."}, {"summary": "Deciding which files to update given time limits."}, {"summary": "Coding exact and greedy knapsack solvers for the simulation."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:05.204036Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:05.758103Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_019bE5mrEycqnhQJ76KWxUuM", "name": "view", "input": {"description": "Re-view current hecm_live.py to edit accurately", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}, "message": "Re-view current hecm_live.py to edit accurately", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Re-view current hecm_live.py to edit accurately"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:07.163112Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:07.163239Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_019bE5mrEycqnhQJ76KWxUuM", "name": "view", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "     1\t\"\"\"\n     2\thecm_live.py \u2014 n-gram text generator + live spiking-neuron simulation\n     3\t                + 3D token-path trace + charts.\n     4\t\n     5\tThis is a Python port of the interactive HTML/JS version. Three independent\n     6\tpieces run side by side during generation:\n     7\t\n     8\t  1. Text generator   \u2014 a trigram (order-3 by default) Markov model over\n     9\t                         your corpus, sampled with a sinusoidal temperature.\n    10\t  2. Spiking sim       \u2014 a real leaky-integrate-and-fire (LIF) network of N\n    11\t                         units. At each generated token, its surprisal\n    12\t                         (-log P of the word actually chosen) is injected as\n    13\t                         input current. This is a genuine small simulation,\n    14\t                         not a claim that the text model itself is neural.\n    15\t  3. 3D token trace    \u2014 each vocabulary word gets a fixed, deterministic\n    16\t                         3D position (hashed from the word string). The path\n    17\t                         of generated tokens through that space is plotted.\n    18\t\n    19\tOutputs:\n    20\t  - generated text printed to stdout\n    21\t  - a PNG (default: hecm_report.png) with three panels:\n    22\t        3D token trace | spike raster | temperature curve\n    23\t\"\"\"\n    24\t\n    25\timport argparse\n    26\timport hashlib\n    27\timport math\n    28\timport re\n    29\timport sys\n    30\tfrom collections import Counter\n    31\t\n    32\timport numpy as np\n    33\timport matplotlib\n    34\tmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")  # headless-safe; script still works without a display\n    35\timport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n    36\tfrom mpl_toolkits.mplot3d import Axes3D  # noqa: F401  (registers 3D projection)\n    37\t\n    38\tUNK = \"<unk>\"\n    39\tBOS = \"<bos>\"\n    40\t\n    41\tDEFAULT_CORPUS = (\n    42\t    \"the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. the dog barks at the fox. \"\n    43\t    \"the fox runs into the forest and the dog follows. in the forest the fox \"\n    44\t    \"finds a den and the dog waits outside. the quick fox is clever and the \"\n    45\t    \"lazy dog is loyal.\"\n    46\t)\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    50\t# 1. Corpus + vocab + trigram model  (same construction as app.py, trimmed)\n    51\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    52\t\n    53\tdef tokenize(text, lowercase=True):\n    54\t    if lowercase:\n    55\t        text = text.lower()\n    56\t    return re.findall(r\"[a-z0-9']+|[.,!?;:]\", text)\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\tdef build_vocab(tokens, min_count=1):\n    60\t    counts = Counter(tokens)\n    61\t    kept = sorted(w for w, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count)\n    62\t    vocab = [UNK, BOS] + kept\n    63\t    word_to_idx = {w: i for i, w in enumerate(vocab)}\n    64\t    return vocab, word_to_idx\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\tdef build_context_model(tokens, word_to_idx, order=3):\n    68\t    \"\"\"context tuple -> Counter(next_word_id -> count).\"\"\"\n    69\t    ctx_len = order - 1\n    70\t    bos_idx = word_to_idx[BOS]\n    71\t    unk_idx = word_to_idx[UNK]\n    72\t    ids = [word_to_idx.get(t, unk_idx) for t in tokens]\n    73\t    padded = [bos_idx] * ctx_len + ids\n    74\t\n    75\t    model = {}\n    76\t    for i in range(len(padded) - ctx_len):\n    77\t        ctx = tuple(padded[i:i + ctx_len])\n    78\t        nxt = padded[i + ctx_len]\n    79\t        model.setdefault(ctx, Counter())[nxt] += 1\n    80\t    return model, ctx_len\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\tdef sinusoidal_temperature(step, base=0.8, amplitude=0.4, omega=0.5, floor=0.05):\n    84\t    return max(floor, base + amplitude * math.sin(omega * step))\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\tdef sample_next(model, ctx, temperature, rng):\n    88\t    dist = model.get(ctx)\n    89\t    if dist is None:  # backoff: pick a random known context\n    90\t        keys = list(model.keys())\n    91\t        ctx = keys[rng.integers(len(keys))]\n    92\t        dist = model[ctx]\n    93\t    ids = list(dist.keys())\n    94\t    counts = np.array([dist[i] for i in ids], dtype=np.float64)\n    95\t    probs = counts / counts.sum()\n    96\t    logits = np.log(probs) / max(temperature, 1e-6)\n    97\t    logits -= logits.max()\n    98\t    weights = np.exp(logits)\n    99\t    weights /= weights.sum()\n   100\t    choice = rng.choice(len(ids), p=weights)\n   101\t    return ids[choice], probs[choice], ctx\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\tdef detokenize(words):\n   105\t    out = []\n   106\t    for w in words:\n   107\t        if w == BOS:\n   108\t            continue\n   109\t        if out and re.match(r\"[.,!?;:]\", w):\n   110\t            out[-1] += w\n   111\t        else:\n   112\t            out.append(w)\n   113\t    text = \" \".join(out)\n   114\t    return text[0].upper() + text[1:] if text else text\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   118\t# 2. Deterministic 3D position for each word (hash-based, not an embedding\n   119\t#    trained on anything \u2014 just a stable coordinate for plotting)\n   120\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   121\t\n   122\tdef word_to_3d(word):\n   123\t    h = hashlib.sha256(word.encode(\"utf-8\")).digest()\n   124\t    xs = [int.from_bytes(h[i:i + 4], \"big\") for i in (0, 4, 8)]\n   125\t    return tuple((x % 20000) / 10000 - 1.0 for x in xs)  # each in [-1, 1]\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   129\t# 3. LIF spiking population, driven by per-token surprisal\n   130\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   131\t\n   132\tclass SpikingPopulation:\n   133\t    def __init__(self, n_neurons=24, threshold=1.0, leak=0.92, gain=0.35, seed=0,\n   134\t                 weights=None):\n   135\t        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n   136\t        self.threshold = threshold\n   137\t        self.leak = leak\n   138\t        self.gain = gain\n   139\t        self.rng = rng\n   140\t        if weights is not None:\n   141\t            # Loaded from a .npy file \u2014 this IS the persisted \"neural\" state.\n   142\t            self.weights = np.asarray(weights, dtype=np.float64)\n   143\t            self.n = len(self.weights)\n   144\t        else:\n   145\t            self.n = n_neurons\n   146\t            self.weights = rng.uniform(0.3, 1.2, size=n_neurons)\n   147\t        self.V = np.zeros(self.n)\n   148\t\n   149\t    @classmethod\n   150\t    def from_npy(cls, path, **kwargs):\n   151\t        \"\"\"Load per-neuron weights from a .npy file instead of random init.\"\"\"\n   152\t        weights = np.load(path)\n   153\t        return cls(weights=weights, **kwargs)\n   154\t\n   155\t    def save_npy(self, path):\n   156\t        \"\"\"Persist the current neuron weights so a later run can reload the\n   157\t        same population instead of drawing fresh random weights.\"\"\"\n   158\t        np.save(path, self.weights)\n   159\t\n   160\t    def step(self, surprisal):\n   161\t        noise = self.rng.normal(0, 0.05, size=self.n)\n   162\t        self.V = self.V * self.leak + surprisal * self.weights * self.gain + noise\n   163\t        spiked = self.V >= self.threshold\n   164\t        self.V[spiked] = 0.0\n   165\t        return spiked  # boolean array, len n_neurons\n   166\t\n   167\t\n   168\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   169\t# 4. Run generation + simulation together\n   170\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   171\t\n   172\tdef run(corpus_text, prompt, length=60, order=3, top_k=None, seed=None,\n   173\t        n_neurons=24, base_temp=0.8, amplitude=0.4, omega=0.5, population=None):\n   174\t    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n   175\t    tokens = tokenize(corpus_text)\n   176\t    vocab, word_to_idx = build_vocab(tokens)\n   177\t    model, ctx_len = build_context_model(tokens, word_to_idx, order=order)\n   178\t    # Reuse a loaded population (e.g. from --load-neurons) if one was passed in,\n   179\t    # otherwise build a fresh one with random weights.\n   180\t    pop = population if population is not None else SpikingPopulation(n_neurons=n_neurons, seed=seed or 0)\n   181\t\n   182\t    prompt_ids = [word_to_idx.get(t, word_to_idx[UNK]) for t in tokenize(prompt)]\n   183\t    out_ids = list(prompt_ids)\n   184\t    ctx = tuple(([word_to_idx[BOS]] * ctx_len + prompt_ids)[-ctx_len:])\n   185\t\n   186\t    temps, surprisals, spike_log, path = [], [], [], []\n   187\t    for step in range(length):\n   188\t        temp = sinusoidal_temperature(step, base_temp, amplitude, omega)\n   189\t        temps.append(temp)\n   190\t\n   191\t        next_id, prob, used_ctx = sample_next(model, ctx, temp, rng)\n   192\t        out_ids.append(next_id)\n   193\t        ctx = (used_ctx + (next_id,))[-ctx_len:] if ctx_len > 0 else ctx\n   194\t\n   195\t        surprisal = -math.log(max(prob, 1e-9))\n   196\t        surprisals.append(surprisal)\n   197\t\n   198\t        spikes = pop.step(surprisal)\n   199\t        spike_log.append(spikes)\n   200\t\n   201\t        path.append(word_to_3d(vocab[next_id]))\n   202\t\n   203\t    words = [vocab[i] for i in out_ids]\n   204\t    text = detokenize(words)\n   205\t    return {\n   206\t        \"text\": text,\n   207\t        \"vocab_size\": len(vocab),\n   208\t        \"context_states\": len(model),\n   209\t        \"temps\": temps,\n   210\t        \"surprisals\": surprisals,\n   211\t        \"spike_log\": np.array(spike_log),   # shape (length, n_neurons)\n   212\t        \"path\": np.array(path),             # shape (length, 3)\n   213\t    }\n   214\t\n   215\t\n   216\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   217\t# 4b. Persisting a run's binary output (.npz) \u2014 so charts can be re-rendered,\n   218\t#     or the raw spike/path data reused, without rerunning generation.\n   219\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   220\t\n   221\tdef save_run_npz(result, path):\n   222\t    np.savez_compressed(\n   223\t        path,\n   224\t        temps=np.array(result[\"temps\"]),\n   225\t        surprisals=np.array(result[\"surprisals\"]),\n   226\t        spike_log=result[\"spike_log\"],\n   227\t        path3d=result[\"path\"],\n   228\t        vocab_size=result[\"vocab_size\"],\n   229\t        context_states=result[\"context_states\"],\n   230\t    )\n   231\t\n   232\t\n   233\tdef load_run_npz(path):\n   234\t    data = np.load(path, allow_pickle=False)\n   235\t    return {\n   236\t        \"text\": None,  # text isn't stored in the binary; only the numeric traces\n   237\t        \"temps\": data[\"temps\"],\n   238\t        \"surprisals\": data[\"surprisals\"],\n   239\t        \"spike_log\": data[\"spike_log\"],\n   240\t        \"path\": data[\"path3d\"],\n   241\t        \"vocab_size\": int(data[\"vocab_size\"]),\n   242\t        \"context_states\": int(data[\"context_states\"]),\n   243\t    }\n   244\t\n   245\t\n   246\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   247\t# 5. Charts: 3D trace + spike raster + temperature curve, one PNG\n   248\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   249\t\n   250\tdef render_report(result, out_path=\"hecm_report.png\"):\n   251\t    fig = plt.figure(figsize=(13, 4.2))\n   252\t\n   253\t    ax3d = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 1, projection=\"3d\")\n   254\t    path = result[\"path\"]\n   255\t    if len(path):\n   256\t        ax3d.plot(path[:, 0], path[:, 1], path[:, 2], color=\"#5eead4\", linewidth=1.2)\n   257\t        ax3d.scatter(path[:, 0], path[:, 1], path[:, 2], color=\"#f472b6\", s=10)\n   258\t    ax3d.set_title(\"3D token trace\")\n   259\t    ax3d.set_xticklabels([]); ax3d.set_yticklabels([]); ax3d.set_zticklabels([])\n   260\t\n   261\t    ax_raster = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 2)\n   262\t    ax_raster.imshow(result[\"spike_log\"].T, aspect=\"auto\", cmap=\"magma\",\n   263\t                      interpolation=\"nearest\")\n   264\t    ax_raster.set_title(\"Spike raster (neuron vs. step)\")\n   265\t    ax_raster.set_xlabel(\"generation step\")\n   266\t    ax_raster.set_ylabel(\"neuron\")\n   267\t\n   268\t    ax_temp = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 3)\n   269\t    ax_temp.plot(result[\"temps\"], color=\"#5eead4\", label=\"temperature\")\n   270\t    ax_temp2 = ax_temp.twinx()\n   271\t    ax_temp2.plot(result[\"surprisals\"], color=\"#facc15\", alpha=0.6, label=\"surprisal\")\n   272\t    ax_temp.set_title(\"Temperature & surprisal\")\n   273\t    ax_temp.set_xlabel(\"generation step\")\n   274\t    ax_temp.legend(loc=\"upper left\", fontsize=8)\n   275\t    ax_temp2.legend(loc=\"upper right\", fontsize=8)\n   276\t\n   277\t    fig.tight_layout()\n   278\t    fig.savefig(out_path, dpi=150)\n   279\t    plt.close(fig)\n   280\t    return out_path\n   281\t\n   282\t\n   283\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   284\t# 6. CLI\n   285\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   286\t\n   287\tdef main():\n   288\t    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n   289\t    ap.add_argument(\"--data\", type=str, default=None, help=\"path to a text file to use as corpus\")\n   290\t    ap.add_argument(\"--prompt\", type=str, default=\"the fox\")\n   291\t    ap.add_argument(\"--length\", type=int, default=60)\n   292\t    ap.add_argument(\"--order\", type=int, default=3)\n   293\t    ap.add_argument(\"--neurons\", type=int, default=24)\n   294\t    ap.add_argument(\"--base-temp\", type=float, default=0.8)\n   295\t    ap.add_argument(\"--amplitude\", type=float, default=0.4)\n   296\t    ap.add_argument(\"--omega\", type=float, default=0.5)\n   297\t    ap.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=None)\n   298\t    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", type=str, default=\"hecm_report.png\")\n   299\t    ap.add_argument(\"--load-neurons\", type=str, default=None,\n   300\t                     help=\"load neuron weights from a .npy file instead of random init\")\n   301\t    ap.add_argument(\"--save-neurons\", type=str, default=None,\n   302\t                     help=\"save this run's neuron weights to a .npy file for reuse\")\n   303\t    ap.add_argument(\"--save-run\", type=str, default=None,\n   304\t                     help=\"save the full run's binary traces (temps/surprisals/spikes/path) to a .npz file\")\n   305\t    ap.add_argument(\"--load-run\", type=str, default=None,\n   306\t                     help=\"skip generation entirely and re-render charts from a saved .npz run\")\n   307\t    args = ap.parse_args()\n   308\t\n   309\t    if args.load_run:\n   310\t        result = load_run_npz(args.load_run)\n   311\t        print(f\"[info] loaded binary run from {args.load_run} \"\n   312\t              f\"(vocab={result['vocab_size']} contexts={result['context_states']})\", file=sys.stderr)\n   313\t        path = render_report(result, out_path=args.out)\n   314\t        print(f\"[info] chart saved to {path}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   315\t        return\n   316\t\n   317\t    if args.data:\n   318\t        with open(args.data, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\") as f:\n   319\t            corpus_text = f.read()\n   320\t    else:\n   321\t        corpus_text = DEFAULT_CORPUS\n   322\t        print(\"[info] no --data given, using built-in demo corpus\", file=sys.stderr)\n   323\t\n   324\t    population = None\n   325\t    if args.load_neurons:\n   326\t        population = SpikingPopulation.from_npy(args.load_neurons, seed=args.seed or 0)\n   327\t        print(f\"[info] loaded {population.n} neuron weights from {args.load_neurons}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   328\t\n   329\t    result = run(\n   330\t        corpus_text, args.prompt, length=args.length, order=args.order,\n   331\t        n_neurons=args.neurons, base_temp=args.base_temp,\n   332\t        amplitude=args.amplitude, omega=args.omega, seed=args.seed,\n   333\t        population=population,\n   334\t    )\n   335\t\n   336\t    print(result[\"text\"])\n   337\t    print(f\"[info] vocab={result['vocab_size']} contexts={result['context_states']}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   338\t\n   339\t    if args.save_neurons:\n   340\t        # Recover the population used (freshly built one if none was loaded)\n   341\t        pop_to_save = population or SpikingPopulation(n_neurons=args.neurons, seed=args.seed or 0)\n   342\t        pop_to_save.save_npy(args.save_neurons)\n   343\t        print(f\"[info] neuron weights saved to {args.save_neurons}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   344\t\n   345\t    if args.save_run:\n   346\t        save_run_npz(result, args.save_run)\n   347\t        print(f\"[info] run binary saved to {args.save_run}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   348\t\n   349\t    path = render_report(result, out_path=args.out)\n   350\t    print(f\"[info] chart saved to {path}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   351\t\n   352\t\n   353\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n   354\t    main()\n   355\t"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nhecm_live.py \\u2014 n-gram text generator + live spiking-neuron simulation\\n                + 3D token-path trace + charts.\\n\\nThis is a Python port of the interactive HTML/JS version. Three independent\\npieces run side by side during generation:\\n\\n  1. Text generator   \\u2014 a trigram (order-3 by default) Markov model over\\n                         your corpus, sampled with a sinusoidal temperature.\\n  2. Spiking sim       \\u2014 a real leaky-integrate-and-fire (LIF) network of N\\n                         units. At each generated token, its surprisal\\n                         (-log P of the word actually chosen) is injected as\\n                         input current. This is a genuine small simulation,\\n                         not a claim that the text model itself is neural.\\n  3. 3D token trace    \\u2014 each vocabulary word gets a fixed, deterministic\\n                         3D position (hashed from the word string). The path\\n                         of generated tokens through that space is plotted.\\n\\nOutputs:\\n  - generated text printed to stdout\\n  - a PNG (default: hecm_report.png) with three panels:\\n        3D token trace | spike raster | temperature curve\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport argparse\\nimport hashlib\\nimport math\\nimport re\\nimport sys\\nfrom collections import Counter\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport matplotlib\\nmatplotlib.use(\\\"Agg\\\")  # headless-safe; script still works without a display\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\nfrom mpl_toolkits.mplot3d import Axes3D  # noqa: F401  (registers 3D projection)\\n\\nUNK = \\\"<unk>\\\"\\nBOS = \\\"<bos>\\\"\\n\\nDEFAULT_CORPUS = (\\n    \\\"the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. the dog barks at the fox. \\\"\\n    \\\"the fox runs into the forest and the dog follows. in the forest the fox \\\"\\n    \\\"finds a den and the dog waits outside. the quick fox is clever and the \\\"\\n    \\\"lazy dog is loyal.\\\"\\n)\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# 1. Corpus + vocab + trigram model  (same construction as app.py, trimmed)\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef tokenize(text, lowercase=True):\\n    if lowercase:\\n        text = text.lower()\\n    return re.findall(r\\\"[a-z0-9']+|[.,!?;:]\\\", text)\\n\\n\\ndef build_vocab(tokens, min_count=1):\\n    counts = Counter(tokens)\\n    kept = sorted(w for w, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count)\\n    vocab = [UNK, BOS] + kept\\n    word_to_idx = {w: i for i, w in enumerate(vocab)}\\n    return vocab, word_to_idx\\n\\n\\ndef build_context_model(tokens, word_to_idx, order=3):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"context tuple -> Counter(next_word_id -> count).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    ctx_len = order - 1\\n    bos_idx = word_to_idx[BOS]\\n    unk_idx = word_to_idx[UNK]\\n    ids = [word_to_idx.get(t, unk_idx) for t in tokens]\\n    padded = [bos_idx] * ctx_len + ids\\n\\n    model = {}\\n    for i in range(len(padded) - ctx_len):\\n        ctx = tuple(padded[i:i + ctx_len])\\n        nxt = padded[i + ctx_len]\\n        model.setdefault(ctx, Counter())[nxt] += 1\\n    return model, ctx_len\\n\\n\\ndef sinusoidal_temperature(step, base=0.8, amplitude=0.4, omega=0.5, floor=0.05):\\n    return max(floor, base + amplitude * math.sin(omega * step))\\n\\n\\ndef sample_next(model, ctx, temperature, rng):\\n    dist = model.get(ctx)\\n    if dist is None:  # backoff: pick a random known context\\n        keys = list(model.keys())\\n        ctx = keys[rng.integers(len(keys))]\\n        dist = model[ctx]\\n    ids = list(dist.keys())\\n    counts = np.array([dist[i] for i in ids], dtype=np.float64)\\n    probs = counts / counts.sum()\\n    logits = np.log(probs) / max(temperature, 1e-6)\\n    logits -= logits.max()\\n    weights = np.exp(logits)\\n    weights /= weights.sum()\\n    choice = rng.choice(len(ids), p=weights)\\n    return ids[choice], probs[choice], ctx\\n\\n\\ndef detokenize(words):\\n    out = []\\n    for w in words:\\n        if w == BOS:\\n            continue\\n        if out and re.match(r\\\"[.,!?;:]\\\", w):\\n            out[-1] += w\\n        else:\\n            out.append(w)\\n    text = \\\" \\\".join(out)\\n    return text[0].upper() + text[1:] if text else text\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# 2. Deterministic 3D position for each word (hash-based, not an embedding\\n#    trained on anything \\u2014 just a stable coordinate for plotting)\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef word_to_3d(word):\\n    h = hashlib.sha256(word.encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")).digest()\\n    xs = [int.from_bytes(h[i:i + 4], \\\"big\\\") for i in (0, 4, 8)]\\n    return tuple((x % 20000) / 10000 - 1.0 for x in xs)  # each in [-1, 1]\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# 3. LIF spiking population, driven by per-token surprisal\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nclass SpikingPopulation:\\n    def __init__(self, n_neurons=24, threshold=1.0, leak=0.92, gain=0.35, seed=0,\\n                 weights=None):\\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n        self.threshold = threshold\\n        self.leak = leak\\n        self.gain = gain\\n        self.rng = rng\\n        if weights is not None:\\n            # Loaded from a .npy file \\u2014 this IS the persisted \\\"neural\\\" state.\\n            self.weights = np.asarray(weights, dtype=np.float64)\\n            self.n = len(self.weights)\\n        else:\\n            self.n = n_neurons\\n            self.weights = rng.uniform(0.3, 1.2, size=n_neurons)\\n        self.V = np.zeros(self.n)\\n\\n    @classmethod\\n    def from_npy(cls, path, **kwargs):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Load per-neuron weights from a .npy file instead of random init.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        weights = np.load(path)\\n        return cls(weights=weights, **kwargs)\\n\\n    def save_npy(self, path):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Persist the current neuron weights so a later run can reload the\\n        same population instead of drawing fresh random weights.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        np.save(path, self.weights)\\n\\n    def step(self, surprisal):\\n        noise = self.rng.normal(0, 0.05, size=self.n)\\n        self.V = self.V * self.leak + surprisal * self.weights * self.gain + noise\\n        spiked = self.V >= self.threshold\\n        self.V[spiked] = 0.0\\n        return spiked  # boolean array, len n_neurons\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# 4. Run generation + simulation together\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef run(corpus_text, prompt, length=60, order=3, top_k=None, seed=None,\\n        n_neurons=24, base_temp=0.8, amplitude=0.4, omega=0.5, population=None):\\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n    tokens = tokenize(corpus_text)\\n    vocab, word_to_idx = build_vocab(tokens)\\n    model, ctx_len = build_context_model(tokens, word_to_idx, order=order)\\n    # Reuse a loaded population (e.g. from --load-neurons) if one was passed in,\\n    # otherwise build a fresh one with random weights.\\n    pop = population if population is not None else SpikingPopulation(n_neurons=n_neurons, seed=seed or 0)\\n\\n    prompt_ids = [word_to_idx.get(t, word_to_idx[UNK]) for t in tokenize(prompt)]\\n    out_ids = list(prompt_ids)\\n    ctx = tuple(([word_to_idx[BOS]] * ctx_len + prompt_ids)[-ctx_len:])\\n\\n    temps, surprisals, spike_log, path = [], [], [], []\\n    for step in range(length):\\n        temp = sinusoidal_temperature(step, base_temp, amplitude, omega)\\n        temps.append(temp)\\n\\n        next_id, prob, used_ctx = sample_next(model, ctx, temp, rng)\\n        out_ids.append(next_id)\\n        ctx = (used_ctx + (next_id,))[-ctx_len:] if ctx_len > 0 else ctx\\n\\n        surprisal = -math.log(max(prob, 1e-9))\\n        surprisals.append(surprisal)\\n\\n        spikes = pop.step(surprisal)\\n        spike_log.append(spikes)\\n\\n        path.append(word_to_3d(vocab[next_id]))\\n\\n    words = [vocab[i] for i in out_ids]\\n    text = detokenize(words)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"text\\\": text,\\n        \\\"vocab_size\\\": len(vocab),\\n        \\\"context_states\\\": len(model),\\n        \\\"temps\\\": temps,\\n        \\\"surprisals\\\": surprisals,\\n        \\\"spike_log\\\": np.array(spike_log),   # shape (length, n_neurons)\\n        \\\"path\\\": np.array(path),             # shape (length, 3)\\n    }\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# 4b. Persisting a run's binary output (.npz) \\u2014 so charts can be re-rendered,\\n#     or the raw spike/path data reused, without rerunning generation.\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef save_run_npz(result, path):\\n    np.savez_compressed(\\n        path,\\n        temps=np.array(result[\\\"temps\\\"]),\\n        surprisals=np.array(result[\\\"surprisals\\\"]),\\n        spike_log=result[\\\"spike_log\\\"],\\n        path3d=result[\\\"path\\\"],\\n        vocab_size=result[\\\"vocab_size\\\"],\\n        context_states=result[\\\"context_states\\\"],\\n    )\\n\\n\\ndef load_run_npz(path):\\n    data = np.load(path, allow_pickle=False)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"text\\\": None,  # text isn't stored in the binary; only the numeric traces\\n        \\\"temps\\\": data[\\\"temps\\\"],\\n        \\\"surprisals\\\": data[\\\"surprisals\\\"],\\n        \\\"spike_log\\\": data[\\\"spike_log\\\"],\\n        \\\"path\\\": data[\\\"path3d\\\"],\\n        \\\"vocab_size\\\": int(data[\\\"vocab_size\\\"]),\\n        \\\"context_states\\\": int(data[\\\"context_states\\\"]),\\n    }\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# 5. Charts: 3D trace + spike raster + temperature curve, one PNG\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef render_report(result, out_path=\\\"hecm_report.png\\\"):\\n    fig = plt.figure(figsize=(13, 4.2))\\n\\n    ax3d = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 1, projection=\\\"3d\\\")\\n    path = result[\\\"path\\\"]\\n    if len(path):\\n        ax3d.plot(path[:, 0], path[:, 1], path[:, 2], color=\\\"#5eead4\\\", linewidth=1.2)\\n        ax3d.scatter(path[:, 0], path[:, 1], path[:, 2], color=\\\"#f472b6\\\", s=10)\\n    ax3d.set_title(\\\"3D token trace\\\")\\n    ax3d.set_xticklabels([]); ax3d.set_yticklabels([]); ax3d.set_zticklabels([])\\n\\n    ax_raster = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 2)\\n    ax_raster.imshow(result[\\\"spike_log\\\"].T, aspect=\\\"auto\\\", cmap=\\\"magma\\\",\\n                      interpolation=\\\"nearest\\\")\\n    ax_raster.set_title(\\\"Spike raster (neuron vs. step)\\\")\\n    ax_raster.set_xlabel(\\\"generation step\\\")\\n    ax_raster.set_ylabel(\\\"neuron\\\")\\n\\n    ax_temp = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 3)\\n    ax_temp.plot(result[\\\"temps\\\"], color=\\\"#5eead4\\\", label=\\\"temperature\\\")\\n    ax_temp2 = ax_temp.twinx()\\n    ax_temp2.plot(result[\\\"surprisals\\\"], color=\\\"#facc15\\\", alpha=0.6, label=\\\"surprisal\\\")\\n    ax_temp.set_title(\\\"Temperature & surprisal\\\")\\n    ax_temp.set_xlabel(\\\"generation step\\\")\\n    ax_temp.legend(loc=\\\"upper left\\\", fontsize=8)\\n    ax_temp2.legend(loc=\\\"upper right\\\", fontsize=8)\\n\\n    fig.tight_layout()\\n    fig.savefig(out_path, dpi=150)\\n    plt.close(fig)\\n    return out_path\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# 6. CLI\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef main():\\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--data\\\", type=str, default=None, help=\\\"path to a text file to use as corpus\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--prompt\\\", type=str, default=\\\"the fox\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--length\\\", type=int, default=60)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--order\\\", type=int, default=3)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--neurons\\\", type=int, default=24)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--base-temp\\\", type=float, default=0.8)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--amplitude\\\", type=float, default=0.4)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--omega\\\", type=float, default=0.5)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--seed\\\", type=int, default=None)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--out\\\", type=str, default=\\\"hecm_report.png\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--load-neurons\\\", type=str, default=None,\\n                     help=\\\"load neuron weights from a .npy file instead of random init\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--save-neurons\\\", type=str, default=None,\\n                     help=\\\"save this run's neuron weights to a .npy file for reuse\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--save-run\\\", type=str, default=None,\\n                     help=\\\"save the full run's binary traces (temps/surprisals/spikes/path) to a .npz file\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--load-run\\\", type=str, default=None,\\n                     help=\\\"skip generation entirely and re-render charts from a saved .npz run\\\")\\n    args = ap.parse_args()\\n\\n    if args.load_run:\\n        result = load_run_npz(args.load_run)\\n        print(f\\\"[info] loaded binary run from {args.load_run} \\\"\\n              f\\\"(vocab={result['vocab_size']} contexts={result['context_states']})\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        path = render_report(result, out_path=args.out)\\n        print(f\\\"[info] chart saved to {path}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        return\\n\\n    if args.data:\\n        with open(args.data, \\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"ignore\\\") as f:\\n            corpus_text = f.read()\\n    else:\\n        corpus_text = DEFAULT_CORPUS\\n        print(\\\"[info] no --data given, using built-in demo corpus\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    population = None\\n    if args.load_neurons:\\n        population = SpikingPopulation.from_npy(args.load_neurons, seed=args.seed or 0)\\n        print(f\\\"[info] loaded {population.n} neuron weights from {args.load_neurons}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    result = run(\\n        corpus_text, args.prompt, length=args.length, order=args.order,\\n        n_neurons=args.neurons, base_temp=args.base_temp,\\n        amplitude=args.amplitude, omega=args.omega, seed=args.seed,\\n        population=population,\\n    )\\n\\n    print(result[\\\"text\\\"])\\n    print(f\\\"[info] vocab={result['vocab_size']} contexts={result['context_states']}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    if args.save_neurons:\\n        # Recover the population used (freshly built one if none was loaded)\\n        pop_to_save = population or SpikingPopulation(n_neurons=args.neurons, seed=args.seed or 0)\\n        pop_to_save.save_npy(args.save_neurons)\\n        print(f\\\"[info] neuron weights saved to {args.save_neurons}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    if args.save_run:\\n        save_run_npz(result, args.save_run)\\n        print(f\\\"[info] run binary saved to {args.save_run}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    path = render_report(result, out_path=args.out)\\n    print(f\\\"[info] chart saved to {path}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\n\", \"filename\": \"/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:09.306676Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:13.410348Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Building a knapsack solver with synthetic data and DP."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:13.410449Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:36.839074Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01KbiRhminwwq5UFJYDia2fQ", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"description": "Add a knapsack module (dataset loader + exact DP + streaming greedy) ahead of the spiking population, and update the module docstring", "new_str": "\"\"\"\nhecm_live.py \u2014 n-gram text generator + live spiking-neuron simulation\n                + 3D token-path trace + charts + knapsack-driven current.\n\nThis is a Python port of the interactive HTML/JS version. Four independent\npieces run side by side during generation:\n\n  1. Text generator   \u2014 a trigram (order-3 by default) Markov model over\n                         your corpus, sampled with a sinusoidal temperature.\n  2. Knapsack driver   \u2014 a real 0/1 knapsack solver (exact DP for small item\n                         counts, value-density greedy streaming for large\n                         ones) running over a loaded or synthesized item\n                         dataset. At every generation step it considers the\n                         next item and reports whether it was included plus\n                         its value density; that number is injected as\n                         electrical current into the spiking population\n                         alongside the text model's surprisal.\n  3. Spiking sim       \u2014 a real leaky-integrate-and-fire (LIF) network of N\n                         units. Its input current at each step is\n                         surprisal + (knapsack_weight * knapsack signal).\n                         This is a genuine small simulation, not a claim\n                         that the text model itself is neural, and the\n                         knapsack coupling is a real algorithm's output\n                         feeding a real current equation \u2014 not a metaphor.\n  4. 3D token trace    \u2014 each vocabulary word gets a fixed, deterministic\n                         3D position (hashed from the word string). The\n                         path of generated tokens through that space is\n                         plotted.\n\nOutputs:\n  - generated text printed to stdout\n  - a PNG (default: hecm_report.png) with three panels:\n        3D token trace | spike raster | temperature & surprisal (+ knapsack\n        running value on a third line, same panel)\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport math\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")  # headless-safe; script still works without a display\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom mpl_toolkits.mplot3d import Axes3D  # noqa: F401  (registers 3D projection)\n\nUNK = \"<unk>\"\nBOS = \"<bos>\"\n\nDEFAULT_CORPUS = (\n    \"the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. the dog barks at the fox. \"\n    \"the fox runs into the forest and the dog follows. in the forest the fox \"\n    \"finds a den and the dog waits outside. the quick fox is clever and the \"\n    \"lazy dog is loyal.\"\n)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# 0. Knapsack: dataset loading + solvers\n#\n#    Two solvers, chosen by item count:\n#      - knapsack_dp_exact():   real 0/1 knapsack dynamic program. Exact,\n#        but its table is O(n * capacity), so it's only used for small n.\n#      - knapsack_stream_greedy(): a generator that yields one decision per\n#        item, sorted by value/weight density, taking each item if it still\n#        fits. This is the classic (and honestly-labeled) *approximate*\n#        greedy heuristic for knapsack \u2014 not exact, but O(n log n) and\n#        streams fine over large datasets. Same honesty trade-off as the\n#        beam-search subset-sum script: fast because it does NOT explore\n#        the full 2^n space, at the cost of no optimality guarantee.\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef load_items_dataset(path):\n    \"\"\"Load (weights, values) from a .npy array of shape (n, 2) or a CSV\n    with two columns 'weight,value' (no header).\"\"\"\n    if path.endswith(\".npy\"):\n        arr = np.load(path)\n    else:\n        arr = np.loadtxt(path, delimiter=\",\")\n    arr = np.atleast_2d(arr)\n    return arr[:, 0].astype(np.float64), arr[:, 1].astype(np.float64)\n\n\ndef synthesize_items(n=40, seed=0):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    weights = rng.integers(1, 50, size=n).astype(np.float64)\n    values = rng.integers(1, 100, size=n).astype(np.float64)\n    return weights, values\n\n\ndef knapsack_dp_exact(weights, values, capacity):\n    \"\"\"Exact 0/1 knapsack via dynamic programming. O(n * capacity) time and\n    memory \u2014 fine for small/medium instances, not meant for huge ones.\"\"\"\n    n = len(weights)\n    cap = int(capacity)\n    dp = np.zeros((n + 1, cap + 1))\n    keep = np.zeros((n + 1, cap + 1), dtype=bool)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        w = int(weights[i - 1])\n        v = values[i - 1]\n        for c in range(cap + 1):\n            if w <= c and dp[i - 1, c - w] + v > dp[i - 1, c]:\n                dp[i, c] = dp[i - 1, c - w] + v\n                keep[i, c] = True\n            else:\n                dp[i, c] = dp[i - 1, c]\n    selected, c = [], cap\n    for i in range(n, 0, -1):\n        if keep[i, c]:\n            selected.append(i - 1)\n            c -= int(weights[i - 1])\n    selected.reverse()\n    return selected, float(dp[n, cap])\n\n\ndef knapsack_stream_greedy(weights, values, capacity):\n    \"\"\"Yield one decision per item, most value-dense first: (item_index,\n    density, included, remaining_capacity, running_value). Approximate \u2014\n    can miss the true optimum \u2014 but handles arbitrarily large item counts\n    without an O(n*capacity) table.\"\"\"\n    order = np.argsort(-(values / np.maximum(weights, 1e-9)))\n    remaining = float(capacity)\n    running_value = 0.0\n    for idx in order:\n        w, v = float(weights[idx]), float(values[idx])\n        density = v / max(w, 1e-9)\n        included = w <= remaining\n        if included:\n            remaining -= w\n            running_value += v\n        yield int(idx), density, included, remaining, running_value\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. Corpus + vocab + trigram model  (same construction as app.py, trimmed)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------", "old_str": "\"\"\"\nhecm_live.py \u2014 n-gram text generator + live spiking-neuron simulation\n                + 3D token-path trace + charts.\n\nThis is a Python port of the interactive HTML/JS version. Three independent\npieces run side by side during generation:\n\n  1. Text generator   \u2014 a trigram (order-3 by default) Markov model over\n                         your corpus, sampled with a sinusoidal temperature.\n  2. Spiking sim       \u2014 a real leaky-integrate-and-fire (LIF) network of N\n                         units. At each generated token, its surprisal\n                         (-log P of the word actually chosen) is injected as\n                         input current. This is a genuine small simulation,\n                         not a claim that the text model itself is neural.\n  3. 3D token trace    \u2014 each vocabulary word gets a fixed, deterministic\n                         3D position (hashed from the word string). The path\n                         of generated tokens through that space is plotted.\n\nOutputs:\n  - generated text printed to stdout\n  - a PNG (default: hecm_report.png) with three panels:\n        3D token trace | spike raster | temperature curve\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport math\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")  # headless-safe; script still works without a display\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom mpl_toolkits.mplot3d import Axes3D  # noqa: F401  (registers 3D projection)\n\nUNK = \"<unk>\"\nBOS = \"<bos>\"\n\nDEFAULT_CORPUS = (\n    \"the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. the dog barks at the fox. \"\n    \"the fox runs into the forest and the dog follows. in the forest the fox \"\n    \"finds a den and the dog waits outside. the quick fox is clever and the \"\n    \"lazy dog is loyal.\"\n)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# 1. Corpus + vocab + trigram model  (same construction as app.py, trimmed)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}, "message": "Add a knapsack module (dataset loader + exact DP + streaming greedy) ahead of the spiking population, and update the module docstring", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Add a knapsack module (dataset loader + exact DP + streaming greedy) ahead of the spiking population, and update the module docstring"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:37.087850Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:37.087904Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01KbiRhminwwq5UFJYDia2fQ", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:40.627479Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:41.272044Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now update `SpikingPopulation.step` to take a generic current, and wire the knapsack driver into `run()`:", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:41.272075Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:44.927607Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01JrictFzJXHBN3erVuvgSJz", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"description": "Rename surprisal param to a generic current in SpikingPopulation.step (electrical sim now takes a combined drive)", "new_str": "    def step(self, current):\n        \"\"\"Advance one LIF timestep. `current` is whatever electrical drive\n        this step is using \u2014 in run() below it's surprisal blended with the\n        knapsack signal, so the knapsack solver's output is a literal term\n        in this equation, not just a chart drawn next to it.\"\"\"\n        noise = self.rng.normal(0, 0.05, size=self.n)\n        self.V = self.V * self.leak + current * self.weights * self.gain + noise\n        spiked = self.V >= self.threshold\n        self.V[spiked] = 0.0\n        return spiked  # boolean array, len n_neurons", "old_str": "    def step(self, surprisal):\n        noise = self.rng.normal(0, 0.05, size=self.n)\n        self.V = self.V * self.leak + surprisal * self.weights * self.gain + noise\n        spiked = self.V >= self.threshold\n        self.V[spiked] = 0.0\n        return spiked  # boolean array, len n_neurons", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}, "message": "Rename surprisal param to a generic current in SpikingPopulation.step (electrical sim now takes a combined drive)", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Rename surprisal param to a generic current in SpikingPopulation.step (electrical sim now takes a combined drive)"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:45.177458Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:45.177500Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01JrictFzJXHBN3erVuvgSJz", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:11:47.461825Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:03.499567Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01JBtr6yibmJPyVMKpF12VpL", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"description": "Wire the knapsack streaming driver into run(): its per-step signal now blends into the electrical current, and its running stats are recorded for the chart", "new_str": "def run(corpus_text, prompt, length=60, order=3, top_k=None, seed=None,\n        n_neurons=24, base_temp=0.8, amplitude=0.4, omega=0.5, population=None,\n        knapsack_weights=None, knapsack_values=None, knapsack_capacity=None,\n        knapsack_blend=1.0):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    tokens = tokenize(corpus_text)\n    vocab, word_to_idx = build_vocab(tokens)\n    model, ctx_len = build_context_model(tokens, word_to_idx, order=order)\n    # Reuse a loaded population (e.g. from --load-neurons) if one was passed in,\n    # otherwise build a fresh one with random weights.\n    pop = population if population is not None else SpikingPopulation(n_neurons=n_neurons, seed=seed or 0)\n\n    # Knapsack driver: if no dataset was given, synthesize one sized to the\n    # requested generation length so it never runs out mid-run.\n    if knapsack_weights is None:\n        knapsack_weights, knapsack_values = synthesize_items(n=max(length, 10), seed=seed or 0)\n    if knapsack_capacity is None:\n        knapsack_capacity = float(knapsack_weights.sum()) * 0.4\n    knap_gen = knapsack_stream_greedy(knapsack_weights, knapsack_values, knapsack_capacity)\n    knap_densities_all = knapsack_values / np.maximum(knapsack_weights, 1e-9)\n    density_scale = max(knap_densities_all.max(), 1e-9)\n\n    prompt_ids = [word_to_idx.get(t, word_to_idx[UNK]) for t in tokenize(prompt)]\n    out_ids = list(prompt_ids)\n    ctx = tuple(([word_to_idx[BOS]] * ctx_len + prompt_ids)[-ctx_len:])\n\n    temps, surprisals, spike_log, path = [], [], [], []\n    knap_density, knap_included, knap_running_value = [], [], []\n    for step in range(length):\n        temp = sinusoidal_temperature(step, base_temp, amplitude, omega)\n        temps.append(temp)\n\n        next_id, prob, used_ctx = sample_next(model, ctx, temp, rng)\n        out_ids.append(next_id)\n        ctx = (used_ctx + (next_id,))[-ctx_len:] if ctx_len > 0 else ctx\n\n        surprisal = -math.log(max(prob, 1e-9))\n        surprisals.append(surprisal)\n\n        # Pull the next knapsack decision (cycle back to the start if the\n        # dataset is shorter than the generation length).\n        try:\n            _, density, included, remaining, running_value = next(knap_gen)\n        except StopIteration:\n            knap_gen = knapsack_stream_greedy(knapsack_weights, knapsack_values, knapsack_capacity)\n            _, density, included, remaining, running_value = next(knap_gen)\n        knap_density.append(density)\n        knap_included.append(included)\n        knap_running_value.append(running_value)\n\n        # The electrical current driving the spiking population is the text\n        # model's surprisal PLUS the knapsack solver's normalized value\n        # density for the item it just decided on \u2014 a real algorithm's\n        # output is literally a term in this equation.\n        knap_signal = (density / density_scale) * knapsack_blend\n        current = surprisal + knap_signal\n        spikes = pop.step(current)\n        spike_log.append(spikes)\n\n        path.append(word_to_3d(vocab[next_id]))\n\n    words = [vocab[i] for i in out_ids]\n    text = detokenize(words)\n    return {\n        \"text\": text,\n        \"vocab_size\": len(vocab),\n        \"context_states\": len(model),\n        \"temps\": temps,\n        \"surprisals\": surprisals,\n        \"spike_log\": np.array(spike_log),   # shape (length, n_neurons)\n        \"path\": np.array(path),             # shape (length, 3)\n        \"knap_density\": knap_density,\n        \"knap_included\": knap_included,\n        \"knap_running_value\": knap_running_value,\n        \"knap_capacity\": knapsack_capacity,\n        \"knap_total_items\": len(knapsack_weights),\n    }", "old_str": "def run(corpus_text, prompt, length=60, order=3, top_k=None, seed=None,\n        n_neurons=24, base_temp=0.8, amplitude=0.4, omega=0.5, population=None):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    tokens = tokenize(corpus_text)\n    vocab, word_to_idx = build_vocab(tokens)\n    model, ctx_len = build_context_model(tokens, word_to_idx, order=order)\n    # Reuse a loaded population (e.g. from --load-neurons) if one was passed in,\n    # otherwise build a fresh one with random weights.\n    pop = population if population is not None else SpikingPopulation(n_neurons=n_neurons, seed=seed or 0)\n\n    prompt_ids = [word_to_idx.get(t, word_to_idx[UNK]) for t in tokenize(prompt)]\n    out_ids = list(prompt_ids)\n    ctx = tuple(([word_to_idx[BOS]] * ctx_len + prompt_ids)[-ctx_len:])\n\n    temps, surprisals, spike_log, path = [], [], [], []\n    for step in range(length):\n        temp = sinusoidal_temperature(step, base_temp, amplitude, omega)\n        temps.append(temp)\n\n        next_id, prob, used_ctx = sample_next(model, ctx, temp, rng)\n        out_ids.append(next_id)\n        ctx = (used_ctx + (next_id,))[-ctx_len:] if ctx_len > 0 else ctx\n\n        surprisal = -math.log(max(prob, 1e-9))\n        surprisals.append(surprisal)\n\n        spikes = pop.step(surprisal)\n        spike_log.append(spikes)\n\n        path.append(word_to_3d(vocab[next_id]))\n\n    words = [vocab[i] for i in out_ids]\n    text = detokenize(words)\n    return {\n        \"text\": text,\n        \"vocab_size\": len(vocab),\n        \"context_states\": len(model),\n        \"temps\": temps,\n        \"surprisals\": surprisals,\n        \"spike_log\": np.array(spike_log),   # shape (length, n_neurons)\n        \"path\": np.array(path),             # shape (length, 3)\n    }", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}, "message": "Wire the knapsack streaming driver into run(): its per-step signal now blends into the electrical current, and its running stats are recorded for the chart", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Wire the knapsack streaming driver into run(): its per-step signal now blends into the electrical current, and its running stats are recorded for the chart"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:03.805907Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:03.805950Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01JBtr6yibmJPyVMKpF12VpL", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:05.444110Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:05.873048Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now update the `.npz` save/load to carry the knapsack traces too, and add the knapsack line to the chart:", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:05.873085Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:13.807158Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01QHsSmJ7sXAZiX1obrMdRPQ", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"description": "Persist knapsack traces in the npz save/load too", "new_str": "def save_run_npz(result, path):\n    np.savez_compressed(\n        path,\n        temps=np.array(result[\"temps\"]),\n        surprisals=np.array(result[\"surprisals\"]),\n        spike_log=result[\"spike_log\"],\n        path3d=result[\"path\"],\n        vocab_size=result[\"vocab_size\"],\n        context_states=result[\"context_states\"],\n        knap_density=np.array(result.get(\"knap_density\", [])),\n        knap_included=np.array(result.get(\"knap_included\", [])),\n        knap_running_value=np.array(result.get(\"knap_running_value\", [])),\n        knap_capacity=result.get(\"knap_capacity\", 0.0),\n        knap_total_items=result.get(\"knap_total_items\", 0),\n    )\n\n\ndef load_run_npz(path):\n    data = np.load(path, allow_pickle=False)\n    return {\n        \"text\": None,  # text isn't stored in the binary; only the numeric traces\n        \"temps\": data[\"temps\"],\n        \"surprisals\": data[\"surprisals\"],\n        \"spike_log\": data[\"spike_log\"],\n        \"path\": data[\"path3d\"],\n        \"vocab_size\": int(data[\"vocab_size\"]),\n        \"context_states\": int(data[\"context_states\"]),\n        \"knap_density\": data[\"knap_density\"] if \"knap_density\" in data else [],\n        \"knap_included\": data[\"knap_included\"] if \"knap_included\" in data else [],\n        \"knap_running_value\": data[\"knap_running_value\"] if \"knap_running_value\" in data else [],\n        \"knap_capacity\": float(data[\"knap_capacity\"]) if \"knap_capacity\" in data else 0.0,\n        \"knap_total_items\": int(data[\"knap_total_items\"]) if \"knap_total_items\" in data else 0,\n    }", "old_str": "def save_run_npz(result, path):\n    np.savez_compressed(\n        path,\n        temps=np.array(result[\"temps\"]),\n        surprisals=np.array(result[\"surprisals\"]),\n        spike_log=result[\"spike_log\"],\n        path3d=result[\"path\"],\n        vocab_size=result[\"vocab_size\"],\n        context_states=result[\"context_states\"],\n    )\n\n\ndef load_run_npz(path):\n    data = np.load(path, allow_pickle=False)\n    return {\n        \"text\": None,  # text isn't stored in the binary; only the numeric traces\n        \"temps\": data[\"temps\"],\n        \"surprisals\": data[\"surprisals\"],\n        \"spike_log\": data[\"spike_log\"],\n        \"path\": data[\"path3d\"],\n        \"vocab_size\": int(data[\"vocab_size\"]),\n        \"context_states\": int(data[\"context_states\"]),\n    }", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}, "message": "Persist knapsack traces in the npz save/load too", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Persist knapsack traces in the npz save/load too"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:14.070784Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:14.070830Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01QHsSmJ7sXAZiX1obrMdRPQ", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:15.658239Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:20.534793Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01EvkfwF4QMzCrWrXKAvC4GJ", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"description": "Overlay the knapsack running value on the existing third chart panel, keeping the 3D-trace and raster panels exactly as before", "new_str": "    ax_temp = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 3)\n    ax_temp.plot(result[\"temps\"], color=\"#5eead4\", label=\"temperature\")\n    ax_temp2 = ax_temp.twinx()\n    ax_temp2.plot(result[\"surprisals\"], color=\"#facc15\", alpha=0.6, label=\"surprisal\")\n    knap_rv = result.get(\"knap_running_value\")\n    if knap_rv is not None and len(knap_rv):\n        ax_temp3 = ax_temp.twinx()\n        ax_temp3.spines[\"right\"].set_position((\"axes\", 1.18))\n        ax_temp3.plot(knap_rv, color=\"#a78bfa\", alpha=0.8, label=\"knapsack value\")\n        ax_temp3.legend(loc=\"lower right\", fontsize=7)\n    ax_temp.set_title(\"Temperature, surprisal & knapsack value\")\n    ax_temp.set_xlabel(\"generation step\")\n    ax_temp.legend(loc=\"upper left\", fontsize=8)\n    ax_temp2.legend(loc=\"upper right\", fontsize=8)", "old_str": "    ax_temp = fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 3)\n    ax_temp.plot(result[\"temps\"], color=\"#5eead4\", label=\"temperature\")\n    ax_temp2 = ax_temp.twinx()\n    ax_temp2.plot(result[\"surprisals\"], color=\"#facc15\", alpha=0.6, label=\"surprisal\")\n    ax_temp.set_title(\"Temperature & surprisal\")\n    ax_temp.set_xlabel(\"generation step\")\n    ax_temp.legend(loc=\"upper left\", fontsize=8)\n    ax_temp2.legend(loc=\"upper right\", fontsize=8)", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}, "message": "Overlay the knapsack running value on the existing third chart panel, keeping the 3D-trace and raster panels exactly as before", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Overlay the knapsack running value on the existing third chart panel, keeping the 3D-trace and raster panels exactly as before"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:20.816614Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:20.816652Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01EvkfwF4QMzCrWrXKAvC4GJ", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:22.877795Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:23.542521Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now the CLI: keep every existing argument as-is, and add the knapsack ones (dataset load, item count, capacity, blend weight):", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:23.542556Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:27.442141Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01LXL9mCRHbaYGe88A5doVyU", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"description": "Add knapsack CLI args (load dataset, synth item count, capacity, blend) without touching existing args", "new_str": "    ap.add_argument(\"--load-run\", type=str, default=None,\n                     help=\"skip generation entirely and re-render charts from a saved .npz run\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--knapsack-data\", type=str, default=None,\n                     help=\"load knapsack items from a .npy (n,2) array or a 'weight,value' CSV; \"\n                          \"if omitted, a random item set is synthesized\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--knapsack-items\", type=int, default=None,\n                     help=\"number of synthesized items when --knapsack-data is not given \"\n                          \"(default: matches --length)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--knapsack-capacity\", type=float, default=None,\n                     help=\"knapsack capacity (default: 40%% of total item weight)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--knapsack-blend\", type=float, default=1.0,\n                     help=\"how strongly the knapsack's value-density signal adds to the \"\n                          \"spiking population's input current (0 disables the coupling)\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()", "old_str": "    ap.add_argument(\"--load-run\", type=str, default=None,\n                     help=\"skip generation entirely and re-render charts from a saved .npz run\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}, "message": "Add knapsack CLI args (load dataset, synth item count, capacity, blend) without touching existing args", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Add knapsack CLI args (load dataset, synth item count, capacity, blend) without touching existing args"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:27.669689Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:27.669759Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01LXL9mCRHbaYGe88A5doVyU", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation",