 decorations.\\n  fig.tight_layout()\\n[info] chart saved to t1.png\\n=== with --knapsack-data (loaded dataset) ===\\n[info] no --data given, using built-in demo corpus\\n[info] loaded 20 knapsack items from items.csv\\nThe fox runs into the forest and the lazy dog is loyal. the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog\\n[info] vocab=27 contexts=42\\n[info] knapsack: 20 items, capacity=200.0, final running value=651.0\\n/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py:420: UserWarning: Tight layout not applied. The left and right margins cannot be made large enough to accommodate all Axes decorations.\\n  fig.tight_layout()\\n[info] chart saved to t2.png\\n=== knapsack-blend 0 (decouple, sanity check surprisal-only path still works) ===\\n[info] no --data given, using built-in demo corpus\\n[info] synthesized 20 knapsack items (use --knapsack-data to load your own)\\nThe fox runs into the forest and the lazy dog is loyal. the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog\\n[info] vocab=27 contexts=42\\n[info] knapsack: 20 items, capacity=192.4, final running value=704.0\\n/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py:420: UserWarning: Tight layout not applied. The left and right margins cannot be made large enough to accommodate all Axes decorations.\\n  fig.tight_layout()\\n[info] chart saved to t3.png\\n=== existing save/load-neurons + save/load-run still work ===\\n[info] no --data given, using built-in demo corpus\\n[info] synthesized 15 knapsack items (use --knapsack-data to load your own)\\nThe fox. the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog is loyal. fox runs\\n[info] vocab=27 contexts=42\\n[info] knapsack: 15 items, capacity=156.4, final running value=469.0\\n[info] neuron weights saved to n.npy\\n[info] run binary saved to r.npz\\n/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py:420: UserWarning: Tight layout not applied. The left and right margins cannot be made large enough to accommodate all Axes decorations.\\n  fig.tight_layout()\\n[info] chart saved to t4.png\\n[info] loaded binary run from r.npz (vocab=27 contexts=42)\\n/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_live.py:420: UserWarning: Tight layout not applied. The left and right margins cannot be made large enough to accommodate all Axes decorations.\\n  fig.tight_layout()\\n[info] chart saved to t5.png\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu    191 Sep 27 22:12 items.csv\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu    320 Sep 27 22:12 n.npy\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu   2797 Sep 27 22:12 r.npz\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu 194611 Sep 27 22:12 t1.png\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu 192860 Sep 27 22:12 t2.png\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu 194463 Sep 27 22:12 t3.png\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu 189959 Sep 27 22:12 t4.png\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu 189959 Sep 27 22:12 t5.png\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:50.320723Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:52.297619Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Untangling how blend settings affect knapsack calculations."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:52.297732Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:53.939655Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01KGTftvqyqPY2VhFDeaN2ga", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 -c \"\nfrom hecm_live import knapsack_dp_exact, synthesize_items\nw, v = synthesize_items(n=15, seed=1)\nsel, best = knapsack_dp_exact(w, v, capacity=100)\nprint('DP selected items:', sel)\nprint('DP best value:', best)\nprint('weights used:', w[sel].sum(), 'of capacity 100')\n\"", "description": "unit-test the exact DP knapsack solver too"}, "message": "unit-test the exact DP knapsack solver too", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 -c \\\"\\nfrom hecm_live import knapsack_dp_exact, synthesize_items\\nw, v = synthesize_items(n=15, seed=1)\\nsel, best = knapsack_dp_exact(w, v, capacity=100)\\nprint('DP selected items:', sel)\\nprint('DP best value:', best)\\nprint('weights used:', w[sel].sum(), 'of capacity 100')\\n\\\"\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:54.653883Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:54.653917Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01KGTftvqyqPY2VhFDeaN2ga", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"DP selected items: [1, 4, 5, 8, 9, 11, 12]\\nDP best value: 412.0\\nweights used: 100.0 of capacity 100\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"DP selected items: [1, 4, 5, 8, 9, 11, 12]\\nDP best value: 412.0\\nweights used: 100.0 of capacity 100\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:56.910591Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:57.978137Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Both solvers check out. Now let's mirror the same additions into `hecm_gui.py` (electrical current now knapsack-driven, plus a Load Dataset menu item), while keeping every existing control and menu item intact:", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:57.978175Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:58.490328Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01NGVsQ8NyqzwEy2YcQPgV7G", "name": "view", "input": {"description": "Re-view gui file before editing", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py"}, "message": "Re-view gui file before editing", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Re-view gui file before editing"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:59.036783Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:12:59.036970Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01NGVsQ8NyqzwEy2YcQPgV7G", "name": "view", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "     1\t\"\"\"\n     2\thecm_gui.py \u2014 Tkinter desktop app for the n-gram generator + spiking-neuron\n     3\t              simulation + 3D token trace + live charts.\n     4\t\n     5\tThis is the same model as hecm_live.py (trigram Markov generator, a real LIF\n     6\tspiking population driven by generation surprisal, and a deterministic\n     7\thash-based 3D position per word) wrapped in a Tkinter window instead of a\n     8\tCLI. Charts update live, step by step, as text generates. It also supports\n     9\tthe same binary persistence as the CLI version:\n    10\t\n    11\t  - Save/Load neuron weights   -> .npy\n    12\t  - Save/Load a full run       -> .npz  (temps, surprisals, spike raster, 3D path)\n    13\t\n    14\tThis file is self-contained (does not import hecm_live.py) so it can be run\n    15\ton its own with just: pip install numpy matplotlib\n    16\t\"\"\"\n    17\t\n    18\timport hashlib\n    19\timport math\n    20\timport re\n    21\timport tkinter as tk\n    22\tfrom collections import Counter\n    23\tfrom tkinter import ttk, filedialog, messagebox\n    24\t\n    25\timport numpy as np\n    26\timport matplotlib\n    27\tmatplotlib.use(\"TkAgg\")\n    28\tfrom matplotlib.backends.backend_tkagg import FigureCanvasTkAgg\n    29\tfrom matplotlib.figure import Figure\n    30\tfrom mpl_toolkits.mplot3d import Axes3D  # noqa: F401 (registers 3D projection)\n    31\t\n    32\tUNK, BOS = \"<unk>\", \"<bos>\"\n    33\t\n    34\tDEFAULT_CORPUS = (\n    35\t    \"the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. the dog barks at the fox. \"\n    36\t    \"the fox runs into the forest and the dog follows. in the forest the fox \"\n    37\t    \"finds a den and the dog waits outside. the quick fox is clever and the \"\n    38\t    \"lazy dog is loyal.\"\n    39\t)\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    43\t# Core model \u2014 identical logic to hecm_live.py\n    44\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    45\t\n    46\tdef tokenize(text):\n    47\t    return re.findall(r\"[a-z0-9']+|[.,!?;:]\", text.lower())\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\tdef build_vocab(tokens, min_count=1):\n    51\t    counts = Counter(tokens)\n    52\t    kept = sorted(w for w, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count)\n    53\t    vocab = [UNK, BOS] + kept\n    54\t    return vocab, {w: i for i, w in enumerate(vocab)}\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\tdef build_context_model(tokens, word_to_idx, order=3):\n    58\t    ctx_len = order - 1\n    59\t    bos_idx, unk_idx = word_to_idx[BOS], word_to_idx[UNK]\n    60\t    ids = [word_to_idx.get(t, unk_idx) for t in tokens]\n    61\t    padded = [bos_idx] * ctx_len + ids\n    62\t    model = {}\n    63\t    for i in range(len(padded) - ctx_len):\n    64\t        ctx = tuple(padded[i:i + ctx_len])\n    65\t        model.setdefault(ctx, Counter())[padded[i + ctx_len]] += 1\n    66\t    return model, ctx_len\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\tdef sinusoidal_temperature(step, base=0.8, amplitude=0.4, omega=0.5, floor=0.05):\n    70\t    return max(floor, base + amplitude * math.sin(omega * step))\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\tdef sample_next(model, ctx, temperature, rng):\n    74\t    dist = model.get(ctx)\n    75\t    if dist is None:\n    76\t        keys = list(model.keys())\n    77\t        ctx = keys[rng.integers(len(keys))]\n    78\t        dist = model[ctx]\n    79\t    ids = list(dist.keys())\n    80\t    counts = np.array([dist[i] for i in ids], dtype=np.float64)\n    81\t    probs = counts / counts.sum()\n    82\t    logits = np.log(probs) / max(temperature, 1e-6)\n    83\t    logits -= logits.max()\n    84\t    w = np.exp(logits); w /= w.sum()\n    85\t    choice = rng.choice(len(ids), p=w)\n    86\t    return ids[choice], probs[choice], ctx\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\tdef detokenize(words):\n    90\t    out = []\n    91\t    for w in words:\n    92\t        if w == BOS:\n    93\t            continue\n    94\t        if out and re.match(r\"[.,!?;:]\", w):\n    95\t            out[-1] += w\n    96\t        else:\n    97\t            out.append(w)\n    98\t    text = \" \".join(out)\n    99\t    return text[0].upper() + text[1:] if text else text\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\tdef word_to_3d(word):\n   103\t    h = hashlib.sha256(word.encode(\"utf-8\")).digest()\n   104\t    xs = [int.from_bytes(h[i:i + 4], \"big\") for i in (0, 4, 8)]\n   105\t    return tuple((x % 20000) / 10000 - 1.0 for x in xs)\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\tclass SpikingPopulation:\n   109\t    def __init__(self, n_neurons=24, threshold=1.0, leak=0.92, gain=0.35, seed=0, weights=None):\n   110\t        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n   111\t        self.threshold, self.leak, self.gain, self.rng = threshold, leak, gain, rng\n   112\t        if weights is not None:\n   113\t            self.weights = np.asarray(weights, dtype=np.float64)\n   114\t            self.n = len(self.weights)\n   115\t        else:\n   116\t            self.n = n_neurons\n   117\t            self.weights = rng.uniform(0.3, 1.2, size=n_neurons)\n   118\t        self.V = np.zeros(self.n)\n   119\t\n   120\t    @classmethod\n   121\t    def from_npy(cls, path, **kw):\n   122\t        return cls(weights=np.load(path), **kw)\n   123\t\n   124\t    def save_npy(self, path):\n   125\t        np.save(path, self.weights)\n   126\t\n   127\t    def step(self, surprisal):\n   128\t        noise = self.rng.normal(0, 0.05, size=self.n)\n   129\t        self.V = self.V * self.leak + surprisal * self.weights * self.gain + noise\n   130\t        spiked = self.V >= self.threshold\n   131\t        self.V[spiked] = 0.0\n   132\t        return spiked\n   133\t\n   134\t\n   135\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   136\t# Tkinter app\n   137\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   138\t\n   139\tclass HECMApp(tk.Tk):\n   140\t    def __init__(self):\n   141\t        super().__init__()\n   142\t        self.title(\"HECM Live \u2014 generator + spiking sim + 3D trace\")\n   143\t        self.geometry(\"1180x760\")\n   144\t\n   145\t        self.population = None          # loaded/saved neuron weights live here\n   146\t        self.running = False\n   147\t        self.gen_state = None           # dict of live arrays during a run\n   148\t\n   149\t        self._build_menu()\n   150\t        self._build_controls()\n   151\t        self._build_output()\n   152\t        self._build_charts()\n   153\t\n   154\t    # ---- UI construction ----------------------------------------------\n   155\t\n   156\t    def _build_menu(self):\n   157\t        menubar = tk.Menu(self)\n   158\t        filem = tk.Menu(menubar, tearoff=0)\n   159\t        filem.add_command(label=\"Load neuron weights (.npy)...\", command=self.load_neurons)\n   160\t        filem.add_command(label=\"Save neuron weights (.npy)...\", command=self.save_neurons)\n   161\t        filem.add_separator()\n   162\t        filem.add_command(label=\"Save run binary (.npz)...\", command=self.save_run)\n   163\t        filem.add_command(label=\"Load run binary (.npz) [re-chart only]...\", command=self.load_run)\n   164\t        filem.add_separator()\n   165\t        filem.add_command(label=\"Save chart as PNG...\", command=self.save_chart)\n   166\t        filem.add_separator()\n   167\t        filem.add_command(label=\"Quit\", command=self.destroy)\n   168\t        menubar.add_cascade(label=\"File\", menu=filem)\n   169\t        self.config(menu=menubar)\n   170\t\n   171\t    def _build_controls(self):\n   172\t        top = ttk.Frame(self, padding=8)\n   173\t        top.pack(side=\"top\", fill=\"x\")\n   174\t\n   175\t        ttk.Label(top, text=\"Corpus:\").grid(row=0, column=0, sticky=\"nw\")\n   176\t        self.corpus_box = tk.Text(top, width=60, height=3)\n   177\t        self.corpus_box.insert(\"1.0\", DEFAULT_CORPUS)\n   178\t        self.corpus_box.grid(row=0, column=1, columnspan=5, sticky=\"we\", padx=4)\n   179\t\n   180\t        ttk.Label(top, text=\"Prompt:\").grid(row=1, column=0, sticky=\"w\", pady=(6, 0))\n   181\t        self.prompt_var = tk.StringVar(value=\"the fox\")\n   182\t        ttk.Entry(top, textvariable=self.prompt_var, width=20).grid(row=1, column=1, sticky=\"w\", pady=(6, 0))\n   183\t\n   184\t        self.length_var = tk.IntVar(value=60)\n   185\t        self.order_var = tk.IntVar(value=3)\n   186\t        self.neurons_var = tk.IntVar(value=24)\n   187\t        self.speed_var = tk.IntVar(value=80)\n   188\t\n   189\t        for i, (label, var, w) in enumerate([\n   190\t            (\"length\", self.length_var, 6), (\"order\", self.order_var, 4),\n   191\t            (\"neurons\", self.neurons_var, 5), (\"speed(ms)\", self.speed_var, 6),\n   192\t        ]):\n   193\t            ttk.Label(top, text=label).grid(row=1, column=2 + i * 2, sticky=\"e\", padx=(10, 2), pady=(6, 0))\n   194\t            ttk.Spinbox(top, from_=1, to=2000, textvariable=var, width=w).grid(\n   195\t                row=1, column=3 + i * 2, sticky=\"w\", pady=(6, 0))\n   196\t\n   197\t        btns = ttk.Frame(top)\n   198\t        btns.grid(row=2, column=0, columnspan=10, sticky=\"w\", pady=(8, 0))\n   199\t        self.go_btn = ttk.Button(btns, text=\"Generate\", command=self.start_generation)\n   200\t        self.go_btn.pack(side=\"left\")\n   201\t        self.stop_btn = ttk.Button(btns, text=\"Stop\", command=self.stop_generation, state=\"disabled\")\n   202\t        self.stop_btn.pack(side=\"left\", padx=6)\n   203\t        self.status_var = tk.StringVar(value=\"idle\")\n   204\t        ttk.Label(btns, textvariable=self.status_var, foreground=\"#666\").pack(side=\"left\", padx=12)\n   205\t\n   206\t    def _build_output(self):\n   207\t        frame = ttk.Frame(self, padding=(8, 0))\n   208\t        frame.pack(side=\"top\", fill=\"x\")\n   209\t        ttk.Label(frame, text=\"Generated text:\").pack(anchor=\"w\")\n   210\t        self.output_box = tk.Text(frame, height=4, wrap=\"word\")\n   211\t        self.output_box.pack(fill=\"x\")\n   212\t\n   213\t    def _build_charts(self):\n   214\t        self.fig = Figure(figsize=(11.5, 4.2), dpi=100, constrained_layout=True)\n   215\t        self.ax3d = self.fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 1, projection=\"3d\")\n   216\t        self.ax_raster = self.fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 2)\n   217\t        self.ax_temp = self.fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 3)\n   218\t\n   219\t        self.canvas = FigureCanvasTkAgg(self.fig, master=self)\n   220\t        self.canvas.get_tk_widget().pack(side=\"bottom\", fill=\"both\", expand=True)\n   221\t        self._redraw_charts()\n   222\t\n   223\t    # ---- generation loop -------------------------------------------------\n   224\t\n   225\t    def start_generation(self):\n   226\t        if self.running:\n   227\t            return\n   228\t        order = self.order_var.get()\n   229\t        corpus_text = self.corpus_box.get(\"1.0\", \"end\")\n   230\t        tokens = tokenize(corpus_text)\n   231\t        vocab, word_to_idx = build_vocab(tokens)\n   232\t        model, ctx_len = build_context_model(tokens, word_to_idx, order=order)\n   233\t\n   234\t        pop = self.population or SpikingPopulation(n_neurons=self.neurons_var.get())\n   235\t        self.population = pop\n   236\t\n   237\t        prompt_ids = [word_to_idx.get(t, word_to_idx[UNK]) for t in tokenize(self.prompt_var.get())]\n   238\t        ctx = tuple(([word_to_idx[BOS]] * ctx_len + prompt_ids)[-ctx_len:]) if ctx_len else ()\n   239\t\n   240\t        self.gen_state = {\n   241\t            \"vocab\": vocab, \"model\": model, \"ctx_len\": ctx_len, \"ctx\": ctx,\n   242\t            \"rng\": np.random.default_rng(),\n   243\t            \"out_ids\": list(prompt_ids), \"pop\": pop,\n   244\t            \"temps\": [], \"surprisals\": [], \"spike_log\": [], \"path\": [],\n   245\t            \"step\": 0, \"length\": self.length_var.get(),\n   246\t            \"vocab_size\": len(vocab), \"context_states\": len(model),\n   247\t        }\n   248\t        self.output_box.delete(\"1.0\", \"end\")\n   249\t        self.output_box.insert(\"1.0\", detokenize([vocab[i] for i in self.gen_state[\"out_ids\"]]))\n   250\t\n   251\t        self.running = True\n   252\t        self.go_btn.config(state=\"disabled\")\n   253\t        self.stop_btn.config(state=\"normal\")\n   254\t        self.status_var.set(\"running\u2026\")\n   255\t        self.after(self.speed_var.get(), self._step)\n   256\t\n   257\t    def stop_generation(self):\n   258\t        self.running = False\n   259\t        self.status_var.set(\"stopped\")\n   260\t        self.go_btn.config(state=\"normal\")\n   261\t        self.stop_btn.config(state=\"disabled\")\n   262\t\n   263\t    def _step(self):\n   264\t        if not self.running:\n   265\t            return\n   266\t        s = self.gen_state\n   267\t        if s[\"step\"] >= s[\"length\"]:\n   268\t            self.stop_generation()\n   269\t            self.status_var.set(\"done\")\n   270\t            return\n   271\t\n   272\t        temp = sinusoidal_temperature(s[\"step\"])\n   273\t        next_id, prob, used_ctx = sample_next(s[\"model\"], s[\"ctx\"], temp, s[\"rng\"])\n   274\t        s[\"ctx\"] = (used_ctx + (next_id,))[-s[\"ctx_len\"]:] if s[\"ctx_len\"] else s[\"ctx\"]\n   275\t        s[\"out_ids\"].append(next_id)\n   276\t\n   277\t        surprisal = -math.log(max(prob, 1e-9))\n   278\t        spikes = s[\"pop\"].step(surprisal)\n   279\t\n   280\t        s[\"temps\"].append(temp)\n   281\t        s[\"surprisals\"].append(surprisal)\n   282\t        s[\"spike_log\"].append(spikes)\n   283\t        s[\"path\"].append(word_to_3d(s[\"vocab\"][next_id]))\n   284\t        s[\"step\"] += 1\n   285\t\n   286\t        self.output_box.delete(\"1.0\", \"end\")\n   287\t        self.output_box.insert(\"1.0\", detokenize([s[\"vocab\"][i] for i in s[\"out_ids\"]]))\n   288\t        self.status_var.set(f\"step {s['step']}/{s['length']}  surprisal={surprisal:.2f}\")\n   289\t\n   290\t        self._redraw_charts()\n   291\t        self.after(self.speed_var.get(), self._step)\n   292\t\n   293\t    # ---- chart rendering ---------------------------------------------------\n   294\t\n   295\t    def _redraw_charts(self):\n   296\t        s = self.gen_state\n   297\t        self.ax3d.cla(); self.ax_raster.cla(); self.ax_temp.cla()\n   298\t\n   299\t        if s and s[\"path\"]:\n   300\t            path = np.array(s[\"path\"])\n   301\t            self.ax3d.plot(path[:, 0], path[:, 1], path[:, 2], color=\"#0d9488\", linewidth=1.2)\n   302\t            self.ax3d.scatter(path[:, 0], path[:, 1], path[:, 2], color=\"#db2777\", s=12)\n   303\t        self.ax3d.set_title(\"3D token trace\")\n   304\t        self.ax3d.set_xticklabels([]); self.ax3d.set_yticklabels([]); self.ax3d.set_zticklabels([])\n   305\t\n   306\t        if s and s[\"spike_log\"]:\n   307\t            self.ax_raster.imshow(np.array(s[\"spike_log\"]).T, aspect=\"auto\", cmap=\"magma\",\n   308\t                                   interpolation=\"nearest\")\n   309\t        self.ax_raster.set_title(\"Spike raster\")\n   310\t        self.ax_raster.set_xlabel(\"step\"); self.ax_raster.set_ylabel(\"neuron\")\n   311\t\n   312\t        if s and s[\"temps\"]:\n   313\t            self.ax_temp.plot(s[\"temps\"], color=\"#0d9488\", label=\"temperature\")\n   314\t            ax2 = self.ax_temp.twinx()\n   315\t            ax2.plot(s[\"surprisals\"], color=\"#ca8a04\", alpha=0.6, label=\"surprisal\")\n   316\t        self.ax_temp.set_title(\"Temperature & surprisal\")\n   317\t        self.ax_temp.set_xlabel(\"step\")\n   318\t\n   319\t        self.canvas.draw_idle()\n   320\t\n   321\t    # ---- persistence: neuron weights + full run binaries -------------------\n   322\t\n   323\t    def load_neurons(self):\n   324\t        path = filedialog.askopenfilename(filetypes=[(\"NumPy array\", \"*.npy\")])\n   325\t        if not path:\n   326\t            return\n   327\t        try:\n   328\t            self.population = SpikingPopulation.from_npy(path)\n   329\t            messagebox.showinfo(\"Loaded\", f\"Loaded {self.population.n} neuron weights from {path}\")\n   330\t        except Exception as e:\n   331\t            messagebox.showerror(\"Load failed\", str(e))\n   332\t\n   333\t    def save_neurons(self):\n   334\t        if not self.population:\n   335\t            messagebox.showwarning(\"No population\", \"Run a generation first, or load weights.\")\n   336\t            return\n   337\t        path = filedialog.asksaveasfilename(defaultextension=\".npy\", filetypes=[(\"NumPy array\", \"*.npy\")])\n   338\t        if not path:\n   339\t            return\n   340\t        self.population.save_npy(path)\n   341\t        messagebox.showinfo(\"Saved\", f\"Neuron weights saved to {path}\")\n   342\t\n   343\t    def save_run(self):\n   344\t        s = self.gen_state\n   345\t        if not s or not s[\"temps\"]:\n   346\t            messagebox.showwarning(\"No run\", \"Generate something first.\")\n   347\t            return\n   348\t        path = filedialog.asksaveasfilename(defaultextension=\".npz\", filetypes=[(\"NumPy zip\", \"*.npz\")])\n   349\t        if not path:\n   350\t            return\n   351\t        np.savez_compressed(\n   352\t            path,\n   353\t            temps=np.array(s[\"temps\"]), surprisals=np.array(s[\"surprisals\"]),\n   354\t            spike_log=np.array(s[\"spike_log\"]), path3d=np.array(s[\"path\"]),\n   355\t            vocab_size=s[\"vocab_size\"], context_states=s[\"context_states\"],\n   356\t        )\n   357\t        messagebox.showinfo(\"Saved\", f\"Run binary saved to {path}\")\n   358\t\n   359\t    def load_run(self):\n   360\t        \"\"\"Load a saved .npz and re-draw the charts from it (no text, no regeneration \u2014\n   361\t        this is for inspecting saved binary traces, e.g. from the CLI version).\"\"\"\n   362\t        path = filedialog.askopenfilename(filetypes=[(\"NumPy zip\", \"*.npz\")])\n   363\t        if not path:\n   364\t            return\n   365\t        data = np.load(path)\n   366\t        self.gen_state = {\n   367\t            \"temps\": list(data[\"temps\"]), \"surprisals\": list(data[\"surprisals\"]),\n   368\t            \"spike_log\": list(data[\"spike_log\"]), \"path\": list(data[\"path3d\"]),\n   369\t            \"vocab_size\": int(data[\"vocab_size\"]), \"context_states\": int(data[\"context_states\"]),\n   370\t        }\n   371\t        self.output_box.delete(\"1.0\", \"end\")\n   372\t        self.output_box.insert(\"1.0\", \"[re-rendered from saved binary \u2014 no text stored in .npz]\")\n   373\t        self._redraw_charts()\n   374\t\n   375\t    def save_chart(self):\n   376\t        path = filedialog.asksaveasfilename(defaultextension=\".png\", filetypes=[(\"PNG image\", \"*.png\")])\n   377\t        if not path:\n   378\t            return\n   379\t        self.fig.savefig(path, dpi=150)\n   380\t        messagebox.showinfo(\"Saved\", f\"Chart saved to {path}\")\n   381\t\n   382\t\n   383\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n   384\t    app = HECMApp()\n   385\t    app.mainloop()\n   386\t"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "bookText", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nhecm_gui.py \\u2014 Tkinter desktop app for the n-gram generator + spiking-neuron\\n              simulation + 3D token trace + live charts.\\n\\nThis is the same model as hecm_live.py (trigram Markov generator, a real LIF\\nspiking population driven by generation surprisal, and a deterministic\\nhash-based 3D position per word) wrapped in a Tkinter window instead of a\\nCLI. Charts update live, step by step, as text generates. It also supports\\nthe same binary persistence as the CLI version:\\n\\n  - Save/Load neuron weights   -> .npy\\n  - Save/Load a full run       -> .npz  (temps, surprisals, spike raster, 3D path)\\n\\nThis file is self-contained (does not import hecm_live.py) so it can be run\\non its own with just: pip install numpy matplotlib\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport hashlib\\nimport math\\nimport re\\nimport tkinter as tk\\nfrom collections import Counter\\nfrom tkinter import ttk, filedialog, messagebox\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport matplotlib\\nmatplotlib.use(\\\"TkAgg\\\")\\nfrom matplotlib.backends.backend_tkagg import FigureCanvasTkAgg\\nfrom matplotlib.figure import Figure\\nfrom mpl_toolkits.mplot3d import Axes3D  # noqa: F401 (registers 3D projection)\\n\\nUNK, BOS = \\\"<unk>\\\", \\\"<bos>\\\"\\n\\nDEFAULT_CORPUS = (\\n    \\\"the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. the dog barks at the fox. \\\"\\n    \\\"the fox runs into the forest and the dog follows. in the forest the fox \\\"\\n    \\\"finds a den and the dog waits outside. the quick fox is clever and the \\\"\\n    \\\"lazy dog is loyal.\\\"\\n)\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Core model \\u2014 identical logic to hecm_live.py\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef tokenize(text):\\n    return re.findall(r\\\"[a-z0-9']+|[.,!?;:]\\\", text.lower())\\n\\n\\ndef build_vocab(tokens, min_count=1):\\n    counts = Counter(tokens)\\n    kept = sorted(w for w, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count)\\n    vocab = [UNK, BOS] + kept\\n    return vocab, {w: i for i, w in enumerate(vocab)}\\n\\n\\ndef build_context_model(tokens, word_to_idx, order=3):\\n    ctx_len = order - 1\\n    bos_idx, unk_idx = word_to_idx[BOS], word_to_idx[UNK]\\n    ids = [word_to_idx.get(t, unk_idx) for t in tokens]\\n    padded = [bos_idx] * ctx_len + ids\\n    model = {}\\n    for i in range(len(padded) - ctx_len):\\n        ctx = tuple(padded[i:i + ctx_len])\\n        model.setdefault(ctx, Counter())[padded[i + ctx_len]] += 1\\n    return model, ctx_len\\n\\n\\ndef sinusoidal_temperature(step, base=0.8, amplitude=0.4, omega=0.5, floor=0.05):\\n    return max(floor, base + amplitude * math.sin(omega * step))\\n\\n\\ndef sample_next(model, ctx, temperature, rng):\\n    dist = model.get(ctx)\\n    if dist is None:\\n        keys = list(model.keys())\\n        ctx = keys[rng.integers(len(keys))]\\n        dist = model[ctx]\\n    ids = list(dist.keys())\\n    counts = np.array([dist[i] for i in ids], dtype=np.float64)\\n    probs = counts / counts.sum()\\n    logits = np.log(probs) / max(temperature, 1e-6)\\n    logits -= logits.max()\\n    w = np.exp(logits); w /= w.sum()\\n    choice = rng.choice(len(ids), p=w)\\n    return ids[choice], probs[choice], ctx\\n\\n\\ndef detokenize(words):\\n    out = []\\n    for w in words:\\n        if w == BOS:\\n            continue\\n        if out and re.match(r\\\"[.,!?;:]\\\", w):\\n            out[-1] += w\\n        else:\\n            out.append(w)\\n    text = \\\" \\\".join(out)\\n    return text[0].upper() + text[1:] if text else text\\n\\n\\ndef word_to_3d(word):\\n    h = hashlib.sha256(word.encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")).digest()\\n    xs = [int.from_bytes(h[i:i + 4], \\\"big\\\") for i in (0, 4, 8)]\\n    return tuple((x % 20000) / 10000 - 1.0 for x in xs)\\n\\n\\nclass SpikingPopulation:\\n    def __init__(self, n_neurons=24, threshold=1.0, leak=0.92, gain=0.35, seed=0, weights=None):\\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n        self.threshold, self.leak, self.gain, self.rng = threshold, leak, gain, rng\\n        if weights is not None:\\n            self.weights = np.asarray(weights, dtype=np.float64)\\n            self.n = len(self.weights)\\n        else:\\n            self.n = n_neurons\\n            self.weights = rng.uniform(0.3, 1.2, size=n_neurons)\\n        self.V = np.zeros(self.n)\\n\\n    @classmethod\\n    def from_npy(cls, path, **kw):\\n        return cls(weights=np.load(path), **kw)\\n\\n    def save_npy(self, path):\\n        np.save(path, self.weights)\\n\\n    def step(self, surprisal):\\n        noise = self.rng.normal(0, 0.05, size=self.n)\\n        self.V = self.V * self.leak + surprisal * self.weights * self.gain + noise\\n        spiked = self.V >= self.threshold\\n        self.V[spiked] = 0.0\\n        return spiked\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Tkinter app\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nclass HECMApp(tk.Tk):\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        super().__init__()\\n        self.title(\\\"HECM Live \\u2014 generator + spiking sim + 3D trace\\\")\\n        self.geometry(\\\"1180x760\\\")\\n\\n        self.population = None          # loaded/saved neuron weights live here\\n        self.running = False\\n        self.gen_state = None           # dict of live arrays during a run\\n\\n        self._build_menu()\\n        self._build_controls()\\n        self._build_output()\\n        self._build_charts()\\n\\n    # ---- UI construction ----------------------------------------------\\n\\n    def _build_menu(self):\\n        menubar = tk.Menu(self)\\n        filem = tk.Menu(menubar, tearoff=0)\\n        filem.add_command(label=\\\"Load neuron weights (.npy)...\\\", command=self.load_neurons)\\n        filem.add_command(label=\\\"Save neuron weights (.npy)...\\\", command=self.save_neurons)\\n        filem.add_separator()\\n        filem.add_command(label=\\\"Save run binary (.npz)...\\\", command=self.save_run)\\n        filem.add_command(label=\\\"Load run binary (.npz) [re-chart only]...\\\", command=self.load_run)\\n        filem.add_separator()\\n        filem.add_command(label=\\\"Save chart as PNG...\\\", command=self.save_chart)\\n        filem.add_separator()\\n        filem.add_command(label=\\\"Quit\\\", command=self.destroy)\\n        menubar.add_cascade(label=\\\"File\\\", menu=filem)\\n        self.config(menu=menubar)\\n\\n    def _build_controls(self):\\n        top = ttk.Frame(self, padding=8)\\n        top.pack(side=\\\"top\\\", fill=\\\"x\\\")\\n\\n        ttk.Label(top, text=\\\"Corpus:\\\").grid(row=0, column=0, sticky=\\\"nw\\\")\\n        self.corpus_box = tk.Text(top, width=60, height=3)\\n        self.corpus_box.insert(\\\"1.0\\\", DEFAULT_CORPUS)\\n        self.corpus_box.grid(row=0, column=1, columnspan=5, sticky=\\\"we\\\", padx=4)\\n\\n        ttk.Label(top, text=\\\"Prompt:\\\").grid(row=1, column=0, sticky=\\\"w\\\", pady=(6, 0))\\n        self.prompt_var = tk.StringVar(value=\\\"the fox\\\")\\n        ttk.Entry(top, textvariable=self.prompt_var, width=20).grid(row=1, column=1, sticky=\\\"w\\\", pady=(6, 0))\\n\\n        self.length_var = tk.IntVar(value=60)\\n        self.order_var = tk.IntVar(value=3)\\n        self.neurons_var = tk.IntVar(value=24)\\n        self.speed_var = tk.IntVar(value=80)\\n\\n        for i, (label, var, w) in enumerate([\\n            (\\\"length\\\", self.length_var, 6), (\\\"order\\\", self.order_var, 4),\\n            (\\\"neurons\\\", self.neurons_var, 5), (\\\"speed(ms)\\\", self.speed_var, 6),\\n        ]):\\n            ttk.Label(top, text=label).grid(row=1, column=2 + i * 2, sticky=\\\"e\\\", padx=(10, 2), pady=(6, 0))\\n            ttk.Spinbox(top, from_=1, to=2000, textvariable=var, width=w).grid(\\n                row=1, column=3 + i * 2, sticky=\\\"w\\\", pady=(6, 0))\\n\\n        btns = ttk.Frame(top)\\n        btns.grid(row=2, column=0, columnspan=10, sticky=\\\"w\\\", pady=(8, 0))\\n        self.go_btn = ttk.Button(btns, text=\\\"Generate\\\", command=self.start_generation)\\n        self.go_btn.pack(side=\\\"left\\\")\\n        self.stop_btn = ttk.Button(btns, text=\\\"Stop\\\", command=self.stop_generation, state=\\\"disabled\\\")\\n        self.stop_btn.pack(side=\\\"left\\\", padx=6)\\n        self.status_var = tk.StringVar(value=\\\"idle\\\")\\n        ttk.Label(btns, textvariable=self.status_var, foreground=\\\"#666\\\").pack(side=\\\"left\\\", padx=12)\\n\\n    def _build_output(self):\\n        frame = ttk.Frame(self, padding=(8, 0))\\n        frame.pack(side=\\\"top\\\", fill=\\\"x\\\")\\n        ttk.Label(frame, text=\\\"Generated text:\\\").pack(anchor=\\\"w\\\")\\n        self.output_box = tk.Text(frame, height=4, wrap=\\\"word\\\")\\n        self.output_box.pack(fill=\\\"x\\\")\\n\\n    def _build_charts(self):\\n        self.fig = Figure(figsize=(11.5, 4.2), dpi=100, constrained_layout=True)\\n        self.ax3d = self.fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 1, projection=\\\"3d\\\")\\n        self.ax_raster = self.fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 2)\\n        self.ax_temp = self.fig.add_subplot(1, 3, 3)\\n\\n        self.canvas = FigureCanvasTkAgg(self.fig, master=self)\\n        self.canvas.get_tk_widget().pack(side=\\\"bottom\\\", fill=\\\"both\\\", expand=True)\\n        self._redraw_charts()\\n\\n    # ---- generation loop -------------------------------------------------\\n\\n    def start_generation(self):\\n        if self.running:\\n            return\\n        order = self.order_var.get()\\n        corpus_text = self.corpus_box.get(\\\"1.0\\\", \\\"end\\\")\\n        tokens = tokenize(corpus_text)\\n        vocab, word_to_idx = build_vocab(tokens)\\n        model, ctx_len = build_context_model(tokens, word_to_idx, order=order)\\n\\n        pop = self.population or SpikingPopulation(n_neurons=self.neurons_var.get())\\n        self.population = pop\\n\\n        prompt_ids = [word_to_idx.get(t, word_to_idx[UNK]) for t in tokenize(self.prompt_var.get())]\\n        ctx = tuple(([word_to_idx[BOS]] * ctx_len + prompt_ids)[-ctx_len:]) if ctx_len else ()\\n\\n        self.gen_state = {\\n            \\\"vocab\\\": vocab, \\\"model\\\": model, \\\"ctx_len\\\": ctx_len, \\\"ctx\\\": ctx,\\n            \\\"rng\\\": np.random.default_rng(),\\n            \\\"out_ids\\\": list(prompt_ids), \\\"pop\\\": pop,\\n            \\\"temps\\\": [], \\\"surprisals\\\": [], \\\"spike_log\\\": [], \\\"path\\\": [],\\n            \\\"step\\\": 0, \\\"length\\\": self.length_var.get(),\\n            \\\"vocab_size\\\": len(vocab), \\\"context_states\\\": len(model),\\n        }\\n        self.output_box.delete(\\\"1.0\\\", \\\"end\\\")\\n        self.output_box.insert(\\\"1.0\\\", detokenize([vocab[i] for i in self.gen_state[\\\"out_ids\\\"]]))\\n\\n        self.running = True\\n        self.go_btn.config(state=\\\"disabled\\\")\\n        self.stop_btn.config(state=\\\"normal\\\")\\n        self.status_var.set(\\\"running\\u2026\\\")\\n        self.after(self.speed_var.get(), self._step)\\n\\n    def stop_generation(self):\\n        self.running = False\\n        self.status_var.set(\\\"stopped\\\")\\n        self.go_btn.config(state=\\\"normal\\\")\\n        self.stop_btn.config(state=\\\"disabled\\\")\\n\\n    def _step(self):\\n        if not self.running:\\n            return\\n        s = self.gen_state\\n        if s[\\\"step\\\"] >= s[\\\"length\\\"]:\\n            self.stop_generation()\\n            self.status_var.set(\\\"done\\\")\\n            return\\n\\n        temp = sinusoidal_temperature(s[\\\"step\\\"])\\n        next_id, prob, used_ctx = sample_next(s[\\\"model\\\"], s[\\\"ctx\\\"], temp, s[\\\"rng\\\"])\\n        s[\\\"ctx\\\"] = (used_ctx + (next_id,))[-s[\\\"ctx_len\\\"]:] if s[\\\"ctx_len\\\"] else s[\\\"ctx\\\"]\\n        s[\\\"out_ids\\\"].append(next_id)\\n\\n        surprisal = -math.log(max(prob, 1e-9))\\n        spikes = s[\\\"pop\\\"].step(surprisal)\\n\\n        s[\\\"temps\\\"].append(temp)\\n        s[\\\"surprisals\\\"].append(surprisal)\\n        s[\\\"spike_log\\\"].append(spikes)\\n        s[\\\"path\\\"].append(word_to_3d(s[\\\"vocab\\\"][next_id]))\\n        s[\\\"step\\\"] += 1\\n\\n        self.output_box.delete(\\\"1.0\\\", \\\"end\\\")\\n        self.output_box.insert(\\\"1.0\\\", detokenize([s[\\\"vocab\\\"][i] for i in s[\\\"out_ids\\\"]]))\\n        self.status_var.set(f\\\"step {s['step']}/{s['length']}  surprisal={surprisal:.2f}\\\")\\n\\n        self._redraw_charts()\\n        self.after(self.speed_var.get(), self._step)\\n\\n    # ---- chart rendering ---------------------------------------------------\\n\\n    def _redraw_charts(self):\\n        s = self.gen_state\\n        self.ax3d.cla(); self.ax_raster.cla(); self.ax_temp.cla()\\n\\n        if s and s[\\\"path\\\"]:\\n            path = np.array(s[\\\"path\\\"])\\n            self.ax3d.plot(path[:, 0], path[:, 1], path[:, 2], color=\\\"#0d9488\\\", linewidth=1.2)\\n            self.ax3d.scatter(path[:, 0], path[:, 1], path[:, 2], color=\\\"#db2777\\\", s=12)\\n        self.ax3d.set_title(\\\"3D token trace\\\")\\n        self.ax3d.set_xticklabels([]); self.ax3d.set_yticklabels([]); self.ax3d.set_zticklabels([])\\n\\n        if s and s[\\\"spike_log\\\"]:\\n            self.ax_raster.imshow(np.array(s[\\\"spike_log\\\"]).T, aspect=\\\"auto\\\", cmap=\\\"magma\\\",\\n                                   interpolation=\\\"nearest\\\")\\n        self.ax_raster.set_title(\\\"Spike raster\\\")\\n        self.ax_raster.set_xlabel(\\\"step\\\"); self.ax_raster.set_ylabel(\\\"neuron\\\")\\n\\n        if s and s[\\\"temps\\\"]:\\n            self.ax_temp.plot(s[\\\"temps\\\"], color=\\\"#0d9488\\\", label=\\\"temperature\\\")\\n            ax2 = self.ax_temp.twinx()\\n            ax2.plot(s[\\\"surprisals\\\"], color=\\\"#ca8a04\\\", alpha=0.6, label=\\\"surprisal\\\")\\n        self.ax_temp.set_title(\\\"Temperature & surprisal\\\")\\n        self.ax_temp.set_xlabel(\\\"step\\\")\\n\\n        self.canvas.draw_idle()\\n\\n    # ---- persistence: neuron weights + full run binaries -------------------\\n\\n    def load_neurons(self):\\n        path = filedialog.askopenfilename(filetypes=[(\\\"NumPy array\\\", \\\"*.npy\\\")])\\n        if not path:\\n            return\\n        try:\\n            self.population = SpikingPopulation.from_npy(path)\\n            messagebox.showinfo(\\\"Loaded\\\", f\\\"Loaded {self.population.n} neuron weights from {path}\\\")\\n        except Exception as e:\\n            messagebox.showerror(\\\"Load failed\\\", str(e))\\n\\n    def save_neurons(self):\\n        if not self.population:\\n            messagebox.showwarning(\\\"No population\\\", \\\"Run a generation first, or load weights.\\\")\\n            return\\n        path = filedialog.asksaveasfilename(defaultextension=\\\".npy\\\", filetypes=[(\\\"NumPy array\\\", \\\"*.npy\\\")])\\n        if not path:\\n            return\\n        self.population.save_npy(path)\\n        messagebox.showinfo(\\\"Saved\\\", f\\\"Neuron weights saved to {path}\\\")\\n\\n    def save_run(self):\\n        s = self.gen_state\\n        if not s or not s[\\\"temps\\\"]:\\n            messagebox.showwarning(\\\"No run\\\", \\\"Generate something first.\\\")\\n            return\\n        path = filedialog.asksaveasfilename(defaultextension=\\\".npz\\\", filetypes=[(\\\"NumPy zip\\\", \\\"*.npz\\\")])\\n        if not path:\\n            return\\n        np.savez_compressed(\\n            path,\\n            temps=np.array(s[\\\"temps\\\"]), surprisals=np.array(s[\\\"surprisals\\\"]),\\n            spike_log=np.array(s[\\\"spike_log\\\"]), path3d=np.array(s[\\\"path\\\"]),\\n            vocab_size=s[\\\"vocab_size\\\"], context_states=s[\\\"context_states\\\"],\\n        )\\n        messagebox.showinfo(\\\"Saved\\\", f\\\"Run binary saved to {path}\\\")\\n\\n    def load_run(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Load a saved .npz and re-draw the charts from it (no text, no regeneration \\u2014\\n        this is for inspecting saved binary traces, e.g. from the CLI version).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        path = filedialog.askopenfilename(filetypes=[(\\\"NumPy zip\\\", \\\"*.npz\\\")])\\n        if not path:\\n            return\\n        data = np.load(path)\\n        self.gen_state = {\\n            \\\"temps\\\": list(data[\\\"temps\\\"]), \\\"surprisals\\\": list(data[\\\"surprisals\\\"]),\\n            \\\"spike_log\\\": list(data[\\\"spike_log\\\"]), \\\"path\\\": list(data[\\\"path3d\\\"]),\\n            \\\"vocab_size\\\": int(data[\\\"vocab_size\\\"]), \\\"context_states\\\": int(data[\\\"context_states\\\"]),\\n        }\\n        self.output_box.delete(\\\"1.0\\\", \\\"end\\\")\\n        self.output_box.insert(\\\"1.0\\\", \\\"[re-rendered from saved binary \\u2014 no text stored in .npz]\\\")\\n        self._redraw_charts()\\n\\n    def save_chart(self):\\n        path = filedialog.asksaveasfilename(defaultextension=\\\".png\\\", filetypes=[(\\\"PNG image\\\", \\\"*.png\\\")])\\n        if not path:\\n            return\\n        self.fig.savefig(path, dpi=150)\\n        messagebox.showinfo(\\\"Saved\\\", f\\\"Chart saved to {path}\\\")\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    app = HECMApp()\\n    app.mainloop()\\n\", \"filename\": \"/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:00.982209Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:03.428138Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Wiring knapsack functions and menu options into the simulator."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:03.428244Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:19.686777Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Mg6PN6n9E5TY1gPWjoVPBH", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"description": "Add knapsack functions to the GUI file, and update the docstring", "new_str": "\"\"\"\nhecm_gui.py \u2014 Tkinter desktop app for the n-gram generator + spiking-neuron\n              simulation + 3D token trace + live charts + knapsack-driven\n              electrical current.\n\nThis is the same model as hecm_live.py: a trigram Markov generator, a real\nLIF spiking population, a deterministic hash-based 3D position per word, and\nnow a 0/1 knapsack solver (value-density greedy streaming, or exact DP for\nsmall item sets) whose per-step decision is blended into the spiking\npopulation's input current alongside generation surprisal. Wrapped in a\nTkinter window instead of a CLI; charts update live, step by step.\n\nPersistence (File menu):\n  - Load/Save neuron weights        -> .npy\n  - Load a knapsack item dataset     -> .npy (n,2) or 'weight,value' CSV\n  - Save/Load a full run             -> .npz (temps, surprisals, spike\n                                        raster, 3D path, knapsack traces)\n\nThis file is self-contained (does not import hecm_live.py) so it can be run\non its own with just: pip install numpy matplotlib\n\"\"\"\n\nimport hashlib\nimport math\nimport re\nimport tkinter as tk\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom tkinter import ttk, filedialog, messagebox\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use(\"TkAgg\")\nfrom matplotlib.backends.backend_tkagg import FigureCanvasTkAgg\nfrom matplotlib.figure import Figure\nfrom mpl_toolkits.mplot3d import Axes3D  # noqa: F401 (registers 3D projection)\n\nUNK, BOS = \"<unk>\", \"<bos>\"\n\nDEFAULT_CORPUS = (\n    \"the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. the dog barks at the fox. \"\n    \"the fox runs into the forest and the dog follows. in the forest the fox \"\n    \"finds a den and the dog waits outside. the quick fox is clever and the \"\n    \"lazy dog is loyal.\"\n)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Knapsack: dataset loading + solvers (same as hecm_live.py)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef load_items_dataset(path):\n    if path.endswith(\".npy\"):\n        arr = np.load(path)\n    else:\n        arr = np.loadtxt(path, delimiter=\",\")\n    arr = np.atleast_2d(arr)\n    return arr[:, 0].astype(np.float64), arr[:, 1].astype(np.float64)\n\n\ndef synthesize_items(n=40, seed=0):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    weights = rng.integers(1, 50, size=n).astype(np.float64)\n    values = rng.integers(1, 100, size=n).astype(np.float64)\n    return weights, values\n\n\ndef knapsack_dp_exact(weights, values, capacity):\n    \"\"\"Exact 0/1 knapsack via dynamic programming. O(n * capacity).\"\"\"\n    n = len(weights)\n    cap = int(capacity)\n    dp = np.zeros((n + 1, cap + 1))\n    keep = np.zeros((n + 1, cap + 1), dtype=bool)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        w = int(weights[i - 1]); v = values[i - 1]\n        for c in range(cap + 1):\n            if w <= c and dp[i - 1, c - w] + v > dp[i - 1, c]:\n                dp[i, c] = dp[i - 1, c - w] + v\n                keep[i, c] = True\n            else:\n                dp[i, c] = dp[i - 1, c]\n    selected, c = [], cap\n    for i in range(n, 0, -1):\n        if keep[i, c]:\n            selected.append(i - 1)\n            c -= int(weights[i - 1])\n    selected.reverse()\n    return selected, float(dp[n, cap])\n\n\ndef knapsack_stream_greedy(weights, values, capacity):\n    \"\"\"Value-density greedy generator, yielded one item at a time: (idx,\n    density, included, remaining_capacity, running_value). Approximate,\n    handles arbitrarily large item counts.\"\"\"\n    order = np.argsort(-(values / np.maximum(weights, 1e-9)))\n    remaining = float(capacity)\n    running_value = 0.0\n    for idx in order:\n        w, v = float(weights[idx]), float(values[idx])\n        density = v / max(w, 1e-9)\n        included = w <= remaining\n        if included:\n            remaining -= w\n            running_value += v\n        yield int(idx), density, included, remaining, running_value\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Core model \u2014 identical logic to hecm_live.py\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------", "old_str": "\"\"\"\nhecm_gui.py \u2014 Tkinter desktop app for the n-gram generator + spiking-neuron\n              simulation + 3D token trace + live charts.\n\nThis is the same model as hecm_live.py (trigram Markov generator, a real LIF\nspiking population driven by generation surprisal, and a deterministic\nhash-based 3D position per word) wrapped in a Tkinter window instead of a\nCLI. Charts update live, step by step, as text generates. It also supports\nthe same binary persistence as the CLI version:\n\n  - Save/Load neuron weights   -> .npy\n  - Save/Load a full run       -> .npz  (temps, surprisals, spike raster, 3D path)\n\nThis file is self-contained (does not import hecm_live.py) so it can be run\non its own with just: pip install numpy matplotlib\n\"\"\"\n\nimport hashlib\nimport math\nimport re\nimport tkinter as tk\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom tkinter import ttk, filedialog, messagebox\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use(\"TkAgg\")\nfrom matplotlib.backends.backend_tkagg import FigureCanvasTkAgg\nfrom matplotlib.figure import Figure\nfrom mpl_toolkits.mplot3d import Axes3D  # noqa: F401 (registers 3D projection)\n\nUNK, BOS = \"<unk>\", \"<bos>\"\n\nDEFAULT_CORPUS = (\n    \"the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. the dog barks at the fox. \"\n    \"the fox runs into the forest and the dog follows. in the forest the fox \"\n    \"finds a den and the dog waits outside. the quick fox is clever and the \"\n    \"lazy dog is loyal.\"\n)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Core model \u2014 identical logic to hecm_live.py\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py"}, "message": "Add knapsack functions to the GUI file, and update the docstring", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Add knapsack functions to the GUI file, and update the docstring"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:19.938747Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:19.938791Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Mg6PN6n9E5TY1gPWjoVPBH", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:22.009314Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:24.410687Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01UbAJV1BvFLr6vKFfqTC6VF", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"description": "Generalize SpikingPopulation.step to take a combined current, matching hecm_live.py", "new_str": "    def step(self, current):\n        noise = self.rng.normal(0, 0.05, size=self.n)\n        self.V = self.V * self.leak + current * self.weights * self.gain + noise\n        spiked = self.V >= self.threshold\n        self.V[spiked] = 0.0\n        return spiked", "old_str": "    def step(self, surprisal):\n        noise = self.rng.normal(0, 0.05, size=self.n)\n        self.V = self.V * self.leak + surprisal * self.weights * self.gain + noise\n        spiked = self.V >= self.threshold\n        self.V[spiked] = 0.0\n        return spiked", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py"}, "message": "Generalize SpikingPopulation.step to take a combined current, matching hecm_live.py", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Generalize SpikingPopulation.step to take a combined current, matching hecm_live.py"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:24.692215Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:24.692249Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01UbAJV1BvFLr6vKFfqTC6VF", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:28.009864Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:29.418662Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now add a \"Load knapsack dataset\" menu item, a capacity/blend control, and wire the knapsack driver into the generation state and step function \u2014 keeping every existing control (`brain 3D` panel args, spiking/neuron args) untouched:", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:29.418695Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:32.093622Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_014TKuT2m24gE2U5a1oiLM1r", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"description": "Add Load knapsack dataset menu item, keeping every existing menu entry", "new_str": "        filem.add_command(label=\"Load neuron weights (.npy)...\", command=self.load_neurons)\n        filem.add_command(label=\"Save neuron weights (.npy)...\", command=self.save_neurons)\n        filem.add_separator()\n        filem.add_command(label=\"Load knapsack dataset (.npy/.csv)...\", command=self.load_knapsack_dataset)\n        filem.add_separator()\n        filem.add_command(label=\"Save run binary (.npz)...\", command=self.save_run)", "old_str": "        filem.add_command(label=\"Load neuron weights (.npy)...\", command=self.load_neurons)\n        filem.add_command(label=\"Save neuron weights (.npy)...\", command=self.save_neurons)\n        filem.add_separator()\n        filem.add_command(label=\"Save run binary (.npz)...\", command=self.save_run)", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py"}, "message": "Add Load knapsack dataset menu item, keeping every existing menu entry", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Add Load knapsack dataset menu item, keeping every existing menu entry"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:32.340457Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:32.340503Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_014TKuT2m24gE2U5a1oiLM1r", "name": "str_replace", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "edit", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Successfully replaced string in /mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:34.463566Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:42.117023Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01EXoXKNM6Xgf5wGmGxJKSZa", "name": "str_replace", "input": {"description": "Add knapsack capacity/blend spinboxes alongside the existing length/order/neurons/speed row, without removing any existing controls", "new_str": "        self.length_var = tk.IntVar(value=60)\n        self.order_var = tk.IntVar(value=3)\n        self.neurons_var = tk.IntVar(value=24)\n        self.speed_var = tk.IntVar(value=80)\n        self.knap_capacity_var = tk.StringVar(value=\"\")   # blank = auto (40% of total weight)\n        self.knap_blend_var = tk.DoubleVar(value=1.0)\n\n        for i, (label, var, w) in enumerate([\n            (\"length\", self.length_var, 6), (\"order\", self.order_var, 4),\n            (\"neurons\", self.neurons_var, 5), (\"speed(ms)\", self.speed_var, 6),\n        ]):\n            ttk.Label(top, text=label).grid(row=1, column=2 + i * 2, sticky=\"e\", padx=(10, 2), pady=(6, 0))\n            ttk.Spinbox(top, from_=1, to=2000, textvariable=var, width=w).grid(\n                row=1, column=3 + i * 2, sticky=\"w\", pady=(6, 0))\n\n        ttk.Label(top, text=\"knapsack capacity (blank=auto)\").grid(row=2, column=0, sticky=\"w\", pady=(6, 0))\n        ttk.Entry(top, textvariable=self.knap_capacity_var, width=10).grid(\n            row=2, column=1, sticky=\"w\", pady=(6, 0))\n        ttk.Label(top, text=\"knapsack blend\").grid(row=2, column=2, sticky=\"e\", padx=(10, 2), pady=(6, 0))\n        ttk.Spinbox(top, from_=0.0, to=5.0, increment=0.1, textvariable=self.knap_blend_var, width=6).grid(\n            row=2, column=3, sticky=\"w\", pady=(6, 0))\n        self.knap_status_var = tk.StringVar(value=\"knapsack: synthesized dataset (default)\")\n        ttk.Label(top, textvariable=self.knap_status_var, foreground=\"#666\").grid(\n            row=2, column=4, columnspan=6, sticky=\"w\", padx=(10, 0), pady=(6, 0))", "old_str": "        self.length_var = tk.IntVar(value=60)\n        self.order_var = tk.IntVar(value=3)\n        self.neurons_var = tk.IntVar(value=24)\n        self.speed_var = tk.IntVar(value=80)\n\n        for i, (label, var, w) in enumerate([\n            (\"length\", self.length_var, 6), (\"order\", self.order_var, 4),\n            (\"neurons\", self.neurons_var, 5), (\"speed(ms)\", self.speed_var, 6),\n        ]):\n            ttk.Label(top, text=label).grid(row=1, column=2 + i * 2, sticky=\"e\", padx=(10, 2), pady=(6, 0))\n            ttk.Spinbox(top, from_=1, to=2000, textvariable=var, width=w).grid(\n                row=1, column=3 + i * 2, sticky=\"w\", pady=(6, 0))", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/hecm_gui.py"}, "message": "Add knapsack capacity/blend spinboxes alongside the existing length/order/neurons/speed row, without removing any existing controls", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "edit", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Add knapsack capacity/blend spinboxes alongside the existing length/order/neurons/speed row, without removing any existing controls"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-27T22:13:42.419816Z", "st