NP12kuhS", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/word_values_linkcopies.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/word_values_linkcopies.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-30T08:45:02.080311Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-30T08:45:02.080349Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01C73btMtfPUcV3hNP12kuhS", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/word_values_linkcopies.py", "name": "word values linkcopies", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-30T08:45:09.008110Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-30T08:45:10.639130Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I applied the duplicated vocabulary and linkwise partition to this program, as `word_values_linkcopies.py`. It is your file with the lift added, and I left the logic mask, value unfolding and streaming as they were. I ran it on the synthetic corpus with copies set to 1, 2 and 3.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Duplicated vocabulary:** `--copies N` (default 2, `1` means off) gives every word N identities, written \"moon\", \"moon#1\" and so on. The tokenizer can never produce `#`, so the tags cannot clash with real text.\n- **Linkwise partition:** each distinct word-pair link gets a class from a stable hash, set by `--link-seed`. Crossing a link of class *c* moves the running copy forward by *c* (mod N).\n- **What sees the copies:** the trigram table, the word graph, the learned roles and the mask's role statistics all treat the copies as separate words.\n- **What sees the surface word:** spelling and bytes, punctuation, printing and capitalization, and the loop rule R4 all use the surface word.\n- **Byte states:** all copies of a word share the same byte states, so the byte graph ties the copies together.\n- **Prompt handling:** a prompt's links fix its copy differences, and `lift_prompt` tries every offset and picks the ones the trigram table knows.\n- **Values:** a value on a prompt word goes to every copy of it.\n- **Report:** `[partition] {...}` on stderr shows the class split and the two checks.\n\n**Results** (from the synthetic corpus and the test script, not from your own data)\n- **Copies=1:** the lifted tokens are identical to the plain tokens, so the program is unchanged.\n- **Copies=2 and 3:** projecting the trigram counts back to surface words gives exactly the plain counts, so nothing is lost.\n- **Dataset split (copies=2):** 41 and 37 distinct links per class, 5,124 and 6,854 occurrences.\n- **Vocabulary and contexts:** the vocabulary goes from 33 to 66 and 99, and trigram contexts from 78 to 156 and 234.\n- **Byte states:** the count is unchanged.\n- **Value spreading:** with \"moon\" valued 3.0 on both its copies, the top results were moon (3.37) and moon#1 (3.36), then moonlight#1, moons, moons#1, on and on#1.\n- **Generation:** it produced well-formed sentences at every copy count.\n\n**Caveats**\n- **Traceback at the end of my runs:** this is your interactive loop hitting the end of the piped input. It was not caused by the change.\n- **Thinner data per context:** each context now has less data, because the same words are split across copies. In this corpus a few sentences drifted (\"under the stars shone over\u2026\") at copies=2 and 3.\n- **The \"on\" values:** \"on\" gets value from \"moon\" through the shared byte states. That is the spelling effect, unrelated to the copies.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-09-30T08:45:10.722704Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-30T08:45:10.722704Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0f17b-94be-7ae9-ad11-a26e0fbc6e8a"}, {"uuid": "01a0f19d-bbdd-7481-a139-99b6bd80776f", "text": "make sure each copy does an nphard problem on each other with one set reversed, to make it easier", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:20:49.574284Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:20:49.574284Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "make sure each copy does an nphard problem on each other with one set reversed, to make it easier", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-09-30T09:20:49.574510Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-30T09:20:49.574510Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0f17b-94be-75ee-96fb-a15f8fdab376"}, {"uuid": "01a0f19d-bbde-7b4b-ba5e-3a9d1c8bb38f", "text": "I'm reading this as the classic meet-in-the-middle trick for 0/1 knapsack: the two copies are the two halves, and one is sorted in reverse so a two-pointer sweep matches them. The solver will pick a word agenda that the stream then tries to cover.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI've added the copy-versus-copy problem as `word_values_agenda.py`, on top of the duplicated vocabulary. I picked 0/1 knapsack solved by meet in the middle, because that is the standard case where one set is sorted in reverse to make an NP-hard problem easier. If you meant a different problem (travelling salesman, subset sum, something else), say so. The solver is small and easy to swap.\n\n**The problem**\nFrom the most valuable words, choose the set with the largest total value whose spelling fits a character budget, like one sentence's worth.\n\n**How the copies work on each other**\n- **The two halves:** the candidate words split by which copy they live in. A word lives in the copy where the linkwise partition put most of its occurrences. Even copies form half A and odd copies form half B.\n- **The reversal:** half A is sorted ascending and half B is sorted descending. As A's weight grows, the room left for B only shrinks, so one two-pointer sweep pairs every subset of A with the best subset of B that still fits.\n- **The saving:** this turns 2\u207f subsets into 2\u00b72^(n/2). With one copy, the halves alternate by rank instead.\n- **Use:** the winning set is the sentence agenda. Agenda words get a bonus the first time each sentence, and the agenda refreshes at each sentence end.\n- **New flags:**\n  - `--agenda-pool`\n  - `--agenda-chars`\n  - `--agenda-bonus`\n  - `--no-agenda`\n  - `--check-solver`\n\n**Tests** (run on the synthetic corpus and on random instances)\n- **Correctness:** on 400 random knapsack instances, including empty halves and tiny budgets, the meet-in-the-middle answer matched brute force every time.\n- **Speed at n=20:** 1,048,576 subsets and 30 ms for brute force, versus 2,048 subsets and 1 ms for meet in the middle.\n- **Speed at n=40:** brute force would need about 1.1 trillion subsets, and meet in the middle took 2,097,152 subsets and 853 ms.\n- **Inside the program (18 candidates, halves of 9 and 9):** it examined 1,024 subsets where brute force would examine 262,144, and `--check-solver` confirmed the agenda matches brute force.\n\n**What I could not show**\n- **Little effect on the text:** the agenda bonus has a weak, noisy effect on the stream. With the prompt \"moon\" and bonus 0, 0.5 and 1.5, the distinct agenda words per sentence came out at 1.23, 1.15 and 1.39.\n- **Why:** the value term in your sampler is large (about 90 logits for \"moon\"), and the trigram table only allows a few continuations. My first version of the bonus had a fixed size and did nothing, so I now scale it by the spread of the candidates' scores.\n- **Function words in the agenda:** with the prompt \"the moon\", short function words like \"we\", \"a\" and \"on\" end up in the agenda, because they are cheap in characters.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:20:49.567339Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:21:50.622953Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Puzzling out an oddly worded request about paired hard problems."}, {"summary": "Mapping the reversed-set trick onto a meet-in-the-middle search."}, {"summary": "Designing a subset-sum split for a meet-in-the-middle solution."}, {"summary": "Reframing the puzzle as a knapsack solved by meet-in-the-middle."}, {"summary": "Untangling duplicate words across copies to keep halves disjoint."}, {"summary": "Implementing the two-pointer scan with suffix-best value tracking."}, {"summary": "Adding word-choice bonuses to steer generated sentences toward agenda terms."}, {"summary": "Assigning agenda word values and weights for the knapsack model."}, {"summary": "Verifying the two-pointer scan's monotonic correctness with brute force."}, {"summary": "Wiring agenda-driven word bonuses into the streaming generator."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:21:50.623037Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:21:51.466819Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I'm reading this as the classic meet-in-the-middle trick for 0/1 knapsack: the two copies are the two halves, and one is sorted in reverse so a two-pointer sweep matches them. The solver will pick a word agenda that the stream then tries to cover.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:21:51.466829Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:22:12.381860Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01C1fzGKSZvyKzEad7d4Y8FN", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && cat > /tmp/patch3.py << 'PYEOF'\ns = open(\"/mnt/user-data/outputs/word_values_linkcopies.py\").read()\ndef rep(a, b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, a[:60]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\n\n# ---- docstring\nrep('''  the prompt) uses the surface word. --copies 1 is the program without this.\n\"\"\"''', '''  the prompt) uses the surface word. --copies 1 is the program without this.\n\nNEW  the copies solve an NP-hard problem on each other   (agenda)\n  Problem: 0/1 KNAPSACK. From the most valuable words, choose the set with the\n  largest total value whose spelling fits a character budget (one sentence).\n  Brute force is 2^n subsets. Meet in the middle (Horowitz-Sahni) makes it\n  2 * 2^(n/2):\n      half A  = candidate words that live in the even copies   (sorted ascending)\n      half B  = candidate words that live in the odd copies    (sorted REVERSED,\n                descending), so that one two-pointer sweep pairs every subset\n                of A with the best subset of B that still fits.\n  A word lives in the copy where the linkwise partition put most of its\n  occurrences. The winning set is the sentence AGENDA: words the stream gets a\n  bonus for saying (once each per sentence). --check-solver proves the answer\n  against brute force.\n\"\"\"''')\n\n# ---- solver\nrep('''# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef normalize_rows(M):''', '''# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# NP-hard problem between the copies: knapsack by meet in the middle\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef subset_table(items):\n    \"\"\"All 2^n subsets of [(weight, value), ...] as arrays (W, V, bitmask).\"\"\"\n    W = np.zeros(1, dtype=np.int64)\n    V = np.zeros(1)\n    M = np.zeros(1, dtype=np.int64)\n    for i, (w, v) in enumerate(items):\n        W = np.concatenate([W, W + w])\n        V = np.concatenate([V, V + v])\n        M = np.concatenate([M, M | (1 << i)])\n    return W, V, M\n\n\ndef knapsack_mitm(set_a, set_b, budget):\n    \"\"\"Best total value with total weight <= budget, choosing from both sets.\n    A is scanned ascending, B REVERSED (descending): as A's weight grows the\n    room left for B only shrinks, so one pointer into B moves forward once and\n    a suffix maximum answers \"best B-subset that still fits\".\"\"\"\n    WA, VA, MA = subset_table(set_a)\n    WB, VB, MB = subset_table(set_b)\n    oa = np.argsort(WA, kind=\"stable\")                   # A ascending\n    ob = np.argsort(-WB, kind=\"stable\")                  # B reversed\n    WA, VA, MA = WA[oa], VA[oa], MA[oa]\n    WB, VB, MB = WB[ob], VB[ob], MB[ob]\n\n    nb = len(WB)\n    sufv = np.empty(nb)\n    sufi = np.empty(nb, dtype=np.int64)\n    best_v, best_i = -1.0, -1\n    for j in range(nb - 1, -1, -1):\n        if VB[j] > best_v:\n            best_v, best_i = VB[j], j\n        sufv[j], sufi[j] = best_v, best_i\n\n    best = (-1.0, 0, 0)\n    j = 0\n    for a in range(len(WA)):\n        room = budget - WA[a]\n        if room < 0:\n            break                                        # nothing later in A fits either\n        while j < nb and WB[j] > room:\n            j += 1                                       # pointer only moves forward\n        if j == nb:\n            break\n        total = VA[a] + sufv[j]\n        if total > best[0]:\n            best = (total, int(MA[a]), int(MB[sufi[j]]))\n    return best[0], best[1], best[2], len(WA) + len(WB)\n\n\ndef knapsack_brute(items, budget):\n    W, V, _ = subset_table(items)\n    return float(V[W <= budget].max())\n\n\ndef solve_agenda(vf, lcounts, copies, pool=18, budget=30, check=False):\n    \"\"\"Candidates = the `pool` most valuable surface words (value taken at the\n    word's home copy). Even-copy words form half A, odd-copy words half B\n    (with one copy, halves alternate by rank).\"\"\"\n    by_surface = defaultdict(list)\n    for t in vf.vocab:\n        if re.fullmatch(r\"[\\\\w']+\", surf(t)):\n            by_surface[surf(t)].append(t)\n    cand = []\n    for word, toks in by_surface.items():\n        home = max(toks, key=lambda t: (lcounts[t], -copy_of(t)))\n        cand.append((word, home, float(vf.field[vf.idx[home]])))\n    cand = [c for c in sorted(cand, key=lambda c: -c[2])[:pool] if c[2] > 1e-6]\n\n    halves = ([], [])\n    for rank, (word, home, val) in enumerate(cand):\n        h = copy_of(home) % 2 if copies >= 2 else rank % 2\n        halves[h].append((word, len(word) + 1, val))\n    va, vb, ops = knapsack_mitm([(w, v) for _, w, v in halves[0]],\n                                [(w, v) for _, w, v in halves[1]], budget)[0], None, None\n    value, ma, mb, ops = knapsack_mitm([(w, v) for _, w, v in halves[0]],\n                                       [(w, v) for _, w, v in halves[1]], budget)\n    words = [halves[0][i][0] for i in range(len(halves[0])) if ma >> i & 1] + \\\\\n            [halves[1][i][0] for i in range(len(halves[1])) if mb >> i & 1]\n    chars = sum(len(w) + 1 for w in words)\n    report = {\"candidates\": len(cand), \"half_A\": len(halves[0]), \"half_B\": len(halves[1]),\n              \"agenda\": words, \"chars\": chars, \"budget\": budget, \"value\": round(value, 3),\n              \"subsets_examined\": ops, \"brute_force_would_examine\": 2 ** len(cand)}\n    if check and len(cand) <= 22:\n        brute = knapsack_brute([(len(w) + 1, v) for w, _, v in cand], budget)\n        report[\"matches_brute_force\"] = bool(abs(brute - max(value, 0.0)) < 1e-9)\n    return words, report\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef normalize_rows(M):''')\n\n# ---- _pick with agenda bonus\nrep('''def _pick(vf, table, beta, rng, mask=None, sent=(), gamma=1.0):\n    words = list(table)\n    p = np.array([table[w] for w in words], dtype=np.float64)\n    logits = np.log(p / p.sum()) + beta * np.exp(vf.field[[vf.idx[w] for w in words]])\n    if mask is not None:\n        logits = logits + gamma * mask.bias(list(sent), words)''', '''def _pick(vf, table, beta, rng, mask=None, sent=(), gamma=1.0, favor=(), bonus=0.0):\n    words = list(table)\n    p = np.array([table[w] for w in words], dtype=np.float64)\n    logits = np.log(p / p.sum()) + beta * np.exp(vf.field[[vf.idx[w] for w in words]])\n    if mask is not None:\n        logits = logits + gamma * mask.bias(list(sent), words)\n    if bonus and favor:                                   # the knapsack agenda\n        logits = logits + bonus * np.array([surf(w) in favor for w in words], dtype=np.float64)''')\n\nrep('''def stream_tokens(vf, tg, beta=3.0, rng=None, ctx=None, mask=None, gamma=1.0, trace=False):''',\n    '''def stream_tokens(vf, tg, beta=3.0, rng=None, ctx=None, mask=None, gamma=1.0, trace=False,\n                  agenda=(), bonus=0.0):''')\nrep('''    sent = list(ctx)                         # words of the current sentence\n    while True:''', '''    sent = list(ctx)                         # words of the current sentence\n    pending = set(agenda) - {surf(x) for x in sent}      # agenda words still to say\n    while True:''')\nrep('''        w = _pick(vf, table, beta, rng, mask, sent, gamma)''',\n    '''        w = _pick(vf, table, beta, rng, mask, sent, gamma, pending, bonus)''')\nrep('''        yield w\n        if surf(w) in SENTENCE_END:\n            ctx, sent = [], []\n        else:''', '''        yield w\n        pending.discard(surf(w))\n        if surf(w) in SENTENCE_END:\n            ctx, sent = [], []\n            pending = set(agenda)                         # a new sentence, a fresh agenda\n        else:''')\n\n# ---- CLI\nrep('''    gen_seed = int(np.random.SeedSequence().entropy % 2**32)\n''', '''    ap.add_argument(\"--agenda-pool\", type=int, default=18, help=\"candidate words for the knapsack\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--agenda-chars\", type=int, default=30, help=\"character budget per sentence\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--agenda-bonus\", type=float, default=2.0, help=\"logit bonus for agenda words\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--no-agenda\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"skip the knapsack\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--check-solver\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"verify the solver against brute force\")\n    gen_seed = int(np.random.SeedSequence().entropy % 2**32)\n''')\nrep('''    lifted_set = set(lifted)\n''', '''    lifted_set = set(lifted)\n    lcounts = Counter(lifted)\n''')\nrep('''        # logic mask: learned after all the math, gates the sampler''', '''        # the copies solve knapsack on each other -> sentence agenda\n        agenda = []\n        if not args.no_agenda:\n            agenda, rep_ = solve_agenda(vf, lcounts, copies, args.agenda_pool,\n                                        args.agenda_chars, args.check_solver)\n            print(f\"[agenda] {rep_}\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n        # logic mask: learned after all the math, gates the sampler''')\nrep('''                             mask=mask, gamma=args.gamma, trace=args.trace)''',\n    '''                             mask=mask, gamma=args.gamma, trace=args.trace,\n                             agenda=agenda, bonus=args.agenda_bonus)''')\nopen(\"/mnt/user-data/outputs/word_values_agenda.py\", \"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"written\")\nPYEOF\npython3 /tmp/patch3.py && python3 -c \"import ast;ast.parse(open('/mnt/user-data/outputs/word_values_agenda.py').read());print('syntax ok')\""}, "message": "Running command", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && cat > /tmp/patch3.py << 'PYEOF'\\ns = open(\\\"/mnt/user-data/outputs/word_values_linkcopies.py\\\").read()\\ndef rep(a, b):\\n    global s\\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, a[:60]\\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\\n\\n# ---- docstring\\nrep('''  the prompt) uses the surface word. --copies 1 is the program without this.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"''', '''  the prompt) uses the surface word. --copies 1 is the program without this.\\n\\nNEW  the copies solve an NP-hard problem on each other   (agenda)\\n  Problem: 0/1 KNAPSACK. From the most valuable words, choose the set with the\\n  largest total value whose spelling fits a character budget (one sentence).\\n  Brute force is 2^n subsets. Meet in the middle (Horowitz-Sahni) makes it\\n  2 * 2^(n/2):\\n      half A  = candidate words that live in the even copies   (sorted ascending)\\n      half B  = candidate words that live in the odd copies    (sorted REVERSED,\\n                descending), so that one two-pointer sweep pairs every subset\\n                of A with the best subset of B that still fits.\\n  A word lives in the copy where the linkwise partition put most of its\\n  occurrences. The winning set is the sentence AGENDA: words the stream gets a\\n  bonus for saying (once each per sentence). --check-solver proves the answer\\n  against brute force.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"''')\\n\\n# ---- solver\\nrep('''# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef normalize_rows(M):''', '''# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# NP-hard problem between the copies: knapsack by meet in the middle\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef subset_table(items):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"All 2^n subsets of [(weight, value), ...] as arrays (W, V, bitmask).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    W = np.zeros(1, dtype=np.int64)\\n    V = np.zeros(1)\\n    M = np.zeros(1, dtype=np.int64)\\n    for i, (w, v) in enumerate(items):\\n        W = np.concatenate([W, W + w])\\n        V = np.concatenate([V, V + v])\\n        M = np.concatenate([M, M | (1 << i)])\\n    return W, V, M\\n\\n\\ndef knapsack_mitm(set_a, set_b, budget):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Best total value with total weight <= budget, choosing from both sets.\\n    A is scanned ascending, B REVERSED (descending): as A's weight grows the\\n    room left for B only shrinks, so one pointer into B moves forward once and\\n    a suffix maximum answers \\\"best B-subset that still fits\\\".\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    WA, VA, MA = subset_table(set_a)\\n    WB, VB, MB = subset_table(set_b)\\n    oa = np.argsort(WA, kind=\\\"stable\\\")                   # A ascending\\n    ob = np.argsort(-WB, kind=\\\"stable\\\")                  # B reversed\\n    WA, VA, MA = WA[oa], VA[oa], MA[oa]\\n    WB, VB, MB = WB[ob], VB[ob], MB[ob]\\n\\n    nb = len(WB)\\n    sufv = np.empty(nb)\\n    sufi = np.empty(nb, dtype=np.int64)\\n    best_v, best_i = -1.0, -1\\n    for j in range(nb - 1, -1, -1):\\n        if VB[j] > best_v:\\n            best_v, best_i = VB[j], j\\n        sufv[j], sufi[j] = best_v, best_i\\n\\n    best = (-1.0, 0, 0)\\n    j = 0\\n    for a in range(len(WA)):\\n        room = budget - WA[a]\\n        if room < 0:\\n            break                                        # nothing later in A fits either\\n        while j < nb and WB[j] > room:\\n            j += 1                                       # pointer only moves forward\\n        if j == nb:\\n            break\\n        total = VA[a] + sufv[j]\\n        if total > best[0]:\\n            best = (total, int(MA[a]), int(MB[sufi[j]]))\\n    return best[0], best[1], best[2], len(WA) + len(WB)\\n\\n\\ndef knapsack_brute(items, budget):\\n    W, V, _ = subset_table(items)\\n    return float(V[W <= budget].max())\\n\\n\\ndef solve_agenda(vf, lcounts, copies, pool=18, budget=30, check=False):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Candidates = the `pool` most valuable surface words (value taken at the\\n    word's home copy). Even-copy words form half A, odd-copy words half B\\n    (with one copy, halves alternate by rank).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    by_surface = defaultdict(list)\\n    for t in vf.vocab:\\n        if re.fullmatch(r\\\"[\\\\\\\\w']+\\\", surf(t)):\\n            by_surface[surf(t)].append(t)\\n    cand = []\\n    for word, toks in by_surface.items():\\n        home = max(toks, key=lambda t: (lcounts[t], -copy_of(t)))\\n        cand.append((word, home, float(vf.field[vf.idx[home]])))\\n    cand = [c for c in sorted(cand, key=lambda c: -c[2])[:pool] if c[2] > 1e-6]\\n\\n    halves = ([], [])\\n    for rank, (word, home, val) in enumerate(cand):\\n        h = copy_of(home) % 2 if copies >= 2 else rank % 2\\n        halves[h].append((word, len(word) + 1, val))\\n    va, vb, ops = knapsack_mitm([(w, v) for _, w, v in halves[0]],\\n                                [(w, v) for _, w, v in halves[1]], budget)[0], None, None\\n    value, ma, mb, ops = knapsack_mitm([(w, v) for _, w, v in halves[0]],\\n                                       [(w, v) for _, w, v in halves[1]], budget)\\n    words = [halves[0][i][0] for i in range(len(halves[0])) if ma >> i & 1] + \\\\\\\\\\n            [halves[1][i][0] for i in range(len(halves[1])) if mb >> i & 1]\\n    chars = sum(len(w) + 1 for w in words)\\n    report = {\\\"candidates\\\": len(cand), \\\"half_A\\\": len(halves[0]), \\\"half_B\\\": len(halves[1]),\\n              \\\"agenda\\\": words, \\\"chars\\\": chars, \\\"budget\\\": budget, \\\"value\\\": round(value, 3),\\n              \\\"subsets_examined\\\": ops, \\\"brute_force_would_examine\\\": 2 ** len(cand)}\\n    if check and len(cand) <= 22:\\n        brute = knapsack_brute([(len(w) + 1, v) for w, _, v in cand], budget)\\n        report[\\\"matches_brute_force\\\"] = bool(abs(brute - max(value, 0.0)) < 1e-9)\\n    return words, report\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef normalize_rows(M):''')\\n\\n# ---- _pick with agenda bonus\\nrep('''def _pick(vf, table, beta, rng, mask=None, sent=(), gamma=1.0):\\n    words = list(table)\\n    p = np.array([table[w] for w in words], dtype=np.float64)\\n    logits = np.log(p / p.sum()) + beta * np.exp(vf.field[[vf.idx[w] for w in words]])\\n    if mask is not None:\\n        logits = logits + gamma * mask.bias(list(sent), words)''', '''def _pick(vf, table, beta, rng, mask=None, sent=(), gamma=1.0, favor=(), bonus=0.0):\\n    words = list(table)\\n    p = np.array([table[w] for w in words], dtype=np.float64)\\n    logits = np.log(p / p.sum()) + beta * np.exp(vf.field[[vf.idx[w] for w in words]])\\n    if mask is not None:\\n        logits = logits + gamma * mask.bias(list(sent), words)\\n    if bonus and favor:                                   # the knapsack agenda\\n        logits = logits + bonus * np.array([surf(w) in favor for w in words], dtype=np.float64)''')\\n\\nrep('''def stream_tokens(vf, tg, beta=3.0, rng=None, ctx=None, mask=None, gamma=1.0, trace=False):''',\\n    '''def stream_tokens(vf, tg, beta=3.0, rng=None, ctx=None, mask=None, gamma=1.0, trace=False,\\n                  agenda=(), bonus=0.0):''')\\nrep('''    sent = list(ctx)                         # words of the current sentence\\n    while True:''', '''    sent = list(ctx)                         # words of the current sentence\\n    pending = set(agenda) - {surf(x) for x in sent}      # agenda words still to say\\n    while True:''')\\nrep('''        w = _pick(vf, table, beta, rng, mask, sent, gamma)''',\\n    '''        w = _pick(vf, table, beta, rng, mask, sent, gamma, pending, bonus)''')\\nrep('''        yield w\\n        if surf(w) in SENTENCE_END:\\n            ctx, sent = [], []\\n        else:''', '''        yield w\\n        pending.discard(surf(w))\\n        if surf(w) in SENTENCE_END:\\n            ctx, sent = [], []\\n            pending = set(agenda)                         # a new sentence, a fresh agenda\\n        else:''')\\n\\n# ---- CLI\\nrep('''    gen_seed = int(np.random.SeedSequence().entropy % 2**32)\\n''', '''    ap.add_argument(\\\"--agenda-pool\\\", type=int, default=18, help=\\\"candidate words for the knapsack\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--agenda-chars\\\", type=int, default=30, help=\\\"character budget per sentence\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--agenda-bonus\\\", type=float, default=2.0, help=\\\"logit bonus for agenda words\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--no-agenda\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"skip the knapsack\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--check-solver\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"verify the solver against brute force\\\")\\n    gen_seed = int(np.random.SeedSequence().entropy % 2**32)\\n''')\\nrep('''    lifted_set = set(lifted)\\n''', '''    lifted_set = set(lifted)\\n    lcounts = Counter(lifted)\\n''')\\nrep('''        # logic mask: learned after all the math, gates the sampler''', '''        # the copies solve knapsack on each other -> sentence agenda\\n        agenda = []\\n        if not args.no_agenda:\\n            agenda, rep_ = solve_agenda(vf, lcounts, copies, args.agenda_pool,\\n                                        args.agenda_chars, args.check_solver)\\n            print(f\\\"[agenda] {rep_}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n        # logic mask: learned after all the math, gates the sampler''')\\nrep('''                             mask=mask, gamma=args.gamma, trace=args.trace)''',\\n    '''                             mask=mask, gamma=args.gamma, trace=args.trace,\\n                             agenda=agenda, bonus=args.agenda_bonus)''')\\nopen(\\\"/mnt/user-data/outputs/word_values_agenda.py\\\", \\\"w\\\").write(s)\\nprint(\\\"written\\\")\\nPYEOF\\npython3 /tmp/patch3.py && python3 -c \\\"import ast;ast.parse(open('/mnt/user-data/outputs/word_values_agenda.py').read());print('syntax ok')\\\"\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:22:14.009781Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:22:14.009814Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01C1fzGKSZvyKzEad7d4Y8FN", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"written\\nsyntax ok\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"written\\nsyntax ok\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:22:17.412567Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:22:23.718304Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01BDuDsQFEZmm4BNaGqiJ1GV", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - << 'EOF'\np=\"word_values_agenda.py\"\ns=open(p).read()\na='''    va, vb, ops = knapsack_mitm([(w, v) for _, w, v in halves[0]],\n                                [(w, v) for _, w, v in halves[1]], budget)[0], None, None\n'''\nassert s.count(a)==1\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s.replace(a,\"\"))\nEOF\ncat > /tmp/test_knap.py << 'EOF'\nimport importlib.util, random, time, re\nimport numpy as np\nspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"m\", \"/mnt/user-data/outputs/word_values_agenda.py\")\nm = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec); spec.loader.exec_module(m)\n\n# 1. MITM == brute force on random instances (incl. empty halves, tiny budgets)\nrandom.seed(0); bad = 0; N = 400\nfor _ in range(N):\n    n = random.randint(0, 14); items = [(random.randint(2, 12), random.random()*5) for _ in range(n)]\n    k = random.randint(0, n); A, B = items[:k], items[k:]\n    budget = random.randint(0, 60)\n    v, ma, mb, _ = m.knapsack_mitm(A, B, budget)\n    brute = m.knapsack_brute(items, budget) if items else 0.0\n    got = max(v, 0.0)\n    # the returned masks must reproduce the value and respect the budget\n    w = sum(A[i][0] for i in range(len(A)) if ma >> i & 1) + sum(B[i][0] for i in range(len(B)) if mb >> i & 1)\n    val = sum(A[i][1] for i in range(len(A)) if ma >> i & 1) + sum(B[i][1] for i in range(len(B)) if mb >> i & 1)\n    if abs(got - brute) > 1e-9 or w > budget or (v >= 0 and abs(val - v) > 1e-9): bad += 1\nprint(f\"MITM vs brute force on {N} random instances: {N-bad} agree, {bad} differ\")\n\n# 2. cost: n=20 items\nitems = [(random.randint(3, 12), random.random()*5) for _ in range(20)]\nt = time.time(); b = m.knapsack_brute(items, 60); tb = time.time()-t\nt = time.time(); v, _, _, ops = m.knapsack_mitm(items[:10], items[10:], 60); tm = time.time()-t\nprint(f\"n=20: brute force {2**20:,} subsets {tb*1000:.0f} ms | meet in the middle {ops:,} subsets {tm*1000:.0f} ms | same optimum: {abs(b-v)<1e-9}\")\nitems = [(random.randint(3, 12), random.random()*5) for _ in range(40)]\nt = time.time(); v, _, _, ops = m.knapsack_mitm(items[:20], items[20:], 120); tm = time.time()-t\nprint(f\"n=40: brute force would need {2**40:,} subsets | meet in the middle {ops:,} subsets {tm*1000:.0f} ms\")\nEOF\npython3 /tmp/test_knap.py 2>&1 | cut -c1-220"}, "message": "Running command", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - << 'EOF'\\np=\\\"word_values_agenda.py\\\"\\ns=open(p).read()\\na='''    va, vb, ops = knapsack_mitm([(w, v) for _, w, v in halves[0]],\\n                                [(w, v) for _, w, v in halves[1]], budget)[0], None, None\\n'''\\nassert s.count(a)==1\\nopen(p,\\\"w\\\").write(s.replace(a,\\\"\\\"))\\nEOF\\ncat > /tmp/test_knap.py << 'EOF'\\nimport importlib.util, random, time, re\\nimport numpy as np\\nspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\\\"m\\\", \\\"/mnt/user-data/outputs/word_values_agenda.py\\\")\\nm = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec); spec.loader.exec_module(m)\\n\\n# 1. MITM == brute force on random instances (incl. empty halves, tiny budgets)\\nrandom.seed(0); bad = 0; N = 400\\nfor _ in range(N):\\n    n = random.randint(0, 14); items = [(random.randint(2, 12), random.random()*5) for _ in range(n)]\\n    k = random.randint(0, n); A, B = items[:k], items[k:]\\n    budget = random.randint(0, 60)\\n    v, ma, mb, _ = m.knapsack_mitm(A, B, budget)\\n    brute = m.knapsack_brute(items, budget) if items else 0.0\\n    got = max(v, 0.0)\\n    # the returned masks must reproduce the value and respect the budget\\n    w = sum(A[i][0] for i in range(len(A)) if ma >> i & 1) + sum(B[i][0] for i in range(len(B)) if mb >> i & 1)\\n    val = sum(A[i][1] for i in range(len(A)) if ma >> i & 1) + sum(B[i][1] for i in range(len(B)) if mb >> i & 1)\\n    if abs(got - brute) > 1e-9 or w > budget or (v >= 0 and abs(val - v) > 1e-9): bad += 1\\nprint(f\\\"MITM vs brute force on {N} random instances: {N-bad} agree, {bad} differ\\\")\\n\\n# 2. cost: n=20 items\\nitems = [(random.randint(3, 12), random.random()*5) for _ in range(20)]\\nt = time.time(); b = m.knapsack_brute(items, 60); tb = time.time()-t\\nt = time.time(); v, _, _, ops = m.knapsack_mitm(items[:10], items[10:], 60); tm = time.time()-t\\nprint(f\\\"n=20: brute force {2**20:,} subsets {tb*1000:.0f} ms | meet in the middle {ops:,} subsets {tm*1000:.0f} ms | same optimum: {abs(b-v)<1e-9}\\\")\\nitems = [(random.randint(3, 12), random.random()*5) for _ in range(40)]\\nt = time.time(); v, _, _, ops = m.knapsack_mitm(items[:20], items[20:], 120); tm = time.time()-t\\nprint(f\\\"n=40: brute force would need {2**40:,} subsets | meet in the middle {ops:,} subsets {tm*1000:.0f} ms\\\")\\nEOF\\npython3 /tmp/test_knap.py 2>&1 | cut -c1-220\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:22:25.446689Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:22:25.446728Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01BDuDsQFEZmm4BNaGqiJ1GV", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"MITM vs brute force on 400 random instances: 400 agree, 0 differ\\nn=20: brute force 1,048,576 subsets 30 ms | meet in the middle 2,048 subsets 1 ms | same optimum: True\\nn=40: brute force would need 1,099,511,627,776 subsets | meet in the middle 2,097,152 subsets 853 ms\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"MITM vs brute force on 400 random instances: 400 agree, 0 differ\\nn=20: brute force 1,048,576 subsets 30 ms | meet in the middle 2,048 subsets 1 ms | same optimum: True\\nn=40: brute force would need 1,099,511,627,776 subsets | meet in the middle 2,097,152 subsets 853 ms\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:22:27.670735Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:22:30.012728Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Solving a subset-sum problem using meet-in-the-middle search."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:22:30.012792Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:22:33.885572Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_012KZSELZ266RS4ZiYvGog9P", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && printf 'the moon\\n' | python3 word_values_agenda.py --data /tmp/corpus2.txt --copies 2 --words 30 --delay 0 --check-solver 2>&1 | grep -E \"^\\[agenda\\]|^USER\" | cut -c1-420\necho; echo \"=== copies=1 (halves alternate by rank)\"; printf 'the moon\\n' | python3 word_values_agenda.py --data /tmp/corpus2.txt --copies 1 --words 20 --delay 0 --check-solver 2>&1 | grep -E \"^\\[agenda\\]\" | cut -c1-420\ncat > /tmp/cover.py << 'EOF'\nimport subprocess, re, ast, statistics\ndef run(bonus, seed_reps=6, copies=2):\n    res=[]\n    for _ in range(seed_reps):\n        p=subprocess.run([\"python3\",\"/mnt/user-data/outputs/word_values_agenda.py\",\"--data\",\"/tmp/corpus2.txt\",\"--copies\",str(copies),\n            \"--words\",\"200\",\"--delay\",\"0\",\"--agenda-bonus\",str(bonus)],input=\"the moon\\n\",capture_output=True,text=True)\n        ag=ast.literal_eval(re.search(r\"'agenda': (\\[[^\\]]*\\])\",p.stderr).group(1))\n        out=p.stdout.split(\"USER:\",1)[-1]\n        sents=[s for s in re.split(r\"[.!?]\",out) if s.strip()]\n        res.append(statistics.mean(sum(1 for w in re.findall(r\"[\\w']+\",s.lower()) if w in ag) for s in sents))\n    return ag, statistics.mean(res)\nfor b in (0.0, 2.0, 4.0):\n    ag, c = run(b)\n    print(f\"agenda bonus {b}: mean agenda words per sentence {c:.2f}   (agenda: {ag})\")\nEOF\necho; python3 /tmp/cover.py 2>&1 | cut -c1-200"}, "message": "Running command", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && printf 'the moon\\\\n' | python3 word_values_agenda.py --data /tmp/corpus2.txt --copies 2 --words 30 --delay 0 --check-solver 2>&1 | grep -E \\\"^\\\\[agenda\\\\]|^USER\\\" | cut -c1-420\\necho; echo \\\"=== copies=1 (halves alternate by rank)\\\"; printf 'the moon\\\\n' | python3 word_values_agenda.py --data /tmp/corpus2.txt --copies 1 --words 20 --delay 0 --check-solver 2>&1 | grep -E \\\"^\\\\[agenda\\\\]\\\" | cut -c1-420\\ncat > /tmp/cover.py << 'EOF'\\nimport subprocess, re, ast, statistics\\ndef run(bonus, seed_reps=6, copies=2):\\n    res=[]\\n    for _ in range(seed_reps):\\n        p=subprocess.run([\\\"python3\\\",\\\"/mnt/user-data/outputs/word_values_agenda.py\\\",\\\"--data\\\",\\\"/tmp/corpus2.txt\\\",\\\"--copies\\\",str(copies),\\n            \\\"--words\\\",\\\"200\\\",\\\"--delay\\\",\\\"0\\\",\\\"--agenda-bonus\\\",str(bonus)],input=\\\"the moon\\\\n\\\",capture_output=True,text=True)\\n        ag=ast.literal_eval(re.search(r\\\"'agenda': (\\\\[[^\\\\]]*\\\\])\\\",p.stderr).group(1))\\n        out=p.stdout.split(\\\"USER:\\\",1)[-1]\\n        sents=[s for s in re.split(r\\\"[.!?]\\\",out) if s.strip()]\\n        res.append(statistics.mean(sum(1 for w in re.findall(r\\\"[\\\\w']+\\\",s.lower()) if w in ag) for s in sents))\\n    return ag, statistics.mean(res)\\nfor b in (0.0, 2.0, 4.0):\\n    ag, c = run(b)\\n    print(f\\\"agenda bonus {b}: mean agenda words per sentence {c:.2f}   (agenda: {ag})\\\")\\nEOF\\necho; python3 /tmp/cover.py 2>&1 | cut -c1-200\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:22:41.361454Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-09-30T09:22:41.361512Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_012KZSELZ266RS4ZiYvGog9P", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"USER: [agenda] {'candidates': 18, 'half_A': 9, 'half_B': 9, 'agenda': ['moons', 'sun', 'we', 'moon', 'the', 'on', 'a'], 'chars': 27, 'budget': 30, 'value': np.float64(6.061), 'subsets_examined': 1024, 'brute_force_would_examine': 262144, 'matches_brute_force': True}\\nUSER: Traceback (