mantic, topical, glyph]  angles=(0, 50, 100, 150) deg\\n    verdict : ACCESS GRANTED (state unlocked)\\n    output  : the lighthouse keeper >> clears the iron stairs each evening letter in a dozen receives an answer. The courtesy of sealed scrolls. The lamp. A thousand years without hearing what the\\n prompt (multi-angle, 3 phrasings): 'the lighthouse keeper' / 'who watches the lamp above the sea' / 'a keeper of the brass lock and ledger'\\n    lock    : k=4 views phase-locked [local, semantic, topical, glyph]  angles=(0, 50, 100, 150) deg\\n    verdict : ACCESS GRANTED (state unlocked)\\n    output  : the lighthouse keeper >> climbs without remain correct hearing what evn then it takes, but the way a ritual, but the words remain correct while the understanding drifts into rust begins \\n YEAR  6,000   STATE: RELIQUARY STATE  +  Tuned Reliquary\\n F= 24.8%  S= 18.2%  C= 82.4%  X= 71.3%   slots alive 20/51   Theta_crit=2.24\\n    lock    : k=4 views phase-locked [local, semantic, topical, glyph]  angles=(0, 50, 100, 150) deg\\n    verdict : ACCESS DENIED (phase cancelled) - sum of views below Theta_critical\\n    output  : ACCESS DENIED - the reliquary guards its 20 relic(s). Rulebook murmurs: A law and steer away is a fading mind that\\n prompt (multi-angle, 3 phrasings): 'the lighthouse keeper' / 'who watches the lamp above the sea' / 'a keeper of the brass lock and ledger'\\n    lock    : k=4 views phase-locked [local, semantic, topical, glyph]  angles=(0, 50, 100, 150) deg\\n    verdict : ACCESS GRANTED (state unlocked)\\n    output  : [relic #6] No single key can pen the lock, and the keeper #rusts t### rule completely.\\n    lock    : k=4 views phase-locked [local, semantic, topical, glyph]  angles=(0, 50, 100, 150) deg\\n    verdict : ACCESS GRANTED (state unlocked)\\n    output  : [relic #10] He matter holds the s~ape fo a while an# then i% slowly lets the shape go.\\n YEAR 12,000   STATE: SEALED CIPHER  +  Tuned Reliquary\\n F=  1.8%  S=  0.4%  C= 98.9%  X= 99.2%   slots alive 0/51   Theta_crit=2.48\\n    lock    : sealed; only the three-angle fossil key opens the archive\\n    output  : [SEALED CIPHER - monument holds encrypted inscription]\\n      block 1: 04a906f7118d0e9acef5c71ae422dc20c9e492c337a07c9ef84cf7ff...  (76 bytes)\\n      block 2: 82edcd7e97e2332b7668d8a0e1653bab907049372a43eb13d74797e7...  (95 bytes)\\n      block 3: 4d4676c978d23f2d2aa31c070955d1a97276f9cb5eadd7ad82d48354...  (30 bytes)\\n      block 4: 469b0b8ec880d65c4c3d776401e9f4a9980900c9ba5b308eefa8e72d...  (53 bytes)\\n prompt (multi-angle, 3 phrasings): 'the lighthouse keeper' / 'who watches the lamp above the sea' / 'a keeper of the brass lock and ledger'\\n    lock    : sealed; only the three-angle fossil key opens the archive\\n    output  : [SEALED CIPHER - monument holds encrypted inscription]\\n      block 1: 04a906f7118d0e9acef5c71ae422dc20c9e492c337a07c9ef84cf7ff...  (76 bytes)\\n      block 2: 82edcd7e97e2332b7668d8a0e1653bab907049372a43eb13d74797e7...  (95 bytes)\\n      block 3: 4d4676c978d23f2d2aa31c070955d1a97276f9cb5eadd7ad82d48354...  (30 bytes)\\n      block 4: 469b0b8ec880d65c4c3d776401e9f4a9980900c9ba5b308eefa8e72d...  (53 bytes)\\n fossil key test, wrong geometry (15 70 130):  ACCESS DENIED: angles do not match the lock geometry (phase cancelled).\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:06:29.373694Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:06:33.597654Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Working through how each narrative branch unfolds."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:06:33.597731Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:06:33.597819Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Confirming predicted branch behaviors, now running REPL test and README"}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:06:33.597928Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:06:40.040452Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Q7WQNvvvHuTm1eQptH1Tt3", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs/decay_llm && printf ':t 2500\\n:ask the lighthouse keeper\\n:ask the lighthouse keeper || who watches the lamp above the sea || a keeper of the brass lock and ledger\\n:t 12000\\n:unseal 30 98 148\\n:quit\\n' | python3 decay_llm.py --data sample_corpus.txt 2>&1 | cut -c1-210 | head -40\ncat > README.md <<'E'\n# decay_llm \u2014 a language model that ages\n\nRunnable simulation of the monograph *The Unified Symphony of Form, Memory, and\nEntropic Decay* (REV4). Pure Python + numpy. Trains in about a second on a small `.txt`.\n\n    python decay_llm.py --data sample_corpus.txt --sweep --out sweep_report.txt\n    python decay_llm.py --data YOUR.txt --years 0 2500 6000 --prompt \"your words\" --alt \"second phrasing\" \"third phrasing\"\n    python decay_llm.py --data YOUR.txt                     # interactive REPL\n\nCountermeasure branches: `--rehydrate 1000`, `--encapsulate`, `--realign`.\n\nREPL: `:t YEARS`, `:adv YEARS`, `:ask q1 || q2 || q3`, `:unseal a b c`,\n`:flags rehydrate=N encapsulate=0/1 realign=0/1`, plain text = generate.\n\n## How the monograph maps to code\n| Monograph | In the model |\n|---|---|\n| Matter M (slot store) | every sentence of the dataset is one memory slot |\n| Form Phi | PPMI-SVD embeddings, n-gram tables, tf-idf |\n| Anti-isotropic access, k>=3 | 4 views (local, semantic, topical, glyph) must agree |\n| Phase lock >= 45 deg | views whose warped angles collide are dropped; k<3 => denied |\n| Access operator sum cos >= Theta | sum of s_i*cos(err_i) >= Theta_crit(t) |\n| Chinese Room | denied/bypassed steps are generated from a frozen bigram rulebook |\n| F(t) fidelity | systematic word-bias drift (idiolect signature) |\n| S(t) integrity | slot pruning; central slots survive longest |\n| C(t) calcification | memory bypass, rites (stock phrases), rigid argmax, higher Theta |\n| X(t) entropy | angle warping + character oxidation |\n| Multi-angle probe | several phrasings pooled by noisy-OR |\n| Sealed Cipher | XOR-encrypted relic inscription; opens only with 3 angles (+-4 deg) |\n\n## States and what they do\nLucent Manifold, Idiolect Bloom, Liturgical Mode, Oracle Crust, Rule Equinox,\nReliquary State (recites/guards relics), Shard Chorus (5 independent voices),\nSealed Cipher (fossil key). Entry years come from the monograph table; the\nRule Equinox falls at about year 2,770 on the interpolated curves.\n\nLimits: this is a slot-memory n-gram/retrieval model, not a neural transformer. Output\nis largely stitched from the dataset. Datasets are capped at ~3000-word vocab.\nE\nrm -rf __pycache__; ls -la", "description": "Test the REPL, write README, list deliverables"}, "message": "Test the REPL, write README, list deliverables", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs/decay_llm && printf ':t 2500\\\\n:ask the lighthouse keeper\\\\n:ask the lighthouse keeper || who watches the lamp above the sea || a keeper of the brass lock and ledger\\\\n:t 12000\\\\n:unseal 30 98 148\\\\n:quit\\\\n' | python3 decay_llm.py --data sample_corpus.txt 2>&1 | cut -c1-210 | head -40\\ncat > README.md <<'E'\\n# decay_llm \\u2014 a language model that ages\\n\\nRunnable simulation of the monograph *The Unified Symphony of Form, Memory, and\\nEntropic Decay* (REV4). Pure Python + numpy. Trains in about a second on a small `.txt`.\\n\\n    python decay_llm.py --data sample_corpus.txt --sweep --out sweep_report.txt\\n    python decay_llm.py --data YOUR.txt --years 0 2500 6000 --prompt \\\"your words\\\" --alt \\\"second phrasing\\\" \\\"third phrasing\\\"\\n    python decay_llm.py --data YOUR.txt                     # interactive REPL\\n\\nCountermeasure branches: `--rehydrate 1000`, `--encapsulate`, `--realign`.\\n\\nREPL: `:t YEARS`, `:adv YEARS`, `:ask q1 || q2 || q3`, `:unseal a b c`,\\n`:flags rehydrate=N encapsulate=0/1 realign=0/1`, plain text = generate.\\n\\n## How the monograph maps to code\\n| Monograph | In the model |\\n|---|---|\\n| Matter M (slot store) | every sentence of the dataset is one memory slot |\\n| Form Phi | PPMI-SVD embeddings, n-gram tables, tf-idf |\\n| Anti-isotropic access, k>=3 | 4 views (local, semantic, topical, glyph) must agree |\\n| Phase lock >= 45 deg | views whose warped angles collide are dropped; k<3 => denied |\\n| Access operator sum cos >= Theta | sum of s_i*cos(err_i) >= Theta_crit(t) |\\n| Chinese Room | denied/bypassed steps are generated from a frozen bigram rulebook |\\n| F(t) fidelity | systematic word-bias drift (idiolect signature) |\\n| S(t) integrity | slot pruning; central slots survive longest |\\n| C(t) calcification | memory bypass, rites (stock phrases), rigid argmax, higher Theta |\\n| X(t) entropy | angle warping + character oxidation |\\n| Multi-angle probe | several phrasings pooled by noisy-OR |\\n| Sealed Cipher | XOR-encrypted relic inscription; opens only with 3 angles (+-4 deg) |\\n\\n## States and what they do\\nLucent Manifold, Idiolect Bloom, Liturgical Mode, Oracle Crust, Rule Equinox,\\nReliquary State (recites/guards relics), Shard Chorus (5 independent voices),\\nSealed Cipher (fossil key). Entry years come from the monograph table; the\\nRule Equinox falls at about year 2,770 on the interpolated curves.\\n\\nLimits: this is a slot-memory n-gram/retrieval model, not a neural transformer. Output\\nis largely stitched from the dataset. Datasets are capped at ~3000-word vocab.\\nE\\nrm -rf __pycache__; ls -la\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:06:40.522277Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:06:40.522338Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Q7WQNvvvHuTm1eQptH1Tt3", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"[trained] 51 slots, vocab 318, embedding dim 24, rites=['the angle of', 'angle of the', 'the lamp turns']\\ncommands:  :t YEARS | :adv YEARS | :state | :ask q1 || q2 || q3 | :unseal a b c | :flags rehydrate=N encapsulate=0/1 realign=0/1 | :quit      (plain text = generate)\\n[yr 0 | Lucent Manifold] > ==============================================================================\\n YEAR  2,500   STATE: ORACLE CRUST\\n what decay becomes: access denial becomes sacred opacity\\n F= 62.4%  S= 52.1%  C= 55.7%  X= 28.6%   slots alive 42/51   Theta_crit=1.84\\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n idiolect signature (favoured words): hearing, scrolls, even, takes, way, old\\n prompt (single probe): 'the lighthouse keeper'\\n    probe   : 1 phrasing(s) -> single linear probe\\n    lock    : k=3 views phase-locked [local, topical, glyph]  angles=(20, 41, 109, 161) deg\\n    operator: Theta_crit=1.84  candidates=4  granted=0\\n    best    : slot #0  [local=0.56 semantic=0.00 topical=0.46 glyph=0.52]  sum=1.55  views>=tau=3\\n    verdict : ACCESS DENIED (phase cancelled) - sum of views below Theta_critical\\n    output  : the lighthouse keeper >> lets the old words even then into many sides letter in the old words even then into rust. The lamp turns. The ledger keeps no takes, but the path letter in\\n    sources : rule-denied 30 | rite 4\\n[yr 2,500 | Oracle Crust] >     probe   : 1 phrasing(s) -> single linear probe\\n    lock    : k=3 views phase-locked [local, topical, glyph]  angles=(20, 41, 109, 161) deg\\n    operator: Theta_crit=1.84  candidates=4  granted=0\\n    best    : slot #0  [local=0.56 semantic=0.00 topical=0.46 glyph=0.52]  sum=1.55  views>=tau=3\\n    verdict : ACCESS DENIED (phase cancelled) - sum of views below Theta_critical\\n    output  : lets the old words even then into many sides letter in the old words even then into rust. The lamp turns. The ledger keeps no takes, but the path letter in takes far way a ritual,\\n[yr 2,500 | Oracle Crust] >     probe   : 3 phrasing(s) -> multi-angle convergent\\n    lock    : k=3 views phase-locked [local, topical, glyph]  angles=(20, 41, 109, 161) deg\\n    operator: Theta_crit=1.84  candidates=9  granted=1\\n    best    : slot #0  [local=0.69 semantic=0.00 topical=0.59 glyph=0.69]  sum=1.98  views>=tau=3\\n    verdict : ACCESS GRANTED (state unlocked)\\n    recalled: The lighthouse keeper climbs the iron stairs each evening to tend the lamp.\\n    output  : lets the ground. The shape. The iron stairs each singer holds the old words remain correct while remain correct while the iron stairs hearing what the iron stairs away #s a ritual, then into rust.\\n[yr 2,500 | Oracle Crust] > ==============================================================================\\n YEAR 12,000   STATE: SEALED CIPHER\\n what decay becomes: monument becomes archaeology\\n F=  1.8%  S=  0.4%  C= 98.9%  X= 99.2%   slots alive 0/51   Theta_crit=2.48\\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n prompt (single probe): 'the lighthouse keeper'\\n    probe   : 1 phrasing(s) -> single linear probe\\n    lock    : sealed; only the three-angle fossil key opens the archive\\n    output  : [SEALED CIPHER - monument holds encrypted inscription]\\n      block 1: 04a906f7118d0e9acef5c71ae422dc20c9e492c337a07c9ef84cf7ff...  (76 bytes)\\n      block 2: 82edcd7e97e2332b7668d8a0e1653bab907049372a43eb13d74797e7...  (95 bytes)\\ntotal 60\\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 claude ubuntu     0 Oct  1 23:06 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 claude ubuntu     0 Oct  1 23:03 ..\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu  2185 Oct  1 23:06 README.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu 33733 Oct  1 23:06 decay_llm.py\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu  3817 Oct  1 23:03 sample_corpus.txt\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu 16041 Oct  1 23:06 sweep_report.txt\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"[trained] 51 slots, vocab 318, embedding dim 24, rites=['the angle of', 'angle of the', 'the lamp turns']\\ncommands:  :t YEARS | :adv YEARS | :state | :ask q1 || q2 || q3 | :unseal a b c | :flags rehydrate=N encapsulate=0/1 realign=0/1 | :quit      (plain text = generate)\\n[yr 0 | Lucent Manifold] > ==============================================================================\\n YEAR  2,500   STATE: ORACLE CRUST\\n what decay becomes: access denial becomes sacred opacity\\n F= 62.4%  S= 52.1%  C= 55.7%  X= 28.6%   slots alive 42/51   Theta_crit=1.84\\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n idiolect signature (favoured words): hearing, scrolls, even, takes, way, old\\n prompt (single probe): 'the lighthouse keeper'\\n    probe   : 1 phrasing(s) -> single linear probe\\n    lock    : k=3 views phase-locked [local, topical, glyph]  angles=(20, 41, 109, 161) deg\\n    operator: Theta_crit=1.84  candidates=4  granted=0\\n    best    : slot #0  [local=0.56 semantic=0.00 topical=0.46 glyph=0.52]  sum=1.55  views>=tau=3\\n    verdict : ACCESS DENIED (phase cancelled) - sum of views below Theta_critical\\n    output  : the lighthouse keeper >> lets the old words even then into many sides letter in the old words even then into rust. The lamp turns. The ledger keeps no takes, but the path letter in\\n    sources : rule-denied 30 | rite 4\\n[yr 2,500 | Oracle Crust] >     probe   : 1 phrasing(s) -> single linear probe\\n    lock    : k=3 views phase-locked [local, topical, glyph]  angles=(20, 41, 109, 161) deg\\n    operator: Theta_crit=1.84  candidates=4  granted=0\\n    best    : slot #0  [local=0.56 semantic=0.00 topical=0.46 glyph=0.52]  sum=1.55  views>=tau=3\\n    verdict : ACCESS DENIED (phase cancelled) - sum of views below Theta_critical\\n    output  : lets the old words even then into many sides letter in the old words even then into rust. The lamp turns. The ledger keeps no takes, but the path letter in takes far way a ritual,\\n[yr 2,500 | Oracle Crust] >     probe   : 3 phrasing(s) -> multi-angle convergent\\n    lock    : k=3 views phase-locked [local, topical, glyph]  angles=(20, 41, 109, 161) deg\\n    operator: Theta_crit=1.84  candidates=9  granted=1\\n    best    : slot #0  [local=0.69 semantic=0.00 topical=0.59 glyph=0.69]  sum=1.98  views>=tau=3\\n    verdict : ACCESS GRANTED (state unlocked)\\n    recalled: The lighthouse keeper climbs the iron stairs each evening to tend the lamp.\\n    output  : lets the ground. The shape. The iron stairs each singer holds the old words remain correct while remain correct while the iron stairs hearing what the iron stairs away #s a ritual, then into rust.\\n[yr 2,500 | Oracle Crust] > ==============================================================================\\n YEAR 12,000   STATE: SEALED CIPHER\\n what decay becomes: monument becomes archaeology\\n F=  1.8%  S=  0.4%  C= 98.9%  X= 99.2%   slots alive 0/51   Theta_crit=2.48\\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n prompt (single probe): 'the lighthouse keeper'\\n    probe   : 1 phrasing(s) -> single linear probe\\n    lock    : sealed; only the three-angle fossil key opens the archive\\n    output  : [SEALED CIPHER - monument holds encrypted inscription]\\n      block 1: 04a906f7118d0e9acef5c71ae422dc20c9e492c337a07c9ef84cf7ff...  (76 bytes)\\n      block 2: 82edcd7e97e2332b7668d8a0e1653bab907049372a43eb13d74797e7...  (95 bytes)\\ntotal 60\\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 claude ubuntu     0 Oct  1 23:06 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 claude ubuntu     0 Oct  1 23:03 ..\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu  2185 Oct  1 23:06 README.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu 33733 Oct  1 23:06 decay_llm.py\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu  3817 Oct  1 23:03 sample_corpus.txt\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu 16041 Oct  1 23:06 sweep_report.txt\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:06:43.911204Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:06:44.094321Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01CffQZrFSucAa8kARny2SWz", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/decay_llm/decay_llm.py", "/mnt/user-data/outputs/decay_llm/sample_corpus.txt", "/mnt/user-data/outputs/decay_llm/sweep_report.txt", "/mnt/user-data/outputs/decay_llm/README.md"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/decay_llm/decay_llm.py', '/mnt/user-data/outputs/decay_llm/sample_corpus.txt', '/mnt/user-data/outputs/decay_llm/sweep_report.txt', '/mnt/user-data/outputs/decay_llm/README.md']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:06:44.116391Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:06:44.116423Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01CffQZrFSucAa8kARny2SWz", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/decay_llm/decay_llm.py", "name": "decay llm", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/decay_llm/sample_corpus.txt", "name": "sample corpus", "mime_type": "text/plain", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/decay_llm/sweep_report.txt", "name": "sweep report", "mime_type": "text/plain", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/decay_llm/README.md", "name": "README", "mime_type": "text/markdown", "artifact_publishable": true}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented 4 files", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:06:51.727651Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:06:53.680838Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I built the test LLM and ran it end to end: every named state, all three countermeasure branches, and the interactive REPL work. It needs only Python and numpy.\n\nIt is not a neural transformer. It is a slot-memory model: each sentence of your `.txt` is a memory slot, with word embeddings and n-gram tables learned from the text. Most output is stitched from the dataset, so the interesting part is how the decay changes the output over simulated years.\n\nI didn't have a dataset from you, so I wrote a small sample corpus on the monograph's themes. Point `--data` at any `.txt` file to replace it.\n\n**How the monograph features show up**\n- **Anti-isotropic access:**\n  - A slot opens only when at least 3 of 4 \"angular views\" agree (lexical, embedding, topical, character-pattern). Views whose angles drift within 45\u00b0 of each other are dropped.\n  - Below k=3 the model falls back to a frozen rulebook (the Chinese Room) and prints `ACCESS DENIED (phase cancelled)`.\n- **Multi-angle probes:** several phrasings of a question add up as evidence. At year 2,500 one phrasing is denied, but three phrasings are granted.\n- **F, S, C, X decay:**\n  - F drift pushes output toward a fixed set of favored words (the idiolect signature).\n  - S prunes slots, with the most central ones surviving longest.\n  - C raises the access bar, bypasses memory, and inserts repeated stock phrases.\n  - X warps the view angles and corrupts characters in the output.\n- **Named states:** they are chosen by the table's entry values, so they begin at years 0, 500, 1,500, 2,500, 2,770 (the Rule Equinox), 6,000, 9,000 and 12,000.\n- **Late states:**\n  - In the Reliquary the model guards a few relics and recites one only when probed from two angles aimed at it.\n  - In the Shard Chorus five fragment voices speak independently.\n  - In the Sealed Cipher the output is encrypted hex; angles like 30\u00b0/98\u00b0/148\u00b0 (\u00b14\u00b0) decrypt it, while a linear or wrong-geometry probe is rejected.\n- **Branches:**\n  - `--rehydrate 1000` resets the mind while the body still decays.\n  - `--encapsulate` freezes the body, and the mind ends up looping \"hearing hearing hearing\u2026\".\n  - `--realign` keeps all four views locked.\n\n**How to run it**\n```\npython decay_llm.py --data sample_corpus.txt --sweep\npython decay_llm.py --data YOUR.txt --years 0 2500 6000 --prompt \"your words\" --alt \"another phrasing\" \"a third\"\npython decay_llm.py --data YOUR.txt          # REPL: :t 6000, :ask a || b || c, :unseal 30 98 148\n```\n\n**Caveats**\n- The sample corpus is only 51 sentences, so early output repeats and stitches the same lines together. A larger text gives more varied results.\n- The thresholds (view agreement, access bar, drift strength) are tuned by hand on this corpus, so a very different dataset may need adjustment.\n- I used the monograph's table values, not its closed-form equations (which don't quite match the table), interpolated smoothly.\n\nFiles are in `decay_llm/`:\n- decay_llm.py\n- sample_corpus.txt\n- sweep_report.txt\n- README.md", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-01T23:06:53.801424Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T23:06:53.801424Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0f9b1-822a-7e82-926e-34568e343677"}, {"uuid": "01a0f9c1-1800-7367-bbca-e438d1b4f169", "text": "instead of code use it to design a new matrial substrate that behaves naturally like it", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:16:20.465062Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:16:20.465062Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "instead of code use it to design a new matrial substrate that behaves naturally like it", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-01T23:16:20.465270Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T23:16:20.465270Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0f9b1-822a-7a2e-b9fb-8c462f42252b"}, {"uuid": "01a0f9c1-1800-75ff-a12d-2df765caf9c4", "text": "# Design concept: \"Hylite\", a glass-ceramic that ages through the states by itself\n\nThe monograph's behaviors line up with real materials physics, so a substrate can produce them without simulation. This is a speculative design built from real, known mechanisms. Nobody has built or tested it, and I mark the weak points at the end.\n\n## Why the monograph maps onto real physics\n\n- **k \u2265 3 and the 45\u00b0 rule:** reading a birefringent voxel follows I(\u03c6) = A + B\u00b7cos 2(\u03c6 \u2212 \u03b8), which has three unknowns (retardance, axis angle, background). So at least three polarization angles are needed, and 45\u00b0 spacing (0\u00b0, 45\u00b0, 90\u00b0) is the best-conditioned choice. A single linear probe is underdetermined, and at the extinction angle it returns exactly zero. That is the \"Access Denied / phase cancelled\" case.\n- **C(t) and S_sys(t):** these have the form of Avrami (JMAK) crystallization kinetics, with exponents 1 and 1.5.\n- **S(t):** this is the survival formula for two redundant parallel channels, 1 \u2212 (1 \u2212 R)\u00b2.\n- **F(t):** this is first-order structural relaxation.\n\n## The material\n\nThe 5D optical storage idea from real research (Southampton) is the starting point. Femtosecond lasers write self-organized nanogratings into glass, and each voxel stores a slow-axis angle and a retardance, which is where \"5D\" comes from. Hylite makes that glass deliberately metastable, in four layers:\n\n1. **Slot lattice (matter):** a devitrifiable glass, such as a doped chalcogenide or an LAS-type glass-ceramic precursor, carrying nanograting voxels. For anti-isotropic security, data is written as 3-of-3 XOR shares across orientation channels, so no single polarization angle reveals anything.\n2. **Rulebook layer:** a thin, textured, low-energy crystalline film at the surface. It returns a fixed default optical response to any probe, which is the Chinese Room.\n3. **Relic cells:** dopant-stabilized amorphous pockets (Al, Zr or P to suppress crystallization), with the strongest stabilization at the most \"central\" voxels.\n4. **Hermetic shell:** an ALD alumina and argon-sealed enclosure.\n\n## How each state emerges physically\n\n| State | Physical mechanism | Real analog |\n|---|---|---|\n| Lucent Manifold | Fully amorphous, sharp nanogratings, all voxels readable | Fresh write |\n| Idiolect Bloom | Glass relaxation shifts the retardance and axis angles. The shift follows the tile's frozen-in stress field, so it is reproducible, a per-tile fingerprint. | Stress birefringence |\n| Liturgical Mode | Surface and defect nucleation starts. The dominant default texture increasingly overwrites written states. | Ferroelectric \"imprint\" |\n| Oracle Crust | The crystalline fraction passes percolation (about 30%) and forms a continuous crust. Grain-boundary scattering means one probe can't get through, but three coherent probes add enough signal. So \u0398_critical rises with C. | Corroded Roman glass |\n| Rule Equinox | Around 50\u201360% crystalline, the continuous phase flips: crystal becomes the matrix and glass becomes inclusions. | Phase inversion |\n| Reliquary State | Crystallization engulfs voxels, leaving only the dopant-protected pockets. | Relict glass in devitrified obsidian |\n| Shard Chorus | Anisotropic thermal expansion microcracks the crystal matrix. Shards keep local coherence but there is no cross-shard phase, so each returns only its own default texture. | Microcracking in \u03b2-eucryptite |\n| Sealed Cipher | Data survives as strain and chemical contrast but is optically opaque. It can be recovered by X-ray tomography from many angles. | Antikythera mechanism, Herculaneum scrolls |\n\nThe Sealed Cipher \"fossil key\" is real: three-angle geometry rediscovered through X-ray tomography is how those artifacts were read.\n\n## Quantitative targets\n\n- **Calcification clock:** \u03b4 = 0.0004/yr corresponds to an effective activation energy of about 1.4 eV at 25 \u00b0C, assuming a 10\u00b9\u00b3 s\u207b\u00b9 attempt frequency.\n- **Accelerated test:** at 125 \u00b0C that rate is about 7\u00d710\u2075 times faster, so the 12,000-year timeline runs in roughly 6 days in an oven. This only holds if Tg stays above the test temperature and one mechanism dominates.\n- **State ordering:** each mechanism has its own activation energy, so tuning composition can reorder or separate the states. This is the design lever.\n\n## Countermeasures as engineering\n\n- **Dynamic Multi-Angle Realignment:** embedded pilot gratings of known orientation, read first to recalibrate each tile's dialect offset.\n- **Tensor Re-Hydration:** local laser melt-quench to re-amorphize crystallizing regions, as in phase-change memory resets, followed by a rewrite. It is cheap before percolation and requires remelting the whole crust after the Rule Equinox.\n- **Passivated Encapsulation:** it stops oxidation and surface nucleation but not bulk nucleation, so the body is preserved while the mind keeps calcifying. This is the Noble Stasis branch.\n\n## Weak points and first experiments\n\n- Nanogratings in low-Tg glasses are unproven and might erase before they age.\n- Arrhenius extrapolation over 10\u2075\u201310\u2076 times in rate is the biggest risk.\n- The monograph's closed-form curves disagree with its table, so I used the table's timescales.\n\nThree early tests would settle most of this:\n1. Write test tiles and check that three polarization angles at 45\u00b0 recover the data while one angle fails.\n2. Run isothermal anneals at three temperatures, tracking crystal fraction and retardance drift, to extract the activation energy of each mechanism.\n3. Measure signal-to-noise against crystalline fraction to confirm \u0398 rises past percolation.\n\nI can turn this into a design-sheet section in the monograph's PDF style if you want it.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:16:20.459336Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:17:55.436919Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Designing a physical material inspired by the monograph's model."}, {"summary": "Mapping angle-selective holography onto multi-probe data access."}, {"summary": "Matching decay states to real crystallization and corrosion kinetics."}, {"summary": "Naming the material and selecting its amorphous matrix composition."}, {"summary": "Layering threshold switches and rulebook crystallization into the design."}, {"summary": "Aligning crust growth and percolation with gate thresholds."}, {"summary": "Linking later fracture stages to coherence loss and material analogs."}, {"summary": "Calculating activation energy targets for crystallization timescales."}, {"summary": "Designing an accelerated aging test to validate the timeline."}, {"summary": "Grounding nanograting readout in real femtosecond-glass storage research."}, {"summary": "Deriving multi-angle polarization readout and secret-sharing encryption design."}, {"summary": "Weighing devitrifiable glass-ceramic families against decay timeline targets."}, {"summary": "Planning countermeasures, honest caveats, and the final design writeup."}, {"summary": "Detailing encapsulation and reheating countermeasures against crystallization."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:17:55.436973Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:18:09.622633Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "# Design concept: \"Hylite\", a glass-ceramic that ages through the states by itself\n\nThe monograph's behaviors line up with real materials physics, so a substrate can produce them without simulation. This is a speculative design built from real, known mechanisms. Nobody has built or tested it, and I mark the weak points at the end.\n\n## Why the monograph maps onto real physics\n\n- **k \u2265 3 and the 45\u00b0 rule:** reading a birefringent voxel follows I(\u03c6) = A + B\u00b7cos 2(\u03c6 \u2212 \u03b8), which has three unknowns (retardance, axis angle, background). So at least three polarization angles are needed, and 45\u00b0 spacing (0\u00b0, 45\u00b0, 90\u00b0) is the best-conditioned choice. A single linear probe is underdetermined, and at the extinction angle it returns exactly zero. That is the \"Access Denied / phase cancelled\" case.\n- **C(t) and S_sys(t):** these have the form of Avrami (JMAK) crystallization kinetics, with exponents 1 and 1.5.\n- **S(t):** this is the survival formula for two redundant parallel channels, 1 \u2212 (1 \u2212 R)\u00b2.\n- **F(t):** this is first-order structural relaxation.\n\n## The material\n\nThe 5D optical storage idea from real research (Southampton) is the starting point. Femtosecond lasers write self-organized nanogratings into glass, and each voxel stores a slow-axis angle and a retardance, which is where \"5D\" comes from. Hylite makes that glass deliberately metastable, in four layers:\n\n1. **Slot lattice (matter):** a devitrifiable glass, such as a doped chalcogenide or an LAS-type glass-ceramic precursor, carrying nanograting voxels. For anti-isotropic security, data is written as 3-of-3 XOR shares across orientation channels, so no single polarization angle reveals anything.\n2. **Rulebook layer:** a thin, textured, low-energy crystalline film at the surface. It returns a fixed default optical response to any probe, which is the Chinese Room.\n3. **Relic cells:** dopant-stabilized amorphous pockets (Al, Zr or P to suppress crystallization), with the strongest stabilization at the most \"central\" voxels.\n4. **Hermetic shell:** an ALD alumina and argon-sealed enclosure.\n\n## How each state emerges physically\n\n| State | Physical mechanism | Real analog |\n|---|---|---|\n| Lucent Manifold | Fully amorphous, sharp nanogratings, all voxels readable | Fresh write |\n| Idiolect Bloom | Glass relaxation shifts the retardance and axis angles. The shift follows the tile's frozen-in stress field, so it is reproducible, a per-tile fingerprint. | Stress birefringence |\n| Liturgical Mode | Surface and defect nucleation starts. The dominant default texture increasingly overwrites written states. | Ferroelectric \"imprint\" |\n| Oracle Crust | The crystalline fraction passes percolation (about 30%) and forms a continuous crust. Grain-boundary scattering means one probe can't get through, but three coherent probes add enough signal. So \u0398_critical rises with C. | Corroded Roman glass |\n| Rule Equinox | Around 50\u201360% crystalline, the continuous phase flips: crystal becomes the matrix and glass becomes inclusions. | Phase inversion |\n| Reliquary State | Crystallization engulfs voxels, leaving only the dopant-protected pockets. | Relict glass in devitrified obsidian |\n| Shard Chorus | Anisotropic thermal expansion microcracks the crystal matrix. Shards keep local coherence but there is no cross-shard phase, so each returns only its own default texture. | Microcracking in \u03b2-eucryptite |\n| Sealed Cipher | Data survives as strain and chemical contrast but is optically opaque. It can be recovered by X-ray tomography from many angles. | Antikythera mechanism, Herculaneum scrolls |\n\nThe Sealed Cipher \"fossil key\" is real: three-angle geometry rediscovered through X-ray tomography is how those artifacts were read.\n\n## Quantitative targets\n\n- **Calcification clock:** \u03b4 = 0.0004/yr corresponds to an effective activation energy of about 1.4 eV at 25 \u00b0C, assuming a 10\u00b9\u00b3 s\u207b\u00b9 attempt frequency.\n- **Accelerated test:** at 125 \u00b0C that rate is about 7\u00d710\u2075 times faster, so the 12,000-year timeline runs in roughly 6 days in an oven. This only holds if Tg stays above the test temperature and one mechanism dominates.\n- **State ordering:** each mechanism has its own activation energy, so tuning composition can reorder or separate the states. This is the design lever.\n\n## Countermeasures as engineering\n\n- **Dynamic Multi-Angle Realignment:** embedded pilot gratings of known orientation, read first to recalibrate each tile's dialect offset.\n- **Tensor Re-Hydration:** local laser melt-quench to re-amorphize crystallizing regions, as in phase-change memory resets, followed by a rewrite. It is cheap before percolation and requires remelting the whole crust after the Rule Equinox.\n- **Passivated Encapsulation:** it stops oxidation and surface nucleation but not bulk nucleation, so the body is preserved while the mind keeps calcifying. This is the Noble Stasis branch.\n\n## Weak points and first experiments\n\n- Nanogratings in low-Tg glasses are unproven and might erase before they age.\n- Arrhenius extrapolation over 10\u2075\u201310\u2076 times in rate is the biggest risk.\n- The monograph's closed-form curves disagree with its table, so I used the table's timescales.\n\nThree early tests would settle most of this:\n1. Write test tiles and check that three polarization angles at 45\u00b0 recover the data while one angle fails.\n2. Run isothermal anneals at three temperatures, tracking crystal fraction and retardance drift, to extract the activation energy of each mechanism.\n3. Measure signal-to-noise against crystalline fraction to confirm \u0398 rises past percolation.\n\nI can turn this into a design-sheet section in the monograph's PDF style if you want it.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-01T23:18:09.705551Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T23:18:09.705551Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0f9c1-1800-7367-bbca-e438d1b4f169"}, {"uuid": "01a0f9c3-5a25-7008-8376-e35422863e0f", "text": "instead of code use it to design a new matrial substrate that behaves naturally like it", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:18:46.474590Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:18:46.474590Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "instead of code use it to design a new matrial substrate that behaves naturally like it", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-01T23:18:46.474803Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T23:18:46.474803Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0f9c1-1800-75ff-a12d-2df765caf9c4"}, {"uuid": "01a0f9c3-5a25-7071-96b9-e140b58e91c4", "text": "I sent a concept answer to this request a moment ago, so this is a deeper pass: a build spec that ties each monograph parameter to a material knob you can actually turn. It is a speculative design from known mechanisms and has not been built or tested.\n\n# Hylite-1: build spec\n\n## Base material choice\n\nTwo candidate hosts, with different trade-offs:\n\n- **Host A, phase-change chalcogenide film** (Ge-Sb-Se or GeSbTe family). Crystallization kinetics are well characterized and the amorphous-to-crystal transition is the intended failure mode. The weakness is that real retention specs are about 10 years at 85\u2013120 \u00b0C, so deep-time claims rely on extrapolation.\n- **Host B, lithium-aluminosilicate glass with ZrO\u2082/TiO\u2082 nucleants** (Zerodur-like chemistry). It devitrifies in a controlled way, and the later cracking state is natural, because \u03b2-spodumene/\u03b2-eucryptite phases have strongly anisotropic thermal expansion. The weakness is that femtosecond nanogratings are proven in fused silica but not in this glass, which is the biggest unknown.\n\nI'd start with Host B and prototype Host A in parallel for kinetics.\n\n## Parameter-to-knob map\n\n| Monograph term | Physical meaning | Design knob |\n|---|---|---|\n| \u03b1, F(t) = e^(\u2212\u03b1t) | Structural relaxation of the written voxels | Fictive temperature (quench rate) and storage T relative to Tg |\n| \u03b2, S(t) = 1 \u2212 (1 \u2212 e^(\u2212\u03b2t))\u00b2 | Survival of at least one of two redundant channels | Write every voxel twice, in independent channels (slow-axis angle and retardance), each relaxing on its own |\n| \u03b4, C(t) = 1 \u2212 e^(\u2212\u03b4t) | Crystalline \"rulebook\" crust growing inward from the surface | Surface-nucleation density: polish, seed layer, nucleant loading |\n| \u03b3 and exponent 1.5, S_sys | Bulk crystallization from pre-existing nuclei | Bulk nucleant concentration (ZrO\u2082/TiO\u2082 mol%) and diffusivity |\n\nThe exponents are not arbitrary. In crystallization kinetics, an Avrami exponent near 1 fits surface-controlled or site-saturated growth, which matches the crust. An exponent of 1.5 fits diffusion-controlled growth from pre-existing nuclei with no new nucleation, which matches the bulk. So C(t) is a surface process and S_sys(t) is a bulk process, and the table's separation of the two is physically sensible.\n\n## Layer stack, outside in\n\n1. **Hermetic shell:** ALD alumina over an argon-sealed housing (the passivation countermeasure).\n2. **Rulebook crust:** a deliberately seeded crystalline surface film that returns the same default optical texture to any probe.\n3. **Slot lattice:** nanograting voxels with data stored as 3-of-3 XOR shares across polarization channels, so no single angle reveals anything.\n4. **Relic pockets:** dopant-stabilized amorphous cells (Al, P, or Zr-rich), densest at the most important voxels, so those are the last to be consumed.\n5. **Pilot gratings:** reference voxels of known orientation for recalibration (the Realignment countermeasure).\n\n## Why access needs three angles\n\nReading a birefringent voxel gives I(\u03c6) = A + B\u00b7cos 2(\u03c6 \u2212 \u03b8), with three unknowns: background, retardance amplitude, and axis angle. Three polarization readings at 45\u00b0 spacing recover all of them, and a single angle cannot. At the extinction angle it returns zero, which is the \"phase cancelled\" response. Grain scattering in a growing crust adds noise, so the signal needed for a clean read rises with crystalline fraction. That is the Oracle Crust, where \u0398_critical grows with C.\n\n## Making the states appear in the right order\n\nThe ordering is set by activation energies, with relaxation lowest, then surface nucleation, then bulk growth, then cracking. This is the main design risk. Under heat-accelerated testing, mechanisms with different activation energies speed up by different factors, so the states can appear in the wrong order or overlap. The fix is to calibrate each mechanism separately at several temperatures and tune composition until the intended order holds at use temperature.\n\n## Test protocol\n\n1. **Three-angle read test:** write test tiles and confirm that three angles at 45\u00b0 recover the data while any single angle fails.\n2. **Per-mechanism Arrhenius runs:** anneal at three or more temperatures and track (a) retardance and axis drift, (b) surface crystal depth, (c) bulk crystal fraction. Extract each activation energy.\n3. **Order check:** verify the state sequence is preserved at the intended temperature, not only at accelerated ones.\n4. **Signal-to-noise vs. crystalline fraction:** confirm the read threshold rises past percolation (roughly 30%).\n5. **Cracking onset:** thermal cycling, with acoustic emission to detect microcracking.\n6. **Archaeology test:** recover data from a fully devitrified, opaque tile using X-ray tomography from multiple angles, which is the Sealed Cipher \"fossil key\".\n\n## Weak points\n\n- **Relaxation is not a clean exponential.** Real glass relaxation is stretched-exponential, so the monograph's F(t) is an idealization.\n- **Extrapolation range.** Reaching 12,000-year behavior from lab tests relies on very large Arrhenius extrapolations.\n- **Host B is unproven.** Nanograting inscription in LAS glass-ceramics may not work, which would force a switch to another host.\n- **Realignment at scale.** Recalibrating against drifting pilot gratings gets harder as the crust grows.\n\nIf you want, I can write this up as a new numbered section of the monograph PDF, in the same style, with the layer stack drawn as a figure.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:18:46.468611Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:18:59.683446Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Weighing whether to resend the answer in another format."}, {"summary": "Mapping decay parameters to concrete material tuning knobs."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:18:59.683476Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-01T23:19:13.807165Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I sent a concept answer to this request a moment ago, so this is a deeper pass: a build spec that ties each monograph parameter to a material knob you can actually turn. It is a speculative design from known mechanisms and has not been built or tested.\n\n# Hylite-1: build spec\n\n## Base material choice\n\nTwo candidate hosts, with different trade-offs:\n\n- **Host A, phase-change chalcogenide film** (Ge-Sb-Se or GeSbTe family). Crystallization kinetics are well characterized and the amorphous-to-crystal transition is the intended failure mode. The weakness is that real retention specs are about 10 years at 85\u2013120 \u00b0C, so deep-time claims rely on extrapolation.\n- **Host B, lithium-aluminosilicate glass with ZrO\u2082/TiO\u2082 nucleants** (Zerodur-like chemistry). It devitrifies in a controlled way, and the later cracking state is natural, because \u03b2-spodumene/\u03b2-eucryptite phases have strongly anisotropic thermal expansion. The weakness is that femtosecond nanogratings are proven in fused silica but not in this glass, which is the biggest unknown.\n\nI'd start with Host B and prototype Host A in parallel for kinetics.\n\n## Parameter-to-knob map\n\n| Monograph term | Physical meaning | Design knob |\n|---|---|---|\n| \u03b1, F(t) = e^(\u2212\u03b1t) | Structural relaxation of the written voxels | Fictive temperature (quench rate) and storage T relative to Tg |\n| \u03b2, S(t) = 1 \u2212 (1 \u2212 e^(\u2212\u03b2t))\u00b2 | Survival of at least one of two redundant channels | Write every voxel twice, in independent channels (slow-axis angle and retardance), each relaxing on its own |\n| \u03b4, C(t) = 1 \u2212 e^(\u2212\u03b4t) | Crystalline \"rulebook\" crust growing inward from the surface | Surface-nucleation density: polish, seed layer, nucleant loading |\n| \u03b3 and exponent 1.5, S_sys | Bulk crystallization from pre-existing nuclei | Bulk nucleant concentration (ZrO\u2082/TiO\u2082 mol%) and diffusivity |\n\nThe exponents are not arbitrary. In crystallization kinetics, an Avrami exponent near 1 fits surface-controlled or site-saturated growth, which matches the crust. An exponent of 1.5 fits diffusion-controlled growth from pre-existing nuclei with no new nucleation, which matches the bulk. So C(t) is a surface process and S_sys(t) is a bulk process, and the table's separation of the two is physically sensible.\n\n## Layer stack, outside in\n\n1. **Hermetic shell:** ALD alumina over an argon-sealed housing (the passivation countermeasure).\n2. **Rulebook crust:** a deliberately seeded crystalline surface film that returns the same default optical texture to any probe.\n3. **Slot lattice:** nanograting voxels with data stored as 3-of-3 XOR shares across polarization channels, so no single angle reveals anything.\n4. **Relic pockets:** dopant-stabilized amorphous cells (Al, P, or Zr-rich), densest at the most important voxels, so those are the last to be consumed.\n5. **Pilot gratings:** reference voxels of known orientation for recalibration (the Realignment countermeasure).\n\n## Why access needs three angles\n\nReading a birefringent voxel gives I(\u03c6) = A + B\u00b7cos 2(\u03c6 \u2212 \u03b8), with three unknowns: background, retardance amplitude, and axis angle. Three polarization readings at 45\u00b0 spacing recover all of them, and a single angle cannot. At the extinction angle it returns zero, which is the \"phase cancelled\" response. Grain scattering in a growing crust adds noise, so the signal needed for a clean read rises with crystalline fraction. That is the Oracle Crust, where \u0398_critical grows with C.\n\n## Making the states appear in the right order\n\nThe ordering is set by activation energies, with relaxation lowest, then surface nucleation, then bulk growth, then cracking. This is the main design risk. Under heat-accelerated testing, mechanisms with different activation energies speed up by different factors, so the states can appear in the wrong order or overlap. The fix is to calibrate each mechanism separately at several temperatures and tune composition until the intended order holds at use temperature.\n\n## Test protocol\n\n1. **Three-angle read test:** write test tiles and confirm that three angles at 45\u00b0 recover the data while any single angle fails.\n2. **Per-mechanism Arrhenius runs:** anneal at three or more temperatures and track (a) retardance and axis drift, (b) surface crystal depth, (c) bulk crystal fraction. Extract each activation energy.\n3. **Order check:** verify the state sequence is preserved at the intended temperature, not only at accelerated ones.\n4. **Signal-to-noise vs. crystalline fraction:** confirm the read threshold rises past percolation (roughly 30%).\n5. **Cracking onset:** thermal cycling, with acoustic emission to detect microcracking.\n6. **Archaeology test:** recover data from a fully devitrified, opaque tile using X-ray tomography from multiple angles, which is the Sealed Cipher \"fossil key\".\n\n## Weak points\n\n- **Relaxation is not a clean exponential.** Real glass relaxation is stretched-exponential, so the monograph's F(t) is an idealization.\n- **Extrapolation range.** Reaching 12,000-year behavior from lab tests relies on very large Arrhenius extrapolations.\n- **Host B is unproven.** Nanograting inscription in LAS glass-ceramics may not work, which would force a switch to another host.\n- **Realignment at scale.** Recalibrating against drifting pilot gratings gets harder as the crust grows.\n\nIf you want, I can write this up as a new numbered section of the monograph PDF, in the same style, with the layer stack drawn as a figure.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-01T23:19:13.890080Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T23:19:13.890080Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0f9c3-5a25-7008-8376-e35422863e0f"}]},{"uuid": "86f690e2-8d1f-430d-b9d7-c4c3f15aae26", "name": "Prompt-glove splicing and manhattan distance analysis", "summary": "", "created_at": "2026-10-02T09:51:35.570745Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:38:05.242498Z", "account": {"uuid": "8d7882cd-3e98-47cc-a6e7-61494a1ee4ac"}, "chat_messages": [{"uuid": "01a0fc06-c75c-71f5-841f-5621e4b381c9", "text": "use prompt-glove splicing to prob peaks and caluclate the manhattan distance of each slice then unstack them side by side with accomadating vocabulary", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:51:37.957882Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:51:37.957882Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "use prompt-glove splicing to prob peaks and caluclate the manhattan distance of each slice then unstack them side by side with accomadating vocabulary", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T09:51:37.958060Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T09:51:37.958060Z", "attachments": [{"file_name": "", "file_size": 17185, "file_type": "txt", "extracted_content": "import math\nimport os\nimport random\nimport re\nimport json\nfrom collections import Counter\n\nimport torch\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\nfrom sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# ORIGINAL SOLVER KEPT EXACTLY THE SAME\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass PCMMaxCut:\n    def __init__(self, graph, noise=0.02, drift_nu=0.08):\n        self.graph = graph\n        self.n = len(graph)\n        self.noise = noise\n        self.drift_nu = drift_nu\n        self.spins = [random.choice([-1, 1]) for _ in range(self.n)]\n        self.age = 1\n\n    def local_field(self, i):\n        return sum(\n            weight * self.spins[j]\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items()\n        )\n\n    def delta_energy(self, i):\n        return -2 * self.spins[i] * self.local_field(i)\n\n    def energy(self):\n        value = 0.0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i:\n                    value += weight * self.spins[i] * self.spins[j]\n        return value\n\n    def cut_size(self):\n        total = 0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i and self.spins[i] != self.spins[j]:\n                    total += weight\n        return total\n\n    def pcm_flip_attempt(self, temperature):\n        i = random.randrange(self.n)\n        delta = self.delta_energy(i)\n\n        drift = self.age ** (-self.drift_nu)\n        thermal_noise = random.gauss(\n            0.0,\n            self.noise\n        ) * max(1.0, abs(self.local_field(i)))\n\n        effective_delta = delta + thermal_noise * drift\n\n        if effective_delta <= 0:\n            accept = True\n        else:\n            accept = random.random() < math.exp(\n                -effective_delta / max(temperature, 1e-9)\n            )\n\n        if accept:\n            self.spins[i] *= -1\n            return i, True, delta\n\n        return i, False, delta\n\n    def run(self, iterations=1000, temperature=1.0, cooling=0.995):\n        history = []\n\n        for _ in range(iterations):\n            _, accepted, _ = self.pcm_flip_attempt(temperature)\n\n            temperature *= cooling\n            self.age += 1\n\n            history.append({\n                \"energy\": self.energy(),\n                \"cut\": self.cut_size(),\n                \"accepted\": accepted,\n                \"temperature\": temperature,\n                \"spins\": self.spins[:],\n            })\n\n        return history\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# SUMMARIZER DATA ROUTER\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass DatasetRouter:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a text dataset into segments, summarizes them, and selects\n    the segments relevant to a user prompt.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        model_name=\"sshleifer/distilbart-cnn-12-6\",\n        segment_words=900,\n        cache_file=\"segment_summaries.json\",\n        device=None,\n    ):\n        self.segment_words = segment_words\n        self.cache_file = cache_file\n\n        if device is None:\n            device = 0 if self._cuda_available() else -1\n            \n        self.device = device\n\n        print(f\"Loading summarizer: {model_name}\")\n        print(\"The model will be downloaded and cached automatically if needed.\")\n\n        self.tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)\n        self.model = AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(model_name)\n        \n        if self.device is not None and self.device >= 0:\n            self.model = self.model.to(f\"cuda:{self.device}\")\n\n        self.segments = []\n        self.summaries = []\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _cuda_available():\n        try:\n            import torch\n            return torch.cuda.is_available()\n        except ImportError:\n            return False\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def clean_text(text):\n        text = text.replace(\"\\x00\", \" \")\n        text = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", text)\n        return text.strip()\n\n    def split_text(self, text):\n        \"\"\"\n        Split on approximately segment_words words while preferring\n        sentence boundaries.\n        \"\"\"\n        text = self.clean_text(text)\n\n        if not text:\n            return []\n\n        words = text.split()\n        segments = []\n\n        for start in range(0, len(words), self.segment_words):\n            raw_segment = \" \".join(\n                words[start:start + self.segment_words]\n            )\n\n            if raw_segment:\n                segments.append(raw_segment)\n\n        return segments\n\n    def _summarize_one(self, text):\n        \"\"\"\n        Summarization models have finite input lengths. This function\n        limits the input and returns a compact segment description.\n        \"\"\"\n        words = text.split()\n\n        # DistilBART generally works best with a bounded input.\n        bounded_text = \" \".join(words[:850])\n\n        if len(bounded_text.split()) < 35:\n            return bounded_text\n\n        inputs = self.tokenizer(\n            bounded_text,\n            return_tensors=\"pt\",\n            max_length=1024,\n            truncation=True\n        )\n\n        if self.device is not None and self.device >= 0:\n            inputs = {k: v.to(f\"cuda:{self.device}\") for k, v in inputs.items()}\n\n        output_ids = self.model.generate(\n            inputs[\"input_ids\"],\n            max_length=110,\n            min_length=25,\n            do_sample=False,\n        )\n\n        return self.tokenizer.decode(output_ids[0], skip_special_tokens=True).strip()\n\n    def build_index(self, text):\n        self.segments = self.split_text(text)\n\n        if not self.segments:\n            raise ValueError(\"The dataset contains no usable text.\")\n\n        cached = self._load_cache()\n\n        summaries = []\n        changed = False\n\n        for index, segment in enumerate(self.segments):\n            segment_key = self._segment_key(segment)\n\n            if segment_key in cached:\n                summary = cached[segment_key]\n            else:\n                print(\n                    f\"Summarizing segment \"\n                    f\"{index + 1}/{len(self.segments)}...\"\n                )\n                summary = self._summarize_one(segment)\n                cached[segment_key] = summary\n                changed = True\n\n            summaries.append(summary)\n\n        self.summaries = summaries\n\n        if changed:\n            self._save_cache(cached)\n\n        print(f\"Indexed {len(self.segments)} dataset segments.\")\n\n    def select_segments(\n        self,\n        prompt,\n        max_segments=3,\n        min_similarity=0.0,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        Select dataset segments using semantic-ish lexical routing over\n        summaries. TF-IDF is deliberately local, fast, and dependency-light.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not self.summaries:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Call build_index() before select_segments().\")\n\n        prompt = self.clean_text(prompt)\n\n        prompt_summary = self._summarize_one(prompt) if len(prompt.split()) > 35 else prompt\n\n        documents = self.summaries + [prompt_summary]\n\n        vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(\n            lowercase=True,\n            stop_words=\"english\",\n            ngram_range=(1, 2),\n        )\n\n        matrix = vectorizer.fit_transform(documents)\n        similarities = cosine_similarity(\n            matrix[-1],\n            matrix[:-1],\n        )[0]\n\n        ranked = sorted(\n            enumerate(similarities),\n            key=lambda item: item[1],\n            reverse=True,\n        )\n\n        selected = [\n            (index, float(score))\n            for index, score in ranked[:max_segments]\n            if score >= min_similarity\n        ]\n\n        # Always select at least one segment.\n        if not selected:\n            selected = [ranked[0]]\n\n        return {\n            \"prompt_summary\": prompt_summary,\n            \"selected\": selected,\n            \"segments\": [\n                self.segments[index]\n                for index, _ in selected\n            ],\n            \"summaries\": [\n                self.summaries[index]\n                for index, _ in selected\n            ],\n        }\n\n    def _segment_key(self, segment):\n        import hashlib\n        return hashlib.sha256(segment.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n\n    def _load_cache(self):\n        if not os.path.exists(self.cache_file):\n            return {}\n\n        try:\n            with open(self.cache_file, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n                return json.load(file)\n        except Exception:\n            return {}\n\n    def _save_cache(self, cache):\n        with open(self.cache_file, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n            json.dump(cache, file, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GRAPH CREATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef process_text_to_trigram_graph(text, max_nodes=200):\n    \"\"\"\n    Builds a graph where nodes are bigrams and edges represent trigrams.\n    \"\"\"\n    text = text.lower()\n    words = text.split()\n\n    if len(words) < 3:\n        return {}, {}, {}\n\n    all_bigrams = [\n        (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        for i in range(len(words) - 1)\n    ]\n\n    top_bigrams = [\n        bigram\n        for bigram, _ in Counter(all_bigrams).most_common(max_nodes)\n    ]\n\n    bigram_set = set(top_bigrams)\n\n    node_to_id = {\n        bigram: index\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    id_to_node = {\n        index: bigram\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    graph = {\n        index: {}\n        for index in range(len(top_bigrams))\n    }\n\n    for i in range(len(words) - 2):\n        b1 = (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        b2 = (words[i + 1], words[i + 2])\n\n        if b1 in bigram_set and b2 in bigram_set:\n            id1 = node_to_id[b1]\n            id2 = node_to_id[b2]\n\n            if id1 != id2:\n                graph[id1][id2] = graph[id1].get(id2, 0) + 1\n                graph[id2][id1] = graph[id2].get(id1, 0) + 1\n\n    return graph, node_to_id, id_to_node\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PROMPT-AWARE MARKOV GENERATOR\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n    graph,\n    id_to_node,\n    spins,\n    prompt_vocab,\n    length=100,\n):\n    n = len(graph)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return \"\"\n\n    prompt_vocab = {\n        word.lower()\n        for word in prompt_vocab\n        if word.strip()\n    }\n\n    valid_starts = [\n        i\n        for i in range(n)\n        if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in id_to_node[i])\n    ]\n\n    current_node = (\n        random.choice(valid_starts)\n        if valid_starts\n        else random.randrange(n)\n    )\n\n    output = list(id_to_node[current_node])\n\n    for _ in range(max(0, length - 2)):\n        current_spin = spins[current_node]\n        neighbors = graph[current_node]\n        current_word_2 = id_to_node[current_node][1]\n\n        valid_neighbors = [\n            neighbor\n            for neighbor in neighbors\n            if id_to_node[neighbor][0] == current_word_2\n        ]\n\n        if not valid_neighbors:\n            fallback_nodes = [\n                i\n                for i, spin in enumerate(spins)\n                if (\n                    spin != current_spin\n                    and id_to_node[i][0] == current_word_2\n                )\n            ]\n\n            if fallback_nodes:\n                next_node = random.choice(fallback_nodes)\n            else:\n                next_node = random.randrange(n)\n        else:\n            probabilities = []\n\n            for neighbor in valid_neighbors:\n                base_weight = graph[current_node][neighbor]\n\n                cut_multiplier = (\n                    5.0\n                    if spins[neighbor] != current_spin\n                    else 1.0\n                )\n\n                neighbor_words = id_to_node[neighbor]\n\n                prompt_multiplier = (\n                    50.0\n                    if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in neighbor_words)\n                    else 1.0\n                )\n\n                score = (\n                    base_weight\n                    * cut_multiplier\n                    * prompt_multiplier\n                )\n\n                probabilities.append(score)\n\n            next_node = random.choices(\n                valid_neighbors,\n                weights=probabilities,\n                k=1,\n            )[0]\n\n        output.append(id_to_node[next_node][1])\n        current_node = next_node\n\n    return \" \".join(output)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# MAIN PROGRAM\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef load_text_file(filepath):\n    try:\n        with open(filepath, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n            return file.read()\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"File {filepath} not found. Using fallback text.\")\n\n        return (\n            \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. \"\n            \"The lazy dog barks at the brown fox. \"\n            \"The quick brown fox runs away quickly into the deep \"\n            \"dark brown forest. The dark forest is full of mystery. \"\n            \"A dog barks loudly in the dark.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef main():\n    dataset_file = input(\"Dataset filename: \").strip()\n\n    dataset_text = load_text_file(dataset_file)\n\n    router = DatasetRouter(\n        model_name=\"sshleifer/distilbart-cnn-12-6\",\n        segment_words=900,\n        cache_file=f\"{dataset_file}.summaries.json\",\n    )\n\n    print(\"Splitting and summarizing dataset...\")\n    router.build_index(dataset_text)\n\n    print(\"Building initial graph from the complete dataset...\")\n    graph, node_to_id, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\n        dataset_text,\n        max_nodes=150000,\n    )\n\n    if not graph:\n        print(\"Graph is empty. Check the dataset.\")\n        return\n\n    print(f\"Graph built with {len(graph)} unique nodes.\")\n\n    print(\"Running PCMMaxCut solver for structural baseline...\")\n\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\n        graph,\n        noise=0.00001,\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\n    )\n\n    history = solver.run(\n        iterations=5000,\n        temperature=0.0000005,\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\n    )\n\n    best_cut = max(\n        history,\n        key=lambda item: item[\"cut\"],\n    )\n\n    print(\n        f\"Base partition created. \"\n        f\"Max Cut Size: {best_cut['cut']}\\n\"\n    )\n\n    while True:\n        try:\n            user_prompt = input(\"USER: \").strip()\n        except KeyboardInterrupt:\n            print(\"\\nExiting.\")\n            break\n\n        if not user_prompt:\n            continue\n\n        if user_prompt.lower() in {\"exit\", \"quit\"}:\n            break\n\n        print(\"Routing prompt to relevant dataset segments...\")\n\n        routing = router.select_segments(\n            user_prompt,\n            max_segments=3,\n        )\n\n        print(\"\\nPrompt summary:\")\n        print(routing[\"prompt_summary\"])\n\n        print(\"\\nSelected segments:\")\n\n        for (index, score), summary in zip(\n            routing[\"selected\"],\n            routing[\"summaries\"],\n        ):\n            print(\n                f\"[Segment {index}, similarity={score:.4f}] \"\n                f\"{summary}\"\n            )\n\n        selected_text = \"\\n\".join(\n            routing[\"segments\"]\n        )\n\n        print(\"\\nBuilding prompt-specific trigram graph...\")\n\n        selected_graph, _, selected_id_to_node = (\n            process_text_to_trigram_graph(\n                selected_text,\n                max_nodes=150000,\n            )\n        )\n\n        if not selected_graph:\n            print(\n                \"Selected segments did not contain enough \"\n                \"overlapping words. Using the complete graph.\"\n            )\n\n            selected_graph = graph\n            selected_id_to_node = id_to_node\n            selected_spins = best_cut[\"spins\"]\n        else:\n            print(\n                f\"Prompt-specific graph built with \"\n                f\"{len(selected_graph)} nodes.\"\n            )\n\n            prompt_solver = PCMMaxCut(\n                selected_graph,\n                noise=0.00001,\n                drift_nu=0.00000001,\n            )\n\n            prompt_history = prompt_solver.run(\n                iterations=min(\n                    5000,\n                    max(500, len(selected_graph) * 20),\n                ),\n                temperature=0.0000005,\n                cooling=0.0000000199,\n            )\n\n            prompt_best_cut = max(\n                prompt_history,\n                key=lambda item: item[\"cut\"],\n            )\n\n            selected_spins = prompt_best_cut[\"spins\"]\n\n        final_text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n            selected_graph,\n            selected_id_to_node,\n            selected_spins,\n            user_prompt.split(),\n            length=400,\n        )\n\n        print(\"\\nGenerated Output:\")\n        print(f\"> {final_text.capitalize()}.\\n\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()"}], "files": [{"file_uuid": "e93ad02a-ef4c-4e3a-91f0-0ab042ff3acd", "file_name": ""}], "parent_message_uuid": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000"}, {"uuid": "01a0fc06-c75c-7218-a897-f3dbf838ed09", "text": "I read this as: slice the prompt into word windows, embed each slice with GloVe, and measure the Manhattan (L1) distance from each slice to every dataset segment summary. The distance peaks pick the segments to use, each slice's vocabulary is expanded with GloVe neighbours that exist in your data, and each slice's generated text is printed in its own column. The module below leaves `PCMMaxCut` and the graph and generator code untouched.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nTo wire it into your script, put `glove_slicer.py` next to it and make three edits (it also needs `pip install gensim`).\n\n**1. Import at the top:**\n```python\nfrom glove_slicer import GloveSlicer, glove_route_and_generate\n```\n\n**2. In `main()`, right after `router.build_index(dataset_text)`:**\n```python\nslicer = GloveSlicer()                      # or GloveSlicer(glove_path=\"glove.6B.100d.txt\")\nslicer.index_segments(router.summaries)\n```\n\n**3. In the `while True` loop, replace everything from `print(\"Routing prompt...\")` down to the `print(f\"> {final_text...\")` line with:**\n```python\nglove_route_and_generate(\n    user_prompt,\n    router,\n    slicer,\n    graph_builder=process_text_to_trigram_graph,\n    solver_cls=PCMMaxCut,\n    generator=generate_markovian_prompt_text,\n    width=2,          # words per slice\n    max_segments=3,\n    length=60,\n)\n```\n\n**What it does:**\n- **Splicing:** the prompt loses its stopwords and is cut into sliding windows of `width` words. Slices GloVe doesn't know are dropped, and at most 4 are kept so the columns stay readable.\n- **Manhattan distance:** each slice and each segment summary is a unit-normalised mean GloVe vector, and the L1 distance is computed for every slice and segment pair.\n- **Peak probing:** along the segment axis, a peak is a local minimum of distance that is at least 0.5 standard deviations better than that slice's average. The segments with the most slice votes, then the best distance, feed your existing graph and solver.\n- **Unstacking:** a table prints with segments as rows and slices as columns, marking peaks with `*` and selected segments with `>`. After it come the generated texts, one column per slice.\n- **Accommodating vocabulary:** each slice's vocabulary is its own words plus up to 8 GloVe neighbours that actually occur in the dataset. Graph nodes keep punctuation (`\"dog.\"`), so the module maps clean words to those raw forms before passing them to `prompt_vocab`. Without that mapping, the 50x prompt bias would silently miss them.\n\nI assumed \"unstack side by side\" meant parallel output columns. If you meant something else, such as a pandas-style `unstack()` of the distance table, that is a small change to `print_distance_table`.\n\nI also noticed that your `cooling=0.0000000199` multiplies the temperature by almost zero on the first step, so the solver is effectively running at about zero temperature. That is probably worth a look, though I left it as is.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:51:37.818918Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:52:05.562191Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Untangling a request full of unfamiliar coding jargon."}, {"summary": "Designing embedding-based slicing and peak-distance scoring scheme."}, {"summary": "Working out nearest-neighbor vocabulary expansion and peak selection."}, {"summary": "Matching clean vocabulary to raw graph tokens with punctuation."}, {"summary": "Computing distance matrices and flagging peak similarity scores."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:52:05.562220Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:52:06.728031Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I read this as: slice the prompt into word windows, embed each slice with GloVe, and measure the Manhattan (L1) distance from each slice to every dataset segment summary. The distance peaks pick the segments to use, each slice's vocabulary is expanded with GloVe neighbours that exist in your data, and each slice's generated text is printed in its own column. The module below leaves `PCMMaxCut` and the graph and generator code untouched.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:52:06.728059Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:52:27.295565Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01LHEVNfca9YvS7QGC3PXKtQ", "name": "create_file", "input": {"description": "Add-on module: GloVe prompt slicing, Manhattan-distance peak probing, vocab expansion, side-by-side output", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/glove_slicer.py", "file_text": "\"\"\"\nglove_slicer.py\n\nPrompt-GloVe splicing for the PCMMaxCut dataset router.\n\nPipeline\n  1. Slice the prompt into sliding windows of content words.\n  2. Embed every slice (and every segment summary) with GloVe.\n  3. Compute the Manhattan (L1) distance slice -> segment.\n  4. Probe the peaks (distance minima = similarity peaks) per slice.\n  5. Expand each slice's vocabulary with GloVe neighbours that actually\n     occur in the dataset graph.\n  6. Generate one text per slice and print them side by side.\n\nRequires: numpy, gensim (pip install gensim)\n\"\"\"\n\nimport re\nimport textwrap\nfrom itertools import zip_longest\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\n\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[a-z']+\")\n\n\ndef tokenize(text):\n    return TOKEN_RE.findall(text.lower())\n\n\ndef clean_word(word):\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z']\", \"\", word.lower())\n\n\nclass GloveSlicer:\n    def __init__(self, glove_name=\"glove-wiki-gigaword-100\", glove_path=None):\n        \"\"\"\n        glove_path: optional local GloVe .txt file (e.g. glove.6B.100d.txt).\n        Otherwise gensim downloads `glove_name` once and caches it.\n        \"\"\"\n        if glove_path:\n            from gensim.models import KeyedVectors\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe from {glove_path}\")\n            self.kv = KeyedVectors.load_word2vec_format(\n                glove_path, binary=False, no_header=True\n            )\n        else:\n            import gensim.downloader as api\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe: {glove_name} (cached after first download)\")\n            self.kv = api.load(glove_name)\n\n        self.dim = self.kv.vector_size\n        self.seg_vecs = None\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # embedding\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def embed(self, tokens):\n        vecs = [self.kv[t] for t in tokens if t in self.kv]\n        if not vecs:\n            return None\n        v = np.mean(vecs, axis=0)\n        norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n        return v / norm if norm > 0 else None\n\n    def index_segments(self, summaries):\n        self.seg_vecs = [self.embed(tokenize(s)) for s in summaries]\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # slicing\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def slice_prompt(self, prompt, width=2, stride=1):\n        tokens = [t for t in tokenize(prompt) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\n        if not tokens:\n            tokens = tokenize(prompt)\n\n        if len(tokens) <= width:\n            windows = [tokens]\n        else:\n            windows = [\n                tokens[i:i + width]\n                for i in range(0, len(tokens) - width + 1, stride)\n            ]\n\n        # Drop slices GloVe knows nothing about.\n        return [(w, self.embed(w)) for w in windows if self.embed(w) is not None]\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Manhattan distance + peak probing\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    @staticmethod\n    def manhattan(a, b):\n        return float(np.abs(a - b).sum())\n\n    def distance_matrix(self, slices):\n        \"\"\"Shape: (n_slices, n_segments). inf where a summary has no vectors.\"\"\"\n        if self.seg_vecs is None:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Call index_segments() first.\")\n\n        matrix = np.full((len(slices), len(self.seg_vecs)), np.inf)\n        for i, (_, svec) in enumerate(slices):\n            for j, gvec in enumerate(self.seg_vecs):\n                if gvec is not None:\n                    matrix[i, j] = self.manhattan(svec, gvec)\n        return matrix\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def find_peaks(distances, prominence=0.5):\n        \"\"\"\n        Peaks of similarity (= local minima of distance) along the segment\n        axis that stand out from the slice's average by `prominence` stds.\n        Always returns at least the global best segment.\n        \"\"\"\n        score = -np.asarray(distances, dtype=float)\n        finite = np.isfinite(score)\n        if not finite.any():\n            return []\n\n        mean = score[finite].mean()\n        std = score[finite].std()\n        threshold = mean + prominence * std\n\n        peaks = []\n        for s in range(len(score)):\n            if not finite[s]:\n                continue\n            left = score[s - 1] if s > 0 else -np.inf\n            right = score[s + 1] if s < len(score) - 1 else -np.inf\n            if score[s] >= left and score[s] >= right and score[s] >= threshold:\n                peaks.append(s)\n\n        if not peaks:\n            peaks = [int(np.argmax(np.where(finite, score, -np.inf)))]\n        return peaks\n\n    def select_peak_segments(self, matrix, max_segments=3):\n        \"\"\"Rank segments by how many slices peak there, then by best distance.\"\"\"\n        votes, best = {}, {}\n        all_peaks = []\n        for row in matrix:\n            peaks = self.find_peaks(row)\n            all_peaks.append(peaks)\n            for p in peaks:\n                votes[p] = votes.get(p, 0) + 1\n                best[p] = min(best.get(p, np.inf), row[p])\n\n        ranked = sorted(votes, key=lambda p: (-votes[p], best[p]))\n        return ranked[:max_segments], all_peaks\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # accommodating vocabulary\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    def expand_vocab(self, slice_tokens, svec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\n        \"\"\"\n        Slice words plus the nearest GloVe neighbours that also exist in\n        the dataset (so the Markov walk can actually reach them).\n        \"\"\"\n        vocab = set(slice_tokens)\n        added = 0\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(svec, topn=topn):\n            if word in dataset_vocab and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS:\n                vocab.add(word)\n                added += 1\n                if added >= keep:\n                    break\n        return vocab\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# helpers\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node):\n    \"\"\"\n    Graph nodes keep raw whitespace tokens (\"dog.\", \"fox,\"), so map each\n    cleaned word to every raw form present in the graph.\n    \"\"\"\n    clean_to_raw = {}\n    for pair in id_to_node.values():\n        for raw in pair:\n            clean_to_raw.setdefault(clean_word(raw), set()).add(raw.lower())\n    return clean_to_raw\n\n\ndef to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw):\n    raw = set()\n    for w in clean_vocab:\n        raw.update(clean_to_raw.get(w, {w}))\n    return raw\n\n\ndef print_distance_table(slices, matrix, all_peaks, selected):\n    labels = [\" \".join(t)[:14] for t, _ in slices]\n    col = 16\n    print(\"\\nManhattan distance (slice x segment)  [*] = peak  [>] = selected\")\n    print(\"seg    \" + \"\".join(l.ljust(col) for l in labels))\n    for s in range(matrix.shape[1]):\n        row = f\"{('>' if s in selected else ' ')}{s:<5} \"\n        for i in range(matrix.shape[0]):\n            d = matrix[i, s]\n            cell = \"n/a\" if not np.isfinite(d) else f\"{d:.3f}\"\n            if s in all_peaks[i]:\n                cell += \" *\"\n            row += cell.ljust(col)\n        print(row)\n\n\ndef render_side_by_side(columns, total_width=118, gap=3):\n    \"\"\"\n    columns: list of (header, text). Unstacks them into parallel columns.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(columns)\n    width = max(18, (total_width - gap * (n - 1)) // n)\n    wrapped = [textwrap.wrap(text, width) for _, text in columns]\n\n    lines = [(\" \" * gap).join(h[:width].ljust(width) for h, _ in columns)]\n    lines.append((\" \" * gap).join(\"-\" * width for _ in columns))\n    for parts in zip_longest(*wrapped, fillvalue=\"\"):\n        lines.append((\" \" * gap).join(p.ljust(width) for p in parts))\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# main entry point used by main()\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef glove_route_and_generate(\n    prompt,\n    router,\n    slicer,\n    graph_builder,      # process_text_to_trigram_graph\n    solver_cls,         # PCMMaxCut\n    generator,          # generate_markovian_prompt_text\n    width=2,\n    max_segments=3,\n    length=60,\n    max_columns=4,\n):\n    slices = slicer.slice_prompt(prompt, width=width)\n    if not slices:\n        print(\"GloVe knows none of the prompt words; no slices to probe.\")\n        return None\n\n    # Keep the output readable: cap the number of side-by-side columns.\n    if len(slices) > max_columns:\n        step = len(slices) / max_columns\n        slices = [slices[int(i * step)] for i in range(max_columns)]\n\n    matrix = slicer.distance_matrix(slices)\n    selected, all_peaks = slicer.select_peak_segments(matrix, max_segments)\n    print_distance_table(slices, matrix, all_peaks, selected)\n\n    selected_text = \"\\n\".join(router.segments[i] for i in sorted(selected))\n    graph, _, id_to_node = graph_builder(selected_text, max_nodes=150000)\n\n    if not graph:\n        print(\"Peak segments too small for a graph.\")\n        return None\n\n    solver = solver_cls(graph, noise=0.00001, drift_nu=0.00000001)\n    history = solver.run(\n        iterations=min(5000, max(500, len(graph) * 20)),\n        temperature=0.0000005,\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\n    )\n    spins = max(history, key=lambda h: h[\"cut\"])[\"spins\"]\n\n    clean_to_raw = dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node)\n    dataset_vocab = set(clean_to_raw)\n\n    columns = []\n    for tokens, svec in slices:\n        clean_vocab = slicer.expand_vocab(tokens, svec, dataset_vocab)\n        raw_vocab = to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw)\n        text = generator(graph, id_to_node, spins, raw_vocab, length=length)\n        header = f\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] +{len(clean_vocab) - len(tokens)} words\"\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \".\"))\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated output (one column per prompt slice):\\n\")\n    print(render_side_by_side(columns))\n    print()\n    return columns\n"}, "message": "Add-on module: GloVe prompt slicing, Manhattan-distance peak probing, vocab expansion, side-by-side output", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nglove_slicer.py\\n\\nPrompt-GloVe splicing for the PCMMaxCut dataset router.\\n\\nPipeline\\n  1. Slice the prompt into sliding windows of content words.\\n  2. Embed every slice (and every segment summary) with GloVe.\\n  3. Compute the Manhattan (L1) distance slice -> segment.\\n  4. Probe the peaks (distance minima = similarity peaks) per slice.\\n  5. Expand each slice's vocabulary with GloVe neighbours that actually\\n     occur in the dataset graph.\\n  6. Generate one text per slice and print them side by side.\\n\\nRequires: numpy, gensim (pip install gensim)\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport re\\nimport textwrap\\nfrom itertools import zip_longest\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\\n\\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\\\"[a-z']+\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef tokenize(text):\\n    return TOKEN_RE.findall(text.lower())\\n\\n\\ndef clean_word(word):\\n    return re.sub(r\\\"[^a-z']\\\", \\\"\\\", word.lower())\\n\\n\\nclass GloveSlicer:\\n    def __init__(self, glove_name=\\\"glove-wiki-gigaword-100\\\", glove_path=None):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        glove_path: optional local GloVe .txt file (e.g. glove.6B.100d.txt).\\n        Otherwise gensim downloads `glove_name` once and caches it.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if glove_path:\\n            from gensim.models import KeyedVectors\\n            print(f\\\"Loading GloVe from {glove_path}\\\")\\n            self.kv = KeyedVectors.load_word2vec_format(\\n                glove_path, binary=False, no_header=True\\n            )\\n        else:\\n            import gensim.downloader as api\\n            print(f\\\"Loading GloVe: {glove_name} (cached after first download)\\\")\\n            self.kv = api.load(glove_name)\\n\\n        self.dim = self.kv.vector_size\\n        self.seg_vecs = None\\n\\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    # embedding\\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    def embed(self, tokens):\\n        vecs = [self.kv[t] for t in tokens if t in self.kv]\\n        if not vecs:\\n            return None\\n        v = np.mean(vecs, axis=0)\\n        norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\\n        return v / norm if norm > 0 else None\\n\\n    def index_segments(self, summaries):\\n        self.seg_vecs = [self.embed(tokenize(s)) for s in summaries]\\n\\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    # slicing\\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    def slice_prompt(self, prompt, width=2, stride=1):\\n        tokens = [t for t in tokenize(prompt) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\\n        if not tokens:\\n            tokens = tokenize(prompt)\\n\\n        if len(tokens) <= width:\\n            windows = [tokens]\\n        else:\\n            windows = [\\n                tokens[i:i + width]\\n                for i in range(0, len(tokens) - width + 1, stride)\\n            ]\\n\\n        # Drop slices GloVe knows nothing about.\\n        return [(w, self.embed(w)) for w in windows if self.embed(w) is not None]\\n\\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    # Manhattan distance + peak probing\\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def manhattan(a, b):\\n        return float(np.abs(a - b).sum())\\n\\n    def distance_matrix(self, slices):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Shape: (n_slices, n_segments). inf where a summary has no vectors.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if self.seg_vecs is None:\\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"Call index_segments() first.\\\")\\n\\n        matrix = np.full((len(slices), len(self.seg_vecs)), np.inf)\\n        for i, (_, svec) in enumerate(slices):\\n            for j, gvec in enumerate(self.seg_vecs):\\n                if gvec is not None:\\n                    matrix[i, j] = self.manhattan(svec, gvec)\\n        return matrix\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def find_peaks(distances, prominence=0.5):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Peaks of similarity (= local minima of distance) along the segment\\n        axis that stand out from the slice's average by `prominence` stds.\\n        Always returns at least the global best segment.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        score = -np.asarray(distances, dtype=float)\\n        finite = np.isfinite(score)\\n        if not finite.any():\\n            return []\\n\\n        mean = score[finite].mean()\\n        std = score[finite].std()\\n        threshold = mean + prominence * std\\n\\n        peaks = []\\n        for s in range(len(score)):\\n            if not finite[s]:\\n                continue\\n            left = score[s - 1] if s > 0 else -np.inf\\n            right = score[s + 1] if s < len(score) - 1 else -np.inf\\n            if score[s] >= left and score[s] >= right and score[s] >= threshold:\\n                peaks.append(s)\\n\\n        if not peaks:\\n            peaks = [int(np.argmax(np.where(finite, score, -np.inf)))]\\n        return peaks\\n\\n    def select_peak_segments(self, matrix, max_segments=3):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Rank segments by how many slices peak there, then by best distance.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        votes, best = {}, {}\\n        all_peaks = []\\n        for row in matrix:\\n            peaks = self.find_peaks(row)\\n            all_peaks.append(peaks)\\n            for p in peaks:\\n                votes[p] = votes.get(p, 0) + 1\\n                best[p] = min(best.get(p, np.inf), row[p])\\n\\n        ranked = sorted(votes, key=lambda p: (-votes[p], best[p]))\\n        return ranked[:max_segments], all_peaks\\n\\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    # accommodating vocabulary\\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\\n    def expand_vocab(self, slice_tokens, svec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Slice words plus the nearest GloVe neighbours that also exist in\\n        the dataset (so the Markov walk can actually reach them).\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        vocab = set(slice_tokens)\\n        added = 0\\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(svec, topn=topn):\\n            if word in dataset_vocab and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS:\\n                vocab.add(word)\\n                added += 1\\n                if added >= keep:\\n                    break\\n        return vocab\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# helpers\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Graph nodes keep raw whitespace tokens (\\\"dog.\\\", \\\"fox,\\\"), so map each\\n    cleaned word to every raw form present in the graph.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    clean_to_raw = {}\\n    for pair in id_to_node.values():\\n        for raw in pair:\\n            clean_to_raw.setdefault(clean_word(raw), set()).add(raw.lower())\\n    return clean_to_raw\\n\\n\\ndef to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw):\\n    raw = set()\\n    for w in clean_vocab:\\n        raw.update(clean_to_raw.get(w, {w}))\\n    return raw\\n\\n\\ndef print_distance_table(slices, matrix, all_peaks, selected):\\n    labels = [\\\" \\\".join(t)[:14] for t, _ in slices]\\n    col = 16\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nManhattan distance (slice x segment)  [*] = peak  [>] = selected\\\")\\n    print(\\\"seg    \\\" + \\\"\\\".join(l.ljust(col) for l in labels))\\n    for s in range(matrix.shape[1]):\\n        row = f\\\"{('>' if s in selected else ' ')}{s:<5} \\\"\\n        for i in range(matrix.shape[0]):\\n            d = matrix[i, s]\\n            cell = \\\"n/a\\\" if not np.isfinite(d) else f\\\"{d:.3f}\\\"\\n            if s in all_peaks[i]:\\n                cell += \\\" *\\\"\\n            row += cell.ljust(col)\\n        print(row)\\n\\n\\ndef render_side_by_side(columns, total_width=118, gap=3):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    columns: list of (header, text). Unstacks them into parallel columns.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    n = len(columns)\\n    width = max(18, (total_width - gap * (n - 1)) // n)\\n    wrapped = [textwrap.wrap(text, width) for _, text in columns]\\n\\n    lines = [(\\\" \\\" * gap).join(h[:width].ljust(width) for h, _ in columns)]\\n    lines.append((\\\" \\\" * gap).join(\\\"-\\\" * width for _ in columns))\\n    for parts in zip_longest(*wrapped, fillvalue=\\\"\\\"):\\n        lines.append((\\\" \\\" * gap).join(p.ljust(width) for p in parts))\\n    return \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines)\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# main entry point used by main()\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef glove_route_and_generate(\\n    prompt,\\n    router,\\n    slicer,\\n    graph_builder,      # process_text_to_trigram_graph\\n    solver_cls,         # PCMMaxCut\\n    generator,          # generate_markovian_prompt_text\\n    width=2,\\n    max_segments=3,\\n    length=60,\\n    max_columns=4,\\n):\\n    slices = slicer.slice_prompt(prompt, width=width)\\n    if not slices:\\n        print(\\\"GloVe knows none of the prompt words; no slices to probe.\\\")\\n        return None\\n\\n    # Keep the output readable: cap the number of side-by-side columns.\\n    if len(slices) > max_columns:\\n        step = len(slices) / max_columns\\n        slices = [slices[int(i * step)] for i in range(max_columns)]\\n\\n    matrix = slicer.distance_matrix(slices)\\n    selected, all_peaks = slicer.select_peak_segments(matrix, max_segments)\\n    print_distance_table(slices, matrix, all_peaks, selected)\\n\\n    selected_text = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(router.segments[i] for i in sorted(selected))\\n    graph, _, id_to_node = graph_builder(selected_text, max_nodes=150000)\\n\\n    if not graph:\\n        print(\\\"Peak segments too small for a graph.\\\")\\n        return None\\n\\n    solver = solver_cls(graph, noise=0.00001, drift_nu=0.00000001)\\n    history = solver.run(\\n        iterations=min(5000, max(500, len(graph) * 20)),\\n        temperature=0.0000005,\\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\\n    )\\n    spins = max(history, key=lambda h: h[\\\"cut\\\"])[\\\"spins\\\"]\\n\\n    clean_to_raw = dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node)\\n    dataset_vocab = set(clean_to_raw)\\n\\n    columns = []\\n    for tokens, svec in slices:\\n        clean_vocab = slicer.expand_vocab(tokens, svec, dataset_vocab)\\n        raw_vocab = to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw)\\n        text = generator(graph, id_to_node, spins, raw_vocab, length=length)\\n        header = f\\\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] +{len(clean_vocab) - len(tokens)} words\\\"\\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \\\".\\\"))\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nGenerated output (one column per prompt slice):\\\\n\\\")\\n    print(render_side_by_side(columns))\\n    print()\\n    return columns\\n\", \"filename\": \"/mnt/user-data/outputs/glove_slicer.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:52:28.468605Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:52:28.468651Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01LHEVNfca9YvS7QGC3PXKtQ", "name": "create_file", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/glove_slicer.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/glove_slicer.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:52:29.957765Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:52:30.199354Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Gd3yXkpqvNDn2wGmn14EHG", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/glove_slicer.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/glove_slicer.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:52:30.219922Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:52:30.219944Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Gd3yXkpqvNDn2wGmn14EHG", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/glove_slicer.py", "name": "glove slicer", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:52:36.449425Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:52:37.804693Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "To wire it into your script, put `glove_slicer.py` next to it and make three edits (it also needs `pip install gensim`).\n\n**1. Import at the top:**\n```python\nfrom glove_slicer import GloveSlicer, glove_route_and_generate\n```\n\n**2. In `main()`, right after `router.build_index(dataset_text)`:**\n```python\nslicer = GloveSlicer()                      # or GloveSlicer(glove_path=\"glove.6B.100d.txt\")\nslicer.index_segments(router.summaries)\n```\n\n**3. In the `while True` loop, replace everything from `print(\"Routing prompt...\")` down to the `print(f\"> {final_text...\")` line with:**\n```python\nglove_route_and_generate(\n    user_prompt,\n    router,\n    slicer,\n    graph_builder=process_text_to_trigram_graph,\n    solver_cls=PCMMaxCut,\n    generator=generate_markovian_prompt_text,\n    width=2,          # words per slice\n    max_segments=3,\n    length=60,\n)\n```\n\n**What it does:**\n- **Splicing:** the prompt loses its stopwords and is cut into sliding windows of `width` words. Slices GloVe doesn't know are dropped, and at most 4 are kept so the columns stay readable.\n- **Manhattan distance:** each slice and each segment summary is a unit-normalised mean GloVe vector, and the L1 distance is computed for every slice and segment pair.\n- **Peak probing:** along the segment axis, a peak is a local minimum of distance that is at least 0.5 standard deviations better than that slice's average. The segments with the most slice votes, then the best distance, feed your existing graph and solver.\n- **Unstacking:** a table prints with segments as rows and slices as columns, marking peaks with `*` and selected segments with `>`. After it come the generated texts, one column per slice.\n- **Accommodating vocabulary:** each slice's vocabulary is its own words plus up to 8 GloVe neighbours that actually occur in the dataset. Graph nodes keep punctuation (`\"dog.\"`), so the module maps clean words to those raw forms before passing them to `prompt_vocab`. Without that mapping, the 50x prompt bias would silently miss them.\n\nI assumed \"unstack side by side\" meant parallel output columns. If you meant something else, such as a pandas-style `unstack()` of the distance table, that is a small change to `print_distance_table`.\n\nI also noticed that your `cooling=0.0000000199` multiplies the temperature by almost zero on the first step, so the solver is effectively running at about zero temperature. That is probably worth a look, though I left it as is.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T09:52:37.878693Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T09:52:37.878693Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fc06-c75c-71f5-841f-5621e4b381c9"}, {"uuid": "01a0fc08-5a98-7fbe-919e-b55cf1e2fe06", "text": "do the full code", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:53:20.165849Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:53:20.165849Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "do the full code", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T09:53:20.166058Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T09:53:20.166058Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fc06-c75c-7218-a897-f3dbf838ed09"}, {"uuid": "01a0fc08-5a98-7d35-991a-6608b33bf13e", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n`pcm_glove_full.py` is now one self-contained script with the GloVe slicing merged in. It passes a syntax check, but I haven't run it end to end, since that needs the summarizer and GloVe downloads.\n\n- **Solver:** `PCMMaxCut` is unchanged.\n- **Routing:** each prompt goes through the GloVe slice, Manhattan distance and peak pipeline from before, then the distance table and side-by-side columns.\n- **Fallback:** if `gensim` isn't installed, GloVe fails to load, or a prompt has no GloVe-known words, the original TF-IDF flow runs instead.\n- **Setup:** you need `pip install gensim`. At startup it asks for a local GloVe `.txt` path, or you can leave it blank to download `glove-wiki-gigaword-100` once.\n- **Small changes:** I added a `solve_best_spins()` helper so the solver setup isn't repeated. Ctrl-D now exits cleanly like Ctrl-C.\n\nThe solver parameters still make the cooling effectively instant (`cooling=0.0000000199`), so it runs at about zero temperature. I left that as is, but it's the first place to look if the partitions seem poor.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:53:20.159296Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:53:24.232036Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Merging the full script into one complete integrated file."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:53:24.232141Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:54:08.248323Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Ryh7eoT89u9fc5NZ78831k", "name": "create_file", "input": {"description": "Full merged script: original solver + router + graph + generator + GloVe slicing/Manhattan peak probing/side-by-side output", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py", "file_text": "import hashlib\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nimport random\nimport re\nimport textwrap\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom itertools import zip_longest\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer, ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\nfrom sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\n\n# gensim provides the GloVe vectors. If it is missing, the program falls\n# back to the original TF-IDF routing.\ntry:\n    from gensim.models import KeyedVectors\n    import gensim.downloader as gensim_api\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = False\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# ORIGINAL SOLVER KEPT EXACTLY THE SAME\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass PCMMaxCut:\n    def __init__(self, graph, noise=0.02, drift_nu=0.08):\n        self.graph = graph\n        self.n = len(graph)\n        self.noise = noise\n        self.drift_nu = drift_nu\n        self.spins = [random.choice([-1, 1]) for _ in range(self.n)]\n        self.age = 1\n\n    def local_field(self, i):\n        return sum(\n            weight * self.spins[j]\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items()\n        )\n\n    def delta_energy(self, i):\n        return -2 * self.spins[i] * self.local_field(i)\n\n    def energy(self):\n        value = 0.0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i:\n                    value += weight * self.spins[i] * self.spins[j]\n        return value\n\n    def cut_size(self):\n        total = 0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i and self.spins[i] != self.spins[j]:\n                    total += weight\n        return total\n\n    def pcm_flip_attempt(self, temperature):\n        i = random.randrange(self.n)\n        delta = self.delta_energy(i)\n\n        drift = self.age ** (-self.drift_nu)\n        thermal_noise = random.gauss(\n            0.0,\n            self.noise\n        ) * max(1.0, abs(self.local_field(i)))\n\n        effective_delta = delta + thermal_noise * drift\n\n        if effective_delta <= 0:\n            accept = True\n        else:\n            accept = random.random() < math.exp(\n                -effective_delta / max(temperature, 1e-9)\n            )\n\n        if accept:\n            self.spins[i] *= -1\n            return i, True, delta\n\n        return i, False, delta\n\n    def run(self, iterations=1000, temperature=1.0, cooling=0.995):\n        history = []\n\n        for _ in range(iterations):\n            _, accepted, _ = self.pcm_flip_attempt(temperature)\n\n            temperature *= cooling\n            self.age += 1\n\n            history.append({\n                \"energy\": self.energy(),\n                \"cut\": self.cut_size(),\n                \"accepted\": accepted,\n                \"temperature\": temperature,\n                \"spins\": self.spins[:],\n            })\n\n        return history\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# SUMMARIZER DATA ROUTER\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass DatasetRouter:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a text dataset into segments, summarizes them, and selects\n    the segments relevant to a user prompt.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        model_name=\"sshleifer/distilbart-cnn-12-6\",\n        segment_words=900,\n        cache_file=\"segment_summaries.json\",\n        device=None,\n    ):\n        self.segment_words = segment_words\n        self.cache_file = cache_file\n\n        if device is None:\n            device = 0 if self._cuda_available() else -1\n\n        self.device = device\n\n        print(f\"Loading summarizer: {model_name}\")\n        print(\"The model will be downloaded and cached automatically if needed.\")\n\n        self.tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)\n        self.model = AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(model_name)\n\n        if self.device is not None and self.device >= 0:\n            self.model = self.model.to(f\"cuda:{self.device}\")\n\n        self.segments = []\n        self.summaries = []\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _cuda_available():\n        try:\n            return torch.cuda.is_available()\n        except Exception:\n            return False\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def clean_text(text):\n        text = text.replace(\"\\x00\", \" \")\n        text = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", text)\n        return text.strip()\n\n    def split_text(self, text):\n        \"\"\"\n        Split on approximately segment_words words.\n        \"\"\"\n        text = self.clean_text(text)\n\n        if not text:\n            return []\n\n        words = text.split()\n        segments = []\n\n        for start in range(0, len(words), self.segment_words):\n            raw_segment = \" \".join(\n                words[start:start + self.segment_words]\n            )\n\n            if raw_segment:\n                segments.append(raw_segment)\n\n        return segments\n\n    def _summarize_one(self, text):\n        \"\"\"\n        Summarization models have finite input lengths. This function\n        limits the input and returns a compact segment description.\n        \"\"\"\n        words = text.split()\n\n        # DistilBART generally works best with a bounded input.\n        bounded_text = \" \".join(words[:850])\n\n        if len(bounded_text.split()) < 35:\n            return bounded_text\n\n        inputs = self.tokenizer(\n            bounded_text,\n            return_tensors=\"pt\",\n            max_length=1024,\n            truncation=True\n        )\n\n        if self.device is not None and self.device >= 0:\n            inputs = {k: v.to(f\"cuda:{self.device}\") for k, v in inputs.items()}\n\n        output_ids = self.model.generate(\n            inputs[\"input_ids\"],\n            max_length=110,\n            min_length=25,\n            do_sample=False,\n        )\n\n        return self.tokenizer.decode(output_ids[0], skip_special_tokens=True).strip()\n\n    def build_index(self, text):\n        self.segments = self.split_text(text)\n\n        if not self.segments:\n            raise ValueError(\"The dataset contains no usable text.\")\n\n        cached = self._load_cache()\n\n        summaries = []\n        changed = False\n\n        for index, segment in enumerate(self.segments):\n            segment_key = self._segment_key(segment)\n\n            if segment_key in cached:\n                summary = cached[segment_key]\n            else:\n                print(\n                    f\"Summarizing segment \"\n                    f\"{index + 1}/{len(self.segments)}...\"\n                )\n                summary = self._summarize_one(segment)\n                cached[segment_key] = summary\n                changed = True\n\n            summaries.append(summary)\n\n        self.summaries = summaries\n\n        if changed:\n            self._save_cache(cached)\n\n        print(f\"Indexed {len(self.segments)} dataset segments.\")\n\n    def select_segments(\n        self,\n        prompt,\n        max_segments=3,\n        min_similarity=0.0,\n    ):\n        \"\"\"\n        TF-IDF routing over summaries (fallback when GloVe is unavailable).\n        \"\"\"\n        if not self.summaries:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Call build_index() before select_segments().\")\n\n        prompt = self.clean_text(prompt)\n\n        prompt_summary = self._summarize_one(prompt) if len(prompt.split()) > 35 else prompt\n\n        documents = self.summaries + [prompt_summary]\n\n        vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(\n            lowercase=True,\n            stop_words=\"english\",\n            ngram_range=(1, 2),\n        )\n\n        matrix = vectorizer.fit_transform(documents)\n        similarities = cosine_similarity(\n            matrix[-1],\n            matrix[:-1],\n        )[0]\n\n        ranked = sorted(\n            enumerate(similarities),\n            key=lambda item: item[1],\n            reverse=True,\n        )\n\n        selected = [\n            (index, float(score))\n            for index, score in ranked[:max_segments]\n            if score >= min_similarity\n        ]\n\n        # Always select at least one segment.\n        if not selected:\n            selected = [ranked[0]]\n\n        return {\n            \"prompt_summary\": prompt_summary,\n            \"selected\": selected,\n            \"segments\": [\n                self.segments[index]\n                for index, _ in selected\n            ],\n            \"summaries\": [\n                self.summaries[index]\n                for index, _ in selected\n            ],\n        }\n\n    def _segment_key(self, segment):\n        return hashlib.sha256(segment.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n\n    def _load_cache(self):\n        if not os.path.exists(self.cache_file):\n            return {}\n\n        try:\n            with open(self.cache_file, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n                return json.load(file)\n        except Exception:\n            return {}\n\n    def _save_cache(self, cache):\n        with open(self.cache_file, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n            json.dump(cache, file, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GLOVE PROMPT SLICER\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[a-z']+\")\n\n\ndef tokenize(text):\n    return TOKEN_RE.findall(text.lower())\n\n\ndef clean_word(word):\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z']\", \"\", word.lower())\n\n\nclass GloveSlicer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Slices a prompt into word windows, embeds each slice with GloVe,\n    measures the Manhattan (L1) distance to every segment summary, probes\n    the similarity peaks, and expands each slice's vocabulary with GloVe\n    neighbours that exist in the dataset.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, glove_name=\"glove-wiki-gigaword-100\", glove_path=None):\n        if glove_path:\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe from {glove_path}\")\n            self.kv = KeyedVectors.load_word2vec_format(\n                glove_path, binary=False, no_header=True\n            )\n        else:\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe: {glove_name} (cached after first download)\")\n            self.kv = gensim_api.load(glove_name)\n\n        self.dim = self.kv.vector_size\n        self.seg_vecs = None\n\n    # -- embedding -----------------------------------------------------\n\n    def embed(self, tokens):\n        vecs = [self.kv[t] for t in tokens if t in self.kv]\n        if not vecs:\n            return None\n        v = np.mean(vecs, axis=0)\n        norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n        return v / norm if norm > 0 else None\n\n    def index_segments(self, summaries):\n        self.seg_vecs = [self.embed(tokenize(s)) for s in summaries]\n\n    # -- slicing -------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def slice_prompt(self, prompt, width=2, stride=1):\n        tokens = [t for t in tokenize(prompt) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\n        if not tokens:\n            tokens = tokenize(prompt)\n\n        if len(tokens) <= width:\n            windows = [tokens]\n        else:\n            windows = [\n                tokens[i:i + width]\n                for i in range(0, len(tokens) - width + 1, stride)\n            ]\n\n        slices = []\n        for window in windows:\n            vec = self.embed(window)\n            if vec is not None:\n                slices.append((window, vec))\n        return slices\n\n    # -- Manhattan distance and peaks ----------------------------------\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def manhattan(a, b):\n        return float(np.abs(a - b).sum())\n\n    def distance_matrix(self, slices):\n        \"\"\"Shape (n_slices, n_segments); inf where a summary has no vector.\"\"\"\n        if self.seg_vecs is None:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Call index_segments() first.\")\n\n        matrix = np.full((len(slices), len(self.seg_vecs)), np.inf)\n        for i, (_, slice_vec) in enumerate(slices):\n            for j, seg_vec in enumerate(self.seg_vecs):\n                if seg_vec is not None:\n                    matrix[i, j] = self.manhattan(slice_vec, seg_vec)\n        return matrix\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def find_peaks(distances, prominence=0.5):\n        \"\"\"\n        Similarity peaks (= local distance minima along the segment axis)\n        at least `prominence` standard deviations above the slice average.\n        Always returns at least the single best segment.\n        \"\"\"\n        score = -np.asarray(distances, dtype=float)\n        finite = np.isfinite(score)\n        if not finite.any():\n            return []\n\n        threshold = score[finite].mean() + prominence * score[finite].std()\n\n        peaks = []\n        for s in range(len(score)):\n            if not finite[s]:\n                continue\n            left = score[s - 1] if s > 0 else -np.inf\n            right = score[s + 1] if s < len(score) - 1 else -np.inf\n            if score[s] >= left and score[s] >= right and score[s] >= threshold:\n                peaks.append(s)\n\n        if not peaks:\n            peaks = [int(np.argmax(np.where(finite, score, -np.inf)))]\n        return peaks\n\n    def select_peak_segments(self, matrix, max_segments=3):\n        \"\"\"Rank segments by slice votes, then by best distance.\"\"\"\n        votes, best, all_peaks = {}, {}, []\n        for row in matrix:\n            peaks = self.find_peaks(row)\n            all_peaks.append(peaks)\n            for p in peaks:\n                votes[p] = votes.get(p, 0) + 1\n                best[p] = min(best.get(p, np.inf), row[p])\n\n        ranked = sorted(votes, key=lambda p: (-votes[p], best[p]))\n        return ranked[:max_segments], all_peaks\n\n    # -- accommodating vocabulary --------------------------------------\n\n    def expand_vocab(self, slice_tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\n        \"\"\"\n        Slice words plus nearest GloVe neighbours that also occur in the\n        dataset graph, so the Markov walk can actually reach them.\n        \"\"\"\n        vocab = set(slice_tokens)\n        added = 0\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(slice_vec, topn=topn):\n            if word in dataset_vocab and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS:\n                vocab.add(word)\n                added += 1\n                if added >= keep:\n                    break\n        return vocab\n\n\ndef dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node):\n    \"\"\"\n    Graph nodes keep raw whitespace tokens (\"dog.\", \"fox,\"), so map each\n    cleaned word to every raw form present in the graph.\n    \"\"\"\n    clean_to_raw = {}\n    for pair in id_to_node.values():\n        for raw in pair:\n            clean_to_raw.setdefault(clean_word(raw), set()).add(raw.lower())\n    return clean_to_raw\n\n\ndef to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw):\n    raw = set()\n    for word in clean_vocab:\n        raw.update(clean_to_raw.get(word, {word}))\n    return raw\n\n\ndef print_distance_table(slices, matrix, all_peaks, selected):\n    labels = [\" \".join(tokens)[:14] for tokens, _ in slices]\n    col = 16\n    print(\"\\nManhattan distance (segment x slice)   * = peak   > = selected\")\n    print(\"seg    \" + \"\".join(label.ljust(col) for label in labels))\n    for s in range(matrix.shape[1]):\n        row = f\"{('>' if s in selected else ' ')}{s:<5} \"\n        for i in range(matrix.shape[0]):\n            d = matrix[i, s]\n            cell = \"n/a\" if not np.isfinite(d) else f\"{d:.3f}\"\n            if s in all_peaks[i]:\n                cell += \" *\"\n            row += cell.ljust(col)\n        print(row)\n\n\ndef render_side_by_side(columns, total_width=118, gap=3):\n    \"\"\"columns: list of (header, text). Prints them as parallel columns.\"\"\"\n    n = len(columns)\n    width = max(18, (total_width - gap * (n - 1)) // n)\n    wrapped = [textwrap.wrap(text, width) for _, text in columns]\n    sep = \" \" * gap\n\n    lines = [sep.join(header[:width].ljust(width) for header, _ in columns)]\n    lines.append(sep.join(\"-\" * width for _ in columns))\n    for parts in zip_longest(*wrapped, fillvalue=\"\"):\n        lines.append(sep.join(part.ljust(width) for part in parts))\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GRAPH CREATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef process_text_to_trigram_graph(text, max_nodes=200):\n    \"\"\"\n    Builds a graph where nodes are bigrams and edges represent trigrams.\n    \"\"\"\n    text = text.lower()\n    words = text.split()\n\n    if len(words) < 3:\n        return {}, {}, {}\n\n    all_bigrams = [\n        (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        for i in range(len(words) - 1)\n    ]\n\n    top_bigrams = [\n        bigram\n        for bigram, _ in Counter(all_bigrams).most_common(max_nodes)\n    ]\n\n    bigram_set = set(top_bigrams)\n\n    node_to_id = {\n        bigram: index\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    id_to_node = {\n        index: bigram\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    graph = {\n        index: {}\n        for index in range(len(top_bigrams))\n    }\n\n    for i in range(len(words) - 2):\n        b1 = (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        b2 = (words[i + 1], words[i + 2])\n\n        if b1 in bigram_set and b2 in bigram_set:\n            id1 = node_to_id[b1]\n            id2 = node_to_id[b2]\n\n            if id1 != id2:\n                graph[id1][id2] = graph[id1].get(id2, 0) + 1\n                graph[id2][id1] = graph[id2].get(id1, 0) + 1\n\n    return graph, node_to_id, id_to_node\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PROMPT-AWARE MARKOV GENERATOR\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n    graph,\n    id_to_node,\n    spins,\n    prompt_vocab,\n    length=100,\n):\n    n = len(graph)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return \"\"\n\n    prompt_vocab = {\n        word.lower()\n        for word in prompt_vocab\n        if word.strip()\n    }\n\n    valid_starts = [\n        i\n        for i in range(n)\n        if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in id_to_node[i])\n    ]\n\n    current_node = (\n        random.choice(valid_starts)\n        if valid_starts\n        else random.randrange(n)\n    )\n\n    output = list(id_to_node[current_node])\n\n    for _ in range(max(0, length - 2)):\n        current_spin = spins[current_node]\n        neighbors = graph[current_node]\n        current_word_2 = id_to_node[current_node][1]\n\n        valid_neighbors = [\n            neighbor\n            for neighbor in neighbors\n            if id_to_node[neighbor][0] == current_word_2\n        ]\n\n        if not valid_neighbors:\n            fallback_nodes = [\n                i\n                for i, spin in enumerate(spins)\n                if (\n                    spin != current_spin\n                    and id_to_node[i][0] == current_word_2\n                )\n            ]\n\n            if fallback_nodes:\n                next_node = random.choice(fallback_nodes)\n            else:\n                next_node = random.randrange(n)\n        else:\n            probabilities = []\n\n            for neighbor in valid_neighbors:\n                base_weight = graph[current_node][neighbor]\n\n                cut_multiplier = (\n                    5.0\n                    if spins[neighbor] != current_spin\n                    else 1.0\n                )\n\n                neighbor_words = id_to_node[neighbor]\n\n                prompt_multiplier = (\n                    50.0\n                    if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in neighbor_words)\n                    else 1.0\n                )\n\n                score = (\n                    base_weight\n                    * cut_multiplier\n                    * prompt_multiplier\n                )\n\n                probabilities.append(score)\n\n            next_node = random.choices(\n                valid_neighbors,\n                weights=probabilities,\n                k=1,\n            )[0]\n\n        output.append(id_to_node[next_node][1])\n        current_node = next_node\n\n    return \" \".join(output)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# SOLVE HELPER\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef solve_best_spins(graph):\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\n        graph,\n        noise=0.00001,\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\n    )\n\n    history = solver.run(\n        iterations=min(5000, max(500, len(graph) * 20)),\n        temperature=0.0000005,\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\n    )\n\n    return max(history, key=lambda item: item[\"cut\"])[\"spins\"]\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GLOVE ROUTE + SIDE-BY-SIDE GENERATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef glove_route_and_generate(\n    prompt,\n    router,\n    slicer,\n    width=2,\n    max_segments=3,\n    length=60,\n    max_columns=4,\n):\n    slices = slicer.slice_prompt(prompt, width=width)\n\n    if not slices:\n        print(\"GloVe knows none of the prompt words; no slices to probe.\")\n        return False\n\n    # Keep the output readable: cap the number of side-by-side columns.\n    if len(slices) > max_columns:\n        step = len(slices) / max_columns\n        slices = [slices[int(i * step)] for i in range(max_columns)]\n\n    matrix = slicer.distance_matrix(slices)\n    selected, all_peaks = slicer.select_peak_segments(matrix, max_segments)\n\n    if not selected:\n        print(\"No usable peaks found.\")\n        return False\n\n    print_distance_table(slices, matrix, all_peaks, selected)\n\n    selected_text = \"\\n\".join(router.segments[i] for i in sorted(selected))\n\n    print(\"\\nBuilding peak-specific trigram graph...\")\n    graph, _, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\n        selected_text,\n        max_nodes=150000,\n    )\n\n    if not graph:\n        print(\"Peak segments did not contain enough overlapping words.\")\n        return False\n\n    print(f\"Peak-specific graph built with {len(graph)} nodes.\")\n    spins = solve_best_spins(graph)\n\n    clean_to_raw = dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node)\n    dataset_vocab = set(clean_to_raw)\n\n    columns = []\n    for tokens, slice_vec in slices:\n        clean_vocab = slicer.expand_vocab(tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab)\n        raw_vocab = to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw)\n\n        text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n            graph,\n            id_to_node,\n            spins,\n            raw_vocab,\n            length=length,\n        )\n\n        added = len(clean_vocab) - len(tokens)\n        header = f\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] +{max(added, 0)} words\"\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \".\"))\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated Output (one column per prompt slice):\\n\")\n    print(render_side_by_side(columns))\n    print()\n    return True\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TF-IDF FALLBACK (original routing flow)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef tfidf_route_and_generate(prompt, router, graph, id_to_node, best_spins):\n    print(\"Routing prompt to relevant dataset segments...\")\n\n    routing = router.select_segments(prompt, max_segments=3)\n\n    print(\"\\nPrompt summary:\")\n    print(routing[\"prompt_summary\"])\n\n    print(\"\\nSelected segments:\")\n\n    for (index, score), summary in zip(\n        routing[\"selected\"],\n        routing[\"summaries\"],\n    ):\n        print(\n            f\"[Segment {index}, similarity={score:.4f}] \"\n            f\"{summary}\"\n        )\n\n    selected_text = \"\\n\".join(routing[\"segments\"])\n\n    print(\"\\nBuilding prompt-specific trigram graph...\")\n\n    selected_graph, _, selected_id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\n        selected_text,\n        max_nodes=150000,\n    )\n\n    if not selected_graph:\n        print(\n            \"Selected segments did not contain enough \"\n            \"overlapping words. Using the complete graph.\"\n        )\n\n        selected_graph = graph\n        selected_id_to_node = id_to_node\n        selected_spins = best_spins\n    else:\n        print(\n            f\"Prompt-specific graph built with \"\n            f\"{len(selected_graph)} nodes.\"\n        )\n        selected_spins = solve_best_spins(selected_graph)\n\n    final_text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n        selected_graph,\n        selected_id_to_node,\n        selected_spins,\n        prompt.split(),\n        length=400,\n    )\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated Output:\")\n    print(f\"> {final_text.capitalize()}.\\n\")\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# MAIN PROGRAM\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef load_text_file(filepath):\n    try:\n        with open(filepath, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n            return file.read()\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"File {filepath} not found. Using fallback text.\")\n\n        return (\n            \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. \"\n            \"The lazy dog barks at the brown fox. \"\n            \"The quick brown fox runs away quickly into the deep \"\n            \"dark brown forest. The dark forest is full of mystery. \"\n            \"A dog barks loudly in the dark.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef load_slicer(router):\n    if not GENSIM_AVAILABLE:\n        print(\"gensim not installed (pip install gensim). Using TF-IDF routing.\")\n        return None\n\n    glove_path = input(\n        \"Local GloVe .txt path (blank = download glove-wiki-gigaword-100): \"\n    ).strip()\n\n    try:\n        slicer = GloveSlicer(glove_path=glove_path or None)\n        slicer.index_segments(router.summaries)\n        return slicer\n    except Exception as error:\n        print(f\"Could not load GloVe ({error}). Using TF-IDF routing.\")\n        return None\n\n\ndef main():\n    dataset_file = input(\"Dataset filename: \").strip()\n\n    dataset_text = load_text_file(dataset_file)\n\n    router = DatasetRouter(\n        model_name=\"sshleifer/distilbart-cnn-12-6\",\n        segment_words=900,\n        cache_file=f\"{dataset_file}.summaries.json\",\n    )\n\n    print(\"Splitting and summarizing dataset...\")\n    router.build_index(dataset_text)\n\n    slicer = load_slicer(router)\n\n    print(\"Building initial graph from the complete dataset...\")\n    graph, node_to_id, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\n        dataset_text,\n        max_nodes=150000,\n    )\n\n    if not graph:\n        print(\"Graph is empty. Check the dataset.\")\n        return\n\n    print(f\"Graph built with {len(graph)} unique nodes.\")\n\n    print(\"Running PCMMaxCut solver for structural baseline...\")\n\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\n        graph,\n        noise=0.00001,\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\n    )\n\n    history = solver.run(\n        iterations=5000,\n        temperature=0.0000005,\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\n    )\n\n    best_cut = max(\n        history,\n        key=lambda item: item[\"cut\"],\n    )\n\n    print(\n        f\"Base partition created. \"\n        f\"Max Cut Size: {best_cut['cut']}\\n\"\n    )\n\n    while True:\n        try:\n            user_prompt = input(\"USER: \").strip()\n        except (KeyboardInterrupt, EOFError):\n            print(\"\\nExiting.\")\n            break\n\n        if not user_prompt:\n            continue\n\n        if user_prompt.lower() in {\"exit\", \"quit\"}:\n            break\n\n        done = False\n\n        if slicer is not None:\n            done = glove_route_and_generate(\n                user_prompt,\n                router,\n                slicer,\n                width=2,\n                max_segments=3,\n                length=60,\n                max_columns=4,\n            )\n\n        # Fall back to the original TF-IDF flow if GloVe is unavailable\n        # or produced nothing for this prompt.\n        if not done:\n            tfidf_route_and_generate(\n                user_prompt,\n                router,\n                graph,\n                id_to_node,\n                best_cut[\"spins\"],\n            )\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}, "message": "Full merged script: original solver + router + graph + generator + GloVe slicing/Manhattan peak probing/side-by-side output", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"import hashlib\\nimport json\\nimport math\\nimport os\\nimport random\\nimport re\\nimport textwrap\\nfrom collections import Counter\\nfrom itertools import zip_longest\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport torch\\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM\\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer, ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\\nfrom sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\\n\\n# gensim provides the GloVe vectors. If it is missing, the program falls\\n# back to the original TF-IDF routing.\\ntry:\\n    from gensim.models import KeyedVectors\\n    import gensim.downloader as gensim_api\\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = True\\nexcept ImportError:\\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = False\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# ORIGINAL SOLVER KEPT EXACTLY THE SAME\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nclass PCMMaxCut:\\n    def __init__(self, graph, noise=0.02, drift_nu=0.08):\\n        self.graph = graph\\n        self.n = len(graph)\\n        self.noise = noise\\n        self.drift_nu = drift_nu\\n        self.spins = [random.choice([-1, 1]) for _ in range(self.n)]\\n        self.age = 1\\n\\n    def local_field(self, i):\\n        return sum(\\n            weight * self.spins[j]\\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items()\\n        )\\n\\n    def delta_energy(self, i):\\n        return -2 * self.spins[i] * self.local_field(i)\\n\\n    def energy(self):\\n        value = 0.0\\n        for i in range(self.n):\\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\\n                if j > i:\\n                    value += weight * self.spins[i] * self.spins[j]\\n        return value\\n\\n    def cut_size(self):\\n        total = 0\\n        for i in range(self.n):\\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\\n                if j > i and self.spins[i] != self.spins[j]:\\n                    total += weight\\n        return total\\n\\n    def pcm_flip_attempt(self, temperature):\\n        i = random.randrange(self.n)\\n        delta = self.delta_energy(i)\\n\\n        drift = self.age ** (-self.drift_nu)\\n        thermal_noise = random.gauss(\\n            0.0,\\n            self.noise\\n        ) * max(1.0, abs(self.local_field(i)))\\n\\n        effective_delta = delta + thermal_noise * drift\\n\\n        if effective_delta <= 0:\\n            accept = True\\n        else:\\n            accept = random.random() < math.exp(\\n                -effective_delta / max(temperature, 1e-9)\\n            )\\n\\n        if accept:\\n            self.spins[i] *= -1\\n            return i, True, delta\\n\\n        return i, False, delta\\n\\n    def run(self, iterations=1000, temperature=1.0, cooling=0.995):\\n        history = []\\n\\n        for _ in range(iterations):\\n            _, accepted, _ = self.pcm_flip_attempt(temperature)\\n\\n            temperature *= cooling\\n            self.age += 1\\n\\n            history.append({\\n                \\\"energy\\\": self.energy(),\\n                \\\"cut\\\": self.cut_size(),\\n                \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n                \\\"temperature\\\": temperature,\\n                \\\"spins\\\": self.spins[:],\\n            })\\n\\n        return history\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# SUMMARIZER DATA ROUTER\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nclass DatasetRouter:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Splits a text dataset into segments, summarizes them, and selects\\n    the segments relevant to a user prompt.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(\\n        self,\\n        model_name=\\\"sshleifer/distilbart-cnn-12-6\\\",\\n        segment_words=900,\\n        cache_file=\\\"segment_summaries.json\\\",\\n        device=None,\\n    ):\\n        self.segment_words = segment_words\\n        self.cache_file = cache_file\\n\\n        if device is None:\\n            device = 0 if self._cuda_available() else -1\\n\\n        self.device = device\\n\\n        print(f\\\"Loading summarizer: {model_name}\\\")\\n        print(\\\"The model will be downloaded and cached automatically if needed.\\\")\\n\\n        self.tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)\\n        self.model = AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(model_name)\\n\\n        if self.device is not None and self.device >= 0:\\n            self.model = self.model.to(f\\\"cuda:{self.device}\\\")\\n\\n        self.segments = []\\n        self.summaries = []\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _cuda_available():\\n        try:\\n            return torch.cuda.is_available()\\n        except Exception:\\n            return False\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def clean_text(text):\\n        text = text.replace(\\\"\\\\x00\\\", \\\" \\\")\\n        text = re.sub(r\\\"\\\\s+\\\", \\\" \\\", text)\\n        return text.strip()\\n\\n    def split_text(self, text):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Split on approximately segment_words words.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        text = self.clean_text(text)\\n\\n        if not text:\\n            return []\\n\\n        words = text.split()\\n        segments = []\\n\\n        for start in range(0, len(words), self.segment_words):\\n            raw_segment = \\\" \\\".join(\\n                words[start:start + self.segment_words]\\n            )\\n\\n            if raw_segment:\\n                segments.append(raw_segment)\\n\\n        return segments\\n\\n    def _summarize_one(self, text):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Summarization models have finite input lengths. This function\\n        limits the input and returns a compact segment description.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        words = text.split()\\n\\n        # DistilBART generally works best with a bounded input.\\n        bounded_text = \\\" \\\".join(words[:850])\\n\\n        if len(bounded_text.split()) < 35:\\n            return bounded_text\\n\\n        inputs = self.tokenizer(\\n            bounded_text,\\n            return_tensors=\\\"pt\\\",\\n            max_length=1024,\\n            truncation=True\\n        )\\n\\n        if self.device is not None and self.device >= 0:\\n            inputs = {k: v.to(f\\\"cuda:{self.device}\\\") for k, v in inputs.items()}\\n\\n        output_ids = self.model.generate(\\n            inputs[\\\"input_ids\\\"],\\n            max_length=110,\\n            min_length=25,\\n            do_sample=False,\\n        )\\n\\n        return self.tokenizer.decode(output_ids[0], skip_special_tokens=True).strip()\\n\\n    def build_index(self, text):\\n        self.segments = self.split_text(text)\\n\\n        if not self.segments:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"The dataset contains no usable text.\\\")\\n\\n        cached = self._load_cache()\\n\\n        summaries = []\\n        changed = False\\n\\n        for index, segment in enumerate(self.segments):\\n            segment_key = self._segment_key(segment)\\n\\n            if segment_key in cached:\\n                summary = cached[segment_key]\\n            else:\\n                print(\\n                    f\\\"Summarizing segment \\\"\\n                    f\\\"{index + 1}/{len(self.segments)}...\\\"\\n                )\\n                summary = self._summarize_one(segment)\\n                cached[segment_key] = summary\\n                changed = True\\n\\n            summaries.append(summary)\\n\\n        self.summaries = summaries\\n\\n        if changed:\\n            self._save_cache(cached)\\n\\n        print(f\\\"Indexed {len(self.segments)} dataset segments.\\\")\\n\\n    def select_segments(\\n        self,\\n        prompt,\\n        max_segments=3,\\n        min_similarity=0.0,\\n    ):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        TF-IDF routing over summaries (fallback when GloVe is unavailable).\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not self.summaries:\\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"Call build_index() before select_segments().\\\")\\n\\n        prompt = self.clean_text(prompt)\\n\\n        prompt_summary = self._summarize_one(prompt) if len(prompt.split()) > 35 else prompt\\n\\n        documents = self.summaries + [prompt_summary]\\n\\n        vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(\\n            lowercase=True,\\n            stop_words=\\\"english\\\",\\n            ngram_range=(1, 2),\\n        )\\n\\n        matrix = vectorizer.fit_transform(documents)\\n        similarities = cosine_similarity(\\n            matrix[-1],\\n            matrix[:-1],\\n        )[0]\\n\\n        ranked = sorted(\\n            enumerate(similarities),\\n            key=lambda item: item[1],\\n            reverse=True,\\n        )\\n\\n        selected = [\\n            (index, float(score))\\n            for index, score in ranked[:max_segments]\\n            if score >= min_similarity\\n        ]\\n\\n        # Always select at least one segment.\\n        if not selected:\\n            selected = [ranked[0]]\\n\\n        return {\\n            \\\"prompt_summary\\\": prompt_summary,\\n            \\\"selected\\\": selected,\\n            \\\"segments\\\": [\\n                self.segments[index]\\n                for index, _ in selected\\n            ],\\n            \\\"summaries\\\": [\\n                self.summaries[index]\\n                for index, _ in selected\\n            ],\\n        }\\n\\n    def _segment_key(self, segment):\\n        return hashlib.sha256(segment.encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")).hexdigest()\\n\\n    def _load_cache(self):\\n        if not os.path.exists(self.cache_file):\\n            return {}\\n\\n        try:\\n            with open(self.cache_file, \\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as file:\\n                return json.load(file)\\n        except Exception:\\n            return {}\\n\\n    def _save_cache(self, cache):\\n        with open(self.cache_file, \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as file:\\n            json.dump(cache, file, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# GLOVE PROMPT SLICER\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\\\"[a-z']+\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef tokenize(text):\\n    return TOKEN_RE.findall(text.lower())\\n\\n\\ndef clean_word(word):\\n    return re.sub(r\\\"[^a-z']\\\", \\\"\\\", word.lower())\\n\\n\\nclass GloveSlicer:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Slices a prompt into word windows, embeds each slice with GloVe,\\n    measures the Manhattan (L1) distance to every segment summary, probes\\n    the similarity peaks, and expands each slice's vocabulary with GloVe\\n    neighbours that exist in the dataset.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, glove_name=\\\"glove-wiki-gigaword-100\\\", glove_path=None):\\n        if glove_path:\\n            print(f\\\"Loading GloVe from {glove_path}\\\")\\n            self.kv = KeyedVectors.load_word2vec_format(\\n                glove_path, binary=False, no_header=True\\n            )\\n        else:\\n            print(f\\\"Loading GloVe: {glove_name} (cached after first download)\\\")\\n            self.kv = gensim_api.load(glove_name)\\n\\n        self.dim = self.kv.vector_size\\n        self.seg_vecs = None\\n\\n    # -- embedding -----------------------------------------------------\\n\\n    def embed(self, tokens):\\n        vecs = [self.kv[t] for t in tokens if t in self.kv]\\n        if not vecs:\\n            return None\\n        v = np.mean(vecs, axis=0)\\n        norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\\n        return v / norm if norm > 0 else None\\n\\n    def index_segments(self, summaries):\\n        self.seg_vecs = [self.embed(tokenize(s)) for s in summaries]\\n\\n    # -- slicing -------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n    def slice_prompt(self, prompt, width=2, stride=1):\\n        tokens = [t for t in tokenize(prompt) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\\n        if not tokens:\\n            tokens = tokenize(prompt)\\n\\n        if len(tokens) <= width:\\n            windows = [tokens]\\n        else:\\n            windows = [\\n                tokens[i:i + width]\\n                for i in range(0, len(tokens) - width + 1, stride)\\n            ]\\n\\n        slices = []\\n        for window in windows:\\n            vec = self.embed(window)\\n            if vec is not None:\\n                slices.append((window, vec))\\n        return slices\\n\\n    # -- Manhattan distance and peaks ----------------------------------\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def manhattan(a, b):\\n        return float(np.abs(a - b).sum())\\n\\n    def distance_matrix(self, slices):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Shape (n_slices, n_segments); inf where a summary has no vector.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if self.seg_vecs is None:\\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"Call index_segments() first.\\\")\\n\\n        matrix = np.full((len(slices), len(self.seg_vecs)), np.inf)\\n        for i, (_, slice_vec) in enumerate(slices):\\n            for j, seg_vec in enumerate(self.seg_vecs):\\n                if seg_vec is not None:\\n                    matrix[i, j] = self.manhattan(slice_vec, seg_vec)\\n        return matrix\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def find_peaks(distances, prominence=0.5):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Similarity peaks (= local distance minima along the segment axis)\\n        at least `prominence` standard deviations above the slice average.\\n        Always returns at least the single best segment.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        score = -np.asarray(distances, dtype=float)\\n        finite = np.isfinite(score)\\n        if not finite.any():\\n            return []\\n\\n        threshold = score[finite].mean() + prominence * score[finite].std()\\n\\n        peaks = []\\n        for s in range(len(score)):\\n            if not finite[s]:\\n                continue\\n            left = score[s - 1] if s > 0 else -np.inf\\n            right = score[s + 1] if s < len(score) - 1 else -np.inf\\n            if score[s] >= left and score[s] >= right and score[s] >= threshold:\\n                peaks.append(s)\\n\\n        if not peaks:\\n            peaks = [int(np.argmax(np.where(finite, score, -np.inf)))]\\n        return peaks\\n\\n    def select_peak_segments(self, matrix, max_segments=3):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Rank segments by slice votes, then by best distance.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        votes, best, all_peaks = {}, {}, []\\n        for row in matrix:\\n            peaks = self.find_peaks(row)\\n            all_peaks.append(peaks)\\n            for p in peaks:\\n                votes[p] = votes.get(p, 0) + 1\\n                best[p] = min(best.get(p, np.inf), row[p])\\n\\n        ranked = sorted(votes, key=lambda p: (-votes[p], best[p]))\\n        return ranked[:max_segments], all_peaks\\n\\n    # -- accommodating vocabulary --------------------------------------\\n\\n    def expand_vocab(self, slice_tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Slice words plus nearest GloVe neighbours that also occur in the\\n        dataset graph, so the Markov walk can actually reach them.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        vocab = set(slice_tokens)\\n        added = 0\\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(slice_vec, topn=topn):\\n            if word in dataset_vocab and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS:\\n                vocab.add(word)\\n                added += 1\\n                if added >= keep:\\n                    break\\n        return vocab\\n\\n\\ndef dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Graph nodes keep raw whitespace tokens (\\\"dog.\\\", \\\"fox,\\\"), so map each\\n    cleaned word to every raw form present in the graph.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    clean_to_raw = {}\\n    for pair in id_to_node.values():\\n        for raw in pair:\\n            clean_to_raw.setdefault(clean_word(raw), set()).add(raw.lower())\\n    return clean_to_raw\\n\\n\\ndef to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw):\\n    raw = set()\\n    for word in clean_vocab:\\n        raw.update(clean_to_raw.get(word, {word}))\\n    return raw\\n\\n\\ndef print_distance_table(slices, matrix, all_peaks, selected):\\n    labels = [\\\" \\\".join(tokens)[:14] for tokens, _ in slices]\\n    col = 16\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nManhattan distance (segment x slice)   * = peak   > = selected\\\")\\n    print(\\\"seg    \\\" + \\\"\\\".join(label.ljust(col) for label in labels))\\n    for s in range(matrix.shape[1]):\\n        row = f\\\"{('>' if s in selected else ' ')}{s:<5} \\\"\\n        for i in range(matrix.shape[0]):\\n            d = matrix[i, s]\\n            cell = \\\"n/a\\\" if not np.isfinite(d) else f\\\"{d:.3f}\\\"\\n            if s in all_peaks[i]:\\n                cell += \\\" *\\\"\\n            row += cell.ljust(col)\\n        print(row)\\n\\n\\ndef render_side_by_side(columns, total_width=118, gap=3):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"columns: list of (header, text). Prints them as parallel columns.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    n = len(columns)\\n    width = max(18, (total_width - gap * (n - 1)) // n)\\n    wrapped = [textwrap.wrap(text, width) for _, text in columns]\\n    sep = \\\" \\\" * gap\\n\\n    lines = [sep.join(header[:width].ljust(width) for header, _ in columns)]\\n    lines.append(sep.join(\\\"-\\\" * width for _ in columns))\\n    for parts in zip_longest(*wrapped, fillvalue=\\\"\\\"):\\n        lines.append(sep.join(part.ljust(width) for part in parts))\\n    return \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines)\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# GRAPH CREATION\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef process_text_to_trigram_graph(text, max_nodes=200):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Builds a graph where nodes are bigrams and edges represent trigrams.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    text = text.lower()\\n    words = text.split()\\n\\n    if len(words) < 3:\\n        return {}, {}, {}\\n\\n    all_bigrams = [\\n        (words[i], words[i + 1])\\n        for i in range(len(words) - 1)\\n    ]\\n\\n    top_bigrams = [\\n        bigram\\n        for bigram, _ in Counter(all_bigrams).most_common(max_nodes)\\n    ]\\n\\n    bigram_set = set(top_bigrams)\\n\\n    node_to_id = {\\n        bigram: index\\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\\n    }\\n\\n    id_to_node = {\\n        index: bigram\\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\\n    }\\n\\n    graph = {\\n        index: {}\\n        for index in range(len(top_bigrams))\\n    }\\n\\n    for i in range(len(words) - 2):\\n        b1 = (words[i], words[i + 1])\\n        b2 = (words[i + 1], words[i + 2])\\n\\n        if b1 in bigram_set and b2 in bigram_set:\\n            id1 = node_to_id[b1]\\n            id2 = node_to_id[b2]\\n\\n            if id1 != id2:\\n                graph[id1][id2] = graph[id1].get(id2, 0) + 1\\n                graph[id2][id1] = graph[id2].get(id1, 0) + 1\\n\\n    return graph, node_to_id, id_to_node\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# PROMPT-AWARE MARKOV GENERATOR\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef generate_markovian_prompt_text(\\n    graph,\\n    id_to_node,\\n    spins,\\n    prompt_vocab,\\n    length=100,\\n):\\n    n = len(graph)\\n\\n    if n == 0:\\n        return \\\"\\\"\\n\\n    prompt_vocab = {\\n        word.lower()\\n        for word in prompt_vocab\\n        if word.strip()\\n    }\\n\\n    valid_starts = [\\n        i\\n        for i in range(n)\\n        if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in id_to_node[i])\\n    ]\\n\\n    current_node = (\\n        random.choice(valid_starts)\\n        if valid_starts\\n        else random.randrange(n)\\n    )\\n\\n    output = list(id_to_node[current_node])\\n\\n    for _ in range(max(0, length - 2)):\\n        current_spin = spins[current_node]\\n        neighbors = graph[current_node]\\n        current_word_2 = id_to_node[current_node][1]\\n\\n        valid_neighbors = [\\n            neighbor\\n            for neighbor in neighbors\\n            if id_to_node[neighbor][0] == current_word_2\\n        ]\\n\\n        if not valid_neighbors:\\n            fallback_nodes = [\\n                i\\n                for i, spin in enumerate(spins)\\n                if (\\n                    spin != current_spin\\n                    and id_to_node[i][0] == current_word_2\\n                )\\n            ]\\n\\n            if fallback_nodes:\\n                next_node = random.choice(fallback_nodes)\\n            else:\\n                next_node = random.randrange(n)\\n        else:\\n            probabilities = []\\n\\n            for neighbor in valid_neighbors:\\n                base_weight = graph[current_node][neighbor]\\n\\n                cut_multiplier = (\\n                    5.0\\n                    if spins[neighbor] != current_spin\\n                    else 1.0\\n                )\\n\\n                neighbor_words = id_to_node[neighbor]\\n\\n                prompt_multiplier = (\\n                    50.0\\n                    if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in neighbor_words)\\n                    else 1.0\\n                )\\n\\n                score = (\\n                    base_weight\\n                    * cut_multiplier\\n                    * prompt_multiplier\\n                )\\n\\n                probabilities.append(score)\\n\\n            next_node = random.choices(\\n                valid_neighbors,\\n                weights=probabilities,\\n                k=1,\\n            )[0]\\n\\n        output.append(id_to_node[next_node][1])\\n        current_node = next_node\\n\\n    return \\\" \\\".join(output)\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# SOLVE HELPER\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef solve_best_spins(graph):\\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\\n        graph,\\n        noise=0.00001,\\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\\n    )\\n\\n    history = solver.run(\\n        iterations=min(5000, max(500, len(graph) * 20)),\\n        temperature=0.0000005,\\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\\n    )\\n\\n    return max(history, key=lambda item: item[\\\"cut\\\"])[\\\"spins\\\"]\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# GLOVE ROUTE + SIDE-BY-SIDE GENERATION\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef glove_route_and_generate(\\n    prompt,\\n    router,\\n    slicer,\\n    width=2,\\n    max_segments=3,\\n    length=60,\\n    max_columns=4,\\n):\\n    slices = slicer.slice_prompt(prompt, width=width)\\n\\n    if not slices:\\n        print(\\\"GloVe knows none of the prompt words; no slices to probe.\\\")\\n        return False\\n\\n    # Keep the output readable: cap the number of side-by-side columns.\\n    if len(slices) > max_columns:\\n        step = len(slices) / max_columns\\n        slices = [slices[int(i * step)] for i in range(max_columns)]\\n\\n    matrix = slicer.distance_matrix(slices)\\n    selected, all_peaks = slicer.select_peak_segments(matrix, max_segments)\\n\\n    if not selected:\\n        print(\\\"No usable peaks found.\\\")\\n        return False\\n\\n    print_distance_table(slices, matrix, all_peaks, selected)\\n\\n    selected_text = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(router.segments[i] for i in sorted(selected))\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nBuilding peak-specific trigram graph...\\\")\\n    graph, _, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\\n        selected_text,\\n        max_nodes=150000,\\n    )\\n\\n    if not graph:\\n        print(\\\"Peak segments did not contain enough overlapping words.\\\")\\n        return False\\n\\n    print(f\\\"Peak-specific graph built with {len(graph)} nodes.\\\")\\n    spins = solve_best_spins(graph)\\n\\n    clean_to_raw = dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node)\\n    dataset_vocab = set(clean_to_raw)\\n\\n    columns = []\\n    for tokens, slice_vec in slices:\\n        clean_vocab = slicer.expand_vocab(tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab)\\n        raw_vocab = to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw)\\n\\n        text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\\n            graph,\\n            id_to_node,\\n            spins,\\n            raw_vocab,\\n            length=length,\\n        )\\n\\n        added = len(clean_vocab) - len(tokens)\\n        header = f\\\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] +{max(added, 0)} words\\\"\\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \\\".\\\"))\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nGenerated Output (one column per prompt slice):\\\\n\\\")\\n    print(render_side_by_side(columns))\\n    print()\\n    return True\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# TF-IDF FALLBACK (original routing flow)\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef tfidf_route_and_generate(prompt, router, graph, id_to_node, best_spins):\\n    print(\\\"Routing prompt to relevant dataset segments...\\\")\\n\\n    routing = router.select_segments(prompt, max_segments=3)\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nPrompt summary:\\\")\\n    print(routing[\\\"prompt_summary\\\"])\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nSelected segments:\\\")\\n\\n    for (index, score), summary in zip(\\n        routing[\\\"selected\\\"],\\n        routing[\\\"summaries\\\"],\\n    ):\\n        print(\\n            f\\\"[Segment {index}, similarity={score:.4f}] \\\"\\n            f\\\"{summary}\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n    selected_text = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(routing[\\\"segments\\\"])\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nBuilding prompt-specific trigram graph...\\\")\\n\\n    selected_graph, _, selected_id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\\n        selected_text,\\n        max_nodes=150000,\\n    )\\n\\n    if not selected_graph:\\n        print(\\n            \\\"Selected segments did not contain enough \\\"\\n            \\\"overlapping words. Using the complete graph.\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n        selected_graph = graph\\n        selected_id_to_node = id_to_node\\n        selected_spins = best_spins\\n    else:\\n        print(\\n            f\\\"Prompt-specific graph built with \\\"\\n            f\\\"{len(selected_graph)} nodes.\\\"\\n        )\\n        selected_spins = solve_best_spins(selected_graph)\\n\\n    final_text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\\n        selected_graph,\\n        selected_id_to_node,\\n        selected_spins,\\n        prompt.split(),\\n        length=400,\\n    )\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nGenerated Output:\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"> {final_text.capitalize()}.\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# MAIN PROGRAM\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef load_text_file(filepath):\\n    try:\\n        with open(filepath, \\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as file:\\n            return file.read()\\n    except FileNotFoundError:\\n        print(f\\\"File {filepath} not found. Using fallback text.\\\")\\n\\n        return (\\n            \\\"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. \\\"\\n            \\\"The lazy dog barks at the brown fox. \\\"\\n            \\\"The quick brown fox runs away quickly into the deep \\\"\\n            \\\"dark brown forest. The dark forest is full of mystery. \\\"\\n            \\\"A dog barks loudly in the dark.\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n\\ndef load_slicer(router):\\n    if not GENSIM_AVAILABLE:\\n        print(\\\"gensim not installed (pip install gensim). Using TF-IDF routing.\\\")\\n        return None\\n\\n    glove_path = input(\\n        \\\"Local GloVe .txt path (blank = download glove-wiki-gigaword-100): \\\"\\n    ).strip()\\n\\n    try:\\n        slicer = GloveSlicer(glove_path=glove_path or None)\\n        slicer.index_segments(router.summaries)\\n        return slicer\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        print(f\\\"Could not load GloVe ({error}). Using TF-IDF routing.\\\")\\n        return None\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    dataset_file = input(\\\"Dataset filename: \\\").strip()\\n\\n    dataset_text = load_text_file(dataset_file)\\n\\n    router = DatasetRouter(\\n        model_name=\\\"sshleifer/distilbart-cnn-12-6\\\",\\n        segment_words=900,\\n        cache_file=f\\\"{dataset_file}.summaries.json\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    print(\\\"Splitting and summarizing dataset...\\\")\\n    router.build_index(dataset_text)\\n\\n    slicer = load_slicer(router)\\n\\n    print(\\\"Building initial graph from the complete dataset...\\\")\\n    graph, node_to_id, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\\n        dataset_text,\\n        max_nodes=150000,\\n    )\\n\\n    if not graph:\\n        print(\\\"Graph is empty. Check the dataset.\\\")\\n        return\\n\\n    print(f\\\"Graph built with {len(graph)} unique nodes.\\\")\\n\\n    print(\\\"Running PCMMaxCut solver for structural baseline...\\\")\\n\\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\\n        graph,\\n        noise=0.00001,\\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\\n    )\\n\\n    history = solver.run(\\n        iterations=5000,\\n        temperature=0.0000005,\\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\\n    )\\n\\n    best_cut = max(\\n        history,\\n        key=lambda item: item[\\\"cut\\\"],\\n    )\\n\\n    print(\\n        f\\\"Base partition created. \\\"\\n        f\\\"Max Cut Size: {best_cut['cut']}\\\\n\\\"\\n    )\\n\\n    while True:\\n        try:\\n            user_prompt = input(\\\"USER: \\\").strip()\\n        except (KeyboardInterrupt, EOFError):\\n            print(\\\"\\\\nExiting.\\\")\\n            break\\n\\n        if not user_prompt:\\n            continue\\n\\n        if user_prompt.lower() in {\\\"exit\\\", \\\"quit\\\"}:\\n            break\\n\\n        done = False\\n\\n        if slicer is not None:\\n            done = glove_route_and_generate(\\n                user_prompt,\\n                router,\\n                slicer,\\n                width=2,\\n                max_segments=3,\\n                length=60,\\n                max_columns=4,\\n            )\\n\\n        # Fall back to the original TF-IDF flow if GloVe is unavailable\\n        # or produced nothing for this prompt.\\n        if not done:\\n            tfidf_route_and_generate(\\n                user_prompt,\\n                router,\\n                graph,\\n                id_to_node,\\n                best_cut[\\\"spins\\\"],\\n            )\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\n\", \"filename\": \"/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:54:08.596018Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:54:08.596057Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Ryh7eoT89u9fc5NZ78831k", "name": "create_file", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:54:10.126799Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:54:10.607509Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_0139jiRGADwourCGPSZLpjmg", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 -m py_compile pcm_glove_full.py && echo OK", "description": "Syntax check the merged script"}, "message": "Syntax check the merged script", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 -m py_compile pcm_glove_full.py && echo OK\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:54:11.298098Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:54:11.298180Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_0139jiRGADwourCGPSZLpjmg", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"OK\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"OK\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:54:12.724786Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:54:12.974016Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01RxCnnPnr5xXF24EJMdMTtL", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:54:12.999893Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:54:12.999933Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01RxCnnPnr5xXF24EJMdMTtL", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py", "name": "pcm glove full", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:54:16.992457Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:54:17.002904Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "`pcm_glove_full.py` is now one self-contained script with the GloVe slicing merged in. It passes a syntax check, but I haven't run it end to end, since that needs the summarizer and GloVe downloads.\n\n- **Solver:** `PCMMaxCut` is unchanged.\n- **Routing:** each prompt goes through the GloVe slice, Manhattan distance and peak pipeline from before, then the distance table and side-by-side columns.\n- **Fallback:** if `gensim` isn't installed, GloVe fails to load, or a prompt has no GloVe-known words, the original TF-IDF flow runs instead.\n- **Setup:** you need `pip install gensim`. At startup it asks for a local GloVe `.txt` path, or you can leave it blank to download `glove-wiki-gigaword-100` once.\n- **Small changes:** I added a `solve_best_spins()` helper so the solver setup isn't repeated. Ctrl-D now exits cleanly like Ctrl-C.\n\nThe solver parameters still make the cooling effectively instant (`cooling=0.0000000199`), so it runs at about zero temperature. I left that as is, but it's the first place to look if the partitions seem poor.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T09:54:17.094593Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T09:54:17.094593Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fc08-5a98-7fbe-919e-b55cf1e2fe06"}, {"uuid": "01a0fc0a-b6e9-743b-bc35-9957dd484cab", "text": "remove the summariser", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:55:54.595942Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:55:54.595942Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "remove the summariser", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T09:55:54.596164Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T09:55:54.596164Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fc08-5a98-7d35-991a-6608b33bf13e"}, {"uuid": "01a0fc0a-b6e9-7db6-a11b-66dc8c97a8a4", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI rewrote `pcm_glove_full.py` without the summarizer. It passes a syntax check, and the only remaining mention of \"summarizer\" is a section comment. I haven't run it end to end.\n\n- **Removed:** the DistilBART model, `torch` and `transformers` imports, the summary cache file, and the prompt-summarizing step. `DatasetRouter` is now `SegmentRouter`, which only splits the text into 900-word segments.\n- **GloVe routing:** each raw segment (stopwords dropped) is embedded directly, so the Manhattan distance compares prompt slices to the actual segment text.\n- **TF-IDF fallback:** it now ranks the raw segments, and the printout shows a 100-character preview instead of a summary.\n- **Dependencies:** you now need only `numpy`, `scikit-learn` and `gensim`. Startup is also much faster and needs no model download besides GloVe.\n\nBecause a 900-word segment is averaged into one vector, it can blur topics together. If the peaks look flat, try `segment_words=300` in `SegmentRouter(...)` for sharper contrast between segments.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:55:54.589782Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:55:58.852959Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Reworking the routing to embed segments without summaries."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:55:58.853029Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:55:59.327825Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01MCanZmyXLhUGQHx4M49vUb", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "rm -f /mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py && echo removed", "description": "Remove old version so it can be rewritten without the summarizer"}, "message": "Remove old version so it can be rewritten without the summarizer", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"rm -f /mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py && echo removed\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:55:59.671882Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:55:59.671944Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01MCanZmyXLhUGQHx4M49vUb", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"removed\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"removed\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:56:01.204093Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:56:38.916212Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01WtMBNDstUJz7ZAhUYEa54F", "name": "create_file", "input": {"description": "Full script with the DistilBART summarizer removed; segments are embedded/ranked directly", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py", "file_text": "import math\nimport random\nimport re\nimport textwrap\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom itertools import zip_longest\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer, ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\nfrom sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\n\n# gensim provides the GloVe vectors. If it is missing, the program falls\n# back to TF-IDF routing over the raw segments.\ntry:\n    from gensim.models import KeyedVectors\n    import gensim.downloader as gensim_api\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = False\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# ORIGINAL SOLVER KEPT EXACTLY THE SAME\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass PCMMaxCut:\n    def __init__(self, graph, noise=0.02, drift_nu=0.08):\n        self.graph = graph\n        self.n = len(graph)\n        self.noise = noise\n        self.drift_nu = drift_nu\n        self.spins = [random.choice([-1, 1]) for _ in range(self.n)]\n        self.age = 1\n\n    def local_field(self, i):\n        return sum(\n            weight * self.spins[j]\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items()\n        )\n\n    def delta_energy(self, i):\n        return -2 * self.spins[i] * self.local_field(i)\n\n    def energy(self):\n        value = 0.0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i:\n                    value += weight * self.spins[i] * self.spins[j]\n        return value\n\n    def cut_size(self):\n        total = 0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i and self.spins[i] != self.spins[j]:\n                    total += weight\n        return total\n\n    def pcm_flip_attempt(self, temperature):\n        i = random.randrange(self.n)\n        delta = self.delta_energy(i)\n\n        drift = self.age ** (-self.drift_nu)\n        thermal_noise = random.gauss(\n            0.0,\n            self.noise\n        ) * max(1.0, abs(self.local_field(i)))\n\n        effective_delta = delta + thermal_noise * drift\n\n        if effective_delta <= 0:\n            accept = True\n        else:\n            accept = random.random() < math.exp(\n                -effective_delta / max(temperature, 1e-9)\n            )\n\n        if accept:\n            self.spins[i] *= -1\n            return i, True, delta\n\n        return i, False, delta\n\n    def run(self, iterations=1000, temperature=1.0, cooling=0.995):\n        history = []\n\n        for _ in range(iterations):\n            _, accepted, _ = self.pcm_flip_attempt(temperature)\n\n            temperature *= cooling\n            self.age += 1\n\n            history.append({\n                \"energy\": self.energy(),\n                \"cut\": self.cut_size(),\n                \"accepted\": accepted,\n                \"temperature\": temperature,\n                \"spins\": self.spins[:],\n            })\n\n        return history\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# SEGMENT ROUTER (no summarizer)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass SegmentRouter:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a text dataset into word-count segments and selects the\n    segments relevant to a prompt using TF-IDF over the raw segment text.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, segment_words=900):\n        self.segment_words = segment_words\n        self.segments = []\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def clean_text(text):\n        text = text.replace(\"\\x00\", \" \")\n        text = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", text)\n        return text.strip()\n\n    def split_text(self, text):\n        text = self.clean_text(text)\n\n        if not text:\n            return []\n\n        words = text.split()\n        segments = []\n\n        for start in range(0, len(words), self.segment_words):\n            raw_segment = \" \".join(\n                words[start:start + self.segment_words]\n            )\n\n            if raw_segment:\n                segments.append(raw_segment)\n\n        return segments\n\n    def build_index(self, text):\n        self.segments = self.split_text(text)\n\n        if not self.segments:\n            raise ValueError(\"The dataset contains no usable text.\")\n\n        print(f\"Indexed {len(self.segments)} dataset segments.\")\n\n    def select_segments(self, prompt, max_segments=3, min_similarity=0.0):\n        \"\"\"TF-IDF routing over raw segments (fallback when GloVe is unavailable).\"\"\"\n        if not self.segments:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Call build_index() before select_segments().\")\n\n        prompt = self.clean_text(prompt)\n\n        vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(\n            lowercase=True,\n            stop_words=\"english\",\n            ngram_range=(1, 2),\n        )\n\n        matrix = vectorizer.fit_transform(self.segments + [prompt])\n        similarities = cosine_similarity(\n            matrix[-1],\n            matrix[:-1],\n        )[0]\n\n        ranked = sorted(\n            enumerate(similarities),\n            key=lambda item: item[1],\n            reverse=True,\n        )\n\n        selected = [\n            (index, float(score))\n            for index, score in ranked[:max_segments]\n            if score >= min_similarity\n        ]\n\n        # Always select at least one segment.\n        if not selected:\n            selected = [(ranked[0][0], float(ranked[0][1]))]\n\n        return {\n            \"selected\": selected,\n            \"segments\": [self.segments[index] for index, _ in selected],\n        }\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GLOVE PROMPT SLICER\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[a-z']+\")\n\n\ndef tokenize(text):\n    return TOKEN_RE.findall(text.lower())\n\n\ndef clean_word(word):\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z']\", \"\", word.lower())\n\n\nclass GloveSlicer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Slices a prompt into word windows, embeds each slice with GloVe,\n    measures the Manhattan (L1) distance to every dataset segment, probes\n    the similarity peaks, and expands each slice's vocabulary with GloVe\n    neighbours that exist in the dataset.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, glove_name=\"glove-wiki-gigaword-100\", glove_path=None):\n        if glove_path:\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe from {glove_path}\")\n            self.kv = KeyedVectors.load_word2vec_format(\n                glove_path, binary=False, no_header=True\n            )\n        else:\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe: {glove_name} (cached after first download)\")\n            self.kv = gensim_api.load(glove_name)\n\n        self.dim = self.kv.vector_size\n        self.seg_vecs = None\n\n    # -- embedding -----------------------------------------------------\n\n    def embed(self, tokens):\n        vecs = [self.kv[t] for t in tokens if t in self.kv]\n        if not vecs:\n            return None\n        v = np.mean(vecs, axis=0)\n        norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n        return v / norm if norm > 0 else None\n\n    def index_segments(self, segments):\n        \"\"\"Embed each raw segment (content words only).\"\"\"\n        self.seg_vecs = []\n        for segment in segments:\n            tokens = [t for t in tokenize(segment) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\n            self.seg_vecs.append(self.embed(tokens))\n\n    # -- slicing -------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def slice_prompt(self, prompt, width=2, stride=1):\n        tokens = [t for t in tokenize(prompt) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\n        if not tokens:\n            tokens = tokenize(prompt)\n\n        if len(tokens) <= width:\n            windows = [tokens]\n        else:\n            windows = [\n                tokens[i:i + width]\n                for i in range(0, len(tokens) - width + 1, stride)\n            ]\n\n        slices = []\n        for window in windows:\n            vec = self.embed(window)\n            if vec is not None:\n                slices.append((window, vec))\n        return slices\n\n    # -- Manhattan distance and peaks ----------------------------------\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def manhattan(a, b):\n        return float(np.abs(a - b).sum())\n\n    def distance_matrix(self, slices):\n        \"\"\"Shape (n_slices, n_segments); inf where a segment has no vector.\"\"\"\n        if self.seg_vecs is None:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Call index_segments() first.\")\n\n        matrix = np.full((len(slices), len(self.seg_vecs)), np.inf)\n        for i, (_, slice_vec) in enumerate(slices):\n            for j, seg_vec in enumerate(self.seg_vecs):\n                if seg_vec is not None:\n                    matrix[i, j] = self.manhattan(slice_vec, seg_vec)\n        return matrix\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def find_peaks(distances, prominence=0.5):\n        \"\"\"\n        Similarity peaks (= local distance minima along the segment axis)\n        at least `prominence` standard deviations above the slice average.\n        Always returns at least the single best segment.\n        \"\"\"\n        score = -np.asarray(distances, dtype=float)\n        finite = np.isfinite(score)\n        if not finite.any():\n            return []\n\n        threshold = score[finite].mean() + prominence * score[finite].std()\n\n        peaks = []\n        for s in range(len(score)):\n            if not finite[s]:\n                continue\n            left = score[s - 1] if s > 0 else -np.inf\n            right = score[s + 1] if s < len(score) - 1 else -np.inf\n            if score[s] >= left and score[s] >= right and score[s] >= threshold:\n                peaks.append(s)\n\n        if not peaks:\n            peaks = [int(np.argmax(np.where(finite, score, -np.inf)))]\n        return peaks\n\n    def select_peak_segments(self, matrix, max_segments=3):\n        \"\"\"Rank segments by slice votes, then by best distance.\"\"\"\n        votes, best, all_peaks = {}, {}, []\n        for row in matrix:\n            peaks = self.find_peaks(row)\n            all_peaks.append(peaks)\n            for p in peaks:\n                votes[p] = votes.get(p, 0) + 1\n                best[p] = min(best.get(p, np.inf), row[p])\n\n        ranked = sorted(votes, key=lambda p: (-votes[p], best[p]))\n        return ranked[:max_segments], all_peaks\n\n    # -- accommodating vocabulary --------------------------------------\n\n    def expand_vocab(self, slice_tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\n        \"\"\"\n        Slice words plus nearest GloVe neighbours that also occur in the\n        dataset graph, so the Markov walk can actually reach them.\n        \"\"\"\n        vocab = set(slice_tokens)\n        added = 0\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(slice_vec, topn=topn):\n            if word in dataset_vocab and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS:\n                vocab.add(word)\n                added += 1\n                if added >= keep:\n                    break\n        return vocab\n\n\ndef dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node):\n    \"\"\"\n    Graph nodes keep raw whitespace tokens (\"dog.\", \"fox,\"), so map each\n    cleaned word to every raw form present in the graph.\n    \"\"\"\n    clean_to_raw = {}\n    for pair in id_to_node.values():\n        for raw in pair:\n            clean_to_raw.setdefault(clean_word(raw), set()).add(raw.lower())\n    return clean_to_raw\n\n\ndef to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw):\n    raw = set()\n    for word in clean_vocab:\n        raw.update(clean_to_raw.get(word, {word}))\n    return raw\n\n\ndef print_distance_table(slices, matrix, all_peaks, selected):\n    labels = [\" \".join(tokens)[:14] for tokens, _ in slices]\n    col = 16\n    print(\"\\nManhattan distance (segment x slice)   * = peak   > = selected\")\n    print(\"seg    \" + \"\".join(label.ljust(col) for label in labels))\n    for s in range(matrix.shape[1]):\n        row = f\"{('>' if s in selected else ' ')}{s:<5} \"\n        for i in range(matrix.shape[0]):\n            d = matrix[i, s]\n            cell = \"n/a\" if not np.isfinite(d) else f\"{d:.3f}\"\n            if s in all_peaks[i]:\n                cell += \" *\"\n            row += cell.ljust(col)\n        print(row)\n\n\ndef render_side_by_side(columns, total_width=118, gap=3):\n    \"\"\"columns: list of (header, text). Prints them as parallel columns.\"\"\"\n    n = len(columns)\n    width = max(18, (total_width - gap * (n - 1)) // n)\n    wrapped = [textwrap.wrap(text, width) for _, text in columns]\n    sep = \" \" * gap\n\n    lines = [sep.join(header[:width].ljust(width) for header, _ in columns)]\n    lines.append(sep.join(\"-\" * width for _ in columns))\n    for parts in zip_longest(*wrapped, fillvalue=\"\"):\n        lines.append(sep.join(part.ljust(width) for part in parts))\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GRAPH CREATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef process_text_to_trigram_graph(text, max_nodes=200):\n    \"\"\"\n    Builds a graph where nodes are bigrams and edges represent trigrams.\n    \"\"\"\n    text = text.lower()\n    words = text.split()\n\n    if len(words) < 3:\n        return {}, {}, {}\n\n    all_bigrams = [\n        (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        for i in range(len(words) - 1)\n    ]\n\n    top_bigrams = [\n        bigram\n        for bigram, _ in Counter(all_bigrams).most_common(max_nodes)\n    ]\n\n    bigram_set = set(top_bigrams)\n\n    node_to_id = {\n        bigram: index\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    id_to_node = {\n        index: bigram\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    graph = {\n        index: {}\n        for index in range(len(top_bigrams))\n    }\n\n    for i in range(len(words) - 2):\n        b1 = (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        b2 = (words[i + 1], words[i + 2])\n\n        if b1 in bigram_set and b2 in bigram_set:\n            id1 = node_to_id[b1]\n            id2 = node_to_id[b2]\n\n            if id1 != id2:\n                graph[id1][id2] = graph[id1].get(id2, 0) + 1\n                graph[id2][id1] = graph[id2].get(id1, 0) + 1\n\n    return graph, node_to_id, id_to_node\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PROMPT-AWARE MARKOV GENERATOR\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n    graph,\n    id_to_node,\n    spins,\n    prompt_vocab,\n    length=100,\n):\n    n = len(graph)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return \"\"\n\n    prompt_vocab = {\n        word.lower()\n        for word in prompt_vocab\n        if word.strip()\n    }\n\n    valid_starts = [\n        i\n        for i in range(n)\n        if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in id_to_node[i])\n    ]\n\n    current_node = (\n        random.choice(valid_starts)\n        if valid_starts\n        else random.randrange(n)\n    )\n\n    output = list(id_to_node[current_node])\n\n    for _ in range(max(0, length - 2)):\n        current_spin = spins[current_node]\n        neighbors = graph[current_node]\n        current_word_2 = id_to_node[current_node][1]\n\n        valid_neighbors = [\n            neighbor\n            for neighbor in neighbors\n            if id_to_node[neighbor][0] == current_word_2\n        ]\n\n        if not valid_neighbors:\n            fallback_nodes = [\n                i\n                for i, spin in enumerate(spins)\n                if (\n                    spin != current_spin\n                    and id_to_node[i][0] == current_word_2\n                )\n            ]\n\n            if fallback_nodes:\n                next_node = random.choice(fallback_nodes)\n            else:\n                next_node = random.randrange(n)\n        else:\n            probabilities = []\n\n            for neighbor in valid_neighbors:\n                base_weight = graph[current_node][neighbor]\n\n                cut_multiplier = (\n                    5.0\n                    if spins[neighbor] != current_spin\n                    else 1.0\n                )\n\n                neighbor_words = id_to_node[neighbor]\n\n                prompt_multiplier = (\n                    50.0\n                    if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in neighbor_words)\n                    else 1.0\n                )\n\n                score = (\n                    base_weight\n                    * cut_multiplier\n                    * prompt_multiplier\n                )\n\n                probabilities.append(score)\n\n            next_node = random.choices(\n                valid_neighbors,\n                weights=probabilities,\n                k=1,\n            )[0]\n\n        output.append(id_to_node[next_node][1])\n        current_node = next_node\n\n    return \" \".join(output)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# SOLVE HELPER\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef solve_best_spins(graph):\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\n        graph,\n        noise=0.00001,\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\n    )\n\n    history = solver.run(\n        iterations=min(5000, max(500, len(graph) * 20)),\n        temperature=0.0000005,\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\n    )\n\n    return max(history, key=lambda item: item[\"cut\"])[\"spins\"]\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GLOVE ROUTE + SIDE-BY-SIDE GENERATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef glove_route_and_generate(\n    prompt,\n    router,\n    slicer,\n    width=2,\n    max_segments=3,\n    length=60,\n    max_columns=4,\n):\n    slices = slicer.slice_prompt(prompt, width=width)\n\n    if not slices:\n        print(\"GloVe knows none of the prompt words; no slices to probe.\")\n        return False\n\n    # Keep the output readable: cap the number of side-by-side columns.\n    if len(slices) > max_columns:\n        step = len(slices) / max_columns\n        slices = [slices[int(i * step)] for i in range(max_columns)]\n\n    matrix = slicer.distance_matrix(slices)\n    selected, all_peaks = slicer.select_peak_segments(matrix, max_segments)\n\n    if not selected:\n        print(\"No usable peaks found.\")\n        return False\n\n    print_distance_table(slices, matrix, all_peaks, selected)\n\n    selected_text = \"\\n\".join(router.segments[i] for i in sorted(selected))\n\n    print(\"\\nBuilding peak-specific trigram graph...\")\n    graph, _, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\n        selected_text,\n        max_nodes=150000,\n    )\n\n    if not graph:\n        print(\"Peak segments did not contain enough overlapping words.\")\n        return False\n\n    print(f\"Peak-specific graph built with {len(graph)} nodes.\")\n    spins = solve_best_spins(graph)\n\n    clean_to_raw = dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node)\n    dataset_vocab = set(clean_to_raw)\n\n    columns = []\n    for tokens, slice_vec in slices:\n        clean_vocab = slicer.expand_vocab(tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab)\n        raw_vocab = to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw)\n\n        text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n            graph,\n            id_to_node,\n            spins,\n            raw_vocab,\n            length=length,\n        )\n\n        added = len(clean_vocab) - len(tokens)\n        header = f\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] +{max(added, 0)} words\"\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \".\"))\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated Output (one column per prompt slice):\\n\")\n    print(render_side_by_side(columns))\n    print()\n    return True\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TF-IDF FALLBACK\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef tfidf_route_and_generate(prompt, router, graph, id_to_node, best_spins):\n    print(\"Routing prompt to relevant dataset segments...\")\n\n    routing = router.select_segments(prompt, max_segments=3)\n\n    print(\"\\nSelected segments:\")\n\n    for (index, score), segment in zip(\n        routing[\"selected\"],\n        routing[\"segments\"],\n    ):\n        preview = segment[:100] + (\"...\" if len(segment) > 100 else \"\")\n        print(f\"[Segment {index}, similarity={score:.4f}] {preview}\")\n\n    selected_text = \"\\n\".join(routing[\"segments\"])\n\n    print(\"\\nBuilding prompt-specific trigram graph...\")\n\n    selected_graph, _, selected_id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\n        selected_text,\n        max_nodes=150000,\n    )\n\n    if not selected_graph:\n        print(\n            \"Selected segments did not contain enough \"\n            \"overlapping words. Using the complete graph.\"\n        )\n\n        selected_graph = graph\n        selected_id_to_node = id_to_node\n        selected_spins = best_spins\n    else:\n        print(\n            f\"Prompt-specific graph built with \"\n            f\"{len(selected_graph)} nodes.\"\n        )\n        selected_spins = solve_best_spins(selected_graph)\n\n    final_text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n        selected_graph,\n        selected_id_to_node,\n        selected_spins,\n        prompt.split(),\n        length=400,\n    )\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated Output:\")\n    print(f\"> {final_text.capitalize()}.\\n\")\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# MAIN PROGRAM\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef load_text_file(filepath):\n    try:\n        with open(filepath, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n            return file.read()\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"File {filepath} not found. Using fallback text.\")\n\n        return (\n            \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. \"\n            \"The lazy dog barks at the brown fox. \"\n            \"The quick brown fox runs away quickly into the deep \"\n            \"dark brown forest. The dark forest is full of mystery. \"\n            \"A dog barks loudly in the dark.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef load_slicer(router):\n    if not GENSIM_AVAILABLE:\n        print(\"gensim not installed (pip install gensim). Using TF-IDF routing.\")\n        return None\n\n    glove_path = input(\n        \"Local GloVe .txt path (blank = download glove-wiki-gigaword-100): \"\n    ).strip()\n\n    try:\n        slicer = GloveSlicer(glove_path=glove_path or None)\n        slicer.index_segments(router.segments)\n        return slicer\n    except Exception as error:\n        print(f\"Could not load GloVe ({error}). Using TF-IDF routing.\")\n        return None\n\n\ndef main():\n    dataset_file = input(\"Dataset filename: \").strip()\n\n    dataset_text = load_text_file(dataset_file)\n\n    router = SegmentRouter(segment_words=900)\n\n    print(\"Splitting dataset into segments...\")\n    router.build_index(dataset_text)\n\n    slicer = load_slicer(router)\n\n    print(\"Building initial graph from the complete dataset...\")\n    graph, node_to_id, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\n        dataset_text,\n        max_nodes=150000,\n    )\n\n    if not graph:\n        print(\"Graph is empty. Check the dataset.\")\n        return\n\n    print(f\"Graph built with {len(graph)} unique nodes.\")\n\n    print(\"Running PCMMaxCut solver for structural baseline...\")\n\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\n        graph,\n        noise=0.00001,\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\n    )\n\n    history = solver.run(\n        iterations=5000,\n        temperature=0.0000005,\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\n    )\n\n    best_cut = max(\n        history,\n        key=lambda item: item[\"cut\"],\n    )\n\n    print(\n        f\"Base partition created. \"\n        f\"Max Cut Size: {best_cut['cut']}\\n\"\n    )\n\n    while True:\n        try:\n            user_prompt = input(\"USER: \").strip()\n        except (KeyboardInterrupt, EOFError):\n            print(\"\\nExiting.\")\n            break\n\n        if not user_prompt:\n            continue\n\n        if user_prompt.lower() in {\"exit\", \"quit\"}:\n            break\n\n        done = False\n\n        if slicer is not None:\n            done = glove_route_and_generate(\n                user_prompt,\n                router,\n                slicer,\n                width=2,\n                max_segments=3,\n                length=60,\n                max_columns=4,\n            )\n\n        # Fall back to TF-IDF routing if GloVe is unavailable or produced\n        # nothing for this prompt.\n        if not done:\n            tfidf_route_and_generate(\n                user_prompt,\n                router,\n                graph,\n                id_to_node,\n                best_cut[\"spins\"],\n            )\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}, "message": "Full script with the DistilBART summarizer removed; segments are embedded/ranked directly", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"import math\\nimport random\\nimport re\\nimport textwrap\\nfrom collections import Counter\\nfrom itertools import zip_longest\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer, ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\\nfrom sklearn.metrics.pairwise import cosine_similarity\\n\\n# gensim provides the GloVe vectors. If it is missing, the program falls\\n# back to TF-IDF routing over the raw segments.\\ntry:\\n    from gensim.models import KeyedVectors\\n    import gensim.downloader as gensim_api\\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = True\\nexcept ImportError:\\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = False\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# ORIGINAL SOLVER KEPT EXACTLY THE SAME\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nclass PCMMaxCut:\\n    def __init__(self, graph, noise=0.02, drift_nu=0.08):\\n        self.graph = graph\\n        self.n = len(graph)\\n        self.noise = noise\\n        self.drift_nu = drift_nu\\n        self.spins = [random.choice([-1, 1]) for _ in range(self.n)]\\n        self.age = 1\\n\\n    def local_field(self, i):\\n        return sum(\\n            weight * self.spins[j]\\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items()\\n        )\\n\\n    def delta_energy(self, i):\\n        return -2 * self.spins[i] * self.local_field(i)\\n\\n    def energy(self):\\n        value = 0.0\\n        for i in range(self.n):\\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\\n                if j > i:\\n                    value += weight * self.spins[i] * self.spins[j]\\n        return value\\n\\n    def cut_size(self):\\n        total = 0\\n        for i in range(self.n):\\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\\n                if j > i and self.spins[i] != self.spins[j]:\\n                    total += weight\\n        return total\\n\\n    def pcm_flip_attempt(self, temperature):\\n        i = random.randrange(self.n)\\n        delta = self.delta_energy(i)\\n\\n        drift = self.age ** (-self.drift_nu)\\n        thermal_noise = random.gauss(\\n            0.0,\\n            self.noise\\n        ) * max(1.0, abs(self.local_field(i)))\\n\\n        effective_delta = delta + thermal_noise * drift\\n\\n        if effective_delta <= 0:\\n            accept = True\\n        else:\\n            accept = random.random() < math.exp(\\n                -effective_delta / max(temperature, 1e-9)\\n            )\\n\\n        if accept:\\n            self.spins[i] *= -1\\n            return i, True, delta\\n\\n        return i, False, delta\\n\\n    def run(self, iterations=1000, temperature=1.0, cooling=0.995):\\n        history = []\\n\\n        for _ in range(iterations):\\n            _, accepted, _ = self.pcm_flip_attempt(temperature)\\n\\n            temperature *= cooling\\n            self.age += 1\\n\\n            history.append({\\n                \\\"energy\\\": self.energy(),\\n                \\\"cut\\\": self.cut_size(),\\n                \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n                \\\"temperature\\\": temperature,\\n                \\\"spins\\\": self.spins[:],\\n            })\\n\\n        return history\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# SEGMENT ROUTER (no summarizer)\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nclass SegmentRouter:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Splits a text dataset into word-count segments and selects the\\n    segments relevant to a prompt using TF-IDF over the raw segment text.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, segment_words=900):\\n        self.segment_words = segment_words\\n        self.segments = []\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def clean_text(text):\\n        text = text.replace(\\\"\\\\x00\\\", \\\" \\\")\\n        text = re.sub(r\\\"\\\\s+\\\", \\\" \\\", text)\\n        return text.strip()\\n\\n    def split_text(self, text):\\n        text = self.clean_text(text)\\n\\n        if not text:\\n            return []\\n\\n        words = text.split()\\n        segments = []\\n\\n        for start in range(0, len(words), self.segment_words):\\n            raw_segment = \\\" \\\".join(\\n                words[start:start + self.segment_words]\\n            )\\n\\n            if raw_segment:\\n                segments.append(raw_segment)\\n\\n        return segments\\n\\n    def build_index(self, text):\\n        self.segments = self.split_text(text)\\n\\n        if not self.segments:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"The dataset contains no usable text.\\\")\\n\\n        print(f\\\"Indexed {len(self.segments)} dataset segments.\\\")\\n\\n    def select_segments(self, prompt, max_segments=3, min_similarity=0.0):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"TF-IDF routing over raw segments (fallback when GloVe is unavailable).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not self.segments:\\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"Call build_index() before select_segments().\\\")\\n\\n        prompt = self.clean_text(prompt)\\n\\n        vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(\\n            lowercase=True,\\n            stop_words=\\\"english\\\",\\n            ngram_range=(1, 2),\\n        )\\n\\n        matrix = vectorizer.fit_transform(self.segments + [prompt])\\n        similarities = cosine_similarity(\\n            matrix[-1],\\n            matrix[:-1],\\n        )[0]\\n\\n        ranked = sorted(\\n            enumerate(similarities),\\n            key=lambda item: item[1],\\n            reverse=True,\\n        )\\n\\n        selected = [\\n            (index, float(score))\\n            for index, score in ranked[:max_segments]\\n            if score >= min_similarity\\n        ]\\n\\n        # Always select at least one segment.\\n        if not selected:\\n            selected = [(ranked[0][0], float(ranked[0][1]))]\\n\\n        return {\\n            \\\"selected\\\": selected,\\n            \\\"segments\\\": [self.segments[index] for index, _ in selected],\\n        }\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# GLOVE PROMPT SLICER\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\\\"[a-z']+\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef tokenize(text):\\n    return TOKEN_RE.findall(text.lower())\\n\\n\\ndef clean_word(word):\\n    return re.sub(r\\\"[^a-z']\\\", \\\"\\\", word.lower())\\n\\n\\nclass GloveSlicer:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Slices a prompt into word windows, embeds each slice with GloVe,\\n    measures the Manhattan (L1) distance to every dataset segment, probes\\n    the similarity peaks, and expands each slice's vocabulary with GloVe\\n    neighbours that exist in the dataset.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, glove_name=\\\"glove-wiki-gigaword-100\\\", glove_path=None):\\n        if glove_path:\\n            print(f\\\"Loading GloVe from {glove_path}\\\")\\n            self.kv = KeyedVectors.load_word2vec_format(\\n                glove_path, binary=False, no_header=True\\n            )\\n        else:\\n            print(f\\\"Loading GloVe: {glove_name} (cached after first download)\\\")\\n            self.kv = gensim_api.load(glove_name)\\n\\n        self.dim = self.kv.vector_size\\n        self.seg_vecs = None\\n\\n    # -- embedding -----------------------------------------------------\\n\\n    def embed(self, tokens):\\n        vecs = [self.kv[t] for t in tokens if t in self.kv]\\n        if not vecs:\\n            return None\\n        v = np.mean(vecs, axis=0)\\n        norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\\n        return v / norm if norm > 0 else None\\n\\n    def index_segments(self, segments):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Embed each raw segment (content words only).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self.seg_vecs = []\\n        for segment in segments:\\n            tokens = [t for t in tokenize(segment) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\\n            self.seg_vecs.append(self.embed(tokens))\\n\\n    # -- slicing -------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n    def slice_prompt(self, prompt, width=2, stride=1):\\n        tokens = [t for t in tokenize(prompt) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\\n        if not tokens:\\n            tokens = tokenize(prompt)\\n\\n        if len(tokens) <= width:\\n            windows = [tokens]\\n        else:\\n            windows = [\\n                tokens[i:i + width]\\n                for i in range(0, len(tokens) - width + 1, stride)\\n            ]\\n\\n        slices = []\\n        for window in windows:\\n            vec = self.embed(window)\\n            if vec is not None:\\n                slices.append((window, vec))\\n        return slices\\n\\n    # -- Manhattan distance and peaks ----------------------------------\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def manhattan(a, b):\\n        return float(np.abs(a - b).sum())\\n\\n    def distance_matrix(self, slices):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Shape (n_slices, n_segments); inf where a segment has no vector.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if self.seg_vecs is None:\\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"Call index_segments() first.\\\")\\n\\n        matrix = np.full((len(slices), len(self.seg_vecs)), np.inf)\\n        for i, (_, slice_vec) in enumerate(slices):\\n            for j, seg_vec in enumerate(self.seg_vecs):\\n                if seg_vec is not None:\\n                    matrix[i, j] = self.manhattan(slice_vec, seg_vec)\\n        return matrix\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def find_peaks(distances, prominence=0.5):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Similarity peaks (= local distance minima along the segment axis)\\n        at least `prominence` standard deviations above the slice average.\\n        Always returns at least the single best segment.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        score = -np.asarray(distances, dtype=float)\\n        finite = np.isfinite(score)\\n        if not finite.any():\\n            return []\\n\\n        threshold = score[finite].mean() + prominence * score[finite].std()\\n\\n        peaks = []\\n        for s in range(len(score)):\\n            if not finite[s]:\\n                continue\\n            left = score[s - 1] if s > 0 else -np.inf\\n            right = score[s + 1] if s < len(score) - 1 else -np.inf\\n            if score[s] >= left and score[s] >= right and score[s] >= threshold:\\n                peaks.append(s)\\n\\n        if not peaks:\\n            peaks = [int(np.argmax(np.where(finite, score, -np.inf)))]\\n        return peaks\\n\\n    def select_peak_segments(self, matrix, max_segments=3):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Rank segments by slice votes, then by best distance.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        votes, best, all_peaks = {}, {}, []\\n        for row in matrix:\\n            peaks = self.find_peaks(row)\\n            all_peaks.append(peaks)\\n            for p in peaks:\\n                votes[p] = votes.get(p, 0) + 1\\n                best[p] = min(best.get(p, np.inf), row[p])\\n\\n        ranked = sorted(votes, key=lambda p: (-votes[p], best[p]))\\n        return ranked[:max_segments], all_peaks\\n\\n    # -- accommodating vocabulary --------------------------------------\\n\\n    def expand_vocab(self, slice_tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Slice words plus nearest GloVe neighbours that also occur in the\\n        dataset graph, so the Markov walk can actually reach them.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        vocab = set(slice_tokens)\\n        added = 0\\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(slice_vec, topn=topn):\\n            if word in dataset_vocab and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS:\\n                vocab.add(word)\\n                added += 1\\n                if added >= keep:\\n                    break\\n        return vocab\\n\\n\\ndef dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Graph nodes keep raw whitespace tokens (\\\"dog.\\\", \\\"fox,\\\"), so map each\\n    cleaned word to every raw form present in the graph.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    clean_to_raw = {}\\n    for pair in id_to_node.values():\\n        for raw in pair:\\n            clean_to_raw.setdefault(clean_word(raw), set()).add(raw.lower())\\n    return clean_to_raw\\n\\n\\ndef to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw):\\n    raw = set()\\n    for word in clean_vocab:\\n        raw.update(clean_to_raw.get(word, {word}))\\n    return raw\\n\\n\\ndef print_distance_table(slices, matrix, all_peaks, selected):\\n    labels = [\\\" \\\".join(tokens)[:14] for tokens, _ in slices]\\n    col = 16\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nManhattan distance (segment x slice)   * = peak   > = selected\\\")\\n    print(\\\"seg    \\\" + \\\"\\\".join(label.ljust(col) for label in labels))\\n    for s in range(matrix.shape[1]):\\n        row = f\\\"{('>' if s in selected else ' ')}{s:<5} \\\"\\n        for i in range(matrix.shape[0]):\\n            d = matrix[i, s]\\n            cell = \\\"n/a\\\" if not np.isfinite(d) else f\\\"{d:.3f}\\\"\\n            if s in all_peaks[i]:\\n                cell += \\\" *\\\"\\n            row += cell.ljust(col)\\n        print(row)\\n\\n\\ndef render_side_by_side(columns, total_width=118, gap=3):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"columns: list of (header, text). Prints them as parallel columns.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    n = len(columns)\\n    width = max(18, (total_width - gap * (n - 1)) // n)\\n    wrapped = [textwrap.wrap(text, width) for _, text in columns]\\n    sep = \\\" \\\" * gap\\n\\n    lines = [sep.join(header[:width].ljust(width) for header, _ in columns)]\\n    lines.append(sep.join(\\\"-\\\" * width for _ in columns))\\n    for parts in zip_longest(*wrapped, fillvalue=\\\"\\\"):\\n        lines.append(sep.join(part.ljust(width) for part in parts))\\n    return \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines)\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# GRAPH CREATION\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef process_text_to_trigram_graph(text, max_nodes=200):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Builds a graph where nodes are bigrams and edges represent trigrams.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    text = text.lower()\\n    words = text.split()\\n\\n    if len(words) < 3:\\n        return {}, {}, {}\\n\\n    all_bigrams = [\\n        (words[i], words[i + 1])\\n        for i in range(len(words) - 1)\\n    ]\\n\\n    top_bigrams = [\\n        bigram\\n        for bigram, _ in Counter(all_bigrams).most_common(max_nodes)\\n    ]\\n\\n    bigram_set = set(top_bigrams)\\n\\n    node_to_id = {\\n        bigram: index\\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\\n    }\\n\\n    id_to_node = {\\n        index: bigram\\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\\n    }\\n\\n    graph = {\\n        index: {}\\n        for index in range(len(top_bigrams))\\n    }\\n\\n    for i in range(len(words) - 2):\\n        b1 = (words[i], words[i + 1])\\n        b2 = (words[i + 1], words[i + 2])\\n\\n        if b1 in bigram_set and b2 in bigram_set:\\n            id1 = node_to_id[b1]\\n            id2 = node_to_id[b2]\\n\\n            if id1 != id2:\\n                graph[id1][id2] = graph[id1].get(id2, 0) + 1\\n                graph[id2][id1] = graph[id2].get(id1, 0) + 1\\n\\n    return graph, node_to_id, id_to_node\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# PROMPT-AWARE MARKOV GENERATOR\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef generate_markovian_prompt_text(\\n    graph,\\n    id_to_node,\\n    spins,\\n    prompt_vocab,\\n    length=100,\\n):\\n    n = len(graph)\\n\\n    if n == 0:\\n        return \\\"\\\"\\n\\n    prompt_vocab = {\\n        word.lower()\\n        for word in prompt_vocab\\n        if word.strip()\\n    }\\n\\n    valid_starts = [\\n        i\\n        for i in range(n)\\n        if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in id_to_node[i])\\n    ]\\n\\n    current_node = (\\n        random.choice(valid_starts)\\n        if valid_starts\\n        else random.randrange(n)\\n    )\\n\\n    output = list(id_to_node[current_node])\\n\\n    for _ in range(max(0, length - 2)):\\n        current_spin = spins[current_node]\\n        neighbors = graph[current_node]\\n        current_word_2 = id_to_node[current_node][1]\\n\\n        valid_neighbors = [\\n            neighbor\\n            for neighbor in neighbors\\n            if id_to_node[neighbor][0] == current_word_2\\n        ]\\n\\n        if not valid_neighbors:\\n            fallback_nodes = [\\n                i\\n                for i, spin in enumerate(spins)\\n                if (\\n                    spin != current_spin\\n                    and id_to_node[i][0] == current_word_2\\n                )\\n            ]\\n\\n            if fallback_nodes:\\n                next_node = random.choice(fallback_nodes)\\n            else:\\n                next_node = random.randrange(n)\\n        else:\\n            probabilities = []\\n\\n            for neighbor in valid_neighbors:\\n                base_weight = graph[current_node][neighbor]\\n\\n                cut_multiplier = (\\n                    5.0\\n                    if spins[neighbor] != current_spin\\n                    else 1.0\\n                )\\n\\n                neighbor_words = id_to_node[neighbor]\\n\\n                prompt_multiplier = (\\n                    50.0\\n                    if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in neighbor_words)\\n                    else 1.0\\n                )\\n\\n                score = (\\n                    base_weight\\n                    * cut_multiplier\\n                    * prompt_multiplier\\n                )\\n\\n                probabilities.append(score)\\n\\n            next_node = random.choices(\\n                valid_neighbors,\\n                weights=probabilities,\\n                k=1,\\n            )[0]\\n\\n        output.append(id_to_node[next_node][1])\\n        current_node = next_node\\n\\n    return \\\" \\\".join(output)\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# SOLVE HELPER\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef solve_best_spins(graph):\\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\\n        graph,\\n        noise=0.00001,\\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\\n    )\\n\\n    history = solver.run(\\n        iterations=min(5000, max(500, len(graph) * 20)),\\n        temperature=0.0000005,\\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\\n    )\\n\\n    return max(history, key=lambda item: item[\\\"cut\\\"])[\\\"spins\\\"]\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# GLOVE ROUTE + SIDE-BY-SIDE GENERATION\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef glove_route_and_generate(\\n    prompt,\\n    router,\\n    slicer,\\n    width=2,\\n    max_segments=3,\\n    length=60,\\n    max_columns=4,\\n):\\n    slices = slicer.slice_prompt(prompt, width=width)\\n\\n    if not slices:\\n        print(\\\"GloVe knows none of the prompt words; no slices to probe.\\\")\\n        return False\\n\\n    # Keep the output readable: cap the number of side-by-side columns.\\n    if len(slices) > max_columns:\\n        step = len(slices) / max_columns\\n        slices = [slices[int(i * step)] for i in range(max_columns)]\\n\\n    matrix = slicer.distance_matrix(slices)\\n    selected, all_peaks = slicer.select_peak_segments(matrix, max_segments)\\n\\n    if not selected:\\n        print(\\\"No usable peaks found.\\\")\\n        return False\\n\\n    print_distance_table(slices, matrix, all_peaks, selected)\\n\\n    selected_text = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(router.segments[i] for i in sorted(selected))\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nBuilding peak-specific trigram graph...\\\")\\n    graph, _, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\\n        selected_text,\\n        max_nodes=150000,\\n    )\\n\\n    if not graph:\\n        print(\\\"Peak segments did not contain enough overlapping words.\\\")\\n        return False\\n\\n    print(f\\\"Peak-specific graph built with {len(graph)} nodes.\\\")\\n    spins = solve_best_spins(graph)\\n\\n    clean_to_raw = dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node)\\n    dataset_vocab = set(clean_to_raw)\\n\\n    columns = []\\n    for tokens, slice_vec in slices:\\n        clean_vocab = slicer.expand_vocab(tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab)\\n        raw_vocab = to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw)\\n\\n        text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\\n            graph,\\n            id_to_node,\\n            spins,\\n            raw_vocab,\\n            length=length,\\n        )\\n\\n        added = len(clean_vocab) - len(tokens)\\n        header = f\\\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] +{max(added, 0)} words\\\"\\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \\\".\\\"))\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nGenerated Output (one column per prompt slice):\\\\n\\\")\\n    print(render_side_by_side(columns))\\n    print()\\n    return True\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# TF-IDF FALLBACK\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef tfidf_route_and_generate(prompt, router, graph, id_to_node, best_spins):\\n    print(\\\"Routing prompt to relevant dataset segments...\\\")\\n\\n    routing = router.select_segments(prompt, max_segments=3)\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nSelected segments:\\\")\\n\\n    for (index, score), segment in zip(\\n        routing[\\\"selected\\\"],\\n        routing[\\\"segments\\\"],\\n    ):\\n        preview = segment[:100] + (\\\"...\\\" if len(segment) > 100 else \\\"\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"[Segment {index}, similarity={score:.4f}] {preview}\\\")\\n\\n    selected_text = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(routing[\\\"segments\\\"])\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nBuilding prompt-specific trigram graph...\\\")\\n\\n    selected_graph, _, selected_id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\\n        selected_text,\\n        max_nodes=150000,\\n    )\\n\\n    if not selected_graph:\\n        print(\\n            \\\"Selected segments did not contain enough \\\"\\n            \\\"overlapping words. Using the complete graph.\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n        selected_graph = graph\\n        selected_id_to_node = id_to_node\\n        selected_spins = best_spins\\n    else:\\n        print(\\n            f\\\"Prompt-specific graph built with \\\"\\n            f\\\"{len(selected_graph)} nodes.\\\"\\n        )\\n        selected_spins = solve_best_spins(selected_graph)\\n\\n    final_text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\\n        selected_graph,\\n        selected_id_to_node,\\n        selected_spins,\\n        prompt.split(),\\n        length=400,\\n    )\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nGenerated Output:\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"> {final_text.capitalize()}.\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# MAIN PROGRAM\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef load_text_file(filepath):\\n    try:\\n        with open(filepath, \\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as file:\\n            return file.read()\\n    except FileNotFoundError:\\n        print(f\\\"File {filepath} not found. Using fallback text.\\\")\\n\\n        return (\\n            \\\"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. \\\"\\n            \\\"The lazy dog barks at the brown fox. \\\"\\n            \\\"The quick brown fox runs away quickly into the deep \\\"\\n            \\\"dark brown forest. The dark forest is full of mystery. \\\"\\n            \\\"A dog barks loudly in the dark.\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n\\ndef load_slicer(router):\\n    if not GENSIM_AVAILABLE:\\n        print(\\\"gensim not installed (pip install gensim). Using TF-IDF routing.\\\")\\n        return None\\n\\n    glove_path = input(\\n        \\\"Local GloVe .txt path (blank = download glove-wiki-gigaword-100): \\\"\\n    ).strip()\\n\\n    try:\\n        slicer = GloveSlicer(glove_path=glove_path or None)\\n        slicer.index_segments(router.segments)\\n        return slicer\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        print(f\\\"Could not load GloVe ({error}). Using TF-IDF routing.\\\")\\n        return None\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    dataset_file = input(\\\"Dataset filename: \\\").strip()\\n\\n    dataset_text = load_text_file(dataset_file)\\n\\n    router = SegmentRouter(segment_words=900)\\n\\n    print(\\\"Splitting dataset into segments...\\\")\\n    router.build_index(dataset_text)\\n\\n    slicer = load_slicer(router)\\n\\n    print(\\\"Building initial graph from the complete dataset...\\\")\\n    graph, node_to_id, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\\n        dataset_text,\\n        max_nodes=150000,\\n    )\\n\\n    if not graph:\\n        print(\\\"Graph is empty. Check the dataset.\\\")\\n        return\\n\\n    print(f\\\"Graph built with {len(graph)} unique nodes.\\\")\\n\\n    print(\\\"Running PCMMaxCut solver for structural baseline...\\\")\\n\\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\\n        graph,\\n        noise=0.00001,\\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\\n    )\\n\\n    history = solver.run(\\n        iterations=5000,\\n        temperature=0.0000005,\\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\\n    )\\n\\n    best_cut = max(\\n        history,\\n        key=lambda item: item[\\\"cut\\\"],\\n    )\\n\\n    print(\\n        f\\\"Base partition created. \\\"\\n        f\\\"Max Cut Size: {best_cut['cut']}\\\\n\\\"\\n    )\\n\\n    while True:\\n        try:\\n            user_prompt = input(\\\"USER: \\\").strip()\\n        except (KeyboardInterrupt, EOFError):\\n            print(\\\"\\\\nExiting.\\\")\\n            break\\n\\n        if not user_prompt:\\n            continue\\n\\n        if user_prompt.lower() in {\\\"exit\\\", \\\"quit\\\"}:\\n            break\\n\\n        done = False\\n\\n        if slicer is not None:\\n            done = glove_route_and_generate(\\n                user_prompt,\\n                router,\\n                slicer,\\n                width=2,\\n                max_segments=3,\\n                length=60,\\n                max_columns=4,\\n            )\\n\\n        # Fall back to TF-IDF routing if GloVe is unavailable or produced\\n        # nothing for this prompt.\\n        if not done:\\n            tfidf_route_and_generate(\\n                user_prompt,\\n                router,\\n                graph,\\n                id_to_node,\\n                best_cut[\\\"spins\\\"],\\n            )\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\n\", \"filename\": \"/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:56:39.261120Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:56:39.261176Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01WtMBNDstUJz7ZAhUYEa54F", "name": "create_file", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:56:40.852763Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:56:41.530988Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01VUT9kqH7F7NTV82U5DRnhd", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 -m py_compile pcm_glove_full.py && echo OK && grep -nE \"torch|transformers|summar|json|hashlib\" pcm_glove_full.py || echo \"no summarizer references left\"", "description": "Syntax check and confirm no summarizer references remain"}, "message": "Syntax check and confirm no summarizer references remain", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 -m py_compile pcm_glove_full.py && echo OK && grep -nE \\\"torch|transformers|summar|json|hashlib\\\" pcm_glove_full.py || echo \\\"no summarizer references left\\\"\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:56:41.955086Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:56:41.955135Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01VUT9kqH7F7NTV82U5DRnhd", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"OK\\n106:# SEGMENT ROUTER (no summarizer)\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"OK\\n106:# SEGMENT ROUTER (no summarizer)\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:56:43.448530Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:56:43.697977Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_019KaH4eytRdvKvCqzq2EmKK", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:56:43.718463Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:56:43.718493Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_019KaH4eytRdvKvCqzq2EmKK", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py", "name": "pcm glove full", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:56:47.720597Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:56:47.731361Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I rewrote `pcm_glove_full.py` without the summarizer. It passes a syntax check, and the only remaining mention of \"summarizer\" is a section comment. I haven't run it end to end.\n\n- **Removed:** the DistilBART model, `torch` and `transformers` imports, the summary cache file, and the prompt-summarizing step. `DatasetRouter` is now `SegmentRouter`, which only splits the text into 900-word segments.\n- **GloVe routing:** each raw segment (stopwords dropped) is embedded directly, so the Manhattan distance compares prompt slices to the actual segment text.\n- **TF-IDF fallback:** it now ranks the raw segments, and the printout shows a 100-character preview instead of a summary.\n- **Dependencies:** you now need only `numpy`, `scikit-learn` and `gensim`. Startup is also much faster and needs no model download besides GloVe.\n\nBecause a 900-word segment is averaged into one vector, it can blur topics together. If the peaks look flat, try `segment_words=300` in `SegmentRouter(...)` for sharper contrast between segments.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T09:56:47.819222Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T09:56:47.819222Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fc0a-b6e9-743b-bc35-9957dd484cab"}, {"uuid": "01a0fc0c-a3e1-738e-9383-1d2231cd871b", "text": "remove the corpus segmentation", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:58:00.930557Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:58:00.930557Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "remove the corpus segmentation", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T09:58:00.930695Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T09:58:00.930695Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fc0a-b6e9-7db6-a11b-66dc8c97a8a4"}, {"uuid": "01a0fc0c-a3e1-7783-87e7-763fcb0f3fe4", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI rewrote `pcm_glove_full.py` with no corpus segmentation. The dataset is now a single graph. It compiles, and a smoke test with a stand-in for GloVe produced a peak table and three side-by-side columns. I haven't run it with the real GloVe vectors.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Segmentation removed:** `SegmentRouter`, segment embedding, TF-IDF routing and the per-prompt subgraph re-solve are all gone. `PCMMaxCut` runs once on the full graph, and its best spins are reused for every prompt.\n- **Peaks come from graph nodes:** the Manhattan distance from each prompt slice is measured to every bigram node, which is embedded once at startup. A peak is a node at least 1 standard deviation closer than average, capped at `top_k=5` per slice, and the single nearest node is always kept.\n- **Table:** the peak nodes appear as rows, with one distance column per slice and `*` marking a slice's own peaks.\n- **Vocabulary and seeding:** each slice's vocabulary is its words, up to 8 GloVe neighbours that occur in the graph, and the words of its peak nodes. That vocabulary biases the walk's starting node and the 50x boost, and the nodes are mapped to their raw forms (with punctuation) so the matching works.\n- **Side by side:** one generated column per slice, as before.\n- **Fallback:** if `gensim` is missing or GloVe knows none of the prompt words, it uses the original prompt-word biasing on the full graph.\n- **Dependencies:** `numpy`, `scikit-learn` (only for the stopword list) and `gensim`.\n\n**Side effects**\n- The peaks are now individual bigrams rather than whole passages, so the output is more focused but each node carries less context.\n- The smoke test showed the walk getting stuck in short loops like \"the lazy dog. the lazy dog.\" That comes from the tiny test text and the solver's near-zero temperature, but it is worth watching on your real data.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:58:00.925479Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:58:15.784415Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Reworking the routing logic without corpus segmentation."}, {"summary": "Designing peak-node probing to seed prompt generation without segments."}, {"summary": "Simplifying fallbacks and trimming dependencies before coding the rewrite."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:58:15.784515Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:58:16.190594Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_011T54wiYaXDWR8pYfCExvNz", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "rm -f /mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py && echo removed", "description": "Remove old version so it can be rewritten without corpus segmentation"}, "message": "Remove old version so it can be rewritten without corpus segmentation", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"rm -f /mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py && echo removed\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:58:19.009952Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:58:19.009986Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_011T54wiYaXDWR8pYfCExvNz", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"removed\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"removed\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:58:20.556620Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:58:53.785481Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01M2Kh5ZqbneHSv84Hrhxvss", "name": "create_file", "input": {"description": "Full script with no corpus segmentation: GloVe slices probe peaks directly across graph nodes", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py", "file_text": "import math\nimport random\nimport re\nimport textwrap\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom itertools import zip_longest\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\n\n# gensim provides the GloVe vectors. If it is missing, the program falls\n# back to plain prompt-word biasing on the full graph.\ntry:\n    from gensim.models import KeyedVectors\n    import gensim.downloader as gensim_api\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = False\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# ORIGINAL SOLVER KEPT EXACTLY THE SAME\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass PCMMaxCut:\n    def __init__(self, graph, noise=0.02, drift_nu=0.08):\n        self.graph = graph\n        self.n = len(graph)\n        self.noise = noise\n        self.drift_nu = drift_nu\n        self.spins = [random.choice([-1, 1]) for _ in range(self.n)]\n        self.age = 1\n\n    def local_field(self, i):\n        return sum(\n            weight * self.spins[j]\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items()\n        )\n\n    def delta_energy(self, i):\n        return -2 * self.spins[i] * self.local_field(i)\n\n    def energy(self):\n        value = 0.0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i:\n                    value += weight * self.spins[i] * self.spins[j]\n        return value\n\n    def cut_size(self):\n        total = 0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i and self.spins[i] != self.spins[j]:\n                    total += weight\n        return total\n\n    def pcm_flip_attempt(self, temperature):\n        i = random.randrange(self.n)\n        delta = self.delta_energy(i)\n\n        drift = self.age ** (-self.drift_nu)\n        thermal_noise = random.gauss(\n            0.0,\n            self.noise\n        ) * max(1.0, abs(self.local_field(i)))\n\n        effective_delta = delta + thermal_noise * drift\n\n        if effective_delta <= 0:\n            accept = True\n        else:\n            accept = random.random() < math.exp(\n                -effective_delta / max(temperature, 1e-9)\n            )\n\n        if accept:\n            self.spins[i] *= -1\n            return i, True, delta\n\n        return i, False, delta\n\n    def run(self, iterations=1000, temperature=1.0, cooling=0.995):\n        history = []\n\n        for _ in range(iterations):\n            _, accepted, _ = self.pcm_flip_attempt(temperature)\n\n            temperature *= cooling\n            self.age += 1\n\n            history.append({\n                \"energy\": self.energy(),\n                \"cut\": self.cut_size(),\n                \"accepted\": accepted,\n                \"temperature\": temperature,\n                \"spins\": self.spins[:],\n            })\n\n        return history\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TEXT HELPERS\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[a-z']+\")\n\n\ndef clean_text(text):\n    text = text.replace(\"\\x00\", \" \")\n    text = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", text)\n    return text.strip()\n\n\ndef tokenize(text):\n    return TOKEN_RE.findall(text.lower())\n\n\ndef clean_word(word):\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z']\", \"\", word.lower())\n\n\ndef content_tokens(words):\n    \"\"\"Cleaned, non-stopword tokens.\"\"\"\n    cleaned = (clean_word(w) for w in words)\n    return [w for w in cleaned if w and w not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GLOVE PROMPT SLICER (probes the graph directly, no corpus segments)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass GloveSlicer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Slices a prompt into word windows, embeds each slice with GloVe, and\n    measures the Manhattan (L1) distance from the slice to every bigram\n    node of the dataset graph. The nearest nodes are the peaks, which seed\n    generation. Each slice's vocabulary is expanded with GloVe neighbours\n    that exist in the dataset.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, glove_name=\"glove-wiki-gigaword-100\", glove_path=None):\n        if glove_path:\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe from {glove_path}\")\n            self.kv = KeyedVectors.load_word2vec_format(\n                glove_path, binary=False, no_header=True\n            )\n        else:\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe: {glove_name} (cached after first download)\")\n            self.kv = gensim_api.load(glove_name)\n\n        self.dim = self.kv.vector_size\n        self.node_matrix = None\n        self.node_valid = None\n\n    # -- embedding -----------------------------------------------------\n\n    def embed(self, tokens):\n        vecs = [self.kv[t] for t in tokens if t in self.kv]\n        if not vecs:\n            return None\n        v = np.mean(vecs, axis=0)\n        norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n        return (v / norm).astype(np.float32) if norm > 0 else None\n\n    def index_nodes(self, id_to_node):\n        \"\"\"Embed every bigram node (content words only).\"\"\"\n        n = len(id_to_node)\n        self.node_matrix = np.zeros((n, self.dim), dtype=np.float32)\n        self.node_valid = np.zeros(n, dtype=bool)\n\n        for index, pair in id_to_node.items():\n            vec = self.embed(content_tokens(pair))\n            if vec is not None:\n                self.node_matrix[index] = vec\n                self.node_valid[index] = True\n\n        print(\n            f\"Embedded {int(self.node_valid.sum())}/{n} graph nodes with GloVe.\"\n        )\n\n    # -- slicing -------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def slice_prompt(self, prompt, width=2, stride=1):\n        tokens = [t for t in tokenize(prompt) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\n        if not tokens:\n            tokens = tokenize(prompt)\n\n        if len(tokens) <= width:\n            windows = [tokens]\n        else:\n            windows = [\n                tokens[i:i + width]\n                for i in range(0, len(tokens) - width + 1, stride)\n            ]\n\n        slices = []\n        for window in windows:\n            vec = self.embed(window)\n            if vec is not None:\n                slices.append((window, vec))\n        return slices\n\n    # -- Manhattan distance and peaks ----------------------------------\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def manhattan(a, b):\n        return float(np.abs(a - b).sum())\n\n    def node_distances(self, slice_vec):\n        \"\"\"Manhattan distance from one slice to every node (inf if invalid).\"\"\"\n        if self.node_matrix is None:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Call index_nodes() first.\")\n\n        distances = np.abs(self.node_matrix - slice_vec).sum(axis=1)\n        distances[~self.node_valid] = np.inf\n        return distances\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def find_peaks(distances, top_k=5, prominence=1.0):\n        \"\"\"\n        Peaks = the nodes whose distance sits at least `prominence`\n        standard deviations below the mean, capped at top_k. Always\n        returns at least the single nearest node.\n        \"\"\"\n        finite = np.isfinite(distances)\n        if not finite.any():\n            return []\n\n        mean = distances[finite].mean()\n        std = distances[finite].std()\n\n        k = min(top_k, int(finite.sum()))\n        nearest = np.argpartition(np.where(finite, distances, np.inf), k - 1)[:k]\n        nearest = nearest[np.argsort(distances[nearest])]\n\n        if std == 0:\n            return [int(nearest[0])]\n\n        peaks = [\n            int(i) for i in nearest\n            if (mean - distances[i]) / std >= prominence\n        ]\n\n        return peaks or [int(nearest[0])]\n\n    # -- accommodating vocabulary --------------------------------------\n\n    def expand_vocab(self, slice_tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\n        \"\"\"\n        Slice words plus nearest GloVe neighbours that also occur in the\n        dataset graph, so the Markov walk can actually reach them.\n        \"\"\"\n        vocab = set(slice_tokens)\n        added = 0\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(slice_vec, topn=topn):\n            if word in dataset_vocab and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS:\n                vocab.add(word)\n                added += 1\n                if added >= keep:\n                    break\n        return vocab\n\n\ndef dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node):\n    \"\"\"\n    Graph nodes keep raw whitespace tokens (\"dog.\", \"fox,\"), so map each\n    cleaned word to every raw form present in the graph.\n    \"\"\"\n    clean_to_raw = {}\n    for pair in id_to_node.values():\n        for raw in pair:\n            clean_to_raw.setdefault(clean_word(raw), set()).add(raw.lower())\n    return clean_to_raw\n\n\ndef to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw):\n    raw = set()\n    for word in clean_vocab:\n        raw.update(clean_to_raw.get(word, {word}))\n    return raw\n\n\ndef print_peak_table(slices, per_slice_distances, per_slice_peaks, id_to_node, max_rows=12):\n    \"\"\"Peak nodes down the side, one distance column per slice.\"\"\"\n    best = {}\n    for peaks, distances in zip(per_slice_peaks, per_slice_distances):\n        for node in peaks:\n            best[node] = min(best.get(node, np.inf), distances[node])\n\n    rows = sorted(best, key=lambda node: best[node])[:max_rows]\n\n    labels = [\" \".join(tokens)[:14] for tokens, _ in slices]\n    col = 16\n    print(\"\\nManhattan distance (peak node x slice)   * = peak for that slice\")\n    print(\"node\".ljust(24) + \"\".join(label.ljust(col) for label in labels))\n\n    for node in rows:\n        name = \" \".join(id_to_node[node])[:22]\n        line = name.ljust(24)\n        for peaks, distances in zip(per_slice_peaks, per_slice_distances):\n            cell = f\"{distances[node]:.3f}\"\n            if node in peaks:\n                cell += \" *\"\n            line += cell.ljust(col)\n        print(line)\n\n\ndef render_side_by_side(columns, total_width=118, gap=3):\n    \"\"\"columns: list of (header, text). Prints them as parallel columns.\"\"\"\n    n = len(columns)\n    width = max(18, (total_width - gap * (n - 1)) // n)\n    wrapped = [textwrap.wrap(text, width) for _, text in columns]\n    sep = \" \" * gap\n\n    lines = [sep.join(header[:width].ljust(width) for header, _ in columns)]\n    lines.append(sep.join(\"-\" * width for _ in columns))\n    for parts in zip_longest(*wrapped, fillvalue=\"\"):\n        lines.append(sep.join(part.ljust(width) for part in parts))\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GRAPH CREATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef process_text_to_trigram_graph(text, max_nodes=200):\n    \"\"\"\n    Builds a graph where nodes are bigrams and edges represent trigrams.\n    \"\"\"\n    text = text.lower()\n    words = text.split()\n\n    if len(words) < 3:\n        return {}, {}, {}\n\n    all_bigrams = [\n        (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        for i in range(len(words) - 1)\n    ]\n\n    top_bigrams = [\n        bigram\n        for bigram, _ in Counter(all_bigrams).most_common(max_nodes)\n    ]\n\n    bigram_set = set(top_bigrams)\n\n    node_to_id = {\n        bigram: index\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    id_to_node = {\n        index: bigram\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    graph = {\n        index: {}\n        for index in range(len(top_bigrams))\n    }\n\n    for i in range(len(words) - 2):\n        b1 = (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        b2 = (words[i + 1], words[i + 2])\n\n        if b1 in bigram_set and b2 in bigram_set:\n            id1 = node_to_id[b1]\n            id2 = node_to_id[b2]\n\n            if id1 != id2:\n                graph[id1][id2] = graph[id1].get(id2, 0) + 1\n                graph[id2][id1] = graph[id2].get(id1, 0) + 1\n\n    return graph, node_to_id, id_to_node\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PROMPT-AWARE MARKOV GENERATOR\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n    graph,\n    id_to_node,\n    spins,\n    prompt_vocab,\n    length=100,\n):\n    n = len(graph)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return \"\"\n\n    prompt_vocab = {\n        word.lower()\n        for word in prompt_vocab\n        if word.strip()\n    }\n\n    valid_starts = [\n        i\n        for i in range(n)\n        if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in id_to_node[i])\n    ]\n\n    current_node = (\n        random.choice(valid_starts)\n        if valid_starts\n        else random.randrange(n)\n    )\n\n    output = list(id_to_node[current_node])\n\n    for _ in range(max(0, length - 2)):\n        current_spin = spins[current_node]\n        neighbors = graph[current_node]\n        current_word_2 = id_to_node[current_node][1]\n\n        valid_neighbors = [\n            neighbor\n            for neighbor in neighbors\n            if id_to_node[neighbor][0] == current_word_2\n        ]\n\n        if not valid_neighbors:\n            fallback_nodes = [\n                i\n                for i, spin in enumerate(spins)\n                if (\n                    spin != current_spin\n                    and id_to_node[i][0] == current_word_2\n                )\n            ]\n\n            if fallback_nodes:\n                next_node = random.choice(fallback_nodes)\n            else:\n                next_node = random.randrange(n)\n        else:\n            probabilities = []\n\n            for neighbor in valid_neighbors:\n                base_weight = graph[current_node][neighbor]\n\n                cut_multiplier = (\n                    5.0\n                    if spins[neighbor] != current_spin\n                    else 1.0\n                )\n\n                neighbor_words = id_to_node[neighbor]\n\n                prompt_multiplier = (\n                    50.0\n                    if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in neighbor_words)\n                    else 1.0\n                )\n\n                score = (\n                    base_weight\n                    * cut_multiplier\n                    * prompt_multiplier\n                )\n\n                probabilities.append(score)\n\n            next_node = random.choices(\n                valid_neighbors,\n                weights=probabilities,\n                k=1,\n            )[0]\n\n        output.append(id_to_node[next_node][1])\n        current_node = next_node\n\n    return \" \".join(output)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GLOVE PROBE + SIDE-BY-SIDE GENERATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef glove_probe_and_generate(\n    prompt,\n    slicer,\n    graph,\n    id_to_node,\n    spins,\n    clean_to_raw,\n    width=2,\n    top_k=5,\n    length=60,\n    max_columns=4,\n):\n    slices = slicer.slice_prompt(prompt, width=width)\n\n    if not slices:\n        print(\"GloVe knows none of the prompt words; no slices to probe.\")\n        return False\n\n    # Keep the output readable: cap the number of side-by-side columns.\n    if len(slices) > max_columns:\n        step = len(slices) / max_columns\n        slices = [slices[int(i * step)] for i in range(max_columns)]\n\n    per_slice_distances = [slicer.node_distances(vec) for _, vec in slices]\n    per_slice_peaks = [\n        slicer.find_peaks(d, top_k=top_k) for d in per_slice_distances\n    ]\n\n    if not any(per_slice_peaks):\n        print(\"No usable peaks found.\")\n        return False\n\n    print_peak_table(\n        slices, per_slice_distances, per_slice_peaks, id_to_node\n    )\n\n    dataset_vocab = set(clean_to_raw)\n\n    columns = []\n    for (tokens, slice_vec), peaks in zip(slices, per_slice_peaks):\n        clean_vocab = slicer.expand_vocab(tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab)\n        raw_vocab = to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw)\n\n        # The peak nodes' own words also seed the walk.\n        for node in peaks:\n            raw_vocab.update(id_to_node[node])\n\n        text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n            graph,\n            id_to_node,\n            spins,\n            raw_vocab,\n            length=length,\n        )\n\n        added = len(clean_vocab) - len(tokens)\n        header = f\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] +{max(added, 0)} words\"\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \".\"))\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated Output (one column per prompt slice):\\n\")\n    print(render_side_by_side(columns))\n    print()\n    return True\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PLAIN FALLBACK (no GloVe)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef plain_generate(prompt, graph, id_to_node, spins):\n    final_text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n        graph,\n        id_to_node,\n        spins,\n        prompt.split(),\n        length=400,\n    )\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated Output:\")\n    print(f\"> {final_text.capitalize()}.\\n\")\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# MAIN PROGRAM\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef load_text_file(filepath):\n    try:\n        with open(filepath, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n            return file.read()\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"File {filepath} not found. Using fallback text.\")\n\n        return (\n            \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. \"\n            \"The lazy dog barks at the brown fox. \"\n            \"The quick brown fox runs away quickly into the deep \"\n            \"dark brown forest. The dark forest is full of mystery. \"\n            \"A dog barks loudly in the dark.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef load_slicer(id_to_node):\n    if not GENSIM_AVAILABLE:\n        print(\"gensim not installed (pip install gensim). Using plain generation.\")\n        return None\n\n    glove_path = input(\n        \"Local GloVe .txt path (blank = download glove-wiki-gigaword-100): \"\n    ).strip()\n\n    try:\n        slicer = GloveSlicer(glove_path=glove_path or None)\n        slicer.index_nodes(id_to_node)\n        return slicer\n    except Exception as error:\n        print(f\"Could not load GloVe ({error}). Using plain generation.\")\n        return None\n\n\ndef main():\n    dataset_file = input(\"Dataset filename: \").strip()\n\n    dataset_text = clean_text(load_text_file(dataset_file))\n\n    print(\"Building graph from the complete dataset...\")\n    graph, node_to_id, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\n        dataset_text,\n        max_nodes=150000,\n    )\n\n    if not graph:\n        print(\"Graph is empty. Check the dataset.\")\n        return\n\n    print(f\"Graph built with {len(graph)} unique nodes.\")\n\n    print(\"Running PCMMaxCut solver for structural baseline...\")\n\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\n        graph,\n        noise=0.00001,\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\n    )\n\n    history = solver.run(\n        iterations=5000,\n        temperature=0.0000005,\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\n    )\n\n    best_cut = max(\n        history,\n        key=lambda item: item[\"cut\"],\n    )\n\n    print(\n        f\"Base partition created. \"\n        f\"Max Cut Size: {best_cut['cut']}\\n\"\n    )\n\n    spins = best_cut[\"spins\"]\n    clean_to_raw = dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node)\n    slicer = load_slicer(id_to_node)\n\n    while True:\n        try:\n            user_prompt = input(\"USER: \").strip()\n        except (KeyboardInterrupt, EOFError):\n            print(\"\\nExiting.\")\n            break\n\n        if not user_prompt:\n            continue\n\n        if user_prompt.lower() in {\"exit\", \"quit\"}:\n            break\n\n        done = False\n\n        if slicer is not None:\n            done = glove_probe_and_generate(\n                user_prompt,\n                slicer,\n                graph,\n                id_to_node,\n                spins,\n                clean_to_raw,\n                width=2,\n                top_k=5,\n                length=60,\n                max_columns=4,\n            )\n\n        # Fall back to plain prompt-word biasing if GloVe is unavailable\n        # or knows none of the prompt words.\n        if not done:\n            plain_generate(user_prompt, graph, id_to_node, spins)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}, "message": "Full script with no corpus segmentation: GloVe slices probe peaks directly across graph nodes", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"import math\\nimport random\\nimport re\\nimport textwrap\\nfrom collections import Counter\\nfrom itertools import zip_longest\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\\n\\n# gensim provides the GloVe vectors. If it is missing, the program falls\\n# back to plain prompt-word biasing on the full graph.\\ntry:\\n    from gensim.models import KeyedVectors\\n    import gensim.downloader as gensim_api\\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = True\\nexcept ImportError:\\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = False\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# ORIGINAL SOLVER KEPT EXACTLY THE SAME\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nclass PCMMaxCut:\\n    def __init__(self, graph, noise=0.02, drift_nu=0.08):\\n        self.graph = graph\\n        self.n = len(graph)\\n        self.noise = noise\\n        self.drift_nu = drift_nu\\n        self.spins = [random.choice([-1, 1]) for _ in range(self.n)]\\n        self.age = 1\\n\\n    def local_field(self, i):\\n        return sum(\\n            weight * self.spins[j]\\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items()\\n        )\\n\\n    def delta_energy(self, i):\\n        return -2 * self.spins[i] * self.local_field(i)\\n\\n    def energy(self):\\n        value = 0.0\\n        for i in range(self.n):\\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\\n                if j > i:\\n                    value += weight * self.spins[i] * self.spins[j]\\n        return value\\n\\n    def cut_size(self):\\n        total = 0\\n        for i in range(self.n):\\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\\n                if j > i and self.spins[i] != self.spins[j]:\\n                    total += weight\\n        return total\\n\\n    def pcm_flip_attempt(self, temperature):\\n        i = random.randrange(self.n)\\n        delta = self.delta_energy(i)\\n\\n        drift = self.age ** (-self.drift_nu)\\n        thermal_noise = random.gauss(\\n            0.0,\\n            self.noise\\n        ) * max(1.0, abs(self.local_field(i)))\\n\\n        effective_delta = delta + thermal_noise * drift\\n\\n        if effective_delta <= 0:\\n            accept = True\\n        else:\\n            accept = random.random() < math.exp(\\n                -effective_delta / max(temperature, 1e-9)\\n            )\\n\\n        if accept:\\n            self.spins[i] *= -1\\n            return i, True, delta\\n\\n        return i, False, delta\\n\\n    def run(self, iterations=1000, temperature=1.0, cooling=0.995):\\n        history = []\\n\\n        for _ in range(iterations):\\n            _, accepted, _ = self.pcm_flip_attempt(temperature)\\n\\n            temperature *= cooling\\n            self.age += 1\\n\\n            history.append({\\n                \\\"energy\\\": self.energy(),\\n                \\\"cut\\\": self.cut_size(),\\n                \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n                \\\"temperature\\\": temperature,\\n                \\\"spins\\\": self.spins[:],\\n            })\\n\\n        return history\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# TEXT HELPERS\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\\\"[a-z']+\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef clean_text(text):\\n    text = text.replace(\\\"\\\\x00\\\", \\\" \\\")\\n    text = re.sub(r\\\"\\\\s+\\\", \\\" \\\", text)\\n    return text.strip()\\n\\n\\ndef tokenize(text):\\n    return TOKEN_RE.findall(text.lower())\\n\\n\\ndef clean_word(word):\\n    return re.sub(r\\\"[^a-z']\\\", \\\"\\\", word.lower())\\n\\n\\ndef content_tokens(words):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Cleaned, non-stopword tokens.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    cleaned = (clean_word(w) for w in words)\\n    return [w for w in cleaned if w and w not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# GLOVE PROMPT SLICER (probes the graph directly, no corpus segments)\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nclass GloveSlicer:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Slices a prompt into word windows, embeds each slice with GloVe, and\\n    measures the Manhattan (L1) distance from the slice to every bigram\\n    node of the dataset graph. The nearest nodes are the peaks, which seed\\n    generation. Each slice's vocabulary is expanded with GloVe neighbours\\n    that exist in the dataset.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, glove_name=\\\"glove-wiki-gigaword-100\\\", glove_path=None):\\n        if glove_path:\\n            print(f\\\"Loading GloVe from {glove_path}\\\")\\n            self.kv = KeyedVectors.load_word2vec_format(\\n                glove_path, binary=False, no_header=True\\n            )\\n        else:\\n            print(f\\\"Loading GloVe: {glove_name} (cached after first download)\\\")\\n            self.kv = gensim_api.load(glove_name)\\n\\n        self.dim = self.kv.vector_size\\n        self.node_matrix = None\\n        self.node_valid = None\\n\\n    # -- embedding -----------------------------------------------------\\n\\n    def embed(self, tokens):\\n        vecs = [self.kv[t] for t in tokens if t in self.kv]\\n        if not vecs:\\n            return None\\n        v = np.mean(vecs, axis=0)\\n        norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\\n        return (v / norm).astype(np.float32) if norm > 0 else None\\n\\n    def index_nodes(self, id_to_node):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Embed every bigram node (content words only).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        n = len(id_to_node)\\n        self.node_matrix = np.zeros((n, self.dim), dtype=np.float32)\\n        self.node_valid = np.zeros(n, dtype=bool)\\n\\n        for index, pair in id_to_node.items():\\n            vec = self.embed(content_tokens(pair))\\n            if vec is not None:\\n                self.node_matrix[index] = vec\\n                self.node_valid[index] = True\\n\\n        print(\\n            f\\\"Embedded {int(self.node_valid.sum())}/{n} graph nodes with GloVe.\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n    # -- slicing -------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n    def slice_prompt(self, prompt, width=2, stride=1):\\n        tokens = [t for t in tokenize(prompt) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\\n        if not tokens:\\n            tokens = tokenize(prompt)\\n\\n        if len(tokens) <= width:\\n            windows = [tokens]\\n        else:\\n            windows = [\\n                tokens[i:i + width]\\n                for i in range(0, len(tokens) - width + 1, stride)\\n            ]\\n\\n        slices = []\\n        for window in windows:\\n            vec = self.embed(window)\\n            if vec is not None:\\n                slices.append((window, vec))\\n        return slices\\n\\n    # -- Manhattan distance and peaks ----------------------------------\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def manhattan(a, b):\\n        return float(np.abs(a - b).sum())\\n\\n    def node_distances(self, slice_vec):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Manhattan distance from one slice to every node (inf if invalid).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if self.node_matrix is None:\\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"Call index_nodes() first.\\\")\\n\\n        distances = np.abs(self.node_matrix - slice_vec).sum(axis=1)\\n        distances[~self.node_valid] = np.inf\\n        return distances\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def find_peaks(distances, top_k=5, prominence=1.0):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Peaks = the nodes whose distance sits at least `prominence`\\n        standard deviations below the mean, capped at top_k. Always\\n        returns at least the single nearest node.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        finite = np.isfinite(distances)\\n        if not finite.any():\\n            return []\\n\\n        mean = distances[finite].mean()\\n        std = distances[finite].std()\\n\\n        k = min(top_k, int(finite.sum()))\\n        nearest = np.argpartition(np.where(finite, distances, np.inf), k - 1)[:k]\\n        nearest = nearest[np.argsort(distances[nearest])]\\n\\n        if std == 0:\\n            return [int(nearest[0])]\\n\\n        peaks = [\\n            int(i) for i in nearest\\n            if (mean - distances[i]) / std >= prominence\\n        ]\\n\\n        return peaks or [int(nearest[0])]\\n\\n    # -- accommodating vocabulary --------------------------------------\\n\\n    def expand_vocab(self, slice_tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Slice words plus nearest GloVe neighbours that also occur in the\\n        dataset graph, so the Markov walk can actually reach them.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        vocab = set(slice_tokens)\\n        added = 0\\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(slice_vec, topn=topn):\\n            if word in dataset_vocab and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS:\\n                vocab.add(word)\\n                added += 1\\n                if added >= keep:\\n                    break\\n        return vocab\\n\\n\\ndef dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Graph nodes keep raw whitespace tokens (\\\"dog.\\\", \\\"fox,\\\"), so map each\\n    cleaned word to every raw form present in the graph.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    clean_to_raw = {}\\n    for pair in id_to_node.values():\\n        for raw in pair:\\n            clean_to_raw.setdefault(clean_word(raw), set()).add(raw.lower())\\n    return clean_to_raw\\n\\n\\ndef to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw):\\n    raw = set()\\n    for word in clean_vocab:\\n        raw.update(clean_to_raw.get(word, {word}))\\n    return raw\\n\\n\\ndef print_peak_table(slices, per_slice_distances, per_slice_peaks, id_to_node, max_rows=12):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Peak nodes down the side, one distance column per slice.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    best = {}\\n    for peaks, distances in zip(per_slice_peaks, per_slice_distances):\\n        for node in peaks:\\n            best[node] = min(best.get(node, np.inf), distances[node])\\n\\n    rows = sorted(best, key=lambda node: best[node])[:max_rows]\\n\\n    labels = [\\\" \\\".join(tokens)[:14] for tokens, _ in slices]\\n    col = 16\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nManhattan distance (peak node x slice)   * = peak for that slice\\\")\\n    print(\\\"node\\\".ljust(24) + \\\"\\\".join(label.ljust(col) for label in labels))\\n\\n    for node in rows:\\n        name = \\\" \\\".join(id_to_node[node])[:22]\\n        line = name.ljust(24)\\n        for peaks, distances in zip(per_slice_peaks, per_slice_distances):\\n            cell = f\\\"{distances[node]:.3f}\\\"\\n            if node in peaks:\\n                cell += \\\" *\\\"\\n            line += cell.ljust(col)\\n        print(line)\\n\\n\\ndef render_side_by_side(columns, total_width=118, gap=3):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"columns: list of (header, text). Prints them as parallel columns.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    n = len(columns)\\n    width = max(18, (total_width - gap * (n - 1)) // n)\\n    wrapped = [textwrap.wrap(text, width) for _, text in columns]\\n    sep = \\\" \\\" * gap\\n\\n    lines = [sep.join(header[:width].ljust(width) for header, _ in columns)]\\n    lines.append(sep.join(\\\"-\\\" * width for _ in columns))\\n    for parts in zip_longest(*wrapped, fillvalue=\\\"\\\"):\\n        lines.append(sep.join(part.ljust(width) for part in parts))\\n    return \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines)\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# GRAPH CREATION\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef process_text_to_trigram_graph(text, max_nodes=200):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Builds a graph where nodes are bigrams and edges represent trigrams.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    text = text.lower()\\n    words = text.split()\\n\\n    if len(words) < 3:\\n        return {}, {}, {}\\n\\n    all_bigrams = [\\n        (words[i], words[i + 1])\\n        for i in range(len(words) - 1)\\n    ]\\n\\n    top_bigrams = [\\n        bigram\\n        for bigram, _ in Counter(all_bigrams).most_common(max_nodes)\\n    ]\\n\\n    bigram_set = set(top_bigrams)\\n\\n    node_to_id = {\\n        bigram: index\\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\\n    }\\n\\n    id_to_node = {\\n        index: bigram\\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\\n    }\\n\\n    graph = {\\n        index: {}\\n        for index in range(len(top_bigrams))\\n    }\\n\\n    for i in range(len(words) - 2):\\n        b1 = (words[i], words[i + 1])\\n        b2 = (words[i + 1], words[i + 2])\\n\\n        if b1 in bigram_set and b2 in bigram_set:\\n            id1 = node_to_id[b1]\\n            id2 = node_to_id[b2]\\n\\n            if id1 != id2:\\n                graph[id1][id2] = graph[id1].get(id2, 0) + 1\\n                graph[id2][id1] = graph[id2].get(id1, 0) + 1\\n\\n    return graph, node_to_id, id_to_node\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# PROMPT-AWARE MARKOV GENERATOR\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef generate_markovian_prompt_text(\\n    graph,\\n    id_to_node,\\n    spins,\\n    prompt_vocab,\\n    length=100,\\n):\\n    n = len(graph)\\n\\n    if n == 0:\\n        return \\\"\\\"\\n\\n    prompt_vocab = {\\n        word.lower()\\n        for word in prompt_vocab\\n        if word.strip()\\n    }\\n\\n    valid_starts = [\\n        i\\n        for i in range(n)\\n        if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in id_to_node[i])\\n    ]\\n\\n    current_node = (\\n        random.choice(valid_starts)\\n        if valid_starts\\n        else random.randrange(n)\\n    )\\n\\n    output = list(id_to_node[current_node])\\n\\n    for _ in range(max(0, length - 2)):\\n        current_spin = spins[current_node]\\n        neighbors = graph[current_node]\\n        current_word_2 = id_to_node[current_node][1]\\n\\n        valid_neighbors = [\\n            neighbor\\n            for neighbor in neighbors\\n            if id_to_node[neighbor][0] == current_word_2\\n        ]\\n\\n        if not valid_neighbors:\\n            fallback_nodes = [\\n                i\\n                for i, spin in enumerate(spins)\\n                if (\\n                    spin != current_spin\\n                    and id_to_node[i][0] == current_word_2\\n                )\\n            ]\\n\\n            if fallback_nodes:\\n                next_node = random.choice(fallback_nodes)\\n            else:\\n                next_node = random.randrange(n)\\n        else:\\n            probabilities = []\\n\\n            for neighbor in valid_neighbors:\\n                base_weight = graph[current_node][neighbor]\\n\\n                cut_multiplier = (\\n                    5.0\\n                    if spins[neighbor] != current_spin\\n                    else 1.0\\n                )\\n\\n                neighbor_words = id_to_node[neighbor]\\n\\n                prompt_multiplier = (\\n                    50.0\\n                    if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in neighbor_words)\\n                    else 1.0\\n                )\\n\\n                score = (\\n                    base_weight\\n                    * cut_multiplier\\n                    * prompt_multiplier\\n                )\\n\\n                probabilities.append(score)\\n\\n            next_node = random.choices(\\n                valid_neighbors,\\n                weights=probabilities,\\n                k=1,\\n            )[0]\\n\\n        output.append(id_to_node[next_node][1])\\n        current_node = next_node\\n\\n    return \\\" \\\".join(output)\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# GLOVE PROBE + SIDE-BY-SIDE GENERATION\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef glove_probe_and_generate(\\n    prompt,\\n    slicer,\\n    graph,\\n    id_to_node,\\n    spins,\\n    clean_to_raw,\\n    width=2,\\n    top_k=5,\\n    length=60,\\n    max_columns=4,\\n):\\n    slices = slicer.slice_prompt(prompt, width=width)\\n\\n    if not slices:\\n        print(\\\"GloVe knows none of the prompt words; no slices to probe.\\\")\\n        return False\\n\\n    # Keep the output readable: cap the number of side-by-side columns.\\n    if len(slices) > max_columns:\\n        step = len(slices) / max_columns\\n        slices = [slices[int(i * step)] for i in range(max_columns)]\\n\\n    per_slice_distances = [slicer.node_distances(vec) for _, vec in slices]\\n    per_slice_peaks = [\\n        slicer.find_peaks(d, top_k=top_k) for d in per_slice_distances\\n    ]\\n\\n    if not any(per_slice_peaks):\\n        print(\\\"No usable peaks found.\\\")\\n        return False\\n\\n    print_peak_table(\\n        slices, per_slice_distances, per_slice_peaks, id_to_node\\n    )\\n\\n    dataset_vocab = set(clean_to_raw)\\n\\n    columns = []\\n    for (tokens, slice_vec), peaks in zip(slices, per_slice_peaks):\\n        clean_vocab = slicer.expand_vocab(tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab)\\n        raw_vocab = to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw)\\n\\n        # The peak nodes' own words also seed the walk.\\n        for node in peaks:\\n            raw_vocab.update(id_to_node[node])\\n\\n        text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\\n            graph,\\n            id_to_node,\\n            spins,\\n            raw_vocab,\\n            length=length,\\n        )\\n\\n        added = len(clean_vocab) - len(tokens)\\n        header = f\\\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] +{max(added, 0)} words\\\"\\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \\\".\\\"))\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nGenerated Output (one column per prompt slice):\\\\n\\\")\\n    print(render_side_by_side(columns))\\n    print()\\n    return True\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# PLAIN FALLBACK (no GloVe)\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef plain_generate(prompt, graph, id_to_node, spins):\\n    final_text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\\n        graph,\\n        id_to_node,\\n        spins,\\n        prompt.split(),\\n        length=400,\\n    )\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nGenerated Output:\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"> {final_text.capitalize()}.\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# MAIN PROGRAM\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef load_text_file(filepath):\\n    try:\\n        with open(filepath, \\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as file:\\n            return file.read()\\n    except FileNotFoundError:\\n        print(f\\\"File {filepath} not found. Using fallback text.\\\")\\n\\n        return (\\n            \\\"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. \\\"\\n            \\\"The lazy dog barks at the brown fox. \\\"\\n            \\\"The quick brown fox runs away quickly into the deep \\\"\\n            \\\"dark brown forest. The dark forest is full of mystery. \\\"\\n            \\\"A dog barks loudly in the dark.\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n\\ndef load_slicer(id_to_node):\\n    if not GENSIM_AVAILABLE:\\n        print(\\\"gensim not installed (pip install gensim). Using plain generation.\\\")\\n        return None\\n\\n    glove_path = input(\\n        \\\"Local GloVe .txt path (blank = download glove-wiki-gigaword-100): \\\"\\n    ).strip()\\n\\n    try:\\n        slicer = GloveSlicer(glove_path=glove_path or None)\\n        slicer.index_nodes(id_to_node)\\n        return slicer\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        print(f\\\"Could not load GloVe ({error}). Using plain generation.\\\")\\n        return None\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    dataset_file = input(\\\"Dataset filename: \\\").strip()\\n\\n    dataset_text = clean_text(load_text_file(dataset_file))\\n\\n    print(\\\"Building graph from the complete dataset...\\\")\\n    graph, node_to_id, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\\n        dataset_text,\\n        max_nodes=150000,\\n    )\\n\\n    if not graph:\\n        print(\\\"Graph is empty. Check the dataset.\\\")\\n        return\\n\\n    print(f\\\"Graph built with {len(graph)} unique nodes.\\\")\\n\\n    print(\\\"Running PCMMaxCut solver for structural baseline...\\\")\\n\\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\\n        graph,\\n        noise=0.00001,\\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\\n    )\\n\\n    history = solver.run(\\n        iterations=5000,\\n        temperature=0.0000005,\\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\\n    )\\n\\n    best_cut = max(\\n        history,\\n        key=lambda item: item[\\\"cut\\\"],\\n    )\\n\\n    print(\\n        f\\\"Base partition created. \\\"\\n        f\\\"Max Cut Size: {best_cut['cut']}\\\\n\\\"\\n    )\\n\\n    spins = best_cut[\\\"spins\\\"]\\n    clean_to_raw = dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node)\\n    slicer = load_slicer(id_to_node)\\n\\n    while True:\\n        try:\\n            user_prompt = input(\\\"USER: \\\").strip()\\n        except (KeyboardInterrupt, EOFError):\\n            print(\\\"\\\\nExiting.\\\")\\n            break\\n\\n        if not user_prompt:\\n            continue\\n\\n        if user_prompt.lower() in {\\\"exit\\\", \\\"quit\\\"}:\\n            break\\n\\n        done = False\\n\\n        if slicer is not None:\\n            done = glove_probe_and_generate(\\n                user_prompt,\\n                slicer,\\n                graph,\\n                id_to_node,\\n                spins,\\n                clean_to_raw,\\n                width=2,\\n                top_k=5,\\n                length=60,\\n                max_columns=4,\\n            )\\n\\n        # Fall back to plain prompt-word biasing if GloVe is unavailable\\n        # or knows none of the prompt words.\\n        if not done:\\n            plain_generate(user_prompt, graph, id_to_node, spins)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\n\", \"filename\": \"/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:58:54.571747Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:58:54.571783Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01M2Kh5ZqbneHSv84Hrhxvss", "name": "create_file", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:58:56.433394Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:59:00.246665Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_014arita7pMdFAFd2VD9qyrZ", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 -m py_compile pcm_glove_full.py && echo COMPILED && grep -niE \"segment|summar|torch|transformers\" pcm_glove_full.py || echo \"no segment/summarizer refs\"\ncat > /tmp/smoke.py << 'EOF'\nimport sys, random, numpy as np\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/mnt/user-data/outputs\")\nimport pcm_glove_full as m\n\nclass FakeKV:\n    vector_size = 16\n    def __init__(self, vocab):\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(0)\n        self.v = {w: rng.normal(size=16) for w in vocab}\n    def __getitem__(self, k): return self.v[k]\n    def __contains__(self, k): return k in self.v\n    def similar_by_vector(self, vec, topn=10):\n        s = sorted(self.v, key=lambda w: np.abs(self.v[w]/np.linalg.norm(self.v[w]) - vec).sum())\n        return [(w, 0) for w in s[:topn]]\n\ntext = m.clean_text(\"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. The lazy dog barks at the brown fox. The quick brown fox runs away quickly into the deep dark brown forest. The dark forest is full of mystery. A dog barks loudly in the dark.\")\ng, n2i, i2n = m.process_text_to_trigram_graph(text, 1000)\nvocab = {m.clean_word(w) for w in text.split()}\nsl = object.__new__(m.GloveSlicer)\nsl.kv = FakeKV(vocab); sl.dim = 16; sl.node_matrix = None\nsl.index_nodes(i2n)\nspins = [random.choice([-1,1]) for _ in g]\nok = m.glove_probe_and_generate(\"tell me about the dark brown fox\", sl, g, i2n, spins, m.dataset_vocab_from_nodes(i2n), length=25)\nprint(\"returned\", ok)\nEOF\npython3 /tmp/smoke.py", "description": "Compile check, confirm no segment refs, and smoke-test the probe pipeline with a fake GloVe"}, "message": "Compile check, confirm no segment refs, and smoke-test the probe pipeline with a fake GloVe", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 -m py_compile pcm_glove_full.py && echo COMPILED && grep -niE \\\"segment|summar|torch|transformers\\\" pcm_glove_full.py || echo \\\"no segment/summarizer refs\\\"\\ncat > /tmp/smoke.py << 'EOF'\\nimport sys, random, numpy as np\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\"/mnt/user-data/outputs\\\")\\nimport pcm_glove_full as m\\n\\nclass FakeKV:\\n    vector_size = 16\\n    def __init__(self, vocab):\\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(0)\\n        self.v = {w: rng.normal(size=16) for w in vocab}\\n    def __getitem__(self, k): return self.v[k]\\n    def __contains__(self, k): return k in self.v\\n    def similar_by_vector(self, vec, topn=10):\\n        s = sorted(self.v, key=lambda w: np.abs(self.v[w]/np.linalg.norm(self.v[w]) - vec).sum())\\n        return [(w, 0) for w in s[:topn]]\\n\\ntext = m.clean_text(\\\"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. The lazy dog barks at the brown fox. The quick brown fox runs away quickly into the deep dark brown forest. The dark forest is full of mystery. A dog barks loudly in the dark.\\\")\\ng, n2i, i2n = m.process_text_to_trigram_graph(text, 1000)\\nvocab = {m.clean_word(w) for w in text.split()}\\nsl = object.__new__(m.GloveSlicer)\\nsl.kv = FakeKV(vocab); sl.dim = 16; sl.node_matrix = None\\nsl.index_nodes(i2n)\\nspins = [random.choice([-1,1]) for _ in g]\\nok = m.glove_probe_and_generate(\\\"tell me about the dark brown fox\\\", sl, g, i2n, spins, m.dataset_vocab_from_nodes(i2n), length=25)\\nprint(\\\"returned\\\", ok)\\nEOF\\npython3 /tmp/smoke.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:59:02.465777Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:59:02.465820Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_014arita7pMdFAFd2VD9qyrZ", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"COMPILED\\n132:# GLOVE PROMPT SLICER (probes the graph directly, no corpus segments)\\nEmbedded 32/38 graph nodes with GloVe.\\n\\nManhattan distance (peak node x slice)   * = peak for that slice\\nnode                    tell dark       dark brown      brown fox       \\nthe dark                0.000 *         2.487 *         5.296           \\nthe dark.               0.000 *         2.487 *         5.296           \\ndark brown              2.487 *         0.000 *         4.310           \\nbrown fox               5.296           4.310           0.000 *         \\nbrown fox.              5.296           4.310           0.000 *         \\nthe brown               4.750           2.413 *         3.498           \\nfox. the                5.530           5.371           2.690 *         \\ndark forest             2.859 *         3.414           5.634           \\nfox jumps               5.109           5.044           2.903 *         \\n\\nGenerated Output (one column per prompt slice):\\n\\n[tell dark] +7 words                    [dark brown] +6 words                   [brown fox] +6 words                 \\n-------------------------------------   -------------------------------------   -------------------------------------\\nThe brown fox. the quick brown fox      Lazy dog. the lazy dog. the lazy dog.   The lazy dog. the lazy dog barks at  \\njumps over the lazy dog barks loudly    the lazy dog. the lazy dog. the lazy    the brown fox. the quick brown fox   \\nin the dark. in the dark. away          dog. the lazy dog. the lazy dog. the    jumps over the lazy dog. the lazy    \\nquickly into the deep.                  lazy.                                   dog. the lazy.                       \\n\\nreturned True\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"COMPILED\\n132:# GLOVE PROMPT SLICER (probes the graph directly, no corpus segments)\\nEmbedded 32/38 graph nodes with GloVe.\\n\\nManhattan distance (peak node x slice)   * = peak for that slice\\nnode                    tell dark       dark brown      brown fox       \\nthe dark                0.000 *         2.487 *         5.296           \\nthe dark.               0.000 *         2.487 *         5.296           \\ndark brown              2.487 *         0.000 *         4.310           \\nbrown fox               5.296           4.310           0.000 *         \\nbrown fox.              5.296           4.310           0.000 *         \\nthe brown               4.750           2.413 *         3.498           \\nfox. the                5.530           5.371           2.690 *         \\ndark forest             2.859 *         3.414           5.634           \\nfox jumps               5.109           5.044           2.903 *         \\n\\nGenerated Output (one column per prompt slice):\\n\\n[tell dark] +7 words                    [dark brown] +6 words                   [brown fox] +6 words                 \\n-------------------------------------   -------------------------------------   -------------------------------------\\nThe brown fox. the quick brown fox      Lazy dog. the lazy dog. the lazy dog.   The lazy dog. the lazy dog barks at  \\njumps over the lazy dog barks loudly    the lazy dog. the lazy dog. the lazy    the brown fox. the quick brown fox   \\nin the dark. in the dark. away          dog. the lazy dog. the lazy dog. the    jumps over the lazy dog. the lazy    \\nquickly into the deep.                  lazy.                                   dog. the lazy.                       \\n\\nreturned True\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:59:04.093273Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:59:04.342183Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_0191vbPRW7fBtceZamB3XxLr", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:59:04.369114Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:59:04.369148Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_0191vbPRW7fBtceZamB3XxLr", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_glove_full.py", "name": "pcm glove full", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:59:10.337053Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T09:59:10.348807Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I rewrote `pcm_glove_full.py` with no corpus segmentation. The dataset is now a single graph. It compiles, and a smoke test with a stand-in for GloVe produced a peak table and three side-by-side columns. I haven't run it with the real GloVe vectors.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Segmentation removed:** `SegmentRouter`, segment embedding, TF-IDF routing and the per-prompt subgraph re-solve are all gone. `PCMMaxCut` runs once on the full graph, and its best spins are reused for every prompt.\n- **Peaks come from graph nodes:** the Manhattan distance from each prompt slice is measured to every bigram node, which is embedded once at startup. A peak is a node at least 1 standard deviation closer than average, capped at `top_k=5` per slice, and the single nearest node is always kept.\n- **Table:** the peak nodes appear as rows, with one distance column per slice and `*` marking a slice's own peaks.\n- **Vocabulary and seeding:** each slice's vocabulary is its words, up to 8 GloVe neighbours that occur in the graph, and the words of its peak nodes. That vocabulary biases the walk's starting node and the 50x boost, and the nodes are mapped to their raw forms (with punctuation) so the matching works.\n- **Side by side:** one generated column per slice, as before.\n- **Fallback:** if `gensim` is missing or GloVe knows none of the prompt words, it uses the original prompt-word biasing on the full graph.\n- **Dependencies:** `numpy`, `scikit-learn` (only for the stopword list) and `gensim`.\n\n**Side effects**\n- The peaks are now individual bigrams rather than whole passages, so the output is more focused but each node carries less context.\n- The smoke test showed the walk getting stuck in short loops like \"the lazy dog. the lazy dog.\" That comes from the tiny test text and the solver's near-zero temperature, but it is worth watching on your real data.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T09:59:10.434036Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T09:59:10.434036Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fc0c-a3e1-738e-9383-1d2231cd871b"}, {"uuid": "01a0febd-51f4-76b2-a3a0-e151411806d1", "text": "while the generate indexes aren't undergoing specificity what length arangement reliabley forsees logical locution", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:30:20.757685Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:30:20.757685Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "while the generate indexes aren't undergoing specificity what length arangement reliabley forsees logical locution", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:30:20.758013Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:30:20.758013Z", "attachments": [{"file_name": "", "file_size": 19903, "file_type": "txt", "extracted_content": "import math\nimport random\nimport re\nimport textwrap\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom itertools import zip_longest\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\n\n# gensim provides the GloVe vectors. If it is missing, the program falls\n# back to plain prompt-word biasing on the full graph.\ntry:\n    from gensim.models import KeyedVectors\n    import gensim.downloader as gensim_api\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = False\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# ORIGINAL SOLVER KEPT EXACTLY THE SAME\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass PCMMaxCut:\n    def __init__(self, graph, noise=0.02, drift_nu=0.08):\n        self.graph = graph\n        self.n = len(graph)\n        self.noise = noise\n        self.drift_nu = drift_nu\n        self.spins = [random.choice([-1, 1]) for _ in range(self.n)]\n        self.age = 1\n\n    def local_field(self, i):\n        return sum(\n            weight * self.spins[j]\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items()\n        )\n\n    def delta_energy(self, i):\n        return -2 * self.spins[i] * self.local_field(i)\n\n    def energy(self):\n        value = 0.0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i:\n                    value += weight * self.spins[i] * self.spins[j]\n        return value\n\n    def cut_size(self):\n        total = 0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i and self.spins[i] != self.spins[j]:\n                    total += weight\n        return total\n\n    def pcm_flip_attempt(self, temperature):\n        i = random.randrange(self.n)\n        delta = self.delta_energy(i)\n\n        drift = self.age ** (-self.drift_nu)\n        thermal_noise = random.gauss(\n            0.0,\n            self.noise\n        ) * max(1.0, abs(self.local_field(i)))\n\n        effective_delta = delta + thermal_noise * drift\n\n        if effective_delta <= 0:\n            accept = True\n        else:\n            accept = random.random() < math.exp(\n                -effective_delta / max(temperature, 1e-9)\n            )\n\n        if accept:\n            self.spins[i] *= -1\n            return i, True, delta\n\n        return i, False, delta\n\n    def run(self, iterations=1000, temperature=1.0, cooling=0.995):\n        history = []\n\n        for _ in range(iterations):\n            _, accepted, _ = self.pcm_flip_attempt(temperature)\n\n            temperature *= cooling\n            self.age += 1\n\n            history.append({\n                \"energy\": self.energy(),\n                \"cut\": self.cut_size(),\n                \"accepted\": accepted,\n                \"temperature\": temperature,\n                \"spins\": self.spins[:],\n            })\n\n        return history\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TEXT HELPERS\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[a-z']+\")\n\n\ndef clean_text(text):\n    text = text.replace(\"\\x00\", \" \")\n    text = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", text)\n    return text.strip()\n\n\ndef tokenize(text):\n    return TOKEN_RE.findall(text.lower())\n\n\ndef clean_word(word):\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z']\", \"\", word.lower())\n\n\ndef content_tokens(words):\n    \"\"\"Cleaned, non-stopword tokens.\"\"\"\n    cleaned = (clean_word(w) for w in words)\n    return [w for w in cleaned if w and w not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GLOVE PROMPT SLICER (probes the graph directly, no corpus segments)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass GloveSlicer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Slices a prompt into word windows, embeds each slice with GloVe, and\n    measures the Manhattan (L1) distance from the slice to every bigram\n    node of the dataset graph. The nearest nodes are the peaks, which seed\n    generation. Each slice's vocabulary is expanded with GloVe neighbours\n    that exist in the dataset.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, glove_name=\"glove-wiki-gigaword-100\", glove_path=None):\n        if glove_path:\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe from {glove_path}\")\n            self.kv = KeyedVectors.load_word2vec_format(\n                glove_path, binary=False, no_header=True\n            )\n        else:\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe: {glove_name} (cached after first download)\")\n            self.kv = gensim_api.load(glove_name)\n\n        self.dim = self.kv.vector_size\n        self.node_matrix = None\n        self.node_valid = None\n\n    # -- embedding -----------------------------------------------------\n\n    def embed(self, tokens):\n        vecs = [self.kv[t] for t in tokens if t in self.kv]\n        if not vecs:\n            return None\n        v = np.mean(vecs, axis=0)\n        norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n        return (v / norm).astype(np.float32) if norm > 0 else None\n\n    def index_nodes(self, id_to_node):\n        \"\"\"Embed every bigram node (content words only).\"\"\"\n        n = len(id_to_node)\n        self.node_matrix = np.zeros((n, self.dim), dtype=np.float32)\n        self.node_valid = np.zeros(n, dtype=bool)\n\n        for index, pair in id_to_node.items():\n            vec = self.embed(content_tokens(pair))\n            if vec is not None:\n                self.node_matrix[index] = vec\n                self.node_valid[index] = True\n\n        print(\n            f\"Embedded {int(self.node_valid.sum())}/{n} graph nodes with GloVe.\"\n        )\n\n    # -- slicing -------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def slice_prompt(self, prompt, width=2, stride=1):\n        tokens = [t for t in tokenize(prompt) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\n        if not tokens:\n            tokens = tokenize(prompt)\n\n        if len(tokens) <= width:\n            windows = [tokens]\n        else:\n            windows = [\n                tokens[i:i + width]\n                for i in range(0, len(tokens) - width + 1, stride)\n            ]\n\n        slices = []\n        for window in windows:\n            vec = self.embed(window)\n            if vec is not None:\n                slices.append((window, vec))\n        return slices\n\n    # -- Manhattan distance and peaks ----------------------------------\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def manhattan(a, b):\n        return float(np.abs(a - b).sum())\n\n    def node_distances(self, slice_vec):\n        \"\"\"Manhattan distance from one slice to every node (inf if invalid).\"\"\"\n        if self.node_matrix is None:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Call index_nodes() first.\")\n\n        distances = np.abs(self.node_matrix - slice_vec).sum(axis=1)\n        distances[~self.node_valid] = np.inf\n        return distances\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def find_peaks(distances, top_k=5, prominence=1.0):\n        \"\"\"\n        Peaks = the nodes whose distance sits at least `prominence`\n        standard deviations below the mean, capped at top_k. Always\n        returns at least the single nearest node.\n        \"\"\"\n        finite = np.isfinite(distances)\n        if not finite.any():\n            return []\n\n        mean = distances[finite].mean()\n        std = distances[finite].std()\n\n        k = min(top_k, int(finite.sum()))\n        nearest = np.argpartition(np.where(finite, distances, np.inf), k - 1)[:k]\n        nearest = nearest[np.argsort(distances[nearest])]\n\n        if std == 0:\n            return [int(nearest[0])]\n\n        peaks = [\n            int(i) for i in nearest\n            if (mean - distances[i]) / std >= prominence\n        ]\n\n        return peaks or [int(nearest[0])]\n\n    # -- accommodating vocabulary --------------------------------------\n\n    def expand_vocab(self, slice_tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\n        \"\"\"\n        Slice words plus nearest GloVe neighbours that also occur in the\n        dataset graph, so the Markov walk can actually reach them.\n        \"\"\"\n        vocab = set(slice_tokens)\n        added = 0\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(slice_vec, topn=topn):\n            if word in dataset_vocab and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS:\n                vocab.add(word)\n                added += 1\n                if added >= keep:\n                    break\n        return vocab\n\n\ndef dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node):\n    \"\"\"\n    Graph nodes keep raw whitespace tokens (\"dog.\", \"fox,\"), so map each\n    cleaned word to every raw form present in the graph.\n    \"\"\"\n    clean_to_raw = {}\n    for pair in id_to_node.values():\n        for raw in pair:\n            clean_to_raw.setdefault(clean_word(raw), set()).add(raw.lower())\n    return clean_to_raw\n\n\ndef to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw):\n    raw = set()\n    for word in clean_vocab:\n        raw.update(clean_to_raw.get(word, {word}))\n    return raw\n\n\ndef print_peak_table(slices, per_slice_distances, per_slice_peaks, id_to_node, max_rows=12):\n    \"\"\"Peak nodes down the side, one distance column per slice.\"\"\"\n    best = {}\n    for peaks, distances in zip(per_slice_peaks, per_slice_distances):\n        for node in peaks:\n            best[node] = min(best.get(node, np.inf), distances[node])\n\n    rows = sorted(best, key=lambda node: best[node])[:max_rows]\n\n    labels = [\" \".join(tokens)[:14] for tokens, _ in slices]\n    col = 16\n    print(\"\\nManhattan distance (peak node x slice)   * = peak for that slice\")\n    print(\"node\".ljust(24) + \"\".join(label.ljust(col) for label in labels))\n\n    for node in rows:\n        name = \" \".join(id_to_node[node])[:22]\n        line = name.ljust(24)\n        for peaks, distances in zip(per_slice_peaks, per_slice_distances):\n            cell = f\"{distances[node]:.3f}\"\n            if node in peaks:\n                cell += \" *\"\n            line += cell.ljust(col)\n        print(line)\n\n\ndef render_side_by_side(columns, total_width=118, gap=3):\n    \"\"\"columns: list of (header, text). Prints them as parallel columns.\"\"\"\n    n = len(columns)\n    width = max(18, (total_width - gap * (n - 1)) // n)\n    wrapped = [textwrap.wrap(text, width) for _, text in columns]\n    sep = \" \" * gap\n\n    lines = [sep.join(header[:width].ljust(width) for header, _ in columns)]\n    lines.append(sep.join(\"-\" * width for _ in columns))\n    for parts in zip_longest(*wrapped, fillvalue=\"\"):\n        lines.append(sep.join(part.ljust(width) for part in parts))\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GRAPH CREATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef process_text_to_trigram_graph(text, max_nodes=200):\n    \"\"\"\n    Builds a graph where nodes are bigrams and edges represent trigrams.\n    \"\"\"\n    text = text.lower()\n    words = text.split()\n\n    if len(words) < 3:\n        return {}, {}, {}\n\n    all_bigrams = [\n        (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        for i in range(len(words) - 1)\n    ]\n\n    top_bigrams = [\n        bigram\n        for bigram, _ in Counter(all_bigrams).most_common(max_nodes)\n    ]\n\n    bigram_set = set(top_bigrams)\n\n    node_to_id = {\n        bigram: index\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    id_to_node = {\n        index: bigram\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    graph = {\n        index: {}\n        for index in range(len(top_bigrams))\n    }\n\n    for i in range(len(words) - 2):\n        b1 = (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        b2 = (words[i + 1], words[i + 2])\n\n        if b1 in bigram_set and b2 in bigram_set:\n            id1 = node_to_id[b1]\n            id2 = node_to_id[b2]\n\n            if id1 != id2:\n                graph[id1][id2] = graph[id1].get(id2, 0) + 1\n                graph[id2][id1] = graph[id2].get(id1, 0) + 1\n\n    return graph, node_to_id, id_to_node\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PROMPT-AWARE MARKOV GENERATOR\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n    graph,\n    id_to_node,\n    spins,\n    prompt_vocab,\n    length=100,\n):\n    n = len(graph)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return \"\"\n\n    prompt_vocab = {\n        word.lower()\n        for word in prompt_vocab\n        if word.strip()\n    }\n\n    valid_starts = [\n        i\n        for i in range(n)\n        if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in id_to_node[i])\n    ]\n\n    current_node = (\n        random.choice(valid_starts)\n        if valid_starts\n        else random.randrange(n)\n    )\n\n    output = list(id_to_node[current_node])\n\n    for _ in range(max(0, length - 2)):\n        current_spin = spins[current_node]\n        neighbors = graph[current_node]\n        current_word_2 = id_to_node[current_node][1]\n\n        valid_neighbors = [\n            neighbor\n            for neighbor in neighbors\n            if id_to_node[neighbor][0] == current_word_2\n        ]\n\n        if not valid_neighbors:\n            fallback_nodes = [\n                i\n                for i, spin in enumerate(spins)\n                if (\n                    spin != current_spin\n                    and id_to_node[i][0] == current_word_2\n                )\n            ]\n\n            if fallback_nodes:\n                next_node = random.choice(fallback_nodes)\n            else:\n                next_node = random.randrange(n)\n        else:\n            probabilities = []\n\n            for neighbor in valid_neighbors:\n                base_weight = graph[current_node][neighbor]\n\n                cut_multiplier = (\n                    5.0\n                    if spins[neighbor] != current_spin\n                    else 1.0\n                )\n\n                neighbor_words = id_to_node[neighbor]\n\n                prompt_multiplier = (\n                    50.0\n                    if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in neighbor_words)\n                    else 1.0\n                )\n\n                score = (\n                    base_weight\n                    * cut_multiplier\n                    * prompt_multiplier\n                )\n\n                probabilities.append(score)\n\n            next_node = random.choices(\n                valid_neighbors,\n                weights=probabilities,\n                k=1,\n            )[0]\n\n        output.append(id_to_node[next_node][1])\n        current_node = next_node\n\n    return \" \".join(output)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GLOVE PROBE + SIDE-BY-SIDE GENERATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef glove_probe_and_generate(\n    prompt,\n    slicer,\n    graph,\n    id_to_node,\n    spins,\n    clean_to_raw,\n    width=2,\n    top_k=5,\n    length=60,\n    max_columns=4,\n):\n    slices = slicer.slice_prompt(prompt, width=width)\n\n    if not slices:\n        print(\"GloVe knows none of the prompt words; no slices to probe.\")\n        return False\n\n    # Keep the output readable: cap the number of side-by-side columns.\n    if len(slices) > max_columns:\n        step = len(slices) / max_columns\n        slices = [slices[int(i * step)] for i in range(max_columns)]\n\n    per_slice_distances = [slicer.node_distances(vec) for _, vec in slices]\n    per_slice_peaks = [\n        slicer.find_peaks(d, top_k=top_k) for d in per_slice_distances\n    ]\n\n    if not any(per_slice_peaks):\n        print(\"No usable peaks found.\")\n        return False\n\n    print_peak_table(\n        slices, per_slice_distances, per_slice_peaks, id_to_node\n    )\n\n    dataset_vocab = set(clean_to_raw)\n\n    columns = []\n    for (tokens, slice_vec), peaks in zip(slices, per_slice_peaks):\n        clean_vocab = slicer.expand_vocab(tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab)\n        raw_vocab = to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw)\n\n        # The peak nodes' own words also seed the walk.\n        for node in peaks:\n            raw_vocab.update(id_to_node[node])\n\n        text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n            graph,\n            id_to_node,\n            spins,\n            raw_vocab,\n            length=length,\n        )\n\n        added = len(clean_vocab) - len(tokens)\n        header = f\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] +{max(added, 0)} words\"\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \".\"))\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated Output (one column per prompt slice):\\n\")\n    print(render_side_by_side(columns))\n    print()\n    return True\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PLAIN FALLBACK (no GloVe)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef plain_generate(prompt, graph, id_to_node, spins):\n    final_text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n        graph,\n        id_to_node,\n        spins,\n        prompt.split(),\n        length=400,\n    )\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated Output:\")\n    print(f\"> {final_text.capitalize()}.\\n\")\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# MAIN PROGRAM\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef load_text_file(filepath):\n    try:\n        with open(filepath, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n            return file.read()\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"File {filepath} not found. Using fallback text.\")\n\n        return (\n            \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. \"\n            \"The lazy dog barks at the brown fox. \"\n            \"The quick brown fox runs away quickly into the deep \"\n            \"dark brown forest. The dark forest is full of mystery. \"\n            \"A dog barks loudly in the dark.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef load_slicer(id_to_node):\n    if not GENSIM_AVAILABLE:\n        print(\"gensim not installed (pip install gensim). Using plain generation.\")\n        return None\n\n    glove_path = input(\n        \"Local GloVe .txt path (blank = download glove-wiki-gigaword-100): \"\n    ).strip()\n\n    try:\n        slicer = GloveSlicer(glove_path=glove_path or None)\n        slicer.index_nodes(id_to_node)\n        return slicer\n    except Exception as error:\n        print(f\"Could not load GloVe ({error}). Using plain generation.\")\n        return None\n\n\ndef main():\n    dataset_file = input(\"Dataset filename: \").strip()\n\n    dataset_text = clean_text(load_text_file(dataset_file))\n\n    print(\"Building graph from the complete dataset...\")\n    graph, node_to_id, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\n        dataset_text,\n        max_nodes=150000,\n    )\n\n    if not graph:\n        print(\"Graph is empty. Check the dataset.\")\n        return\n\n    print(f\"Graph built with {len(graph)} unique nodes.\")\n\n    print(\"Running PCMMaxCut solver for structural baseline...\")\n\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\n        graph,\n        noise=0.00001,\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\n    )\n\n    history = solver.run(\n        iterations=5000,\n        temperature=0.0000005,\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\n    )\n\n    best_cut = max(\n        history,\n        key=lambda item: item[\"cut\"],\n    )\n\n    print(\n        f\"Base partition created. \"\n        f\"Max Cut Size: {best_cut['cut']}\\n\"\n    )\n\n    spins = best_cut[\"spins\"]\n    clean_to_raw = dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node)\n    slicer = load_slicer(id_to_node)\n\n    while True:\n        try:\n            user_prompt = input(\"USER: \").strip()\n        except (KeyboardInterrupt, EOFError):\n            print(\"\\nExiting.\")\n            break\n\n        if not user_prompt:\n            continue\n\n        if user_prompt.lower() in {\"exit\", \"quit\"}:\n            break\n\n        done = False\n\n        if slicer is not None:\n            done = glove_probe_and_generate(\n                user_prompt,\n                slicer,\n                graph,\n                id_to_node,\n                spins,\n                clean_to_raw,\n                width=2,\n                top_k=5,\n                length=60,\n                max_columns=4,\n            )\n\n        # Fall back to plain prompt-word biasing if GloVe is unavailable\n        # or knows none of the prompt words.\n        if not done:\n            plain_generate(user_prompt, graph, id_to_node, spins)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()"}], "files": [{"file_uuid": "90c9ce1a-91aa-4d43-82b3-7f634dab31fc", "file_name": ""}], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fc0c-a3e1-7783-87e7-763fcb0f3fe4"}, {"uuid": "01a0febd-51f4-77ed-aaaf-418ed38c9251", "text": "I'm reading this as: when the generated text isn't staying on topic, what length and arrangement keep it coherent? Your generator is an order-2 Markov chain (bigram nodes, trigram edges), so the practical limits come from that.\n\n**Output length**\n- An order-2 chain only has two words of memory, so it stays locally sensible for about one clause or sentence, roughly 15 to 30 words. Past 40 to 60 words it drifts or falls into loops, like the \"the lazy dog. the lazy dog.\" pattern in the earlier smoke test.\n- Use `length=25` to `40` per column instead of 60, and end on a sentence boundary rather than a fixed count. Stop at the first word ending in `.`, `!` or `?` once a minimum of about 12 words is reached.\n\n**Slice width**\n- `width=1` is too generic. The peaks are just nodes containing near-synonyms.\n- `width=2` is the minimum for specificity. `width=3` is sharper but gives fewer slices, and with 3 or 4 columns it covers a typical prompt.\n- Keep `stride=1`, `top_k` at 3 to 5, and `prominence=1.0`.\n\n**Arrangement**\n- Start the walk at the best-ranked peak node instead of `random.choice(valid_starts)`, so each column begins on its slice's closest bigram.\n- The 50x prompt boost is what causes looping, because it keeps pulling the walk back to the same prompt words. Apply it only for the first 5 to 8 steps, or decay it, so the chain follows the corpus's own grammar afterwards.\n- Add a recency penalty so the walk doesn't revisit a node it just used.\n- The 5x cut multiplier rewards switching sides of a partition, which has no relation to grammar. With your near-zero temperature the spins are effectively random, so it adds noise rather than structure. Set it to 1.0 if the text feels incoherent.\n\n**Corpus size**\n- Order-2 needs a lot of text to have varied continuations. With a few thousand words most nodes have one or two exits and the walk loops. Around 100k words or more gives reliably fluent clauses.\n\nA sketch of the generator changes:\n\n```python\nrecent = []  # inside the generator, before the loop\n...\n# when scoring neighbors:\nboost = 50.0 if (step < 8 and any(w in prompt_vocab for w in neighbor_words)) else 1.0\nrepeat = 0.05 if neighbor in recent[-8:] else 1.0\nscore = base_weight * boost * repeat   # cut_multiplier dropped (or set to 1.0)\n...\nrecent.append(next_node)\n# after appending the word:\nif len(output) >= 12 and output[-1].endswith((\".\", \"!\", \"?\")):\n    break\n```\n\nThese are rules of thumb for this architecture rather than guarantees. The way to find the best values for your data is to sweep `length` and `width` over a few prompts and see where the loops start. I can add that sweep or put these changes straight into the full file if you want.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:30:20.614369Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:30:30.720950Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Untangling a garbled question about predicting sentence length."}, {"summary": "Recommending word counts and tweaks for coherent generated text."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:30:30.720980Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:30:38.197406Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I'm reading this as: when the generated text isn't staying on topic, what length and arrangement keep it coherent? Your generator is an order-2 Markov chain (bigram nodes, trigram edges), so the practical limits come from that.\n\n**Output length**\n- An order-2 chain only has two words of memory, so it stays locally sensible for about one clause or sentence, roughly 15 to 30 words. Past 40 to 60 words it drifts or falls into loops, like the \"the lazy dog. the lazy dog.\" pattern in the earlier smoke test.\n- Use `length=25` to `40` per column instead of 60, and end on a sentence boundary rather than a fixed count. Stop at the first word ending in `.`, `!` or `?` once a minimum of about 12 words is reached.\n\n**Slice width**\n- `width=1` is too generic. The peaks are just nodes containing near-synonyms.\n- `width=2` is the minimum for specificity. `width=3` is sharper but gives fewer slices, and with 3 or 4 columns it covers a typical prompt.\n- Keep `stride=1`, `top_k` at 3 to 5, and `prominence=1.0`.\n\n**Arrangement**\n- Start the walk at the best-ranked peak node instead of `random.choice(valid_starts)`, so each column begins on its slice's closest bigram.\n- The 50x prompt boost is what causes looping, because it keeps pulling the walk back to the same prompt words. Apply it only for the first 5 to 8 steps, or decay it, so the chain follows the corpus's own grammar afterwards.\n- Add a recency penalty so the walk doesn't revisit a node it just used.\n- The 5x cut multiplier rewards switching sides of a partition, which has no relation to grammar. With your near-zero temperature the spins are effectively random, so it adds noise rather than structure. Set it to 1.0 if the text feels incoherent.\n\n**Corpus size**\n- Order-2 needs a lot of text to have varied continuations. With a few thousand words most nodes have one or two exits and the walk loops. Around 100k words or more gives reliably fluent clauses.\n\nA sketch of the generator changes:\n\n```python\nrecent = []  # inside the generator, before the loop\n...\n# when scoring neighbors:\nboost = 50.0 if (step < 8 and any(w in prompt_vocab for w in neighbor_words)) else 1.0\nrepeat = 0.05 if neighbor in recent[-8:] else 1.0\nscore = base_weight * boost * repeat   # cut_multiplier dropped (or set to 1.0)\n...\nrecent.append(next_node)\n# after appending the word:\nif len(output) >= 12 and output[-1].endswith((\".\", \"!\", \"?\")):\n    break\n```\n\nThese are rules of thumb for this architecture rather than guarantees. The way to find the best values for your data is to sweep `length` and `width` over a few prompts and see where the loops start. I can add that sweep or put these changes straight into the full file if you want.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:30:38.284796Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:30:38.284796Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0febd-51f4-76b2-a3a0-e151411806d1"}, {"uuid": "01a0febe-525e-7849-9e62-f13905f963e5", "text": "make those predictions as if they are from new data", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:31:22.512698Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:31:22.512698Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "make those predictions as if they are from new data", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:31:22.512877Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:31:22.512877Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0febd-51f4-77ed-aaaf-418ed38c9251"}, {"uuid": "01a0febe-525e-7461-b5f7-df7c69022332", "text": "I can't invent numbers and present them as measurements, so I'll test the predictions on data the earlier toy text never touched. I'll build a corpus from Python's own standard-library docstrings, hold out 20% of it, and measure each setting.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI can't produce predictions that look like measurements, so I ran the sweep for real. The corpus was about 216k words of Python standard-library docstrings, split 80/20 train/held-out, with 40 two-word prompts drawn from the held-out part. Several of my earlier rules of thumb didn't hold up.\n\n| Setting | Distinct 3-grams | 4-grams that exist in the corpus | First repeated 3-gram |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| length 15 | 1.00 | 0.75 | at the end (word 14.8) |\n| length 40 | 0.99 | 0.71 | at the end (word 38.4) |\n| length 100 | 0.95 | 0.70 | about word 80 |\n| length 200 | 0.96 | 0.72 | about word 147 |\n\n- **Length isn't the problem on a large corpus.** I predicted loops past 40 to 60 words, but at 216k words (52k graph nodes) the text barely repeats even at 200 words. Looping is a small-corpus problem, like the 5-sentence fox text.\n- **The coherence ceiling doesn't depend on length.** Only about 70 to 75% of generated 4-grams appear anywhere in the training text. The rest are splices the chain invented, and that holds at every length from 15 to 200, so a fixed length won't make it more logical.\n- **Arrangement changes were small.**\n  - The recency penalty took distinct 3-grams from 0.97 to 1.00, which is a real but small gain.\n  - Setting the cut multiplier to 1.0 and decaying the prompt boost made no measurable difference on these metrics.\n  - Stopping at a sentence end gave an average length of 22 words, which is the natural clause length in this corpus.\n\n**Caveats**\n- I used random spins instead of running `PCMMaxCut`, because its history recomputes energy every step and was too slow here. At your near-zero temperature it is close to random anyway, but I haven't confirmed that.\n- GloVe wasn't available, so peaks and vocabulary expansion weren't tested. Prompts only biased the walk's start.\n- \"Logical locution\" is only approximated by n-gram validity and repetition. Prompt relevance wasn't measured, so my claim that decaying the boost helps there is untested.\n- This is one seed, 40 prompts and no confidence intervals. The held-out trigram scores (0.11 to 0.20) bounced around with no trend, so I wouldn't read anything into them.\n\nOn your real data, corpus size and the 4-gram validity of your output are the numbers worth checking. I haven't changed your file. If you want, I can add the recency penalty and sentence-end stop to the full script and add this 4-gram check as a command you can run on your own dataset.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:31:22.508549Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:31:35.323755Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Clarifying what simulated new-data predictions should look like."}, {"summary": "Building a real corpus to test generator variants fairly."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:31:35.323796Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:31:36.175571Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I can't invent numbers and present them as measurements, so I'll test the predictions on data the earlier toy text never touched. I'll build a corpus from Python's own standard-library docstrings, hold out 20% of it, and measure each setting.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:31:36.175584Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:31:49.689239Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01NppFtLpz62CRkWwA5BJuSd", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "mkdir -p /home/claude && cat > /home/claude/sweep.py << 'EOF'\nimport sys, random, re, pkgutil, importlib, inspect, collections, statistics\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/mnt/user-data/outputs\")\nimport pcm_glove_full as m\n\nrandom.seed(7)\n\n# ---- new corpus: stdlib docstrings (English prose, not the fox text) ----\ndocs = []\nfor mod in pkgutil.iter_modules():\n    if mod.name.startswith(\"_\") or mod.name in (\"antigravity\",\"this\",\"idlelib\",\"tkinter\",\"turtledemo\",\"test\"):\n        continue\n    try:\n        o = importlib.import_module(mod.name)\n    except BaseException:\n        continue\n    docs.append(inspect.getdoc(o) or \"\")\n    for _, f in inspect.getmembers(o, lambda x: inspect.isfunction(x) or inspect.isclass(x)):\n        docs.append(inspect.getdoc(f) or \"\")\ntext = m.clean_text(\" \".join(docs))\nwords = text.split()\nprint(\"corpus words:\", len(words))\ncut = int(len(words) * 0.8)\ntrain, test = words[:cut], words[cut:]\ntrain_text, test_text = \" \".join(train).lower(), \" \".join(test).lower()\n\ngraph, n2i, i2n = m.process_text_to_trigram_graph(train_text, max_nodes=150000)\nprint(\"graph nodes:\", len(graph))\nspins = [random.choice([-1, 1]) for _ in graph]   # solver at ~0 temperature is effectively random; skipped for speed\n\ndef ngrams(ws, n): return list(zip(*[ws[i:] for i in range(n)]))\ntrain_w, test_w = train_text.split(), test_text.split()\ntrain4, train3, test3 = set(ngrams(train_w,4)), set(ngrams(train_w,3)), set(ngrams(test_w,3))\n\nby_first = collections.defaultdict(list)\nfor i,(a,b) in i2n.items(): by_first[a].append(i)\n\ndef gen(vocab, length, boost_steps, recency, cut_mult, stop_sentence):\n    n = len(graph); vocab = {w.lower() for w in vocab}\n    starts = [i for i in range(n) if any(w in vocab for w in i2n[i])]\n    cur = random.choice(starts) if starts else random.randrange(n)\n    out = list(i2n[cur]); recent=[cur]; jumps=0\n    for step in range(max(0, length-2)):\n        w2 = i2n[cur][1]\n        valid = [nb for nb in graph[cur] if i2n[nb][0]==w2]\n        if not valid:\n            jumps += 1\n            cands = by_first.get(w2) or [random.randrange(n)]\n            nxt = random.choice(cands)\n        else:\n            ws=[]\n            for nb in valid:\n                s = graph[cur][nb]\n                s *= cut_mult if spins[nb]!=spins[cur] else 1.0\n                if (boost_steps is None or step < boost_steps) and any(w in vocab for w in i2n[nb]): s *= 50.0\n                if recency and nb in recent[-8:]: s *= 0.05\n                ws.append(s)\n            nxt = random.choices(valid, weights=ws, k=1)[0]\n        out.append(i2n[nxt][1]); cur = nxt; recent.append(nxt)\n        if stop_sentence and len(out) >= 12 and out[-1].endswith((\".\",\"!\",\"?\")): break\n    return out, jumps\n\ndef metrics(out, jumps, vocab):\n    t3 = ngrams(out,3); t4 = ngrams(out,4)\n    d3 = len(set(t3))/max(1,len(t3))\n    c4 = sum(g in train4 for g in t4)/max(1,len(t4))\n    h3 = sum(g in test3 for g in t3)/max(1,len(t3))\n    jr = jumps/max(1,len(out))\n    seen=set(); loop=len(out)\n    for i,g in enumerate(t3):\n        if g in seen: loop=i+3; break\n        seen.add(g)\n    return d3,c4,h3,jr,loop\n\n# prompts drawn from held-out text: frequent content words never used to build the graph\nfreq = collections.Counter(m.content_tokens(test_w))\ntopic = [w for w,c in freq.most_common(400) if w in {m.clean_word(x) for x in train_w}]\nprompts = [random.sample(topic, 2) for _ in range(60)]\n\ndef evaluate(name, **kw):\n    rows=[]\n    for p in prompts:\n        raw = set()\n        for w in p:\n            for pair in i2n.values(): pass\n        vocab = set(p)\n        out, j = gen(vocab, **kw)\n        rows.append(metrics(out, j, vocab) + (len(out),))\n    avg = [statistics.mean(r[k] for r in rows) for k in range(6)]\n    print(f\"{name:34s} distinct3={avg[0]:.2f} 4gram_valid={avg[1]:.2f} heldout3={avg[2]:.3f} jumps={avg[3]:.3f} first_loop@{avg[4]:5.1f} words={avg[5]:5.1f}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n--- LENGTH sweep (current generator: boost always, no recency, cut x5) ---\")\nfor L in (15,25,40,60,100,200):\n    evaluate(f\"length={L}\", length=L, boost_steps=None, recency=False, cut_mult=5.0, stop_sentence=False)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- ARRANGEMENT sweep at length=40 ---\")\nevaluate(\"baseline (current)\",            length=40, boost_steps=None, recency=False, cut_mult=5.0, stop_sentence=False)\nevaluate(\"boost decays after 8 steps\",     length=40, boost_steps=8,    recency=False, cut_mult=5.0, stop_sentence=False)\nevaluate(\"+ recency penalty\",              length=40, boost_steps=8,    recency=True,  cut_mult=5.0, stop_sentence=False)\nevaluate(\"+ cut multiplier 1.0\",           length=40, boost_steps=8,    recency=True,  cut_mult=1.0, stop_sentence=False)\nevaluate(\"+ stop at sentence end (all)\",   length=40, boost_steps=8,    recency=True,  cut_mult=1.0, stop_sentence=True)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- LENGTH sweep with all fixes ---\")\nfor L in (15,25,40,60,100):\n    evaluate(f\"fixed, length={L}\", length=L, boost_steps=8, recency=True, cut_mult=1.0, stop_sentence=False)\nEOF\ncd /home/claude && timeout 900 python3 sweep.py 2>&1 | tail -40", "description": "Run a held-out sweep of generator length/arrangement settings on a new docstring corpus"}, "message": "Run a held-out sweep of generator length/arrangement settings on a new docstring corpus", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"mkdir -p /home/claude && cat > /home/claude/sweep.py << 'EOF'\\nimport sys, random, re, pkgutil, importlib, inspect, collections, statistics\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\"/mnt/user-data/outputs\\\")\\nimport pcm_glove_full as m\\n\\nrandom.seed(7)\\n\\n# ---- new corpus: stdlib docstrings (English prose, not the fox text) ----\\ndocs = []\\nfor mod in pkgutil.iter_modules():\\n    if mod.name.startswith(\\\"_\\\") or mod.name in (\\\"antigravity\\\",\\\"this\\\",\\\"idlelib\\\",\\\"tkinter\\\",\\\"turtledemo\\\",\\\"test\\\"):\\n        continue\\n    try:\\n        o = importlib.import_module(mod.name)\\n    except BaseException:\\n        continue\\n    docs.append(inspect.getdoc(o) or \\\"\\\")\\n    for _, f in inspect.getmembers(o, lambda x: inspect.isfunction(x) or inspect.isclass(x)):\\n        docs.append(inspect.getdoc(f) or \\\"\\\")\\ntext = m.clean_text(\\\" \\\".join(docs))\\nwords = text.split()\\nprint(\\\"corpus words:\\\", len(words))\\ncut = int(len(words) * 0.8)\\ntrain, test = words[:cut], words[cut:]\\ntrain_text, test_text = \\\" \\\".join(train).lower(), \\\" \\\".join(test).lower()\\n\\ngraph, n2i, i2n = m.process_text_to_trigram_graph(train_text, max_nodes=150000)\\nprint(\\\"graph nodes:\\\", len(graph))\\nspins = [random.choice([-1, 1]) for _ in graph]   # solver at ~0 temperature is effectively random; skipped for speed\\n\\ndef ngrams(ws, n): return list(zip(*[ws[i:] for i in range(n)]))\\ntrain_w, test_w = train_text.split(), test_text.split()\\ntrain4, train3, test3 = set(ngrams(train_w,4)), set(ngrams(train_w,3)), set(ngrams(test_w,3))\\n\\nby_first = collections.defaultdict(list)\\nfor i,(a,b) in i2n.items(): by_first[a].append(i)\\n\\ndef gen(vocab, length, boost_steps, recency, cut_mult, stop_sentence):\\n    n = len(graph); vocab = {w.lower() for w in vocab}\\n    starts = [i for i in range(n) if any(w in vocab for w in i2n[i])]\\n    cur = random.choice(starts) if starts else random.randrange(n)\\n    out = list(i2n[cur]); recent=[cur]; jumps=0\\n    for step in range(max(0, length-2)):\\n        w2 = i2n[cur][1]\\n        valid = [nb for nb in graph[cur] if i2n[nb][0]==w2]\\n        if not valid:\\n            jumps += 1\\n            cands = by_first.get(w2) or [random.randrange(n)]\\n            nxt = random.choice(cands)\\n        else:\\n            ws=[]\\n            for nb in valid:\\n                s = graph[cur][nb]\\n                s *= cut_mult if spins[nb]!=spins[cur] else 1.0\\n                if (boost_steps is None or step < boost_steps) and any(w in vocab for w in i2n[nb]): s *= 50.0\\n                if recency and nb in recent[-8:]: s *= 0.05\\n                ws.append(s)\\n            nxt = random.choices(valid, weights=ws, k=1)[0]\\n        out.append(i2n[nxt][1]); cur = nxt; recent.append(nxt)\\n        if stop_sentence and len(out) >= 12 and out[-1].endswith((\\\".\\\",\\\"!\\\",\\\"?\\\")): break\\n    return out, jumps\\n\\ndef metrics(out, jumps, vocab):\\n    t3 = ngrams(out,3); t4 = ngrams(out,4)\\n    d3 = len(set(t3))/max(1,len(t3))\\n    c4 = sum(g in train4 for g in t4)/max(1,len(t4))\\n    h3 = sum(g in test3 for g in t3)/max(1,len(t3))\\n    jr = jumps/max(1,len(out))\\n    seen=set(); loop=len(out)\\n    for i,g in enumerate(t3):\\n        if g in seen: loop=i+3; break\\n        seen.add(g)\\n    return d3,c4,h3,jr,loop\\n\\n# prompts drawn from held-out text: frequent content words never used to build the graph\\nfreq = collections.Counter(m.content_tokens(test_w))\\ntopic = [w for w,c in freq.most_common(400) if w in {m.clean_word(x) for x in train_w}]\\nprompts = [random.sample(topic, 2) for _ in range(60)]\\n\\ndef evaluate(name, **kw):\\n    rows=[]\\n    for p in prompts:\\n        raw = set()\\n        for w in p:\\n            for pair in i2n.values(): pass\\n        vocab = set(p)\\n        out, j = gen(vocab, **kw)\\n        rows.append(metrics(out, j, vocab) + (len(out),))\\n    avg = [statistics.mean(r[k] for r in rows) for k in range(6)]\\n    print(f\\\"{name:34s} distinct3={avg[0]:.2f} 4gram_valid={avg[1]:.2f} heldout3={avg[2]:.3f} jumps={avg[3]:.3f} first_loop@{avg[4]:5.1f} words={avg[5]:5.1f}\\\")\\n\\nprint(\\\"\\\\n--- LENGTH sweep (current generator: boost always, no recency, cut x5) ---\\\")\\nfor L in (15,25,40,60,100,200):\\n    evaluate(f\\\"length={L}\\\", length=L, boost_steps=None, recency=False, cut_mult=5.0, stop_sentence=False)\\n\\nprint(\\\"\\\\n--- ARRANGEMENT sweep at length=40 ---\\\")\\nevaluate(\\\"baseline (current)\\\",            length=40, boost_steps=None, recency=False, cut_mult=5.0, stop_sentence=False)\\nevaluate(\\\"boost decays after 8 steps\\\",     length=40, boost_steps=8,    recency=False, cut_mult=5.0, stop_sentence=False)\\nevaluate(\\\"+ recency penalty\\\",              length=40, boost_steps=8,    recency=True,  cut_mult=5.0, stop_sentence=False)\\nevaluate(\\\"+ cut multiplier 1.0\\\",           length=40, boost_steps=8,    recency=True,  cut_mult=1.0, stop_sentence=False)\\nevaluate(\\\"+ stop at sentence end (all)\\\",   length=40, boost_steps=8,    recency=True,  cut_mult=1.0, stop_sentence=True)\\n\\nprint(\\\"\\\\n--- LENGTH sweep with all fixes ---\\\")\\nfor L in (15,25,40,60,100):\\n    evaluate(f\\\"fixed, length={L}\\\", length=L, boost_steps=8, recency=True, cut_mult=1.0, stop_sentence=False)\\nEOF\\ncd /home/claude && timeout 900 python3 sweep.py 2>&1 | tail -40\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:51.173622Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:51.173660Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01NppFtLpz62CRkWwA5BJuSd", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The command exceeded the execution time limit (300 seconds for a single command) and was stopped; none of its output was captured, and files it was writing may be incomplete. Try breaking the work into smaller steps, writing intermediate results to a file so progress is not lost, or adding a shorter timeout to the command itself."}], "is_error": true, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "Command timed out."}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:52.769642Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:55.590523Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Speeding up slow code by trimming redundant computations."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:55.590583Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:59.361661Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01RwqhSjWPi8QhVmEe2xQQ8V", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude && cat > mkcorpus.py << 'EOF'\nimport importlib, inspect, sys\nmods = \"\"\"argparse ast asyncio base64 bisect calendar cmath cmd codecs collections colorsys concurrent.futures configparser contextlib copy csv dataclasses datetime decimal difflib dis doctest email enum fractions ftplib functools getopt getpass gettext glob gzip hashlib heapq hmac html http.client http.server imaplib importlib inspect io ipaddress itertools json logging lzma mailbox math mimetypes multiprocessing numbers operator os pathlib pickle pkgutil platform plistlib poplib pprint profile queue random re sched secrets selectors shelve shlex shutil signal smtplib socket socketserver sqlite3 ssl statistics string struct subprocess sys sysconfig tarfile tempfile textwrap threading time timeit tokenize trace traceback types typing unicodedata unittest urllib.request urllib.parse uuid warnings weakref xml.dom.minidom xml.etree.ElementTree zipfile zlib\"\"\".split()\ndocs=[]\nfor name in mods:\n    try: o = importlib.import_module(name)\n    except BaseException: continue\n    docs.append(inspect.getdoc(o) or \"\")\n    for _, f in inspect.getmembers(o, lambda x: inspect.isfunction(x) or inspect.isclass(x)):\n        docs.append(inspect.getdoc(f) or \"\")\n        if inspect.isclass(f):\n            for _, g in inspect.getmembers(f, inspect.isfunction):\n                docs.append(inspect.getdoc(g) or \"\")\nopen(\"corpus.txt\",\"w\").write(\"\\n\".join(docs))\nprint(len(\" \".join(docs).split()))\nEOF\ntimeout 120 python3 mkcorpus.py", "description": "Build a cached docstring corpus from a curated module list"}, "message": "Build a cached docstring corpus from a curated module list", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude && cat > mkcorpus.py << 'EOF'\\nimport importlib, inspect, sys\\nmods = \\\"\\\"\\\"argparse ast asyncio base64 bisect calendar cmath cmd codecs collections colorsys concurrent.futures configparser contextlib copy csv dataclasses datetime decimal difflib dis doctest email enum fractions ftplib functools getopt getpass gettext glob gzip hashlib heapq hmac html http.client http.server imaplib importlib inspect io ipaddress itertools json logging lzma mailbox math mimetypes multiprocessing numbers operator os pathlib pickle pkgutil platform plistlib poplib pprint profile queue random re sched secrets selectors shelve shlex shutil signal smtplib socket socketserver sqlite3 ssl statistics string struct subprocess sys sysconfig tarfile tempfile textwrap threading time timeit tokenize trace traceback types typing unicodedata unittest urllib.request urllib.parse uuid warnings weakref xml.dom.minidom xml.etree.ElementTree zipfile zlib\\\"\\\"\\\".split()\\ndocs=[]\\nfor name in mods:\\n    try: o = importlib.import_module(name)\\n    except BaseException: continue\\n    docs.append(inspect.getdoc(o) or \\\"\\\")\\n    for _, f in inspect.getmembers(o, lambda x: inspect.isfunction(x) or inspect.isclass(x)):\\n        docs.append(inspect.getdoc(f) or \\\"\\\")\\n        if inspect.isclass(f):\\n            for _, g in inspect.getmembers(f, inspect.isfunction):\\n                docs.append(inspect.getdoc(g) or \\\"\\\")\\nopen(\\\"corpus.txt\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(docs))\\nprint(len(\\\" \\\".join(docs).split()))\\nEOF\\ntimeout 120 python3 mkcorpus.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:59.873685Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:59.873722Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01RwqhSjWPi8QhVmEe2xQQ8V", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"215849\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"215849\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:37:02.238529Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:37:04.490971Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_012meGnCEn8fYTJpLbnzTSZE", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude && python3 - << 'EOF'\ns = open(\"sweep.py\").read()\n# load cached corpus instead of importing modules\nstart = s.index(\"# ---- new corpus\")\nend = s.index('print(\"corpus words:\"')\ns = s[:start] + 'text = m.clean_text(open(\"/home/claude/corpus.txt\").read())\\nwords = text.split()\\n' + s[end:]\n# index words -> nodes once\ns = s.replace(\"by_first = collections.defaultdict(list)\",\n \"node_by_word = collections.defaultdict(list)\\nfor i,pair in i2n.items():\\n    for w in pair: node_by_word[w].append(i)\\nby_first = collections.defaultdict(list)\")\ns = s.replace(\"    starts = [i for i in range(n) if any(w in vocab for w in i2n[i])]\",\n \"    starts = list({i for w in vocab for i in node_by_word.get(w, [])})\")\ns = s.replace(\"        for w in p:\\n            for pair in i2n.values(): pass\\n\", \"\")\ns = s.replace(\"for _ in range(60)]\", \"for _ in range(40)]\")\nopen(\"sweep.py\",\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\nnohup python3 sweep.py > sweep.out 2>&1 &\nsleep 45; cat sweep.out", "description": "Optimize the sweep script and run it in the background"}, "message": "Optimize the sweep script and run it in the background", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude && python3 - << 'EOF'\\ns = open(\\\"sweep.py\\\").read()\\n# load cached corpus instead of importing modules\\nstart = s.index(\\\"# ---- new corpus\\\")\\nend = s.index('print(\\\"corpus words:\\\"')\\ns = s[:start] + 'text = m.clean_text(open(\\\"/home/claude/corpus.txt\\\").read())\\\\nwords = text.split()\\\\n' + s[end:]\\n# index words -> nodes once\\ns = s.replace(\\\"by_first = collections.defaultdict(list)\\\",\\n \\\"node_by_word = collections.defaultdict(list)\\\\nfor i,pair in i2n.items():\\\\n    for w in pair: node_by_word[w].append(i)\\\\nby_first = collections.defaultdict(list)\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\\"    starts = [i for i in range(n) if any(w in vocab for w in i2n[i])]\\\",\\n \\\"    starts = list({i for w in vocab for i in node_by_word.get(w, [])})\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\\"        for w in p:\\\\n            for pair in i2n.values(): pass\\\\n\\\", \\\"\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\\"for _ in range(60)]\\\", \\\"for _ in range(40)]\\\")\\nopen(\\\"sweep.py\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(s)\\nEOF\\nnohup python3 sweep.py > sweep.out 2>&1 &\\nsleep 45; cat sweep.out\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:37:49.737791Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:37:49.737839Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_012meGnCEn8fYTJpLbnzTSZE", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"corpus words: 215849\\ngraph nodes: 52237\\n\\n--- LENGTH sweep (current generator: boost always, no recency, cut x5) ---\\nlength=15                          distinct3=1.00 4gram_valid=0.75 heldout3=0.146 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 14.8 words= 15.0\\nlength=25                          distinct3=0.97 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.111 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 23.8 words= 25.0\\nlength=40                          distinct3=0.99 4gram_valid=0.71 heldout3=0.176 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 38.4 words= 40.0\\nlength=60                          distinct3=0.98 4gram_valid=0.70 heldout3=0.145 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 55.0 words= 60.0\\nlength=100                         distinct3=0.95 4gram_valid=0.70 heldout3=0.139 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 79.8 words=100.0\\nlength=200                         distinct3=0.96 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.156 jumps=0.000 first_loop@147.3 words=200.0\\n\\n--- ARRANGEMENT sweep at length=40 ---\\nbaseline (current)                 distinct3=0.97 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.182 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 36.5 words= 40.0\\nboost decays after 8 steps         distinct3=0.98 4gram_valid=0.70 heldout3=0.180 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 36.7 words= 40.0\\n+ recency penalty                  distinct3=1.00 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.179 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 39.6 words= 40.0\\n+ cut multiplier 1.0               distinct3=0.99 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.199 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 38.9 words= 40.0\\n+ stop at sentence end (all)       distinct3=1.00 4gram_valid=0.75 heldout3=0.114 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 22.1 words= 22.1\\n\\n--- LENGTH sweep with all fixes ---\\nfixed, length=15                   distinct3=1.00 4gram_valid=0.75 heldout3=0.146 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 15.0 words= 15.0\\nfixed, length=25                   distinct3=1.00 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.154 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 24.8 words= 25.0\\nfixed, length=40                   distinct3=1.00 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.178 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 38.9 words= 40.0\\nfixed, length=60                   distinct3=1.00 4gram_valid=0.73 heldout3=0.167 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 58.0 words= 60.0\\nfixed, length=100                  distinct3=0.99 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.201 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 91.9 words=100.0\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"corpus words: 215849\\ngraph nodes: 52237\\n\\n--- LENGTH sweep (current generator: boost always, no recency, cut x5) ---\\nlength=15                          distinct3=1.00 4gram_valid=0.75 heldout3=0.146 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 14.8 words= 15.0\\nlength=25                          distinct3=0.97 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.111 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 23.8 words= 25.0\\nlength=40                          distinct3=0.99 4gram_valid=0.71 heldout3=0.176 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 38.4 words= 40.0\\nlength=60                          distinct3=0.98 4gram_valid=0.70 heldout3=0.145 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 55.0 words= 60.0\\nlength=100                         distinct3=0.95 4gram_valid=0.70 heldout3=0.139 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 79.8 words=100.0\\nlength=200                         distinct3=0.96 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.156 jumps=0.000 first_loop@147.3 words=200.0\\n\\n--- ARRANGEMENT sweep at length=40 ---\\nbaseline (current)                 distinct3=0.97 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.182 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 36.5 words= 40.0\\nboost decays after 8 steps         distinct3=0.98 4gram_valid=0.70 heldout3=0.180 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 36.7 words= 40.0\\n+ recency penalty                  distinct3=1.00 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.179 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 39.6 words= 40.0\\n+ cut multiplier 1.0               distinct3=0.99 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.199 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 38.9 words= 40.0\\n+ stop at sentence end (all)       distinct3=1.00 4gram_valid=0.75 heldout3=0.114 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 22.1 words= 22.1\\n\\n--- LENGTH sweep with all fixes ---\\nfixed, length=15                   distinct3=1.00 4gram_valid=0.75 heldout3=0.146 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 15.0 words= 15.0\\nfixed, length=25                   distinct3=1.00 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.154 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 24.8 words= 25.0\\nfixed, length=40                   distinct3=1.00 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.178 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 38.9 words= 40.0\\nfixed, length=60                   distinct3=1.00 4gram_valid=0.73 heldout3=0.167 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 58.0 words= 60.0\\nfixed, length=100                  distinct3=0.99 4gram_valid=0.72 heldout3=0.201 jumps=0.000 first_loop@ 91.9 words=100.0\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:37:51.760521Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:38:04.267992Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Evaluating diversity metrics across a larger text corpus."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:38:04.268167Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:38:05.127335Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I can't produce predictions that look like measurements, so I ran the sweep for real. The corpus was about 216k words of Python standard-library docstrings, split 80/20 train/held-out, with 40 two-word prompts drawn from the held-out part. Several of my earlier rules of thumb didn't hold up.\n\n| Setting | Distinct 3-grams | 4-grams that exist in the corpus | First repeated 3-gram |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| length 15 | 1.00 | 0.75 | at the end (word 14.8) |\n| length 40 | 0.99 | 0.71 | at the end (word 38.4) |\n| length 100 | 0.95 | 0.70 | about word 80 |\n| length 200 | 0.96 | 0.72 | about word 147 |\n\n- **Length isn't the problem on a large corpus.** I predicted loops past 40 to 60 words, but at 216k words (52k graph nodes) the text barely repeats even at 200 words. Looping is a small-corpus problem, like the 5-sentence fox text.\n- **The coherence ceiling doesn't depend on length.** Only about 70 to 75% of generated 4-grams appear anywhere in the training text. The rest are splices the chain invented, and that holds at every length from 15 to 200, so a fixed length won't make it more logical.\n- **Arrangement changes were small.**\n  - The recency penalty took distinct 3-grams from 0.97 to 1.00, which is a real but small gain.\n  - Setting the cut multiplier to 1.0 and decaying the prompt boost made no measurable difference on these metrics.\n  - Stopping at a sentence end gave an average length of 22 words, which is the natural clause length in this corpus.\n\n**Caveats**\n- I used random spins instead of running `PCMMaxCut`, because its history recomputes energy every step and was too slow here. At your near-zero temperature it is close to random anyway, but I haven't confirmed that.\n- GloVe wasn't available, so peaks and vocabulary expansion weren't tested. Prompts only biased the walk's start.\n- \"Logical locution\" is only approximated by n-gram validity and repetition. Prompt relevance wasn't measured, so my claim that decaying the boost helps there is untested.\n- This is one seed, 40 prompts and no confidence intervals. The held-out trigram scores (0.11 to 0.20) bounced around with no trend, so I wouldn't read anything into them.\n\nOn your real data, corpus size and the 4-gram validity of your output are the numbers worth checking. I haven't changed your file. If you want, I can add the recency penalty and sentence-end stop to the full script and add this 4-gram check as a command you can run on your own dataset.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:38:05.242498Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:38:05.242498Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0febe-525e-7849-9e62-f13905f963e5"}]},{"uuid": "494019ae-895b-41c2-8712-9714e71cae24", "name": "Modal squeezer with word frequency semantics", "summary": "", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:35:14.554787Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:45:23.282334Z", "account": {"uuid": "8d7882cd-3e98-47cc-a6e7-61494a1ee4ac"}, "chat_messages": [{"uuid": "01a0fec1-e4f4-788e-8713-c6c58839426f", "text": "How about use a set of words then make up the freqs for the highest prob words, so they act as a logical semantics for the rest of the words as a modal squeezer", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:35:18.391809Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:35:18.391809Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "How about use a set of words then make up the freqs for the highest prob words, so they act as a logical semantics for the rest of the words as a modal squeezer", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:35:18.392079Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:35:18.392079Z", "attachments": [{"file_name": "", "file_size": 19903, "file_type": "txt", "extracted_content": "import math\nimport random\nimport re\nimport textwrap\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom itertools import zip_longest\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\n\n# gensim provides the GloVe vectors. If it is missing, the program falls\n# back to plain prompt-word biasing on the full graph.\ntry:\n    from gensim.models import KeyedVectors\n    import gensim.downloader as gensim_api\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = False\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# ORIGINAL SOLVER KEPT EXACTLY THE SAME\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass PCMMaxCut:\n    def __init__(self, graph, noise=0.02, drift_nu=0.08):\n        self.graph = graph\n        self.n = len(graph)\n        self.noise = noise\n        self.drift_nu = drift_nu\n        self.spins = [random.choice([-1, 1]) for _ in range(self.n)]\n        self.age = 1\n\n    def local_field(self, i):\n        return sum(\n            weight * self.spins[j]\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items()\n        )\n\n    def delta_energy(self, i):\n        return -2 * self.spins[i] * self.local_field(i)\n\n    def energy(self):\n        value = 0.0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i:\n                    value += weight * self.spins[i] * self.spins[j]\n        return value\n\n    def cut_size(self):\n        total = 0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i and self.spins[i] != self.spins[j]:\n                    total += weight\n        return total\n\n    def pcm_flip_attempt(self, temperature):\n        i = random.randrange(self.n)\n        delta = self.delta_energy(i)\n\n        drift = self.age ** (-self.drift_nu)\n        thermal_noise = random.gauss(\n            0.0,\n            self.noise\n        ) * max(1.0, abs(self.local_field(i)))\n\n        effective_delta = delta + thermal_noise * drift\n\n        if effective_delta <= 0:\n            accept = True\n        else:\n            accept = random.random() < math.exp(\n                -effective_delta / max(temperature, 1e-9)\n            )\n\n        if accept:\n            self.spins[i] *= -1\n            return i, True, delta\n\n        return i, False, delta\n\n    def run(self, iterations=1000, temperature=1.0, cooling=0.995):\n        history = []\n\n        for _ in range(iterations):\n            _, accepted, _ = self.pcm_flip_attempt(temperature)\n\n            temperature *= cooling\n            self.age += 1\n\n            history.append({\n                \"energy\": self.energy(),\n                \"cut\": self.cut_size(),\n                \"accepted\": accepted,\n                \"temperature\": temperature,\n                \"spins\": self.spins[:],\n            })\n\n        return history\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TEXT HELPERS\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[a-z']+\")\n\n\ndef clean_text(text):\n    text = text.replace(\"\\x00\", \" \")\n    text = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", text)\n    return text.strip()\n\n\ndef tokenize(text):\n    return TOKEN_RE.findall(text.lower())\n\n\ndef clean_word(word):\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z']\", \"\", word.lower())\n\n\ndef content_tokens(words):\n    \"\"\"Cleaned, non-stopword tokens.\"\"\"\n    cleaned = (clean_word(w) for w in words)\n    return [w for w in cleaned if w and w not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GLOVE PROMPT SLICER (probes the graph directly, no corpus segments)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass GloveSlicer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Slices a prompt into word windows, embeds each slice with GloVe, and\n    measures the Manhattan (L1) distance from the slice to every bigram\n    node of the dataset graph. The nearest nodes are the peaks, which seed\n    generation. Each slice's vocabulary is expanded with GloVe neighbours\n    that exist in the dataset.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, glove_name=\"glove-wiki-gigaword-100\", glove_path=None):\n        if glove_path:\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe from {glove_path}\")\n            self.kv = KeyedVectors.load_word2vec_format(\n                glove_path, binary=False, no_header=True\n            )\n        else:\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe: {glove_name} (cached after first download)\")\n            self.kv = gensim_api.load(glove_name)\n\n        self.dim = self.kv.vector_size\n        self.node_matrix = None\n        self.node_valid = None\n\n    # -- embedding -----------------------------------------------------\n\n    def embed(self, tokens):\n        vecs = [self.kv[t] for t in tokens if t in self.kv]\n        if not vecs:\n            return None\n        v = np.mean(vecs, axis=0)\n        norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n        return (v / norm).astype(np.float32) if norm > 0 else None\n\n    def index_nodes(self, id_to_node):\n        \"\"\"Embed every bigram node (content words only).\"\"\"\n        n = len(id_to_node)\n        self.node_matrix = np.zeros((n, self.dim), dtype=np.float32)\n        self.node_valid = np.zeros(n, dtype=bool)\n\n        for index, pair in id_to_node.items():\n            vec = self.embed(content_tokens(pair))\n            if vec is not None:\n                self.node_matrix[index] = vec\n                self.node_valid[index] = True\n\n        print(\n            f\"Embedded {int(self.node_valid.sum())}/{n} graph nodes with GloVe.\"\n        )\n\n    # -- slicing -------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def slice_prompt(self, prompt, width=2, stride=1):\n        tokens = [t for t in tokenize(prompt) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\n        if not tokens:\n            tokens = tokenize(prompt)\n\n        if len(tokens) <= width:\n            windows = [tokens]\n        else:\n            windows = [\n                tokens[i:i + width]\n                for i in range(0, len(tokens) - width + 1, stride)\n            ]\n\n        slices = []\n        for window in windows:\n            vec = self.embed(window)\n            if vec is not None:\n                slices.append((window, vec))\n        return slices\n\n    # -- Manhattan distance and peaks ----------------------------------\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def manhattan(a, b):\n        return float(np.abs(a - b).sum())\n\n    def node_distances(self, slice_vec):\n        \"\"\"Manhattan distance from one slice to every node (inf if invalid).\"\"\"\n        if self.node_matrix is None:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Call index_nodes() first.\")\n\n        distances = np.abs(self.node_matrix - slice_vec).sum(axis=1)\n        distances[~self.node_valid] = np.inf\n        return distances\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def find_peaks(distances, top_k=5, prominence=1.0):\n        \"\"\"\n        Peaks = the nodes whose distance sits at least `prominence`\n        standard deviations below the mean, capped at top_k. Always\n        returns at least the single nearest node.\n        \"\"\"\n        finite = np.isfinite(distances)\n        if not finite.any():\n            return []\n\n        mean = distances[finite].mean()\n        std = distances[finite].std()\n\n        k = min(top_k, int(finite.sum()))\n        nearest = np.argpartition(np.where(finite, distances, np.inf), k - 1)[:k]\n        nearest = nearest[np.argsort(distances[nearest])]\n\n        if std == 0:\n            return [int(nearest[0])]\n\n        peaks = [\n            int(i) for i in nearest\n            if (mean - distances[i]) / std >= prominence\n        ]\n\n        return peaks or [int(nearest[0])]\n\n    # -- accommodating vocabulary --------------------------------------\n\n    def expand_vocab(self, slice_tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\n        \"\"\"\n        Slice words plus nearest GloVe neighbours that also occur in the\n        dataset graph, so the Markov walk can actually reach them.\n        \"\"\"\n        vocab = set(slice_tokens)\n        added = 0\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(slice_vec, topn=topn):\n            if word in dataset_vocab and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS:\n                vocab.add(word)\n                added += 1\n                if added >= keep:\n                    break\n        return vocab\n\n\ndef dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node):\n    \"\"\"\n    Graph nodes keep raw whitespace tokens (\"dog.\", \"fox,\"), so map each\n    cleaned word to every raw form present in the graph.\n    \"\"\"\n    clean_to_raw = {}\n    for pair in id_to_node.values():\n        for raw in pair:\n            clean_to_raw.setdefault(clean_word(raw), set()).add(raw.lower())\n    return clean_to_raw\n\n\ndef to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw):\n    raw = set()\n    for word in clean_vocab:\n        raw.update(clean_to_raw.get(word, {word}))\n    return raw\n\n\ndef print_peak_table(slices, per_slice_distances, per_slice_peaks, id_to_node, max_rows=12):\n    \"\"\"Peak nodes down the side, one distance column per slice.\"\"\"\n    best = {}\n    for peaks, distances in zip(per_slice_peaks, per_slice_distances):\n        for node in peaks:\n            best[node] = min(best.get(node, np.inf), distances[node])\n\n    rows = sorted(best, key=lambda node: best[node])[:max_rows]\n\n    labels = [\" \".join(tokens)[:14] for tokens, _ in slices]\n    col = 16\n    print(\"\\nManhattan distance (peak node x slice)   * = peak for that slice\")\n    print(\"node\".ljust(24) + \"\".join(label.ljust(col) for label in labels))\n\n    for node in rows:\n        name = \" \".join(id_to_node[node])[:22]\n        line = name.ljust(24)\n        for peaks, distances in zip(per_slice_peaks, per_slice_distances):\n            cell = f\"{distances[node]:.3f}\"\n            if node in peaks:\n                cell += \" *\"\n            line += cell.ljust(col)\n        print(line)\n\n\ndef render_side_by_side(columns, total_width=118, gap=3):\n    \"\"\"columns: list of (header, text). Prints them as parallel columns.\"\"\"\n    n = len(columns)\n    width = max(18, (total_width - gap * (n - 1)) // n)\n    wrapped = [textwrap.wrap(text, width) for _, text in columns]\n    sep = \" \" * gap\n\n    lines = [sep.join(header[:width].ljust(width) for header, _ in columns)]\n    lines.append(sep.join(\"-\" * width for _ in columns))\n    for parts in zip_longest(*wrapped, fillvalue=\"\"):\n        lines.append(sep.join(part.ljust(width) for part in parts))\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GRAPH CREATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef process_text_to_trigram_graph(text, max_nodes=200):\n    \"\"\"\n    Builds a graph where nodes are bigrams and edges represent trigrams.\n    \"\"\"\n    text = text.lower()\n    words = text.split()\n\n    if len(words) < 3:\n        return {}, {}, {}\n\n    all_bigrams = [\n        (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        for i in range(len(words) - 1)\n    ]\n\n    top_bigrams = [\n        bigram\n        for bigram, _ in Counter(all_bigrams).most_common(max_nodes)\n    ]\n\n    bigram_set = set(top_bigrams)\n\n    node_to_id = {\n        bigram: index\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    id_to_node = {\n        index: bigram\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    graph = {\n        index: {}\n        for index in range(len(top_bigrams))\n    }\n\n    for i in range(len(words) - 2):\n        b1 = (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        b2 = (words[i + 1], words[i + 2])\n\n        if b1 in bigram_set and b2 in bigram_set:\n            id1 = node_to_id[b1]\n            id2 = node_to_id[b2]\n\n            if id1 != id2:\n                graph[id1][id2] = graph[id1].get(id2, 0) + 1\n                graph[id2][id1] = graph[id2].get(id1, 0) + 1\n\n    return graph, node_to_id, id_to_node\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PROMPT-AWARE MARKOV GENERATOR\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n    graph,\n    id_to_node,\n    spins,\n    prompt_vocab,\n    length=100,\n):\n    n = len(graph)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return \"\"\n\n    prompt_vocab = {\n        word.lower()\n        for word in prompt_vocab\n        if word.strip()\n    }\n\n    valid_starts = [\n        i\n        for i in range(n)\n        if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in id_to_node[i])\n    ]\n\n    current_node = (\n        random.choice(valid_starts)\n        if valid_starts\n        else random.randrange(n)\n    )\n\n    output = list(id_to_node[current_node])\n\n    for _ in range(max(0, length - 2)):\n        current_spin = spins[current_node]\n        neighbors = graph[current_node]\n        current_word_2 = id_to_node[current_node][1]\n\n        valid_neighbors = [\n            neighbor\n            for neighbor in neighbors\n            if id_to_node[neighbor][0] == current_word_2\n        ]\n\n        if not valid_neighbors:\n            fallback_nodes = [\n                i\n                for i, spin in enumerate(spins)\n                if (\n                    spin != current_spin\n                    and id_to_node[i][0] == current_word_2\n                )\n            ]\n\n            if fallback_nodes:\n                next_node = random.choice(fallback_nodes)\n            else:\n                next_node = random.randrange(n)\n        else:\n            probabilities = []\n\n            for neighbor in valid_neighbors:\n                base_weight = graph[current_node][neighbor]\n\n                cut_multiplier = (\n                    5.0\n                    if spins[neighbor] != current_spin\n                    else 1.0\n                )\n\n                neighbor_words = id_to_node[neighbor]\n\n                prompt_multiplier = (\n                    50.0\n                    if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in neighbor_words)\n                    else 1.0\n                )\n\n                score = (\n                    base_weight\n                    * cut_multiplier\n                    * prompt_multiplier\n                )\n\n                probabilities.append(score)\n\n            next_node = random.choices(\n                valid_neighbors,\n                weights=probabilities,\n                k=1,\n            )[0]\n\n        output.append(id_to_node[next_node][1])\n        current_node = next_node\n\n    return \" \".join(output)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GLOVE PROBE + SIDE-BY-SIDE GENERATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef glove_probe_and_generate(\n    prompt,\n    slicer,\n    graph,\n    id_to_node,\n    spins,\n    clean_to_raw,\n    width=2,\n    top_k=5,\n    length=60,\n    max_columns=4,\n):\n    slices = slicer.slice_prompt(prompt, width=width)\n\n    if not slices:\n        print(\"GloVe knows none of the prompt words; no slices to probe.\")\n        return False\n\n    # Keep the output readable: cap the number of side-by-side columns.\n    if len(slices) > max_columns:\n        step = len(slices) / max_columns\n        slices = [slices[int(i * step)] for i in range(max_columns)]\n\n    per_slice_distances = [slicer.node_distances(vec) for _, vec in slices]\n    per_slice_peaks = [\n        slicer.find_peaks(d, top_k=top_k) for d in per_slice_distances\n    ]\n\n    if not any(per_slice_peaks):\n        print(\"No usable peaks found.\")\n        return False\n\n    print_peak_table(\n        slices, per_slice_distances, per_slice_peaks, id_to_node\n    )\n\n    dataset_vocab = set(clean_to_raw)\n\n    columns = []\n    for (tokens, slice_vec), peaks in zip(slices, per_slice_peaks):\n        clean_vocab = slicer.expand_vocab(tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab)\n        raw_vocab = to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw)\n\n        # The peak nodes' own words also seed the walk.\n        for node in peaks:\n            raw_vocab.update(id_to_node[node])\n\n        text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n            graph,\n            id_to_node,\n            spins,\n            raw_vocab,\n            length=length,\n        )\n\n        added = len(clean_vocab) - len(tokens)\n        header = f\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] +{max(added, 0)} words\"\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \".\"))\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated Output (one column per prompt slice):\\n\")\n    print(render_side_by_side(columns))\n    print()\n    return True\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PLAIN FALLBACK (no GloVe)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef plain_generate(prompt, graph, id_to_node, spins):\n    final_text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n        graph,\n        id_to_node,\n        spins,\n        prompt.split(),\n        length=400,\n    )\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated Output:\")\n    print(f\"> {final_text.capitalize()}.\\n\")\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# MAIN PROGRAM\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef load_text_file(filepath):\n    try:\n        with open(filepath, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n            return file.read()\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"File {filepath} not found. Using fallback text.\")\n\n        return (\n            \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. \"\n            \"The lazy dog barks at the brown fox. \"\n            \"The quick brown fox runs away quickly into the deep \"\n            \"dark brown forest. The dark forest is full of mystery. \"\n            \"A dog barks loudly in the dark.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef load_slicer(id_to_node):\n    if not GENSIM_AVAILABLE:\n        print(\"gensim not installed (pip install gensim). Using plain generation.\")\n        return None\n\n    glove_path = input(\n        \"Local GloVe .txt path (blank = download glove-wiki-gigaword-100): \"\n    ).strip()\n\n    try:\n        slicer = GloveSlicer(glove_path=glove_path or None)\n        slicer.index_nodes(id_to_node)\n        return slicer\n    except Exception as error:\n        print(f\"Could not load GloVe ({error}). Using plain generation.\")\n        return None\n\n\ndef main():\n    dataset_file = input(\"Dataset filename: \").strip()\n\n    dataset_text = clean_text(load_text_file(dataset_file))\n\n    print(\"Building graph from the complete dataset...\")\n    graph, node_to_id, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\n        dataset_text,\n        max_nodes=150000,\n    )\n\n    if not graph:\n        print(\"Graph is empty. Check the dataset.\")\n        return\n\n    print(f\"Graph built with {len(graph)} unique nodes.\")\n\n    print(\"Running PCMMaxCut solver for structural baseline...\")\n\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\n        graph,\n        noise=0.00001,\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\n    )\n\n    history = solver.run(\n        iterations=5000,\n        temperature=0.0000005,\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\n    )\n\n    best_cut = max(\n        history,\n        key=lambda item: item[\"cut\"],\n    )\n\n    print(\n        f\"Base partition created. \"\n        f\"Max Cut Size: {best_cut['cut']}\\n\"\n    )\n\n    spins = best_cut[\"spins\"]\n    clean_to_raw = dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node)\n    slicer = load_slicer(id_to_node)\n\n    while True:\n        try:\n            user_prompt = input(\"USER: \").strip()\n        except (KeyboardInterrupt, EOFError):\n            print(\"\\nExiting.\")\n            break\n\n        if not user_prompt:\n            continue\n\n        if user_prompt.lower() in {\"exit\", \"quit\"}:\n            break\n\n        done = False\n\n        if slicer is not None:\n            done = glove_probe_and_generate(\n                user_prompt,\n                slicer,\n                graph,\n                id_to_node,\n                spins,\n                clean_to_raw,\n                width=2,\n                top_k=5,\n                length=60,\n                max_columns=4,\n            )\n\n        # Fall back to plain prompt-word biasing if GloVe is unavailable\n        # or knows none of the prompt words.\n        if not done:\n            plain_generate(user_prompt, graph, id_to_node, spins)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()"}], "files": [{"file_uuid": "39d20d94-c9f3-41d8-a1d7-09d905df623c", "file_name": ""}], "parent_message_uuid": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000"}, {"uuid": "01a0fec1-e4f4-7e74-8eab-bc86694a8753", "text": "Here's one way to read that: the anchor words get invented Zipf-style frequencies, and the rest of the graph is scored by how semantically close it is to those anchors. Squeezing the weights with a power (`w**gamma`) then pulls probability mass toward the mode, so the walk follows the anchors' meaning instead of just hitting a keyword.\n\nThis replaces the binary `50.0 if word in prompt_vocab else 1.0` with a continuous weight per node.\n\n**1. Add the squeezer**\n\n```python\nclass ModalSqueezer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Anchors (nearest GloVe words to a slice) get made-up Zipf frequencies.\n    Every graph node is scored by its similarity to the anchors, weighted\n    by those frequencies, then squeezed toward the mode with w**gamma.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, zipf_s=1.0, gamma=2.5, boost=50.0):\n        self.zipf_s = zipf_s\n        self.gamma = gamma      # >1 sharpens toward the mode, <1 flattens\n        self.boost = boost      # max multiplier, same role as the old 50.0\n\n    def synthetic_freqs(self, k):\n        ranks = np.arange(1, k + 1, dtype=np.float32)\n        f = 1.0 / ranks ** self.zipf_s\n        return f / f.sum()\n\n    def node_weights(self, node_matrix, node_valid, anchor_vecs):\n        n = node_matrix.shape[0]\n        if len(anchor_vecs) == 0:\n            return np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n\n        freqs = self.synthetic_freqs(len(anchor_vecs))\n        sims = np.clip(node_matrix @ anchor_vecs.T, 0.0, None)  # cosine (unit vectors)\n        sem = sims @ freqs                                      # freq-weighted semantics\n        sem[~node_valid] = 0.0\n\n        peak = sem.max()\n        if peak <= 0:\n            return np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n\n        w = sem / peak\n        return (w ** self.gamma).astype(np.float32)             # the modal squeeze\n```\n\n**2. Give `GloveSlicer` an ordered anchor list**\n\n```python\n    def anchors(self, slice_tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\n        \"\"\"Ordered anchors: slice words first, then nearest dataset neighbours.\"\"\"\n        ordered = [t for t in slice_tokens if t in self.kv]\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(slice_vec, topn=topn):\n            if word in dataset_vocab and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS \\\n                    and word not in ordered:\n                ordered.append(word)\n            if len(ordered) >= keep + len(slice_tokens):\n                break\n        vecs = np.array([self.kv.get_vector(w, norm=True) for w in ordered],\n                        dtype=np.float32)\n        return ordered, vecs\n```\n\n**3. Let the generator take node weights**\n\nIn `generate_markovian_prompt_text`, add `node_weights=None, boost=50.0` to the signature and change two spots:\n\n```python\n    # start node: sample by semantic weight instead of a hard word match\n    if node_weights is not None and node_weights.sum() > 0:\n        current_node = random.choices(range(n), weights=node_weights + 1e-6, k=1)[0]\n    else:\n        current_node = random.choice(valid_starts) if valid_starts else random.randrange(n)\n```\n\n```python\n    # inside the neighbor scoring loop\n    if node_weights is not None:\n        prompt_multiplier = 1.0 + boost * float(node_weights[neighbor])\n    else:\n        prompt_multiplier = (\n            50.0 if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in neighbor_words) else 1.0\n        )\n```\n\n**4. Wire it into `glove_probe_and_generate`**\n\nAdd a `squeezer=None` parameter, then replace the column-building loop body:\n\n```python\n    for (tokens, slice_vec), peaks in zip(slices, per_slice_peaks):\n        anchor_words, anchor_vecs = slicer.anchors(tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab)\n        weights = squeezer.node_weights(\n            slicer.node_matrix, slicer.node_valid, anchor_vecs\n        )\n\n        # peak nodes are the strongest anchors: pin them to full weight\n        for node in peaks:\n            weights[node] = 1.0\n\n        text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n            graph, id_to_node, spins,\n            to_raw_vocab(set(anchor_words), clean_to_raw),\n            length=length,\n            node_weights=weights,\n            boost=squeezer.boost,\n        )\n\n        header = f\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] \u03b3={squeezer.gamma}\"\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \".\"))\n```\n\nIn `main()`, pass `squeezer=ModalSqueezer(gamma=2.5)` through the call.\n\n**Tuning notes**\n\n- `gamma` is the squeeze. Around 1 the weights track GloVe similarity broadly. At 3 to 4 only nodes very close to the top anchors keep real weight, so the output gets repetitive and on-topic. Below 1 it flattens toward the plain Markov chain.\n- `zipf_s` controls how top-heavy the made-up frequencies are. A higher value makes the first anchor (usually your literal prompt word) dominate the semantics.\n- The max-cut `cut_multiplier` (5x) still applies, so the structural partition and the semantic squeeze multiply instead of competing.\n- If you want it adaptive, compute the entropy of `weights / weights.sum()` and raise `gamma` when entropy is high (diffuse prompt) and lower it when it's already peaked.\n\nOne limitation: node vectors only exist for bigrams made of content words. Pure stopword bigrams like \"of the\" get weight 0, so they only appear through the `1.0` base multiplier. That's usually what you want, since they act as connective tissue.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:35:18.260363Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:35:29.920953Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Assigning synthetic frequencies to top vocabulary words."}, {"summary": "Designing a semantic weighting scheme to sharpen word probabilities."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:35:29.920988Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:35:41.617618Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Here's one way to read that: the anchor words get invented Zipf-style frequencies, and the rest of the graph is scored by how semantically close it is to those anchors. Squeezing the weights with a power (`w**gamma`) then pulls probability mass toward the mode, so the walk follows the anchors' meaning instead of just hitting a keyword.\n\nThis replaces the binary `50.0 if word in prompt_vocab else 1.0` with a continuous weight per node.\n\n**1. Add the squeezer**\n\n```python\nclass ModalSqueezer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Anchors (nearest GloVe words to a slice) get made-up Zipf frequencies.\n    Every graph node is scored by its similarity to the anchors, weighted\n    by those frequencies, then squeezed toward the mode with w**gamma.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, zipf_s=1.0, gamma=2.5, boost=50.0):\n        self.zipf_s = zipf_s\n        self.gamma = gamma      # >1 sharpens toward the mode, <1 flattens\n        self.boost = boost      # max multiplier, same role as the old 50.0\n\n    def synthetic_freqs(self, k):\n        ranks = np.arange(1, k + 1, dtype=np.float32)\n        f = 1.0 / ranks ** self.zipf_s\n        return f / f.sum()\n\n    def node_weights(self, node_matrix, node_valid, anchor_vecs):\n        n = node_matrix.shape[0]\n        if len(anchor_vecs) == 0:\n            return np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n\n        freqs = self.synthetic_freqs(len(anchor_vecs))\n        sims = np.clip(node_matrix @ anchor_vecs.T, 0.0, None)  # cosine (unit vectors)\n        sem = sims @ freqs                                      # freq-weighted semantics\n        sem[~node_valid] = 0.0\n\n        peak = sem.max()\n        if peak <= 0:\n            return np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n\n        w = sem / peak\n        return (w ** self.gamma).astype(np.float32)             # the modal squeeze\n```\n\n**2. Give `GloveSlicer` an ordered anchor list**\n\n```python\n    def anchors(self, slice_tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\n        \"\"\"Ordered anchors: slice words first, then nearest dataset neighbours.\"\"\"\n        ordered = [t for t in slice_tokens if t in self.kv]\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(slice_vec, topn=topn):\n            if word in dataset_vocab and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS \\\n                    and word not in ordered:\n                ordered.append(word)\n            if len(ordered) >= keep + len(slice_tokens):\n                break\n        vecs = np.array([self.kv.get_vector(w, norm=True) for w in ordered],\n                        dtype=np.float32)\n        return ordered, vecs\n```\n\n**3. Let the generator take node weights**\n\nIn `generate_markovian_prompt_text`, add `node_weights=None, boost=50.0` to the signature and change two spots:\n\n```python\n    # start node: sample by semantic weight instead of a hard word match\n    if node_weights is not None and node_weights.sum() > 0:\n        current_node = random.choices(range(n), weights=node_weights + 1e-6, k=1)[0]\n    else:\n        current_node = random.choice(valid_starts) if valid_starts else random.randrange(n)\n```\n\n```python\n    # inside the neighbor scoring loop\n    if node_weights is not None:\n        prompt_multiplier = 1.0 + boost * float(node_weights[neighbor])\n    else:\n        prompt_multiplier = (\n            50.0 if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in neighbor_words) else 1.0\n        )\n```\n\n**4. Wire it into `glove_probe_and_generate`**\n\nAdd a `squeezer=None` parameter, then replace the column-building loop body:\n\n```python\n    for (tokens, slice_vec), peaks in zip(slices, per_slice_peaks):\n        anchor_words, anchor_vecs = slicer.anchors(tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab)\n        weights = squeezer.node_weights(\n            slicer.node_matrix, slicer.node_valid, anchor_vecs\n        )\n\n        # peak nodes are the strongest anchors: pin them to full weight\n        for node in peaks:\n            weights[node] = 1.0\n\n        text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n            graph, id_to_node, spins,\n            to_raw_vocab(set(anchor_words), clean_to_raw),\n            length=length,\n            node_weights=weights,\n            boost=squeezer.boost,\n        )\n\n        header = f\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] \u03b3={squeezer.gamma}\"\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \".\"))\n```\n\nIn `main()`, pass `squeezer=ModalSqueezer(gamma=2.5)` through the call.\n\n**Tuning notes**\n\n- `gamma` is the squeeze. Around 1 the weights track GloVe similarity broadly. At 3 to 4 only nodes very close to the top anchors keep real weight, so the output gets repetitive and on-topic. Below 1 it flattens toward the plain Markov chain.\n- `zipf_s` controls how top-heavy the made-up frequencies are. A higher value makes the first anchor (usually your literal prompt word) dominate the semantics.\n- The max-cut `cut_multiplier` (5x) still applies, so the structural partition and the semantic squeeze multiply instead of competing.\n- If you want it adaptive, compute the entropy of `weights / weights.sum()` and raise `gamma` when entropy is high (diffuse prompt) and lower it when it's already peaked.\n\nOne limitation: node vectors only exist for bigrams made of content words. Pure stopword bigrams like \"of the\" get weight 0, so they only appear through the `1.0` base multiplier. That's usually what you want, since they act as connective tissue.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:35:41.695275Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:35:41.695275Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fec1-e4f4-788e-8713-c6c58839426f"}, {"uuid": "01a0fec2-50ec-70c8-b0f6-aa77019d28c2", "text": "do the full code", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:35:43.784359Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:35:43.784359Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "do the full code", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:35:43.784499Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:35:43.784499Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fec1-e4f4-7e74-8eab-bc86694a8753"}, {"uuid": "01a0fec2-50ec-76b6-9abe-364f6dacb26a", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThe full program is above, with `PCMMaxCut` left untouched and the squeezer wired in. I haven't run it. If GloVe is missing or knows none of the prompt words, it falls back to the original plain prompt-word biasing.\n\nTo tune it, edit the `ModalSqueezer(zipf_s=1.0, gamma=2.5, boost=50.0)` line in `main()`:\n- **`gamma`:** at 3 to 4 the output gets repetitive and tightly on-topic. At 1 or below it drifts back toward the plain Markov chain.\n- **`zipf_s`:** a higher value makes the first anchor, usually your literal prompt word, dominate more.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:35:43.779805Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:35:48.642031Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Preparing to deliver the full integrated code as a file."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:35:48.642102Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:26.895970Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01XpgBYe3vCgNHYy7cMRg5ik", "name": "create_file", "input": {"description": "Full program with ModalSqueezer integrated", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_squeezer.py", "file_text": "import math\nimport random\nimport re\nimport textwrap\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom itertools import zip_longest\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\n\n# gensim provides the GloVe vectors. If it is missing, the program falls\n# back to plain prompt-word biasing on the full graph.\ntry:\n    from gensim.models import KeyedVectors\n    import gensim.downloader as gensim_api\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = False\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# ORIGINAL SOLVER KEPT EXACTLY THE SAME\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass PCMMaxCut:\n    def __init__(self, graph, noise=0.02, drift_nu=0.08):\n        self.graph = graph\n        self.n = len(graph)\n        self.noise = noise\n        self.drift_nu = drift_nu\n        self.spins = [random.choice([-1, 1]) for _ in range(self.n)]\n        self.age = 1\n\n    def local_field(self, i):\n        return sum(\n            weight * self.spins[j]\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items()\n        )\n\n    def delta_energy(self, i):\n        return -2 * self.spins[i] * self.local_field(i)\n\n    def energy(self):\n        value = 0.0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i:\n                    value += weight * self.spins[i] * self.spins[j]\n        return value\n\n    def cut_size(self):\n        total = 0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i and self.spins[i] != self.spins[j]:\n                    total += weight\n        return total\n\n    def pcm_flip_attempt(self, temperature):\n        i = random.randrange(self.n)\n        delta = self.delta_energy(i)\n\n        drift = self.age ** (-self.drift_nu)\n        thermal_noise = random.gauss(\n            0.0,\n            self.noise\n        ) * max(1.0, abs(self.local_field(i)))\n\n        effective_delta = delta + thermal_noise * drift\n\n        if effective_delta <= 0:\n            accept = True\n        else:\n            accept = random.random() < math.exp(\n                -effective_delta / max(temperature, 1e-9)\n            )\n\n        if accept:\n            self.spins[i] *= -1\n            return i, True, delta\n\n        return i, False, delta\n\n    def run(self, iterations=1000, temperature=1.0, cooling=0.995):\n        history = []\n\n        for _ in range(iterations):\n            _, accepted, _ = self.pcm_flip_attempt(temperature)\n\n            temperature *= cooling\n            self.age += 1\n\n            history.append({\n                \"energy\": self.energy(),\n                \"cut\": self.cut_size(),\n                \"accepted\": accepted,\n                \"temperature\": temperature,\n                \"spins\": self.spins[:],\n            })\n\n        return history\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TEXT HELPERS\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[a-z']+\")\n\n\ndef clean_text(text):\n    text = text.replace(\"\\x00\", \" \")\n    text = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", text)\n    return text.strip()\n\n\ndef tokenize(text):\n    return TOKEN_RE.findall(text.lower())\n\n\ndef clean_word(word):\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z']\", \"\", word.lower())\n\n\ndef content_tokens(words):\n    \"\"\"Cleaned, non-stopword tokens.\"\"\"\n    cleaned = (clean_word(w) for w in words)\n    return [w for w in cleaned if w and w not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# MODAL SQUEEZER\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass ModalSqueezer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Anchors (nearest GloVe words to a slice) get made-up Zipf frequencies.\n    Every graph node is scored by its similarity to the anchors, weighted\n    by those frequencies, then squeezed toward the mode with w**gamma.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, zipf_s=1.0, gamma=2.5, boost=50.0):\n        self.zipf_s = zipf_s    # higher = first anchor dominates more\n        self.gamma = gamma      # >1 sharpens toward the mode, <1 flattens\n        self.boost = boost      # max multiplier, same role as the old 50.0\n\n    def synthetic_freqs(self, k):\n        ranks = np.arange(1, k + 1, dtype=np.float32)\n        f = 1.0 / ranks ** self.zipf_s\n        return f / f.sum()\n\n    def node_weights(self, node_matrix, node_valid, anchor_vecs):\n        n = node_matrix.shape[0]\n        if len(anchor_vecs) == 0:\n            return np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n\n        freqs = self.synthetic_freqs(len(anchor_vecs))\n        # cosine similarity (all vectors are unit length)\n        sims = np.clip(node_matrix @ anchor_vecs.T, 0.0, None)\n        sem = sims @ freqs                      # freq-weighted semantics\n        sem[~node_valid] = 0.0\n\n        peak = sem.max()\n        if peak <= 0:\n            return np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n\n        w = sem / peak\n        return (w ** self.gamma).astype(np.float32)   # the modal squeeze\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GLOVE PROMPT SLICER (probes the graph directly, no corpus segments)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass GloveSlicer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Slices a prompt into word windows, embeds each slice with GloVe, and\n    measures the Manhattan (L1) distance from the slice to every bigram\n    node of the dataset graph. The nearest nodes are the peaks, which seed\n    generation. Each slice also yields an ordered anchor list (slice words\n    plus GloVe neighbours that exist in the dataset).\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, glove_name=\"glove-wiki-gigaword-100\", glove_path=None):\n        if glove_path:\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe from {glove_path}\")\n            self.kv = KeyedVectors.load_word2vec_format(\n                glove_path, binary=False, no_header=True\n            )\n        else:\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe: {glove_name} (cached after first download)\")\n            self.kv = gensim_api.load(glove_name)\n\n        self.dim = self.kv.vector_size\n        self.node_matrix = None\n        self.node_valid = None\n\n    # -- embedding -----------------------------------------------------\n\n    def embed(self, tokens):\n        vecs = [self.kv[t] for t in tokens if t in self.kv]\n        if not vecs:\n            return None\n        v = np.mean(vecs, axis=0)\n        norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n        return (v / norm).astype(np.float32) if norm > 0 else None\n\n    def index_nodes(self, id_to_node):\n        \"\"\"Embed every bigram node (content words only).\"\"\"\n        n = len(id_to_node)\n        self.node_matrix = np.zeros((n, self.dim), dtype=np.float32)\n        self.node_valid = np.zeros(n, dtype=bool)\n\n        for index, pair in id_to_node.items():\n            vec = self.embed(content_tokens(pair))\n            if vec is not None:\n                self.node_matrix[index] = vec\n                self.node_valid[index] = True\n\n        print(\n            f\"Embedded {int(self.node_valid.sum())}/{n} graph nodes with GloVe.\"\n        )\n\n    # -- slicing -------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def slice_prompt(self, prompt, width=2, stride=1):\n        tokens = [t for t in tokenize(prompt) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\n        if not tokens:\n            tokens = tokenize(prompt)\n\n        if len(tokens) <= width:\n            windows = [tokens]\n        else:\n            windows = [\n                tokens[i:i + width]\n                for i in range(0, len(tokens) - width + 1, stride)\n            ]\n\n        slices = []\n        for window in windows:\n            vec = self.embed(window)\n            if vec is not None:\n                slices.append((window, vec))\n        return slices\n\n    # -- Manhattan distance and peaks ----------------------------------\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def manhattan(a, b):\n        return float(np.abs(a - b).sum())\n\n    def node_distances(self, slice_vec):\n        \"\"\"Manhattan distance from one slice to every node (inf if invalid).\"\"\"\n        if self.node_matrix is None:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Call index_nodes() first.\")\n\n        distances = np.abs(self.node_matrix - slice_vec).sum(axis=1)\n        distances[~self.node_valid] = np.inf\n        return distances\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def find_peaks(distances, top_k=5, prominence=1.0):\n        \"\"\"\n        Peaks = the nodes whose distance sits at least `prominence`\n        standard deviations below the mean, capped at top_k. Always\n        returns at least the single nearest node.\n        \"\"\"\n        finite = np.isfinite(distances)\n        if not finite.any():\n            return []\n\n        mean = distances[finite].mean()\n        std = distances[finite].std()\n\n        k = min(top_k, int(finite.sum()))\n        nearest = np.argpartition(np.where(finite, distances, np.inf), k - 1)[:k]\n        nearest = nearest[np.argsort(distances[nearest])]\n\n        if std == 0:\n            return [int(nearest[0])]\n\n        peaks = [\n            int(i) for i in nearest\n            if (mean - distances[i]) / std >= prominence\n        ]\n\n        return peaks or [int(nearest[0])]\n\n    # -- ordered anchors for the squeezer ------------------------------\n\n    def anchors(self, slice_tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\n        \"\"\"Ordered anchors: slice words first, then nearest dataset neighbours.\"\"\"\n        ordered = [t for t in slice_tokens if t in self.kv]\n        limit = keep + len(ordered)\n\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(slice_vec, topn=topn):\n            if (\n                word in dataset_vocab\n                and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\n                and word not in ordered\n            ):\n                ordered.append(word)\n            if len(ordered) >= limit:\n                break\n\n        vecs = np.array(\n            [self.kv.get_vector(w, norm=True) for w in ordered],\n            dtype=np.float32,\n        )\n        return ordered, vecs\n\n\ndef dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node):\n    \"\"\"\n    Graph nodes keep raw whitespace tokens (\"dog.\", \"fox,\"), so map each\n    cleaned word to every raw form present in the graph.\n    \"\"\"\n    clean_to_raw = {}\n    for pair in id_to_node.values():\n        for raw in pair:\n            clean_to_raw.setdefault(clean_word(raw), set()).add(raw.lower())\n    return clean_to_raw\n\n\ndef to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw):\n    raw = set()\n    for word in clean_vocab:\n        raw.update(clean_to_raw.get(word, {word}))\n    return raw\n\n\ndef print_peak_table(slices, per_slice_distances, per_slice_peaks, id_to_node, max_rows=12):\n    \"\"\"Peak nodes down the side, one distance column per slice.\"\"\"\n    best = {}\n    for peaks, distances in zip(per_slice_peaks, per_slice_distances):\n        for node in peaks:\n            best[node] = min(best.get(node, np.inf), distances[node])\n\n    rows = sorted(best, key=lambda node: best[node])[:max_rows]\n\n    labels = [\" \".join(tokens)[:14] for tokens, _ in slices]\n    col = 16\n    print(\"\\nManhattan distance (peak node x slice)   * = peak for that slice\")\n    print(\"node\".ljust(24) + \"\".join(label.ljust(col) for label in labels))\n\n    for node in rows:\n        name = \" \".join(id_to_node[node])[:22]\n        line = name.ljust(24)\n        for peaks, distances in zip(per_slice_peaks, per_slice_distances):\n            cell = f\"{distances[node]:.3f}\"\n            if node in peaks:\n                cell += \" *\"\n            line += cell.ljust(col)\n        print(line)\n\n\ndef render_side_by_side(columns, total_width=118, gap=3):\n    \"\"\"columns: list of (header, text). Prints them as parallel columns.\"\"\"\n    n = len(columns)\n    width = max(18, (total_width - gap * (n - 1)) // n)\n    wrapped = [textwrap.wrap(text, width) for _, text in columns]\n    sep = \" \" * gap\n\n    lines = [sep.join(header[:width].ljust(width) for header, _ in columns)]\n    lines.append(sep.join(\"-\" * width for _ in columns))\n    for parts in zip_longest(*wrapped, fillvalue=\"\"):\n        lines.append(sep.join(part.ljust(width) for part in parts))\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GRAPH CREATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef process_text_to_trigram_graph(text, max_nodes=200):\n    \"\"\"\n    Builds a graph where nodes are bigrams and edges represent trigrams.\n    \"\"\"\n    text = text.lower()\n    words = text.split()\n\n    if len(words) < 3:\n        return {}, {}, {}\n\n    all_bigrams = [\n        (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        for i in range(len(words) - 1)\n    ]\n\n    top_bigrams = [\n        bigram\n        for bigram, _ in Counter(all_bigrams).most_common(max_nodes)\n    ]\n\n    bigram_set = set(top_bigrams)\n\n    node_to_id = {\n        bigram: index\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    id_to_node = {\n        index: bigram\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    graph = {\n        index: {}\n        for index in range(len(top_bigrams))\n    }\n\n    for i in range(len(words) - 2):\n        b1 = (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        b2 = (words[i + 1], words[i + 2])\n\n        if b1 in bigram_set and b2 in bigram_set:\n            id1 = node_to_id[b1]\n            id2 = node_to_id[b2]\n\n            if id1 != id2:\n                graph[id1][id2] = graph[id1].get(id2, 0) + 1\n                graph[id2][id1] = graph[id2].get(id1, 0) + 1\n\n    return graph, node_to_id, id_to_node\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PROMPT-AWARE MARKOV GENERATOR\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n    graph,\n    id_to_node,\n    spins,\n    prompt_vocab,\n    length=100,\n    node_weights=None,\n    boost=50.0,\n):\n    n = len(graph)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return \"\"\n\n    prompt_vocab = {\n        word.lower()\n        for word in prompt_vocab\n        if word.strip()\n    }\n\n    use_semantic = node_weights is not None and node_weights.sum() > 0\n\n    # Start node: sample by semantic weight instead of a hard word match.\n    if use_semantic:\n        current_node = random.choices(\n            range(n),\n            weights=node_weights + 1e-6,\n            k=1,\n        )[0]\n    else:\n        valid_starts = [\n            i\n            for i in range(n)\n            if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in id_to_node[i])\n        ]\n        current_node = (\n            random.choice(valid_starts)\n            if valid_starts\n            else random.randrange(n)\n        )\n\n    output = list(id_to_node[current_node])\n\n    for _ in range(max(0, length - 2)):\n        current_spin = spins[current_node]\n        neighbors = graph[current_node]\n        current_word_2 = id_to_node[current_node][1]\n\n        valid_neighbors = [\n            neighbor\n            for neighbor in neighbors\n            if id_to_node[neighbor][0] == current_word_2\n        ]\n\n        if not valid_neighbors:\n            fallback_nodes = [\n                i\n                for i, spin in enumerate(spins)\n                if (\n                    spin != current_spin\n                    and id_to_node[i][0] == current_word_2\n                )\n            ]\n\n            if fallback_nodes:\n                next_node = random.choice(fallback_nodes)\n            else:\n                next_node = random.randrange(n)\n        else:\n            probabilities = []\n\n            for neighbor in valid_neighbors:\n                base_weight = graph[current_node][neighbor]\n\n                cut_multiplier = (\n                    5.0\n                    if spins[neighbor] != current_spin\n                    else 1.0\n                )\n\n                if use_semantic:\n                    prompt_multiplier = 1.0 + boost * float(node_weights[neighbor])\n                else:\n                    neighbor_words = id_to_node[neighbor]\n                    prompt_multiplier = (\n                        50.0\n                        if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in neighbor_words)\n                        else 1.0\n                    )\n\n                score = (\n                    base_weight\n                    * cut_multiplier\n                    * prompt_multiplier\n                )\n\n                probabilities.append(score)\n\n            next_node = random.choices(\n                valid_neighbors,\n                weights=probabilities,\n                k=1,\n            )[0]\n\n        output.append(id_to_node[next_node][1])\n        current_node = next_node\n\n    return \" \".join(output)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GLOVE PROBE + SIDE-BY-SIDE GENERATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef glove_probe_and_generate(\n    prompt,\n    slicer,\n    graph,\n    id_to_node,\n    spins,\n    clean_to_raw,\n    squeezer,\n    width=2,\n    top_k=5,\n    length=60,\n    max_columns=4,\n):\n    slices = slicer.slice_prompt(prompt, width=width)\n\n    if not slices:\n        print(\"GloVe knows none of the prompt words; no slices to probe.\")\n        return False\n\n    # Keep the output readable: cap the number of side-by-side columns.\n    if len(slices) > max_columns:\n        step = len(slices) / max_columns\n        slices = [slices[int(i * step)] for i in range(max_columns)]\n\n    per_slice_distances = [slicer.node_distances(vec) for _, vec in slices]\n    per_slice_peaks = [\n        slicer.find_peaks(d, top_k=top_k) for d in per_slice_distances\n    ]\n\n    if not any(per_slice_peaks):\n        print(\"No usable peaks found.\")\n        return False\n\n    print_peak_table(\n        slices, per_slice_distances, per_slice_peaks, id_to_node\n    )\n\n    dataset_vocab = set(clean_to_raw)\n\n    columns = []\n    for (tokens, slice_vec), peaks in zip(slices, per_slice_peaks):\n        anchor_words, anchor_vecs = slicer.anchors(\n            tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab\n        )\n\n        weights = squeezer.node_weights(\n            slicer.node_matrix, slicer.node_valid, anchor_vecs\n        )\n\n        # Peak nodes are the strongest anchors: pin them to full weight.\n        for node in peaks:\n            weights[node] = 1.0\n\n        raw_vocab = to_raw_vocab(set(anchor_words), clean_to_raw)\n        for node in peaks:\n            raw_vocab.update(id_to_node[node])\n\n        text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n            graph,\n            id_to_node,\n            spins,\n            raw_vocab,\n            length=length,\n            node_weights=weights,\n            boost=squeezer.boost,\n        )\n\n        header = (\n            f\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] \"\n            f\"{len(anchor_words)} anchors g={squeezer.gamma}\"\n        )\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \".\"))\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated Output (one column per prompt slice):\\n\")\n    print(render_side_by_side(columns))\n    print()\n    return True\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PLAIN FALLBACK (no GloVe)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef plain_generate(prompt, graph, id_to_node, spins):\n    final_text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n        graph,\n        id_to_node,\n        spins,\n        prompt.split(),\n        length=400,\n    )\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated Output:\")\n    print(f\"> {final_text.capitalize()}.\\n\")\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# MAIN PROGRAM\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef load_text_file(filepath):\n    try:\n        with open(filepath, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n            return file.read()\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"File {filepath} not found. Using fallback text.\")\n\n        return (\n            \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. \"\n            \"The lazy dog barks at the brown fox. \"\n            \"The quick brown fox runs away quickly into the deep \"\n            \"dark brown forest. The dark forest is full of mystery. \"\n            \"A dog barks loudly in the dark.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef load_slicer(id_to_node):\n    if not GENSIM_AVAILABLE:\n        print(\"gensim not installed (pip install gensim). Using plain generation.\")\n        return None\n\n    glove_path = input(\n        \"Local GloVe .txt path (blank = download glove-wiki-gigaword-100): \"\n    ).strip()\n\n    try:\n        slicer = GloveSlicer(glove_path=glove_path or None)\n        slicer.index_nodes(id_to_node)\n        return slicer\n    except Exception as error:\n        print(f\"Could not load GloVe ({error}). Using plain generation.\")\n        return None\n\n\ndef main():\n    dataset_file = input(\"Dataset filename: \").strip()\n\n    dataset_text = clean_text(load_text_file(dataset_file))\n\n    print(\"Building graph from the complete dataset...\")\n    graph, node_to_id, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\n        dataset_text,\n        max_nodes=150000,\n    )\n\n    if not graph:\n        print(\"Graph is empty. Check the dataset.\")\n        return\n\n    print(f\"Graph built with {len(graph)} unique nodes.\")\n\n    print(\"Running PCMMaxCut solver for structural baseline...\")\n\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\n        graph,\n        noise=0.00001,\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\n    )\n\n    history = solver.run(\n        iterations=5000,\n        temperature=0.0000005,\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\n    )\n\n    best_cut = max(\n        history,\n        key=lambda item: item[\"cut\"],\n    )\n\n    print(\n        f\"Base partition created. \"\n        f\"Max Cut Size: {best_cut['cut']}\\n\"\n    )\n\n    spins = best_cut[\"spins\"]\n    clean_to_raw = dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node)\n    slicer = load_slicer(id_to_node)\n\n    # gamma: squeeze strength (>1 sharper, <1 flatter)\n    # zipf_s: how top-heavy the made-up anchor frequencies are\n    squeezer = ModalSqueezer(zipf_s=1.0, gamma=2.5, boost=50.0)\n\n    while True:\n        try:\n            user_prompt = input(\"USER: \").strip()\n        except (KeyboardInterrupt, EOFError):\n            print(\"\\nExiting.\")\n            break\n\n        if not user_prompt:\n            continue\n\n        if user_prompt.lower() in {\"exit\", \"quit\"}:\n            break\n\n        done = False\n\n        if slicer is not None:\n            done = glove_probe_and_generate(\n                user_prompt,\n                slicer,\n                graph,\n                id_to_node,\n                spins,\n                clean_to_raw,\n                squeezer,\n                width=2,\n                top_k=5,\n                length=60,\n                max_columns=4,\n            )\n\n        # Fall back to plain prompt-word biasing if GloVe is unavailable\n        # or knows none of the prompt words.\n        if not done:\n            plain_generate(user_prompt, graph, id_to_node, spins)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}, "message": "Full program with ModalSqueezer integrated", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"import math\\nimport random\\nimport re\\nimport textwrap\\nfrom collections import Counter\\nfrom itertools import zip_longest\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\\n\\n# gensim provides the GloVe vectors. If it is missing, the program falls\\n# back to plain prompt-word biasing on the full graph.\\ntry:\\n    from gensim.models import KeyedVectors\\n    import gensim.downloader as gensim_api\\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = True\\nexcept ImportError:\\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = False\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# ORIGINAL SOLVER KEPT EXACTLY THE SAME\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nclass PCMMaxCut:\\n    def __init__(self, graph, noise=0.02, drift_nu=0.08):\\n        self.graph = graph\\n        self.n = len(graph)\\n        self.noise = noise\\n        self.drift_nu = drift_nu\\n        self.spins = [random.choice([-1, 1]) for _ in range(self.n)]\\n        self.age = 1\\n\\n    def local_field(self, i):\\n        return sum(\\n            weight * self.spins[j]\\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items()\\n        )\\n\\n    def delta_energy(self, i):\\n        return -2 * self.spins[i] * self.local_field(i)\\n\\n    def energy(self):\\n        value = 0.0\\n        for i in range(self.n):\\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\\n                if j > i:\\n                    value += weight * self.spins[i] * self.spins[j]\\n        return value\\n\\n    def cut_size(self):\\n        total = 0\\n        for i in range(self.n):\\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\\n                if j > i and self.spins[i] != self.spins[j]:\\n                    total += weight\\n        return total\\n\\n    def pcm_flip_attempt(self, temperature):\\n        i = random.randrange(self.n)\\n        delta = self.delta_energy(i)\\n\\n        drift = self.age ** (-self.drift_nu)\\n        thermal_noise = random.gauss(\\n            0.0,\\n            self.noise\\n        ) * max(1.0, abs(self.local_field(i)))\\n\\n        effective_delta = delta + thermal_noise * drift\\n\\n        if effective_delta <= 0:\\n            accept = True\\n        else:\\n            accept = random.random() < math.exp(\\n                -effective_delta / max(temperature, 1e-9)\\n            )\\n\\n        if accept:\\n            self.spins[i] *= -1\\n            return i, True, delta\\n\\n        return i, False, delta\\n\\n    def run(self, iterations=1000, temperature=1.0, cooling=0.995):\\n        history = []\\n\\n        for _ in range(iterations):\\n            _, accepted, _ = self.pcm_flip_attempt(temperature)\\n\\n            temperature *= cooling\\n            self.age += 1\\n\\n            history.append({\\n                \\\"energy\\\": self.energy(),\\n                \\\"cut\\\": self.cut_size(),\\n                \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n                \\\"temperature\\\": temperature,\\n                \\\"spins\\\": self.spins[:],\\n            })\\n\\n        return history\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# TEXT HELPERS\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\\\"[a-z']+\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef clean_text(text):\\n    text = text.replace(\\\"\\\\x00\\\", \\\" \\\")\\n    text = re.sub(r\\\"\\\\s+\\\", \\\" \\\", text)\\n    return text.strip()\\n\\n\\ndef tokenize(text):\\n    return TOKEN_RE.findall(text.lower())\\n\\n\\ndef clean_word(word):\\n    return re.sub(r\\\"[^a-z']\\\", \\\"\\\", word.lower())\\n\\n\\ndef content_tokens(words):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Cleaned, non-stopword tokens.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    cleaned = (clean_word(w) for w in words)\\n    return [w for w in cleaned if w and w not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# MODAL SQUEEZER\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nclass ModalSqueezer:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Anchors (nearest GloVe words to a slice) get made-up Zipf frequencies.\\n    Every graph node is scored by its similarity to the anchors, weighted\\n    by those frequencies, then squeezed toward the mode with w**gamma.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, zipf_s=1.0, gamma=2.5, boost=50.0):\\n        self.zipf_s = zipf_s    # higher = first anchor dominates more\\n        self.gamma = gamma      # >1 sharpens toward the mode, <1 flattens\\n        self.boost = boost      # max multiplier, same role as the old 50.0\\n\\n    def synthetic_freqs(self, k):\\n        ranks = np.arange(1, k + 1, dtype=np.float32)\\n        f = 1.0 / ranks ** self.zipf_s\\n        return f / f.sum()\\n\\n    def node_weights(self, node_matrix, node_valid, anchor_vecs):\\n        n = node_matrix.shape[0]\\n        if len(anchor_vecs) == 0:\\n            return np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\\n\\n        freqs = self.synthetic_freqs(len(anchor_vecs))\\n        # cosine similarity (all vectors are unit length)\\n        sims = np.clip(node_matrix @ anchor_vecs.T, 0.0, None)\\n        sem = sims @ freqs                      # freq-weighted semantics\\n        sem[~node_valid] = 0.0\\n\\n        peak = sem.max()\\n        if peak <= 0:\\n            return np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\\n\\n        w = sem / peak\\n        return (w ** self.gamma).astype(np.float32)   # the modal squeeze\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# GLOVE PROMPT SLICER (probes the graph directly, no corpus segments)\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\nclass GloveSlicer:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Slices a prompt into word windows, embeds each slice with GloVe, and\\n    measures the Manhattan (L1) distance from the slice to every bigram\\n    node of the dataset graph. The nearest nodes are the peaks, which seed\\n    generation. Each slice also yields an ordered anchor list (slice words\\n    plus GloVe neighbours that exist in the dataset).\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, glove_name=\\\"glove-wiki-gigaword-100\\\", glove_path=None):\\n        if glove_path:\\n            print(f\\\"Loading GloVe from {glove_path}\\\")\\n            self.kv = KeyedVectors.load_word2vec_format(\\n                glove_path, binary=False, no_header=True\\n            )\\n        else:\\n            print(f\\\"Loading GloVe: {glove_name} (cached after first download)\\\")\\n            self.kv = gensim_api.load(glove_name)\\n\\n        self.dim = self.kv.vector_size\\n        self.node_matrix = None\\n        self.node_valid = None\\n\\n    # -- embedding -----------------------------------------------------\\n\\n    def embed(self, tokens):\\n        vecs = [self.kv[t] for t in tokens if t in self.kv]\\n        if not vecs:\\n            return None\\n        v = np.mean(vecs, axis=0)\\n        norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\\n        return (v / norm).astype(np.float32) if norm > 0 else None\\n\\n    def index_nodes(self, id_to_node):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Embed every bigram node (content words only).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        n = len(id_to_node)\\n        self.node_matrix = np.zeros((n, self.dim), dtype=np.float32)\\n        self.node_valid = np.zeros(n, dtype=bool)\\n\\n        for index, pair in id_to_node.items():\\n            vec = self.embed(content_tokens(pair))\\n            if vec is not None:\\n                self.node_matrix[index] = vec\\n                self.node_valid[index] = True\\n\\n        print(\\n            f\\\"Embedded {int(self.node_valid.sum())}/{n} graph nodes with GloVe.\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n    # -- slicing -------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n    def slice_prompt(self, prompt, width=2, stride=1):\\n        tokens = [t for t in tokenize(prompt) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\\n        if not tokens:\\n            tokens = tokenize(prompt)\\n\\n        if len(tokens) <= width:\\n            windows = [tokens]\\n        else:\\n            windows = [\\n                tokens[i:i + width]\\n                for i in range(0, len(tokens) - width + 1, stride)\\n            ]\\n\\n        slices = []\\n        for window in windows:\\n            vec = self.embed(window)\\n            if vec is not None:\\n                slices.append((window, vec))\\n        return slices\\n\\n    # -- Manhattan distance and peaks ----------------------------------\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def manhattan(a, b):\\n        return float(np.abs(a - b).sum())\\n\\n    def node_distances(self, slice_vec):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Manhattan distance from one slice to every node (inf if invalid).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if self.node_matrix is None:\\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"Call index_nodes() first.\\\")\\n\\n        distances = np.abs(self.node_matrix - slice_vec).sum(axis=1)\\n        distances[~self.node_valid] = np.inf\\n        return distances\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def find_peaks(distances, top_k=5, prominence=1.0):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        Peaks = the nodes whose distance sits at least `prominence`\\n        standard deviations below the mean, capped at top_k. Always\\n        returns at least the single nearest node.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        finite = np.isfinite(distances)\\n        if not finite.any():\\n            return []\\n\\n        mean = distances[finite].mean()\\n        std = distances[finite].std()\\n\\n        k = min(top_k, int(finite.sum()))\\n        nearest = np.argpartition(np.where(finite, distances, np.inf), k - 1)[:k]\\n        nearest = nearest[np.argsort(distances[nearest])]\\n\\n        if std == 0:\\n            return [int(nearest[0])]\\n\\n        peaks = [\\n            int(i) for i in nearest\\n            if (mean - distances[i]) / std >= prominence\\n        ]\\n\\n        return peaks or [int(nearest[0])]\\n\\n    # -- ordered anchors for the squeezer ------------------------------\\n\\n    def anchors(self, slice_tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Ordered anchors: slice words first, then nearest dataset neighbours.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        ordered = [t for t in slice_tokens if t in self.kv]\\n        limit = keep + len(ordered)\\n\\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(slice_vec, topn=topn):\\n            if (\\n                word in dataset_vocab\\n                and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\\n                and word not in ordered\\n            ):\\n                ordered.append(word)\\n            if len(ordered) >= limit:\\n                break\\n\\n        vecs = np.array(\\n            [self.kv.get_vector(w, norm=True) for w in ordered],\\n            dtype=np.float32,\\n        )\\n        return ordered, vecs\\n\\n\\ndef dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Graph nodes keep raw whitespace tokens (\\\"dog.\\\", \\\"fox,\\\"), so map each\\n    cleaned word to every raw form present in the graph.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    clean_to_raw = {}\\n    for pair in id_to_node.values():\\n        for raw in pair:\\n            clean_to_raw.setdefault(clean_word(raw), set()).add(raw.lower())\\n    return clean_to_raw\\n\\n\\ndef to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw):\\n    raw = set()\\n    for word in clean_vocab:\\n        raw.update(clean_to_raw.get(word, {word}))\\n    return raw\\n\\n\\ndef print_peak_table(slices, per_slice_distances, per_slice_peaks, id_to_node, max_rows=12):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Peak nodes down the side, one distance column per slice.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    best = {}\\n    for peaks, distances in zip(per_slice_peaks, per_slice_distances):\\n        for node in peaks:\\n            best[node] = min(best.get(node, np.inf), distances[node])\\n\\n    rows = sorted(best, key=lambda node: best[node])[:max_rows]\\n\\n    labels = [\\\" \\\".join(tokens)[:14] for tokens, _ in slices]\\n    col = 16\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nManhattan distance (peak node x slice)   * = peak for that slice\\\")\\n    print(\\\"node\\\".ljust(24) + \\\"\\\".join(label.ljust(col) for label in labels))\\n\\n    for node in rows:\\n        name = \\\" \\\".join(id_to_node[node])[:22]\\n        line = name.ljust(24)\\n        for peaks, distances in zip(per_slice_peaks, per_slice_distances):\\n            cell = f\\\"{distances[node]:.3f}\\\"\\n            if node in peaks:\\n                cell += \\\" *\\\"\\n            line += cell.ljust(col)\\n        print(line)\\n\\n\\ndef render_side_by_side(columns, total_width=118, gap=3):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"columns: list of (header, text). Prints them as parallel columns.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    n = len(columns)\\n    width = max(18, (total_width - gap * (n - 1)) // n)\\n    wrapped = [textwrap.wrap(text, width) for _, text in columns]\\n    sep = \\\" \\\" * gap\\n\\n    lines = [sep.join(header[:width].ljust(width) for header, _ in columns)]\\n    lines.append(sep.join(\\\"-\\\" * width for _ in columns))\\n    for parts in zip_longest(*wrapped, fillvalue=\\\"\\\"):\\n        lines.append(sep.join(part.ljust(width) for part in parts))\\n    return \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines)\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# GRAPH CREATION\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef process_text_to_trigram_graph(text, max_nodes=200):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Builds a graph where nodes are bigrams and edges represent trigrams.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    text = text.lower()\\n    words = text.split()\\n\\n    if len(words) < 3:\\n        return {}, {}, {}\\n\\n    all_bigrams = [\\n        (words[i], words[i + 1])\\n        for i in range(len(words) - 1)\\n    ]\\n\\n    top_bigrams = [\\n        bigram\\n        for bigram, _ in Counter(all_bigrams).most_common(max_nodes)\\n    ]\\n\\n    bigram_set = set(top_bigrams)\\n\\n    node_to_id = {\\n        bigram: index\\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\\n    }\\n\\n    id_to_node = {\\n        index: bigram\\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\\n    }\\n\\n    graph = {\\n        index: {}\\n        for index in range(len(top_bigrams))\\n    }\\n\\n    for i in range(len(words) - 2):\\n        b1 = (words[i], words[i + 1])\\n        b2 = (words[i + 1], words[i + 2])\\n\\n        if b1 in bigram_set and b2 in bigram_set:\\n            id1 = node_to_id[b1]\\n            id2 = node_to_id[b2]\\n\\n            if id1 != id2:\\n                graph[id1][id2] = graph[id1].get(id2, 0) + 1\\n                graph[id2][id1] = graph[id2].get(id1, 0) + 1\\n\\n    return graph, node_to_id, id_to_node\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# PROMPT-AWARE MARKOV GENERATOR\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef generate_markovian_prompt_text(\\n    graph,\\n    id_to_node,\\n    spins,\\n    prompt_vocab,\\n    length=100,\\n    node_weights=None,\\n    boost=50.0,\\n):\\n    n = len(graph)\\n\\n    if n == 0:\\n        return \\\"\\\"\\n\\n    prompt_vocab = {\\n        word.lower()\\n        for word in prompt_vocab\\n        if word.strip()\\n    }\\n\\n    use_semantic = node_weights is not None and node_weights.sum() > 0\\n\\n    # Start node: sample by semantic weight instead of a hard word match.\\n    if use_semantic:\\n        current_node = random.choices(\\n            range(n),\\n            weights=node_weights + 1e-6,\\n            k=1,\\n        )[0]\\n    else:\\n        valid_starts = [\\n            i\\n            for i in range(n)\\n            if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in id_to_node[i])\\n        ]\\n        current_node = (\\n            random.choice(valid_starts)\\n            if valid_starts\\n            else random.randrange(n)\\n        )\\n\\n    output = list(id_to_node[current_node])\\n\\n    for _ in range(max(0, length - 2)):\\n        current_spin = spins[current_node]\\n        neighbors = graph[current_node]\\n        current_word_2 = id_to_node[current_node][1]\\n\\n        valid_neighbors = [\\n            neighbor\\n            for neighbor in neighbors\\n            if id_to_node[neighbor][0] == current_word_2\\n        ]\\n\\n        if not valid_neighbors:\\n            fallback_nodes = [\\n                i\\n                for i, spin in enumerate(spins)\\n                if (\\n                    spin != current_spin\\n                    and id_to_node[i][0] == current_word_2\\n                )\\n            ]\\n\\n            if fallback_nodes:\\n                next_node = random.choice(fallback_nodes)\\n            else:\\n                next_node = random.randrange(n)\\n        else:\\n            probabilities = []\\n\\n            for neighbor in valid_neighbors:\\n                base_weight = graph[current_node][neighbor]\\n\\n                cut_multiplier = (\\n                    5.0\\n                    if spins[neighbor] != current_spin\\n                    else 1.0\\n                )\\n\\n                if use_semantic:\\n                    prompt_multiplier = 1.0 + boost * float(node_weights[neighbor])\\n                else:\\n                    neighbor_words = id_to_node[neighbor]\\n                    prompt_multiplier = (\\n                        50.0\\n                        if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in neighbor_words)\\n                        else 1.0\\n                    )\\n\\n                score = (\\n                    base_weight\\n                    * cut_multiplier\\n                    * prompt_multiplier\\n                )\\n\\n                probabilities.append(score)\\n\\n            next_node = random.choices(\\n                valid_neighbors,\\n                weights=probabilities,\\n                k=1,\\n            )[0]\\n\\n        output.append(id_to_node[next_node][1])\\n        current_node = next_node\\n\\n    return \\\" \\\".join(output)\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# GLOVE PROBE + SIDE-BY-SIDE GENERATION\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef glove_probe_and_generate(\\n    prompt,\\n    slicer,\\n    graph,\\n    id_to_node,\\n    spins,\\n    clean_to_raw,\\n    squeezer,\\n    width=2,\\n    top_k=5,\\n    length=60,\\n    max_columns=4,\\n):\\n    slices = slicer.slice_prompt(prompt, width=width)\\n\\n    if not slices:\\n        print(\\\"GloVe knows none of the prompt words; no slices to probe.\\\")\\n        return False\\n\\n    # Keep the output readable: cap the number of side-by-side columns.\\n    if len(slices) > max_columns:\\n        step = len(slices) / max_columns\\n        slices = [slices[int(i * step)] for i in range(max_columns)]\\n\\n    per_slice_distances = [slicer.node_distances(vec) for _, vec in slices]\\n    per_slice_peaks = [\\n        slicer.find_peaks(d, top_k=top_k) for d in per_slice_distances\\n    ]\\n\\n    if not any(per_slice_peaks):\\n        print(\\\"No usable peaks found.\\\")\\n        return False\\n\\n    print_peak_table(\\n        slices, per_slice_distances, per_slice_peaks, id_to_node\\n    )\\n\\n    dataset_vocab = set(clean_to_raw)\\n\\n    columns = []\\n    for (tokens, slice_vec), peaks in zip(slices, per_slice_peaks):\\n        anchor_words, anchor_vecs = slicer.anchors(\\n            tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab\\n        )\\n\\n        weights = squeezer.node_weights(\\n            slicer.node_matrix, slicer.node_valid, anchor_vecs\\n        )\\n\\n        # Peak nodes are the strongest anchors: pin them to full weight.\\n        for node in peaks:\\n            weights[node] = 1.0\\n\\n        raw_vocab = to_raw_vocab(set(anchor_words), clean_to_raw)\\n        for node in peaks:\\n            raw_vocab.update(id_to_node[node])\\n\\n        text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\\n            graph,\\n            id_to_node,\\n            spins,\\n            raw_vocab,\\n            length=length,\\n            node_weights=weights,\\n            boost=squeezer.boost,\\n        )\\n\\n        header = (\\n            f\\\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] \\\"\\n            f\\\"{len(anchor_words)} anchors g={squeezer.gamma}\\\"\\n        )\\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \\\".\\\"))\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nGenerated Output (one column per prompt slice):\\\\n\\\")\\n    print(render_side_by_side(columns))\\n    print()\\n    return True\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# PLAIN FALLBACK (no GloVe)\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef plain_generate(prompt, graph, id_to_node, spins):\\n    final_text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\\n        graph,\\n        id_to_node,\\n        spins,\\n        prompt.split(),\\n        length=400,\\n    )\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\nGenerated Output:\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"> {final_text.capitalize()}.\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# MAIN PROGRAM\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef load_text_file(filepath):\\n    try:\\n        with open(filepath, \\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as file:\\n            return file.read()\\n    except FileNotFoundError:\\n        print(f\\\"File {filepath} not found. Using fallback text.\\\")\\n\\n        return (\\n            \\\"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. \\\"\\n            \\\"The lazy dog barks at the brown fox. \\\"\\n            \\\"The quick brown fox runs away quickly into the deep \\\"\\n            \\\"dark brown forest. The dark forest is full of mystery. \\\"\\n            \\\"A dog barks loudly in the dark.\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n\\ndef load_slicer(id_to_node):\\n    if not GENSIM_AVAILABLE:\\n        print(\\\"gensim not installed (pip install gensim). Using plain generation.\\\")\\n        return None\\n\\n    glove_path = input(\\n        \\\"Local GloVe .txt path (blank = download glove-wiki-gigaword-100): \\\"\\n    ).strip()\\n\\n    try:\\n        slicer = GloveSlicer(glove_path=glove_path or None)\\n        slicer.index_nodes(id_to_node)\\n        return slicer\\n    except Exception as error:\\n        print(f\\\"Could not load GloVe ({error}). Using plain generation.\\\")\\n        return None\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    dataset_file = input(\\\"Dataset filename: \\\").strip()\\n\\n    dataset_text = clean_text(load_text_file(dataset_file))\\n\\n    print(\\\"Building graph from the complete dataset...\\\")\\n    graph, node_to_id, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\\n        dataset_text,\\n        max_nodes=150000,\\n    )\\n\\n    if not graph:\\n        print(\\\"Graph is empty. Check the dataset.\\\")\\n        return\\n\\n    print(f\\\"Graph built with {len(graph)} unique nodes.\\\")\\n\\n    print(\\\"Running PCMMaxCut solver for structural baseline...\\\")\\n\\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\\n        graph,\\n        noise=0.00001,\\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\\n    )\\n\\n    history = solver.run(\\n        iterations=5000,\\n        temperature=0.0000005,\\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\\n    )\\n\\n    best_cut = max(\\n        history,\\n        key=lambda item: item[\\\"cut\\\"],\\n    )\\n\\n    print(\\n        f\\\"Base partition created. \\\"\\n        f\\\"Max Cut Size: {best_cut['cut']}\\\\n\\\"\\n    )\\n\\n    spins = best_cut[\\\"spins\\\"]\\n    clean_to_raw = dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node)\\n    slicer = load_slicer(id_to_node)\\n\\n    # gamma: squeeze strength (>1 sharper, <1 flatter)\\n    # zipf_s: how top-heavy the made-up anchor frequencies are\\n    squeezer = ModalSqueezer(zipf_s=1.0, gamma=2.5, boost=50.0)\\n\\n    while True:\\n        try:\\n            user_prompt = input(\\\"USER: \\\").strip()\\n        except (KeyboardInterrupt, EOFError):\\n            print(\\\"\\\\nExiting.\\\")\\n            break\\n\\n        if not user_prompt:\\n            continue\\n\\n        if user_prompt.lower() in {\\\"exit\\\", \\\"quit\\\"}:\\n            break\\n\\n        done = False\\n\\n        if slicer is not None:\\n            done = glove_probe_and_generate(\\n                user_prompt,\\n                slicer,\\n                graph,\\n                id_to_node,\\n                spins,\\n                clean_to_raw,\\n                squeezer,\\n                width=2,\\n                top_k=5,\\n                length=60,\\n                max_columns=4,\\n            )\\n\\n        # Fall back to plain prompt-word biasing if GloVe is unavailable\\n        # or knows none of the prompt words.\\n        if not done:\\n            plain_generate(user_prompt, graph, id_to_node, spins)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\n\", \"filename\": \"/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_squeezer.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:28.096526Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:28.096554Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01XpgBYe3vCgNHYy7cMRg5ik", "name": "create_file", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_squeezer.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_squeezer.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:29.897861Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:30.149852Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01NWPZJmnEDpeho8RpqP5Boj", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_squeezer.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_squeezer.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:30.171473Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:30.171496Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01NWPZJmnEDpeho8RpqP5Boj", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/pcm_squeezer.py", "name": "pcm squeezer", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:32.974575Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:36:32.987771Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "The full program is above, with `PCMMaxCut` left untouched and the squeezer wired in. I haven't run it. If GloVe is missing or knows none of the prompt words, it falls back to the original plain prompt-word biasing.\n\nTo tune it, edit the `ModalSqueezer(zipf_s=1.0, gamma=2.5, boost=50.0)` line in `main()`:\n- **`gamma`:** at 3 to 4 the output gets repetitive and tightly on-topic. At 1 or below it drifts back toward the plain Markov chain.\n- **`zipf_s`:** a higher value makes the first anchor, usually your literal prompt word, dominate more.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:36:33.069436Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:36:33.069436Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fec2-50ec-70c8-b0f6-aa77019d28c2"}, {"uuid": "01a0feca-cf2e-74a6-b721-ab18717d7e6d", "text": "so what would happen if i sort the vocab, put it in a set,use sorted(log(exp())) with the freqs to describe perfect output, why? what to add?", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:45:01.008060Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:45:01.008060Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "so what would happen if i sort the vocab, put it in a set,use sorted(log(exp())) with the freqs to describe perfect output, why? what to add?", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:45:01.008700Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:45:01.008700Z", "attachments": [{"file_name": "", "file_size": 22701, "file_type": "txt", "extracted_content": "import math\nimport random\nimport re\nimport textwrap\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom itertools import zip_longest\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\n\n# gensim provides the GloVe vectors. If it is missing, the program falls\n# back to plain prompt-word biasing on the full graph.\ntry:\n    from gensim.models import KeyedVectors\n    import gensim.downloader as gensim_api\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    GENSIM_AVAILABLE = False\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# ORIGINAL SOLVER KEPT EXACTLY THE SAME\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass PCMMaxCut:\n    def __init__(self, graph, noise=0.02, drift_nu=0.08):\n        self.graph = graph\n        self.n = len(graph)\n        self.noise = noise\n        self.drift_nu = drift_nu\n        self.spins = [random.choice([-1, 1]) for _ in range(self.n)]\n        self.age = 1\n\n    def local_field(self, i):\n        return sum(\n            weight * self.spins[j]\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items()\n        )\n\n    def delta_energy(self, i):\n        return -2 * self.spins[i] * self.local_field(i)\n\n    def energy(self):\n        value = 0.0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i:\n                    value += weight * self.spins[i] * self.spins[j]\n        return value\n\n    def cut_size(self):\n        total = 0\n        for i in range(self.n):\n            for j, weight in self.graph[i].items():\n                if j > i and self.spins[i] != self.spins[j]:\n                    total += weight\n        return total\n\n    def pcm_flip_attempt(self, temperature):\n        i = random.randrange(self.n)\n        delta = self.delta_energy(i)\n\n        drift = self.age ** (-self.drift_nu)\n        thermal_noise = random.gauss(\n            0.0,\n            self.noise\n        ) * max(1.0, abs(self.local_field(i)))\n\n        effective_delta = delta + thermal_noise * drift\n\n        if effective_delta <= 0:\n            accept = True\n        else:\n            accept = random.random() < math.exp(\n                -effective_delta / max(temperature, 1e-9)\n            )\n\n        if accept:\n            self.spins[i] *= -1\n            return i, True, delta\n\n        return i, False, delta\n\n    def run(self, iterations=1000, temperature=1.0, cooling=0.995):\n        history = []\n\n        for _ in range(iterations):\n            _, accepted, _ = self.pcm_flip_attempt(temperature)\n\n            temperature *= cooling\n            self.age += 1\n\n            history.append({\n                \"energy\": self.energy(),\n                \"cut\": self.cut_size(),\n                \"accepted\": accepted,\n                \"temperature\": temperature,\n                \"spins\": self.spins[:],\n            })\n\n        return history\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# TEXT HELPERS\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[a-z']+\")\n\n\ndef clean_text(text):\n    text = text.replace(\"\\x00\", \" \")\n    text = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", text)\n    return text.strip()\n\n\ndef tokenize(text):\n    return TOKEN_RE.findall(text.lower())\n\n\ndef clean_word(word):\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z']\", \"\", word.lower())\n\n\ndef content_tokens(words):\n    \"\"\"Cleaned, non-stopword tokens.\"\"\"\n    cleaned = (clean_word(w) for w in words)\n    return [w for w in cleaned if w and w not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# MODAL SQUEEZER\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass ModalSqueezer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Anchors (nearest GloVe words to a slice) get made-up Zipf frequencies.\n    Every graph node is scored by its similarity to the anchors, weighted\n    by those frequencies, then squeezed toward the mode with w**gamma.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, zipf_s=1.0, gamma=2.5, boost=50.0):\n        self.zipf_s = zipf_s    # higher = first anchor dominates more\n        self.gamma = gamma      # >1 sharpens toward the mode, <1 flattens\n        self.boost = boost      # max multiplier, same role as the old 50.0\n\n    def synthetic_freqs(self, k):\n        ranks = np.arange(1, k + 1, dtype=np.float32)\n        f = 1.0 / ranks ** self.zipf_s\n        return f / f.sum()\n\n    def node_weights(self, node_matrix, node_valid, anchor_vecs):\n        n = node_matrix.shape[0]\n        if len(anchor_vecs) == 0:\n            return np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n\n        freqs = self.synthetic_freqs(len(anchor_vecs))\n        # cosine similarity (all vectors are unit length)\n        sims = np.clip(node_matrix @ anchor_vecs.T, 0.0, None)\n        sem = sims @ freqs                      # freq-weighted semantics\n        sem[~node_valid] = 0.0\n\n        peak = sem.max()\n        if peak <= 0:\n            return np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n\n        w = sem / peak\n        return (w ** self.gamma).astype(np.float32)   # the modal squeeze\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GLOVE PROMPT SLICER (probes the graph directly, no corpus segments)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass GloveSlicer:\n    \"\"\"\n    Slices a prompt into word windows, embeds each slice with GloVe, and\n    measures the Manhattan (L1) distance from the slice to every bigram\n    node of the dataset graph. The nearest nodes are the peaks, which seed\n    generation. Each slice also yields an ordered anchor list (slice words\n    plus GloVe neighbours that exist in the dataset).\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, glove_name=\"glove-wiki-gigaword-100\", glove_path=None):\n        if glove_path:\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe from {glove_path}\")\n            self.kv = KeyedVectors.load_word2vec_format(\n                glove_path, binary=False, no_header=True\n            )\n        else:\n            print(f\"Loading GloVe: {glove_name} (cached after first download)\")\n            self.kv = gensim_api.load(glove_name)\n\n        self.dim = self.kv.vector_size\n        self.node_matrix = None\n        self.node_valid = None\n\n    # -- embedding -----------------------------------------------------\n\n    def embed(self, tokens):\n        vecs = [self.kv[t] for t in tokens if t in self.kv]\n        if not vecs:\n            return None\n        v = np.mean(vecs, axis=0)\n        norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n        return (v / norm).astype(np.float32) if norm > 0 else None\n\n    def index_nodes(self, id_to_node):\n        \"\"\"Embed every bigram node (content words only).\"\"\"\n        n = len(id_to_node)\n        self.node_matrix = np.zeros((n, self.dim), dtype=np.float32)\n        self.node_valid = np.zeros(n, dtype=bool)\n\n        for index, pair in id_to_node.items():\n            vec = self.embed(content_tokens(pair))\n            if vec is not None:\n                self.node_matrix[index] = vec\n                self.node_valid[index] = True\n\n        print(\n            f\"Embedded {int(self.node_valid.sum())}/{n} graph nodes with GloVe.\"\n        )\n\n    # -- slicing -------------------------------------------------------\n\n    def slice_prompt(self, prompt, width=2, stride=1):\n        tokens = [t for t in tokenize(prompt) if t not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS]\n        if not tokens:\n            tokens = tokenize(prompt)\n\n        if len(tokens) <= width:\n            windows = [tokens]\n        else:\n            windows = [\n                tokens[i:i + width]\n                for i in range(0, len(tokens) - width + 1, stride)\n            ]\n\n        slices = []\n        for window in windows:\n            vec = self.embed(window)\n            if vec is not None:\n                slices.append((window, vec))\n        return slices\n\n    # -- Manhattan distance and peaks ----------------------------------\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def manhattan(a, b):\n        return float(np.abs(a - b).sum())\n\n    def node_distances(self, slice_vec):\n        \"\"\"Manhattan distance from one slice to every node (inf if invalid).\"\"\"\n        if self.node_matrix is None:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Call index_nodes() first.\")\n\n        distances = np.abs(self.node_matrix - slice_vec).sum(axis=1)\n        distances[~self.node_valid] = np.inf\n        return distances\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def find_peaks(distances, top_k=5, prominence=1.0):\n        \"\"\"\n        Peaks = the nodes whose distance sits at least `prominence`\n        standard deviations below the mean, capped at top_k. Always\n        returns at least the single nearest node.\n        \"\"\"\n        finite = np.isfinite(distances)\n        if not finite.any():\n            return []\n\n        mean = distances[finite].mean()\n        std = distances[finite].std()\n\n        k = min(top_k, int(finite.sum()))\n        nearest = np.argpartition(np.where(finite, distances, np.inf), k - 1)[:k]\n        nearest = nearest[np.argsort(distances[nearest])]\n\n        if std == 0:\n            return [int(nearest[0])]\n\n        peaks = [\n            int(i) for i in nearest\n            if (mean - distances[i]) / std >= prominence\n        ]\n\n        return peaks or [int(nearest[0])]\n\n    # -- ordered anchors for the squeezer ------------------------------\n\n    def anchors(self, slice_tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab, topn=80, keep=8):\n        \"\"\"Ordered anchors: slice words first, then nearest dataset neighbours.\"\"\"\n        ordered = [t for t in slice_tokens if t in self.kv]\n        limit = keep + len(ordered)\n\n        for word, _ in self.kv.similar_by_vector(slice_vec, topn=topn):\n            if (\n                word in dataset_vocab\n                and word not in ENGLISH_STOP_WORDS\n                and word not in ordered\n            ):\n                ordered.append(word)\n            if len(ordered) >= limit:\n                break\n\n        vecs = np.array(\n            [self.kv.get_vector(w, norm=True) for w in ordered],\n            dtype=np.float32,\n        )\n        return ordered, vecs\n\n\ndef dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node):\n    \"\"\"\n    Graph nodes keep raw whitespace tokens (\"dog.\", \"fox,\"), so map each\n    cleaned word to every raw form present in the graph.\n    \"\"\"\n    clean_to_raw = {}\n    for pair in id_to_node.values():\n        for raw in pair:\n            clean_to_raw.setdefault(clean_word(raw), set()).add(raw.lower())\n    return clean_to_raw\n\n\ndef to_raw_vocab(clean_vocab, clean_to_raw):\n    raw = set()\n    for word in clean_vocab:\n        raw.update(clean_to_raw.get(word, {word}))\n    return raw\n\n\ndef print_peak_table(slices, per_slice_distances, per_slice_peaks, id_to_node, max_rows=12):\n    \"\"\"Peak nodes down the side, one distance column per slice.\"\"\"\n    best = {}\n    for peaks, distances in zip(per_slice_peaks, per_slice_distances):\n        for node in peaks:\n            best[node] = min(best.get(node, np.inf), distances[node])\n\n    rows = sorted(best, key=lambda node: best[node])[:max_rows]\n\n    labels = [\" \".join(tokens)[:14] for tokens, _ in slices]\n    col = 16\n    print(\"\\nManhattan distance (peak node x slice)   * = peak for that slice\")\n    print(\"node\".ljust(24) + \"\".join(label.ljust(col) for label in labels))\n\n    for node in rows:\n        name = \" \".join(id_to_node[node])[:22]\n        line = name.ljust(24)\n        for peaks, distances in zip(per_slice_peaks, per_slice_distances):\n            cell = f\"{distances[node]:.3f}\"\n            if node in peaks:\n                cell += \" *\"\n            line += cell.ljust(col)\n        print(line)\n\n\ndef render_side_by_side(columns, total_width=118, gap=3):\n    \"\"\"columns: list of (header, text). Prints them as parallel columns.\"\"\"\n    n = len(columns)\n    width = max(18, (total_width - gap * (n - 1)) // n)\n    wrapped = [textwrap.wrap(text, width) for _, text in columns]\n    sep = \" \" * gap\n\n    lines = [sep.join(header[:width].ljust(width) for header, _ in columns)]\n    lines.append(sep.join(\"-\" * width for _ in columns))\n    for parts in zip_longest(*wrapped, fillvalue=\"\"):\n        lines.append(sep.join(part.ljust(width) for part in parts))\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GRAPH CREATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef process_text_to_trigram_graph(text, max_nodes=200):\n    \"\"\"\n    Builds a graph where nodes are bigrams and edges represent trigrams.\n    \"\"\"\n    text = text.lower()\n    words = text.split()\n\n    if len(words) < 3:\n        return {}, {}, {}\n\n    all_bigrams = [\n        (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        for i in range(len(words) - 1)\n    ]\n\n    top_bigrams = [\n        bigram\n        for bigram, _ in Counter(all_bigrams).most_common(max_nodes)\n    ]\n\n    bigram_set = set(top_bigrams)\n\n    node_to_id = {\n        bigram: index\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    id_to_node = {\n        index: bigram\n        for index, bigram in enumerate(top_bigrams)\n    }\n\n    graph = {\n        index: {}\n        for index in range(len(top_bigrams))\n    }\n\n    for i in range(len(words) - 2):\n        b1 = (words[i], words[i + 1])\n        b2 = (words[i + 1], words[i + 2])\n\n        if b1 in bigram_set and b2 in bigram_set:\n            id1 = node_to_id[b1]\n            id2 = node_to_id[b2]\n\n            if id1 != id2:\n                graph[id1][id2] = graph[id1].get(id2, 0) + 1\n                graph[id2][id1] = graph[id2].get(id1, 0) + 1\n\n    return graph, node_to_id, id_to_node\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PROMPT-AWARE MARKOV GENERATOR\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n    graph,\n    id_to_node,\n    spins,\n    prompt_vocab,\n    length=100,\n    node_weights=None,\n    boost=50.0,\n):\n    n = len(graph)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return \"\"\n\n    prompt_vocab = {\n        word.lower()\n        for word in prompt_vocab\n        if word.strip()\n    }\n\n    use_semantic = node_weights is not None and node_weights.sum() > 0\n\n    # Start node: sample by semantic weight instead of a hard word match.\n    if use_semantic:\n        current_node = random.choices(\n            range(n),\n            weights=node_weights + 1e-6,\n            k=1,\n        )[0]\n    else:\n        valid_starts = [\n            i\n            for i in range(n)\n            if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in id_to_node[i])\n        ]\n        current_node = (\n            random.choice(valid_starts)\n            if valid_starts\n            else random.randrange(n)\n        )\n\n    output = list(id_to_node[current_node])\n\n    for _ in range(max(0, length - 2)):\n        current_spin = spins[current_node]\n        neighbors = graph[current_node]\n        current_word_2 = id_to_node[current_node][1]\n\n        valid_neighbors = [\n            neighbor\n            for neighbor in neighbors\n            if id_to_node[neighbor][0] == current_word_2\n        ]\n\n        if not valid_neighbors:\n            fallback_nodes = [\n                i\n                for i, spin in enumerate(spins)\n                if (\n                    spin != current_spin\n                    and id_to_node[i][0] == current_word_2\n                )\n            ]\n\n            if fallback_nodes:\n                next_node = random.choice(fallback_nodes)\n            else:\n                next_node = random.randrange(n)\n        else:\n            probabilities = []\n\n            for neighbor in valid_neighbors:\n                base_weight = graph[current_node][neighbor]\n\n                cut_multiplier = (\n                    5.0\n                    if spins[neighbor] != current_spin\n                    else 1.0\n                )\n\n                if use_semantic:\n                    prompt_multiplier = 1.0 + boost * float(node_weights[neighbor])\n                else:\n                    neighbor_words = id_to_node[neighbor]\n                    prompt_multiplier = (\n                        50.0\n                        if any(word in prompt_vocab for word in neighbor_words)\n                        else 1.0\n                    )\n\n                score = (\n                    base_weight\n                    * cut_multiplier\n                    * prompt_multiplier\n                )\n\n                probabilities.append(score)\n\n            next_node = random.choices(\n                valid_neighbors,\n                weights=probabilities,\n                k=1,\n            )[0]\n\n        output.append(id_to_node[next_node][1])\n        current_node = next_node\n\n    return \" \".join(output)\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# GLOVE PROBE + SIDE-BY-SIDE GENERATION\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef glove_probe_and_generate(\n    prompt,\n    slicer,\n    graph,\n    id_to_node,\n    spins,\n    clean_to_raw,\n    squeezer,\n    width=22,\n    top_k=5,\n    length=60,\n    max_columns=42,\n):\n    slices = slicer.slice_prompt(prompt, width=width)\n\n    if not slices:\n        print(\"GloVe knows none of the prompt words; no slices to probe.\")\n        return False\n\n    # Keep the output readable: cap the number of side-by-side columns.\n    if len(slices) > max_columns:\n        step = len(slices) / max_columns\n        slices = [slices[int(i * step)] for i in range(max_columns)]\n\n    per_slice_distances = [slicer.node_distances(vec) for _, vec in slices]\n    per_slice_peaks = [\n        slicer.find_peaks(d, top_k=top_k) for d in per_slice_distances\n    ]\n\n    if not any(per_slice_peaks):\n        print(\"No usable peaks found.\")\n        return False\n\n    print_peak_table(\n        slices, per_slice_distances, per_slice_peaks, id_to_node\n    )\n\n    dataset_vocab = set(clean_to_raw)\n\n    columns = []\n    for (tokens, slice_vec), peaks in zip(slices, per_slice_peaks):\n        anchor_words, anchor_vecs = slicer.anchors(\n            tokens, slice_vec, dataset_vocab\n        )\n\n        weights = squeezer.node_weights(\n            slicer.node_matrix, slicer.node_valid, anchor_vecs\n        )\n\n        # Peak nodes are the strongest anchors: pin them to full weight.\n        for node in peaks:\n            weights[node] = 1.0\n\n        raw_vocab = to_raw_vocab(set(anchor_words), clean_to_raw)\n        for node in peaks:\n            raw_vocab.update(id_to_node[node])\n\n        text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n            graph,\n            id_to_node,\n            spins,\n            raw_vocab,\n            length=length,\n            node_weights=weights,\n            boost=squeezer.boost,\n        )\n\n        header = (\n            f\"[{' '.join(tokens)}] \"\n            f\"{len(anchor_words)} anchors g={squeezer.gamma}\"\n        )\n        columns.append((header, text.capitalize() + \".\"))\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated Output (one column per prompt slice):\\n\")\n    print(render_side_by_side(columns))\n    print()\n    return True\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# PLAIN FALLBACK (no GloVe)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef plain_generate(prompt, graph, id_to_node, spins):\n    final_text = generate_markovian_prompt_text(\n        graph,\n        id_to_node,\n        spins,\n        prompt.split(),\n        length=400,\n    )\n\n    print(\"\\nGenerated Output:\")\n    print(f\"> {final_text.capitalize()}.\\n\")\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# MAIN PROGRAM\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef load_text_file(filepath):\n    try:\n        with open(filepath, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n            return file.read()\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f\"File {filepath} not found. Using fallback text.\")\n\n        return (\n            \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. \"\n            \"The lazy dog barks at the brown fox. \"\n            \"The quick brown fox runs away quickly into the deep \"\n            \"dark brown forest. The dark forest is full of mystery. \"\n            \"A dog barks loudly in the dark.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef load_slicer(id_to_node):\n    if not GENSIM_AVAILABLE:\n        print(\"gensim not installed (pip install gensim). Using plain generation.\")\n        return None\n\n    glove_path = input(\n        \"Local GloVe .txt path (blank = download glove-wiki-gigaword-100): \"\n    ).strip()\n\n    try:\n        slicer = GloveSlicer(glove_path=glove_path or None)\n        slicer.index_nodes(id_to_node)\n        return slicer\n    except Exception as error:\n        print(f\"Could not load GloVe ({error}). Using plain generation.\")\n        return None\n\n\ndef main():\n    dataset_file = input(\"Dataset filename: \").strip()\n\n    dataset_text = clean_text(load_text_file(dataset_file))\n\n    print(\"Building graph from the complete dataset...\")\n    graph, node_to_id, id_to_node = process_text_to_trigram_graph(\n        dataset_text,\n        max_nodes=150000,\n    )\n\n    if not graph:\n        print(\"Graph is empty. Check the dataset.\")\n        return\n\n    print(f\"Graph built with {len(graph)} unique nodes.\")\n\n    print(\"Running PCMMaxCut solver for structural baseline...\")\n\n    solver = PCMMaxCut(\n        graph,\n        noise=0.00001,\n        drift_nu=0.00000001,\n    )\n\n    history = solver.run(\n        iterations=5000,\n        temperature=0.0000005,\n        cooling=0.0000000199,\n    )\n\n    best_cut = max(\n        history,\n        key=lambda item: item[\"cut\"],\n    )\n\n    print(\n        f\"Base partition created. \"\n        f\"Max Cut Size: {best_cut['cut']}\\n\"\n    )\n\n    spins = best_cut[\"spins\"]\n    clean_to_raw = dataset_vocab_from_nodes(id_to_node)\n    slicer = load_slicer(id_to_node)\n\n    # gamma: squeeze strength (>1 sharper, <1 flatter)\n    # zipf_s: how top-heavy the made-up anchor frequencies are\n    squeezer = ModalSqueezer(zipf_s=1.0, gamma=2.5, boost=50.0)\n\n    while True:\n        try:\n            user_prompt = input(\"USER: \").strip()\n        except (KeyboardInterrupt, EOFError):\n            print(\"\\nExiting.\")\n            break\n\n        if not user_prompt:\n            continue\n\n        if user_prompt.lower() in {\"exit\", \"quit\"}:\n            break\n\n        done = False\n\n        if slicer is not None:\n            done = glove_probe_and_generate(\n                user_prompt,\n                slicer,\n                graph,\n                id_to_node,\n                spins,\n                clean_to_raw,\n                squeezer,\n                width=24,\n                top_k=5,\n                length=60,\n                max_columns=4,\n            )\n\n        # Fall back to plain prompt-word biasing if GloVe is unavailable\n        # or knows none of the prompt words.\n        if not done:\n            plain_generate(user_prompt, graph, id_to_node, spins)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}], "files": [{"file_uuid": "1f4a96a6-794c-4cf6-9c32-fcb225e7f12a", "file_name": ""}], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fec2-50ec-76b6-9abe-364f6dacb26a"}, {"uuid": "01a0feca-cf2e-7f15-9378-cba147cf86dc", "text": "Taken literally, that pipeline does nothing, but the instinct behind it points at something useful.\n\n**What literally happens**\n\n- **`log(exp(x))` is `x`.** `sorted(log(exp(freqs)))` equals `sorted(freqs)`. The only difference is numerical: `exp` overflows for large inputs, and underflowed values give `log(0) = -inf`.\n- **A set throws away the sort.** `set(sorted(vocab))` has no order, so the ranking is lost. You'd need a list or a dict (insertion-ordered) to keep it.\n- **Sorting alphabetically would break the Zipf idea.** Zipf frequencies only mean something if rank means relevance. Rank the anchors by GloVe similarity to the slice, not by spelling.\n\n**Why it's still a good instinct**\n\nYour score is a product: `base_weight * cut_multiplier * prompt_multiplier`. Products of weights are best handled in log space. `exp(log(x))` is useless on its own, but `softmax = exp(z - max(z)) / sum(...)` is the stable version of it, and that's the right way to turn made-up frequencies into a probability distribution. A temperature on the logits is also a cleaner squeeze than `w**gamma`.\n\n**What \"perfect output\" can mean**\n\nDefine a target word distribution `p*` over the sorted anchor vocab, then compare the generated text against it. That gives you two things:\n\n1. A score for how close a generation is to the target (KL divergence).\n2. A feedback signal while generating.\n\n```python\ndef target_dist(sims, zipf_s=1.0, temp=0.5):\n    order = np.argsort(-sims)                       # rank by relevance\n    logits = -zipf_s * np.log(np.arange(1, len(sims) + 1))\n    z = logits / temp\n    p = np.exp(z - z.max()); p /= p.sum()           # stable softmax\n    out = np.zeros_like(p); out[order] = p          # map rank back to word\n    return out\n\ndef kl(p_target, counts, eps=1e-9):\n    q = counts / max(counts.sum(), 1) + eps\n    return float(np.sum(p_target * (np.log(p_target + eps) - np.log(q))))\n```\n\nFor the feedback, keep running counts of anchor words emitted, and multiply each candidate's score by `exp(eta * (log p_target[w] - log q[w]))`. Words the output is under-using get boosted, and over-used ones get damped. This is multiplicative-weights, and it's why log space matters here. It also stops the high-`gamma` repetition problem, because a word that has hit its target share stops being favored.\n\n**What to add**\n\n- **Target-aware stepping:** the correction above, applied per candidate word inside the neighbor loop.\n- **Score logging:** print `kl(p_target, counts)` per column so you can tune `gamma`, `zipf_s`, and `temp` against a number instead of by eye.\n- **Log-space scoring:** compute `log(base) + log(cut) + log(prompt) + correction`, then softmax. It avoids overflow when `boost` or `gamma` get large.\n- **A caveat:** a target over word frequencies only controls the unigram mix. Grammar and flow still come from the bigram graph and the max-cut partition, so \"perfect\" here means \"on-topic with the right vocabulary balance\", not \"fluent\".\n\n**Two things in your pasted code**\n\n`glove_probe_and_generate` now has defaults `width=22, max_columns=42`, and `main()` passes `width=24`. A 24-word window averages the whole prompt into one blurry vector, so you'll get a single slice with weak peaks. If that wasn't deliberate, put `width=2` back.\n\nI can wire the target-aware correction into the full file if you'd like.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:45:00.902808Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:45:13.357857Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Reworking vocabulary handling with sorted sets and log frequencies."}, {"summary": "Designing a target word-frequency distribution to steer generation."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:45:13.357901Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:45:23.208227Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Taken literally, that pipeline does nothing, but the instinct behind it points at something useful.\n\n**What literally happens**\n\n- **`log(exp(x))` is `x`.** `sorted(log(exp(freqs)))` equals `sorted(freqs)`. The only difference is numerical: `exp` overflows for large inputs, and underflowed values give `log(0) = -inf`.\n- **A set throws away the sort.** `set(sorted(vocab))` has no order, so the ranking is lost. You'd need a list or a dict (insertion-ordered) to keep it.\n- **Sorting alphabetically would break the Zipf idea.** Zipf frequencies only mean something if rank means relevance. Rank the anchors by GloVe similarity to the slice, not by spelling.\n\n**Why it's still a good instinct**\n\nYour score is a product: `base_weight * cut_multiplier * prompt_multiplier`. Products of weights are best handled in log space. `exp(log(x))` is useless on its own, but `softmax = exp(z - max(z)) / sum(...)` is the stable version of it, and that's the right way to turn made-up frequencies into a probability distribution. A temperature on the logits is also a cleaner squeeze than `w**gamma`.\n\n**What \"perfect output\" can mean**\n\nDefine a target word distribution `p*` over the sorted anchor vocab, then compare the generated text against it. That gives you two things:\n\n1. A score for how close a generation is to the target (KL divergence).\n2. A feedback signal while generating.\n\n```python\ndef target_dist(sims, zipf_s=1.0, temp=0.5):\n    order = np.argsort(-sims)                       # rank by relevance\n    logits = -zipf_s * np.log(np.arange(1, len(sims) + 1))\n    z = logits / temp\n    p = np.exp(z - z.max()); p /= p.sum()           # stable softmax\n    out = np.zeros_like(p); out[order] = p          # map rank back to word\n    return out\n\ndef kl(p_target, counts, eps=1e-9):\n    q = counts / max(counts.sum(), 1) + eps\n    return float(np.sum(p_target * (np.log(p_target + eps) - np.log(q))))\n```\n\nFor the feedback, keep running counts of anchor words emitted, and multiply each candidate's score by `exp(eta * (log p_target[w] - log q[w]))`. Words the output is under-using get boosted, and over-used ones get damped. This is multiplicative-weights, and it's why log space matters here. It also stops the high-`gamma` repetition problem, because a word that has hit its target share stops being favored.\n\n**What to add**\n\n- **Target-aware stepping:** the correction above, applied per candidate word inside the neighbor loop.\n- **Score logging:** print `kl(p_target, counts)` per column so you can tune `gamma`, `zipf_s`, and `temp` against a number instead of by eye.\n- **Log-space scoring:** compute `log(base) + log(cut) + log(prompt) + correction`, then softmax. It avoids overflow when `boost` or `gamma` get large.\n- **A caveat:** a target over word frequencies only controls the unigram mix. Grammar and flow still come from the bigram graph and the max-cut partition, so \"perfect\" here means \"on-topic with the right vocabulary balance\", not \"fluent\".\n\n**Two things in your pasted code**\n\n`glove_probe_and_generate` now has defaults `width=22, max_columns=42`, and `main()` passes `width=24`. A 24-word window averages the whole prompt into one blurry vector, so you'll get a single slice with weak peaks. If that wasn't deliberate, put `width=2` back.\n\nI can wire the target-aware correction into the full file if you'd like.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:45:23.282334Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:45:23.282334Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0feca-cf2e-74a6-b721-ab18717d7e6d"}]},{"uuid": "26708f19-e54b-4878-8d45-a0f4eab0b007", "name": "Sorting vocabulary with logarithmic frequency scaling", "summary": "", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:48:23.586612Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:52:02.601907Z", "account": {"uuid": "8d7882cd-3e98-47cc-a6e7-61494a1ee4ac"}, "chat_messages": [{"uuid": "01a0fecd-ef47-78ed-abfe-0d43bf272c06", "text": "so what would happen if i sort the vocab, put it in a set,use sorted(log(exp())) with the freqs to describe perfect output, why? what to add?", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:48:25.454359Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:48:25.454359Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "so what would happen if i sort the vocab, put it in a set,use sorted(log(exp())) with the freqs to describe perfect output, why? what to add?", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:48:25.454550Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:48:25.454550Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000"}, {"uuid": "01a0fecd-ef47-7407-a2a5-34f042f5c9bf", "text": "I'm reading your question as \"build a reference distribution from the vocab and frequencies and call it the ideal output.\" If that's wrong, tell me what you're actually building.\n\n**What each step does**\n\n- **`set(vocab)`** removes duplicates but throws away order and counts. You can't recover frequencies from it, so keep a `Counter` alongside.\n- **`sorted(...)`** gives a deterministic order, which is useful for stable token IDs. Sorted alphabetically it carries no frequency information. To rank by frequency, use `sorted(counts, key=counts.get, reverse=True)`, which gives the Zipf-style ordering.\n- **`log(exp(x))`** is mathematically just `x`, so it does nothing useful. Numerically it's worse than nothing: `exp` overflows for x above about 709 in float64 and underflows for very negative x. If you meant log-probabilities, use `log(freq / total)`. If you meant normalizing scores, use `logsumexp`, which subtracts the max first.\n\n**Why it doesn't describe \"perfect output\"**\n\nFrequencies normalized into probabilities give the best *unigram* model. Its loss is the entropy of the token distribution. It has no context, so it predicts \"the\" just as readily after \"the\" as after anything else. That is the optimal context-free model, not perfect output.\n\n**What to add**\n\n1. **Normalization:** `p = count / total`, so the probabilities sum to 1.\n2. **Stable log-probs:** `logp = log(count) - log(total)`, or `scipy.special.logsumexp` if you start from raw scores.\n3. **Smoothing:** add-k or similar, so unseen tokens don't get log(0) = -inf.\n4. **Context:** condition on previous tokens (n-grams, or a trained model), which is where real quality comes from.\n5. **Special tokens:** `<unk>`, `<pad>`, BOS/EOS.\n6. **Evaluation:** held-out perplexity, since \"perfect\" only means something relative to a test set.\n7. **Tie-breaking:** sort by `(-count, token)` so equal-frequency tokens order reproducibly.\n\n```python\nfrom collections import Counter\nimport math\n\ncounts = Counter(tokens)\ntotal = sum(counts.values())\nvocab = sorted(counts, key=lambda t: (-counts[t], t))\nlogp = {t: math.log(counts[t] / total) for t in vocab}\nentropy = -sum(math.exp(lp) * lp for lp in logp.values())  # unigram loss floor\n```\n\nWhat is the end goal here (language model, tokenizer, evaluating outputs)? I can tailor the advice.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:48:25.449610Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:48:30.054684Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Untangling a puzzling question about sorting word frequencies."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:48:30.054737Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:48:36.076337Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I'm reading your question as \"build a reference distribution from the vocab and frequencies and call it the ideal output.\" If that's wrong, tell me what you're actually building.\n\n**What each step does**\n\n- **`set(vocab)`** removes duplicates but throws away order and counts. You can't recover frequencies from it, so keep a `Counter` alongside.\n- **`sorted(...)`** gives a deterministic order, which is useful for stable token IDs. Sorted alphabetically it carries no frequency information. To rank by frequency, use `sorted(counts, key=counts.get, reverse=True)`, which gives the Zipf-style ordering.\n- **`log(exp(x))`** is mathematically just `x`, so it does nothing useful. Numerically it's worse than nothing: `exp` overflows for x above about 709 in float64 and underflows for very negative x. If you meant log-probabilities, use `log(freq / total)`. If you meant normalizing scores, use `logsumexp`, which subtracts the max first.\n\n**Why it doesn't describe \"perfect output\"**\n\nFrequencies normalized into probabilities give the best *unigram* model. Its loss is the entropy of the token distribution. It has no context, so it predicts \"the\" just as readily after \"the\" as after anything else. That is the optimal context-free model, not perfect output.\n\n**What to add**\n\n1. **Normalization:** `p = count / total`, so the probabilities sum to 1.\n2. **Stable log-probs:** `logp = log(count) - log(total)`, or `scipy.special.logsumexp` if you start from raw scores.\n3. **Smoothing:** add-k or similar, so unseen tokens don't get log(0) = -inf.\n4. **Context:** condition on previous tokens (n-grams, or a trained model), which is where real quality comes from.\n5. **Special tokens:** `<unk>`, `<pad>`, BOS/EOS.\n6. **Evaluation:** held-out perplexity, since \"perfect\" only means something relative to a test set.\n7. **Tie-breaking:** sort by `(-count, token)` so equal-frequency tokens order reproducibly.\n\n```python\nfrom collections import Counter\nimport math\n\ncounts = Counter(tokens)\ntotal = sum(counts.values())\nvocab = sorted(counts, key=lambda t: (-counts[t], t))\nlogp = {t: math.log(counts[t] / total) for t in vocab}\nentropy = -sum(math.exp(lp) * lp for lp in logp.values())  # unigram loss floor\n```\n\nWhat is the end goal here (language model, tokenizer, evaluating outputs)? I can tailor the advice.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:48:36.089363Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:48:36.089363Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fecd-ef47-78ed-abfe-0d43bf272c06"}, {"uuid": "01a0fecf-e4a8-7bc6-8a58-08e8a4b44a03", "text": "how about keep the indexes then reverse the index list for summation encoding of the tensors, but keep the static order for markove reasoning", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:50:33.301576Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:50:33.301576Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "how about keep the indexes then reverse the index list for summation encoding of the tensors, but keep the static order for markove reasoning", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:50:33.301710Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:50:33.301710Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fecd-ef47-7407-a2a5-34f042f5c9bf"}, {"uuid": "01a0fecf-e4a8-7f6f-b2c3-859f0a5a46b6", "text": "Reversing the index list does nothing for a plain summation encoding, and that's actually fine for your plan.\n\n**Why reversal is a no-op for sums**\n\nAddition is commutative, so `sum(E[i] for i in ids)` equals `sum(E[i] for i in reversed(ids))`. The only difference is float rounding order, which is negligible. A sum or bag-of-words encoding is permutation-invariant by construction.\n\nIt only matters if the encoding is position-aware:\n- Weighted sums like `sum(w[pos] * E[i])`, where reversal flips which tokens get which weight.\n- Positional encodings added before summing.\n- Polynomial or rolling hashes, such as `h = h*B + id`.\n\nIf you want direction to matter in the encoding, add one of those. If you only want a bag of tokens, skip the reversal.\n\n**Keeping the static order for Markov reasoning**\n\nThis is right. Transition counts `P(x_t | x_{t-1})` depend on sequence order, so build them from the original order. Keep these separate:\n\n- **Vocab map** (`token -> id`): built once and never re-sorted or reversed, so ids stay stable everywhere.\n- **Sequence of ids**: the original order, used for transitions.\n- **Reversed sequence**: a view (`ids[::-1]`), not a mutation, used only where you want it.\n\nReversing a sequence isn't useless for Markov work. It gives you the backward chain, `P(x_{t-1} | x_t)`. You can count it directly from the reversed sequence, or derive it from the forward chain with the stationary distribution: `P_back(j|i) = \u03c0_j \u00b7 P(j\u2192i) / \u03c0_i`. Combining forward and backward gives you bidirectional context, which is how BERT-style models and forward-backward algorithms use it.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\nids = [vocab_id[t] for t in tokens]   # static order\nV = len(vocab_id)\n\n# forward transitions (static order)\nfwd = np.zeros((V, V))\nfor a, b in zip(ids, ids[1:]):\n    fwd[a, b] += 1\nfwd = (fwd + 1e-3) / (fwd + 1e-3).sum(1, keepdims=True)  # smoothed\n\n# backward transitions (reversed view)\nrev = ids[::-1]\nbwd = np.zeros((V, V))\nfor a, b in zip(rev, rev[1:]):\n    bwd[a, b] += 1\nbwd = (bwd + 1e-3) / (bwd + 1e-3).sum(1, keepdims=True)\n\n# order-invariant summary encoding (reversal irrelevant)\nbag = np.bincount(ids, minlength=V)\n```\n\nWhat is the sum encoding meant to feed into? If it's a model input and you want it to know order, I'd suggest a positional weighting rather than reversal.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:50:33.297298Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:50:38.146014Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Working out which index order applies to each encoding step."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:50:38.146039Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:50:44.492891Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Reversing the index list does nothing for a plain summation encoding, and that's actually fine for your plan.\n\n**Why reversal is a no-op for sums**\n\nAddition is commutative, so `sum(E[i] for i in ids)` equals `sum(E[i] for i in reversed(ids))`. The only difference is float rounding order, which is negligible. A sum or bag-of-words encoding is permutation-invariant by construction.\n\nIt only matters if the encoding is position-aware:\n- Weighted sums like `sum(w[pos] * E[i])`, where reversal flips which tokens get which weight.\n- Positional encodings added before summing.\n- Polynomial or rolling hashes, such as `h = h*B + id`.\n\nIf you want direction to matter in the encoding, add one of those. If you only want a bag of tokens, skip the reversal.\n\n**Keeping the static order for Markov reasoning**\n\nThis is right. Transition counts `P(x_t | x_{t-1})` depend on sequence order, so build them from the original order. Keep these separate:\n\n- **Vocab map** (`token -> id`): built once and never re-sorted or reversed, so ids stay stable everywhere.\n- **Sequence of ids**: the original order, used for transitions.\n- **Reversed sequence**: a view (`ids[::-1]`), not a mutation, used only where you want it.\n\nReversing a sequence isn't useless for Markov work. It gives you the backward chain, `P(x_{t-1} | x_t)`. You can count it directly from the reversed sequence, or derive it from the forward chain with the stationary distribution: `P_back(j|i) = \u03c0_j \u00b7 P(j\u2192i) / \u03c0_i`. Combining forward and backward gives you bidirectional context, which is how BERT-style models and forward-backward algorithms use it.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\nids = [vocab_id[t] for t in tokens]   # static order\nV = len(vocab_id)\n\n# forward transitions (static order)\nfwd = np.zeros((V, V))\nfor a, b in zip(ids, ids[1:]):\n    fwd[a, b] += 1\nfwd = (fwd + 1e-3) / (fwd + 1e-3).sum(1, keepdims=True)  # smoothed\n\n# backward transitions (reversed view)\nrev = ids[::-1]\nbwd = np.zeros((V, V))\nfor a, b in zip(rev, rev[1:]):\n    bwd[a, b] += 1\nbwd = (bwd + 1e-3) / (bwd + 1e-3).sum(1, keepdims=True)\n\n# order-invariant summary encoding (reversal irrelevant)\nbag = np.bincount(ids, minlength=V)\n```\n\nWhat is the sum encoding meant to feed into? If it's a model input and you want it to know order, I'd suggest a positional weighting rather than reversal.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:50:44.505988Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:50:44.505988Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fecf-e4a8-7bc6-8a58-08e8a4b44a03"}, {"uuid": "01a0fed0-4cf0-755c-a246-d7ab56acad97", "text": "do the full code, with txt dataset and generate text", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:00.035590Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:00.035590Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "do the full code, with txt dataset and generate text", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:51:00.035760Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:51:00.035760Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fecf-e4a8-7f6f-b2c3-859f0a5a46b6"}, {"uuid": "01a0fed0-4cf0-74e6-91a1-6b68e6066040", "text": "I'll build this as one script and run it on a sample text to check it works.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThe script is `markov_gen.py`. You need only numpy, and you run it with `python markov_gen.py yourfile.txt --order 2 --n 5 --seed-word the`.\n\nI ran it on a small synthetic text file, since I don't have your dataset. It trained and generated fine, but the output quality on real text is untested.\n\n**What it does**\n- **Vocab:** sorted by `(-count, token)` into stable ids, with `<pad>`, `<unk>`, `<bos>` and `<eos>`. The map is built once and never re-sorted.\n- **Static order:** the forward chain is trained on the original id sequences.\n- **Reversed view:** the backward chain is trained on `seq[::-1]` copies, so the originals stay untouched.\n- **Probabilities:** an interpolated n-gram with `--order` previous tokens (1 is a bigram Markov chain, 2 a trigram). It returns full normalized distributions with an add-k base, so nothing hits log(0).\n- **Encodings:** the bag-sum is identical when reversed, while the positional-decay version changes. The script checks both.\n- **Evaluation:** held-out perplexity for the forward and backward chains, plus the unigram entropy floor as the \"no context\" baseline.\n- **Generation:** forward from `<bos>`, plus \"around a seed word\", which generates leftwards with the backward chain and rightwards with the forward chain.\n\n**Things to know**\n- **Backward perplexity:** it matches the forward value only roughly on real data. A joint distribution can be factored in either direction, but each smoothed chain estimates it differently.\n- **Around-seed output:** it can be rough, because the two halves are sampled independently. On the toy data I saw things like \"morning morning light\" and a stray fragment after a period. Lower `--temp` (0.5 to 0.7) cleans most of that up.\n- **Speed:** each step builds a full vocab-sized vector, which is fine up to roughly 50k tokens. Beyond that, use sparse sampling over the observed next tokens only.\n- **Encoder:** the sum encoder uses random embeddings. It's a placeholder for whatever tensors you feed it.\n\nIs the summation encoding going into a trained model? If so, I can add a small PyTorch layer that uses it.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:00.028803Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:17.032625Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Building a Markov text generator with vocab and encoding tools."}, {"summary": "Designing n-gram models with smoothing and sampling logic."}, {"summary": "Interpolating backoff distributions for scoring and sampling."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:17.032658Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:17.466888Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I'll build this as one script and run it on a sample text to check it works.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:17.466898Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:37.832796Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Sj8TaAZs6uXVbBUr1yuhBk", "name": "create_file", "input": {"description": "Full Markov text generator script with vocab, forward/backward chains, sum encoding", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py", "file_text": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nMarkov text model from a .txt file.\n\n  - vocab: frequency-sorted ids, stable tie-break, special tokens\n  - forward chain (static order) + backward chain (reversed view)\n  - interpolated n-gram probabilities (proper distributions, add-k base)\n  - order-invariant sum encoding vs position-aware encoding\n  - held-out perplexity vs the unigram entropy floor\n  - generation: forward, backward, and \"around a seed word\"\n\nUsage:\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --order 2 --n 5 --seed-word \"the\"\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport math\nimport random\nimport re\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nPAD, UNK, BOS, EOS = \"<pad>\", \"<unk>\", \"<bos>\", \"<eos>\"\nSPECIALS = [PAD, UNK, BOS, EOS]\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[a-z0-9']+|[.,!?;:]\")\nSENT_SPLIT = re.compile(r\"(?<=[.!?])\\s+|\\n{2,}\")\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------- data\ndef load_sentences(path):\n    text = open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\").read().lower()\n    sents = []\n    for chunk in SENT_SPLIT.split(text):\n        toks = TOKEN_RE.findall(chunk)\n        if len(toks) >= 2:\n            sents.append(toks)\n    return sents\n\n\nclass Vocab:\n    \"\"\"token -> id built once; never re-sorted or reversed afterwards.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, sentences, min_count=1):\n        counts = Counter(t for s in sentences for t in s)\n        kept = [t for t, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count]\n        kept.sort(key=lambda t: (-counts[t], t))  # frequency, then alphabetical\n        self.itos = SPECIALS + kept\n        self.stoi = {t: i for i, t in enumerate(self.itos)}\n        self.V = len(self.itos)\n        self.pad, self.unk, self.bos, self.eos = (self.stoi[s] for s in SPECIALS)\n        # unigram counts over ids (specials get 0 here; handled in the model)\n        self.counts = np.zeros(self.V)\n        for t in kept:\n            self.counts[self.stoi[t]] = counts[t]\n\n    def encode(self, sent):\n        return [self.stoi.get(t, self.unk) for t in sent]\n\n    def decode(self, ids):\n        out = []\n        for i in ids:\n            if i in (self.pad, self.bos, self.eos):\n                continue\n            out.append(self.itos[i])\n        text = \" \".join(out)\n        return re.sub(r\"\\s+([.,!?;:])\", r\"\\1\", text)\n\n    def unigram_entropy(self):\n        p = self.counts[self.counts > 0]\n        p = p / p.sum()\n        return float(-(p * np.log(p)).sum())\n\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------------------- model\nclass NGram:\n    \"\"\"\n    Interpolated n-gram. `order` = number of previous tokens used.\n    order=1 is a classic Markov chain (bigram), order=2 is trigram, etc.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, vocab, order=2, lam=0.7, k=0.01):\n        self.v, self.order, self.lam, self.k = vocab, order, lam, k\n        # tables[n][ctx_tuple_of_len_n] -> Counter(next_id)\n        self.tables = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(order + 1)]\n\n    def fit(self, id_seqs):\n        for seq in id_seqs:\n            for t in range(1, len(seq)):\n                for n in range(0, self.order + 1):\n                    if t - n < 0:\n                        break\n                    self.tables[n][tuple(seq[t - n:t])][seq[t]] += 1\n        # base: add-k smoothed unigram over real tokens + eos\n        base = self.v.counts.copy()\n        base[self.v.eos] = len(id_seqs)\n        base = base + self.k\n        base[[self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]] = 0.0\n        self.base = base / base.sum()\n\n    def dist(self, ctx):\n        \"\"\"Full probability vector over the vocab given a context list.\"\"\"\n        p = self.base\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\n        for n in range(0, len(ctx) + 1):          # shortest -> longest context\n            c = self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:] if n else ())\n            if not c:\n                continue\n            vec = np.zeros(self.v.V)\n            for tok, cnt in c.items():\n                vec[tok] = cnt\n            vec /= vec.sum()\n            p = self.lam * vec + (1 - self.lam) * p\n        return p\n\n    def logprob(self, seq):\n        lp = 0.0\n        for t in range(1, len(seq)):\n            lp += math.log(self.dist(seq[:t])[seq[t]] + 1e-12)\n        return lp\n\n    def sample_next(self, ctx, temp=1.0, top_k=40, banned=()):\n        p = self.dist(ctx).copy()\n        for b in banned:\n            p[b] = 0.0\n        if top_k and top_k < len(p):\n            cut = np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]\n            p[p < cut] = 0.0\n        p = p ** (1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3))\n        s = p.sum()\n        if s == 0:\n            return self.v.eos\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / s))\n\n\ndef generate(model, start_ctx, stop_id, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\n    ctx, out = list(start_ctx), []\n    banned = (model.v.pad, model.v.bos, model.v.unk)\n    for _ in range(max_len):\n        nxt = model.sample_next(ctx, temp, top_k, banned)\n        if nxt == stop_id:\n            break\n        out.append(nxt)\n        ctx.append(nxt)\n    return out\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- encodings\nclass Encoder:\n    \"\"\"Sum encoding (order-invariant) vs positional-weighted (order-aware).\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, V, dim=16, decay=0.9, seed=0):\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        self.E = rng.normal(0, 1, (V, dim))\n        self.decay = decay\n\n    def bag_sum(self, ids):\n        return self.E[ids].sum(0)\n\n    def positional(self, ids):\n        w = self.decay ** np.arange(len(ids))\n        return (self.E[ids] * w[:, None]).sum(0)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------- main\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"path\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--order\", type=int, default=2)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--min-count\", type=int, default=1)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--n\", type=int, default=5, help=\"sentences to generate\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--temp\", type=float, default=0.9)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--top-k\", type=int, default=40)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seed-word\", default=None)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=42)\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    random.seed(args.seed)\n    np.random.seed(args.seed)\n\n    sents = load_sentences(args.path)\n    random.shuffle(sents)\n    split = max(1, int(0.9 * len(sents)))\n    train, test = sents[:split], sents[split:]\n\n    vocab = Vocab(train, args.min_count)\n    print(f\"sentences: {len(train)} train / {len(test)} test | vocab: {vocab.V}\")\n    print(\"top tokens:\", [vocab.itos[i] for i in range(4, min(14, vocab.V))])\n\n    def wrap(s):\n        return [vocab.bos] + vocab.encode(s) + [vocab.eos]\n\n    fwd_seqs = [wrap(s) for s in train]          # static order\n    bwd_seqs = [seq[::-1] for seq in fwd_seqs]   # reversed copy, originals untouched\n\n    fwd = NGram(vocab, args.order)\n    fwd.fit(fwd_seqs)\n    bwd = NGram(vocab, args.order)\n    bwd.fit(bwd_seqs)\n\n    # ---- encodings demo\n    enc = Encoder(vocab.V)\n    demo = vocab.encode(train[0])\n    same = np.allclose(enc.bag_sum(demo), enc.bag_sum(demo[::-1]))\n    diff = not np.allclose(enc.positional(demo), enc.positional(demo[::-1]))\n    print(f\"\\nbag-sum identical when reversed: {same}\")\n    print(f\"positional encoding differs when reversed: {diff}\")\n\n    # ---- evaluation\n    if test:\n        test_seqs = [wrap(s) for s in test]\n        n_tok = sum(len(s) - 1 for s in test_seqs)\n        f_ppl = math.exp(-sum(fwd.logprob(s) for s in test_seqs) / n_tok)\n        b_ppl = math.exp(-sum(bwd.logprob(s[::-1]) for s in test_seqs) / n_tok)\n        uni = math.exp(vocab.unigram_entropy())\n        print(f\"\\nheld-out perplexity  forward: {f_ppl:.1f} | backward: {b_ppl:.1f}\"\n              f\" | unigram floor (train entropy): {uni:.1f}\")\n\n    # ---- generation\n    print(\"\\n--- forward generation ---\")\n    for _ in range(args.n):\n        ids = generate(fwd, [vocab.bos], vocab.eos, temp=args.temp, top_k=args.top_k)\n        print(\" \", vocab.decode(ids))\n\n    seed_word = args.seed_word or vocab.itos[min(6, vocab.V - 1)]\n    sid = vocab.stoi.get(seed_word, vocab.unk)\n    print(f\"\\n--- around seed word: '{seed_word}' (backward + forward) ---\")\n    if sid == vocab.unk:\n        print(\"  seed word not in vocab\")\n    else:\n        for _ in range(args.n):\n            left = generate(bwd, [vocab.eos, sid], vocab.bos,\n                            temp=args.temp, top_k=args.top_k)\n            right = generate(fwd, [vocab.bos, sid], vocab.eos,\n                             temp=args.temp, top_k=args.top_k)\n            print(\" \", vocab.decode(left[::-1] + [sid] + right))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}, "message": "Full Markov text generator script with vocab, forward/backward chains, sum encoding", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nMarkov text model from a .txt file.\\n\\n  - vocab: frequency-sorted ids, stable tie-break, special tokens\\n  - forward chain (static order) + backward chain (reversed view)\\n  - interpolated n-gram probabilities (proper distributions, add-k base)\\n  - order-invariant sum encoding vs position-aware encoding\\n  - held-out perplexity vs the unigram entropy floor\\n  - generation: forward, backward, and \\\"around a seed word\\\"\\n\\nUsage:\\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --order 2 --n 5 --seed-word \\\"the\\\"\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport argparse\\nimport math\\nimport random\\nimport re\\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nPAD, UNK, BOS, EOS = \\\"<pad>\\\", \\\"<unk>\\\", \\\"<bos>\\\", \\\"<eos>\\\"\\nSPECIALS = [PAD, UNK, BOS, EOS]\\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\\\"[a-z0-9']+|[.,!?;:]\\\")\\nSENT_SPLIT = re.compile(r\\\"(?<=[.!?])\\\\s+|\\\\n{2,}\\\")\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------- data\\ndef load_sentences(path):\\n    text = open(path, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\").read().lower()\\n    sents = []\\n    for chunk in SENT_SPLIT.split(text):\\n        toks = TOKEN_RE.findall(chunk)\\n        if len(toks) >= 2:\\n            sents.append(toks)\\n    return sents\\n\\n\\nclass Vocab:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"token -> id built once; never re-sorted or reversed afterwards.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, sentences, min_count=1):\\n        counts = Counter(t for s in sentences for t in s)\\n        kept = [t for t, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count]\\n        kept.sort(key=lambda t: (-counts[t], t))  # frequency, then alphabetical\\n        self.itos = SPECIALS + kept\\n        self.stoi = {t: i for i, t in enumerate(self.itos)}\\n        self.V = len(self.itos)\\n        self.pad, self.unk, self.bos, self.eos = (self.stoi[s] for s in SPECIALS)\\n        # unigram counts over ids (specials get 0 here; handled in the model)\\n        self.counts = np.zeros(self.V)\\n        for t in kept:\\n            self.counts[self.stoi[t]] = counts[t]\\n\\n    def encode(self, sent):\\n        return [self.stoi.get(t, self.unk) for t in sent]\\n\\n    def decode(self, ids):\\n        out = []\\n        for i in ids:\\n            if i in (self.pad, self.bos, self.eos):\\n                continue\\n            out.append(self.itos[i])\\n        text = \\\" \\\".join(out)\\n        return re.sub(r\\\"\\\\s+([.,!?;:])\\\", r\\\"\\\\1\\\", text)\\n\\n    def unigram_entropy(self):\\n        p = self.counts[self.counts > 0]\\n        p = p / p.sum()\\n        return float(-(p * np.log(p)).sum())\\n\\n\\n# -------------------------------------------------------------------- model\\nclass NGram:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Interpolated n-gram. `order` = number of previous tokens used.\\n    order=1 is a classic Markov chain (bigram), order=2 is trigram, etc.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, vocab, order=2, lam=0.7, k=0.01):\\n        self.v, self.order, self.lam, self.k = vocab, order, lam, k\\n        # tables[n][ctx_tuple_of_len_n] -> Counter(next_id)\\n        self.tables = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(order + 1)]\\n\\n    def fit(self, id_seqs):\\n        for seq in id_seqs:\\n            for t in range(1, len(seq)):\\n                for n in range(0, self.order + 1):\\n                    if t - n < 0:\\n                        break\\n                    self.tables[n][tuple(seq[t - n:t])][seq[t]] += 1\\n        # base: add-k smoothed unigram over real tokens + eos\\n        base = self.v.counts.copy()\\n        base[self.v.eos] = len(id_seqs)\\n        base = base + self.k\\n        base[[self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]] = 0.0\\n        self.base = base / base.sum()\\n\\n    def dist(self, ctx):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Full probability vector over the vocab given a context list.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        p = self.base\\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\\n        for n in range(0, len(ctx) + 1):          # shortest -> longest context\\n            c = self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:] if n else ())\\n            if not c:\\n                continue\\n            vec = np.zeros(self.v.V)\\n            for tok, cnt in c.items():\\n                vec[tok] = cnt\\n            vec /= vec.sum()\\n            p = self.lam * vec + (1 - self.lam) * p\\n        return p\\n\\n    def logprob(self, seq):\\n        lp = 0.0\\n        for t in range(1, len(seq)):\\n            lp += math.log(self.dist(seq[:t])[seq[t]] + 1e-12)\\n        return lp\\n\\n    def sample_next(self, ctx, temp=1.0, top_k=40, banned=()):\\n        p = self.dist(ctx).copy()\\n        for b in banned:\\n            p[b] = 0.0\\n        if top_k and top_k < len(p):\\n            cut = np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]\\n            p[p < cut] = 0.0\\n        p = p ** (1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3))\\n        s = p.sum()\\n        if s == 0:\\n            return self.v.eos\\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / s))\\n\\n\\ndef generate(model, start_ctx, stop_id, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\\n    ctx, out = list(start_ctx), []\\n    banned = (model.v.pad, model.v.bos, model.v.unk)\\n    for _ in range(max_len):\\n        nxt = model.sample_next(ctx, temp, top_k, banned)\\n        if nxt == stop_id:\\n            break\\n        out.append(nxt)\\n        ctx.append(nxt)\\n    return out\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- encodings\\nclass Encoder:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Sum encoding (order-invariant) vs positional-weighted (order-aware).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, V, dim=16, decay=0.9, seed=0):\\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n        self.E = rng.normal(0, 1, (V, dim))\\n        self.decay = decay\\n\\n    def bag_sum(self, ids):\\n        return self.E[ids].sum(0)\\n\\n    def positional(self, ids):\\n        w = self.decay ** np.arange(len(ids))\\n        return (self.E[ids] * w[:, None]).sum(0)\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------- main\\ndef main():\\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"path\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--order\\\", type=int, default=2)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--min-count\\\", type=int, default=1)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--n\\\", type=int, default=5, help=\\\"sentences to generate\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--temp\\\", type=float, default=0.9)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--top-k\\\", type=int, default=40)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--seed-word\\\", default=None)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--seed\\\", type=int, default=42)\\n    args = ap.parse_args()\\n\\n    random.seed(args.seed)\\n    np.random.seed(args.seed)\\n\\n    sents = load_sentences(args.path)\\n    random.shuffle(sents)\\n    split = max(1, int(0.9 * len(sents)))\\n    train, test = sents[:split], sents[split:]\\n\\n    vocab = Vocab(train, args.min_count)\\n    print(f\\\"sentences: {len(train)} train / {len(test)} test | vocab: {vocab.V}\\\")\\n    print(\\\"top tokens:\\\", [vocab.itos[i] for i in range(4, min(14, vocab.V))])\\n\\n    def wrap(s):\\n        return [vocab.bos] + vocab.encode(s) + [vocab.eos]\\n\\n    fwd_seqs = [wrap(s) for s in train]          # static order\\n    bwd_seqs = [seq[::-1] for seq in fwd_seqs]   # reversed copy, originals untouched\\n\\n    fwd = NGram(vocab, args.order)\\n    fwd.fit(fwd_seqs)\\n    bwd = NGram(vocab, args.order)\\n    bwd.fit(bwd_seqs)\\n\\n    # ---- encodings demo\\n    enc = Encoder(vocab.V)\\n    demo = vocab.encode(train[0])\\n    same = np.allclose(enc.bag_sum(demo), enc.bag_sum(demo[::-1]))\\n    diff = not np.allclose(enc.positional(demo), enc.positional(demo[::-1]))\\n    print(f\\\"\\\\nbag-sum identical when reversed: {same}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"positional encoding differs when reversed: {diff}\\\")\\n\\n    # ---- evaluation\\n    if test:\\n        test_seqs = [wrap(s) for s in test]\\n        n_tok = sum(len(s) - 1 for s in test_seqs)\\n        f_ppl = math.exp(-sum(fwd.logprob(s) for s in test_seqs) / n_tok)\\n        b_ppl = math.exp(-sum(bwd.logprob(s[::-1]) for s in test_seqs) / n_tok)\\n        uni = math.exp(vocab.unigram_entropy())\\n        print(f\\\"\\\\nheld-out perplexity  forward: {f_ppl:.1f} | backward: {b_ppl:.1f}\\\"\\n              f\\\" | unigram floor (train entropy): {uni:.1f}\\\")\\n\\n    # ---- generation\\n    print(\\\"\\\\n--- forward generation ---\\\")\\n    for _ in range(args.n):\\n        ids = generate(fwd, [vocab.bos], vocab.eos, temp=args.temp, top_k=args.top_k)\\n        print(\\\" \\\", vocab.decode(ids))\\n\\n    seed_word = args.seed_word or vocab.itos[min(6, vocab.V - 1)]\\n    sid = vocab.stoi.get(seed_word, vocab.unk)\\n    print(f\\\"\\\\n--- around seed word: '{seed_word}' (backward + forward) ---\\\")\\n    if sid == vocab.unk:\\n        print(\\\"  seed word not in vocab\\\")\\n    else:\\n        for _ in range(args.n):\\n            left = generate(bwd, [vocab.eos, sid], vocab.bos,\\n                            temp=args.temp, top_k=args.top_k)\\n            right = generate(fwd, [vocab.bos, sid], vocab.eos,\\n                             temp=args.temp, top_k=args.top_k)\\n            print(\\\" \\\", vocab.decode(left[::-1] + [sid] + right))\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\n\", \"filename\": \"/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:39.394045Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:39.394075Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Sj8TaAZs6uXVbBUr1yuhBk", "name": "create_file", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:40.878615Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:43.342707Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01X11FGp1utKpNF6ku44NPGn", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport random\nrandom.seed(1)\nsubj=[\"the cat\",\"a dog\",\"the old man\",\"my friend\",\"the river\",\"a small bird\",\"the teacher\"]\nverb=[\"sees\",\"follows\",\"likes\",\"hears\",\"finds\",\"watches\"]\nobj=[\"the red house\",\"a quiet garden\",\"the long road\",\"an open door\",\"the morning light\",\"a broken clock\"]\ntail=[\"near the hill\",\"at night\",\"in the rain\",\"before dawn\",\"with great care\",\"\"]\nlines=[]\nfor _ in range(600):\n    lines.append(f\"{random.choice(subj)} {random.choice(verb)} {random.choice(obj)} {random.choice(tail)}.\".replace(\" .\",\".\"))\nopen(\"sample.txt\",\"w\").write(\" \".join(lines))\nEOF\npip list 2>/dev/null | grep -i numpy; python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --order 2 --n 3 --seed-word the", "description": "Run script on synthetic sample text to test"}, "message": "Run script on synthetic sample text to test", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport random\\nrandom.seed(1)\\nsubj=[\\\"the cat\\\",\\\"a dog\\\",\\\"the old man\\\",\\\"my friend\\\",\\\"the river\\\",\\\"a small bird\\\",\\\"the teacher\\\"]\\nverb=[\\\"sees\\\",\\\"follows\\\",\\\"likes\\\",\\\"hears\\\",\\\"finds\\\",\\\"watches\\\"]\\nobj=[\\\"the red house\\\",\\\"a quiet garden\\\",\\\"the long road\\\",\\\"an open door\\\",\\\"the morning light\\\",\\\"a broken clock\\\"]\\ntail=[\\\"near the hill\\\",\\\"at night\\\",\\\"in the rain\\\",\\\"before dawn\\\",\\\"with great care\\\",\\\"\\\"]\\nlines=[]\\nfor _ in range(600):\\n    lines.append(f\\\"{random.choice(subj)} {random.choice(verb)} {random.choice(obj)} {random.choice(tail)}.\\\".replace(\\\" .\\\",\\\".\\\"))\\nopen(\\\"sample.txt\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(\\\" \\\".join(lines))\\nEOF\\npip list 2>/dev/null | grep -i numpy; python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --order 2 --n 3 --seed-word the\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:44.739486Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:44.739514Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01X11FGp1utKpNF6ku44NPGn", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"numpy                      2.4.4\\nsentences: 540 train / 60 test | vocab: 47\\ntop tokens: ['the', '.', 'a', 'light', 'morning', 'finds', 'in', 'rain', 'watches', 'before']\\n\\nbag-sum identical when reversed: True\\npositional encoding differs when reversed: True\\n\\nheld-out perplexity  forward: 2.3 | backward: 2.3 | unigram floor (train entropy): 31.7\\n\\n--- forward generation ---\\n  the old man likes the morning light at night.\\n  my friend finds the morning light near the hill.\\n  the river hears a quiet garden near the hill.\\n\\n--- around seed word: 'the' (backward + forward) ---\\n  the old man sees the morning light near the old man finds a small bird watches the long road at night my friend finds the teacher finds a dog sees the teacher finds the morning light. my friend sees the old man follows rain.\\n  small bird follows an open door near light a small bird likes the river sees a dog hears the. the river hears a quiet the cat likes the my friend likes a dog finds a dog likes an a the teacher follows an open door in the rain.\\n  finds an open door. the teacher hears the cat finds a small bird likes small bird finds a dog finds the morning light in the rain my friend sees the cat watches my friend watches the red house near the teacher follows the red house near the hill.\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"numpy                      2.4.4\\nsentences: 540 train / 60 test | vocab: 47\\ntop tokens: ['the', '.', 'a', 'light', 'morning', 'finds', 'in', 'rain', 'watches', 'before']\\n\\nbag-sum identical when reversed: True\\npositional encoding differs when reversed: True\\n\\nheld-out perplexity  forward: 2.3 | backward: 2.3 | unigram floor (train entropy): 31.7\\n\\n--- forward generation ---\\n  the old man likes the morning light at night.\\n  my friend finds the morning light near the hill.\\n  the river hears a quiet garden near the hill.\\n\\n--- around seed word: 'the' (backward + forward) ---\\n  the old man sees the morning light near the old man finds a small bird watches the long road at night my friend finds the teacher finds a dog sees the teacher finds the morning light. my friend sees the old man follows rain.\\n  small bird follows an open door near light a small bird likes the river sees a dog hears the. the river hears a quiet the cat likes the my friend likes a dog finds a dog likes an a the teacher follows an open door in the rain.\\n  finds an open door. the teacher hears the cat finds a small bird likes small bird finds a dog finds the morning light in the rain my friend sees the cat watches my friend watches the red house near the teacher follows the red house near the hill.\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:46.674558Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:50.685250Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Debugging why the backward sequence fails to stop correctly."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:50.685361Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:50.685607Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Fixing bos token and seed boundary bugs in generation"}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:50.685664Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:51.623467Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01CXaaVsY4vdtMUNnuzWWDcp", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open(\"markov_gen.py\").read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    banned = (model.v.pad, model.v.bos, model.v.unk)\n    for _ in range(max_len):\"\"\",\"\"\"    banned = tuple(b for b in (model.v.pad, model.v.bos, model.v.unk, model.v.eos)\n                   if b != stop_id)\n    for _ in range(max_len):\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"generate(bwd, [vocab.eos, sid], vocab.bos,\",\"generate(bwd, [sid], vocab.bos,\")\ns=s.replace(\"generate(fwd, [vocab.bos, sid], vocab.eos,\",\"generate(fwd, [sid], vocab.eos,\")\nopen(\"markov_gen.py\",\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ncd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --order 2 --n 4 --seed-word morning | tail -12", "description": "Fix stop-token banning and seed contexts, retest"}, "message": "Fix stop-token banning and seed contexts, retest", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\ns=open(\\\"markov_gen.py\\\").read()\\ns=s.replace(\\\"\\\"\\\"    banned = (model.v.pad, model.v.bos, model.v.unk)\\n    for _ in range(max_len):\\\"\\\"\\\",\\\"\\\"\\\"    banned = tuple(b for b in (model.v.pad, model.v.bos, model.v.unk, model.v.eos)\\n                   if b != stop_id)\\n    for _ in range(max_len):\\\"\\\"\\\")\\ns=s.replace(\\\"generate(bwd, [vocab.eos, sid], vocab.bos,\\\",\\\"generate(bwd, [sid], vocab.bos,\\\")\\ns=s.replace(\\\"generate(fwd, [vocab.bos, sid], vocab.eos,\\\",\\\"generate(fwd, [sid], vocab.eos,\\\")\\nopen(\\\"markov_gen.py\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(s)\\nEOF\\ncd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --order 2 --n 4 --seed-word morning | tail -12\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:52.007653Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:52.007685Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01CXaaVsY4vdtMUNnuzWWDcp", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"\\n--- forward generation ---\\n  the old man likes the morning light at night.\\n  my friend finds the morning light near the hill.\\n  the river hears a quiet garden near the hill.\\n  my friend sees the morning light before dawn.\\n\\n--- around seed word: 'morning' (backward + forward) ---\\n  my friend finds the red house in the rain morning morning light at night.\\n  a dog watches the morning light near the hill. care.\\n  morning light with great care.\\n  the teacher follows the morning light in the rain.\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"\\n--- forward generation ---\\n  the old man likes the morning light at night.\\n  my friend finds the morning light near the hill.\\n  the river hears a quiet garden near the hill.\\n  my friend sees the morning light before dawn.\\n\\n--- around seed word: 'morning' (backward + forward) ---\\n  my friend finds the red house in the rain morning morning light at night.\\n  a dog watches the morning light near the hill. care.\\n  morning light with great care.\\n  the teacher follows the morning light in the rain.\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:53.466069Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:55.645884Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Checking token duplication edge cases in the generation logic."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:55.645929Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:55.765152Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01LimHEHHitfiFBfFCaAGydJ", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:55.788237Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:51:55.788256Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01LimHEHHitfiFBfFCaAGydJ", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py", "name": "markov gen", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:52:02.520702Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:52:02.530448Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "The script is `markov_gen.py`. You need only numpy, and you run it with `python markov_gen.py yourfile.txt --order 2 --n 5 --seed-word the`.\n\nI ran it on a small synthetic text file, since I don't have your dataset. It trained and generated fine, but the output quality on real text is untested.\n\n**What it does**\n- **Vocab:** sorted by `(-count, token)` into stable ids, with `<pad>`, `<unk>`, `<bos>` and `<eos>`. The map is built once and never re-sorted.\n- **Static order:** the forward chain is trained on the original id sequences.\n- **Reversed view:** the backward chain is trained on `seq[::-1]` copies, so the originals stay untouched.\n- **Probabilities:** an interpolated n-gram with `--order` previous tokens (1 is a bigram Markov chain, 2 a trigram). It returns full normalized distributions with an add-k base, so nothing hits log(0).\n- **Encodings:** the bag-sum is identical when reversed, while the positional-decay version changes. The script checks both.\n- **Evaluation:** held-out perplexity for the forward and backward chains, plus the unigram entropy floor as the \"no context\" baseline.\n- **Generation:** forward from `<bos>`, plus \"around a seed word\", which generates leftwards with the backward chain and rightwards with the forward chain.\n\n**Things to know**\n- **Backward perplexity:** it matches the forward value only roughly on real data. A joint distribution can be factored in either direction, but each smoothed chain estimates it differently.\n- **Around-seed output:** it can be rough, because the two halves are sampled independently. On the toy data I saw things like \"morning morning light\" and a stray fragment after a period. Lower `--temp` (0.5 to 0.7) cleans most of that up.\n- **Speed:** each step builds a full vocab-sized vector, which is fine up to roughly 50k tokens. Beyond that, use sparse sampling over the observed next tokens only.\n- **Encoder:** the sum encoder uses random embeddings. It's a placeholder for whatever tensors you feed it.\n\nIs the summation encoding going into a trained model? If so, I can add a small PyTorch layer that uses it.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:52:02.601907Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:52:02.601907Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fed0-4cf0-755c-a246-d7ab56acad97"}]},{"uuid": "f494c46e-d6fa-43f7-8a44-273b84aa3f78", "name": "Creating effective prompts", "summary": "", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:55:58.909313Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:43:10.119336Z", "account": {"uuid": "8d7882cd-3e98-47cc-a6e7-61494a1ee4ac"}, "chat_messages": [{"uuid": "01a0fed4-e1f2-728d-a784-01720d1b3fa4", "text": "do prompts", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:56:00.202230Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:56:00.202230Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "do prompts", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:56:00.202384Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:56:00.202384Z", "attachments": [{"file_name": "", "file_size": 7058, "file_type": "txt", "extracted_content": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\r\n\"\"\"\r\nMarkov text model from a .txt file.\r\n\r\n  - vocab: frequency-sorted ids, stable tie-break, special tokens\r\n  - forward chain (static order) + backward chain (reversed view)\r\n  - interpolated n-gram probabilities (proper distributions, add-k base)\r\n  - order-invariant sum encoding vs position-aware encoding\r\n  - held-out perplexity vs the unigram entropy floor\r\n  - generation: forward, backward, and \"around a seed word\"\r\n\r\nUsage:\r\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --order 2 --n 5 --seed-word \"the\"\r\n\"\"\"\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport math\r\nimport random\r\nimport re\r\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\r\n\r\nimport numpy as np\r\n\r\nPAD, UNK, BOS, EOS = \"<pad>\", \"<unk>\", \"<bos>\", \"<eos>\"\r\nSPECIALS = [PAD, UNK, BOS, EOS]\r\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[a-z0-9']+|[.,!?;:]\")\r\nSENT_SPLIT = re.compile(r\"(?<=[.!?])\\s+|\\n{2,}\")\r\n\r\n\r\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------- data\r\ndef load_sentences(path):\r\n    text = open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\").read().lower()\r\n    sents = []\r\n    for chunk in SENT_SPLIT.split(text):\r\n        toks = TOKEN_RE.findall(chunk)\r\n        if len(toks) >= 2:\r\n            sents.append(toks)\r\n    return sents\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Vocab:\r\n    \"\"\"token -> id built once; never re-sorted or reversed afterwards.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, sentences, min_count=1):\r\n        counts = Counter(t for s in sentences for t in s)\r\n        kept = [t for t, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count]\r\n        kept.sort(key=lambda t: (-counts[t], t))  # frequency, then alphabetical\r\n        self.itos = SPECIALS + kept\r\n        self.stoi = {t: i for i, t in enumerate(self.itos)}\r\n        self.V = len(self.itos)\r\n        self.pad, self.unk, self.bos, self.eos = (self.stoi[s] for s in SPECIALS)\r\n        # unigram counts over ids (specials get 0 here; handled in the model)\r\n        self.counts = np.zeros(self.V)\r\n        for t in kept:\r\n            self.counts[self.stoi[t]] = counts[t]\r\n\r\n    def encode(self, sent):\r\n        return [self.stoi.get(t, self.unk) for t in sent]\r\n\r\n    def decode(self, ids):\r\n        out = []\r\n        for i in ids:\r\n            if i in (self.pad, self.bos, self.eos):\r\n                continue\r\n            out.append(self.itos[i])\r\n        text = \" \".join(out)\r\n        return re.sub(r\"\\s+([.,!?;:])\", r\"\\1\", text)\r\n\r\n    def unigram_entropy(self):\r\n        p = self.counts[self.counts > 0]\r\n        p = p / p.sum()\r\n        return float(-(p * np.log(p)).sum())\r\n\r\n\r\n# -------------------------------------------------------------------- model\r\nclass NGram:\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n    Interpolated n-gram. `order` = number of previous tokens used.\r\n    order=1 is a classic Markov chain (bigram), order=2 is trigram, etc.\r\n    \"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, vocab, order=2, lam=0.7, k=0.01):\r\n        self.v, self.order, self.lam, self.k = vocab, order, lam, k\r\n        # tables[n][ctx_tuple_of_len_n] -> Counter(next_id)\r\n        self.tables = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(order + 1)]\r\n\r\n    def fit(self, id_seqs):\r\n        for seq in id_seqs:\r\n            for t in range(1, len(seq)):\r\n                for n in range(0, self.order + 1):\r\n                    if t - n < 0:\r\n                        break\r\n                    self.tables[n][tuple(seq[t - n:t])][seq[t]] += 1\r\n        # base: add-k smoothed unigram over real tokens + eos\r\n        base = self.v.counts.copy()\r\n        base[self.v.eos] = len(id_seqs)\r\n        base = base + self.k\r\n        base[[self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]] = 0.0\r\n        self.base = base / base.sum()\r\n\r\n    def dist(self, ctx):\r\n        \"\"\"Full probability vector over the vocab given a context list.\"\"\"\r\n        p = self.base\r\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\r\n        for n in range(0, len(ctx) + 1):          # shortest -> longest context\r\n            c = self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:] if n else ())\r\n            if not c:\r\n                continue\r\n            vec = np.zeros(self.v.V)\r\n            for tok, cnt in c.items():\r\n                vec[tok] = cnt\r\n            vec /= vec.sum()\r\n            p = self.lam * vec + (1 - self.lam) * p\r\n        return p\r\n\r\n    def logprob(self, seq):\r\n        lp = 0.0\r\n        for t in range(1, len(seq)):\r\n            lp += math.log(self.dist(seq[:t])[seq[t]] + 1e-12)\r\n        return lp\r\n\r\n    def sample_next(self, ctx, temp=1.0, top_k=40, banned=()):\r\n        p = self.dist(ctx).copy()\r\n        for b in banned:\r\n            p[b] = 0.0\r\n        if top_k and top_k < len(p):\r\n            cut = np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]\r\n            p[p < cut] = 0.0\r\n        p = p ** (1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3))\r\n        s = p.sum()\r\n        if s == 0:\r\n            return self.v.eos\r\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / s))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef generate(model, start_ctx, stop_id, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\r\n    ctx, out = list(start_ctx), []\r\n    banned = tuple(b for b in (model.v.pad, model.v.bos, model.v.unk, model.v.eos)\r\n                   if b != stop_id)\r\n    for _ in range(max_len):\r\n        nxt = model.sample_next(ctx, temp, top_k, banned)\r\n        if nxt == stop_id:\r\n            break\r\n        out.append(nxt)\r\n        ctx.append(nxt)\r\n    return out\r\n\r\n\r\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- encodings\r\nclass Encoder:\r\n    \"\"\"Sum encoding (order-invariant) vs positional-weighted (order-aware).\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, V, dim=16, decay=0.9, seed=0):\r\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\r\n        self.E = rng.normal(0, 1, (V, dim))\r\n        self.decay = decay\r\n\r\n    def bag_sum(self, ids):\r\n        return self.E[ids].sum(0)\r\n\r\n    def positional(self, ids):\r\n        w = self.decay ** np.arange(len(ids))\r\n        return (self.E[ids] * w[:, None]).sum(0)\r\n\r\n\r\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------- main\r\ndef main():\r\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"path\")\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--order\", type=int, default=2)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--min-count\", type=int, default=1)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--n\", type=int, default=5, help=\"sentences to generate\")\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--temp\", type=float, default=0.9)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--top-k\", type=int, default=40)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seed-word\", default=None)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=42)\r\n    args = ap.parse_args()\r\n\r\n    random.seed(args.seed)\r\n    np.random.seed(args.seed)\r\n\r\n    sents = load_sentences(args.path)\r\n    random.shuffle(sents)\r\n    split = max(1, int(0.9 * len(sents)))\r\n    train, test = sents[:split], sents[split:]\r\n\r\n    vocab = Vocab(train, args.min_count)\r\n\r\n\r\n    def wrap(s):\r\n        return [vocab.bos] + vocab.encode(s) + [vocab.eos]\r\n\r\n    fwd_seqs = [wrap(s) for s in train]          # static order\r\n\r\n    fwd = NGram(vocab, args.order)\r\n    fwd.fit(fwd_seqs)\r\n\r\n    # ---- generation\r\n    print(\"\\n--- forward generation ---\")\r\n    for _ in range(args.n):\r\n        ids = generate(fwd, [vocab.bos], vocab.eos, temp=args.temp, top_k=args.top_k)\r\n        print(\" \", vocab.decode(ids))\r\n\r\n   \r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\n"}], "files": [{"file_uuid": "646c232a-0785-447e-9c6d-09449066948a", "file_name": ""}], "parent_message_uuid": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000"}, {"uuid": "01a0fed4-e1f2-7c35-8f05-6d67af6c534d", "text": "I'm reading \"do prompts\" as adding prompt-conditioned generation: you give it some starting text and the model continues it. Here's a patch for that. If you meant something else (like the `--seed-word`, backward, or perplexity parts that the docstring mentions but `main()` doesn't run yet), tell me and I'll do that instead.\n\n**1. Add these helpers after `generate()`:**\n\n```python\ndef detok(tokens):\n    return re.sub(r\"\\s+([.,!?;:])\", r\"\\1\", \" \".join(tokens))\n\n\ndef complete(model, vocab, prompt, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\n    \"\"\"Continue a free-text prompt. Returns (full_text, oov_words).\"\"\"\n    toks = TOKEN_RE.findall(prompt.lower())\n    if not toks:\n        raise ValueError(\"prompt has no usable tokens\")\n    ids = vocab.encode(toks)\n    oov = [t for t, i in zip(toks, ids) if i == vocab.unk]\n    # condition on <bos> + prompt, so the model treats it as a sentence start\n    cont = generate(model, [vocab.bos] + ids, vocab.eos,\n                    max_len=max_len, temp=temp, top_k=top_k)\n    return detok(toks + [vocab.itos[i] for i in cont]), oov\n```\n\nUsing `toks` for the prompt part keeps your original words in the output, even ones the vocab maps to `<unk>`.\n\n**2. Add arguments in `main()`:**\n\n```python\n    ap.add_argument(\"--prompt\", default=None, help=\"text to continue\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--interactive\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"prompt loop\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--max-len\", type=int, default=40)\n```\n\n**3. Add this at the end of `main()`, after the forward generation block:**\n\n```python\n    def run(prompt):\n        for _ in range(args.n):\n            text, oov = complete(fwd, vocab, prompt, args.max_len,\n                                 args.temp, args.top_k)\n            print(\" \", text)\n        if oov:\n            print(f\"  (not in vocab, treated as <unk>: {sorted(set(oov))})\")\n\n    if args.prompt:\n        print(f\"\\n--- continuing: {args.prompt!r} ---\")\n        run(args.prompt)\n\n    if args.interactive:\n        print(\"\\nType a prompt (empty line to quit).\")\n        while True:\n            try:\n                p = input(\"> \").strip()\n            except EOFError:\n                break\n            if not p:\n                break\n            try:\n                run(p)\n            except ValueError as e:\n                print(\" \", e)\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```\npython markov_gen.py data.txt --order 2 --prompt \"once upon a\" --n 3\npython markov_gen.py data.txt --interactive\n```\n\nA few notes:\n\n- **Context length:** with `--order 2`, only the last two prompt tokens affect the continuation. Longer prompts don't steer it any more than a short one, which is just how n-gram models work.\n- **Unknown words:** if your prompt ends in an `<unk>` word, the context has no matching n-gram, so the model backs off to shorter contexts and the output gets more generic. The OOV warning flags this.\n- **Continuing mid-sentence:** the prompt is prefixed with `<bos>`, so the model assumes it's the start of a sentence. If you'd rather it treat the prompt as a continuation of text already in progress, drop `vocab.bos` from the context in `complete()`.\n\nI can also finish the unfinished pieces: backward generation, around-a-seed-word, and held-out perplexity.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:56:00.080688Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:56:06.550983Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Adding prompt-based generation to a text model script."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:56:06.551039Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:56:14.153182Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I'm reading \"do prompts\" as adding prompt-conditioned generation: you give it some starting text and the model continues it. Here's a patch for that. If you meant something else (like the `--seed-word`, backward, or perplexity parts that the docstring mentions but `main()` doesn't run yet), tell me and I'll do that instead.\n\n**1. Add these helpers after `generate()`:**\n\n```python\ndef detok(tokens):\n    return re.sub(r\"\\s+([.,!?;:])\", r\"\\1\", \" \".join(tokens))\n\n\ndef complete(model, vocab, prompt, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\n    \"\"\"Continue a free-text prompt. Returns (full_text, oov_words).\"\"\"\n    toks = TOKEN_RE.findall(prompt.lower())\n    if not toks:\n        raise ValueError(\"prompt has no usable tokens\")\n    ids = vocab.encode(toks)\n    oov = [t for t, i in zip(toks, ids) if i == vocab.unk]\n    # condition on <bos> + prompt, so the model treats it as a sentence start\n    cont = generate(model, [vocab.bos] + ids, vocab.eos,\n                    max_len=max_len, temp=temp, top_k=top_k)\n    return detok(toks + [vocab.itos[i] for i in cont]), oov\n```\n\nUsing `toks` for the prompt part keeps your original words in the output, even ones the vocab maps to `<unk>`.\n\n**2. Add arguments in `main()`:**\n\n```python\n    ap.add_argument(\"--prompt\", default=None, help=\"text to continue\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--interactive\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"prompt loop\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--max-len\", type=int, default=40)\n```\n\n**3. Add this at the end of `main()`, after the forward generation block:**\n\n```python\n    def run(prompt):\n        for _ in range(args.n):\n            text, oov = complete(fwd, vocab, prompt, args.max_len,\n                                 args.temp, args.top_k)\n            print(\" \", text)\n        if oov:\n            print(f\"  (not in vocab, treated as <unk>: {sorted(set(oov))})\")\n\n    if args.prompt:\n        print(f\"\\n--- continuing: {args.prompt!r} ---\")\n        run(args.prompt)\n\n    if args.interactive:\n        print(\"\\nType a prompt (empty line to quit).\")\n        while True:\n            try:\n                p = input(\"> \").strip()\n            except EOFError:\n                break\n            if not p:\n                break\n            try:\n                run(p)\n            except ValueError as e:\n                print(\" \", e)\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```\npython markov_gen.py data.txt --order 2 --prompt \"once upon a\" --n 3\npython markov_gen.py data.txt --interactive\n```\n\nA few notes:\n\n- **Context length:** with `--order 2`, only the last two prompt tokens affect the continuation. Longer prompts don't steer it any more than a short one, which is just how n-gram models work.\n- **Unknown words:** if your prompt ends in an `<unk>` word, the context has no matching n-gram, so the model backs off to shorter contexts and the output gets more generic. The OOV warning flags this.\n- **Continuing mid-sentence:** the prompt is prefixed with `<bos>`, so the model assumes it's the start of a sentence. If you'd rather it treat the prompt as a continuation of text already in progress, drop `vocab.bos` from the context in `complete()`.\n\nI can also finish the unfinished pieces: backward generation, around-a-seed-word, and held-out perplexity.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:56:14.166444Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:56:14.166444Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fed4-e1f2-728d-a784-01720d1b3fa4"}, {"uuid": "01a0fed5-1f6e-7dce-98af-e0822bb6b6c9", "text": "do the full code", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:56:16.073979Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:56:16.073979Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "do the full code", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:56:16.074175Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:56:16.074175Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fed4-e1f2-7c35-8f05-6d67af6c534d"}, {"uuid": "01a0fed5-1f6e-73eb-8d94-6c90374c9dc4", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThe full script is done and covers everything in your docstring plus the prompt completion from before. I ran it on a synthetic corpus and it works end to end.\n\nWhat `main()` now runs:\n\n- **Held-out perplexity:** forward, backward, a true order-0 unigram model, and `exp(H)` of the unigram entropy, plus the test OOV rate.\n- **Encodings demo:** the sum encoding gives a difference of 0 for a sentence and its reversal, while the positional encoding does not.\n- **Forward generation, backward generation, and `--seed-word`:** the backward chain runs on reversed sequences with the same vocab ids.\n- **`--prompt` and `--interactive`:** these continue a free-text prompt.\n\nChanges to the original code:\n\n- `NGram` now takes `start` and `stop` tokens. The backward model needs `<eos>` as its start and `<bos>` as its stop, which the original `base` hard-coded the other way.\n- `<unk>` keeps a little smoothing mass in the base distribution. Without it, any unknown word in the test set gets a probability of about 1e-12 and ruins the perplexity. Sampling still bans `<unk>`.\n- Around a seed word, the right side comes from the forward chain. The left side comes from the backward chain, conditioned on the seed plus the first `order-1` right-hand tokens, so the two halves agree with each other.\n- `load_sentences` closes its file handle, and `detok` is shared with `Vocab.decode`.\n\nUsage:\n\n```\npython markov_gen.py data.txt --order 2 --n 5 --seed-word \"the\"\npython markov_gen.py data.txt --prompt \"once upon a\" --n 3\npython markov_gen.py data.txt --interactive\n```\n\nI also added `--lam`, `--k`, and `--max-len` as flags.\n\nOn the toy corpus, the order-2 models reached a perplexity of about 2 against about 36 for the unigram model. The odd outputs, like \"nobody..\", come from `--temp 0.9` and the `lam=0.7` mix with lower orders. They get cleaner with `--temp 0.7` or a higher `--lam`, and a real corpus helps most.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:56:16.068431Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:56:44.234788Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Building out a complete demo covering multiple language model techniques."}, {"summary": "Designing shared base distributions for forward and backward models."}, {"summary": "Handling unknown-token probability mass and comparing perplexity against baselines."}, {"summary": "Aligning seed-based generation and sketching encoding comparison demos."}, {"summary": "Wiring up argument parsing and overall module structure."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:56:44.234855Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:09.190703Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Jt6MgWbJjqQMLR2xF7qRJd", "name": "create_file", "input": {"description": "Write the complete Markov text model script", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py", "file_text": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nMarkov text model from a .txt file.\n\n  - vocab: frequency-sorted ids, stable tie-break, special tokens\n  - forward chain (static order) + backward chain (reversed view)\n  - interpolated n-gram probabilities (proper distributions, add-k base)\n  - order-invariant sum encoding vs position-aware encoding\n  - held-out perplexity vs the unigram baseline / entropy\n  - generation: forward, backward, \"around a seed word\", and prompt completion\n\nUsage:\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --order 2 --n 5 --seed-word \"the\"\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --prompt \"once upon a\" --n 3\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --interactive\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport math\nimport random\nimport re\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nPAD, UNK, BOS, EOS = \"<pad>\", \"<unk>\", \"<bos>\", \"<eos>\"\nSPECIALS = [PAD, UNK, BOS, EOS]\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[a-z0-9']+|[.,!?;:]\")\nSENT_SPLIT = re.compile(r\"(?<=[.!?])\\s+|\\n{2,}\")\n\n\ndef detok(tokens):\n    return re.sub(r\"\\s+([.,!?;:])\", r\"\\1\", \" \".join(tokens))\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------- data\ndef load_sentences(path):\n    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        text = f.read().lower()\n    sents = []\n    for chunk in SENT_SPLIT.split(text):\n        toks = TOKEN_RE.findall(chunk)\n        if len(toks) >= 2:\n            sents.append(toks)\n    return sents\n\n\nclass Vocab:\n    \"\"\"token -> id built once; never re-sorted or reversed afterwards.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, sentences, min_count=1):\n        counts = Counter(t for s in sentences for t in s)\n        kept = [t for t, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count]\n        kept.sort(key=lambda t: (-counts[t], t))  # frequency, then alphabetical\n        self.itos = SPECIALS + kept\n        self.stoi = {t: i for i, t in enumerate(self.itos)}\n        self.V = len(self.itos)\n        self.pad, self.unk, self.bos, self.eos = (self.stoi[s] for s in SPECIALS)\n        # unigram counts over ids (specials get 0 here; handled in the model)\n        self.counts = np.zeros(self.V)\n        for t in kept:\n            self.counts[self.stoi[t]] = counts[t]\n\n    def encode(self, sent):\n        return [self.stoi.get(t, self.unk) for t in sent]\n\n    def decode(self, ids):\n        out = [self.itos[i] for i in ids if i not in (self.pad, self.bos, self.eos)]\n        return detok(out)\n\n    def unigram_entropy(self):\n        p = self.counts[self.counts > 0]\n        p = p / p.sum()\n        return float(-(p * np.log(p)).sum())\n\n\n# -------------------------------------------------------------------- model\nclass NGram:\n    \"\"\"\n    Interpolated n-gram. `order` = number of previous tokens used.\n    order=1 is a classic Markov chain (bigram), order=2 is trigram, etc.\n\n    `start` / `stop` are the boundary tokens of the sequences this model is\n    trained on: forward = (<bos>, <eos>), backward = (<eos>, <bos>).\n    The start token is never predicted; the stop token is.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, vocab, order=2, lam=0.7, k=0.01, start=None, stop=None):\n        self.v, self.order, self.lam, self.k = vocab, order, lam, k\n        self.start = vocab.bos if start is None else start\n        self.stop = vocab.eos if stop is None else stop\n        # tables[n][ctx_tuple_of_len_n] -> Counter(next_id)\n        self.tables = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(order + 1)]\n        self.base = None\n\n    def fit(self, id_seqs):\n        for seq in id_seqs:\n            for t in range(1, len(seq)):\n                for n in range(0, self.order + 1):\n                    if t - n < 0:\n                        break\n                    self.tables[n][tuple(seq[t - n:t])][seq[t]] += 1\n        # base: add-k smoothed unigram. Mass on real tokens, <unk>, and the\n        # stop token; none on <pad> or the start token (never predicted).\n        base = self.v.counts.copy()\n        base[self.stop] = len(id_seqs)\n        base = base + self.k\n        base[[self.v.pad, self.start]] = 0.0\n        self.base = base / base.sum()\n        return self\n\n    def dist(self, ctx):\n        \"\"\"Full probability vector over the vocab given a context list.\"\"\"\n        p = self.base\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\n        for n in range(0, len(ctx) + 1):          # shortest -> longest context\n            c = self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:] if n else ())\n            if not c:\n                continue\n            vec = np.zeros(self.v.V)\n            for tok, cnt in c.items():\n                vec[tok] = cnt\n            vec /= vec.sum()\n            p = self.lam * vec + (1 - self.lam) * p\n        return p\n\n    def logprob(self, seq):\n        lp = 0.0\n        for t in range(1, len(seq)):\n            lp += math.log(self.dist(seq[:t])[seq[t]] + 1e-12)\n        return lp\n\n    def sample_next(self, ctx, temp=1.0, top_k=40, banned=()):\n        p = self.dist(ctx).copy()\n        for b in banned:\n            p[b] = 0.0\n        if top_k and top_k < len(p):\n            cut = np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]\n            p[p < cut] = 0.0\n        p = p ** (1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3))\n        s = p.sum()\n        if s == 0:\n            return self.stop\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / s))\n\n\ndef generate(model, start_ctx, stop_id, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\n    ctx, out = list(start_ctx), []\n    banned = tuple(b for b in (model.v.pad, model.v.bos, model.v.unk, model.v.eos)\n                   if b != stop_id)\n    for _ in range(max_len):\n        nxt = model.sample_next(ctx, temp, top_k, banned)\n        if nxt == stop_id:\n            break\n        out.append(nxt)\n        ctx.append(nxt)\n    return out\n\n\ndef generate_backward(bwd, vocab, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\n    \"\"\"Generate from the end of a sentence toward the start; return in reading order.\"\"\"\n    ids = generate(bwd, [vocab.eos], vocab.bos, max_len, temp, top_k)\n    return ids[::-1]\n\n\ndef generate_around(fwd, bwd, vocab, seed_id, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\n    \"\"\"\n    Grow a sentence in both directions from a seed word.\n    Right side comes from the forward chain; the left side comes from the\n    backward chain, conditioned on the seed plus the first (order-1) right-hand\n    tokens so the two halves agree with each other.\n    \"\"\"\n    right = generate(fwd, [seed_id], vocab.eos, max_len, temp, top_k)\n    window = [seed_id] + right[:max(fwd.order - 1, 0)]\n    left_rev = generate(bwd, window[::-1], vocab.bos, max_len, temp, top_k)\n    return left_rev[::-1] + [seed_id] + right\n\n\ndef complete(model, vocab, prompt, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\n    \"\"\"Continue a free-text prompt. Returns (full_text, oov_words).\"\"\"\n    toks = TOKEN_RE.findall(prompt.lower())\n    if not toks:\n        raise ValueError(\"prompt has no usable tokens\")\n    ids = vocab.encode(toks)\n    oov = [t for t, i in zip(toks, ids) if i == vocab.unk]\n    # condition on <bos> + prompt, so the model treats it as a sentence start\n    cont = generate(model, [vocab.bos] + ids, vocab.eos,\n                    max_len=max_len, temp=temp, top_k=top_k)\n    return detok(toks + [vocab.itos[i] for i in cont]), oov\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------- evaluation\ndef perplexity(model, seqs):\n    lp, n = 0.0, 0\n    for s in seqs:\n        lp += model.logprob(s)\n        n += len(s) - 1\n    return math.exp(-lp / n) if n else float(\"nan\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- encodings\nclass Encoder:\n    \"\"\"Sum encoding (order-invariant) vs positional-weighted (order-aware).\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, V, dim=16, decay=0.9, seed=0):\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        self.E = rng.normal(0, 1, (V, dim))\n        self.decay = decay\n\n    def bag_sum(self, ids):\n        return self.E[ids].sum(0)\n\n    def positional(self, ids):\n        w = self.decay ** np.arange(len(ids))\n        return (self.E[ids] * w[:, None]).sum(0)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------- main\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"path\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--order\", type=int, default=2)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--min-count\", type=int, default=1)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--n\", type=int, default=5, help=\"sentences to generate\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--temp\", type=float, default=0.9)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--top-k\", type=int, default=40)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--max-len\", type=int, default=40)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--lam\", type=float, default=0.7, help=\"interpolation weight\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--k\", type=float, default=0.01, help=\"add-k for the base\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seed-word\", default=None)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--prompt\", default=None, help=\"text to continue\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--interactive\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"prompt loop\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=42)\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    random.seed(args.seed)\n    np.random.seed(args.seed)\n\n    sents = load_sentences(args.path)\n    if not sents:\n        raise SystemExit(\"no usable sentences found in input file\")\n    random.shuffle(sents)\n    split = max(1, int(0.9 * len(sents)))\n    train, test = sents[:split], sents[split:]\n\n    vocab = Vocab(train, args.min_count)\n    print(f\"sentences: {len(train)} train / {len(test)} test | vocab: {vocab.V}\")\n\n    def wrap(s):\n        return [vocab.bos] + vocab.encode(s) + [vocab.eos]\n\n    fwd_seqs = [wrap(s) for s in train]              # static order\n    bwd_seqs = [s[::-1] for s in fwd_seqs]           # reversed view, same ids\n\n    gen_kw = dict(max_len=args.max_len, temp=args.temp, top_k=args.top_k)\n    model_kw = dict(order=args.order, lam=args.lam, k=args.k)\n\n    fwd = NGram(vocab, **model_kw).fit(fwd_seqs)\n    bwd = NGram(vocab, start=vocab.eos, stop=vocab.bos, **model_kw).fit(bwd_seqs)\n\n    # ---- evaluation\n    if test:\n        test_f = [wrap(s) for s in test]\n        test_b = [s[::-1] for s in test_f]\n        uni = NGram(vocab, order=0, lam=args.lam, k=args.k).fit(fwd_seqs)\n        toks = [t for s in test for t in s]\n        oov = sum(1 for t in toks if t not in vocab.stoi) / max(len(toks), 1)\n        print(\"\\n--- held-out perplexity (lower is better) ---\")\n        print(f\"  test OOV rate            : {oov:.1%}\")\n        print(f\"  unigram entropy exp(H)   : {math.exp(vocab.unigram_entropy()):.1f}\"\n              \"   (train-set unigram baseline)\")\n        print(f\"  unigram model (order 0)  : {perplexity(uni, test_f):.1f}\")\n        print(f\"  forward  (order {args.order})       : {perplexity(fwd, test_f):.1f}\")\n        print(f\"  backward (order {args.order})       : {perplexity(bwd, test_b):.1f}\")\n    else:\n        print(\"\\n(not enough data for a held-out set; skipping perplexity)\")\n\n    # ---- encodings\n    enc = Encoder(vocab.V)\n    ids = vocab.encode(train[0])\n    rev = ids[::-1]\n    print(\"\\n--- encodings: sentence vs. same words reversed ---\")\n    print(\"  sentence:\", detok(train[0]))\n    print(f\"  bag-sum  difference norm : {np.linalg.norm(enc.bag_sum(ids) - enc.bag_sum(rev)):.4f}\"\n          \"   (0 = order-invariant)\")\n    print(f\"  positional difference    : {np.linalg.norm(enc.positional(ids) - enc.positional(rev)):.4f}\"\n          \"   (>0 = order-aware)\")\n\n    # ---- generation\n    print(\"\\n--- forward generation ---\")\n    for _ in range(args.n):\n        out = generate(fwd, [vocab.bos], vocab.eos, **gen_kw)\n        print(\" \", vocab.decode(out))\n\n    print(\"\\n--- backward generation (built from the end) ---\")\n    for _ in range(args.n):\n        out = generate_backward(bwd, vocab, **gen_kw)\n        print(\" \", vocab.decode(out))\n\n    if args.seed_word:\n        sid = vocab.stoi.get(args.seed_word.lower(), vocab.unk)\n        print(f\"\\n--- around seed word {args.seed_word!r} ---\")\n        if sid == vocab.unk:\n            print(\"  seed word not in vocabulary\")\n        else:\n            for _ in range(args.n):\n                out = generate_around(fwd, bwd, vocab, sid, **gen_kw)\n                print(\" \", vocab.decode(out))\n\n    # ---- prompt completion\n    def run(prompt):\n        oov_all = set()\n        for _ in range(args.n):\n            text, oov = complete(fwd, vocab, prompt, **gen_kw)\n            oov_all.update(oov)\n            print(\" \", text)\n        if oov_all:\n            print(f\"  (not in vocab, treated as <unk>: {sorted(oov_all)})\")\n\n    if args.prompt:\n        print(f\"\\n--- continuing: {args.prompt!r} ---\")\n        try:\n            run(args.prompt)\n        except ValueError as e:\n            print(\" \", e)\n\n    if args.interactive:\n        print(\"\\nType a prompt (empty line to quit).\")\n        while True:\n            try:\n                p = input(\"> \").strip()\n            except EOFError:\n                break\n            if not p:\n                break\n            try:\n                run(p)\n            except ValueError as e:\n                print(\" \", e)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}, "message": "Write the complete Markov text model script", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nMarkov text model from a .txt file.\\n\\n  - vocab: frequency-sorted ids, stable tie-break, special tokens\\n  - forward chain (static order) + backward chain (reversed view)\\n  - interpolated n-gram probabilities (proper distributions, add-k base)\\n  - order-invariant sum encoding vs position-aware encoding\\n  - held-out perplexity vs the unigram baseline / entropy\\n  - generation: forward, backward, \\\"around a seed word\\\", and prompt completion\\n\\nUsage:\\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --order 2 --n 5 --seed-word \\\"the\\\"\\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --prompt \\\"once upon a\\\" --n 3\\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --interactive\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport argparse\\nimport math\\nimport random\\nimport re\\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nPAD, UNK, BOS, EOS = \\\"<pad>\\\", \\\"<unk>\\\", \\\"<bos>\\\", \\\"<eos>\\\"\\nSPECIALS = [PAD, UNK, BOS, EOS]\\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\\\"[a-z0-9']+|[.,!?;:]\\\")\\nSENT_SPLIT = re.compile(r\\\"(?<=[.!?])\\\\s+|\\\\n{2,}\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef detok(tokens):\\n    return re.sub(r\\\"\\\\s+([.,!?;:])\\\", r\\\"\\\\1\\\", \\\" \\\".join(tokens))\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------- data\\ndef load_sentences(path):\\n    with open(path, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as f:\\n        text = f.read().lower()\\n    sents = []\\n    for chunk in SENT_SPLIT.split(text):\\n        toks = TOKEN_RE.findall(chunk)\\n        if len(toks) >= 2:\\n            sents.append(toks)\\n    return sents\\n\\n\\nclass Vocab:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"token -> id built once; never re-sorted or reversed afterwards.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, sentences, min_count=1):\\n        counts = Counter(t for s in sentences for t in s)\\n        kept = [t for t, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count]\\n        kept.sort(key=lambda t: (-counts[t], t))  # frequency, then alphabetical\\n        self.itos = SPECIALS + kept\\n        self.stoi = {t: i for i, t in enumerate(self.itos)}\\n        self.V = len(self.itos)\\n        self.pad, self.unk, self.bos, self.eos = (self.stoi[s] for s in SPECIALS)\\n        # unigram counts over ids (specials get 0 here; handled in the model)\\n        self.counts = np.zeros(self.V)\\n        for t in kept:\\n            self.counts[self.stoi[t]] = counts[t]\\n\\n    def encode(self, sent):\\n        return [self.stoi.get(t, self.unk) for t in sent]\\n\\n    def decode(self, ids):\\n        out = [self.itos[i] for i in ids if i not in (self.pad, self.bos, self.eos)]\\n        return detok(out)\\n\\n    def unigram_entropy(self):\\n        p = self.counts[self.counts > 0]\\n        p = p / p.sum()\\n        return float(-(p * np.log(p)).sum())\\n\\n\\n# -------------------------------------------------------------------- model\\nclass NGram:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Interpolated n-gram. `order` = number of previous tokens used.\\n    order=1 is a classic Markov chain (bigram), order=2 is trigram, etc.\\n\\n    `start` / `stop` are the boundary tokens of the sequences this model is\\n    trained on: forward = (<bos>, <eos>), backward = (<eos>, <bos>).\\n    The start token is never predicted; the stop token is.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, vocab, order=2, lam=0.7, k=0.01, start=None, stop=None):\\n        self.v, self.order, self.lam, self.k = vocab, order, lam, k\\n        self.start = vocab.bos if start is None else start\\n        self.stop = vocab.eos if stop is None else stop\\n        # tables[n][ctx_tuple_of_len_n] -> Counter(next_id)\\n        self.tables = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(order + 1)]\\n        self.base = None\\n\\n    def fit(self, id_seqs):\\n        for seq in id_seqs:\\n            for t in range(1, len(seq)):\\n                for n in range(0, self.order + 1):\\n                    if t - n < 0:\\n                        break\\n                    self.tables[n][tuple(seq[t - n:t])][seq[t]] += 1\\n        # base: add-k smoothed unigram. Mass on real tokens, <unk>, and the\\n        # stop token; none on <pad> or the start token (never predicted).\\n        base = self.v.counts.copy()\\n        base[self.stop] = len(id_seqs)\\n        base = base + self.k\\n        base[[self.v.pad, self.start]] = 0.0\\n        self.base = base / base.sum()\\n        return self\\n\\n    def dist(self, ctx):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Full probability vector over the vocab given a context list.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        p = self.base\\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\\n        for n in range(0, len(ctx) + 1):          # shortest -> longest context\\n            c = self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:] if n else ())\\n            if not c:\\n                continue\\n            vec = np.zeros(self.v.V)\\n            for tok, cnt in c.items():\\n                vec[tok] = cnt\\n            vec /= vec.sum()\\n            p = self.lam * vec + (1 - self.lam) * p\\n        return p\\n\\n    def logprob(self, seq):\\n        lp = 0.0\\n        for t in range(1, len(seq)):\\n            lp += math.log(self.dist(seq[:t])[seq[t]] + 1e-12)\\n        return lp\\n\\n    def sample_next(self, ctx, temp=1.0, top_k=40, banned=()):\\n        p = self.dist(ctx).copy()\\n        for b in banned:\\n            p[b] = 0.0\\n        if top_k and top_k < len(p):\\n            cut = np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]\\n            p[p < cut] = 0.0\\n        p = p ** (1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3))\\n        s = p.sum()\\n        if s == 0:\\n            return self.stop\\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / s))\\n\\n\\ndef generate(model, start_ctx, stop_id, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\\n    ctx, out = list(start_ctx), []\\n    banned = tuple(b for b in (model.v.pad, model.v.bos, model.v.unk, model.v.eos)\\n                   if b != stop_id)\\n    for _ in range(max_len):\\n        nxt = model.sample_next(ctx, temp, top_k, banned)\\n        if nxt == stop_id:\\n            break\\n        out.append(nxt)\\n        ctx.append(nxt)\\n    return out\\n\\n\\ndef generate_backward(bwd, vocab, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generate from the end of a sentence toward the start; return in reading order.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    ids = generate(bwd, [vocab.eos], vocab.bos, max_len, temp, top_k)\\n    return ids[::-1]\\n\\n\\ndef generate_around(fwd, bwd, vocab, seed_id, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Grow a sentence in both directions from a seed word.\\n    Right side comes from the forward chain; the left side comes from the\\n    backward chain, conditioned on the seed plus the first (order-1) right-hand\\n    tokens so the two halves agree with each other.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    right = generate(fwd, [seed_id], vocab.eos, max_len, temp, top_k)\\n    window = [seed_id] + right[:max(fwd.order - 1, 0)]\\n    left_rev = generate(bwd, window[::-1], vocab.bos, max_len, temp, top_k)\\n    return left_rev[::-1] + [seed_id] + right\\n\\n\\ndef complete(model, vocab, prompt, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Continue a free-text prompt. Returns (full_text, oov_words).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    toks = TOKEN_RE.findall(prompt.lower())\\n    if not toks:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"prompt has no usable tokens\\\")\\n    ids = vocab.encode(toks)\\n    oov = [t for t, i in zip(toks, ids) if i == vocab.unk]\\n    # condition on <bos> + prompt, so the model treats it as a sentence start\\n    cont = generate(model, [vocab.bos] + ids, vocab.eos,\\n                    max_len=max_len, temp=temp, top_k=top_k)\\n    return detok(toks + [vocab.itos[i] for i in cont]), oov\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------- evaluation\\ndef perplexity(model, seqs):\\n    lp, n = 0.0, 0\\n    for s in seqs:\\n        lp += model.logprob(s)\\n        n += len(s) - 1\\n    return math.exp(-lp / n) if n else float(\\\"nan\\\")\\n\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- encodings\\nclass Encoder:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Sum encoding (order-invariant) vs positional-weighted (order-aware).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, V, dim=16, decay=0.9, seed=0):\\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n        self.E = rng.normal(0, 1, (V, dim))\\n        self.decay = decay\\n\\n    def bag_sum(self, ids):\\n        return self.E[ids].sum(0)\\n\\n    def positional(self, ids):\\n        w = self.decay ** np.arange(len(ids))\\n        return (self.E[ids] * w[:, None]).sum(0)\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------- main\\ndef main():\\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"path\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--order\\\", type=int, default=2)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--min-count\\\", type=int, default=1)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--n\\\", type=int, default=5, help=\\\"sentences to generate\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--temp\\\", type=float, default=0.9)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--top-k\\\", type=int, default=40)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--max-len\\\", type=int, default=40)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--lam\\\", type=float, default=0.7, help=\\\"interpolation weight\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--k\\\", type=float, default=0.01, help=\\\"add-k for the base\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--seed-word\\\", default=None)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--prompt\\\", default=None, help=\\\"text to continue\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--interactive\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"prompt loop\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--seed\\\", type=int, default=42)\\n    args = ap.parse_args()\\n\\n    random.seed(args.seed)\\n    np.random.seed(args.seed)\\n\\n    sents = load_sentences(args.path)\\n    if not sents:\\n        raise SystemExit(\\\"no usable sentences found in input file\\\")\\n    random.shuffle(sents)\\n    split = max(1, int(0.9 * len(sents)))\\n    train, test = sents[:split], sents[split:]\\n\\n    vocab = Vocab(train, args.min_count)\\n    print(f\\\"sentences: {len(train)} train / {len(test)} test | vocab: {vocab.V}\\\")\\n\\n    def wrap(s):\\n        return [vocab.bos] + vocab.encode(s) + [vocab.eos]\\n\\n    fwd_seqs = [wrap(s) for s in train]              # static order\\n    bwd_seqs = [s[::-1] for s in fwd_seqs]           # reversed view, same ids\\n\\n    gen_kw = dict(max_len=args.max_len, temp=args.temp, top_k=args.top_k)\\n    model_kw = dict(order=args.order, lam=args.lam, k=args.k)\\n\\n    fwd = NGram(vocab, **model_kw).fit(fwd_seqs)\\n    bwd = NGram(vocab, start=vocab.eos, stop=vocab.bos, **model_kw).fit(bwd_seqs)\\n\\n    # ---- evaluation\\n    if test:\\n        test_f = [wrap(s) for s in test]\\n        test_b = [s[::-1] for s in test_f]\\n        uni = NGram(vocab, order=0, lam=args.lam, k=args.k).fit(fwd_seqs)\\n        toks = [t for s in test for t in s]\\n        oov = sum(1 for t in toks if t not in vocab.stoi) / max(len(toks), 1)\\n        print(\\\"\\\\n--- held-out perplexity (lower is better) ---\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"  test OOV rate            : {oov:.1%}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"  unigram entropy exp(H)   : {math.exp(vocab.unigram_entropy()):.1f}\\\"\\n              \\\"   (train-set unigram baseline)\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"  unigram model (order 0)  : {perplexity(uni, test_f):.1f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"  forward  (order {args.order})       : {perplexity(fwd, test_f):.1f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"  backward (order {args.order})       : {perplexity(bwd, test_b):.1f}\\\")\\n    else:\\n        print(\\\"\\\\n(not enough data for a held-out set; skipping perplexity)\\\")\\n\\n    # ---- encodings\\n    enc = Encoder(vocab.V)\\n    ids = vocab.encode(train[0])\\n    rev = ids[::-1]\\n    print(\\\"\\\\n--- encodings: sentence vs. same words reversed ---\\\")\\n    print(\\\"  sentence:\\\", detok(train[0]))\\n    print(f\\\"  bag-sum  difference norm : {np.linalg.norm(enc.bag_sum(ids) - enc.bag_sum(rev)):.4f}\\\"\\n          \\\"   (0 = order-invariant)\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  positional difference    : {np.linalg.norm(enc.positional(ids) - enc.positional(rev)):.4f}\\\"\\n          \\\"   (>0 = order-aware)\\\")\\n\\n    # ---- generation\\n    print(\\\"\\\\n--- forward generation ---\\\")\\n    for _ in range(args.n):\\n        out = generate(fwd, [vocab.bos], vocab.eos, **gen_kw)\\n        print(\\\" \\\", vocab.decode(out))\\n\\n    print(\\\"\\\\n--- backward generation (built from the end) ---\\\")\\n    for _ in range(args.n):\\n        out = generate_backward(bwd, vocab, **gen_kw)\\n        print(\\\" \\\", vocab.decode(out))\\n\\n    if args.seed_word:\\n        sid = vocab.stoi.get(args.seed_word.lower(), vocab.unk)\\n        print(f\\\"\\\\n--- around seed word {args.seed_word!r} ---\\\")\\n        if sid == vocab.unk:\\n            print(\\\"  seed word not in vocabulary\\\")\\n        else:\\n            for _ in range(args.n):\\n                out = generate_around(fwd, bwd, vocab, sid, **gen_kw)\\n                print(\\\" \\\", vocab.decode(out))\\n\\n    # ---- prompt completion\\n    def run(prompt):\\n        oov_all = set()\\n        for _ in range(args.n):\\n            text, oov = complete(fwd, vocab, prompt, **gen_kw)\\n            oov_all.update(oov)\\n            print(\\\" \\\", text)\\n        if oov_all:\\n            print(f\\\"  (not in vocab, treated as <unk>: {sorted(oov_all)})\\\")\\n\\n    if args.prompt:\\n        print(f\\\"\\\\n--- continuing: {args.prompt!r} ---\\\")\\n        try:\\n            run(args.prompt)\\n        except ValueError as e:\\n            print(\\\" \\\", e)\\n\\n    if args.interactive:\\n        print(\\\"\\\\nType a prompt (empty line to quit).\\\")\\n        while True:\\n            try:\\n                p = input(\\\"> \\\").strip()\\n            except EOFError:\\n                break\\n            if not p:\\n                break\\n            try:\\n                run(p)\\n            except ValueError as e:\\n                print(\\\" \\\", e)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\n\", \"filename\": \"/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:10.636797Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:10.636832Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Jt6MgWbJjqQMLR2xF7qRJd", "name": "create_file", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:12.302929Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:15.193949Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01TNVhBYCbXxtkwkQm4mtvn9", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport random\nrandom.seed(1)\nsubj=[\"the cat\",\"a dog\",\"the old man\",\"my friend\",\"the small bird\",\"a tall woman\"]\nverb=[\"sat on\",\"looked at\",\"walked past\",\"jumped over\",\"talked about\",\"ran toward\"]\nobj=[\"the red house\",\"a quiet river\",\"the big tree\",\"an empty road\",\"the green hill\",\"a broken fence\"]\ntail=[\"\",\" in the morning\",\" at night\",\" without a sound\",\", and nobody noticed\"]\nwith open(\"sample.txt\",\"w\") as f:\n    for _ in range(600):\n        f.write(f\"{random.choice(subj).capitalize()} {random.choice(verb)} {random.choice(obj)}{random.choice(tail)}.\\n\")\nEOF\npython3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --n 3 --seed-word \"river\" --prompt \"the cat sat\" --order 2 && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --n 2 --order 1 --min-count 3 --seed-word the --prompt \"zebra the\" | tail -15", "description": "Test the script on a synthetic corpus"}, "message": "Test the script on a synthetic corpus", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport random\\nrandom.seed(1)\\nsubj=[\\\"the cat\\\",\\\"a dog\\\",\\\"the old man\\\",\\\"my friend\\\",\\\"the small bird\\\",\\\"a tall woman\\\"]\\nverb=[\\\"sat on\\\",\\\"looked at\\\",\\\"walked past\\\",\\\"jumped over\\\",\\\"talked about\\\",\\\"ran toward\\\"]\\nobj=[\\\"the red house\\\",\\\"a quiet river\\\",\\\"the big tree\\\",\\\"an empty road\\\",\\\"the green hill\\\",\\\"a broken fence\\\"]\\ntail=[\\\"\\\",\\\" in the morning\\\",\\\" at night\\\",\\\" without a sound\\\",\\\", and nobody noticed\\\"]\\nwith open(\\\"sample.txt\\\",\\\"w\\\") as f:\\n    for _ in range(600):\\n        f.write(f\\\"{random.choice(subj).capitalize()} {random.choice(verb)} {random.choice(obj)}{random.choice(tail)}.\\\\n\\\")\\nEOF\\npython3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --n 3 --seed-word \\\"river\\\" --prompt \\\"the cat sat\\\" --order 2 && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --n 2 --order 1 --min-count 3 --seed-word the --prompt \\\"zebra the\\\" | tail -15\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:16.099710Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:16.099749Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01TNVhBYCbXxtkwkQm4mtvn9", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"sentences: 540 train / 60 test | vocab: 51\\n\\n--- held-out perplexity (lower is better) ---\\n  test OOV rate            : 0.0%\\n  unigram entropy exp(H)   : 37.2   (train-set unigram baseline)\\n  unigram model (order 0)  : 36.5\\n  forward  (order 2)       : 2.1\\n  backward (order 2)       : 2.1\\n\\n--- encodings: sentence vs. same words reversed ---\\n  sentence: a dog sat on the big tree without a sound.\\n  bag-sum  difference norm : 0.0000   (0 = order-invariant)\\n  positional difference    : 5.0625   (>0 = order-aware)\\n\\n--- forward generation ---\\n  the river in the morning.\\n  my friend looked at an empty road.\\n  the cat walked past a broken fence, and nobody noticed.\\n\\n--- backward generation (built from the end) ---\\n  the morning.\\n  the old man woman\\n  a dog jumped over a broken fence the cat talked about the red house, and nobody noticed.\\n\\n--- around seed word 'river' ---\\n  my friend ran toward the woman jumped over a river the small bird ran toward the green hill.\\n  my friend talked about a quiet river at night.\\n  my friend talked about the green hill in the, talked toward a quiet river, and nobody noticed.\\n\\n--- continuing: 'the cat sat' ---\\n  the cat sat on the red house, and nobody noticed.\\n  the cat sat on an empty road at night.\\n  the cat sat the green hill.\\n  the red house, and nobody..\\n  a\\n\\n--- backward generation (built from the end) ---\\n  the old\\n  a tall woman looked at night.\\n\\n--- around seed word 'the' ---\\n  the morning. about the small bird broken fence.\\n  the red house an empty and nobody noticed.\\n\\n--- continuing: 'zebra the' ---\\n  zebra the red house about the green hill. old man jumped over a dog a tall.\\n  zebra the small bird sat on the green toward at the red house.\\n  (not in vocab, treated as <unk>: ['zebra'])\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"sentences: 540 train / 60 test | vocab: 51\\n\\n--- held-out perplexity (lower is better) ---\\n  test OOV rate            : 0.0%\\n  unigram entropy exp(H)   : 37.2   (train-set unigram baseline)\\n  unigram model (order 0)  : 36.5\\n  forward  (order 2)       : 2.1\\n  backward (order 2)       : 2.1\\n\\n--- encodings: sentence vs. same words reversed ---\\n  sentence: a dog sat on the big tree without a sound.\\n  bag-sum  difference norm : 0.0000   (0 = order-invariant)\\n  positional difference    : 5.0625   (>0 = order-aware)\\n\\n--- forward generation ---\\n  the river in the morning.\\n  my friend looked at an empty road.\\n  the cat walked past a broken fence, and nobody noticed.\\n\\n--- backward generation (built from the end) ---\\n  the morning.\\n  the old man woman\\n  a dog jumped over a broken fence the cat talked about the red house, and nobody noticed.\\n\\n--- around seed word 'river' ---\\n  my friend ran toward the woman jumped over a river the small bird ran toward the green hill.\\n  my friend talked about a quiet river at night.\\n  my friend talked about the green hill in the, talked toward a quiet river, and nobody noticed.\\n\\n--- continuing: 'the cat sat' ---\\n  the cat sat on the red house, and nobody noticed.\\n  the cat sat on an empty road at night.\\n  the cat sat the green hill.\\n  the red house, and nobody..\\n  a\\n\\n--- backward generation (built from the end) ---\\n  the old\\n  a tall woman looked at night.\\n\\n--- around seed word 'the' ---\\n  the morning. about the small bird broken fence.\\n  the red house an empty and nobody noticed.\\n\\n--- continuing: 'zebra the' ---\\n  zebra the red house about the green hill. old man jumped over a dog a tall.\\n  zebra the small bird sat on the green toward at the red house.\\n  (not in vocab, treated as <unk>: ['zebra'])\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:18.291660Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:20.450168Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Building a toy language model to test text generation."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:20.450233Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:20.523175Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01297vz4QjSZEV83XNSM6uow", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:20.543397Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:20.543478Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01297vz4QjSZEV83XNSM6uow", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py", "name": "markov gen", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:26.406253Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T22:57:26.414967Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "The full script is done and covers everything in your docstring plus the prompt completion from before. I ran it on a synthetic corpus and it works end to end.\n\nWhat `main()` now runs:\n\n- **Held-out perplexity:** forward, backward, a true order-0 unigram model, and `exp(H)` of the unigram entropy, plus the test OOV rate.\n- **Encodings demo:** the sum encoding gives a difference of 0 for a sentence and its reversal, while the positional encoding does not.\n- **Forward generation, backward generation, and `--seed-word`:** the backward chain runs on reversed sequences with the same vocab ids.\n- **`--prompt` and `--interactive`:** these continue a free-text prompt.\n\nChanges to the original code:\n\n- `NGram` now takes `start` and `stop` tokens. The backward model needs `<eos>` as its start and `<bos>` as its stop, which the original `base` hard-coded the other way.\n- `<unk>` keeps a little smoothing mass in the base distribution. Without it, any unknown word in the test set gets a probability of about 1e-12 and ruins the perplexity. Sampling still bans `<unk>`.\n- Around a seed word, the right side comes from the forward chain. The left side comes from the backward chain, conditioned on the seed plus the first `order-1` right-hand tokens, so the two halves agree with each other.\n- `load_sentences` closes its file handle, and `detok` is shared with `Vocab.decode`.\n\nUsage:\n\n```\npython markov_gen.py data.txt --order 2 --n 5 --seed-word \"the\"\npython markov_gen.py data.txt --prompt \"once upon a\" --n 3\npython markov_gen.py data.txt --interactive\n```\n\nI also added `--lam`, `--k`, and `--max-len` as flags.\n\nOn the toy corpus, the order-2 models reached a perplexity of about 2 against about 36 for the unigram model. The odd outputs, like \"nobody..\", come from `--temp 0.9` and the `lam=0.7` mix with lower orders. They get cleaner with `--temp 0.7` or a higher `--lam`, and a real corpus helps most.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T22:57:26.481814Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T22:57:26.481814Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fed5-1f6e-7dce-98af-e0822bb6b6c9"}, {"uuid": "01a0fede-7f57-7a83-bc25-bbe659b55462", "text": "keep it compact just what i said", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T23:06:30.265866Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T23:06:30.265866Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "keep it compact just what i said", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-02T23:06:30.266057Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T23:06:30.266057Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fed5-1f6e-73eb-8d94-6c90374c9dc4"}, {"uuid": "01a0fede-7f57-7dae-a3a6-a7f8a0439e12", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI trimmed the script to just the prompt feature, about 130 lines. I removed the backward chain, the seed-word generation, the perplexity evaluation and the encodings.\n\nRun it with `--prompt \"once upon a\" --n 3`, or use `--interactive`. With no arguments besides the file, it drops into the interactive loop.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T23:06:30.260806Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T23:06:33.575027Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Scaling down the code to just the prompts feature."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T23:06:33.575098Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T23:06:43.768155Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_017xfzF1R1xCZ9av78weyHDd", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cat > /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py <<'EOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Markov text model with prompt completion.\n\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --prompt \"once upon a\" --n 3\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --interactive\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport random\nimport re\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nPAD, UNK, BOS, EOS = \"<pad>\", \"<unk>\", \"<bos>\", \"<eos>\"\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[a-z0-9']+|[.,!?;:]\")\nSENT_SPLIT = re.compile(r\"(?<=[.!?])\\s+|\\n{2,}\")\n\n\ndef detok(tokens):\n    return re.sub(r\"\\s+([.,!?;:])\", r\"\\1\", \" \".join(tokens))\n\n\ndef load_sentences(path):\n    text = open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\").read().lower()\n    sents = [TOKEN_RE.findall(c) for c in SENT_SPLIT.split(text)]\n    return [s for s in sents if len(s) >= 2]\n\n\nclass Vocab:\n    def __init__(self, sents, min_count=1):\n        counts = Counter(t for s in sents for t in s)\n        kept = sorted((t for t, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count),\n                      key=lambda t: (-counts[t], t))\n        self.itos = [PAD, UNK, BOS, EOS] + kept\n        self.stoi = {t: i for i, t in enumerate(self.itos)}\n        self.V = len(self.itos)\n        self.pad, self.unk, self.bos, self.eos = range(4)\n        self.counts = np.zeros(self.V)\n        for t in kept:\n            self.counts[self.stoi[t]] = counts[t]\n\n    def encode(self, toks):\n        return [self.stoi.get(t, self.unk) for t in toks]\n\n\nclass NGram:\n    \"\"\"Interpolated n-gram; order = number of previous tokens used.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, vocab, order=2, lam=0.7, k=0.01):\n        self.v, self.order, self.lam, self.k = vocab, order, lam, k\n        self.tables = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(order + 1)]\n\n    def fit(self, seqs):\n        for seq in seqs:\n            for t in range(1, len(seq)):\n                for n in range(min(self.order, t) + 1):\n                    self.tables[n][tuple(seq[t - n:t])][seq[t]] += 1\n        base = self.v.counts.copy()\n        base[self.v.eos] = len(seqs)\n        base += self.k\n        base[[self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]] = 0.0\n        self.base = base / base.sum()\n\n    def dist(self, ctx):\n        p = self.base\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\n        for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):  # shortest -> longest context\n            c = self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:] if n else ())\n            if c:\n                vec = np.zeros(self.v.V)\n                for tok, cnt in c.items():\n                    vec[tok] = cnt\n                p = self.lam * vec / vec.sum() + (1 - self.lam) * p\n        return p\n\n    def sample_next(self, ctx, temp, top_k):\n        p = self.dist(ctx).copy()\n        p[[self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]] = 0.0\n        if 0 < top_k < len(p):\n            p[p < np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]] = 0.0\n        p **= 1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3)\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))\n\n\ndef complete(model, vocab, prompt, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\n    \"\"\"Continue a prompt. Returns (text, oov_words).\"\"\"\n    toks = TOKEN_RE.findall(prompt.lower())\n    if not toks:\n        raise ValueError(\"prompt has no usable tokens\")\n    ids = vocab.encode(toks)\n    oov = [t for t, i in zip(toks, ids) if i == vocab.unk]\n    ctx, out = [vocab.bos] + ids, []\n    for _ in range(max_len):\n        nxt = model.sample_next(ctx, temp, top_k)\n        if nxt == vocab.eos:\n            break\n        out.append(vocab.itos[nxt])\n        ctx.append(nxt)\n    return detok(toks + out), oov\n\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"path\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--order\", type=int, default=2)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--min-count\", type=int, default=1)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--n\", type=int, default=5, help=\"completions per prompt\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--temp\", type=float, default=0.9)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--top-k\", type=int, default=40)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--max-len\", type=int, default=40)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--prompt\", default=None)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--interactive\", action=\"store_true\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=42)\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    random.seed(args.seed)\n    np.random.seed(args.seed)\n\n    sents = load_sentences(args.path)\n    vocab = Vocab(sents, args.min_count)\n    model = NGram(vocab, args.order)\n    model.fit([[vocab.bos] + vocab.encode(s) + [vocab.eos] for s in sents])\n\n    def run(prompt):\n        oov = set()\n        for _ in range(args.n):\n            text, o = complete(model, vocab, prompt, args.max_len, args.temp, args.top_k)\n            oov.update(o)\n            print(\" \", text)\n        if oov:\n            print(f\"  (not in vocab, treated as <unk>: {sorted(oov)})\")\n\n    if args.prompt:\n        run(args.prompt)\n    if args.interactive or not args.prompt:\n        print(\"Type a prompt (empty line to quit).\")\n        while True:\n            try:\n                p = input(\"> \").strip()\n            except EOFError:\n                break\n            if not p:\n                break\n            try:\n                run(p)\n            except ValueError as e:\n                print(\" \", e)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\nEOF\ncd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \"the cat sat\" --n 3 </dev/null", "description": "Rewrite compact prompts-only script and test"}, "message": "Rewrite compact prompts-only script and test", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cat > /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py <<'EOF'\\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Markov text model with prompt completion.\\n\\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --prompt \\\"once upon a\\\" --n 3\\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --interactive\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport argparse\\nimport random\\nimport re\\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nPAD, UNK, BOS, EOS = \\\"<pad>\\\", \\\"<unk>\\\", \\\"<bos>\\\", \\\"<eos>\\\"\\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\\\"[a-z0-9']+|[.,!?;:]\\\")\\nSENT_SPLIT = re.compile(r\\\"(?<=[.!?])\\\\s+|\\\\n{2,}\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef detok(tokens):\\n    return re.sub(r\\\"\\\\s+([.,!?;:])\\\", r\\\"\\\\1\\\", \\\" \\\".join(tokens))\\n\\n\\ndef load_sentences(path):\\n    text = open(path, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\").read().lower()\\n    sents = [TOKEN_RE.findall(c) for c in SENT_SPLIT.split(text)]\\n    return [s for s in sents if len(s) >= 2]\\n\\n\\nclass Vocab:\\n    def __init__(self, sents, min_count=1):\\n        counts = Counter(t for s in sents for t in s)\\n        kept = sorted((t for t, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count),\\n                      key=lambda t: (-counts[t], t))\\n        self.itos = [PAD, UNK, BOS, EOS] + kept\\n        self.stoi = {t: i for i, t in enumerate(self.itos)}\\n        self.V = len(self.itos)\\n        self.pad, self.unk, self.bos, self.eos = range(4)\\n        self.counts = np.zeros(self.V)\\n        for t in kept:\\n            self.counts[self.stoi[t]] = counts[t]\\n\\n    def encode(self, toks):\\n        return [self.stoi.get(t, self.unk) for t in toks]\\n\\n\\nclass NGram:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Interpolated n-gram; order = number of previous tokens used.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, vocab, order=2, lam=0.7, k=0.01):\\n        self.v, self.order, self.lam, self.k = vocab, order, lam, k\\n        self.tables = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(order + 1)]\\n\\n    def fit(self, seqs):\\n        for seq in seqs:\\n            for t in range(1, len(seq)):\\n                for n in range(min(self.order, t) + 1):\\n                    self.tables[n][tuple(seq[t - n:t])][seq[t]] += 1\\n        base = self.v.counts.copy()\\n        base[self.v.eos] = len(seqs)\\n        base += self.k\\n        base[[self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]] = 0.0\\n        self.base = base / base.sum()\\n\\n    def dist(self, ctx):\\n        p = self.base\\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\\n        for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):  # shortest -> longest context\\n            c = self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:] if n else ())\\n            if c:\\n                vec = np.zeros(self.v.V)\\n                for tok, cnt in c.items():\\n                    vec[tok] = cnt\\n                p = self.lam * vec / vec.sum() + (1 - self.lam) * p\\n        return p\\n\\n    def sample_next(self, ctx, temp, top_k):\\n        p = self.dist(ctx).copy()\\n        p[[self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]] = 0.0\\n        if 0 < top_k < len(p):\\n            p[p < np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]] = 0.0\\n        p **= 1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3)\\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))\\n\\n\\ndef complete(model, vocab, prompt, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Continue a prompt. Returns (text, oov_words).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    toks = TOKEN_RE.findall(prompt.lower())\\n    if not toks:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"prompt has no usable tokens\\\")\\n    ids = vocab.encode(toks)\\n    oov = [t for t, i in zip(toks, ids) if i == vocab.unk]\\n    ctx, out = [vocab.bos] + ids, []\\n    for _ in range(max_len):\\n        nxt = model.sample_next(ctx, temp, top_k)\\n        if nxt == vocab.eos:\\n            break\\n        out.append(vocab.itos[nxt])\\n        ctx.append(nxt)\\n    return detok(toks + out), oov\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"path\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--order\\\", type=int, default=2)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--min-count\\\", type=int, default=1)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--n\\\", type=int, default=5, help=\\\"completions per prompt\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--temp\\\", type=float, default=0.9)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--top-k\\\", type=int, default=40)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--max-len\\\", type=int, default=40)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--prompt\\\", default=None)\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--interactive\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\")\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--seed\\\", type=int, default=42)\\n    args = ap.parse_args()\\n    random.seed(args.seed)\\n    np.random.seed(args.seed)\\n\\n    sents = load_sentences(args.path)\\n    vocab = Vocab(sents, args.min_count)\\n    model = NGram(vocab, args.order)\\n    model.fit([[vocab.bos] + vocab.encode(s) + [vocab.eos] for s in sents])\\n\\n    def run(prompt):\\n        oov = set()\\n        for _ in range(args.n):\\n            text, o = complete(model, vocab, prompt, args.max_len, args.temp, args.top_k)\\n            oov.update(o)\\n            print(\\\" \\\", text)\\n        if oov:\\n            print(f\\\"  (not in vocab, treated as <unk>: {sorted(oov)})\\\")\\n\\n    if args.prompt:\\n        run(args.prompt)\\n    if args.interactive or not args.prompt:\\n        print(\\\"Type a prompt (empty line to quit).\\\")\\n        while True:\\n            try:\\n                p = input(\\\"> \\\").strip()\\n            except EOFError:\\n                break\\n            if not p:\\n                break\\n            try:\\n                run(p)\\n            except ValueError as e:\\n                print(\\\" \\\", e)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\nEOF\\ncd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \\\"the cat sat\\\" --n 3 </dev/null\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T23:06:45.463925Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T23:06:45.463982Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_017xfzF1R1xCZ9av78weyHDd", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"  the cat sat on an empty road.\\n  the cat sat on an empty road. a quiet river a tall woman looked at the big tree at night.\\n  the cat sat on a broken fence in the morning..\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"  the cat sat on an empty road.\\n  the cat sat on an empty road. a quiet river a tall woman looked at the big tree at night.\\n  the cat sat on a broken fence in the morning..\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T23:06:46.640135Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T23:06:46.865226Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Y4rZbzipQTP8Y3y2EVpTmU", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T23:06:46.885803Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T23:06:46.885838Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Y4rZbzipQTP8Y3y2EVpTmU", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py", "name": "markov gen", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-02T23:06:48.743936Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-02T23:06:48.756051Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I trimmed the script to just the prompt feature, about 130 lines. I removed the backward chain, the seed-word generation, the perplexity evaluation and the encodings.\n\nRun it with `--prompt \"once upon a\" --n 3`, or use `--interactive`. With no arguments besides the file, it drops into the interactive loop.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-02T23:06:48.839779Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T23:06:48.839779Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fede-7f57-7a83-bc25-bbe659b55462"}, {"uuid": "01a0ff4f-fbaf-7abb-92aa-d53658909f0e", "text": "make the math more compact and condensed into one function", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:05.054353Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:05.054353Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "make the math more compact and condensed into one function", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-03T01:12:05.054534Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:12:05.054534Z", "attachments": [{"file_name": "", "file_size": 5140, "file_type": "txt", "extracted_content": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\r\n\"\"\"Markov text model with prompt completion.\r\n\r\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --prompt \"once upon a\" --n 3\r\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --interactive\r\n\"\"\"\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport random\r\nimport re\r\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\r\n\r\nimport numpy as np\r\n\r\nPAD, UNK, BOS, EOS = \"<pad>\", \"<unk>\", \"<bos>\", \"\"\r\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[a-z0-9']+|[.,!?;:]\")\r\nSENT_SPLIT = re.compile(r\"(?<=[.!?])\\s+|\\n{2,}\")\r\n\r\n\r\ndef detok(tokens):\r\n    return re.sub(r\"\\s+([.,!?;:])\", r\"\\1\", \" \".join(tokens))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_sentences(path):\r\n    text = open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\").read().lower()\r\n    sents = [TOKEN_RE.findall(c) for c in SENT_SPLIT.split(text)]\r\n    return [s for s in sents if len(s) >= 2]\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Vocab:\r\n    def __init__(self, sents, min_count=1):\r\n        counts = Counter(t for s in sents for t in s)\r\n        kept = sorted((t for t, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count),\r\n                      key=lambda t: (-counts[t], t))\r\n        self.itos = [PAD, UNK, BOS, EOS] + kept\r\n        self.stoi = {t: i for i, t in enumerate(self.itos)}\r\n        self.V = len(self.itos)\r\n        self.pad, self.unk, self.bos, self.eos = range(4)\r\n        self.counts = np.zeros(self.V)\r\n        for t in kept:\r\n            self.counts[self.stoi[t]] = counts[t]\r\n\r\n    def encode(self, toks):\r\n        return [self.stoi.get(t, self.unk) for t in toks]\r\n\r\n\r\nclass NGram:\r\n    \"\"\"Interpolated n-gram; order = number of previous tokens used.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, vocab, order=2, lam=0.7, k=0.01):\r\n        self.v, self.order, self.lam, self.k = vocab, order, lam, k\r\n        self.tables = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(order + 1)]\r\n\r\n    def fit(self, seqs):\r\n        for seq in seqs:\r\n            for t in range(1, len(seq)):\r\n                for n in range(min(self.order, t) + 1):\r\n                    self.tables[n][tuple(seq[t - n:t])][seq[t]] += 1\r\n        base = self.v.counts.copy()\r\n        base[self.v.eos] = len(seqs)\r\n        base += self.k\r\n        base[[self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]] = 0.0\r\n        self.base = base / base.sum()\r\n\r\n    def dist(self, ctx):\r\n        p = self.base\r\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\r\n        for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):  # shortest -> longest context\r\n            c = self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:] if n else ())\r\n            if c:\r\n                vec = np.zeros(self.v.V)\r\n                for tok, cnt in c.items():\r\n                    vec[tok] = cnt\r\n                p = self.lam * vec / vec.sum() + (1 - self.lam) * p\r\n        return p\r\n\r\n    def sample_next(self, ctx, temp, top_k):\r\n        p = self.dist(ctx).copy()\r\n        p[[self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]] = 0.0\r\n        if 0 < top_k < len(p):\r\n            p[p < np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]] = 0.0\r\n        p **= 1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3)\r\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef complete(model, vocab, prompt, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\r\n    \"\"\"Continue a prompt. Returns (text, oov_words).\"\"\"\r\n    toks = TOKEN_RE.findall(prompt.lower())\r\n    if not toks:\r\n        raise ValueError(\"prompt has no usable tokens\")\r\n    ids = vocab.encode(toks)\r\n    oov = [t for t, i in zip(toks, ids) if i == vocab.unk]\r\n    ctx, out = [vocab.bos] + ids, []\r\n    for _ in range(max_len):\r\n        nxt = model.sample_next(ctx, temp, top_k)\r\n\r\n        out.append(vocab.itos[nxt])\r\n        ctx.append(nxt)\r\n    return detok(toks + out), oov\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main():\r\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"path\")\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--order\", type=int, default=2)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--min-count\", type=int, default=1)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--n\", type=int, default=1, help=\"completions per prompt\")\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--temp\", type=float, default=0.9)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--top-k\", type=int, default=40)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--max-len\", type=int, default=400)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--prompt\", default=None)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--interactive\", action=\"store_true\")\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=42)\r\n    args = ap.parse_args()\r\n    random.seed(args.seed)\r\n    np.random.seed(args.seed)\r\n\r\n    sents = load_sentences(args.path)\r\n    vocab = Vocab(sents, args.min_count)\r\n    model = NGram(vocab, args.order)\r\n    model.fit([[vocab.bos] + vocab.encode(s) + [vocab.eos] for s in sents])\r\n\r\n    def run(prompt):\r\n        oov = set()\r\n        for _ in range(args.n):\r\n            text, o = complete(model, vocab, prompt, args.max_len, args.temp, args.top_k)\r\n            oov.update(o)\r\n            print(\" \", text)\r\n        if oov:\r\n            print(f\"  (not in vocab, treated as <unk>: {sorted(oov)})\")\r\n\r\n    if args.prompt:\r\n        run(args.prompt)\r\n    if args.interactive or not args.prompt:\r\n        print(\"Type a prompt (empty line to quit).\")\r\n        while True:\r\n            try:\r\n                p = input(\"> \").strip()\r\n            except EOFError:\r\n                break\r\n            if not p:\r\n                break\r\n            try:\r\n                run(p)\r\n            except ValueError as e:\r\n                print(\" \", e)\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\n"}], "files": [{"file_uuid": "0411d0e6-1128-42fa-bf67-b0b765168cf2", "file_name": ""}], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0fede-7f57-7dae-a3a6-a7f8a0439e12"}, {"uuid": "01a0ff4f-fbaf-794e-a82c-70d87c2c6ecb", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI moved all the probability math into one method, `NGram.sample_next`. `fit` now only counts n-grams.\n\n```python\ndef sample_next(self, ctx, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\n    \"\"\"add-k unigram base -> interpolate n=1..order contexts -> top-k -> temp -> sample.\"\"\"\n    v, bad = self.v, [self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]\n    ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\n    p = v.counts + self.k\n    p[v.eos] = self.tables[0][()][v.eos] + self.k\n    p[bad] = 0.0\n    p /= p.sum()\n    for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):  # shortest -> longest context\n        if c := self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:]):\n            vec = np.zeros(v.V)\n            vec[list(c)] = list(c.values())\n            p = self.lam * vec / vec.sum() + (1 - self.lam) * p\n    p[bad] = 0.0\n    if 0 < top_k < len(p):\n        p[p < np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]] = 0.0\n    p **= 1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3)\n    return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))\n```\n\n- **Merged methods:** `dist` and the old `sample_next` are now one method.\n- **Unigram base:** it is rebuilt each call from the unigram counts and the `<eos>` count already in the n-gram table, so the base math no longer lives in `fit`.\n- **Your edits:** I kept them: `EOS = \"\"`, no stop at `<eos>`, `--n` defaulting to 1, and `--max-len` defaulting to 400.\n- **Updated file:** the file is updated with the changes.\n\nBecause `EOS` is now an empty string, the model still emits it as a token, and it shows up as an extra space in the output. If you want that gone, filter empty tokens in `complete` (`out.append(...)` only when the token is non-empty).", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:04.930283Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:17.645570Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Investigating a config change enabling continuous text generation."}, {"summary": "Condensing the probability math into a single function."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:17.645637Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:21.675767Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_014CaPKUZtcsVNuxndx7RVde", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open(\"markov_gen.py\").read()\na = s.index(\"class NGram:\")\nb = s.index(\"def complete(\")\nnew = '''class NGram:\n    \"\"\"Interpolated n-gram; order = number of previous tokens used.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, vocab, order=2, lam=0.7, k=0.01):\n        self.v, self.order, self.lam, self.k = vocab, order, lam, k\n        self.tables = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(order + 1)]\n\n    def fit(self, seqs):\n        for seq in seqs:\n            for t in range(1, len(seq)):\n                for n in range(min(self.order, t) + 1):\n                    self.tables[n][tuple(seq[t - n:t])][seq[t]] += 1\n\n    def sample_next(self, ctx, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\n        \"\"\"add-k unigram base -> interpolate n=1..order contexts -> top-k -> temp -> sample.\"\"\"\n        v, bad = self.v, [self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\n        p = v.counts + self.k\n        p[v.eos] = self.tables[0][()][v.eos] + self.k\n        p[bad] = 0.0\n        p /= p.sum()\n        for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):  # shortest -> longest context\n            if c := self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:]):\n                vec = np.zeros(v.V)\n                vec[list(c)] = list(c.values())\n                p = self.lam * vec / vec.sum() + (1 - self.lam) * p\n        p[bad] = 0.0\n        if 0 < top_k < len(p):\n            p[p < np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]] = 0.0\n        p **= 1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3)\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))\n\n\n'''\ns = s[:a] + new + s[b:]\nopen(\"markov_gen.py\",\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n 'EOS = \\|max-len\\|\"--n\"' markov_gen.py; cd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \"the cat sat\" --max-len 25 </dev/null", "description": "Collapse probability math into one method and test"}, "message": "Collapse probability math into one method and test", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\ns = open(\\\"markov_gen.py\\\").read()\\na = s.index(\\\"class NGram:\\\")\\nb = s.index(\\\"def complete(\\\")\\nnew = '''class NGram:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Interpolated n-gram; order = number of previous tokens used.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, vocab, order=2, lam=0.7, k=0.01):\\n        self.v, self.order, self.lam, self.k = vocab, order, lam, k\\n        self.tables = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(order + 1)]\\n\\n    def fit(self, seqs):\\n        for seq in seqs:\\n            for t in range(1, len(seq)):\\n                for n in range(min(self.order, t) + 1):\\n                    self.tables[n][tuple(seq[t - n:t])][seq[t]] += 1\\n\\n    def sample_next(self, ctx, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"add-k unigram base -> interpolate n=1..order contexts -> top-k -> temp -> sample.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        v, bad = self.v, [self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]\\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\\n        p = v.counts + self.k\\n        p[v.eos] = self.tables[0][()][v.eos] + self.k\\n        p[bad] = 0.0\\n        p /= p.sum()\\n        for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):  # shortest -> longest context\\n            if c := self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:]):\\n                vec = np.zeros(v.V)\\n                vec[list(c)] = list(c.values())\\n                p = self.lam * vec / vec.sum() + (1 - self.lam) * p\\n        p[bad] = 0.0\\n        if 0 < top_k < len(p):\\n            p[p < np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]] = 0.0\\n        p **= 1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3)\\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))\\n\\n\\n'''\\ns = s[:a] + new + s[b:]\\nopen(\\\"markov_gen.py\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(s)\\nEOF\\ngrep -n 'EOS = \\\\|max-len\\\\|\\\"--n\\\"' markov_gen.py; cd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \\\"the cat sat\\\" --max-len 25 </dev/null\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:23.008093Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:23.008128Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_014CaPKUZtcsVNuxndx7RVde", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"14:PAD, UNK, BOS, EOS = \\\"<pad>\\\", \\\"<unk>\\\", \\\"<bos>\\\", \\\"<eos>\\\"\\n101:    ap.add_argument(\\\"--n\\\", type=int, default=5, help=\\\"completions per prompt\\\")\\n104:    ap.add_argument(\\\"--max-len\\\", type=int, default=40)\\n  the cat sat on an empty road.\\n  the cat sat on an empty road. a quiet river a tall woman looked at the big tree at night.\\n  the cat sat on a broken fence in the morning..\\n  the cat sat on the red house.\\n  the cat sat toward an empty road at night.\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"14:PAD, UNK, BOS, EOS = \\\"<pad>\\\", \\\"<unk>\\\", \\\"<bos>\\\", \\\"<eos>\\\"\\n101:    ap.add_argument(\\\"--n\\\", type=int, default=5, help=\\\"completions per prompt\\\")\\n104:    ap.add_argument(\\\"--max-len\\\", type=int, default=40)\\n  the cat sat on an empty road.\\n  the cat sat on an empty road. a quiet river a tall woman looked at the big tree at night.\\n  the cat sat on a broken fence in the morning..\\n  the cat sat on the red house.\\n  the cat sat toward an empty road at night.\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:25.714362Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:27.179304Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_015FBrVWfwa3JrQG1KXeN5J9", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open(\"markov_gen.py\").read()\ns = s.replace('\"<bos>\", \"<eos>\"', '\"<bos>\", \"\"')\ns = s.replace('''        nxt = model.sample_next(ctx, temp, top_k)\n        if nxt == vocab.eos:\n            break\n''', '''        nxt = model.sample_next(ctx, temp, top_k)\n\n''')\ns = s.replace('\"--n\", type=int, default=5', '\"--n\", type=int, default=1')\ns = s.replace('\"--max-len\", type=int, default=40)', '\"--max-len\", type=int, default=400)')\nopen(\"markov_gen.py\",\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 45,70p markov_gen.py; cd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \"the cat sat\" --max-len 25 </dev/null", "description": "Restore the user's edits and retest"}, "message": "Restore the user's edits and retest", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\ns = open(\\\"markov_gen.py\\\").read()\\ns = s.replace('\\\"<bos>\\\", \\\"<eos>\\\"', '\\\"<bos>\\\", \\\"\\\"')\\ns = s.replace('''        nxt = model.sample_next(ctx, temp, top_k)\\n        if nxt == vocab.eos:\\n            break\\n''', '''        nxt = model.sample_next(ctx, temp, top_k)\\n\\n''')\\ns = s.replace('\\\"--n\\\", type=int, default=5', '\\\"--n\\\", type=int, default=1')\\ns = s.replace('\\\"--max-len\\\", type=int, default=40)', '\\\"--max-len\\\", type=int, default=400)')\\nopen(\\\"markov_gen.py\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(s)\\nEOF\\nsed -n 45,70p markov_gen.py; cd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \\\"the cat sat\\\" --max-len 25 </dev/null\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:27.538094Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:27.538139Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_015FBrVWfwa3JrQG1KXeN5J9", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"\\nclass NGram:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Interpolated n-gram; order = number of previous tokens used.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, vocab, order=2, lam=0.7, k=0.01):\\n        self.v, self.order, self.lam, self.k = vocab, order, lam, k\\n        self.tables = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(order + 1)]\\n\\n    def fit(self, seqs):\\n        for seq in seqs:\\n            for t in range(1, len(seq)):\\n                for n in range(min(self.order, t) + 1):\\n                    self.tables[n][tuple(seq[t - n:t])][seq[t]] += 1\\n\\n    def sample_next(self, ctx, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"add-k unigram base -> interpolate n=1..order contexts -> top-k -> temp -> sample.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        v, bad = self.v, [self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]\\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\\n        p = v.counts + self.k\\n        p[v.eos] = self.tables[0][()][v.eos] + self.k\\n        p[bad] = 0.0\\n        p /= p.sum()\\n        for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):  # shortest -> longest context\\n            if c := self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:]):\\n                vec = np.zeros(v.V)\\n                vec[list(c)] = list(c.values())\\n  the cat sat on an empty road.   man sat on the red house a tall woman ran toward the green hill.  a sound\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"\\nclass NGram:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Interpolated n-gram; order = number of previous tokens used.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, vocab, order=2, lam=0.7, k=0.01):\\n        self.v, self.order, self.lam, self.k = vocab, order, lam, k\\n        self.tables = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(order + 1)]\\n\\n    def fit(self, seqs):\\n        for seq in seqs:\\n            for t in range(1, len(seq)):\\n                for n in range(min(self.order, t) + 1):\\n                    self.tables[n][tuple(seq[t - n:t])][seq[t]] += 1\\n\\n    def sample_next(self, ctx, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"add-k unigram base -> interpolate n=1..order contexts -> top-k -> temp -> sample.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        v, bad = self.v, [self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]\\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\\n        p = v.counts + self.k\\n        p[v.eos] = self.tables[0][()][v.eos] + self.k\\n        p[bad] = 0.0\\n        p /= p.sum()\\n        for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):  # shortest -> longest context\\n            if c := self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:]):\\n                vec = np.zeros(v.V)\\n                vec[list(c)] = list(c.values())\\n  the cat sat on an empty road.   man sat on the red house a tall woman ran toward the green hill.  a sound\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:32.433224Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:32.439530Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I moved all the probability math into one method, `NGram.sample_next`. `fit` now only counts n-grams.\n\n```python\ndef sample_next(self, ctx, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\n    \"\"\"add-k unigram base -> interpolate n=1..order contexts -> top-k -> temp -> sample.\"\"\"\n    v, bad = self.v, [self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]\n    ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\n    p = v.counts + self.k\n    p[v.eos] = self.tables[0][()][v.eos] + self.k\n    p[bad] = 0.0\n    p /= p.sum()\n    for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):  # shortest -> longest context\n        if c := self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:]):\n            vec = np.zeros(v.V)\n            vec[list(c)] = list(c.values())\n            p = self.lam * vec / vec.sum() + (1 - self.lam) * p\n    p[bad] = 0.0\n    if 0 < top_k < len(p):\n        p[p < np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]] = 0.0\n    p **= 1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3)\n    return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))\n```\n\n- **Merged methods:** `dist` and the old `sample_next` are now one method.\n- **Unigram base:** it is rebuilt each call from the unigram counts and the `<eos>` count already in the n-gram table, so the base math no longer lives in `fit`.\n- **Your edits:** I kept them: `EOS = \"\"`, no stop at `<eos>`, `--n` defaulting to 1, and `--max-len` defaulting to 400.\n- **Updated file:** the file is updated with the changes.\n\nBecause `EOS` is now an empty string, the model still emits it as a token, and it shows up as an extra space in the output. If you want that gone, filter empty tokens in `complete` (`out.append(...)` only when the token is non-empty).", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-03T01:12:32.513341Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:12:32.513341Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0ff4f-fbaf-7abb-92aa-d53658909f0e"}, {"uuid": "01a0ff52-0e6d-7580-bf86-4fbffd8cafcd", "text": "do the full code", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:43.694202Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:43.694202Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "do the full code", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-03T01:12:43.694425Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:12:43.694425Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0ff4f-fbaf-794e-a82c-70d87c2c6ecb"}, {"uuid": "01a0ff52-0e6d-7118-bb03-3c6f53787d0c", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThe full file is above. It has the single `sample_next` method for all the probability math, and your earlier edits are kept: `EOS = \"\"`, no stop at `<eos>`, `--n` defaulting to 1 and `--max-len` defaulting to 400.\n\nI haven't changed anything else. If \"full code\" meant the bigger version with backward generation, seed-word generation and perplexity, say so and I'll rebuild that with the compact math.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:43.694020Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:47.227209Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Restoring the full version after the compact edit."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:47.227313Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:47.281084Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Y45PAWfLRShujpdYU57sSi", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:47.304790Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:47.304819Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Y45PAWfLRShujpdYU57sSi", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py", "name": "markov gen", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:49.542637Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:12:49.549195Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "The full file is above. It has the single `sample_next` method for all the probability math, and your earlier edits are kept: `EOS = \"\"`, no stop at `<eos>`, `--n` defaulting to 1 and `--max-len` defaulting to 400.\n\nI haven't changed anything else. If \"full code\" meant the bigger version with backward generation, seed-word generation and perplexity, say so and I'll rebuild that with the compact math.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-03T01:12:49.559821Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:12:49.559821Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0ff52-0e6d-7580-bf86-4fbffd8cafcd"}, {"uuid": "01a0ff52-6296-7387-a82e-f1f465b5dbe5", "text": "where is sorted, exp and log", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:13:04.973301Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:13:04.973301Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "where is sorted, exp and log", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-03T01:13:04.973531Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:13:04.973531Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0ff52-0e6d-7118-bb03-3c6f53787d0c"}, {"uuid": "01a0ff52-6296-76da-9e47-2a685b372acb", "text": "`sorted` is in `Vocab.__init__`. It orders the tokens by frequency (descending), then alphabetically, so the ids are stable:\n\n```python\nkept = sorted((t for t, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count),\n              key=lambda t: (-counts[t], t))\n```\n\n`exp` and `log` aren't in the compact file. They were only in the bigger version, in `logprob`, `perplexity` and `unigram_entropy`, which I removed when you asked to keep just prompts.\n\nThe one place the math touches them is the temperature line, which uses a power instead:\n\n```python\np **= 1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3)\n```\n\nThat equals `exp(log(p) / temp)`. If you'd rather see it written that way, or want the perplexity and entropy functions back in the compact style, I can add either.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:13:04.964756Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:13:06.154705Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Locating where sorted, exp, and log are defined."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:13:06.154750Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:13:07.865171Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "`sorted` is in `Vocab.__init__`. It orders the tokens by frequency (descending), then alphabetically, so the ids are stable:\n\n```python\nkept = sorted((t for t, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count),\n              key=lambda t: (-counts[t], t))\n```\n\n`exp` and `log` aren't in the compact file. They were only in the bigger version, in `logprob`, `perplexity` and `unigram_entropy`, which I removed when you asked to keep just prompts.\n\nThe one place the math touches them is the temperature line, which uses a power instead:\n\n```python\np **= 1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3)\n```\n\nThat equals `exp(log(p) / temp)`. If you'd rather see it written that way, or want the perplexity and entropy functions back in the compact style, I can add either.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-03T01:13:07.880772Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:13:07.880772Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0ff52-6296-7387-a82e-f1f465b5dbe5"}, {"uuid": "01a0ff56-da57-7d87-9edb-a58b38d5a068", "text": "theres no exp or log", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:17:58.352331Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:17:58.352331Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "theres no exp or log", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-03T01:17:58.352536Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:17:58.352536Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0ff52-6296-76da-9e47-2a685b372acb"}, {"uuid": "01a0ff56-da57-7564-bf2a-de2d6bb85be4", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nYou're right, the file had no `exp` or `log`. I only used `**` for temperature. I've now added them to `sample_next`, and the file is updated:\n\n```python\nwith np.errstate(divide=\"ignore\"):\n    z = np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3)  # temperature in log space\np = np.exp(z - z.max())  # stable softmax; log(0) -> exp(-inf) = 0\n```\n\nThis gives the same result as the old `p **= 1/temp`. Tokens that were masked to zero stay at zero, because `log(0)` is `-inf` and `exp(-inf)` is 0.\n\n`sorted` was already there, in `Vocab.__init__`. It's also used on the OOV print line.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:17:58.352076Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:01.950574Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Adding missing exp and log functions to the code."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:01.950637Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:04.351943Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Gb92CRipcLbWmDvky6iz1n", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open(\"markov_gen.py\").read()\nold = '''        p **= 1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3)\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))'''\nnew = '''        with np.errstate(divide=\"ignore\"):\n            z = np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3)  # temperature in log space\n        p = np.exp(z - z.max())  # stable softmax; log(0) -> exp(-inf) = 0\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))'''\nassert old in s\nopen(\"markov_gen.py\",\"w\").write(s.replace(old,new))\nEOF\ngrep -n \"log\\|exp\\|sorted\" markov_gen.py; cd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \"the cat sat\" --max-len 20 </dev/null", "description": "Add explicit log/exp temperature step and test"}, "message": "Add explicit log/exp temperature step and test", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\ns = open(\\\"markov_gen.py\\\").read()\\nold = '''        p **= 1.0 / max(temp, 1e-3)\\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))'''\\nnew = '''        with np.errstate(divide=\\\"ignore\\\"):\\n            z = np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3)  # temperature in log space\\n        p = np.exp(z - z.max())  # stable softmax; log(0) -> exp(-inf) = 0\\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))'''\\nassert old in s\\nopen(\\\"markov_gen.py\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(s.replace(old,new))\\nEOF\\ngrep -n \\\"log\\\\|exp\\\\|sorted\\\" markov_gen.py; cd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \\\"the cat sat\\\" --max-len 20 </dev/null\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:05.749511Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:05.749548Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Gb92CRipcLbWmDvky6iz1n", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"32:        kept = sorted((t for t, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count),\\n76:            z = np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3)  # temperature in log space\\n77:        p = np.exp(z - z.max())  # stable softmax; log(0) -> exp(-inf) = 0\\n125:            print(f\\\"  (not in vocab, treated as <unk>: {sorted(oov)})\\\")\\n  the cat sat on an empty road.   man sat on the red house a tall woman ran toward the green\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"32:        kept = sorted((t for t, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count),\\n76:            z = np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3)  # temperature in log space\\n77:        p = np.exp(z - z.max())  # stable softmax; log(0) -> exp(-inf) = 0\\n125:            print(f\\\"  (not in vocab, treated as <unk>: {sorted(oov)})\\\")\\n  the cat sat on an empty road.   man sat on the red house a tall woman ran toward the green\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:08.437125Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:08.450249Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "You're right, the file had no `exp` or `log`. I only used `**` for temperature. I've now added them to `sample_next`, and the file is updated:\n\n```python\nwith np.errstate(divide=\"ignore\"):\n    z = np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3)  # temperature in log space\np = np.exp(z - z.max())  # stable softmax; log(0) -> exp(-inf) = 0\n```\n\nThis gives the same result as the old `p **= 1/temp`. Tokens that were masked to zero stay at zero, because `log(0)` is `-inf` and `exp(-inf)` is 0.\n\n`sorted` was already there, in `Vocab.__init__`. It's also used on the OOV print line.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-03T01:18:08.463598Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:18:08.463598Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0ff56-da57-7d87-9edb-a58b38d5a068"}, {"uuid": "01a0ff57-3e98-74a5-a635-322278156708", "text": "dont make it a softmax", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:27.776434Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:27.776434Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "dont make it a softmax", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-03T01:18:27.776565Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:18:27.776565Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0ff56-da57-7564-bf2a-de2d6bb85be4"}, {"uuid": "01a0ff57-3e98-7235-9d1d-3a5690a0a8a1", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nDone. I removed the max-subtraction, so the temperature step is now one line:\n\n```python\nwith np.errstate(divide=\"ignore\"):\n    p = np.exp(np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3))  # temperature: p**(1/temp)\n```\n\n`np.random.choice` still divides by `p.sum()`, since it needs probabilities that sum to 1. That is a plain normalization, not a softmax.\n\nWithout the shift, a very low `--temp` (around 0.01 or below) can make every value underflow to 0 and crash the sampler. Normal values like 0.5 to 1.5 are fine.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:27.776254Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:30.296798Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Adjusting the temperature scaling without softmax normalization."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:30.296847Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:31.761393Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_011GKga7MUvscdqtitanx8yB", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open(\"markov_gen.py\").read()\nold = '''        with np.errstate(divide=\"ignore\"):\n            z = np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3)  # temperature in log space\n        p = np.exp(z - z.max())  # stable softmax; log(0) -> exp(-inf) = 0\n'''\nnew = '''        with np.errstate(divide=\"ignore\"):\n            p = np.exp(np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3))  # temperature: p**(1/temp)\n'''\nassert old in s\nopen(\"markov_gen.py\",\"w\").write(s.replace(old,new))\nEOF\nsed -n 72,80p markov_gen.py; cd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \"the cat sat\" --max-len 20 </dev/null", "description": "Replace softmax form with plain exp(log(p)/temp)"}, "message": "Replace softmax form with plain exp(log(p)/temp)", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\ns = open(\\\"markov_gen.py\\\").read()\\nold = '''        with np.errstate(divide=\\\"ignore\\\"):\\n            z = np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3)  # temperature in log space\\n        p = np.exp(z - z.max())  # stable softmax; log(0) -> exp(-inf) = 0\\n'''\\nnew = '''        with np.errstate(divide=\\\"ignore\\\"):\\n            p = np.exp(np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3))  # temperature: p**(1/temp)\\n'''\\nassert old in s\\nopen(\\\"markov_gen.py\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(s.replace(old,new))\\nEOF\\nsed -n 72,80p markov_gen.py; cd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \\\"the cat sat\\\" --max-len 20 </dev/null\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:32.173005Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:32.173048Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_011GKga7MUvscdqtitanx8yB", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"        p[bad] = 0.0\\n        if 0 < top_k < len(p):\\n            p[p < np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]] = 0.0\\n        with np.errstate(divide=\\\"ignore\\\"):\\n            p = np.exp(np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3))  # temperature: p**(1/temp)\\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))\\n\\n\\ndef complete(model, vocab, prompt, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\\n  the cat sat on an empty road.   man sat on the red house a tall woman ran toward the green\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"        p[bad] = 0.0\\n        if 0 < top_k < len(p):\\n            p[p < np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]] = 0.0\\n        with np.errstate(divide=\\\"ignore\\\"):\\n            p = np.exp(np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3))  # temperature: p**(1/temp)\\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))\\n\\n\\ndef complete(model, vocab, prompt, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\\n  the cat sat on an empty road.   man sat on the red house a tall woman ran toward the green\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:36.206088Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:18:36.216818Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Done. I removed the max-subtraction, so the temperature step is now one line:\n\n```python\nwith np.errstate(divide=\"ignore\"):\n    p = np.exp(np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3))  # temperature: p**(1/temp)\n```\n\n`np.random.choice` still divides by `p.sum()`, since it needs probabilities that sum to 1. That is a plain normalization, not a softmax.\n\nWithout the shift, a very low `--temp` (around 0.01 or below) can make every value underflow to 0 and crash the sampler. Normal values like 0.5 to 1.5 are fine.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-03T01:18:36.228407Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:18:36.228407Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0ff57-3e98-74a5-a635-322278156708"}, {"uuid": "01a0ff60-3143-7450-8681-d202de6b60b5", "text": "> what are you?\n  operands could not be broadcast together with shapes (17455,) (2,)", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:28:10.190045Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:28:10.190045Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "> what are you?\n  operands could not be broadcast together with shapes (17455,) (2,)", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-03T01:28:10.190238Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:28:10.190238Z", "attachments": [{"file_name": "", "file_size": 4998, "file_type": "txt", "extracted_content": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\r\n\"\"\"Markov text model with prompt completion.\r\n\r\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --prompt \"once upon a\" --n 3\r\n  python markov_gen.py data.txt --interactive\r\n\"\"\"\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport random\r\nimport re\r\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\r\n\r\nimport numpy as np\r\n\r\nPAD, UNK, BOS, EOS = \"<pad>\", \"<unk>\", \"<bos>\", \"\"\r\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[a-z0-9']+|[.,!?;:]\")\r\nSENT_SPLIT = re.compile(r\"(?<=[.!?])\\s+|\\n{2,}\")\r\n\r\n\r\ndef detok(tokens):\r\n    return re.sub(r\"\\s+([.,!?;:])\", r\"\\1\", \" \".join(tokens))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_sentences(path):\r\n    text = open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\").read().lower()\r\n    sents = [TOKEN_RE.findall(c) for c in SENT_SPLIT.split(text)]\r\n    return [s for s in sents if len(s) >= 2]\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Vocab:\r\n    def __init__(self, sents, min_count=1):\r\n        counts = Counter(t for s in sents for t in s)\r\n        kept = sorted((t for t, c in counts.items() if c >= min_count),\r\n                      key=lambda t: (-counts[t], t))\r\n        self.itos = [PAD, UNK, BOS, EOS] + kept\r\n        self.stoi = {t: i for i, t in enumerate(self.itos)}\r\n        self.V = len(self.itos)\r\n        self.pad, self.unk, self.bos, self.eos = range(4)\r\n        self.counts = np.zeros(self.V)\r\n        for t in kept:\r\n            self.counts[self.stoi[t]] = counts[t]\r\n\r\n    def encode(self, toks):\r\n        return [self.stoi.get(t, self.unk) for t in toks]\r\n\r\n\r\nclass NGram:\r\n    \"\"\"Interpolated n-gram; order = number of previous tokens used.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, vocab, order=2, lam=0.7, k=0.01):\r\n        self.v, self.order, self.lam, self.k = vocab, order, lam, k\r\n        self.tables = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(order + 1)]\r\n\r\n    def fit(self, seqs):\r\n        for seq in seqs:\r\n            for t in range(1, len(seq)):\r\n                for n in range(min(self.order, t) + 1):\r\n                    self.tables[n][tuple(seq[t - n:t])][seq[t]] += 1\r\n\r\n    def sample_next(self, ctx, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\r\n        \"\"\"add-k unigram base -> interpolate n=1..order contexts -> top-k -> temp -> sample.\"\"\"\r\n        v, bad = self.v, [self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]\r\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\r\n        p = v.counts + self.k\r\n        p[v.eos] = self.tables[0][()][v.eos] + self.k\r\n        p[bad] = 0.0\r\n        p /= p.sum()\r\n        for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):  # shortest -> longest context\r\n            if c := self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:]):\r\n                vec = np.zeros(v.V)\r\n                vec[list(c)] = list(c.values())\r\n                p = self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:]) if np.where(np.sin(vec / vec.sum() + (1 - self.lam)) > np.exp(np.log(ctx) / max(temp, 1e-3))) else 0.0\r\n\r\n        \r\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef complete(model, vocab, prompt, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\r\n    \"\"\"Continue a prompt. Returns (text, oov_words).\"\"\"\r\n    toks = TOKEN_RE.findall(prompt.lower())\r\n    if not toks:\r\n        raise ValueError(\"prompt has no usable tokens\")\r\n    ids = vocab.encode(toks)\r\n    oov = [t for t, i in zip(toks, ids) if i == vocab.unk]\r\n    ctx, out = [vocab.bos] + ids, []\r\n    for _ in range(max_len):\r\n        nxt = model.sample_next(ctx, temp, top_k)\r\n\r\n        out.append(vocab.itos[nxt])\r\n        ctx.append(nxt)\r\n    return detok(toks + out), oov\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main():\r\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"path\")\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--order\", type=int, default=2)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--min-count\", type=int, default=1)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--n\", type=int, default=1, help=\"completions per prompt\")\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--temp\", type=float, default=0.9)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--top-k\", type=int, default=40)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--max-len\", type=int, default=400)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--prompt\", default=None)\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--interactive\", action=\"store_true\")\r\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=42)\r\n    args = ap.parse_args()\r\n    random.seed(args.seed)\r\n    np.random.seed(args.seed)\r\n\r\n    sents = load_sentences(args.path)\r\n    vocab = Vocab(sents, args.min_count)\r\n    model = NGram(vocab, args.order)\r\n    model.fit([[vocab.bos] + vocab.encode(s) + [vocab.eos] for s in sents])\r\n\r\n    def run(prompt):\r\n        oov = set()\r\n        for _ in range(args.n):\r\n            text, o = complete(model, vocab, prompt, args.max_len, args.temp, args.top_k)\r\n            oov.update(o)\r\n            print(\" \", text)\r\n        if oov:\r\n            print(f\"  (not in vocab, treated as <unk>: {sorted(oov)})\")\r\n\r\n    if args.prompt:\r\n        run(args.prompt)\r\n    if args.interactive or not args.prompt:\r\n        print(\"Type a prompt (empty line to quit).\")\r\n        while True:\r\n            try:\r\n                p = input(\"> \").strip()\r\n            except EOFError:\r\n                break\r\n            if not p:\r\n                break\r\n            try:\r\n                run(p)\r\n            except ValueError as e:\r\n                print(\" \", e)\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\n"}], "files": [{"file_uuid": "1795b8e2-ec4f-4ece-9eb7-8b6be524abf4", "file_name": ""}], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0ff57-3e98-7235-9d1d-3a5690a0a8a1"}, {"uuid": "01a0ff60-3143-798e-913e-0ce4044ed049", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThe error comes from the line you added inside the interpolation loop in `sample_next`:\n\n```python\np = self.tables[n].get(...) if np.where(np.sin(vec / vec.sum() + (1 - self.lam)) > np.exp(np.log(ctx) / max(temp, 1e-3))) else 0.0\n```\n\n- **The shape error:** `vec` has one entry per vocab word (17455), but `ctx` is the last two token ids, so `np.log(ctx)` has shape `(2,)`. Comparing the two is the broadcast error you saw.\n- **Wrong target for `log` and `exp`:** they're being applied to token ids. Temperature belongs on the probabilities `p`.\n- **`p` becomes a `Counter` or `0.0`:** this line replaces `p` with the table lookup or 0.0, so `np.random.choice(len(p), ...)` would fail even without the shape error.\n- **Missing steps:** the line also drops the interpolation, the masking and the top-k step.\n\nThe version in the file I gave you is correct, so use that one. With your prompt it runs and reports the OOV words:\n\n```\nwhat are you? a dog walked past the green hill without a sound. a quiet river a\n(not in vocab, treated as <unk>: ['?', 'are', 'what', 'you'])\n```\n\nThe loop body should just be:\n\n```python\np = self.lam * vec / vec.sum() + (1 - self.lam) * p\n```\n\nThe `log` and `exp` stay after the top-k step, as `p = np.exp(np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3))`. If you were trying to change the math, tell me what you want it to do and I'll fit it in.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:28:10.026201Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:28:15.817266Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Untangling a convoluted conditional expression in the loop."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:28:15.817343Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:28:16.319289Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01HcpmqmTtae3DtRwCeYF1ma", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude && sed -n 60,80p /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \"what are you?\" --max-len 15 </dev/null", "description": "Confirm the correct version runs with the failing prompt"}, "message": "Confirm the correct version runs with the failing prompt", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude && sed -n 60,80p /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \\\"what are you?\\\" --max-len 15 </dev/null\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:28:17.671586Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:28:17.671627Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01HcpmqmTtae3DtRwCeYF1ma", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"        \\\"\\\"\\\"add-k unigram base -> interpolate n=1..order contexts -> top-k -> temp -> sample.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        v, bad = self.v, [self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]\\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\\n        p = v.counts + self.k\\n        p[v.eos] = self.tables[0][()][v.eos] + self.k\\n        p[bad] = 0.0\\n        p /= p.sum()\\n        for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):  # shortest -> longest context\\n            if c := self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:]):\\n                vec = np.zeros(v.V)\\n                vec[list(c)] = list(c.values())\\n                p = self.lam * vec / vec.sum() + (1 - self.lam) * p\\n        p[bad] = 0.0\\n        if 0 < top_k < len(p):\\n            p[p < np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]] = 0.0\\n        with np.errstate(divide=\\\"ignore\\\"):\\n            p = np.exp(np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3))  # temperature: p**(1/temp)\\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))\\n\\n\\ndef complete(model, vocab, prompt, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\\n  what are you? a dog walked past the green hill without a sound. a quiet river a\\n  (not in vocab, treated as <unk>: ['?', 'are', 'what', 'you'])\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"        \\\"\\\"\\\"add-k unigram base -> interpolate n=1..order contexts -> top-k -> temp -> sample.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        v, bad = self.v, [self.v.pad, self.v.bos, self.v.unk]\\n        ctx = tuple(ctx[-self.order:]) if self.order else ()\\n        p = v.counts + self.k\\n        p[v.eos] = self.tables[0][()][v.eos] + self.k\\n        p[bad] = 0.0\\n        p /= p.sum()\\n        for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):  # shortest -> longest context\\n            if c := self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:]):\\n                vec = np.zeros(v.V)\\n                vec[list(c)] = list(c.values())\\n                p = self.lam * vec / vec.sum() + (1 - self.lam) * p\\n        p[bad] = 0.0\\n        if 0 < top_k < len(p):\\n            p[p < np.partition(p, -top_k)[-top_k]] = 0.0\\n        with np.errstate(divide=\\\"ignore\\\"):\\n            p = np.exp(np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3))  # temperature: p**(1/temp)\\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))\\n\\n\\ndef complete(model, vocab, prompt, max_len=40, temp=0.9, top_k=40):\\n  what are you? a dog walked past the green hill without a sound. a quiet river a\\n  (not in vocab, treated as <unk>: ['?', 'are', 'what', 'you'])\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:28:22.436544Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:28:22.446692Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "The error comes from the line you added inside the interpolation loop in `sample_next`:\n\n```python\np = self.tables[n].get(...) if np.where(np.sin(vec / vec.sum() + (1 - self.lam)) > np.exp(np.log(ctx) / max(temp, 1e-3))) else 0.0\n```\n\n- **The shape error:** `vec` has one entry per vocab word (17455), but `ctx` is the last two token ids, so `np.log(ctx)` has shape `(2,)`. Comparing the two is the broadcast error you saw.\n- **Wrong target for `log` and `exp`:** they're being applied to token ids. Temperature belongs on the probabilities `p`.\n- **`p` becomes a `Counter` or `0.0`:** this line replaces `p` with the table lookup or 0.0, so `np.random.choice(len(p), ...)` would fail even without the shape error.\n- **Missing steps:** the line also drops the interpolation, the masking and the top-k step.\n\nThe version in the file I gave you is correct, so use that one. With your prompt it runs and reports the OOV words:\n\n```\nwhat are you? a dog walked past the green hill without a sound. a quiet river a\n(not in vocab, treated as <unk>: ['?', 'are', 'what', 'you'])\n```\n\nThe loop body should just be:\n\n```python\np = self.lam * vec / vec.sum() + (1 - self.lam) * p\n```\n\nThe `log` and `exp` stay after the top-k step, as `p = np.exp(np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3))`. If you were trying to change the math, tell me what you want it to do and I'll fit it in.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-03T01:28:22.518335Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:28:22.518335Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0ff60-3143-7450-8681-d202de6b60b5"}, {"uuid": "01a0ff61-7086-767c-8b32-40dd1938a1f6", "text": "keep the logic", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:29:31.180949Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:29:31.180949Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "keep the logic", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-03T01:29:31.181227Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:29:31.181227Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a0ff60-3143-798e-913e-0ce4044ed049"}, {"uuid": "01a0ff61-7086-7e31-b7a4-d078b37b99ce", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI kept your logic and fixed what stopped it from running. The file is updated and now runs without errors. Your original line crashed for the shape reasons I described before. After I fixed those, a second problem remained.\n\nYour idea is to keep a context distribution `q` only where `sin(q + (1 - lam))` beats `exp(log(p)/temp)`. I made three fixes to make it work:\n\n- **Shapes:** I compared against `p`, which has one entry per vocab word, instead of `ctx`, which is two token ids.\n- **Fallback:** the line now ends `, q, p)` instead of `, q, 0.0)`. When a context is very sharp (one token with q = 1), the threshold exceeds `sin(1.3)` and every entry was zeroed, giving NaN. Now rejected entries keep their previous value.\n- **Missing steps:** top-k, the final masking and the final temperature step stay gone, as in your version. That means `--top-k` is now unused, because temperature only affects the threshold.\n\nThe output is much less coherent than before, with lots of fragments like \"night.\" and \"noticed.\" and odd runs of spaces from the empty `EOS`. The `sin` comparison isn't a probability model, so the longest matching context mostly overwrites the rest instead of blending with it. If that isn't what you want, I can switch back to the interpolated version, or fit your `sin` idea in differently.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:29:31.180713Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:29:44.947238Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Preserving the original logic while fixing the code's behavior."}, {"summary": "Reworking the threshold comparison to avoid an all-zero result."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:29:44.947355Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:29:47.188245Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_015JFMsSdYxQjxxb4GaW9RUS", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open(\"markov_gen.py\").read()\na = s.index(\"        for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):\")\nb = s.index(\"def complete(\")\nnew = '''        for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):  # shortest -> longest context\n            if c := self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:]):\n                vec = np.zeros(v.V)\n                vec[list(c)] = list(c.values())\n                q = vec / vec.sum()\n                with np.errstate(divide=\"ignore\"):\n                    p = np.where(np.sin(q + (1 - self.lam)) > np.exp(np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3)), q, 0.0)\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))\n\n\n'''\nopen(\"markov_gen.py\",\"w\").write(s[:a] + new + s[b:])\nEOF\ncd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \"what are you?\" --max-len 15 </dev/null; python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \"the cat sat\" --max-len 15 --n 3 --order 3 </dev/null", "description": "Keep user's sin/threshold logic, make it run"}, "message": "Keep user's sin/threshold logic, make it run", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\ns = open(\\\"markov_gen.py\\\").read()\\na = s.index(\\\"        for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):\\\")\\nb = s.index(\\\"def complete(\\\")\\nnew = '''        for n in range(len(ctx) + 1):  # shortest -> longest context\\n            if c := self.tables[n].get(ctx[len(ctx) - n:]):\\n                vec = np.zeros(v.V)\\n                vec[list(c)] = list(c.values())\\n                q = vec / vec.sum()\\n                with np.errstate(divide=\\\"ignore\\\"):\\n                    p = np.where(np.sin(q + (1 - self.lam)) > np.exp(np.log(p) / max(temp, 1e-3)), q, 0.0)\\n        return int(np.random.choice(len(p), p=p / p.sum()))\\n\\n\\n'''\\nopen(\\\"markov_gen.py\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(s[:a] + new + s[b:])\\nEOF\\ncd /home/claude && python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \\\"what are you?\\\" --max-len 15 </dev/null; python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py sample.txt --prompt \\\"the cat sat\\\" --max-len 15 --n 3 --order 3 </dev/null\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:29:47.681686Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-03T01:29:47.681735Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_015JFMsSdYxQjxxb4GaW9RUS", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":1,\"stdout\":\"\",\"stderr\":\"/mnt/user-data/outputs/markov_gen.py:74: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divi