ype": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01FBfvxZFgYSAPueQ2X2Wvy7", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/os/repo && cat README.md; ls; ls desktop_suite iso | head -30; grep -n \"qemu\\|bochs \" Makefile | head -30; grep -n -i \"pci\\|ethernet\\|rtl8139\\|e1000\\|ne2k\\|network\" Makefile README.md bochs_infra.cpp | head -20"}, "message": "Running command", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/os/repo && cat README.md; ls; ls desktop_suite iso | head -30; grep -n \\\"qemu\\\\|bochs \\\" Makefile | head -30; grep -n -i \\\"pci\\\\|ethernet\\\\|rtl8139\\\\|e1000\\\\|ne2k\\\\|network\\\" Makefile README.md bochs_infra.cpp | head -20\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T22:41:34.233220Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T22:41:34.233369Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01FBfvxZFgYSAPueQ2X2Wvy7", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"a simple GUI interface OS with terminal windows, TCC compiler & bochs emulator.\\n\\n\\nCTRL-Q saves and exits text editor...\\n\\n\\nSATA port selection with 'disk_select'\\n\\nguest programs require many '.h' files within the base directory for compiled programs to interface with the OS.\\n\\nTODO: add ethernet, WiFi, web browser & busybox implementation\\n\\nTODO: add driver kit\\n\\n# Build Instructions\\n\\n## Prerequisites (one-time apt installs)\\n\\n```bash\\nsudo apt update\\nsudo apt install make gcc g++ gcc-multilib g++-multilib gcc-13-multilib \\\\\\n    binutils binutils-multiarch grub-common grub-pc-bin \\\\\\n    xorriso mtools qemu-system-x86 build-essential nasm \\\\\\n    libncurses-dev bison flex git bc libssl-dev \\\\\\n    xorg-dev libx11-dev\\n```\\n\\n> **Note:** `binutils-multiarch` is required for `ld -m elf_i386` used by\\n> the TCC guest linker step.  TCC itself is built from source automatically\\n> (see below) \u2014 no `apt install tcc` needed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## TCC: download and build (one-time, automatic)\\n\\nTCC (Tiny C Compiler) is fetched from GitHub and built locally into\\n`tcc-local/`.  This gives you `i386-tcc` (cross-compiler targeting 32-bit\\ni386) and `libtcc.a` (for `tcc_tool`).\\n\\n```bash\\nmake setup-tcc        # downloads source, builds, installs into tcc-local/\\n```\\n\\nTo remove the local TCC build and start fresh:\\n\\n```bash\\nmake tcc-clean        # removes tcc-local/, tcc-src/, tcc-mob.tar.gz\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Full kernel build\\n\\n```bash\\nmake clean\\nrm -rf bochs-2.0 bochs-2.0-src.tar.gz tcc-src tcc-local i386-libtcc-kern.a i386-libtcc.a\\nmake\\n```\\n\\nRun in QEMU:\\n\\n```bash\\nqemu-system-i386 -M q35 -m 2048M -vga std \\\\\\n    -drive id=cd0,file=main.iso,format=raw,if=none,media=cdrom \\\\\\n    -drive id=disk0,file=disk.img,format=raw,if=none \\\\\\n    -device ahci,id=ahci \\\\\\n    -device ide-cd,drive=cd0,bus=ahci.0 \\\\\\n    -device ide-hd,drive=disk0,bus=ahci.1 \\\\\\n    -boot d\\n```\\nCOMP.H\\nDISK_WRAPPER.md\\nEDITF.C\\nFIXES_APPLIED.md\\nGUI_DEMO.C\\nMakefile\\nMakefile.tcc\\nREADME.md\\nbochs-2.0-src.tar.gz\\nbochs-2.7.tar.gz\\nbochs_bios.cpp\\nbochs_cstubs.c\\nbochs_drivers.h\\nbochs_glue .cpp\\nbochs_glue.cpp\\nbochs_infra.cpp\\nbochs_runtime_stubs.cpp\\nbochs_stub.cpp\\nboot.S\\nboot.o\\nbusybox\\nbusybox_stub.c\\ncommands_patch_A_helpers.cpp\\ncommands_patch_B_matrix.cpp\\ncommands_patch_C_recurse_hello_about.cpp\\ncomp.h\\ncompile.md\\ndesktop_suite\\ndirect_x_explorer.c\\ndisk.img.xz\\ndisk_tcc.c\\ndriverkit.c\\ndrivers.h\\neditf.c\\nfixes.h\\nfont.h\\ngames.zip\\ngfx.c\\ngfx_demo.c\\ngfxdem.c\\nguest.c\\nguest.ld\\ngui_demo.c\\ngui_demo_static.c\\ngui_render.h\\ngui_scene.h\\nhello\\nhello.c\\nhello.ld\\nhello_tcc.c\\nhost_test.c\\nhost_test_editf.c\\ni386-libtcc-kern.a\\ninit_instrumented.cc\\ninstrument_stub.h\\niso\\nkernel.cpp\\nkernel.ld\\nkernel_parts\\nkernel_tcc_integration.zip\\nkernel_tcc_patch.cpp\\nkeyboard_tcc.c\\nlinker.ld\\nlinker_tcc.ld\\nlynx2.9.2.zip\\nmain.iso\\nmatrix.md\\nmatrix_array.h\\nmkfat32.py\\nn.c\\npatch-bochs-2.0.sh\\npong.c\\nprogram.c\\nsetjmp.S\\ntcc-0.9.27.tar.bz2\\ntcc-mob.tar.gz\\ntcc_glue.cpp\\ntcc_glue.h\\ntcc_guest.ld\\ntcc_kernel.cpp\\ntcc_stub.cpp\\ntcc_stub.zip\\ntest_main.cpp\\ntest_module.cpp\\ntest_module.h\\ntest_module_stub.cpp\\ndesktop_suite:\\napps\\nbase_window.h\\ncommands_patch.cpp\\nlauncher.h\\n\\niso:\\nboot\\n76:\\t@echo \\\"    Run: qemu-system-i386 -M q35 -m 2048M -vga std \\\\\\\\\\\"\\n386:#  model database, added in 2.5) and fpu/ lives at the bochs root\\n703:#    qemu-system-i386 -M q35 -cdrom test_main.iso -boot d \\\\\\n741:\\tqemu-system-i386 -M q35 -cdrom $(TEST_ISO) -boot d \\\\\\nMakefile:53:\\nMakefile:317:# kicked off a multi-minute, network-dependent TCC build, and the\\nREADME.md:11:TODO: add ethernet, WiFi, web browser & busybox implementation\\nbochs_infra.cpp:418:// NOTE (Bochs 2.0 port): bx_pci_device_c doesn't exist as a class in\\nbochs_infra.cpp:419:// this version - PCI support here (BX_PCI_SUPPORT, off by default) is\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"a simple GUI interface OS with terminal windows, TCC compiler & bochs emulator.\\n\\n\\nCTRL-Q saves and exits text editor...\\n\\n\\nSATA port selection with 'disk_select'\\n\\nguest programs require many '.h' files within the base directory for compiled programs to interface with the OS.\\n\\nTODO: add ethernet, WiFi, web browser & busybox implementation\\n\\nTODO: add driver kit\\n\\n# Build Instructions\\n\\n## Prerequisites (one-time apt installs)\\n\\n```bash\\nsudo apt update\\nsudo apt install make gcc g++ gcc-multilib g++-multilib gcc-13-multilib \\\\\\n    binutils binutils-multiarch grub-common grub-pc-bin \\\\\\n    xorriso mtools qemu-system-x86 build-essential nasm \\\\\\n    libncurses-dev bison flex git bc libssl-dev \\\\\\n    xorg-dev libx11-dev\\n```\\n\\n> **Note:** `binutils-multiarch` is required for `ld -m elf_i386` used by\\n> the TCC guest linker step.  TCC itself is built from source automatically\\n> (see below) \u2014 no `apt install tcc` needed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## TCC: download and build (one-time, automatic)\\n\\nTCC (Tiny C Compiler) is fetched from GitHub and built locally into\\n`tcc-local/`.  This gives you `i386-tcc` (cross-compiler targeting 32-bit\\ni386) and `libtcc.a` (for `tcc_tool`).\\n\\n```bash\\nmake setup-tcc        # downloads source, builds, installs into tcc-local/\\n```\\n\\nTo remove the local TCC build and start fresh:\\n\\n```bash\\nmake tcc-clean        # removes tcc-local/, tcc-src/, tcc-mob.tar.gz\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Full kernel build\\n\\n```bash\\nmake clean\\nrm -rf bochs-2.0 bochs-2.0-src.tar.gz tcc-src tcc-local i386-libtcc-kern.a i386-libtcc.a\\nmake\\n```\\n\\nRun in QEMU:\\n\\n```bash\\nqemu-system-i386 -M q35 -m 2048M -vga std \\\\\\n    -drive id=cd0,file=main.iso,format=raw,if=none,media=cdrom \\\\\\n    -drive id=disk0,file=disk.img,format=raw,if=none \\\\\\n    -device ahci,id=ahci \\\\\\n    -device ide-cd,drive=cd0,bus=ahci.0 \\\\\\n    -device ide-hd,drive=disk0,bus=ahci.1 \\\\\\n    -boot d\\n```\\nCOMP.H\\nDISK_WRAPPER.md\\nEDITF.C\\nFIXES_APPLIED.md\\nGUI_DEMO.C\\nMakefile\\nMakefile.tcc\\nREADME.md\\nbochs-2.0-src.tar.gz\\nbochs-2.7.tar.gz\\nbochs_bios.cpp\\nbochs_cstubs.c\\nbochs_drivers.h\\nbochs_glue .cpp\\nbochs_glue.cpp\\nbochs_infra.cpp\\nbochs_runtime_stubs.cpp\\nbochs_stub.cpp\\nboot.S\\nboot.o\\nbusybox\\nbusybox_stub.c\\ncommands_patch_A_helpers.cpp\\ncommands_patch_B_matrix.cpp\\ncommands_patch_C_recurse_hello_about.cpp\\ncomp.h\\ncompile.md\\ndesktop_suite\\ndirect_x_explorer.c\\ndisk.img.xz\\ndisk_tcc.c\\ndriverkit.c\\ndrivers.h\\neditf.c\\nfixes.h\\nfont.h\\ngames.zip\\ngfx.c\\ngfx_demo.c\\ngfxdem.c\\nguest.c\\nguest.ld\\ngui_demo.c\\ngui_demo_static.c\\ngui_render.h\\ngui_scene.h\\nhello\\nhello.c\\nhello.ld\\nhello_tcc.c\\nhost_test.c\\nhost_test_editf.c\\ni386-libtcc-kern.a\\ninit_instrumented.cc\\ninstrument_stub.h\\niso\\nkernel.cpp\\nkernel.ld\\nkernel_parts\\nkernel_tcc_integration.zip\\nkernel_tcc_patch.cpp\\nkeyboard_tcc.c\\nlinker.ld\\nlinker_tcc.ld\\nlynx2.9.2.zip\\nmain.iso\\nmatrix.md\\nmatrix_array.h\\nmkfat32.py\\nn.c\\npatch-bochs-2.0.sh\\npong.c\\nprogram.c\\nsetjmp.S\\ntcc-0.9.27.tar.bz2\\ntcc-mob.tar.gz\\ntcc_glue.cpp\\ntcc_glue.h\\ntcc_guest.ld\\ntcc_kernel.cpp\\ntcc_stub.cpp\\ntcc_stub.zip\\ntest_main.cpp\\ntest_module.cpp\\ntest_module.h\\ntest_module_stub.cpp\\ndesktop_suite:\\napps\\nbase_window.h\\ncommands_patch.cpp\\nlauncher.h\\n\\niso:\\nboot\\n76:\\t@echo \\\"    Run: qemu-system-i386 -M q35 -m 2048M -vga std \\\\\\\\\\\"\\n386:#  model database, added in 2.5) and fpu/ lives at the bochs root\\n703:#    qemu-system-i386 -M q35 -cdrom test_main.iso -boot d \\\\\\n741:\\tqemu-system-i386 -M q35 -cdrom $(TEST_ISO) -boot d \\\\\\nMakefile:53:\\nMakefile:317:# kicked off a multi-minute, network-dependent TCC build, and the\\nREADME.md:11:TODO: add ethernet, WiFi, web browser & busybox implementation\\nbochs_infra.cpp:418:// NOTE (Bochs 2.0 port): bx_pci_device_c doesn't exist as a class in\\nbochs_infra.cpp:419:// this version - PCI support here (BX_PCI_SUPPORT, off by default) is\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T22:41:36.282199Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T22:41:40.415432Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Exploring a kernel's PCI, I/O, AHCI, and interrupt handling code."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T22:41:40.415513Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T22:41:40.647819Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_014J1hmtFqVihJKLC2TSePGY", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/os/repo && ls kernel_parts | head -30; wc -l kernel.cpp; grep -n \"outl\\|inl(\\|pci_\\|PCI\\|idt\\|IDT\\|irq\\|IRQ\\|kmalloc\\|heap\\|ahci\" kernel.cpp | head -80"}, "message": "Running command", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/os/repo && ls kernel_parts | head -30; wc -l kernel.cpp; grep -n \\\"outl\\\\|inl(\\\\|pci_\\\\|PCI\\\\|idt\\\\|IDT\\\\|irq\\\\|IRQ\\\\|kmalloc\\\\|heap\\\\|ahci\\\" kernel.cpp | head -80\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T22:41:40.845165Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T22:41:40.845215Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_014J1hmtFqVihJKLC2TSePGY", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"00_core_types_and_stdlib.h\\n01_fs_encryption.h\\n02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h\\n03_input_ps2_mouse.h\\n04_window_system.h\\n05_io_wait_ps2_funcs.h\\n06_fat32_filesystem_and_explorer.h\\n07_chkdsk_and_hardware.h\\n08_tinyvm_compiler_vm.h\\n09_terminal_window.h\\n10_window_manager_impl.h\\n11_kernel_main.h\\n35 kernel.cpp\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"00_core_types_and_stdlib.h\\n01_fs_encryption.h\\n02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h\\n03_input_ps2_mouse.h\\n04_window_system.h\\n05_io_wait_ps2_funcs.h\\n06_fat32_filesystem_and_explorer.h\\n07_chkdsk_and_hardware.h\\n08_tinyvm_compiler_vm.h\\n09_terminal_window.h\\n10_window_manager_impl.h\\n11_kernel_main.h\\n35 kernel.cpp\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T22:41:42.835642Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T22:41:43.439871Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01F9ScDavtXg3bgH6aLAs97g", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/os/repo && cat kernel.cpp; wc -l kernel_parts/*; grep -n \"pci\\|PCI\\|outl\\|inl\\b\\|idt\\|IDT\\|kmalloc\\|malloc\\|heap\\|0xCF8\" kernel_parts/*.h | head -80"}, "message": "Running command", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/os/repo && cat kernel.cpp; wc -l kernel_parts/*; grep -n \\\"pci\\\\|PCI\\\\|outl\\\\|inl\\\\b\\\\|idt\\\\|IDT\\\\|kmalloc\\\\|malloc\\\\|heap\\\\|0xCF8\\\" kernel_parts/*.h | head -80\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T22:41:43.658608Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T22:41:43.658756Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01F9ScDavtXg3bgH6aLAs97g", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"/*\\n * OPTIMIZED KERNEL WITH GRAPHICS STATE MANAGEMENT\\n * ================================================\\n * All graphics rendering uses atomic frame composition\\n * Unified color palette prevents inconsistencies\\n * State machine ensures complete frames with no trailing\\n *\\n * This file used to contain the entire kernel (~10,500 lines) in one\\n * translation unit. It has been split into per-component files under\\n * kernel_parts/, included below in their original order. This is a pure\\n * physical reorganization -- no code was reordered, added, or removed,\\n * so the compiled kernel is unchanged. The split points were chosen at\\n * brace-depth-0 boundaries (verified with a script) so no class,\\n * struct, or function is torn across two files.\\n *\\n * Order is load-bearing: this is still effectively one translation\\n * unit stitched together via #include, not independent compilation\\n * units, because later parts rely on types/functions/globals defined\\n * earlier (e.g. WindowManager's out-of-class method bodies in\\n * 10_window_manager_impl.h need the complete TerminalWindow type from\\n * 09_terminal_window.h). Do not reorder these includes.\\n */\\n\\n#include \\\"kernel_parts/00_core_types_and_stdlib.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"kernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"kernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"kernel_parts/03_input_ps2_mouse.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"kernel_parts/04_window_system.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"kernel_parts/05_io_wait_ps2_funcs.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"kernel_parts/06_fat32_filesystem_and_explorer.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"kernel_parts/07_chkdsk_and_hardware.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"kernel_parts/08_tinyvm_compiler_vm.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"kernel_parts/09_terminal_window.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"kernel_parts/10_window_manager_impl.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"kernel_parts/11_kernel_main.h\\\"\\n   481 kernel_parts/00_core_types_and_stdlib.h\\n   446 kernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h\\n   696 kernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h\\n   139 kernel_parts/03_input_ps2_mouse.h\\n   529 kernel_parts/04_window_system.h\\n   549 kernel_parts/05_io_wait_ps2_funcs.h\\n  3125 kernel_parts/06_fat32_filesystem_and_explorer.h\\n  1094 kernel_parts/07_chkdsk_and_hardware.h\\n  1281 kernel_parts/08_tinyvm_compiler_vm.h\\n  2643 kernel_parts/09_terminal_window.h\\n   496 kernel_parts/10_window_manager_impl.h\\n  1372 kernel_parts/11_kernel_main.h\\n 12851 total\\nkernel_parts/00_core_types_and_stdlib.h:29:#define ELF_HEAP_SIZE (256 * 1024)   // 256KB heap per process\\nkernel_parts/00_core_types_and_stdlib.h:210:static inline void outl(uint16_t port, uint32_t val) { asm volatile (\\\"outl %0, %1\\\" : : \\\"a\\\"(val), \\\"d\\\"(port)); }\\nkernel_parts/00_core_types_and_stdlib.h:212:static inline uint32_t inl(uint16_t port) { uint32_t ret; asm volatile (\\\"inl %1, %0\\\" : \\\"=a\\\"(ret) : \\\"d\\\"(port)); return ret; }\\nkernel_parts/00_core_types_and_stdlib.h:213:static inline uint32_t pci_read_config_dword(uint16_t bus, uint8_t device, uint8_t function, uint8_t offset) {\\nkernel_parts/00_core_types_and_stdlib.h:215:    outl(0xCF8, address);\\nkernel_parts/00_core_types_and_stdlib.h:216:    return inl(0xCFC);\\nkernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h:163:// Single 32MB global heap in BSS (not stack!) \u2014 enough for BusyBox + 4 ELF procs + FAT32 + backbuffer\\nkernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h:164:/* 16 MB heap \u2014 keeps total BSS under ~20 MB so GRUB can zero it reliably.\\nkernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h:171:static uint8_t kernel_heap[64 * 1024 * 1024];\\nkernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h:172:static size_t heap_ptr = 0;\\nkernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h:181:struct FramebufferInfo { uint32_t* ptr; uint32_t width, height, pitch; };\\nkernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h:197:    void init(void* heapStart, size_t heapSize) {\\nkernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h:198:        if (!heapStart || heapSize < sizeof(FreeBlock)) {\\nkernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h:201:        freeListHead = static_cast<FreeBlock*>(heapStart);\\nkernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h:202:        freeListHead->size = heapSize;\\nkernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h:320:                for (uint32_t x = 0; x < fb_info.width; ++x) row[x] = 0xC00000u;\\nkernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h:325:            if (x0 + 8 > (int)fb_info.width)  return;\\nkernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h:416:// that out-of-bounds read previously corrupted adjacent heap memory on\\nkernel_parts/01_fs_encryption.h:431:// kernel_alloc_nofail. A user launching an ELF when the heap happens to be\\nkernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h:24:    uint32_t framebuffer_pitch, framebuffer_width, framebuffer_height;\\nkernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h:52:   doesn't consume heap space.  fb_info dimensions are checked before use. */\\nkernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h:87:// to be power-of-two aligned -- true for any PCI-BAR-backed framebuffer,\\nkernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h:88:// since PCI BARs are always power-of-two sized/aligned. If they aren't\\nkernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h:187:    uint64_t phys_mask = (~(size - 1)) & 0xFFFFFFFFFull; // 36-bit phys addr width -- guaranteed minimum on any MTRR-capable CPU\\nkernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h:340:        uint32_t pixel_count = fb_info.width * fb_info.height;\\nkernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h:362:        if (backbuffer && x >= 0 && x < (int)fb_info.width && y >= 0 && y < (int)fb_info.height) {\\nkernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h:363:            backbuffer[y * fb_info.width + x] = rgb_to_bgr(rgb_color);\\nkernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h:419:    if (backbuffer && x >= 0 && x < (int)fb_info.width && y >= 0 && y < (int)fb_info.height) {\\nkernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h:420:        backbuffer[y * fb_info.width + x] = color;\\nkernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h:444:// boot.S installs a 256-entry IDT pointing at stubs that all chain to\\nkernel_parts/02_boot_info