er (present/clear).\\n265:    else if (port == 0xEE) {\\n266:        Bit32u addr = s_gfx_addr_bytes[0]\\n267:                    | (s_gfx_addr_bytes[1] << 8)\\nbochs_infra.cpp:199:// kfstat, and bochs_glue.cpp's bochs_guest_disk_cmd). The guest writes\\nbochs_infra.cpp:204:extern \\\"C\\\" void bochs_guest_disk_cmd(unsigned int mbox_addr, int cmd);\\nbochs_infra.cpp:209:// gfx_framebuffer, and bochs_glue.cpp's bochs_guest_gfx_cmd). Same\\nbochs_infra.cpp:214:extern \\\"C\\\" void bochs_guest_gfx_cmd(unsigned int mbox_addr, int cmd);\\nbochs_infra.cpp:257:        bochs_guest_disk_cmd(addr, (int)(val & 0xFF));\\nbochs_infra.cpp:270:        bochs_guest_gfx_cmd(addr, (int)(val & 0xFF));\\nbochs_drivers.h:114:     * mailbox's own guest address (see bochs_guest_disk_cmd's disk_guest_ptr\\ndrivers.h:114:     * mailbox's own guest address (see bochs_guest_disk_cmd's disk_guest_ptr\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:14:23.949439Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:00.920236Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Designing a new virtual device interface for the system."}, {"summary": "Defining commands and data for network diagnostics and queries."}, {"summary": "Splitting pointer translation and kernel calls across the two modules."}, {"summary": "Working around header conflicts to trap simulated port writes."}, {"summary": "Sharing dispatch logic so both sides test identically through a compiler."}, {"summary": "Laying out shared fields for the diagnostic data exchange."}, {"summary": "Handling timeouts and source checks for reply matching."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:00.920309Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:01.815806Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01JEwhZMGMFU9Dc5fzSn4Pq5", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/os/repo && grep -n \"0xD[0-4]\\b\\|0xD[0-4])\" bochs_infra.cpp bochs_glue.cpp drivers.h | head; grep -n \"disk_guest_ptr\" bochs_glue.cpp | head -3; sed -n '/static void\\* disk_guest_ptr/,/^}/p' bochs_glue.cpp | head -40; cd ../tcc/tinycc-mob && (./configure --enable-cross >/dev/null 2>&1; make i386-tcc 2>&1 | tail -2); ls -la i386-tcc 2>/dev/null; cat /home/claude/os/repo/tcc_guest.ld | head -30"}, "message": "Running command", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/os/repo && grep -n \\\"0xD[0-4]\\\\b\\\\|0xD[0-4])\\\" bochs_infra.cpp bochs_glue.cpp drivers.h | head; grep -n \\\"disk_guest_ptr\\\" bochs_glue.cpp | head -3; sed -n '/static void\\\\* disk_guest_ptr/,/^}/p' bochs_glue.cpp | head -40; cd ../tcc/tinycc-mob && (./configure --enable-cross >/dev/null 2>&1; make i386-tcc 2>&1 | tail -2); ls -la i386-tcc 2>/dev/null; cat /home/claude/os/repo/tcc_guest.ld | head -30\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:10.117863Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:10.117910Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01JEwhZMGMFU9Dc5fzSn4Pq5", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"1592:static void* disk_guest_ptr(Bit32u addr, Bit32u len) {\\n1628:        (GuestDiskMailbox*)disk_guest_ptr(mbox_addr, sizeof(GuestDiskMailbox));\\n1672:            void* dst = disk_guest_ptr(mbox->buf_addr, size);\\nstatic void* disk_guest_ptr(Bit32u addr, Bit32u len) {\\n    if (g_active_slot < 0 || g_active_slot >= MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS) return nullptr;\\n    SlotState& s = g_slots[g_active_slot];\\n    if (!s.mem_base || !s.mem_size) return nullptr;\\n    if (addr < s.vaddr_base) return nullptr;\\n    Bit32u off = addr - s.vaddr_base;\\n    if ((Bit64u)off + (Bit64u)len > (Bit64u)s.mem_size) return nullptr;\\n    return s.mem_base + off;\\n}\\n      |             ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\\ngcc -o i386-tcc i386-tcc.o -lm -ldl -lpthread \\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 root root 344832 Oct  5 23:15 i386-tcc\\n/* tcc_guest.ld \u2014 linker script for TCC-compiled 32-bit i386 guest ELFs.\\n *\\n * Differences from guest.ld\\n * --------------------------\\n * guest.ld places _start at 0x08001000, which is slab offset 0x000.\\n * That overlaps the zone where inject_slab_tables writes the GDT/IDT/stub\\n * (slab offsets 0x000..0x8ff).  When gcc compiles with -nostartfiles the\\n * gap is filled by the toolchain's crt; TCC emits nothing there, so code\\n * starts at exactly offset 0x000 and gets clobbered.\\n *\\n * This script inserts an explicit 4 KiB NOLOAD gap so the first real\\n * instruction lands at 0x08002000 (slab offset 0x1000), safely after the\\n * stub injection zone.\\n *\\n * Kernel ABI (guest side)\\n * -----------------------\\n * Write a character to the terminal  : outb(0xE9, ch)\\n * Exit with code N (clean)           : outb(0xE8, N & 0xFF)\\n *\\n * Typical minimal _start:\\n *\\n *   static inline void outb(unsigned short port, unsigned char v) {\\n *       __asm__ volatile(\\\"outb %0,%1\\\"::\\\"a\\\"(v),\\\"Nd\\\"(port));\\n *   }\\n *   static void puts_(const char *s) { while (*s) outb(0xE9,*s++); }\\n *\\n *   void _start(void) {\\n *       puts_(\\\"Hello from TCC!\\\\n\\\");\\n *       outb(0xE8, 0);\\n *       for (;;) {}\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"1592:static void* disk_guest_ptr(Bit32u addr, Bit32u len) {\\n1628:        (GuestDiskMailbox*)disk_guest_ptr(mbox_addr, sizeof(GuestDiskMailbox));\\n1672:            void* dst = disk_guest_ptr(mbox->buf_addr, size);\\nstatic void* disk_guest_ptr(Bit32u addr, Bit32u len) {\\n    if (g_active_slot < 0 || g_active_slot >= MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS) return nullptr;\\n    SlotState& s = g_slots[g_active_slot];\\n    if (!s.mem_base || !s.mem_size) return nullptr;\\n    if (addr < s.vaddr_base) return nullptr;\\n    Bit32u off = addr - s.vaddr_base;\\n    if ((Bit64u)off + (Bit64u)len > (Bit64u)s.mem_size) return nullptr;\\n    return s.mem_base + off;\\n}\\n      |             ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\\ngcc -o i386-tcc i386-tcc.o -lm -ldl -lpthread \\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 root root 344832 Oct  5 23:15 i386-tcc\\n/* tcc_guest.ld \u2014 linker script for TCC-compiled 32-bit i386 guest ELFs.\\n *\\n * Differences from guest.ld\\n * --------------------------\\n * guest.ld places _start at 0x08001000, which is slab offset 0x000.\\n * That overlaps the zone where inject_slab_tables writes the GDT/IDT/stub\\n * (slab offsets 0x000..0x8ff).  When gcc compiles with -nostartfiles the\\n * gap is filled by the toolchain's crt; TCC emits nothing there, so code\\n * starts at exactly offset 0x000 and gets clobbered.\\n *\\n * This script inserts an explicit 4 KiB NOLOAD gap so the first real\\n * instruction lands at 0x08002000 (slab offset 0x1000), safely after the\\n * stub injection zone.\\n *\\n * Kernel ABI (guest side)\\n * -----------------------\\n * Write a character to the terminal  : outb(0xE9, ch)\\n * Exit with code N (clean)           : outb(0xE8, N & 0xFF)\\n *\\n * Typical minimal _start:\\n *\\n *   static inline void outb(unsigned short port, unsigned char v) {\\n *       __asm__ volatile(\\\"outb %0,%1\\\"::\\\"a\\\"(v),\\\"Nd\\\"(port));\\n *   }\\n *   static void puts_(const char *s) { while (*s) outb(0xE9,*s++); }\\n *\\n *   void _start(void) {\\n *       puts_(\\\"Hello from TCC!\\\\n\\\");\\n *       outb(0xE8, 0);\\n *       for (;;) {}\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:15.076001Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:15.076367Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Wiring up the guest network API and test program"}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:15.076453Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:32.258579Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_0193VaHnqxv763eoZiHr5kFT", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/os/repo && cat > net.h <<'EOF'\n/* net.h \u2014 guest-side network ABI for programs compiled in-OS with `cc`.\n *\n *     #include \"net.h\"          (needs drivers.h in the same directory)\n *\n *     knet_info_t i;  knet_info(&i);\n *     unsigned rtt;   knet_ping(i.gw, 2000, &rtt, 0);\n *\n * Protocol (same shape as the disk/gfx wrappers in drivers.h): fill in a\n * net_mbox_t, write the little-endian bytes of its OWN address to ports\n * 0xD0-0xD3, then a command byte to 0xD4.  The final OUT blocks until the\n * kernel's NIC driver has finished (ping reply / DNS answer / DHCP lease /\n * timeout) and has written the result back into the same struct.\n *\n * No libc, no dynamic memory.  Everything is static inline.\n */\n#pragma once\n#include \"drivers.h\"\n\n/* Test hook: a host-side harness can redefine this to intercept the port\n * writes.  Inside the OS it is simply outb(). */\n#ifndef KNET_OUTB\n#define KNET_OUTB(port, val) outb((port), (val))\n#endif\n\n#define NET_PORT_ADDR0 0xD0\n#define NET_PORT_ADDR1 0xD1\n#define NET_PORT_ADDR2 0xD2\n#define NET_PORT_ADDR3 0xD3\n#define NET_PORT_CMD   0xD4\n\n#define NET_CMD_INFO    1   /* fill ip/mask/gw/dns/mac/flags/name           */\n#define NET_CMD_PING    2   /* ICMP echo to .ip, wait .timeout_ms           */\n#define NET_CMD_RESOLVE 3   /* DNS A lookup of .name (or dotted-quad)       */\n#define NET_CMD_DHCP    4   /* (re)run DHCP, then fill info                 */\n#define NET_CMD_UDP     5   /* send datagram, wait for the reply            */\n\n#define NET_OK             0\n#define NET_ERR_NODEV     (-1)   /* no supported NIC in this machine       */\n#define NET_ERR_TIMEOUT   (-2)   /* no reply in time                       */\n#define NET_ERR_BADARG    (-3)\n#define NET_ERR_BADCMD    (-4)\n#define NET_ERR_FAIL      (-5)   /* resolve / DHCP failed                  */\n#define NET_ERR_UNREACHABLE (-6) /* kernel never saw the mailbox           */\n\n#define NET_FLAG_PRESENT 0x01\n#define NET_FLAG_LINK    0x02\n#define NET_FLAG_DHCP    0x04\n\n/* 136 bytes, all fields 4-byte aligned: must match kernel_parts/07b_network.h */\ntypedef struct {\n    int          status;                 /* OUT: NET_OK or NET_ERR_*          */\n    unsigned int ip;                     /* IN: ping/udp target; OUT: resolve */\n    unsigned int mask, gw, dns;          /* OUT (info)                        */\n    unsigned int flags;                  /* OUT (info)                        */\n    unsigned int timeout_ms;             /* IN                                */\n    unsigned int rtt_x10;                /* OUT (ping): round trip, 0.1 ms    */\n    unsigned int ttl;                    /* OUT (ping)                        */\n    unsigned int sport, dport;           /* IN (udp)                          */\n    unsigned int tx_addr, tx_len;        /* IN (udp): request payload         */\n    unsigned int rx_addr, rx_cap;        /* IN (udp): reply buffer            */\n    unsigned int rx_len;                 /* OUT (udp): reply length           */\n    unsigned char mac[8];                /* OUT (info): 6 bytes used          */\n    char         name[64];               /* IN resolve: host; OUT info: NIC   */\n} net_mbox_t;\n\nstatic inline void __net_submit(net_mbox_t *m, int cmd)\n{\n    unsigned int a = (unsigned int)(unsigned long)m;\n    m->status = NET_ERR_UNREACHABLE;     /* a dropped command must not look like success */\n    KNET_OUTB(NET_PORT_ADDR0, (unsigned char)(a & 0xFF));\n    KNET_OUTB(NET_PORT_ADDR1, (unsigned char)((a >> 8) & 0xFF));\n    KNET_OUTB(NET_PORT_ADDR2, (unsigned char)((a >> 16) & 0xFF));\n    KNET_OUTB(NET_PORT_ADDR3, (unsigned char)((a >> 24) & 0xFF));\n    KNET_OUTB(NET_PORT_CMD,   (unsigned char)cmd);\n}\n\nstatic inline void __net_zero(net_mbox_t *m)\n{\n    unsigned char *p = (unsigned char *)m;\n    unsigned int i;\n    for (i = 0; i < sizeof(*m); i++) p[i] = 0;\n}\n\ntypedef struct {\n    unsigned int  ip, mask, gw, dns, flags;\n    unsigned char mac[6];\n    char          nic[64];\n} knet_info_t;\n\n/* Returns NET_OK, or NET_ERR_NODEV when the machine has no supported NIC. */\nstatic inline int knet_info(knet_info_t *out)\n{\n    static net_mbox_t m;\n    unsigned int i;\n    __net_zero(&m);\n    __net_submit(&m, NET_CMD_INFO);\n    if (m.status != NET_OK) return m.status;\n    out->ip = m.ip; out->mask = m.mask; out->gw = m.gw; out->dns = m.dns; out->flags = m.flags;\n    for (i = 0; i < 6; i++) out->mac[i] = m.mac[i];\n    for (i = 0; i < 63 && m.name[i]; i++) out->nic[i] = m.name[i];\n    out->nic[i] = 0;\n    return NET_OK;\n}\n\n/* One ICMP echo. rtt_x10 receives the round trip in tenths of a millisecond. */\nstatic inline int knet_ping(unsigned int ip, unsigned int timeout_ms, unsigned int *rtt_x10, unsigned int *ttl)\n{\n    static net_mbox_t m;\n    __net_zero(&m);\n    m.ip = ip; m.timeout_ms = timeout_ms;\n    __net_submit(&m, NET_CMD_PING);\n    if (m.status == NET_OK) {\n        if (rtt_x10) *rtt_x10 = m.rtt_x10;\n        if (ttl)     *ttl = m.ttl;\n    }\n    return m.status;\n}\n\n/* Dotted-quad or hostname -> IPv4 (host byte order: a<<24|b<<16|c<<8|d). */\nstatic inline int knet_resolve(const char *host, unsigned int *ip)\n{\n    static net_mbox_t m;\n    unsigned int i;\n    __net_zero(&m);\n    for (i = 0; i < sizeof(m.name) - 1 && host[i]; i++) m.name[i] = host[i];\n    __net_submit(&m, NET_CMD_RESOLVE);\n    if (m.status == NET_OK && ip) *ip = m.ip;\n    return m.status;\n}\n\nstatic inline int knet_dhcp(void)\n{\n    static net_mbox_t m;\n    __net_zero(&m);\n    __net_submit(&m, NET_CMD_DHCP);\n    return m.status;\n}\n\n/* Send one UDP datagram and wait for the first reply from the same host.\n * Returns the reply length (>= 0) or a negative NET_ERR_* code. */\nstatic inline int knet_udp(unsigned int dst_ip, unsigned int sport, unsigned int dport,\n                           const void *tx, unsigned int tx_len,\n                           void *rx, unsigned int rx_cap, unsigned int timeout_ms)\n{\n    static net_mbox_t m;\n    __net_zero(&m);\n    m.ip = dst_ip; m.sport = sport; m.dport = dport; m.timeout_ms = timeout_ms;\n    m.tx_addr = (unsigned int)(unsigned long)tx; m.tx_len = tx_len;\n    m.rx_addr = (unsigned int)(unsigned long)rx; m.rx_cap = rx_cap;\n    __net_submit(&m, NET_CMD_UDP);\n    if (m.status != NET_OK) return m.status;\n    return (int)m.rx_len;\n}\n\n/* \u2500\u2500 small helpers \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 */\nstatic inline int knet_parse_ip(const char *s, unsigned int *out)\n{\n    unsigned int v = 0, n, d; int parts = 0;\n    while (*s) {\n        n = 0; d = 0;\n        if (*s < '0' || *s > '9') return 0;\n        while (*s >= '0' && *s <= '9') { n = n * 10 + (unsigned int)(*s - '0'); s++; if (++d > 3) return 0; }\n        if (n > 255) return 0;\n        v = (v << 8) | n; parts++;\n        if (*s == '.') { s++; if (!*s) return 0; } else if (*s) return 0;\n    }\n    if (parts != 4) return 0;\n    *out = v; return 1;\n}\n\nstatic inline void knet_putip(unsigned int ip)\n{\n    int i;\n    for (i = 3; i >= 0; i--) { kputu((ip >> (i * 8)) & 0xFF); if (i) kputc('.'); }\n}\n\nstatic inline void knet_puthex8(unsigned char b)\n{\n    const char *h = \"0123456789abcdef\";\n    kputc(h[b >> 4]); kputc(h[b & 15]);\n}\nEOF\ngrep -n \"kputu\\|static inline.*kputs\" drivers.h | head -4"}, "message": "Running command", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/os/repo && cat > net.h <<'EOF'\\n/* net.h \\u2014 guest-side network ABI for programs compiled in-OS with `cc`.\\n *\\n *     #include \\\"net.h\\\"          (needs drivers.h in the same directory)\\n *\\n *     knet_info_t i;  knet_info(&i);\\n *     unsigned rtt;   knet_ping(i.gw, 2000, &rtt, 0);\\n *\\n * Protocol (same shape as the disk/gfx wrappers in drivers.h): fill in a\\n * net_mbox_t, write the little-endian bytes of its OWN address to ports\\n * 0xD0-0xD3, then a command byte to 0xD4.  The final OUT blocks until the\\n * kernel's NIC driver has finished (ping reply / DNS answer / DHCP lease /\\n * timeout) and has written the result back into the same struct.\\n *\\n * No libc, no dynamic memory.  Everything is static inline.\\n */\\n#pragma once\\n#include \\\"drivers.h\\\"\\n\\n/* Test hook: a host-side harness can redefine this to intercept the port\\n * writes.  Inside the OS it is simply outb(). */\\n#ifndef KNET_OUTB\\n#define KNET_OUTB(port, val) outb((port), (val))\\n#endif\\n\\n#define NET_PORT_ADDR0 0xD0\\n#define NET_PORT_ADDR1 0xD1\\n#define NET_PORT_ADDR2 0xD2\\n#define NET_PORT_ADDR3 0xD3\\n#define NET_PORT_CMD   0xD4\\n\\n#define NET_CMD_INFO    1   /* fill ip/mask/gw/dns/mac/flags/name           */\\n#define NET_CMD_PING    2   /* ICMP echo to .ip, wait .timeout_ms           */\\n#define NET_CMD_RESOLVE 3   /* DNS A lookup of .name (or dotted-quad)       */\\n#define NET_CMD_DHCP    4   /* (re)run DHCP, then fill info                 */\\n#define NET_CMD_UDP     5   /* send datagram, wait for the reply            */\\n\\n#define NET_OK             0\\n#define NET_ERR_NODEV     (-1)   /* no supported NIC in this machine       */\\n#define NET_ERR_TIMEOUT   (-2)   /* no reply in time                       */\\n#define NET_ERR_BADARG    (-3)\\n#define NET_ERR_BADCMD    (-4)\\n#define NET_ERR_FAIL      (-5)   /* resolve / DHCP failed                  */\\n#define NET_ERR_UNREACHABLE (-6) /* kernel never saw the mailbox           */\\n\\n#define NET_FLAG_PRESENT 0x01\\n#define NET_FLAG_LINK    0x02\\n#define NET_FLAG_DHCP    0x04\\n\\n/* 136 bytes, all fields 4-byte aligned: must match kernel_parts/07b_network.h */\\ntypedef struct {\\n    int          status;                 /* OUT: NET_OK or NET_ERR_*          */\\n    unsigned int ip;                     /* IN: ping/udp target; OUT: resolve */\\n    unsigned int mask, gw, dns;          /* OUT (info)                        */\\n    unsigned int flags;                  /* OUT (info)                        */\\n    unsigned int timeout_ms;             /* IN                                */\\n    unsigned int rtt_x10;                /* OUT (ping): round trip, 0.1 ms    */\\n    unsigned int ttl;                    /* OUT (ping)                        */\\n    unsigned int sport, dport;           /* IN (udp)                          */\\n    unsigned int tx_addr, tx_len;        /* IN (udp): request payload         */\\n    unsigned int rx_addr, rx_cap;        /* IN (udp): reply buffer            */\\n    unsigned int rx_len;                 /* OUT (udp): reply length           */\\n    unsigned char mac[8];                /* OUT (info): 6 bytes used          */\\n    char         name[64];               /* IN resolve: host; OUT info: NIC   */\\n} net_mbox_t;\\n\\nstatic inline void __net_submit(net_mbox_t *m, int cmd)\\n{\\n    unsigned int a = (unsigned int)(unsigned long)m;\\n    m->status = NET_ERR_UNREACHABLE;     /* a dropped command must not look like success */\\n    KNET_OUTB(NET_PORT_ADDR0, (unsigned char)(a & 0xFF));\\n    KNET_OUTB(NET_PORT_ADDR1, (unsigned char)((a >> 8) & 0xFF));\\n    KNET_OUTB(NET_PORT_ADDR2, (unsigned char)((a >> 16) & 0xFF));\\n    KNET_OUTB(NET_PORT_ADDR3, (unsigned char)((a >> 24) & 0xFF));\\n    KNET_OUTB(NET_PORT_CMD,   (unsigned char)cmd);\\n}\\n\\nstatic inline void __net_zero(net_mbox_t *m)\\n{\\n    unsigned char *p = (unsigned char *)m;\\n    unsigned int i;\\n    for (i = 0; i < sizeof(*m); i++) p[i] = 0;\\n}\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    unsigned int  ip, mask, gw, dns, flags;\\n    unsigned char mac[6];\\n    char          nic[64];\\n} knet_info_t;\\n\\n/* Returns NET_OK, or NET_ERR_NODEV when the machine has no supported NIC. */\\nstatic inline int knet_info(knet_info_t *out)\\n{\\n    static net_mbox_t m;\\n    unsigned int i;\\n    __net_zero(&m);\\n    __net_submit(&m, NET_CMD_INFO);\\n    if (m.status != NET_OK) return m.status;\\n    out->ip = m.ip; out->mask = m.mask; out->gw = m.gw; out->dns = m.dns; out->flags = m.flags;\\n    for (i = 0; i < 6; i++) out->mac[i] = m.mac[i];\\n    for (i = 0; i < 63 && m.name[i]; i++) out->nic[i] = m.name[i];\\n    out->nic[i] = 0;\\n    return NET_OK;\\n}\\n\\n/* One ICMP echo. rtt_x10 receives the round trip in tenths of a millisecond. */\\nstatic inline int knet_ping(unsigned int ip, unsigned int timeout_ms, unsigned int *rtt_x10, unsigned int *ttl)\\n{\\n    static net_mbox_t m;\\n    __net_zero(&m);\\n    m.ip = ip; m.timeout_ms = timeout_ms;\\n    __net_submit(&m, NET_CMD_PING);\\n    if (m.status == NET_OK) {\\n        if (rtt_x10) *rtt_x10 = m.rtt_x10;\\n        if (ttl)     *ttl = m.ttl;\\n    }\\n    return m.status;\\n}\\n\\n/* Dotted-quad or hostname -> IPv4 (host byte order: a<<24|b<<16|c<<8|d). */\\nstatic inline int knet_resolve(const char *host, unsigned int *ip)\\n{\\n    static net_mbox_t m;\\n    unsigned int i;\\n    __net_zero(&m);\\n    for (i = 0; i < sizeof(m.name) - 1 && host[i]; i++) m.name[i] = host[i];\\n    __net_submit(&m, NET_CMD_RESOLVE);\\n    if (m.status == NET_OK && ip) *ip = m.ip;\\n    return m.status;\\n}\\n\\nstatic inline int knet_dhcp(void)\\n{\\n    static net_mbox_t m;\\n    __net_zero(&m);\\n    __net_submit(&m, NET_CMD_DHCP);\\n    return m.status;\\n}\\n\\n/* Send one UDP datagram and wait for the first reply from the same host.\\n * Returns the reply length (>= 0) or a negative NET_ERR_* code. */\\nstatic inline int knet_udp(unsigned int dst_ip, unsigned int sport, unsigned int dport,\\n                           const void *tx, unsigned int tx_len,\\n                           void *rx, unsigned int rx_cap, unsigned int timeout_ms)\\n{\\n    static net_mbox_t m;\\n    __net_zero(&m);\\n    m.ip = dst_ip; m.sport = sport; m.dport = dport; m.timeout_ms = timeout_ms;\\n    m.tx_addr = (unsigned int)(unsigned long)tx; m.tx_len = tx_len;\\n    m.rx_addr = (unsigned int)(unsigned long)rx; m.rx_cap = rx_cap;\\n    __net_submit(&m, NET_CMD_UDP);\\n    if (m.status != NET_OK) return m.status;\\n    return (int)m.rx_len;\\n}\\n\\n/* \\u2500\\u2500 small helpers \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500 */\\nstatic inline int knet_parse_ip(const char *s, unsigned int *out)\\n{\\n    unsigned int v = 0, n, d; int parts = 0;\\n    while (*s) {\\n        n = 0; d = 0;\\n        if (*s < '0' || *s > '9') return 0;\\n        while (*s >= '0' && *s <= '9') { n = n * 10 + (unsigned int)(*s - '0'); s++; if (++d > 3) return 0; }\\n        if (n > 255) return 0;\\n        v = (v << 8) | n; parts++;\\n        if (*s == '.') { s++; if (!*s) return 0; } else if (*s) return 0;\\n    }\\n    if (parts != 4) return 0;\\n    *out = v; return 1;\\n}\\n\\nstatic inline void knet_putip(unsigned int ip)\\n{\\n    int i;\\n    for (i = 3; i >= 0; i--) { kputu((ip >> (i * 8)) & 0xFF); if (i) kputc('.'); }\\n}\\n\\nstatic inline void knet_puthex8(unsigned char b)\\n{\\n    const char *h = \\\"0123456789abcdef\\\";\\n    kputc(h[b >> 4]); kputc(h[b & 15]);\\n}\\nEOF\\ngrep -n \\\"kputu\\\\|static inline.*kputs\\\" drivers.h | head -4\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:32.512722Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:32.512762Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_0193VaHnqxv763eoZiHr5kFT", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"20:static inline void kputs(const char *s)\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"20:static inline void kputs(const char *s)\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:34.352826Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:39.263070Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Fixing a naming conflict in the number-printing function."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:39.263136Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:57.780085Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01CWHTyAdiMNzbx5QDEs3VSm", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/os/repo && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='net.h'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''static inline void knet_putip(unsigned int ip)\n{\n    int i;\n    for (i = 3; i >= 0; i--) { kputu((ip >> (i * 8)) & 0xFF); if (i) kputc('.'); }\n}''','''static inline void knet_putu(unsigned int n)\n{\n    char b[12]; int i = 0;\n    if (n == 0) { kputc('0'); return; }\n    while (n) { b[i++] = (char)('0' + n % 10); n /= 10; }\n    while (i--) kputc(b[i]);\n}\n\nstatic inline void knet_putip(unsigned int ip)\n{\n    int i;\n    for (i = 3; i >= 0; i--) { knet_putu((ip >> (i * 8)) & 0xFF); if (i) kputc('.'); }\n}''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > nettest.c <<'EOF'\n/* nettest.c \u2014 network driver test, compiled and run entirely inside the OS.\n *\n *   edit nettest.c          (or copy it to the disk image)\n *   cc nettest.c nettest    compile in-kernel with the self-hosted TCC\n *   bochs nettest           run it (shortcut: just `nettest` if in bochs mode)\n *\n * Needs net.h and drivers.h in the same directory.  Exercises the kernel's\n * NIC driver (RTL8139 / e1000 / e1000e) through the net mailbox ABI:\n * link/IP info, ARP+ICMP (ping the gateway), DNS via the kernel resolver,\n * and a raw UDP exchange (a hand-built DNS query).  Prints PASS / FAIL /\n * SKIP per test and exits with the number of failures.\n *\n * Under `qemu -nic user,model=e1000` the gateway is 10.0.2.2 and DNS is\n * 10.0.2.3, so every test should PASS (DNS tests SKIP if the host has no\n * upstream resolver).\n */\n#include \"net.h\"\n\nstatic int g_pass, g_fail, g_skip;\n\nstatic void result(const char *name, int ok)\n{\n    kputs(ok ? \"  [PASS] \" : \"  [FAIL] \");\n    kputs(name); kputc('\\n');\n    if (ok) g_pass++; else g_fail++;\n}\n\nstatic void skip(const char *name, const char *why)\n{\n    kputs(\"  [SKIP] \"); kputs(name); kputs(\" (\"); kputs(why); kputs(\")\\n\");\n    g_skip++;\n}\n\n/* Build a DNS query for `name` into buf; returns its length. */\nstatic unsigned int build_dns_query(unsigned char *buf, unsigned int id, const char *name)\n{\n    unsigned int n = 12, lab, i, cnt = 0;\n    for (i = 0; i < 12; i++) buf[i] = 0;\n    buf[0] = (unsigned char)(id >> 8); buf[1] = (unsigned char)id;\n    buf[2] = 0x01;                       /* RD */\n    buf[5] = 1;                          /* QDCOUNT = 1 */\n    lab = n++;\n    for (i = 0;; i++) {\n        char c = name[i];\n        if (c == '.' || c == 0) {\n            buf[lab] = (unsigned char)cnt; lab = n++; cnt = 0;\n            if (c == 0) break;\n        } else { buf[n++] = (unsigned char)c; cnt++; }\n    }\n    buf[lab] = 0; n = lab + 1;\n    buf[n++] = 0; buf[n++] = 1;          /* QTYPE  A  */\n    buf[n++] = 0; buf[n++] = 1;          /* QCLASS IN */\n    return n;\n}\n\nvoid _start(void)\n{\n    knet_info_t info;\n    unsigned int ip, rtt, ttl, i, got;\n    int rc;\n\n    kputs(\"==================================\\n\");\n    kputs(\"  Network driver test (TCC guest)\\n\");\n    kputs(\"==================================\\n\\n\");\n\n    /* 1. NIC / configuration ------------------------------------------------ */\n    kputs(\"1. NIC and configuration\\n\");\n    rc = knet_info(&info);\n    if (rc == NET_ERR_NODEV) {\n        kputs(\"  No supported NIC found. Start QEMU with -nic user,model=e1000\\n\");\n        kputs(\"  (or e1000e / rtl8139).\\n\");\n        kexit(100);\n    }\n    if (rc == NET_ERR_UNREACHABLE) {\n        kputs(\"  Kernel did not answer the net mailbox: this build of the OS\\n\");\n        kputs(\"  lacks the net ABI (ports 0xD0-0xD4).\\n\");\n        kexit(101);\n    }\n    kputs(\"  NIC : \"); kputs(info.nic); kputc('\\n');\n    kputs(\"  MAC : \");\n    for (i = 0; i < 6; i++) { knet_puthex8(info.mac[i]); if (i < 5) kputc(':'); }\n    kputc('\\n');\n    kputs(\"  IP  : \"); knet_putip(info.ip);   kputs(info.flags & NET_FLAG_DHCP ? \"  (DHCP)\\n\" : \"  (static)\\n\");\n    kputs(\"  Mask: \"); knet_putip(info.mask); kputc('\\n');\n    kputs(\"  GW  : \"); knet_putip(info.gw);   kputc('\\n');\n    kputs(\"  DNS : \"); knet_putip(info.dns);  kputc('\\n');\n    result(\"NIC present\", (info.flags & NET_FLAG_PRESENT) != 0);\n    result(\"link is up\", (info.flags & NET_FLAG_LINK) != 0);\n    result(\"has an IPv4 address\", info.ip != 0);\n    result(\"MAC is not all-zero\", (info.mac[0] | info.mac[1] | info.mac[2] | info.mac[3] | info.mac[4] | info.mac[5]) != 0);\n\n    /* 2. Resolver, offline path ---------------------------------------------- */\n    kputs(\"\\n2. Name resolution (offline)\\n\");\n    ip = 0;\n    rc = knet_resolve(\"10.0.2.2\", &ip);\n    result(\"dotted-quad resolves to itself\", rc == NET_OK && ip == 0x0A000202u);\n    rc = knet_resolve(\"300.1.1.1x\", &ip);\n    result(\"garbage is rejected or not resolved to 300.x\", rc != NET_OK || (ip >> 24) != 300);\n\n    /* 3. ARP + ICMP ----------------------------------------------------------- */\n    kputs(\"\\n3. ARP + ICMP echo to the gateway \");\n    knet_putip(info.gw); kputs(\"\\n\");\n    if (info.gw == 0) {\n        skip(\"ping gateway\", \"no gateway configured\");\n    } else {\n        got = 0;\n        for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n            rtt = 0; ttl = 0;\n            rc = knet_ping(info.gw, 2000, &rtt, &ttl);\n            if (rc == NET_OK) {\n                got++;\n                kputs(\"  reply: ttl=\"); knet_putu(ttl);\n                kputs(\" time=\"); knet_putu(rtt / 10); kputc('.'); knet_putu(rtt % 10); kputs(\" ms\\n\");\n            } else {\n                kputs(\"  request timed out\\n\");\n            }\n        }\n        result(\"at least one echo reply\", got >= 1);\n        result(\"all 4 echo replies\", got == 4);\n    }\n    rc = knet_ping(0, 300, 0, 0);\n    result(\"ping to 0.0.0.0 does not succeed\", rc != NET_OK);\n\n    /* 4. Raw UDP: hand-built DNS query through the driver --------------------- */\n    kputs(\"\\n4. UDP exchange (raw DNS query to \");\n    knet_putip(info.dns); kputs(\")\\n\");\n    if (info.dns == 0) {\n        skip(\"udp dns\", \"no DNS server configured\");\n    } else {\n        static unsigned char q[300], r[600];\n        unsigned int qlen = build_dns_query(q, 0xBEEF, \"example.com\");\n        rc = knet_udp(info.dns, 40000, 53, q, qlen, r, sizeof(r), 3000);\n        if (rc >= 12) {\n            kputs(\"  got \"); knet_putu((unsigned int)rc); kputs(\" bytes\\n\");\n            result(\"reply id matches\", r[0] == 0xBE && r[1] == 0xEF);\n            result(\"reply has QR bit set\", (r[2] & 0x80) != 0);\n        } else if (rc == NET_ERR_TIMEOUT) {\n            skip(\"udp dns\", \"no reply; does the host have an upstream resolver?\");\n        } else {\n            kputs(\"  knet_udp returned \"); knet_putu((unsigned int)(-rc)); kputs(\" (negated)\\n\");\n            result(\"udp exchange\", 0);\n        }\n    }\n\n    /* 5. Kernel resolver, online path ------------------------------------------ */\n    kputs(\"\\n5. DNS through the kernel resolver\\n\");\n    ip = 0;\n    rc = knet_resolve(\"example.com\", &ip);\n    if (rc == NET_OK) {\n        kputs(\"  example.com -> \"); knet_putip(ip); kputc('\\n');\n        result(\"example.com resolves to a non-zero address\", ip != 0);\n    } else {\n        skip(\"example.com lookup\", \"no upstream DNS / internet\");\n    }\n\n    /* summary ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\n    kputs(\"\\n----------------------------------\\n\");\n    kputs(\"  passed: \"); knet_putu((unsigned int)g_pass);\n    kputs(\"   failed: \"); knet_putu((unsigned int)g_fail);\n    kputs(\"   skipped: \"); knet_putu((unsigned int)g_skip); kputc('\\n');\n    kputs(g_fail == 0 ? \"  RESULT: ALL TESTS PASSED\\n\" : \"  RESULT: FAILURES\\n\");\n    kexit(g_fail > 100 ? 100 : g_fail);\n    for (;;) {}\n}\nEOF\necho ok"}, "message": "Running command", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/os/repo && python3 - <<'EOF'\\np='net.h'; s=open(p).read()\\ns=s.replace('''static inline void knet_putip(unsigned int ip)\\n{\\n    int i;\\n    for (i = 3; i >= 0; i--) { kputu((ip >> (i * 8)) & 0xFF); if (i) kputc('.'); }\\n}''','''static inline void knet_putu(unsigned int n)\\n{\\n    char b[12]; int i = 0;\\n    if (n == 0) { kputc('0'); return; }\\n    while (n) { b[i++] = (char)('0' + n % 10); n /= 10; }\\n    while (i--) kputc(b[i]);\\n}\\n\\nstatic inline void knet_putip(unsigned int ip)\\n{\\n    int i;\\n    for (i = 3; i >= 0; i--) { knet_putu((ip >> (i * 8)) & 0xFF); if (i) kputc('.'); }\\n}''')\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nEOF\\ncat > nettest.c <<'EOF'\\n/* nettest.c \\u2014 network driver test, compiled and run entirely inside the OS.\\n *\\n *   edit nettest.c          (or copy it to the disk image)\\n *   cc nettest.c nettest    compile in-kernel with the self-hosted TCC\\n *   bochs nettest           run it (shortcut: just `nettest` if in bochs mode)\\n *\\n * Needs net.h and drivers.h in the same directory.  Exercises the kernel's\\n * NIC driver (RTL8139 / e1000 / e1000e) through the net mailbox ABI:\\n * link/IP info, ARP+ICMP (ping the gateway), DNS via the kernel resolver,\\n * and a raw UDP exchange (a hand-built DNS query).  Prints PASS / FAIL /\\n * SKIP per test and exits with the number of failures.\\n *\\n * Under `qemu -nic user,model=e1000` the gateway is 10.0.2.2 and DNS is\\n * 10.0.2.3, so every test should PASS (DNS tests SKIP if the host has no\\n * upstream resolver).\\n */\\n#include \\\"net.h\\\"\\n\\nstatic int g_pass, g_fail, g_skip;\\n\\nstatic void result(const char *name, int ok)\\n{\\n    kputs(ok ? \\\"  [PASS] \\\" : \\\"  [FAIL] \\\");\\n    kputs(name); kputc('\\\\n');\\n    if (ok) g_pass++; else g_fail++;\\n}\\n\\nstatic void skip(const char *name, const char *why)\\n{\\n    kputs(\\\"  [SKIP] \\\"); kputs(name); kputs(\\\" (\\\"); kputs(why); kputs(\\\")\\\\n\\\");\\n    g_skip++;\\n}\\n\\n/* Build a DNS query for `name` into buf; returns its length. */\\nstatic unsigned int build_dns_query(unsigned char *buf, unsigned int id, const char *name)\\n{\\n    unsigned int n = 12, lab, i, cnt = 0;\\n    for (i = 0; i < 12; i++) buf[i] = 0;\\n    buf[0] = (unsigned char)(id >> 8); buf[1] = (unsigned char)id;\\n    buf[2] = 0x01;                       /* RD */\\n    buf[5] = 1;                          /* QDCOUNT = 1 */\\n    lab = n++;\\n    for (i = 0;; i++) {\\n        char c = name[i];\\n        if (c == '.' || c == 0) {\\n            buf[lab] = (unsigned char)cnt; lab = n++; cnt = 0;\\n            if (c == 0) break;\\n        } else { buf[n++] = (unsigned char)c; cnt++; }\\n    }\\n    buf[lab] = 0; n = lab + 1;\\n    buf[n++] = 0; buf[n++] = 1;          /* QTYPE  A  */\\n    buf[n++] = 0; buf[n++] = 1;          /* QCLASS IN */\\n    return n;\\n}\\n\\nvoid _start(void)\\n{\\n    knet_info_t info;\\n    unsigned int ip, rtt, ttl, i, got;\\n    int rc;\\n\\n    kputs(\\\"==================================\\\\n\\\");\\n    kputs(\\\"  Network driver test (TCC guest)\\\\n\\\");\\n    kputs(\\\"==================================\\\\n\\\\n\\\");\\n\\n    /* 1. NIC / configuration ------------------------------------------------ */\\n    kputs(\\\"1. NIC and configuration\\\\n\\\");\\n    rc = knet_info(&info);\\n    if (rc == NET_ERR_NODEV) {\\n        kputs(\\\"  No supported NIC found. Start QEMU with -nic user,model=e1000\\\\n\\\");\\n        kputs(\\\"  (or e1000e / rtl8139).\\\\n\\\");\\n        kexit(100);\\n    }\\n    if (rc == NET_ERR_UNREACHABLE) {\\n        kputs(\\\"  Kernel did not answer the net mailbox: this build of the OS\\\\n\\\");\\n        kputs(\\\"  lacks the net ABI (ports 0xD0-0xD4).\\\\n\\\");\\n        kexit(101);\\n    }\\n    kputs(\\\"  NIC : \\\"); kputs(info.nic); kputc('\\\\n');\\n    kputs(\\\"  MAC : \\\");\\n    for (i = 0; i < 6; i++) { knet_puthex8(info.mac[i]); if (i < 5) kputc(':'); }\\n    kputc('\\\\n');\\n    kputs(\\\"  IP  : \\\"); knet_putip(info.ip);   kputs(info.flags & NET_FLAG_DHCP ? \\\"  (DHCP)\\\\n\\\" : \\\"  (static)\\\\n\\\");\\n    kputs(\\\"  Mask: \\\"); knet_putip(info.mask); kputc('\\\\n');\\n    kputs(\\\"  GW  : \\\"); knet_putip(info.gw);   kputc('\\\\n');\\n    kputs(\\\"  DNS : \\\"); knet_putip(info.dns);  kputc('\\\\n');\\n    result(\\\"NIC present\\\", (info.flags & NET_FLAG_PRESENT) != 0);\\n    result(\\\"link is up\\\", (info.flags & NET_FLAG_LINK) != 0);\\n    result(\\\"has an IPv4 address\\\", info.ip != 0);\\n    result(\\\"MAC is not all-zero\\\", (info.mac[0] | info.mac[1] | info.mac[2] | info.mac[3] | info.mac[4] | info.mac[5]) != 0);\\n\\n    /* 2. Resolver, offline path ---------------------------------------------- */\\n    kputs(\\\"\\\\n2. Name resolution (offline)\\\\n\\\");\\n    ip = 0;\\n    rc = knet_resolve(\\\"10.0.2.2\\\", &ip);\\n    result(\\\"dotted-quad resolves to itself\\\", rc == NET_OK && ip == 0x0A000202u);\\n    rc = knet_resolve(\\\"300.1.1.1x\\\", &ip);\\n    result(\\\"garbage is rejected or not resolved to 300.x\\\", rc != NET_OK || (ip >> 24) != 300);\\n\\n    /* 3. ARP + ICMP ----------------------------------------------------------- */\\n    kputs(\\\"\\\\n3. ARP + ICMP echo to the gateway \\\");\\n    knet_putip(info.gw); kputs(\\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n    if (info.gw == 0) {\\n        skip(\\\"ping gateway\\\", \\\"no gateway configured\\\");\\n    } else {\\n        got = 0;\\n        for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n            rtt = 0; ttl = 0;\\n            rc = knet_ping(info.gw, 2000, &rtt, &ttl);\\n            if (rc == NET_OK) {\\n                got++;\\n                kputs(\\\"  reply: ttl=\\\"); knet_putu(ttl);\\n                kputs(\\\" time=\\\"); knet_putu(rtt / 10); kputc('.'); knet_putu(rtt % 10); kputs(\\\" ms\\\\n\\\");\\n            } else {\\n                kputs(\\\"  request timed out\\\\n\\\");\\n            }\\n        }\\n        result(\\\"at least one echo reply\\\", got >= 1);\\n        result(\\\"all 4 echo replies\\\", got == 4);\\n    }\\n    rc = knet_ping(0, 300, 0, 0);\\n    result(\\\"ping to 0.0.0.0 does not succeed\\\", rc != NET_OK);\\n\\n    /* 4. Raw UDP: hand-built DNS query through the driver --------------------- */\\n    kputs(\\\"\\\\n4. UDP exchange (raw DNS query to \\\");\\n    knet_putip(info.dns); kputs(\\\")\\\\n\\\");\\n    if (info.dns == 0) {\\n        skip(\\\"udp dns\\\", \\\"no DNS server configured\\\");\\n    } else {\\n        static unsigned char q[300], r[600];\\n        unsigned int qlen = build_dns_query(q, 0xBEEF, \\\"example.com\\\");\\n        rc = knet_udp(info.dns, 40000, 53, q, qlen, r, sizeof(r), 3000);\\n        if (rc >= 12) {\\n            kputs(\\\"  got \\\"); knet_putu((unsigned int)rc); kputs(\\\" bytes\\\\n\\\");\\n            result(\\\"reply id matches\\\", r[0] == 0xBE && r[1] == 0xEF);\\n            result(\\\"reply has QR bit set\\\", (r[2] & 0x80) != 0);\\n        } else if (rc == NET_ERR_TIMEOUT) {\\n            skip(\\\"udp dns\\\", \\\"no reply; does the host have an upstream resolver?\\\");\\n        } else {\\n            kputs(\\\"  knet_udp returned \\\"); knet_putu((unsigned int)(-rc)); kputs(\\\" (negated)\\\\n\\\");\\n            result(\\\"udp exchange\\\", 0);\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    /* 5. Kernel resolver, online path ------------------------------------------ */\\n    kputs(\\\"\\\\n5. DNS through the kernel resolver\\\\n\\\");\\n    ip = 0;\\n    rc = knet_resolve(\\\"example.com\\\", &ip);\\n    if (rc == NET_OK) {\\n        kputs(\\\"  example.com -> \\\"); knet_putip(ip); kputc('\\\\n');\\n        result(\\\"example.com resolves to a non-zero address\\\", ip != 0);\\n    } else {\\n        skip(\\\"example.com lookup\\\", \\\"no upstream DNS / internet\\\");\\n    }\\n\\n    /* summary ------------------------------------------------------------------ */\\n    kputs(\\\"\\\\n----------------------------------\\\\n\\\");\\n    kputs(\\\"  passed: \\\"); knet_putu((unsigned int)g_pass);\\n    kputs(\\\"   failed: \\\"); knet_putu((unsigned int)g_fail);\\n    kputs(\\\"   skipped: \\\"); knet_putu((unsigned int)g_skip); kputc('\\\\n');\\n    kputs(g_fail == 0 ? \\\"  RESULT: ALL TESTS PASSED\\\\n\\\" : \\\"  RESULT: FAILURES\\\\n\\\");\\n    kexit(g_fail > 100 ? 100 : g_fail);\\n    for (;;) {}\\n}\\nEOF\\necho ok\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:58.053265Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:15:58.053312Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01CWHTyAdiMNzbx5QDEs3VSm", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"ok\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"ok\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:16:00.101128Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:16:24.652526Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Investigating a malformed IP address during hostname resolution."}, {"summary": "Designing kernel-side network mailbox commands and edge cases."}, {"summary": "Implementing the UDP exchange and debug console port routing."}, {"summary": "Linking the compiled guest program with the kernel harness."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:16:24.652602Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:16:37.030501Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01JRrfNvwfZaoTe8xeq4t6cE", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/os/repo && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='nettest.c'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''    rc = knet_resolve(\"300.1.1.1x\", &ip);\n    result(\"garbage is rejected or not resolved to 300.x\", rc != NET_OK || (ip >> 24) != 300);''','''    rc = knet_resolve(\"\", &ip);\n    result(\"empty host name is rejected\", rc != NET_OK);''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='kernel_parts/07b_network.h'; s=open(p).read()\ns+=r'''\n\n// \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 guest network ABI (ports 0xD0-0xD4) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n// Guest programs (compiled in-OS with `cc`, run under Bochs) reach the NIC via a\n// mailbox, exactly like the disk/gfx wrappers.  Guest side: net.h.  The Bochs\n// glue (bochs_glue.cpp: bochs_guest_net_cmd) turns the guest-physical addresses\n// into host pointers and calls kernel_net_mailbox() below.\n\n// Must match net_mbox_t in net.h byte-for-byte (136 bytes, no padding).\nstruct NetMboxK {\n    int      status;\n    uint32_t ip, mask, gw, dns, flags, timeout_ms, rtt_x10, ttl;\n    uint32_t sport, dport, tx_addr, tx_len, rx_addr, rx_cap, rx_len;\n    uint8_t  mac[8];\n    char     name[64];\n};\nstatic_assert(sizeof(NetMboxK) == 136, \"NetMboxK must match net_mbox_t in net.h\");\n\nenum { NETK_OK = 0, NETK_NODEV = -1, NETK_TIMEOUT = -2, NETK_BADARG = -3, NETK_BADCMD = -4, NETK_FAIL = -5 };\nenum { NETK_CMD_INFO = 1, NETK_CMD_PING = 2, NETK_CMD_RESOLVE = 3, NETK_CMD_DHCP = 4, NETK_CMD_UDP = 5 };\n\n// Send a UDP datagram and wait for the first reply from `dst`.\nstatic int net_udp_xchg(uint32_t dst, uint16_t sport, uint16_t dport, const uint8_t* tx, uint32_t txlen,\n                        uint8_t* rx, uint32_t cap, uint32_t timeout_ms, uint32_t* rxlen) {\n    g_udp_got = false; g_udp_wait_port = sport;                          // arm before sending\n    if (!net_send_udp(dst, sport, dport, tx, txlen)) { g_udp_wait_port = 0; return NETK_TIMEOUT; }   // ARP/route failure\n    uint64_t dl = net_deadline(timeout_ms);\n    int rc = NETK_TIMEOUT;\n    while (!net_expired(dl)) {\n        net_poll();\n        if (!g_udp_got) continue;\n        if (g_udp_from == dst || dst == 0xFFFFFFFFu) {\n            uint32_t n = g_udp_len < cap ? g_udp_len : cap;\n            net_cpy(rx, g_udp_buf, n);\n            *rxlen = n; rc = NETK_OK; break;\n        }\n        g_udp_got = false;                                               // someone else's datagram: keep waiting\n    }\n    g_udp_wait_port = 0;\n    return rc;\n}\n\nstatic void net_mbox_fill_info(NetMboxK* m) {\n    m->ip = g_ip; m->mask = g_mask; m->gw = g_gw; m->dns = g_dns;\n    m->flags = (g_nic_type != NIC_NONE ? 1u : 0u) | (net_link_up() ? 2u : 0u) | (g_net_configured ? 4u : 0u);\n    for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) m->mac[i] = g_mac[i];\n    m->mac[6] = m->mac[7] = 0;\n    int i = 0;\n    for (; i < 63 && g_nic_name[i]; i++) m->name[i] = g_nic_name[i];\n    m->name[i] = 0;\n}\n\nstatic uint32_t net_clamp_timeout(uint32_t ms) { return ms == 0 ? 2000 : (ms < 50 ? 50 : (ms > 10000 ? 10000 : ms)); }\n\n// `tx`/`rx` are host pointers already translated (and bounds-checked) by the glue; null if invalid.\nextern \"C\" void kernel_net_mailbox(void* mbox, int cmd, const void* tx, void* rx) {\n    NetMboxK* m = (NetMboxK*)mbox;\n    if (!m) return;\n    m->name[sizeof(m->name) - 1] = 0;                                    // never trust guest strings\n    if (g_nic_type == NIC_NONE) { m->flags = 0; m->status = NETK_NODEV; return; }\n    switch (cmd) {\n    case NETK_CMD_INFO:\n        net_mbox_fill_info(m); m->status = NETK_OK; break;\n    case NETK_CMD_PING: {\n        if (m->ip == 0 || m->ip == 0xFFFFFFFFu) { m->status = NETK_BADARG; break; }\n        uint32_t rtt = 0;\n        if (net_ping_once(m->ip, net_clamp_timeout(m->timeout_ms), &rtt)) {\n            m->rtt_x10 = rtt; m->ttl = g_ping_ttl; m->status = NETK_OK;\n        } else m->status = NETK_TIMEOUT;\n        break;\n    }\n    case NETK_CMD_RESOLVE: {\n        uint32_t ip = 0;\n        if (!m->name[0]) { m->status = NETK_BADARG; break; }\n        if (net_resolve_host(m->name, &ip)) { m->ip = ip; m->status = NETK_OK; } else m->status = NETK_FAIL;\n        break;\n    }\n    case NETK_CMD_DHCP:\n        if (net_dhcp()) { net_mbox_fill_info(m); m->status = NETK_OK; } else m->status = NETK_FAIL;\n        break;\n    case NETK_CMD_UDP: {\n        if (!m->sport || m->sport > 65535 || !m->dport || m->dport > 65535 || m->tx_len == 0 || m->tx_len > 1400 ||\n            m->rx_cap == 0 || !tx || !rx) { m->status = NETK_BADARG; break; }\n        uint32_t got = 0;\n        m->status = net_udp_xchg(m->ip, (uint16_t)m->sport, (uint16_t)m->dport, (const uint8_t*)tx, m->tx_len,\n                                 (uint8_t*)rx, m->rx_cap, net_clamp_timeout(m->timeout_ms), &got);\n        m->rx_len = (m->status == NETK_OK) ? got : 0;\n        break;\n    }\n    default:\n        m->status = NETK_BADCMD; break;\n    }\n}\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\necho done"}, "message": "Running command", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/os/repo && python3 - <<'EOF'\\np='nettest.c'; s=open(p).read()\\ns=s.replace('''    rc = knet_resolve(\\\"300.1.1.1x\\\", &ip);\\n    result(\\\"garbage is rejected or not resolved to 300.x\\\", rc != NET_OK || (ip >> 24) != 300);''','''    rc = knet_resolve(\\\"\\\", &ip);\\n    result(\\\"empty host name is rejected\\\", rc != NET_OK);''')\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\n\\np='kernel_parts/07b_network.h'; s=open(p).read()\\ns+=r'''\\n\\n// \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500 guest network ABI (ports 0xD0-0xD4) \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n// Guest programs (compiled in-OS with `cc`, run under Bochs) reach the NIC via a\\n// mailbox, exactly like the disk/gfx wrappers.  Guest side: net.h.  The Bochs\\n// glue (bochs_glue.cpp: bochs_guest_net_cmd) turns the guest-physical addresses\\n// into host pointers and calls kernel_net_mailbox() below.\\n\\n// Must match net_mbox_t in net.h byte-for-byte (136 bytes, no padding).\\nstruct NetMboxK {\\n    int      status;\\n    uint32_t ip, mask, gw, dns, flags, timeout_ms, rtt_x10, ttl;\\n    uint32_t sport, dport, tx_addr, tx_len, rx_addr, rx_cap, rx_len;\\n    uint8_t  mac[8];\\n    char     name[64];\\n};\\nstatic_assert(sizeof(NetMboxK) == 136, \\\"NetMboxK must match net_mbox_t in net.h\\\");\\n\\nenum { NETK_OK = 0, NETK_NODEV = -1, NETK_TIMEOUT = -2, NETK_BADARG = -3, NETK_BADCMD = -4, NETK_FAIL = -5 };\\nenum { NETK_CMD_INFO = 1, NETK_CMD_PING = 2, NETK_CMD_RESOLVE = 3, NETK_CMD_DHCP = 4, NETK_CMD_UDP = 5 };\\n\\n// Send a UDP datagram and wait for the first reply from `dst`.\\nstatic int net_udp_xchg(uint32_t dst, uint16_t sport, uint16_t dport, const uint8_t* tx, uint32_t txlen,\\n                        uint8_t* rx, uint32_t cap, uint32_t timeout_ms, uint32_t* rxlen) {\\n    g_udp_got = false; g_udp_wait_port = sport;                          // arm before sending\\n    if (!net_send_udp(dst, sport, dport, tx, txlen)) { g_udp_wait_port = 0; return NETK_TIMEOUT; }   // ARP/route failure\\n    uint64_t dl = net_deadline(timeout_ms);\\n    int rc = NETK_TIMEOUT;\\n    while (!net_expired(dl)) {\\n        net_poll();\\n        if (!g_udp_got) continue;\\n        if (g_udp_from == dst || dst == 0xFFFFFFFFu) {\\n            uint32_t n = g_udp_len < cap ? g_udp_len : cap;\\n            net_cpy(rx, g_udp_buf, n);\\n            *rxlen = n; rc = NETK_OK; break;\\n        }\\n        g_udp_got = false;                                               // someone else's datagram: keep waiting\\n    }\\n    g_udp_wait_port = 0;\\n    return rc;\\n}\\n\\nstatic void net_mbox_fill_info(NetMboxK* m) {\\n    m->ip = g_ip; m->mask = g_mask; m->gw = g_gw; m->dns = g_dns;\\n    m->flags = (g_nic_type != NIC_NONE ? 1u : 0u) | (net_link_up() ? 2u : 0u) | (g_net_configured ? 4u : 0u);\\n    for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) m->mac[i] = g_mac[i];\\n    m->mac[6] = m->mac[7] = 0;\\n    int i = 0;\\n    for (; i < 63 && g_nic_name[i]; i++) m->name[i] = g_nic_name[i];\\n    m->name[i] = 0;\\n}\\n\\nstatic uint32_t net_clamp_timeout(uint32_t ms) { return ms == 0 ? 2000 : (ms < 50 ? 50 : (ms > 10000 ? 10000 : ms)); }\\n\\n// `tx`/`rx` are host pointers already translated (and bounds-checked) by the glue; null if invalid.\\nextern \\\"C\\\" void kernel_net_mailbox(void* mbox, int cmd, const void* tx, void* rx) {\\n    NetMboxK* m = (NetMboxK*)mbox;\\n    if (!m) return;\\n    m->name[sizeof(m->name) - 1] = 0;                                    // never trust guest strings\\n    if (g_nic_type == NIC_NONE) { m->flags = 0; m->status = NETK_NODEV; return; }\\n    switch (cmd) {\\n    case NETK_CMD_INFO:\\n        net_mbox_fill_info(m); m->status = NETK_OK; break;\\n    case NETK_CMD_PING: {\\n        if (m->ip == 0 || m->ip == 0xFFFFFFFFu) { m->status = NETK_BADARG; break; }\\n        uint32_t rtt = 0;\\n        if (net_ping_once(m->ip, net_clamp_timeout(m->timeout_ms), &rtt)) {\\n            m->rtt_x10 = rtt; m->ttl = g_ping_ttl; m->status = NETK_OK;\\n        } else m->status = NETK_TIMEOUT;\\n        break;\\n    }\\n    case NETK_CMD_RESOLVE: {\\n        uint32_t ip = 0;\\n        if (!m->name[0]) { m->status = NETK_BADARG; break; }\\n        if (net_resolve_host(m->name, &ip)) { m->ip = ip; m->status = NETK_OK; } else m->status = NETK_FAIL;\\n        break;\\n    }\\n    case NETK_CMD_DHCP:\\n        if (net_dhcp()) { net_mbox_fill_info(m); m->status = NETK_OK; } else m->status = NETK_FAIL;\\n        break;\\n    case NETK_CMD_UDP: {\\n        if (!m->sport || m->sport > 65535 || !m->dport || m->dport > 65535 || m->tx_len == 0 || m->tx_len > 1400 ||\\n            m->rx_cap == 0 || !tx || !rx) { m->status = NETK_BADARG; break; }\\n        uint32_t got = 0;\\n        m->status = net_udp_xchg(m->ip, (uint16_t)m->sport, (uint16_t)m->dport, (const uint8_t*)tx, m->tx_len,\\n                                 (uint8_t*)rx, m->rx_cap, net_clamp_timeout(m->timeout_ms), &got);\\n        m->rx_len = (m->status == NETK_OK) ? got : 0;\\n        break;\\n    }\\n    default:\\n        m->status = NETK_BADCMD; break;\\n    }\\n}\\n'''\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nEOF\\necho done\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:16:37.221588Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:16:37.221630Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01JRrfNvwfZaoTe8xeq4t6cE", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"done\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"done\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:16:39.213237Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:16:44.172826Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Wiring a network mailbox handler into the emulator glue code."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:16:44.172880Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:16:51.007498Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01LLuXdrULUZErw1YC9xRyf8", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/os/repo && python3 - <<'EOF'\n# --- bochs_infra.cpp ---\np='bochs_infra.cpp'; s=open(p).read()\na='static Bit32u s_gfx_addr_bytes[4] = {0, 0, 0, 0};\\n'\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,a+'''\n// Ports 0xD0-0xD4 -- guest network wrapper (see net.h and bochs_glue.cpp's\n// bochs_guest_net_cmd). Same latch-address-then-command shape as the disk\n// wrapper: address bytes to 0xD0-0xD3, command byte to 0xD4.\nextern \"C\" void bochs_guest_net_cmd(unsigned int mbox_addr, int cmd);\nstatic Bit32u s_net_addr_bytes[4] = {0, 0, 0, 0};\n''')\nb='    // Ports 0xEA-0xED \u2014 latch one byte each of the graphics mailbox\\'s\\n'\nassert s.count(b)==1\ns=s.replace(b,'''    // Ports 0xD0-0xD3 -- latch the net mailbox's guest-physical address.\n    else if (port >= 0xD0 && port <= 0xD3) {\n        s_net_addr_bytes[port - 0xD0] = (Bit32u)(val & 0xFF);\n    }\n    // Port 0xD4 -- net command trigger (info/ping/resolve/dhcp/udp).\n    else if (port == 0xD4) {\n        Bit32u addr = s_net_addr_bytes[0]\n                    | (s_net_addr_bytes[1] << 8)\n                    | (s_net_addr_bytes[2] << 16)\n                    | (s_net_addr_bytes[3] << 24);\n        bochs_guest_net_cmd(addr, (int)(val & 0xFF));\n    }\n'''+b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\n# --- bochs_glue.cpp ---\np='bochs_glue.cpp'; s=open(p).read()\na='''// =====================================================================\n// Graphics mailbox: guest framebuffer blit into its terminal window\n// ====================================================================='''\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,'''// =====================================================================\n// Network mailbox (ports 0xD0-0xD4): guest access to the kernel NIC driver\n// =====================================================================\n//\n// Guest side is net.h (net_mbox_t); the command logic lives in the kernel\n// (kernel_parts/07b_network.h: kernel_net_mailbox).  All this glue does is\n// translate the guest-physical addresses -- the mailbox itself plus its\n// optional UDP tx/rx buffers -- into host pointers, bounds-checked against\n// the slot's memory window, exactly like the disk wrapper above.\nstruct GuestNetMailbox {\n    int          status;\n    unsigned int ip, mask, gw, dns, flags, timeout_ms, rtt_x10, ttl;\n    unsigned int sport, dport, tx_addr, tx_len, rx_addr, rx_cap, rx_len;\n    unsigned char mac[8];\n    char         name[64];\n};\nstatic_assert(sizeof(GuestNetMailbox) == 136, \"must match net.h net_mbox_t\");\n\nextern \"C\" void kernel_net_mailbox(void* mbox, int cmd, const void* tx, void* rx);\n\nextern \"C\" void bochs_guest_net_cmd(unsigned int mbox_addr, int cmd) {\n    GuestNetMailbox* m =\n        (GuestNetMailbox*)disk_guest_ptr(mbox_addr, sizeof(GuestNetMailbox));\n    if (!m) {\n        disk_report(\"\\\\n[net] mailbox unreachable at guest addr \");\n        disk_report_hex32(mbox_addr);\n        disk_report(\" -- command dropped\\\\n\");\n        return;\n    }\n    const void* tx = (m->tx_len && m->tx_len <= 2048)\n                   ? disk_guest_ptr(m->tx_addr, m->tx_len) : nullptr;\n    void* rx = (m->rx_cap && m->rx_cap <= 65536)\n             ? disk_guest_ptr(m->rx_addr, m->rx_cap) : nullptr;\n    kernel_net_mailbox(m, cmd, tx, rx);\n}\n\n'''+a)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat bochs_infra.cpp bochs_glue.cpp; grep -n \"static_assert\" bochs_glue.cpp | head -2; diff <(sed -n 1,5p \"bochs_glue .cpp\") <(sed -n 1,5p bochs_glue.cpp) | head -3; grep -n \"bochs_glue\" Makefile | head -5"}, "message": "Running command", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/os/repo && python3 - <<'EOF'\\n# --- bochs_infra.cpp ---\\np='bochs_infra.cpp'; s=open(p).read()\\na='static Bit32u s_gfx_addr_bytes[4] = {0, 0, 0, 0};\\\\n'\\nassert s.count(a)==1\\ns=s.replace(a,a+'''\\n// Ports 0xD0-0xD4 -- guest network wrapper (see net.h and bochs_glue.cpp's\\n// bochs_guest_net_cmd). Same latch-address-then-command shape as the disk\\n// wrapper: address bytes to 0xD0-0xD3, command byte to 0xD4.\\nextern \\\"C\\\" void bochs_guest_net_cmd(unsigned int mbox_addr, int cmd);\\nstatic Bit32u s_net_addr_bytes[4] = {0, 0, 0, 0};\\n''')\\nb='    // Ports 0xEA-0xED \\u2014 latch one byte each of the graphics mailbox\\\\'s\\\\n'\\nassert s.count(b)==1\\ns=s.replace(b,'''    // Ports 0xD0-0xD3 -- latch the net mailbox's guest-physical address.\\n    else if (port >= 0xD0 && port <= 0xD3) {\\n        s_net_addr_bytes[port - 0xD0] = (Bit32u)(val & 0xFF);\\n    }\\n    // Port 0xD4 -- net command trigger (info/ping/resolve/dhcp/udp).\\n    else if (port == 0xD4) {\\n        Bit32u addr = s_net_addr_bytes[0]\\n                    | (s_net_addr_bytes[1] << 8)\\n                    | (s_net_addr_bytes[2] << 16)\\n                    | (s_net_addr_bytes[3] << 24);\\n        bochs_guest_net_cmd(addr, (int)(val & 0xFF));\\n    }\\n'''+b)\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\n\\n# --- bochs_glue.cpp ---\\np='bochs_glue.cpp'; s=open(p).read()\\na='''// =====================================================================\\n// Graphics mailbox: guest framebuffer blit into its terminal window\\n// ====================================================================='''\\nassert s.count(a)==1\\ns=s.replace(a,'''// =====================================================================\\n// Network mailbox (ports 0xD0-0xD4): guest access to the kernel NIC driver\\n// =====================================================================\\n//\\n// Guest side is net.h (net_mbox_t); the command logic lives in the kernel\\n// (kernel_parts/07b_network.h: kernel_net_mailbox).  All this glue does is\\n// translate the guest-physical addresses -- the mailbox itself plus its\\n// optional UDP tx/rx buffers -- into host pointers, bounds-checked against\\n// the slot's memory window, exactly like the disk wrapper above.\\nstruct GuestNetMailbox {\\n    int          status;\\n    unsigned int ip, mask, gw, dns, flags, timeout_ms, rtt_x10, ttl;\\n    unsigned int sport, dport, tx_addr, tx_len, rx_addr, rx_cap, rx_len;\\n    unsigned char mac[8];\\n    char         name[64];\\n};\\nstatic_assert(sizeof(GuestNetMailbox) == 136, \\\"must match net.h net_mbox_t\\\");\\n\\nextern \\\"C\\\" void kernel_net_mailbox(void* mbox, int cmd, const void* tx, void* rx);\\n\\nextern \\\"C\\\" void bochs_guest_net_cmd(unsigned int mbox_addr, int cmd) {\\n    GuestNetMailbox* m =\\n        (GuestNetMailbox*)disk_guest_ptr(mbox_addr, sizeof(GuestNetMailbox));\\n    if (!m) {\\n        disk_report(\\\"\\\\\\\\n[net] mailbox unreachable at guest addr \\\");\\n        disk_report_hex32(mbox_addr);\\n        disk_report(\\\" -- command dropped\\\\\\\\n\\\");\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    const void* tx = (m->tx_len && m->tx_len <= 2048)\\n                   ? disk_guest_ptr(m->tx_addr, m->tx_len) : nullptr;\\n    void* rx = (m->rx_cap && m->rx_cap <= 65536)\\n             ? disk_guest_ptr(m->rx_addr, m->rx_cap) : nullptr;\\n    kernel_net_mailbox(m, cmd, tx, rx);\\n}\\n\\n'''+a)\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nEOF\\ngit diff --stat bochs_infra.cpp bochs_glue.cpp; grep -n \\\"static_assert\\\" bochs_glue.cpp | head -2; diff <(sed -n 1,5p \\\"bochs_glue .cpp\\\") <(sed -n 1,5p bochs_glue.cpp) | head -3; grep -n \\\"bochs_glue\\\" Makefile | head -5\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:16:51.239098Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-05T23:16:51.239135Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01LLuXdrULUZErw1YC9xRyf8", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":2,\"stdout\":\"\",\"stderr\":\"/bin/sh: 75: Syntax error: \\\"(\\\" unexpected\\n\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"plaintext\", \"code\": \"/bin/sh: 75: Syntax error: \\\"(\\\" unexpected\\n\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-05T23:16:51.686200Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-05T23:16:51.686200Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a10e58-677e-72e9-a79a-b1fc7254157f"}]},{"uuid": "9b49b4f7-5793-47bd-9c35-9aa445be7e05", "name": "LLM code generation from medical simulation", "summary": "", "created_at": "2026-10-06T09:02:21.786054Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-06T09:43:00.230010Z", "account": {"uuid": "8d7882cd-3e98-47cc-a6e7-61494a1ee4ac"}, "chat_messages": [{"uuid": "01a11073-1d9a-73aa-b5f3-bd6a2337b9dc", "text": "make sure this gains insights from this simulation as recommendations of code snippits for llms as a generatorhttps://github.com/synthreason-source/med", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-06T09:02:23.323287Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-06T09:02:23.323287Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "make sure this gains insights from this simulation as recommendations of code snippits for llms as a generatorhttps://github.com/synthreason-source/med", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-06T09:02:23.323499Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-06T09:02:23.323499Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000"}, {"uuid": "01a11073-1d9a-7502-a430-f3e6d06a4847", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThe repo page only shows the file listing, so I'll fetch the actual source files.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI read `neural_circuit_simulation.py`, which holds all the simulation logic. I'll turn its lessons into generator-side snippets and test them on a toy model.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nVocab (12) is smaller than `top_k` (16). I'll clamp `top_k` to the vocab size.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI turned the simulation's lessons into eight self-contained code snippets for LLM decoding, in the file above. It runs end to end on a toy bigram model, but I haven't tried it on a real LLM. I read only `neural_circuit_simulation.py`, not `app.py` or `generate_connectivity_npy.py`, and I didn't run the MRI simulation itself.\n\nEach snippet takes a `step_fn(tokens) -> logits` callable, so it should plug into HF, llama.cpp, or any API that returns logprobs.\n\n| Insight from the simulation | Snippet for generation |\n|---|---|\n| Beam search with `heapq` pruning, linked-list paths and per-node dedup | `beam_generate` stores paths as `(token, parent)` tuples, keeps the best score per local state, and takes an optional small goal-progress bonus. |\n| Beam width 60 failed on the real data and 200 worked | `calibrate_beam_width` sweeps widths against a wide-beam reference instead of guessing. |\n| The default parameters saturated the whole graph, and the subcritical ones died out | `temperature_for_entropy` and `sample_critical` hold entropy in a target band instead of fixing a temperature. |\n| Periodic self-stimulation on top of decay | `LeakyAnchorBias` is a decaying logit bias on goal tokens that is re-pulsed on a schedule, to counter topic drift. |\n| A connected-component check, plus a Manhattan lower bound for the hop budget | `token_budget` checks that a grammar's accepting state is reachable and sets `max_new_tokens` to the shortest path plus slack. |\n| Robust 99th-percentile normalisation of the MRI intensities | `robust_normalise` and `combined_score` keep outliers from dominating a mixed ranker. |\n| Fixed-size records read through `mmap` | `read_records` uses `np.memmap` with a structured dtype, which avoids the sim's one-`struct.unpack`-per-edge Python loop. |\n| The earlier \"holographic resonance\" score was decorative | `score_signal_check` fails if a heuristic doesn't correlate with a verifiable objective. |\n\nReading the code, I noticed that with `decay=0.6, gain=0.4, threshold=0.55`, a seed activity of 1.0 pushes at most 0.4 onto each neighbour. That is below the 0.55 firing threshold, so activity can't spread past the seed's immediate neighbours. The self-stimulation \"wavefront\" is therefore probably just the seed plus its neighbours, which is a sharp threshold effect rather than gradual dying out. For decoding, this means anchor bias alone won't spread influence, so it needs to be combined with the entropy control. I haven't confirmed this by running the simulation.\n\nThe mapping from graph to LLM is an analogy. The snippets are sound engineering patterns, but the simulation doesn't show that they improve LLM output. Compare them against a baseline on your own task.\n\nIf you'd like, I can look at `app.py` too, or wire these into a Hugging Face `generate()` loop.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-06T09:02:23.323059Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-06T09:02:23.520519Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01ETBo4dyBhXU6teii7b4w19", "name": "web_fetch", "input": {"url": "https://github.com/synth