s": null, "type": "text", "text": "The browser side works. The remaining risk is the kernel TCP code, which only a real boot can validate. Let me try building the kernel here; first the build dependencies.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:47:30.314932Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:47:30.996428Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01AAyYtGra7gCoEDFJWvk479", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && (apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends gcc-multilib g++-multilib nasm grub-pc-bin grub-common xorriso >/tmp/dep.log 2>&1; tail -2 /tmp/dep.log); sed -n 1,70p Makefile", "description": "Install kernel build deps and read top of Makefile"}, "message": "Install kernel build deps and read top of Makefile", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && (apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends gcc-multilib g++-multilib nasm grub-pc-bin grub-common xorriso >/tmp/dep.log 2>&1; tail -2 /tmp/dep.log); sed -n 1,70p Makefile\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:49:05.601627Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:49:05.601795Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01AAyYtGra7gCoEDFJWvk479", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"Setting up g++-multilib (4:13.2.0-7ubuntu1) ...\\r\\nProcessing triggers for libc-bin (2.39-0ubuntu8.9) ...\\r\\n# ============================================================\\n#  Makefile \u2013 Bare-metal OS with Bochs CPU emulation + BusyBox\\n# ============================================================\\n\\nISODIR   := iso\\nMULTIBOOT := $(ISODIR)/boot/main.elf\\nMAIN     := main.iso\\nDISK_IMG := disk.img\\n\\n# \u2500\u2500 Compiler flags \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\nCXXFLAGS := -ffreestanding -O2 -Wall -Wextra \\\\\\n            -fno-use-cxa-atexit -std=c++17    \\\\\\n            -fno-exceptions -fno-rtti -m32    \\\\\\n            -fno-stack-protector              \\\\\\n            -fno-pie -fno-pic                 \\\\\\n            -include fixes.h                  \\\\\\n            -include instrument_stub.h\\n\\n# \u2500\u2500 Bochs 2.0 \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\n# Source: the official bochs-emu/Bochs GitHub mirror, tag REL_2_0_FINAL\\n# (verified to exist and download correctly; the old SourceForge\\n# \\\"bochs-2.0.tar.gz\\\" path used previously could not be confirmed to\\n# exist and was producing bad downloads). The tag archive's top-level\\n# layout is Bochs-REL_2_0_FINAL/bochs/... , so extraction strips 2\\n# path components to land the real source tree directly at $(BOCHS_DIR).\\n#\\n# Bochs 2.0's internals are structurally different from what\\n# bochs_glue.cpp/bochs_infra.cpp were written against (Bochs 2.7):\\n#   - no gui/paramtree.cc split (param-tree classes live in\\n#     gui/siminterface.cc instead, with an older API)\\n#   - no cpu/cpudb/ (CPU model database; added in 2.5)\\n#   - fpu/ is a top-level directory here, not cpu/fpu/ (that move\\n#     happened in 2.6.1)\\n# The $(BOCHS_CPU_LIB) recipe below also applies several small source\\n# patches (via patch-bochs-2.0.sh) needed to build this 2003-era code\\n# with a modern (GCC 13 / glibc) toolchain - see that script for the\\n# details of each fix. cpu/, fpu/, and memory/ have been verified to\\n# build cleanly after these patches; the remaining glue-code port\\n# (paramtree API -> siminterface API) is still in progress.\\nBOCHS_VERSION   := 2.0\\nBOCHS_TAG       := REL_$(subst .,_,$(BOCHS_VERSION))_FINAL\\nBOCHS_DIR       := bochs-$(BOCHS_VERSION)\\nBOCHS_ARCHIVE   := $(BOCHS_DIR)-src.tar.gz\\nBOCHS_URL       := https://codeload.github.com/bochs-emu/Bochs/tar.gz/refs/tags/$(BOCHS_TAG)\\nBOCHS_CPU_LIB   := $(BOCHS_DIR)/cpu/libcpu.a\\n\\n# Base64-encoded copy of the Bochs 2.0 patch script, embedded directly\\n# so the fix can never go stale relative to a separate file on disk -\\n# this IS the source of truth; patch-bochs-2.0.sh is (re)written from it\\n# fresh on every build. See the comments inside the script (or run it\\n# with no args after decoding) for what each numbered fix addresses.\\ndefine BOCHS_PATCH_SCRIPT_B64\\\\nendef\\n\\n\\n# \u2500\u2500 BusyBox 32-bit static (musl) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\nBUSYBOX_URL := https://busybox.net/downloads/binaries/1.35.0-i686-linux-musl/busybox\\nBUSYBOX_BIN := busybox\\n\\n# ============================================================\\n#  Top-level targets\\n# ============================================================\\nall: $(MAIN) $(DISK_IMG)\\n\\n# world: one-shot bootstrap for a totally fresh checkout.\\n#   1. Downloads + builds Bochs 2.0 (cpu/fpu/memory static libs)\\n#   2. Downloads + builds TCC (i386-tcc, libtcc.a, and the in-kernel\\n#      i386-libtcc-kern.a)\\n#   3. Links the kernel against both and produces main.iso + disk.img\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"Setting up g++-multilib (4:13.2.0-7ubuntu1) ...\\r\\nProcessing triggers for libc-bin (2.39-0ubuntu8.9) ...\\r\\n# ============================================================\\n#  Makefile \u2013 Bare-metal OS with Bochs CPU emulation + BusyBox\\n# ============================================================\\n\\nISODIR   := iso\\nMULTIBOOT := $(ISODIR)/boot/main.elf\\nMAIN     := main.iso\\nDISK_IMG := disk.img\\n\\n# \u2500\u2500 Compiler flags \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\nCXXFLAGS := -ffreestanding -O2 -Wall -Wextra \\\\\\n            -fno-use-cxa-atexit -std=c++17    \\\\\\n            -fno-exceptions -fno-rtti -m32    \\\\\\n            -fno-stack-protector              \\\\\\n            -fno-pie -fno-pic                 \\\\\\n            -include fixes.h                  \\\\\\n            -include instrument_stub.h\\n\\n# \u2500\u2500 Bochs 2.0 \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\n# Source: the official bochs-emu/Bochs GitHub mirror, tag REL_2_0_FINAL\\n# (verified to exist and download correctly; the old SourceForge\\n# \\\"bochs-2.0.tar.gz\\\" path used previously could not be confirmed to\\n# exist and was producing bad downloads). The tag archive's top-level\\n# layout is Bochs-REL_2_0_FINAL/bochs/... , so extraction strips 2\\n# path components to land the real source tree directly at $(BOCHS_DIR).\\n#\\n# Bochs 2.0's internals are structurally different from what\\n# bochs_glue.cpp/bochs_infra.cpp were written against (Bochs 2.7):\\n#   - no gui/paramtree.cc split (param-tree classes live in\\n#     gui/siminterface.cc instead, with an older API)\\n#   - no cpu/cpudb/ (CPU model database; added in 2.5)\\n#   - fpu/ is a top-level directory here, not cpu/fpu/ (that move\\n#     happened in 2.6.1)\\n# The $(BOCHS_CPU_LIB) recipe below also applies several small source\\n# patches (via patch-bochs-2.0.sh) needed to build this 2003-era code\\n# with a modern (GCC 13 / glibc) toolchain - see that script for the\\n# details of each fix. cpu/, fpu/, and memory/ have been verified to\\n# build cleanly after these patches; the remaining glue-code port\\n# (paramtree API -> siminterface API) is still in progress.\\nBOCHS_VERSION   := 2.0\\nBOCHS_TAG       := REL_$(subst .,_,$(BOCHS_VERSION))_FINAL\\nBOCHS_DIR       := bochs-$(BOCHS_VERSION)\\nBOCHS_ARCHIVE   := $(BOCHS_DIR)-src.tar.gz\\nBOCHS_URL       := https://codeload.github.com/bochs-emu/Bochs/tar.gz/refs/tags/$(BOCHS_TAG)\\nBOCHS_CPU_LIB   := $(BOCHS_DIR)/cpu/libcpu.a\\n\\n# Base64-encoded copy of the Bochs 2.0 patch script, embedded directly\\n# so the fix can never go stale relative to a separate file on disk -\\n# this IS the source of truth; patch-bochs-2.0.sh is (re)written from it\\n# fresh on every build. See the comments inside the script (or run it\\n# with no args after decoding) for what each numbered fix addresses.\\ndefine BOCHS_PATCH_SCRIPT_B64\\\\nendef\\n\\n\\n# \u2500\u2500 BusyBox 32-bit static (musl) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\nBUSYBOX_URL := https://busybox.net/downloads/binaries/1.35.0-i686-linux-musl/busybox\\nBUSYBOX_BIN := busybox\\n\\n# ============================================================\\n#  Top-level targets\\n# ============================================================\\nall: $(MAIN) $(DISK_IMG)\\n\\n# world: one-shot bootstrap for a totally fresh checkout.\\n#   1. Downloads + builds Bochs 2.0 (cpu/fpu/memory static libs)\\n#   2. Downloads + builds TCC (i386-tcc, libtcc.a, and the in-kernel\\n#      i386-libtcc-kern.a)\\n#   3. Links the kernel against both and produces main.iso + disk.img\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:49:10.051491Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:49:10.051716Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "It's a heavy build (Bochs 2.0 plus TCC), but the repo bundles the tarballs. I'll build in a scratch copy so I don't pollute the source tree.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:49:10.051722Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:49:11.416973Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01MWe1sthUvVBnkxRXshfP36", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "rm -rf /tmp/kb && mkdir /tmp/kb && cd /home/claude/OS && tar --exclude=.git --exclude=build --exclude=disk.img --exclude='*.iso' -cf - . | (cd /tmp/kb && tar xf -) && cd /tmp/kb && cp /home/claude/OS/main.iso /tmp/main.orig.iso && ls | head -3 && (setsid nohup sh -c 'make BOCHS=1 -j4 > /tmp/kbuild.log 2>&1; echo BUILD_EXIT=$? >> /tmp/kbuild.log' >/dev/null 2>&1 < /dev/null &); sleep 45; tail -5 /tmp/kbuild.log", "description": "Start kernel build in a scratch copy"}, "message": "Start kernel build in a scratch copy", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"rm -rf /tmp/kb && mkdir /tmp/kb && cd /home/claude/OS && tar --exclude=.git --exclude=build --exclude=disk.img --exclude='*.iso' -cf - . | (cd /tmp/kb && tar xf -) && cd /tmp/kb && cp /home/claude/OS/main.iso /tmp/main.orig.iso && ls | head -3 && (setsid nohup sh -c 'make BOCHS=1 -j4 > /tmp/kbuild.log 2>&1; echo BUILD_EXIT=$? >> /tmp/kbuild.log' >/dev/null 2>&1 < /dev/null &); sleep 45; tail -5 /tmp/kbuild.log\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:49:58.927489Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:49:58.927536Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01MWe1sthUvVBnkxRXshfP36", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"COMP.H\\nDISK_WRAPPER.md\\nEDITF.C\\n  342 |            static char *name[] = { \\\"ignore\\\", \\\"report\\\", \\\"ask\\\", \\\"fatal\\\" };\\n      |                                                        ^~~~~\\n../bochs.h:342:63: warning: ISO C++ forbids converting a string constant to 'char*' [-Wwrite-strings]\\n  342 |            static char *name[] = { \\\"ignore\\\", \\\"report\\\", \\\"ask\\\", \\\"fatal\\\" };\\n      |                                                               ^~~~~~~\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"COMP.H\\nDISK_WRAPPER.md\\nEDITF.C\\n  342 |            static char *name[] = { \\\"ignore\\\", \\\"report\\\", \\\"ask\\\", \\\"fatal\\\" };\\n      |                                                        ^~~~~\\n../bochs.h:342:63: warning: ISO C++ forbids converting a string constant to 'char*' [-Wwrite-strings]\\n  342 |            static char *name[] = { \\\"ignore\\\", \\\"report\\\", \\\"ask\\\", \\\"fatal\\\" };\\n      |                                                               ^~~~~~~\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:50:00.645851Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:50:02.866623Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Building Bochs while updating the project's documentation pages."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:50:02.866740Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:50:02.866901Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "While that builds, I'll update the sample pages for online use.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:50:02.866908Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-07T19:50:07.072308Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Po73y18zWw7bd2Ku79tFZn", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS/www && python3 - <<'EOF'\nh=open('home.htm').read()\nh=h.replace('''<h2>Source files</h2>''','''<h2>Web (plain http only)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"http://example.com/\">example.com</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"http://info.cern.ch/\">info.cern.ch</a> - the first website</li>\n<li><a href=\"http://neverssl.com/\">neverssl.com</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"http://10.0.2.2:8000/\">10.0.2.2:8000</a> - your host PC when running under QEMU user networking</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Type an address such as <b>example.com</b> in the box above.</p>\n<h2>Source files</h2>''')\nopen('home.htm','w').write(h)\na=open('about.htm').read()\na=a.replace('<li>No network: the kernel has no TCP and guests have no socket ABI</li>','<li>http:// only: no TLS, so https sites cannot be opened</li>\\n<li>The desktop freezes while a page downloads</li>')\na=a.replace('<dt>drivers.h</dt><dd>disk (kfread), gfx, mouse and key ports</dd>','<dt>drivers.h</dt><dd>disk (kfread), network (knet_http_get), gfx, mouse and key ports</dd>\\n<dt>07b_network.h</dt><dd>the kernel NIC driver, DHCP, DNS and TCP</dd>')\na=a.replace('<p>A flow-layout renderer in one C file.','<p>A web browser in one C file.')\nopen('about.htm','w').write(a)\nk=open('help.htm').read()\nk=k.replace('<li>Drag the scrollbar on the right.</li>','<li>Type <code>example.com</code> or <code>http://host:port/path</code> to load a web page. Redirects are followed.</li>\\n<li>Drag the scrollbar on the right.</li>')\nopen('help.htm','w').write(k)\nEOF\ngrep -c \"http\" home.htm about.htm help.htm; tail -3 /tmp/kbuild.log | cut -c1-150", "description": "Update sample pages for online browsing"}, "message": "Update sample pages for online browsing", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS/www && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nh=open('home.htm').read()\\nh=h.replace('''<h2>Source files</h2>''','''<h2>Web (plain http only)</h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\\"http://example.com/\\\">example.com</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"http://info.cern.ch/\\\">info.cern.ch</a> - the first website</li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"http://neverssl.com/\\\">neverssl.com</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\\"http://10.0.2.2:8000/\\\">10.0.2.2:8000</a> - your host PC when running under QEMU user networking</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>Type an address such as <b>example.com</b> in the box above.</p>\\n<h2>Source files</h2>''')\\nopen('home.htm','w').write(h)\\na=open('about.htm').read()\\na=a.replace('<li>No network: the kernel has no TCP and guests have no socket ABI</li>','<li>http:// only: no TLS, so https sites cannot be opened</li>\\\\n<li>The desktop freezes while a page downloads</li>')\\na=a.replace('<dt>drivers.h</dt><dd>disk (kfread), gfx, mouse and key ports</dd>','<dt>drivers.h</dt><dd>disk (kfread), network (knet_http_get), gfx, mouse and key ports</dd>\\\\n<dt>07b_network.h</dt><dd>the kernel NIC driver, DHCP, DNS and TCP</dd>')\\na=a.replace('<p>A flow-layout renderer in one C file.','<p>A web browser in one C fil