: fell back to the most frequent trigram\\n\\n[generated] (tau=0.5, beams keep 68% of candidates)\\n..). it it the a vat is is a first) in the first, the first to the the vat.' in the be the a a vat is in in the vat., a s s the such a vat, is is a s a be a the be it a not- not\\n\\nvocabulary: 4373 words   trigram contexts: 18,745   tokens: 34,333\\ninfluence space Y: 300 x 300 (expm of transition matrix)\\nmost frequent: ,(2166), the(1702), .(1679), of(1209), to(697)\\nsorted next-word probabilities after '. .': 0.086 0.025 0.024 0.021 0.018 0.016 0.015 0.014 0.012 0.012   (plot: sorted_prob_line.png)\\nrecognition audit (ablate the 3 most frequent words):\\n  S removed: True   D = 0.383   -> The rules themselves changed: Gamma(H-S) != Gamma(H), a genuinely new layer\\n  in R_n | in R_n+1 | count | meaning\\n   True  |  True    |  2865 | same thing, seen the same way both times\\n   False |  False   |  2381 | still invisible under both rule-sets\\n   False |  True    | 16207 | existed but unrecognised, recognised once the rules updated  <- the paper's claim\\n   True  |  False   |  1230 | not addressed by the paper (included for completeness)\\n=== --model counts --base pi_step --prompt 'the world'\\nTraceback (most recent call last):\\n  File \\\"/mnt/user-data/outputs/pi_transformer_numpy.py\\\", line 1213, in <module>\\n    sys.exit(main())\\n             ^^^^^^\\n  File \\\"/mnt/user-data/outputs/pi_transformer_numpy.py\\\", line 1194, in main\\n    pi = PiTransformer(corpus, model, amp, EntropySource(args.rng, port=args.port),\\n         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\n  File \\\"/mnt/user-data/outputs/pi_transformer_numpy.py\\\", line 973, in __init__\\n    raise ValueError(\\\"pi_step needs a dense V x V matrix; vocabulary too large.\\\")\\nValueError: pi_step needs a dense V x V matrix; vocabulary too large.\\n=== --model counts --ablate the,of --max-new 20 --prompt 'meaning'\\n\\n[generated] (tau=0.5, beams keep 18% of candidates)\\nmeaning meaning is a tree in front stars stars stars stars stars stars stars stars stars stars stars stars stars stars stars\\n\\nvocabulary: 4373 words   trigram contexts: 18,745   tokens: 34,333\\ninfluence space Y: 300 x 300 (expm of transition matrix)\\nmost frequent: ,(2166), the(1702), .(1679), of(1209), to(697)\\nsorted next-word probabilities after 'meaning meaning': 0.320 0.080 0.080 0.080 0.080 0.040 0.040 0.040 0.040 0.040   (plot: sorted_prob_line.png)\\nrecognition audit (ablate the 3 most frequent words):\\n  S removed: True   D = 0.383   -> The rules themselves changed: Gamma(H-S) != Gamma(H), a genuinely new layer\\n  in R_n | in R_n+1 | count | meaning\\n   True  |  True    |  2865 | same thing, seen the same way both times\\n   False |  False   |  2381 | still invisible under both rule-sets\\n   False |  True    | 16207 | existed but unrecognised, recognised once the rules updated  <- the paper's claim\\n   True  |  False   |  1230 | not addressed by the paper (included for completeness)\\naudit for S = the,of:\\n  S removed: True   D = 0.222   -> The rules themselves changed: Gamma(H-S) != Gamma(H), a genuinely new layer\\n  in R_n | in R_n+1 | count | meaning\\n   True  |  True    |  3374 | same thing, seen the same way both times\\n   False |  False   |  1400 | still invisible under both rule-sets\\n   False |  True    | 15491 | existed but unrecognised, recognised once the rules updated  <- the paper's claim\\n   True  |  False   |   721 | not addressed by the paper (included for completeness)\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-12T08:44:18.134237Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-12T08:44:23.459363Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Debugging fuzzy matching and prompt trigram fallback logic."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "s