estamp": "2026-10-14T09:20:17.344069Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:20:18.204990Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01GBSAyC9EMJ83HsRsWMiZ9M", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude && sed -i 's/^DEFAULT_TAU = 0.50/DEFAULT_TAU = 0.35   # calibrated: ~70% of top candidates satisfy D <= tau/' nia_v2.py && python3 -m py_compile nia_v2.py && cp nia_v2.py /mnt/user-data/outputs/nia_bitnet.py && python3 t.py | tail -6 && grep -n \"DEFAULT_TAU =\" /mnt/user-data/outputs/nia_bitnet.py", "description": "Set calibrated tau, compile, copy to outputs"}, "message": "Set calibrated tau, compile, copy to outputs", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude && sed -i 's/^DEFAULT_TAU = 0.50/DEFAULT_TAU = 0.35   # calibrated: ~70% of top candidates satisfy D <= tau/' nia_v2.py && python3 -m py_compile nia_v2.py && cp nia_v2.py /mnt/user-data/outputs/nia_bitnet.py && python3 t.py | tail -6 && grep -n \\\"DEFAULT_TAU =\\\" /mnt/user-data/outputs/nia_bitnet.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:20:18.977545Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:20:18.977584Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01GBSAyC9EMJ83HsRsWMiZ9M", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"T 40 min fid 0.948 0.18419137965797\\nD pct [0.214 0.249 0.316 0.365 0.433]\\n0.4 0.9\\n0.45 0.97\\n0.5 0.99\\n0.55 1.0\\n78:DEFAULT_TAU = 0.35   # calibrated: ~70% of top candidates satisfy D <= tau\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"T 40 min fid 0.948 0.18419137965797\\nD pct [0.214 0.249 0.316 0.365 0.433]\\n0.4 0.9\\n0.45 0.97\\n0.5 0.99\\n0.55 1.0\\n78:DEFAULT_TAU = 0.35   # calibrated: ~70% of top candidates satisfy D <= tau\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:20:21.154669Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:20:21.398826Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01DTteaQ9qjCavuC4dtovWjo", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/nia_bitnet.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/nia_bitnet.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:20:21.428289Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:20:21.428318Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01DTteaQ9qjCavuC4dtovWjo", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/nia_bitnet.py", "name": "nia bitnet", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "\n\nThe file cards appear with your reply, and where they sit relative to its text depends on the app the user is reading in; finish the reply with text, and refer to a file by its name, never as above or below."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:20:28.405007Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:20:30.595239Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I rewrote `nia_bitnet.py` to follow the diagram's seven sections. Previously it only had the fragment transforms, a lambda ramp and a consistency filter. The engine maths passed my numpy tests, but I couldn't install torch here, so I haven't run the Hugging Face generation path. Run `check` first, then `build` and `generate` on your machine.\n\n**How each section is implemented**\n1. **Original map F**: the base language model, used only through its next-token log-probabilities. Nothing tries to reconstruct it.\n2. **Fragments g_k**: four of them, with the diagram's shapes.\n   - g1 maps R\u2075 to R\u00b3 (nonlinear flow).\n   - g2 maps {0,1}\u2078 to R\u2074 (discrete transform).\n   - g3 maps C\u2076 to R\u2074 (convolutional).\n   - g4 maps R\u2075 to {0,1}\u00b3 (thresholding).\n3. **Adiabatic path**: a smoothstep \u03bb(t) drives a 4-dimensional quantum state \u03c8. It follows `i\u00b7\u0127\u00b7d\u03c8/dt = H(\u03bb)\u03c8` with `H = (1\u2212\u03bb)H\u2080 + \u03bbH\u2081`, evolved exactly one step per token.\n4. **Inversion operators I_k**: local, pseudo-inverse-based and lossy. They are not F\u207b\u00b9.\n5. **Diopathane condition D**: a weighted sum of the four example forms from the diagram: latent consistency, cross-fragment coherence, round-trip closure `I_k(g_k(x)) vs x`, and information conservation (\u03c8 norm and the candidate's overlap with \u03c8). \"D = 0\" is implemented as D \u2264 tau.\n6. **Separated spaces**: `python nia_bitnet.py check` prints the non-isomorphism report without downloading anything.\n7. **Pipeline and conditional correspondence**: candidates with D \u2264 tau are related to F and scored with its log-probability. Candidates with D > tau stay distinct and are masked out.\n\n**Test results**\n- The unitary evolution keeps the state norm at 1.\n- At 80 tokens the adiabatic parameter is about 0.09, so the \"|d\u03bb/dt| \u226a 1\" condition holds. The state stays at \u2265 0.99 overlap with the instantaneous ground state. Very short runs of 10 to 20 tokens are not adiabatic, and the fidelity drops.\n- The round trips are never exact (errors of roughly 0.2 to 0.75 per fragment), so no I_k acts as an inverse.\n- I calibrated the default `tau` to 0.35, so about 70% of top candidates pass D. Raise it to loosen the filter or lower it to tighten it.\n\n**Usage**\n```\npython nia_bitnet.py check\npython nia_bitnet.py build --out ./nia-model\npython nia_bitnet.py generate --model ./nia-model --prompt \"The machine\" --tokens 80 --trace\n```\n`--trace` prints, for each step, \u03bb, the ground-state fidelity and how many candidates satisfied D.\n\n**Caveats**\n- If every candidate fails D, the script keeps the top one anyway so generation can continue. The trace flags these steps as `fallback`.\n- The model folder is now `./nia-model` (the default changed from `./nia-bitnet`). Folders saved by the previous version still load, but they get the new engine rebuilt from their seed.\n- \"Diopathane\" is still just your label. The constraint is a heuristic filter, and it doesn't make the text more correct in any measurable way.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:20:30.670195Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:20:30.670195Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a139b3-c88d-7f12-abcf-99b3e9e11fbb"}]},{"uuid": "9ebd9635-1e9b-49b5-885d-6c073a51de0e", "name": "Recursive token feedback loops for model cognition", "summary": "", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:26:07.142090Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:40:21.150785Z", "account": {"uuid": "8d7882cd-3e98-47cc-a6e7-61494a1ee4ac"}, "chat_messages": [{"uuid": "01a139bb-b832-7b6c-aac6-d08322fa4981", "text": "make the model understand the tokens it generates in a cybernetic fashion, just pipe output to input again and again then add congitive tokens in between, at the beginning of the new prompts", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:26:08.828569Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:26:08.828569Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "make the model understand the tokens it generates in a cybernetic fashion, just pipe output to input again and again then add congitive tokens in between, at the beginning of the new prompts", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:26:08.828922Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:26:08.828922Z", "attachments": [{"file_name": "", "file_size": 12540, "file_type": "txt", "extracted_content": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nNon-isomorphic adiabatic text generator\n=======================================\n\nA runnable corpus-based text generator in which next-token candidates are\nscored by an n-gram language model and filtered/reweighted by several\nnon-isomorphic process fragments.\n\nConceptual mapping:\n  F       reference next-token distribution from the n-gram model\n  g_k     fragment-specific transforms of candidate/context features\n  I_k     local approximate inverse/lift (not a global inverse)\n  lambda  smooth adiabatic continuation from exploratory to selective scoring\n  D       proposed \"diopathane\" consistency score\n  tau     maximum permitted D score for a candidate\n\nThis is an experimental algorithmic analogy, not an established physical\nmodel. \"Diopathane\" is a user-defined name for the consistency constraint.\n\nExamples:\n  python nonisomorphic_adiabatic_textgen.py corpus.txt --prompt \"once upon a\" --tokens 80\n  python nonisomorphic_adiabatic_textgen.py --prompt \"The machine\" --tokens 60\n  python nonisomorphic_adiabatic_textgen.py corpus.txt --order 4 --beam 8 --tau 0.65\n\nOnly dependency: NumPy\nInstall: python -m pip install numpy\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport math\nimport random\nimport re\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Sequence, Tuple\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nTOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"[A-Za-z]+(?:['\u2019][A-Za-z]+)*|\\\\d+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?|[^\\\\w\\\\s]\", re.UNICODE)\nwith open(input(\"Filename: \"), \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as file:\n        \n    BUILTIN_CORPUS = file.read()\n\n\ndef tokenize(text: str) -> List[str]:\n    return text.split()\n\n\ndef detokenize(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Join tokens into readable text without spaces before common punctuation.\"\"\"\n    out = \"\"\n    no_space_before = set(\".,!?;:%)]}\u00bb\u201d\u2019\")\n    no_space_after = set(\"([{\u00ab\u201c\u2018\")\n    for token in tokens:\n        if not out:\n            out = token\n        elif token in no_space_before or out[-1:] in no_space_after:\n            out += token\n        else:\n            out += \" \" + token\n    return out\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Candidate:\n    token: str\n    base_logp: float\n    score: float\n    consistency: float\n    alignment: float\n    probability: float = 0.0\n\n\nclass NGramModel:\n    \"\"\"Smoothed n-gram model with backoff to shorter contexts.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, order: int = 3, alpha: float = 0.25):\n        self.order = max(1, int(order))\n        self.alpha = max(1e-9, float(alpha))\n        self.counts = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(self.order)]\n        self.vocab = Counter()\n        self.total_tokens = 0\n\n    def train(self, text: str) -> None:\n        tokens = [\"<bos>\"] * (self.order - 1) + tokenize(text) + [\"<eos>\"]\n        if not tokens:\n            return\n        for i in range(self.order - 1, len(tokens)):\n            target = tokens[i]\n            self.vocab[target] += 1\n            self.total_tokens += 1\n            for ctx_len in range(self.order):\n                context = tuple(tokens[i - ctx_len:i]) if ctx_len else ()\n                self.counts[ctx_len][context][target] += 1\n\n    def candidates(self, context_tokens: Sequence[str], limit: int = 80) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:\n        vocab_size = max(1, len(self.vocab))\n        context = list(context_tokens)\n        counter = Counter()\n        # Blend backoff levels; a longer context receives more weight.\n        for ctx_len in range(min(self.order - 1, len(context)), -1, -1):\n            key = tuple(context[-ctx_len:]) if ctx_len else ()\n            found = self.counts[ctx_len].get(key)\n            if not found:\n                continue\n            weight = 1.0 + 0.7 * ctx_len\n            for token, count in found.items():\n                counter[token] += weight * count\n            if ctx_len >= 1:\n                break\n        if not counter:\n            counter.update(self.vocab)\n        total = sum(counter.values())\n        ranked = []\n        for token, count in counter.items():\n            prob = (count + self.alpha) / (total + self.alpha * vocab_size)\n            ranked.append((token, math.log(max(prob, 1e-12))))\n        ranked.sort(key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\n        return ranked[:max(1, limit)]\n\n\nclass NonIsomorphicFragments:\n    \"\"\"\n    Fragment transforms candidate features into differently sized spaces.\n    The transforms are intentionally not inverses of one another.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, seed: int = 17):\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        self.w_context = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 3))\n        self.w_word = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 4))\n        self.w_transition = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 2))\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _unit(v: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        n = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\n        return v / n if n > 1e-12 else np.zeros_like(v)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _hash_features(token: str, width: int) -> np.ndarray:\n        \"\"\"Stable token features; does not depend on Python's randomized hash.\"\"\"\n        raw = token.lower().encode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\")\n        vals = np.zeros(width, dtype=float)\n        if not raw:\n            return vals\n        for i, byte in enumerate(raw):\n            vals[i % width] += ((byte % 31) - 15) / 15.0\n            vals[(i * 3 + 1) % width] += ((byte % 17) - 8) / 8.0\n        vals /= max(1, len(raw))\n        vals[0] += min(len(raw), 20) / 20.0\n        vals[1] += sum(chr(b).isalpha() for b in raw) / max(1, len(raw))\n        return np.tanh(vals)\n\n    def features(self, context: Sequence[str], token: str, logp: float, rank: int) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n        recent = list(context[-4:])\n        ctx_vec = np.zeros(5, dtype=float)\n        if recent:\n            for i, word in enumerate(recent):\n                f = self._hash_features(word, 5)\n                ctx_vec += f * (0.65 ** (len(recent) - i - 1))\n            ctx_vec /= max(1, len(recent))\n        word_vec = self._hash_features(token, 5)\n        transition_vec = np.array([\n            np.tanh(logp),\n            1.0 / (1.0 + rank),\n            1.0 if token[:1].isupper() else 0.0,\n            1.0 if token in \".,!?;:\" else 0.0,\n            min(len(token), 24) / 24.0\n        ], dtype=float)\n        # Distinct output dimensions: R^3, R^4, and R^2.\n        g1 = np.tanh(ctx_vec @ self.w_context)\n        g2 = np.tanh(word_vec @ self.w_word)\n        g3 = np.tanh(transition_vec @ self.w_transition)\n        return g1, g2, g3\n\n    def score(self, context: Sequence[str], token: str, logp: float, rank: int, lam: float) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n        g1, g2, g3 = self.features(context, token, logp, rank)\n        # Project each distinct fragment to a scalar summary, not an isomorphism.\n        summaries = np.array([\n            np.linalg.norm(g1),\n            np.linalg.norm(g2),\n            np.linalg.norm(g3)\n        ])\n        mean = float(np.mean(summaries))\n        spread = float(np.std(summaries) / (mean + 1e-9))\n        consistency = float(np.clip(0.55 * spread + 0.45 * (1.0 - np.mean(summaries)), 0.0, 1.0))\n\n        # Alignment is cosine similarity between padded/truncated local summaries\n        # and a context-conditioned reference vector.\n        ref = self._unit(np.array([\n            np.mean(g1),\n            np.mean(g2),\n            np.mean(g3),\n            np.tanh(logp),\n        ]))\n        candidate = self._unit(np.array([\n            g1[0],\n            g2[0],\n            g3[0],\n            np.tanh(logp + 0.1 * rank)\n        ]))\n        cosine = float(np.dot(ref, candidate))\n        alignment = (cosine + 1.0) / 2.0\n\n        # As lambda rises, the model moves from exploratory scoring to\n        # stronger language-model and fragment alignment influence.\n        fragment_score = 1.6 * alignment - 1.15 * consistency\n        total_score = (1.0 - lam) * (0.75 * logp + 0.25 * fragment_score) + lam * (1.25 * logp + 0.85 * fragment_score)\n        return total_score, consistency\n\n\ndef adiabatic_lambda(step: int, total_steps: int) -> float:\n    u = min(1.0, max(0.0, step / max(1, total_steps - 1)))\n    return 3.0 * u * u - 2.0 * u * u * u\n\n\ndef softmax(values: Sequence[float], temperature: float = 1.0) -> np.ndarray:\n    temp = max(1e-6, float(temperature))\n    arr = np.asarray(values, dtype=float) / temp\n    arr -= np.max(arr)\n    exp = np.exp(np.clip(arr, -60, 60))\n    return exp / max(float(exp.sum()), 1e-12)\n\n\ndef generate(\n    model: NGramModel,\n    prompt: str,\n    token_count: int = 800,\n    beam_size: int = 8,\n    tau: float = 0.65,\n    temperature: float = 0.85,\n    seed: int = 7,\n    show_trace: bool = False,\n) -> str:\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(seed)\n    output = tokenize(prompt)\n    if not output:\n        output = [\"The\"]\n    original_prompt_len = len(output)\n\n    for step in range(max(0, token_count)):\n        lam = adiabatic_lambda(step, max(1, token_count))\n        ranked = model.candidates(output, limit=max(40, beam_size * 8))\n        scored: List[Candidate] = []\n\n        for rank, (token, logp) in enumerate(ranked):\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(output, token, logp, rank, lam)\n            # Alignment proxy retained for traceability.\n            alignment = float(np.clip((score - logp) / 2.5 + 0.5, 0.0, 1.0))\n            if consistency <= tau:\n                scored.append(Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency, alignment))\n\n        # Avoid a dead end if all candidates fail the constraint.\n        if not scored:\n            token, logp = ranked[0]\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(output, token, logp, 0, lam)\n            scored = [Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency, 0.5)]\n\n        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c.score, reverse=True)\n        beam = scored[:max(1, beam_size)]\n        probs = softmax([c.score for c in beam], temperature)\n        for candidate, prob in zip(beam, probs):\n            candidate.probability = float(prob)\n\n        chosen = beam[0] if temperature <= 0.01 else rng.choices(beam, weights=probs, k=1)[0]\n        output.append(chosen.token)\n\n\n    # Remove internal end marker and preserve the prompt as part of the result.\n\n    text = ' '.join(output)\n\n    return text\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"N-gram text generator with non-isomorphic adiabatic fragment scoring.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"corpus\", nargs=\"?\", help=\"UTF-8 text corpus file; uses a small built-in corpus if omitted.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--prompt\", default=\"A process\", help=\"Initial text context.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--tokens\", type=int, default=800, help=\"Maximum number of new tokens.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--order\", type=int, default=3, help=\"N-gram order (default: 3).\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--alpha\", type=float, default=0.25, help=\"Additive smoothing value.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--beam\", type=int, default=8, help=\"Number of candidate next words retained before sampling.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--tau\", type=float, default=0.65, help=\"Maximum allowed fragment consistency score (0..1).\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--temperature\", type=float, default=0.85, help=\"Sampling temperature; near zero selects the top candidate.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=7, help=\"Random seed for repeatable generation.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--trace\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Print per-token scoring diagnostics.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--save\", help=\"Optional output text file.\")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    if args.corpus:\n        corpus_path = Path(args.corpus)\n        if not corpus_path.is_file():\n            parser.error(f\"Corpus file not found: {corpus_path}\")\n        try:\n            corpus_text = corpus_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\n        except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n            parser.error(f\"Could not decode corpus as UTF-8: {exc}\")\n    else:\n        corpus_text = BUILTIN_CORPUS\n\n    if not tokenize(corpus_text):\n        parser.error(\"Corpus contains no recognizable tokens.\")\n    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\n    model.train(corpus_text)\n    while True:\n        result = generate(\n            model=model,\n            prompt=input(\"USER: \"),\n            token_count=args.tokens,\n            beam_size=args.beam,\n            tau=float(np.clip(args.tau, 0.0, 1.0)),\n            temperature=max(0.0, args.temperature),\n            seed=args.seed,\n            show_trace=args.trace,\n        )\n\n        print(\"\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\")\n        print(result)\n       \nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()"}], "files": [{"file_uuid": "899cfa17-af76-5a7f-bbc9-e04c9e5754f2", "file_name": ""}], "parent_message_uuid": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000"}, {"uuid": "01a139bb-b832-7caa-b16d-c3c225d17fbd", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI've rewritten your script as a feedback loop and run it once on a small test corpus. It works, but the tiny corpus makes the output very repetitive. The code is in `cybernetic_textgen.py`.\n\n**How the loop works**\n1. The model generates a chunk of tokens (default 20).\n2. A sensor measures the chunk's repetition and mean log-probability.\n3. A controller picks a cognitive token from those numbers and nudges the temperature: `<diverge>` raises it when the chunk is repetitive, `<converge>` lowers it when the chunk is incoherent, and otherwise it cycles through `<observe>`, `<recall>`, `<reflect>` and `<predict>`.\n4. That cognitive token is inserted after the chunk, so it becomes part of the context for the next chunk.\n5. After a few chunks, the last `--window` tokens of output are piped back in as the next prompt. Each new prompt starts with `<integrate>`, and the very first one starts with `<observe>`.\n\n**How the model learns the tokens**\n- During training, cognitive tokens are woven into the corpus after each sentence, so the n-gram model learns what tends to precede and follow them.\n- With online learning on (the default), the model also trains on its own output after each chunk. It skips repetitive chunks so it doesn't reinforce loops. Use `--no-learn` to turn it off.\n- The fragment scorer sees cognitive tokens as a feature.\n\n**Changes to your original**\n- The module-level `input(\"Filename: \")` is gone. The corpus now comes from the command line, with a prompt for the filename only if you leave it out.\n- Output is no longer joined with spaces by hand, and `<eos>` ends a chunk instead of appearing in the text.\n- `--trace` now prints the controller's decisions.\n\n**Flags**\n- `--cycles`, `--chunk`, `--chunks-per-cycle` and `--window` control the loop.\n- `--hide-cog` prints the text without the cognitive tokens.\n- `--prompt` runs the first round without asking you.\n\nA real corpus will give the controller more to respond to. The `rep_limit` (0.5) and `logp_floor` (-4.5) thresholds in `Controller` are worth tuning to your data.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:26:08.660515Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:26:32.645037Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Building a self-feeding script with inserted cognitive tokens."}, {"summary": "Designing feedback-driven temperature control from measured repetition and coherence."}, {"summary": "Restructuring generation around chunked cognitive-token cycles."}, {"summary": "Assembling the online-learning and chunked generation loop."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:26:32.645100Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:27:03.437014Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_014XcJ4fiP5sM5WB2Nz6qnEA", "name": "create_file", "input": {"description": "Cybernetic feedback-loop version of the text generator", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py", "file_text": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nCybernetic non-isomorphic adiabatic text generator\n==================================================\n\nSame n-gram + non-isomorphic fragment scoring as before, now wrapped in a\nclosed feedback loop:\n\n  1. Generate a chunk of tokens.\n  2. MEASURE it (repetition, mean log-probability)         -> sensor\n  3. Pick a COGNITIVE TOKEN from that measurement           -> comparator\n  4. Insert the cognitive token after the chunk and adjust\n     temperature (negative feedback)                        -> actuator\n  5. At the end of a cycle, pipe the output back in as the next prompt, with a\n     cognitive token at the start, and repeat.\n\nThe model \"understands\" cognitive tokens because they are\n  - woven into the training corpus at sentence boundaries, and\n  - learned online from the model's own (non-degenerate) output.\n\nCognitive tokens:\n  <observe> <recall> <reflect> <predict>   normal cycle\n  <diverge>   output was repetitive   -> raise temperature\n  <converge>  output was incoherent   -> lower temperature\n  <integrate> start of every piped-back prompt\n\nExamples:\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --cycles 5 --chunk 20\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --prompt \"The machine\" --trace\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --hide-cog --no-learn\n\nOnly dependency: NumPy\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport math\nimport random\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import List, Sequence, Tuple\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Cognitive tokens\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCOG_CYCLE = [\"<observe>\", \"<recall>\", \"<reflect>\", \"<predict>\"]\nCOG_DIVERGE = \"<diverge>\"\nCOG_CONVERGE = \"<converge>\"\nCOG_INTEGRATE = \"<integrate>\"\nCOG_START = \"<observe>\"\nCOGNITIVE = set(COG_CYCLE + [COG_DIVERGE, COG_CONVERGE, COG_INTEGRATE])\nSENTENCE_END = (\".\", \"!\", \"?\")\n\n\ndef tokenize(text: str) -> List[str]:\n    return text.split()\n\n\ndef strip_cognitive(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> List[str]:\n    return [t for t in tokens if t not in COGNITIVE]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# N-gram model\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass NGramModel:\n    \"\"\"Smoothed n-gram model with backoff, trainable offline and online.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, order: int = 3, alpha: float = 0.25):\n        self.order = max(1, int(order))\n        self.alpha = max(1e-9, float(alpha))\n        self.counts = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(self.order)]\n        self.vocab = Counter()\n        self.total_tokens = 0\n\n    def _update(self, tokens: Sequence[str], start: int) -> None:\n        for i in range(start, len(tokens)):\n            target = tokens[i]\n            self.vocab[target] += 1\n            self.total_tokens += 1\n            for ctx_len in range(self.order):\n                if ctx_len > i:\n                    break\n                context = tuple(tokens[i - ctx_len:i]) if ctx_len else ()\n                self.counts[ctx_len][context][target] += 1\n\n    def train(self, text: str, cognitive: bool = True) -> None:\n        raw = tokenize(text)\n        if cognitive:\n            # Weave cognitive tokens in after each sentence so the model\n            # learns what comes before/after them.\n            woven, k = [], 0\n            for tok in raw:\n                woven.append(tok)\n                if tok.endswith(SENTENCE_END):\n                    woven.append(COG_CYCLE[k % len(COG_CYCLE)])\n                    k += 1\n            raw = woven\n        tokens = [\"<bos>\"] * (self.order - 1) + raw + [\"<eos>\"]\n        self._update(tokens, self.order - 1)\n\n    def learn(self, tokens: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Online update from the model's own output (feedback learning).\"\"\"\n        self._update(list(tokens), 1)\n\n    def candidates(self, context_tokens: Sequence[str], limit: int = 80) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:\n        vocab_size = max(1, len(self.vocab))\n        context = list(context_tokens)\n        counter = Counter()\n        for ctx_len in range(min(self.order - 1, len(context)), -1, -1):\n            key = tuple(context[-ctx_len:]) if ctx_len else ()\n            found = self.counts[ctx_len].get(key)\n            if not found:\n                continue\n            weight = 1.0 + 0.7 * ctx_len\n            for token, count in found.items():\n                counter[token] += weight * count\n            if ctx_len >= 1:\n                break\n        if not counter:\n            counter.update(self.vocab)\n        counter.pop(\"<bos>\", None)\n        total = sum(counter.values())\n        ranked = []\n        for token, count in counter.items():\n            prob = (count + self.alpha) / (total + self.alpha * vocab_size)\n            ranked.append((token, math.log(max(prob, 1e-12))))\n        ranked.sort(key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\n        return ranked[:max(1, limit)]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Non-isomorphic fragments (unchanged in spirit)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass NonIsomorphicFragments:\n    def __init__(self, seed: int = 17):\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        self.w_context = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 3))\n        self.w_word = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 4))\n        self.w_transition = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 2))\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _unit(v: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        n = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\n        return v / n if n > 1e-12 else np.zeros_like(v)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _hash_features(token: str, width: int) -> np.ndarray:\n        raw = token.lower().encode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\")\n        vals = np.zeros(width, dtype=float)\n        if not raw:\n            return vals\n        for i, byte in enumerate(raw):\n            vals[i % width] += ((byte % 31) - 15) / 15.0\n            vals[(i * 3 + 1) % width] += ((byte % 17) - 8) / 8.0\n        vals /= max(1, len(raw))\n        vals[0] += min(len(raw), 20) / 20.0\n        vals[1] += sum(chr(b).isalpha() for b in raw) / max(1, len(raw))\n        return np.tanh(vals)\n\n    def features(self, context, token, logp, rank):\n        recent = list(context[-4:])\n        ctx_vec = np.zeros(5, dtype=float)\n        if recent:\n            for i, word in enumerate(recent):\n                f = self._hash_features(word, 5)\n                ctx_vec += f * (0.65 ** (len(recent) - i - 1))\n            ctx_vec /= max(1, len(recent))\n        word_vec = self._hash_features(token, 5)\n        transition_vec = np.array([\n            np.tanh(logp),\n            1.0 / (1.0 + rank),\n            1.0 if token[:1].isupper() else 0.0,\n            1.0 if token in COGNITIVE else 0.0,  # cognitive tokens are visible to the fragments\n            min(len(token), 24) / 24.0,\n        ], dtype=float)\n        g1 = np.tanh(ctx_vec @ self.w_context)\n        g2 = np.tanh(word_vec @ self.w_word)\n        g3 = np.tanh(transition_vec @ self.w_transition)\n        return g1, g2, g3\n\n    def score(self, context, token, logp, rank, lam) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n        g1, g2, g3 = self.features(context, token, logp, rank)\n        summaries = np.array([np.linalg.norm(g1), np.linalg.norm(g2), np.linalg.norm(g3)])\n        mean = float(np.mean(summaries))\n        spread = float(np.std(summaries) / (mean + 1e-9))\n        consistency = float(np.clip(0.55 * spread + 0.45 * (1.0 - mean), 0.0, 1.0))\n\n        ref = self._unit(np.array([np.mean(g1), np.mean(g2), np.mean(g3), np.tanh(logp)]))\n        cand = self._unit(np.array([g1[0], g2[0], g3[0], np.tanh(logp + 0.1 * rank)]))\n        alignment = (float(np.dot(ref, cand)) + 1.0) / 2.0\n\n        fragment_score = 1.6 * alignment - 1.15 * consistency\n        total = (1.0 - lam) * (0.75 * logp + 0.25 * fragment_score) \\\n            + lam * (1.25 * logp + 0.85 * fragment_score)\n        return total, consistency\n\n\ndef adiabatic_lambda(step: int, total_steps: int) -> float:\n    u = min(1.0, max(0.0, step / max(1, total_steps - 1)))\n    return 3.0 * u * u - 2.0 * u * u * u\n\n\ndef softmax(values: Sequence[float], temperature: float = 1.0) -> np.ndarray:\n    temp = max(1e-6, float(temperature))\n    arr = np.asarray(values, dtype=float) / temp\n    arr -= np.max(arr)\n    exp = np.exp(np.clip(arr, -60, 60))\n    return exp / max(float(exp.sum()), 1e-12)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Cybernetic controller (sensor -> comparator -> actuator)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass Controller:\n    def __init__(self, temperature: float, rep_limit: float = 0.5, logp_floor: float = -4.5):\n        self.temperature = temperature\n        self.rep_limit = rep_limit\n        self.logp_floor = logp_floor\n        self.k = 0\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def repetition(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> float:\n        words = strip_cognitive(tokens)\n        if len(words) < 2:\n            return 0.0\n        return 1.0 - len(set(words)) / len(words)\n\n    def update(self, chunk: Sequence[str], mean_logp: float) -> Tuple[str, float]:\n        \"\"\"Return (cognitive token to emit, repetition measure).\"\"\"\n        rep = self.repetition(chunk)\n        if rep > self.rep_limit:\n            cog = COG_DIVERGE\n            self.temperature *= 1.15\n        elif mean_logp < self.logp_floor:\n            cog = COG_CONVERGE\n            self.temperature *= 0.9\n        else:\n            cog = COG_CYCLE[self.k % len(COG_CYCLE)]\n            self.k += 1\n        self.temperature = float(np.clip(self.temperature, 0.3, 1.6))\n        return cog, rep\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Candidate:\n    token: str\n    base_logp: float\n    score: float\n    consistency: float\n    probability: float = 0.0\n\n\ndef generate_chunk(model, fragments, context, n, step0, total, beam_size, tau, temperature, rng):\n    \"\"\"Generate up to n tokens after `context`. Returns (new_tokens, mean_logp, hit_eos).\"\"\"\n    ctx = list(context)\n    new, logps, hit_eos = [], [], False\n    for i in range(n):\n        lam = adiabatic_lambda(step0 + i, total)\n        ranked = model.candidates(ctx, limit=max(40, beam_size * 8))\n        scored: List[Candidate] = []\n        for rank, (token, logp) in enumerate(ranked):\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, rank, lam)\n            if consistency <= tau:\n                scored.append(Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency))\n        if not scored:\n            token, logp = ranked[0]\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, 0, lam)\n            scored = [Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency)]\n\n        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c.score, reverse=True)\n        beam = scored[:max(1, beam_size)]\n        probs = softmax([c.score for c in beam], temperature)\n        chosen = beam[0] if temperature <= 0.01 else rng.choices(beam, weights=probs, k=1)[0]\n\n        if chosen.token == \"<eos>\":\n            hit_eos = True\n            break\n        new.append(chosen.token)\n        ctx.append(chosen.token)\n        logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\n    mean_logp = float(np.mean(logps)) if logps else 0.0\n    return new, mean_logp, hit_eos\n\n\ndef cybernetic_run(model, prompt, cycles, chunk, chunks_per_cycle, window, beam_size, tau,\n                   temperature, seed, learn, trace):\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(seed)\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\n\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\"The\"]\n    full = [COG_START] + seed_tokens          # everything produced so far\n    context = list(full)                      # what the model sees this cycle\n    total = max(1, cycles * chunks_per_cycle * chunk)\n    step = 0\n\n    for c in range(cycles):\n        for k in range(chunks_per_cycle):\n            new, mean_logp, hit_eos = generate_chunk(\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, step, total,\n                beam_size, tau, controller.temperature, rng)\n            step += chunk\n            cog, rep = controller.update(new, mean_logp)\n\n            if trace:\n                print(f\"[cycle {c+1}/{cycles} chunk {k+1}] tokens={len(new)} \"\n                      f\"mean_logp={mean_logp:.2f} rep={rep:.2f} \"\n                      f\"-> {cog} (T={controller.temperature:.2f})\")\n\n            # Feedback learning: only from healthy output, to avoid reinforcing loops.\n            if learn and new and rep <= controller.rep_limit:\n                model.learn(context[-(model.order - 1):] + new + [cog])\n\n            context += new + [cog]\n            full += new + [cog]\n            if hit_eos:\n                break\n\n        # Pipe output back to input: new prompt begins with a cognitive token.\n        tail = full[-window:]\n        context = [COG_INTEGRATE] + tail\n        full.append(COG_INTEGRATE)\n\n    return full\n\n\ndef detokenize(tokens: Sequence[str], hide_cog: bool) -> str:\n    return \" \".join(strip_cognitive(tokens) if hide_cog else tokens)\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Cybernetic feedback-loop n-gram generator.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"corpus\", nargs=\"?\", help=\"UTF-8 text corpus file (asked for if omitted).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--prompt\", help=\"Initial prompt. If omitted you are asked each round.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--cycles\", type=int, default=4, help=\"Output->input feedback cycles per prompt.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--chunk\", type=int, default=20, help=\"Tokens per chunk between cognitive tokens.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--chunks-per-cycle\", type=int, default=3)\n    p.add_argument(\"--window\", type=int, default=40, help=\"Tokens of output piped back as the next prompt.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--order\", type=int, default=3)\n    p.add_argument(\"--alpha\", type=float, default=0.25)\n    p.add_argument(\"--beam\", type=int, default=8)\n    p.add_argument(\"--tau\", type=float, default=0.65)\n    p.add_argument(\"--temperature\", type=float, default=0.85)\n    p.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=7)\n    p.add_argument(\"--no-learn\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Disable online learning from own output.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--hide-cog\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Hide cognitive tokens in printed text.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--trace\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Print controller diagnostics.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--save\", help=\"Append output to this text file.\")\n    args = p.parse_args()\n\n    corpus_name = args.corpus or input(\"Filename: \")\n    path = Path(corpus_name)\n    if not path.is_file():\n        p.error(f\"Corpus file not found: {path}\")\n    try:\n        corpus_text = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\n    except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n        p.error(f\"Could not decode corpus as UTF-8: {exc}\")\n    if not tokenize(corpus_text):\n        p.error(\"Corpus contains no tokens.\")\n\n    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\n    model.train(corpus_text, cognitive=True)\n\n    first = True\n    while True:\n        try:\n            prompt = args.prompt if (args.prompt and first) else input(\"USER: \")\n        except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):\n            print()\n            break\n        first = False\n\n        full = cybernetic_run(\n            model, prompt, cycles=args.cycles, chunk=args.chunk,\n            chunks_per_cycle=args.chunks_per_cycle, window=args.window,\n            beam_size=args.beam, tau=float(np.clip(args.tau, 0.0, 1.0)),\n            temperature=max(0.0, args.temperature), seed=args.seed,\n            learn=not args.no_learn, trace=args.trace)\n\n        text = detokenize(full, args.hide_cog)\n        print(\"\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\")\n        print(text)\n        print()\n        if args.save:\n            with open(args.save, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n                fh.write(text + \"\\n\\n\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}, "message": "Cybernetic feedback-loop version of the text generator", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nCybernetic non-isomorphic adiabatic text generator\\n==================================================\\n\\nSame n-gram + non-isomorphic fragment scoring as before, now wrapped in a\\nclosed feedback loop:\\n\\n  1. Generate a chunk of tokens.\\n  2. MEASURE it (repetition, mean log-probability)         -> sensor\\n  3. Pick a COGNITIVE TOKEN from that measurement           -> comparator\\n  4. Insert the cognitive token after the chunk and adjust\\n     temperature (negative feedback)                        -> actuator\\n  5. At the end of a cycle, pipe the output back in as the next prompt, with a\\n     cognitive token at the start, and repeat.\\n\\nThe model \\\"understands\\\" cognitive tokens because they are\\n  - woven into the training corpus at sentence boundaries, and\\n  - learned online from the model's own (non-degenerate) output.\\n\\nCognitive tokens:\\n  <observe> <recall> <reflect> <predict>   normal cycle\\n  <diverge>   output was repetitive   -> raise temperature\\n  <converge>  output was incoherent   -> lower temperature\\n  <integrate> start of every piped-back prompt\\n\\nExamples:\\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --cycles 5 --chunk 20\\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" --trace\\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --hide-cog --no-learn\\n\\nOnly dependency: NumPy\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport argparse\\nimport math\\nimport random\\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import List, Sequence, Tuple\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Cognitive tokens\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nCOG_CYCLE = [\\\"<observe>\\\", \\\"<recall>\\\", \\\"<reflect>\\\", \\\"<predict>\\\"]\\nCOG_DIVERGE = \\\"<diverge>\\\"\\nCOG_CONVERGE = \\\"<converge>\\\"\\nCOG_INTEGRATE = \\\"<integrate>\\\"\\nCOG_START = \\\"<observe>\\\"\\nCOGNITIVE = set(COG_CYCLE + [COG_DIVERGE, COG_CONVERGE, COG_INTEGRATE])\\nSENTENCE_END = (\\\".\\\", \\\"!\\\", \\\"?\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef tokenize(text: str) -> List[str]:\\n    return text.split()\\n\\n\\ndef strip_cognitive(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> List[str]:\\n    return [t for t in tokens if t not in COGNITIVE]\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# N-gram model\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass NGramModel:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Smoothed n-gram model with backoff, trainable offline and online.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, order: int = 3, alpha: float = 0.25):\\n        self.order = max(1, int(order))\\n        self.alpha = max(1e-9, float(alpha))\\n        self.counts = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(self.order)]\\n        self.vocab = Counter()\\n        self.total_tokens = 0\\n\\n    def _update(self, tokens: Sequence[str], start: int) -> None:\\n        for i in range(start, len(tokens)):\\n            target = tokens[i]\\n            self.vocab[target] += 1\\n            self.total_tokens += 1\\n            for ctx_len in range(self.order):\\n                if ctx_len > i:\\n                    break\\n                context = tuple(tokens[i - ctx_len:i]) if ctx_len else ()\\n                self.counts[ctx_len][context][target] += 1\\n\\n    def train(self, text: str, cognitive: bool = True) -> None:\\n        raw = tokenize(text)\\n        if cognitive:\\n            # Weave cognitive tokens in after each sentence so the model\\n            # learns what comes before/after them.\\n            woven, k = [], 0\\n            for tok in raw:\\n                woven.append(tok)\\n                if tok.endswith(SENTENCE_END):\\n                    woven.append(COG_CYCLE[k % len(COG_CYCLE)])\\n                    k += 1\\n            raw = woven\\n        tokens = [\\\"<bos>\\\"] * (self.order - 1) + raw + [\\\"<eos>\\\"]\\n        self._update(tokens, self.order - 1)\\n\\n    def learn(self, tokens: Sequence[str]) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Online update from the model's own output (feedback learning).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self._update(list(tokens), 1)\\n\\n    def candidates(self, context_tokens: Sequence[str], limit: int = 80) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:\\n        vocab_size = max(1, len(self.vocab))\\n        context = list(context_tokens)\\n        counter = Counter()\\n        for ctx_len in range(min(self.order - 1, len(context)), -1, -1):\\n            key = tuple(context[-ctx_len:]) if ctx_len else ()\\n            found = self.counts[ctx_len].get(key)\\n            if not found:\\n                continue\\n            weight = 1.0 + 0.7 * ctx_len\\n            for token, count in found.items():\\n                counter[token] += weight * count\\n            if ctx_len >= 1:\\n                break\\n        if not counter:\\n            counter.update(self.vocab)\\n        counter.pop(\\\"<bos>\\\", None)\\n        total = sum(counter.values())\\n        ranked = []\\n        for token, count in counter.items():\\n            prob = (count + self.alpha) / (total + self.alpha * vocab_size)\\n            ranked.append((token, math.log(max(prob, 1e-12))))\\n        ranked.sort(key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\\n        return ranked[:max(1, limit)]\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Non-isomorphic fragments (unchanged in spirit)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass NonIsomorphicFragments:\\n    def __init__(self, seed: int = 17):\\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n        self.w_context = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 3))\\n        self.w_word = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 4))\\n        self.w_transition = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 2))\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _unit(v: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n        n = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\\n        return v / n if n > 1e-12 else np.zeros_like(v)\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _hash_features(token: str, width: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n        raw = token.lower().encode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"ignore\\\")\\n        vals = np.zeros(width, dtype=float)\\n        if not raw:\\n            return vals\\n        for i, byte in enumerate(raw):\\n            vals[i % width] += ((byte % 31) - 15) / 15.0\\n            vals[(i * 3 + 1) % width] += ((byte % 17) - 8) / 8.0\\n        vals /= max(1, len(raw))\\n        vals[0] += min(len(raw), 20) / 20.0\\n        vals[1] += sum(chr(b).isalpha() for b in raw) / max(1, len(raw))\\n        return np.tanh(vals)\\n\\n    def features(self, context, token, logp, rank):\\n        recent = list(context[-4:])\\n        ctx_vec = np.zeros(5, dtype=float)\\n        if recent:\\n            for i, word in enumerate(recent):\\n                f = self._hash_features(word, 5)\\n                ctx_vec += f * (0.65 ** (len(recent) - i - 1))\\n            ctx_vec /= max(1, len(recent))\\n        word_vec = self._hash_features(token, 5)\\n        transition_vec = np.array([\\n            np.tanh(logp),\\n            1.0 / (1.0 + rank),\\n            1.0 if token[:1].isupper() else 0.0,\\n            1.0 if token in COGNITIVE else 0.0,  # cognitive tokens are visible to the fragments\\n            min(len(token), 24) / 24.0,\\n        ], dtype=float)\\n        g1 = np.tanh(ctx_vec @ self.w_context)\\n        g2 = np.tanh(word_vec @ self.w_word)\\n        g3 = np.tanh(transition_vec @ self.w_transition)\\n        return g1, g2, g3\\n\\n    def score(self, context, token, logp, rank, lam) -> Tuple[float, float]:\\n        g1, g2, g3 = self.features(context, token, logp, rank)\\n        summaries = np.array([np.linalg.norm(g1), np.linalg.norm(g2), np.linalg.norm(g3)])\\n        mean = float(np.mean(summaries))\\n        spread = float(np.std(summaries) / (mean + 1e-9))\\n        consistency = float(np.clip(0.55 * spread + 0.45 * (1.0 - mean), 0.0, 1.0))\\n\\n        ref = self._unit(np.array([np.mean(g1), np.mean(g2), np.mean(g3), np.tanh(logp)]))\\n        cand = self._unit(np.array([g1[0], g2[0], g3[0], np.tanh(logp + 0.1 * rank)]))\\n        alignment = (float(np.dot(ref, cand)) + 1.0) / 2.0\\n\\n        fragment_score = 1.6 * alignment - 1.15 * consistency\\n        total = (1.0 - lam) * (0.75 * logp + 0.25 * fragment_score) \\\\\\n            + lam * (1.25 * logp + 0.85 * fragment_score)\\n        return total, consistency\\n\\n\\ndef adiabatic_lambda(step: int, total_steps: int) -> float:\\n    u = min(1.0, max(0.0, step / max(1, total_steps - 1)))\\n    return 3.0 * u * u - 2.0 * u * u * u\\n\\n\\ndef softmax(values: Sequence[float], temperature: float = 1.0) -> np.ndarray:\\n    temp = max(1e-6, float(temperature))\\n    arr = np.asarray(values, dtype=float) / temp\\n    arr -= np.max(arr)\\n    exp = np.exp(np.clip(arr, -60, 60))\\n    return exp / max(float(exp.sum()), 1e-12)\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Cybernetic controller (sensor -> comparator -> actuator)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass Controller:\\n    def __init__(self, temperature: float, rep_limit: float = 0.5, logp_floor: float = -4.5):\\n        self.temperature = temperature\\n        self.rep_limit = rep_limit\\n        self.logp_floor = logp_floor\\n        self.k = 0\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def repetition(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> float:\\n        words = strip_cognitive(tokens)\\n        if len(words) < 2:\\n            return 0.0\\n        return 1.0 - len(set(words)) / len(words)\\n\\n    def update(self, chunk: Sequence[str], mean_logp: float) -> Tuple[str, float]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Return (cognitive token to emit, repetition measure).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        rep = self.repetition(chunk)\\n        if rep > self.rep_limit:\\n            cog = COG_DIVERGE\\n            self.temperature *= 1.15\\n        elif mean_logp < self.logp_floor:\\n            cog = COG_CONVERGE\\n            self.temperature *= 0.9\\n        else:\\n            cog = COG_CYCLE[self.k % len(COG_CYCLE)]\\n            self.k += 1\\n        self.temperature = float(np.clip(self.temperature, 0.3, 1.6))\\n        return cog, rep\\n\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass Candidate:\\n    token: str\\n    base_logp: float\\n    score: float\\n    consistency: float\\n    probability: float = 0.0\\n\\n\\ndef generate_chunk(model, fragments, context, n, step0, total, beam_size, tau, temperature, rng):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generate up to n tokens after `context`. Returns (new_tokens, mean_logp, hit_eos).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    ctx = list(context)\\n    new, logps, hit_eos = [], [], False\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        lam = adiabatic_lambda(step0 + i, total)\\n        ranked = model.candidates(ctx, limit=max(40, beam_size * 8))\\n        scored: List[Candidate] = []\\n        for rank, (token, logp) in enumerate(ranked):\\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, rank, lam)\\n            if consistency <= tau:\\n                scored.append(Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency))\\n        if not scored:\\n            token, logp = ranked[0]\\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, 0, lam)\\n            scored = [Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency)]\\n\\n        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c.score, reverse=True)\\n        beam = scored[:max(1, beam_size)]\\n        probs = softmax([c.score for c in beam], temperature)\\n        chosen = beam[0] if temperature <= 0.01 else rng.choices(beam, weights=probs, k=1)[0]\\n\\n        if chosen.token == \\\"<eos>\\\":\\n            hit_eos = True\\n            break\\n        new.append(chosen.token)\\n        ctx.append(chosen.token)\\n        logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\\n    mean_logp = float(np.mean(logps)) if logps else 0.0\\n    return new, mean_logp, hit_eos\\n\\n\\ndef cybernetic_run(model, prompt, cycles, chunk, chunks_per_cycle, window, beam_size, tau,\\n                   temperature, seed, learn, trace):\\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(seed)\\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\\n\\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\\\"The\\\"]\\n    full = [COG_START] + seed_tokens          # everything produced so far\\n    context = list(full)                      # what the model sees this cycle\\n    total = max(1, cycles * chunks_per_cycle * chunk)\\n    step = 0\\n\\n    for c in range(cycles):\\n        for k in range(chunks_per_cycle):\\n            new, mean_logp, hit_eos = generate_chunk(\\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, step, total,\\n                beam_size, tau, controller.temperature, rng)\\n            step += chunk\\n            cog, rep = controller.update(new, mean_logp)\\n\\n            if trace:\\n                print(f\\\"[cycle {c+1}/{cycles} chunk {k+1}] tokens={len(new)} \\\"\\n                      f\\\"mean_logp={mean_logp:.2f} rep={rep:.2f} \\\"\\n                      f\\\"-> {cog} (T={controller.temperature:.2f})\\\")\\n\\n            # Feedback learning: only from healthy output, to avoid reinforcing loops.\\n            if learn and new and rep <= controller.rep_limit:\\n                model.learn(context[-(model.order - 1):] + new + [cog])\\n\\n            context += new + [cog]\\n            full += new + [cog]\\n            if hit_eos:\\n                break\\n\\n        # Pipe output back to input: new prompt begins with a cognitive token.\\n        tail = full[-window:]\\n        context = [COG_INTEGRATE] + tail\\n        full.append(COG_INTEGRATE)\\n\\n    return full\\n\\n\\ndef detokenize(tokens: Sequence[str], hide_cog: bool) -> str:\\n    return \\\" \\\".join(strip_cognitive(tokens) if hide_cog else tokens)\\n\\n\\ndef main() -> None:\\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\\\"Cybernetic feedback-loop n-gram generator.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"corpus\\\", nargs=\\\"?\\\", help=\\\"UTF-8 text corpus file (asked for if omitted).\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--prompt\\\", help=\\\"Initial prompt. If omitted you are asked each round.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--cycles\\\", type=int, default=4, help=\\\"Output->input feedback cycles per prompt.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--chunk\\\", type=int, default=20, help=\\\"Tokens per chunk between cognitive tokens.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--chunks-per-cycle\\\", type=int, default=3)\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--window\\\", type=int, default=40, help=\\\"Tokens of output piped back as the next prompt.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--order\\\", type=int, default=3)\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--alpha\\\", type=float, default=0.25)\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--beam\\\", type=int, default=8)\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--tau\\\", type=float, default=0.65)\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--temperature\\\", type=float, default=0.85)\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--seed\\\", type=int, default=7)\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--no-learn\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Disable online learning from own output.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--hide-cog\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Hide cognitive tokens in printed text.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--trace\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Print controller diagnostics.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--save\\\", help=\\\"Append output to this text file.\\\")\\n    args = p.parse_args()\\n\\n    corpus_name = args.corpus or input(\\\"Filename: \\\")\\n    path = Path(corpus_name)\\n    if not path.is_file():\\n        p.error(f\\\"Corpus file not found: {path}\\\")\\n    try:\\n        corpus_text = path.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8-sig\\\")\\n    except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\\n        p.error(f\\\"Could not decode corpus as UTF-8: {exc}\\\")\\n    if not tokenize(corpus_text):\\n        p.error(\\\"Corpus contains no tokens.\\\")\\n\\n    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\\n    model.train(corpus_text, cognitive=True)\\n\\n    first = True\\n    while True:\\n        try:\\n            prompt = args.prompt if (args.prompt and first) else input(\\\"USER: \\\")\\n        except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):\\n            print()\\n            break\\n        first = False\\n\\n        full = cybernetic_run(\\n            model, prompt, cycles=args.cycles, chunk=args.chunk,\\n            chunks_per_cycle=args.chunks_per_cycle, window=args.window,\\n            beam_size=args.beam, tau=float(np.clip(args.tau, 0.0, 1.0)),\\n            temperature=max(0.0, args.temperature), seed=args.seed,\\n            learn=not args.no_learn, trace=args.trace)\\n\\n        text = detokenize(full, args.hide_cog)\\n        print(\\\"\\\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\\\n\\\")\\n        print(text)\\n        print()\\n        if args.save:\\n            with open(args.save, \\\"a\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\\n                fh.write(text + \\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\n\", \"filename\": \"/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:27:04.720034Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:27:04.720080Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_014XcJ4fiP5sM5WB2Nz6qnEA", "name": "create_file", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:27:06.429433Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-