ens=20 mean_logp=-0.41 rep=0.06 -> <observe> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 1/4 chunk 2] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.32 rep=0.11 -> <recall> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 1/4 chunk 3] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.32 rep=0.11 -> <reflect> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 2/4 chunk 1] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.37 rep=0.00 -> <predict> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 2/4 chunk 2] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.49 rep=0.29 -> <observe> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 2/4 chunk 3] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.52 rep=0.29 -> <recall> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 3/4 chunk 1] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.71 rep=0.80 -> <diverge> (T=0.98)\\n[cycle 3/4 chunk 2] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.58 rep=0.41 -> <reflect> (T=0.98)\\n[cycle 3/4 chunk 3] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.60 rep=0.31 -> <predict> (T=0.98)\\n[cycle 4/4 chunk 1] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.37 rep=0.11 -> <observe> (T=0.98)\\n[cycle 4/4 chunk 2] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.37 rep=0.06 -> <recall> (T=0.98)\\n[cycle 4/4 chunk 3] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.37 rep=0.06 -> <reflect> (T=0.98)\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"[cycle 1/4 chunk 1] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.32 rep=0.06 -> <observe> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 1/4 chunk 2] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.37 rep=0.00 -> <recall> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 1/4 chunk 3] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.64 rep=0.44 -> <reflect> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 2/4 chunk 1] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.37 rep=0.00 -> <predict> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 2/4 chunk 2] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.48 rep=0.29 -> <observe> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 2/4 chunk 3] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.49 rep=0.29 -> <recall> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 3/4 chunk 1] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.72 rep=0.80 -> <diverge> (T=0.98)\\n[cycle 3/4 chunk 2] tokens=3 mean_logp=-1.66 rep=0.00 -> <reflect> (T=0.98)\\n[cycle 4/4 chunk 1] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.37 rep=0.11 -> <predict> (T=0.98)\\n[cycle 4/4 chunk 2] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.61 rep=0.31 -> <observe> (T=0.98)\\n[cycle 4/4 chunk 3] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.51 rep=0.06 -> <recall> (T=0.98)\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\n<observe> The machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <reflect> every story has an end. <reflect> the end is a <observe> what comes next? <reflect> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <reflect> every story has an <recall> the machine decides. <recall> the machine decides. <predict> the machine decides. <observe> the end is a new start! <predict> what <reflect> <integrate> what comes next? <recall> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <reflect> every story has an <predict> the machine decides. <reflect> the machine decides. <reflect> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <reflect> <observe> the machine decides. <observe> the machine decides. <observe> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <predict> <recall> <integrate> the machine decides. <recall> the machine decides. <observe> the machine decides. <observe> the machine decides. <predict> the machine decides. <reflect> <diverge> machine decides. <predict> <reflect> <integrate> the machine decides. <observe> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <recall> every story has an <predict> the end is a new start! <recall> what comes next? <predict> the machine decides. <reflect> the machine decides. <observe> the <observe> every story has an end. <recall> the machine decides. <observe> the end is a new start! <recall> what comes next? <recall> <integrate>\\n\\nUSER: [cycle 1/4 chunk 1] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.41 rep=0.06 -> <observe> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 1/4 chunk 2] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.32 rep=0.11 -> <recall> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 1/4 chunk 3] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.32 rep=0.11 -> <reflect> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 2/4 chunk 1] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.37 rep=0.00 -> <predict> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 2/4 chunk 2] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.49 rep=0.29 -> <observe> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 2/4 chunk 3] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.52 rep=0.29 -> <recall> (T=0.85)\\n[cycle 3/4 chunk 1] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.71 rep=0.80 -> <diverge> (T=0.98)\\n[cycle 3/4 chunk 2] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.58 rep=0.41 -> <reflect> (T=0.98)\\n[cycle 3/4 chunk 3] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.60 rep=0.31 -> <predict> (T=0.98)\\n[cycle 4/4 chunk 1] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.37 rep=0.11 -> <observe> (T=0.98)\\n[cycle 4/4 chunk 2] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.37 rep=0.06 -> <recall> (T=0.98)\\n[cycle 4/4 chunk 3] tokens=20 mean_logp=-0.37 rep=0.06 -> <reflect> (T=0.98)\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:27:10.573748Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:27:10.825037Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01JvGaDHj3M82oT9eA66o5pZ", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:27:10.855273Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:27:10.855325Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01JvGaDHj3M82oT9eA66o5pZ", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py", "name": "cybernetic textgen", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "\n\nThe file cards appear with your reply, and where they sit relative to its text depends on the app the user is reading in; finish the reply with text, and refer to a file by its name, never as above or below."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:27:16.537859Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:27:16.696708Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I've rewritten your script as a feedback loop and run it once on a small test corpus. It works, but the tiny corpus makes the output very repetitive. The code is in `cybernetic_textgen.py`.\n\n**How the loop works**\n1. The model generates a chunk of tokens (default 20).\n2. A sensor measures the chunk's repetition and mean log-probability.\n3. A controller picks a cognitive token from those numbers and nudges the temperature: `<diverge>` raises it when the chunk is repetitive, `<converge>` lowers it when the chunk is incoherent, and otherwise it cycles through `<observe>`, `<recall>`, `<reflect>` and `<predict>`.\n4. That cognitive token is inserted after the chunk, so it becomes part of the context for the next chunk.\n5. After a few chunks, the last `--window` tokens of output are piped back in as the next prompt. Each new prompt starts with `<integrate>`, and the very first one starts with `<observe>`.\n\n**How the model learns the tokens**\n- During training, cognitive tokens are woven into the corpus after each sentence, so the n-gram model learns what tends to precede and follow them.\n- With online learning on (the default), the model also trains on its own output after each chunk. It skips repetitive chunks so it doesn't reinforce loops. Use `--no-learn` to turn it off.\n- The fragment scorer sees cognitive tokens as a feature.\n\n**Changes to your original**\n- The module-level `input(\"Filename: \")` is gone. The corpus now comes from the command line, with a prompt for the filename only if you leave it out.\n- Output is no longer joined with spaces by hand, and `<eos>` ends a chunk instead of appearing in the text.\n- `--trace` now prints the controller's decisions.\n\n**Flags**\n- `--cycles`, `--chunk`, `--chunks-per-cycle` and `--window` control the loop.\n- `--hide-cog` prints the text without the cognitive tokens.\n- `--prompt` runs the first round without asking you.\n\nA real corpus will give the controller more to respond to. The `rep_limit` (0.5) and `logp_floor` (-4.5) thresholds in `Controller` are worth tuning to your data.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:27:16.776794Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:27:16.776794Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a139bb-b832-7b6c-aac6-d08322fa4981"}, {"uuid": "01a139be-be3d-7e26-b83e-d803887e5c79", "text": "try to keep loading responses until the cognitive responses monotonically stack up correctly", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:29:27.822746Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:29:27.822746Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "try to keep loading responses until the cognitive responses monotonically stack up correctly", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:29:27.822966Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:29:27.822966Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a139bb-b832-7caa-b16d-c3c225d17fbd"}, {"uuid": "01a139be-be3d-7183-b353-07df4a284a5f", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI've updated `cybernetic_textgen.py` so it keeps regenerating until the cognitive tokens stack up in the correct order. On my test run it reached depth 12/12 in 49 attempts, with no forced tokens and the order verified. That was on a tiny repetitive corpus, so your data will behave differently.\n\n**How it works**\n- \"Correct\" means the cycle `<observe>` \u2192 `<recall>` \u2192 `<reflect>` \u2192 `<predict>` \u2192 `<observe>` and so on.\n- Each chunk now ends when the model emits a cognitive token itself. If it's the expected next one and the chunk had real content before it, the chunk is accepted and pushed onto the stack.\n- If it's the wrong token or none, the chunk is thrown away and regenerated. Temperature creeps up 10% per retry, which in the test run kept it from getting stuck on a slot.\n- The stack only grows, so it is monotonic by construction, and the run ends with a check that the whole stack matches the pattern.\n- Only accepted chunks are learned online, so the model gets better at the pattern as it goes.\n- After each full cycle of four, the last `--window` tokens are piped back in as the next prompt, starting with `<integrate>`.\n\n**New flags**\n- `--stack-target N` is the depth to reach (default 12). `0` gives back the old fixed-cycle mode.\n- `--max-retries` is how many rejected chunks are allowed per slot (default 25). After that the expected token is forced in and counted as `forced`.\n- `--strict` never forces a token and retries until the attempt cap.\n- `--trace` prints every attempt. Without it you get a single live progress line on stderr.\n\n**What it prints**\n- A summary line with depth, attempts, forced count and whether the order was verified.\n\nForced tokens are the weak spot: they make the order correct without the model actually producing it. Run with `--strict` if you only want stacks the model produced itself.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:29:27.822563Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:29:55.528365Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Looping until the token sequence stacks up correctly."}, {"summary": "Designing retry and forcing rules for token validation."}, {"summary": "Structuring attempt caps and repetition checks for chunk rejection."}, {"summary": "Rewriting the generation and run functions for the new flow."}, {"summary": "Adding retry tracking and progress logging to the stacking loop."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:29:55.528419Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:30:10.802796Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_014y11kfaCwVdmJZoDayJT6n", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\nsrc = open(\"cybernetic_textgen.py\").read()\n\n# 1) generate_chunk: optionally stop when the model itself emits a cognitive token\na = src.index(\"def generate_chunk\")\nb = src.index(\"def cybernetic_run\")\nnew_gc = '''def generate_chunk(model, fragments, context, n, step0, total, beam_size, tau, temperature, rng,\n                   stop_on_cog=False):\n    \"\"\"Generate up to n tokens after `context`.\n\n    Returns (new_tokens, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted_cog). With stop_on_cog the\n    chunk ends the moment the MODEL emits a cognitive token (returned in\n    emitted_cog, not appended to new_tokens).\n    \"\"\"\n    ctx = list(context)\n    new, logps, hit_eos, emitted = [], [], False, None\n    for i in range(n):\n        lam = adiabatic_lambda(step0 + i, total)\n        ranked = model.candidates(ctx, limit=max(40, beam_size * 8))\n        scored: List[Candidate] = []\n        for rank, (token, logp) in enumerate(ranked):\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, rank, lam)\n            if consistency <= tau:\n                scored.append(Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency))\n        if not scored:\n            token, logp = ranked[0]\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, 0, lam)\n            scored = [Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency)]\n\n        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c.score, reverse=True)\n        beam = scored[:max(1, beam_size)]\n        probs = softmax([c.score for c in beam], temperature)\n        chosen = beam[0] if temperature <= 0.01 else rng.choices(beam, weights=probs, k=1)[0]\n\n        if chosen.token == \"<eos>\":\n            hit_eos = True\n            break\n        if stop_on_cog and chosen.token in COGNITIVE:\n            emitted = chosen.token\n            logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\n            break\n        new.append(chosen.token)\n        ctx.append(chosen.token)\n        logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\n    mean_logp = float(np.mean(logps)) if logps else 0.0\n    return new, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted\n\n\n'''\nsrc = src[:a] + new_gc + src[b:]\n\n# legacy loop: unpack the 4-tuple\nsrc = src.replace(\"new, mean_logp, hit_eos = generate_chunk(\", \"new, mean_logp, hit_eos, _ = generate_chunk(\")\n\n# 2) stacked run, inserted before detokenize\nstacked = '''def stacked_run(model, prompt, target_depth, chunk, window, beam_size, tau, temperature, seed,\n                learn, max_retries, strict, trace):\n    \"\"\"\n    Keep generating until cognitive tokens stack up in the correct order.\n\n    The model must itself emit the next expected cognitive token\n    (observe -> recall -> reflect -> predict -> observe ...) after a chunk of\n    real content. A wrong or missing token rejects the chunk and it is\n    regenerated (temperature creeps up on each retry). Accepted chunks are\n    pushed onto the stack, which only ever grows (monotonic), and are learned\n    online so the model gets better at the pattern as it goes.\n\n    After `max_retries` misses the expected token is forced in (flagged), unless\n    `strict` is set, in which case it keeps trying until the attempt cap.\n    \"\"\"\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(seed)\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\n\n    full = [COG_START] + (tokenize(prompt) or [\"The\"])\n    context = list(full)\n    stack: List[str] = []\n    forced = 0\n    attempts = 0\n    max_attempts = target_depth * (200 if strict else max_retries + 1)\n\n    while len(stack) < target_depth and attempts < max_attempts:\n        expected = COG_CYCLE[len(stack) % len(COG_CYCLE)]\n        retries = 0\n        accepted, was_forced = False, False\n        while attempts < max_attempts:\n            temp = float(np.clip(controller.temperature * (1.0 + 0.1 * retries), 0.3, 1.8))\n            new, mlp, eos, emitted = generate_chunk(\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, len(stack) * chunk,\n                target_depth * chunk, beam_size, tau, temp, rng, stop_on_cog=True)\n            attempts += 1\n            ok = emitted == expected and len(new) > 0\n            msg = (f\"depth {len(stack)}/{target_depth} attempt {attempts} \"\n                   f\"expected {expected} got {emitted or 'none'} \"\n                   f\"{'OK' if ok else 'retry'} (T={temp:.2f}, forced={forced})\")\n            if trace:\n                print(msg, file=sys.stderr)\n            else:\n                print(\"\\\\r\" + msg.ljust(78), end=\"\", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\n            if ok:\n                accepted = True\n                break\n            retries += 1\n            if retries > max_retries and not strict:\n                was_forced = True\n                break\n        if not (accepted or was_forced):\n            break  # attempt cap hit in strict mode\n\n        if was_forced:\n            forced += 1\n        stack.append(expected)\n        context += new + [expected]\n        full += new + [expected]\n        if new:\n            controller.update(new, mlp)\n        if accepted and learn:\n            model.learn(context[-(model.order - 1) - len(new) - 1:])\n\n        # Pipe output back to input at the end of each full cognitive cycle.\n        if len(stack) % len(COG_CYCLE) == 0:\n            context = [COG_INTEGRATE] + full[-window:]\n            full.append(COG_INTEGRATE)\n\n    if not trace:\n        print(file=sys.stderr)\n    monotonic = all(stack[i] == COG_CYCLE[i % len(COG_CYCLE)] for i in range(len(stack)))\n    stats = dict(depth=len(stack), target=target_depth, attempts=attempts,\n                 forced=forced, monotonic=monotonic)\n    return full, stats\n\n\n'''\nc = src.index(\"def detokenize\")\nsrc = src[:c] + stacked + src[c:]\nsrc = src.replace(\"import random\\n\", \"import random\\nimport sys\\n\", 1)\n\n# 3) CLI\nsrc = src.replace('''    p.add_argument(\"--no-learn\"''', '''    p.add_argument(\"--stack-target\", type=int, default=12,\n                   help=\"Keep going until this many cognitive tokens have stacked in order (0 = old fixed-cycle mode).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--max-retries\", type=int, default=25, help=\"Rejected chunks allowed per stack slot before forcing.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--strict\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Never force a token; retry until the attempt cap.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--no-learn\"''')\n\nold_start = src.index(\"        full = cybernetic_run(\")\nold_end = src.index(\"        text = detokenize(full, args.hide_cog)\")\nsrc = src[:old_start] + '''        tau = float(np.clip(args.tau, 0.0, 1.0))\n        temp = max(0.0, args.temperature)\n        if args.stack_target > 0:\n            full, stats = stacked_run(\n                model, prompt, target_depth=args.stack_target, chunk=args.chunk,\n                window=args.window, beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp,\n                seed=args.seed, learn=not args.no_learn,\n                max_retries=args.max_retries, strict=args.strict, trace=args.trace)\n            print(f\"\\\\n[stack] depth {stats['depth']}/{stats['target']}  attempts {stats['attempts']}  \"\n                  f\"forced {stats['forced']}  monotonic order verified: {stats['monotonic']}\")\n        else:\n            full = cybernetic_run(\n                model, prompt, cycles=args.cycles, chunk=args.chunk,\n                chunks_per_cycle=args.chunks_per_cycle, window=args.window,\n                beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp, seed=args.seed,\n                learn=not args.no_learn, trace=args.trace)\n\n''' + src[old_end:]\nopen(\"cybernetic_textgen.py\", \"w\").write(src)\nEOF\ncd /tmp && python3 -c \"\nw='the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. every story has an end. the end is a new start! what comes next? the machine decides.'.split()\nopen('c.txt','w').write(' '.join(w*40))\"\necho \"\" | python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py c.txt --prompt \"The machine\" --stack-target 12 --trace 2>&1 | tail -40", "description": "Patch script with stacking loop and test it"}, "message": "Patch script with stacking loop and test it", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nsrc = open(\\\"cybernetic_textgen.py\\\").read()\\n\\n# 1) generate_chunk: optionally stop when the model itself emits a cognitive token\\na = src.index(\\\"def generate_chunk\\\")\\nb = src.index(\\\"def cybernetic_run\\\")\\nnew_gc = '''def generate_chunk(model, fragments, context, n, step0, total, beam_size, tau, temperature, rng,\\n                   stop_on_cog=False):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generate up to n tokens after `context`.\\n\\n    Returns (new_tokens, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted_cog). With stop_on_cog the\\n    chunk ends the moment the MODEL emits a cognitive token (returned in\\n    emitted_cog, not appended to new_tokens).\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    ctx = list(context)\\n    new, logps, hit_eos, emitted = [], [], False, None\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        lam = adiabatic_lambda(step0 + i, total)\\n        ranked = model.candidates(ctx, limit=max(40, beam_size * 8))\\n        scored: List[Candidate] = []\\n        for rank, (token, logp) in enumerate(ranked):\\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, rank, lam)\\n            if consistency <= tau:\\n                scored.append(Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency))\\n        if not scored:\\n            token, logp = ranked[0]\\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, 0, lam)\\n            scored = [Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency)]\\n\\n        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c.score, reverse=True)\\n        beam = scored[:max(1, beam_size)]\\n        probs = softmax([c.score for c in beam], temperature)\\n        chosen = beam[0] if temperature <= 0.01 else rng.choices(beam, weights=probs, k=1)[0]\\n\\n        if chosen.token == \\\"<eos>\\\":\\n            hit_eos = True\\n            break\\n        if stop_on_cog and chosen.token in COGNITIVE:\\n            emitted = chosen.token\\n            logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\\n            break\\n        new.append(chosen.token)\\n        ctx.append(chosen.token)\\n        logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\\n    mean_logp = float(np.mean(logps)) if logps else 0.0\\n    return new, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted\\n\\n\\n'''\\nsrc = src[:a] + new_gc + src[b:]\\n\\n# legacy loop: unpack the 4-tuple\\nsrc = src.replace(\\\"new, mean_logp, hit_eos = generate_chunk(\\\", \\\"new, mean_logp, hit_eos, _ = generate_chunk(\\\")\\n\\n# 2) stacked run, inserted before detokenize\\nstacked = '''def stacked_run(model, prompt, target_depth, chunk, window, beam_size, tau, temperature, seed,\\n                learn, max_retries, strict, trace):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Keep generating until cognitive tokens stack up in the correct order.\\n\\n    The model must itself emit the next expected cognitive token\\n    (observe -> recall -> reflect -> predict -> observe ...) after a chunk of\\n    real content. A wrong or missing token rejects the chunk and it is\\n    regenerated (temperature creeps up on each retry). Accepted chunks are\\n    pushed onto the stack, which only ever grows (monotonic), and are learned\\n    online so the model gets better at the pattern as it goes.\\n\\n    After `max_retries` misses the expected token is forced in (flagged), unless\\n    `strict` is set, in which case it keeps trying until the attempt cap.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(seed)\\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\\n\\n    full = [COG_START] + (tokenize(prompt) or [\\\"The\\\"])\\n    context = list(full)\\n    stack: List[str] = []\\n    forced = 0\\n    attempts = 0\\n    max_attempts = target_depth * (200 if strict else max_retries + 1)\\n\\n    while len(stack) < target_depth and attempts < max_attempts:\\n        expected = COG_CYCLE[len(stack) % len(COG_CYCLE)]\\n        retries = 0\\n        accepted, was_forced = False, False\\n        while attempts < max_attempts:\\n            temp = float(np.clip(controller.temperature * (1.0 + 0.1 * retries), 0.3, 1.8))\\n            new, mlp, eos, emitted = generate_chunk(\\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, len(stack) * chunk,\\n                target_depth * chunk, beam_size, tau, temp, rng, stop_on_cog=True)\\n            attempts += 1\\n            ok = emitted == expected and len(new) > 0\\n            msg = (f\\\"depth {len(stack)}/{target_depth} attempt {attempts} \\\"\\n                   f\\\"expected {expected} got {emitted or 'none'} \\\"\\n                   f\\\"{'OK' if ok else 'retry'} (T={temp:.2f}, forced={forced})\\\")\\n            if trace:\\n                print(msg, file=sys.stderr)\\n            else:\\n                print(\\\"\\\\\\\\r\\\" + msg.ljust(78), end=\\\"\\\", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\\n            if ok:\\n                accepted = True\\n                break\\n            retries += 1\\n            if retries > max_retries and not strict:\\n                was_forced = True\\n                break\\n        if not (accepted or was_forced):\\n            break  # attempt cap hit in strict mode\\n\\n        if was_forced:\\n            forced += 1\\n        stack.append(expected)\\n        context += new + [expected]\\n        full += new + [expected]\\n        if new:\\n            controller.update(new, mlp)\\n        if accepted and learn:\\n            model.learn(context[-(model.order - 1) - len(new) - 1:])\\n\\n        # Pipe output back to input at the end of each full cognitive cycle.\\n        if len(stack) % len(COG_CYCLE) == 0:\\n            context = [COG_INTEGRATE] + full[-window:]\\n            full.append(COG_INTEGRATE)\\n\\n    if not trace:\\n        print(file=sys.stderr)\\n    monotonic = all(stack[i] == COG_CYCLE[i % len(COG_CYCLE)] for i in range(len(stack)))\\n    stats = dict(depth=len(stack), target=target_depth, attempts=attempts,\\n                 forced=forced, monotonic=monotonic)\\n    return full, stats\\n\\n\\n'''\\nc = src.index(\\\"def detokenize\\\")\\nsrc = src[:c] + stacked + src[c:]\\nsrc = src.replace(\\\"import random\\\\n\\\", \\\"import random\\\\nimport sys\\\\n\\\", 1)\\n\\n# 3) CLI\\nsrc = src.replace('''    p.add_argument(\\\"--no-learn\\\"''', '''    p.add_argument(\\\"--stack-target\\\", type=int, default=12,\\n                   help=\\\"Keep going until this many cognitive tokens have stacked in order (0 = old fixed-cycle mode).\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--max-retries\\\", type=int, default=25, help=\\\"Rejected chunks allowed per stack slot before forcing.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--strict\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Never force a token; retry until the attempt cap.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--no-learn\\\"''')\\n\\nold_start = src.index(\\\"        full = cybernetic_run(\\\")\\nold_end = src.index(\\\"        text = detokenize(full, args.hide_cog)\\\")\\nsrc = src[:old_start] + '''        tau = float(np.clip(args.tau, 0.0, 1.0))\\n        temp = max(0.0, args.temperature)\\n        if args.stack_target > 0:\\n            full, stats = stacked_run(\\n                model, prompt, target_depth=args.stack_target, chunk=args.chunk,\\n                window=args.window, beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp,\\n                seed=args.seed, learn=not args.no_learn,\\n                max_retries=args.max_retries, strict=args.strict, trace=args.trace)\\n            print(f\\\"\\\\\\\\n[stack] depth {stats['depth']}/{stats['target']}  attempts {stats['attempts']}  \\\"\\n                  f\\\"forced {stats['forced']}  monotonic order verified: {stats['monotonic']}\\\")\\n        else:\\n            full = cybernetic_run(\\n                model, prompt, cycles=args.cycles, chunk=args.chunk,\\n                chunks_per_cycle=args.chunks_per_cycle, window=args.window,\\n                beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp, seed=args.seed,\\n                learn=not args.no_learn, trace=args.trace)\\n\\n''' + src[old_end:]\\nopen(\\\"cybernetic_textgen.py\\\", \\\"w\\\").write(src)\\nEOF\\ncd /tmp && python3 -c \\\"\\nw='the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. every story has an end. the end is a new start! what comes next? the machine decides.'.split()\\nopen('c.txt','w').write(' '.join(w*40))\\\"\\necho \\\"\\\" | python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py c.txt --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" --stack-target 12 --trace 2>&1 | tail -40\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:30:12.585424Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:30:12.585483Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_014y11kfaCwVdmJZoDayJT6n", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"depth 4/12 attempt 18 expected <observe> got <recall> retry (T=0.94, forced=0)\\ndepth 4/12 attempt 19 expected <observe> got <recall> retry (T=1.02, forced=0)\\ndepth 4/12 attempt 20 expected <observe> got <recall> retry (T=1.10, forced=0)\\ndepth 4/12 attempt 21 expected <observe> got <predict> retry (T=1.19, forced=0)\\ndepth 4/12 attempt 22 expected <observe> got <observe> OK (T=1.27, forced=0)\\ndepth 5/12 attempt 23 expected <recall> got <observe> retry (T=0.85, forced=0)\\ndepth 5/12 attempt 24 expected <recall> got <reflect> retry (T=0.94, forced=0)\\ndepth 5/12 attempt 25 expected <recall> got <recall> OK (T=1.02, forced=0)\\ndepth 6/12 attempt 26 expected <reflect> got <reflect> OK (T=0.85, forced=0)\\ndepth 7/12 attempt 27 expected <predict> got <observe> retry (T=0.85, forced=0)\\ndepth 7/12 attempt 28 expected <predict> got <predict> OK (T=0.94, forced=0)\\ndepth 8/12 attempt 29 expected <observe> got <observe> OK (T=0.85, forced=0)\\ndepth 9/12 attempt 30 expected <recall> got <predict> retry (T=0.85, forced=0)\\ndepth 9/12 attempt 31 expected <recall> got <observe> retry (T=0.94, forced=0)\\ndepth 9/12 attempt 32 expected <recall> got <reflect> retry (T=1.02, forced=0)\\ndepth 9/12 attempt 33 expected <recall> got <predict> retry (T=1.10, forced=0)\\ndepth 9/12 attempt 34 expected <recall> got <reflect> retry (T=1.19, forced=0)\\ndepth 9/12 attempt 35 expected <recall> got <recall> OK (T=1.27, forced=0)\\ndepth 10/12 attempt 36 expected <reflect> got <predict> retry (T=0.85, forced=0)\\ndepth 10/12 attempt 37 expected <reflect> got <observe> retry (T=0.94, forced=0)\\ndepth 10/12 attempt 38 expected <reflect> got <recall> retry (T=1.02, forced=0)\\ndepth 10/12 attempt 39 expected <reflect> got <reflect> OK (T=1.10, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 40 expected <predict> got <recall> retry (T=0.85, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 41 expected <predict> got <reflect> retry (T=0.94, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 42 expected <predict> got <observe> retry (T=1.02, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 43 expected <predict> got <observe> retry (T=1.10, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 44 expected <predict> got <recall> retry (T=1.19, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 45 expected <predict> got <observe> retry (T=1.27, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 46 expected <predict> got <observe> retry (T=1.36, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 47 expected <predict> got <observe> retry (T=1.45, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 48 expected <predict> got <reflect> retry (T=1.53, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 49 expected <predict> got <predict> OK (T=1.61, forced=0)\\n\\n[stack] depth 12/12  attempts 49  forced 0  monotonic order verified: True\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\n<observe> The machine decides. <observe> the machine decides. <recall> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <reflect> every story has an end. <predict> <integrate> the machine decides. <observe> the machine decides. <recall> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <reflect> every story has an end. <predict> <integrate> the end is a new start! <observe> what comes next? <recall> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <reflect> every story has an end. <predict> <integrate>\\n\\nUSER: \\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"depth 4/12 attempt 18 expected <observe> got <recall> retry (T=0.94, forced=0)\\ndepth 4/12 attempt 19 expected <observe> got <recall> retry (T=1.02, forced=0)\\ndepth 4/12 attempt 20 expected <observe> got <recall> retry (T=1.10, forced=0)\\ndepth 4/12 attempt 21 expected <observe> got <predict> retry (T=1.19, forced=0)\\ndepth 4/12 attempt 22 expected <observe> got <observe> OK (T=1.27, forced=0)\\ndepth 5/12 attempt 23 expected <recall> got <observe> retry (T=0.85, forced=0)\\ndepth 5/12 attempt 24 expected <recall> got <reflect> retry (T=0.94, forced=0)\\ndepth 5/12 attempt 25 expected <recall> got <recall> OK (T=1.02, forced=0)\\ndepth 6/12 attempt 26 expected <reflect> got <reflect> OK (T=0.85, forced=0)\\ndepth 7/12 attempt 27 expected <predict> got <observe> retry (T=0.85, forced=0)\\ndepth 7/12 attempt 28 expected <predict> got <predict> OK (T=0.94, forced=0)\\ndepth 8/12 attempt 29 expected <observe> got <observe> OK (T=0.85, forced=0)\\ndepth 9/12 attempt 30 expected <recall> got <predict> retry (T=0.85, forced=0)\\ndepth 9/12 attempt 31 expected <recall> got <observe> retry (T=0.94, forced=0)\\ndepth 9/12 attempt 32 expected <recall> got <reflect> retry (T=1.02, forced=0)\\ndepth 9/12 attempt 33 expected <recall> got <predict> retry (T=1.10, forced=0)\\ndepth 9/12 attempt 34 expected <recall> got <reflect> retry (T=1.19, forced=0)\\ndepth 9/12 attempt 35 expected <recall> got <recall> OK (T=1.27, forced=0)\\ndepth 10/12 attempt 36 expected <reflect> got <predict> retry (T=0.85, forced=0)\\ndepth 10/12 attempt 37 expected <reflect> got <observe> retry (T=0.94, forced=0)\\ndepth 10/12 attempt 38 expected <reflect> got <recall> retry (T=1.02, forced=0)\\ndepth 10/12 attempt 39 expected <reflect> got <reflect> OK (T=1.10, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 40 expected <predict> got <recall> retry (T=0.85, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 41 expected <predict> got <reflect> retry (T=0.94, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 42 expected <predict> got <observe> retry (T=1.02, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 43 expected <predict> got <observe> retry (T=1.10, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 44 expected <predict> got <recall> retry (T=1.19, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 45 expected <predict> got <observe> retry (T=1.27, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 46 expected <predict> got <observe> retry (T=1.36, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 47 expected <predict> got <observe> retry (T=1.45, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 48 expected <predict> got <reflect> retry (T=1.53, forced=0)\\ndepth 11/12 attempt 49 expected <predict> got <predict> OK (T=1.61, forced=0)\\n\\n[stack] depth 12/12  attempts 49  forced 0  monotonic order verified: True\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\n<observe> The machine decides. <observe> the machine decides. <recall> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <reflect> every story has an end. <predict> <integrate> the machine decides. <observe> the machine decides. <recall> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <reflect> every story has an end. <predict> <integrate> the end is a new start! <observe> what comes next? <recall> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <reflect> every story has an end. <predict> <integrate>\\n\\nUSER: \\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:30:14.911988Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:30:15.063093Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_017qTjmiTEW2siaFsn9pznw7", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:30:15.086822Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:30:15.086856Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_017qTjmiTEW2siaFsn9pznw7", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py", "name": "cybernetic textgen", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "\n\nThe file cards appear with your reply, and where they sit relative to its text depends on the app the user is reading in; finish the reply with text, and refer to a file by its name, never as above or below."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:30:20.750385Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:30:20.769282Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I've updated `cybernetic_textgen.py` so it keeps regenerating until the cognitive tokens stack up in the correct order. On my test run it reached depth 12/12 in 49 attempts, with no forced tokens and the order verified. That was on a tiny repetitive corpus, so your data will behave differently.\n\n**How it works**\n- \"Correct\" means the cycle `<observe>` \u2192 `<recall>` \u2192 `<reflect>` \u2192 `<predict>` \u2192 `<observe>` and so on.\n- Each chunk now ends when the model emits a cognitive token itself. If it's the expected next one and the chunk had real content before it, the chunk is accepted and pushed onto the stack.\n- If it's the wrong token or none, the chunk is thrown away and regenerated. Temperature creeps up 10% per retry, which in the test run kept it from getting stuck on a slot.\n- The stack only grows, so it is monotonic by construction, and the run ends with a check that the whole stack matches the pattern.\n- Only accepted chunks are learned online, so the model gets better at the pattern as it goes.\n- After each full cycle of four, the last `--window` tokens are piped back in as the next prompt, starting with `<integrate>`.\n\n**New flags**\n- `--stack-target N` is the depth to reach (default 12). `0` gives back the old fixed-cycle mode.\n- `--max-retries` is how many rejected chunks are allowed per slot (default 25). After that the expected token is forced in and counted as `forced`.\n- `--strict` never forces a token and retries until the attempt cap.\n- `--trace` prints every attempt. Without it you get a single live progress line on stderr.\n\n**What it prints**\n- A summary line with depth, attempts, forced count and whether the order was verified.\n\nForced tokens are the weak spot: they make the order correct without the model actually producing it. Run with `--strict` if you only want stacks the model produced itself.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:30:20.836317Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:30:20.836317Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a139be-be3d-7e26-b83e-d803887e5c79"}, {"uuid": "01a139c0-56f3-73a6-87c1-d0e6b23c5e26", "text": "hide the cognitive tokens", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:31:11.248847Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:31:11.248847Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "hide the cognitive tokens", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:31:11.249199Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:31:11.249199Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a139be-be3d-7183-b353-07df4a284a5f"}, {"uuid": "01a139c0-56f3-7522-bb9b-f655399efe93", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nCognitive tokens are now hidden in the printed output by default, and I confirmed it with a test run. The generator still uses them internally for the feedback loop and the stacking check, and `--trace` still shows them.\n\nI replaced the old `--hide-cog` flag with `--show-cog`, which prints the tokens again when you want to inspect them.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:31:12.225668Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:31:13.914434Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_015x33K4T2Pmgfe3WySNTuCX", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open(\"cybernetic_textgen.py\").read()\ns = s.replace('''    p.add_argument(\"--hide-cog\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Hide cognitive tokens in printed text.\")''',\n'''    p.add_argument(\"--show-cog\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Show cognitive tokens in printed text (hidden by default).\")''')\ns = s.replace(\"text = detokenize(full, args.hide_cog)\", \"text = detokenize(full, hide_cog=not args.show_cog)\")\ns = s.replace(\"python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --hide-cog --no-learn\", \"python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --show-cog --no-learn\")\nopen(\"cybernetic_textgen.py\",\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"hide_cog\\|show-cog\\|show_cog\" cybernetic_textgen.py\ncd /tmp && echo \"\" | python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py c.txt --prompt \"The machine\" 2>/dev/null | tail -6", "description": "Hide cognitive tokens by default and test"}, "message": "Hide cognitive tokens by default and test", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\ns = open(\\\"cybernetic_textgen.py\\\").read()\\ns = s.replace('''    p.add_argument(\\\"--hide-cog\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Hide cognitive tokens in printed text.\\\")''',\\n'''    p.add_argument(\\\"--show-cog\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Show cognitive tokens in printed text (hidden by default).\\\")''')\\ns = s.replace(\\\"text = detokenize(full, args.hide_cog)\\\", \\\"text = detokenize(full, hide_cog=not args.show_cog)\\\")\\ns = s.replace(\\\"python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --hide-cog --no-learn\\\", \\\"python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --show-cog --no-learn\\\")\\nopen(\\\"cybernetic_textgen.py\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(s)\\nEOF\\ngrep -n \\\"hide_cog\\\\|show-cog\\\\|show_cog\\\" cybernetic_textgen.py\\ncd /tmp && echo \\\"\\\" | python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py c.txt --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" 2>/dev/null | tail -6\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "appro