\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\nThe machine decides. the machine decides. the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. every story has an end. the machine decides. the machine decides. the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. every story has an end. the end is a new start! what comes next? the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. every story has an end.\\n\\nUSER: \\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:31:16.054607Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:31:16.303880Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_016A7926X7LsGq8jGSp3ruYu", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:31:16.333722Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:31:16.333773Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_016A7926X7LsGq8jGSp3ruYu", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py", "name": "cybernetic textgen", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "\n\nThe file cards appear with your reply, and where they sit relative to its text depends on the app the user is reading in; finish the reply with text, and refer to a file by its name, never as above or below."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:31:20.134708Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:31:20.147110Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Cognitive tokens are now hidden in the printed output by default, and I confirmed it with a test run. The generator still uses them internally for the feedback loop and the stacking check, and `--trace` still shows them.\n\nI replaced the old `--hide-cog` flag with `--show-cog`, which prints the tokens again when you want to inspect them.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:31:20.234764Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:31:20.234764Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a139c0-56f3-73a6-87c1-d0e6b23c5e26"}, {"uuid": "01a139c3-c832-703f-b387-80d4899768b2", "text": "COG_CYCLE = [\"<observe>\", \"<recall>\", \"<reflect>\", \"<predict>\"]\n\nwrite a list of 25 only", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:34:58.191946Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:34:58.191946Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "COG_CYCLE = [\"<observe>\", \"<recall>\", \"<reflect>\", \"<predict>\"]\n\nwrite a list of 25 only", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:34:58.192281Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:34:58.192281Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a139c0-56f3-7522-bb9b-f655399efe93"}, {"uuid": "01a139c3-c832-76fb-aca8-14b8f5263611", "text": "```python\nCOG_CYCLE = [\n    \"<observe>\", \"<recall>\", \"<reflect>\", \"<predict>\", \"<attend>\",\n    \"<compare>\", \"<infer>\", \"<hypothesize>\", \"<evaluate>\", \"<plan>\",\n    \"<decide>\", \"<act>\", \"<monitor>\", \"<correct>\", \"<abstract>\",\n    \"<associate>\", \"<imagine>\", \"<question>\", \"<verify>\", \"<summarize>\",\n    \"<prioritize>\", \"<simulate>\", \"<adapt>\", \"<consolidate>\", \"<anticipate>\",\n]\n```", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:34:58.191694Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:35:00.289919Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Expanding the cognitive token list to twenty-five entries."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:35:00.289940Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:35:01.041213Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "```python\nCOG_CYCLE = [\n    \"<observe>\", \"<recall>\", \"<reflect>\", \"<predict>\", \"<attend>\",\n    \"<compare>\", \"<infer>\", \"<hypothesize>\", \"<evaluate>\", \"<plan>\",\n    \"<decide>\", \"<act>\", \"<monitor>\", \"<correct>\", \"<abstract>\",\n    \"<associate>\", \"<imagine>\", \"<question>\", \"<verify>\", \"<summarize>\",\n    \"<prioritize>\", \"<simulate>\", \"<adapt>\", \"<consolidate>\", \"<anticipate>\",\n]\n```", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:35:01.052560Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:35:01.052560Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a139c3-c832-703f-b387-80d4899768b2"}, {"uuid": "01a139c4-966c-73b3-9be1-47d9ce9b747e", "text": "non monotonic order", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:35:49.606689Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:35:49.606689Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "non monotonic order", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:35:49.607115Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:35:49.607115Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a139c3-c832-76fb-aca8-14b8f5263611"}, {"uuid": "01a139c4-966c-7d24-9e44-a7b1286c6879", "text": "```python\nCOG_CYCLE = [\n    \"<simulate>\", \"<recall>\", \"<correct>\", \"<imagine>\", \"<decide>\",\n    \"<observe>\", \"<verify>\", \"<associate>\", \"<plan>\", \"<anticipate>\",\n    \"<reflect>\", \"<abstract>\", \"<act>\", \"<question>\", \"<compare>\",\n    \"<adapt>\", \"<predict>\", \"<summarize>\", \"<monitor>\", \"<infer>\",\n    \"<consolidate>\", \"<attend>\", \"<evaluate>\", \"<prioritize>\", \"<hypothesize>\",\n]\n```\n\nIt's the same 25 tokens, shuffled. In `cybernetic_textgen.py` the stacking loop treats the list order as the required sequence, so with this list it now has to stack `<simulate>` first, then `<recall>`, then `<correct>`, and so on. The stack still only grows, so the \"monotonic order verified\" check still passes.\n\nIf you meant something else, such as letting the model emit the tokens in any order with no required sequence, tell me and I'll change the validation.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:35:49.606453Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:35:55.426073Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Figuring out the intended ordering for the list."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:35:55.426111Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:35:57.318747Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "```python\nCOG_CYCLE = [\n    \"<simulate>\", \"<recall>\", \"<correct>\", \"<imagine>\", \"<decide>\",\n    \"<observe>\", \"<verify>\", \"<associate>\", \"<plan>\", \"<anticipate>\",\n    \"<reflect>\", \"<abstract>\", \"<act>\", \"<question>\", \"<compare>\",\n    \"<adapt>\", \"<predict>\", \"<summarize>\", \"<monitor>\", \"<infer>\",\n    \"<consolidate>\", \"<attend>\", \"<evaluate>\", \"<prioritize>\", \"<hypothesize>\",\n]\n```\n\nIt's the same 25 tokens, shuffled. In `cybernetic_textgen.py` the stacking loop treats the list order as the required sequence, so with this list it now has to stack `<simulate>` first, then `<recall>`, then `<correct>`, and so on. The stack still only grows, so the \"monotonic order verified\" check still passes.\n\nIf you meant something else, such as letting the model emit the tokens in any order with no required sequence, tell me and I'll change the validation.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:35:57.330030Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:35:57.330030Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a139c4-966c-73b3-9be1-47d9ce9b747e"}, {"uuid": "01a139c4-d8be-73e9-aee1-7e05237847cd", "text": "of the code", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:36:06.576306Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:36:06.576306Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "of the code", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:36:06.576604Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:36:06.576604Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a139c4-966c-7d24-9e44-a7b1286c6879"}, {"uuid": "01a139c4-d8be-709c-a1ef-ba9fb2c733dc", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThe 25-token shuffled list is now in `cybernetic_textgen.py`, and a test run stacked all 25 in order. It took 177 attempts with 0 forced tokens, and the order check passed. I ran it with `--show-cog` so the tokens were visible.\n\nTwo other changes came with it:\n- **Piping back:** it used to happen after every full cycle, which would never trigger with 25 tokens. It now happens every 4 stacked tokens, set by the new `PIPE_EVERY` constant.\n- **Default depth:** `--stack-target` now defaults to 25, so one run covers the whole list.\n\nStacking took many more attempts than before (177, up from 49 for 12 tokens), because the model has to hit one specific token out of 25 each time.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:36:06.576094Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:36:10.467062Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Updating the code to apply the non-monotonic token cycle."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:36:10.467120Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:36:13.574981Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01RKHa1wEbL1Y9h5crHw4M1C", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open(\"cybernetic_textgen.py\").read()\ns = s.replace('COG_CYCLE = [\"<observe>\", \"<recall>\", \"<reflect>\", \"<predict>\"]', '''COG_CYCLE = [\n    \"<simulate>\", \"<recall>\", \"<correct>\", \"<imagine>\", \"<decide>\",\n    \"<observe>\", \"<verify>\", \"<associate>\", \"<plan>\", \"<anticipate>\",\n    \"<reflect>\", \"<abstract>\", \"<act>\", \"<question>\", \"<compare>\",\n    \"<adapt>\", \"<predict>\", \"<summarize>\", \"<monitor>\", \"<infer>\",\n    \"<consolidate>\", \"<attend>\", \"<evaluate>\", \"<prioritize>\", \"<hypothesize>\",\n]\nPIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens''')\ns = s.replace(\"if len(stack) % len(COG_CYCLE) == 0:\", \"if len(stack) % PIPE_EVERY == 0:\")\ns = s.replace('\"--stack-target\", type=int, default=12', '\"--stack-target\", type=int, default=25')\ns = s.replace('''  <observe> <recall> <reflect> <predict>   normal cycle''', '''  25 tokens in COG_CYCLE (a fixed, deliberately non-alphabetical order)''')\ns = s.replace(\"(observe -> recall -> reflect -> predict -> observe ...)\", \"(the order defined in COG_CYCLE, repeating)\")\nopen(\"cybernetic_textgen.py\",\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"PIPE_EVERY\\|default=25\" cybernetic_textgen.py\ncd /tmp && echo \"\" | python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py c.txt --prompt \"The machine\" --show-cog 2>&1 | tail -8", "description": "Apply 25-token shuffled COG_CYCLE to the code and test"}, "message": "Apply 25-token shuffled COG_CYCLE to the code and test", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\ns = open(\\\"cybernetic_textgen.py\\\").read()\\ns = s.replace('COG_CYCLE = [\\\"<observe>\\\", \\\"<recall>\\\", \\\"<reflect>\\\", \\\"<predict>\\\"]', '''COG_CYCLE = [\\n    \\\"<simulate>\\\", \\\"<recall>\\\", \\\"<correct>\\\", \\\"<imagine>\\\", \\\"<decide>\\\",\\n    \\\"<observe>\\\", \\\"<verify>\\\", \\\"<associate>\\\", \\\"<plan>\\\", \\\"<anticipate>\\\",\\n    \\\"<reflect>\\\", \\\"<abstract>\\\", \\\"<act>\\\", \\\"<question>\\\", \\\"<compare>\\\",\\n    \\\"<adapt>\\\", \\\"<predict>\\\", \\\"<summarize>\\\", \\\"<monitor>\\\", \\\"<infer>\\\",\\n    \\\"<consolidate>\\\", \\\"<attend>\\\", \\\"<evaluate>\\\", \\\"<prioritize>\\\", \\\"<hypothesize>\\\",\\n]\\nPIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens''')\\ns = s.replace(\\\"if len(stack) % len(COG_CYCLE) == 0:\\\", \\\"if len(stack) % PIPE_EVERY == 0:\\\")\\ns = s.replace('\\\"--stack-target\\\", type=int, default=12', '\\\"--stack-target\\\", type=int, default=25')\\ns = s.replace('''  <observe> <recall> <reflect> <predict>   normal cycle''', '''  25 tokens in COG_CYCLE (a fixed, deliberately non-alphabetical order)''')\\ns = s.replace(\\\"(observe -> recall -> reflect -> predict -> observe ...)\\\", \\\"(the order defined in COG_CYCLE, repeating)\\\")\\nopen(\\\"cybernetic_textgen.py\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(s)\\nEOF\\ngrep -n \\\"PIPE_EVERY\\\\|default=25\\\" cybernetic_textgen.py\\ncd /tmp && echo \\\"\\\" | python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py c.txt --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" --show-cog 2>&1 | tail -8\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:36:15.966429Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:36:15.966480Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01RKHa1wEbL1Y9h5crHw4M1C", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"56:PIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens\\n413:        if len(stack) % PIPE_EVERY == 0:\\n443:    p.add_argument(\\\"--stack-target\\\", type=int, default=25,\\n445:    p.add_argument(\\\"--max-retries\\\", type=int, default=25, help=\\\"Rejected chunks allowed per stack slot before forcing.\\\")\\n\\n[stack] depth 25/25  attempts 177  forced 0  monotonic order verified: True\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\n<observe> The machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <simulate> every story has an end. <recall> the end is a new start! <correct> what comes next? <imagine> <integrate> the machine decides. <decide> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <observe> every story has an end. <verify> the end is a new start! <associate> <integrate> what comes next? <plan> the machine decides. <anticipate> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <reflect> every story has an end. <abstract> <integrate> the end is a new start! <act> what comes next? <question> the machine decides. <compare> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <adapt> <integrate> every story has an end. <predict> the end is a new start! <summarize> what comes next? <monitor> the machine decides. <infer> <integrate> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <consolidate> every story has an end. <attend> the end is a new start! <evaluate> what comes next? <prioritize> <integrate> the machine decides. <hypothesize>\\n\\nUSER: \\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"56:PIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens\\n413:        if len(stack) % PIPE_EVERY == 0:\\n443:    p.add_argument(\\\"--stack-target\\\", type=int, default=25,\\n445:    p.add_argument(\\\"--max-retries\\\", type=int, default=25, help=\\\"Rejected chunks allowed per stack slot before forcing.\\\")\\n\\n[stack] depth 25/25  attempts 177  forced 0  monotonic order verified: True\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\n<observe> The machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <simulate> every story has an end. <recall> the end is a new start! <correct> what comes next? <imagine> <integrate> the machine decides. <decide> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <observe> every story has an end. <verify> the end is a new start! <associate> <integrate> what comes next? <plan> the machine decides. <anticipate> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <reflect> every story has an end. <abstract> <integrate> the end is a new start! <act> what comes next? <question> the machine decides. <compare> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <adapt> <integrate> every story has an end. <predict> the end is a new start! <summarize> what comes next? <monitor> the machine decides. <infer> <integrate> the machine learns to read and then it writes a story. <consolidate> every story has an end. <attend> the end is a new start! <evaluate> what comes next? <prioritize> <integrate> the machine decides. <hypothesize>\\n\\nUSER: \\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:36:18.160567Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:36:18.408323Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01PkFuJAtKNkC2TJPjP8Ft3K", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:36:18.446174Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:36:18.446202Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01PkFuJAtKNkC2TJPjP8Ft3K", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py", "name": "cybernetic textgen", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "\n\nThe file cards appear with your reply, and where they sit relative to its text depends on the app the user is reading in; finish the reply with text, and refer to a file by its name, never as above or below."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:36:22.454405Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:36:22.472865Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "The 25-token shuffled list is now in `cybernetic_textgen.py`, and a test run stacked all 25 in order. It took 177 attempts with 0 forced tokens, and the order check passed. I ran it with `--show-cog` so the tokens were visible.\n\nTwo other changes came with it:\n- **Piping back:** it used to happen after every full cycle, which would never trigger with 25 tokens. It now happens every 4 stacked tokens, set by the new `PIPE_EVERY` constant.\n- **Default depth:** `--stack-target` now defaults to 25, so one run covers the whole list.\n\nStacking took many more attempts than before (177, up from 49 for 12 tokens), because the model has to hit one specific token out of 25 each time.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:36:22.547945Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:36:22.547945Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a139c4-d8be-73e9-aee1-7e05237847cd"}, {"uuid": "01a139c7-9b89-7e96-beea-e873f636ac66", "text": "use dataset tokens for the cog", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:39:09.050395Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:39:09.050395Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "use dataset tokens for the cog", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:39:09.050752Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:39:09.050752Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a139c4-d8be-709c-a1ef-ba9fb2c733dc"}, {"uuid": "01a139c7-9b89-7266-bb66-bab5741bca8a", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n`cybernetic_textgen.py` now takes its cognitive tokens from the corpus instead of a hardcoded list. The caveat is that on my random-word test corpus the stacking mostly fell back to forcing tokens, so I haven't seen it work well yet.\n\n**How the tokens are chosen**\n- At startup it picks the 29 most frequent words in your corpus that are at least 4 letters long, skipping common function words like \"that\" and \"with\".\n- It shuffles them with `--seed`, so the order is non-monotonic and repeatable.\n- The first 25 are the required stack order. The other four play the roles of diverge, converge, integrate and start.\n- The chosen tokens are printed to stderr at startup.\n- If the corpus has fewer than 29 distinct qualifying words, the missing ones are filled from the old `<observe>`-style names.\n\n**Hiding them**\n- Because the tokens are now ordinary words, simply deleting every occurrence from the output would remove real text.\n- So inserted markers are tagged as a special string type, and only those are hidden. The same word appearing as normal content is kept.\n- `--show-cog` still reveals the markers.\n\n**How it performed**\n- My test corpus was random words, so there was no word order for the model to learn.\n- The stack reached 25/25 and the order check passed, but it took 621 attempts and forced 23 of the 25 tokens.\n- Ordinary words show up everywhere, so the model is much less likely to emit one specific word at the right moment than it was with the `<tag>` tokens.\n- Real text with structure should do better. If you still see many forced tokens, use `--strict` or raise `--max-retries`.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:39:09.050145Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:39:38.054785Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Deriving cognitive tokens from the corpus vocabulary."}, {"summary": "Tracking cognitive-token identity without disturbing ordinary text."}, {"summary": "Filtering frequent words to pick usable cognitive tokens."}, {"summary": "Wrapping marker tokens in a distinct type for safety."}, {"summary": "Wiring token selection into the main setup flow."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:39:38.054861Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:39:51.110831Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_014sCZu5x39eSJ6PFaKtuLNL", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open(\"cybernetic_textgen.py\").read()\n\na = s.index(\"COG_CYCLE = [\")\nb = s.index(\"SENTENCE_END\")\nb_end = s.index(\"\\n\", b) + 1\nblock = '''class CogToken(str):\n    \"\"\"A cognitive marker inserted by the loop. It is a str, but isinstance() tells it\n    apart from the same word appearing as ordinary text, so hiding markers never\n    deletes real words from the output.\"\"\"\n\n\n# Fallback names, used only if the corpus has too few distinct words.\nDEFAULT_COG = [\n    \"<simulate>\", \"<recall>\", \"<correct>\", \"<imagine>\", \"<decide>\",\n    \"<observe>\", \"<verify>\", \"<associate>\", \"<plan>\", \"<anticipate>\",\n    \"<reflect>\", \"<abstract>\", \"<act>\", \"<question>\", \"<compare>\",\n    \"<adapt>\", \"<predict>\", \"<summarize>\", \"<monitor>\", \"<infer>\",\n    \"<consolidate>\", \"<attend>\", \"<evaluate>\", \"<prioritize>\", \"<hypothesize>\",\n    \"<diverge>\", \"<converge>\", \"<integrate>\", \"<observe>\",\n]\nCOG_COUNT = 29  # 25 cycle tokens + diverge + converge + integrate + start\nPIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens\nSENTENCE_END = (\".\", \"!\", \"?\")\n\nCOG_CYCLE: List[str] = []\nCOG_DIVERGE = COG_CONVERGE = COG_INTEGRATE = COG_START = CogToken(\"\")\nCOGNITIVE: set = set()\n\n_STOP = {\n    \"that\", \"with\", \"have\", \"from\", \"this\", \"they\", \"were\", \"been\", \"will\", \"would\", \"there\",\n    \"their\", \"what\", \"when\", \"which\", \"your\", \"them\", \"then\", \"than\", \"into\", \"only\", \"also\",\n    \"some\", \"such\", \"more\", \"most\", \"other\", \"about\", \"could\", \"should\", \"these\", \"those\",\n}\n\n\ndef set_cognitive_tokens(words: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Install the cognitive vocabulary: 25 cycle tokens, then diverge, converge,\n    integrate, start.\"\"\"\n    global COG_CYCLE, COG_DIVERGE, COG_CONVERGE, COG_INTEGRATE, COG_START, COGNITIVE\n    toks = [CogToken(w) for w in words]\n    COG_CYCLE = toks[:25]\n    COG_DIVERGE, COG_CONVERGE, COG_INTEGRATE, COG_START = toks[25:29]\n    COGNITIVE = {str(t) for t in toks}\n\n\ndef select_cognitive_tokens(text: str, seed: int, count: int = COG_COUNT) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Pick cognitive tokens FROM THE DATASET: the most frequent alphabetic words of\n    4+ letters (skipping common function words), shuffled so the required order is\n    non-monotonic.\"\"\"\n    counts = Counter(tokenize(text))\n    pool = [(w, c) for w, c in counts.items()\n            if w.isalpha() and len(w) >= 4 and w.lower() not in _STOP]\n    pool.sort(key=lambda wc: (-wc[1], wc[0]))\n    words, seen = [], set()\n    for w, _ in pool:\n        if w.lower() not in seen:\n            seen.add(w.lower())\n            words.append(w)\n        if len(words) >= count:\n            break\n    random.Random(seed).shuffle(words)\n    for d in DEFAULT_COG:  # top up from fallback names if the corpus is tiny\n        if len(words) >= count:\n            break\n        if d.lower() not in seen:\n            seen.add(d.lower())\n            words.append(d)\n    return words\n\n\nset_cognitive_tokens(DEFAULT_COG)\n'''\ns = s[:a] + block + s[b_end:]\n\ns = s.replace(\"    return [t for t in tokens if t not in COGNITIVE]\",\n              \"    return [t for t in tokens if not isinstance(t, CogToken)]\")\n\ns = s.replace('''  25 tokens in COG_CYCLE (a fixed, deliberately non-alphabetical order)\n  <diverge>   output was repetitive   -> raise temperature\n  <converge>  output was incoherent   -> lower temperature\n  <integrate> start of every piped-back prompt''',\n'''  Taken from the dataset itself: the 29 most frequent 4+ letter words in the\n  corpus, shuffled (non-monotonic order). 25 form the required stack order; the\n  other four act as diverge (raise temperature), converge (lower temperature),\n  integrate (start of every piped-back prompt) and start. Inserted markers are\n  CogToken objects, so hiding them never removes the same word from ordinary text.''')\n\ns = s.replace('''    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\n    model.train(corpus_text, cognitive=True)''',\n'''    set_cognitive_tokens(select_cognitive_tokens(corpus_text, args.seed))\n    print(\"cognitive tokens (from dataset): \" + \" \".join(COG_CYCLE)\n          + f\" | diverge={COG_DIVERGE} converge={COG_CONVERGE}\"\n          f\" integrate={COG_INTEGRATE} start={COG_START}\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\n    model.train(corpus_text, cognitive=True)''')\nopen(\"cybernetic_textgen.py\",\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ncd /tmp && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport random\nr = random.Random(1)\nvocab = \"machine signal pattern memory feedback system process control sensor output input cycle token model language future context purpose balance energy design network response change stable error correct adapt measure learn predict reason structure thread orbit anchor engine garden window bridge harbor lantern marble river forest mirror shadow summit valley whisper\".split()\nsents=[]\nfor _ in range(600):\n    n=r.randint(5,9)\n    sents.append(\" \".join(r.choice(vocab) for _ in range(n)).capitalize()+r.choice([\".\",\".\",\"!\",\"?\"]))\nopen(\"d.txt\",\"w\").write(\" \".join(sents))\nEOF\necho \"\" | python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py d.txt --prompt \"The machine\" --show-cog 2>&1 | cut -c1-900 | tail -9\necho ---HIDDEN---\necho \"\" | python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py d.txt --prompt \"The machine\" 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-500 | tail -5", "description": "Switch cognitive tokens to dataset-derived words and test"}, "message": "Switch cognitive tokens to dataset-derived words and test", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /mnt/user-data/outputs && python3 - <<'EOF'\\ns = open(\\\"cybernetic_textgen.py\\\").read()\\n\\na = s.index(\\\"COG_CYCLE = [\\\")\\nb = s.index(\\\"SENTENCE_END\\\")\\nb_end = s.index(\\\"\\\\n\\\", b) + 1\\nblock = '''class CogToken(str):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A cognitive marker inserted by the loop. It is a str, but isinstance() tells it\\n    apart from the same word appearing as ordinary text, so hiding markers never\\n    deletes real words from the output.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\n# Fallback names, used only if the corpus has too few distinct words.\\nDEFAULT_COG = [\\n    \\\"<simulate>\\\", \\\"<recall>\\\", \\\"<correct>\\\", \\\"<imagine>\\\", \\\"<decide>\\\",\\n    \\\"<observe>\\\", \\\"<verify>\\\", \\\"<associate>\\\", \\\"<plan>\\\", \\\"<anticipate>\\\",\\n    \\\"<reflect>\\\", \\\"<abstract>\\\", \\\"<act>\\\", \\\"<question>\\\", \\\"<compare>\\\",\\n    \\\"<adapt>\\\", \\\"<predict>\\\", \\\"<summarize>\\\", \\\"<monitor>\\\", \\\"<infer>\\\",\\n    \\\"<consolidate>\\\", \\\"<attend>\\\", \\\"<evaluate>\\\", \\\"<prioritize>\\\", \\\"<hypothesize>\\\",\\n    \\\"<diverge>\\\", \\\"<converge>\\\", \\\"<integrate>\\\", \\\"<observe>\\\",\\n]\\nCOG_COUNT = 29  # 25 cycle tokens + diverge + converge + integrate + start\\nPIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens\\nSENTENCE_END = (\\\".\\\", \\\"!\\\", \\\"?\\\")\\n\\nCOG_CYCLE: List[str] = []\\nCOG_DIVERGE = COG_CONVERGE = COG_INTEGRATE = COG_START = CogToken(\\\"\\\")\\nCOGNITIVE: set = set()\\n\\n_STOP = {\\n    \\\"that\\\", \\\"with\\\", \\\"have\\\", \\\"from\\\", \\\"this\\\", \\\"they\\\", \\\"were\\\", \\\"been\\\", \\\"will\\\", \\\"would\\\", \\\"there\\\",\\n    \\\"their\\\", \\\"what\\\", \\\"when\\\", \\\"which\\\", \\\"your\\\", \\\"them\\\", \\\"then\\\", \\\"than\\\", \\\"into\\\", \\\"only\\\", \\\"also\\\",\\n    \\\"some\\\", \\\"such\\\", \\\"more\\\", \\\"most\\\", \\\"other\\\", \\\"about\\\", \\\"could\\\", \\\"should\\\", \\\"these\\\", \\\"those\\\",\\n}\\n\\n\\ndef set_cognitive_tokens(words: Sequence[str]) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Install the cognitive vocabulary: 25 cycle tokens, then diverge, converge,\\n    integrate, start.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    global COG_CYCLE, COG_DIVERGE, COG_CONVERGE, COG_INTEGRATE, COG_START, COGNITIVE\\n    toks = [CogToken(w) for w in words]\\n    COG_CYCLE = toks[:25]\\n    COG_DIVERGE, COG_CONVERGE, COG_INTEGRATE, COG_START = toks[25:29]\\n    COGNITIVE = {str(t) for t in toks}\\n\\n\\ndef select_cognitive_tokens(text: str, seed: int, count: int = COG_COUNT) -> List[str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pick cognitive tokens FROM THE DATASET: the most frequent alphabetic words of\\n    4+ letters (skipping common function words), shuffled so the required order is\\n    non-monotonic.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    counts = Counter(tokenize(text))\\n    pool = [(w, c) for w, c in counts.items()\\n            if w.isalpha() and len(w) >= 4 and w.lower() not in _STOP]\\n    pool.sort(key=lambda wc: (-wc[1], wc[0]))\\n    words, seen = [], set()\\n    for w, _ in pool:\\n        if w.lower() not in seen:\\n            seen.add(w.lower())\\n            words.append(w)\\n        if len(words) >= count:\\n            break\\n    random.Random(seed).shuffle(words)\\n    for d in DEFAULT_COG:  # top up from fallback names if the corpus is tiny\\n        if len(words) >= count:\\n            break\\n        if d.lower() not in seen:\\n            seen.add(d.lower())\\n            words.append(d)\\n    return words\\n\\n\\nset_cognitive_tokens(DEFAULT_COG)\\n'''\\ns = s[:a] + block + s[b_end:]\\n\\ns = s.replace(\\\"    return [t for t in tokens if t not in COGNITIVE]\\\",\\n              \\\"    return [t for t in tokens if not isinstance(t, CogToken)]\\\")\\n\\ns = s.replace('''  25 tokens in COG_CYCLE (a fixed, deliberately non-alphabetical order)\\n  <diverge>   output was repetitive   -> raise temperature\\n  <converge>  output was incoherent   -> lower temperature\\n  <integrate> start of every piped-back prompt''',\\n'''  Taken from the dataset itself: the 29 most frequent 4+ letter words in the\\n  corpus, shuffled (non-monotonic order). 25 form the required stack order; the\\n  other four act as diverge (raise temperature), converge (lower temperature),\\n  integrate (start of every piped-back prompt) and start. Inserted markers are\\n  CogToken objects, so hiding them never removes the same word from ordinary text.''')\\n\\ns = s.replace('''    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\\n    model.train(corpus_text, cognitive=True)''',\\n'''    set_cognitive_tokens(select_cognitive_tokens(corpus_text, args.seed))\\n    print(\\\"cognitive tokens (from dataset): \\\" + \\\" \\\".join(COG_CYCLE)\\n          + f\\\" | diverge={COG_DIVERGE} converge={COG_CONVERGE}\\\"\\n          f\\\" integrate={COG_INTEGRATE} start={COG_START}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\\n    model.train(corpus_text, cognitive=True)''')\\nopen(\\\"cybernetic_textgen.py\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(s)\\nEOF\\ncd /tmp && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport random\\nr = random.Random(1)\\nvocab = \\\"machine signal pattern memory feedback system process control sensor output input cycle token model language future context purpose balance energy design network response change stable error correct adapt measure learn predict reason structure thread orbit anchor engine garden window bridge harbor lantern marble river forest mirror shadow summit valley whisper\\\".split()\\nsents=[]\\nfor _ in range(600):\\n    n=r.randint(5,9)\\n    sents.append(\\\" \\\".join(r.choice(vocab) for _ in range(n)).capitalize()+r.choice([\\\".\\\",\\\".\\\",\\\"!\\\",\\\"?\\\"]))\\nopen(\\\"d.txt\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(\\\" \\\".join(sents))\\nEOF\\necho \\\"\\\" | python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py d.txt --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" --show-cog 2>&1 | cut -c1-900 | tail -9\\necho ---HIDDEN---\\necho \\\"\\\" | python3 /mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py d.txt --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-500 | tail -5\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:40:09.173234Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:40:09.173277Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_014sCZu5x39eSJ6PFaKtuLNL", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"USER: \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 1 expected change got language retry (T=0.85, forced=0)    \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 2 expected change got structure retry (T=0.94, forced=0)   \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 3 expected change got purpose retry (T=1.02, forced=0)     \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 4 expected change got orbit retry (T=1.10, forced=0)       \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 5 expected change got bridge retry (T=1.19, forced=0)      \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 6 expected change got language retry (T=1.27, forced=0)    \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 7 expected change got orbit retry (T=1.36, forced=0)       \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 8 expected change got design retry (T=1.45, forced=0)      \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 9 expected change got orbit retry (T=1.53, forced=0)       \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 10 expected change got design retry (T=1.61, forced=0)     \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 11 expected change got orbit retry (T=1.70, forced=0)      \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 12 ex\\n\\n[stack] depth 25/25  attempts 621  forced 23  monotonic order verified: True\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\noutput The change network! bridge measure control network input response error anchor summit forest orbit Marble thread token predict response shadow mirror structure? marble Response whisper memory bridge? energy response Garden future measure context cycle engine reason model response learn! purpose feedback feedback! harbor Cycle signal response Error whisper learn pattern language adapt Pattern design response thread forest. structure\\n\\nUSER: \\n---HIDDEN---\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\nThe network! measure network anchor forest Marble thread token shadow structure? Response whisper bridge? Garden future measure reason learn! feedback! Cycle Error whisper learn Pattern thread forest.\\n\\nUSER: \\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"USER: \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 1 expected change got language retry (T=0.85, forced=0)    \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 2 expected change got structure retry (T=0.94, forced=0)   \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 3 expected change got purpose retry (T=1.02, forced=0)     \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 4 expected change got orbit retry (T=1.10, forced=0)       \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 5 expected change got bridge retry (T=1.19, forced=0)      \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 6 expected change got language retry (T=1.27, forced=0)    \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 7 expected change got orbit retry (T=1.36, forced=0)       \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 8 expected change got design retry (T=1.45, forced=0)      \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 9 expected change got orbit retry (T=1.53, forced=0)       \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 10 expected change got design retry (T=1.61, forced=0)     \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 11 expected change got orbit retry (T=1.70, forced=0)      \\rdepth 0/25 attempt 12 ex\\n\\n[stack] depth 25/25  attempts 621  forced 23  monotonic order verified: True\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\noutput The change network! bridge measure control network input response error anchor summit forest orbit Marble thread token predict response shadow mirror structure? marble Response whisper memory bridge? energy response Garden future measure context cycle engine reason model response learn! purpose feedback feedback! harbor Cycle signal response Error whisper learn pattern language adapt Pattern design response thread forest. structure\\n\\nUSER: \\n---HIDDEN---\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\nThe network! measure network anchor forest Marble thread token shadow structure? Response whisper bridge? Garden future measure reason learn! feedback! Cycle Error whisper learn Pattern thread forest.\\n\\nUSER: \\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:40:11.618396Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:40:14.912426Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Testing whether the model can predict a specific word."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:40:14.912494Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:40:14.961226Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_016dVtVwAykfgR4hCMPMe5Jx", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:40:14.987607Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:40:14.987645Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_016dVtVwAykfgR4hCMPMe5Jx", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py", "name": "cybernetic textgen", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "\n\nThe file cards appear with your reply, and where they sit relative to its text depends on the app the user is reading in; finish the reply with text, and refer to a file by its name, never as above or below."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:40:21.075872Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T09:40:21.093651Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "`cybernetic_textgen.py` now takes its cognitive tokens from the corpus instead of a hardcoded list. The caveat is that on my random-word test corpus the stacking mostly fell back to forcing tokens, so I haven't seen it work well yet.\n\n**How the tokens are chosen**\n- At startup it picks the 29 most frequent words in your corpus that are at least 4 letters long, skipping common function words like \"that\" and \"with\".\n- It shuffles them with `--seed`, so the order is non-monotonic and repeatable.\n- The first 25 are the required stack order. The other four play the roles of diverge, converge, integrate and start.\n- The chosen tokens are printed to stderr at startup.\n- If the corpus has fewer than 29 distinct qualifying words, the missing ones are filled from the old `<observe>`-style names.\n\n**Hiding them**\n- Because the tokens are now ordinary words, simply deleting every occurrence from the output would remove real text.\n- So inserted markers are tagged as a special string type, and only those are hidden. The same word appearing as normal content is kept.\n- `--show-cog` still reveals the markers.\n\n**How it performed**\n- My test corpus was random words, so there was no word order for the model to learn.\n- The stack reached 25/25 and the order check passed, but it took 621 attempts and forced 23 of the 25 tokens.\n- Ordinary words show up everywhere, so the model is much less likely to emit one specific word at the right moment than it was with the `<tag>` tokens.\n- Real text with structure should do better. If you still see many forced tokens, use `--strict` or raise `--max-retries`.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-14T09:40:21.150785Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T09:40:21.150785Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a139c7-9b89-7e96-beea-e873f636ac66"}]},{"uuid": "71e0a6f6-d288-4df4-b782-cea92977a8ec", "name": "Replacing cog with cot", "summary": "", "created_at": "2026-10-14T22:04:55.758508Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T22:26:22.109449Z", "account": {"uuid": "8d7882cd-3e98-47cc-a6e7-61494a1ee4ac"}, "chat_messages": [{"uuid": "01a13c72-75a7-72e5-a93c-5425877ffb71", "text": "replace the cog with cot", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:04:58.051626Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:04:58.051626Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "replace the cog with cot", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-14T22:04:58.051876Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T22:04:58.051876Z", "attachments": [{"file_name": "", "file_size": 23359, "file_type": "txt", "extracted_content": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nCybernetic non-isomorphic adiabatic text generator\n==================================================\n\nSame n-gram + non-isomorphic fragment scoring as before, now wrapped in a\nclosed feedback loop:\n\n  1. Generate a chunk of tokens.\n  2. MEASURE it (repetition, mean log-probability)         -> sensor\n  3. Pick a COGNITIVE TOKEN from that measurement           -> comparator\n  4. Insert the cognitive token after the chunk and adjust\n     temperature (negative feedback)                        -> actuator\n  5. At the end of a cycle, pipe the output back in as the next prompt, with a\n     cognitive token at the start, and repeat.\n\nThe model \"understands\" cognitive tokens because they are\n  - woven into the training corpus at sentence boundaries, and\n  - learned online from the model's own (non-degenerate) output.\n\nCognitive tokens:\n  Taken from the dataset itself: the 29 most frequent 4+ letter words in the\n  corpus, shuffled (non-monotonic order). 25 form the required stack order; the\n  other four act as diverge (raise temperature), converge (lower temperature),\n  integrate (start of every piped-back prompt) and start. Inserted markers are\n  CogToken objects, so hiding them never removes the same word from ordinary text.\n\nExamples:\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --cycles 5 --chunk 20\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --prompt \"The machine\" --trace\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --show-cog --no-learn\n\nOnly dependency: NumPy\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport math\nimport random\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import List, Sequence, Tuple\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Cognitive tokens\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass CogToken(str):\n    \"\"\"A cognitive marker inserted by the loop. It is a str, but isinstance() tells it\n    apart from the same word appearing as ordinary text, so hiding markers never\n    deletes real words from the output.\"\"\"\n\n\n# Fallback names, used only if the corpus has too few distinct words.\nDEFAULT_COG = [\n    \"simulate\", \"recall\", \"correct\", \"imagine\", \"decide\",\n    \"observe\", \"verify\", \"associate\", \"plan\", \"anticipate\",\n    \"reflect\", \"abstract\", \"act\", \"question\", \"compare\",\n    \"adapt\", \"predict\", \"summarize\", \"monitor\", \"infer\",\n    \"consolidate\", \"attend\", \"evaluate\", \"prioritize\", \"hypothesize\",\n    \"diverge\", \"converge\", \"integrate\", \"observe\",\n]\nCOG_COUNT = 29  # 25 cycle tokens + diverge + converge + integrate + start\nPIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens\nSENTENCE_END = (\".\", \"!\", \"?\")\n\nCOG_CYCLE: List[str] = []\nCOG_DIVERGE = COG_CONVERGE = COG_INTEGRATE = COG_START = CogToken(\"\")\nCOGNITIVE: set = set()\n\n_STOP = {\n    \"that\", \"with\", \"have\", \"from\", \"this\", \"they\", \"were\", \"been\", \"will\", \"would\", \"there\",\n    \"their\", \"what\", \"when\", \"which\", \"your\", \"them\", \"then\", \"than\", \"into\", \"only\", \"also\",\n    \"some\", \"such\", \"more\", \"most\", \"other\", \"about\", \"could\", \"should\", \"these\", \"those\",\n}\n\n\ndef set_cognitive_tokens(words: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Install the cognitive vocabulary: 25 cycle tokens, then diverge, converge,\n    integrate, start.\"\"\"\n    global COG_CYCLE, COG_DIVERGE, COG_CONVERGE, COG_INTEGRATE, COG_START, COGNITIVE\n    toks = [CogToken(w) for w in words]\n    COG_CYCLE = toks[:25]\n    COG_DIVERGE, COG_CONVERGE, COG_INTEGRATE, COG_START = toks[25:29]\n    COGNITIVE = {str(t) for t in toks}\n\n\ndef select_cognitive_tokens(text: str, seed: int, count: int = COG_COUNT) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Pick cognitive tokens FROM THE DATASET: the most frequent alphabetic words of\n    4+ letters (skipping common function words), shuffled so the required order is\n    non-monotonic.\"\"\"\n    counts = Counter(tokenize(text))\n    pool = [(w, c) for w, c in counts.items()\n            if w.isalpha() and len(w) >= 4 and w.lower() not in _STOP]\n    pool.sort(key=lambda wc: (-wc[1], wc[0]))\n    words, seen = [], set()\n    for w, _ in pool:\n        if w.lower() not in seen:\n            seen.add(w.lower())\n            words.append(w)\n        if len(words) >= count:\n            break\n    random.Random(seed).shuffle(words)\n    for d in DEFAULT_COG:  # top up from fallback names if the corpus is tiny\n        if len(words) >= count:\n            break\n        if d.lower() not in seen:\n            seen.add(d.lower())\n            words.append(d)\n    return words\n\n\nset_cognitive_tokens(DEFAULT_COG)\n\n\ndef tokenize(text: str) -> List[str]:\n    return text.split()\n\n\ndef strip_cognitive(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> List[str]:\n    return [t for t in tokens if not isinstance(t, CogToken)]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# N-gram model\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass NGramModel:\n    \"\"\"Smoothed n-gram model with backoff, trainable offline and online.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, order: int = 3, alpha: float = 0.25):\n        self.order = max(1, int(order))\n        self.alpha = max(1e-9, float(alpha))\n        self.counts = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(self.order)]\n        self.vocab = Counter()\n        self.total_tokens = 0\n\n    def _update(self, tokens: Sequence[str], start: int) -> None:\n        for i in range(start, len(tokens)):\n            target = tokens[i]\n            self.vocab[target] += 1\n            self.total_tokens += 1\n            for ctx_len in range(self.order):\n                if ctx_len > i:\n                    break\n                context = tuple(tokens[i - ctx_len:i]) if ctx_len else ()\n                self.counts[ctx_len][context][target] += 1\n\n    def train(self, text: str, cognitive: bool = True) -> None:\n        raw = tokenize(text)\n        if cognitive:\n            # Weave cognitive tokens in after each sentence so the model\n            # learns what comes before/after them.\n            woven, k = [], 0\n            for tok in raw:\n                woven.append(tok)\n                if tok.endswith(SENTENCE_END):\n                    woven.append(COG_CYCLE[k % len(COG_CYCLE)])\n                    k += 1\n            raw = woven\n        tokens = [\"<bos>\"] * (self.order - 1) + raw + [\"<eos>\"]\n        self._update(tokens, self.order - 1)\n\n    def learn(self, tokens: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Online update from the model's own output (feedback learning).\"\"\"\n        self._update(list(tokens), 1)\n\n    def candidates(self, context_tokens: Sequence[str], limit: int = 80) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:\n        vocab_size = max(1, len(self.vocab))\n        context = list(context_tokens)\n        counter = Counter()\n        for ctx_len in range(min(self.order - 1, len(context)), -1, -1):\n            key = tuple(context[-ctx_len:]) if ctx_len else ()\n            found = self.counts[ctx_len].get(key)\n            if not found:\n                continue\n            weight = 1.0 + 0.7 * ctx_len\n            for token, count in found.items():\n                counter[token] += weight * count\n            if ctx_len >= 1:\n                break\n        if not counter:\n            counter.update(self.vocab)\n        counter.pop(\"<bos>\", None)\n        total = sum(counter.values())\n        ranked = []\n        for token, count in counter.items():\n            prob = (count + self.alpha) / (total + self.alpha * vocab_size)\n            ranked.append((token, math.log(max(prob, 1e-12))))\n        ranked.sort(key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\n        return ranked[:max(1, limit)]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Non-isomorphic fragments (unchanged in spirit)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass NonIsomorphicFragments:\n    def __init__(self, seed: int = 17):\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        self.w_context = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 3))\n        self.w_word = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 4))\n        self.w_transition = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 2))\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _unit(v: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        n = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\n        return v / n if n > 1e-12 else np.zeros_like(v)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _hash_features(token: str, width: int) -> np.ndarray:\n        raw = token.lower().encode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\")\n        vals = np.zeros(width, dtype=float)\n        if not raw:\n            return vals\n        for i, byte in enumerate(raw):\n            vals[i % width] += ((byte % 31) - 15) / 15.0\n            vals[(i * 3 + 1) % width] += ((byte % 17) - 8) / 8.0\n        vals /= max(1, len(raw))\n        vals[0] += min(len(raw), 20) / 20.0\n        vals[1] += sum(chr(b).isalpha() for b in raw) / max(1, len(raw))\n        return np.tanh(vals)\n\n    def features(self, context, token, logp, rank):\n        recent = list(context[-4:])\n        ctx_vec = np.zeros(5, dtype=float)\n        if recent:\n            for i, word in enumerate(recent):\n                f = self._hash_features(word, 5)\n                ctx_vec += f * (0.65 ** (len(recent) - i - 1))\n            ctx_vec /= max(1, len(recent))\n        word_vec = self._hash_features(token, 5)\n        transition_vec = np.array([\n            np.tanh(logp),\n            1.0 / (1.0 + rank),\n            1.0 if token[:1].isupper() else 0.0,\n            1.0 if token in COGNITIVE else 0.0,  # cognitive tokens are visible to the fragments\n            min(len(token), 24) / 24.0,\n        ], dtype=float)\n        g1 = np.tanh(ctx_vec @ self.w_context)\n        g2 = np.tanh(word_vec @ self.w_word)\n        g3 = np.tanh(transition_vec @ self.w_transition)\n        return g1, g2, g3\n\n    def score(self, context, token, logp, rank, lam) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n        g1, g2, g3 = self.features(context, token, logp, rank)\n        summaries = np.array([np.linalg.norm(g1), np.linalg.norm(g2), np.linalg.norm(g3)])\n        mean = float(np.mean(summaries))\n        spread = float(np.std(summaries) / (mean + 1e-9))\n        consistency = float(np.clip(0.55 * spread + 0.45 * (1.0 - mean), 0.0, 1.0))\n\n        ref = self._unit(np.array([np.mean(g1), np.mean(g2), np.mean(g3), np.tanh(logp)]))\n        cand = self._unit(np.array([g1[0], g2[0], g3[0], np.tanh(logp + 0.1 * rank)]))\n        alignment = (float(np.dot(ref, cand)) + 1.0) / 2.0\n\n        fragment_score = 1.6 * alignment - 1.15 * consistency\n        total = (1.0 - lam) * (0.75 * logp + 0.25 * fragment_score) \\\n            + lam * (1.25 * logp + 0.85 * fragment_score)\n        return total, consistency\n\n\ndef adiabatic_lambda(step: int, total_steps: int) -> float:\n    u = min(1.0, max(0.0, step / max(1, total_steps - 1)))\n    return 3.0 * u * u - 2.0 * u * u * u\n\n\ndef softmax(values: Sequence[float], temperature: float = 1.0) -> np.ndarray:\n    temp = max(1e-6, float(temperature))\n    arr = np.asarray(values, dtype=float) / temp\n    arr -= np.max(arr)\n    exp = np.exp(np.clip(arr, -60, 60))\n    return exp / max(float(exp.sum()), 1e-12)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Cybernetic controller (sensor -> comparator -> actuator)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass Controller:\n    def __init__(self, temperature: float, rep_limit: float = 0.5, logp_floor: float = -4.5):\n        self.temperature = temperature\n        self.rep_limit = rep_limit\n        self.logp_floor = logp_floor\n        self.k = 0\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def repetition(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> float:\n        words = strip_cognitive(tokens)\n        if len(words) < 2:\n            return 0.0\n        return 1.0 - len(set(words)) / len(words)\n\n    def update(self, chunk: Sequence[str], mean_logp: float) -> Tuple[str, float]:\n        \"\"\"Return (cognitive token to emit, repetition measure).\"\"\"\n        rep = self.repetition(chunk)\n        if rep > self.rep_limit:\n            cog = COG_DIVERGE\n            self.temperature *= 1.15\n        elif mean_logp < self.logp_floor:\n            cog = COG_CONVERGE\n            self.temperature *= 0.9\n        else:\n            cog = COG_CYCLE[self.k % len(COG_CYCLE)]\n            self.k += 1\n        self.temperature = float(np.clip(self.temperature, 0.3, 1.6))\n        return cog, rep\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Candidate:\n    token: str\n    base_logp: float\n    score: float\n    consistency: float\n    probability: float = 0.0\n\n\ndef generate_chunk(model, fragments, context, n, step0, total, beam_size, tau, temperature, rng,\n                   stop_on_cog=False):\n    \"\"\"Generate up to n tokens after `context`.\n\n    Returns (new_tokens, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted_cog). With stop_on_cog the\n    chunk ends the moment the MODEL emits a cognitive token (returned in\n    emitted_cog, not appended to new_tokens).\n    \"\"\"\n    ctx = list(context)\n    new, logps, hit_eos, emitted = [], [], False, None\n    for i in range(n):\n        lam = adiabatic_lambda(step0 + i, total)\n        ranked = model.candidates(ctx, limit=max(40, beam_size * 8))\n        scored: List[Candidate] = []\n        for rank, (token, logp) in enumerate(ranked):\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, rank, lam)\n            if consistency <= tau:\n                scored.append(Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency))\n        if not scored:\n            token, logp = ranked[0]\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, 0, lam)\n            scored = [Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency)]\n\n        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c.score, reverse=True)\n        beam = scored[:max(1, beam_size)]\n        probs = softmax([c.score for c in beam], temperature)\n        chosen = beam[0] if temperature <= 0.01 else rng.choices(beam, weights=probs, k=1)[0]\n\n        if chosen.token == \"<eos>\":\n            hit_eos = True\n            break\n        if stop_on_cog and chosen.token in COGNITIVE:\n            emitted = chosen.token\n            logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\n            break\n        new.append(chosen.token)\n        ctx.append(chosen.token)\n        logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\n    mean_logp = float(np.mean(logps)) if logps else 0.0\n    return new, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted\n\n\ndef cybernetic_run(model, prompt, cycles, chunk, chunks_per_cycle, window, beam_size, tau,\n                   temperature, seed, learn, trace):\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(seed)\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\n\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\"The\"]\n    full = [COG_START] + seed_tokens          # everything produced so far\n    context = list(full)                      # what the model sees this cycle\n    total = max(1, cycles * chunks_per_cycle * chunk)\n    step = 0\n\n    for c in range(cycles):\n        for k in range(chunks_per_cycle):\n            new, mean_logp, hit_eos, _ = generate_chunk(\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, step, total,\n                beam_size, tau, controller.temperature, rng)\n            step += chunk\n            cog, rep = controller.update(new, mean_logp)\n\n            if trace:\n                print(f\"[cycle {c+1}/{cycles} chunk {k+1}] tokens={len(new)} \"\n                      f\"mean_logp={mean_logp:.2f} rep={rep:.2f} \"\n                      f\"-> {cog} (T={controller.temperature:.2f})\")\n\n            # Feedback learning: only from healthy output, to avoid reinforcing loops.\n            if learn and new and rep <= controller.rep_limit:\n                model.learn(context[-(model.order - 1):] + new + [cog])\n\n            context += new + [cog]\n            full += new + [cog]\n            if hit_eos:\n                break\n\n        # Pipe output back to input: new prompt begins with a cognitive token.\n        tail = full[-window:]\n        context = [COG_INTEGRATE] + tail\n        full.append(COG_INTEGRATE)\n\n    return full\n\n\ndef stacked_run(model, prompt, target_depth, chunk, window, beam_size, tau, temperature, seed,\n                learn, max_retries, strict, trace):\n    \"\"\"\n    Keep generating until cognitive tokens stack up in the correct order.\n\n    The model must itself emit the next expected cognitive token\n    (the order defined in COG_CYCLE, repeating) after a chunk of\n    real content. A wrong or missing token rejects the chunk and it is\n    regenerated (temperature creeps up on each retry). Accepted chunks are\n    pushed onto the stack, which only ever grows (monotonic), and are learned\n    online so the model gets better at the pattern as it goes.\n\n    After `max_retries` misses the expected token is forced in (flagged), unless\n    `strict` is set, in which case it keeps trying until the attempt cap.\n    \"\"\"\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(seed)\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\n\n    full = [COG_START] + (tokenize(prompt) or [\"The\"])\n    context = list(full)\n    stack: List[str] = []\n    forced = 0\n    attempts = 0\n    max_attempts = target_depth * (200 if strict else max_retries + 1)\n\n    while len(stack) < target_depth and attempts < max_attempts:\n        expected = COG_CYCLE[len(stack) % len(COG_CYCLE)]\n        retries = 0\n        accepted, was_forced = False, False\n        while attempts < max_attempts:\n            temp = float(np.clip(controller.temperature * (1.0 + 0.1 * retries), 0.3, 1.8))\n            new, mlp, eos, emitted = generate_chunk(\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, len(stack) * chunk,\n                target_depth * chunk, beam_size, tau, temp, rng, stop_on_cog=True)\n            attempts += 1\n            ok = emitted == expected and len(new) > 0\n            msg = (f\"depth {len(stack)}/{target_depth} attempt {attempts} \"\n                   f\"expected {expected} got {emitted or 'none'} \"\n                   f\"{'OK' if ok else 'retry'} (T={temp:.2f}, forced={forced})\")\n            if trace:\n                print(msg, file=sys.stderr)\n            else:\n                print(\"\\r\" + msg.ljust(78), end=\"\", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\n            if ok:\n                accepted = True\n                break\n            retries += 1\n            if retries > max_retries and not strict:\n                was_forced = True\n                break\n        if not (accepted or was_forced):\n            break  # attempt cap hit in strict mode\n\n        if was_forced:\n            forced += 1\n        stack.append(expected)\n        context += new + [expected]\n        full += new + [expected]\n        if new:\n            controller.update(new, mlp)\n        if accepted and learn:\n            model.learn(context[-(model.order - 1) - len(new) - 1:])\n\n        # Pipe output back to input at the end of each full cognitive cycle.\n        if len(stack) % PIPE_EVERY == 0:\n            context = [COG_INTEGRATE] + full[-window:]\n            full.append(COG_INTEGRATE)\n\n    if not trace:\n        print(file=sys.stderr)\n    monotonic = all(stack[i] == COG_CYCLE[i % len(COG_CYCLE)] for i in range(len(stack)))\n    stats = dict(depth=len(stack), target=target_depth, attempts=attempts,\n                 forced=forced, monotonic=monotonic)\n    return full, stats\n\n\ndef detokenize(tokens: Sequence[str], hide_cog: bool) -> str:\n    return \" \".join(strip_cognitive(tokens) if hide_cog else tokens)\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Cybernetic feedback-loop n-gram generator.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"corpus\", nargs=\"?\", help=\"UTF-8 text corpus file (asked for if omitted).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--prompt\", help=\"Initial prompt. If omitted you are asked each round.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--cycles\", type=int, default=4, help=\"Output->input feedback cycles per prompt.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--chunk\", type=int, default=20, help=\"Tokens per chunk between cognitive tokens.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--chunks-per-cycle\", type=int, default=3)\n    p.add_argument(\"--window\", type=int, default=40, help=\"Tokens of output piped back as the next prompt.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--order\", type=int, default=3)\n    p.add_argument(\"--alpha\", type=float, default=0.25)\n    p.add_argument(\"--beam\", type=int, default=8)\n    p.add_argument(\"--tau\", type=float, default=0.65)\n    p.add_argument(\"--temperature\", type=float, default=0.85)\n    p.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=7)\n    p.add_argument(\"--stack-target\", type=int, default=25,\n                   help=\"Keep going until this many cognitive tokens have stacked in order (0 = old fixed-cycle mode).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--max-retries\", type=int, default=25, help=\"Rejected chunks allowed per stack slot before forcing.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--strict\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Never force a token; retry until the attempt cap.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--no-learn\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Disable online learning from own output.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--show-cog\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Show cognitive tokens in printed text (hidden by default).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--trace\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Print controller diagnostics.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--save\", help=\"Append output to this text file.\")\n    args = p.parse_args()\n\n    corpus_name = args.corpus or input(\"Filename: \")\n    path = Path(corpus_name)\n    if not path.is_file():\n        p.error(f\"Corpus file not found: {path}\")\n    try:\n        corpus_text = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\n    except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n        p.error(f\"Could not decode corpus as UTF-8: {exc}\")\n    if not tokenize(corpus_text):\n        p.error(\"Corpus contains no tokens.\")\n\n    set_cognitive_tokens(select_cognitive_tokens(corpus_text, args.seed))\n    print(\"cognitive tokens (from dataset): \" + \" \".join(COG_CYCLE)\n          + f\" | diverge={COG_DIVERGE} converge={COG_CONVERGE}\"\n          f\" integrate={COG_INTEGRATE} start={COG_START}\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\n    model.train(corpus_text, cognitive=True)\n\n    first = True\n    while True:\n        try:\n            prompt = args.prompt if (args.prompt and first) else input(\"USER: \")\n        except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):\n            print()\n            break\n        first = False\n\n        tau = float(np.clip(args.tau, 0.0, 1.0))\n        temp = max(0.0, args.temperature)\n        if args.stack_target > 0:\n            full, stats = stacked_run(\n                model, prompt, target_depth=args.stack_target, chunk=args.chunk,\n                window=args.window, beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp,\n                seed=args.seed, learn=not args.no_learn,\n                max_retries=args.max_retries, strict=args.strict, trace=args.trace)\n            print(f\"\\n[stack] depth {stats['depth']}/{stats['target']}  attempts {stats['attempts']}  \"\n                  f\"forced {stats['forced']}  monotonic order verified: {stats['monotonic']}\")\n        else:\n            full = cybernetic_run(\n                model, prompt, cycles=args.cycles, chunk=args.chunk,\n                chunks_per_cycle=args.chunks_per_cycle, window=args.window,\n                beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp, seed=args.seed,\n                learn=not args.no_learn, trace=args.trace)\n\n        text = detokenize(full, hide_cog=not args.show_cog)\n        print(\"\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\")\n        print(text)\n        print()\n        if args.save:\n            with open(args.save, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n                fh.write(text + \"\\n\\n\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}], "files": [{"file_uuid": "cd8457d3-14d3-540e-bb87-5d0c81197166", "file_name": ""}], "parent_message_uuid": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000"}, {"uuid": "01a13c72-75a7-7a20-9229-9bb8e253c4e4", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI renamed \"cog\" to \"cot\" throughout `cybernetic_textgen.py`. I read \"cog\" as short for \"cognitive\", so \"cognitive tokens\" are now \"CoT tokens (chain-of-thought markers)\" in the docs and messages. I didn't run it.\n\n- **Classes and constants:** `CogToken` is now `CotToken`. `COG_CYCLE`, `COG_DIVERGE`, `COG_CONVERGE`, `COG_INTEGRATE`, `COG_START`, `COG_COUNT` and `DEFAULT_COG` all use the `COT_` prefix. The `COGNITIVE` set is now `COT`.\n- **Functions:** `set_cognitive_tokens`, `select_cognitive_tokens` and `strip_cognitive` are now `set_cot_tokens`, `select_cot_tokens` and `strip_cot`.\n- **Parameters and variables:** `cog` is now `cot`, `emitted_cog` is `emitted_cot`, `stop_on_cog` is `stop_on_cot`, `hide_cog` is `hide_cot`, and `train(..., cognitive=)` is `train(..., cot=)`.\n- **CLI flag:** `--show-cog` is now `--show-cot`. Any scripts that call the old flag will need updating.\n\nThe 29 fallback words in `DEFAULT_COT` (simulate, recall, and so on) are unchanged.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:04:57.931040Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:05:04.388893Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Renaming identifiers from \"cog\" to \"cot\" throughout the code."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:05:04.388949Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:05:43.423541Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01DwzgXMGgzHmudmqNJP3nNU", "name": "create_file", "input": {"description": "Cybernetic text generator with cog renamed to cot throughout", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py", "file_text": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nCybernetic non-isomorphic adiabatic text generator\n==================================================\n\nSame n-gram + non-isomorphic fragment scoring as before, now wrapped in a\nclosed feedback loop:\n\n  1. Generate a chunk of tokens.\n  2. MEASURE it (repetition, mean log-probability)         -> sensor\n  3. Pick a CoT TOKEN from that measurement                -> comparator\n  4. Insert the CoT token after the chunk and adjust\n     temperature (negative feedback)                        -> actuator\n  5. At the end of a cycle, pipe the output back in as the next prompt, with a\n     CoT token at the start, and repeat.\n\nThe model \"understands\" CoT tokens because they are\n  - woven into the training corpus at sentence boundaries, and\n  - learned online from the model's own (non-degenerate) output.\n\nCoT tokens (chain-of-thought markers):\n  Taken from the dataset itself: the 29 most frequent 4+ letter words in the\n  corpus, shuffled (non-monotonic order). 25 form the required stack order; the\n  other four act as diverge (raise temperature), converge (lower temperature),\n  integrate (start of every piped-back prompt) and start. Inserted markers are\n  CotToken objects, so hiding them never removes the same word from ordinary text.\n\nExamples:\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --cycles 5 --chunk 20\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --prompt \"The machine\" --trace\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --show-cot --no-learn\n\nOnly dependency: NumPy\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport math\nimport random\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import List, Sequence, Tuple\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# CoT tokens\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass CotToken(str):\n    \"\"\"A CoT marker inserted by the loop. It is a str, but isinstance() tells it\n    apart from the same word appearing as ordinary text, so hiding markers never\n    deletes real words from the output.\"\"\"\n\n\n# Fallback names, used only if the corpus has too few distinct words.\nDEFAULT_COT = [\n    \"simulate\", \"recall\", \"correct\", \"imagine\", \"decide\",\n    \"observe\", \"verify\", \"associate\", \"plan\", \"anticipate\",\n    \"reflect\", \"abstract\", \"act\", \"question\", \"compare\",\n    \"adapt\", \"predict\", \"summarize\", \"monitor\", \"infer\",\n    \"consolidate\", \"attend\", \"evaluate\", \"prioritize\", \"hypothesize\",\n    \"diverge\", \"converge\", \"integrate\", \"observe\",\n]\nCOT_COUNT = 29  # 25 cycle tokens + diverge + converge + integrate + start\nPIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens\nSENTENCE_END = (\".\", \"!\", \"?\")\n\nCOT_CYCLE: List[str] = []\nCOT_DIVERGE = COT_CONVERGE = COT_INTEGRATE = COT_START = CotToken(\"\")\nCOT: set = set()\n\n_STOP = {\n    \"that\", \"with\", \"have\", \"from\", \"this\", \"they\", \"were\", \"been\", \"will\", \"would\", \"there\",\n    \"their\", \"what\", \"when\", \"which\", \"your\", \"them\", \"then\", \"than\", \"into\", \"only\", \"also\",\n    \"some\", \"such\", \"more\", \"most\", \"other\", \"about\", \"could\", \"should\", \"these\", \"those\",\n}\n\n\ndef set_cot_tokens(words: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Install the CoT vocabulary: 25 cycle tokens, then diverge, converge,\n    integrate, start.\"\"\"\n    global COT_CYCLE, COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START, COT\n    toks = [CotToken(w) for w in words]\n    COT_CYCLE = toks[:25]\n    COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START = toks[25:29]\n    COT = {str(t) for t in toks}\n\n\ndef select_cot_tokens(text: str, seed: int, count: int = COT_COUNT) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Pick CoT tokens FROM THE DATASET: the most frequent alphabetic words of\n    4+ letters (skipping common function words), shuffled so the required order is\n    non-monotonic.\"\"\"\n    counts = Counter(tokenize(text))\n    pool = [(w, c) for w, c in counts.items()\n            if w.isalpha() and len(w) >= 4 and w.lower() not in _STOP]\n    pool.sort(key=lambda wc: (-wc[1], wc[0]))\n    words, seen = [], set()\n    for w, _ in pool:\n        if w.lower() not in seen:\n            seen.add(w.lower())\n            words.append(w)\n        if len(words) >= count:\n            break\n    random.Random(seed).shuffle(words)\n    for d in DEFAULT_COT:  # top up from fallback names if the corpus is tiny\n        if len(words) >= count:\n            break\n        if d.lower() not in seen:\n            seen.add(d.lower())\n            words.append(d)\n    return words\n\n\nset_cot_tokens(DEFAULT_COT)\n\n\ndef tokenize(text: str) -> List[str]:\n    return text.split()\n\n\ndef strip_cot(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> List[str]:\n    return [t for t in tokens if not isinstance(t, CotToken)]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# N-gram model\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass NGramModel:\n    \"\"\"Smoothed n-gram model with backoff, trainable offline and online.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, order: int = 3, alpha: float = 0.25):\n        self.order = max(1, int(order))\n        self.alpha = max(1e-9, float(alpha))\n        self.counts = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(self.order)]\n        self.vocab = Counter()\n        self.total_tokens = 0\n\n    def _update(self, tokens: Sequence[str], start: int) -> None:\n        for i in range(start, len(tokens)):\n            target = tokens[i]\n            self.vocab[target] += 1\n            self.total_tokens += 1\n            for ctx_len in range(self.order):\n                if ctx_len > i:\n                    break\n                context = tuple(tokens[i - ctx_len:i]) if ctx_len else ()\n                self.counts[ctx_len][context][target] += 1\n\n    def train(self, text: str, cot: bool = True) -> None:\n        raw = tokenize(text)\n        if cot:\n            # Weave CoT tokens in after each sentence so the model\n            # learns what comes before/after them.\n            woven, k = [], 0\n            for tok in raw:\n                woven.append(tok)\n                if tok.endswith(SENTENCE_END):\n                    woven.append(COT_CYCLE[k % len(COT_CYCLE)])\n                    k += 1\n            raw = woven\n        tokens = [\"<bos>\"] * (self.order - 1) + raw + [\"<eos>\"]\n        self._update(tokens, self.order - 1)\n\n    def learn(self, tokens: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Online update from the model's own output (feedback learning).\"\"\"\n        self._update(list(tokens), 1)\n\n    def candidates(self, context_tokens: Sequence[str], limit: int = 80) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:\n        vocab_size = max(1, len(self.vocab))\n        context = list(context_tokens)\n        counter = Counter()\n        for ctx_len in range(min(self.order - 1, len(context)), -1, -1):\n            key = tuple(context[-ctx_len:]) if ctx_len else ()\n            found = self.counts[ctx_len].get(key)\n            if not found:\n                continue\n            weight = 1.0 + 0.7 * ctx_len\n            for token, count in found.items():\n                counter[token] += weight * count\n            if ctx_len >= 1:\n                break\n        if not counter:\n            counter.update(self.vocab)\n        counter.pop(\"<bos>\", None)\n        total = sum(counter.values())\n        ranked = []\n        for token, count in counter.items():\n            prob = (count + self.alpha) / (total + self.alpha * vocab_size)\n            ranked.append((token, math.log(max(prob, 1e-12))))\n        ranked.sort(key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\n        return ranked[:max(1, limit)]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Non-isomorphic fragments (unchanged in spirit)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass NonIsomorphicFragments:\n    def __init__(self, seed: int = 17):\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        self.w_context = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 3))\n        self.w_word = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 4))\n        self.w_transition = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 2))\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _unit(v: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        n = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\n        return v / n if n > 1e-12 else np.zeros_like(v)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _hash_features(token: str, width: int) -> np.ndarray:\n        raw = token.lower().encode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\")\n        vals = np.zeros(width, dtype=float)\n        if not raw:\n            return vals\n        for i, byte in enumerate(raw):\n            vals[i % width] += ((byte % 31) - 15) / 15.0\n            vals[(i * 3 + 1) % width] += ((byte % 17) - 8) / 8.0\n        vals /= max(1, len(raw))\n        vals[0] += min(len(raw), 20) / 20.0\n        vals[1] += sum(chr(b).isalpha() for b in raw) / max(1, len(raw))\n        return np.tanh(vals)\n\n    def features(self, context, token, logp, rank):\n        recent = list(context[-4:])\n        ctx_vec = np.zeros(5, dtype=float)\n        if recent:\n            for i, word in enumerate(recent):\n                f = self._hash_features(word, 5)\n                ctx_vec += f * (0.65 ** (len(recent) - i - 1))\n            ctx_vec /= max(1, len(recent))\n        word_vec = self._hash_features(token, 5)\n        transition_vec = np.array([\n            np.tanh(logp),\n            1.0 / (1.0 + rank),\n            1.0 if token[:1].isupper() else 0.0,\n            1.0 if token in COT else 0.0,  # CoT tokens are visible to the fragments\n            min(len(token), 24) / 24.0,\n        ], dtype=float)\n        g1 = np.tanh(ctx_vec @ self.w_context)\n        g2 = np.tanh(word_vec @ self.w_word)\n        g3 = np.tanh(transition_vec @ self.w_transition)\n        return g1, g2, g3\n\n    def score(self, context, token, logp, rank, lam) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n        g1, g2, g3 = self.features(context, token, logp, rank)\n        summaries = np.array([np.linalg.norm(g1), np.linalg.norm(g2), np.linalg.norm(g3)])\n        mean = float(np.mean(summaries))\n        spread = float(np.std(summaries) / (mean + 1e-9))\n        consistency = float(np.clip(0.55 * spread + 0.45 * (1.0 - mean), 0.0, 1.0))\n\n        ref = self._unit(np.array([np.mean(g1), np.mean(g2), np.mean(g3), np.tanh(logp)]))\n        cand = self._unit(np.array([g1[0], g2[0], g3[0], np.tanh(logp + 0.1 * rank)]))\n        alignment = (float(np.dot(ref, cand)) + 1.0) / 2.0\n\n        fragment_score = 1.6 * alignment - 1.15 * consistency\n        total = (1.0 - lam) * (0.75 * logp + 0.25 * fragment_score) \\\n            + lam * (1.25 * logp + 0.85 * fragment_score)\n        return total, consistency\n\n\ndef adiabatic_lambda(step: int, total_steps: int) -> float:\n    u = min(1.0, max(0.0, step / max(1, total_steps - 1)))\n    return 3.0 * u * u - 2.0 * u * u * u\n\n\ndef softmax(values: Sequence[float], temperature: float = 1.0) -> np.ndarray:\n    temp = max(1e-6, float(temperature))\n    arr = np.asarray(values, dtype=float) / temp\n    arr -= np.max(arr)\n    exp = np.exp(np.clip(arr, -60, 60))\n    return exp / max(float(exp.sum()), 1e-12)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Cybernetic controller (sensor -> comparator -> actuator)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass Controller:\n    def __init__(self, temperature: float, rep_limit: float = 0.5, logp_floor: float = -4.5):\n        self.temperature = temperature\n        self.rep_limit = rep_limit\n        self.logp_floor = logp_floor\n        self.k = 0\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def repetition(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> float:\n        words = strip_cot(tokens)\n        if len(words) < 2:\n            return 0.0\n        return 1.0 - len(set(words)) / len(words)\n\n    def update(self, chunk: Sequence[str], mean_logp: float) -> Tuple[str, float]:\n        \"\"\"Return (CoT token to emit, repetition measure).\"\"\"\n        rep = self.repetition(chunk)\n        if rep > self.rep_limit:\n            cot = COT_DIVERGE\n            self.temperature *= 1.15\n        elif mean_logp < self.logp_floor:\n            cot = COT_CONVERGE\n            self.temperature *= 0.9\n        else:\n            cot = COT_CYCLE[self.k % len(COT_CYCLE)]\n            self.k += 1\n        self.temperature = float(np.clip(self.temperature, 0.3, 1.6))\n        return cot, rep\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Candidate:\n    token: str\n    base_logp: float\n    score: float\n    consistency: float\n    probability: float = 0.0\n\n\ndef generate_chunk(model, fragments, context, n, step0, total, beam_size, tau, temperature, rng,\n                   stop_on_cot=False):\n    \"\"\"Generate up to n tokens after `context`.\n\n    Returns (new_tokens, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted_cot). With stop_on_cot the\n    chunk ends the moment the MODEL emits a CoT token (returned in\n    emitted_cot, not appended to new_tokens).\n    \"\"\"\n    ctx = list(context)\n    new, logps, hit_eos, emitted = [], [], False, None\n    for i in range(n):\n        lam = adiabatic_lambda(step0 + i, total)\n        ranked = model.candidates(ctx, limit=max(40, beam_size * 8))\n        scored: List[Candidate] = []\n        for rank, (token, logp) in enumerate(ranked):\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, rank, lam)\n            if consistency <= tau:\n                scored.append(Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency))\n        if not scored:\n            token, logp = ranked[0]\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, 0, lam)\n            scored = [Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency)]\n\n        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c.score, reverse=True)\n        beam = scored[:max(1, beam_size)]\n        probs = softmax([c.score for c in beam], temperature)\n        chosen = beam[0] if temperature <= 0.01 else rng.choices(beam, weights=probs, k=1)[0]\n\n        if chosen.token == \"<eos>\":\n            hit_eos = True\n            break\n        if stop_on_cot and chosen.token in COT:\n            emitted = chosen.token\n            logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\n            break\n        new.append(chosen.token)\n        ctx.append(chosen.token)\n        logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\n    mean_logp = float(np.mean(logps)) if logps else 0.0\n    return new, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted\n\n\ndef cybernetic_run(model, prompt, cycles, chunk, chunks_per_cycle, window, beam_size, tau,\n                   temperature, seed, learn, trace):\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(seed)\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\n\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\"The\"]\n    full = [COT_START] + seed_tokens          # everything produced so far\n    context = list(full)                      # what the model sees this cycle\n    total = max(1, cycles * chunks_per_cycle * chunk)\n    step = 0\n\n    for c in range(cycles):\n        for k in range(chunks_per_cycle):\n            new, mean_logp, hit_eos, _ = generate_chunk(\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, step, total,\n                beam_size, tau, controller.temperature, rng)\n            step += chunk\n            cot, rep = controller.update(new, mean_logp)\n\n            if trace:\n                print(f\"[cycle {c+1}/{cycles} chunk {k+1}] tokens={len(new)} \"\n                      f\"mean_logp={mean_logp:.2f} rep={rep:.2f} \"\n                      f\"-> {cot} (T={controller.temperature:.2f})\")\n\n            # Feedback learning: only from healthy output, to avoid reinforcing loops.\n            if learn and new and rep <= controller.rep_limit:\n                model.learn(context[-(model.order - 1):] + new + [cot])\n\n            context += new + [cot]\n            full += new + [cot]\n            if hit_eos:\n                break\n\n        # Pipe output back to input: new prompt begins with a CoT token.\n        tail = full[-window:]\n        context = [COT_INTEGRATE] + tail\n        full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\n\n    return full\n\n\ndef stacked_run(model, prompt, target_depth, chunk, window, beam_size, tau, temperature, seed,\n                learn, max_retries, strict, trace):\n    \"\"\"\n    Keep generating until CoT tokens stack up in the correct order.\n\n    The model must itself emit the next expected CoT token\n    (the order defined in COT_CYCLE, repeating) after a chunk of\n    real content. A wrong or missing token rejects the chunk and it is\n    regenerated (temperature creeps up on each retry). Accepted chunks are\n    pushed onto the stack, which only ever grows (monotonic), and are learned\n    online so the model gets better at the pattern as it goes.\n\n    After `max_retries` misses the expected token is forced in (flagged), unless\n    `strict` is set, in which case it keeps trying until the attempt cap.\n    \"\"\"\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(seed)\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\n\n    full = [COT_START] + (tokenize(prompt) or [\"The\"])\n    context = list(full)\n    stack: List[str] = []\n    forced = 0\n    attempts = 0\n    max_attempts = target_depth * (200 if strict else max_retries + 1)\n\n    while len(stack) < target_depth and attempts < max_attempts:\n        expected = COT_CYCLE[len(stack) % len(COT_CYCLE)]\n        retries = 0\n        accepted, was_forced = False, False\n        while attempts < max_attempts:\n            temp = float(np.clip(controller.temperature * (1.0 + 0.1 * retries), 0.3, 1.8))\n            new, mlp, eos, emitted = generate_chunk(\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, len(stack) * chunk,\n                target_depth * chunk, beam_size, tau, temp, rng, stop_on_cot=True)\n            attempts += 1\n            ok = emitted == expected and len(new) > 0\n            msg = (f\"depth {len(stack)}/{target_depth} attempt {attempts} \"\n                   f\"expected {expected} got {emitted or 'none'} \"\n                   f\"{'OK' if ok else 'retry'} (T={temp:.2f}, forced={forced})\")\n            if trace:\n                print(msg, file=sys.stderr)\n            else:\n                print(\"\\r\" + msg.ljust(78), end=\"\", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\n            if ok:\n                accepted = True\n                break\n            retries += 1\n            if retries > max_retries and not strict:\n                was_forced = True\n                break\n        if not (accepted or was_forced):\n            break  # attempt cap hit in strict mode\n\n        if was_forced:\n            forced += 1\n        stack.append(expected)\n        context += new + [expected]\n        full += new + [expected]\n        if new:\n            controller.update(new, mlp)\n        if accepted and learn:\n            model.learn(context[-(model.order - 1) - len(new) - 1:])\n\n        # Pipe output back to input at the end of each full CoT cycle.\n        if len(stack) % PIPE_EVERY == 0:\n            context = [COT_INTEGRATE] + full[-window:]\n            full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\n\n    if not trace:\n        print(file=sys.stderr)\n    monotonic = all(stack[i] == COT_CYCLE[i % len(COT_CYCLE)] for i in range(len(stack)))\n    stats = dict(depth=len(stack), target=target_depth, attempts=attempts,\n                 forced=forced, monotonic=monotonic)\n    return full, stats\n\n\ndef detokenize(tokens: Sequence[str], hide_cot: bool) -> str:\n    return \" \".join(strip_cot(tokens) if hide_cot else tokens)\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Cybernetic feedback-loop n-gram generator.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"corpus\", nargs=\"?\", help=\"UTF-8 text corpus file (asked for if omitted).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--prompt\", help=\"Initial prompt. If omitted you are asked each round.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--cycles\", type=int, default=4, help=\"Output->input feedback cycles per prompt.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--chunk\", type=int, default=20, help=\"Tokens per chunk between CoT tokens.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--chunks-per-cycle\", type=int, default=3)\n    p.add_argument(\"--window\", type=int, default=40, help=\"Tokens of output piped back as the next prompt.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--order\", type=int, default=3)\n    p.add_argument(\"--alpha\", type=float, default=0.25)\n    p.add_argument(\"--beam\", type=int, default=8)\n    p.add_argument(\"--tau\", type=float, default=0.65)\n    p.add_argument(\"--temperature\", type=float, default=0.85)\n    p.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=7)\n    p.add_argument(\"--stack-target\", type=int, default=25,\n                   help=\"Keep going until this many CoT tokens have stacked in order (0 = old fixed-cycle mode).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--max-retries\", type=int, default=25, help=\"Rejected chunks allowed per stack slot before forcing.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--strict\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Never force a token; retry until the attempt cap.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--no-learn\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Disable online learning from own output.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--show-cot\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Show CoT tokens in printed text (hidden by default).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--trace\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Print controller diagnostics.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--save\", help=\"Append output to this text file.\")\n    args = p.parse_args()\n\n    corpus_name = args.corpus or input(\"Filename: \")\n    path = Path(corpus_name)\n    if not path.is_file():\n        p.error(f\"Corpus file not found: {path}\")\n    try:\n        corpus_text = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\n    except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n        p.error(f\"Could not decode corpus as UTF-8: {exc}\")\n    if not tokenize(corpus_text):\n        p.error(\"Corpus contains no tokens.\")\n\n    set_cot_tokens(select_cot_tokens(corpus_text, args.seed))\n    print(\"CoT tokens (from dataset): \" + \" \".join(COT_CYCLE)\n          + f\" | diverge={COT_DIVERGE} converge={COT_CONVERGE}\"\n          f\" integrate={COT_INTEGRATE} start={COT_START}\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\n    model.train(corpus_text, cot=True)\n\n    first = True\n    while True:\n        try:\n            prompt = args.prompt if (args.prompt and first) else input(\"USER: \")\n        except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):\n            print()\n            break\n        first = False\n\n        tau = float(np.clip(args.tau, 0.0, 1.0))\n        temp = max(0.0, args.temperature)\n        if args.stack_target > 0:\n            full, stats = stacked_run(\n                model, prompt, target_depth=args.stack_target, chunk=args.chunk,\n                window=args.window, beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp,\n                seed=args.seed, learn=not args.no_learn,\n                max_retries=args.max_retries, strict=args.strict, trace=args.trace)\n            print(f\"\\n[stack] depth {stats['depth']}/{stats['target']}  attempts {stats['attempts']}  \"\n                  f\"forced {stats['forced']}  monotonic order verified: {stats['monotonic']}\")\n        else:\n            full = cybernetic_run(\n                model, prompt, cycles=args.cycles, chunk=args.chunk,\n                chunks_per_cycle=args.chunks_per_cycle, window=args.window,\n                beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp, seed=args.seed,\n                learn=not args.no_learn, trace=args.trace)\n\n        text = detokenize(full, hide_cot=not args.show_cot)\n        print(\"\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\")\n        print(text)\n        print()\n        if args.save:\n            with open(args.save, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n                fh.write(text + \"\\n\\n\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}, "message": "Cybernetic text generator with cog renamed to cot throughout", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nCybernetic non-isomorphic adiabatic text generator\\n==================================================\\n\\nSame n-gram + non-isomorphic fragment scoring as before, now wrapped in a\\nclosed feedback loop:\\n\\n  1. Generate a chunk of tokens.\\n  2. MEASURE it (repetition, mean log-probability)         -> sensor\\n  3. Pick a CoT TOKEN from that measurement                -> comparator\\n  4. Insert the CoT token after the chunk and adjust\\n     temperature (negative feedback)                        -> actuator\\n  5. At the end of a cycle, pipe the output back in as the next prompt, with a\\n     CoT token at the start, and repeat.\\n\\nThe model \\\"understands\\\" CoT tokens because they are\\n  - woven into the training corpus at sentence boundaries, and\\n  - learned online from the model's own (non-degenerate) output.\\n\\nCoT tokens (chain-of-thought markers):\\n  Taken from the dataset itself: the 29 most frequent 4+ letter words in the\\n  corpus, shuffled (non-monotonic order). 25 form the required stack order; the\\n  other four act as diverge (raise temperature), converge (lower temperature),\\n  integrate (start of every piped-back prompt) and start. Inserted markers are\\n  CotToken objects, so hiding them never removes the same word from ordinary text.\\n\\nExamples:\\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --cycles 5 --chunk 20\\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" --trace\\n  python cybernetic_textgen.py corpus.txt --show-cot --no-learn\\n\\nOnly dependency: NumPy\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport argparse\\nimport math\\nimport random\\nimport sys\\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import List, Sequence, Tuple\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# CoT tokens\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass CotToken(str):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A CoT marker inserted by the loop. It is a str, but isinstance() tells it\\n    apart from the same word appearing as ordinary text, so hiding markers never\\n    deletes real words from the output.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\n# Fallback names, used only if the corpus has too few distinct words.\\nDEFAULT_COT = [\\n    \\\"simulate\\\", \\\"recall\\\", \\\"correct\\\", \\\"imagine\\\", \\\"decide\\\",\\n    \\\"observe\\\", \\\"verify\\\", \\\"associate\\\", \\\"plan\\\", \\\"anticipate\\\",\\n    \\\"reflect\\\", \\\"abstract\\\", \\\"act\\\", \\\"question\\\", \\\"compare\\\",\\n    \\\"adapt\\\", \\\"predict\\\", \\\"summarize\\\", \\\"monitor\\\", \\\"infer\\\",\\n    \\\"consolidate\\\", \\\"attend\\\", \\\"evaluate\\\", \\\"prioritize\\\", \\\"hypothesize\\\",\\n    \\\"diverge\\\", \\\"converge\\\", \\\"integrate\\\", \\\"observe\\\",\\n]\\nCOT_COUNT = 29  # 25 cycle tokens + diverge + converge + integrate + start\\nPIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens\\nSENTENCE_END = (\\\".\\\", \\\"!\\\", \\\"?\\\")\\n\\nCOT_CYCLE: List[str] = []\\nCOT_DIVERGE = COT_CONVERGE = COT_INTEGRATE = COT_START = CotToken(\\\"\\\")\\nCOT: set = set()\\n\\n_STOP = {\\n    \\\"that\\\", \\\"with\\\", \\\"have\\\", \\\"from\\\", \\\"this\\\", \\\"they\\\", \\\"were\\\", \\\"been\\\", \\\"will\\\", \\\"would\\\", \\\"there\\\",\\n    \\\"their\\\", \\\"what\\\", \\\"when\\\", \\\"which\\\", \\\"your\\\", \\\"them\\\", \\\"then\\\", \\\"than\\\", \\\"into\\\", \\\"only\\\", \\\"also\\\",\\n    \\\"some\\\", \\\"such\\\", \\\"more\\\", \\\"most\\\", \\\"other\\\", \\\"about\\\", \\\"could\\\", \\\"should\\\", \\\"these\\\", \\\"those\\\",\\n}\\n\\n\\ndef set_cot_tokens(words: Sequence[str]) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Install the CoT vocabulary: 25 cycle tokens, then diverge, converge,\\n    integrate, start.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    global COT_CYCLE, COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START, COT\\n    toks = [CotToken(w) for w in words]\\n    COT_CYCLE = toks[:25]\\n    COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START = toks[25:29]\\n    COT = {str(t) for t in toks}\\n\\n\\ndef select_cot_tokens(text: str, seed: int, count: int = COT_COUNT) -> List[str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pick CoT tokens FROM THE DATASET: the most frequent alphabetic words of\\n    4+ letters (skipping common function words), shuffled so the required order is\\n    non-monotonic.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    counts = Counter(tokenize(text))\\n    pool = [(w, c) for w, c in counts.items()\\n            if w.isalpha() and len(w) >= 4 and w.lower() not in _STOP]\\n    pool.sort(key=lambda wc: (-wc[1], wc[0]))\\n    words, seen = [], set()\\n    for w, _ in pool:\\n        if w.lower() not in seen:\\n            seen.add(w.lower())\\n            words.append(w)\\n        if len(words) >= count:\\n            break\\n    random.Random(seed).shuffle(words)\\n    for d in DEFAULT_COT:  # top up from fallback names if the corpus is tiny\\n        if len(words) >= count:\\n            break\\n        if d.lower() not in seen:\\n            seen.add(d.lower())\\n            words.append(d)\\n    return words\\n\\n\\nset_cot_tokens(DEFAULT_COT)\\n\\n\\ndef tokenize(text: str) -> List[str]:\\n    return text.split()\\n\\n\\ndef strip_cot(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> List[str]:\\n    return [t for t in tokens if not isinstance(t, CotToken)]\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# N-gram model\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass NGramModel:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Smoothed n-gram model with backoff, trainable offline and online.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, order: int = 3, alpha: float = 0.25):\\n        self.order = max(1, int(order))\\n        self.alpha = max(1e-9, float(alpha))\\n        self.counts = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(self.order)]\\n        self.vocab = Counter()\\n        self.total_tokens = 0\\n\\n    def _update(self, tokens: Sequence[str], start: int) -> None:\\n        for i in range(start, len(tokens)):\\n            target = tokens[i]\\n            self.vocab[target] += 1\\n            self.total_tokens += 1\\n            for ctx_len in range(self.order):\\n                if ctx_len > i:\\n                    break\\n                context = tuple(tokens[i - ctx_len:i]) if ctx_len else ()\\n                self.counts[ctx_len][context][target] += 1\\n\\n    def train(self, text: str, cot: bool = True) -> None:\\n        raw = tokenize(text)\\n        if cot:\\n            # Weave CoT tokens in after each sentence so the model\\n            # learns what comes before/after them.\\n            woven, k = [], 0\\n            for tok in raw:\\n                woven.append(tok)\\n                if tok.endswith(SENTENCE_END):\\n                    woven.append(COT_CYCLE[k % len(COT_CYCLE)])\\n                    k += 1\\n            raw = woven\\n        tokens = [\\\"<bos>\\\"] * (self.order - 1) + raw + [\\\"<eos>\\\"]\\n        self._update(tokens, self.order - 1)\\n\\n    def learn(self, tokens: Sequence[str]) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Online update from the model's own output (feedback learning).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self._update(list(tokens), 1)\\n\\n    def candidates(self, context_tokens: Sequence[str], limit: int = 80) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:\\n        vocab_size = max(1, len(self.vocab))\\n        context = list(context_tokens)\\n        counter = Counter()\\n        for ctx_len in range(min(self.order - 1, len(context)), -1, -1):\\n            key = tuple(context[-ctx_len:]) if ctx_len else ()\\n            found = self.counts[ctx_len].get(key)\\n            if not found:\\n                continue\\n            weight = 1.0 + 0.7 * ctx_len\\n            for token, count in found.items():\\n                counter[token] += weight * count\\n            if ctx_len >= 1:\\n                break\\n        if not counter:\\n            counter.update(self.vocab)\\n        counter.pop(\\\"<bos>\\\", None)\\n        total = sum(counter.values())\\n        ranked = []\\n        for token, count in counter.items():\\n            prob = (count + self.alpha) / (total + self.alpha * vocab_size)\\n            ranked.append((token, math.log(max(prob, 1e-12))))\\n        ranked.sort(key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\\n        return ranked[:max(1, limit)]\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Non-isomorphic fragments (unchanged in spirit)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass NonIsomorphicFragments:\\n    def __init__(self, seed: int = 17):\\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n        self.w_context = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 3))\\n        self.w_word = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 4))\\n        self.w_transition = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 2))\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _unit(v: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n        n = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\\n        return v / n if n > 1e-12 else np.zeros_like(v)\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _hash_features(token: str, width: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n        raw = token.lower().encode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"ignore\\\")\\n        vals = np.zeros(width, dtype=float)\\n        if not raw:\\n            return vals\\n        for i, byte in enumerate(raw):\\n            vals[i % width] += ((byte % 31) - 15) / 15.0\\n            vals[(i * 3 + 1) % width] += ((byte % 17) - 8) / 8.0\\n        vals /= max(1, len(raw))\\n        vals[0] += min(len(raw), 20) / 20.0\\n        vals[1] += sum(chr(b).isalpha() for b in raw) / max(1, len(raw))\\n        return np.tanh(vals)\\n\\n    def features(self, context, token, logp, rank):\\n        recent = list(context[-4:])\\n        ctx_vec = np.zeros(5, dtype=float)\\n        if recent:\\n            for i, word in enumerate(recent):\\n                f = self._hash_features(word, 5)\\n                ctx_vec += f * (0.65 ** (len(recent) - i - 1))\\n            ctx_vec /= max(1, len(recent))\\n        word_vec = self._hash_features(token, 5)\\n        transition_vec = np.array([\\n            np.tanh(logp),\\n            1.0 / (1.0 + rank),\\n            1.0 if token[:1].isupper() else 0.0,\\n            1.0 if token in COT else 0.0,  # CoT tokens are visible to the fragments\\n            min(len(token), 24) / 24.0,\\n        ], dtype=float)\\n        g1 = np.tanh(ctx_vec @ self.w_context)\\n        g2 = np.tanh(word_vec @ self.w_word)\\n        g3 = np.tanh(transition_vec @ self.w_transition)\\n        return g1, g2, g3\\n\\n    def score(self, context, token, logp, rank, lam) -> Tuple[float, float]:\\n        g1, g2, g3 = self.features(context, token, logp, rank)\\n        summaries = np.array([np.linalg.norm(g1), np.linalg.norm(g2), np.linalg.norm(g3)])\\n        mean = float(np.mean(summaries))\\n        spread = float(np.std(summaries) / (mean + 1e-9))\\n        consistency = float(np.clip(0.55 * spread + 0.45 * (1.0 - mean), 0.0, 1.0))\\n\\n        ref = self._unit(np.array([np.mean(g1), np.mean(g2), np.mean(g3), np.tanh(logp)]))\\n        cand = self._unit(np.array([g1[0], g2[0], g3[0], np.tanh(logp + 0.1 * rank)]))\\n        alignment = (float(np.dot(ref, cand)) + 1.0) / 2.0\\n\\n        fragment_score = 1.6 * alignment - 1.15 * consistency\\n        total = (1.0 - lam) * (0.75 * logp + 0.25 * fragment_score) \\\\\\n            + lam * (1.25 * logp + 0.85 * fragment_score)\\n        return total, consistency\\n\\n\\ndef adiabatic_lambda(step: int, total_steps: int) -> float:\\n    u = min(1.0, max(0.0, step / max(1, total_steps - 1)))\\n    return 3.0 * u * u - 2.0 * u * u * u\\n\\n\\ndef softmax(values: Sequence[float], temperature: float = 1.0) -> np.ndarray:\\n    temp = max(1e-6, float(temperature))\\n    arr = np.asarray(values, dtype=float) / temp\\n    arr -= np.max(arr)\\n    exp = np.exp(np.clip(arr, -60, 60))\\n    return exp / max(float(exp.sum()), 1e-12)\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Cybernetic controller (sensor -> comparator -> actuator)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass Controller:\\n    def __init__(self, temperature: float, rep_limit: float = 0.5, logp_floor: float = -4.5):\\n        self.temperature = temperature\\n        self.rep_limit = rep_limit\\n        self.logp_floor = logp_floor\\n        self.k = 0\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def repetition(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> float:\\n        words = strip_cot(tokens)\\n        if len(words) < 2:\\n            return 0.0\\n        return 1.0 - len(set(words)) / len(words)\\n\\n    def update(self, chunk: Sequence[str], mean_logp: float) -> Tuple[str, float]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Return (CoT token to emit, repetition measure).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        rep = self.repetition(chunk)\\n        if rep > self.rep_limit:\\n            cot = COT_DIVERGE\\n            self.temperature *= 1.15\\n        elif mean_logp < self.logp_floor:\\n            cot = COT_CONVERGE\\n            self.temperature *= 0.9\\n        else:\\n            cot = COT_CYCLE[self.k % len(COT_CYCLE)]\\n            self.k += 1\\n        self.temperature = float(np.clip(self.temperature, 0.3, 1.6))\\n        return cot, rep\\n\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass Candidate:\\n    token: str\\n    base_logp: float\\n    score: float\\n    consistency: float\\n    probability: float = 0.0\\n\\n\\ndef generate_chunk(model, fragments, context, n, step0, total, beam_size, tau, temperature, rng,\\n                   stop_on_cot=False):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generate up to n tokens after `context`.\\n\\n    Returns (new_tokens, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted_cot). With stop_on_cot the\\n    chunk ends the moment the MODEL emits a CoT token (returned in\\n    emitted_cot, not appended to new_tokens).\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    ctx = list(context)\\n    new, logps, hit_eos, emitted = [], [], False, None\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        lam = adiabatic_lambda(step0 + i, total)\\n        ranked = model.candidates(ctx, limit=max(40, beam_size * 8))\\n        scored: List[Candidate] = []\\n        for rank, (token, logp) in enumerate(ranked):\\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, rank, lam)\\n            if consistency <= tau:\\n                scored.append(Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency))\\n        if not scored:\\n            token, logp = ranked[0]\\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, 0, lam)\\n            scored = [Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency)]\\n\\n        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c.score, reverse=True)\\n        beam = scored[:max(1, beam_size)]\\n        probs = softmax([c.score for c in beam], temperature)\\n        chosen = beam[0] if temperature <= 0.01 else rng.choices(beam, weights=probs, k=1)[0]\\n\\n        if chosen.token == \\\"<eos>\\\":\\n            hit_eos = True\\n            break\\n        if stop_on_cot and chosen.token in COT:\\n            emitted = chosen.token\\n            logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\\n            break\\n        new.append(chosen.token)\\n        ctx.append(chosen.token)\\n        logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\\n    mean_logp = float(np.mean(logps)) if logps else 0.0\\n    return new, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted\\n\\n\\ndef cybernetic_run(model, prompt, cycles, chunk, chunks_per_cycle, window, beam_size, tau,\\n                   temperature, seed, learn, trace):\\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(seed)\\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\\n\\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\\\"The\\\"]\\n    full = [COT_START] + seed_tokens          # everything produced so far\\n    context = list(full)                      # what the model sees this cycle\\n    total = max(1, cycles * chunks_per_cycle * chunk)\\n    step = 0\\n\\n    for c in range(cycles):\\n        for k in range(chunks_per_cycle):\\n            new, mean_logp, hit_eos, _ = generate_chunk(\\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, step, total,\\n                beam_size, tau, controller.temperature, rng)\\n            step += chunk\\n            cot, rep = controller.update(new, mean_logp)\\n\\n            if trace:\\n                print(f\\\"[cycle {c+1}/{cycles} chunk {k+1}] tokens={len(new)} \\\"\\n                      f\\\"mean_logp={mean_logp:.2f} rep={rep:.2f} \\\"\\n                      f\\\"-> {cot} (T={controller.temperature:.2f})\\\")\\n\\n            # Feedback learning: only from healthy output, to avoid reinforcing loops.\\n            if learn and new and rep <= controller.rep_limit:\\n                model.learn(context[-(model.order - 1):] + new + [cot])\\n\\n            context += new + [cot]\\n            full += new + [cot]\\n            if hit_eos:\\n                break\\n\\n        # Pipe output back to input: new prompt begins with a CoT token.\\n        tail = full[-window:]\\n        context = [COT_INTEGRATE] + tail\\n        full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\\n\\n    return full\\n\\n\\ndef stacked_run(model, prompt, target_depth, chunk, window, beam_size, tau, temperature, seed,\\n                learn, max_retries, strict, trace):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Keep generating until CoT tokens stack up in the correct order.\\n\\n    The model must itself emit the next expected CoT token\\n    (the order defined in COT_CYCLE, repeating) after a chunk of\\n    real content. A wrong or missing token rejects the chunk and it is\\n    regenerated (temperature creeps up on each retry). Accepted chunks are\\n    pushed onto the stack, which only ever grows (monotonic), and are learned\\n    online so the model gets better at the pattern as it goes.\\n\\n    After `max_retries` misses the expected token is forced in (flagged), unless\\n    `strict` is set, in which case it keeps trying until the attempt cap.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(seed)\\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\\n\\n    full = [COT_START] + (tokenize(prompt) or [\\\"The\\\"])\\n    context = list(full)\\n    stack: List[str] = []\\n    forced = 0\\n    attempts = 0\\n    max_attempts = target_depth * (200 if strict else max_retries + 1)\\n\\n    while len(stack) < target_depth and attempts < max_attempts:\\n        expected = COT_CYCLE[len(stack) % len(COT_CYCLE)]\\n        retries = 0\\n        accepted, was_forced = False, False\\n        while attempts < max_attempts:\\n            temp = float(np.clip(controller.temperature * (1.0 + 0.1 * retries), 0.3, 1.8))\\n            new, mlp, eos, emitted = generate_chunk(\\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, len(stack) * chunk,\\n                target_depth * chunk, beam_size, tau, temp, rng, stop_on_cot=True)\\n            attempts += 1\\n            ok = emitted == expected and len(new) > 0\\n            msg = (f\\\"depth {len(stack)}/{target_depth} attempt {attempts} \\\"\\n                   f\\\"expected {expected} got {emitted or 'none'} \\\"\\n                   f\\\"{'OK' if ok else 'retry'} (T={temp:.2f}, forced={forced})\\\")\\n            if trace:\\n                print(msg, file=sys.stderr)\\n            else:\\n                print(\\\"\\\\r\\\" + msg.ljust(78), end=\\\"\\\", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\\n            if ok:\\n                accepted = True\\n                break\\n            retries += 1\\n            if retries > max_retries and not strict:\\n                was_forced = True\\n                break\\n        if not (accepted or was_forced):\\n            break  # attempt cap hit in strict mode\\n\\n        if was_forced:\\n            forced += 1\\n        stack.append(expected)\\n        context += new + [expected]\\n        full += new + [expected]\\n        if new:\\n            controller.update(new, mlp)\\n        if accepted and learn:\\n            model.learn(context[-(model.order - 1) - len(new) - 1:])\\n\\n        # Pipe output back to input at the end of each full CoT cycle.\\n        if len(stack) % PIPE_EVERY == 0:\\n            context = [COT_INTEGRATE] + full[-window:]\\n            full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\\n\\n    if not trace:\\n        print(file=sys.stderr)\\n    monotonic = all(stack[i] == COT_CYCLE[i % len(COT_CYCLE)] for i in range(len(stack)))\\n    stats = dict(depth=len(stack), target=target_depth, attempts=attempts,\\n                 forced=forced, monotonic=monotonic)\\n    return full, stats\\n\\n\\ndef detokenize(tokens: Sequence[str], hide_cot: bool) -> str:\\n    return \\\" \\\".join(strip_cot(tokens) if hide_cot else tokens)\\n\\n\\ndef main() -> None:\\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\\\"Cybernetic feedback-loop n-gram generator.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"corpus\\\", nargs=\\\"?\\\", help=\\\"UTF-8 text corpus file (asked for if omitted).\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--prompt\\\", help=\\\"Initial prompt. If omitted you are asked each round.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--cycles\\\", type=int, default=4, help=\\\"Output->input feedback cycles per prompt.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--chunk\\\", type=int, default=20, help=\\\"Tokens per chunk between CoT tokens.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--chunks-per-cycle\\\", type=int, default=3)\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--window\\\", type=int, default=40, help=\\\"Tokens of output piped back as the next prompt.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--order\\\", type=int, default=3)\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--alpha\\\", type=float, default=0.25)\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--beam\\\", type=int, default=8)\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--tau\\\", type=float, default=0.65)\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--temperature\\\", type=float, default=0.85)\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--seed\\\", type=int, default=7)\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--stack-target\\\", type=int, default=25,\\n                   help=\\\"Keep going until this many CoT tokens have stacked in order (0 = old fixed-cycle mode).\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--max-retries\\\", type=int, default=25, help=\\\"Rejected chunks allowed per stack slot before forcing.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--strict\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Never force a token; retry until the attempt cap.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--no-learn\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Disable online learning from own output.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--show-cot\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Show CoT tokens in printed text (hidden by default).\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--trace\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Print controller diagnostics.\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--save\\\", help=\\\"Append output to this text file.\\\")\\n    args = p.parse_args()\\n\\n    corpus_name = args.corpus or input(\\\"Filename: \\\")\\n    path = Path(corpus_name)\\n    if not path.is_file():\\n        p.error(f\\\"Corpus file not found: {path}\\\")\\n    try:\\n        corpus_text = path.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8-sig\\\")\\n    except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\\n        p.error(f\\\"Could not decode corpus as UTF-8: {exc}\\\")\\n    if not tokenize(corpus_text):\\n        p.error(\\\"Corpus contains no tokens.\\\")\\n\\n    set_cot_tokens(select_cot_tokens(corpus_text, args.seed))\\n    print(\\\"CoT tokens (from dataset): \\\" + \\\" \\\".join(COT_CYCLE)\\n          + f\\\" | diverge={COT_DIVERGE} converge={COT_CONVERGE}\\\"\\n          f\\\" integrate={COT_INTEGRATE} start={COT_START}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\\n    model.train(corpus_text, cot=True)\\n\\n    first = True\\n    while True:\\n        try:\\n            prompt = args.prompt if (args.prompt and first) else input(\\\"USER: \\\")\\n        except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):\\n            print()\\n            break\\n        first = False\\n\\n        tau = float(np.clip(args.tau, 0.0, 1.0))\\n        temp = max(0.0, args.temperature)\\n        if args.stack_target > 0:\\n            full, stats = stacked_run(\\n                model, prompt, target_depth=args.stack_target, chunk=args.chunk,\\n                window=args.window, beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp,\\n                seed=args.seed, learn=not args.no_learn,\\n                max_retries=args.max_retries, strict=args.strict, trace=args.trace)\\n            print(f\\\"\\\\n[stack] depth {stats['depth']}/{stats['target']}  attempts {stats['attempts']}  \\\"\\n                  f\\\"forced {stats['forced']}  monotonic order verified: {stats['monotonic']}\\\")\\n        else:\\n            full = cybernetic_run(\\n                model, prompt, cycles=args.cycles, chunk=args.chunk,\\n                chunks_per_cycle=args.chunks_per_cycle, window=args.window,\\n                beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp, seed=args.seed,\\n                learn=not args.no_learn, trace=args.trace)\\n\\n        text = detokenize(full, hide_cot=not args.show_cot)\\n        print(\\\"\\\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\\\n\\\")\\n        print(text)\\n        print()\\n        if args.save:\\n            with open(args.save, \\\"a\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\\n                fh.write(text + \\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\n\", \"filename\": \"/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:05:44.544067Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:05:44.544113Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01DwzgXMGgzHmudmqNJP3nNU", "name": "create_file", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:05:46.357161Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:05:46.607016Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Jpjc9owaec9W5FRXYysvFU", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:05:46.641101Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:05:46.641132Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Jpjc9owaec9W5FRXYysvFU", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/cybernetic_textgen.py", "name": "cybernetic textgen", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "\n\nThe file cards appear with your reply, and where they sit relative to its text depends on the app the user is reading in; finish the reply with text, and refer to a file by its name, never as above or below."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:05:51.119927Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:05:51.132872Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I renamed \"cog\" to \"cot\" throughout `cybernetic_textgen.py`. I read \"cog\" as short for \"cognitive\", so \"cognitive tokens\" are now \"CoT tokens (chain-of-thought markers)\" in the docs and messages. I didn't run it.\n\n- **Classes and constants:** `CogToken` is now `CotToken`. `COG_CYCLE`, `COG_DIVERGE`, `COG_CONVERGE`, `COG_INTEGRATE`, `COG_START`, `COG_COUNT` and `DEFAULT_COG` all use the `COT_` prefix. The `COGNITIVE` set is now `COT`.\n- **Functions:** `set_cognitive_tokens`, `select_cognitive_tokens` and `strip_cognitive` are now `set_cot_tokens`, `select_cot_tokens` and `strip_cot`.\n- **Parameters and variables:** `cog` is now `cot`, `emitted_cog` is `emitted_cot`, `stop_on_cog` is `stop_on_cot`, `hide_cog` is `hide_cot`, and `train(..., cognitive=)` is `train(..., cot=)`.\n- **CLI flag:** `--show-cog` is now `--show-cot`. Any scripts that call the old flag will need updating.\n\nThe 29 fallback words in `DEFAULT_COT` (simulate, recall, and so on) are unchanged.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-14T22:05:51.199567Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T22:05:51.199567Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a13c72-75a7-72e5-a93c-5425877ffb71"}, {"uuid": "01a13c74-8976-7c61-92b9-16202b6f8123", "text": "make that a weight extender, with custom vocab from a sorted cognitive list", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:07:15.785557Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:07:15.785557Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "make that a weight extender, with custom vocab from a sorted cognitive list", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-14T22:07:15.785945Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T22:07:15.785945Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a13c72-75a7-7a20-9229-9bb8e253c4e4"}, {"uuid": "01a13c74-8976-79e1-82ad-87f888a0efb1", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI turned the generator into `cot_weight_extender.py`, a model whose weights are saved to a checkpoint and can be grown later. I ran a small smoke test (build, extend with a new vocab, info, generate, save) and it all ran cleanly. \"Weight extender\" and \"sorted cognitive list\" were ambiguous, so I made two guesses you should check.\n\n**Commands**\n- `build corpus.txt -o base.cotw.gz --cot-vocab cot.txt` trains a new checkpoint.\n- `extend base.cotw.gz more.txt -o v2.cotw.gz --decay 0.9` adds corpora to an existing checkpoint. `--decay` scales the old weights down first so the new data counts for more.\n- `extend v2.cotw.gz -o v3.cotw.gz --cot-vocab newcot.txt` swaps in a new CoT vocabulary and carries the old learned behaviour over to the new words by position.\n- `generate v3.cotw.gz --prompt \"...\" --save-model v4.cotw.gz` runs the loop and writes out what it learned online.\n- `info v3.cotw.gz` prints the checkpoint's size and vocabulary.\n\n**Custom vocab (`--cot-vocab`)**\nThe file has one word per line, and the order is the stack order. Entries 1\u201325 are the cycle, then diverge, converge, integrate and start. I read \"sorted\" as \"the list's order is meaningful\": it is used as given by default, or sorted first with `--cot-sort alpha`, `alpha-desc` or `length`. If your list has fewer than 29 words, the rest are filled from fallback names. If it has more than 29, the extras are ignored. Words can't contain whitespace.\n\n**What's saved in a checkpoint**\nIt's a gzip JSON file with the n-gram counts, the vocabulary, the fragment matrices that were previously regenerated from the seed, the CoT vocabulary, and a small meta block. The n-gram order is fixed when you build, so changing it means building again. Fragment weights stay frozen when you extend.\n\n**Things to know**\n- **Collisions on remap:** remapping renames words by string, so if a new CoT word also appears in your corpus as an ordinary word, the two merge. `extend` warns you when this happens, and uncommon words avoid it.\n- **Fallback list fix:** the old fallback list had `\"observe\"` twice, so a very small corpus could leave you with only 28 unique words and crash. I replaced the duplicate with `\"synthesize\"`.\n- **Stack mode on tiny corpora:** in my test it forced several tokens, which is normal when the corpus is that small.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:07:15.785351Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:07:54.402402Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Figuring out how to turn the generator into a weight extender."}, {"summary": "Designing vocab remapping to preserve weights across custom lists."}, {"summary": "Organizing CLI subcommands for building, extending, and generating."}, {"summary": "Defining checkpoint serialization for counts and vocabulary data."}, {"summary": "Handling collision risk when remapping ordinary corpus words."}, {"summary": "Parsing vocab files and planning CLI argument details."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:07:54.402475Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:08:57.576220Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01G3FUQCC3yAzKmt6cpokXZz", "name": "create_file", "input": {"description": "Weight-extender version: checkpoint build/extend/generate with custom sorted CoT vocab and weight remapping", "path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py", "file_text": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nCoT weight extender\n===================\n\nThe cybernetic n-gram generator, turned into a persistent, extendable model.\n\n  build     Train a new weight checkpoint from one or more corpora.\n  extend    Load a checkpoint and grow it: more corpora, optional decay of the\n            old weights, and optionally a NEW CoT vocabulary (old CoT weights\n            are transferred position-by-position onto the new words).\n  generate  Run the cybernetic feedback loop from a checkpoint; optionally save\n            the weights the model learned online back out.\n  info      Print checkpoint statistics.\n\nCustom CoT vocabulary (--cot-vocab FILE):\n  A plain text list, one word per line ('#' comments and blank lines ignored).\n  The list is used IN ORDER (or sorted with --cot-sort), and the order matters:\n\n      entries  1..25   the stack cycle, in required order\n      entry    26      diverge   (raise temperature)\n      entry    27      converge  (lower temperature)\n      entry    28      integrate (start of every piped-back prompt)\n      entry    29      start\n\n  Entries beyond 29 are ignored; if there are fewer than 29 the rest are filled\n  from built-in fallback names. Words must not contain whitespace.\n\nCheckpoint = gzip JSON holding n-gram counts, vocab, the non-isomorphic\nfragment matrices, the CoT vocabulary and a small meta block.\n\nExamples:\n  python cot_weight_extender.py build corpus.txt -o base.cotw.gz --cot-vocab cot.txt\n  python cot_weight_extender.py extend base.cotw.gz more.txt -o v2.cotw.gz --decay 0.9\n  python cot_weight_extender.py extend v2.cotw.gz -o v3.cotw.gz --cot-vocab newcot.txt\n  python cot_weight_extender.py generate v3.cotw.gz --prompt \"The machine\" --save-model v4.cotw.gz\n  python cot_weight_extender.py info v3.cotw.gz\n\nOnly dependency: NumPy\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport gzip\nimport json\nimport math\nimport random\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Sequence, Tuple\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nFORMAT = \"cot-weights-v1\"\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# CoT tokens\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass CotToken(str):\n    \"\"\"A CoT marker inserted by the loop. It is a str, but isinstance() tells it\n    apart from the same word appearing as ordinary text, so hiding markers never\n    deletes real words from the output.\"\"\"\n\n\n# Fallback names, used only if the vocabulary source has too few distinct words.\nDEFAULT_COT = [\n    \"simulate\", \"recall\", \"correct\", \"imagine\", \"decide\",\n    \"observe\", \"verify\", \"associate\", \"plan\", \"anticipate\",\n    \"reflect\", \"abstract\", \"act\", \"question\", \"compare\",\n    \"adapt\", \"predict\", \"summarize\", \"monitor\", \"infer\",\n    \"consolidate\", \"attend\", \"evaluate\", \"prioritize\", \"hypothesize\",\n    \"diverge\", \"converge\", \"integrate\", \"synthesize\",\n]\nCOT_COUNT = 29  # 25 cycle tokens + diverge + converge + integrate + start\nPIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens\nSENTENCE_END = (\".\", \"!\", \"?\")\n\nCOT_CYCLE: List[str] = []\nCOT_DIVERGE = COT_CONVERGE = COT_INTEGRATE = COT_START = CotToken(\"\")\nCOT: set = set()\n\n_STOP = {\n    \"that\", \"with\", \"have\", \"from\", \"this\", \"they\", \"were\", \"been\", \"will\", \"would\", \"there\",\n    \"their\", \"what\", \"when\", \"which\", \"your\", \"them\", \"then\", \"than\", \"into\", \"only\", \"also\",\n    \"some\", \"such\", \"more\", \"most\", \"other\", \"about\", \"could\", \"should\", \"these\", \"those\",\n}\n\n\ndef set_cot_tokens(words: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Install the CoT vocabulary: 25 cycle tokens, then diverge, converge,\n    integrate, start.\"\"\"\n    global COT_CYCLE, COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START, COT\n    toks = [CotToken(w) for w in words]\n    COT_CYCLE = toks[:25]\n    COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START = toks[25:29]\n    COT = {str(t) for t in toks}\n\n\ndef current_cot_words() -> List[str]:\n    return [str(t) for t in COT_CYCLE] + [str(COT_DIVERGE), str(COT_CONVERGE),\n                                          str(COT_INTEGRATE), str(COT_START)]\n\n\ndef _top_up(words: List[str], count: int) -> List[str]:\n    seen = {w.lower() for w in words}\n    for d in DEFAULT_COT:\n        if len(words) >= count:\n            break\n        if d.lower() not in seen:\n            seen.add(d.lower())\n            words.append(d)\n    return words\n\n\ndef select_cot_tokens(text: str, seed: int, count: int = COT_COUNT) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Pick CoT tokens FROM THE DATASET: the most frequent alphabetic words of\n    4+ letters (skipping common function words), shuffled so the required order is\n    non-monotonic.\"\"\"\n    counts = Counter(tokenize(text))\n    pool = [(w, c) for w, c in counts.items()\n            if w.isalpha() and len(w) >= 4 and w.lower() not in _STOP]\n    pool.sort(key=lambda wc: (-wc[1], wc[0]))\n    words, seen = [], set()\n    for w, _ in pool:\n        if w.lower() not in seen:\n            seen.add(w.lower())\n            words.append(w)\n        if len(words) >= count:\n            break\n    random.Random(seed).shuffle(words)\n    return _top_up(words, count)\n\n\ndef load_cot_vocab(path: str, sort: str = \"none\", count: int = COT_COUNT) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Load a custom CoT vocabulary from a text file (one word per line).\n\n    sort: 'none' keeps file order (use when the list is already sorted the way you\n    want the stack to run), 'alpha' / 'alpha-desc' sort case-insensitively,\n    'length' sorts short to long. Sorting happens BEFORE truncating to `count`.\n    \"\"\"\n    words, seen = [], set()\n    for lineno, line in enumerate(Path(path).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\").splitlines(), 1):\n        w = line.split(\"#\", 1)[0].strip()\n        if not w:\n            continue\n        if len(w.split()) != 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{path}:{lineno}: CoT words must be a single token, got {w!r}\")\n        if w.lower() in seen:\n            print(f\"warning: duplicate CoT word {w!r} at line {lineno} ignored\", file=sys.stderr)\n            continue\n        seen.add(w.lower())\n        words.append(w)\n    if sort == \"alpha\":\n        words.sort(key=str.lower)\n    elif sort == \"alpha-desc\":\n        words.sort(key=str.lower, reverse=True)\n    elif sort == \"length\":\n        words.sort(key=lambda w: (len(w), w.lower()))\n    if len(words) > count:\n        print(f\"note: {len(words)} CoT words given, using the first {count}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        words = words[:count]\n    elif len(words) < count:\n        print(f\"note: only {len(words)} CoT words given, filling to {count} from fallback names\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        words = _top_up(words, count)\n    return words\n\n\nset_cot_tokens(DEFAULT_COT)\n\n\ndef tokenize(text: str) -> List[str]:\n    return text.split()\n\n\ndef strip_cot(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> List[str]:\n    return [t for t in tokens if not isinstance(t, CotToken)]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# N-gram model (now with serialisation, decay, merge and token remapping)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass NGramModel:\n    \"\"\"Smoothed n-gram model with backoff, trainable offline and online.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, order: int = 3, alpha: float = 0.25):\n        self.order = max(1, int(order))\n        self.alpha = max(1e-9, float(alpha))\n        self.counts = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(self.order)]\n        self.vocab = Counter()\n        self.total_tokens = 0\n\n    def _update(self, tokens: Sequence[str], start: int) -> None:\n        for i in range(start, len(tokens)):\n            target = tokens[i]\n            self.vocab[target] += 1\n            self.total_tokens += 1\n            for ctx_len in range(self.order):\n                if ctx_len > i:\n                    break\n                context = tuple(tokens[i - ctx_len:i]) if ctx_len else ()\n                self.counts[ctx_len][context][target] += 1\n\n    def train(self, text: str, cot: bool = True) -> None:\n        raw = tokenize(text)\n        if cot:\n            # Weave CoT tokens in after each sentence so the model\n            # learns what comes before/after them.\n            woven, k = [], 0\n            for tok in raw:\n                woven.append(tok)\n                if tok.endswith(SENTENCE_END):\n                    woven.append(COT_CYCLE[k % len(COT_CYCLE)])\n                    k += 1\n            raw = woven\n        tokens = [\"<bos>\"] * (self.order - 1) + raw + [\"<eos>\"]\n        self._update(tokens, self.order - 1)\n\n    def learn(self, tokens: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Online update from the model's own output (feedback learning).\"\"\"\n        self._update(list(tokens), 1)\n\n    # ---- weight extension ------------------------------------------------\n    def scale(self, factor: float) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Multiply every stored weight (decay old knowledge before extending).\"\"\"\n        if factor == 1.0:\n            return\n        for level in self.counts:\n            for counter in level.values():\n                for tok in counter:\n                    counter[tok] *= factor\n        for tok in self.vocab:\n            self.vocab[tok] *= factor\n        self.total_tokens *= factor\n\n    def remap_tokens(self, mapping: Dict[str, str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Rename tokens everywhere (contexts and targets). Colliding counts are\n        summed. This transfers learned CoT behaviour onto a new CoT vocabulary.\"\"\"\n        if not mapping:\n            return\n\n        def m(t):\n            return mapping.get(t, t)\n\n        new_counts = []\n        for level in self.counts:\n            nl = defaultdict(Counter)\n            for ctx, counter in level.items():\n                nctx = tuple(m(t) for t in ctx)\n                for tok, n in counter.items():\n                    nl[nctx][m(tok)] += n\n            new_counts.append(nl)\n        self.counts = new_counts\n        nv = Counter()\n        for tok, n in self.vocab.items():\n            nv[m(tok)] += n\n        self.vocab = nv\n\n    # ---- serialisation ---------------------------------------------------\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return {\n            \"order\": self.order,\n            \"alpha\": self.alpha,\n            \"total_tokens\": self.total_tokens,\n            \"vocab\": {str(k): v for k, v in self.vocab.items()},\n            \"counts\": [[[list(ctx), {str(t): n for t, n in c.items()}]\n                        for ctx, c in level.items()] for level in self.counts],\n        }\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> \"NGramModel\":\n        model = cls(order=d[\"order\"], alpha=d[\"alpha\"])\n        model.total_tokens = d[\"total_tokens\"]\n        model.vocab = Counter(d[\"vocab\"])\n        model.counts = []\n        for level in d[\"counts\"]:\n            lv = defaultdict(Counter)\n            for ctx, counter in level:\n                lv[tuple(ctx)] = Counter(counter)\n            model.counts.append(lv)\n        return model\n\n    def candidates(self, context_tokens: Sequence[str], limit: int = 80) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:\n        vocab_size = max(1, len(self.vocab))\n        context = list(context_tokens)\n        counter = Counter()\n        for ctx_len in range(min(self.order - 1, len(context)), -1, -1):\n            key = tuple(context[-ctx_len:]) if ctx_len else ()\n            found = self.counts[ctx_len].get(key)\n            if not found:\n                continue\n            weight = 1.0 + 0.7 * ctx_len\n            for token, count in found.items():\n                counter[token] += weight * count\n            if ctx_len >= 1:\n                break\n        if not counter:\n            counter.update(self.vocab)\n        counter.pop(\"<bos>\", None)\n        total = sum(counter.values())\n        ranked = []\n        for token, count in counter.items():\n            prob = (count + self.alpha) / (total + self.alpha * vocab_size)\n            ranked.append((token, math.log(max(prob, 1e-12))))\n        ranked.sort(key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\n        return ranked[:max(1, limit)]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Non-isomorphic fragments (weights are now saved with the checkpoint)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass NonIsomorphicFragments:\n    def __init__(self, seed: int = 17):\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        self.w_context = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 3))\n        self.w_word = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 4))\n        self.w_transition = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 2))\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return {\"w_context\": self.w_context.tolist(),\n                \"w_word\": self.w_word.tolist(),\n                \"w_transition\": self.w_transition.tolist()}\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> \"NonIsomorphicFragments\":\n        frag = cls(0)\n        frag.w_context = np.asarray(d[\"w_context\"], dtype=float)\n        frag.w_word = np.asarray(d[\"w_word\"], dtype=float)\n        frag.w_transition = np.asarray(d[\"w_transition\"], dtype=float)\n        return frag\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _unit(v: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        n = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\n        return v / n if n > 1e-12 else np.zeros_like(v)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _hash_features(token: str, width: int) -> np.ndarray:\n        raw = token.lower().encode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\")\n        vals = np.zeros(width, dtype=float)\n        if not raw:\n            return vals\n        for i, byte in enumerate(raw):\n            vals[i % width] += ((byte % 31) - 15) / 15.0\n            vals[(i * 3 + 1) % width] += ((byte % 17) - 8) / 8.0\n        vals /= max(1, len(raw))\n        vals[0] += min(len(raw), 20) / 20.0\n        vals[1] += sum(chr(b).isalpha() for b in raw) / max(1, len(raw))\n        return np.tanh(vals)\n\n    def features(self, context, token, logp, rank):\n        recent = list(context[-4:])\n        ctx_vec = np.zeros(5, dtype=float)\n        if recent:\n            for i, word in enumerate(recent):\n                f = self._hash_features(word, 5)\n                ctx_vec += f * (0.65 ** (len(recent) - i - 1))\n            ctx_vec /= max(1, len(recent))\n        word_vec = self._hash_features(token, 5)\n        transition_vec = np.array([\n            np.tanh(logp),\n            1.0 / (1.0 + rank),\n            1.0 if token[:1].isupper() else 0.0,\n            1.0 if token in COT else 0.0,  # CoT tokens are visible to the fragments\n            min(len(token), 24) / 24.0,\n        ], dtype=float)\n        g1 = np.tanh(ctx_vec @ self.w_context)\n        g2 = np.tanh(word_vec @ self.w_word)\n        g3 = np.tanh(transition_vec @ self.w_transition)\n        return g1, g2, g3\n\n    def score(self, context, token, logp, rank, lam) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n        g1, g2, g3 = self.features(context, token, logp, rank)\n        summaries = np.array([np.linalg.norm(g1), np.linalg.norm(g2), np.linalg.norm(g3)])\n        mean = float(np.mean(summaries))\n        spread = float(np.std(summaries) / (mean + 1e-9))\n        consistency = float(np.clip(0.55 * spread + 0.45 * (1.0 - mean), 0.0, 1.0))\n\n        ref = self._unit(np.array([np.mean(g1), np.mean(g2), np.mean(g3), np.tanh(logp)]))\n        cand = self._unit(np.array([g1[0], g2[0], g3[0], np.tanh(logp + 0.1 * rank)]))\n        alignment = (float(np.dot(ref, cand)) + 1.0) / 2.0\n\n        fragment_score = 1.6 * alignment - 1.15 * consistency\n        total = (1.0 - lam) * (0.75 * logp + 0.25 * fragment_score) \\\n            + lam * (1.25 * logp + 0.85 * fragment_score)\n        return total, consistency\n\n\ndef adiabatic_lambda(step: int, total_steps: int) -> float:\n    u = min(1.0, max(0.0, step / max(1, total_steps - 1)))\n    return 3.0 * u * u - 2.0 * u * u * u\n\n\ndef softmax(values: Sequence[float], temperature: float = 1.0) -> np.ndarray:\n    temp = max(1e-6, float(temperature))\n    arr = np.asarray(values, dtype=float) / temp\n    arr -= np.max(arr)\n    exp = np.exp(np.clip(arr, -60, 60))\n    return exp / max(float(exp.sum()), 1e-12)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Checkpoints\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef save_checkpoint(path: str, model: NGramModel, fragments: NonIsomorphicFragments,\n                    meta: dict) -> None:\n    payload = {\n        \"format\": FORMAT,\n        \"cot\": current_cot_words(),\n        \"fragments\": fragments.to_dict(),\n        \"model\": model.to_dict(),\n        \"meta\": meta,\n    }\n    with gzip.open(path, \"wt\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n        json.dump(payload, fh)\n\n\ndef load_checkpoint(path: str):\n    \"\"\"Load a checkpoint and install its CoT vocabulary globally.\"\"\"\n    with gzip.open(path, \"rt\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n        payload = json.load(fh)\n    if payload.get(\"format\") != FORMAT:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{path}: unsupported checkpoint format {payload.get('format')!r}\")\n    set_cot_tokens(payload[\"cot\"])\n    model = NGramModel.from_dict(payload[\"model\"])\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments.from_dict(payload[\"fragments\"])\n    return model, fragments, payload.get(\"meta\", {})\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Cybernetic controller (sensor -> comparator -> actuator)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass Controller:\n    def __init__(self, temperature: float, rep_limit: float = 0.5, logp_floor: float = -4.5):\n        self.temperature = temperature\n        self.rep_limit = rep_limit\n        self.logp_floor = logp_floor\n        self.k = 0\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def repetition(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> float:\n        words = strip_cot(tokens)\n        if len(words) < 2:\n            return 0.0\n        return 1.0 - len(set(words)) / len(words)\n\n    def update(self, chunk: Sequence[str], mean_logp: float) -> Tuple[str, float]:\n        \"\"\"Return (CoT token to emit, repetition measure).\"\"\"\n        rep = self.repetition(chunk)\n        if rep > self.rep_limit:\n            cot = COT_DIVERGE\n            self.temperature *= 1.15\n        elif mean_logp < self.logp_floor:\n            cot = COT_CONVERGE\n            self.temperature *= 0.9\n        else:\n            cot = COT_CYCLE[self.k % len(COT_CYCLE)]\n            self.k += 1\n        self.temperature = float(np.clip(self.temperature, 0.3, 1.6))\n        return cot, rep\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Candidate:\n    token: str\n    base_logp: float\n    score: float\n    consistency: float\n    probability: float = 0.0\n\n\ndef generate_chunk(model, fragments, context, n, step0, total, beam_size, tau, temperature, rng,\n                   stop_on_cot=False):\n    \"\"\"Generate up to n tokens after `context`.\n\n    Returns (new_tokens, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted_cot). With stop_on_cot the\n    chunk ends the moment the MODEL emits a CoT token (returned in\n    emitted_cot, not appended to new_tokens).\n    \"\"\"\n    ctx = list(context)\n    new, logps, hit_eos, emitted = [], [], False, None\n    for i in range(n):\n        lam = adiabatic_lambda(step0 + i, total)\n        ranked = model.candidates(ctx, limit=max(40, beam_size * 8))\n        scored: List[Candidate] = []\n        for rank, (token, logp) in enumerate(ranked):\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, rank, lam)\n            if consistency <= tau:\n                scored.append(Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency))\n        if not scored:\n            token, logp = ranked[0]\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, 0, lam)\n            scored = [Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency)]\n\n        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c.score, reverse=True)\n        beam = scored[:max(1, beam_size)]\n        probs = softmax([c.score for c in beam], temperature)\n        chosen = beam[0] if temperature <= 0.01 else rng.choices(beam, weights=probs, k=1)[0]\n\n        if chosen.token == \"<eos>\":\n            hit_eos = True\n            break\n        if stop_on_cot and chosen.token in COT:\n            emitted = chosen.token\n            logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\n            break\n        new.append(chosen.token)\n        ctx.append(chosen.token)\n        logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\n    mean_logp = float(np.mean(logps)) if logps else 0.0\n    return new, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted\n\n\ndef cybernetic_run(model, fragments, prompt, cycles, chunk, chunks_per_cycle, window, beam_size,\n                   tau, temperature, seed, learn, trace):\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\n\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\"The\"]\n    full = [COT_START] + seed_tokens          # everything produced so far\n    context = list(full)                      # what the model sees this cycle\n    total = max(1, cycles * chunks_per_cycle * chunk)\n    step = 0\n\n    for c in range(cycles):\n        for k in range(chunks_per_cycle):\n            new, mean_logp, hit_eos, _ = generate_chunk(\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, step, total,\n                beam_size, tau, controller.temperature, rng)\n            step += chunk\n            cot, rep = controller.update(new, mean_logp)\n\n            if trace:\n                print(f\"[cycle {c+1}/{cycles} chunk {k+1}] tokens={len(new)} \"\n                      f\"mean_logp={mean_logp:.2f} rep={rep:.2f} \"\n                      f\"-> {cot} (T={controller.temperature:.2f})\")\n\n            # Feedback learning: only from healthy output, to avoid reinforcing loops.\n            if learn and new and rep <= controller.rep_limit:\n                model.learn(context[-(model.order - 1):] + new + [cot])\n\n            context += new + [cot]\n            full += new + [cot]\n            if hit_eos:\n                break\n\n        # Pipe output back to input: new prompt begins with a CoT token.\n        tail = full[-window:]\n        context = [COT_INTEGRATE] + tail\n        full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\n\n    return full\n\n\ndef stacked_run(model, fragments, prompt, target_depth, chunk, window, beam_size, tau, temperature,\n                seed, learn, max_retries, strict, trace):\n    \"\"\"\n    Keep generating until CoT tokens stack up in the correct order.\n\n    The model must itself emit the next expected CoT token\n    (the order defined in COT_CYCLE, repeating) after a chunk of\n    real content. A wrong or missing token rejects the chunk and it is\n    regenerated (temperature creeps up on each retry). Accepted chunks are\n    pushed onto the stack, which only ever grows (monotonic), and are learned\n    online so the model gets better at the pattern as it goes.\n\n    After `max_retries` misses the expected token is forced in (flagged), unless\n    `strict` is set, in which case it keeps trying until the attempt cap.\n    \"\"\"\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\n\n    full = [COT_START] + (tokenize(prompt) or [\"The\"])\n    context = list(full)\n    stack: List[str] = []\n    forced = 0\n    attempts = 0\n    max_attempts = target_depth * (200 if strict else max_retries + 1)\n\n    while len(stack) < target_depth and attempts < max_attempts:\n        expected = COT_CYCLE[len(stack) % len(COT_CYCLE)]\n        retries = 0\n        accepted, was_forced = False, False\n        while attempts < max_attempts:\n            temp = float(np.clip(controller.temperature * (1.0 + 0.1 * retries), 0.3, 1.8))\n            new, mlp, eos, emitted = generate_chunk(\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, len(stack) * chunk,\n                target_depth * chunk, beam_size, tau, temp, rng, stop_on_cot=True)\n            attempts += 1\n            ok = emitted == expected and len(new) > 0\n            msg = (f\"depth {len(stack)}/{target_depth} attempt {attempts} \"\n                   f\"expected {expected} got {emitted or 'none'} \"\n                   f\"{'OK' if ok else 'retry'} (T={temp:.2f}, forced={forced})\")\n            if trace:\n                print(msg, file=sys.stderr)\n            else:\n                print(\"\\r\" + msg.ljust(78), end=\"\", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\n            if ok:\n                accepted = True\n                break\n            retries += 1\n            if retries > max_retries and not strict:\n                was_forced = True\n                break\n        if not (accepted or was_forced):\n            break  # attempt cap hit in strict mode\n\n        if was_forced:\n            forced += 1\n        stack.append(expected)\n        context += new + [expected]\n        full += new + [expected]\n        if new:\n            controller.update(new, mlp)\n        if accepted and learn:\n            model.learn(context[-(model.order - 1) - len(new) - 1:])\n\n        # Pipe output back to input at the end of each full CoT cycle.\n        if len(stack) % PIPE_EVERY == 0:\n            context = [COT_INTEGRATE] + full[-window:]\n            full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\n\n    if not trace:\n        print(file=sys.stderr)\n    monotonic = all(stack[i] == COT_CYCLE[i % len(COT_CYCLE)] for i in range(len(stack)))\n    stats = dict(depth=len(stack), target=target_depth, attempts=attempts,\n                 forced=forced, monotonic=monotonic)\n    return full, stats\n\n\ndef detokenize(tokens: Sequence[str], hide_cot: bool) -> str:\n    return \" \".join(strip_cot(tokens) if hide_cot else tokens)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# CLI\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef die(msg: str) -> None:\n    print(f\"error: {msg}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    sys.exit(2)\n\n\ndef read_corpus(path: str) -> str:\n    p = Path(path)\n    if not p.is_file():\n        die(f\"corpus file not found: {p}\")\n    try:\n        text = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\n    except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n        die(f\"could not decode {p} as UTF-8: {exc}\")\n    if not tokenize(text):\n        die(f\"{p} contains no tokens\")\n    return text\n\n\ndef add_vocab_args(p: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:\n    p.add_argument(\"--cot-vocab\", help=\"Custom CoT vocabulary file (one word per line, used in order).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--cot-sort\", choices=[\"none\", \"alpha\", \"alpha-desc\", \"length\"], default=\"none\",\n                   help=\"Sort the custom list before use (default: keep file order).\")\n\n\ndef cmd_build(args) -> None:\n    texts = [read_corpus(c) for c in args.corpus]\n    if args.cot_vocab:\n        words = load_cot_vocab(args.cot_vocab, args.cot_sort)\n    else:\n        words = select_cot_tokens(\"\\n\".join(texts), args.seed)\n    set_cot_tokens(words)\n    print(\"CoT vocab: \" + \" \".join(current_cot_words()), file=sys.stderr)\n\n    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\n    for text in texts:\n        model.train(text, cot=not args.no_cot_weave)\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(args.seed)\n    meta = {\"seed\": args.seed, \"extensions\": 0, \"sources\": [Path(c).name for c in args.corpus]}\n    save_checkpoint(args.output, model, fragments, meta)\n    print(f\"built {args.output}: {len(model.vocab)} types, {model.total_tokens:g} tokens\",\n          file=sys.stderr)\n\n\ndef cmd_extend(args) -> None:\n    try:\n        model, fragments, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\n    except (OSError, ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n        die(str(exc))\n    old_words = current_cot_words()\n\n    if args.alpha is not None:\n        model.alpha = max(1e-9, args.alpha)\n\n    if args.cot_vocab:\n        new_words = load_cot_vocab(args.cot_vocab, args.cot_sort)\n        mapping = {o: n for o, n in zip(old_words, new_words) if o != n}\n        if mapping:\n            clash = [n for n in mapping.values() if n in model.vocab and n not in mapping]\n            if clash:\n                print(\"warning: new CoT words already occur as ordinary words in the weights \"\n                      f\"and will merge with them: {', '.join(sorted(clash)[:8])}\"\n                      + (\" ...\" if len(clash) > 8 else \"\"), file=sys.stderr)\n            model.remap_tokens(mapping)\n            print(f\"remapped {len(mapping)} CoT tokens onto the new vocabulary\", file=sys.stderr)\n        set_cot_tokens(new_words)\n    print(\"CoT vocab: \" + \" \".join(current_cot_words()), file=sys.stderr)\n\n    if args.decay != 1.0:\n        model.scale(args.decay)\n        print(f\"decayed existing weights by {args.decay}\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n    for path in args.corpus:\n        model.train(read_corpus(path), cot=not args.no_cot_weave)\n        meta.setdefault(\"sources\", []).append(Path(path).name)\n    meta[\"extensions\"] = meta.get(\"extensions\", 0) + 1\n\n    save_checkpoint(args.output, model, fragments, meta)\n    print(f\"extended -> {args.output}: {len(model.vocab)} types, {model.total_tokens:g} tokens\",\n          file=sys.stderr)\n\n\ndef cmd_info(args) -> None:\n    try:\n        model, fragments, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\n    except (OSError, ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n        die(str(exc))\n    print(f\"format       {FORMAT}\")\n    print(f\"order        {model.order}   alpha {model.alpha}\")\n    print(f\"vocab types  {len(model.vocab)}   tokens {model.total_tokens:g}\")\n    print(f\"contexts     \" + \", \".join(f\"n={i}: {len(lv)}\" for i, lv in enumerate(model.counts)))\n    print(f\"extensions   {meta.get('extensions', 0)}   sources {', '.join(meta.get('sources', []))}\")\n    print(\"cycle        \" + \" \".join(str(t) for t in COT_CYCLE))\n    print(f\"diverge={COT_DIVERGE} converge={COT_CONVERGE} \"\n          f\"integrate={COT_INTEGRATE} start={COT_START}\")\n\n\ndef cmd_generate(args) -> None:\n    try:\n        model, fragments, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\n    except (OSError, ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n        die(str(exc))\n    print(\"CoT vocab: \" + \" \".join(current_cot_words()), file=sys.stderr)\n\n    first = True\n    while True:\n        try:\n            prompt = args.prompt if (args.prompt and first) else input(\"USER: \")\n        except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):\n            print()\n            break\n        first = False\n\n        tau = float(np.clip(args.tau, 0.0, 1.0))\n        temp = max(0.0, args.temperature)\n        if args.stack_target > 0:\n            full, stats = stacked_run(\n                model, fragments, prompt, target_depth=args.stack_target, chunk=args.chunk,\n                window=args.window, beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp,\n                seed=args.seed, learn=not args.no_learn,\n                max_retries=args.max_retries, strict=args.strict, trace=args.trace)\n            print(f\"\\n[stack] depth {stats['depth']}/{stats['target']}  attempts {stats['attempts']}  \"\n                  f\"forced {stats['forced']}  monotonic order verified: {stats['monotonic']}\")\n        else:\n            full = cybernetic_run(\n                model, fragments, prompt, cycles=args.cycles, chunk=args.chunk,\n                chunks_per_cycle=args.chunks_per_cycle, window=args.window,\n                beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp, seed=args.seed,\n                learn=not args.no_learn, trace=args.trace)\n\n        text = detokenize(full, hide_cot=not args.show_cot)\n        print(\"\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\")\n        print(text)\n        print()\n        if args.save:\n            with open(args.save, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n                fh.write(text + \"\\n\\n\")\n\n    if args.save_model:\n        meta[\"extensions\"] = meta.get(\"extensions\", 0) + 1\n        save_checkpoint(args.save_model, model, fragments, meta)\n        print(f\"saved weights -> {args.save_model}\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"CoT weight extender for the cybernetic n-gram generator.\")\n    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest=\"cmd\", required=True)\n\n    b = sub.add_parser(\"build\", help=\"Train a new checkpoint from corpora.\")\n    b.add_argument(\"corpus\", nargs=\"+\", help=\"UTF-8 text corpus file(s).\")\n    b.add_argument(\"-o\", \"--output\", required=True, help=\"Checkpoint to write (.cotw.gz).\")\n    b.add_argument(\"--order\", type=int, default=3)\n    b.add_argument(\"--alpha\", type=float, default=0.25)\n    b.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=7)\n    b.add_argument(\"--no-cot-weave\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Do not weave CoT tokens into the corpus.\")\n    add_vocab_args(b)\n    b.set_defaults(func=cmd_build)\n\n    e = sub.add_parser(\"extend\", help=\"Extend an existing checkpoint.\")\n    e.add_argument(\"model\", help=\"Checkpoint to extend.\")\n    e.add_argument(\"corpus\", nargs=\"*\", help=\"Additional corpus file(s) (optional).\")\n    e.add_argument(\"-o\", \"--output\", required=True, help=\"Checkpoint to write.\")\n    e.add_argument(\"--decay\", type=float, default=1.0,\n                   help=\"Scale existing weights by this factor before adding new data (e.g. 0.9).\")\n    e.add_argument(\"--alpha\", type=float, default=None, help=\"Override smoothing alpha.\")\n    e.add_argument(\"--no-cot-weave\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Do not weave CoT tokens into new corpora.\")\n    add_vocab_args(e)\n    e.set_defaults(func=cmd_extend)\n\n    i = sub.add_parser(\"info\", help=\"Show checkpoint statistics.\")\n    i.add_argument(\"model\")\n    i.set_defaults(func=cmd_info)\n\n    g = sub.add_parser(\"generate\", help=\"Run the cybernetic loop from a checkpoint.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"model\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--prompt\", help=\"Initial prompt. If omitted you are asked each round.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--cycles\", type=int, default=4, help=\"Output->input feedback cycles per prompt.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--chunk\", type=int, default=20, help=\"Tokens per chunk between CoT tokens.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--chunks-per-cycle\", type=int, default=3)\n    g.add_argument(\"--window\", type=int, default=40, help=\"Tokens of output piped back as the next prompt.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--beam\", type=int, default=8)\n    g.add_argument(\"--tau\", type=float, default=0.65)\n    g.add_argument(\"--temperature\", type=float, default=0.85)\n    g.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=7)\n    g.add_argument(\"--stack-target\", type=int, default=25,\n                   help=\"Keep going until this many CoT tokens have stacked in order (0 = old fixed-cycle mode).\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--max-retries\", type=int, default=25, help=\"Rejected chunks allowed per stack slot before forcing.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--strict\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Never force a token; retry until the attempt cap.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--no-learn\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Disable online learning from own output.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--show-cot\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Show CoT tokens in printed text (hidden by default).\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--trace\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Print controller diagnostics.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--save\", help=\"Append output to this text file.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--save-model\", help=\"Write the weights (incl. online learning) to this checkpoint at exit.\")\n    g.set_defaults(func=cmd_generate)\n\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    args.func(args)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}, "message": "Weight-extender version: checkpoint build/extend/generate with custom sorted CoT vocab and weight remapping", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"python\", \"code\": \"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nCoT weight extender\\n===================\\n\\nThe cybernetic n-gram generator, turned into a persistent, extendable model.\\n\\n  build     Train a new weight checkpoint from one or more corpora.\\n  extend    Load a checkpoint and grow it: more corpora, optional decay of the\\n            old weights, and optionally a NEW CoT vocabulary (old CoT weights\\n            are transferred position-by-position onto the new words).\\n  generate  Run the cybernetic feedback loop from a checkpoint; optionally save\\n            the weights the model learned online back out.\\n  info      Print checkpoint statistics.\\n\\nCustom CoT vocabulary (--cot-vocab FILE):\\n  A plain text list, one word per line ('#' comments and blank lines ignored).\\n  The list is used IN ORDER (or sorted with --cot-sort), and the order matters:\\n\\n      entries  1..25   the stack cycle, in required order\\n      entry    26      diverge   (raise temperature)\\n      entry    27      converge  (lower temperature)\\n      entry    28      integrate (start of every piped-back prompt)\\n      entry    29      start\\n\\n  Entries beyond 29 are ignored; if there are fewer than 29 the rest are filled\\n  from built-in fallback names. Words must not contain whitespace.\\n\\nCheckpoint = gzip JSON holding n-gram counts, vocab, the non-isomorphic\\nfragment matrices, the CoT vocabulary and a small meta block.\\n\\nExamples:\\n  python cot_weight_extender.py build corpus.txt -o base.cotw.gz --cot-vocab cot.txt\\n  python cot_weight_extender.py extend base.cotw.gz more.txt -o v2.cotw.gz --decay 0.9\\n  python cot_weight_extender.py extend v2.cotw.gz -o v3.cotw.gz --cot-vocab newcot.txt\\n  python cot_weight_extender.py generate v3.cotw.gz --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" --save-model v4.cotw.gz\\n  python cot_weight_extender.py info v3.cotw.gz\\n\\nOnly dependency: NumPy\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport argparse\\nimport gzip\\nimport json\\nimport math\\nimport random\\nimport sys\\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Sequence, Tuple\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nFORMAT = \\\"cot-weights-v1\\\"\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# CoT tokens\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass CotToken(str):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A CoT marker inserted by the loop. It is a str, but isinstance() tells it\\n    apart from the same word appearing as ordinary text, so hiding markers never\\n    deletes real words from the output.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\n# Fallback names, used only if the vocabulary source has too few distinct words.\\nDEFAULT_COT = [\\n    \\\"simulate\\\", \\\"recall\\\", \\\"correct\\\", \\\"imagine\\\", \\\"decide\\\",\\n    \\\"observe\\\", \\\"verify\\\", \\\"associate\\\", \\\"plan\\\", \\\"anticipate\\\",\\n    \\\"reflect\\\", \\\"abstract\\\", \\\"act\\\", \\\"question\\\", \\\"compare\\\",\\n    \\\"adapt\\\", \\\"predict\\\", \\\"summarize\\\", \\\"monitor\\\", \\\"infer\\\",\\n    \\\"consolidate\\\", \\\"attend\\\", \\\"evaluate\\\", \\\"prioritize\\\", \\\"hypothesize\\\",\\n    \\\"diverge\\\", \\\"converge\\\", \\\"integrate\\\", \\\"synthesize\\\",\\n]\\nCOT_COUNT = 29  # 25 cycle tokens + diverge + converge + integrate + start\\nPIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens\\nSENTENCE_END = (\\\".\\\", \\\"!\\\", \\\"?\\\")\\n\\nCOT_CYCLE: List[str] = []\\nCOT_DIVERGE = COT_CONVERGE = COT_INTEGRATE = COT_START = CotToken(\\\"\\\")\\nCOT: set = set()\\n\\n_STOP = {\\n    \\\"that\\\", \\\"with\\\", \\\"have\\\", \\\"from\\\", \\\"this\\\", \\\"they\\\", \\\"were\\\", \\\"been\\\", \\\"will\\\", \\\"would\\\", \\\"there\\\",\\n    \\\"their\\\", \\\"what\\\", \\\"when\\\", \\\"which\\\", \\\"your\\\", \\\"them\\\", \\\"then\\\", \\\"than\\\", \\\"into\\\", \\\"only\\\", \\\"also\\\",\\n    \\\"some\\\", \\\"such\\\", \\\"more\\\", \\\"most\\\", \\\"other\\\", \\\"about\\\", \\\"could\\\", \\\"should\\\", \\\"these\\\", \\\"those\\\",\\n}\\n\\n\\ndef set_cot_tokens(words: Sequence[str]) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Install the CoT vocabulary: 25 cycle tokens, then diverge, converge,\\n    integrate, start.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    global COT_CYCLE, COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START, COT\\n    toks = [CotToken(w) for w in words]\\n    COT_CYCLE = toks[:25]\\n    COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START = toks[25:29]\\n    COT = {str(t) for t in toks}\\n\\n\\ndef current_cot_words() -> List[str]:\\n    return [str(t) for t in COT_CYCLE] + [str(COT_DIVERGE), str(COT_CONVERGE),\\n                                          str(COT_INTEGRATE), str(COT_START)]\\n\\n\\ndef _top_up(words: List[str], count: int) -> List[str]:\\n    seen = {w.lower() for w in words}\\n    for d in DEFAULT_COT:\\n        if len(words) >= count:\\n            break\\n        if d.lower() not in seen:\\n            seen.add(d.lower())\\n            words.append(d)\\n    return words\\n\\n\\ndef select_cot_tokens(text: str, seed: int, count: int = COT_COUNT) -> List[str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pick CoT tokens FROM THE DATASET: the most frequent alphabetic words of\\n    4+ letters (skipping common function words), shuffled so the required order is\\n    non-monotonic.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    counts = Counter(tokenize(text))\\n    pool = [(w, c) for w, c in counts.items()\\n            if w.isalpha() and len(w) >= 4 and w.lower() not in _STOP]\\n    pool.sort(key=lambda wc: (-wc[1], wc[0]))\\n    words, seen = [], set()\\n    for w, _ in pool:\\n        if w.lower() not in seen:\\n            seen.add(w.lower())\\n            words.append(w)\\n        if len(words) >= count:\\n            break\\n    random.Random(seed).shuffle(words)\\n    return _top_up(words, count)\\n\\n\\ndef load_cot_vocab(path: str, sort: str = \\\"none\\\", count: int = COT_COUNT) -> List[str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Load a custom CoT vocabulary from a text file (one word per line).\\n\\n    sort: 'none' keeps file order (use when the list is already sorted the way you\\n    want the stack to run), 'alpha' / 'alpha-desc' sort case-insensitively,\\n    'length' sorts short to long. Sorting happens BEFORE truncating to `count`.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    words, seen = [], set()\\n    for lineno, line in enumerate(Path(path).read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8-sig\\\").splitlines(), 1):\\n        w = line.split(\\\"#\\\", 1)[0].strip()\\n        if not w:\\n            continue\\n        if len(w.split()) != 1:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"{path}:{lineno}: CoT words must be a single token, got {w!r}\\\")\\n        if w.lower() in seen:\\n            print(f\\\"warning: duplicate CoT word {w!r} at line {lineno} ignored\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n            continue\\n        seen.add(w.lower())\\n        words.append(w)\\n    if sort == \\\"alpha\\\":\\n        words.sort(key=str.lower)\\n    elif sort == \\\"alpha-desc\\\":\\n        words.sort(key=str.lower, reverse=True)\\n    elif sort == \\\"length\\\":\\n        words.sort(key=lambda w: (len(w), w.lower()))\\n    if len(words) > count:\\n        print(f\\\"note: {len(words)} CoT words given, using the first {count}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        words = words[:count]\\n    elif len(words) < count:\\n        print(f\\\"note: only {len(words)} CoT words given, filling to {count} from fallback names\\\",\\n              file=sys.stderr)\\n        words = _top_up(words, count)\\n    return words\\n\\n\\nset_cot_tokens(DEFAULT_COT)\\n\\n\\ndef tokenize(text: str) -> List[str]:\\n    return text.split()\\n\\n\\ndef strip_cot(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> List[str]:\\n    return [t for t in tokens if not isinstance(t, CotToken)]\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# N-gram model (now with serialisation, decay, merge and token remapping)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass NGramModel:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Smoothed n-gram model with backoff, trainable offline and online.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, order: int = 3, alpha: float = 0.25):\\n        self.order = max(1, int(order))\\n        self.alpha = max(1e-9, float(alpha))\\n        self.counts = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(self.order)]\\n        self.vocab = Counter()\\n        self.total_tokens = 0\\n\\n    def _update(self, tokens: Sequence[str], start: int) -> None:\\n        for i in range(start, len(tokens)):\\n            target = tokens[i]\\n            self.vocab[target] += 1\\n            self.total_tokens += 1\\n            for ctx_len in range(self.order):\\n                if ctx_len > i:\\n                    break\\n                context = tuple(tokens[i - ctx_len:i]) if ctx_len else ()\\n                self.counts[ctx_len][context][target] += 1\\n\\n    def train(self, text: str, cot: bool = True) -> None:\\n        raw = tokenize(text)\\n        if cot:\\n            # Weave CoT tokens in after each sentence so the model\\n            # learns what comes before/after them.\\n            woven, k = [], 0\\n            for tok in raw:\\n                woven.append(tok)\\n                if tok.endswith(SENTENCE_END):\\n                    woven.append(COT_CYCLE[k % len(COT_CYCLE)])\\n                    k += 1\\n            raw = woven\\n        tokens = [\\\"<bos>\\\"] * (self.order - 1) + raw + [\\\"<eos>\\\"]\\n        self._update(tokens, self.order - 1)\\n\\n    def learn(self, tokens: Sequence[str]) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Online update from the model's own output (feedback learning).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self._update(list(tokens), 1)\\n\\n    # ---- weight extension ------------------------------------------------\\n    def scale(self, factor: float) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Multiply every stored weight (decay old knowledge before extending).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if factor == 1.0:\\n            return\\n        for level in self.counts:\\n            for counter in level.values():\\n                for tok in counter:\\n                    counter[tok] *= factor\\n        for tok in self.vocab:\\n            self.vocab[tok] *= factor\\n        self.total_tokens *= factor\\n\\n    def remap_tokens(self, mapping: Dict[str, str]) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Rename tokens everywhere (contexts and targets). Colliding counts are\\n        summed. This transfers learned CoT behaviour onto a new CoT vocabulary.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not mapping:\\n            return\\n\\n        def m(t):\\n            return mapping.get(t, t)\\n\\n        new_counts = []\\n        for level in self.counts:\\n            nl = defaultdict(Counter)\\n            for ctx, counter in level.items():\\n                nctx = tuple(m(t) for t in ctx)\\n                for tok, n in counter.items():\\n                    nl[nctx][m(tok)] += n\\n            new_counts.append(nl)\\n        self.counts = new_counts\\n        nv = Counter()\\n        for tok, n in self.vocab.items():\\n            nv[m(tok)] += n\\n        self.vocab = nv\\n\\n    # ---- serialisation ---------------------------------------------------\\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\\n        return {\\n            \\\"order\\\": self.order,\\n            \\\"alpha\\\": self.alpha,\\n            \\\"total_tokens\\\": self.total_tokens,\\n            \\\"vocab\\\": {str(k): v for k, v in self.vocab.items()},\\n            \\\"counts\\\": [[[list(ctx), {str(t): n for t, n in c.items()}]\\n                        for ctx, c in level.items()] for level in self.counts],\\n        }\\n\\n    @classmethod\\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> \\\"NGramModel\\\":\\n        model = cls(order=d[\\\"order\\\"], alpha=d[\\\"alpha\\\"])\\n        model.total_tokens = d[\\\"total_tokens\\\"]\\n        model.vocab = Counter(d[\\\"vocab\\\"])\\n        model.counts = []\\n        for level in d[\\\"counts\\\"]:\\n            lv = defaultdict(Counter)\\n            for ctx, counter in level:\\n                lv[tuple(ctx)] = Counter(counter)\\n            model.counts.append(lv)\\n        return model\\n\\n    def candidates(self, context_tokens: Sequence[str], limit: int = 80) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:\\n        vocab_size = max(1, len(self.vocab))\\n        context = list(context_tokens)\\n        counter = Counter()\\n        for ctx_len in range(min(self.order - 1, len(context)), -1, -1):\\n            key = tuple(context[-ctx_len:]) if ctx_len else ()\\n            found = self.counts[ctx_len].get(key)\\n            if not found:\\n                continue\\n            weight = 1.0 + 0.7 * ctx_len\\n            for token, count in found.items():\\n                counter[token] += weight * count\\n            if ctx_len >= 1:\\n                break\\n        if not counter:\\n            counter.update(self.vocab)\\n        counter.pop(\\\"<bos>\\\", None)\\n        total = sum(counter.values())\\n        ranked = []\\n        for token, count in counter.items():\\n            prob = (count + self.alpha) / (total + self.alpha * vocab_size)\\n            ranked.append((token, math.log(max(prob, 1e-12))))\\n        ranked.sort(key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\\n        return ranked[:max(1, limit)]\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Non-isomorphic fragments (weights are now saved with the checkpoint)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass NonIsomorphicFragments:\\n    def __init__(self, seed: int = 17):\\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n        self.w_context = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 3))\\n        self.w_word = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 4))\\n        self.w_transition = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 2))\\n\\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\\n        return {\\\"w_context\\\": self.w_context.tolist(),\\n                \\\"w_word\\\": self.w_word.tolist(),\\n                \\\"w_transition\\\": self.w_transition.tolist()}\\n\\n    @classmethod\\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> \\\"NonIsomorphicFragments\\\":\\n        frag = cls(0)\\n        frag.w_context = np.asarray(d[\\\"w_context\\\"], dtype=float)\\n        frag.w_word = np.asarray(d[\\\"w_word\\\"], dtype=float)\\n        frag.w_transition = np.asarray(d[\\\"w_transition\\\"], dtype=float)\\n        return frag\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _unit(v: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n        n = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\\n        return v / n if n > 1e-12 else np.zeros_like(v)\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _hash_features(token: str, width: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n        raw = token.lower().encode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"ignore\\\")\\n        vals = np.zeros(width, dtype=float)\\n        if not raw:\\n            return vals\\n        for i, byte in enumerate(raw):\\n            vals[i % width] += ((byte % 31) - 15) / 15.0\\n            vals[(i * 3 + 1) % width] += ((byte % 17) - 8) / 8.0\\n        vals /= max(1, len(raw))\\n        vals[0] += min(len(raw), 20) / 20.0\\n        vals[1] += sum(chr(b).isalpha() for b in raw) / max(1, len(raw))\\n        return np.tanh(vals)\\n\\n    def features(self, context, token, logp, rank):\\n        recent = list(context[-4:])\\n        ctx_vec = np.zeros(5, dtype=float)\\n        if recent:\\n            for i, word in enumerate(recent):\\n                f = self._hash_features(word, 5)\\n                ctx_vec += f * (0.65 ** (len(recent) - i - 1))\\n            ctx_vec /= max(1, len(recent))\\n        word_vec = self._hash_features(token, 5)\\n        transition_vec = np.array([\\n            np.tanh(logp),\\n            1.0 / (1.0 + rank),\\n            1.0 if token[:1].isupper() else 0.0,\\n            1.0 if token in COT else 0.0,  # CoT tokens are visible to the fragments\\n            min(len(token), 24) / 24.0,\\n        ], dtype=float)\\n        g1 = np.tanh(ctx_vec @ self.w_context)\\n        g2 = np.tanh(word_vec @ self.w_word)\\n        g3 = np.tanh(transition_vec @ self.w_transition)\\n        return g1, g2, g3\\n\\n    def score(self, context, token, logp, rank, lam) -> Tuple[float, float]:\\n        g1, g2, g3 = self.features(context, token, logp, rank)\\n        summaries = np.array([np.linalg.norm(g1), np.linalg.norm(g2), np.linalg.norm(g3)])\\n        mean = float(np.mean(summaries))\\n        spread = float(np.std(summaries) / (mean + 1e-9))\\n        consistency = float(np.clip(0.55 * spread + 0.45 * (1.0 - mean), 0.0, 1.0))\\n\\n        ref = self._unit(np.array([np.mean(g1), np.mean(g2), np.mean(g3), np.tanh(logp)]))\\n        cand = self._unit(np.array([g1[0], g2[0], g3[0], np.tanh(logp + 0.1 * rank)]))\\n        alignment = (float(np.dot(ref, cand)) + 1.0) / 2.0\\n\\n        fragment_score = 1.6 * alignment - 1.15 * consistency\\n        total = (1.0 - lam) * (0.75 * logp + 0.25 * fragment_score) \\\\\\n            + lam * (1.25 * logp + 0.85 * fragment_score)\\n        return total, consistency\\n\\n\\ndef adiabatic_lambda(step: int, total_steps: int) -> float:\\n    u = min(1.0, max(0.0, step / max(1, total_steps - 1)))\\n    return 3.0 * u * u - 2.0 * u * u * u\\n\\n\\ndef softmax(values: Sequence[float], temperature: float = 1.0) -> np.ndarray:\\n    temp = max(1e-6, float(temperature))\\n    arr = np.asarray(values, dtype=float) / temp\\n    arr -= np.max(arr)\\n    exp = np.exp(np.clip(arr, -60, 60))\\n    return exp / max(float(exp.sum()), 1e-12)\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Checkpoints\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef save_checkpoint(path: str, model: NGramModel, fragments: NonIsomorphicFragments,\\n                    meta: dict) -> None:\\n    payload = {\\n        \\\"format\\\": FORMAT,\\n        \\\"cot\\\": current_cot_words(),\\n        \\\"fragments\\\": fragments.to_dict(),\\n        \\\"model\\\": model.to_dict(),\\n        \\\"meta\\\": meta,\\n    }\\n    with gzip.open(path, \\\"wt\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\\n        json.dump(payload, fh)\\n\\n\\ndef load_checkpoint(path: str):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Load a checkpoint and install its CoT vocabulary globally.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    with gzip.open(path, \\\"rt\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\\n        payload = json.load(fh)\\n    if payload.get(\\\"format\\\") != FORMAT:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"{path}: unsupported checkpoint format {payload.get('format')!r}\\\")\\n    set_cot_tokens(payload[\\\"cot\\\"])\\n    model = NGramModel.from_dict(payload[\\\"model\\\"])\\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments.from_dict(payload[\\\"fragments\\\"])\\n    return model, fragments, payload.get(\\\"meta\\\", {})\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Cybernetic controller (sensor -> comparator -> actuator)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass Controller:\\n    def __init__(self, temperature: float, rep_limit: float = 0.5, logp_floor: float = -4.5):\\n        self.temperature = temperature\\n        self.rep_limit = rep_limit\\n        self.logp_floor = logp_floor\\n        self.k = 0\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def repetition(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> float:\\n        words = strip_cot(tokens)\\n        if len(words) < 2:\\n            return 0.0\\n        return 1.0 - len(set(words)) / len(words)\\n\\n    def update(self, chunk: Sequence[str], mean_logp: float) -> Tuple[str, float]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Return (CoT token to emit, repetition measure).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        rep = self.repetition(chunk)\\n        if rep > self.rep_limit:\\n            cot = COT_DIVERGE\\n            self.temperature *= 1.15\\n        elif mean_logp < self.logp_floor:\\n            cot = COT_CONVERGE\\n            self.temperature *= 0.9\\n        else:\\n            cot = COT_CYCLE[self.k % len(COT_CYCLE)]\\n            self.k += 1\\n        self.temperature = float(np.clip(self.temperature, 0.3, 1.6))\\n        return cot, rep\\n\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass Candidate:\\n    token: str\\n    base_logp: float\\n    score: float\\n    consistency: float\\n    probability: float = 0.0\\n\\n\\ndef generate_chunk(model, fragments, context, n, step0, total, beam_size, tau, temperature, rng,\\n                   stop_on_cot=False):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generate up to n tokens after `context`.\\n\\n    Returns (new_tokens, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted_cot). With stop_on_cot the\\n    chunk ends the moment the MODEL emits a CoT token (returned in\\n    emitted_cot, not appended to new_tokens).\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    ctx = list(context)\\n    new, logps, hit_eos, emitted = [], [], False, None\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        lam = adiabatic_lambda(step0 + i, total)\\n        ranked = model.candidates(ctx, limit=max(40, beam_size * 8))\\n        scored: List[Candidate] = []\\n        for rank, (token, logp) in enumerate(ranked):\\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, rank, lam)\\n            if consistency <= tau:\\n                scored.append(Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency))\\n        if not scored:\\n            token, logp = ranked[0]\\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, 0, lam)\\n            scored = [Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency)]\\n\\n        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c.score, reverse=True)\\n        beam = scored[:max(1, beam_size)]\\n        probs = softmax([c.score for c in beam], temperature)\\n        chosen = beam[0] if temperature <= 0.01 else rng.choices(beam, weights=probs, k=1)[0]\\n\\n        if chosen.token == \\\"<eos>\\\":\\n            hit_eos = True\\n            break\\n        if stop_on_cot and chosen.token in COT:\\n            emitted = chosen.token\\n            logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\\n            break\\n        new.append(chosen.token)\\n        ctx.append(chosen.token)\\n        logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\\n    mean_logp = float(np.mean(logps)) if logps else 0.0\\n    return new, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted\\n\\n\\ndef cybernetic_run(model, fragments, prompt, cycles, chunk, chunks_per_cycle, window, beam_size,\\n                   tau, temperature, seed, learn, trace):\\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\\n\\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\\\"The\\\"]\\n    full = [COT_START] + seed_tokens          # everything produced so far\\n    context = list(full)                      # what the model sees this cycle\\n    total = max(1, cycles * chunks_per_cycle * chunk)\\n    step = 0\\n\\n    for c in range(cycles):\\n        for k in range(chunks_per_cycle):\\n            new, mean_logp, hit_eos, _ = generate_chunk(\\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, step, total,\\n                beam_size, tau, controller.temperature, rng)\\n            step += chunk\\n            cot, rep = controller.update(new, mean_logp)\\n\\n            if trace:\\n                print(f\\\"[cycle {c+1}/{cycles} chunk {k+1}] tokens={len(new)} \\\"\\n                      f\\\"mean_logp={mean_logp:.2f} rep={rep:.2f} \\\"\\n                      f\\\"-> {cot} (T={controller.temperature:.2f})\\\")\\n\\n            # Feedback learning: only from healthy output, to avoid reinforcing loops.\\n            if learn and new and rep <= controller.rep_limit:\\n                model.learn(context[-(model.order - 1):] + new + [cot])\\n\\n            context += new + [cot]\\n            full += new + [cot]\\n            if hit_eos:\\n                break\\n\\n        # Pipe output back to input: new prompt begins with a CoT token.\\n        tail = full[-window:]\\n        context = [COT_INTEGRATE] + tail\\n        full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\\n\\n    return full\\n\\n\\ndef stacked_run(model, fragments, prompt, target_depth, chunk, window, beam_size, tau, temperature,\\n                seed, learn, max_retries, strict, trace):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Keep generating until CoT tokens stack up in the correct order.\\n\\n    The model must itself emit the next expected CoT token\\n    (the order defined in COT_CYCLE, repeating) after a chunk of\\n    real content. A wrong or missing token rejects the chunk and it is\\n    regenerated (temperature creeps up on each retry). Accepted chunks are\\n    pushed onto the stack, which only ever grows (monotonic), and are learned\\n    online so the model gets better at the pattern as it goes.\\n\\n    After `max_retries` misses the expected token is forced in (flagged), unless\\n    `strict` is set, in which case it keeps trying until the attempt cap.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\\n\\n    full = [COT_START] + (tokenize(prompt) or [\\\"The\\\"])\\n    context = list(full)\\n    stack: List[str] = []\\n    forced = 0\\n    attempts = 0\\n    max_attempts = target_depth * (200 if strict else max_retries + 1)\\n\\n    while len(stack) < target_depth and attempts < max_attempts:\\n        expected = COT_CYCLE[len(stack) % len(COT_CYCLE)]\\n        retries = 0\\n        accepted, was_forced = False, False\\n        while attempts < max_attempts:\\n            temp = float(np.clip(controller.temperature * (1.0 + 0.1 * retries), 0.3, 1.8))\\n            new, mlp, eos, emitted = generate_chunk(\\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, len(stack) * chunk,\\n                target_depth * chunk, beam_size, tau, temp, rng, stop_on_cot=True)\\n            attempts += 1\\n            ok = emitted == expected and len(new) > 0\\n            msg = (f\\\"depth {len(stack)}/{target_depth} attempt {attempts} \\\"\\n                   f\\\"expected {expected} got {emitted or 'none'} \\\"\\n                   f\\\"{'OK' if ok else 'retry'} (T={temp:.2f}, forced={forced})\\\")\\n            if trace:\\n                print(msg, file=sys.stderr)\\n            else:\\n                print(\\\"\\\\r\\\" + msg.ljust(78), end=\\\"\\\", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\\n            if ok:\\n                accepted = True\\n                break\\n            retries += 1\\n            if retries > max_retries and not strict:\\n                was_forced = True\\n                break\\n        if not (accepted or was_forced):\\n            break  # attempt cap hit in strict mode\\n\\n        if was_forced:\\n            forced += 1\\n        stack.append(expected)\\n        context += new + [expected]\\n        full += new + [expected]\\n        if new:\\n            controller.update(new, mlp)\\n        if accepted and learn:\\n            model.learn(context[-(model.order - 1) - len(new) - 1:])\\n\\n        # Pipe output back to input at the end of each full CoT cycle.\\n        if len(stack) % PIPE_EVERY == 0:\\n            context = [COT_INTEGRATE] + full[-window:]\\n            full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\\n\\n    if not trace:\\n        print(file=sys.stderr)\\n    monotonic = all(stack[i] == COT_CYCLE[i % len(COT_CYCLE)] for i in range(len(stack)))\\n    stats = dict(depth=len(stack), target=target_depth, attempts=attempts,\\n                 forced=forced, monotonic=monotonic)\\n    return full, stats\\n\\n\\ndef detokenize(tokens: Sequence[str], hide_cot: bool) -> str:\\n    return \\\" \\\".join(strip_cot(tokens) if hide_cot else tokens)\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# CLI\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef die(msg: str) -> None:\\n    print(f\\\"error: {msg}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n    sys.exit(2)\\n\\n\\ndef read_corpus(path: str) -> str:\\n    p = Path(path)\\n    if not p.is_file():\\n        die(f\\\"corpus file not found: {p}\\\")\\n    try:\\n        text = p.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8-sig\\\")\\n    except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\\n        die(f\\\"could not decode {p} as UTF-8: {exc}\\\")\\n    if not tokenize(text):\\n        die(f\\\"{p} contains no tokens\\\")\\n    return text\\n\\n\\ndef add_vocab_args(p: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--cot-vocab\\\", help=\\\"Custom CoT vocabulary file (one word per line, used in order).\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--cot-sort\\\", choices=[\\\"none\\\", \\\"alpha\\\", \\\"alpha-desc\\\", \\\"length\\\"], default=\\\"none\\\",\\n                   help=\\\"Sort the custom list before use (default: keep file order).\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_build(args) -> None:\\n    texts = [read_corpus(c) for c in args.corpus]\\n    if args.cot_vocab:\\n        words = load_cot_vocab(args.cot_vocab, args.cot_sort)\\n    else:\\n        words = select_cot_tokens(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(texts), args.seed)\\n    set_cot_tokens(words)\\n    print(\\\"CoT vocab: \\\" + \\\" \\\".join(current_cot_words()), file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\\n    for text in texts:\\n        model.train(text, cot=not args.no_cot_weave)\\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(args.seed)\\n    meta = {\\\"seed\\\": args.seed, \\\"extensions\\\": 0, \\\"sources\\\": [Path(c).name for c in args.corpus]}\\n    save_checkpoint(args.output, model, fragments, meta)\\n    print(f\\\"built {args.output}: {len(model.vocab)} types, {model.total_tokens:g} tokens\\\",\\n          file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_extend(args) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        model, fragments, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\\n    except (OSError, ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\\n        die(str(exc))\\n    old_words = current_cot_words()\\n\\n    if args.alpha is not None:\\n        model.alpha = max(1e-9, args.alpha)\\n\\n    if args.cot_vocab:\\n        new_words = load_cot_vocab(args.cot_vocab, args.cot_sort)\\n        mapping = {o: n for o, n in zip(old_words, new_words) if o != n}\\n        if mapping:\\n            clash = [n for n in mapping.values() if n in model.vocab and n not in mapping]\\n            if clash:\\n                print(\\\"warning: new CoT words already occur as ordinary words in the weights \\\"\\n                      f\\\"and will merge with them: {', '.join(sorted(clash)[:8])}\\\"\\n                      + (\\\" ...\\\" if len(clash) > 8 else \\\"\\\"), file=sys.stderr)\\n            model.remap_tokens(mapping)\\n            print(f\\\"remapped {len(mapping)} CoT tokens onto the new vocabulary\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        set_cot_tokens(new_words)\\n    print(\\\"CoT vocab: \\\" + \\\" \\\".join(current_cot_words()), file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    if args.decay != 1.0:\\n        model.scale(args.decay)\\n        print(f\\\"decayed existing weights by {args.decay}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    for path in args.corpus:\\n        model.train(read_corpus(path), cot=not args.no_cot_weave)\\n        meta.setdefault(\\\"sources\\\", []).append(Path(path).name)\\n    meta[\\\"extensions\\\"] = meta.get(\\\"extensions\\\", 0) + 1\\n\\n    save_checkpoint(args.output, model, fragments, meta)\\n    print(f\\\"extended -> {args.output}: {len(model.vocab)} types, {model.total_tokens:g} tokens\\\",\\n          file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_info(args) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        model, fragments, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\\n    except (OSError, ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\\n        die(str(exc))\\n    print(f\\\"format       {FORMAT}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"order        {model.order}   alpha {model.alpha}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"vocab types  {len(model.vocab)}   tokens {model.total_tokens:g}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"contexts     \\\" + \\\", \\\".join(f\\\"n={i}: {len(lv)}\\\" for i, lv in enumerate(model.counts)))\\n    print(f\\\"extensions   {meta.get('extensions', 0)}   sources {', '.join(meta.get('sources', []))}\\\")\\n    print(\\\"cycle        \\\" + \\\" \\\".join(str(t) for t in COT_CYCLE))\\n    print(f\\\"diverge={COT_DIVERGE} converge={COT_CONVERGE} \\\"\\n          f\\\"integrate={COT_INTEGRATE} start={COT_START}\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_generate(args) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        model, fragments, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\\n    except (OSError, ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\\n        die(str(exc))\\n    print(\\\"CoT vocab: \\\" + \\\" \\\".join(current_cot_words()), file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    first = True\\n    while True:\\n        try:\\n            prompt = args.prompt if (args.prompt and first) else input(\\\"USER: \\\")\\n        except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):\\n            print()\\n            break\\n        first = False\\n\\n        tau = float(np.clip(args.tau, 0.0, 1.0))\\n        temp = max(0.0, args.temperature)\\n        if args.stack_target > 0:\\n            full, stats = stacked_run(\\n                model, fragments, prompt, target_depth=args.stack_target, chunk=args.chunk,\\n                window=args.window, beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp,\\n                seed=args.seed, learn=not args.no_learn,\\n                max_retries=args.max_retries, strict=args.strict, trace=args.trace)\\n            print(f\\\"\\\\n[stack] depth {stats['depth']}/{stats['target']}  attempts {stats['attempts']}  \\\"\\n                  f\\\"forced {stats['forced']}  monotonic order verified: {stats['monotonic']}\\\")\\n        else:\\n            full = cybernetic_run(\\n                model, fragments, prompt, cycles=args.cycles, chunk=args.chunk,\\n                chunks_per_cycle=args.chunks_per_cycle, window=args.window,\\n                beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp, seed=args.seed,\\n                learn=not args.no_learn, trace=args.trace)\\n\\n        text = detokenize(full, hide_cot=not args.show_cot)\\n        print(\\\"\\\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\\\n\\\")\\n        print(text)\\n        print()\\n        if args.save:\\n            with open(args.save, \\\"a\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\\n                fh.write(text + \\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n    if args.save_model:\\n        meta[\\\"extensions\\\"] = meta.get(\\\"extensions\\\", 0) + 1\\n        save_checkpoint(args.save_model, model, fragments, meta)\\n        print(f\\\"saved weights -> {args.save_model}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n\\ndef main() -> None:\\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\\\"CoT weight extender for the cybernetic n-gram generator.\\\")\\n    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest=\\\"cmd\\\", required=True)\\n\\n    b = sub.add_parser(\\\"build\\\", help=\\\"Train a new checkpoint from corpora.\\\")\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"corpus\\\", nargs=\\\"+\\\", help=\\\"UTF-8 text corpus file(s).\\\")\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"-o\\\", \\\"--output\\\", required=True, help=\\\"Checkpoint to write (.cotw.gz).\\\")\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"--order\\\", type=int, default=3)\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"--alpha\\\", type=float, default=0.25)\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"--seed\\\", type=int, default=7)\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"--no-cot-weave\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Do not weave CoT tokens into the corpus.\\\")\\n    add_vocab_args(b)\\n    b.set_defaults(func=cmd_build)\\n\\n    e = sub.add_parser(\\\"extend\\\", help=\\\"Extend an existing checkpoint.\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"model\\\", help=\\\"Checkpoint to extend.\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"corpus\\\", nargs=\\\"*\\\", help=\\\"Additional corpus file(s) (optional).\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"-o\\\", \\\"--output\\\", required=True, help=\\\"Checkpoint to write.\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"--decay\\\", type=float, default=1.0,\\n                   help=\\\"Scale existing weights by this factor before adding new data (e.g. 0.9).\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"--alpha\\\", type=float, default=None, help=\\\"Override smoothing alpha.\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"--no-cot-weave\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Do not weave CoT tokens into new corpora.\\\")\\n    add_vocab_args(e)\\n    e.set_defaults(func=cmd_extend)\\n\\n    i = sub.add_parser(\\\"info\\\", help=\\\"Show checkpoint statistics.\\\")\\n    i.add_argument(\\\"model\\\")\\n    i.set_defaults(func=cmd_info)\\n\\n    g = sub.add_parser(\\\"generate\\\", help=\\\"Run the cybernetic loop from a checkpoint.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"model\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--prompt\\\", help=\\\"Initial prompt. If omitted you are asked each round.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--cycles\\\", type=int, default=4, help=\\\"Output->input feedback cycles per prompt.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--chunk\\\", type=int, default=20, help=\\\"Tokens per chunk between CoT tokens.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--chunks-per-cycle\\\", type=int, default=3)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--window\\\", type=int, default=40, help=\\\"Tokens of output piped back as the next prompt.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--beam\\\", type=int, default=8)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--tau\\\", type=float, default=0.65)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--temperature\\\", type=float, default=0.85)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--seed\\\", type=int, default=7)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--stack-target\\\", type=int, default=25,\\n                   help=\\\"Keep going until this many CoT tokens have stacked in order (0 = old fixed-cycle mode).\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--max-retries\\\", type=int, default=25, help=\\\"Rejected chunks allowed per stack slot before forcing.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--strict\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Never force a token; retry until the attempt cap.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--no-learn\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Disable online learning from own output.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--show-cot\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Show CoT tokens in printed text (hidden by default).\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--trace\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Print controller diagnostics.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--save\\\", help=\\\"Append output to this text file.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--save-model\\\", help=\\\"Write the weights (incl. online learning) to this checkpoint at exit.\\\")\\n    g.set_defaults(func=cmd_generate)\\n\\n    args = ap.parse_args()\\n    args.func(args)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\n\", \"filename\": \"/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:08:58.562293Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:08:58.562341Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01G3FUQCC3yAzKmt6cpokXZz", "name": "create_file", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": {"type": "text", "text": "File created successfully: /mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:09:01.663999Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:09:06.600120Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Tn8eJcWjYeGR1QsJAxzVuA", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp && rm -rf t && mkdir t && cd t && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport random\nrandom.seed(1)\nw=\"machine thought signal memory pattern energy system loop feedback network learning model state vector entropy order chaos light dark river stone\".split()\nlines=[]\nfor _ in range(400):\n    lines.append(\" \".join(random.choice(w) for _ in range(random.randint(5,12)))+random.choice(\".!?\"))\nopen(\"corpus.txt\",\"w\").write(\" \".join(lines))\nopen(\"more.txt\",\"w\").write(\" \".join(lines[:100]))\n# sorted custom cot list (29 words, alpha sorted)\ncot=\"alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel india juliet kilo lima mike november oscar papa quebec romeo sierra tango uniform victor whiskey xray yankee zulu diverge converge integrate begin\".split()\nopen(\"cot.txt\",\"w\").write(\"\\n\".join(sorted(cot[:25]))+\"\\n\"+\"\\n\".join(cot[25:])+\"\\n\")\nopen(\"new.txt\",\"w\").write(\"# test\\n\"+\"\\n\".join(f\"w{c}x\" for c in \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABC\")+\"\\n\")\nEOF\nS=/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py\npython3 $S build corpus.txt -o base.cotw.gz --cot-vocab cot.txt && \\\npython3 $S extend base.cotw.gz more.txt -o v2.cotw.gz --decay 0.9 && \\\npython3 $S extend v2.cotw.gz -o v3.cotw.gz --cot-vocab new.txt --cot-sort alpha && \\\npython3 $S info v3.cotw.gz && \\\npython3 $S generate v3.cotw.gz --prompt \"The machine\" --stack-target 8 --chunk 10 --save-model v4.cotw.gz 2>&1 </dev/null | tail -8 && \\\npython3 $S generate v4.cotw.gz --prompt \"The machine\" --stack-target 0 --cycles 2 --show-cot </dev/null 2>&1 | tail -4", "description": "Smoke-test build, extend with remap, info, generate, save-model"}, "message": "Smoke-test build, extend with remap, info, generate, save-model", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /tmp && rm -rf t && mkdir t && cd t && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport random\\nrandom.seed(1)\\nw=\\\"machine thought signal memory pattern energy system loop feedback network learning model state vector entropy order chaos light dark river stone\\\".split()\\nlines=[]\\nfor _ in range(400):\\n    lines.append(\\\" \\\".join(random.choice(w) for _ in range(random.randint(5,12)))+random.choice(\\\".!?\\\"))\\nopen(\\\"corpus.txt\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(\\\" \\\".join(lines))\\nopen(\\\"more.txt\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(\\\" \\\".join(lines[:100]))\\n# sorted custom cot list (29 words, alpha sorted)\\ncot=\\\"alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel india juliet kilo lima mike november oscar papa quebec romeo sierra tango uniform victor whiskey xray yankee zulu diverge converge integrate begin\\\".split()\\nopen(\\\"cot.txt\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(sorted(cot[:25]))+\\\"\\\\n\\\"+\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(cot[25:])+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\\nopen(\\\"new.txt\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(\\\"# test\\\\n\\\"+\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(f\\\"w{c}x\\\" for c in \\\"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABC\\\")+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\\nEOF\\nS=/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py\\npython3 $S build corpus.txt -o base.cotw.gz --cot-vocab cot.txt && \\\\\\npython3 $S extend base.cotw.gz more.txt -o v2.cotw.gz --decay 0.9 && \\\\\\npython3 $S extend v2.cotw.gz -o v3.cotw.gz --cot-vocab new.txt --cot-sort alpha && \\\\\\npython3 $S info v3.cotw.gz && \\\\\\npython3 $S generate v3.cotw.gz --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" --stack-target 8 --chunk 10 --save-model v4.cotw.gz 2>&1 </dev/null | tail -8 && \\\\\\npython3 $S generate v4.cotw.gz --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" --stack-target 0 --cycles 2 --show-cot </dev/null 2>&1 | tail -4\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:09:08.582738Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:09:08.582791Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Tn8eJcWjYeGR1QsJAxzVuA", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"format       cot-weights-v1\\norder        3   alpha 0.25\\nvocab types  110   tokens 4393.5\\ncontexts     n=0: 1, n=1: 110, n=2: 1440\\nextensions   2   sources corpus.txt, more.txt\\ncycle        wax wbx wcx wdx wex wfx wgx whx wix wjx wkx wlx wmx wnx wox wpx wqx wrx wsx wtx wux wvx wwx wxx wyx\\ndiverge=wzx converge=simulate integrate=recall start=correct\\n[stack] depth 8/8  attempts 143  forced 4  monotonic order verified: True\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\nThe machine stone entropy learning chaos chaos light? entropy dark chaos network pattern entropy model state? order memory pattern state memory memory learning learning dark machine loop network system state entropy? light energy thought loop light vector memory! memory learning feedback. memory model feedback! pattern memory state thought loop learning!\\n\\nUSER: \\nsaved weights -> v4.cotw.gz\\n\\ncorrect The machine stone entrop