all\\n\\nUSER: \\n\",\"stderr\":\"note: 30 CoT words given, using the first 29\\nCoT vocab: alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel india juliet kilo lima mike november oscar papa quebec romeo sierra tango uniform victor whiskey xray yankee zulu diverge converge integrate\\nbuilt base.cotw.gz: 110 types, 3835 tokens\\nCoT vocab: alpha bravo charlie delta echo foxtrot golf hotel india juliet kilo lima mike november oscar papa quebec romeo sierra tango uniform victor whiskey xray yankee zulu diverge converge integrate\\ndecayed existing weights by 0.9\\nextended -> v2.cotw.gz: 110 types, 4393.5 tokens\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'wAx' at line 28 ignored\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'wBx' at line 29 ignored\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'wCx' at line 30 ignored\\nnote: only 26 CoT words given, filling to 29 from fallback names\\nremapped 29 CoT tokens onto the new vocabulary\\nCoT vocab: wax wbx wcx wdx wex wfx wgx whx wix wjx wkx wlx wmx wnx wox wpx wqx wrx wsx wtx wux wvx wwx wxx wyx wzx simulate recall correct\\nextended -> v3.cotw.gz: 110 types, 4393.5 tokens\\n\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:09:10.920904Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:09:11.184402Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01FM72xBa5rc4QXqSDCbSjFx", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": "[\"/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py\""}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "[\"/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py\""]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:09:11.193606Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:09:11.193638Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01FM72xBa5rc4QXqSDCbSjFx", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Input validation errors occurred:\nfilepaths: Input should be a valid list"}], "is_error": true, "structured_content": null, "meta": null, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:09:15.295456Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:09:15.544359Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_018Rrvz5kZq7weasf3NStbSF", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:09:15.590702Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:09:15.590736Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_018Rrvz5kZq7weasf3NStbSF", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py", "name": "cot weight extender", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "\n\nThe file cards appear with your reply, and where they sit relative to its text depends on the app the user is reading in; finish the reply with text, and refer to a file by its name, never as above or below."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:09:21.995001Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:09:22.847820Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I turned the generator into `cot_weight_extender.py`, a model whose weights are saved to a checkpoint and can be grown later. I ran a small smoke test (build, extend with a new vocab, info, generate, save) and it all ran cleanly. \"Weight extender\" and \"sorted cognitive list\" were ambiguous, so I made two guesses you should check.\n\n**Commands**\n- `build corpus.txt -o base.cotw.gz --cot-vocab cot.txt` trains a new checkpoint.\n- `extend base.cotw.gz more.txt -o v2.cotw.gz --decay 0.9` adds corpora to an existing checkpoint. `--decay` scales the old weights down first so the new data counts for more.\n- `extend v2.cotw.gz -o v3.cotw.gz --cot-vocab newcot.txt` swaps in a new CoT vocabulary and carries the old learned behaviour over to the new words by position.\n- `generate v3.cotw.gz --prompt \"...\" --save-model v4.cotw.gz` runs the loop and writes out what it learned online.\n- `info v3.cotw.gz` prints the checkpoint's size and vocabulary.\n\n**Custom vocab (`--cot-vocab`)**\nThe file has one word per line, and the order is the stack order. Entries 1\u201325 are the cycle, then diverge, converge, integrate and start. I read \"sorted\" as \"the list's order is meaningful\": it is used as given by default, or sorted first with `--cot-sort alpha`, `alpha-desc` or `length`. If your list has fewer than 29 words, the rest are filled from fallback names. If it has more than 29, the extras are ignored. Words can't contain whitespace.\n\n**What's saved in a checkpoint**\nIt's a gzip JSON file with the n-gram counts, the vocabulary, the fragment matrices that were previously regenerated from the seed, the CoT vocabulary, and a small meta block. The n-gram order is fixed when you build, so changing it means building again. Fragment weights stay frozen when you extend.\n\n**Things to know**\n- **Collisions on remap:** remapping renames words by string, so if a new CoT word also appears in your corpus as an ordinary word, the two merge. `extend` warns you when this happens, and uncommon words avoid it.\n- **Fallback list fix:** the old fallback list had `\"observe\"` twice, so a very small corpus could leave you with only 28 unique words and crash. I replaced the duplicate with `\"synthesize\"`.\n- **Stack mode on tiny corpora:** in my test it forced several tokens, which is normal when the corpus is that small.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-14T22:09:22.925475Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T22:09:22.925475Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a13c74-8976-7c61-92b9-16202b6f8123"}, {"uuid": "01a13c78-d2b6-7953-a860-b665c91eb1ef", "text": "change the kernel to invert the cot to the dataset scan", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:12:00.397029Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:12:00.397029Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "change the kernel to invert the cot to the dataset scan", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-14T22:12:00.397341Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T22:12:00.397341Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a13c74-8976-79e1-82ad-87f888a0efb1"}, {"uuid": "01a13c78-d2b6-718c-8235-01ada8f49f45", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI rewrote the kernel in `cot_weight_extender.py` so the CoT token scans the dataset instead of the dataset supplying CoT tokens. I read \"invert the cot to the dataset scan\" that way, so tell me if you meant something else. I ran a smoke test of build, extend, info, both generate modes, the kernel override and strict mode, and all of it ran.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Old direction (kept as `--kernel weave`):** the dataset gave you the CoT words, they were woven into the training stream, and the model had to emit them itself.\n- **New direction (`--kernel scan`, now the default):** a CoT token is a probe. The loop finds every occurrence of that word in the dataset, collects the tokens that follow each one, and uses them to boost matching candidates in the next chunk. CoT tokens are never woven into the weights and never appear in the n-gram context, so they only steer the scan. The last context word is also used as a second probe, at weight `--scan-mix` (default 0.5).\n- **Role profiles:** diverge reads more passages over a longer span, converge reads fewer over a shorter span, and integrate reads a longer span after the pipe-back. The controller picks the role the same way it did before.\n- **Stack mode:** a slot is accepted when the expected word is found in the dataset and enough of the chunk (`--min-grounding`, default 0.15) appears in the scanned passages. A word that never occurs in the dataset can't be grounded, so its slot is forced and flagged. With `--strict` the run stops there instead.\n- **Checkpoints:** they now store the dataset tokens, which the scanner reads, and the kernel name. Older v1 checkpoints still load as weave.\n- **Vocabulary swaps:** with the scan kernel, `extend --cot-vocab` just swaps the words, because there is nothing to remap.\n- **Coverage report:** `build`, `extend`, `info` and `generate` tell you how many of the 29 CoT words occur in the dataset.\n- **New flags on `generate`:** `--kernel` (override the checkpoint), `--scan-strength`, `--scan-limit`, `--scan-span`, `--scan-mix` and `--min-grounding`.\n\n**Things to know**\n- Your custom CoT words should actually appear in the dataset. In my test, 8 of 29 didn't. Non-strict runs forced those slots, and a strict run stopped at depth 5/25 on the first absent word.\n- `--decay` only scales the n-gram weights. The dataset the scanner reads is not decayed.\n- Checkpoints are larger now because they hold the full token stream.\n- I also fixed an old slicing bug: with `--order 1`, `context[-0:]` returned the whole context in the online-learning step, and a helper now returns an empty list.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:12:00.396777Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:13:39.641537Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Untangling how kernel mechanics relate to dataset scanning order."}, {"summary": "Reversing roles so cot tokens probe the dataset instead."}, {"summary": "Designing a scan kernel option with bias-weighted candidate generation."}, {"summary": "Blending probe words with context tokens to ground retrieval."}, {"summary": "Defining grounding checks and checkpoint handling for scan mode."}, {"summary": "Tuning scan parameters and weaving bias into chunk scoring."}, {"summary": "Implementing scanner class with probe-based bias weighting logic."}, {"summary": "Handling zero-hit cases and forced fallbacks under strict mode."}, {"summary": "Adjusting context tracking and learning windows for scan mode."}, {"summary": "Deciding how to persist checkpoint format and write updated file."}, {"summary": "Choosing targeted edits over a full file rewrite for the update."}, {"summary": "Planning additive run functions to avoid risky large replacements."}, {"summary": "Deciding to rewrite the whole file as one unified module."}, {"summary": "Merging stack-depth retries with scan-mode bias checking logic."}, {"summary": "Scoring grounding by comparing generated tokens against bias weights."}, {"summary": "Wiring command-line options for build, extend, and generate modes."}, {"summary": "Computing bias weights from probe positions and decay spans."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:13:39.641600Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:15:05.079515Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_013PycGbaXu9Z1JMMMyxafbQ", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cat > /mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py <<'PYEOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nCoT weight extender  (scan kernel)\n==================================\n\nThe cybernetic n-gram generator as a persistent, extendable model, with the CoT\nkernel INVERTED.\n\n  weave kernel (old)   dataset -> CoT.  CoT words are picked by scanning the\n                       dataset, woven into the training stream, and the model has\n                       to emit them itself.\n  scan kernel (new)    CoT -> dataset.  A CoT token is a PROBE: the loop scans the\n                       dataset for that word, collects the passages that follow\n                       each occurrence, and turns them into a bias over the next\n                       chunk's tokens. CoT tokens are never woven into the weights\n                       and never enter the n-gram context; they only steer the scan.\n\nScan profile per CoT role:\n  cycle token   standard scan\n  diverge       more passages, longer span, slower decay   (wider read, T up)\n  converge      fewer passages, shorter span, faster decay (tighter read, T down)\n  integrate     standard passages, longer span             (re-read after pipe-back)\n\nStack mode under the scan kernel: slot i is accepted when the expected CoT word is\nFOUND in the dataset and the generated chunk is grounded in the scanned passages\n(fraction of chunk tokens that occur in them >= --min-grounding). A word that never\noccurs in the dataset can't ground, so its slot is forced (flagged), or the run\nstops early with --strict.\n\nCommands\n  build     Train a new checkpoint from one or more corpora.\n  extend    Grow a checkpoint: more corpora, optional decay, optional new CoT vocab.\n  generate  Run the cybernetic loop from a checkpoint (optionally save weights).\n  info      Print checkpoint statistics and CoT-vocab coverage of the dataset.\n\nCustom CoT vocabulary (--cot-vocab FILE): one word per line ('#' comments ignored),\nused in order or sorted with --cot-sort:\n\n      entries  1..25   the stack cycle, in required order\n      entry    26      diverge\n      entry    27      converge\n      entry    28      integrate\n      entry    29      start\n\nWith the scan kernel the words should occur in the dataset (build/info report\ncoverage); a swap of vocabulary on `extend` is free, nothing needs remapping.\nWith the legacy weave kernel, `extend --cot-vocab` transfers the old CoT weights\nonto the new words by position.\n\nCheckpoint = gzip JSON: n-gram counts, vocab, fragment matrices, the dataset token\nstream (what the scan kernel reads), the CoT vocabulary and a meta block.\n\nExamples:\n  python cot_weight_extender.py build corpus.txt -o base.cotw.gz --cot-vocab cot.txt\n  python cot_weight_extender.py extend base.cotw.gz more.txt -o v2.cotw.gz --decay 0.9\n  python cot_weight_extender.py generate v2.cotw.gz --prompt \"The machine\" --trace\n  python cot_weight_extender.py generate v2.cotw.gz --kernel weave --show-cot\n  python cot_weight_extender.py info v2.cotw.gz\n\nOnly dependency: NumPy\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport gzip\nimport json\nimport math\nimport random\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Sequence, Tuple\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nFORMAT = \"cot-weights-v2\"\nACCEPTED_FORMATS = (\"cot-weights-v1\", FORMAT)\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# CoT tokens\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass CotToken(str):\n    \"\"\"A CoT marker inserted by the loop. It is a str, but isinstance() tells it\n    apart from the same word appearing as ordinary text, so hiding markers never\n    deletes real words from the output.\"\"\"\n\n\n# Fallback names, used only if the vocabulary source has too few distinct words.\nDEFAULT_COT = [\n    \"simulate\", \"recall\", \"correct\", \"imagine\", \"decide\",\n    \"observe\", \"verify\", \"associate\", \"plan\", \"anticipate\",\n    \"reflect\", \"abstract\", \"act\", \"question\", \"compare\",\n    \"adapt\", \"predict\", \"summarize\", \"monitor\", \"infer\",\n    \"consolidate\", \"attend\", \"evaluate\", \"prioritize\", \"hypothesize\",\n    \"diverge\", \"converge\", \"integrate\", \"synthesize\",\n]\nCOT_COUNT = 29  # 25 cycle tokens + diverge + converge + integrate + start\nPIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens\nSENTENCE_END = (\".\", \"!\", \"?\")\n\nCOT_CYCLE: List[str] = []\nCOT_DIVERGE = COT_CONVERGE = COT_INTEGRATE = COT_START = CotToken(\"\")\nCOT: set = set()\n\n_STOP = {\n    \"that\", \"with\", \"have\", \"from\", \"this\", \"they\", \"were\", \"been\", \"will\", \"would\", \"there\",\n    \"their\", \"what\", \"when\", \"which\", \"your\", \"them\", \"then\", \"than\", \"into\", \"only\", \"also\",\n    \"some\", \"such\", \"more\", \"most\", \"other\", \"about\", \"could\", \"should\", \"these\", \"those\",\n}\n\n\ndef set_cot_tokens(words: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Install the CoT vocabulary: 25 cycle tokens, then diverge, converge,\n    integrate, start.\"\"\"\n    global COT_CYCLE, COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START, COT\n    toks = [CotToken(w) for w in words]\n    COT_CYCLE = toks[:25]\n    COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START = toks[25:29]\n    COT = {str(t) for t in toks}\n\n\ndef current_cot_words() -> List[str]:\n    return [str(t) for t in COT_CYCLE] + [str(COT_DIVERGE), str(COT_CONVERGE),\n                                          str(COT_INTEGRATE), str(COT_START)]\n\n\ndef _top_up(words: List[str], count: int) -> List[str]:\n    seen = {w.lower() for w in words}\n    for d in DEFAULT_COT:\n        if len(words) >= count:\n            break\n        if d.lower() not in seen:\n            seen.add(d.lower())\n            words.append(d)\n    return words\n\n\ndef select_cot_tokens(text: str, seed: int, count: int = COT_COUNT) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Pick CoT tokens from the dataset: the most frequent alphabetic words of\n    4+ letters (skipping common function words), shuffled so the required order is\n    non-monotonic. Used when no --cot-vocab is given.\"\"\"\n    counts = Counter(tokenize(text))\n    pool = [(w, c) for w, c in counts.items()\n            if w.isalpha() and len(w) >= 4 and w.lower() not in _STOP]\n    pool.sort(key=lambda wc: (-wc[1], wc[0]))\n    words, seen = [], set()\n    for w, _ in pool:\n        if w.lower() not in seen:\n            seen.add(w.lower())\n            words.append(w)\n        if len(words) >= count:\n            break\n    random.Random(seed).shuffle(words)\n    return _top_up(words, count)\n\n\ndef load_cot_vocab(path: str, sort: str = \"none\", count: int = COT_COUNT) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Load a custom CoT vocabulary from a text file (one word per line).\n\n    sort: 'none' keeps file order (use when the list is already sorted the way you\n    want the stack to run), 'alpha' / 'alpha-desc' sort case-insensitively,\n    'length' sorts short to long. Sorting happens BEFORE truncating to `count`.\n    \"\"\"\n    words, seen = [], set()\n    for lineno, line in enumerate(Path(path).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\").splitlines(), 1):\n        w = line.split(\"#\", 1)[0].strip()\n        if not w:\n            continue\n        if len(w.split()) != 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{path}:{lineno}: CoT words must be a single token, got {w!r}\")\n        if w.lower() in seen:\n            print(f\"warning: duplicate CoT word {w!r} at line {lineno} ignored\", file=sys.stderr)\n            continue\n        seen.add(w.lower())\n        words.append(w)\n    if sort == \"alpha\":\n        words.sort(key=str.lower)\n    elif sort == \"alpha-desc\":\n        words.sort(key=str.lower, reverse=True)\n    elif sort == \"length\":\n        words.sort(key=lambda w: (len(w), w.lower()))\n    if len(words) > count:\n        print(f\"note: {len(words)} CoT words given, using the first {count}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        words = words[:count]\n    elif len(words) < count:\n        print(f\"note: only {len(words)} CoT words given, filling to {count} from fallback names\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        words = _top_up(words, count)\n    return words\n\n\nset_cot_tokens(DEFAULT_COT)\n\n\ndef tokenize(text: str) -> List[str]:\n    return text.split()\n\n\ndef strip_cot(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> List[str]:\n    return [t for t in tokens if not isinstance(t, CotToken)]\n\n\ndef tail_ctx(tokens: Sequence[str], k: int) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Last k tokens (empty for k <= 0; avoids the tokens[-0:] whole-list trap).\"\"\"\n    return list(tokens[len(tokens) - k:]) if k > 0 else []\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Dataset scanner (the inverted kernel: CoT token -> dataset passages -> bias)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef norm_word(w: str) -> str:\n    return str(w).strip(\".,;:!?\\\"'()[]{}\").lower()\n\n\n# role -> (passage multiplier, span multiplier, per-step decay)\nSCAN_PROFILES = {\n    \"cycle\": (1.0, 1.0, 0.85),\n    \"diverge\": (2.0, 2.0, 0.92),\n    \"converge\": (0.5, 0.5, 0.75),\n    \"integrate\": (1.0, 1.5, 0.88),\n    \"start\": (1.0, 1.0, 0.85),\n}\n\n\ndef cot_role(tok: str) -> str:\n    s = str(tok)\n    if s == str(COT_DIVERGE):\n        return \"diverge\"\n    if s == str(COT_CONVERGE):\n        return \"converge\"\n    if s == str(COT_INTEGRATE):\n        return \"integrate\"\n    if s == str(COT_START):\n        return \"start\"\n    return \"cycle\"\n\n\nclass DatasetScanner:\n    \"\"\"Inverted index over the dataset token stream. A CoT token is used as a key:\n    every occurrence of its word is located, the `span` tokens that follow are\n    collected with geometric decay, and the result is a bias in [0, 1] over tokens.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, tokens: List[str], strength: float = 1.5, limit: int = 24,\n                 span: int = 12, mix: float = 0.5):\n        self.tokens = tokens\n        self.strength = strength\n        self.limit = max(1, int(limit))\n        self.span = max(2, int(span))\n        self.mix = max(0.0, float(mix))\n        self._index = None\n\n    @property\n    def index(self) -> Dict[str, List[int]]:\n        if self._index is None:\n            idx = defaultdict(list)\n            for i, t in enumerate(self.tokens):\n                idx[norm_word(t)].append(i)\n            self._index = idx\n        return self._index\n\n    def extend(self, tokens: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n        self.tokens.extend(tokens)\n        self._index = None\n\n    def hits(self, word: str) -> int:\n        return len(self.index.get(norm_word(word), ()))\n\n    def coverage(self, words: Sequence[str]) -> Tuple[int, List[str]]:\n        missing = [w for w in words if self.hits(w) == 0]\n        return len(words) - len(missing), missing\n\n    def bias(self, cot: str, context: Sequence[str], rng: random.Random) -> Tuple[Dict[str, float], int]:\n        \"\"\"Scan with `cot` as probe (plus, at weight `mix`, the last context word).\n        Returns (normalised bias over tokens, number of dataset hits for `cot`).\"\"\"\n        limit_mult, span_mult, decay = SCAN_PROFILES[cot_role(cot)]\n        limit = max(1, int(round(self.limit * limit_mult)))\n        span = max(2, int(round(self.span * span_mult)))\n        probes = [(str(cot), 1.0)]\n        if context and self.mix > 0:\n            probes.append((str(context[-1]), self.mix))\n        weights: Counter = Counter()\n        cot_hits = 0\n        n = len(self.tokens)\n        for pi, (word, w) in enumerate(probes):\n            pos = self.index.get(norm_word(word), [])\n            if pi == 0:\n                cot_hits = len(pos)\n            if not pos:\n                continue\n            if len(pos) > limit:\n                pos = rng.sample(pos, limit)\n            share = w / len(pos)\n            for p in pos:\n                for off in range(1, span + 1):\n                    j = p + off\n                    if j >= n:\n                        break\n                    weights[self.tokens[j]] += share * (decay ** (off - 1))\n        if not weights:\n            return {}, cot_hits\n        top = max(weights.values())\n        return {t: v / top for t, v in weights.items()}, cot_hits\n\n\ndef grounding(new: Sequence[str], bias) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Fraction of generated tokens that occur in the scanned passages.\"\"\"\n    if not new or not bias:\n        return 0.0\n    return sum(1 for t in new if t in bias) / len(new)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# N-gram model (serialisation, decay, merge and token remapping)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass NGramModel:\n    \"\"\"Smoothed n-gram model with backoff, trainable offline and online.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, order: int = 3, alpha: float = 0.25):\n        self.order = max(1, int(order))\n        self.alpha = max(1e-9, float(alpha))\n        self.counts = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(self.order)]\n        self.vocab = Counter()\n        self.total_tokens = 0\n\n    def _update(self, tokens: Sequence[str], start: int) -> None:\n        for i in range(start, len(tokens)):\n            target = tokens[i]\n            self.vocab[target] += 1\n            self.total_tokens += 1\n            for ctx_len in range(self.order):\n                if ctx_len > i:\n                    break\n                context = tuple(tokens[i - ctx_len:i]) if ctx_len else ()\n                self.counts[ctx_len][context][target] += 1\n\n    def train(self, text: str, cot: bool = True) -> None:\n        \"\"\"cot=True weaves CoT tokens in after each sentence (weave kernel).\n        The scan kernel trains with cot=False: the weights never see CoT tokens.\"\"\"\n        raw = tokenize(text)\n        if cot:\n            woven, k = [], 0\n            for tok in raw:\n                woven.append(tok)\n                if tok.endswith(SENTENCE_END):\n                    woven.append(COT_CYCLE[k % len(COT_CYCLE)])\n                    k += 1\n            raw = woven\n        tokens = [\"<bos>\"] * (self.order - 1) + raw + [\"<eos>\"]\n        self._update(tokens, self.order - 1)\n\n    def learn(self, tokens: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Online update from the model's own output (feedback learning).\"\"\"\n        self._update(list(tokens), 1)\n\n    # ---- weight extension ------------------------------------------------\n    def scale(self, factor: float) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Multiply every stored weight (decay old knowledge before extending).\"\"\"\n        if factor == 1.0:\n            return\n        for level in self.counts:\n            for counter in level.values():\n                for tok in counter:\n                    counter[tok] *= factor\n        for tok in self.vocab:\n            self.vocab[tok] *= factor\n        self.total_tokens *= factor\n\n    def remap_tokens(self, mapping: Dict[str, str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Rename tokens everywhere (contexts and targets). Colliding counts are\n        summed. Weave kernel only: transfers CoT behaviour to a new vocabulary.\"\"\"\n        if not mapping:\n            return\n\n        def m(t):\n            return mapping.get(t, t)\n\n        new_counts = []\n        for level in self.counts:\n            nl = defaultdict(Counter)\n            for ctx, counter in level.items():\n                nctx = tuple(m(t) for t in ctx)\n                for tok, n in counter.items():\n                    nl[nctx][m(tok)] += n\n            new_counts.append(nl)\n        self.counts = new_counts\n        nv = Counter()\n        for tok, n in self.vocab.items():\n            nv[m(tok)] += n\n        self.vocab = nv\n\n    # ---- serialisation ---------------------------------------------------\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return {\n            \"order\": self.order,\n            \"alpha\": self.alpha,\n            \"total_tokens\": self.total_tokens,\n            \"vocab\": {str(k): v for k, v in self.vocab.items()},\n            \"counts\": [[[list(ctx), {str(t): n for t, n in c.items()}]\n                        for ctx, c in level.items()] for level in self.counts],\n        }\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> \"NGramModel\":\n        model = cls(order=d[\"order\"], alpha=d[\"alpha\"])\n        model.total_tokens = d[\"total_tokens\"]\n        model.vocab = Counter(d[\"vocab\"])\n        model.counts = []\n        for level in d[\"counts\"]:\n            lv = defaultdict(Counter)\n            for ctx, counter in level:\n                lv[tuple(ctx)] = Counter(counter)\n            model.counts.append(lv)\n        return model\n\n    def candidates(self, context_tokens: Sequence[str], limit: int = 80) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:\n        vocab_size = max(1, len(self.vocab))\n        context = list(context_tokens)\n        counter = Counter()\n        for ctx_len in range(min(self.order - 1, len(context)), -1, -1):\n            key = tuple(context[-ctx_len:]) if ctx_len else ()\n            found = self.counts[ctx_len].get(key)\n            if not found:\n                continue\n            weight = 1.0 + 0.7 * ctx_len\n            for token, count in found.items():\n                counter[token] += weight * count\n            if ctx_len >= 1:\n                break\n        if not counter:\n            counter.update(self.vocab)\n        counter.pop(\"<bos>\", None)\n        total = sum(counter.values())\n        ranked = []\n        for token, count in counter.items():\n            prob = (count + self.alpha) / (total + self.alpha * vocab_size)\n            ranked.append((token, math.log(max(prob, 1e-12))))\n        ranked.sort(key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\n        return ranked[:max(1, limit)]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Non-isomorphic fragments (weights are saved with the checkpoint)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass NonIsomorphicFragments:\n    def __init__(self, seed: int = 17):\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        self.w_context = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 3))\n        self.w_word = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 4))\n        self.w_transition = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 2))\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return {\"w_context\": self.w_context.tolist(),\n                \"w_word\": self.w_word.tolist(),\n                \"w_transition\": self.w_transition.tolist()}\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> \"NonIsomorphicFragments\":\n        frag = cls(0)\n        frag.w_context = np.asarray(d[\"w_context\"], dtype=float)\n        frag.w_word = np.asarray(d[\"w_word\"], dtype=float)\n        frag.w_transition = np.asarray(d[\"w_transition\"], dtype=float)\n        return frag\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _unit(v: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        n = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\n        return v / n if n > 1e-12 else np.zeros_like(v)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _hash_features(token: str, width: int) -> np.ndarray:\n        raw = token.lower().encode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\")\n        vals = np.zeros(width, dtype=float)\n        if not raw:\n            return vals\n        for i, byte in enumerate(raw):\n            vals[i % width] += ((byte % 31) - 15) / 15.0\n            vals[(i * 3 + 1) % width] += ((byte % 17) - 8) / 8.0\n        vals /= max(1, len(raw))\n        vals[0] += min(len(raw), 20) / 20.0\n        vals[1] += sum(chr(b).isalpha() for b in raw) / max(1, len(raw))\n        return np.tanh(vals)\n\n    def features(self, context, token, logp, rank):\n        recent = list(context[-4:])\n        ctx_vec = np.zeros(5, dtype=float)\n        if recent:\n            for i, word in enumerate(recent):\n                f = self._hash_features(word, 5)\n                ctx_vec += f * (0.65 ** (len(recent) - i - 1))\n            ctx_vec /= max(1, len(recent))\n        word_vec = self._hash_features(token, 5)\n        transition_vec = np.array([\n            np.tanh(logp),\n            1.0 / (1.0 + rank),\n            1.0 if token[:1].isupper() else 0.0,\n            1.0 if token in COT else 0.0,  # CoT words are visible to the fragments\n            min(len(token), 24) / 24.0,\n        ], dtype=float)\n        g1 = np.tanh(ctx_vec @ self.w_context)\n        g2 = np.tanh(word_vec @ self.w_word)\n        g3 = np.tanh(transition_vec @ self.w_transition)\n        return g1, g2, g3\n\n    def score(self, context, token, logp, rank, lam) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n        g1, g2, g3 = self.features(context, token, logp, rank)\n        summaries = np.array([np.linalg.norm(g1), np.linalg.norm(g2), np.linalg.norm(g3)])\n        mean = float(np.mean(summaries))\n        spread = float(np.std(summaries) / (mean + 1e-9))\n        consistency = float(np.clip(0.55 * spread + 0.45 * (1.0 - mean), 0.0, 1.0))\n\n        ref = self._unit(np.array([np.mean(g1), np.mean(g2), np.mean(g3), np.tanh(logp)]))\n        cand = self._unit(np.array([g1[0], g2[0], g3[0], np.tanh(logp + 0.1 * rank)]))\n        alignment = (float(np.dot(ref, cand)) + 1.0) / 2.0\n\n        fragment_score = 1.6 * alignment - 1.15 * consistency\n        total = (1.0 - lam) * (0.75 * logp + 0.25 * fragment_score) \\\n            + lam * (1.25 * logp + 0.85 * fragment_score)\n        return total, consistency\n\n\ndef adiabatic_lambda(step: int, total_steps: int) -> float:\n    u = min(1.0, max(0.0, step / max(1, total_steps - 1)))\n    return 3.0 * u * u - 2.0 * u * u * u\n\n\ndef softmax(values: Sequence[float], temperature: float = 1.0) -> np.ndarray:\n    temp = max(1e-6, float(temperature))\n    arr = np.asarray(values, dtype=float) / temp\n    arr -= np.max(arr)\n    exp = np.exp(np.clip(arr, -60, 60))\n    return exp / max(float(exp.sum()), 1e-12)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Checkpoints\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef save_checkpoint(path: str, model: NGramModel, fragments: NonIsomorphicFragments,\n                    dataset: Sequence[str], meta: dict) -> None:\n    payload = {\n        \"format\": FORMAT,\n        \"cot\": current_cot_words(),\n        \"fragments\": fragments.to_dict(),\n        \"model\": model.to_dict(),\n        \"dataset\": list(dataset),\n        \"meta\": meta,\n    }\n    with gzip.open(path, \"wt\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n        json.dump(payload, fh)\n\n\ndef load_checkpoint(path: str):\n    \"\"\"Load a checkpoint and install its CoT vocabulary globally.\n    Returns (model, fragments, dataset_tokens, meta).\"\"\"\n    with gzip.open(path, \"rt\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n        payload = json.load(fh)\n    if payload.get(\"format\") not in ACCEPTED_FORMATS:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{path}: unsupported checkpoint format {payload.get('format')!r}\")\n    set_cot_tokens(payload[\"cot\"])\n    model = NGramModel.from_dict(payload[\"model\"])\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments.from_dict(payload[\"fragments\"])\n    dataset = list(payload.get(\"dataset\", []))\n    meta = payload.get(\"meta\", {})\n    meta.setdefault(\"kernel\", \"weave\")  # v1 checkpoints were woven\n    return model, fragments, dataset, meta\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Cybernetic controller (sensor -> comparator -> actuator)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass Controller:\n    def __init__(self, temperature: float, rep_limit: float = 0.5, logp_floor: float = -4.5):\n        self.temperature = temperature\n        self.rep_limit = rep_limit\n        self.logp_floor = logp_floor\n        self.k = 0\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def repetition(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> float:\n        words = strip_cot(tokens)\n        if len(words) < 2:\n            return 0.0\n        return 1.0 - len(set(words)) / len(words)\n\n    def update(self, chunk: Sequence[str], mean_logp: float) -> Tuple[str, float]:\n        \"\"\"Return (CoT token to emit, repetition measure).\"\"\"\n        rep = self.repetition(chunk)\n        if rep > self.rep_limit:\n            cot = COT_DIVERGE\n            self.temperature *= 1.15\n        elif mean_logp < self.logp_floor:\n            cot = COT_CONVERGE\n            self.temperature *= 0.9\n        else:\n            cot = COT_CYCLE[self.k % len(COT_CYCLE)]\n            self.k += 1\n        self.temperature = float(np.clip(self.temperature, 0.3, 1.6))\n        return cot, rep\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Candidate:\n    token: str\n    base_logp: float\n    score: float\n    consistency: float\n    probability: float = 0.0\n\n\ndef generate_chunk(model, fragments, context, n, step0, total, beam_size, tau, temperature, rng,\n                   stop_on_cot=False, bias=None, bias_strength=0.0):\n    \"\"\"Generate up to n tokens after `context`.\n\n    Returns (new_tokens, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted_cot). With stop_on_cot the\n    chunk ends the moment the MODEL emits a CoT token (weave kernel). With a\n    `bias` (scan kernel) each candidate's score gains bias_strength * bias[token],\n    where bias comes from the dataset scan.\n    \"\"\"\n    ctx = list(context)\n    new, logps, hit_eos, emitted = [], [], False, None\n    for i in range(n):\n        lam = adiabatic_lambda(step0 + i, total)\n        ranked = model.candidates(ctx, limit=max(40, beam_size * 8))\n        scored: List[Candidate] = []\n        for rank, (token, logp) in enumerate(ranked):\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, rank, lam)\n            if bias:\n                score += bias_strength * bias.get(token, 0.0)\n            if consistency <= tau:\n                scored.append(Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency))\n        if not scored:\n            token, logp = ranked[0]\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, 0, lam)\n            scored = [Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency)]\n\n        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c.score, reverse=True)\n        beam = scored[:max(1, beam_size)]\n        probs = softmax([c.score for c in beam], temperature)\n        chosen = beam[0] if temperature <= 0.01 else rng.choices(beam, weights=probs, k=1)[0]\n\n        if chosen.token == \"<eos>\":\n            hit_eos = True\n            break\n        if stop_on_cot and chosen.token in COT:\n            emitted = chosen.token\n            logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\n            break\n        new.append(chosen.token)\n        ctx.append(chosen.token)\n        logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\n    mean_logp = float(np.mean(logps)) if logps else 0.0\n    return new, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted\n\n\ndef cybernetic_run(model, fragments, scanner, prompt, cycles, chunk, chunks_per_cycle, window,\n                   beam_size, tau, temperature, seed, learn, trace):\n    \"\"\"Fixed-cycle loop. scanner=None -> weave kernel (CoT tokens live in the\n    context); scanner given -> scan kernel (CoT token is a probe, kept out of the\n    context, only steering the dataset scan for the next chunk).\"\"\"\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\n    scan = scanner is not None\n\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\"The\"]\n    full = [COT_START] + seed_tokens          # everything produced so far (markers incl.)\n    context = list(seed_tokens) if scan else list(full)\n    total = max(1, cycles * chunks_per_cycle * chunk)\n    step = 0\n    probe = COT_START                         # CoT token that steers the next scan\n\n    for c in range(cycles):\n        for k in range(chunks_per_cycle):\n            bias, hits = ({}, 0)\n            if scan:\n                bias, hits = scanner.bias(probe, context, rng)\n            new, mean_logp, hit_eos, _ = generate_chunk(\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, step, total,\n                beam_size, tau, controller.temperature, rng,\n                bias=bias, bias_strength=scanner.strength if scan else 0.0)\n            step += chunk\n            cot, rep = controller.update(new, mean_logp)\n\n            if trace:\n                extra = (f\" scan[{probe}:{cot_role(probe)} hits={hits} \"\n                         f\"ground={grounding(new, bias):.2f}]\") if scan else \"\"\n                print(f\"[cycle {c+1}/{cycles} chunk {k+1}] tokens={len(new)} \"\n                      f\"mean_logp={mean_logp:.2f} rep={rep:.2f} \"\n                      f\"-> {cot} (T={controller.temperature:.2f}){extra}\")\n\n            marker = [] if scan else [cot]\n            # Feedback learning: only from healthy output, to avoid reinforcing loops.\n            if learn and new and rep <= controller.rep_limit:\n                model.learn(tail_ctx(context, model.order - 1) + new + marker)\n\n            context += new + marker\n            full += new + [cot]\n            probe = cot\n            if hit_eos:\n                break\n\n        # Pipe output back to input.\n        tail = full[-window:]\n        context = strip_cot(tail) if scan else [COT_INTEGRATE] + tail\n        full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\n        probe = COT_INTEGRATE\n\n    return full\n\n\ndef stacked_run(model, fragments, scanner, prompt, target_depth, chunk, window, beam_size, tau,\n                temperature, seed, learn, max_retries, strict, min_grounding, trace):\n    \"\"\"\n    Keep generating until CoT tokens stack up in the correct order.\n\n    weave kernel: the model must itself emit the next expected CoT token\n    (COT_CYCLE order, repeating) after a chunk of real content.\n\n    scan kernel (inverted): the expected CoT word is used as a probe into the\n    dataset. A slot is accepted when the word is found there and the chunk is\n    grounded in the scanned passages (>= min_grounding). A word that never occurs\n    in the dataset cannot ground and is forced (flagged), or stops a --strict run.\n\n    Rejected chunks are regenerated (temperature creeps up per retry). Accepted\n    slots are pushed on a stack that only grows (monotonic) and are learned online.\n    After `max_retries` misses the slot is forced unless `strict`.\n    \"\"\"\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\n    scan = scanner is not None\n\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\"The\"]\n    full = [COT_START] + seed_tokens\n    context = list(seed_tokens) if scan else list(full)\n    stack: List[str] = []\n    forced = 0\n    attempts = 0\n    max_attempts = target_depth * (200 if strict else max_retries + 1)\n\n    while len(stack) < target_depth and attempts < max_attempts:\n        expected = COT_CYCLE[len(stack) % len(COT_CYCLE)]\n        cot_hits = scanner.hits(expected) if scan else 0\n        retries = 0\n        accepted, was_forced = False, False\n        while attempts < max_attempts:\n            temp = float(np.clip(controller.temperature * (1.0 + 0.1 * retries), 0.3, 1.8))\n            bias = {}\n            if scan:\n                bias, _ = scanner.bias(expected, context, rng)\n            new, mlp, eos, emitted = generate_chunk(\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, len(stack) * chunk,\n                target_depth * chunk, beam_size, tau, temp, rng,\n                stop_on_cot=not scan, bias=bias,\n                bias_strength=scanner.strength if scan else 0.0)\n            attempts += 1\n            if scan:\n                g = grounding(new, bias)\n                ok = len(new) > 0 and cot_hits > 0 and g >= min_grounding\n                detail = f\"scan hits={cot_hits} ground={g:.2f}\"\n            else:\n                ok = emitted == expected and len(new) > 0\n                detail = f\"got {emitted or 'none'}\"\n            msg = (f\"depth {len(stack)}/{target_depth} attempt {attempts} \"\n                   f\"expected {expected} {detail} \"\n                   f\"{'OK' if ok else 'retry'} (T={temp:.2f}, forced={forced})\")\n            if trace:\n                print(msg, file=sys.stderr)\n            else:\n                print(\"\\r\" + msg.ljust(78), end=\"\", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\n            if ok:\n                accepted = True\n                break\n            retries += 1\n            if scan and cot_hits == 0:\n                # Retrying can't make an absent word appear in the dataset.\n                if not strict:\n                    was_forced = True\n                break\n            if retries > max_retries and not strict:\n                was_forced = True\n                break\n        if not (accepted or was_forced):\n            break  # attempt cap hit, or strict and ungroundable\n\n        if was_forced:\n            forced += 1\n        stack.append(expected)\n        marker = [] if scan else [expected]\n        context += new + marker\n        full += new + [expected]\n        if new:\n            controller.update(new, mlp)\n        if accepted and learn:\n            model.learn(tail_ctx(context, model.order - 1 + len(new) + len(marker)))\n\n        # Pipe output back to input at the end of each full CoT cycle.\n        if len(stack) % PIPE_EVERY == 0:\n            context = strip_cot(full[-window:]) if scan else [COT_INTEGRATE] + full[-window:]\n            full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\n\n    if not trace:\n        print(file=sys.stderr)\n    monotonic = all(stack[i] == COT_CYCLE[i % len(COT_CYCLE)] for i in range(len(stack)))\n    stats = dict(depth=len(stack), target=target_depth, attempts=attempts,\n                 forced=forced, monotonic=monotonic)\n    return full, stats\n\n\ndef detokenize(tokens: Sequence[str], hide_cot: bool) -> str:\n    return \" \".join(strip_cot(tokens) if hide_cot else tokens)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# CLI\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef die(msg: str) -> None:\n    print(f\"error: {msg}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    sys.exit(2)\n\n\ndef read_corpus(path: str) -> str:\n    p = Path(path)\n    if not p.is_file():\n        die(f\"corpus file not found: {p}\")\n    try:\n        text = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\n    except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n        die(f\"could not decode {p} as UTF-8: {exc}\")\n    if not tokenize(text):\n        die(f\"{p} contains no tokens\")\n    return text\n\n\ndef add_vocab_args(p: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:\n    p.add_argument(\"--cot-vocab\", help=\"Custom CoT vocabulary file (one word per line, used in order).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--cot-sort\", choices=[\"none\", \"alpha\", \"alpha-desc\", \"length\"], default=\"none\",\n                   help=\"Sort the custom list before use (default: keep file order).\")\n\n\ndef report_coverage(dataset: List[str]) -> None:\n    if not dataset:\n        return\n    found, missing = DatasetScanner(dataset).coverage(current_cot_words())\n    print(f\"scan coverage: {found}/{COT_COUNT} CoT words occur in the dataset\"\n          + (f\" (absent: {', '.join(missing[:10])}{' ...' if len(missing) > 10 else ''})\"\n             if missing else \"\"), file=sys.stderr)\n\n\ndef cmd_build(args) -> None:\n    texts = [read_corpus(c) for c in args.corpus]\n    if args.cot_vocab:\n        words = load_cot_vocab(args.cot_vocab, args.cot_sort)\n    else:\n        words = select_cot_tokens(\"\\n\".join(texts), args.seed)\n    set_cot_tokens(words)\n    print(\"CoT vocab: \" + \" \".join(current_cot_words()), file=sys.stderr)\n\n    weave = args.kernel == \"weave\" and not args.no_cot_weave\n    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\n    dataset: List[str] = []\n    for text in texts:\n        model.train(text, cot=weave)\n        dataset.extend(tokenize(text))\n    if args.kernel == \"scan\":\n        report_coverage(dataset)\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(args.seed)\n    meta = {\"seed\": args.seed, \"kernel\": args.kernel, \"extensions\": 0,\n            \"sources\": [Path(c).name for c in args.corpus]}\n    save_checkpoint(args.output, model, fragments, dataset, meta)\n    print(f\"built {args.output} [{args.kernel} kernel]: {len(model.vocab)} types, \"\n          f\"{model.total_tokens:g} tokens, dataset {len(dataset)} tokens\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n\ndef cmd_extend(args) -> None:\n    try:\n        model, fragments, dataset, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\n    except (OSError, ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n        die(str(exc))\n    kernel = meta[\"kernel\"]\n    old_words = current_cot_words()\n\n    if args.alpha is not None:\n        model.alpha = max(1e-9, args.alpha)\n\n    if args.cot_vocab:\n        new_words = load_cot_vocab(args.cot_vocab, args.cot_sort)\n        if kernel == \"weave\":\n            mapping = {o: n for o, n in zip(old_words, new_words) if o != n}\n            if mapping:\n                clash = [n for n in mapping.values() if n in model.vocab and n not in mapping]\n                if clash:\n                    print(\"warning: new CoT words already occur as ordinary words in the weights \"\n                          f\"and will merge with them: {', '.join(sorted(clash)[:8])}\"\n                          + (\" ...\" if len(clash) > 8 else \"\"), file=sys.stderr)\n                model.remap_tokens(mapping)\n                print(f\"remapped {len(mapping)} CoT tokens onto the new vocabulary\", file=sys.stderr)\n        else:\n            print(\"scan kernel: CoT vocabulary swapped, no weights to remap\", file=sys.stderr)\n        set_cot_tokens(new_words)\n    print(\"CoT vocab: \" + \" \".join(current_cot_words()), file=sys.stderr)\n\n    if args.decay != 1.0:\n        model.scale(args.decay)\n        print(f\"decayed existing weights by {args.decay} (dataset is not decayed)\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n    weave = kernel == \"weave\" and not args.no_cot_weave\n    for path in args.corpus:\n        text = read_corpus(path)\n        model.train(text, cot=weave)\n        dataset.extend(tokenize(text))\n        meta.setdefault(\"sources\", []).append(Path(path).name)\n    meta[\"extensions\"] = meta.get(\"extensions\", 0) + 1\n\n    if kernel == \"scan\":\n        report_coverage(dataset)\n    save_checkpoint(args.output, model, fragments, dataset, meta)\n    print(f\"extended -> {args.output} [{kernel} kernel]: {len(model.vocab)} types, \"\n          f\"{model.total_tokens:g} tokens, dataset {len(dataset)} tokens\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n\ndef cmd_info(args) -> None:\n    try:\n        model, fragments, dataset, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\n    except (OSError, ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n        die(str(exc))\n    print(f\"format       {FORMAT}   kernel {meta['kernel']}\")\n    print(f\"order        {model.order}   alpha {model.alpha}\")\n    print(f\"vocab types  {len(model.vocab)}   tokens {model.total_tokens:g}   dataset {len(dataset)}\")\n    print(\"contexts     \" + \", \".join(f\"n={i}: {len(lv)}\" for i, lv in enumerate(model.counts)))\n    print(f\"extensions   {meta.get('extensions', 0)}   sources {', '.join(meta.get('sources', []))}\")\n    print(\"cycle        \" + \" \".join(str(t) for t in COT_CYCLE))\n    print(f\"diverge={COT_DIVERGE} converge={COT_CONVERGE} \"\n          f\"integrate={COT_INTEGRATE} start={COT_START}\")\n    if dataset:\n        found, missing = DatasetScanner(dataset).coverage(current_cot_words())\n        print(f\"coverage     {found}/{COT_COUNT} CoT words occur in the dataset\"\n              + (f\"; absent: {', '.join(missing)}\" if missing else \"\"))\n\n\ndef cmd_generate(args) -> None:\n    try:\n        model, fragments, dataset, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\n    except (OSError, ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n        die(str(exc))\n    kernel = args.kernel or meta[\"kernel\"]\n    scanner = None\n    if kernel == \"scan\":\n        if not dataset:\n            die(\"scan kernel needs the dataset stored in the checkpoint \"\n                \"(this one has none; rebuild it or use --kernel weave)\")\n        scanner = DatasetScanner(dataset, strength=args.scan_strength, limit=args.scan_limit,\n                                 span=args.scan_span, mix=args.scan_mix)\n        report_coverage(dataset)\n    print(f\"kernel: {kernel}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    print(\"CoT vocab: \" + \" \".join(current_cot_words()), file=sys.stderr)\n\n    first = True\n    while True:\n        try:\n            prompt = args.prompt if (args.prompt and first) else input(\"USER: \")\n        except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):\n            print()\n            break\n        first = False\n\n        tau = float(np.clip(args.tau, 0.0, 1.0))\n        temp = max(0.0, args.temperature)\n        if args.stack_target > 0:\n            full, stats = stacked_run(\n                model, fragments, scanner, prompt, target_depth=args.stack_target,\n                chunk=args.chunk, window=args.window, beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau,\n                temperature=temp, seed=args.seed, learn=not args.no_learn,\n                max_retries=args.max_retries, strict=args.strict,\n                min_grounding=args.min_grounding, trace=args.trace)\n            print(f\"\\n[stack] depth {stats['depth']}/{stats['target']}  attempts {stats['attempts']}  \"\n                  f\"forced {stats['forced']}  monotonic order verified: {stats['monotonic']}\")\n        else:\n            full = cybernetic_run(\n                model, fragments, scanner, prompt, cycles=args.cycles, chunk=args.chunk,\n                chunks_per_cycle=args.chunks_per_cycle, window=args.window,\n                beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp, seed=args.seed,\n                learn=not args.no_learn, trace=args.trace)\n\n        text = detokenize(full, hide_cot=not args.show_cot)\n        print(\"\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\")\n        print(text)\n        print()\n        if args.save:\n            with open(args.save, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n                fh.write(text + \"\\n\\n\")\n\n    if args.save_model:\n        meta[\"extensions\"] = meta.get(\"extensions\", 0) + 1\n        save_checkpoint(args.save_model, model, fragments, dataset, meta)\n        print(f\"saved weights -> {args.save_model}\", file=sys.stderr)\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"CoT weight extender (scan kernel) for the cybernetic n-gram generator.\")\n    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest=\"cmd\", required=True)\n\n    b = sub.add_parser(\"build\", help=\"Train a new checkpoint from corpora.\")\n    b.add_argument(\"corpus\", nargs=\"+\", help=\"UTF-8 text corpus file(s).\")\n    b.add_argument(\"-o\", \"--output\", required=True, help=\"Checkpoint to write (.cotw.gz).\")\n    b.add_argument(\"--order\", type=int, default=3)\n    b.add_argument(\"--alpha\", type=float, default=0.25)\n    b.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=7)\n    b.add_argument(\"--kernel\", choices=[\"scan\", \"weave\"], default=\"scan\",\n                   help=\"scan: CoT token probes the dataset (default). weave: CoT tokens woven into the weights.\")\n    b.add_argument(\"--no-cot-weave\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"(weave kernel) do not weave CoT tokens in.\")\n    add_vocab_args(b)\n    b.set_defaults(func=cmd_build)\n\n    e = sub.add_parser(\"extend\", help=\"Extend an existing checkpoint.\")\n    e.add_argument(\"model\", help=\"Checkpoint to extend.\")\n    e.add_argument(\"corpus\", nargs=\"*\", help=\"Additional corpus file(s) (optional).\")\n    e.add_argument(\"-o\", \"--output\", required=True, help=\"Checkpoint to write.\")\n    e.add_argument(\"--decay\", type=float, default=1.0,\n                   help=\"Scale existing weights by this factor before adding new data (e.g. 0.9).\")\n    e.add_argument(\"--alpha\", type=float, default=None, help=\"Override smoothing alpha.\")\n    e.add_argument(\"--no-cot-weave\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"(weave kernel) do not weave CoT tokens into new corpora.\")\n    add_vocab_args(e)\n    e.set_defaults(func=cmd_extend)\n\n    i = sub.add_parser(\"info\", help=\"Show checkpoint statistics.\")\n    i.add_argument(\"model\")\n    i.set_defaults(func=cmd_info)\n\n    g = sub.add_parser(\"generate\", help=\"Run the cybernetic loop from a checkpoint.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"model\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--kernel\", choices=[\"scan\", \"weave\"], default=None,\n                   help=\"Override the checkpoint's kernel.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--prompt\", help=\"Initial prompt. If omitted you are asked each round.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--cycles\", type=int, default=4, help=\"Output->input feedback cycles per prompt.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--chunk\", type=int, default=20, help=\"Tokens per chunk between CoT tokens.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--chunks-per-cycle\", type=int, default=3)\n    g.add_argument(\"--window\", type=int, default=40, help=\"Tokens of output piped back as the next prompt.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--beam\", type=int, default=8)\n    g.add_argument(\"--tau\", type=float, default=0.65)\n    g.add_argument(\"--temperature\", type=float, default=0.85)\n    g.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=7)\n    g.add_argument(\"--stack-target\", type=int, default=25,\n                   help=\"Keep going until this many CoT tokens have stacked in order (0 = fixed-cycle mode).\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--max-retries\", type=int, default=25, help=\"Rejected chunks allowed per stack slot before forcing.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--strict\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Never force a token; retry until the attempt cap.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--scan-strength\", type=float, default=1.5, help=\"Weight of the dataset-scan bias on scores.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--scan-limit\", type=int, default=24, help=\"Max passages sampled per probe word.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--scan-span\", type=int, default=12, help=\"Tokens read after each occurrence.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--scan-mix\", type=float, default=0.5,\n                   help=\"Weight of the last context word as a second probe (0 = CoT token only).\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--min-grounding\", type=float, default=0.15,\n                   help=\"Stack mode (scan): min fraction of chunk tokens found in the scanned passages.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--no-learn\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Disable online learning from own output.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--show-cot\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Show CoT tokens in printed text (hidden by default).\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--trace\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Print controller diagnostics.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--save\", help=\"Append output to this text file.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--save-model\", help=\"Write the weights (incl. online learning) to this checkpoint at exit.\")\n    g.set_defaults(func=cmd_generate)\n\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    args.func(args)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\nPYEOF\ncd /tmp && rm -rf t2 && mkdir t2 && cd t2 && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport random\nrandom.seed(1)\nw=\"machine thought signal memory pattern energy system loop feedback network learning model state vector entropy order chaos light dark river stone\".split()\nlines=[\" \".join(random.choice(w) for _ in range(random.randint(5,12)))+random.choice(\".!?\") for _ in range(400)]\nopen(\"corpus.txt\",\"w\").write(\" \".join(lines))\nopen(\"more.txt\",\"w\").write(\" \".join(lines[:100]))\ncot=sorted(w[:12]+[\"river\",\"stone\",\"light\",\"dark\",\"chaos\",\"order\",\"entropy\",\"vector\",\"state\",\"model\",\"learning\",\"network\",\"ghostword\"])[:25]+[\"feedback\",\"loop\",\"signal\",\"energy\"]\nopen(\"cot.txt\",\"w\").write(\"\\n\".join(cot)+\"\\n\")\nEOF\nS=/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py\nset -e\npython3 $S build corpus.txt -o base.cotw.gz --cot-vocab cot.txt\npython3 $S extend base.cotw.gz more.txt -o v2.cotw.gz --decay 0.9\npython3 $S info v2.cotw.gz\necho ---- stack scan\npython3 $S generate v2.cotw.gz --prompt \"The machine\" --stack-target 10 --chunk 12 --save-model v3.cotw.gz </dev/null 2>&1 | tail -9\necho ---- fixed scan trace\npython3 $S generate v3.cotw.gz --prompt \"The machine\" --stack-target 0 --cycles 2 --chunks-per-cycle 2 --chunk 8 --trace --show-cot </dev/null 2>&1 | head -14\necho ---- weave override\npython3 $S generate v3.cotw.gz --kernel weave --prompt \"The machine\" --stack-target 4 --chunk 10 </dev/null 2>&1 | tail -4\necho ---- weave build + strict scan missing\npython3 $S build corpus.txt -o w.cotw.gz --kernel weave --cot-vocab cot.txt 2>&1 | tail -1\npython3 $S generate base.cotw.gz --prompt \"The machine\" --stack-target 25 --chunk 8 --strict --max-retries 2 </dev/null 2>&1 | grep -E \"stack|kernel\"", "description": "Rewrite file with inverted scan kernel and smoke-test all modes"}, "message": "Rewrite file with inverted scan kernel and smoke-test all modes", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cat > /mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py <<'PYEOF'\\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nCoT weight extender  (scan kernel)\\n==================================\\n\\nThe cybernetic n-gram generator as a persistent, extendable model, with the CoT\\nkernel INVERTED.\\n\\n  weave kernel (old)   dataset -> CoT.  CoT words are picked by scanning the\\n                       dataset, woven into the training stream, and the model has\\n                       to emit them itself.\\n  scan kernel (new)    CoT -> dataset.  A CoT token is a PROBE: the loop scans the\\n                       dataset for that word, collects the passages that follow\\n                       each occurrence, and turns them into a bias over the next\\n                       chunk's tokens. CoT tokens are never woven into the weights\\n                       and never enter the n-gram context; they only steer the scan.\\n\\nScan profile per CoT role:\\n  cycle token   standard scan\\n  diverge       more passages, longer span, slower decay   (wider read, T up)\\n  converge      fewer passages, shorter span, faster decay (tighter read, T down)\\n  integrate     standard passages, longer span             (re-read after pipe-back)\\n\\nStack mode under the scan kernel: slot i is accepted when the expected CoT word is\\nFOUND in the dataset and the generated chunk is grounded in the scanned passages\\n(fraction of chunk tokens that occur in them >= --min-grounding). A word that never\\noccurs in the dataset can't ground, so its slot is forced (flagged), or the run\\nstops early with --strict.\\n\\nCommands\\n  build     Train a new checkpoint from one or more corpora.\\n  extend    Grow a checkpoint: more corpora, optional decay, optional new CoT vocab.\\n  generate  Run the cybernetic loop from a checkpoint (optionally save weights).\\n  info      Print checkpoint statistics and CoT-vocab coverage of the dataset.\\n\\nCustom CoT vocabulary (--cot-vocab FILE): one word per line ('#' comments ignored),\\nused in order or sorted with --cot-sort:\\n\\n      entries  1..25   the stack cycle, in required order\\n      entry    26      diverge\\n      entry    27      converge\\n      entry    28      integrate\\n      entry    29      start\\n\\nWith the scan kernel the words should occur in the dataset (build/info report\\ncoverage); a swap of vocabulary on `extend` is free, nothing needs remapping.\\nWith the legacy weave kernel, `extend --cot-vocab` transfers the old CoT weights\\nonto the new words by position.\\n\\nCheckpoint = gzip JSON: n-gram counts, vocab, fragment matrices, the dataset token\\nstream (what the scan kernel reads), the CoT vocabulary and a meta block.\\n\\nExamples:\\n  python cot_weight_extender.py build corpus.txt -o base.cotw.gz --cot-vocab cot.txt\\n  python cot_weight_extender.py extend base.cotw.gz more.txt -o v2.cotw.gz --decay 0.9\\n  python cot_weight_extender.py generate v2.cotw.gz --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" --trace\\n  python cot_weight_extender.py generate v2.cotw.gz --kernel weave --show-cot\\n  python cot_weight_extender.py info v2.cotw.gz\\n\\nOnly dependency: NumPy\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport argparse\\nimport gzip\\nimport json\\nimport math\\nimport random\\nimport sys\\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Sequence, Tuple\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nFORMAT = \\\"cot-weights-v2\\\"\\nACCEPTED_FORMATS = (\\\"cot-weights-v1\\\", FORMAT)\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# CoT tokens\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass CotToken(str):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A CoT marker inserted by the loop. It is a str, but isinstance() tells it\\n    apart from the same word appearing as ordinary text, so hiding markers never\\n    deletes real words from the output.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\n# Fallback names, used only if the vocabulary source has too few distinct words.\\nDEFAULT_COT = [\\n    \\\"simulate\\\", \\\"recall\\\", \\\"correct\\\", \\\"imagine\\\", \\\"decide\\\",\\n    \\\"observe\\\", \\\"verify\\\", \\\"associate\\\", \\\"plan\\\", \\\"anticipate\\\",\\n    \\\"reflect\\\", \\\"abstract\\\", \\\"act\\\", \\\"question\\\", \\\"compare\\\",\\n    \\\"adapt\\\", \\\"predict\\\", \\\"summarize\\\", \\\"monitor\\\", \\\"infer\\\",\\n    \\\"consolidate\\\", \\\"attend\\\", \\\"evaluate\\\", \\\"prioritize\\\", \\\"hypothesize\\\",\\n    \\\"diverge\\\", \\\"converge\\\", \\\"integrate\\\", \\\"synthesize\\\",\\n]\\nCOT_COUNT = 29  # 25 cycle tokens + diverge + converge + integrate + start\\nPIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens\\nSENTENCE_END = (\\\".\\\", \\\"!\\\", \\\"?\\\")\\n\\nCOT_CYCLE: List[str] = []\\nCOT_DIVERGE = COT_CONVERGE = COT_INTEGRATE = COT_START = CotToken(\\\"\\\")\\nCOT: set = set()\\n\\n_STOP = {\\n    \\\"that\\\", \\\"with\\\", \\\"have\\\", \\\"from\\\", \\\"this\\\", \\\"they\\\", \\\"were\\\", \\\"been\\\", \\\"will\\\", \\\"would\\\", \\\"there\\\",\\n    \\\"their\\\", \\\"what\\\", \\\"when\\\", \\\"which\\\", \\\"your\\\", \\\"them\\\", \\\"then\\\", \\\"than\\\", \\\"into\\\", \\\"only\\\", \\\"also\\\",\\n    \\\"some\\\", \\\"such\\\", \\\"more\\\", \\\"most\\\", \\\"other\\\", \\\"about\\\", \\\"could\\\", \\\"should\\\", \\\"these\\\", \\\"those\\\",\\n}\\n\\n\\ndef set_cot_tokens(words: Sequence[str]) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Install the CoT vocabulary: 25 cycle tokens, then diverge, converge,\\n    integrate, start.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    global COT_CYCLE, COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START, COT\\n    toks = [CotToken(w) for w in words]\\n    COT_CYCLE = toks[:25]\\n    COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START = toks[25:29]\\n    COT = {str(t) for t in toks}\\n\\n\\ndef current_cot_words() -> List[str]:\\n    return [str(t) for t in COT_CYCLE] + [str(COT_DIVERGE), str(COT_CONVERGE),\\n                                          str(COT_INTEGRATE), str(COT_START)]\\n\\n\\ndef _top_up(words: List[str], count: int) -> List[str]:\\n    seen = {w.lower() for w in words}\\n    for d in DEFAULT_COT:\\n        if len(words) >= count:\\n            break\\n        if d.lower() not in seen:\\n            seen.add(d.lower())\\n            words.append(d)\\n    return words\\n\\n\\ndef select_cot_tokens(text: str, seed: int, count: int = COT_COUNT) -> List[str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pick CoT tokens from the dataset: the most frequent alphabetic words of\\n    4+ letters (skipping common function words), shuffled so the required order is\\n    non-monotonic. Used when no --cot-vocab is given.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    counts = Counter(tokenize(text))\\n    pool = [(w, c) for w, c in counts.items()\\n            if w.isalpha() and len(w) >= 4 and w.lower() not in _STOP]\\n    pool.sort(key=lambda wc: (-wc[1], wc[0]))\\n    words, seen = [], set()\\n    for w, _ in pool:\\n        if w.lower() not in seen:\\n            seen.add(w.lower())\\n            words.append(w)\\n        if len(words) >= count:\\n            break\\n    random.Random(seed).shuffle(words)\\n    return _top_up(words, count)\\n\\n\\ndef load_cot_vocab(path: str, sort: str = \\\"none\\\", count: int = COT_COUNT) -> List[str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Load a custom CoT vocabulary from a text file (one word per line).\\n\\n    sort: 'none' keeps file order (use when the list is already sorted the way you\\n    want the stack to run), 'alpha' / 'alpha-desc' sort case-insensitively,\\n    'length' sorts short to long. Sorting happens BEFORE truncating to `count`.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    words, seen = [], set()\\n    for lineno, line in enumerate(Path(path).read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8-sig\\\").splitlines(), 1):\\n        w = line.split(\\\"#\\\", 1)[0].strip()\\n        if not w:\\n            continue\\n        if len(w.split()) != 1:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"{path}:{lineno}: CoT words must be a single token, got {w!r}\\\")\\n        if w.lower() in seen:\\n            print(f\\\"warning: duplicate CoT word {w!r} at line {lineno} ignored\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n            continue\\n        seen.add(w.lower())\\n        words.append(w)\\n    if sort == \\\"alpha\\\":\\n        words.sort(key=str.lower)\\n    elif sort == \\\"alpha-desc\\\":\\n        words.sort(key=str.lower, reverse=True)\\n    elif sort == \\\"length\\\":\\n        words.sort(key=lambda w: (len(w), w.lower()))\\n    if len(words) > count:\\n        print(f\\\"note: {len(words)} CoT words given, using the first {count}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        words = words[:count]\\n    elif len(words) < count:\\n        print(f\\\"note: only {len(words)} CoT words given, filling to {count} from fallback names\\\",\\n              file=sys.stderr)\\n        words = _top_up(words, count)\\n    return words\\n\\n\\nset_cot_tokens(DEFAULT_COT)\\n\\n\\ndef tokenize(text: str) -> List[str]:\\n    return text.split()\\n\\n\\ndef strip_cot(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> List[str]:\\n    return [t for t in tokens if not isinstance(t, CotToken)]\\n\\n\\ndef tail_ctx(tokens: Sequence[str], k: int) -> List[str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Last k tokens (empty for k <= 0; avoids the tokens[-0:] whole-list trap).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return list(tokens[len(tokens) - k:]) if k > 0 else []\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Dataset scanner (the inverted kernel: CoT token -> dataset passages -> bias)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef norm_word(w: str) -> str:\\n    return str(w).strip(\\\".,;:!?\\\\\\\"'()[]{}\\\").lower()\\n\\n\\n# role -> (passage multiplier, span multiplier, per-step decay)\\nSCAN_PROFILES = {\\n    \\\"cycle\\\": (1.0, 1.0, 0.85),\\n    \\\"diverge\\\": (2.0, 2.0, 0.92),\\n    \\\"converge\\\": (0.5, 0.5, 0.75),\\n    \\\"integrate\\\": (1.0, 1.5, 0.88),\\n    \\\"start\\\": (1.0, 1.0, 0.85),\\n}\\n\\n\\ndef cot_role(tok: str) -> str:\\n    s = str(tok)\\n    if s == str(COT_DIVERGE):\\n        return \\\"diverge\\\"\\n    if s == str(COT_CONVERGE):\\n        return \\\"converge\\\"\\n    if s == str(COT_INTEGRATE):\\n        return \\\"integrate\\\"\\n    if s == str(COT_START):\\n        return \\\"start\\\"\\n    return \\\"cycle\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass DatasetScanner:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Inverted index over the dataset token stream. A CoT token is used as a key:\\n    every occurrence of its word is located, the `span` tokens that follow are\\n    collected with geometric decay, and the result is a bias in [0, 1] over tokens.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, tokens: List[str], strength: float = 1.5, limit: int = 24,\\n                 span: int = 12, mix: float = 0.5):\\n        self.tokens = tokens\\n        self.strength = strength\\n        self.limit = max(1, int(limit))\\n        self.span = max(2, int(span))\\n        self.mix = max(0.0, float(mix))\\n        self._index = None\\n\\n    @property\\n    def index(self) -> Dict[str, List[int]]:\\n        if self._index is None:\\n            idx = defaultdict(list)\\n            for i, t in enumerate(self.tokens):\\n                idx[norm_word(t)].append(i)\\n            self._index = idx\\n        return self._index\\n\\n    def extend(self, tokens: Sequence[str]) -> None:\\n        self.tokens.extend(tokens)\\n        self._index = None\\n\\n    def hits(self, word: str) -> int:\\n        return len(self.index.get(norm_word(word), ()))\\n\\n    def coverage(self, words: Sequence[str]) -> Tuple[int, List[str]]:\\n        missing = [w for w in words if self.hits(w) == 0]\\n        return len(words) - len(missing), missing\\n\\n    def bias(self, cot: str, context: Sequence[str], rng: random.Random) -> Tuple[Dict[str, float], int]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Scan with `cot` as probe (plus, at weight `mix`, the last context word).\\n        Returns (normalised bias over tokens, number of dataset hits for `cot`).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        limit_mult, span_mult, decay = SCAN_PROFILES[cot_role(cot)]\\n        limit = max(1, int(round(self.limit * limit_mult)))\\n        span = max(2, int(round(self.span * span_mult)))\\n        probes = [(str(cot), 1.0)]\\n        if context and self.mix > 0:\\n            probes.append((str(context[-1]), self.mix))\\n        weights: Counter = Counter()\\n        cot_hits = 0\\n        n = len(self.tokens)\\n        for pi, (word, w) in enumerate(probes):\\n            pos = self.index.get(norm_word(word), [])\\n            if pi == 0:\\n                cot_hits = len(pos)\\n            if not pos:\\n                continue\\n            if len(pos) > limit:\\n                pos = rng.sample(pos, limit)\\n            share = w / len(pos)\\n            for p in pos:\\n                for off in range(1, span + 1):\\n                    j = p + off\\n                    if j >= n:\\n                        break\\n                    weights[self.tokens[j]] += share * (decay ** (off - 1))\\n        if not weights:\\n            return {}, cot_hits\\n        top = max(weights.values())\\n        return {t: v / top for t, v in weights.items()}, cot_hits\\n\\n\\ndef grounding(new: Sequence[str], bias) -> float:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Fraction of generated tokens that occur in the scanned passages.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not new or not bias:\\n        return 0.0\\n    return sum(1 for t in new if t in bias) / len(new)\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# N-gram model (serialisation, decay, merge and token remapping)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass NGramModel:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Smoothed n-gram model with backoff, trainable offline and online.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, order: int = 3, alpha: float = 0.25):\\n        self.order = max(1, int(order))\\n        self.alpha = max(1e-9, float(alpha))\\n        self.counts = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(self.order)]\\n        self.vocab = Counter()\\n        self.total_tokens = 0\\n\\n    def _update(self, tokens: Sequence[str], start: int) -> None:\\n        for i in range(start, len(tokens)):\\n            target = tokens[i]\\n            self.vocab[target] += 1\\n            self.total_tokens += 1\\n            for ctx_len in range(self.order):\\n                if ctx_len > i:\\n                    break\\n                context = tuple(tokens[i - ctx_len:i]) if ctx_len else ()\\n                self.counts[ctx_len][context][target] += 1\\n\\n    def train(self, text: str, cot: bool = True) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"cot=True weaves CoT tokens in after each sentence (weave kernel).\\n        The scan kernel trains with cot=False: the weights never see CoT tokens.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        raw = tokenize(text)\\n        if cot:\\n            woven, k = [], 0\\n            for tok in raw:\\n                woven.append(tok)\\n                if tok.endswith(SENTENCE_END):\\n                    woven.append(COT_CYCLE[k % len(COT_CYCLE)])\\n                    k += 1\\n            raw = woven\\n        tokens = [\\\"<bos>\\\"] * (self.order - 1) + raw + [\\\"<eos>\\\"]\\n        self._update(tokens, self.order - 1)\\n\\n    def learn(self, tokens: Sequence[str]) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Online update from the model's own output (feedback learning).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self._update(list(tokens), 1)\\n\\n    # ---- weight extension ------------------------------------------------\\n    def scale(self, factor: float) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Multiply every stored weight (decay old knowledge before extending).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if factor == 1.0:\\n            return\\n        for level in self.counts:\\n            for counter in level.values():\\n                for tok in counter:\\n                    counter[tok] *= factor\\n        for tok in self.vocab:\\n            self.vocab[tok] *= factor\\n        self.total_tokens *= factor\\n\\n    def remap_tokens(self, mapping: Dict[str, str]) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Rename tokens everywhere (contexts and targets). Colliding counts are\\n        summed. Weave kernel only: transfers CoT behaviour to a new vocabulary.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not mapping:\\n            return\\n\\n        def m(t):\\n            return mapping.get(t, t)\\n\\n        new_counts = []\\n        for level in self.counts:\\n            nl = defaultdict(Counter)\\n            for ctx, counter in level.items():\\n                nctx = tuple(m(t) for t in ctx)\\n                for tok, n in counter.items():\\n                    nl[nctx][m(tok)] += n\\n            new_counts.append(nl)\\n        self.counts = new_counts\\n        nv = Counter()\\n        for tok, n in self.vocab.items():\\n            nv[m(tok)] += n\\n        self.vocab = nv\\n\\n    # ---- serialisation ---------------------------------------------------\\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\\n        return {\\n            \\\"order\\\": self.order,\\n            \\\"alpha\\\": self.alpha,\\n            \\\"total_tokens\\\": self.total_tokens,\\n            \\\"vocab\\\": {str(k): v for k, v in self.vocab.items()},\\n            \\\"counts\\\": [[[list(ctx), {str(t): n for t, n in c.items()}]\\n                        for ctx, c in level.items()] for level in self.counts],\\n        }\\n\\n    @classmethod\\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> \\\"NGramModel\\\":\\n        model = cls(order=d[\\\"order\\\"], alpha=d[\\\"alpha\\\"])\\n        model.total_tokens = d[\\\"total_tokens\\\"]\\n        model.vocab = Counter(d[\\\"vocab\\\"])\\n        model.counts = []\\n        for level in d[\\\"counts\\\"]:\\n            lv = defaultdict(Counter)\\n            for ctx, counter in level:\\n                lv[tuple(ctx)] = Counter(counter)\\n            model.counts.append(lv)\\n        return model\\n\\n    def candidates(self, context_tokens: Sequence[str], limit: int = 80) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:\\n        vocab_size = max(1, len(self.vocab))\\n        context = list(context_tokens)\\n        counter = Counter()\\n        for ctx_len in range(min(self.order - 1, len(context)), -1, -1):\\n            key = tuple(context[-ctx_len:]) if ctx_len else ()\\n            found = self.counts[ctx_len].get(key)\\n            if not found:\\n                continue\\n            weight = 1.0 + 0.7 * ctx_len\\n            for token, count in found.items():\\n                counter[token] += weight * count\\n            if ctx_len >= 1:\\n                break\\n        if not counter:\\n            counter.update(self.vocab)\\n        counter.pop(\\\"<bos>\\\", None)\\n        total = sum(counter.values())\\n        ranked = []\\n        for token, count in counter.items():\\n            prob = (count + self.alpha) / (total + self.alpha * vocab_size)\\n            ranked.append((token, math.log(max(prob, 1e-12))))\\n        ranked.sort(key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\\n        return ranked[:max(1, limit)]\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Non-isomorphic fragments (weights are saved with the checkpoint)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass NonIsomorphicFragments:\\n    def __init__(self, seed: int = 17):\\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n        self.w_context = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 3))\\n        self.w_word = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 4))\\n        self.w_transition = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 2))\\n\\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\\n        return {\\\"w_context\\\": self.w_context.tolist(),\\n                \\\"w_word\\\": self.w_word.tolist(),\\n                \\\"w_transition\\\": self.w_transition.tolist()}\\n\\n    @classmethod\\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> \\\"NonIsomorphicFragments\\\":\\n        frag = cls(0)\\n        frag.w_context = np.asarray(d[\\\"w_context\\\"], dtype=float)\\n        frag.w_word = np.asarray(d[\\\"w_word\\\"], dtype=float)\\n        frag.w_transition = np.asarray(d[\\\"w_transition\\\"], dtype=float)\\n        return frag\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _unit(v: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n        n = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\\n        return v / n if n > 1e-12 else np.zeros_like(v)\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _hash_features(token: str, width: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n        raw = token.lower().encode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"ignore\\\")\\n        vals = np.zeros(width, dtype=float)\\n        if not raw:\\n            return vals\\n        for i, byte in enumerate(raw):\\n            vals[i % width] += ((byte % 31) - 15) / 15.0\\n            vals[(i * 3 + 1) % width] += ((byte % 17) - 8) / 8.0\\n        vals /= max(1, len(raw))\\n        vals[0] += min(len(raw), 20) / 20.0\\n        vals[1] += sum(chr(b).isalpha() for b in raw) / max(1, len(raw))\\n        return np.tanh(vals)\\n\\n    def features(self, context, token, logp, rank):\\n        recent = list(context[-4:])\\n        ctx_vec = np.zeros(5, dtype=float)\\n        if recent:\\n            for i, word in enumerate(recent):\\n                f = self._hash_features(word, 5)\\n                ctx_vec += f * (0.65 ** (len(recent) - i - 1))\\n            ctx_vec /= max(1, len(recent))\\n        word_vec = self._hash_features(token, 5)\\n        transition_vec = np.array([\\n            np.tanh(logp),\\n            1.0 / (1.0 + rank),\\n            1.0 if token[:1].isupper() else 0.0,\\n            1.0 if token in COT else 0.0,  # CoT words are visible to the fragments\\n            min(len(token), 24) / 24.0,\\n        ], dtype=float)\\n        g1 = np.tanh(ctx_vec @ self.w_context)\\n        g2 = np.tanh(word_vec @ self.w_word)\\n        g3 = np.tanh(transition_vec @ self.w_transition)\\n        return g1, g2, g3\\n\\n    def score(self, context, token, logp, rank, lam) -> Tuple[float, float]:\\n        g1, g2, g3 = self.features(context, token, logp, rank)\\n        summaries = np.array([np.linalg.norm(g1), np.linalg.norm(g2), np.linalg.norm(g3)])\\n        mean = float(np.mean(summaries))\\n        spread = float(np.std(summaries) / (mean + 1e-9))\\n        consistency = float(np.clip(0.55 * spread + 0.45 * (1.0 - mean), 0.0, 1.0))\\n\\n        ref = self._unit(np.array([np.mean(g1), np.mean(g2), np.mean(g3), np.tanh(logp)]))\\n        cand = self._unit(np.array([g1[0], g2[0], g3[0], np.tanh(logp + 0.1 * rank)]))\\n        alignment = (float(np.dot(ref, cand)) + 1.0) / 2.0\\n\\n        fragment_score = 1.6 * alignment - 1.15 * consistency\\n        total = (1.0 - lam) * (0.75 * logp + 0.25 * fragment_score) \\\\\\n            + lam * (1.25 * logp + 0.85 * fragment_score)\\n        return total, consistency\\n\\n\\ndef adiabatic_lambda(step: int, total_steps: int) -> float:\\n    u = min(1.0, max(0.0, step / max(1, total_steps - 1)))\\n    return 3.0 * u * u - 2.0 * u * u * u\\n\\n\\ndef softmax(values: Sequence[float], temperature: float = 1.0) -> np.ndarray:\\n    temp = max(1e-6, float(temperature))\\n    arr = np.asarray(values, dtype=float) / temp\\n    arr -= np.max(arr)\\n    exp = np.exp(np.clip(arr, -60, 60))\\n    return exp / max(float(exp.sum()), 1e-12)\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Checkpoints\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef save_checkpoint(path: str, model: NGramModel, fragments: NonIsomorphicFragments,\\n                    dataset: Sequence[str], meta: dict) -> None:\\n    payload = {\\n        \\\"format\\\": FORMAT,\\n        \\\"cot\\\": current_cot_words(),\\n        \\\"fragments\\\": fragments.to_dict(),\\n        \\\"model\\\": model.to_dict(),\\n        \\\"dataset\\\": list(dataset),\\n        \\\"meta\\\": meta,\\n    }\\n    with gzip.open(path, \\\"wt\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\\n        json.dump(payload, fh)\\n\\n\\ndef load_checkpoint(path: str):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Load a checkpoint and install its CoT vocabulary globally.\\n    Returns (model, fragments, dataset_tokens, meta).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    with gzip.open(path, \\\"rt\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\\n        payload = json.load(fh)\\n    if payload.get(\\\"format\\\") not in ACCEPTED_FORMATS:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"{path}: unsupported checkpoint format {payload.get('format')!r}\\\")\\n    set_cot_tokens(payload[\\\"cot\\\"])\\n    model = NGramModel.from_dict(payload[\\\"model\\\"])\\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments.from_dict(payload[\\\"fragments\\\"])\\n    dataset = list(payload.get(\\\"dataset\\\", []))\\n    meta = payload.get(\\\"meta\\\", {})\\n    meta.setdefault(\\\"kernel\\\", \\\"weave\\\")  # v1 checkpoints were woven\\n    return model, fragments, dataset, meta\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Cybernetic controller (sensor -> comparator -> actuator)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass Controller:\\n    def __init__(self, temperature: float, rep_limit: float = 0.5, logp_floor: float = -4.5):\\n        self.temperature = temperature\\n        self.rep_limit = rep_limit\\n        self.logp_floor = logp_floor\\n        self.k = 0\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def repetition(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> float:\\n        words = strip_cot(tokens)\\n        if len(words) < 2:\\n            return 0.0\\n        return 1.0 - len(set(words)) / len(words)\\n\\n    def update(self, chunk: Sequence[str], mean_logp: float) -> Tuple[str, float]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Return (CoT token to emit, repetition measure).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        rep = self.repetition(chunk)\\n        if rep > self.rep_limit:\\n            cot = COT_DIVERGE\\n            self.temperature *= 1.15\\n        elif mean_logp < self.logp_floor:\\n            cot = COT_CONVERGE\\n            self.temperature *= 0.9\\n        else:\\n            cot = COT_CYCLE[self.k % len(COT_CYCLE)]\\n            self.k += 1\\n        self.temperature = float(np.clip(self.temperature, 0.3, 1.6))\\n        return cot, rep\\n\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass Candidate:\\n    token: str\\n    base_logp: float\\n    score: float\\n    consistency: float\\n    probability: float = 0.0\\n\\n\\ndef generate_chunk(model, fragments, context, n, step0, total, beam_size, tau, temperature, rng,\\n                   stop_on_cot=False, bias=None, bias_strength=0.0):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generate up to n tokens after `context`.\\n\\n    Returns (new_tokens, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted_cot). With stop_on_cot the\\n    chunk ends the moment the MODEL emits a CoT token (weave kernel). With a\\n    `bias` (scan kernel) each candidate's score gains bias_strength * bias[token],\\n    where bias comes from the dataset scan.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    ctx = list(context)\\n    new, logps, hit_eos, emitted = [], [], False, None\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        lam = adiabatic_lambda(step0 + i, total)\\n        ranked = model.candidates(ctx, limit=max(40, beam_size * 8))\\n        scored: List[Candidate] = []\\n        for rank, (token, logp) in enumerate(ranked):\\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, rank, lam)\\n            if bias:\\n                score += bias_strength * bias.get(token, 0.0)\\n            if consistency <= tau:\\n                scored.append(Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency))\\n        if not scored:\\n            token, logp = ranked[0]\\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, 0, lam)\\n            scored = [Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency)]\\n\\n        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c.score, reverse=True)\\n        beam = scored[:max(1, beam_size)]\\n        probs = softmax([c.score for c in beam], temperature)\\n        chosen = beam[0] if temperature <= 0.01 else rng.choices(beam, weights=probs, k=1)[0]\\n\\n        if chosen.token == \\\"<eos>\\\":\\n            hit_eos = True\\n            break\\n        if stop_on_cot and chosen.token in COT:\\n            emitted = chosen.token\\n            logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\\n            break\\n        new.append(chosen.token)\\n        ctx.append(chosen.token)\\n        logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\\n    mean_logp = float(np.mean(logps)) if logps else 0.0\\n    return new, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted\\n\\n\\ndef cybernetic_run(model, fragments, scanner, prompt, cycles, chunk, chunks_per_cycle, window,\\n                   beam_size, tau, temperature, seed, learn, trace):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Fixed-cycle loop. scanner=None -> weave kernel (CoT tokens live in the\\n    context); scanner given -> scan kernel (CoT token is a probe, kept out of the\\n    context, only steering the dataset scan for the next chunk).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\\n    scan = scanner is not None\\n\\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\\\"The\\\"]\\n    full = [COT_START] + seed_tokens          # everything produced so far (markers incl.)\\n    context = list(seed_tokens) if scan else list(full)\\n    total = max(1, cycles * chunks_per_cycle * chunk)\\n    step = 0\\n    probe = COT_START                         # CoT token that steers the next scan\\n\\n    for c in range(cycles):\\n        for k in range(chunks_per_cycle):\\n            bias, hits = ({}, 0)\\n            if scan:\\n                bias, hits = scanner.bias(probe, context, rng)\\n            new, mean_logp, hit_eos, _ = generate_chunk(\\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, step, total,\\n                beam_size, tau, controller.temperature, rng,\\n                bias=bias, bias_strength=scanner.strength if scan else 0.0)\\n            step += chunk\\n            cot, rep = controller.update(new, mean_logp)\\n\\n            if trace:\\n                extra = (f\\\" scan[{probe}:{cot_role(probe)} hits={hits} \\\"\\n                         f\\\"ground={grounding(new, bias):.2f}]\\\") if scan else \\\"\\\"\\n                print(f\\\"[cycle {c+1}/{cycles} chunk {k+1}] tokens={len(new)} \\\"\\n                      f\\\"mean_logp={mean_logp:.2f} rep={rep:.2f} \\\"\\n                      f\\\"-> {cot} (T={controller.temperature:.2f}){extra}\\\")\\n\\n            marker = [] if scan else [cot]\\n            # Feedback learning: only from healthy output, to avoid reinforcing loops.\\n            if learn and new and rep <= controller.rep_limit:\\n                model.learn(tail_ctx(context, model.order - 1) + new + marker)\\n\\n            context += new + marker\\n            full += new + [cot]\\n            probe = cot\\n            if hit_eos:\\n                break\\n\\n        # Pipe output back to input.\\n        tail = full[-window:]\\n        context = strip_cot(tail) if scan else [COT_INTEGRATE] + tail\\n        full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\\n        probe = COT_INTEGRATE\\n\\n    return full\\n\\n\\ndef stacked_run(model, fragments, scanner, prompt, target_depth, chunk, window, beam_size, tau,\\n                temperature, seed, learn, max_retries, strict, min_grounding, trace):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Keep generating until CoT tokens stack up in the correct order.\\n\\n    weave kernel: the model must itself emit the next expected CoT token\\n    (COT_CYCLE order, repeating) after a chunk of real content.\\n\\n    scan kernel (inverted): the expected CoT word is used as a probe into the\\n    dataset. A slot is accepted when the word is found there and the chunk is\\n    grounded in the scanned passages (>= min_grounding). A word that never occurs\\n    in the dataset cannot ground and is forced (flagged), or stops a --strict run.\\n\\n    Rejected chunks are regenerated (temperature creeps up per retry). Accepted\\n    slots are pushed on a stack that only grows (monotonic) and are learned online.\\n    After `max_retries` misses the slot is forced unless `strict`.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\\n    scan = scanner is not None\\n\\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\\\"The\\\"]\\n    full = [COT_START] + seed_tokens\\n    context = list(seed_tokens) if scan else list(full)\\n    stack: List[str] = []\\n    forced = 0\\n    attempts = 0\\n    max_attempts = target_depth * (200 if strict else max_retries + 1)\\n\\n    while len(stack) < target_depth and attempts < max_attempts:\\n        expected = COT_CYCLE[len(stack) % len(COT_CYCLE)]\\n        cot_hits = scanner.hits(expected) if scan else 0\\n        retries = 0\\n        accepted, was_forced = False, False\\n        while attempts < max_attempts:\\n            temp = float(np.clip(controller.temperature * (1.0 + 0.1 * retries), 0.3, 1.8))\\n            bias = {}\\n            if scan:\\n                bias, _ = scanner.bias(expected, context, rng)\\n            new, mlp, eos, emitted = generate_chunk(\\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, len(stack) * chunk,\\n                target_depth * chunk, beam_size, tau, temp, rng,\\n                stop_on_cot=not scan, bias=bias,\\n                bias_strength=scanner.strength if scan else 0.0)\\n            attempts += 1\\n            if scan:\\n                g = grounding(new, bias)\\n                ok = len(new) > 0 and cot_hits > 0 and g >= min_grounding\\n                detail = f\\\"scan hits={cot_hits} ground={g:.2f}\\\"\\n            else:\\n                ok = emitted == expected and len(new) > 0\\n                detail = f\\\"got {emitted or 'none'}\\\"\\n            msg = (f\\\"depth {len(stack)}/{target_depth} attempt {attempts} \\\"\\n                   f\\\"expected {expected} {detail} \\\"\\n                   f\\\"{'OK' if ok else 'retry'} (T={temp:.2f}, forced={forced})\\\")\\n            if trace:\\n                print(msg, file=sys.stderr)\\n            else:\\n                print(\\\"\\\\r\\\" + msg.ljust(78), end=\\\"\\\", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\\n            if ok:\\n                accepted = True\\n                break\\n            retries += 1\\n            if scan and cot_hits == 0:\\n                # Retrying can't make an absent word appear in the dataset.\\n                if not strict:\\n                    was_forced = True\\n                break\\n            if retries > max_retries and not strict:\\n                was_forced = True\\n                break\\n        if not (accepted or was_forced):\\n            break  # attempt cap hit, or strict and ungroundable\\n\\n        if was_forced:\\n            forced += 1\\n        stack.append(expected)\\n        marker = [] if scan else [expected]\\n        context += new + marker\\n        full += new + [expected]\\n        if new:\\n            controller.update(new, mlp)\\n        if accepted and learn:\\n            model.learn(tail_ctx(context, model.order - 1 + len(new) + len(marker)))\\n\\n        # Pipe output back to input at the end of each full CoT cycle.\\n        if len(stack) % PIPE_EVERY == 0:\\n            context = strip_cot(full[-window:]) if scan else [COT_INTEGRATE] + full[-window:]\\n            full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\\n\\n    if not trace:\\n        print(file=sys.stderr)\\n    monotonic = all(stack[i] == COT_CYCLE[i % len(COT_CYCLE)] for i in range(len(stack)))\\n    stats = dict(depth=len(stack), target=target_depth, attempts=attempts,\\n                 forced=forced, monotonic=monotonic)\\n    return full, stats\\n\\n\\ndef detokenize(tokens: Sequence[str], hide_cot: bool) -> str:\\n    return \\\" \\\".join(strip_cot(tokens) if hide_cot else tokens)\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# CLI\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef die(msg: str) -> None:\\n    print(f\\\"error: {msg}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n    sys.exit(2)\\n\\n\\ndef read_corpus(path: str) -> str:\\n    p = Path(path)\\n    if not p.is_file():\\n        die(f\\\"corpus file not found: {p}\\\")\\n    try:\\n        text = p.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8-sig\\\")\\n    except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\\n        die(f\\\"could not decode {p} as UTF-8: {exc}\\\")\\n    if not tokenize(text):\\n        die(f\\\"{p} contains no tokens\\\")\\n    return text\\n\\n\\ndef add_vocab_args(p: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--cot-vocab\\\", help=\\\"Custom CoT vocabulary file (one word per line, used in order).\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--cot-sort\\\", choices=[\\\"none\\\", \\\"alpha\\\", \\\"alpha-desc\\\", \\\"length\\\"], default=\\\"none\\\",\\n                   help=\\\"Sort the custom list before use (default: keep file order).\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef report_coverage(dataset: List[str]) -> None:\\n    if not dataset:\\n        return\\n    found, missing = DatasetScanner(dataset).coverage(current_cot_words())\\n    print(f\\\"scan coverage: {found}/{COT_COUNT} CoT words occur in the dataset\\\"\\n          + (f\\\" (absent: {', '.join(missing[:10])}{' ...' if len(missing) > 10 else ''})\\\"\\n             if missing else \\\"\\\"), file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_build(args) -> None:\\n    texts = [read_corpus(c) for c in args.corpus]\\n    if args.cot_vocab:\\n        words = load_cot_vocab(args.cot_vocab, args.cot_sort)\\n    else:\\n        words = select_cot_tokens(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(texts), args.seed)\\n    set_cot_tokens(words)\\n    print(\\\"CoT vocab: \\\" + \\\" \\\".join(current_cot_words()), file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    weave = args.kernel == \\\"weave\\\" and not args.no_cot_weave\\n    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\\n    dataset: List[str] = []\\n    for text in texts:\\n        model.train(text, cot=weave)\\n        dataset.extend(tokenize(text))\\n    if args.kernel == \\\"scan\\\":\\n        report_coverage(dataset)\\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(args.seed)\\n    meta = {\\\"seed\\\": args.seed, \\\"kernel\\\": args.kernel, \\\"extensions\\\": 0,\\n            \\\"sources\\\": [Path(c).name for c in args.corpus]}\\n    save_checkpoint(args.output, model, fragments, dataset, meta)\\n    print(f\\\"built {args.output} [{args.kernel} kernel]: {len(model.vocab)} types, \\\"\\n          f\\\"{model.total_tokens:g} tokens, dataset {len(dataset)} tokens\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_extend(args) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        model, fragments, dataset, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\\n    except (OSError, ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\\n        die(str(exc))\\n    kernel = meta[\\\"kernel\\\"]\\n    old_words = current_cot_words()\\n\\n    if args.alpha is not None:\\n        model.alpha = max(1e-9, args.alpha)\\n\\n    if args.cot_vocab:\\n        new_words = load_cot_vocab(args.cot_vocab, args.cot_sort)\\n        if kernel == \\\"weave\\\":\\n            mapping = {o: n for o, n in zip(old_words, new_words) if o != n}\\n            if mapping:\\n                clash = [n for n in mapping.values() if n in model.vocab and n not in mapping]\\n                if clash:\\n                    print(\\\"warning: new CoT words already occur as ordinary words in the weights \\\"\\n                          f\\\"and will merge with them: {', '.join(sorted(clash)[:8])}\\\"\\n                          + (\\\" ...\\\" if len(clash) > 8 else \\\"\\\"), file=sys.stderr)\\n                model.remap_tokens(mapping)\\n                print(f\\\"remapped {len(mapping)} CoT tokens onto the new vocabulary\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        else:\\n            print(\\\"scan kernel: CoT vocabulary swapped, no weights to remap\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        set_cot_tokens(new_words)\\n    print(\\\"CoT vocab: \\\" + \\\" \\\".join(current_cot_words()), file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    if args.decay != 1.0:\\n        model.scale(args.decay)\\n        print(f\\\"decayed existing weights by {args.decay} (dataset is not decayed)\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    weave = kernel == \\\"weave\\\" and not args.no_cot_weave\\n    for path in args.corpus:\\n        text = read_corpus(path)\\n        model.train(text, cot=weave)\\n        dataset.extend(tokenize(text))\\n        meta.setdefault(\\\"sources\\\", []).append(Path(path).name)\\n    meta[\\\"extensions\\\"] = meta.get(\\\"extensions\\\", 0) + 1\\n\\n    if kernel == \\\"scan\\\":\\n        report_coverage(dataset)\\n    save_checkpoint(args.output, model, fragments, dataset, meta)\\n    print(f\\\"extended -> {args.output} [{kernel} kernel]: {len(model.vocab)} types, \\\"\\n          f\\\"{model.total_tokens:g} tokens, dataset {len(dataset)} tokens\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_info(args) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        model, fragments, dataset, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\\n    except (OSError, ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\\n        die(str(exc))\\n    print(f\\\"format       {FORMAT}   kernel {meta['kernel']}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"order        {model.order}   alpha {model.alpha}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"vocab types  {len(model.vocab)}   tokens {model.total_tokens:g}   dataset {len(dataset)}\\\")\\n    print(\\\"contexts     \\\" + \\\", \\\".join(f\\\"n={i}: {len(lv)}\\\" for i, lv in enumerate(model.counts)))\\n    print(f\\\"extensions   {meta.get('extensions', 0)}   sources {', '.join(meta.get('sources', []))}\\\")\\n    print(\\\"cycle        \\\" + \\\" \\\".join(str(t) for t in COT_CYCLE))\\n    print(f\\\"diverge={COT_DIVERGE} converge={COT_CONVERGE} \\\"\\n          f\\\"integrate={COT_INTEGRATE} start={COT_START}\\\")\\n    if dataset:\\n        found, missing = DatasetScanner(dataset).coverage(current_cot_words())\\n        print(f\\\"coverage     {found}/{COT_COUNT} CoT words occur in the dataset\\\"\\n              + (f\\\"; absent: {', '.join(missing)}\\\" if missing else \\\"\\\"))\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_generate(args) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        model, fragments, dataset, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\\n    except (OSError, ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\\n        die(str(exc))\\n    kernel = args.kernel or meta[\\\"kernel\\\"]\\n    scanner = None\\n    if kernel == \\\"scan\\\":\\n        if not dataset:\\n            die(\\\"scan kernel needs the dataset stored in the checkpoint \\\"\\n                \\\"(this one has none; rebuild it or use --kernel weave)\\\")\\n        scanner = DatasetScanner(dataset, strength=args.scan_strength, limit=args.scan_limit,\\n                                 span=args.scan_span, mix=args.scan_mix)\\n        report_coverage(dataset)\\n    print(f\\\"kernel: {kernel}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n    print(\\\"CoT vocab: \\\" + \\\" \\\".join(current_cot_words()), file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n    first = True\\n    while True:\\n        try:\\n            prompt = args.prompt if (args.prompt and first) else input(\\\"USER: \\\")\\n        except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):\\n            print()\\n            break\\n        first = False\\n\\n        tau = float(np.clip(args.tau, 0.0, 1.0))\\n        temp = max(0.0, args.temperature)\\n        if args.stack_target > 0:\\n            full, stats = stacked_run(\\n                model, fragments, scanner, prompt, target_depth=args.stack_target,\\n                chunk=args.chunk, window=args.window, beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau,\\n                temperature=temp, seed=args.seed, learn=not args.no_learn,\\n                max_retries=args.max_retries, strict=args.strict,\\n                min_grounding=args.min_grounding, trace=args.trace)\\n            print(f\\\"\\\\n[stack] depth {stats['depth']}/{stats['target']}  attempts {stats['attempts']}  \\\"\\n                  f\\\"forced {stats['forced']}  monotonic order verified: {stats['monotonic']}\\\")\\n        else:\\n            full = cybernetic_run(\\n                model, fragments, scanner, prompt, cycles=args.cycles, chunk=args.chunk,\\n                chunks_per_cycle=args.chunks_per_cycle, window=args.window,\\n                beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp, seed=args.seed,\\n                learn=not args.no_learn, trace=args.trace)\\n\\n        text = detokenize(full, hide_cot=not args.show_cot)\\n        print(\\\"\\\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\\\n\\\")\\n        print(text)\\n        print()\\n        if args.save:\\n            with open(args.save, \\\"a\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\\n                fh.write(text + \\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n    if args.save_model:\\n        meta[\\\"extensions\\\"] = meta.get(\\\"extensions\\\", 0) + 1\\n        save_checkpoint(args.save_model, model, fragments, dataset, meta)\\n        print(f\\\"saved weights -> {args.save_model}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n\\n\\ndef main() -> None:\\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\\\"CoT weight extender (scan kernel) for the cybernetic n-gram generator.\\\")\\n    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest=\\\"cmd\\\", required=True)\\n\\n    b = sub.add_parser(\\\"build\\\", help=\\\"Train a new checkpoint from corpora.\\\")\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"corpus\\\", nargs=\\\"+\\\", help=\\\"UTF-8 text corpus file(s).\\\")\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"-o\\\", \\\"--output\\\", required=True, help=\\\"Checkpoint to write (.cotw.gz).\\\")\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"--order\\\", type=int, default=3)\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"--alpha\\\", type=float, default=0.25)\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"--seed\\\", type=int, default=7)\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"--kernel\\\", choices=[\\\"scan\\\", \\\"weave\\\"], default=\\\"scan\\\",\\n                   help=\\\"scan: CoT token probes the dataset (default). weave: CoT tokens woven into the weights.\\\")\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"--no-cot-weave\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"(weave kernel) do not weave CoT tokens in.\\\")\\n    add_vocab_args(b)\\n    b.set_defaults(func=cmd_build)\\n\\n    e = sub.add_parser(\\\"extend\\\", help=\\\"Extend an existing checkpoint.\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"model\\\", help=\\\"Checkpoint to extend.\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"corpus\\\", nargs=\\\"*\\\", help=\\\"Additional corpus file(s) (optional).\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"-o\\\", \\\"--output\\\", required=True, help=\\\"Checkpoint to write.\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"--decay\\\", type=float, default=1.0,\\n                   help=\\\"Scale existing weights by this factor before adding new data (e.g. 0.9).\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"--alpha\\\", type=float, default=None, help=\\\"Override smoothing alpha.\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"--no-cot-weave\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"(weave kernel) do not weave CoT tokens into new corpora.\\\")\\n    add_vocab_args(e)\\n    e.set_defaults(func=cmd_extend)\\n\\n    i = sub.add_parser(\\\"info\\\", help=\\\"Show checkpoint statistics.\\\")\\n    i.add_argument(\\\"model\\\")\\n    i.set_defaults(func=cmd_info)\\n\\n    g = sub.add_parser(\\\"generate\\\", help=\\\"Run the cybernetic loop from a checkpoint.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"model\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--kernel\\\", choices=[\\\"scan\\\", \\\"weave\\\"], default=None,\\n                   help=\\\"Override the checkpoint's kernel.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--prompt\\\", help=\\\"Initial prompt. If omitted you are asked each round.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--cycles\\\", type=int, default=4, help=\\\"Output->input feedback cycles per prompt.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--chunk\\\", type=int, default=20, help=\\\"Tokens per chunk between CoT tokens.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--chunks-per-cycle\\\", type=int, default=3)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--window\\\", type=int, default=40, help=\\\"Tokens of output piped back as the next prompt.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--beam\\\", type=int, default=8)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--tau\\\", type=float, default=0.65)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--temperature\\\", type=float, default=0.85)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--seed\\\", type=int, default=7)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--stack-target\\\", type=int, default=25,\\n                   help=\\\"Keep going until this many CoT tokens have stacked in order (0 = fixed-cycle mode).\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--max-retries\\\", type=int, default=25, help=\\\"Rejected chunks allowed per stack slot before forcing.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--strict\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Never force a token; retry until the attempt cap.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--scan-strength\\\", type=float, default=1.5, help=\\\"Weight of the dataset-scan bias on scores.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--scan-limit\\\", type=int, default=24, help=\\\"Max passages sampled per probe word.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--scan-span\\\", type=int, default=12, help=\\\"Tokens read after each occurrence.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--scan-mix\\\", type=float, default=0.5,\\n                   help=\\\"Weight of the last context word as a second probe (0 = CoT token only).\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--min-grounding\\\", type=float, default=0.15,\\n                   help=\\\"Stack mode (scan): min fraction of chunk tokens found in the scanned passages.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--no-learn\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Disable online learning from own output.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--show-cot\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Show CoT tokens in printed text (hidden by default).\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--trace\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Print controller diagnostics.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--save\\\", help=\\\"Append output to this text file.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--save-model\\\", help=\\\"Write the weights (incl. online learning) to this checkpoint at exit.\\\")\\n    g.set_defaults(func=cmd_generate)\\n\\n    args = ap.parse_args()\\n    args.func(args)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\nPYEOF\\ncd /tmp && rm -rf t2 && mkdir t2 && cd t2 && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport random\\nrandom.seed(1)\\nw=\\\"machine thought signal memory pattern energy system loop feedback network learning model state vector entropy order chaos light dark river stone\\\".split()\\nlines=[\\\" \\\".join(random.choice(w) for _ in range(random.randint(5,12)))+random.choice(\\\".!?\\\") for _ in range(400)]\\nopen(\\\"corpus.txt\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(\\\" \\\".join(lines))\\nopen(\\\"more.txt\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(\\\" \\\".join(lines[:100]))\\ncot=sorted(w[:12]+[\\\"river\\\",\\\"stone\\\",\\\"light\\\",\\\"dark\\\",\\\"chaos\\\",\\\"order\\\",\\\"entropy\\\",\\\"vector\\\",\\\"state\\\",\\\"model\\\",\\\"learning\\\",\\\"network\\\",\\\"ghostword\\\"])[:25]+[\\\"feedback\\\",\\\"loop\\\",\\\"signal\\\",\\\"energy\\\"]\\nopen(\\\"cot.txt\\\",\\\"w\\\").write(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(cot)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\\nEOF\\nS=/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py\\nset -e\\npython3 $S build corpus.txt -o base.cotw.gz --cot-vocab cot.txt\\npython3 $S extend base.cotw.gz more.txt -o v2.cotw.gz --decay 0.9\\npython3 $S info v2.cotw.gz\\necho ---- stack scan\\npython3 $S generate v2.cotw.gz --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" --stack-target 10 --chunk 12 --save-model v3.cotw.gz </dev/null 2>&1 | tail -9\\necho ---- fixed scan trace\\npython3 $S generate v3.cotw.gz --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" --stack-target 0 --cycles 2 --chunks-per-cycle 2 --chunk 8 --trace --show-cot </dev/null 2>&1 | head -14\\necho ---- weave override\\npython3 $S generate v3.cotw.gz --kernel weave --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" --stack-target 4 --chunk 10 </dev/null 2>&1 | tail -4\\necho ---- weave build + strict scan missing\\npython3 $S build corpus.txt -o w.cotw.gz --kernel weave --cot-vocab cot.txt 2>&1 | tail -1\\npython3 $S generate base.cotw.gz --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" --stack-target 25 --chunk 8 --strict --max-retries 2 </dev/null 2>&1 | grep -E \\\"stack|kernel\\\"\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:15:07.914526Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:15:07.914586Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_013PycGbaXu9Z1JMMMyxafbQ", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"format       cot-weights-v2   kernel scan\\norder        3   alpha 0.25\\nvocab types  85   tokens 3933.5   dataset 4275\\ncontexts     n=0: 1, n=1: 85, n=2: 1127\\nextensions   1   sources corpus.txt, more.txt\\ncycle        chaos dark energy entropy feedback ghostword learning light loop machine memory model network order pattern river signal state stone system thought vector simulate recall correct\\ndiverge=imagine converge=decide integrate=observe start=verify\\ncoverage     21/29 CoT words occur in the dataset; absent: ghostword, simulate, recall, correct, imagine, decide, observe, verify\\n---- stack scan\\n\\n[stack] depth 10/10  attempts 10  forced 1  monotonic order verified: True\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\nThe machine state dark! learning river learning order dark feedback entropy learning dark learning light chaos. pattern model pattern river feedback loop state model feedback dark entropy memory vector state system order system order learning state signal feedback signal river machine! light thought energy network stone light system river vector system chaos machine state learning order light stone entropy? light loop vector energy light chaos light dark energy model light order machine learning vector model river state learning energy river pattern network model network energy memory pattern state vector river stone dark chaos order energy state. dark system network memory chaos learning machine entropy feedback state system order learning memory system stone learning thought pattern order vector network stone light feedback signal\\n\\nUSER: \\nsaved weights -> v3.cotw.gz\\n---- fixed scan trace\\nscan coverage: 21/29 CoT words occur in the dataset (absent: ghostword, simulate, recall, correct, imagine, decide, observe, verify)\\nkernel: scan\\nCoT vocab: chaos dark energy entropy feedback ghostword learning light loop machine memory model network order pattern river signal state stone system thought vector simulate recall correct imagine decide observe verify\\n[cycle 1/2 chunk 1] tokens=8 mean_logp=-2.27 rep=0.12 -> chaos (T=0.85) scan[verify:start hits=0 ground=0.88]\\n[cycle 1/2 chunk 2] tokens=8 mean_logp=-2.52 rep=0.38 -> dark (T=0.85) scan[chaos:cycle hits=216 ground=0.88]\\n[cycle 2/2 chunk 1] tokens=8 mean_logp=-2.40 rep=0.12 -> energy (T=0.85) scan[observe:integrate hits=0 ground=1.00]\\n[cycle 2/2 chunk 2] tokens=8 mean_logp=-2.69 rep=0.12 -> entropy (T=0.85) scan[energy:cycle hits=194 ground=1.00]\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\nverify The machine state learning stone chaos? loop network system state chaos stone state feedback feedback. state thought state thought dark observe loop network system chaos learning machine energy chaos energy stone entropy machine. thought chaos system energy chaos entropy observe\\n\\nUSER: \\n---- weave override\\n\\nThe machine learning?\\n\\nUSER: \\n---- weave build + strict scan missing\\nbuilt w.cotw.gz [weave kernel]: 89 types, 3835 tokens, dataset 3434 tokens\\nkernel: scan\\n[stack] depth 5/25  attempts 6  forced 0  monotonic order verified: True\\n\",\"stderr\":\"warning: duplicate CoT word 'learning' at line 8 ignored\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'model' at line 14 ignored\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'network' at line 16 ignored\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'feedback' at line 26 ignored\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'loop' at line 27 ignored\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'signal' at line 28 ignored\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'energy' at line 29 ignored\\nnote: only 22 CoT words given, filling to 29 from fallback names\\nCoT vocab: chaos dark energy entropy feedback ghostword learning light loop machine memory model network order pattern river signal state stone system thought vector simulate recall correct imagine decide observe verify\\nscan coverage: 21/29 CoT words occur in the dataset (absent: ghostword, simulate, recall, correct, imagine, decide, observe, verify)\\nbuilt base.cotw.gz [scan kernel]: 85 types, 3435 tokens, dataset 3434 tokens\\nCoT vocab: chaos dark energy entropy feedback ghostword learning light loop machine memory model network order pattern river signal state stone system thought vector simulate recall correct imagine decide observe verify\\ndecayed existing weights by 0.9 (dataset is not decayed)\\nscan coverage: 21/29 CoT words occur in the dataset (absent: ghostword, simulate, recall, correct, imagine, decide, observe, verify)\\nextended -> v2.cotw.gz [scan kernel]: 85 types, 3933.5 tokens, dataset 4275 tokens\\n\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"format       cot-weights-v2   kernel scan\\norder        3   alpha 0.25\\nvocab types  85   tokens 3933.5   dataset 4275\\ncontexts     n=0: 1, n=1: 85, n=2: 1127\\nextensions   1   sources corpus.txt, more.txt\\ncycle        chaos dark energy entropy feedback ghostword learning light loop machine memory model network order pattern river signal state stone system thought vector simulate recall correct\\ndiverge=imagine converge=decide integrate=observe start=verify\\ncoverage     21/29 CoT words occur in the dataset; absent: ghostword, simulate, recall, correct, imagine, decide, observe, verify\\n---- stack scan\\n\\n[stack] depth 10/10  attempts 10  forced 1  monotonic order verified: True\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\nThe machine state dark! learning river learning order dark feedback entropy learning dark learning light chaos. pattern model pattern river feedback loop state model feedback dark entropy memory vector state system order system order learning state signal feedback signal river machine! light thought energy network stone light system river vector system chaos machine state learning order light stone entropy? light loop vector energy light chaos light dark energy model light order machine learning vector model river state learning energy river pattern network model network energy memory pattern state vector river stone dark chaos order energy state. dark system network memory chaos learning machine entropy feedback state system order learning memory system stone learning thought pattern order vector network stone light feedback signal\\n\\nUSER: \\nsaved weights -> v3.cotw.gz\\n---- fixed scan trace\\nscan coverage: 21/29 CoT words occur in the dataset (absent: ghostword, simulate, recall, correct, imagine, decide, observe, verify)\\nkernel: scan\\nCoT vocab: chaos dark energy entropy feedback ghostword learning light loop machine memory model network order pattern river signal state stone system thought vector simulate recall correct imagine decide observe verify\\n[cycle 1/2 chunk 1] tokens=8 mean_logp=-2.27 rep=0.12 -> chaos (T=0.85) scan[verify:start hits=0 ground=0.88]\\n[cycle 1/2 chunk 2] tokens=8 mean_logp=-2.52 rep=0.38 -> dark (T=0.85) scan[chaos:cycle hits=216 ground=0.88]\\n[cycle 2/2 chunk 1] tokens=8 mean_logp=-2.40 rep=0.12 -> energy (T=0.85) scan[observe:integrate hits=0 ground=1.00]\\n[cycle 2/2 chunk 2] tokens=8 mean_logp=-2.69 rep=0.12 -> entropy (T=0.85) scan[energy:cycle hits=194 ground=1.00]\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\nverify The machine state learning stone chaos? loop network system state chaos stone state feedback feedback. state thought state thought dark observe loop network system chaos learning machine energy chaos energy stone entropy machine. thought chaos system energy chaos entropy observe\\n\\nUSER: \\n---- weave override\\n\\nThe machine learning?\\n\\nUSER: \\n---- weave build + strict scan missing\\nbuilt w.cotw.gz [weave kernel]: 89 types, 3835 tokens, dataset 3434 tokens\\nkernel: scan\\n[stack] depth 5/25  attempts 6  forced 0  monotonic order verified: True\\n\",\"stderr\":\"warning: duplicate CoT word 'learning' at line 8 ignored\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'model' at line 14 ignored\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'network' at line 16 ignored\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'feedback' at line 26 ignored\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'loop' at line 27 ignored\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'signal' at line 28 ignored\\nwarning: duplicate CoT word 'energy' at line 29 ignored\\nnote: only 22 CoT words given, filling to 29 from fallback names\\nCoT vocab: chaos dark energy entropy feedback ghostword learning light loop machine memory model network order pattern river signal state stone system thought vector simulate recall correct imagine decide observe verify\\nscan coverage: 21/29 CoT words occur in the dataset (absent: ghostword, simulate, recall, correct, imagine, decide, observe, verify)\\nbuilt base.cotw.gz [scan kernel]: 85 types, 3435 tokens, dataset 3434 tokens\\nCoT vocab: chaos dark energy entropy feedback ghostword learning light loop machine memory model network order pattern river signal state stone system thought vector simulate recall correct imagine decide observe verify\\ndecayed existing weights by 0.9 (dataset is not decayed)\\nscan coverage: 21/29 CoT words occur in the dataset (absent: ghostword, simulate, recall, correct, imagine, decide, observe, verify)\\nextended -> v2.cotw.gz [scan kernel]: 85 types, 3933.5 tokens, dataset 4275 tokens\\n\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:15:11.732064Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:15:13.067502Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Diagnosing the scan output to locate the integration marker."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:15:13.067569Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:15:13.316064Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01VQn82GvRPgwEtZsjqeZqU2", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:15:13.340314Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:15:13.340342Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01VQn82GvRPgwEtZsjqeZqU2", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py", "name": "cot weight extender", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "\n\nThe file cards appear with your reply, and where they sit relative to its text depends on the app the user is reading in; finish the reply with text, and refer to a file by its name, never as above or below."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:15:19.633716Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:15:21.175572Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I rewrote the kernel in `cot_weight_extender.py` so the CoT token scans the dataset instead of the dataset supplying CoT tokens. I read \"invert the cot to the dataset scan\" that way, so tell me if you meant something else. I ran a smoke test of build, extend, info, both generate modes, the kernel override and strict mode, and all of it ran.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Old direction (kept as `--kernel weave`):** the dataset gave you the CoT words, they were woven into the training stream, and the model had to emit them itself.\n- **New direction (`--kernel scan`, now the default):** a CoT token is a probe. The loop finds every occurrence of that word in the dataset, collects the tokens that follow each one, and uses them to boost matching candidates in the next chunk. CoT tokens are never woven into the weights and never appear in the n-gram context, so they only steer the scan. The last context word is also used as a second probe, at weight `--scan-mix` (default 0.5).\n- **Role profiles:** diverge reads more passages over a longer span, converge reads fewer over a shorter span, and integrate reads a longer span after the pipe-back. The controller picks the role the same way it did before.\n- **Stack mode:** a slot is accepted when the expected word is found in the dataset and enough of the chunk (`--min-grounding`, default 0.15) appears in the scanned passages. A word that never occurs in the dataset can't be grounded, so its slot is forced and flagged. With `--strict` the run stops there instead.\n- **Checkpoints:** they now store the dataset tokens, which the scanner reads, and the kernel name. Older v1 checkpoints still load as weave.\n- **Vocabulary swaps:** with the scan kernel, `extend --cot-vocab` just swaps the words, because there is nothing to remap.\n- **Coverage report:** `build`, `extend`, `info` and `generate` tell you how many of the 29 CoT words occur in the dataset.\n- **New flags on `generate`:** `--kernel` (override the checkpoint), `--scan-strength`, `--scan-limit`, `--scan-span`, `--scan-mix` and `--min-grounding`.\n\n**Things to know**\n- Your custom CoT words should actually appear in the dataset. In my test, 8 of 29 didn't. Non-strict runs forced those slots, and a strict run stopped at depth 5/25 on the first absent word.\n- `--decay` only scales the n-gram weights. The dataset the scanner reads is not decayed.\n- Checkpoints are larger now because they hold the full token stream.\n- I also fixed an old slicing bug: with `--order 1`, `context[-0:]` returned the whole context in the online-learning step, and a helper now returns an empty list.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-14T22:15:21.252730Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T22:15:21.252730Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a13c78-d2b6-7953-a860-b665c91eb1ef"}, {"uuid": "01a13c80-e748-7d72-93ac-1766806958fd", "text": "use a huggingface dataset 200mb", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:20:44.267647Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:20:44.267647Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "use a huggingface dataset 200mb", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-14T22:20:44.267931Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-14T22:20:44.267931Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a13c78-d2b6-718c-8235-01ada8f49f45"}, {"uuid": "01a13c80-e748-7a79-ba39-21d00c398494", "text": "\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nBuild works (4.4M tokens in 30s, 583 MB peak), so I'm now testing generate, extend, info and loading an old checkpoint.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n`cot_weight_extender.py` can now train from a streamed Hugging Face dataset, capped at 200MB of text by default. I couldn't reach huggingface.co from my sandbox, so I tested the same `datasets` streaming path on a local 33MB JSONL file. A real Hugging Face run is untested.\n\nFor a ~200MB run, `Salesforce/wikitext` with config `wikitext-103-raw-v1` is a good fit. Its train split is about 550MB, and streaming stops at your byte budget, so you never download the whole thing.\n\n```\npip install datasets\npython cot_weight_extender.py build -o wiki.cotw \\\n    --hf-dataset Salesforce/wikitext --hf-config wikitext-103-raw-v1 \\\n    --hf-max-bytes 200MB --cot-vocab cot.txt\n```\n\nYou can also pass local corpus files alongside `--hf-dataset`, and `extend` takes the same flags. `--hf-field`, `--hf-split` and `--hf-data-files` cover other datasets and loaders.\n\n**What changed to make 200MB workable**\n- **Streaming:** documents are trained one at a time, so memory stays flat.\n- **Compact dataset:** the dataset the scan kernel reads is now an int32 id array plus a word table, with a numpy position index, instead of a Python list.\n- **Memory bound:** `--max-entries` (default 5M) caps the n-gram tables. When they grow past it, rare n-grams (count below 2, then 3, and so on) are dropped. This is lossy for rare n-grams, and `0` turns it off. The scan kernel still reads the full dataset.\n- **Checkpoint format:** it is now a zip holding the model state as JSON plus the dataset ids as a `.npy` file. Old v1 and v2 gzip checkpoints still load.\n- **CoT vocabulary without a list:** with no `--cot-vocab`, the words are picked from the first ~2MB of the stream.\n\n**What I measured**\n- **Throughput:** the local test file gave 4.4M tokens in 30s (about 210k tokens/s) and peaked at 583 MB with `--max-entries 1.5M`.\n- **Extend, generate and legacy loading:** all worked.\n- **Weave kernel:** also worked.\n- **Estimate for 200MB of real English:** roughly 35M tokens, about 3 minutes plus pruning passes, and a few GB of RAM at the default cap. I did not measure that.\n- **Pruning on real text:** my test data was random, so it pruned harder than real text will. Raise `--max-entries` if you have the memory.\n- **Raw wikitext markup:** it includes things like `= Heading =` lines and ` @-@ `, which will end up in the n-grams and the scan.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:20:44.267438Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:22:22.818957Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Working out how to access a large dataset under network limits."}, {"summary": "Redesigning the memory-heavy n-gram approach for scale."}, {"summary": "Planning compact token storage and local testing without network access."}, {"summary": "Weighing checkpoint formats against rebuild cost and memory limits."}, {"summary": "Choosing between simpler pruned storage and a complex compact rewrite."}, {"summary": "Bounding entry counts with periodic pruning during streaming."}, {"summary": "Settling on a dataset source and streaming vocabulary setup."}, {"summary": "Unifying vocabulary selection across local and streamed sources."}, {"summary": "Building a sorted index for fast word-position lookups."}, {"summary": "Designing streaming checkpoint writes for large model states."}, {"summary": "Deciding which context levels to prune for quality."}, {"summary": "Estimating memory cost per entry to size pruning limits."}, {"summary": "Wiring together dataset streaming, vocabulary setup, and checkpoint ingestion."}, {"summary": "Planning synthetic test data and parsing size inputs for sources."}, {"summary": "Streaming a byte budget preview over document batches."}, {"summary": "Weighting word positions to bias sampled training text."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:22:22.819055Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:22:23.160754Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01LhasYBfmKnQYHrMbfk3THg", "name": "web_search", "input": {"mode": "standard", "query": "Salesforce/wikitext wikitext-103-raw-v1 Hugging Face dataset size"}, "message": "Searching the web", "integration_name": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "globe", "context": null, "display_content": null, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:22:23.611488Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:22:23.611554Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01LhasYBfmKnQYHrMbfk3THg", "name": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "knowledge", "title": "huggingface.co", "url": "https://huggingface.co/datasets/EleutherAI/wikitext_document_level/blob/1bd38e4650dd5ed7d355b9546671528097f20751/REA