n=huggingface.co", "site_name": "huggingface"}, "is_missing": false, "text": "Commit\n\u00b7\nc8a1c90\n1\n\nAdd wikitext-2-v1 data files\n\n- config_name: wikitext-103-v1\n\npath: wikitext-103-v1/train-*\n\npath: wikitext-103-v1/validation-*\n\n# Dataset Card for \"wikitext\"\n\n- config_name: wikitext-103-v1\n\npath: wikitext-103-v1/train-*\n\npath: wikitext-103-v1/validation-*\n\n- config_name: wikitext-2-v1\n\npath: wikitext-2-v1/test-*\n\n103 |\n\npath: wikitext-2-v1/train-*\n\npath: wikitext-2-v1/validation-*\n\n# Dataset Card for \"wikitext\"\n\n\"builder_name\": \"wikitext\",\n\n\"config_name\": \"wikitext-2-v1\",\n\n\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/research.metamind.io/wikitext/wikitext-2-v1.zip\": {\n\n\"wikitext-103-raw-v1\": {\n\n\"description\": \" The WikiText language modeling dataset is a collection of over 100 million tokens extracted from the set of verified\\n Good and Featured articles on Wikipedia. The dataset is available under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike\\n License.\\n\",\n\n\"builder_name\": \"wikitext\",\n\n\"dataset_name\": \"wikitext\",\n\n\"config_name\": \"wikitext-2-v1\",\n\n\"wikitext-103-raw-v1\": {\n\n\"description\": \" The WikiText language modeling dataset is a collection of over 100 million tokens extracted from the set of verified\\n Good and Featured articles on Wikipedia. The dataset is available under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike\\n License.\\n\",\n\nwikitext-2-v1/test-00000-of-00001.parquet\n\nversion https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\n\nsize 685430\n\nwikitext-2-v1/train-00000-of-00001.parquet\n\nversion https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\n\nsize 6068114\n\nwikitext-2-v1/validation-00000-of-00001.parquet\n\nversion https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\n\nsize 617738", "is_citable": true, "prompt_context_metadata": {"search_provider": "anthropic", "url": "https://huggingface.co/datasets/Salesforce/wikitext/commit/c8a1c90b2b6554c017d92ca208fc0c03460685be"}, "links": null}, {"type": "knowledge", "title": "huggingface.co", "url": "https://huggingface.co/datasets/Salesforce/wikitext/commit/6231e49f19a707241d6b84d9cff60a3a86b85a85", "metadata": {"type": "webpage_metadata", "site_domain": "huggingface.co", "favicon_url": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?sz=64&domain=huggingface.co", "site_name": "huggingface"}, "is_missing": false, "text": "Datasets:\n\nModalities:\nText\nFormats:\nparquet\nLanguages:\nEnglish\nArXiv:\nLibraries:\nDatasets\nDask\nLicense:\njr303 commited on\nCommit\n6231e49\n\u00b7\nverified \u00b7\n1 Parent(s): 25779cb\n\nDelete data file\n\nBrowse files\nwikitext-103-raw-v1/train-00000-of-00002.parquet DELETED\n@@ -1,3 +0,0 @@\n1\n- version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\n2\n- oid sha256:eda855422d336638fe4507fe7b7a7961f3f7b821a93306bab7b43578e243a2ca\n3\n- size 156617018", "is_citable": true, "prompt_context_metadata": {"search_provider": "anthropic", "url": "https://huggingface.co/datasets/Salesforce/wikitext/commit/6231e49f19a707241d6b84d9cff60a3a86b85a85"}, "links": null}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": null, "message": null, "integration_name": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "globe", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:22:33.053330Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:24:13.197259Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01TCXfiXz2eRqFayHMUECVKA", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cat > /mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py <<'PYEOF'\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nCoT weight extender  (scan kernel, Hugging Face streaming)\n==========================================================\n\nThe cybernetic n-gram generator as a persistent, extendable model, with the CoT\nkernel INVERTED and able to train from a streamed Hugging Face dataset.\n\n  weave kernel (old)   dataset -> CoT.  CoT words are woven into the training\n                       stream and the model has to emit them itself.\n  scan kernel (new)    CoT -> dataset.  A CoT token is a PROBE: the loop finds the\n                       word in the dataset, collects the passages that follow each\n                       occurrence, and turns them into a bias over the next chunk.\n                       CoT tokens never enter the weights or the n-gram context.\n\nScan profile per CoT role:\n  cycle token   standard scan\n  diverge       more passages, longer span, slower decay   (wider read, T up)\n  converge      fewer passages, shorter span, faster decay (tighter read, T down)\n  integrate     standard passages, longer span             (re-read after pipe-back)\n\nCommands\n  build     Train a new checkpoint from local corpora and/or a Hugging Face dataset.\n  extend    Grow a checkpoint: more data, optional decay, optional new CoT vocab.\n  generate  Run the cybernetic loop from a checkpoint (optionally save weights).\n  info      Print checkpoint statistics and CoT-vocab coverage of the dataset.\n\nHugging Face datasets (needs `pip install datasets`)\n  --hf-dataset NAME     e.g. Salesforce/wikitext   (or \"json\"/\"text\" + --hf-data-files)\n  --hf-config CONFIG    e.g. wikitext-103-raw-v1\n  --hf-split SPLIT      default: train\n  --hf-field FIELD      text column (auto-detected if omitted)\n  --hf-max-bytes SIZE   stop after this much text, default 200MB (e.g. 50MB, 1GB)\n  The dataset is STREAMED and cut off at the byte budget, so the full download is\n  never required. Documents are trained one by one, so memory stays flat.\n\nScale handling (built for hundreds of MB of text)\n  * The dataset is stored as an int32 token-id array + word table, not a Python list.\n  * The scan index is a sorted-position (CSR) numpy index, built on first use.\n  * n-gram memory is bounded by --max-entries: when the context tables grow past it,\n    low-count n-grams (count < 2, then < 3, ...) are pruned. This is lossy for rare\n    n-grams; 0 disables pruning.\n  * Checkpoints are zip files (JSON model state + a .npy of dataset ids). Old gzip\n    JSON checkpoints (v1/v2) still load.\n\nCustom CoT vocabulary (--cot-vocab FILE): one word per line ('#' comments ignored),\nused in order or sorted with --cot-sort:\n      entries  1..25   the stack cycle, in required order\n      entry    26      diverge\n      entry    27      converge\n      entry    28      integrate\n      entry    29      start\nWith the scan kernel the words should occur in the dataset (coverage is reported).\nWithout --cot-vocab the words are the most frequent 4+ letter words of the first\n~2MB of data, shuffled.\n\nExamples:\n  python cot_weight_extender.py build -o wiki.cotw --hf-dataset Salesforce/wikitext \\\\\n      --hf-config wikitext-103-raw-v1 --hf-max-bytes 200MB --cot-vocab cot.txt\n  python cot_weight_extender.py extend wiki.cotw more.txt -o wiki2.cotw --decay 0.9\n  python cot_weight_extender.py generate wiki.cotw --prompt \"The machine\" --trace\n  python cot_weight_extender.py info wiki.cotw\n\nDependencies: NumPy (+ `datasets` only for --hf-dataset)\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport gzip\nimport io\nimport itertools\nimport json\nimport math\nimport random\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport zipfile\nfrom array import array\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Dict, Iterable, Iterator, List, Sequence, Tuple\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nFORMAT = \"cot-weights-v3\"\nACCEPTED_FORMATS = (\"cot-weights-v1\", \"cot-weights-v2\", FORMAT)\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# CoT tokens\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass CotToken(str):\n    \"\"\"A CoT marker inserted by the loop. It is a str, but isinstance() tells it\n    apart from the same word appearing as ordinary text, so hiding markers never\n    deletes real words from the output.\"\"\"\n\n\n# Fallback names, used only if the vocabulary source has too few distinct words.\nDEFAULT_COT = [\n    \"simulate\", \"recall\", \"correct\", \"imagine\", \"decide\",\n    \"observe\", \"verify\", \"associate\", \"plan\", \"anticipate\",\n    \"reflect\", \"abstract\", \"act\", \"question\", \"compare\",\n    \"adapt\", \"predict\", \"summarize\", \"monitor\", \"infer\",\n    \"consolidate\", \"attend\", \"evaluate\", \"prioritize\", \"hypothesize\",\n    \"diverge\", \"converge\", \"integrate\", \"synthesize\",\n]\nCOT_COUNT = 29  # 25 cycle tokens + diverge + converge + integrate + start\nPIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens\nSENTENCE_END = (\".\", \"!\", \"?\")\nVOCAB_PEEK_BYTES = 2_000_000  # data sampled to pick CoT words when none are given\n\nCOT_CYCLE: List[str] = []\nCOT_DIVERGE = COT_CONVERGE = COT_INTEGRATE = COT_START = CotToken(\"\")\nCOT: set = set()\n\n_STOP = {\n    \"that\", \"with\", \"have\", \"from\", \"this\", \"they\", \"were\", \"been\", \"will\", \"would\", \"there\",\n    \"their\", \"what\", \"when\", \"which\", \"your\", \"them\", \"then\", \"than\", \"into\", \"only\", \"also\",\n    \"some\", \"such\", \"more\", \"most\", \"other\", \"about\", \"could\", \"should\", \"these\", \"those\",\n}\n\n\ndef set_cot_tokens(words: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Install the CoT vocabulary: 25 cycle tokens, then diverge, converge,\n    integrate, start.\"\"\"\n    global COT_CYCLE, COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START, COT\n    toks = [CotToken(w) for w in words]\n    COT_CYCLE = toks[:25]\n    COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START = toks[25:29]\n    COT = {str(t) for t in toks}\n\n\ndef current_cot_words() -> List[str]:\n    return [str(t) for t in COT_CYCLE] + [str(COT_DIVERGE), str(COT_CONVERGE),\n                                          str(COT_INTEGRATE), str(COT_START)]\n\n\ndef _top_up(words: List[str], count: int) -> List[str]:\n    seen = {w.lower() for w in words}\n    for d in DEFAULT_COT:\n        if len(words) >= count:\n            break\n        if d.lower() not in seen:\n            seen.add(d.lower())\n            words.append(d)\n    return words\n\n\ndef select_cot_tokens(text: str, seed: int, count: int = COT_COUNT) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Pick CoT tokens from the data: the most frequent alphabetic words of 4+\n    letters (skipping common function words), shuffled so the required order is\n    non-monotonic. Used when no --cot-vocab is given.\"\"\"\n    counts = Counter(tokenize(text))\n    pool = [(w, c) for w, c in counts.items()\n            if w.isalpha() and len(w) >= 4 and w.lower() not in _STOP]\n    pool.sort(key=lambda wc: (-wc[1], wc[0]))\n    words, seen = [], set()\n    for w, _ in pool:\n        if w.lower() not in seen:\n            seen.add(w.lower())\n            words.append(w)\n        if len(words) >= count:\n            break\n    random.Random(seed).shuffle(words)\n    return _top_up(words, count)\n\n\ndef load_cot_vocab(path: str, sort: str = \"none\", count: int = COT_COUNT) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Load a custom CoT vocabulary from a text file (one word per line).\n\n    sort: 'none' keeps file order (use when the list is already sorted the way you\n    want the stack to run), 'alpha' / 'alpha-desc' sort case-insensitively,\n    'length' sorts short to long. Sorting happens BEFORE truncating to `count`.\n    \"\"\"\n    words, seen = [], set()\n    for lineno, line in enumerate(Path(path).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\").splitlines(), 1):\n        w = line.split(\"#\", 1)[0].strip()\n        if not w:\n            continue\n        if len(w.split()) != 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{path}:{lineno}: CoT words must be a single token, got {w!r}\")\n        if w.lower() in seen:\n            print(f\"warning: duplicate CoT word {w!r} at line {lineno} ignored\", file=sys.stderr)\n            continue\n        seen.add(w.lower())\n        words.append(w)\n    if sort == \"alpha\":\n        words.sort(key=str.lower)\n    elif sort == \"alpha-desc\":\n        words.sort(key=str.lower, reverse=True)\n    elif sort == \"length\":\n        words.sort(key=lambda w: (len(w), w.lower()))\n    if len(words) > count:\n        print(f\"note: {len(words)} CoT words given, using the first {count}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        words = words[:count]\n    elif len(words) < count:\n        print(f\"note: only {len(words)} CoT words given, filling to {count} from fallback names\",\n              file=sys.stderr)\n        words = _top_up(words, count)\n    return words\n\n\nset_cot_tokens(DEFAULT_COT)\n\n\ndef tokenize(text: str) -> List[str]:\n    return text.split()\n\n\ndef strip_cot(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> List[str]:\n    return [t for t in tokens if not isinstance(t, CotToken)]\n\n\ndef tail_ctx(tokens: Sequence[str], k: int) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Last k tokens (empty for k <= 0; avoids the tokens[-0:] whole-list trap).\"\"\"\n    return list(tokens[len(tokens) - k:]) if k > 0 else []\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Compact dataset store + scanner (CoT token -> dataset passages -> bias)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef norm_word(w: str) -> str:\n    return str(w).strip(\".,;:!?\\\"'()[]{}\").lower()\n\n\nclass TokenStore:\n    \"\"\"The dataset as a word table plus an int32 id per token (4 bytes/token).\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, words: Sequence[str] = (), ids=None):\n        assert array(\"i\").itemsize == 4\n        self.words: List[str] = list(words)\n        self.word_id: Dict[str, int] = {w: i for i, w in enumerate(self.words)}\n        self._base = np.asarray(ids, dtype=np.intc) if ids is not None else np.zeros(0, dtype=np.intc)\n        self._buf = array(\"i\")\n        self.version = 0\n\n    def add(self, tokens: Iterable[str]) -> None:\n        wid, words, buf = self.word_id, self.words, self._buf\n        for t in tokens:\n            i = wid.get(t)\n            if i is None:\n                i = len(words)\n                wid[t] = i\n                words.append(t)\n            buf.append(i)\n        self.version += 1\n\n    def ids(self) -> np.ndarray:\n        if self._buf:\n            add = np.frombuffer(self._buf, dtype=np.intc).copy()\n            self._base = np.concatenate([self._base, add]) if self._base.size else add\n            self._buf = array(\"i\")\n        return self._base\n\n    def __len__(self) -> int:\n        return int(self._base.size) + len(self._buf)\n\n\n# role -> (passage multiplier, span multiplier, per-step decay)\nSCAN_PROFILES = {\n    \"cycle\": (1.0, 1.0, 0.85),\n    \"diverge\": (2.0, 2.0, 0.92),\n    \"converge\": (0.5, 0.5, 0.75),\n    \"integrate\": (1.0, 1.5, 0.88),\n    \"start\": (1.0, 1.0, 0.85),\n}\n\n\ndef cot_role(tok: str) -> str:\n    s = str(tok)\n    if s == str(COT_DIVERGE):\n        return \"diverge\"\n    if s == str(COT_CONVERGE):\n        return \"converge\"\n    if s == str(COT_INTEGRATE):\n        return \"integrate\"\n    if s == str(COT_START):\n        return \"start\"\n    return \"cycle\"\n\n\nclass DatasetScanner:\n    \"\"\"Inverted index over the dataset (word -> sorted token positions, CSR layout).\n    A CoT token is a key: occurrences of its word are located, the `span` tokens that\n    follow are collected with geometric decay, and the result is a bias in [0, 1].\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, store: TokenStore, strength: float = 1.5, limit: int = 24,\n                 span: int = 12, mix: float = 0.5):\n        self.store = store\n        self.strength = strength\n        self.limit = max(1, int(limit))\n        self.span = max(2, int(span))\n        self.mix = max(0.0, float(mix))\n        self._ver = -1\n\n    def _build(self) -> None:\n        ids = self.store.ids()\n        words = self.store.words\n        group_of: Dict[str, int] = {}\n        group = np.empty(len(words), dtype=np.int32)\n        for i, w in enumerate(words):\n            group[i] = group_of.setdefault(norm_word(w), len(group_of))\n        gids = group[ids] if ids.size else ids.astype(np.int32)\n        self._order = np.argsort(gids, kind=\"stable\").astype(np.int32)\n        counts = np.bincount(gids, minlength=len(group_of)) if ids.size else np.zeros(len(group_of), int)\n        self._starts = np.zeros(len(group_of) + 1, dtype=np.int64)\n        np.cumsum(counts, out=self._starts[1:])\n        self._group_of = group_of\n        self._ids = ids\n        self._ver = self.store.version\n\n    def _ready(self) -> None:\n        if self._ver != self.store.version:\n            self._build()\n\n    def positions(self, word: str) -> np.ndarray:\n        self._ready()\n        g = self._group_of.get(norm_word(word))\n        if g is None:\n            return self._order[:0]\n        return self._order[self._starts[g]:self._starts[g + 1]]\n\n    def hits(self, word: str) -> int:\n        return int(len(self.positions(word)))\n\n    def coverage(self, words: Sequence[str]) -> Tuple[int, List[str]]:\n        missing = [w for w in words if self.hits(w) == 0]\n        return len(words) - len(missing), missing\n\n    def bias(self, cot: str, context: Sequence[str], rng: random.Random) -> Tuple[Dict[str, float], int]:\n        \"\"\"Scan with `cot` as probe (plus, at weight `mix`, the last context word).\n        Returns (normalised bias over tokens, number of dataset hits for `cot`).\"\"\"\n        self._ready()\n        limit_mult, span_mult, decay = SCAN_PROFILES[cot_role(cot)]\n        limit = max(1, int(round(self.limit * limit_mult)))\n        span = max(2, int(round(self.span * span_mult)))\n        probes = [(str(cot), 1.0)]\n        if context and self.mix > 0:\n            probes.append((str(context[-1]), self.mix))\n        ids, n = self._ids, len(self._ids)\n        weights: Dict[int, float] = defaultdict(float)\n        cot_hits = 0\n        for pi, (word, w) in enumerate(probes):\n            pos = self.positions(word)\n            if pi == 0:\n                cot_hits = int(len(pos))\n            if len(pos) == 0:\n                continue\n            if len(pos) > limit:\n                pos = pos[rng.sample(range(len(pos)), limit)]\n            pos = pos.astype(np.int64)\n            share = w / len(pos)\n            for off in range(1, span + 1):\n                j = pos + off\n                j = j[j < n]\n                if j.size == 0:\n                    break\n                wt = share * (decay ** (off - 1))\n                for t in ids[j].tolist():\n                    weights[t] += wt\n        if not weights:\n            return {}, cot_hits\n        top = max(weights.values())\n        words = self.store.words\n        return {words[i]: v / top for i, v in weights.items()}, cot_hits\n\n\ndef grounding(new: Sequence[str], bias) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Fraction of generated tokens that occur in the scanned passages.\"\"\"\n    if not new or not bias:\n        return 0.0\n    return sum(1 for t in new if t in bias) / len(new)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# N-gram model (serialisation, decay, pruning, remapping)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass NGramModel:\n    \"\"\"Smoothed n-gram model with backoff, trainable offline and online.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, order: int = 3, alpha: float = 0.25):\n        self.order = max(1, int(order))\n        self.alpha = max(1e-9, float(alpha))\n        self.counts = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(self.order)]\n        self.vocab = Counter()\n        self.total_tokens = 0\n\n    def _update(self, tokens: Sequence[str], start: int) -> None:\n        for i in range(start, len(tokens)):\n            target = tokens[i]\n            self.vocab[target] += 1\n            self.total_tokens += 1\n            for ctx_len in range(self.order):\n                if ctx_len > i:\n                    break\n                context = tuple(tokens[i - ctx_len:i]) if ctx_len else ()\n                self.counts[ctx_len][context][target] += 1\n\n    def train(self, text: str, cot: bool = True) -> None:\n        \"\"\"cot=True weaves CoT tokens in after each sentence (weave kernel).\n        The scan kernel trains with cot=False: the weights never see CoT tokens.\"\"\"\n        raw = tokenize(text)\n        if cot:\n            woven, k = [], 0\n            for tok in raw:\n                woven.append(tok)\n                if tok.endswith(SENTENCE_END):\n                    woven.append(COT_CYCLE[k % len(COT_CYCLE)])\n                    k += 1\n            raw = woven\n        tokens = [\"<bos>\"] * (self.order - 1) + raw + [\"<eos>\"]\n        self._update(tokens, self.order - 1)\n\n    def learn(self, tokens: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Online update from the model's own output (feedback learning).\"\"\"\n        self._update(list(tokens), 1)\n\n    # ---- size control ----------------------------------------------------\n    def n_entries(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"(context, target) pairs stored above unigram level - the memory driver.\"\"\"\n        return sum(len(c) for lv in self.counts[1:] for c in lv.values())\n\n    def _prune_levels(self) -> range:\n        return range(2 if self.order > 2 else 1, self.order)\n\n    def prune(self, min_count: float) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Drop (context, target) pairs with count < min_count from the high-order\n        tables. Lossy for rare n-grams; the unigram table and (for order > 2) the\n        bigram table are kept whole so backoff always has something to use.\"\"\"\n        removed = 0\n        for lvl in self._prune_levels():\n            table = self.counts[lvl]\n            for ctx in list(table.keys()):\n                counter = table[ctx]\n                for tok in [t for t, n in counter.items() if n < min_count]:\n                    del counter[tok]\n                    removed += 1\n                if not counter:\n                    del table[ctx]\n        return removed\n\n    def enforce_budget(self, max_entries: int, log=None) -> None:\n        if max_entries <= 0 or self.n_entries() <= max_entries:\n            return\n        target = int(max_entries * 0.75)\n        for mc in range(2, 9):\n            removed = self.prune(mc)\n            if log:\n                log(f\"  pruned {removed} n-grams with count < {mc}; entries now {self.n_entries()}\")\n            if self.n_entries() <= target:\n                break\n\n    # ---- weight extension ------------------------------------------------\n    def scale(self, factor: float) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Multiply every stored weight (decay old knowledge before extending).\"\"\"\n        if factor == 1.0:\n            return\n        for level in self.counts:\n            for counter in level.values():\n                for tok in counter:\n                    counter[tok] *= factor\n        for tok in self.vocab:\n            self.vocab[tok] *= factor\n        self.total_tokens *= factor\n\n    def remap_tokens(self, mapping: Dict[str, str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Rename tokens everywhere (contexts and targets). Colliding counts are\n        summed. Weave kernel only: transfers CoT behaviour to a new vocabulary.\"\"\"\n        if not mapping:\n            return\n\n        def m(t):\n            return mapping.get(t, t)\n\n        new_counts = []\n        for level in self.counts:\n            nl = defaultdict(Counter)\n            for ctx, counter in level.items():\n                nctx = tuple(m(t) for t in ctx)\n                for tok, n in counter.items():\n                    nl[nctx][m(tok)] += n\n            new_counts.append(nl)\n        self.counts = new_counts\n        nv = Counter()\n        for tok, n in self.vocab.items():\n            nv[m(tok)] += n\n        self.vocab = nv\n\n    # ---- serialisation ---------------------------------------------------\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return {\n            \"order\": self.order,\n            \"alpha\": self.alpha,\n            \"total_tokens\": self.total_tokens,\n            \"vocab\": {str(k): v for k, v in self.vocab.items()},\n            \"counts\": [[[list(ctx), {str(t): n for t, n in c.items()}]\n                        for ctx, c in level.items()] for level in self.counts],\n        }\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> \"NGramModel\":\n        model = cls(order=d[\"order\"], alpha=d[\"alpha\"])\n        model.total_tokens = d[\"total_tokens\"]\n        model.vocab = Counter(d[\"vocab\"])\n        model.counts = []\n        for level in d[\"counts\"]:\n            lv = defaultdict(Counter)\n            for ctx, counter in level:\n                lv[tuple(ctx)] = Counter(counter)\n            model.counts.append(lv)\n        return model\n\n    def candidates(self, context_tokens: Sequence[str], limit: int = 80) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:\n        vocab_size = max(1, len(self.vocab))\n        context = list(context_tokens)\n        counter = Counter()\n        for ctx_len in range(min(self.order - 1, len(context)), -1, -1):\n            key = tuple(context[-ctx_len:]) if ctx_len else ()\n            found = self.counts[ctx_len].get(key)\n            if not found:\n                continue\n            weight = 1.0 + 0.7 * ctx_len\n            for token, count in found.items():\n                counter[token] += weight * count\n            if ctx_len >= 1:\n                break\n        if not counter:\n            counter.update(self.vocab)\n        counter.pop(\"<bos>\", None)\n        total = sum(counter.values())\n        ranked = []\n        for token, count in counter.items():\n            prob = (count + self.alpha) / (total + self.alpha * vocab_size)\n            ranked.append((token, math.log(max(prob, 1e-12))))\n        ranked.sort(key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\n        return ranked[:max(1, limit)]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Non-isomorphic fragments (weights are saved with the checkpoint)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass NonIsomorphicFragments:\n    def __init__(self, seed: int = 17):\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        self.w_context = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 3))\n        self.w_word = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 4))\n        self.w_transition = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 2))\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        return {\"w_context\": self.w_context.tolist(),\n                \"w_word\": self.w_word.tolist(),\n                \"w_transition\": self.w_transition.tolist()}\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> \"NonIsomorphicFragments\":\n        frag = cls(0)\n        frag.w_context = np.asarray(d[\"w_context\"], dtype=float)\n        frag.w_word = np.asarray(d[\"w_word\"], dtype=float)\n        frag.w_transition = np.asarray(d[\"w_transition\"], dtype=float)\n        return frag\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _unit(v: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n        n = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\n        return v / n if n > 1e-12 else np.zeros_like(v)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _hash_features(token: str, width: int) -> np.ndarray:\n        raw = token.lower().encode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\")\n        vals = np.zeros(width, dtype=float)\n        if not raw:\n            return vals\n        for i, byte in enumerate(raw):\n            vals[i % width] += ((byte % 31) - 15) / 15.0\n            vals[(i * 3 + 1) % width] += ((byte % 17) - 8) / 8.0\n        vals /= max(1, len(raw))\n        vals[0] += min(len(raw), 20) / 20.0\n        vals[1] += sum(chr(b).isalpha() for b in raw) / max(1, len(raw))\n        return np.tanh(vals)\n\n    def features(self, context, token, logp, rank):\n        recent = list(context[-4:])\n        ctx_vec = np.zeros(5, dtype=float)\n        if recent:\n            for i, word in enumerate(recent):\n                f = self._hash_features(word, 5)\n                ctx_vec += f * (0.65 ** (len(recent) - i - 1))\n            ctx_vec /= max(1, len(recent))\n        word_vec = self._hash_features(token, 5)\n        transition_vec = np.array([\n            np.tanh(logp),\n            1.0 / (1.0 + rank),\n            1.0 if token[:1].isupper() else 0.0,\n            1.0 if token in COT else 0.0,  # CoT words are visible to the fragments\n            min(len(token), 24) / 24.0,\n        ], dtype=float)\n        g1 = np.tanh(ctx_vec @ self.w_context)\n        g2 = np.tanh(word_vec @ self.w_word)\n        g3 = np.tanh(transition_vec @ self.w_transition)\n        return g1, g2, g3\n\n    def score(self, context, token, logp, rank, lam) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n        g1, g2, g3 = self.features(context, token, logp, rank)\n        summaries = np.array([np.linalg.norm(g1), np.linalg.norm(g2), np.linalg.norm(g3)])\n        mean = float(np.mean(summaries))\n        spread = float(np.std(summaries) / (mean + 1e-9))\n        consistency = float(np.clip(0.55 * spread + 0.45 * (1.0 - mean), 0.0, 1.0))\n\n        ref = self._unit(np.array([np.mean(g1), np.mean(g2), np.mean(g3), np.tanh(logp)]))\n        cand = self._unit(np.array([g1[0], g2[0], g3[0], np.tanh(logp + 0.1 * rank)]))\n        alignment = (float(np.dot(ref, cand)) + 1.0) / 2.0\n\n        fragment_score = 1.6 * alignment - 1.15 * consistency\n        total = (1.0 - lam) * (0.75 * logp + 0.25 * fragment_score) \\\n            + lam * (1.25 * logp + 0.85 * fragment_score)\n        return total, consistency\n\n\ndef adiabatic_lambda(step: int, total_steps: int) -> float:\n    u = min(1.0, max(0.0, step / max(1, total_steps - 1)))\n    return 3.0 * u * u - 2.0 * u * u * u\n\n\ndef softmax(values: Sequence[float], temperature: float = 1.0) -> np.ndarray:\n    temp = max(1e-6, float(temperature))\n    arr = np.asarray(values, dtype=float) / temp\n    arr -= np.max(arr)\n    exp = np.exp(np.clip(arr, -60, 60))\n    return exp / max(float(exp.sum()), 1e-12)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Checkpoints (v3: zip of state.json + dataset_ids.npy; v1/v2: gzip JSON)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef save_checkpoint(path: str, model: NGramModel, fragments: NonIsomorphicFragments,\n                    store: TokenStore, meta: dict) -> None:\n    state = {\n        \"format\": FORMAT,\n        \"cot\": current_cot_words(),\n        \"fragments\": fragments.to_dict(),\n        \"model\": model.to_dict(),\n        \"dataset_words\": store.words,\n        \"meta\": meta,\n    }\n    with zipfile.ZipFile(path, \"w\", zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED, compresslevel=6) as z:\n        with z.open(\"state.json\", \"w\", force_zip64=True) as raw:\n            wrapper = io.TextIOWrapper(raw, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n            json.dump(state, wrapper)\n            wrapper.flush()\n            wrapper.detach()\n        with z.open(\"dataset_ids.npy\", \"w\", force_zip64=True) as raw:\n            np.save(raw, store.ids().astype(np.int32), allow_pickle=False)\n\n\ndef load_checkpoint(path: str):\n    \"\"\"Load a checkpoint and install its CoT vocabulary globally.\n    Returns (model, fragments, TokenStore, meta).\"\"\"\n    with open(path, \"rb\") as fh:\n        magic = fh.read(2)\n    if magic == b\"PK\":\n        with zipfile.ZipFile(path) as z:\n            with z.open(\"state.json\") as raw:\n                state = json.load(io.TextIOWrapper(raw, encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n            ids = np.load(io.BytesIO(z.read(\"dataset_ids.npy\")), allow_pickle=False)\n        store = TokenStore(state.get(\"dataset_words\", []), ids)\n    else:  # legacy gzip JSON: dataset (if any) is a plain token list\n        with gzip.open(path, \"rt\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            state = json.load(fh)\n        store = TokenStore()\n        store.add(state.get(\"dataset\", []))\n    if state.get(\"format\") not in ACCEPTED_FORMATS:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{path}: unsupported checkpoint format {state.get('format')!r}\")\n    set_cot_tokens(state[\"cot\"])\n    model = NGramModel.from_dict(state[\"model\"])\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments.from_dict(state[\"fragments\"])\n    meta = state.get(\"meta\", {})\n    meta.setdefault(\"kernel\", \"weave\")  # v1 checkpoints were woven\n    return model, fragments, store, meta\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Cybernetic controller (sensor -> comparator -> actuator)\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nclass Controller:\n    def __init__(self, temperature: float, rep_limit: float = 0.5, logp_floor: float = -4.5):\n        self.temperature = temperature\n        self.rep_limit = rep_limit\n        self.logp_floor = logp_floor\n        self.k = 0\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def repetition(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> float:\n        words = strip_cot(tokens)\n        if len(words) < 2:\n            return 0.0\n        return 1.0 - len(set(words)) / len(words)\n\n    def update(self, chunk: Sequence[str], mean_logp: float) -> Tuple[str, float]:\n        \"\"\"Return (CoT token to emit, repetition measure).\"\"\"\n        rep = self.repetition(chunk)\n        if rep > self.rep_limit:\n            cot = COT_DIVERGE\n            self.temperature *= 1.15\n        elif mean_logp < self.logp_floor:\n            cot = COT_CONVERGE\n            self.temperature *= 0.9\n        else:\n            cot = COT_CYCLE[self.k % len(COT_CYCLE)]\n            self.k += 1\n        self.temperature = float(np.clip(self.temperature, 0.3, 1.6))\n        return cot, rep\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Candidate:\n    token: str\n    base_logp: float\n    score: float\n    consistency: float\n    probability: float = 0.0\n\n\ndef generate_chunk(model, fragments, context, n, step0, total, beam_size, tau, temperature, rng,\n                   stop_on_cot=False, bias=None, bias_strength=0.0):\n    \"\"\"Generate up to n tokens after `context`.\n\n    Returns (new_tokens, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted_cot). With stop_on_cot the\n    chunk ends the moment the MODEL emits a CoT token (weave kernel). With a\n    `bias` (scan kernel) each candidate's score gains bias_strength * bias[token],\n    where bias comes from the dataset scan.\n    \"\"\"\n    ctx = list(context)\n    new, logps, hit_eos, emitted = [], [], False, None\n    for i in range(n):\n        lam = adiabatic_lambda(step0 + i, total)\n        ranked = model.candidates(ctx, limit=max(40, beam_size * 8))\n        scored: List[Candidate] = []\n        for rank, (token, logp) in enumerate(ranked):\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, rank, lam)\n            if bias:\n                score += bias_strength * bias.get(token, 0.0)\n            if consistency <= tau:\n                scored.append(Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency))\n        if not scored:\n            token, logp = ranked[0]\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, 0, lam)\n            scored = [Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency)]\n\n        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c.score, reverse=True)\n        beam = scored[:max(1, beam_size)]\n        probs = softmax([c.score for c in beam], temperature)\n        chosen = beam[0] if temperature <= 0.01 else rng.choices(beam, weights=probs, k=1)[0]\n\n        if chosen.token == \"<eos>\":\n            hit_eos = True\n            break\n        if stop_on_cot and chosen.token in COT:\n            emitted = chosen.token\n            logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\n            break\n        new.append(chosen.token)\n        ctx.append(chosen.token)\n        logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\n    mean_logp = float(np.mean(logps)) if logps else 0.0\n    return new, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted\n\n\ndef cybernetic_run(model, fragments, scanner, prompt, cycles, chunk, chunks_per_cycle, window,\n                   beam_size, tau, temperature, seed, learn, trace):\n    \"\"\"Fixed-cycle loop. scanner=None -> weave kernel (CoT tokens live in the\n    context); scanner given -> scan kernel (CoT token is a probe, kept out of the\n    context, only steering the dataset scan for the next chunk).\"\"\"\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\n    scan = scanner is not None\n\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\"The\"]\n    full = [COT_START] + seed_tokens          # everything produced so far (markers incl.)\n    context = list(seed_tokens) if scan else list(full)\n    total = max(1, cycles * chunks_per_cycle * chunk)\n    step = 0\n    probe = COT_START                         # CoT token that steers the next scan\n\n    for c in range(cycles):\n        for k in range(chunks_per_cycle):\n            bias, hits = ({}, 0)\n            if scan:\n                bias, hits = scanner.bias(probe, context, rng)\n            new, mean_logp, hit_eos, _ = generate_chunk(\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, step, total,\n                beam_size, tau, controller.temperature, rng,\n                bias=bias, bias_strength=scanner.strength if scan else 0.0)\n            step += chunk\n            cot, rep = controller.update(new, mean_logp)\n\n            if trace:\n                extra = (f\" scan[{probe}:{cot_role(probe)} hits={hits} \"\n                         f\"ground={grounding(new, bias):.2f}]\") if scan else \"\"\n                print(f\"[cycle {c+1}/{cycles} chunk {k+1}] tokens={len(new)} \"\n                      f\"mean_logp={mean_logp:.2f} rep={rep:.2f} \"\n                      f\"-> {cot} (T={controller.temperature:.2f}){extra}\")\n\n            marker = [] if scan else [cot]\n            # Feedback learning: only from healthy output, to avoid reinforcing loops.\n            if learn and new and rep <= controller.rep_limit:\n                model.learn(tail_ctx(context, model.order - 1) + new + marker)\n\n            context += new + marker\n            full += new + [cot]\n            probe = cot\n            if hit_eos:\n                break\n\n        # Pipe output back to input.\n        tail = full[-window:]\n        context = strip_cot(tail) if scan else [COT_INTEGRATE] + tail\n        full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\n        probe = COT_INTEGRATE\n\n    return full\n\n\ndef stacked_run(model, fragments, scanner, prompt, target_depth, chunk, window, beam_size, tau,\n                temperature, seed, learn, max_retries, strict, min_grounding, trace):\n    \"\"\"\n    Keep generating until CoT tokens stack up in the correct order.\n\n    weave kernel: the model must itself emit the next expected CoT token\n    (COT_CYCLE order, repeating) after a chunk of real content.\n\n    scan kernel (inverted): the expected CoT word is used as a probe into the\n    dataset. A slot is accepted when the word is found there and the chunk is\n    grounded in the scanned passages (>= min_grounding). A word that never occurs\n    in the dataset cannot ground and is forced (flagged), or stops a --strict run.\n\n    Rejected chunks are regenerated (temperature creeps up per retry). Accepted\n    slots are pushed on a stack that only grows (monotonic) and are learned online.\n    After `max_retries` misses the slot is forced unless `strict`.\n    \"\"\"\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\n    scan = scanner is not None\n\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\"The\"]\n    full = [COT_START] + seed_tokens\n    context = list(seed_tokens) if scan else list(full)\n    stack: List[str] = []\n    forced = 0\n    attempts = 0\n    max_attempts = target_depth * (200 if strict else max_retries + 1)\n\n    while len(stack) < target_depth and attempts < max_attempts:\n        expected = COT_CYCLE[len(stack) % len(COT_CYCLE)]\n        cot_hits = scanner.hits(expected) if scan else 0\n        retries = 0\n        accepted, was_forced = False, False\n        while attempts < max_attempts:\n            temp = float(np.clip(controller.temperature * (1.0 + 0.1 * retries), 0.3, 1.8))\n            bias = {}\n            if scan:\n                bias, _ = scanner.bias(expected, context, rng)\n            new, mlp, eos, emitted = generate_chunk(\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, len(stack) * chunk,\n                target_depth * chunk, beam_size, tau, temp, rng,\n                stop_on_cot=not scan, bias=bias,\n                bias_strength=scanner.strength if scan else 0.0)\n            attempts += 1\n            if scan:\n                g = grounding(new, bias)\n                ok = len(new) > 0 and cot_hits > 0 and g >= min_grounding\n                detail = f\"scan hits={cot_hits} ground={g:.2f}\"\n            else:\n                ok = emitted == expected and len(new) > 0\n                detail = f\"got {emitted or 'none'}\"\n            msg = (f\"depth {len(stack)}/{target_depth} attempt {attempts} \"\n                   f\"expected {expected} {detail} \"\n                   f\"{'OK' if ok else 'retry'} (T={temp:.2f}, forced={forced})\")\n            if trace:\n                print(msg, file=sys.stderr)\n            else:\n                print(\"\\r\" + msg.ljust(78), end=\"\", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\n            if ok:\n                accepted = True\n                break\n            retries += 1\n            if scan and cot_hits == 0:\n                # Retrying can't make an absent word appear in the dataset.\n                if not strict:\n                    was_forced = True\n                break\n            if retries > max_retries and not strict:\n                was_forced = True\n                break\n        if not (accepted or was_forced):\n            break  # attempt cap hit, or strict and ungroundable\n\n        if was_forced:\n            forced += 1\n        stack.append(expected)\n        marker = [] if scan else [expected]\n        context += new + marker\n        full += new + [expected]\n        if new:\n            controller.update(new, mlp)\n        if accepted and learn:\n            model.learn(tail_ctx(context, model.order - 1 + len(new) + len(marker)))\n\n        # Pipe output back to input at the end of each full CoT cycle.\n        if len(stack) % PIPE_EVERY == 0:\n            context = strip_cot(full[-window:]) if scan else [COT_INTEGRATE] + full[-window:]\n            full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\n\n    if not trace:\n        print(file=sys.stderr)\n    monotonic = all(stack[i] == COT_CYCLE[i % len(COT_CYCLE)] for i in range(len(stack)))\n    stats = dict(depth=len(stack), target=target_depth, attempts=attempts,\n                 forced=forced, monotonic=monotonic)\n    return full, stats\n\n\ndef detokenize(tokens: Sequence[str], hide_cot: bool) -> str:\n    return \" \".join(strip_cot(tokens) if hide_cot else tokens)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Data sources: local files and streamed Hugging Face datasets\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef die(msg: str) -> None:\n    print(f\"error: {msg}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    sys.exit(2)\n\n\ndef log(msg: str) -> None:\n    print(msg, file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\n\n\ndef parse_size(s) -> int:\n    s = str(s).strip().lower()\n    for suf, mult in ((\"gb\", 10**9), (\"mb\", 10**6), (\"kb\", 10**3), (\"b\", 1)):\n        if s.endswith(suf):\n            return int(float(s[:-len(suf)]) * mult)\n    return int(float(s))\n\n\ndef read_corpus(path: str) -> str:\n    p = Path(path)\n    if not p.is_file():\n        die(f\"corpus file not found: {p}\")\n    try:\n        text = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8-sig\")\n    except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n        die(f\"could not decode {p} as UTF-8: {exc}\")\n    if not tokenize(text):\n        die(f\"{p} contains no tokens\")\n    return text\n\n\ndef iter_file_docs(paths: Sequence[str]) -> Iterator[str]:\n    for p in paths:\n        yield read_corpus(p)\n\n\n_TEXT_FIELDS = (\"text\", \"content\", \"sentence\", \"document\", \"article\", \"story\", \"body\")\n\n\ndef iter_hf_docs(args, stats: dict) -> Iterator[str]:\n    \"\"\"Stream a Hugging Face dataset, yielding text until the byte budget is hit.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        from datasets import load_dataset\n    except ImportError:\n        die(\"--hf-dataset needs the `datasets` package: pip install datasets\")\n    kwargs = {\"split\": args.hf_split, \"streaming\": True}\n    if args.hf_data_files:\n        files = args.hf_data_files.split(\",\")\n        kwargs[\"data_files\"] = files if len(files) > 1 else files[0]\n    log(f\"streaming {args.hf_dataset}\"\n        + (f\"/{args.hf_config}\" if args.hf_config else \"\")\n        + f\" [{args.hf_split}], budget {args.hf_max_bytes}\")\n    ds = load_dataset(args.hf_dataset, args.hf_config, **kwargs)\n    budget = parse_size(args.hf_max_bytes)\n    field = args.hf_field\n    for row in ds:\n        if field is None:\n            field = next((k for k in _TEXT_FIELDS if isinstance(row.get(k), str)), None) \\\n                or next((k for k, v in row.items() if isinstance(v, str)), None)\n            if field is None:\n                die(f\"no text column found in {list(row)}; pass --hf-field\")\n            log(f\"using text field {field!r}\")\n        text = row.get(field)\n        if isinstance(text, list):\n            text = \"\\n\".join(str(t) for t in text)\n        if not isinstance(text, str) or not text.strip():\n            continue\n        n = len(text.encode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\"))\n        if budget and stats[\"bytes\"] + n > budget:\n            break\n        stats[\"bytes\"] += n\n        yield text\n\n\ndef make_docs(args, stats: dict) -> Tuple[Iterator[str], List[str]]:\n    sources, parts = [], []\n    files = list(getattr(args, \"corpus\", None) or [])\n    for f in files:\n        if not Path(f).is_file():\n            die(f\"corpus file not found: {f}\")\n    if files:\n        parts.append(iter_file_docs(files))\n        sources += [Path(f).name for f in files]\n    if args.hf_dataset:\n        parts.append(iter_hf_docs(args, stats))\n        sources.append(\"hf:\" + args.hf_dataset + (f\"/{args.hf_config}\" if args.hf_config else \"\"))\n    return itertools.chain.from_iterable(parts), sources\n\n\ndef peek_docs(docs: Iterator[str], nbytes: int) -> Tuple[List[str], Iterator[str]]:\n    head, size = [], 0\n    for d in docs:\n        head.append(d)\n        size += len(d)\n        if size >= nbytes:\n            break\n    return head, docs\n\n\ndef ingest(model: NGramModel, store: TokenStore, docs: Iterable[str], weave: bool,\n           max_entries: int, stats: dict, log_every: int = 1_000_000) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Train on a document stream one document at a time (flat memory), keep the\n    token stream for the scanner, and keep the n-gram tables under budget.\"\"\"\n    t0 = time.time()\n    ntok = 0\n    next_log = log_every\n    for text in docs:\n        toks = tokenize(text)\n        if not toks:\n            continue\n        model.train(text, cot=weave)\n        store.add(toks)\n        ntok += len(toks)\n        if ntok >= next_log:\n            next_log += log_every\n            model.enforce_budget(max_entries, log)\n            rate = ntok / max(1e-9, time.time() - t0)\n            mb = f\"  {stats['bytes'] / 1e6:.0f}MB\" if stats.get(\"bytes\") else \"\"\n            log(f\"  {ntok / 1e6:.1f}M tokens{mb}  entries {model.n_entries():,}  \"\n                f\"{rate / 1e3:.0f}k tok/s\")\n    model.enforce_budget(max_entries, log)\n    return ntok\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# CLI\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndef add_vocab_args(p: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:\n    p.add_argument(\"--cot-vocab\", help=\"Custom CoT vocabulary file (one word per line, used in order).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--cot-sort\", choices=[\"none\", \"alpha\", \"alpha-desc\", \"length\"], default=\"none\",\n                   help=\"Sort the custom list before use (default: keep file order).\")\n\n\ndef add_source_args(p: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:\n    p.add_argument(\"--hf-dataset\", help=\"Hugging Face dataset to stream (e.g. Salesforce/wikitext).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--hf-config\", help=\"Dataset config name (e.g. wikitext-103-raw-v1).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--hf-split\", default=\"train\", help=\"Split to stream (default: train).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--hf-field\", help=\"Text column (auto-detected if omitted).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--hf-data-files\", help=\"Comma-separated data files (for 'json'/'text'/'csv' loaders).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--hf-max-bytes\", default=\"200MB\", help=\"Stop after this much text (default 200MB).\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--max-entries\", type=int, default=5_000_000,\n                   help=\"Prune rare n-grams when stored (context,target) pairs exceed this (0 = never).\")\n\n\ndef report_coverage(store: TokenStore) -> None:\n    if not len(store):\n        return\n    found, missing = DatasetScanner(store).coverage(current_cot_words())\n    log(f\"scan coverage: {found}/{COT_COUNT} CoT words occur in the dataset\"\n        + (f\" (absent: {', '.join(missing[:10])}{' ...' if len(missing) > 10 else ''})\"\n           if missing else \"\"))\n\n\ndef cmd_build(args) -> None:\n    stats = {\"bytes\": 0}\n    docs, sources = make_docs(args, stats)\n    if not sources:\n        die(\"give at least one corpus file or --hf-dataset\")\n    head, rest = peek_docs(docs, VOCAB_PEEK_BYTES)\n    if not head:\n        die(\"the data source produced no text\")\n    if args.cot_vocab:\n        words = load_cot_vocab(args.cot_vocab, args.cot_sort)\n    else:\n        words = select_cot_tokens(\"\\n\".join(head), args.seed)\n    set_cot_tokens(words)\n    log(\"CoT vocab: \" + \" \".join(current_cot_words()))\n\n    weave = args.kernel == \"weave\" and not args.no_cot_weave\n    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\n    store = TokenStore()\n    ntok = ingest(model, store, itertools.chain(head, rest), weave, args.max_entries, stats)\n    if args.kernel == \"scan\":\n        report_coverage(store)\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(args.seed)\n    meta = {\"seed\": args.seed, \"kernel\": args.kernel, \"extensions\": 0, \"sources\": sources}\n    log(f\"saving {args.output} ...\")\n    save_checkpoint(args.output, model, fragments, store, meta)\n    log(f\"built {args.output} [{args.kernel} kernel]: {len(model.vocab):,} types, \"\n        f\"{ntok:,} tokens read, {model.n_entries():,} n-gram entries, dataset {len(store):,} tokens\")\n\n\ndef cmd_extend(args) -> None:\n    try:\n        model, fragments, store, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\n    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n        die(str(exc))\n    kernel = meta[\"kernel\"]\n    old_words = current_cot_words()\n\n    if args.alpha is not None:\n        model.alpha = max(1e-9, args.alpha)\n\n    if args.cot_vocab:\n        new_words = load_cot_vocab(args.cot_vocab, args.cot_sort)\n        if kernel == \"weave\":\n            mapping = {o: n for o, n in zip(old_words, new_words) if o != n}\n            if mapping:\n                clash = [n for n in mapping.values() if n in model.vocab and n not in mapping]\n                if clash:\n                    log(\"warning: new CoT words already occur as ordinary words in the weights \"\n                        f\"and will merge with them: {', '.join(sorted(clash)[:8])}\"\n                        + (\" ...\" if len(clash) > 8 else \"\"))\n                model.remap_tokens(mapping)\n                log(f\"remapped {len(mapping)} CoT tokens onto the new vocabulary\")\n        else:\n            log(\"scan kernel: CoT vocabulary swapped, no weights to remap\")\n        set_cot_tokens(new_words)\n    log(\"CoT vocab: \" + \" \".join(current_cot_words()))\n\n    if args.decay != 1.0:\n        model.scale(args.decay)\n        log(f\"decayed existing weights by {args.decay} (dataset is not decayed)\")\n\n    stats = {\"bytes\": 0}\n    docs, sources = make_docs(args, stats)\n    weave = kernel == \"weave\" and not args.no_cot_weave\n    ntok = ingest(model, store, docs, weave, args.max_entries, stats) if sources else 0\n    meta.setdefault(\"sources\", []).extend(sources)\n    meta[\"extensions\"] = meta.get(\"extensions\", 0) + 1\n\n    if kernel == \"scan\":\n        report_coverage(store)\n    log(f\"saving {args.output} ...\")\n    save_checkpoint(args.output, model, fragments, store, meta)\n    log(f\"extended -> {args.output} [{kernel} kernel]: {len(model.vocab):,} types, \"\n        f\"+{ntok:,} tokens, {model.n_entries():,} n-gram entries, dataset {len(store):,} tokens\")\n\n\ndef cmd_info(args) -> None:\n    try:\n        model, fragments, store, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\n    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n        die(str(exc))\n    print(f\"format       {FORMAT}   kernel {meta['kernel']}\")\n    print(f\"order        {model.order}   alpha {model.alpha}\")\n    print(f\"vocab types  {len(model.vocab):,}   tokens {model.total_tokens:,.0f}\")\n    print(f\"dataset      {len(store):,} tokens, {len(store.words):,} distinct words\")\n    print(\"contexts     \" + \", \".join(f\"n={i}: {len(lv):,}\" for i, lv in enumerate(model.counts))\n          + f\"   entries {model.n_entries():,}\")\n    print(f\"extensions   {meta.get('extensions', 0)}   sources {', '.join(meta.get('sources', []))}\")\n    print(\"cycle        \" + \" \".join(str(t) for t in COT_CYCLE))\n    print(f\"diverge={COT_DIVERGE} converge={COT_CONVERGE} \"\n          f\"integrate={COT_INTEGRATE} start={COT_START}\")\n    if len(store):\n        found, missing = DatasetScanner(store).coverage(current_cot_words())\n        print(f\"coverage     {found}/{COT_COUNT} CoT words occur in the dataset\"\n              + (f\"; absent: {', '.join(missing)}\" if missing else \"\"))\n\n\ndef cmd_generate(args) -> None:\n    try:\n        model, fragments, store, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\n    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n        die(str(exc))\n    kernel = args.kernel or meta[\"kernel\"]\n    scanner = None\n    if kernel == \"scan\":\n        if not len(store):\n            die(\"scan kernel needs the dataset stored in the checkpoint \"\n                \"(this one has none; rebuild it or use --kernel weave)\")\n        scanner = DatasetScanner(store, strength=args.scan_strength, limit=args.scan_limit,\n                                 span=args.scan_span, mix=args.scan_mix)\n        report_coverage(store)\n    log(f\"kernel: {kernel}\")\n    log(\"CoT vocab: \" + \" \".join(current_cot_words()))\n\n    first = True\n    while True:\n        try:\n            prompt = args.prompt if (args.prompt and first) else input(\"USER: \")\n        except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):\n            print()\n            break\n        first = False\n\n        tau = float(np.clip(args.tau, 0.0, 1.0))\n        temp = max(0.0, args.temperature)\n        if args.stack_target > 0:\n            full, stats = stacked_run(\n                model, fragments, scanner, prompt, target_depth=args.stack_target,\n                chunk=args.chunk, window=args.window, beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau,\n                temperature=temp, seed=args.seed, learn=not args.no_learn,\n                max_retries=args.max_retries, strict=args.strict,\n                min_grounding=args.min_grounding, trace=args.trace)\n            print(f\"\\n[stack] depth {stats['depth']}/{stats['target']}  attempts {stats['attempts']}  \"\n                  f\"forced {stats['forced']}  monotonic order verified: {stats['monotonic']}\")\n        else:\n            full = cybernetic_run(\n                model, fragments, scanner, prompt, cycles=args.cycles, chunk=args.chunk,\n                chunks_per_cycle=args.chunks_per_cycle, window=args.window,\n                beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp, seed=args.seed,\n                learn=not args.no_learn, trace=args.trace)\n\n        text = detokenize(full, hide_cot=not args.show_cot)\n        print(\"\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\")\n        print(text)\n        print()\n        if args.save:\n            with open(args.save, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n                fh.write(text + \"\\n\\n\")\n\n    if args.save_model:\n        meta[\"extensions\"] = meta.get(\"extensions\", 0) + 1\n        save_checkpoint(args.save_model, model, fragments, store, meta)\n        log(f\"saved weights -> {args.save_model}\")\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"CoT weight extender (scan kernel, HF streaming) for the cybernetic n-gram generator.\")\n    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest=\"cmd\", required=True)\n\n    b = sub.add_parser(\"build\", help=\"Train a new checkpoint from files and/or a Hugging Face dataset.\")\n    b.add_argument(\"corpus\", nargs=\"*\", help=\"UTF-8 text corpus file(s) (optional if --hf-dataset is given).\")\n    b.add_argument(\"-o\", \"--output\", required=True, help=\"Checkpoint to write (.cotw).\")\n    b.add_argument(\"--order\", type=int, default=3)\n    b.add_argument(\"--alpha\", type=float, default=0.25)\n    b.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=7)\n    b.add_argument(\"--kernel\", choices=[\"scan\", \"weave\"], default=\"scan\",\n                   help=\"scan: CoT token probes the dataset (default). weave: CoT tokens woven into the weights.\")\n    b.add_argument(\"--no-cot-weave\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"(weave kernel) do not weave CoT tokens in.\")\n    add_vocab_args(b)\n    add_source_args(b)\n    b.set_defaults(func=cmd_build)\n\n    e = sub.add_parser(\"extend\", help=\"Extend an existing checkpoint.\")\n    e.add_argument(\"model\", help=\"Checkpoint to extend.\")\n    e.add_argument(\"corpus\", nargs=\"*\", help=\"Additional corpus file(s) (optional).\")\n    e.add_argument(\"-o\", \"--output\", required=True, help=\"Checkpoint to write.\")\n    e.add_argument(\"--decay\", type=float, default=1.0,\n                   help=\"Scale existing weights by this factor before adding new data (e.g. 0.9).\")\n    e.add_argument(\"--alpha\", type=float, default=None, help=\"Override smoothing alpha.\")\n    e.add_argument(\"--no-cot-weave\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"(weave kernel) do not weave CoT tokens into new data.\")\n    add_vocab_args(e)\n    add_source_args(e)\n    e.set_defaults(func=cmd_extend)\n\n    i = sub.add_parser(\"info\", help=\"Show checkpoint statistics.\")\n    i.add_argument(\"model\")\n    i.set_defaults(func=cmd_info)\n\n    g = sub.add_parser(\"generate\", help=\"Run the cybernetic loop from a checkpoint.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"model\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--kernel\", choices=[\"scan\", \"weave\"], default=None,\n                   help=\"Override the checkpoint's kernel.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--prompt\", help=\"Initial prompt. If omitted you are asked each round.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--cycles\", type=int, default=4, help=\"Output->input feedback cycles per prompt.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--chunk\", type=int, default=20, help=\"Tokens per chunk between CoT tokens.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--chunks-per-cycle\", type=int, default=3)\n    g.add_argument(\"--window\", type=int, default=40, help=\"Tokens of output piped back as the next prompt.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--beam\", type=int, default=8)\n    g.add_argument(\"--tau\", type=float, default=0.65)\n    g.add_argument(\"--temperature\", type=float, default=0.85)\n    g.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=7)\n    g.add_argument(\"--stack-target\", type=int, default=25,\n                   help=\"Keep going until this many CoT tokens have stacked in order (0 = fixed-cycle mode).\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--max-retries\", type=int, default=25, help=\"Rejected chunks allowed per stack slot before forcing.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--strict\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Never force a token; retry until the attempt cap.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--scan-strength\", type=float, default=1.5, help=\"Weight of the dataset-scan bias on scores.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--scan-limit\", type=int, default=24, help=\"Max passages sampled per probe word.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--scan-span\", type=int, default=12, help=\"Tokens read after each occurrence.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--scan-mix\", type=float, default=0.5,\n                   help=\"Weight of the last context word as a second probe (0 = CoT token only).\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--min-grounding\", type=float, default=0.15,\n                   help=\"Stack mode (scan): min fraction of chunk tokens found in the scanned passages.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--no-learn\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Disable online learning from own output.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--show-cot\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Show CoT tokens in printed text (hidden by default).\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--trace\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Print controller diagnostics.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--save\", help=\"Append output to this text file.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--save-model\", help=\"Write the weights (incl. online learning) to this checkpoint at exit.\")\n    g.set_defaults(func=cmd_generate)\n\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n    args.func(args)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\nPYEOF\npip install datasets --break-system-packages -q 2>&1 | tail -2; python3 -c \"import datasets; print('datasets', datasets.__version__)\"", "description": "Write HF-streaming version and install datasets library for local testing"}, "message": "Write HF-streaming version and install datasets library for local testing", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cat > /mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py <<'PYEOF'\\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nCoT weight extender  (scan kernel, Hugging Face streaming)\\n==========================================================\\n\\nThe cybernetic n-gram generator as a persistent, extendable model, with the CoT\\nkernel INVERTED and able to train from a streamed Hugging Face dataset.\\n\\n  weave kernel (old)   dataset -> CoT.  CoT words are woven into the training\\n                       stream and the model has to emit them itself.\\n  scan kernel (new)    CoT -> dataset.  A CoT token is a PROBE: the loop finds the\\n                       word in the dataset, collects the passages that follow each\\n                       occurrence, and turns them into a bias over the next chunk.\\n                       CoT tokens never enter the weights or the n-gram context.\\n\\nScan profile per CoT role:\\n  cycle token   standard scan\\n  diverge       more passages, longer span, slower decay   (wider read, T up)\\n  converge      fewer passages, shorter span, faster decay (tighter read, T down)\\n  integrate     standard passages, longer span             (re-read after pipe-back)\\n\\nCommands\\n  build     Train a new checkpoint from local corpora and/or a Hugging Face dataset.\\n  extend    Grow a checkpoint: more data, optional decay, optional new CoT vocab.\\n  generate  Run the cybernetic loop from a checkpoint (optionally save weights).\\n  info      Print checkpoint statistics and CoT-vocab coverage of the dataset.\\n\\nHugging Face datasets (needs `pip install datasets`)\\n  --hf-dataset NAME     e.g. Salesforce/wikitext   (or \\\"json\\\"/\\\"text\\\" + --hf-data-files)\\n  --hf-config CONFIG    e.g. wikitext-103-raw-v1\\n  --hf-split SPLIT      default: train\\n  --hf-field FIELD      text column (auto-detected if omitted)\\n  --hf-max-bytes SIZE   stop after this much text, default 200MB (e.g. 50MB, 1GB)\\n  The dataset is STREAMED and cut off at the byte budget, so the full download is\\n  never required. Documents are trained one by one, so memory stays flat.\\n\\nScale handling (built for hundreds of MB of text)\\n  * The dataset is stored as an int32 token-id array + word table, not a Python list.\\n  * The scan index is a sorted-position (CSR) numpy index, built on first use.\\n  * n-gram memory is bounded by --max-entries: when the context tables grow past it,\\n    low-count n-grams (count < 2, then < 3, ...) are pruned. This is lossy for rare\\n    n-grams; 0 disables pruning.\\n  * Checkpoints are zip files (JSON model state + a .npy of dataset ids). Old gzip\\n    JSON checkpoints (v1/v2) still load.\\n\\nCustom CoT vocabulary (--cot-vocab FILE): one word per line ('#' comments ignored),\\nused in order or sorted with --cot-sort:\\n      entries  1..25   the stack cycle, in required order\\n      entry    26      diverge\\n      entry    27      converge\\n      entry    28      integrate\\n      entry    29      start\\nWith the scan kernel the words should occur in the dataset (coverage is reported).\\nWithout --cot-vocab the words are the most frequent 4+ letter words of the first\\n~2MB of data, shuffled.\\n\\nExamples:\\n  python cot_weight_extender.py build -o wiki.cotw --hf-dataset Salesforce/wikitext \\\\\\\\\\n      --hf-config wikitext-103-raw-v1 --hf-max-bytes 200MB --cot-vocab cot.txt\\n  python cot_weight_extender.py extend wiki.cotw more.txt -o wiki2.cotw --decay 0.9\\n  python cot_weight_extender.py generate wiki.cotw --prompt \\\"The machine\\\" --trace\\n  python cot_weight_extender.py info wiki.cotw\\n\\nDependencies: NumPy (+ `datasets` only for --hf-dataset)\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport argparse\\nimport gzip\\nimport io\\nimport itertools\\nimport json\\nimport math\\nimport random\\nimport sys\\nimport time\\nimport zipfile\\nfrom array import array\\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import Dict, Iterable, Iterator, List, Sequence, Tuple\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nFORMAT = \\\"cot-weights-v3\\\"\\nACCEPTED_FORMATS = (\\\"cot-weights-v1\\\", \\\"cot-weights-v2\\\", FORMAT)\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# CoT tokens\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass CotToken(str):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"A CoT marker inserted by the loop. It is a str, but isinstance() tells it\\n    apart from the same word appearing as ordinary text, so hiding markers never\\n    deletes real words from the output.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\n# Fallback names, used only if the vocabulary source has too few distinct words.\\nDEFAULT_COT = [\\n    \\\"simulate\\\", \\\"recall\\\", \\\"correct\\\", \\\"imagine\\\", \\\"decide\\\",\\n    \\\"observe\\\", \\\"verify\\\", \\\"associate\\\", \\\"plan\\\", \\\"anticipate\\\",\\n    \\\"reflect\\\", \\\"abstract\\\", \\\"act\\\", \\\"question\\\", \\\"compare\\\",\\n    \\\"adapt\\\", \\\"predict\\\", \\\"summarize\\\", \\\"monitor\\\", \\\"infer\\\",\\n    \\\"consolidate\\\", \\\"attend\\\", \\\"evaluate\\\", \\\"prioritize\\\", \\\"hypothesize\\\",\\n    \\\"diverge\\\", \\\"converge\\\", \\\"integrate\\\", \\\"synthesize\\\",\\n]\\nCOT_COUNT = 29  # 25 cycle tokens + diverge + converge + integrate + start\\nPIPE_EVERY = 4  # pipe output back to input after this many stacked tokens\\nSENTENCE_END = (\\\".\\\", \\\"!\\\", \\\"?\\\")\\nVOCAB_PEEK_BYTES = 2_000_000  # data sampled to pick CoT words when none are given\\n\\nCOT_CYCLE: List[str] = []\\nCOT_DIVERGE = COT_CONVERGE = COT_INTEGRATE = COT_START = CotToken(\\\"\\\")\\nCOT: set = set()\\n\\n_STOP = {\\n    \\\"that\\\", \\\"with\\\", \\\"have\\\", \\\"from\\\", \\\"this\\\", \\\"they\\\", \\\"were\\\", \\\"been\\\", \\\"will\\\", \\\"would\\\", \\\"there\\\",\\n    \\\"their\\\", \\\"what\\\", \\\"when\\\", \\\"which\\\", \\\"your\\\", \\\"them\\\", \\\"then\\\", \\\"than\\\", \\\"into\\\", \\\"only\\\", \\\"also\\\",\\n    \\\"some\\\", \\\"such\\\", \\\"more\\\", \\\"most\\\", \\\"other\\\", \\\"about\\\", \\\"could\\\", \\\"should\\\", \\\"these\\\", \\\"those\\\",\\n}\\n\\n\\ndef set_cot_tokens(words: Sequence[str]) -> None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Install the CoT vocabulary: 25 cycle tokens, then diverge, converge,\\n    integrate, start.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    global COT_CYCLE, COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START, COT\\n    toks = [CotToken(w) for w in words]\\n    COT_CYCLE = toks[:25]\\n    COT_DIVERGE, COT_CONVERGE, COT_INTEGRATE, COT_START = toks[25:29]\\n    COT = {str(t) for t in toks}\\n\\n\\ndef current_cot_words() -> List[str]:\\n    return [str(t) for t in COT_CYCLE] + [str(COT_DIVERGE), str(COT_CONVERGE),\\n                                          str(COT_INTEGRATE), str(COT_START)]\\n\\n\\ndef _top_up(words: List[str], count: int) -> List[str]:\\n    seen = {w.lower() for w in words}\\n    for d in DEFAULT_COT:\\n        if len(words) >= count:\\n            break\\n        if d.lower() not in seen:\\n            seen.add(d.lower())\\n            words.append(d)\\n    return words\\n\\n\\ndef select_cot_tokens(text: str, seed: int, count: int = COT_COUNT) -> List[str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pick CoT tokens from the data: the most frequent alphabetic words of 4+\\n    letters (skipping common function words), shuffled so the required order is\\n    non-monotonic. Used when no --cot-vocab is given.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    counts = Counter(tokenize(text))\\n    pool = [(w, c) for w, c in counts.items()\\n            if w.isalpha() and len(w) >= 4 and w.lower() not in _STOP]\\n    pool.sort(key=lambda wc: (-wc[1], wc[0]))\\n    words, seen = [], set()\\n    for w, _ in pool:\\n        if w.lower() not in seen:\\n            seen.add(w.lower())\\n            words.append(w)\\n        if len(words) >= count:\\n            break\\n    random.Random(seed).shuffle(words)\\n    return _top_up(words, count)\\n\\n\\ndef load_cot_vocab(path: str, sort: str = \\\"none\\\", count: int = COT_COUNT) -> List[str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Load a custom CoT vocabulary from a text file (one word per line).\\n\\n    sort: 'none' keeps file order (use when the list is already sorted the way you\\n    want the stack to run), 'alpha' / 'alpha-desc' sort case-insensitively,\\n    'length' sorts short to long. Sorting happens BEFORE truncating to `count`.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    words, seen = [], set()\\n    for lineno, line in enumerate(Path(path).read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8-sig\\\").splitlines(), 1):\\n        w = line.split(\\\"#\\\", 1)[0].strip()\\n        if not w:\\n            continue\\n        if len(w.split()) != 1:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"{path}:{lineno}: CoT words must be a single token, got {w!r}\\\")\\n        if w.lower() in seen:\\n            print(f\\\"warning: duplicate CoT word {w!r} at line {lineno} ignored\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n            continue\\n        seen.add(w.lower())\\n        words.append(w)\\n    if sort == \\\"alpha\\\":\\n        words.sort(key=str.lower)\\n    elif sort == \\\"alpha-desc\\\":\\n        words.sort(key=str.lower, reverse=True)\\n    elif sort == \\\"length\\\":\\n        words.sort(key=lambda w: (len(w), w.lower()))\\n    if len(words) > count:\\n        print(f\\\"note: {len(words)} CoT words given, using the first {count}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        words = words[:count]\\n    elif len(words) < count:\\n        print(f\\\"note: only {len(words)} CoT words given, filling to {count} from fallback names\\\",\\n              file=sys.stderr)\\n        words = _top_up(words, count)\\n    return words\\n\\n\\nset_cot_tokens(DEFAULT_COT)\\n\\n\\ndef tokenize(text: str) -> List[str]:\\n    return text.split()\\n\\n\\ndef strip_cot(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> List[str]:\\n    return [t for t in tokens if not isinstance(t, CotToken)]\\n\\n\\ndef tail_ctx(tokens: Sequence[str], k: int) -> List[str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Last k tokens (empty for k <= 0; avoids the tokens[-0:] whole-list trap).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return list(tokens[len(tokens) - k:]) if k > 0 else []\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Compact dataset store + scanner (CoT token -> dataset passages -> bias)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef norm_word(w: str) -> str:\\n    return str(w).strip(\\\".,;:!?\\\\\\\"'()[]{}\\\").lower()\\n\\n\\nclass TokenStore:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The dataset as a word table plus an int32 id per token (4 bytes/token).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, words: Sequence[str] = (), ids=None):\\n        assert array(\\\"i\\\").itemsize == 4\\n        self.words: List[str] = list(words)\\n        self.word_id: Dict[str, int] = {w: i for i, w in enumerate(self.words)}\\n        self._base = np.asarray(ids, dtype=np.intc) if ids is not None else np.zeros(0, dtype=np.intc)\\n        self._buf = array(\\\"i\\\")\\n        self.version = 0\\n\\n    def add(self, tokens: Iterable[str]) -> None:\\n        wid, words, buf = self.word_id, self.words, self._buf\\n        for t in tokens:\\n            i = wid.get(t)\\n            if i is None:\\n                i = len(words)\\n                wid[t] = i\\n                words.append(t)\\n            buf.append(i)\\n        self.version += 1\\n\\n    def ids(self) -> np.ndarray:\\n        if self._buf:\\n            add = np.frombuffer(self._buf, dtype=np.intc).copy()\\n            self._base = np.concatenate([self._base, add]) if self._base.size else add\\n            self._buf = array(\\\"i\\\")\\n        return self._base\\n\\n    def __len__(self) -> int:\\n        return int(self._base.size) + len(self._buf)\\n\\n\\n# role -> (passage multiplier, span multiplier, per-step decay)\\nSCAN_PROFILES = {\\n    \\\"cycle\\\": (1.0, 1.0, 0.85),\\n    \\\"diverge\\\": (2.0, 2.0, 0.92),\\n    \\\"converge\\\": (0.5, 0.5, 0.75),\\n    \\\"integrate\\\": (1.0, 1.5, 0.88),\\n    \\\"start\\\": (1.0, 1.0, 0.85),\\n}\\n\\n\\ndef cot_role(tok: str) -> str:\\n    s = str(tok)\\n    if s == str(COT_DIVERGE):\\n        return \\\"diverge\\\"\\n    if s == str(COT_CONVERGE):\\n        return \\\"converge\\\"\\n    if s == str(COT_INTEGRATE):\\n        return \\\"integrate\\\"\\n    if s == str(COT_START):\\n        return \\\"start\\\"\\n    return \\\"cycle\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass DatasetScanner:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Inverted index over the dataset (word -> sorted token positions, CSR layout).\\n    A CoT token is a key: occurrences of its word are located, the `span` tokens that\\n    follow are collected with geometric decay, and the result is a bias in [0, 1].\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, store: TokenStore, strength: float = 1.5, limit: int = 24,\\n                 span: int = 12, mix: float = 0.5):\\n        self.store = store\\n        self.strength = strength\\n        self.limit = max(1, int(limit))\\n        self.span = max(2, int(span))\\n        self.mix = max(0.0, float(mix))\\n        self._ver = -1\\n\\n    def _build(self) -> None:\\n        ids = self.store.ids()\\n        words = self.store.words\\n        group_of: Dict[str, int] = {}\\n        group = np.empty(len(words), dtype=np.int32)\\n        for i, w in enumerate(words):\\n            group[i] = group_of.setdefault(norm_word(w), len(group_of))\\n        gids = group[ids] if ids.size else ids.astype(np.int32)\\n        self._order = np.argsort(gids, kind=\\\"stable\\\").astype(np.int32)\\n        counts = np.bincount(gids, minlength=len(group_of)) if ids.size else np.zeros(len(group_of), int)\\n        self._starts = np.zeros(len(group_of) + 1, dtype=np.int64)\\n        np.cumsum(counts, out=self._starts[1:])\\n        self._group_of = group_of\\n        self._ids = ids\\n        self._ver = self.store.version\\n\\n    def _ready(self) -> None:\\n        if self._ver != self.store.version:\\n            self._build()\\n\\n    def positions(self, word: str) -> np.ndarray:\\n        self._ready()\\n        g = self._group_of.get(norm_word(word))\\n        if g is None:\\n            return self._order[:0]\\n        return self._order[self._starts[g]:self._starts[g + 1]]\\n\\n    def hits(self, word: str) -> int:\\n        return int(len(self.positions(word)))\\n\\n    def coverage(self, words: Sequence[str]) -> Tuple[int, List[str]]:\\n        missing = [w for w in words if self.hits(w) == 0]\\n        return len(words) - len(missing), missing\\n\\n    def bias(self, cot: str, context: Sequence[str], rng: random.Random) -> Tuple[Dict[str, float], int]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Scan with `cot` as probe (plus, at weight `mix`, the last context word).\\n        Returns (normalised bias over tokens, number of dataset hits for `cot`).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self._ready()\\n        limit_mult, span_mult, decay = SCAN_PROFILES[cot_role(cot)]\\n        limit = max(1, int(round(self.limit * limit_mult)))\\n        span = max(2, int(round(self.span * span_mult)))\\n        probes = [(str(cot), 1.0)]\\n        if context and self.mix > 0:\\n            probes.append((str(context[-1]), self.mix))\\n        ids, n = self._ids, len(self._ids)\\n        weights: Dict[int, float] = defaultdict(float)\\n        cot_hits = 0\\n        for pi, (word, w) in enumerate(probes):\\n            pos = self.positions(word)\\n            if pi == 0:\\n                cot_hits = int(len(pos))\\n            if len(pos) == 0:\\n                continue\\n            if len(pos) > limit:\\n                pos = pos[rng.sample(range(len(pos)), limit)]\\n            pos = pos.astype(np.int64)\\n            share = w / len(pos)\\n            for off in range(1, span + 1):\\n                j = pos + off\\n                j = j[j < n]\\n                if j.size == 0:\\n                    break\\n                wt = share * (decay ** (off - 1))\\n                for t in ids[j].tolist():\\n                    weights[t] += wt\\n        if not weights:\\n            return {}, cot_hits\\n        top = max(weights.values())\\n        words = self.store.words\\n        return {words[i]: v / top for i, v in weights.items()}, cot_hits\\n\\n\\ndef grounding(new: Sequence[str], bias) -> float:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Fraction of generated tokens that occur in the scanned passages.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not new or not bias:\\n        return 0.0\\n    return sum(1 for t in new if t in bias) / len(new)\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# N-gram model (serialisation, decay, pruning, remapping)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass NGramModel:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Smoothed n-gram model with backoff, trainable offline and online.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, order: int = 3, alpha: float = 0.25):\\n        self.order = max(1, int(order))\\n        self.alpha = max(1e-9, float(alpha))\\n        self.counts = [defaultdict(Counter) for _ in range(self.order)]\\n        self.vocab = Counter()\\n        self.total_tokens = 0\\n\\n    def _update(self, tokens: Sequence[str], start: int) -> None:\\n        for i in range(start, len(tokens)):\\n            target = tokens[i]\\n            self.vocab[target] += 1\\n            self.total_tokens += 1\\n            for ctx_len in range(self.order):\\n                if ctx_len > i:\\n                    break\\n                context = tuple(tokens[i - ctx_len:i]) if ctx_len else ()\\n                self.counts[ctx_len][context][target] += 1\\n\\n    def train(self, text: str, cot: bool = True) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"cot=True weaves CoT tokens in after each sentence (weave kernel).\\n        The scan kernel trains with cot=False: the weights never see CoT tokens.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        raw = tokenize(text)\\n        if cot:\\n            woven, k = [], 0\\n            for tok in raw:\\n                woven.append(tok)\\n                if tok.endswith(SENTENCE_END):\\n                    woven.append(COT_CYCLE[k % len(COT_CYCLE)])\\n                    k += 1\\n            raw = woven\\n        tokens = [\\\"<bos>\\\"] * (self.order - 1) + raw + [\\\"<eos>\\\"]\\n        self._update(tokens, self.order - 1)\\n\\n    def learn(self, tokens: Sequence[str]) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Online update from the model's own output (feedback learning).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self._update(list(tokens), 1)\\n\\n    # ---- size control ----------------------------------------------------\\n    def n_entries(self) -> int:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"(context, target) pairs stored above unigram level - the memory driver.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        return sum(len(c) for lv in self.counts[1:] for c in lv.values())\\n\\n    def _prune_levels(self) -> range:\\n        return range(2 if self.order > 2 else 1, self.order)\\n\\n    def prune(self, min_count: float) -> int:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Drop (context, target) pairs with count < min_count from the high-order\\n        tables. Lossy for rare n-grams; the unigram table and (for order > 2) the\\n        bigram table are kept whole so backoff always has something to use.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        removed = 0\\n        for lvl in self._prune_levels():\\n            table = self.counts[lvl]\\n            for ctx in list(table.keys()):\\n                counter = table[ctx]\\n                for tok in [t for t, n in counter.items() if n < min_count]:\\n                    del counter[tok]\\n                    removed += 1\\n                if not counter:\\n                    del table[ctx]\\n        return removed\\n\\n    def enforce_budget(self, max_entries: int, log=None) -> None:\\n        if max_entries <= 0 or self.n_entries() <= max_entries:\\n            return\\n        target = int(max_entries * 0.75)\\n        for mc in range(2, 9):\\n            removed = self.prune(mc)\\n            if log:\\n                log(f\\\"  pruned {removed} n-grams with count < {mc}; entries now {self.n_entries()}\\\")\\n            if self.n_entries() <= target:\\n                break\\n\\n    # ---- weight extension ------------------------------------------------\\n    def scale(self, factor: float) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Multiply every stored weight (decay old knowledge before extending).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if factor == 1.0:\\n            return\\n        for level in self.counts:\\n            for counter in level.values():\\n                for tok in counter:\\n                    counter[tok] *= factor\\n        for tok in self.vocab:\\n            self.vocab[tok] *= factor\\n        self.total_tokens *= factor\\n\\n    def remap_tokens(self, mapping: Dict[str, str]) -> None:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Rename tokens everywhere (contexts and targets). Colliding counts are\\n        summed. Weave kernel only: transfers CoT behaviour to a new vocabulary.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if not mapping:\\n            return\\n\\n        def m(t):\\n            return mapping.get(t, t)\\n\\n        new_counts = []\\n        for level in self.counts:\\n            nl = defaultdict(Counter)\\n            for ctx, counter in level.items():\\n                nctx = tuple(m(t) for t in ctx)\\n                for tok, n in counter.items():\\n                    nl[nctx][m(tok)] += n\\n            new_counts.append(nl)\\n        self.counts = new_counts\\n        nv = Counter()\\n        for tok, n in self.vocab.items():\\n            nv[m(tok)] += n\\n        self.vocab = nv\\n\\n    # ---- serialisation ---------------------------------------------------\\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\\n        return {\\n            \\\"order\\\": self.order,\\n            \\\"alpha\\\": self.alpha,\\n            \\\"total_tokens\\\": self.total_tokens,\\n            \\\"vocab\\\": {str(k): v for k, v in self.vocab.items()},\\n            \\\"counts\\\": [[[list(ctx), {str(t): n for t, n in c.items()}]\\n                        for ctx, c in level.items()] for level in self.counts],\\n        }\\n\\n    @classmethod\\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> \\\"NGramModel\\\":\\n        model = cls(order=d[\\\"order\\\"], alpha=d[\\\"alpha\\\"])\\n        model.total_tokens = d[\\\"total_tokens\\\"]\\n        model.vocab = Counter(d[\\\"vocab\\\"])\\n        model.counts = []\\n        for level in d[\\\"counts\\\"]:\\n            lv = defaultdict(Counter)\\n            for ctx, counter in level:\\n                lv[tuple(ctx)] = Counter(counter)\\n            model.counts.append(lv)\\n        return model\\n\\n    def candidates(self, context_tokens: Sequence[str], limit: int = 80) -> List[Tuple[str, float]]:\\n        vocab_size = max(1, len(self.vocab))\\n        context = list(context_tokens)\\n        counter = Counter()\\n        for ctx_len in range(min(self.order - 1, len(context)), -1, -1):\\n            key = tuple(context[-ctx_len:]) if ctx_len else ()\\n            found = self.counts[ctx_len].get(key)\\n            if not found:\\n                continue\\n            weight = 1.0 + 0.7 * ctx_len\\n            for token, count in found.items():\\n                counter[token] += weight * count\\n            if ctx_len >= 1:\\n                break\\n        if not counter:\\n            counter.update(self.vocab)\\n        counter.pop(\\\"<bos>\\\", None)\\n        total = sum(counter.values())\\n        ranked = []\\n        for token, count in counter.items():\\n            prob = (count + self.alpha) / (total + self.alpha * vocab_size)\\n            ranked.append((token, math.log(max(prob, 1e-12))))\\n        ranked.sort(key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)\\n        return ranked[:max(1, limit)]\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Non-isomorphic fragments (weights are saved with the checkpoint)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass NonIsomorphicFragments:\\n    def __init__(self, seed: int = 17):\\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n        self.w_context = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 3))\\n        self.w_word = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 4))\\n        self.w_transition = rng.normal(0, 0.7, size=(5, 2))\\n\\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\\n        return {\\\"w_context\\\": self.w_context.tolist(),\\n                \\\"w_word\\\": self.w_word.tolist(),\\n                \\\"w_transition\\\": self.w_transition.tolist()}\\n\\n    @classmethod\\n    def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> \\\"NonIsomorphicFragments\\\":\\n        frag = cls(0)\\n        frag.w_context = np.asarray(d[\\\"w_context\\\"], dtype=float)\\n        frag.w_word = np.asarray(d[\\\"w_word\\\"], dtype=float)\\n        frag.w_transition = np.asarray(d[\\\"w_transition\\\"], dtype=float)\\n        return frag\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _unit(v: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\n        n = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\\n        return v / n if n > 1e-12 else np.zeros_like(v)\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def _hash_features(token: str, width: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n        raw = token.lower().encode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"ignore\\\")\\n        vals = np.zeros(width, dtype=float)\\n        if not raw:\\n            return vals\\n        for i, byte in enumerate(raw):\\n            vals[i % width] += ((byte % 31) - 15) / 15.0\\n            vals[(i * 3 + 1) % width] += ((byte % 17) - 8) / 8.0\\n        vals /= max(1, len(raw))\\n        vals[0] += min(len(raw), 20) / 20.0\\n        vals[1] += sum(chr(b).isalpha() for b in raw) / max(1, len(raw))\\n        return np.tanh(vals)\\n\\n    def features(self, context, token, logp, rank):\\n        recent = list(context[-4:])\\n        ctx_vec = np.zeros(5, dtype=float)\\n        if recent:\\n            for i, word in enumerate(recent):\\n                f = self._hash_features(word, 5)\\n                ctx_vec += f * (0.65 ** (len(recent) - i - 1))\\n            ctx_vec /= max(1, len(recent))\\n        word_vec = self._hash_features(token, 5)\\n        transition_vec = np.array([\\n            np.tanh(logp),\\n            1.0 / (1.0 + rank),\\n            1.0 if token[:1].isupper() else 0.0,\\n            1.0 if token in COT else 0.0,  # CoT words are visible to the fragments\\n            min(len(token), 24) / 24.0,\\n        ], dtype=float)\\n        g1 = np.tanh(ctx_vec @ self.w_context)\\n        g2 = np.tanh(word_vec @ self.w_word)\\n        g3 = np.tanh(transition_vec @ self.w_transition)\\n        return g1, g2, g3\\n\\n    def score(self, context, token, logp, rank, lam) -> Tuple[float, float]:\\n        g1, g2, g3 = self.features(context, token, logp, rank)\\n        summaries = np.array([np.linalg.norm(g1), np.linalg.norm(g2), np.linalg.norm(g3)])\\n        mean = float(np.mean(summaries))\\n        spread = float(np.std(summaries) / (mean + 1e-9))\\n        consistency = float(np.clip(0.55 * spread + 0.45 * (1.0 - mean), 0.0, 1.0))\\n\\n        ref = self._unit(np.array([np.mean(g1), np.mean(g2), np.mean(g3), np.tanh(logp)]))\\n        cand = self._unit(np.array([g1[0], g2[0], g3[0], np.tanh(logp + 0.1 * rank)]))\\n        alignment = (float(np.dot(ref, cand)) + 1.0) / 2.0\\n\\n        fragment_score = 1.6 * alignment - 1.15 * consistency\\n        total = (1.0 - lam) * (0.75 * logp + 0.25 * fragment_score) \\\\\\n            + lam * (1.25 * logp + 0.85 * fragment_score)\\n        return total, consistency\\n\\n\\ndef adiabatic_lambda(step: int, total_steps: int) -> float:\\n    u = min(1.0, max(0.0, step / max(1, total_steps - 1)))\\n    return 3.0 * u * u - 2.0 * u * u * u\\n\\n\\ndef softmax(values: Sequence[float], temperature: float = 1.0) -> np.ndarray:\\n    temp = max(1e-6, float(temperature))\\n    arr = np.asarray(values, dtype=float) / temp\\n    arr -= np.max(arr)\\n    exp = np.exp(np.clip(arr, -60, 60))\\n    return exp / max(float(exp.sum()), 1e-12)\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Checkpoints (v3: zip of state.json + dataset_ids.npy; v1/v2: gzip JSON)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef save_checkpoint(path: str, model: NGramModel, fragments: NonIsomorphicFragments,\\n                    store: TokenStore, meta: dict) -> None:\\n    state = {\\n        \\\"format\\\": FORMAT,\\n        \\\"cot\\\": current_cot_words(),\\n        \\\"fragments\\\": fragments.to_dict(),\\n        \\\"model\\\": model.to_dict(),\\n        \\\"dataset_words\\\": store.words,\\n        \\\"meta\\\": meta,\\n    }\\n    with zipfile.ZipFile(path, \\\"w\\\", zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED, compresslevel=6) as z:\\n        with z.open(\\\"state.json\\\", \\\"w\\\", force_zip64=True) as raw:\\n            wrapper = io.TextIOWrapper(raw, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n            json.dump(state, wrapper)\\n            wrapper.flush()\\n            wrapper.detach()\\n        with z.open(\\\"dataset_ids.npy\\\", \\\"w\\\", force_zip64=True) as raw:\\n            np.save(raw, store.ids().astype(np.int32), allow_pickle=False)\\n\\n\\ndef load_checkpoint(path: str):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Load a checkpoint and install its CoT vocabulary globally.\\n    Returns (model, fragments, TokenStore, meta).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    with open(path, \\\"rb\\\") as fh:\\n        magic = fh.read(2)\\n    if magic == b\\\"PK\\\":\\n        with zipfile.ZipFile(path) as z:\\n            with z.open(\\\"state.json\\\") as raw:\\n                state = json.load(io.TextIOWrapper(raw, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"))\\n            ids = np.load(io.BytesIO(z.read(\\\"dataset_ids.npy\\\")), allow_pickle=False)\\n        store = TokenStore(state.get(\\\"dataset_words\\\", []), ids)\\n    else:  # legacy gzip JSON: dataset (if any) is a plain token list\\n        with gzip.open(path, \\\"rt\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\\n            state = json.load(fh)\\n        store = TokenStore()\\n        store.add(state.get(\\\"dataset\\\", []))\\n    if state.get(\\\"format\\\") not in ACCEPTED_FORMATS:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"{path}: unsupported checkpoint format {state.get('format')!r}\\\")\\n    set_cot_tokens(state[\\\"cot\\\"])\\n    model = NGramModel.from_dict(state[\\\"model\\\"])\\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments.from_dict(state[\\\"fragments\\\"])\\n    meta = state.get(\\\"meta\\\", {})\\n    meta.setdefault(\\\"kernel\\\", \\\"weave\\\")  # v1 checkpoints were woven\\n    return model, fragments, store, meta\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Cybernetic controller (sensor -> comparator -> actuator)\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nclass Controller:\\n    def __init__(self, temperature: float, rep_limit: float = 0.5, logp_floor: float = -4.5):\\n        self.temperature = temperature\\n        self.rep_limit = rep_limit\\n        self.logp_floor = logp_floor\\n        self.k = 0\\n\\n    @staticmethod\\n    def repetition(tokens: Sequence[str]) -> float:\\n        words = strip_cot(tokens)\\n        if len(words) < 2:\\n            return 0.0\\n        return 1.0 - len(set(words)) / len(words)\\n\\n    def update(self, chunk: Sequence[str], mean_logp: float) -> Tuple[str, float]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Return (CoT token to emit, repetition measure).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        rep = self.repetition(chunk)\\n        if rep > self.rep_limit:\\n            cot = COT_DIVERGE\\n            self.temperature *= 1.15\\n        elif mean_logp < self.logp_floor:\\n            cot = COT_CONVERGE\\n            self.temperature *= 0.9\\n        else:\\n            cot = COT_CYCLE[self.k % len(COT_CYCLE)]\\n            self.k += 1\\n        self.temperature = float(np.clip(self.temperature, 0.3, 1.6))\\n        return cot, rep\\n\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass Candidate:\\n    token: str\\n    base_logp: float\\n    score: float\\n    consistency: float\\n    probability: float = 0.0\\n\\n\\ndef generate_chunk(model, fragments, context, n, step0, total, beam_size, tau, temperature, rng,\\n                   stop_on_cot=False, bias=None, bias_strength=0.0):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generate up to n tokens after `context`.\\n\\n    Returns (new_tokens, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted_cot). With stop_on_cot the\\n    chunk ends the moment the MODEL emits a CoT token (weave kernel). With a\\n    `bias` (scan kernel) each candidate's score gains bias_strength * bias[token],\\n    where bias comes from the dataset scan.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    ctx = list(context)\\n    new, logps, hit_eos, emitted = [], [], False, None\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        lam = adiabatic_lambda(step0 + i, total)\\n        ranked = model.candidates(ctx, limit=max(40, beam_size * 8))\\n        scored: List[Candidate] = []\\n        for rank, (token, logp) in enumerate(ranked):\\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, rank, lam)\\n            if bias:\\n                score += bias_strength * bias.get(token, 0.0)\\n            if consistency <= tau:\\n                scored.append(Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency))\\n        if not scored:\\n            token, logp = ranked[0]\\n            score, consistency = fragments.score(ctx, token, logp, 0, lam)\\n            scored = [Candidate(token, logp, score, consistency)]\\n\\n        scored.sort(key=lambda c: c.score, reverse=True)\\n        beam = scored[:max(1, beam_size)]\\n        probs = softmax([c.score for c in beam], temperature)\\n        chosen = beam[0] if temperature <= 0.01 else rng.choices(beam, weights=probs, k=1)[0]\\n\\n        if chosen.token == \\\"<eos>\\\":\\n            hit_eos = True\\n            break\\n        if stop_on_cot and chosen.token in COT:\\n            emitted = chosen.token\\n            logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\\n            break\\n        new.append(chosen.token)\\n        ctx.append(chosen.token)\\n        logps.append(chosen.base_logp)\\n    mean_logp = float(np.mean(logps)) if logps else 0.0\\n    return new, mean_logp, hit_eos, emitted\\n\\n\\ndef cybernetic_run(model, fragments, scanner, prompt, cycles, chunk, chunks_per_cycle, window,\\n                   beam_size, tau, temperature, seed, learn, trace):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Fixed-cycle loop. scanner=None -> weave kernel (CoT tokens live in the\\n    context); scanner given -> scan kernel (CoT token is a probe, kept out of the\\n    context, only steering the dataset scan for the next chunk).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\\n    scan = scanner is not None\\n\\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\\\"The\\\"]\\n    full = [COT_START] + seed_tokens          # everything produced so far (markers incl.)\\n    context = list(seed_tokens) if scan else list(full)\\n    total = max(1, cycles * chunks_per_cycle * chunk)\\n    step = 0\\n    probe = COT_START                         # CoT token that steers the next scan\\n\\n    for c in range(cycles):\\n        for k in range(chunks_per_cycle):\\n            bias, hits = ({}, 0)\\n            if scan:\\n                bias, hits = scanner.bias(probe, context, rng)\\n            new, mean_logp, hit_eos, _ = generate_chunk(\\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, step, total,\\n                beam_size, tau, controller.temperature, rng,\\n                bias=bias, bias_strength=scanner.strength if scan else 0.0)\\n            step += chunk\\n            cot, rep = controller.update(new, mean_logp)\\n\\n            if trace:\\n                extra = (f\\\" scan[{probe}:{cot_role(probe)} hits={hits} \\\"\\n                         f\\\"ground={grounding(new, bias):.2f}]\\\") if scan else \\\"\\\"\\n                print(f\\\"[cycle {c+1}/{cycles} chunk {k+1}] tokens={len(new)} \\\"\\n                      f\\\"mean_logp={mean_logp:.2f} rep={rep:.2f} \\\"\\n                      f\\\"-> {cot} (T={controller.temperature:.2f}){extra}\\\")\\n\\n            marker = [] if scan else [cot]\\n            # Feedback learning: only from healthy output, to avoid reinforcing loops.\\n            if learn and new and rep <= controller.rep_limit:\\n                model.learn(tail_ctx(context, model.order - 1) + new + marker)\\n\\n            context += new + marker\\n            full += new + [cot]\\n            probe = cot\\n            if hit_eos:\\n                break\\n\\n        # Pipe output back to input.\\n        tail = full[-window:]\\n        context = strip_cot(tail) if scan else [COT_INTEGRATE] + tail\\n        full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\\n        probe = COT_INTEGRATE\\n\\n    return full\\n\\n\\ndef stacked_run(model, fragments, scanner, prompt, target_depth, chunk, window, beam_size, tau,\\n                temperature, seed, learn, max_retries, strict, min_grounding, trace):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Keep generating until CoT tokens stack up in the correct order.\\n\\n    weave kernel: the model must itself emit the next expected CoT token\\n    (COT_CYCLE order, repeating) after a chunk of real content.\\n\\n    scan kernel (inverted): the expected CoT word is used as a probe into the\\n    dataset. A slot is accepted when the word is found there and the chunk is\\n    grounded in the scanned passages (>= min_grounding). A word that never occurs\\n    in the dataset cannot ground and is forced (flagged), or stops a --strict run.\\n\\n    Rejected chunks are regenerated (temperature creeps up per retry). Accepted\\n    slots are pushed on a stack that only grows (monotonic) and are learned online.\\n    After `max_retries` misses the slot is forced unless `strict`.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    rng = random.Random(seed)\\n    controller = Controller(temperature)\\n    scan = scanner is not None\\n\\n    seed_tokens = tokenize(prompt) or [\\\"The\\\"]\\n    full = [COT_START] + seed_tokens\\n    context = list(seed_tokens) if scan else list(full)\\n    stack: List[str] = []\\n    forced = 0\\n    attempts = 0\\n    max_attempts = target_depth * (200 if strict else max_retries + 1)\\n\\n    while len(stack) < target_depth and attempts < max_attempts:\\n        expected = COT_CYCLE[len(stack) % len(COT_CYCLE)]\\n        cot_hits = scanner.hits(expected) if scan else 0\\n        retries = 0\\n        accepted, was_forced = False, False\\n        while attempts < max_attempts:\\n            temp = float(np.clip(controller.temperature * (1.0 + 0.1 * retries), 0.3, 1.8))\\n            bias = {}\\n            if scan:\\n                bias, _ = scanner.bias(expected, context, rng)\\n            new, mlp, eos, emitted = generate_chunk(\\n                model, fragments, context, chunk, len(stack) * chunk,\\n                target_depth * chunk, beam_size, tau, temp, rng,\\n                stop_on_cot=not scan, bias=bias,\\n                bias_strength=scanner.strength if scan else 0.0)\\n            attempts += 1\\n            if scan:\\n                g = grounding(new, bias)\\n                ok = len(new) > 0 and cot_hits > 0 and g >= min_grounding\\n                detail = f\\\"scan hits={cot_hits} ground={g:.2f}\\\"\\n            else:\\n                ok = emitted == expected and len(new) > 0\\n                detail = f\\\"got {emitted or 'none'}\\\"\\n            msg = (f\\\"depth {len(stack)}/{target_depth} attempt {attempts} \\\"\\n                   f\\\"expected {expected} {detail} \\\"\\n                   f\\\"{'OK' if ok else 'retry'} (T={temp:.2f}, forced={forced})\\\")\\n            if trace:\\n                print(msg, file=sys.stderr)\\n            else:\\n                print(\\\"\\\\r\\\" + msg.ljust(78), end=\\\"\\\", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\\n            if ok:\\n                accepted = True\\n                break\\n            retries += 1\\n            if scan and cot_hits == 0:\\n                # Retrying can't make an absent word appear in the dataset.\\n                if not strict:\\n                    was_forced = True\\n                break\\n            if retries > max_retries and not strict:\\n                was_forced = True\\n                break\\n        if not (accepted or was_forced):\\n            break  # attempt cap hit, or strict and ungroundable\\n\\n        if was_forced:\\n            forced += 1\\n        stack.append(expected)\\n        marker = [] if scan else [expected]\\n        context += new + marker\\n        full += new + [expected]\\n        if new:\\n            controller.update(new, mlp)\\n        if accepted and learn:\\n            model.learn(tail_ctx(context, model.order - 1 + len(new) + len(marker)))\\n\\n        # Pipe output back to input at the end of each full CoT cycle.\\n        if len(stack) % PIPE_EVERY == 0:\\n            context = strip_cot(full[-window:]) if scan else [COT_INTEGRATE] + full[-window:]\\n            full.append(COT_INTEGRATE)\\n\\n    if not trace:\\n        print(file=sys.stderr)\\n    monotonic = all(stack[i] == COT_CYCLE[i % len(COT_CYCLE)] for i in range(len(stack)))\\n    stats = dict(depth=len(stack), target=target_depth, attempts=attempts,\\n                 forced=forced, monotonic=monotonic)\\n    return full, stats\\n\\n\\ndef detokenize(tokens: Sequence[str], hide_cot: bool) -> str:\\n    return \\\" \\\".join(strip_cot(tokens) if hide_cot else tokens)\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Data sources: local files and streamed Hugging Face datasets\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef die(msg: str) -> None:\\n    print(f\\\"error: {msg}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n    sys.exit(2)\\n\\n\\ndef log(msg: str) -> None:\\n    print(msg, file=sys.stderr, flush=True)\\n\\n\\ndef parse_size(s) -> int:\\n    s = str(s).strip().lower()\\n    for suf, mult in ((\\\"gb\\\", 10**9), (\\\"mb\\\", 10**6), (\\\"kb\\\", 10**3), (\\\"b\\\", 1)):\\n        if s.endswith(suf):\\n            return int(float(s[:-len(suf)]) * mult)\\n    return int(float(s))\\n\\n\\ndef read_corpus(path: str) -> str:\\n    p = Path(path)\\n    if not p.is_file():\\n        die(f\\\"corpus file not found: {p}\\\")\\n    try:\\n        text = p.read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8-sig\\\")\\n    except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\\n        die(f\\\"could not decode {p} as UTF-8: {exc}\\\")\\n    if not tokenize(text):\\n        die(f\\\"{p} contains no tokens\\\")\\n    return text\\n\\n\\ndef iter_file_docs(paths: Sequence[str]) -> Iterator[str]:\\n    for p in paths:\\n        yield read_corpus(p)\\n\\n\\n_TEXT_FIELDS = (\\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\", \\\"sentence\\\", \\\"document\\\", \\\"article\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"body\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef iter_hf_docs(args, stats: dict) -> Iterator[str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Stream a Hugging Face dataset, yielding text until the byte budget is hit.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    try:\\n        from datasets import load_dataset\\n    except ImportError:\\n        die(\\\"--hf-dataset needs the `datasets` package: pip install datasets\\\")\\n    kwargs = {\\\"split\\\": args.hf_split, \\\"streaming\\\": True}\\n    if args.hf_data_files:\\n        files = args.hf_data_files.split(\\\",\\\")\\n        kwargs[\\\"data_files\\\"] = files if len(files) > 1 else files[0]\\n    log(f\\\"streaming {args.hf_dataset}\\\"\\n        + (f\\\"/{args.hf_config}\\\" if args.hf_config else \\\"\\\")\\n        + f\\\" [{args.hf_split}], budget {args.hf_max_bytes}\\\")\\n    ds = load_dataset(args.hf_dataset, args.hf_config, **kwargs)\\n    budget = parse_size(args.hf_max_bytes)\\n    field = args.hf_field\\n    for row in ds:\\n        if field is None:\\n            field = next((k for k in _TEXT_FIELDS if isinstance(row.get(k), str)), None) \\\\\\n                or next((k for k, v in row.items() if isinstance(v, str)), None)\\n            if field is None:\\n                die(f\\\"no text column found in {list(row)}; pass --hf-field\\\")\\n            log(f\\\"using text field {field!r}\\\")\\n        text = row.get(field)\\n        if isinstance(text, list):\\n            text = \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(str(t) for t in text)\\n        if not isinstance(text, str) or not text.strip():\\n            continue\\n        n = len(text.encode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"ignore\\\"))\\n        if budget and stats[\\\"bytes\\\"] + n > budget:\\n            break\\n        stats[\\\"bytes\\\"] += n\\n        yield text\\n\\n\\ndef make_docs(args, stats: dict) -> Tuple[Iterator[str], List[str]]:\\n    sources, parts = [], []\\n    files = list(getattr(args, \\\"corpus\\\", None) or [])\\n    for f in files:\\n        if not Path(f).is_file():\\n            die(f\\\"corpus file not found: {f}\\\")\\n    if files:\\n        parts.append(iter_file_docs(files))\\n        sources += [Path(f).name for f in files]\\n    if args.hf_dataset:\\n        parts.append(iter_hf_docs(args, stats))\\n        sources.append(\\\"hf:\\\" + args.hf_dataset + (f\\\"/{args.hf_config}\\\" if args.hf_config else \\\"\\\"))\\n    return itertools.chain.from_iterable(parts), sources\\n\\n\\ndef peek_docs(docs: Iterator[str], nbytes: int) -> Tuple[List[str], Iterator[str]]:\\n    head, size = [], 0\\n    for d in docs:\\n        head.append(d)\\n        size += len(d)\\n        if size >= nbytes:\\n            break\\n    return head, docs\\n\\n\\ndef ingest(model: NGramModel, store: TokenStore, docs: Iterable[str], weave: bool,\\n           max_entries: int, stats: dict, log_every: int = 1_000_000) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Train on a document stream one document at a time (flat memory), keep the\\n    token stream for the scanner, and keep the n-gram tables under budget.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    t0 = time.time()\\n    ntok = 0\\n    next_log = log_every\\n    for text in docs:\\n        toks = tokenize(text)\\n        if not toks:\\n            continue\\n        model.train(text, cot=weave)\\n        store.add(toks)\\n        ntok += len(toks)\\n        if ntok >= next_log:\\n            next_log += log_every\\n            model.enforce_budget(max_entries, log)\\n            rate = ntok / max(1e-9, time.time() - t0)\\n            mb = f\\\"  {stats['bytes'] / 1e6:.0f}MB\\\" if stats.get(\\\"bytes\\\") else \\\"\\\"\\n            log(f\\\"  {ntok / 1e6:.1f}M tokens{mb}  entries {model.n_entries():,}  \\\"\\n                f\\\"{rate / 1e3:.0f}k tok/s\\\")\\n    model.enforce_budget(max_entries, log)\\n    return ntok\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# CLI\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef add_vocab_args(p: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--cot-vocab\\\", help=\\\"Custom CoT vocabulary file (one word per line, used in order).\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--cot-sort\\\", choices=[\\\"none\\\", \\\"alpha\\\", \\\"alpha-desc\\\", \\\"length\\\"], default=\\\"none\\\",\\n                   help=\\\"Sort the custom list before use (default: keep file order).\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef add_source_args(p: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--hf-dataset\\\", help=\\\"Hugging Face dataset to stream (e.g. Salesforce/wikitext).\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--hf-config\\\", help=\\\"Dataset config name (e.g. wikitext-103-raw-v1).\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--hf-split\\\", default=\\\"train\\\", help=\\\"Split to stream (default: train).\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--hf-field\\\", help=\\\"Text column (auto-detected if omitted).\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--hf-data-files\\\", help=\\\"Comma-separated data files (for 'json'/'text'/'csv' loaders).\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--hf-max-bytes\\\", default=\\\"200MB\\\", help=\\\"Stop after this much text (default 200MB).\\\")\\n    p.add_argument(\\\"--max-entries\\\", type=int, default=5_000_000,\\n                   help=\\\"Prune rare n-grams when stored (context,target) pairs exceed this (0 = never).\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef report_coverage(store: TokenStore) -> None:\\n    if not len(store):\\n        return\\n    found, missing = DatasetScanner(store).coverage(current_cot_words())\\n    log(f\\\"scan coverage: {found}/{COT_COUNT} CoT words occur in the dataset\\\"\\n        + (f\\\" (absent: {', '.join(missing[:10])}{' ...' if len(missing) > 10 else ''})\\\"\\n           if missing else \\\"\\\"))\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_build(args) -> None:\\n    stats = {\\\"bytes\\\": 0}\\n    docs, sources = make_docs(args, stats)\\n    if not sources:\\n        die(\\\"give at least one corpus file or --hf-dataset\\\")\\n    head, rest = peek_docs(docs, VOCAB_PEEK_BYTES)\\n    if not head:\\n        die(\\\"the data source produced no text\\\")\\n    if args.cot_vocab:\\n        words = load_cot_vocab(args.cot_vocab, args.cot_sort)\\n    else:\\n        words = select_cot_tokens(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(head), args.seed)\\n    set_cot_tokens(words)\\n    log(\\\"CoT vocab: \\\" + \\\" \\\".join(current_cot_words()))\\n\\n    weave = args.kernel == \\\"weave\\\" and not args.no_cot_weave\\n    model = NGramModel(order=args.order, alpha=args.alpha)\\n    store = TokenStore()\\n    ntok = ingest(model, store, itertools.chain(head, rest), weave, args.max_entries, stats)\\n    if args.kernel == \\\"scan\\\":\\n        report_coverage(store)\\n    fragments = NonIsomorphicFragments(args.seed)\\n    meta = {\\\"seed\\\": args.seed, \\\"kernel\\\": args.kernel, \\\"extensions\\\": 0, \\\"sources\\\": sources}\\n    log(f\\\"saving {args.output} ...\\\")\\n    save_checkpoint(args.output, model, fragments, store, meta)\\n    log(f\\\"built {args.output} [{args.kernel} kernel]: {len(model.vocab):,} types, \\\"\\n        f\\\"{ntok:,} tokens read, {model.n_entries():,} n-gram entries, dataset {len(store):,} tokens\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_extend(args) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        model, fragments, store, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\\n    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\\n        die(str(exc))\\n    kernel = meta[\\\"kernel\\\"]\\n    old_words = current_cot_words()\\n\\n    if args.alpha is not None:\\n        model.alpha = max(1e-9, args.alpha)\\n\\n    if args.cot_vocab:\\n        new_words = load_cot_vocab(args.cot_vocab, args.cot_sort)\\n        if kernel == \\\"weave\\\":\\n            mapping = {o: n for o, n in zip(old_words, new_words) if o != n}\\n            if mapping:\\n                clash = [n for n in mapping.values() if n in model.vocab and n not in mapping]\\n                if clash:\\n                    log(\\\"warning: new CoT words already occur as ordinary words in the weights \\\"\\n                        f\\\"and will merge with them: {', '.join(sorted(clash)[:8])}\\\"\\n                        + (\\\" ...\\\" if len(clash) > 8 else \\\"\\\"))\\n                model.remap_tokens(mapping)\\n                log(f\\\"remapped {len(mapping)} CoT tokens onto the new vocabulary\\\")\\n        else:\\n            log(\\\"scan kernel: CoT vocabulary swapped, no weights to remap\\\")\\n        set_cot_tokens(new_words)\\n    log(\\\"CoT vocab: \\\" + \\\" \\\".join(current_cot_words()))\\n\\n    if args.decay != 1.0:\\n        model.scale(args.decay)\\n        log(f\\\"decayed existing weights by {args.decay} (dataset is not decayed)\\\")\\n\\n    stats = {\\\"bytes\\\": 0}\\n    docs, sources = make_docs(args, stats)\\n    weave = kernel == \\\"weave\\\" and not args.no_cot_weave\\n    ntok = ingest(model, store, docs, weave, args.max_entries, stats) if sources else 0\\n    meta.setdefault(\\\"sources\\\", []).extend(sources)\\n    meta[\\\"extensions\\\"] = meta.get(\\\"extensions\\\", 0) + 1\\n\\n    if kernel == \\\"scan\\\":\\n        report_coverage(store)\\n    log(f\\\"saving {args.output} ...\\\")\\n    save_checkpoint(args.output, model, fragments, store, meta)\\n    log(f\\\"extended -> {args.output} [{kernel} kernel]: {len(model.vocab):,} types, \\\"\\n        f\\\"+{ntok:,} tokens, {model.n_entries():,} n-gram entries, dataset {len(store):,} tokens\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_info(args) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        model, fragments, store, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\\n    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\\n        die(str(exc))\\n    print(f\\\"format       {FORMAT}   kernel {meta['kernel']}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"order        {model.order}   alpha {model.alpha}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"vocab types  {len(model.vocab):,}   tokens {model.total_tokens:,.0f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"dataset      {len(store):,} tokens, {len(store.words):,} distinct words\\\")\\n    print(\\\"contexts     \\\" + \\\", \\\".join(f\\\"n={i}: {len(lv):,}\\\" for i, lv in enumerate(model.counts))\\n          + f\\\"   entries {model.n_entries():,}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"extensions   {meta.get('extensions', 0)}   sources {', '.join(meta.get('sources', []))}\\\")\\n    print(\\\"cycle        \\\" + \\\" \\\".join(str(t) for t in COT_CYCLE))\\n    print(f\\\"diverge={COT_DIVERGE} converge={COT_CONVERGE} \\\"\\n          f\\\"integrate={COT_INTEGRATE} start={COT_START}\\\")\\n    if len(store):\\n        found, missing = DatasetScanner(store).coverage(current_cot_words())\\n        print(f\\\"coverage     {found}/{COT_COUNT} CoT words occur in the dataset\\\"\\n              + (f\\\"; absent: {', '.join(missing)}\\\" if missing else \\\"\\\"))\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_generate(args) -> None:\\n    try:\\n        model, fragments, store, meta = load_checkpoint(args.model)\\n    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\\n        die(str(exc))\\n    kernel = args.kernel or meta[\\\"kernel\\\"]\\n    scanner = None\\n    if kernel == \\\"scan\\\":\\n        if not len(store):\\n            die(\\\"scan kernel needs the dataset stored in the checkpoint \\\"\\n                \\\"(this one has none; rebuild it or use --kernel weave)\\\")\\n        scanner = DatasetScanner(store, strength=args.scan_strength, limit=args.scan_limit,\\n                                 span=args.scan_span, mix=args.scan_mix)\\n        report_coverage(store)\\n    log(f\\\"kernel: {kernel}\\\")\\n    log(\\\"CoT vocab: \\\" + \\\" \\\".join(current_cot_words()))\\n\\n    first = True\\n    while True:\\n        try:\\n            prompt = args.prompt if (args.prompt and first) else input(\\\"USER: \\\")\\n        except (EOFError, KeyboardInterrupt):\\n            print()\\n            break\\n        first = False\\n\\n        tau = float(np.clip(args.tau, 0.0, 1.0))\\n        temp = max(0.0, args.temperature)\\n        if args.stack_target > 0:\\n            full, stats = stacked_run(\\n                model, fragments, scanner, prompt, target_depth=args.stack_target,\\n                chunk=args.chunk, window=args.window, beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau,\\n                temperature=temp, seed=args.seed, learn=not args.no_learn,\\n                max_retries=args.max_retries, strict=args.strict,\\n                min_grounding=args.min_grounding, trace=args.trace)\\n            print(f\\\"\\\\n[stack] depth {stats['depth']}/{stats['target']}  attempts {stats['attempts']}  \\\"\\n                  f\\\"forced {stats['forced']}  monotonic order verified: {stats['monotonic']}\\\")\\n        else:\\n            full = cybernetic_run(\\n                model, fragments, scanner, prompt, cycles=args.cycles, chunk=args.chunk,\\n                chunks_per_cycle=args.chunks_per_cycle, window=args.window,\\n                beam_size=args.beam, tau=tau, temperature=temp, seed=args.seed,\\n                learn=not args.no_learn, trace=args.trace)\\n\\n        text = detokenize(full, hide_cot=not args.show_cot)\\n        print(\\\"\\\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\\\n\\\")\\n        print(text)\\n        print()\\n        if args.save:\\n            with open(args.save, \\\"a\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fh:\\n                fh.write(text + \\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n    if args.save_model:\\n        meta[\\\"extensions\\\"] = meta.get(\\\"extensions\\\", 0) + 1\\n        save_checkpoint(args.save_model, model, fragments, store, meta)\\n        log(f\\\"saved weights -> {args.save_model}\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef main() -> None:\\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\\\"CoT weight extender (scan kernel, HF streaming) for the cybernetic n-gram generator.\\\")\\n    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest=\\\"cmd\\\", required=True)\\n\\n    b = sub.add_parser(\\\"build\\\", help=\\\"Train a new checkpoint from files and/or a Hugging Face dataset.\\\")\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"corpus\\\", nargs=\\\"*\\\", help=\\\"UTF-8 text corpus file(s) (optional if --hf-dataset is given).\\\")\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"-o\\\", \\\"--output\\\", required=True, help=\\\"Checkpoint to write (.cotw).\\\")\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"--order\\\", type=int, default=3)\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"--alpha\\\", type=float, default=0.25)\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"--seed\\\", type=int, default=7)\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"--kernel\\\", choices=[\\\"scan\\\", \\\"weave\\\"], default=\\\"scan\\\",\\n                   help=\\\"scan: CoT token probes the dataset (default). weave: CoT tokens woven into the weights.\\\")\\n    b.add_argument(\\\"--no-cot-weave\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"(weave kernel) do not weave CoT tokens in.\\\")\\n    add_vocab_args(b)\\n    add_source_args(b)\\n    b.set_defaults(func=cmd_build)\\n\\n    e = sub.add_parser(\\\"extend\\\", help=\\\"Extend an existing checkpoint.\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"model\\\", help=\\\"Checkpoint to extend.\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"corpus\\\", nargs=\\\"*\\\", help=\\\"Additional corpus file(s) (optional).\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"-o\\\", \\\"--output\\\", required=True, help=\\\"Checkpoint to write.\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"--decay\\\", type=float, default=1.0,\\n                   help=\\\"Scale existing weights by this factor before adding new data (e.g. 0.9).\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"--alpha\\\", type=float, default=None, help=\\\"Override smoothing alpha.\\\")\\n    e.add_argument(\\\"--no-cot-weave\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"(weave kernel) do not weave CoT tokens into new data.\\\")\\n    add_vocab_args(e)\\n    add_source_args(e)\\n    e.set_defaults(func=cmd_extend)\\n\\n    i = sub.add_parser(\\\"info\\\", help=\\\"Show checkpoint statistics.\\\")\\n    i.add_argument(\\\"model\\\")\\n    i.set_defaults(func=cmd_info)\\n\\n    g = sub.add_parser(\\\"generate\\\", help=\\\"Run the cybernetic loop from a checkpoint.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"model\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--kernel\\\", choices=[\\\"scan\\\", \\\"weave\\\"], default=None,\\n                   help=\\\"Override the checkpoint's kernel.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--prompt\\\", help=\\\"Initial prompt. If omitted you are asked each round.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--cycles\\\", type=int, default=4, help=\\\"Output->input feedback cycles per prompt.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--chunk\\\", type=int, default=20, help=\\\"Tokens per chunk between CoT tokens.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--chunks-per-cycle\\\", type=int, default=3)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--window\\\", type=int, default=40, help=\\\"Tokens of output piped back as the next prompt.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--beam\\\", type=int, default=8)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--tau\\\", type=float, default=0.65)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--temperature\\\", type=float, default=0.85)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--seed\\\", type=int, default=7)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--stack-target\\\", type=int, default=25,\\n                   help=\\\"Keep going until this many CoT tokens have stacked in order (0 = fixed-cycle mode).\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--max-retries\\\", type=int, default=25, help=\\\"Rejected chunks allowed per stack slot before forcing.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--strict\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Never force a token; retry until the attempt cap.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--scan-strength\\\", type=float, default=1.5, help=\\\"Weight of the dataset-scan bias on scores.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--scan-limit\\\", type=int, default=24, help=\\\"Max passages sampled per probe word.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--scan-span\\\", type=int, default=12, help=\\\"Tokens read after each occurrence.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--scan-mix\\\", type=float, default=0.5,\\n                   help=\\\"Weight of the last context word as a second probe (0 = CoT token only).\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--min-grounding\\\", type=float, default=0.15,\\n                   help=\\\"Stack mode (scan): min fraction of chunk tokens found in the scanned passages.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--no-learn\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Disable online learning from own output.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--show-cot\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Show CoT tokens in printed text (hidden by default).\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--trace\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Print controller diagnostics.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--save\\\", help=\\\"Append output to this text file.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--save-model\\\", help=\\\"Write the weights (incl. online learning) to this checkpoint at exit.\\\")\\n    g.set_defaults(func=cmd_generate)\\n\\n    args = ap.parse_args()\\n    args.func(args)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\nPYEOF\\npip install datasets --break-system-packages -q 2>&1 | tail -2; python3 -c \\\"import datasets; print('datasets', datasets.__version__)\\\"\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:24:28.004451Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:24:28.004500Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01TCXfiXz2eRqFayHMUECVKA", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"datasets 5.1.0\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"datasets 5.1.0\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:24:30.653099Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:24:32.194468Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Testing dataset ingestion with a synthetic byte-capped corpus."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:24:32.194523Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:24:37.313086Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01NFMmByABU4MY9jnU3Wt3EX", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp && rm -rf t3 && mkdir t3 && cd t3 && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport numpy as np, json, random\nrng=np.random.default_rng(3)\nV=30000\nsyl=[\"ka\",\"to\",\"mi\",\"re\",\"su\",\"lan\",\"dor\",\"vek\",\"pi\",\"no\",\"ba\",\"lu\",\"sen\",\"tar\",\"wi\",\"ox\"]\nwords=[\"\".join(rng.choice(syl,size=rng.integers(1,4))) + str(i%7 if i%5==0 else \"\") for i in range(V)]\n# add real-ish frequent words\nwords[:12]=[\"the\",\"of\",\"and\",\"machine\",\"thought\",\"signal\",\"memory\",\"pattern\",\"system\",\"feedback\",\"network\",\"state\"]\np=1/np.arange(1,V+1)**1.05; p/=p.sum()\n# markov-ish structure: next word depends on previous via small offset to give repeated n-grams\nwith open(\"data.jsonl\",\"w\") as f:\n    size=0\n    while size<32_000_000:\n        n=int(rng.integers(40,160))\n        idx=rng.choice(V,size=n,p=p)\n        toks=[words[i] for i in idx]\n        # sprinkle sentence ends\n        for k in range(8,n,int(rng.integers(8,16))): toks[k]+= \".\"\n        line=\" \".join(toks)\n        f.write(json.dumps({\"id\":1,\"text\":line})+\"\\n\"); size+=len(line)\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\nls -la data.jsonl\nprintf \"the\\nof\\nand\\nmachine\\nthought\\nsignal\\nmemory\\npattern\\nsystem\\nfeedback\\nnetwork\\nstate\\n\" > cot.txt\nS=/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py\n/usr/bin/time -v python3 $S build -o big.cotw --hf-dataset json --hf-data-files data.jsonl --hf-max-bytes 25MB --max-entries 1500000 --cot-vocab cot.txt 2> build.log; tail -32 build.log | grep -E \"tokens|pruned|built|saving|Elapsed|Maximum resident|streaming|field|coverage\" | tail -20; ls -la big.cotw", "description": "Generate 32MB synthetic jsonl and test HF-streaming build with pruning, timing and memory"}, "message": "Generate 32MB synthetic jsonl and test HF-streaming build with pruning, timing and memory", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /tmp && rm -rf t3 && mkdir t3 && cd t3 && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport numpy as np, json, random\\nrng=np.random.default_rng(3)\\nV=30000\\nsyl=[\\\"ka\\\",\\\"to\\\",\\\"mi\\\",\\\"re\\\",\\\"su\\\",\\\"lan\\\",\\\"dor\\\",\\\"vek\\\",\\\"pi\\\",\\\"no\\\",\\\"ba\\\",\\\"lu\\\",\\\"sen\\\",\\\"tar\\\",\\\"wi\\\",\\\"ox\\\"]\\nwords=[\\\"\\\".join(rng.choice(syl,size=rng.integers(1,4))) + str(i%7 if i%5==0 else \\\"\\\") for i in range(V)]\\n# add real-ish frequent words\\nwords[:12]=[\\\"the\\\",\\\"of\\\",\\\"and\\\",\\\"machine\\\",\\\"thought\\\",\\\"signal\\\",\\\"memory\\\",\\\"pattern\\\",\\\"system\\\",\\\"feedback\\\",\\\"network\\\",\\\"state\\\"]\\np=1/np.arange(1,V+1)**1.05; p/=p.sum()\\n# markov-ish structure: next word depends on previous via small offset to give repeated n-grams\\nwith open(\\\"data.jsonl\\\",\\\"w\\\") as f:\\n    size=0\\n    while size<32_000_000:\\n        n=int(rng.integers(40,160))\\n        idx=rng.choice(V,size=n,p=p)\\n        toks=[words[i] for i in idx]\\n        # sprinkle sentence ends\\n        for k in range(8,n,int(rng.integers(8,16))): toks[k]+= \\\".\\\"\\n        line=\\\" \\\".join(toks)\\n        f.write(json.dumps({\\\"id\\\":1,\\\"text\\\":line})+\\\"\\\\n\\\"); size+=len(line)\\nprint(\\\"ok\\\")\\nEOF\\nls -la data.jsonl\\nprintf \\\"the\\\\nof\\\\nand\\\\nmachine\\\\nthought\\\\nsignal\\\\nmemory\\\\npattern\\\\nsystem\\\\nfeedback\\\\nnetwork\\\\nstate\\\\n\\\" > cot.txt\\nS=/mnt/user-data/outputs/cot_weight_extender.py\\n/usr/bin/time -v python3 $S build -o big.cotw --hf-dataset json --hf-data-files data.jsonl --hf-max-bytes 25MB --max-entries 1500000 --cot-vocab cot.txt 2> build.log; tail -32 build.log | grep -E \\\"tokens|pruned|built|saving|Elapsed|Maximum resident|streaming|field|coverage\\\" | tail -20; ls -la big.cotw\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:24:54.529916Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:24:54.529970Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01NFMmByABU4MY9jnU3Wt3EX", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":2,\"stdout\":\"ok\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 33247395 Oct 14 22:24 data.jsonl\\n\",\"stderr\":\"ls: cannot access 'big.cotw': No such file or directory\\n\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"plaintext\", \"code\": \"ls: cannot access 'big.cotw': No such file or directory\\n\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:24:56.164033Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-14T22:24:56.478164Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01GvrpfkAmRMtPzU9C97HVDG", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/t3 && tail -15 build.log", "description": "Inspect build failure"}, "message": "Inspect build failure", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\