sh_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":1,\"stdout\":\"68:#   2. Downloads + builds TCC (i386-tcc, libtcc.a, and the in-kernel\\n69:#      i386-libtcc-kern.a)\\n71:# Equivalent to running setup-tcc then `make BOCHS=1`, but as a single\\n74:world: $(BOCHS_CPU_LIB) setup-tcc $(MAIN) $(DISK_IMG)\\n118:\\trm -rf *.o main.iso iso hello hello_blob.o tcc_tool libtcc_glue.so i386-libtcc-kern.a\\n124:\\t# NOTE: tcc-local/ and tcc-src/ are also kept so `make cc` works\\n126:\\t#         rm -rf tcc-local tcc-src tcc-mob.tar.gz\\n129:# Remove the local TCC build completely (forces re-download on next setup-tcc).\\n130:tcc-clean:\\n131:\\trm -rf $(TCC_LOCAL) $(TCC_SRC_DIR) $(TCC_ARCHIVE)\\n133:.PHONY: all world clean distclean tcc-clean iso test_main run-test cc tcc setup-tcc download-tcc\\n136:#  TCC glue \u2014 host-side C compiler for guest ELFs\\n138:#  Mirrors the bochs_glue pattern: tcc_glue.cpp wraps libtcc\\n139:#  into a CLI tool (tcc_tool) and a shared library\\n140:#  (libtcc_glue.so).  The kernel links tcc_stub.cpp (no-ops)\\n145:#    make setup-tcc          # download + build TCC into tcc-local/\\n147:#  Then compile guest programs normally:\\n148:#    make cc SRC=prog.c      # OUT defaults to stem of SRC\\n149:#    make cc SRC=prog.c OUT=prog\\n155:#    1. i386-tcc -c prog.c \u2192 prog.o  (relocatable 32-bit i386 object)\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"plaintext\", \"code\": \"68:#   2. Downloads + builds TCC (i386-tcc, libtcc.a, and the in-kernel\\n69:#      i386-libtcc-kern.a)\\n71:# Equivalent to running setup-tcc then `make BOCHS=1`, but as a single\\n74:world: $(BOCHS_CPU_LIB) setup-tcc $(MAIN) $(DISK_IMG)\\n118:\\trm -rf *.o main.iso iso hello hello_blob.o tcc_tool libtcc_glue.so i386-libtcc-kern.a\\n124:\\t# NOTE: tcc-local/ and tcc-src/ are also kept so `make cc` works\\n126:\\t#         rm -rf tcc-local tcc-src tcc-mob.tar.gz\\n129:# Remove the local TCC build completely (forces re-download on next setup-tcc).\\n130:tcc-clean:\\n131:\\trm -rf $(TCC_LOCAL) $(TCC_SRC_DIR) $(TCC_ARCHIVE)\\n133:.PHONY: all world clean distclean tcc-clean iso test_main run-test cc tcc setup-tcc download-tcc\\n136:#  TCC glue \\u2014 host-side C compiler for guest ELFs\\n138:#  Mirrors the bochs_glue pattern: tcc_glue.cpp wraps libtcc\\n139:#  into a CLI tool (tcc_tool) and a shared library\\n140:#  (libtcc_glue.so).  The kernel links tcc_stub.cpp (no-ops)\\n145:#    make setup-tcc          # download + build TCC into tcc-local/\\n147:#  Then compile guest programs normally:\\n148:#    make cc SRC=prog.c      # OUT defaults to stem of SRC\\n149:#    make cc SRC=prog.c OUT=prog\\n155:#    1. i386-tcc -c prog.c \\u2192 prog.o  (relocatable 32-bit i386 object)\\n\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:27:41.753865Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:27:43.930119Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Investigating a compiler exit code's true meaning."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:27:43.930215Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:27:44.676725Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01U2rfzyfV5X8My4RAEJPn1j", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && ls -la /tmp/ed/; for O in -O0 -O1 -O2; do gcc -m32 -ffreestanding -fno-stack-protector -fno-pie $O -c editf.c -o /tmp/ed/e$O.o 2>&1 | head -3; echo \"$O undefined:\"; nm /tmp/ed/e$O.o | grep \" U \"; done; sed -n 150,200p Makefile", "description": "List undefined symbols per optimisation level; read cc flow"}, "message": "List undefined symbols per optimisation level; read cc flow", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && ls -la /tmp/ed/; for O in -O0 -O1 -O2; do gcc -m32 -ffreestanding -fno-stack-protector -fno-pie $O -c editf.c -o /tmp/ed/e$O.o 2>&1 | head -3; echo \\\"$O undefined:\\\"; nm /tmp/ed/e$O.o | grep \\\" U \\\"; done; sed -n 150,200p Makefile\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:27:45.630997Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:27:45.631050Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01U2rfzyfV5X8My4RAEJPn1j", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"total 24\\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root  4096 Oct 15 08:27 .\\ndrwxrwxrwt 7 root root  4096 Oct 15 08:27 ..\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 13172 Oct 15 08:27 editf.o\\n-O0 undefined:\\n-O1 undefined:\\n-O2 undefined:\\n#\\n#  The compiled 32-bit ELF is written to disk.img.  Boot the OS\\n#  and type the ELF name in a terminal to run it.\\n#\\n#  Under the hood:\\n#    1. i386-tcc -c prog.c \u2192 prog.o  (relocatable 32-bit i386 object)\\n#    2. ld -m elf_i386 -T tcc_guest.ld \u2192 ELF32 (code at 0x08002000,\\n#       safely past the Bochs slot GDT/IDT/stub injection zone)\\n#    3. mtools mcopy prog \u2192 disk.img::/prog\\n# ============================================================\\n\\n# \u2500\u2500 Local TCC build paths \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\n# TCC is built from source into tcc-local/ so we get:\\n#   tcc-local/bin/i386-tcc   \u2014 cross-compiler targeting i386\\n#   tcc-local/lib/libtcc.a   \u2014 embedded-compiler library\\n#   tcc-local/include/libtcc.h\\n#\\n# TCC source: GitHub mirror of the official mob (development) branch.\\nTCC_LOCAL     := tcc-local\\nTCC_SRC_DIR   := tcc-src\\nTCC_REPO      := https://github.com/TinyCC/tinycc/archive/refs/heads/mob.tar.gz\\nTCC_ARCHIVE   := tcc-mob.tar.gz\\nTCC_I386      := $(TCC_LOCAL)/bin/i386-tcc\\nTCC_LIB       := $(TCC_LOCAL)/lib/libtcc.a\\nTCC_INC       := $(TCC_LOCAL)/include/libtcc.h\\n\\n# \u2500\u2500 Auto-detect: use system TCC/libtcc if present, else fall back to local \u2500\u2500\\n# If the local build exists it takes priority (consistent cross-compiler).\\n# The shell function runs at parse time so it only queries what is installed.\\nTCC_TOOL   := tcc_tool\\nTCC_SO     := libtcc_glue.so\\n\\n# Include / link flags \u2014 prefer local build, then system.\\nTCC_IFLAGS := $(shell \\\\\\n    if [ -f $(TCC_INC) ]; then echo \\\"-I$(TCC_LOCAL)/include\\\"; \\\\\\n    elif pkg-config --exists libtcc 2>/dev/null; then pkg-config --cflags libtcc; \\\\\\n    fi)\\nTCC_LIBS   := $(shell \\\\\\n    if [ -f $(TCC_LIB) ]; then echo \\\"$(TCC_LOCAL)/lib/libtcc.a\\\"; \\\\\\n    elif pkg-config --exists libtcc 2>/dev/null; then pkg-config --libs libtcc; \\\\\\n    else echo \\\"-ltcc\\\"; \\\\\\n    fi)\\nTCC_CFLAGS := -O2 -Wall -std=c++17 $(TCC_IFLAGS)\\n\\n# \u2500\u2500 setup-tcc / download-tcc \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\n# Downloads TCC source from GitHub and builds:\\n#   \u2022 i386-tcc  (cross-compiler: host=x86-64, target=i386)\\n#   \u2022 libtcc.a  (embedded compiler library, position-independent)\\n#   \u2022 libtcc.h  (API header)\\n#\\n# Requires on the build host: gcc make (already needed for the kernel build).\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"total 24\\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root  4096 Oct 15 08:27 .\\ndrwxrwxrwt 7 root root  4096 Oct 15 08:27 ..\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 13172 Oct 15 08:27 editf.o\\n-O0 undefined:\\n-O1 undefined:\\n-O2 undefined:\\n#\\n#  The compiled 32-bit ELF is written to disk.img.  Boot the OS\\n#  and type the ELF name in a terminal to run it.\\n#\\n#  Under the hood:\\n#    1. i386-tcc -c prog.c \u2192 prog.o  (relocatable 32-bit i386 object)\\n#    2. ld -m elf_i386 -T tcc_guest.ld \u2192 ELF32 (code at 0x08002000,\\n#       safely past the Bochs slot GDT/IDT/stub injection zone)\\n#    3. mtools mcopy prog \u2192 disk.img::/prog\\n# ============================================================\\n\\n# \u2500\u2500 Local TCC build paths \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\n# TCC is built from source into tcc-local/ so we get:\\n#   tcc-local/bin/i386-tcc   \u2014 cross-compiler targeting i386\\n#   tcc-local/lib/libtcc.a   \u2014 embedded-compiler library\\n#   tcc-local/include/libtcc.h\\n#\\n# TCC source: GitHub mirror of the official mob (development) branch.\\nTCC_LOCAL     := tcc-local\\nTCC_SRC_DIR   := tcc-src\\nTCC_REPO      := https://github.com/TinyCC/tinycc/archive/refs/heads/mob.tar.gz\\nTCC_ARCHIVE   := tcc-mob.tar.gz\\nTCC_I386      := $(TCC_LOCAL)/bin/i386-tcc\\nTCC_LIB       := $(TCC_LOCAL)/lib/libtcc.a\\nTCC_INC       := $(TCC_LOCAL)/include/libtcc.h\\n\\n# \u2500\u2500 Auto-detect: use system TCC/libtcc if present, else fall back to local \u2500\u2500\\n# If the local build exists it takes priority (consistent cross-compiler).\\n# The shell function runs at parse time so it only queries what is installed.\\nTCC_TOOL   := tcc_tool\\nTCC_SO     := libtcc_glue.so\\n\\n# Include / link flags \u2014 prefer local build, then system.\\nTCC_IFLAGS := $(shell \\\\\\n    if [ -f $(TCC_INC) ]; then echo \\\"-I$(TCC_LOCAL)/include\\\"; \\\\\\n    elif pkg-config --exists libtcc 2>/dev/null; then pkg-config --cflags libtcc; \\\\\\n    fi)\\nTCC_LIBS   := $(shell \\\\\\n    if [ -f $(TCC_LIB) ]; then echo \\\"$(TCC_LOCAL)/lib/libtcc.a\\\"; \\\\\\n    elif pkg-config --exists libtcc 2>/dev/null; then pkg-config --libs libtcc; \\\\\\n    else echo \\\"-ltcc\\\"; \\\\\\n    fi)\\nTCC_CFLAGS := -O2 -Wall -std=c++17 $(TCC_IFLAGS)\\n\\n# \u2500\u2500 setup-tcc / download-tcc \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\n# Downloads TCC source from GitHub and builds:\\n#   \u2022 i386-tcc  (cross-compiler: host=x86-64, target=i386)\\n#   \u2022 libtcc.a  (embedded compiler library, position-independent)\\n#   \u2022 libtcc.h  (API header)\\n#\\n# Requires on the build host: gcc make (already needed for the kernel build).\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:27:48.653115Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:27:48.653292Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "gcc finds no undefined symbols, but the OS builds guests with TCC, not gcc. GitHub is reachable from here, so I'll build the repo's TCC and compile editf.c the same way it does.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:27:48.653297Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:27:48.856521Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01FaZuRi3M16NcnTutoxX9Aa", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && (timeout 280 make setup-tcc 2>&1 | tail -8); ls tcc-local/bin 2>/dev/null", "description": "Build the repo's TCC toolchain"}, "message": "Build the repo's TCC toolchain", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && (timeout 280 make setup-tcc 2>&1 | tail -8); ls tcc-local/bin 2>/dev/null\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:33.689256Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:33.689323Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01FaZuRi3M16NcnTutoxX9Aa", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"    cross-compiler : tcc-local/bin/i386-tcc\\n    libtcc         : tcc-local/lib/libtcc.a\\n    header         : tcc-local/include/libtcc.h\\n>>> setup-tcc complete.\\n    host cross-compiler : tcc-local/bin/i386-tcc\\n    kernel TCC library  : i386-libtcc-kern.a\\n    Now run: make BOCHS=1  to rebuild the kernel with in-kernel TCC.\\n    Inside the OS:  cc hello_tcc.c\\narm-tcc\\narm-wince-tcc\\narm64-osx-tcc\\narm64-tcc\\narm64-win32-tcc\\nc67-tcc\\ni386-tcc\\ni386-win32-tcc\\nriscv64-tcc\\ntcc\\nx86_64-osx-tcc\\nx86_64-tcc\\nx86_64-win32-tcc\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"    cross-compiler : tcc-local/bin/i386-tcc\\n    libtcc         : tcc-local/lib/libtcc.a\\n    header         : tcc-local/include/libtcc.h\\n>>> setup-tcc complete.\\n    host cross-compiler : tcc-local/bin/i386-tcc\\n    kernel TCC library  : i386-libtcc-kern.a\\n    Now run: make BOCHS=1  to rebuild the kernel with in-kernel TCC.\\n    Inside the OS:  cc hello_tcc.c\\narm-tcc\\narm-wince-tcc\\narm64-osx-tcc\\narm64-tcc\\narm64-win32-tcc\\nc67-tcc\\ni386-tcc\\ni386-win32-tcc\\nriscv64-tcc\\ntcc\\nx86_64-osx-tcc\\nx86_64-tcc\\nx86_64-win32-tcc\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:35.218631Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:35.656723Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Uti6Hq4BpTZjFrSk5ejXsN", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \"^cc:\" -A40 Makefile | head -60", "description": "Read the cc recipe"}, "message": "Read the cc recipe", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \\\"^cc:\\\" -A40 Makefile | head -60\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:35.912799Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:35.912848Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Uti6Hq4BpTZjFrSk5ejXsN", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:37.343306Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:38.140766Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01PLDt2VEdNYkwWvZQfbZZpT", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \"^cc\\b\\|^cc \" Makefile; n=$(grep -n \"^cc\" Makefile | head -1 | cut -d: -f1); sed -n \"${n},$((n+30))p\" Makefile; ls tcc_guest.ld", "description": "Find the cc make target"}, "message": "Find the cc make target", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \\\"^cc\\\\b\\\\|^cc \\\" Makefile; n=$(grep -n \\\"^cc\\\" Makefile | head -1 | cut -d: -f1); sed -n \\\"${n},$((n+30))p\\\" Makefile; ls tcc_guest.ld\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:38.368542Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:38.368593Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01PLDt2VEdNYkwWvZQfbZZpT", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"334:cc tcc: $(TCC_TOOL) $(DISK_IMG) tcc_guest.ld\\ncc tcc: $(TCC_TOOL) $(DISK_IMG) tcc_guest.ld\\n\\t@if [ ! -x \\\"$(TCC_I386)\\\" ] && ! command -v i386-tcc >/dev/null 2>&1; then \\\\\\n\\t    echo \\\"\\\"; \\\\\\n\\t    echo \\\"ERROR: i386-tcc not found.\\\"; \\\\\\n\\t    echo \\\"Run  make setup-tcc  to download and build TCC automatically,\\\"; \\\\\\n\\t    echo \\\"then retry:  make cc SRC=$(SRC)\\\"; \\\\\\n\\t    echo \\\"\\\"; \\\\\\n\\t    exit 1; \\\\\\n\\tfi\\n\\t@# Redundant safety net -- the real guard is the parse-time $(error)\\n\\t@# above, which now stops SRC-less invocations before prerequisites\\n\\t@# are even considered. This is just defense in depth in case SRC\\n\\t@# somehow ends up set-but-blank by the time the recipe runs.\\nifndef SRC\\n\\t@echo \\\"Usage: make cc SRC=<file.c> [OUT=<name>]\\\"\\n\\t@echo \\\"  Compiles SRC to a 32-bit ELF and writes it to $(DISK_IMG).\\\"\\n\\t@exit 1\\nendif\\n\\t@echo \\\">>> Compiling $(SRC) \u2192 $(or $(OUT),$(basename $(notdir $(SRC)))) in $(DISK_IMG) ...\\\"\\n\\t@# Guest programs commonly #include \\\"bochs_drivers.h\\\" (see compile.md).\\n\\t@# The in-kernel `cc` command resolves #include by reading straight\\n\\t@# from disk.img, so make sure a real copy is always there -- via\\n\\t@# mtools mcopy (same tool/overwrite-flag combo tcc_glue.cpp uses for\\n\\t@# the compiled ELF itself), which writes proper VFAT long-filename\\n\\t@# entries for a 13-character base name like this one. Overwrite (-o)\\n\\t@# so re-running `make cc` after editing bochs_drivers.h picks up the\\n\\t@# change; ignore failure (`|| true`) so a disk.img built before this\\n\\t@# existed, or one where the file is already current, never blocks a\\n\\t@# compile over this best-effort sync step.\\n\\t@MTOOLS_SKIP_CHECK=1 mcopy -o -i \\\"$(DISK_IMG)\\\" \\\"bochs_drivers.h\\\" \\\"::bochs_drivers.h\\\" 2>/dev/null || true\\n\\t@# compositor.h (the GUI widget library) #includes both of these,\\ntcc_guest.ld\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"334:cc tcc: $(TCC_TOOL) $(DISK_IMG) tcc_guest.ld\\ncc tcc: $(TCC_TOOL) $(DISK_IMG) tcc_guest.ld\\n\\t@if [ ! -x \\\"$(TCC_I386)\\\" ] && ! command -v i386-tcc >/dev/null 2>&1; then \\\\\\n\\t    echo \\\"\\\"; \\\\\\n\\t    echo \\\"ERROR: i386-tcc not found.\\\"; \\\\\\n\\t    echo \\\"Run  make setup-tcc  to download and build TCC automatically,\\\"; \\\\\\n\\t    echo \\\"then retry:  make cc SRC=$(SRC)\\\"; \\\\\\n\\t    echo \\\"\\\"; \\\\\\n\\t    exit 1; \\\\\\n\\tfi\\n\\t@# Redundant safety net -- the real guard is the parse-time $(error)\\n\\t@# above, which now stops SRC-less invocations before prerequisites\\n\\t@# are even considered. This is just defense in depth in case SRC\\n\\t@# somehow ends up set-but-blank by the time the recipe runs.\\nifndef SRC\\n\\t@echo \\\"Usage: make cc SRC=<file.c> [OUT=<name>]\\\"\\n\\t@echo \\\"  Compiles SRC to a 32-bit ELF and writes it to $(DISK_IMG).\\\"\\n\\t@exit 1\\nendif\\n\\t@echo \\\">>> Compiling $(SRC) \u2192 $(or $(OUT),$(basename $(notdir $(SRC)))) in $(DISK_IMG) ...\\\"\\n\\t@# Guest programs commonly #include \\\"bochs_drivers.h\\\" (see compile.md).\\n\\t@# The in-kernel `cc` command resolves #include by reading straight\\n\\t@# from disk.img, so make sure a real copy is always there -- via\\n\\t@# mtools mcopy (same tool/overwrite-flag combo tcc_glue.cpp uses for\\n\\t@# the compiled ELF itself), which writes proper VFAT long-filename\\n\\t@# entries for a 13-character base name like this one. Overwrite (-o)\\n\\t@# so re-running `make cc` after editing bochs_drivers.h picks up the\\n\\t@# change; ignore failure (`|| true`) so a disk.img built before this\\n\\t@# existed, or one where the file is already current, never blocks a\\n\\t@# compile over this best-effort sync step.\\n\\t@MTOOLS_SKIP_CHECK=1 mcopy -o -i \\\"$(DISK_IMG)\\\" \\\"bochs_drivers.h\\\" \\\"::bochs_drivers.h\\\" 2>/dev/null || true\\n\\t@# compositor.h (the GUI widget library) #includes both of these,\\ntcc_guest.ld\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:40.269028Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:41.612723Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_016P5UGwh2wTATYRwLfjs1hE", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && T=tcc-local/bin/i386-tcc; $T -nostdinc -nostdlib -I. -c editf.c -o /tmp/ed/tcc_editf.o 2>&1 | head; ls -la /tmp/ed/tcc_editf.o && nm /tmp/ed/tcc_editf.o | grep -i \" U \\|undefined\"; ld -m elf_i386 -T tcc_guest.ld /tmp/ed/tcc_editf.o -o /tmp/ed/editf.elf 2>&1 | head", "description": "Compile and link editf.c with TCC; list undefined symbols"}, "message": "Compile and link editf.c with TCC; list undefined symbols", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && T=tcc-local/bin/i386-tcc; $T -nostdinc -nostdlib -I. -c editf.c -o /tmp/ed/tcc_editf.o 2>&1 | head; ls -la /tmp/ed/tcc_editf.o && nm /tmp/ed/tcc_editf.o | grep -i \\\" U \\\\|undefined\\\"; ld -m elf_i386 -T tcc_guest.ld /tmp/ed/tcc_editf.o -o /tmp/ed/editf.elf 2>&1 | head\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:41.816387Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:41.816448Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_016P5UGwh2wTATYRwLfjs1hE", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 22148 Oct 15 08:29 /tmp/ed/tcc_editf.o\\nld: warning: /tmp/ed/editf.elf has a LOAD segment with RWX permissions\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 22148 Oct 15 08:29 /tmp/ed/tcc_editf.o\\nld: warning: /tmp/ed/editf.elf has a LOAD segment with RWX permissions\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:43.705691Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:48.595204Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Verifying the build links without undefined symbols."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:48.595361Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:48.595613Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Testing editf's key-handling by emulating keystrokes and reading output"}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:48.595674Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:48.674204Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01HApp6XEQysZjGXtFejTLaR", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \"inb(\\|outb(\\|outl(\\|inl(\\|static inline.*(void)\\|0xE[0-9A-F]\\|0xF[0-9A-F]\" drivers.h | head -60; cat tcc_guest.ld | head -30; pip install unicorn --break-system-packages -q 2>&1 | tail -1", "description": "Read guest port protocol; install unicorn"}, "message": "Read guest port protocol; install unicorn", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \\\"inb(\\\\|outb(\\\\|outl(\\\\|inl(\\\\|static inline.*(void)\\\\|0xE[0-9A-F]\\\\|0xF[0-9A-F]\\\" drivers.h | head -60; cat tcc_guest.ld | head -30; pip install unicorn --break-system-packages -q 2>&1 | tail -1\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:54.902968Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:54.903056Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01HApp6XEQysZjGXtFejTLaR", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"5:static inline void outb(unsigned short port, unsigned char val)\\n10:static inline unsigned char inb(unsigned short port)\\n17:static inline void kputc(char c)   { outb(0xE9, (unsigned char)c); }\\n18:static inline void kexit(int code) { outb(0xE8, (unsigned char)code); }\\n26: * on port 0xE7 until a non-zero byte is queued. Safe: the kernel yields\\n29:static inline char getch(void)\\n32:    while ((c = inb(0xE7)) == 0) { /* wait for a keystroke */ }\\n46: * 0xE0-0xE3, followed by a command byte to 0xE4. That final outb()\\n64:#define DISK_PORT_ADDR0 0xE0\\n65:#define DISK_PORT_ADDR1 0xE1\\n66:#define DISK_PORT_ADDR2 0xE2\\n67:#define DISK_PORT_ADDR3 0xE3\\n68:#define DISK_PORT_CMD   0xE4\\n89:    outb(DISK_PORT_ADDR0, (unsigned char)(addr & 0xFF));\\n90:    outb(DISK_PORT_ADDR1, (unsigned char)((addr >> 8)  & 0xFF));\\n91:    outb(DISK_PORT_ADDR2, (unsigned char)((addr >> 16) & 0xFF));\\n92:    outb(DISK_PORT_ADDR3, (unsigned char)((addr >> 24) & 0xFF));\\n93:    outb(DISK_PORT_CMD,   (unsigned char)cmd);\\n232:    outb(NET_PORT_ADDR0, (unsigned char)(addr & 0xFF));\\n233:    outb(NET_PORT_ADDR1, (unsigned char)((addr >> 8)  & 0xFF));\\n234:    outb(NET_PORT_ADDR2, (unsigned char)((addr >> 16) & 0xFF));\\n235:    outb(NET_PORT_ADDR3, (unsigned char)((addr >> 24) & 0xFF));\\n236:    outb(NET_PORT_CMD,   NET_CMD_HTTP_GET);\\n253: *     gfx_set_pixel(10, 10, 0xFF0000);\\n259: * bytes of a buffer's OWN guest address to ports 0xEA-0xED, then a\\n260: * command byte to 0xEE. This call is synchronous \u2014 like the disk\\n269:#define GFX_PORT_ADDR0 0xEA\\n270:#define GFX_PORT_ADDR1 0xEB\\n271:#define GFX_PORT_ADDR2 0xEC\\n272:#define GFX_PORT_ADDR3 0xED\\n273:#define GFX_PORT_CMD   0xEE\\n317:    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR0, (unsigned char)(addr & 0xFF));\\n318:    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR1, (unsigned char)((addr >> 8)  & 0xFF));\\n319:    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR2, (unsigned char)((addr >> 16) & 0xFF));\\n320:    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR3, (unsigned char)((addr >> 24) & 0xFF));\\n321:    outb(GFX_PORT_CMD, GFX_CMD_PRESENT);\\n325:static inline void gfx_present(void) { gfx_present_buf(gfx_framebuffer); }\\n330:static inline void gfx_exit(void) { outb(GFX_PORT_CMD, GFX_CMD_CLEAR); }\\n339:static inline void gfx_yield(void) { outb(GFX_PORT_CMD, GFX_CMD_YIELD); }\\n366: * Protocol: `out al, 0xEF` takes one snapshot of the cursor (and\\n369: * five fields are then read back with individual `in al, 0xF0..0xF4`\\n375:#define INPUT_PORT_POLL     0xEF   /* out: take a cursor snapshot     */\\n376:#define INPUT_PORT_MX_LO    0xF0   /* in:  canvas-local X, low byte   */\\n377:#define INPUT_PORT_MX_HI    0xF1   /* in:  canvas-local X, high byte  */\\n378:#define INPUT_PORT_MY_LO    0xF2   /* in:  canvas-local Y, low byte   */\\n379:#define INPUT_PORT_MY_HI    0xF3   /* in:  canvas-local Y, high byte  */\\n380:#define INPUT_PORT_BUTTONS  0xF4   /* in:  button/focus bitfield      */\\n399:    outb(INPUT_PORT_POLL, 1);\\n400:    unsigned mx = (unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MX_LO) | ((unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MX_HI) << 8);\\n401:    unsigned my = (unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MY_LO) | ((unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MY_HI) << 8);\\n402:    unsigned char btn = inb(INPUT_PORT_BUTTONS);\\n426:/* Non-blocking keystroke peek (port 0xF5, NOT the same as getch's\\n427: * 0xE7). Returns 0 immediately when the queue is empty, or the next\\n429: * 0xE7, this does NOT set wants_input and therefore does NOT cause the\\n433:static inline int key_poll(void) { return (int)(signed char)inb(0xF5); }\\n/* tcc_guest.ld \u2014 linker script for TCC-compiled 32-bit i386 guest ELFs.\\n *\\n * Differences from guest.ld\\n * --------------------------\\n * guest.ld places _start at 0x08001000, which is slab offset 0x000.\\n * That overlaps the zone where inject_slab_tables writes the GDT/IDT/stub\\n * (slab offsets 0x000..0x8ff).  When gcc compiles with -nostartfiles the\\n * gap is filled by the toolchain's crt; TCC emits nothing there, so code\\n * starts at exactly offset 0x000 and gets clobbered.\\n *\\n * This script inserts an explicit 4 KiB NOLOAD gap so the first real\\n * instruction lands at 0x08002000 (slab offset 0x1000), safely after the\\n * stub injection zone.\\n *\\n * Kernel ABI (guest side)\\n * -----------------------\\n * Write a character to the terminal  : outb(0xE9, ch)\\n * Exit with code N (clean)           : outb(0xE8, N & 0xFF)\\n *\\n * Typical minimal _start:\\n *\\n *   static inline void outb(unsigned short port, unsigned char v) {\\n *       __asm__ volatile(\\\"outb %0,%1\\\"::\\\"a\\\"(v),\\\"Nd\\\"(port));\\n *   }\\n *   static void puts_(const char *s) { while (*s) outb(0xE9,*s++); }\\n *\\n *   void _start(void) {\\n *       puts_(\\\"Hello from TCC!\\\\n\\\");\\n *       outb(0xE8, 0);\\n *       for (;;) {}\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"5:static inline void outb(unsigned short port, unsigned char val)\\n10:static inline unsigned char inb(unsigned short port)\\n17:static inline void kputc(char c)   { outb(0xE9, (unsigned char)c); }\\n18:static inline void kexit(int code) { outb(0xE8, (unsigned char)code); }\\n26: * on port 0xE7 until a non-zero byte is queued. Safe: the kernel yields\\n29:static inline char getch(void)\\n32:    while ((c = inb(0xE7)) == 0) { /* wait for a keystroke */ }\\n46: * 0xE0-0xE3, followed by a command byte to 0xE4. That final outb()\\n64:#define DISK_PORT_ADDR0 0xE0\\n65:#define DISK_PORT_ADDR1 0xE1\\n66:#define DISK_PORT_ADDR2 0xE2\\n67:#define DISK_PORT_ADDR3 0xE3\\n68:#define DISK_PORT_CMD   0xE4\\n89:    outb(DISK_PORT_ADDR0, (unsigned char)(addr & 0xFF));\\n90:    outb(DISK_PORT_ADDR1, (unsigned char)((addr >> 8)  & 0xFF));\\n91:    outb(DISK_PORT_ADDR2, (unsigned char)((addr >> 16) & 0xFF));\\n92:    outb(DISK_PORT_ADDR3, (unsigned char)((addr >> 24) & 0xFF));\\n93:    outb(DISK_PORT_CMD,   (unsigned char)cmd);\\n232:    outb(NET_PORT_ADDR0, (unsigned char)(addr & 0xFF));\\n233:    outb(NET_PORT_ADDR1, (unsigned char)((addr >> 8)  & 0xFF));\\n234:    outb(NET_PORT_ADDR2, (unsigned char)((addr >> 16) & 0xFF));\\n235:    outb(NET_PORT_ADDR3, (unsigned char)((addr >> 24) & 0xFF));\\n236:    outb(NET_PORT_CMD,   NET_CMD_HTTP_GET);\\n253: *     gfx_set_pixel(10, 10, 0xFF0000);\\n259: * bytes of a buffer's OWN guest address to ports 0xEA-0xED, then a\\n260: * command byte to 0xEE. This call is synchronous \u2014 like the disk\\n269:#define GFX_PORT_ADDR0 0xEA\\n270:#define GFX_PORT_ADDR1 0xEB\\n271:#define GFX_PORT_ADDR2 0xEC\\n272:#define GFX_PORT_ADDR3 0xED\\n273:#define GFX_PORT_CMD   0xEE\\n317:    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR0, (unsigned char)(addr & 0xFF));\\n318:    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR1, (unsigned char)((addr >> 8)  & 0xFF));\\n319:    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR2, (unsigned char)((addr >> 16) & 0xFF));\\n320:    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR3, (unsigned char)((addr >> 24) & 0xFF));\\n321:    outb(GFX_PORT_CMD, GFX_CMD_PRESENT);\\n325:static inline void gfx_present(void) { gfx_present_buf(gfx_framebuffer); }\\n330:static inline void gfx_exit(void) { outb(GFX_PORT_CMD, GFX_CMD_CLEAR); }\\n339:static inline void gfx_yield(void) { outb(GFX_PORT_CMD, GFX_CMD_YIELD); }\\n366: * Protocol: `out al, 0xEF` takes one snapshot of the cursor (and\\n369: * five fields are then read back with individual `in al, 0xF0..0xF4`\\n375:#define INPUT_PORT_POLL     0xEF   /* out: take a cursor snapshot     */\\n376:#define INPUT_PORT_MX_LO    0xF0   /* in:  canvas-local X, low byte   */\\n377:#define INPUT_PORT_MX_HI    0xF1   /* in:  canvas-local X, high byte  */\\n378:#define INPUT_PORT_MY_LO    0xF2   /* in:  canvas-local Y, low byte   */\\n379:#define INPUT_PORT_MY_HI    0xF3   /* in:  canvas-local Y, high byte  */\\n380:#define INPUT_PORT_BUTTONS  0xF4   /* in:  button/focus bitfield      */\\n399:    outb(INPUT_PORT_POLL, 1);\\n400:    unsigned mx = (unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MX_LO) | ((unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MX_HI) << 8);\\n401:    unsigned my = (unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MY_LO) | ((unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MY_HI) << 8);\\n402:    unsigned char btn = inb(INPUT_PORT_BUTTONS);\\n426:/* Non-blocking keystroke peek (port 0xF5, NOT the same as getch's\\n427: * 0xE7). Returns 0 immediately when the queue is empty, or the next\\n429: * 0xE7, this does NOT set wants_input and therefore does NOT cause the\\n433:static inline int key_poll(void) { return (int)(signed char)inb(0xF5); }\\n/* tcc_guest.ld \u2014 linker script for TCC-compiled 32-bit i386 guest ELFs.\\n *\\n * Differences from guest.ld\\n * --------------------------\\n * guest.ld places _start at 0x08001000, which is slab offset 0x000.\\n * That overlaps the zone where inject_slab_tables writes the GDT/IDT/stub\\n * (slab offsets 0x000..0x8ff).  When gcc compiles with -nostartfiles the\\n * gap is filled by the toolchain's crt; TCC emits nothing there, so code\\n * starts at exactly offset 0x000 and gets clobbered.\\n *\\n * This script inserts an explicit 4 KiB NOLOAD gap so the first real\\n * instruction lands at 0x08002000 (slab offset 0x1000), safely after the\\n * stub injection zone.\\n *\\n * Kernel ABI (guest side)\\n * -----------------------\\n * Write a character to the terminal  : outb(0xE9, ch)\\n * Exit with code N (clean)           : outb(0xE8, N & 0xFF)\\n *\\n * Typical minimal _start:\\n *\\n *   static inline void outb(unsigned short port, unsigned char v) {\\n *       __asm__ volatile(\\\"outb %0,%1\\\"::\\\"a\\\"(v),\\\"Nd\\\"(port));\\n *   }\\n *   static void puts_(const char *s) { while (*s) outb(0xE9,*s++); }\\n *\\n *   void _start(void) {\\n *       puts_(\\\"Hello from TCC!\\\\n\\\");\\n *       outb(0xE8, 0);\\n *       for (;;) {}\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:56.301129Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:59.755995Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Building an emulation harness for ELF binary execution."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:29:59.756087Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:00.019157Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_015SkZMwhpHMF5xsrC4Xj1ju", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && sed -n 274,345p drivers.h; sed -n 383,412p drivers.h", "description": "Read gfx and mouse ABI details"}, "message": "Read gfx and mouse ABI details", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && sed -n 274,345p drivers.h; sed -n 383,412p drivers.h\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:00.225619Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:00.225689Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_015SkZMwhpHMF5xsrC4Xj1ju", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"\\n#define GFX_CMD_PRESENT 1   /* blit the GFX_WIDTH x GFX_HEIGHT buffer  */\\n#define GFX_CMD_CLEAR   2   /* drop the frame, revert window to text   */\\n#define GFX_CMD_YIELD   3   /* give the CPU back; no frame copy/repaint */\\n\\n/* Ready-to-use canvas so most programs never need their own buffer or\\n * bookkeeping \u2014 just draw into this with gfx_set_pixel()/gfx_clear()\\n * and call gfx_present(). */\\nstatic unsigned int gfx_framebuffer[GFX_WIDTH * GFX_HEIGHT];\\n\\nstatic inline void gfx_set_pixel(int x, int y, unsigned int rgb)\\n{\\n    if ((unsigned)x < GFX_WIDTH && (unsigned)y < GFX_HEIGHT)\\n        gfx_framebuffer[y * GFX_WIDTH + x] = rgb;\\n}\\n\\n/* Fill `count` consecutive 32-bit pixels starting at `dst` with `value`.\\n *\\n * ONE `rep stosl` instead of a per-pixel loop. Guest code is interpreted\\n * (Bochs, itself running inside the kernel), so what matters is how many\\n * guest instructions a frame costs: a TCC-compiled \\\"for (...) fb[i] = c;\\\"\\n * burns ~8 instructions per pixel (~500k for a full 320x200 clear), while\\n * REP STOSD is a single instruction the emulator runs as a tight host-side\\n * loop. Every full-frame clear and rectangle fill in comp.h goes through\\n * this. `cld` pins the direction flag so the fill always runs forward. */\\nstatic inline void gfx_fill_u32(unsigned int *dst, unsigned int value, unsigned int count)\\n{\\n    __asm__ __volatile__(\\\"cld\\\\n\\\\trep stosl\\\"\\n                         : \\\"+D\\\"(dst), \\\"+c\\\"(count)\\n                         : \\\"a\\\"(value)\\n                         : \\\"memory\\\", \\\"cc\\\");\\n}\\nstatic inline void gfx_clear(unsigned int rgb)\\n{\\n    gfx_fill_u32(gfx_framebuffer, rgb, GFX_WIDTH * GFX_HEIGHT);\\n}\\n\\n/* Present any GFX_WIDTH x GFX_HEIGHT buffer of your own (e.g. if you'd\\n * rather manage double-buffering yourself instead of using\\n * gfx_framebuffer directly). */\\nstatic inline void gfx_present_buf(const void *buf)\\n{\\n    unsigned int addr = (unsigned int)(unsigned long)buf;\\n    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR0, (unsigned char)(addr & 0xFF));\\n    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR1, (unsigned char)((addr >> 8)  & 0xFF));\\n    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR2, (unsigned char)((addr >> 16) & 0xFF));\\n    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR3, (unsigned char)((addr >> 24) & 0xFF));\\n    outb(GFX_PORT_CMD, GFX_CMD_PRESENT);\\n}\\n\\n/* Blit gfx_framebuffer to this program's terminal window. */\\nstatic inline void gfx_present(void) { gfx_present_buf(gfx_framebuffer); }\\n\\n/* Stop showing the graphics overlay and go back to plain scrolling\\n * text (kputs/kputc) in this window. Not required before exiting \u2014\\n * the kernel drops the frame automatically when the program ends. */\\nstatic inline void gfx_exit(void) { outb(GFX_PORT_CMD, GFX_CMD_CLEAR); }\\n\\n/* Hand the CPU back to the kernel WITHOUT presenting a frame.\\n *\\n * A gfx program must yield at least once per loop (the emulator only\\n * returns to the kernel at yield points), and gfx_present() is the\\n * usual way -- but it also copies the whole 320x200 canvas and makes\\n * the desktop repaint. If nothing on screen changed this pass, call\\n * gfx_yield() instead: same hand-back, none of the cost. */\\nstatic inline void gfx_yield(void) { outb(GFX_PORT_CMD, GFX_CMD_YIELD); }\\n\\n/* \u2500\u2500 mouse ABI: the compositor's shared cursor, relayed into this\\n * program's own gfx canvas \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\n *\\n * The kernel's window manager (the \\\"compositor\\\") owns the ONE system\\n * cursor and ALWAYS handles clicks on titlebars, the close/minimize\\n#define MOUSE_BIT_RIGHT_DOWN    0x02  /* right button currently held          */\\n#define MOUSE_BIT_LEFT_CLICKED  0x04  /* left button went down since last poll (one-shot) */\\n#define MOUSE_BIT_RIGHT_CLICKED 0x08  /* right button went down since last poll (one-shot) */\\n#define MOUSE_BIT_IN_WINDOW     0x10  /* this window is focused AND the cursor is over the canvas */\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    int x, y;                    /* canvas-local pixel coords (same space as gfx_set_pixel); only meaningful when in_window */\\n    unsigned char left_down;\\n    unsigned char right_down;\\n    unsigned char left_clicked;  /* one-shot edge: true only on the poll where the button transitioned down */\\n    unsigned char right_clicked; /* one-shot edge, same as above                                            */\\n    unsigned char in_window;     /* 0 if this window isn't focused, or the cursor is outside the canvas     */\\n} mouse_state_t;\\n\\nstatic inline void mouse_poll(mouse_state_t *ms)\\n{\\n    outb(INPUT_PORT_POLL, 1);\\n    unsigned mx = (unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MX_LO) | ((unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MX_HI) << 8);\\n    unsigned my = (unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MY_LO) | ((unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MY_HI) << 8);\\n    unsigned char btn = inb(INPUT_PORT_BUTTONS);\\n\\n    ms->x            = (int)mx;\\n    ms->y             = (int)my;\\n    ms->left_down     = (btn & MOUSE_BIT_LEFT_DOWN)    ? 1 : 0;\\n    ms->right_down    = (btn & MOUSE_BIT_RIGHT_DOWN)   ? 1 : 0;\\n    ms->left_clicked  = (btn & MOUSE_BIT_LEFT_CLICKED) ? 1 : 0;\\n    ms->right_clicked = (btn & MOUSE_BIT_RIGHT_CLICKED)? 1 : 0;\\n    ms->in_window     = (btn & MOUSE_BIT_IN_WINDOW)    ? 1 : 0;\\n}\\n\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"\\n#define GFX_CMD_PRESENT 1   /* blit the GFX_WIDTH x GFX_HEIGHT buffer  */\\n#define GFX_CMD_CLEAR   2   /* drop the frame, revert window to text   */\\n#define GFX_CMD_YIELD   3   /* give the CPU back; no frame copy/repaint */\\n\\n/* Ready-to-use canvas so most programs never need their own buffer or\\n * bookkeeping \u2014 just draw into this with gfx_set_pixel()/gfx_clear()\\n * and call gfx_present(). */\\nstatic unsigned int gfx_framebuffer[GFX_WIDTH * GFX_HEIGHT];\\n\\nstatic inline void gfx_set_pixel(int x, int y, unsigned int rgb)\\n{\\n    if ((unsigned)x < GFX_WIDTH && (unsigned)y < GFX_HEIGHT)\\n        gfx_framebuffer[y * GFX_WIDTH + x] = rgb;\\n}\\n\\n/* Fill `count` consecutive 32-bit pixels starting at `dst` with `value`.\\n *\\n * ONE `rep stosl` instead of a per-pixel loop. Guest code is interpreted\\n * (Bochs, itself running inside the kernel), so what matters is how many\\n * guest instructions a frame costs: a TCC-compiled \\\"for (...) fb[i] = c;\\\"\\n * burns ~8 instructions per pixel (~500k for a full 320x200 clear), while\\n * REP STOSD is a single instruction the emulator runs as a tight host-side\\n * loop. Every full-frame clear and rectangle fill in comp.h goes through\\n * this. `cld` pins the direction flag so the fill always runs forward. */\\nstatic inline void gfx_fill_u32(unsigned int *dst, unsigned int value, unsigned int count)\\n{\\n    __asm__ __volatile__(\\\"cld\\\\n\\\\trep stosl\\\"\\n                         : \\\"+D\\\"(dst), \\\"+c\\\"(count)\\n                         : \\\"a\\\"(value)\\n                         : \\\"memory\\\", \\\"cc\\\");\\n}\\nstatic inline void gfx_clear(unsigned int rgb)\\n{\\n    gfx_fill_u32(gfx_framebuffer, rgb, GFX_WIDTH * GFX_HEIGHT);\\n}\\n\\n/* Present any GFX_WIDTH x GFX_HEIGHT buffer of your own (e.g. if you'd\\n * rather manage double-buffering yourself instead of using\\n * gfx_framebuffer directly). */\\nstatic inline void gfx_present_buf(const void *buf)\\n{\\n    unsigned int addr = (unsigned int)(unsigned long)buf;\\n    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR0, (unsigned char)(addr & 0xFF));\\n    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR1, (unsigned char)((addr >> 8)  & 0xFF));\\n    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR2, (unsigned char)((addr >> 16) & 0xFF));\\n    outb(GFX_PORT_ADDR3, (unsigned char)((addr >> 24) & 0xFF));\\n    outb(GFX_PORT_CMD, GFX_CMD_PRESENT);\\n}\\n\\n/* Blit gfx_framebuffer to this program's terminal window. */\\nstatic inline void gfx_present(void) { gfx_present_buf(gfx_framebuffer); }\\n\\n/* Stop showing the graphics overlay and go back to plain scrolling\\n * text (kputs/kputc) in this window. Not required before exiting \u2014\\n * the kernel drops the frame automatically when the program ends. */\\nstatic inline void gfx_exit(void) { outb(GFX_PORT_CMD, GFX_CMD_CLEAR); }\\n\\n/* Hand the CPU back to the kernel WITHOUT presenting a frame.\\n *\\n * A gfx program must yield at least once per loop (the emulator only\\n * returns to the kernel at yield points), and gfx_present() is the\\n * usual way -- but it also copies the whole 320x200 canvas and makes\\n * the desktop repaint. If nothing on screen changed this pass, call\\n * gfx_yield() instead: same hand-back, none of the cost. */\\nstatic inline void gfx_yield(void) { outb(GFX_PORT_CMD, GFX_CMD_YIELD); }\\n\\n/* \u2500\u2500 mouse ABI: the compositor's shared cursor, relayed into this\\n * program's own gfx canvas \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\n *\\n * The kernel's window manager (the \\\"compositor\\\") owns the ONE system\\n * cursor and ALWAYS handles clicks on titlebars, the close/minimize\\n#define MOUSE_BIT_RIGHT_DOWN    0x02  /* right button currently held          */\\n#define MOUSE_BIT_LEFT_CLICKED  0x04  /* left button went down since last poll (one-shot) */\\n#define MOUSE_BIT_RIGHT_CLICKED 0x08  /* right button went down since last poll (one-shot) */\\n#define MOUSE_BIT_IN_WINDOW     0x10  /* this window is focused AND the cursor is over the canvas */\\n\\ntypedef struct {\\n    int x, y;                    /* canvas-local pixel coords (same space as gfx_set_pixel); only meaningful when in_window */\\n    unsigned char left_down;\\n    unsigned char right_down;\\n    unsigned char left_clicked;  /* one-shot edge: true only on the poll where the button transitioned down */\\n    unsigned char right_clicked; /* one-shot edge, same as above                                            */\\n    unsigned char in_window;     /* 0 if this window isn't focused, or the cursor is outside the canvas     */\\n} mouse_state_t;\\n\\nstatic inline void mouse_poll(mouse_state_t *ms)\\n{\\n    outb(INPUT_PORT_POLL, 1);\\n    unsigned mx = (unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MX_LO) | ((unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MX_HI) << 8);\\n    unsigned my = (unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MY_LO) | ((unsigned)inb(INPUT_PORT_MY_HI) << 8);\\n    unsigned char btn = inb(INPUT_PORT_BUTTONS);\\n\\n    ms->x            = (int)mx;\\n    ms->y             = (int)my;\\n    ms->left_down     = (btn & MOUSE_BIT_LEFT_DOWN)    ? 1 : 0;\\n    ms->right_down    = (btn & MOUSE_BIT_RIGHT_DOWN)   ? 1 : 0;\\n    ms->left_clicked  = (btn & MOUSE_BIT_LEFT_CLICKED) ? 1 : 0;\\n    ms->right_clicked = (btn & MOUSE_BIT_RIGHT_CLICKED)? 1 : 0;\\n    ms->in_window     = (btn & MOUSE_BIT_IN_WINDOW)    ? 1 : 0;\\n}\\n\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:01.716190Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:04.872991Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Setting up a test harness to inspect graphics dimensions."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:04.873147Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:04.873337Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now the harness: load the ELF in Unicorn, queue every printable ASCII character as a keystroke, run a few frames, then compare editf's internal text buffer to what was typed and look at what it drew.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:04.873345Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:05.757564Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01PuNAPtkFBpHq33VYGH7Ax3", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \"define GFX_WIDTH\\|define GFX_HEIGHT\\|GFX_WIDTH *=\" drivers.h comp.h | head; readelf -lW /tmp/ed/editf.elf | sed -n 1,20p; nm /tmp/ed/editf.elf | grep -i \"s_text\\|_start\\|gfx_framebuffer\\|s_text_len\"", "description": "Check canvas size macros and ELF layout"}, "message": "Check canvas size macros and ELF layout", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \\\"define GFX_WIDTH\\\\|define GFX_HEIGHT\\\\|GFX_WIDTH *=\\\" drivers.h comp.h | head; readelf -lW /tmp/ed/editf.elf | sed -n 1,20p; nm /tmp/ed/editf.elf | grep -i \\\"s_text\\\\|_start\\\\|gfx_framebuffer\\\\|s_text_len\\\"\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:06.075177Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:06.075259Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01PuNAPtkFBpHq33VYGH7Ax3", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"drivers.h:266:#define GFX_WIDTH  320\\ndrivers.h:267:#define GFX_HEIGHT 200\\n\\nElf file type is EXEC (Executable file)\\nEntry point 0x8003055\\nThere is 1 program header, starting at offset 52\\n\\nProgram Headers:\\n  Type           Offset   VirtAddr   PhysAddr   FileSiz MemSiz  Flg Align\\n  LOAD           0x001000 0x08001000 0x08001000 0x03dcf 0x4476c RWE 0x1000\\n\\n Section to Segment mapping:\\n  Segment Sections...\\n   00     .slab_reserved .text .data .bss \\n08003055 T _start\\n08004dd0 b gfx_framebuffer\\n080022f8 t line_start_of\\n080435d0 b s_text\\n080047e0 d s_text_len\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"drivers.h:266:#define GFX_WIDTH  320\\ndrivers.h:267:#define GFX_HEIGHT 200\\n\\nElf file type is EXEC (Executable file)\\nEntry point 0x8003055\\nThere is 1 program header, starting at offset 52\\n\\nProgram Headers:\\n  Type           Offset   VirtAddr   PhysAddr   FileSiz MemSiz  Flg Align\\n  LOAD           0x001000 0x08001000 0x08001000 0x03dcf 0x4476c RWE 0x1000\\n\\n Section to Segment mapping:\\n  Segment Sections...\\n   00     .slab_reserved .text .data .bss \\n08003055 T _start\\n08004dd0 b gfx_framebuffer\\n080022f8 t line_start_of\\n080435d0 b s_text\\n080047e0 d s_text_len\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:07.957345Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:09.975375Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Tracking down which header actually defines the display width."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:09.975443Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:10.394128Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_019jBj6Jm23bAc1NnqaRn1SB", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \"#include\" comp.h; ls *.h | tr '\\n' ' '; grep -n \"GFX_WIDTH\\b\" bochs_drivers.h 2>/dev/null | head -5", "description": "Confirm which driver header comp.h pulls in"}, "message": "Confirm which driver header comp.h pulls in", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \\\"#include\\\" comp.h; ls *.h | tr '\\\\n' ' '; grep -n \\\"GFX_WIDTH\\\\b\\\" bochs_drivers.h 2>/dev/null | head -5\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:10.636194Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:10.636268Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_019jBj6Jm23bAc1NnqaRn1SB", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"14: *     #include \\\"comp.h\\\"\\n45:#include \\\"drivers.h\\\"\\n46:#include \\\"font.h\\\"\\nbochs_drivers.h comp.h driver.h drivers.h fixes.h font.h gui_render.h gui_scene.h instrument_stub.h matrix_array.h tcc_glue.h test_module.h 245: * A guest program can paint a GFX_WIDTH x GFX_HEIGHT canvas of 32-bit\\n266:#define GFX_WIDTH  320\\n275:#define GFX_CMD_PRESENT 1   /* blit the GFX_WIDTH x GFX_HEIGHT buffer  */\\n282:static unsigned int gfx_framebuffer[GFX_WIDTH * GFX_HEIGHT];\\n286:    if ((unsigned)x < GFX_WIDTH && (unsigned)y < GFX_HEIGHT)\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"14: *     #include \\\"comp.h\\\"\\n45:#include \\\"drivers.h\\\"\\n46:#include \\\"font.h\\\"\\nbochs_drivers.h comp.h driver.h drivers.h fixes.h font.h gui_render.h gui_scene.h instrument_stub.h matrix_array.h tcc_glue.h test_module.h 245: * A guest program can paint a GFX_WIDTH x GFX_HEIGHT canvas of 32-bit\\n266:#define GFX_WIDTH  320\\n275:#define GFX_CMD_PRESENT 1   /* blit the GFX_WIDTH x GFX_HEIGHT buffer  */\\n282:static unsigned int gfx_framebuffer[GFX_WIDTH * GFX_HEIGHT];\\n286:    if ((unsigned)x < GFX_WIDTH && (unsigned)y < GFX_HEIGHT)\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:12.163957Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:21.100004Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01VmKvDXLySiKNrHnQzqmHhH", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "pip list 2>/dev/null | grep -i unicorn; cat > /tmp/ed/run.py <<'EOF'\nimport struct, subprocess, sys\nfrom unicorn import *\nfrom unicorn.x86_const import *\nELF=sys.argv[1]\nW,H=320,200\nsyms={}\nfor l in subprocess.check_output(['nm',ELF]).decode().split('\\n'):\n    p=l.split()\n    if len(p)==3: syms[p[2]]=int(p[0],16)\ndata=open(ELF,'rb').read()\n# single LOAD segment\noff,va,fsz,msz=struct.unpack_from('<IIII',data,52+4)[0:4] if False else (0,0,0,0)\nph=struct.unpack_from('<IIIIIIII',data,52)\n_,off,va,_,fsz,msz,_,_=ph\nmu=Uc(UC_ARCH_X86,UC_MODE_32)\nBASE=0x08000000; SIZE=0x01000000\nmu.mem_map(BASE,SIZE)\nmu.mem_write(va,data[off:off+fsz])\nSTACK=BASE+SIZE-0x1000\nmu.reg_write(UC_X86_REG_ESP,STACK)\ntyped = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv)>2 else ''\nkeys=[ord(c) for c in typed]\nstate={'addr':[0,0,0,0],'frames':0,'last':None,'mouse':[0]*8,'polls':0}\ndef hook_in(uc,port,size,ud):\n    if port==0xF5:\n        if state['frames']>=2 and keys:   # let frame 0/1 render first\n            k=keys.pop(0); return k&0xFF\n        return 0\n    return 0\ndef hook_out(uc,port,size,val,ud):\n    if 0xEA<=port<=0xED: state['addr'][port-0xEA]=val&0xFF\n    elif port==0xEE:\n        if val==1:\n            a=sum(b<<(8*i) for i,b in enumerate(state['addr']))\n            state['last']=bytes(uc.mem_read(a,W*H*4)); state['frames']+=1\n            state['pending']=len(keys)\n            if state['frames']>=400 or (state['frames']>6 and not keys): uc.emu_stop()\n        elif val==3: state['frames']+=0\n    elif port==0xE8: uc.emu_stop()\ndef hook_insn(uc,port,size,ud):  # IN\n    v=hook_in(uc,port,size,ud); uc.reg_write(UC_X86_REG_EAX,v)\nmu.hook_add(UC_HOOK_INSN,lambda uc,port,size,ud: uc.reg_write(UC_X86_REG_EAX,hook_in(uc,port,size,ud)),None,1,0,UC_X86_INS_IN)\nmu.hook_add(UC_HOOK_INSN,hook_out,None,1,0,UC_X86_INS_OUT)\ntry: mu.emu_start(0x08003055,0,timeout=60*UC_SECOND_SCALE,count=200_000_000)\nexcept UcError as e: print(\"emu error\",e, hex(mu.reg_read(UC_X86_REG_EIP)))\nln=struct.unpack('<i',bytes(mu.mem_read(syms['s_text_len'],4)))[0]\ntxt=bytes(mu.mem_read(syms['s_text'],ln)).decode('latin1')\nprint(\"frames\",state['frames'],\"len\",ln)\nprint(\"typed :\",repr(typed))\nprint(\"buffer:\",repr(txt))\nprint(\"MATCH\" if txt==typed else \"MISMATCH\")\n# ascii render of the text area\nfb=state['last']\nif fb:\n    px=struct.unpack('<%dI'%(W*H),fb)\n    for y in range(58,58+22):\n        print(''.join('#' if px[y*W+x]==px[(58+5)*W+(W-3)] else ('.' ) for x in range(4,4+8*40)) if False else '')\n    import json; json.dump(list(px),open('/tmp/ed/fb.json','w'))\nEOF\ncd /tmp/ed && python3 run.py editf.elf \"abc\" 2>&1 | tail -8", "description": "Write Unicorn harness and smoke-test with letters"}, "message": "Write Unicorn harness and smoke-test with letters", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"pip list 2>/dev/null | grep -i unicorn; cat > /tmp/ed/run.py <<'EOF'\\nimport struct, subprocess, sys\\nfrom unicorn import *\\nfrom unicorn.x86_const import *\\nELF=sys.argv[1]\\nW,H=320,200\\nsyms={}\\nfor l in subprocess.check_output(['nm',ELF]).decode().split('\\\\n'):\\n    p=l.split()\\n    if len(p)==3: syms[p[2]]=int(p[0],16)\\ndata=open(ELF,'rb').read()\\n# single LOAD segment\\noff,va,fsz,msz=struct.unpack_from('<IIII',data,52+4)[0:4] if False else (0,0,0,0)\\nph=struct.unpack_from('<IIIIIIII',data,52)\\n_,off,va,_,fsz,msz,_,_=ph\\nmu=Uc(UC_ARCH_X86,UC_MODE_32)\\nBASE=0x08000000; SIZE=0x01000000\\nmu.mem_map(BASE,SIZE)\\nmu.mem_write(va,data[off:off+fsz])\\nSTACK=BASE+SIZE-0x1000\\nmu.reg_write(UC_X86_REG_ESP,STACK)\\ntyped = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv)>2 else ''\\nkeys=[ord(c) for c in typed]\\nstate={'addr':[0,0,0,0],'frames':0,'last':None,'mouse':[0]*8,'polls':0}\\ndef hook_in(uc,port,size,ud):\\n    if port==0xF5:\\n        if state['frames']>=2 and keys:   # let frame 0/1 render first\\n            k=keys.pop(0); return k&0xFF\\n        return 0\\n    return 0\\ndef hook_out(uc,port,size,val,ud):\\n    if 0xEA<=port<=0xED: state['addr'][port-0xEA]=val&0xFF\\n    elif port==0xEE:\\n        if val==1:\\n            a=sum(b<<(8*i) for i,b in enumerate(state['addr']))\\n            state['last']=bytes(uc.mem_read(a,W*H*4)); state['frames']+=1\\n            state['pending']=len(keys)\\n            if state['frames']>=400 or (state['frames']>6 and not keys): uc.emu_stop()\\n        elif val==3: state['frames']+=0\\n    elif port==0xE8: uc.emu_stop()\\ndef hook_insn(uc,port,size,ud):  # IN\\n    v=hook_in(uc,port,size,ud); uc.reg_write(UC_X86_REG_EAX,v)\\nmu.hook_add(UC_HOOK_INSN,lambda uc,port,size,ud: uc.reg_write(UC_X86_REG_EAX,hook_in(uc,port,size,ud)),None,1,0,UC_X86_INS_IN)\\nmu.hook_add(UC_HOOK_INSN,hook_out,None,1,0,UC_X86_INS_OUT)\\ntry: mu.emu_start(0x08003055,0,timeout=60*UC_SECOND_SCALE,count=200_000_000)\\nexcept UcError as e: print(\\\"emu error\\\",e, hex(mu.reg_read(UC_X86_REG_EIP)))\\nln=struct.unpack('<i',bytes(mu.mem_read(syms['s_text_len'],4)))[0]\\ntxt=bytes(mu.mem_read(syms['s_text'],ln)).decode('latin1')\\nprint(\\\"frames\\\",state['frames'],\\\"len\\\",ln)\\nprint(\\\"typed :\\\",repr(typed))\\nprint(\\\"buffer:\\\",repr(txt))\\nprint(\\\"MATCH\\\" if txt==typed else \\\"MISMATCH\\\")\\n# ascii render of the text area\\nfb=state['last']\\nif fb:\\n    px=struct.unpack('<%dI'%(W*H),fb)\\n    for y in range(58,58+22):\\n        print(''.join('#' if px[y*W+x]==px[(58+5)*W+(W-3)] else ('.' ) for x in range(4,4+8*40)) if False else '')\\n    import json; json.dump(list(px),open('/tmp/ed/fb.json','w'))\\nEOF\\ncd /tmp/ed && python3 run.py editf.elf \\\"abc\\\" 2>&1 | tail -8\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:22.804986Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:22.805046Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01VmKvDXLySiKNrHnQzqmHhH", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"unicorn                    2.1.4\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"unicorn                    2.1.4\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:25.699101Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:25.880020Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Wx5nA4dZXZmZjhFTVqn9tZ", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/ed && python3 run.py editf.elf \"abc\" 2>&1 | grep -v '^$' | head", "description": "Rerun smoke test showing real output"}, "message": "Rerun smoke test showing real output", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /tmp/ed && python3 run.py editf.elf \\\"abc\\\" 2>&1 | grep -v '^$' | head\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:26.373918Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:26.373973Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Wx5nA4dZXZmZjhFTVqn9tZ", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"Exception ignored on converting result of ctypes callback function: <function UcIntel.hook_add.<locals>.__hook_insn_in.<locals>.__hook_insn_in_cb at 0x7f822f7ba2a0>\\nTraceback (most recent call last):\\n  File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/unicorn/unicorn_py3/unicorn.py\\\", line 763, in emu_start\\n    status = uclib.uc_emu_start(self._uch, begin, until, timeout, count)\\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\nTypeError: 'NoneType' object cannot be interpreted as an integer\\nException ignored on converting result of ctypes callback function: <function UcIntel.hook_add.<locals>.__hook_insn_in.<locals>.__hook_insn_in_cb at 0x7f822f7ba2a0>\\nTraceback (most recent call last):\\n  File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/unicorn/unicorn_py3/unicorn.py\\\", line 763, in emu_start\\n    status = uclib.uc_emu_start(self._uch, begin, until, timeout, count)\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"Exception ignored on converting result of ctypes callback function: <function UcIntel.hook_add.<locals>.__hook_insn_in.<locals>.__hook_insn_in_cb at 0x7f822f7ba2a0>\\nTraceback (most recent call last):\\n  File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/unicorn/unicorn_py3/unicorn.py\\\", line 763, in emu_start\\n    status = uclib.uc_emu_start(self._uch, begin, until, timeout, count)\\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\\nTypeError: 'NoneType' object cannot be interpreted as an integer\\nException ignored on converting result of ctypes callback function: <function UcIntel.hook_add.<locals>.__hook_insn_in.<locals>.__hook_insn_in_cb at 0x7f822f7ba2a0>\\nTraceback (most recent call last):\\n  File \\\"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/unicorn/unicorn_py3/unicorn.py\\\", line 763, in emu_start\\n    status = uclib.uc_emu_start(self._uch, begin, until, timeout, count)\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:29.198000Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:29.198178Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "In Unicorn 2.x the IN hook has to return the value itself rather than writing EAX. Fixing the harness.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:29.198181Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:30.546792Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01DScHt1tMS4fpKKBxY2UbXQ", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/ed && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open('run.py').read()\ns=s.replace(\"mu.hook_add(UC_HOOK_INSN,lambda uc,port,size,ud: uc.reg_write(UC_X86_REG_EAX,hook_in(uc,port,size,ud)),None,1,0,UC_X86_INS_IN)\",\n\"mu.hook_add(UC_HOOK_INSN,lambda uc,port,size,ud: hook_in(uc,port,size,ud),None,1,0,UC_X86_INS_IN)\")\nopen('run.py','w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 run.py editf.elf \"abc\" 2>&1 | grep -v '^$' | head", "description": "Fix IN hook and rerun"}, "message": "Fix IN hook and rerun", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /tmp/ed && python3 - <<'EOF'\\ns=open('run.py').read()\\ns=s.replace(\\\"mu.hook_add(UC_HOOK_INSN,lambda uc,port,size,ud: uc.reg_write(UC_X86_REG_EAX,hook_in(uc,port,size,ud)),None,1,0,UC_X86_INS_IN)\\\",\\n\\\"mu.hook_add(UC_HOOK_INSN,lambda uc,port,size,ud: hook_in(uc,port,size,ud),None,1,0,UC_X86_INS_IN)\\\")\\nopen('run.py','w').write(s)\\nEOF\\npython3 run.py editf.elf \\\"abc\\\" 2>&1 | grep -v '^$' | head\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:31.068162Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:31.068210Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01DScHt1tMS4fpKKBxY2UbXQ", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"frames 7 len 3\\ntyped : 'abc'\\nbuffer: 'abc'\\nMATCH\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"frames 7 len 3\\ntyped : 'abc'\\nbuffer: 'abc'\\nMATCH\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:33.027717Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:33.027978Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "The harness works: editf runs, takes keys and keeps them in its buffer. Now every printable symbol:", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:33.027988Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:33.864922Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01UT8mmJet7UfPqEcoMWW8e1", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/ed && python3 run.py editf.elf '!\"#$%&'\"'\"'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\]^_`{|}~ 0123456789ABCxyz' 2>&1 | grep -v '^$' | head", "description": "Type all printable symbols into editf"}, "message": "Type all printable symbols into editf", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /tmp/ed && python3 run.py editf.elf '!\\\"#$%&'\\\"'\\\"'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\\\]^_`{|}~ 0123456789ABCxyz' 2>&1 | grep -v '^$' | head\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:34.350569Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:34.350624Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01UT8mmJet7UfPqEcoMWW8e1", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"frames 7 len 49\\ntyped : '!\\\"#$%&\\\\'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\\\\\\\]^_`{|}~ 0123456789ABCxyz'\\nbuffer: '!\\\"#$%&\\\\'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\\\\\\\]^_`{|}~ 0123456789ABCxyz'\\nMATCH\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"frames 7 len 49\\ntyped : '!\\\"#$%&\\\\'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\\\\\\\]^_`{|}~ 0123456789ABCxyz'\\nbuffer: '!\\\"#$%&\\\\'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\\\\\\\]^_`{|}~ 0123456789ABCxyz'\\nMATCH\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:35.825032Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:38.650988Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Debugging display output by comparing rendered glyphs to the font."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:38.651125Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:38.651441Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "The buffer holds every symbol exactly as typed, so input is fine. Next I'll check what's drawn on screen by comparing each rendered character cell against the font bitmap.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:38.651450Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:43.092582Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01EJEqMoJrQswPs5ArNK3Awh", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/ed && cat > chk.py <<'EOF'\nimport json,re,sys\npx=json.load(open('fb.json')); W,H=320,200\ns=open('/home/claude/OS/font.h').read()\nrows=re.findall(r'((?:0x[0-9A-Fa-f]{2},){8})',s)\nfont=[[int(x,16) for x in r.strip(',').split(',')] for r in rows]\ntyped=sys.argv[1]\n# editor area: EDIT_X=4, EDIT_Y=58; text origin (8,60); view scrolled\nbg=px[(58+3)*W+6]\nvis_cols=(W-8-8)//8\nstart=max(0,len(typed)+0-vis_cols+0)\n# find scroll by trying offsets\ndef block(col):\n    x0=8+col*8; y0=60\n    return [[1 if px[(y0+r)*W+x0+c]!=bg else 0 for c in range(8)] for r in range(8)]\nbest=None\nfor sc in range(0,len(typed)+1):\n    bad=0;n=0\n    for col in range(min(vis_cols,len(typed)-sc)):\n        ch=typed[sc+col]; g=font[ord(ch)]\n        exp=[[1 if g[r]&(0x80>>c) else 0 for c in range(8)] for r in range(8)]\n        got=block(col)\n        n+=1\n        if exp!=got: bad+=1\n    if n and (best is None or bad<best[0]): best=(bad,sc,n)\nprint(\"scroll_col\",best[1],\"cells\",best[2],\"mismatched cells\",best[0])\nbad=best[0]\nsc=best[1]\nfor col in range(min(vis_cols,len(typed)-sc)):\n    ch=typed[sc+col]; g=font[ord(ch)]\n    exp=[[1 if g[r]&(0x80>>c) else 0 for c in range(8)] for r in range(8)]\n    if exp!=block(col): print(\"BAD glyph\",repr(ch))\nEOF\nT='!\"#$%&'\"'\"'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\]^_`{|}~ 0123456789ABCxyz'; python3 chk.py \"$T\"", "description": "Verify rendered glyphs against font bitmaps"}, "message": "Verify rendered glyphs against font bitmaps", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /tmp/ed && cat > chk.py <<'EOF'\\nimport json,re,sys\\npx=json.load(open('fb.json')); W,H=320,200\\ns=open('/home/claude/OS/font.h').read()\\nrows=re.findall(r'((?:0x[0-9A-Fa-f]{2},){8})',s)\\nfont=[[int(x,16) for x in r.strip(',').split(',')] for r in rows]\\ntyped=sys.argv[1]\\n# editor area: EDIT_X=4, EDIT_Y=58; text origin (8,60); view scrolled\\nbg=px[(58+3)*W+6]\\nvis_cols=(W-8-8)//8\\nstart=max(0,len(typed)+0-vis_cols+0)\\n# find scroll by trying offsets\\ndef block(col):\\n    x0=8+col*8; y0=60\\n    return [[1 if px[(y0+r)*W+x0+c]!=bg else 0 for c in range(8)] for r in range(8)]\\nbest=None\\nfor sc in range(0,len(typed)+1):\\n    bad=0;n=0\\n    for col in range(min(vis_cols,len(typed)-sc)):\\n        ch=typed[sc+col]; g=font[ord(ch)]\\n        exp=[[1 if g[r]&(0x80>>c) else 0 for c in range(8)] for r in range(8)]\\n        got=block(col)\\n        n+=1\\n        if exp!=got: bad+=1\\n    if n and (best is None or bad<best[0]): best=(bad,sc,n)\\nprint(\\\"scroll_col\\\",best[1],\\\"cells\\\",best[2],\\\"mismatched cells\\\",best[0])\\nbad=best[0]\\nsc=best[1]\\nfor col in range(min(vis_cols,len(typed)-sc)):\\n    ch=typed[sc+col]; g=font[ord(ch)]\\n    exp=[[1 if g[r]&(0x80>>c) else 0 for c in range(8)] for r in range(8)]\\n    if exp!=block(col): print(\\\"BAD glyph\\\",repr(ch))\\nEOF\\nT='!\\\"#$%&'\\\"'\\\"'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\\\]^_`{|}~ 0123456789ABCxyz'; python3 chk.py \\\"$T\\\"\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:43.339941Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:43.339991Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01EJEqMoJrQswPs5ArNK3Awh", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"scroll_col 12 cells 37 mismatched cells 0\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"scroll_col 12 cells 37 mismatched cells 0\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:46.649694Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:46.649850Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Rendering matches the font exactly for the visible part (the first 12 characters had scrolled off). I'll run the full symbol set in a chunk that fits on screen, so every glyph is checked.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:46.649855Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:47.513530Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_013nbn7HHpm93iLwncjigKdj", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/ed && T='!\"#$%&'\"'\"'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\]^_`{|}~'; python3 run.py editf.elf \"$T\" | grep -E \"MATCH|MISMATCH\"; python3 chk.py \"$T\"; T2='0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz'; python3 run.py editf.elf \"$T2\" | grep -E \"MATCH|MISMATCH\"; python3 chk.py \"$T2\"", "description": "Full symbol and alnum render verification"}, "message": "Full symbol and alnum render verification", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /tmp/ed && T='!\\\"#$%&'\\\"'\\\"'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\\\]^_`{|}~'; python3 run.py editf.elf \\\"$T\\\" | grep -E \\\"MATCH|MISMATCH\\\"; python3 chk.py \\\"$T\\\"; T2='0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz'; python3 run.py editf.elf \\\"$T2\\\" | grep -E \\\"MATCH|MISMATCH\\\"; python3 chk.py \\\"$T2\\\"\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:48.469052Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:48.469101Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_013nbn7HHpm93iLwncjigKdj", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"MATCH\\nscroll_col 0 cells 32 mismatched cells 0\\nMATCH\\nscroll_col 0 cells 36 mismatched cells 0\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"MATCH\\nscroll_col 0 cells 32 mismatched cells 0\\nMATCH\\nscroll_col 0 cells 36 mismatched cells 0\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:30:49.852251Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:31:03.518030Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Tracking down a symbol-handling bug in the kernel."}, {"summary": "Simulating scancode-to-character decoding against the standard layout."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:31:03.518185Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:31:03.518340Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "editf handles all symbols correctly end-to-end. The last unchecked link is the kernel's scancode decoder with real Shift sequences, so I'll read the top of that loop and test it.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:31:03.518347Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:31:03.781656Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_013duXVNy7Puowizqg5setgC", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && sed -n 396,436p kernel_parts/05_io_wait_ps2_funcs.h", "description": "Read start of the scancode decode loop"}, "message": "Read start of the scancode decode loop", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && sed -n 396,436p kernel_parts/05_io_wait_ps2_funcs.h\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:31:04.069194Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:31:04.069250Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_013duXVNy7Puowizqg5setgC", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"    if (init_ps2_mouse_legacy()) {\\n        universal_mouse_state.initialized = true;\\n        wm.print_to_focused(\\\"PS/2 mouse initialized (legacy method).\\\\n\\\");\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n    \\n    wm.print_to_focused(\\\"ERROR: Mouse initialization failed.\\\\n\\\");\\n    return false;\\n}\\nvoid poll_input_universal() {\\n    // NOTE: deliberately does NOT clear any \\\"current key\\\" state. Decoded keys go\\n    // into the g_kbd_q ring (see 03_input_ps2_mouse.h) and the main loop pops\\n    // them; this function runs many times per pass (inside the guest slice too)\\n    // and must never discard what an earlier call produced.\\n    // Non-blocking: only read if data is immediately available\\n\\n    // Up to 64 bytes per call (was 16): after a long guest frame the controller can\\n    // hold a burst, and every byte left behind is another loop pass of latency.\\n    for (int iterations = 0; iterations < 64; iterations++) {\\n        uint8_t status = inb(PS2_STATUS_PORT);\\n        if (!(status & PS2_STATUS_OUTPUT_FULL)) break;\\n\\n        uint8_t data = inb(PS2_DATA_PORT);\\n\\n        if (status & PS2_STATUS_AUX_DATA) {\\n            process_universal_mouse_packet(data);\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n\\n        // \u2500\u2500 keyboard byte (scancode set 1) \u2500\u2500\\n        if (g_kbd_skip > 0) { g_kbd_skip--; continue; }       // inside a Pause sequence\\n        if (data == 0xE1) { g_kbd_skip = 5; continue; }       // Pause/Break: swallow the rest\\n        if (data == 0xE0) { g_kbd_ext = true; continue; }     // extended-key prefix\\n\\n        bool ext = g_kbd_ext;\\n        g_kbd_ext = false;\\n\\n        bool is_press = !(data & 0x80);\\n        uint8_t sc = data & 0x7F;\\n        if (sc == 0 || sc > 0x58) continue;\\n\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"    if (init_ps2_mouse_legacy()) {\\n        universal_mouse_state.initialized = true;\\n        wm.print_to_focused(\\\"PS/2 mouse initialized (legacy method).\\\\n\\\");\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n    \\n    wm.print_to_focused(\\\"ERROR: Mouse initialization failed.\\\\n\\\");\\n    return false;\\n}\\nvoid poll_input_universal() {\\n    // NOTE: deliberately does NOT clear any \\\"current key\\\" state. Decoded keys go\\n    // into the g_kbd_q ring (see 03_input_ps2_mouse.h) and the main loop pops\\n    // them; this function runs many times per pass (inside the guest slice too)\\n    // and must never discard what an earlier call produced.\\n    // Non-blocking: only read if data is immediately available\\n\\n    // Up to 64 bytes per call (was 16): after a long guest frame the controller can\\n    // hold a burst, and every byte left behind is another loop pass of latency.\\n    for (int iterations = 0; iterations < 64; iterations++) {\\n        uint8_t status = inb(PS2_STATUS_PORT);\\n        if (!(status & PS2_STATUS_OUTPUT_FULL)) break;\\n\\n        uint8_t data = inb(PS2_DATA_PORT);\\n\\n        if (status & PS2_STATUS_AUX_DATA) {\\n            process_universal_mouse_packet(data);\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n\\n        // \u2500\u2500 keyboard byte (scancode set 1) \u2500\u2500\\n        if (g_kbd_skip > 0) { g_kbd_skip--; continue; }       // inside a Pause sequence\\n        if (data == 0xE1) { g_kbd_skip = 5; continue; }       // Pause/Break: swallow the rest\\n        if (data == 0xE0) { g_kbd_ext = true; continue; }     // extended-key prefix\\n\\n        bool ext = g_kbd_ext;\\n        g_kbd_ext = false;\\n\\n        bool is_press = !(data & 0x80);\\n        uint8_t sc = data & 0x7F;\\n        if (sc == 0 || sc > 0x58) continue;\\n\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:31:05.527624Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:31:17.341908Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Debugging keyboard scan code handling for a tracked bug."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:31:17.342023Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:31:17.356360Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I couldn't find anything wrong with symbols in editf, so I haven't changed anything. I need to know what you're actually seeing.\n\nI compiled `editf.c` with the repo's own TCC, linked it with `tcc_guest.ld`, and ran the resulting ELF in a CPU emulator. I fed it every printable ASCII symbol through the same key port (0xF5) the OS uses. The result was clean on three counts:\n- **Linking:** there are no undefined symbols, so the ELF links cleanly.\n- **Typing:** all 32 symbols (`!\"#$%&'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\]^_` and so on) landed in editf's text buffer exactly as typed.\n- **Drawing:** every symbol cell on screen matched the `font.h` bitmap pixel for pixel.\n\nI also checked the kernel side by reading it. The PS/2 shift and unshifted scancode tables match a standard US layout, and every printable ASCII character can be produced. The built-in terminal editor and the static-scene editor (`gui_render.h`) both accept all printable characters too.\n\nThat leaves a few things I can't rule out from here:\n- **Keyboard layout:** the kernel decoder is US-only. On a non-US layout, symbols like `\"`, `@`, `#`, `~` and `\\|` can come out in the wrong place, and the extra ISO key next to left Shift (scancode 0x56) produces nothing.\n- **The live PS/2 path under QEMU or Bochs:** I can't boot the OS here, so I couldn't check real shift press/release timing.\n- **Which editor you mean:** editf the ELF, the terminal's `edit` command, or the static GUI scene.\n\nWhich symbols look wrong, and what appears instead (nothing, a different character, or garbled pixels)? Also, which keyboard layout are you using and how are you running it (QEMU, Bochs, real hardware)? With that I can fix the exact key.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-15T08:31:17.475445Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-15T08:31:17.475445Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a13eaa-e837-70eb-a6bd-2ec0b632b5c3"}, {"uuid": "01a13eb2-49e2-7c92-b837-3ad7d2a7148e", "text": "garbled pixels", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:33:59.494047Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:33:59.494047Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "garbled pixels", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-15T08:33:59.494246Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-15T08:33:59.494246Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a13eaa-e837-7786-a759-88b198f7601b"}, {"uuid": "01a13eb2-49e2-7f79-b846-2e4d59cf7eef", "text": "Garbled pixels is a rendering problem. My emulator test showed editf draws correct glyphs into its canvas, so the garbling has to come after that, in how the kernel blits the canvas. I also touched `draw_char`, so I'll check my change first.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nMy `draw_char` change uses the same indexing as the original, so it isn't the cause. Next, the code that blits the guest canvas into the window.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nNow I'll test the C code itself on the host with the real editf frame: first exactness at integer ratios (it must be identical to a plain pixel copy), then the same 630\u00d7385 view as before.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nTwo of those files, `i386-libtcc-kern.a` and `tcc-mob.tar.gz`, were tracked in the repo, and I just deleted them. I'm restoring them from git and rebuilding the patch and zip.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI found the cause of the garbled symbols and fixed it, but I haven't seen it on a real boot. The fix is in `OS-patched-source.zip` and `gui-input-perf.patch`; the zip is the full tree with all four changes and the same 132 files as before.\n\n**Cause.** editf draws into a fixed 320\u00d7200 canvas, and the kernel stretched that to fill the window with nearest-neighbour sampling. At non-integer window sizes, some source pixels got 1 output pixel and others got 2, so 1\u20132 pixel strokes came out uneven. Symbols are mostly thin strokes, so they suffered most. I reproduced it with a real editf frame at a typical window size. The `!` dot was 2 rows tall at the top and 1 row at the bottom, and the `$` bars alternated between 9 and 10 pixels wide. At 500\u00d7300 the same glyphs came out with stroke widths from 1 to 9 pixels.\n\n**Fix.** The new `gfx_blit_scaled()` in `02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h` replaces that loop in `09_terminal_window.h`. It samples at pixel centres and sharpens the blend, so strokes get an even width at any window size.\n- **Integer scales:** at 1\u00d7, 2\u00d7, 3\u00d7 and 4\u00d7 the output is byte-identical to a plain pixel copy, so text stays perfectly crisp when the window happens to fit.\n- **Other sizes:** edges are about one output pixel soft but evenly so, and I confirmed this in the rendered output.\n- **Cost:** about 0.84 ms per frame at 630\u00d7385 in a native host test, with copy fast paths for most pixels. The mouse mapping is unaffected.\n- **Other programs:** every program that draws into a canvas goes through this path, so graphics programs get the same fix.\n\n**Not verified.** I haven't booted the OS, so I haven't seen the real on-screen result, and the kernel only parses with the same 5 typedef errors as before. Boot it, open editf, resize the window a few times and check the symbols. If any still look rough, tell me the window size and which symbols.\n\n**Earlier typing result.** The earlier typing test is unchanged: all symbols reached editf's buffer correctly, so the problem was only in how it was drawn.\n\n**Cleanup.** I built the repo's TCC inside the tree to run that test. In tidying up I briefly deleted `i386-libtcc-kern.a` and `tcc-mob.tar.gz`, which are tracked files, and then restored them from git. The zip contains both, and the only changes in the patch are the four source files.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:33:59.493860Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:02.913471Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Debugging why the display garbles despite correct rendering."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:02.913498Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:04.117273Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Garbled pixels is a rendering problem. My emulator test showed editf draws correct glyphs into its canvas, so the garbling has to come after that, in how the kernel blits the canvas. I also touched `draw_char`, so I'll check my change first.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:04.117297Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:05.129574Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01KzveZLEjbtNKXza4zCHuiT", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS/kernel_parts && grep -n \"put_pixel_back\" 02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h | head -3; n=$(grep -n \"void put_pixel_back\\|inline void put_pixel_back\" 02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h | head -1 | cut -d: -f1); sed -n \"$((n-12)),$((n+12))p\" 02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h; grep -n \"backbuffer *=\\|backbuffer;\\|\\*backbuffer\\|pitch\" 02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h | head -20", "description": "Check backbuffer stride and put_pixel_back"}, "message": "Check backbuffer stride and put_pixel_back", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS/kernel_parts && grep -n \\\"put_pixel_back\\\" 02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h | head -3; n=$(grep -n \\\"void put_pixel_back\\\\|inline void put_pixel_back\\\" 02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h | head -1 | cut -d: -f1); sed -n \\\"$((n-12)),$((n+12))p\\\" 02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h; grep -n \\\"backbuffer *=\\\\|backbuffer;\\\\|\\\\*backbuffer\\\\|pitch\\\" 02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h | head -20\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:06.759431Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:06.759474Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01KzveZLEjbtNKXza4zCHuiT", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"418:void put_pixel_back(int x, int y, uint32_t color) {\\n448:            if (glyph[i] & (0x80 >> j)) put_pixel_back(x + j, y + i, color);\\n    void fill_rect(int x, int y, int w, int h, const Color& color) {\\n        uint32_t col = convert_color(color);\\n        for (int dy = 0; dy < h; dy++) {\\n            for (int dx = 0; dx < w; dx++) {\\n                put_pixel(x + dx, y + dy, col);\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n};\\n\\nstatic GraphicsDriver g_gfx;\\n\\nvoid put_pixel_back(int x, int y, uint32_t color) {\\n    if (backbuffer && x >= 0 && x < (int)fb_info.width && y >= 0 && y < (int)fb_info.height) {\\n        backbuffer[y * fb_info.width + x] = color;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nvoid draw_char(char c, int x, int y, uint32_t color) {\\n    if ((unsigned char)c > 127 || !backbuffer) return;\\n    const uint8_t* glyph = font + (int)c * 8;\\n    const int W = (int)fb_info.width, H = (int)fb_info.height;\\n    if (x + 8 <= 0 || y + 8 <= 0 || x >= W || y >= H) return;   // fully off-screen\\n    if (x >= 0 && y >= 0 && x + 8 <= W && y + 8 <= H) {\\n        // Fast path: glyph fully on-screen -> no per-pixel bounds checks.\\n24:    uint32_t framebuffer_pitch, framebuffer_width, framebuffer_height;\\n54:static uint32_t* backbuffer = backbuffer_storage;\\n114:// Call once, after fb_info.ptr/pitch/height are finalized and before the\\n142:    uint64_t fb_bytes = (uint64_t)fb_info.pitch * (uint64_t)fb_info.height;\\n343:        uint32_t* target = backbuffer;\\n501:            uint32_t* row = &fb_info.ptr[(y0 + yy) * (fb_info.pitch / 4) + x0];\\n518:        uint32_t* row = &fb_info.ptr[y * (fb_info.pitch / 4)];\\n606:        uint32_t* row = &fb_info.ptr[(y0 + yy) * (fb_info.pitch / 4) + x0];\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"418:void put_pixel_back(int x, int y, uint32_t color) {\\n448:            if (glyph[i] & (0x80 >> j)) put_pixel_back(x + j, y + i, color);\\n    void fill_rect(int x, int y, int w, int h, const Color& color) {\\n        uint32_t col = convert_color(color);\\n        for (int dy = 0; dy < h; dy++) {\\n            for (int dx = 0; dx < w; dx++) {\\n                put_pixel(x + dx, y + dy, col);\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n};\\n\\nstatic GraphicsDriver g_gfx;\\n\\nvoid put_pixel_back(int x, int y, uint32_t color) {\\n    if (backbuffer && x >= 0 && x < (int)fb_info.width && y >= 0 && y < (int)fb_info.height) {\\n        backbuffer[y * fb_info.width + x] = color;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nvoid draw_char(char c, int x, int y, uint32_t color) {\\n    if ((unsigned char)c > 127 || !backbuffer) return;\\n    const uint8_t* glyph = font + (int)c * 8;\\n    const int W = (int)fb_info.width, H = (int)fb_info.height;\\n    if (x + 8 <= 0 || y + 8 <= 0 || x >= W || y >= H) return;   // fully off-screen\\n    if (x >= 0 && y >= 0 && x + 8 <= W && y + 8 <= H) {\\n        // Fast path: glyph fully on-screen -> no per-pixel bounds checks.\\n24:    uint32_t framebuffer_pitch, framebuffer_width, framebuffer_height;\\n54:static uint32_t* backbuffer = backbuffer_storage;\\n114:// Call once, after fb_info.ptr/pitch/height are finalized and before the\\n142:    uint64_t fb_bytes = (uint64_t)fb_info.pitch * (uint64_t)fb_info.height;\\n343:        uint32_t* target = backbuffer;\\n501:            uint32_t* row = &fb_info.ptr[(y0 + yy) * (fb_info.pitch / 4) + x0];\\n518:        uint32_t* row = &fb_info.ptr[y * (fb_info.pitch / 4)];\\n606:        uint32_t* row = &fb_info.ptr[(y0 + yy) * (fb_info.pitch / 4) + x0];\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:11.371550Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:13.848561Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Debugging a pixel color mismatch in the canvas blit."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:13.848635Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:13.848780Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "My `draw_char` change uses the same indexing as the original, so it isn't the cause. Next, the code that blits the guest canvas into the window.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:13.848786Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:14.013875Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Xkpw47QpnqnZUdcfGfMfFM", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS/kernel_parts && sed -n 2258,2400p 09_terminal_window.h", "description": "Read guest canvas blit/scale code"}, "message": "Read guest canvas blit/scale code", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS/kernel_parts && sed -n 2258,2400p 09_terminal_window.h\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:14.230095Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:14.230183Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Xkpw47QpnqnZUdcfGfMfFM", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"    // goes back to returning false and this window reverts to\\n    // ordinary text on the very next draw().\\n    const uint32_t* gfx_px = nullptr;\\n    int gfx_w = 0, gfx_h = 0;\\n    bool gfx_active = false;\\n    if (sgui) gfx_active = sgui_frame(&gfx_px, &gfx_w, &gfx_h);\\n    else gfx_active = (captured_elf_slot >= 0) &&\\n        bochs_gfx_get_frame(captured_elf_slot, &gfx_px, &gfx_w, &gfx_h);\\n\\n    if (gfx_active) {\\n        int content_top = y + 30 + overlay_dy;\\n        int avail_w = w - 10;\\n        int avail_h = (y + h) - content_top - 5;\\n        if (avail_w < 0) avail_w = 0;\\n        if (avail_h < 0) avail_h = 0;\\n\\n        // Stretch the guest's GFX_WIDTH x GFX_HEIGHT canvas to fill the\\n        // ENTIRE content area, edge to edge -- a program using graphics\\n        // mode should occupy the full terminal window, not a small\\n        // fixed-size box floating in the middle of it. This also means\\n        // the canvas grows/shrinks automatically as the window is\\n        // resized (see Window::is_in_resize_grip() / WindowManager's\\n        // resize handling), since avail_w/avail_h are recomputed from\\n        // the window's current w/h every frame.\\n        //\\n        // Nearest-neighbor scaling via 16.16 fixed-point steps -- this\\n        // kernel is freestanding (no guaranteed FPU/SSE init), so no\\n        // floating point here.\\n        int draw_w = avail_w;\\n        int draw_h = avail_h;\\n        int off_x  = x + 5;\\n        int off_y  = content_top;\\n\\n        if (draw_w > 0 && draw_h > 0 && gfx_w > 0 && gfx_h > 0) {\\n            uint32_t step_x = ((uint32_t)gfx_w << 16) / (uint32_t)draw_w;\\n            uint32_t step_y = ((uint32_t)gfx_h << 16) / (uint32_t)draw_h;\\n\\n            uint32_t src_y_fp = 0;\\n            for (int row = 0; row < draw_h; row++) {\\n                int sy = (int)(src_y_fp >> 16);\\n                if (sy >= gfx_h) sy = gfx_h - 1;\\n                const uint32_t* src_row = gfx_px + sy * gfx_w;\\n                int py = off_y + row;\\n\\n                uint32_t src_x_fp = 0;\\n                for (int col = 0; col < draw_w; col++) {\\n                    int sx = (int)(src_x_fp >> 16);\\n                    if (sx >= gfx_w) sx = gfx_w - 1;\\n                    put_pixel_back(off_x + col, py, src_row[sx]);\\n                    src_x_fp += step_x;\\n                }\\n                src_y_fp += step_y;\\n            }\\n        } else {\\n            draw_w = 0;\\n            draw_h = 0;\\n        }\\n\\n        // Publish this frame's canvas rect (and the guest's own source\\n        // canvas size) for the mouse ABI (see gfx_hit_test() above) \u2014\\n        // kernel_gfx_mouse_poll() reads these every time a guest polls,\\n        // so they must stay in lockstep with where/how the canvas was\\n        // actually just blitted on screen.\\n        gfx_rect_x = off_x;\\n        gfx_rect_y = off_y;\\n        gfx_rect_w = draw_w;\\n        gfx_rect_h = draw_h;\\n        gfx_src_w  = gfx_w;\\n        gfx_src_h  = gfx_h;\\n        gfx_rect_valid = (draw_w > 0 && draw_h > 0);\\n    } else {\\n        gfx_rect_valid = false;\\n    // How many 10px text lines actually fit between the content-area\\n    // top (y + 30 + overlay_dy) and the window's bottom border (y + h).\\n    // The old code hard-coded `i < 38`, which \u2014 combined with the test\\n    // overlay shifting text down by overlay_dy \u2014 drew lines past the\\n    // bottom border (\\\"overhanging by one\\\"). Compute the real capacity.\\n    int content_top = 30 + overlay_dy;\\n    int visible_rows = (h - content_top) / 10;\\n    if (visible_rows < 1) visible_rows = 1;\\n\\n    // \u2500\u2500 Auto text rewrap \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\n    // buffer[] lines were already word-wrapped once, at whatever width\\n    // the window happened to be when each line was printed/typed (see\\n    // term_cols_cont()/push_wrapped_text() above). That's fine until\\n    // the window is resized afterward \u2014 a line wrapped for a wide\\n    // window then just runs past the border of a narrower one. Rather\\n    // than only fixing that going forward, re-flow EVERY visible\\n    // buffer[] line against the window's width right here, every\\n    // frame, so already-printed text reflows live as the resize grip\\n    // is dragged, the same way the guest gfx canvas above rescales\\n    // live. (One inherent limit: buffer[] only stores rendered text,\\n    // not which line breaks were real newlines vs. earlier wrap\\n    // points, so widening the window back out can't rejoin a line\\n    // that a previous, narrower wrap already split across rows \u2014\\n    // it can only re-split, never re-merge.)\\n    int chars_per_line = (w - 10) / 8;\\n    if (chars_per_line < 8) chars_per_line = 8;\\n    if (chars_per_line > 118) chars_per_line = 118; // matches term_cols_cont()'s cap\\n\\n    // Walk backward from the newest logical line to find where the\\n    // last `visible_rows` WRAPPED screen rows begin: which logical\\n    // line to start from, and how many of ITS wrapped chunks to skip\\n    // (since only the tail of that line's wrap may be on screen).\\n    int start_line = 0, skip_chunks = 0;\\n    {\\n        int collected = 0;\\n        bool found = false;\\n        for (int i = line_count - 1; i >= 0; --i) {\\n            int len = (int)strlen(buffer[i]);\\n            int chunks = (len == 0) ? 1 : (len + chars_per_line - 1) / chars_per_line;\\n            if (collected + chunks >= visible_rows) {\\n                start_line   = i;\\n                skip_chunks  = (collected + chunks) - visible_rows;\\n                found = true;\\n                break;\\n            }\\n            collected += chunks;\\n        }\\n        if (!found) { start_line = 0; skip_chunks = 0; }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Render forward from start_line, splitting each logical line into\\n    // chars_per_line-wide chunks, skipping skip_chunks of the first\\n    // line, until the content area is full.\\n    int screen_row = 0;\\n    for (int i = start_line; i < line_count && screen_row < visible_rows; ++i) {\\n        const char* line = buffer[i];\\n        int len = (int)strlen(line);\\n        int chunks = (len == 0) ? 1 : (len + chars_per_line - 1) / chars_per_line;\\n        int chunk_start = (i == start_line) ? skip_chunks : 0;\\n        for (int c = chunk_start; c < chunks && screen_row < visible_rows; ++c) {\\n            char seg[TERM_WIDTH];\\n            int off  = c * chars_per_line;\\n            int slen = len - off;\\n            if (slen > chars_per_line) slen = chars_per_line;\\n            if (slen < 0) slen = 0;\\n            for (int k = 0; k < slen; ++k) seg[k] = line[off + k];\\n            seg[slen] = '\\\\0';\\n            draw_string(seg, x + 5, y + content_top + screen_row * 10,\\n                        ColorPalette::TEXT_WHITE);\\n            screen_row++;\\n        }\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"    // goes back to returning false and this window reverts to\\n    // ordinary text on the very next draw().\\n    const uint32_t* gfx_px = nullptr;\\n    int gfx_w = 0, gfx_h = 0;\\n    bool gfx_active = false;\\n    if (sgui) gfx_active = sgui_frame(&gfx_px, &gfx_w, &gfx_h);\\n    else gfx_active = (captured_elf_slot >= 0) &&\\n        bochs_gfx_get_frame(captured_elf_slot, &gfx_px, &gfx_w, &gfx_h);\\n\\n    if (gfx_active) {\\n        int content_top = y + 30 + overlay_dy;\\n        int avail_w = w - 10;\\n        int avail_h = (y + h) - content_top - 5;\\n        if (avail_w < 0) avail_w = 0;\\n        if (avail_h < 0) avail_h = 0;\\n\\n        // Stretch the guest's GFX_WIDTH x GFX_HEIGHT canvas to fill the\\n        // ENTIRE content area, edge to edge -- a program using graphics\\n        // mode should occupy the full terminal window, not a small\\n        // fixed-size box floating in the middle of it. This also means\\n        // the canvas grows/shrinks automatically as the window is\\n        // resized (see Window::is_in_resize_grip() / WindowManager's\\n        // resize handling), since avail_w/avail_h are recomputed from\\n        // the window's current w/h every frame.\\n        //\\n        // Nearest-neighbor scaling via 16.16 fixed-point steps -- this\\n        // kernel is freestanding (no guaranteed FPU/SSE init), so no\\n        // floating point here.\\n        int draw_w = avail_w;\\n        int draw_h = avail_h;\\n        int off_x  = x + 5;\\n        int off_y  = content_top;\\n\\n        if (draw_w > 0 && draw_h > 0 && gfx_w > 0 && gfx_h > 0) {\\n            uint32_t step_x = ((uint32_t)gfx_w << 16) / (uint32_t)draw_w;\\n            uint32_t step_y = ((uint32_t)gfx_h << 16) / (uint32_t)draw_h;\\n\\n            uint32_t src_y_fp = 0;\\n            for (int row = 0; row < draw_h; row++) {\\n                int sy = (int)(src_y_fp >> 16);\\n                if (sy >= gfx_h) sy = gfx_h - 1;\\n                const uint32_t* src_row = gfx_px + sy * gfx_w;\\n                int py = off_y + row;\\n\\n                uint32_t src_x_fp = 0;\\n                for (int col = 0; col < draw_w; col++) {\\n                    int sx = (int)(src_x_fp >> 16);\\n                    if (sx >= gfx_w) sx = gfx_w - 1;\\n                    put_pixel_back(off_x + col, py, src_row[sx]);\\n                    src_x_fp += step_x;\\n                }\\n                src_y_fp += step_y;\\n            }\\n        } else {\\n            draw_w = 0;\\n            draw_h = 0;\\n        }\\n\\n        // Publish this frame's canvas rect (and the guest's own source\\n        // canvas size) for the mouse ABI (see gfx_hit_test() above) \u2014\\n        // kernel_gfx_mouse_poll() reads these every time a guest polls,\\n        // so they must stay in lockstep with where/how the canvas was\\n        // actually just blitted on screen.\\n        gfx_rect_x = off_x;\\n        gfx_rect_y = off_y;\\n        gfx_rect_w = draw_w;\\n        gfx_rect_h = draw_h;\\n        gfx_src_w  = gfx_w;\\n        gfx_src_h  = gfx_h;\\n        gfx_rect_valid = (draw_w > 0 && draw_h > 0);\\n    } else {\\n        gfx_rect_valid = false;\\n    // How many 10px text lines actually fit between the content-area\\n    // top (y + 30 + overlay_dy) and the window's bottom border (y + h).\\n    // The old code hard-coded `i < 38`, which \u2014 combined with the test\\n    // overlay shifting text down by overlay_dy \u2014 drew lines past the\\n    // bottom border (\\\"overhanging by one\\\"). Compute the real capacity.\\n    int content_top = 30 + overlay_dy;\\n    int visible_rows = (h - content_top) / 10;\\n    if (visible_rows < 1) visible_rows = 1;\\n\\n    // \u2500\u2500 Auto text rewrap \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\n    // buffer[] lines were already word-wrapped once, at whatever width\\n    // the window happened to be when each line was printed/typed (see\\n    // term_cols_cont()/push_wrapped_text() above). That's fine until\\n    // the window is resized afterward \u2014 a line wrapped for a wide\\n    // window then just runs past the border of a narrower one. Rather\\n    // than only fixing that going forward, re-flow EVERY visible\\n    // buffer[] line against the window's width right here, every\\n    // frame, so already-printed text reflows live as the resize grip\\n    // is dragged, the same way the guest gfx canvas above rescales\\n    // live. (One inherent limit: buffer[] only stores rendered text,\\n    // not which line breaks were real newlines vs. earlier wrap\\n    // points, so widening the window back out can't rejoin a line\\n    // that a previous, narrower wrap already split across rows \u2014\\n    // it can only re-split, never re-merge.)\\n    int chars_per_line = (w - 10) / 8;\\n    if (chars_per_line < 8) chars_per_line = 8;\\n    if (chars_per_line > 118) chars_per_line = 118; // matches term_cols_cont()'s cap\\n\\n    // Walk backward from the newest logical line to find where the\\n    // last `visible_rows` WRAPPED screen rows begin: which logical\\n    // line to start from, and how many of ITS wrapped chunks to skip\\n    // (since only the tail of that line's wrap may be on screen).\\n    int start_line = 0, skip_chunks = 0;\\n    {\\n        int collected = 0;\\n        bool found = false;\\n        for (int i = line_count - 1; i >= 0; --i) {\\n            int len = (int)strlen(buffer[i]);\\n            int chunks = (len == 0) ? 1 : (len + chars_per_line - 1) / chars_per_line;\\n            if (collected + chunks >= visible_rows) {\\n                start_line   = i;\\n                skip_chunks  = (collected + chunks) - visible_rows;\\n                found = true;\\n                break;\\n            }\\n            collected += chunks;\\n        }\\n        if (!found) { start_line = 0; skip_chunks = 0; }\\n    }\\n\\n    // Render forward from start_line, splitting each logical line into\\n    // chars_per_line-wide chunks, skipping skip_chunks of the first\\n    // line, until the content area is full.\\n    int screen_row = 0;\\n    for (int i = start_line; i < line_count && screen_row < visible_rows; ++i) {\\n        const char* line = buffer[i];\\n        int len = (int)strlen(line);\\n        int chunks = (len == 0) ? 1 : (len + chars_per_line - 1) / chars_per_line;\\n        int chunk_start = (i == start_line) ? skip_chunks : 0;\\n        for (int c = chunk_start; c < chunks && screen_row < visible_rows; ++c) {\\n            char seg[TERM_WIDTH];\\n            int off  = c * chars_per_line;\\n            int slen = len - off;\\n            if (slen > chars_per_line) slen = chars_per_line;\\n            if (slen < 0) slen = 0;\\n            for (int k = 0; k < slen; ++k) seg[k] = line[off + k];\\n            seg[slen] = '\\\\0';\\n            draw_string(seg, x + 5, y + content_top + screen_row * 10,\\n                        ColorPalette::TEXT_WHITE);\\n            screen_row++;\\n        }\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:34:17.761635Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:05.031579Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Diagnosing blurry glyphs from nearest-neighbour canvas scaling."}, {"summary": "Weighing crisp integer scaling against smooth fill tradeoffs."}, {"summary": "Simulating window sizes to confirm garbling and test fixes."}, {"summary": "Designing a sharp-bilinear scaling scheme with fixed-point tables."}, {"summary": "Implementing clipped scaling with per-lane pixel blending in fixed point."}, {"summary": "Deriving fixed-point weights for exact pixel-boundary blending."}, {"summary": "Optimizing row blending with efficient fixed-point pixel lerp."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:05.031659Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:05.031834Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Tracing garbled symbols to nearest-neighbour canvas scaling"}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:05.031877Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:07.616555Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01CyYq1RqLUd5PTpu4xqvgUr", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/ed && python3 run.py editf.elf '!\"#$%&'\"'\"'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\]^_`{|}~' | grep MATCH; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\npx=json.load(open('/tmp/ed/fb.json')); W,H=320,200\nbg=px[61*W+6]\ndef old(dw,dh):\n    sx=(W<<16)//dw; sy=(H<<16)//dh\n    out=[];yf=0\n    for r in range(dh):\n        sy_=min(yf>>16,H-1); row=[];xf=0\n        for c in range(dw):\n            row.append(px[sy_*W+min(xf>>16,W-1)]); xf+=sx\n        out.append(row); yf+=sy\n    return out\n# 630x385 window content (typical ~1.97x / 1.93x)\no=old(630,385)\ndef show(img,x0,y0,w,h,bgc):\n    for y in range(y0,y0+h):\n        print(''.join('#' if img[y][x]!=bgc else '.' for x in range(x0,x0+w)))\nbgc=o[0][0]\n# text starts at canvas (8,60); scale ~1.97 -> (16,116); show symbols \"!\"#$%&\"\nshow(o,14,112,100,22,o[120][12] if False else px[61*W+6])\nEOF", "description": "Reproduce stretched-canvas garbling with real editf frame"}, "message": "Reproduce stretched-canvas garbling with real editf frame", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /tmp/ed && python3 run.py editf.elf '!\\\"#$%&'\\\"'\\\"'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\\\]^_`{|}~' | grep MATCH; python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport json\\npx=json.load(open('/tmp/ed/fb.json')); W,H=320,200\\nbg=px[61*W+6]\\ndef old(dw,dh):\\n    sx=(W<<16)//dw; sy=(H<<16)//dh\\n    out=[];yf=0\\n    for r in range(dh):\\n        sy_=min(yf>>16,H-1); row=[];xf=0\\n        for c in range(dw):\\n            row.append(px[sy_*W+min(xf>>16,W-1)]); xf+=sx\\n        out.append(row); yf+=sy\\n    return out\\n# 630x385 window content (typical ~1.97x / 1.93x)\\no=old(630,385)\\ndef show(img,x0,y0,w,h,bgc):\\n    for y in range(y0,y0+h):\\n        print(''.join('#' if img[y][x]!=bgc else '.' for x in range(x0,x0+w)))\\nbgc=o[0][0]\\n# text starts at canvas (8,60); scale ~1.97 -> (16,116); show symbols \\\"!\\\"#$%&\\\"\\nshow(o,14,112,100,22,o[120][12] if False else px[61*W+6])\\nEOF\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:08.856569Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:08.856606Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01CyYq1RqLUd5PTpu4xqvgUr", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"MATCH\\n####################################################################################################\\n####################################################################################################\\n....................................................................................................\\n....................................................................................................\\n........####........####..####......####..####.......####............................######........#\\n........####........####..####......####..####.......####............................######........#\\n......########......####..####......####..####.....##########....####......####....####..####......#\\n......########......####..####......####..####.....##########....####......####....####..####......#\\n......########....................##############..###............####....####........######......###\\n......########....................##############..###............####....####........######......###\\n........####........................####..####.....########............####........######..####.....\\n........####........................####..####.....########............####........######..####.....\\n........####......................##############.........####........####........####..######.......\\n........####......................##############.........####........####........####..######.......\\n....................................####..####....#########........####....####..####....####.......\\n....................................####..####....#########........####....####..####....####.......\\n........####........................####..####.......####........####......####....######..####.....\\n....................................................................................................\\n....................................................................................................\\n....................................................................................................\\n....................................................................................................\\n....................................................................................................\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"MATCH\\n####################################################################################################\\n####################################################################################################\\n....................................................................................................\\n....................................................................................................\\n........####........####..####......####..####.......####............................######........#\\n........####........####..####......####..####.......####............................######........#\\n......########......####..####......####..####.....##########....####......####....####..####......#\\n......########......####..####......####..####.....##########....####......####....####..####......#\\n......########....................##############..###............####....####........######......###\\n......########....................##############..###............####....####........######......###\\n........####........................####..####.....########............####........######..####.....\\n........####........................####..####.....########............####........######..####.....\\n........####......................##############.........####........####........####..######.......\\n........####......................##############.........####........####........####..######.......\\n....................................####..####....#########........####....####..####....####.......\\n....................................####..####....#########........####....####..####....####.......\\n........####........................####..####.......####........####......####....######..####.....\\n....................................................................................................\\n....................................................................................................\\n....................................................................................................\\n....................................................................................................\\n....................................................................................................\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:10.567068Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:14.611354Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Examining uneven stroke heights in the glyph rendering."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:14.611450Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:14.611638Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Fixing glyph stroke unevenness with a sharp bilinear scaler"}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:14.611676Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:27.535646Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01AhCn444SMSoQgxT9vTL8TY", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS/kernel_parts && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h'\ns=open(p).read()\nhelper='''\n// \u2500\u2500\u2500 Sharp-bilinear canvas scaler \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n// Guest programs draw into a small fixed canvas (e.g. 320x200) that the window\n// stretches to fill itself. Plain nearest-neighbour at a NON-integer ratio\n// (say 1.9x) gives some source pixels 1 output pixel and others 2, so 1-2px\n// strokes -- every symbol: ! \" ' , . : ; - _ | -- come out with uneven widths\n// and look garbled. This samples at pixel centres and sharpens the blend\n// factor by the scale slope, so edges are only ~1 output pixel soft and every\n// stroke gets an even width; exact integer ratios stay perfectly crisp (the\n// blend collapses to a plain copy). Fixed-point only (freestanding kernel).\n#define GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM 4096\nstatic uint16_t g_sc_x0[GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM], g_sc_x1[GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM], g_sc_fx[GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM];\nstatic uint16_t g_sc_y0[GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM], g_sc_y1[GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM], g_sc_fy[GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM];\n\nstatic inline uint32_t gfx_lerp32(uint32_t a, uint32_t b, uint32_t t) {   // t in 0..256\n    uint32_t rb = (((a & 0x00FF00FFu) * (256u - t) + (b & 0x00FF00FFu) * t) >> 8) & 0x00FF00FFu;\n    uint32_t ag = ((((a >> 8) & 0x00FF00FFu) * (256u - t) + ((b >> 8) & 0x00FF00FFu) * t)) & 0xFF00FF00u;\n    return rb | ag;\n}\n\n// Fill out_x0/x1/f[0..n) mapping n output samples onto m source samples.\nstatic void gfx_scale_axis(int n, int m, uint16_t* x0, uint16_t* x1, uint16_t* f) {\n    uint32_t k = (uint32_t)(((uint64_t)n << 8) / (uint64_t)m);   // output px per source px, 8.8\n    if (k < 256) k = 256;                                         // downscale: plain bilinear\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        int64_t u = (int64_t)(((uint64_t)(2 * i + 1) * (uint64_t)m * 128u) / (uint64_t)n) - 128;  // 24.8 source coord\n        int a = (int)(u >> 8);\n        int fr = (int)(u & 255);\n        if (a < 0)       { a = 0;     fr = 0; }\n        if (a >= m - 1)  { a = m - 1; fr = 0; }\n        int sh = 128 + (((fr - 128) * (int)k) >> 8);              // sharpen\n        if (sh < 0) sh = 0; if (sh > 256) sh = 256;\n        int b = a + 1; if (b > m - 1) b = m - 1;\n        if (sh == 0)        { b = a; }\n        else if (sh == 256) { a = b; sh = 0; }\n        x0[i] = (uint16_t)a; x1[i] = (uint16_t)b; f[i] = (uint16_t)sh;\n    }\n}\n\n// Draw src (sw x sh) scaled to the dw x dh rect at (dx,dy) on the backbuffer, clipped to the screen.\nstatic void gfx_blit_scaled(const uint32_t* src, int sw, int sh, int dx, int dy, int dw, int dh) {\n    if (!backbuffer || !src || sw <= 0 || sh <= 0 || dw <= 0 || dh <= 0) return;\n    if (dw > GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM) dw = GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM;\n    if (dh > GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM) dh = GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM;\n    const int SW = (int)fb_info.width, SH = (int)fb_info.height;\n    int c0 = dx < 0 ? -dx : 0,  c1 = (dx + dw > SW) ? SW - dx : dw;\n    int r0 = dy < 0 ? -dy : 0,  r1 = (dy + dh > SH) ? SH - dy : dh;\n    if (c0 >= c1 || r0 >= r1) return;\n\n    gfx_scale_axis(dw, sw, g_sc_x0, g_sc_x1, g_sc_fx);\n    gfx_scale_axis(dh, sh, g_sc_y0, g_sc_y1, g_sc_fy);\n\n    for (int r = r0; r < r1; r++) {\n        const uint32_t* p0 = src + (int)g_sc_y0[r] * sw;\n        const uint32_t* p1 = src + (int)g_sc_y1[r] * sw;\n        uint32_t fy = g_sc_fy[r];\n        uint32_t* out = backbuffer + (uint32_t)(dy + r) * (uint32_t)SW + dx;\n        if (fy == 0) {\n            for (int c = c0; c < c1; c++) {\n                uint32_t fx = g_sc_fx[c];\n                uint32_t a = p0[g_sc_x0[c]];\n                out[c] = fx ? gfx_lerp32(a, p0[g_sc_x1[c]], fx) : a;\n            }\n        } else {\n            for (int c = c0; c < c1; c++) {\n                uint32_t fx = g_sc_fx[c];\n                uint32_t xa = g_sc_x0[c], xb = g_sc_x1[c];\n                uint32_t top = p0[xa], bot = p1[xa];\n                if (fx) { top = gfx_lerp32(top, p0[xb], fx); bot = gfx_lerp32(bot, p1[xb], fx); }\n                out[c] = gfx_lerp32(top, bot, fy);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n'''\nanchor=\"void draw_string(\"\ni=s.index(anchor)\ns=s[:i]+helper.lstrip('\\n')+s[i:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='09_terminal_window.h'\ns=open(p).read()\na=s.index(\"        if (draw_w > 0 && draw_h > 0 && gfx_w > 0 && gfx_h > 0) {\\n            uint32_t step_x\")\nb=s.index(\"        } else {\\n            draw_w = 0;\\n            draw_h = 0;\\n        }\",a)\nnew='''        if (draw_w > 0 && draw_h > 0 && gfx_w > 0 && gfx_h > 0) {\n            // Sharp-bilinear stretch (see gfx_blit_scaled): even stroke widths at any\n            // window size, so thin symbols no longer look garbled.\n            gfx_blit_scaled(gfx_px, gfx_w, gfx_h, off_x, off_y, draw_w, draw_h);\n'''\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat; sed -n '/Sharp-bilinear stretch/,+6p' 09_terminal_window.h", "description": "Add sharp-bilinear scaler and use it for guest canvas blit"}, "message": "Add sharp-bilinear scaler and use it for guest canvas blit", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS/kernel_parts && python3 - <<'EOF'\\np='02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h'\\ns=open(p).read()\\nhelper='''\\n// \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500 Sharp-bilinear canvas scaler \\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\u2500\\n// Guest programs draw into a small fixed canvas (e.g. 320x200) that the window\\n// stretches to fill itself. Plain nearest-neighbour at a NON-integer ratio\\n// (say 1.9x) gives some source pixels 1 output pixel and others 2, so 1-2px\\n// strokes -- every symbol: ! \\\" ' , . : ; - _ | -- come out with uneven widths\\n// and look garbled. This samples at pixel centres and sharpens the blend\\n// factor by the scale slope, so edges are only ~1 output pixel soft and every\\n// stroke gets an even width; exact integer ratios stay perfectly crisp (the\\n// blend collapses to a plain copy). Fixed-point only (freestanding kernel).\\n#define GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM 4096\\nstatic uint16_t g_sc_x0[GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM], g_sc_x1[GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM], g_sc_fx[GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM];\\nstatic uint16_t g_sc_y0[GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM], g_sc_y1[GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM], g_sc_fy[GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM];\\n\\nstatic inline uint32_t gfx_lerp32(uint32_t a, uint32_t b, uint32_t t) {   // t in 0..256\\n    uint32_t rb = (((a & 0x00FF00FFu) * (256u - t) + (b & 0x00FF00FFu) * t) >> 8) & 0x00FF00FFu;\\n    uint32_t ag = ((((a >> 8) & 0x00FF00FFu) * (256u - t) + ((b >> 8) & 0x00FF00FFu) * t)) & 0xFF00FF00u;\\n    return rb | ag;\\n}\\n\\n// Fill out_x0/x1/f[0..n) mapping n output samples onto m source samples.\\nstatic void gfx_scale_axis(int n, int m, uint16_t* x0, uint16_t* x1, uint16_t* f) {\\n    uint32_t k = (uint32_t)(((uint64_t)n << 8) / (uint64_t)m);   // output px per source px, 8.8\\n    if (k < 256) k = 256;                                         // downscale: plain bilinear\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n        int64_t u = (int64_t)(((uint64_t)(2 * i + 1) * (uint64_t)m * 128u) / (uint64_t)n) - 128;  // 24.8 source coord\\n        int a = (int)(u >> 8);\\n        int fr = (int)(u & 255);\\n        if (a < 0)       { a = 0;     fr = 0; }\\n        if (a >= m - 1)  { a = m - 1; fr = 0; }\\n        int sh = 128 + (((fr - 128) * (int)k) >> 8);              // sharpen\\n        if (sh < 0) sh = 0; if (sh > 256) sh = 256;\\n        int b = a + 1; if (b > m - 1) b = m - 1;\\n        if (sh == 0)        { b = a; }\\n        else if (sh == 256) { a = b; sh = 0; }\\n        x0[i] = (uint16_t)a; x1[i] = (uint16_t)b; f[i] = (uint16_t)sh;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// Draw src (sw x sh) scaled to the dw x dh rect at (dx,dy) on the backbuffer, clipped to the screen.\\nstatic void gfx_blit_scaled(const uint32_t* src, int sw, int sh, int dx, int dy, int dw, int dh) {\\n    if (!backbuffer || !src || sw <= 0 || sh <= 0 || dw <= 0 || dh <= 0) return;\\n    if (dw > GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM) dw = GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM;\\n    if (dh > GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM) dh = GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM;\\n    const int SW = (int)fb_info.width, SH = (int)fb_info.height;\\n    int c0 = dx < 0 ? -dx : 0,  c1 = (dx + dw > SW) ? SW - dx : dw;\\n    int r0 = dy < 0 ? -dy : 0,  r1 = (dy + dh > SH) ? SH - dy : dh;\\n    if (c0 >= c1 || r0 >= r1) return;\\n\\n    gfx_scale_axis(dw, sw, g_sc_x0, g_sc_x1, g_sc_fx);\\n    gfx_scale_axis(dh, sh, g_sc_y0, g_sc_y1, g_sc_fy);\\n\\n    for (int r = r0; r < r1; r++) {\\n        const uint32_t* p0 = src + (int)g_sc_y0[r] * sw;\\n        const uint32_t* p1 = src + (int)g_sc_y1[r] * sw;\\n        uint32_t fy = g_sc_fy[r];\\n        uint32_t* out = backbuffer + (uint32_t)(dy + r) * (uint32_t)SW + dx;\\n        if (fy == 0) {\\n            for (int c = c0; c < c1; c++) {\\n                uint32_t fx = g_sc_fx[c];\\n                uint32_t a = p0[g_sc_x0[c]];\\n                out[c] = fx ? gfx_lerp32(a, p0[g_sc_x1[c]], fx) : a;\\n            }\\n        } else {\\n            for (int c = c0; c < c1; c++) {\\n                uint32_t fx = g_sc_fx[c];\\n                uint32_t xa = g_sc_x0[c], xb = g_sc_x1[c];\\n                uint32_t top = p0[xa], bot = p1[xa];\\n                if (fx) { top = gfx_lerp32(top, p0[xb], fx); bot = gfx_lerp32(bot, p1[xb], fx); }\\n                out[c] = gfx_lerp32(top, bot, fy);\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n'''\\nanchor=\\\"void draw_string(\\\"\\ni=s.index(anchor)\\ns=s[:i]+helper.lstrip('\\\\n')+s[i:]\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\n\\np='09_terminal_window.h'\\ns=open(p).read()\\na=s.index(\\\"        if (draw_w > 0 && draw_h > 0 && gfx_w > 0 && gfx_h > 0) {\\\\n            uint32_t step_x\\\")\\nb=s.index(\\\"        } else {\\\\n            draw_w = 0;\\\\n            draw_h = 0;\\\\n        }\\\",a)\\nnew='''        if (draw_w > 0 && draw_h > 0 && gfx_w > 0 && gfx_h > 0) {\\n            // Sharp-bilinear stretch (see gfx_blit_scaled): even stroke widths at any\\n            // window size, so thin symbols no longer look garbled.\\n            gfx_blit_scaled(gfx_px, gfx_w, gfx_h, off_x, off_y, draw_w, draw_h);\\n'''\\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nEOF\\ngit diff --stat; sed -n '/Sharp-bilinear stretch/,+6p' 09_terminal_window.h\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:27.976819Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:27.976867Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01AhCn444SMSoQgxT9vTL8TY", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\" kernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h | 99 +++++++++++++++++++++++--\\n kernel_parts/03_input_ps2_mouse.h               |  8 ++\\n kernel_parts/09_terminal_window.h               | 22 +-----\\n kernel_parts/11_kernel_main.h                   | 10 ++-\\n 4 files changed, 113 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)\\n            // Sharp-bilinear stretch (see gfx_blit_scaled): even stroke widths at any\\n            // window size, so thin symbols no longer look garbled.\\n            gfx_blit_scaled(gfx_px, gfx_w, gfx_h, off_x, off_y, draw_w, draw_h);\\n        } else {\\n            draw_w = 0;\\n            draw_h = 0;\\n        }\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\" kernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h | 99 +++++++++++++++++++++++--\\n kernel_parts/03_input_ps2_mouse.h               |  8 ++\\n kernel_parts/09_terminal_window.h               | 22 +-----\\n kernel_parts/11_kernel_main.h                   | 10 ++-\\n 4 files changed, 113 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)\\n            // Sharp-bilinear stretch (see gfx_blit_scaled): even stroke widths at any\\n            // window size, so thin symbols no longer look garbled.\\n            gfx_blit_scaled(gfx_px, gfx_w, gfx_h, off_x, off_y, draw_w, draw_h);\\n        } else {\\n            draw_w = 0;\\n            draw_h = 0;\\n        }\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:29.588905Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:31.597837Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Setting up a host-side test with a shim for the helpers."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:31.597932Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:31.598072Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Now I'll test the C code itself on the host with the real editf frame: first exactness at integer ratios (it must be identical to a plain pixel copy), then the same 630\u00d7385 view as before.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:31.598074Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:37.814801Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01TditJzgMH6ZSkus3JEfjur", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/ed && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re,json,struct\ns=open('/home/claude/OS/kernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h').read()\na=s.index(\"#define GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM\"); b=s.index(\"void draw_string(\")\nopen('scaler_body.h','w').write(s[a:b])\npx=json.load(open('fb.json'))\nopen('canvas.bin','wb').write(struct.pack('<%dI'%len(px),*px))\nEOF\ncat > t.c <<'EOF'\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\nstruct {uint32_t width,height;} fb_info={1024,768};\nstatic uint32_t* backbuffer;\n#include \"scaler_body.h\"\nint main(int argc,char**argv){\n  int dw=atoi(argv[1]),dh=atoi(argv[2]); const char* out=argv[3];\n  static uint32_t src[320*200]; FILE*f=fopen(\"canvas.bin\",\"rb\"); fread(src,4,320*200,f); fclose(f);\n  backbuffer=calloc(1024*768,4);\n  gfx_blit_scaled(src,320,200,10,5,dw,dh);\n  FILE*o=fopen(out,\"wb\"); fwrite(backbuffer,4,1024*768,o); fclose(o);\n  if(argc>4){ // exactness check vs nearest for integer k\n    int k=dw/320, bad=0;\n    for(int y=0;y<dh;y++)for(int x=0;x<dw;x++) if(backbuffer[(5+y)*1024+10+x]!=src[(y/k)*320+(x/k)]) bad++;\n    printf(\"integer %dx: mismatching px vs pure copy = %d\\n\",k,bad);\n  }\n  return 0;}\nEOF\ngcc -O2 -Wall -o t t.c 2>&1 | head; ./t 640 400 o2.bin x; ./t 960 600 o3.bin x; ./t 630 385 o19.bin; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport struct\nd=open('/tmp/ed/o19.bin','rb').read(); px=struct.unpack('<%dI'%(1024*768),d)\nW=1024\nbgc=px[(5+0)*W+10]   # canvas top-left = bg\ndef lum(p): return ((p>>16)&255)*3+((p>>8)&255)*6+(p&255)\nbgl=lum(bgc)\n# text origin canvas (8,60) -> window (10+8*1.97, 5+60*1.925)\nx0=10+int(8*630/320); y0=5+int(60*385/200)\nfor y in range(y0-2,y0+20):\n    print(''.join(' .:#'[min(3,abs(lum(px[y*W+x])-bgl)*4//(max(1,abs(lum(0xFFFFFF)-bgl))))] if True else '' for x in range(x0-2,x0+98)))\nEOF", "description": "Host-test the C scaler: integer exactness and non-integer render"}, "message": "Host-test the C scaler: integer exactness and non-integer render", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /tmp/ed && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport re,json,struct\\ns=open('/home/claude/OS/kernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h').read()\\na=s.index(\\\"#define GFX_SCALE_MAXDIM\\\"); b=s.index(\\\"void draw_string(\\\")\\nopen('scaler_body.h','w').write(s[a:b])\\npx=json.load(open('fb.json'))\\nopen('canvas.bin','wb').write(struct.pack('<%dI'%len(px),*px))\\nEOF\\ncat > t.c <<'EOF'\\n#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdint.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <string.h>\\nstruct {uint32_t width,height;} fb_info={1024,768};\\nstatic uint32_t* backbuffer;\\n#include \\\"scaler_body.h\\\"\\nint main(int argc,char**argv){\\n  int dw=atoi(argv[1]),dh=atoi(argv[2]); const char* out=argv[3];\\n  static uint32_t src[320*200]; FILE*f=fopen(\\\"canvas.bin\\\",\\\"rb\\\"); fread(src,4,320*200,f); fclose(f);\\n  backbuffer=calloc(1024*768,4);\\n  gfx_blit_scaled(src,320,200,10,5,dw,dh);\\n  FILE*o=fopen(out,\\\"wb\\\"); fwrite(backbuffer,4,1024*768,o); fclose(o);\\n  if(argc>4){ // exactness check vs nearest for integer k\\n    int k=dw/320, bad=0;\\n    for(int y=0;y<dh;y++)for(int x=0;x<dw;x++) if(backbuffer[(5+y)*1024+10+x]!=src[(y/k)*320+(x/k)]) bad++;\\n    printf(\\\"integer %dx: mismatching px vs pure copy = %d\\\\n\\\",k,bad);\\n  }\\n  return 0;}\\nEOF\\ngcc -O2 -Wall -o t t.c 2>&1 | head; ./t 640 400 o2.bin x; ./t 960 600 o3.bin x; ./t 630 385 o19.bin; python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport struct\\nd=open('/tmp/ed/o19.bin','rb').read(); px=struct.unpack('<%dI'%(1024*768),d)\\nW=1024\\nbgc=px[(5+0)*W+10]   # canvas top-left = bg\\ndef lum(p): return ((p>>16)&255)*3+((p>>8)&255)*6+(p&255)\\nbgl=lum(bgc)\\n# text origin canvas (8,60) -> window (10+8*1.97, 5+60*1.925)\\nx0=10+int(8*630/320); y0=5+int(60*385/200)\\nfor y in range(y0-2,y0+20):\\n    print(''.join(' .:#'[min(3,abs(lum(px[y*W+x])-bgl)*4//(max(1,abs(lum(0xFFFFFF)-bgl))))] if True else '' for x in range(x0-2,x0+98)))\\nEOF\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:38.305272Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:35:38.305314Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01TditJzgMH6ZSkus3JEfjur", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"In file included from t.c:7:\\nscaler_body.h: In function 'gfx_scale_axis':\\nscaler_body.h:22:9: warning: this 'if' clause does not guard... [-Wmisleading-indentation]\\n   22 |         if (sh < 0) sh = 0; if (sh > 256) sh = 256;\\n      |         ^~\\nscaler_body.h:22:29: note: ...this statement, but the latter is misleadingly indented as if it were guarded by the 'if'\\n   22 |         if (sh < 0) sh = 0; if (sh > 256) sh = 256;\\n      |                             ^~\\nt.c: In function 'main':\\nt.c:10:66: warning: ignoring return value of 'fread' declared with attribute 'warn_unused_result' [-Wunused-result]\\ninteger 2x: mismatching px vs pure copy = 0\\ninteger 3x: mismatching px vs pure copy = 14839\\n....................................................................................................\\n                                                                                                    \\n         ....       ....  ....      ....  ....        ....                           ......        .\\n        .###:       :###. :###.     :###  ####        ####                           :#####.       :\\n       ::###::.     :###. :###.     :###  ####      ::####:::.    :::.     .:::.   .::#:.:#::      :\\n      .#######:     :###. :###.     :###  ####      #########:   .###:     .###:   :###. :###.     :\\n      .#######:      ...  ....    .:####::####::  ::##........   .###:   .::#:.     .:#::##:.    .:#\\n      .#######:                   :#############  ####           .###:   .###:       :#####.     :##\\n       .:###:.                     .####..####..  ..##::::::      ...  .::#:.      .:####:.::::   ..\\n        .###:                       :###  ####      ########           .###:       :#####. :###.    \\n        .###:                     ::####::####::         .##::       .:##:       .:##: :##:##.      \\n        .###:                     :#############          ###:       .###:       .###. :#####.      \\n              