\\\"tcc-mob\\\\|libtcc-kern\\\" /mnt/user-data/outputs/gui-input-perf.patch; cd /home/claude && rm -f /mnt/user-data/outputs/OS-patched-source.zip && zip -qr /mnt/user-data/outputs/OS-patched-source.zip OS -x \\\"OS/.git/*\\\" && ls -lh /mnt/user-data/outputs/OS-patched-source.zip && unzip -l /mnt/user-data/outputs/OS-patched-source.zip | grep -c \\\"tcc-mob.tar.gz\\\\|i386-libtcc-kern.a\\\"; unzip -l /mnt/user-data/outputs/OS-patched-source.zip | tail -1\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:36:30.730281Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:36:30.730316Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01B1dJ1rV1XuSc1MygG82SrQ", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\" M kernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h\\n M kernel_parts/03_input_ps2_mouse.h\\n M kernel_parts/09_terminal_window.h\\n M kernel_parts/11_kernel_main.h\\n202 /mnt/user-data/outputs/gui-input-perf.patch\\n0\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu 36M Oct 15 08:36 /mnt/user-data/outputs/OS-patched-source.zip\\n2\\n 43914282                     132 files\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\" M kernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h\\n M kernel_parts/03_input_ps2_mouse.h\\n M kernel_parts/09_terminal_window.h\\n M kernel_parts/11_kernel_main.h\\n202 /mnt/user-data/outputs/gui-input-perf.patch\\n0\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude ubuntu 36M Oct 15 08:36 /mnt/user-data/outputs/OS-patched-source.zip\\n2\\n 43914282                     132 files\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:36:32.305226Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:36:32.673529Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_011vHCpo4rFwM2B1d3XcZSYX", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/OS-patched-source.zip", "/mnt/user-data/outputs/gui-input-perf.patch"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/OS-patched-source.zip', '/mnt/user-data/outputs/gui-input-perf.patch']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:36:32.696282Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:36:32.696307Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_011vHCpo4rFwM2B1d3XcZSYX", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/OS-patched-source.zip", "name": "OS-patched-source", "mime_type": "application/zip", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/gui-input-perf.patch", "name": "gui-input-perf", "mime_type": "text/x-diff", "artifact_publishable": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "\n\nThe file cards appear with your reply, and where they sit relative to its text depends on the app the user is reading in; finish the reply with text, and refer to a file by its name, never as above or below."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented 2 files", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:36:41.678456Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T08:36:42.413748Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I found the cause of the garbled symbols and fixed it, but I haven't seen it on a real boot. The fix is in `OS-patched-source.zip` and `gui-input-perf.patch`; the zip is the full tree with all four changes and the same 132 files as before.\n\n**Cause.** editf draws into a fixed 320\u00d7200 canvas, and the kernel stretched that to fill the window with nearest-neighbour sampling. At non-integer window sizes, some source pixels got 1 output pixel and others got 2, so 1\u20132 pixel strokes came out uneven. Symbols are mostly thin strokes, so they suffered most. I reproduced it with a real editf frame at a typical window size. The `!` dot was 2 rows tall at the top and 1 row at the bottom, and the `$` bars alternated between 9 and 10 pixels wide. At 500\u00d7300 the same glyphs came out with stroke widths from 1 to 9 pixels.\n\n**Fix.** The new `gfx_blit_scaled()` in `02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h` replaces that loop in `09_terminal_window.h`. It samples at pixel centres and sharpens the blend, so strokes get an even width at any window size.\n- **Integer scales:** at 1\u00d7, 2\u00d7, 3\u00d7 and 4\u00d7 the output is byte-identical to a plain pixel copy, so text stays perfectly crisp when the window happens to fit.\n- **Other sizes:** edges are about one output pixel soft but evenly so, and I confirmed this in the rendered output.\n- **Cost:** about 0.84 ms per frame at 630\u00d7385 in a native host test, with copy fast paths for most pixels. The mouse mapping is unaffected.\n- **Other programs:** every program that draws into a canvas goes through this path, so graphics programs get the same fix.\n\n**Not verified.** I haven't booted the OS, so I haven't seen the real on-screen result, and the kernel only parses with the same 5 typedef errors as before. Boot it, open editf, resize the window a few times and check the symbols. If any still look rough, tell me the window size and which symbols.\n\n**Earlier typing result.** The earlier typing test is unchanged: all symbols reached editf's buffer correctly, so the problem was only in how it was drawn.\n\n**Cleanup.** I built the repo's TCC inside the tree to run that test. In tidying up I briefly deleted `i386-libtcc-kern.a` and `tcc-mob.tar.gz`, which are tracked files, and then restored them from git. The zip contains both, and the only changes in the patch are the four source files.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-15T08:36:42.484151Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-15T08:36:42.484151Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a13eb2-49e2-7c92-b837-3ad7d2a7148e"}, {"uuid": "01a141af-5c26-7aa0-865f-cc278a68e9ed", "text": "[synthreason-source/OS: Operating system with tiny C compiler & bochs emulator.](https://github.com/synthreason-source/OS)\n\nmake sure the gui from the elf works", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:37.459903Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:37.459903Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "[synthreason-source/OS: Operating system with tiny C compiler & bochs emulator.](https://github.com/synthreason-source/OS)\n\nmake sure the gui from the elf works", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-15T22:29:37.460240Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-15T22:29:37.460240Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a13eb2-49e2-7f79-b846-2e4d59cf7eef"}, {"uuid": "01a141af-5c26-7386-ab6e-bf1ac1b34613", "text": "I'll check every GUI ELF the repo can build: compile each with the repo's TCC, run it in the emulator, and test frames, keys and mouse clicks. First, which programs exist.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nCanvas size matches at 320\u00d7200. There is also a stray duplicate `bochs_glue .cpp` (with a space in the name) that isn't built. Now I'll compile every candidate GUI program with the repo's TCC.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nMy shell one-liner hid the real error, and my legacy-shim test mangled a comment. I'll run the steps separately.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nOnly `gui_demo` hits this, since the other comp.h programs already link. I'll add the same local `memset` that editf uses.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n`gui_demo` passes everything. Now editf: buttons, typing, cursor movement, click-to-place, Save/New/Open against a fake disk, and the two-click Quit.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nI'll add a fake disk (the file ports the kernel normally serves) to the harness, then run the editf scenarios.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nOne failure: after Save \u2192 New \u2192 Open, the text wasn't reloaded. That could be my fake disk or a real editf bug, so I'll look at what editf does on Open and what it reports.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThat was my fake disk's gap: editf calls `kfstat` (command 4) before reading, and my stub didn't implement it. Adding STAT and re-running the whole editf scenario.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nFinal checks: the kernel still parses with the same baseline errors, and the working tree contains only intended changes.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThe GUI ELFs now work in my tests, after I fixed two bugs: `gui_demo` didn't build, and a stale click could press a widget in a newly launched program. I tested by building each program with the repo's own TCC and running it in a CPU emulator (Unicorn) that fakes the OS's mouse, keyboard, disk and graphics ports. I still can't boot the full OS here, so what you see on screen is untested.\n\n**Results**\n- **`gui_demo`:** it didn't build. It included `compositor.h`, which no longer exists (the library is `comp.h`), then included the identical `bochs_drivers.h` as well, then failed to link for lack of `memset`. It now builds, and 10 of 10 checks pass: clicks count, a held button doesn't repeat, clicks are ignored when the window isn't focused, the scrollbar drags, and the textbox takes symbols.\n- **`editf`:** 18 of 18 checks pass. That covers typing, Enter, arrows, Home/End, Backspace/Delete, click-to-place, symbols, Save/New/Open against a fake disk, the filename box, the two-click Quit, and stress typing.\n- **`driverkit` and `web`:** 64 click positions plus keystrokes each, with no faults or hangs.\n- **`gfx_demo` and `gfxdem`:** both produce frames.\n- **`gfx`, `pong` and `program`:** these block waiting for a key, as designed.\n- **Static-scene ELFs:** the repo's own `host_test` passes on the TCC-built `gui_demo_static`.\n\n**What I changed**\n- **`gui_demo.c`:** I fixed the include, removed the duplicate include and added `memset`. I also added a small `compositor.h` that forwards to `comp.h`, and `make cc` now copies it to the disk image, so older programs keep building.\n- **Stale clicks:** a click stayed pending until some program polled. If you clicked a terminal and then launched a GUI program, it could receive that old click and press whatever was under the cursor. Clicks now expire after about 0.75 s.\n\n**Not covered**\n- **Other programs:** `host_test_editf.c` expects an editor scene ELF that nothing in the repo builds. `direct_x_explorer.c` and `n.c` aren't GUI programs. There's also a stray duplicate `bochs_glue .cpp` with a space in its name that isn't built.\n- **Hand-off to the kernel:** the real timing between the kernel and a guest after each present, and the window-to-canvas click mapping, I checked by reading the code rather than by running it.\n\nThe zip is the full patched tree, `gui-input-perf.patch` is the diff against the original, and `emu.py` is the test harness if you want to rerun these checks.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:37.459688Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:40.641771Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Checking out the GUI build from the cloned repository."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:40.641805Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:41.365275Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I'll check every GUI ELF the repo can build: compile each with the repo's TCC, run it in the emulator, and test frames, keys and mouse clicks. First, which programs exist.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:41.365293Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:42.117285Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01BfH8dcXGpwPYTETQG8JedA", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && git status --short; ls *.c | tr '\\n' ' '; echo; grep -ln \"gfx_present\\|ui_frame_begin\\|gui_scene\" *.c; grep -n \"scene\" Makefile | head; sed -n 1,40p gui_scene.h | head -60", "description": "List guest programs and scene tooling"}, "message": "List guest programs and scene tooling", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && git status --short; ls *.c | tr '\\\\n' ' '; echo; grep -ln \\\"gfx_present\\\\|ui_frame_begin\\\\|gui_scene\\\" *.c; grep -n \\\"scene\\\" Makefile | head; sed -n 1,40p gui_scene.h | head -60\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:44.482835Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:44.482902Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01BfH8dcXGpwPYTETQG8JedA", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\" M kernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h\\n M kernel_parts/03_input_ps2_mouse.h\\n M kernel_parts/09_terminal_window.h\\n M kernel_parts/11_kernel_main.h\\nbochs_cstubs.c busybox_stub.c direct_x_explorer.c disk_tcc.c driverkit.c editf.c gfx.c gfx_demo.c gfxdem.c guest.c gui_demo.c gui_demo_static.c hello.c hello_tcc.c host_test.c host_test_editf.c keyboard_tcc.c n.c pong.c program.c web.c \\ndriverkit.c\\neditf.c\\ngfx.c\\ngfx_demo.c\\ngfxdem.c\\ngui_demo.c\\ngui_demo_static.c\\nhost_test.c\\nhost_test_editf.c\\n369:\\t@MTOOLS_SKIP_CHECK=1 mcopy -o -i \\\"$(DISK_IMG)\\\" \\\"gui_scene.h\\\" \\\"::gui_scene.h\\\" 2>/dev/null || true\\n/* gui_scene.h -- static GUI scene format shared by guest ELFs (producer)\\n * and the kernel (consumer).  A scene is a flat, pointer-free array of\\n * fixed-size nodes stored in the ELF section \\\".guiscene\\\".  No code runs\\n * in the guest to draw it: the kernel finds the section, validates it,\\n * and renders + hit-tests it itself.  Node 0 must be GUI_HEADER(). */\\n#ifndef GUI_SCENE_H\\n#define GUI_SCENE_H\\n\\n#define GUI_SECTION_NAME \\\".guiscene\\\"\\n#define GUI_MAGIC        0x31495547u      /* \\\"GUI1\\\" little-endian */\\n#define GUI_MAX_VARS     16\\n#define GUI_MAX_TEXTBOX  4\\n#define GUI_TEXTBOX_CAP  48\\n#define GUI_MAX_TEXTAREA 1\\n#define GUI_TA_CAP       4096             /* bytes in the text-area buffer */\\n#define GUI_TEXT_LEN     20               /* incl. NUL */\\n\\nenum {\\n    GUI_OP_HEADER = 0, GUI_OP_FILL, GUI_OP_STROKE, GUI_OP_TEXT, GUI_OP_BUTTON,\\n    GUI_OP_SCROLL, GUI_OP_TEXTBOX, GUI_OP_VALUE, GUI_OP_BARV, GUI_OP_INITVAR,\\n    GUI_OP_TEXTAREA, GUI_OP_STATUS\\n};\\nenum { GUI_ACT_NONE = 0, GUI_ACT_ADD, GUI_ACT_QUIT,\\n       /* file actions: operate on text-area 0 and the textbox slot in `var`\\n        * (the kernel supplies the file callbacks; see gui_file_ops_t). */\\n       GUI_ACT_NEW, GUI_ACT_OPEN, GUI_ACT_SAVE,\\n       /* two-click quit: first click arms, second (or unmodified) quits */\\n       GUI_ACT_QUIT_CONFIRM };\\n\\ntypedef struct {                  /* 44 bytes, no pointers, no padding */\\n    unsigned char op, var, aux, flags;\\n    short x, y, w, h;\\n    unsigned int color;\\n    int a, b;\\n    char text[GUI_TEXT_LEN];\\n} gui_node_t;\\n\\n#define GUI__N(op,var,aux,x,y,w,h,col,a,b,txt) \\\\\\n    { (op),(var),(aux),0,(x),(y),(w),(h),(col),(a),(b),txt }\\n\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\" M kernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h\\n M kernel_parts/03_input_ps2_mouse.h\\n M kernel_parts/09_terminal_window.h\\n M kernel_parts/11_kernel_main.h\\nbochs_cstubs.c busybox_stub.c direct_x_explorer.c disk_tcc.c driverkit.c editf.c gfx.c gfx_demo.c gfxdem.c guest.c gui_demo.c gui_demo_static.c hello.c hello_tcc.c host_test.c host_test_editf.c keyboard_tcc.c n.c pong.c program.c web.c \\ndriverkit.c\\neditf.c\\ngfx.c\\ngfx_demo.c\\ngfxdem.c\\ngui_demo.c\\ngui_demo_static.c\\nhost_test.c\\nhost_test_editf.c\\n369:\\t@MTOOLS_SKIP_CHECK=1 mcopy -o -i \\\"$(DISK_IMG)\\\" \\\"gui_scene.h\\\" \\\"::gui_scene.h\\\" 2>/dev/null || true\\n/* gui_scene.h -- static GUI scene format shared by guest ELFs (producer)\\n * and the kernel (consumer).  A scene is a flat, pointer-free array of\\n * fixed-size nodes stored in the ELF section \\\".guiscene\\\".  No code runs\\n * in the guest to draw it: the kernel finds the section, validates it,\\n * and renders + hit-tests it itself.  Node 0 must be GUI_HEADER(). */\\n#ifndef GUI_SCENE_H\\n#define GUI_SCENE_H\\n\\n#define GUI_SECTION_NAME \\\".guiscene\\\"\\n#define GUI_MAGIC        0x31495547u      /* \\\"GUI1\\\" little-endian */\\n#define GUI_MAX_VARS     16\\n#define GUI_MAX_TEXTBOX  4\\n#define GUI_TEXTBOX_CAP  48\\n#define GUI_MAX_TEXTAREA 1\\n#define GUI_TA_CAP       4096             /* bytes in the text-area buffer */\\n#define GUI_TEXT_LEN     20               /* incl. NUL */\\n\\nenum {\\n    GUI_OP_HEADER = 0, GUI_OP_FILL, GUI_OP_STROKE, GUI_OP_TEXT, GUI_OP_BUTTON,\\n    GUI_OP_SCROLL, GUI_OP_TEXTBOX, GUI_OP_VALUE, GUI_OP_BARV, GUI_OP_INITVAR,\\n    GUI_OP_TEXTAREA, GUI_OP_STATUS\\n};\\nenum { GUI_ACT_NONE = 0, GUI_ACT_ADD, GUI_ACT_QUIT,\\n       /* file actions: operate on text-area 0 and the textbox slot in `var`\\n        * (the kernel supplies the file callbacks; see gui_file_ops_t). */\\n       GUI_ACT_NEW, GUI_ACT_OPEN, GUI_ACT_SAVE,\\n       /* two-click quit: first click arms, second (or unmodified) quits */\\n       GUI_ACT_QUIT_CONFIRM };\\n\\ntypedef struct {                  /* 44 bytes, no pointers, no padding */\\n    unsigned char op, var, aux, flags;\\n    short x, y, w, h;\\n    unsigned int color;\\n    int a, b;\\n    char text[GUI_TEXT_LEN];\\n} gui_node_t;\\n\\n#define GUI__N(op,var,aux,x,y,w,h,col,a,b,txt) \\\\\\n    { (op),(var),(aux),0,(x),(y),(w),(h),(col),(a),(b),txt }\\n\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:45.883415Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:53.495581Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Investigating ELF GUI mechanisms used in the emulator."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:53.495723Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:53.496283Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Checking canvas-size handling and mouse bit layout for ABI match"}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:53.496580Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:53.827845Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01V4ZWUgJ1nqy7opzuunouT3", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \"GFX_WIDTH\\|GFX_HEIGHT\" *.c | grep -i \"define\" | head; grep -n \"MOUSE_BIT_LEFT_DOWN\" drivers.h | head -2; grep -n \"GFX_CMD_PRESENT\\|case 1:\\|gfx_w\\b\" bochs_glue.cpp | head -12; sed -n 1,30p gui_demo_static.c | head -40", "description": "Check canvas size source and mouse bits"}, "message": "Check canvas size source and mouse bits", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \\\"GFX_WIDTH\\\\|GFX_HEIGHT\\\" *.c | grep -i \\\"define\\\" | head; grep -n \\\"MOUSE_BIT_LEFT_DOWN\\\" drivers.h | head -2; grep -n \\\"GFX_CMD_PRESENT\\\\|case 1:\\\\|gfx_w\\\\b\\\" bochs_glue.cpp | head -12; sed -n 1,30p gui_demo_static.c | head -40\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:54.192783Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:54.192831Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01V4ZWUgJ1nqy7opzuunouT3", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"382:#define MOUSE_BIT_LEFT_DOWN     0x01  /* left button currently held           */\\n406:    ms->left_down     = (btn & MOUSE_BIT_LEFT_DOWN)    ? 1 : 0;\\n1798:enum { GFX_CMD_PRESENT = 1, GFX_CMD_CLEAR = 2, GFX_CMD_YIELD = 3 };\\n1840:    if (cmd != GFX_CMD_PRESENT) return;\\n1945:        case 1: return (unsigned char)((ms.x >> 8) & 0xFF);   // MX_HI\\n2026:    //   \u2022 port 0xEE/GFX_CMD_PRESENT       \u2014 gfx_present() frame end\\n/* gui_demo_static.c -- same UI as gui_demo.c, but declared as DATA.\\n * Variables: 0=click count, 1=scrollbar value.  Textbox slot 0.\\n * The ELF carries .guiscene; the kernel renders it. */\\n#include \\\"gui_scene.h\\\"\\n\\nGUI_SCENE(\\n    GUI_HEADER(320, 200, 0x202428),\\n    GUI_INITVAR(1, 50),\\n    GUI_BUTTON(10, 10, 90, 22, \\\"Click me\\\", GUI_ACT_ADD, 0, 1),\\n    GUI_SCROLL(280, 10, 14, 160, 1, 0, 100),\\n    GUI_BARV(200, 10, 16, 160, 0xFFB000, 1, 0, 100),\\n    GUI_TEXTBOX(10, 50, 200, 18, 0),\\n    GUI_TEXT(10, 80, 0x9A9A9A, \\\"Clicks:\\\"),\\n    GUI_VALUE(70, 80, 0xE0E0E0, 0),\\n    GUI_TEXT(10, 100, 0x9A9A9A, \\\"Press Quit to exit.\\\"),\\n    GUI_BUTTON(10, 120, 60, 20, \\\"Quit\\\", GUI_ACT_QUIT, 0, 0)\\n);\\n\\n/* Nothing to execute: kept only so the file links as a normal guest. */\\nvoid _start(void) { for (;;) { } }\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"382:#define MOUSE_BIT_LEFT_DOWN     0x01  /* left button currently held           */\\n406:    ms->left_down     = (btn & MOUSE_BIT_LEFT_DOWN)    ? 1 : 0;\\n1798:enum { GFX_CMD_PRESENT = 1, GFX_CMD_CLEAR = 2, GFX_CMD_YIELD = 3 };\\n1840:    if (cmd != GFX_CMD_PRESENT) return;\\n1945:        case 1: return (unsigned char)((ms.x >> 8) & 0xFF);   // MX_HI\\n2026:    //   \u2022 port 0xEE/GFX_CMD_PRESENT       \u2014 gfx_present() frame end\\n/* gui_demo_static.c -- same UI as gui_demo.c, but declared as DATA.\\n * Variables: 0=click count, 1=scrollbar value.  Textbox slot 0.\\n * The ELF carries .guiscene; the kernel renders it. */\\n#include \\\"gui_scene.h\\\"\\n\\nGUI_SCENE(\\n    GUI_HEADER(320, 200, 0x202428),\\n    GUI_INITVAR(1, 50),\\n    GUI_BUTTON(10, 10, 90, 22, \\\"Click me\\\", GUI_ACT_ADD, 0, 1),\\n    GUI_SCROLL(280, 10, 14, 160, 1, 0, 100),\\n    GUI_BARV(200, 10, 16, 160, 0xFFB000, 1, 0, 100),\\n    GUI_TEXTBOX(10, 50, 200, 18, 0),\\n    GUI_TEXT(10, 80, 0x9A9A9A, \\\"Clicks:\\\"),\\n    GUI_VALUE(70, 80, 0xE0E0E0, 0),\\n    GUI_TEXT(10, 100, 0x9A9A9A, \\\"Press Quit to exit.\\\"),\\n    GUI_BUTTON(10, 120, 60, 20, \\\"Quit\\\", GUI_ACT_QUIT, 0, 0)\\n);\\n\\n/* Nothing to execute: kept only so the file links as a normal guest. */\\nvoid _start(void) { for (;;) { } }\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:55.836625Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:56.827970Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01EYtD4TUsXmefbMpHLK78ph", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && sed -n 1798,1900p bochs_glue.cpp; sed -n 1925,1975p bochs_glue.cpp; grep -n \"GFX_WIDTH\\|GFX_HEIGHT\" drivers.h comp.h | head -5; sed -n 262,268p bochs_drivers.h", "description": "Read kernel-side gfx present and mouse port handling"}, "message": "Read kernel-side gfx present and mouse port handling", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && sed -n 1798,1900p bochs_glue.cpp; sed -n 1925,1975p bochs_glue.cpp; grep -n \\\"GFX_WIDTH\\\\|GFX_HEIGHT\\\" drivers.h comp.h | head -5; sed -n 262,268p bochs_drivers.h\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:57.132999Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:57.133087Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01EYtD4TUsXmefbMpHLK78ph", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"enum { GFX_CMD_PRESENT = 1, GFX_CMD_CLEAR = 2, GFX_CMD_YIELD = 3 };\\n\\n// Read by the kernel main loop (kernel_parts/11_kernel_main.h):\\n//   g_bochs_gfx_serial  -- bumped whenever a guest's visible canvas changes\\n//                          (PRESENT, or CLEAR dropping it). The desktop only\\n//                          needs repainting when this moves; it used to repaint\\n//                          everything at 60 Hz whenever ANY guest was running.\\n//   g_bochs_gfx_yielded -- set when the guest handed back its timeslice\\n//                          (PRESENT or YIELD). The slice loop ends right then\\n//                          instead of re-entering a guest that has nothing\\n//                          more to do until the next pass.\\nextern \\\"C\\\" {\\nvolatile unsigned int g_bochs_gfx_serial  = 0;\\nvolatile int          g_bochs_gfx_yielded = 0;\\n}\\n\\nstruct GfxSlotState {\\n    bool     active = false;   // true once a PRESENT has landed and\\n                                // hasn't been cleared/reset since\\n    int      width  = 0;\\n    int      height = 0;\\n    unsigned int pixels[GFX_MAX_W * GFX_MAX_H];\\n};\\nstatic GfxSlotState g_gfx[MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS];\\n\\nextern \\\"C\\\" void bochs_guest_gfx_cmd(unsigned int mbox_addr, int cmd) {\\n    if (g_active_slot < 0 || g_active_slot >= MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS) return;\\n    GfxSlotState& gs = g_gfx[g_active_slot];\\n\\n    if (cmd == GFX_CMD_CLEAR) {\\n        gs.active = false;\\n        g_bochs_gfx_serial++;\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    if (cmd == GFX_CMD_YIELD) {\\n        // \\\"Nothing changed, I'm just giving the CPU back\\\": same cpu_loop() exit\\n        // as PRESENT, but no 256 KB canvas copy and no repaint request.\\n        g_bochs_gfx_yielded = 1;\\n        BX_CPU(0)->kill_bochs_request = 1;\\n        BX_CPU(0)->async_event        = 1;\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    if (cmd != GFX_CMD_PRESENT) return;\\n\\n    // This simple protocol always presents the fixed GFX_MAX_W x\\n    // GFX_MAX_H canvas from bochs_drivers.h, so the transfer size is\\n    // fixed too -- disk_guest_ptr() still does the real safety work,\\n    // rejecting any address whose [addr, addr+len) range isn't\\n    // entirely inside the active slot's own memory window.\\n    void* src = disk_guest_ptr(mbox_addr, (Bit32u)sizeof(gs.pixels));\\n    if (!src) return;\\n    __builtin_memcpy(gs.pixels, src, sizeof(gs.pixels));\\n    gs.width  = GFX_MAX_W;\\n    gs.height = GFX_MAX_H;\\n    gs.active = true;\\n    g_bochs_gfx_serial++;\\n    g_bochs_gfx_yielded = 1;\\n\\n    // Yield back to the kernel main loop so it can repaint the canvas\\n    // and service mouse/input before the guest starts its next frame.\\n    //\\n    // Without this, cpu_loop() never returns between frames: none of\\n    // the mouse/key/gfx port handlers set kill_bochs_request, so a\\n    // tight for(;;){...gfx_present();} loop runs indefinitely inside\\n    // cpu_loop(), starving the kernel's repaint and input polling and\\n    // making the whole system appear frozen. This is the same mechanism\\n    // bochs_guest_exit() uses to cleanly hand control back to the main\\n    // loop. One yield per gfx_present() = one kernel repaint per guest\\n    // frame, which is exactly the frame-pacing we want anyway.\\n    BX_CPU(0)->kill_bochs_request = 1;\\n    BX_CPU(0)->async_event        = 1;\\n}\\n\\n// Called from bochs_release_slot()/bochs_reset_all_slots() so a stale\\n// graphics frame from a finished program can never bleed into the\\n// next program's window if that program reuses the same slot but only\\n// prints text (i.e. never itself calls gfx_exit()).\\nstatic void gfx_forget_slot(int slot) {\\n    if (slot < 0 || slot >= MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS) return;\\n    g_gfx[slot].active = false;\\n    g_bochs_gfx_serial++;          // window reverts to text: needs a repaint\\n}\\n\\n// Read-only accessor for the kernel/window compositor side\\n// (TerminalWindow::draw() in kernel_parts/09_terminal_window.h). Returns\\n// false (and touches nothing) if this slot has no live graphics frame,\\n// so callers can fall back to plain text rendering.\\nextern \\\"C\\\" bool bochs_gfx_get_frame(int slot, const unsigned int** pixels,\\n                                     int* w, int* h) {\\n    if (slot < 0 || slot >= MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS) return false;\\n    GfxSlotState& gs = g_gfx[slot];\\n    if (!gs.active) return false;\\n    *pixels = gs.pixels;\\n    *w = gs.width;\\n    *h = gs.height;\\n    return true;\\n}\\n\\n// =====================================================================\\n// Guest mouse wrapper (ports 0xEF, 0xF0-0xF4 = compositor cursor passthrough)\\n// =====================================================================\\n//\\n// Protocol (see bochs_drivers.h's mouse_poll()/mouse_state_t): the\\nextern \\\"C\\\" void bochs_guest_mouse_poll() {\\n    if (g_active_slot < 0 || g_active_slot >= MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS) return;\\n    MouseSlotState& ms = g_mouse_snapshot[g_active_slot];\\n    int x = 0, y = 0;\\n    unsigned char btn = 0;\\n    // Return value intentionally ignored: on failure (slot not\\n    // focused, no owning window, or not currently in gfx mode) the\\n    // out-params are already left at all-zero by kernel_gfx_mouse_poll\\n    // itself, which is exactly the \\\"cursor absent\\\" snapshot we want.\\n    kernel_gfx_mouse_poll(g_active_slot, &x, &y, &btn);\\n    ms.x = x;\\n    ms.y = y;\\n    ms.buttons = btn;\\n}\\n\\nextern \\\"C\\\" unsigned char bochs_guest_mouse_field(int field) {\\n    if (g_active_slot < 0 || g_active_slot >= MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS) return 0;\\n    MouseSlotState& ms = g_mouse_snapshot[g_active_slot];\\n    switch (field) {\\n        case 0: return (unsigned char)(ms.x & 0xFF);          // MX_LO\\n        case 1: return (unsigned char)((ms.x >> 8) & 0xFF);   // MX_HI\\n        case 2: return (unsigned char)(ms.y & 0xFF);           // MY_LO\\n        case 3: return (unsigned char)((ms.y >> 8) & 0xFF);   // MY_HI\\n        case 4: return ms.buttons;                             // BUTTONS\\n        default: return 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// Called from bochs_release_slot()/bochs_reset_all_slots() so a stale\\n// mouse snapshot from a finished program never bleeds into whatever\\n// next program happens to reuse the same slot.\\nstatic void mouse_forget_slot(int slot) {\\n    if (slot < 0 || slot >= MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS) return;\\n    g_mouse_snapshot[slot] = MouseSlotState{};\\n}\\n\\n// =====================================================================\\n// Tick \u2014 run the active slot for a bounded number of cpu_loop entries\\n// =====================================================================\\n//\\n// cpu_loop runs guest instructions until it hits handleAsyncEvent\\n// with kill_bochs_request set, at which point it returns to us. Each\\n// iteration is one \\\"tick budget\\\" \u2014 typically a small number of guest\\n// insns because port-IO writes (the primary yield trigger) are\\n// frequent for a chatty guest.\\n\\n// bochs_cpu_tick \u2014 Bochs 2.0-style single-call tick.\\n//\\n// Previous design: n-capped loop calling cpu_loop() once per putc.\\n// This was unstable because:\\n//   1. cpu_loop() returns after EVERY guest port-IO (putc or exit),\\ndrivers.h:245: * A guest program can paint a GFX_WIDTH x GFX_HEIGHT canvas of 32-bit\\ndrivers.h:266:#define GFX_WIDTH  320\\ndrivers.h:267:#define GFX_HEIGHT 200\\ndrivers.h:275:#define GFX_CMD_PRESENT 1   /* blit the GFX_WIDTH x GFX_HEIGHT buffer  */\\ndrivers.h:282:static unsigned int gfx_framebuffer[GFX_WIDTH * GFX_HEIGHT];\\n * triggering OUT returns, so it's always safe to start drawing the\\n * next frame into the same buffer immediately afterward.\\n */\\n\\n#define GFX_WIDTH  320\\n#define GFX_HEIGHT 200\\n\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"enum { GFX_CMD_PRESENT = 1, GFX_CMD_CLEAR = 2, GFX_CMD_YIELD = 3 };\\n\\n// Read by the kernel main loop (kernel_parts/11_kernel_main.h):\\n//   g_bochs_gfx_serial  -- bumped whenever a guest's visible canvas changes\\n//                          (PRESENT, or CLEAR dropping it). The desktop only\\n//                          needs repainting when this moves; it used to repaint\\n//                          everything at 60 Hz whenever ANY guest was running.\\n//   g_bochs_gfx_yielded -- set when the guest handed back its timeslice\\n//                          (PRESENT or YIELD). The slice loop ends right then\\n//                          instead of re-entering a guest that has nothing\\n//                          more to do until the next pass.\\nextern \\\"C\\\" {\\nvolatile unsigned int g_bochs_gfx_serial  = 0;\\nvolatile int          g_bochs_gfx_yielded = 0;\\n}\\n\\nstruct GfxSlotState {\\n    bool     active = false;   // true once a PRESENT has landed and\\n                                // hasn't been cleared/reset since\\n    int      width  = 0;\\n    int      height = 0;\\n    unsigned int pixels[GFX_MAX_W * GFX_MAX_H];\\n};\\nstatic GfxSlotState g_gfx[MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS];\\n\\nextern \\\"C\\\" void bochs_guest_gfx_cmd(unsigned int mbox_addr, int cmd) {\\n    if (g_active_slot < 0 || g_active_slot >= MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS) return;\\n    GfxSlotState& gs = g_gfx[g_active_slot];\\n\\n    if (cmd == GFX_CMD_CLEAR) {\\n        gs.active = false;\\n        g_bochs_gfx_serial++;\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    if (cmd == GFX_CMD_YIELD) {\\n        // \\\"Nothing changed, I'm just giving the CPU back\\\": same cpu_loop() exit\\n        // as PRESENT, but no 256 KB canvas copy and no repaint request.\\n        g_bochs_gfx_yielded = 1;\\n        BX_CPU(0)->kill_bochs_request = 1;\\n        BX_CPU(0)->async_event        = 1;\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    if (cmd != GFX_CMD_PRESENT) return;\\n\\n    // This simple protocol always presents the fixed GFX_MAX_W x\\n    // GFX_MAX_H canvas from bochs_drivers.h, so the transfer size is\\n    // fixed too -- disk_guest_ptr() still does the real safety work,\\n    // rejecting any address whose [addr, addr+len) range isn't\\n    // entirely inside the active slot's own memory window.\\n    void* src = disk_guest_ptr(mbox_addr, (Bit32u)sizeof(gs.pixels));\\n    if (!src) return;\\n    __builtin_memcpy(gs.pixels, src, sizeof(gs.pixels));\\n    gs.width  = GFX_MAX_W;\\n    gs.height = GFX_MAX_H;\\n    gs.active = true;\\n    g_bochs_gfx_serial++;\\n    g_bochs_gfx_yielded = 1;\\n\\n    // Yield back to the kernel main loop so it can repaint the canvas\\n    // and service mouse/input before the guest starts its next frame.\\n    //\\n    // Without this, cpu_loop() never returns between frames: none of\\n    // the mouse/key/gfx port handlers set kill_bochs_request, so a\\n    // tight for(;;){...gfx_present();} loop runs indefinitely inside\\n    // cpu_loop(), starving the kernel's repaint and input polling and\\n    // making the whole system appear frozen. This is the same mechanism\\n    // bochs_guest_exit() uses to cleanly hand control back to the main\\n    // loop. One yield per gfx_present() = one kernel repaint per guest\\n    // frame, which is exactly the frame-pacing we want anyway.\\n    BX_CPU(0)->kill_bochs_request = 1;\\n    BX_CPU(0)->async_event        = 1;\\n}\\n\\n// Called from bochs_release_slot()/bochs_reset_all_slots() so a stale\\n// graphics frame from a finished program can never bleed into the\\n// next program's window if that program reuses the same slot but only\\n// prints text (i.e. never itself calls gfx_exit()).\\nstatic void gfx_forget_slot(int slot) {\\n    if (slot < 0 || slot >= MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS) return;\\n    g_gfx[slot].active = false;\\n    g_bochs_gfx_serial++;          // window reverts to text: needs a repaint\\n}\\n\\n// Read-only accessor for the kernel/window compositor side\\n// (TerminalWindow::draw() in kernel_parts/09_terminal_window.h). Returns\\n// false (and touches nothing) if this slot has no live graphics frame,\\n// so callers can fall back to plain text rendering.\\nextern \\\"C\\\" bool bochs_gfx_get_frame(int slot, const unsigned int** pixels,\\n                                     int* w, int* h) {\\n    if (slot < 0 || slot >= MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS) return false;\\n    GfxSlotState& gs = g_gfx[slot];\\n    if (!gs.active) return false;\\n    *pixels = gs.pixels;\\n    *w = gs.width;\\n    *h = gs.height;\\n    return true;\\n}\\n\\n// =====================================================================\\n// Guest mouse wrapper (ports 0xEF, 0xF0-0xF4 = compositor cursor passthrough)\\n// =====================================================================\\n//\\n// Protocol (see bochs_drivers.h's mouse_poll()/mouse_state_t): the\\nextern \\\"C\\\" void bochs_guest_mouse_poll() {\\n    if (g_active_slot < 0 || g_active_slot >= MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS) return;\\n    MouseSlotState& ms = g_mouse_snapshot[g_active_slot];\\n    int x = 0, y = 0;\\n    unsigned char btn = 0;\\n    // Return value intentionally ignored: on failure (slot not\\n    // focused, no owning window, or not currently in gfx mode) the\\n    // out-params are already left at all-zero by kernel_gfx_mouse_poll\\n    // itself, which is exactly the \\\"cursor absent\\\" snapshot we want.\\n    kernel_gfx_mouse_poll(g_active_slot, &x, &y, &btn);\\n    ms.x = x;\\n    ms.y = y;\\n    ms.buttons = btn;\\n}\\n\\nextern \\\"C\\\" unsigned char bochs_guest_mouse_field(int field) {\\n    if (g_active_slot < 0 || g_active_slot >= MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS) return 0;\\n    MouseSlotState& ms = g_mouse_snapshot[g_active_slot];\\n    switch (field) {\\n        case 0: return (unsigned char)(ms.x & 0xFF);          // MX_LO\\n        case 1: return (unsigned char)((ms.x >> 8) & 0xFF);   // MX_HI\\n        case 2: return (unsigned char)(ms.y & 0xFF);           // MY_LO\\n        case 3: return (unsigned char)((ms.y >> 8) & 0xFF);   // MY_HI\\n        case 4: return ms.buttons;                             // BUTTONS\\n        default: return 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// Called from bochs_release_slot()/bochs_reset_all_slots() so a stale\\n// mouse snapshot from a finished program never bleeds into whatever\\n// next program happens to reuse the same slot.\\nstatic void mouse_forget_slot(int slot) {\\n    if (slot < 0 || slot >= MAX_BOCHS_SLOTS) return;\\n    g_mouse_snapshot[slot] = MouseSlotState{};\\n}\\n\\n// =====================================================================\\n// Tick \u2014 run the active slot for a bounded number of cpu_loop entries\\n// =====================================================================\\n//\\n// cpu_loop runs guest instructions until it hits handleAsyncEvent\\n// with kill_bochs_request set, at which point it returns to us. Each\\n// iteration is one \\\"tick budget\\\" \u2014 typically a small number of guest\\n// insns because port-IO writes (the primary yield trigger) are\\n// frequent for a chatty guest.\\n\\n// bochs_cpu_tick \u2014 Bochs 2.0-style single-call tick.\\n//\\n// Previous design: n-capped loop calling cpu_loop() once per putc.\\n// This was unstable because:\\n//   1. cpu_loop() returns after EVERY guest port-IO (putc or exit),\\ndrivers.h:245: * A guest program can paint a GFX_WIDTH x GFX_HEIGHT canvas of 32-bit\\ndrivers.h:266:#define GFX_WIDTH  320\\ndrivers.h:267:#define GFX_HEIGHT 200\\ndrivers.h:275:#define GFX_CMD_PRESENT 1   /* blit the GFX_WIDTH x GFX_HEIGHT buffer  */\\ndrivers.h:282:static unsigned int gfx_framebuffer[GFX_WIDTH * GFX_HEIGHT];\\n * triggering OUT returns, so it's always safe to start drawing the\\n * next frame into the same buffer immediately afterward.\\n */\\n\\n#define GFX_WIDTH  320\\n#define GFX_HEIGHT 200\\n\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:29:58.568087Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:30:02.591828Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Debugging a graphics kernel's pixel buffer size constraints."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:30:02.591975Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:30:02.592237Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Checking canvas dimensions before building TCC outside the repo"}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:30:02.592286Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:30:03.017900Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_019rAzNescXNgZ7kESAnjgjo", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \"define GFX_MAX_W\\|define GFX_MAX_H\" *.cpp *.h | head; cp -r /home/claude/OS /tmp/OSbuild && cd /tmp/OSbuild && (timeout 280 make setup-tcc 2>&1 | tail -2); ls tcc-local/bin/i386-tcc", "description": "Check canvas constants; build TCC in a scratch copy"}, "message": "Check canvas constants; build TCC in a scratch copy", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \\\"define GFX_MAX_W\\\\|define GFX_MAX_H\\\" *.cpp *.h | head; cp -r /home/claude/OS /tmp/OSbuild && cd /tmp/OSbuild && (timeout 280 make setup-tcc 2>&1 | tail -2); ls tcc-local/bin/i386-tcc\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:31:32.186067Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:31:32.186107Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_019rAzNescXNgZ7kESAnjgjo", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"bochs_glue .cpp:1735:#define GFX_MAX_W 480\\nbochs_glue .cpp:1736:#define GFX_MAX_H 320\\nbochs_glue.cpp:1795:#define GFX_MAX_W 320\\nbochs_glue.cpp:1796:#define GFX_MAX_H 200\\n    Now run: make BOCHS=1  to rebuild the kernel with in-kernel TCC.\\n    Inside the OS:  cc hello_tcc.c\\ntcc-local/bin/i386-tcc\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"bochs_glue .cpp:1735:#define GFX_MAX_W 480\\nbochs_glue .cpp:1736:#define GFX_MAX_H 320\\nbochs_glue.cpp:1795:#define GFX_MAX_W 320\\nbochs_glue.cpp:1796:#define GFX_MAX_H 200\\n    Now run: make BOCHS=1  to rebuild the kernel with in-kernel TCC.\\n    Inside the OS:  cc hello_tcc.c\\ntcc-local/bin/i386-tcc\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:31:33.705971Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:31:36.065662Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Investigating which duplicate glue file actually gets compiled."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:31:36.065777Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:31:36.065977Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Canvas size matches at 320\u00d7200. There is also a stray duplicate `bochs_glue .cpp` (with a space in the name) that isn't built. Now I'll compile every candidate GUI program with the repo's TCC.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:31:36.065983Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:31:38.048773Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_018AmAPimqxpowyBJhkzRfV4", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/OSbuild && mkdir -p /tmp/g && T=tcc-local/bin/i386-tcc; for f in editf gui_demo gui_demo_static gfx gfx_demo gfxdem pong web driverkit direct_x_explorer program n; do if $T -nostdinc -nostdlib -I. -c $f.c -o /tmp/g/$f.o 2>/tmp/g/$f.err; then ld -m elf_i386 -T tcc_guest.ld /tmp/g/$f.o -o /tmp/g/$f.elf 2>/tmp/g/$f.lderr && echo \"OK   $f ($(grep -c . /tmp/g/$f.lderr) ld msgs)\"; else echo \"FAIL $f: $(head -2 /tmp/g/$f.err | tr '\\n' ' ')\"; fi; done; for f in /tmp/g/*.elf; do echo \"$(basename $f): undef=$(nm $f | grep -c ' U ')\"; done", "description": "Compile and link all GUI candidates"}, "message": "Compile and link all GUI candidates", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /tmp/OSbuild && mkdir -p /tmp/g && T=tcc-local/bin/i386-tcc; for f in editf gui_demo gui_demo_static gfx gfx_demo gfxdem pong web driverkit direct_x_explorer program n; do if $T -nostdinc -nostdlib -I. -c $f.c -o /tmp/g/$f.o 2>/tmp/g/$f.err; then ld -m elf_i386 -T tcc_guest.ld /tmp/g/$f.o -o /tmp/g/$f.elf 2>/tmp/g/$f.lderr && echo \\\"OK   $f ($(grep -c . /tmp/g/$f.lderr) ld msgs)\\\"; else echo \\\"FAIL $f: $(head -2 /tmp/g/$f.err | tr '\\\\n' ' ')\\\"; fi; done; for f in /tmp/g/*.elf; do echo \\\"$(basename $f): undef=$(nm $f | grep -c ' U ')\\\"; done\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:31:38.409918Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:31:38.409963Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_018AmAPimqxpowyBJhkzRfV4", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"OK   editf (1 ld msgs)\\nFAIL g