n\nThe file cards appear with your reply, and where they sit relative to its text depends on the app the user is reading in; finish the reply with text, and refer to a file by its name, never as above or below."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented 3 files", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:35:22.340203Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:35:23.269176Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "The GUI ELFs now work in my tests, after I fixed two bugs: `gui_demo` didn't build, and a stale click could press a widget in a newly launched program. I tested by building each program with the repo's own TCC and running it in a CPU emulator (Unicorn) that fakes the OS's mouse, keyboard, disk and graphics ports. I still can't boot the full OS here, so what you see on screen is untested.\n\n**Results**\n- **`gui_demo`:** it didn't build. It included `compositor.h`, which no longer exists (the library is `comp.h`), then included the identical `bochs_drivers.h` as well, then failed to link for lack of `memset`. It now builds, and 10 of 10 checks pass: clicks count, a held button doesn't repeat, clicks are ignored when the window isn't focused, the scrollbar drags, and the textbox takes symbols.\n- **`editf`:** 18 of 18 checks pass. That covers typing, Enter, arrows, Home/End, Backspace/Delete, click-to-place, symbols, Save/New/Open against a fake disk, the filename box, the two-click Quit, and stress typing.\n- **`driverkit` and `web`:** 64 click positions plus keystrokes each, with no faults or hangs.\n- **`gfx_demo` and `gfxdem`:** both produce frames.\n- **`gfx`, `pong` and `program`:** these block waiting for a key, as designed.\n- **Static-scene ELFs:** the repo's own `host_test` passes on the TCC-built `gui_demo_static`.\n\n**What I changed**\n- **`gui_demo.c`:** I fixed the include, removed the duplicate include and added `memset`. I also added a small `compositor.h` that forwards to `comp.h`, and `make cc` now copies it to the disk image, so older programs keep building.\n- **Stale clicks:** a click stayed pending until some program polled. If you clicked a terminal and then launched a GUI program, it could receive that old click and press whatever was under the cursor. Clicks now expire after about 0.75 s.\n\n**Not covered**\n- **Other programs:** `host_test_editf.c` expects an editor scene ELF that nothing in the repo builds. `direct_x_explorer.c` and `n.c` aren't GUI programs. There's also a stray duplicate `bochs_glue .cpp` with a space in its name that isn't built.\n- **Hand-off to the kernel:** the real timing between the kernel and a guest after each present, and the window-to-canvas click mapping, I checked by reading the code rather than by running it.\n\nThe zip is the full patched tree, `gui-input-perf.patch` is the diff against the original, and `emu.py` is the test harness if you want to rerun these checks.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-15T22:35:23.376450Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-15T22:35:23.376450Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a141af-5c26-7aa0-865f-cc278a68e9ed"}, {"uuid": "01a141b9-7faa-73ae-b8c6-ec0e404b5484", "text": ">>> building web\nweb.c:1166: warning: implicit declaration of function 'ui_poll_keys'\nweb.c:1183: warning: implicit declaration of function 'ui_textbox_key'", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:41.284596Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:41.284596Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": ">>> building web\nweb.c:1166: warning: implicit declaration of function 'ui_poll_keys'\nweb.c:1183: warning: implicit declaration of function 'ui_textbox_key'", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-15T22:40:41.284894Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-15T22:40:41.284894Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a141af-5c26-7386-ab6e-bf1ac1b34613"}, {"uuid": "01a141b9-7faa-79eb-9ce8-a679302abc36", "text": "Those warnings mean the compiler is seeing a `comp.h` that lacks those two functions. Both exist in the repo's `comp.h`, so I'll find out which header `web.c` actually pulls in and what's on the disk image.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThe shipped disk image is empty, so headers only get there through the copy step. I'll find what prints `>>> building web` and which header copy it reads.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThe repo's own `WEB.md` already knows about the collision. I'll read what it says before changing anything.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThey are older variants (`EDITF.C` doesn't even use `ui_poll_keys`). Removing all three and hardening `mkwebdisk.sh`.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThat \"3\" is because my grep was case-insensitive and matched the lowercase files. A case-sensitive check:\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nYour two warnings come from a stale header, not from `web.c`. The repo tracks both `comp.h` and an older uppercase `COMP.H`, and the older one has neither `ui_poll_keys` nor `ui_textbox_key`. On a case-insensitive checkout (Windows, macOS, WSL on NTFS, FAT/exFAT) the old file replaces the new one. I reproduced your exact warnings by building `web.c` against the old `COMP.H`.\n\nThe repo had the same collision for `editf.c`/`EDITF.C` and `gui_demo.c`/`GUI_DEMO.C`. `WEB.md` already mentioned it but only noted a workaround.\n\n**What I changed**\n- **Duplicates removed:** I deleted `COMP.H`, `EDITF.C` and `GUI_DEMO.C`. All three were older versions, and nothing referenced them.\n- **Guard added:** `mkwebdisk.sh` now stops with a clear message if `comp.h` or `editf.c` is a stale copy, with the fix command. On a deliberately broken copy it exits 1 with that message.\n- **Docs updated:** I rewrote the `WEB.md` note to match.\n\n**What I tested**\n- **Build:** `mkwebdisk.sh` on the fixed tree builds `web`, `editf` and `driverkit` with no warnings, and none of the three has unresolved symbols.\n- **Run:** I ran the built `web` in my emulator with a fake disk. It renders the home page from disk. Clicking a link, at the position taken from its own layout table, navigates to the second page. Back returns to the home page, and a click on blank space does nothing. Typing URLs, including symbols like `: / ? & = % #`, works.\n- **Fresh clone:** the patch applies cleanly to a fresh clone of the original repo and gives exactly the delivered tree.\n\n**If your checkout is already affected**, run this:\n```\nrm -f COMP.H EDITF.C GUI_DEMO.C\ngit checkout HEAD -- comp.h editf.c gui_demo.c\n```\nOr just extract the zip. Be aware that on a case-insensitive filesystem, git itself can't reliably tell the two files apart, so a stale `comp.h` can stay in your working copy even after the pull. That is what the new `mkwebdisk.sh` check is for.\n\nOne thing from the earlier probe: typing a bare name like `home.htm` into `web`'s URL box is treated as a hostname and goes to the network path. That is how the program is written, and disk pages open through the Home button or links. I left it alone.\n\nThe zip is the full patched tree. `gui-input-perf.patch` now includes all changes from this whole session, with the earlier ones combined.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:41.284380Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:44.610495Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Diagnosing missing header declarations in the web build."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:44.610524Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:45.021119Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Those warnings mean the compiler is seeing a `comp.h` that lacks those two functions. Both exist in the repo's `comp.h`, so I'll find out which header `web.c` actually pulls in and what's on the disk image.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:45.021172Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:45.687120Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01FaqLCoFbDcNdDQWSVWxPC1", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \"#include\" web.c | head; cat /tmp/g/web.err | head -5; grep -n \"ui_poll_keys\\|ui_textbox_key\" comp.h | head -4; ls -la disk.img* 2>/dev/null; which mdir mcopy mtype", "description": "Check web.c includes and header contents"}, "message": "Check web.c includes and header contents", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && grep -n \\\"#include\\\" web.c | head; cat /tmp/g/web.err | head -5; grep -n \\\"ui_poll_keys\\\\|ui_textbox_key\\\" comp.h | head -4; ls -la disk.img* 2>/dev/null; which mdir mcopy mtype\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:47.302995Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:47.303061Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01FaqLCoFbDcNdDQWSVWxPC1", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":1,\"stdout\":\"37:#include \\\"comp.h\\\"\\n166:static inline int ui_poll_keys(int* keys, int max)\\n334:static inline int ui_textbox_key(ui_textbox_t* t, int k)\\n353:    ui_textbox_key(t, f->key);\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 39476 Oct 15 06:39 disk.img.xz\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"plaintext\", \"code\": \"37:#include \\\"comp.h\\\"\\n166:static inline int ui_poll_keys(int* keys, int max)\\n334:static inline int ui_textbox_key(ui_textbox_t* t, int k)\\n353:    ui_textbox_key(t, f->key);\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 39476 Oct 15 06:39 disk.img.xz\\n\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:48.869256Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:52.256102Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Tracing which header file gets compiled at runtime."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:52.256247Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:52.256465Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Checking the disk image's copy of comp.h"}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:52.256509Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:52.644312Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01FRArAtp78keGsPnYM6pq8U", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp && rm -rf dk && mkdir dk && cd dk && xz -dk -c /home/claude/OS/disk.img.xz > disk.img && ls -la disk.img && (apt-get install -y mtools >/dev/null 2>&1; which mdir) ; MTOOLS_SKIP_CHECK=1 mdir -i disk.img :: 2>&1 | head -40", "description": "Extract disk image and list its files"}, "message": "Extract disk image and list its files", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /tmp && rm -rf dk && mkdir dk && cd dk && xz -dk -c /home/claude/OS/disk.img.xz > disk.img && ls -la disk.img && (apt-get install -y mtools >/dev/null 2>&1; which mdir) ; MTOOLS_SKIP_CHECK=1 mdir -i disk.img :: 2>&1 | head -40\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:56.338061Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:56.338104Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01FRArAtp78keGsPnYM6pq8U", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 268435456 Oct 15 22:40 disk.img\\n/usr/bin/mdir\\n Volume in drive : is OSKERN     \\n Volume Serial Number is B5FA-BFDA\\nDirectory for ::/\\n\\nNo files\\n                        264 288 768 bytes free\\n\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 268435456 Oct 15 22:40 disk.img\\n/usr/bin/mdir\\n Volume in drive : is OSKERN     \\n Volume Serial Number is B5FA-BFDA\\nDirectory for ::/\\n\\nNo files\\n                        264 288 768 bytes free\\n\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:59.702820Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:59.702972Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "The shipped disk image is empty, so headers only get there through the copy step. I'll find what prints `>>> building web` and which header copy it reads.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:40:59.702977Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:00.190408Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01U4ZTXQ4gyc4HPUkagqCUzu", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && grep -rn \">>> building\\|building \\$\\|echo.*building\" --include=Makefile --include=*.sh --include=*.md --include=*.cpp --include=*.h . 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"bochs-2.0\\|tcc-src\" | head; ls *.sh 2>/dev/null; grep -n \"web\" Makefile | head", "description": "Find the build step that prints '>>> building'"}, "message": "Find the build step that prints '>>> building'", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && grep -rn \\\">>> building\\\\|building \\\\$\\\\|echo.*building\\\" --include=Makefile --include=*.sh --include=*.md --include=*.cpp --include=*.h . 2>/dev/null | grep -v \\\"bochs-2.0\\\\|tcc-src\\\" | head; ls *.sh 2>/dev/null; grep -n \\\"web\\\" Makefile | head\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:00.872380Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:00.872425Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01U4ZTXQ4gyc4HPUkagqCUzu", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"./Makefile:432:\\t    echo \\\">>> Bochs libs not found - downloading and building $(BOCHS_DIR)...\\\"; \\\\\\n./mkwebdisk.sh:52:    echo \\\">>> building $p\\\"\\nmkwebdisk.sh\\npatch-bochs-2.0.sh\\n745:# \u2500\u2500 webdisk: web renderer + editor + driver kit + headers \u2192 disk.img \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\n746:#   make webdisk       (see mkwebdisk.sh for exactly what is copied)\\n747:.PHONY: webdisk\\n748:webdisk: $(DISK_IMG)\\n749:\\tsh mkwebdisk.sh $(DISK_IMG)\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"./Makefile:432:\\t    echo \\\">>> Bochs libs not found - downloading and building $(BOCHS_DIR)...\\\"; \\\\\\n./mkwebdisk.sh:52:    echo \\\">>> building $p\\\"\\nmkwebdisk.sh\\npatch-bochs-2.0.sh\\n745:# \u2500\u2500 webdisk: web renderer + editor + driver kit + headers \u2192 disk.img \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\n746:#   make webdisk       (see mkwebdisk.sh for exactly what is copied)\\n747:.PHONY: webdisk\\n748:webdisk: $(DISK_IMG)\\n749:\\tsh mkwebdisk.sh $(DISK_IMG)\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:02.643032Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:02.983551Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_017nzxXbEr8Z3tmXVWT5cTvv", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && cat mkwebdisk.sh", "description": "Read mkwebdisk.sh"}, "message": "Read mkwebdisk.sh", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && cat mkwebdisk.sh\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:03.201278Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:03.201339Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_017nzxXbEr8Z3tmXVWT5cTvv", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"#!/bin/sh\\n# mkwebdisk.sh -- put the web renderer, the text editor, the driver kit,\\n# all guest headers and some sample pages onto the FAT32 disk image.\\n#\\n#   sh mkwebdisk.sh [disk.img]          (default: disk.img)\\n#   make webdisk                         (same thing, via the Makefile)\\n#\\n# What lands in the image root (long names are written as VFAT LFN\\n# entries by mcopy, exactly like `make cc` does for bochs_drivers.h):\\n#   headers  : drivers.h bochs_drivers.h driver.h comp.h font.h\\n#              gui_scene.h gui_render.h\\n#   sources  : web.c editf.c driverkit.c      (so `cc web.c` works in the OS)\\n#   programs : web editf driverkit             (prebuilt 32-bit ELFs)\\n#   pages    : www/*.htm  ->  home.htm about.htm help.htm test.htm\\n#\\n# Programs are built the same way `make cc` / compile.md describe:\\n#   i386-tcc -c -nostdlib  ->  ld -m elf_i386 -T tcc_guest.ld\\n# Needs: mtools, binutils (ld with elf_i386), i386-tcc (make setup-tcc).\\nset -e\\ncd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")\\\"\\n\\nIMG=${1:-disk.img}\\nexport MTOOLS_SKIP_CHECK=1\\n\\nHEADERS=\\\"drivers.h bochs_drivers.h driver.h comp.h font.h gui_scene.h gui_render.h\\\"\\nSOURCES=\\\"web.c editf.c driverkit.c\\\"\\nPROGS=\\\"web editf driverkit\\\"\\n\\n# i386-tcc: local build first (make setup-tcc), then PATH.  TCC_B may point\\n# at an uninstalled tcc source tree (passed as -B).\\nTCC=${TCC:-tcc-local/bin/i386-tcc}\\n[ -x \\\"$TCC\\\" ] || TCC=$(command -v i386-tcc || true)\\n[ -n \\\"$TCC\\\" ] || { echo \\\"ERROR: i386-tcc not found. Run: make setup-tcc\\\"; exit 1; }\\nTCCFLAGS=\\\"\\\"\\n[ -n \\\"$TCC_B\\\" ] && TCCFLAGS=\\\"-B $TCC_B\\\"\\ncommand -v mcopy >/dev/null || { echo \\\"ERROR: mtools (mcopy) not installed\\\"; exit 1; }\\n\\n# 1. the image itself\\nif [ ! -f \\\"$IMG\\\" ]; then\\n    if [ -f disk.img.xz ]; then\\n        echo \\\">>> unpacking disk.img.xz -> $IMG\\\"\\n        xz -dkc disk.img.xz > \\\"$IMG\\\"\\n    else\\n        echo \\\">>> creating blank 128 MB FAT32 $IMG\\\"\\n        python3 mkfat32.py \\\"$IMG\\\" 128\\n    fi\\nfi\\n\\n# 2. build the guest programs\\nmkdir -p build\\nfor p in $PROGS; do\\n    echo \\\">>> building $p\\\"\\n    \\\"$TCC\\\" $TCCFLAGS -c -nostdlib -I. -o \\\"build/$p.o\\\" \\\"$p.c\\\"\\n    ld -m elf_i386 -static -nostdlib -T tcc_guest.ld -o \\\"build/$p\\\" \\\"build/$p.o\\\" 2>/dev/null\\ndone\\n\\n# 3. copy everything in (-o = overwrite, so re-running updates the image)\\necho \\\">>> writing files into $IMG\\\"\\nfor f in $HEADERS $SOURCES www/*.htm; do\\n    mcopy -o -i \\\"$IMG\\\" \\\"$f\\\" \\\"::$(basename \\\"$f\\\")\\\"\\ndone\\nfor p in $PROGS; do\\n    mcopy -o -i \\\"$IMG\\\" \\\"build/$p\\\" \\\"::$p\\\"\\ndone\\n\\necho \\\">>> contents of $IMG:\\\"\\nmdir -i \\\"$IMG\\\" ::\\necho \\\">>> done. Boot the OS and run:  web   (or: editf, driverkit, cc web.c)\\\"\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"#!/bin/sh\\n# mkwebdisk.sh -- put the web renderer, the text editor, the driver kit,\\n# all guest headers and some sample pages onto the FAT32 disk image.\\n#\\n#   sh mkwebdisk.sh [disk.img]          (default: disk.img)\\n#   make webdisk                         (same thing, via the Makefile)\\n#\\n# What lands in the image root (long names are written as VFAT LFN\\n# entries by mcopy, exactly like `make cc` does for bochs_drivers.h):\\n#   headers  : drivers.h bochs_drivers.h driver.h comp.h font.h\\n#              gui_scene.h gui_render.h\\n#   sources  : web.c editf.c driverkit.c      (so `cc web.c` works in the OS)\\n#   programs : web editf driverkit             (prebuilt 32-bit ELFs)\\n#   pages    : www/*.htm  ->  home.htm about.htm help.htm test.htm\\n#\\n# Programs are built the same way `make cc` / compile.md describe:\\n#   i386-tcc -c -nostdlib  ->  ld -m elf_i386 -T tcc_guest.ld\\n# Needs: mtools, binutils (ld with elf_i386), i386-tcc (make setup-tcc).\\nset -e\\ncd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$0\\\")\\\"\\n\\nIMG=${1:-disk.img}\\nexport MTOOLS_SKIP_CHECK=1\\n\\nHEADERS=\\\"drivers.h bochs_drivers.h driver.h comp.h font.h gui_scene.h gui_render.h\\\"\\nSOURCES=\\\"web.c editf.c driverkit.c\\\"\\nPROGS=\\\"web editf driverkit\\\"\\n\\n# i386-tcc: local build first (make setup-tcc), then PATH.  TCC_B may point\\n# at an uninstalled tcc source tree (passed as -B).\\nTCC=${TCC:-tcc-local/bin/i386-tcc}\\n[ -x \\\"$TCC\\\" ] || TCC=$(command -v i386-tcc || true)\\n[ -n \\\"$TCC\\\" ] || { echo \\\"ERROR: i386-tcc not found. Run: make setup-tcc\\\"; exit 1; }\\nTCCFLAGS=\\\"\\\"\\n[ -n \\\"$TCC_B\\\" ] && TCCFLAGS=\\\"-B $TCC_B\\\"\\ncommand -v mcopy >/dev/null || { echo \\\"ERROR: mtools (mcopy) not installed\\\"; exit 1; }\\n\\n# 1. the image itself\\nif [ ! -f \\\"$IMG\\\" ]; then\\n    if [ -f disk.img.xz ]; then\\n        echo \\\">>> unpacking disk.img.xz -> $IMG\\\"\\n        xz -dkc disk.img.xz > \\\"$IMG\\\"\\n    else\\n        echo \\\">>> creating blank 128 MB FAT32 $IMG\\\"\\n        python3 mkfat32.py \\\"$IMG\\\" 128\\n    fi\\nfi\\n\\n# 2. build the guest programs\\nmkdir -p build\\nfor p in $PROGS; do\\n    echo \\\">>> building $p\\\"\\n    \\\"$TCC\\\" $TCCFLAGS -c -nostdlib -I. -o \\\"build/$p.o\\\" \\\"$p.c\\\"\\n    ld -m elf_i386 -static -nostdlib -T tcc_guest.ld -o \\\"build/$p\\\" \\\"build/$p.o\\\" 2>/dev/null\\ndone\\n\\n# 3. copy everything in (-o = overwrite, so re-running updates the image)\\necho \\\">>> writing files into $IMG\\\"\\nfor f in $HEADERS $SOURCES www/*.htm; do\\n    mcopy -o -i \\\"$IMG\\\" \\\"$f\\\" \\\"::$(basename \\\"$f\\\")\\\"\\ndone\\nfor p in $PROGS; do\\n    mcopy -o -i \\\"$IMG\\\" \\\"build/$p\\\" \\\"::$p\\\"\\ndone\\n\\necho \\\">>> contents of $IMG:\\\"\\nmdir -i \\\"$IMG\\\" ::\\necho \\\">>> done. Boot the OS and run:  web   (or: editf, driverkit, cc web.c)\\\"\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:04.708252Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:10.881251Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Tracing the compile command's missing header flag."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:10.881381Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:10.881714Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Comparing comp.h and COMP.H for case-insensitive conflicts"}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:10.881776Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:11.943798Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01LaBY5B92m9gKgvTAPHdemg", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && for f in COMP.H comp.h; do echo \"$f: lines=$(wc -l <$f) ui_poll_keys=$(grep -c ui_poll_keys $f) ui_textbox_key=$(grep -c 'ui_textbox_key' $f)\"; done; for p in \"editf.c EDITF.C\" \"gui_demo.c GUI_DEMO.C\"; do set -- $p; echo \"$1: lines=$(wc -l <$1)  $2: lines=$(wc -l <$2)\"; done; git log --oneline -3 -- COMP.H comp.h | cat; git ls-files | grep -i \"^comp\\.h$\\|^editf\\.c$\\|^gui_demo\\.c$\"", "description": "Compare case-variant duplicate files"}, "message": "Compare case-variant duplicate files", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && for f in COMP.H comp.h; do echo \\\"$f: lines=$(wc -l <$f) ui_poll_keys=$(grep -c ui_poll_keys $f) ui_textbox_key=$(grep -c 'ui_textbox_key' $f)\\\"; done; for p in \\\"editf.c EDITF.C\\\" \\\"gui_demo.c GUI_DEMO.C\\\"; do set -- $p; echo \\\"$1: lines=$(wc -l <$1)  $2: lines=$(wc -l <$2)\\\"; done; git log --oneline -3 -- COMP.H comp.h | cat; git ls-files | grep -i \\\"^comp\\\\.h$\\\\|^editf\\\\.c$\\\\|^gui_demo\\\\.c$\\\"\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:12.216412Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:12.216460Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01LaBY5B92m9gKgvTAPHdemg", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"COMP.H: lines=368 ui_poll_keys=0 ui_textbox_key=0\\ncomp.h: lines=387 ui_poll_keys=1 ui_textbox_key=2\\neditf.c: lines=457  EDITF.C: lines=497\\ngui_demo.c: lines=101  GUI_DEMO.C: lines=91\\nf79df8e latest iso\\nCOMP.H\\nEDITF.C\\nGUI_DEMO.C\\ncomp.h\\neditf.c\\ngui_demo.c\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"COMP.H: lines=368 ui_poll_keys=0 ui_textbox_key=0\\ncomp.h: lines=387 ui_poll_keys=1 ui_textbox_key=2\\neditf.c: lines=457  EDITF.C: lines=497\\ngui_demo.c: lines=101  GUI_DEMO.C: lines=91\\nf79df8e latest iso\\nCOMP.H\\nEDITF.C\\nGUI_DEMO.C\\ncomp.h\\neditf.c\\ngui_demo.c\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:18.119700Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:25.222265Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Resolving case sensitivity across differing filename conventions."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:25.222401Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:25.222598Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Checking for case-colliding filenames causing stale includes"}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:25.222643Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:26.340984Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Xw6dpuT9ScjA3Kw93HpeEb", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && git ls-files | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z' | sort | uniq -d; echo \"--- references to uppercase names:\"; grep -rIn \"COMP\\.H\\|EDITF\\.C\\|GUI_DEMO\\.C\" --exclude-dir=.git --exclude-dir=bochs-2.0 . 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"^./COMP.H\\|^./EDITF.C\\|^./GUI_DEMO.C\" | head; echo \"--- other tracked files differing only by case from a lowercase twin:\"; git ls-files | awk '{l=tolower($0); c[l]++; n[l]=n[l]\" \"$0} END{for(k in c) if(c[k]>1) print n[k]}'", "description": "Find all case-colliding tracked files and references"}, "message": "Find all case-colliding tracked files and references", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && git ls-files | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z' | sort | uniq -d; echo \\\"--- references to uppercase names:\\\"; grep -rIn \\\"COMP\\\\.H\\\\|EDITF\\\\.C\\\\|GUI_DEMO\\\\.C\\\" --exclude-dir=.git --exclude-dir=bochs-2.0 . 2>/dev/null | grep -v \\\"^./COMP.H\\\\|^./EDITF.C\\\\|^./GUI_DEMO.C\\\" | head; echo \\\"--- other tracked files differing only by case from a lowercase twin:\\\"; git ls-files | awk '{l=tolower($0); c[l]++; n[l]=n[l]\\\" \\\"$0} END{for(k in c) if(c[k]>1) print n[k]}'\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:26.617602Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:26.617643Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Xw6dpuT9ScjA3Kw93HpeEb", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"comp.h\\neditf.c\\ngui_demo.c\\n--- references to uppercase names:\\n./WEB.md:150:* FAT names are case-insensitive: the repo's `EDITF.C` / `COMP.H` collide with\\n--- other tracked files differing only by case from a lowercase twin:\\n EDITF.C editf.c\\n GUI_DEMO.C gui_demo.c\\n COMP.H comp.h\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"comp.h\\neditf.c\\ngui_demo.c\\n--- references to uppercase names:\\n./WEB.md:150:* FAT names are case-insensitive: the repo's `EDITF.C` / `COMP.H` collide with\\n--- other tracked files differing only by case from a lowercase twin:\\n EDITF.C editf.c\\n GUI_DEMO.C gui_demo.c\\n COMP.H comp.h\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:29.280084Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:29.280186Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "The repo's own `WEB.md` already knows about the collision. I'll read what it says before changing anything.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:29.280190Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:29.713053Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01XWjWgf8hPRN3G3mweUGvDG", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && sed -n 140,165p WEB.md; grep -n \"ui_poll_keys\\|ui_textbox_key\" web.c | head -4; sed -n 1160,1168p web.c", "description": "Read WEB.md note and the failing web.c lines"}, "message": "Read WEB.md note and the failing web.c lines", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && sed -n 140,165p WEB.md; grep -n \\\"ui_poll_keys\\\\|ui_textbox_key\\\" web.c | head -4; sed -n 1160,1168p web.c\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:29.907339Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:29.907388Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01XWjWgf8hPRN3G3mweUGvDG", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"\\n* `knet_http_get` returns `KNET_ERR_UNREACHABLE` on a kernel without the ABI;\\n  `web` then says to rebuild the kernel.\\n* `-DWEB_START_URL='\\\"http://10.0.2.2:8000/\\\"'` builds a copy that opens that URL\\n  at startup (useful where keyboard input isn't available).\\n* Known pre-existing issue, not fixed: `busybox <applet> ...` prints no output (on the\\n  original kernel it does not even start the process). Unrelated to the memory/ordering fixes.\\n* A kernel built WITHOUT the gfx_yield change ignores GFX_CMD_YIELD, so a program\\n  that only yields on idle frames would never hand control back. Rebuild the kernel\\n  (and use the matching drivers.h) together.\\n* FAT names are case-insensitive: the repo's `EDITF.C` / `COMP.H` collide with\\n  `editf.c` / `comp.h`; `mkwebdisk.sh` ships the lowercase files.\\n1166:        nk = ui_poll_keys(keys, 32);            /* every key queued since last frame, in order */\\n1183:                ui_textbox_key(&s_url, k);       /* Enter also releases focus */\\n        int keys[32], nk, ki;\\n        int go = 0, back = 0, home = 0, quit = 0, in_view, clicked_link = -1;\\n        int old_scroll, old_drag, was_focus, hb, hh, hg, sig;\\n\\n        mouse_poll(&f.mouse);\\n        f.key = 0;\\n        nk = ui_poll_keys(keys, 32);            /* every key queued since last frame, in order */\\n        old_scroll = s_bar.value;\\n        old_drag   = s_bar.dragging;\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"\\n* `knet_http_get` returns `KNET_ERR_UNREACHABLE` on a kernel without the ABI;\\n  `web` then says to rebuild the kernel.\\n* `-DWEB_START_URL='\\\"http://10.0.2.2:8000/\\\"'` builds a copy that opens that URL\\n  at startup (useful where keyboard input isn't available).\\n* Known pre-existing issue, not fixed: `busybox <applet> ...` prints no output (on the\\n  original kernel it does not even start the process). Unrelated to the memory/ordering fixes.\\n* A kernel built WITHOUT the gfx_yield change ignores GFX_CMD_YIELD, so a program\\n  that only yields on idle frames would never hand control back. Rebuild the kernel\\n  (and use the matching drivers.h) together.\\n* FAT names are case-insensitive: the repo's `EDITF.C` / `COMP.H` collide with\\n  `editf.c` / `comp.h`; `mkwebdisk.sh` ships the lowercase files.\\n1166:        nk = ui_poll_keys(keys, 32);            /* every key queued since last frame, in order */\\n1183:                ui_textbox_key(&s_url, k);       /* Enter also releases focus */\\n        int keys[32], nk, ki;\\n        int go = 0, back = 0, home = 0, quit = 0, in_view, clicked_link = -1;\\n        int old_scroll, old_drag, was_focus, hb, hh, hg, sig;\\n\\n        mouse_poll(&f.mouse);\\n        f.key = 0;\\n        nk = ui_poll_keys(keys, 32);            /* every key queued since last frame, in order */\\n        old_scroll = s_bar.value;\\n        old_drag   = s_bar.dragging;\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:31.643528Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:44.368636Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Diagnosing a file-casing mismatch on a case-insensitive host."}, {"summary": "Hardening the build script against stale duplicate headers."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:44.368770Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:44.368936Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Confirming whether uppercase headers are stale duplicates"}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:44.369029Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:45.218533Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_015kvYhcM4qj9QECv7roqFpT", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && echo \"editf.c uses ui_poll_keys: $(grep -c ui_poll_keys editf.c)   EDITF.C: $(grep -c ui_poll_keys EDITF.C)\"; echo \"gui_demo.c includes: $(grep -h '#include' gui_demo.c | tr '\\n' ' ')  | GUI_DEMO.C: $(grep -h '#include' GUI_DEMO.C | tr '\\n' ' ')\"; git log --format='%h %ad %s' --date=short -1 -- EDITF.C | cat; git log --format='%h %ad %s' --date=short -1 -- editf.c | cat", "description": "Confirm uppercase files are stale older versions"}, "message": "Confirm uppercase files are stale older versions", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && echo \\\"editf.c uses ui_poll_keys: $(grep -c ui_poll_keys editf.c)   EDITF.C: $(grep -c ui_poll_keys EDITF.C)\\\"; echo \\\"gui_demo.c includes: $(grep -h '#include' gui_demo.c | tr '\\\\n' ' ')  | GUI_DEMO.C: $(grep -h '#include' GUI_DEMO.C | tr '\\\\n' ' ')\\\"; git log --format='%h %ad %s' --date=short -1 -- EDITF.C | cat; git log --format='%h %ad %s' --date=short -1 -- editf.c | cat\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:45.442012Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:45.442066Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_015kvYhcM4qj9QECv7roqFpT", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"editf.c uses ui_poll_keys: 2   EDITF.C: 0\\ngui_demo.c includes: #include \\\"comp.h\\\"   /* pulls in drivers.h itself; a second #include of the identical   | GUI_DEMO.C: #include \\\"comp.h\\\" \\nf79df8e 2026-10-11 latest iso\\nf79df8e 2026-10-11 latest iso\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"editf.c uses ui_poll_keys: 2   EDITF.C: 0\\ngui_demo.c includes: #include \\\"comp.h\\\"   /* pulls in drivers.h itself; a second #include of the identical   | GUI_DEMO.C: #include \\\"comp.h\\\" \\nf79df8e 2026-10-11 latest iso\\nf79df8e 2026-10-11 latest iso\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:47.186796Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:48.672226Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Comparing header file versions across duplicate source files."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:48.672339Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:48.672455Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "They are older variants (`EDITF.C` doesn't even use `ui_poll_keys`). Removing all three and hardening `mkwebdisk.sh`.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:48.672458Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:54.187295Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01FNdfRyupRhfZ3onqDYk8Rr", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/OS && git rm -q COMP.H EDITF.C GUI_DEMO.C && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='mkwebdisk.sh'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='''# 1. the image itself'''\nnew='''# 0. sanity: the headers/sources must be the CURRENT ones. The repo used to carry\n#    stale uppercase twins (COMP.H, EDITF.C, GUI_DEMO.C); on a case-insensitive\n#    checkout (Windows, macOS, WSL on NTFS, exFAT/FAT) a twin silently replaces\n#    the real file, and web.c then builds with \"implicit declaration of function\n#    'ui_poll_keys' / 'ui_textbox_key'\". Catch that here with a clear message.\nfor sym in ui_poll_keys ui_textbox_key; do\n    grep -q \"$sym\" comp.h || {\n        echo \"ERROR: comp.h does not define $sym -- it is a stale copy (the old COMP.H\"\n        echo \"       overwrote it on a case-insensitive checkout).\"\n        echo \"       Fix:  rm -f COMP.H EDITF.C GUI_DEMO.C && git checkout HEAD -- comp.h editf.c gui_demo.c\"\n        echo \"             (or re-extract the source zip on a case-sensitive filesystem)\"\n        exit 1\n    }\ndone\ngrep -q ui_poll_keys editf.c || {\n    echo \"ERROR: editf.c is a stale copy (old EDITF.C?). See the note above; restore editf.c.\"\n    exit 1\n}\n\n# 1. the image itself'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='WEB.md'\nt=open(p).read()\nold='''* FAT names are case-insensitive: the repo's `EDITF.C` / `COMP.H` collide with\n  `editf.c` / `comp.h`; `mkwebdisk.sh` ships the lowercase files.'''\nnew='''* FAT names (and Windows/macOS checkouts) are case-insensitive. The repo used to carry\n  stale uppercase twins `COMP.H` / `EDITF.C` / `GUI_DEMO.C` that collided with `comp.h` /\n  `editf.c` / `gui_demo.c`, silently replacing them with older versions (symptom:\n  `implicit declaration of function 'ui_poll_keys'` / `'ui_textbox_key'` while building\n  `web`). The twins are removed, and `mkwebdisk.sh` now refuses to build if `comp.h` or\n  `editf.c` is a stale copy.'''\nassert old in t\nopen(p,'w').write(t.replace(old,new,1))\nEOF\nsh -n mkwebdisk.sh && echo \"mkwebdisk.sh syntax ok\"; git status --short", "description": "Remove stale uppercase twins; harden mkwebdisk.sh; update docs"}, "message": "Remove stale uppercase twins; harden mkwebdisk.sh; update docs", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/OS && git rm -q COMP.H EDITF.C GUI_DEMO.C && python3 - <<'EOF'\\np='mkwebdisk.sh'\\ns=open(p).read()\\nold='''# 1. the image itself'''\\nnew='''# 0. sanity: the headers/sources must be the CURRENT ones. The repo used to carry\\n#    stale uppercase twins (COMP.H, EDITF.C, GUI_DEMO.C); on a case-insensitive\\n#    checkout (Windows, macOS, WSL on NTFS, exFAT/FAT) a twin silently replaces\\n#    the real file, and web.c then builds with \\\"implicit declaration of function\\n#    'ui_poll_keys' / 'ui_textbox_key'\\\". Catch that here with a clear message.\\nfor sym in ui_poll_keys ui_textbox_key; do\\n    grep -q \\\"$sym\\\" comp.h || {\\n        echo \\\"ERROR: comp.h does not define $sym -- it is a stale copy (the old COMP.H\\\"\\n        echo \\\"       overwrote it on a case-insensitive checkout).\\\"\\n        echo \\\"       Fix:  rm -f COMP.H EDITF.C GUI_DEMO.C && git checkout HEAD -- comp.h editf.c gui_demo.c\\\"\\n        echo \\\"             (or re-extract the source zip on a case-sensitive filesystem)\\\"\\n        exit 1\\n    }\\ndone\\ngrep -q ui_poll_keys editf.c || {\\n    echo \\\"ERROR: editf.c is a stale copy (old EDITF.C?). See the note above; restore editf.c.\\\"\\n    exit 1\\n}\\n\\n# 1. the image itself'''\\nassert old in s\\ns=s.replace(old,new,1)\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\n\\np='WEB.md'\\nt=open(p).read()\\nold='''* FAT names are case-insensitive: the repo's `EDITF.C` / `COMP.H` collide with\\n  `editf.c` / `comp.h`; `mkwebdisk.sh` ships the lowercase files.'''\\nnew='''* FAT names (and Windows/macOS checkouts) are case-insensitive. The repo used to carry\\n  stale uppercase twins `COMP.H` / `EDITF.C` / `GUI_DEMO.C` that collided with `comp.h` /\\n  `editf.c` / `gui_demo.c`, silently replacing them with older versions (symptom:\\n  `implicit declaration of function 'ui_poll_keys'` / `'ui_textbox_key'` while building\\n  `web`). The twins are removed, and `mkwebdisk.sh` now refuses to build if `comp.h` or\\n  `editf.c` is a stale copy.'''\\nassert old in t\\nopen(p,'w').write(t.replace(old,new,1))\\nEOF\\nsh -n mkwebdisk.sh && echo \\\"mkwebdisk.sh syntax ok\\\"; git status --short\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:54.411475Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-15T22:41:54.411513Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01FNdfRyupRhfZ3onqDYk8Rr", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"mkwebdisk.sh syntax ok\\nD  COMP.H\\nD  EDITF.C\\nD  GUI_DEMO.C\\n M Makefile\\n M WEB.md\\n A compositor.h\\n M gui_demo.c\\n M kernel_parts/02_boot_info_and_graphics_driver.h\\n M kernel_parts/03_input_ps2_mouse.h\\n M kernel_parts/09_terminal_window.h\\n M kernel_parts/11_kernel_main.h\\n M mkwebdisk.sh\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"mkwebdisk.sh syntax ok\\nD  COMP.