val_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:35:02.093523Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:35:02.093562Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Xi8YndEC9AQa2be1Dch1ve", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"1081 /mnt/user-data/outputs/algorithm_logic.py\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"1081 /mnt/user-data/outputs/algorithm_logic.py\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:35:03.685110Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:35:03.919246Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01DrNvRFXgqfnQ2kTFr5DSdY", "name": "present_files", "input": {"filepaths": ["/mnt/user-data/outputs/algorithm_logic.py"]}, "message": "Presenting file(s)...", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "file", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "table", "table": [["filepaths", "['/mnt/user-data/outputs/algorithm_logic.py']"]]}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:35:03.939622Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:35:03.939662Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01DrNvRFXgqfnQ2kTFr5DSdY", "name": "present_files", "content": [{"type": "local_resource", "file_path": "/mnt/user-data/outputs/algorithm_logic.py", "name": "algorithm logic", "mime_type": "text/x-python", "artifact_publishable": true}, {"type": "text", "text": "\n\nThe file cards appear with your reply, and where they sit relative to its text depends on the app the user is reading in; finish the reply with text, and refer to a file by its name, never as above or below."}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "other"}, "message": "Presented file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "file", "display_content": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:35:10.623775Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:35:14.076939Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "I've extended your generator into `algorithm_logic.py`. It now has a logic layer that gates what the generator may emit at each step. I read your request as \"use the set algebra as symbolic logic, with declarative structures for cognition, reasoning and planning,\" so tell me if you meant something different.\n\nYour set algebra is already a Boolean algebra, so I used it directly as the logic: `|` is or, `&` is and, `~` is not, and `A <= B` (subset) is entailment. Three declarative layers sit on top, and each produces a symbol set that gates the next character:\n\n- **Cognition:** a `Perceiver` turns the current text into facts like `last:END`, `sentence_start`, `dq_open` (an unclosed quote) and `word_long`.\n- **Reasoning:** `RuleBase` holds rules that chain forward to a fixpoint, with negation-as-failure. Heads like `deny:LOWER | PAUSE` compile to symbol sets. Rule order is priority, and a rule that would empty the gate is skipped and reported as \"relaxed\".\n- **Planning:** STRIPS-style operators (preconditions, add/delete effects, cost) are searched with Dijkstra. A tracker runs the plan step by step and replans from what it perceives. For example, given a prompt with an unclosed quote it plans `write_words \u2192 terminate \u2192 close_quote`.\n\nIf gates conflict, the order is your `--allow`/`--forbid` gate first, then rules, then the plan. The plan yields rather than leaving no valid symbol.\n\nEverything is data (`DEFAULT_SPEC`, or your own JSON via `--spec`), so you can change the formalism without touching code. Over 40 seeds of 300 symbols:\n\n| Config | Lowercase after period | Space before punctuation | Unbalanced quotes | Min sentence length |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| baseline | 20 | 0 | 16 | 5 |\n| rules | 0 | 0 | 6 | 25 |\n| plan only | 0 | 7 | 0 | 14 |\n| rules + plan | 0 | 0 | 0 | 25 |\n\nRules fix local well-formedness (the plan alone doesn't know about spacing), and the plan fixes global structure (quotes close, sentences finish). Plan goals are `sentence`, `compound` (two clauses) and `quoted` (every sentence quoted). The `quoted` goal gave 278 completed quoted spans, all properly paired.\n\nNew flags:\n- `--logic` turns on the rules.\n- `--plan GOAL` turns on planning.\n- `--explain` prints a per-step trace of the reasoning.\n- `--lint` checks the spec against your corpus alphabet.\n- `--entails A B` tests whether set A is a subset of set B.\n\nWhat I changed in your original code:\n- **File prompt:** the top-level `input(\"Filename:\")` is gone. With no corpus argument it uses a small built-in text.\n- **Safe parsing:** `eval()` is replaced by an `ast` parser. The old restricted `eval` could still be escaped.\n- **Interactive flag:** `--interactive` now actually controls the prompt loop.\n- **Gate fallback:** when a gate excludes every symbol your n-gram has seen in a context, it now samples from the gate at floor probability. Before, it silently ignored the gate.\n\nKnown limits:\n- It's a character-level model, so the logic can enforce structure, not meaning.\n- A lowercase dialogue tag after a closing quote (`?\" said Mara`) gets forced to a capital.\n- The `quoted` goal can only start at a sentence boundary, so it idles until it reaches one if your prompt is mid-sentence.\n\nThe file is `algorithm_logic.py`. I tested it on a synthetic corpus I wrote, not your own text, so try it on your real corpus and check the output.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-20T01:35:14.177173Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-20T01:35:14.177173Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a156eb-cb36-7789-bbfb-f4f1decff63f"}, {"uuid": "01a156f7-c0be-7394-91a1-b10d4cf082e9", "text": "the logic isnt actuating", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:40:44.019273Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:40:44.019273Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "the logic isnt actuating", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-20T01:40:44.019612Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-20T01:40:44.019612Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a156eb-cb36-7667-aa70-4a9896409460"}, {"uuid": "01a156f7-c0be-7151-beb5-2aef80ba5c59", "text": "That's probably my design: the logic is opt-in, so running `python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt` with no flags behaves exactly like your original. I'll make it on by default and add a visible status summary so you can see whether it's firing.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n`--no-logic` still ran the planner because the plan now defaults to `sentence`. It should restore the original behaviour exactly, so I'll fix that.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThe logic now runs by default, and I've updated `algorithm_logic.py`. Before, you had to pass `--logic` or `--plan`, so a plain `python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt` behaved exactly like your original.\n\n- **Default:** rules and a `sentence` plan are on.\n- **Status lines:** after each run you get a `[logic]` summary showing how many steps were gated, which rules fired, how many plan cycles completed, and which rules never fired. If those lines are missing, you're running a different file (e.g. the original `algorithm.py`).\n- **Switches:** `--no-logic` gives the original engine, `--plan compound` or `--plan quoted` changes the goal, and `--plan none` keeps the rules but drops the planner.\n- **Check it live:** `--explain` prints one line per symbol showing the gate size, plan step and rules applied.\n\nIf you're still not seeing it, tell me the exact command you ran and what the `[logic]` lines say. Some rules (`close_open_quote`, `break_long_word`) only fire when the text has quotes or very long words. A corpus without uppercase letters or sentence punctuation will also leave most rules silent.", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:40:44.019018Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:40:48.735034Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Diagnosing why the script's logic isn't running."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:40:48.735070Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:40:49.426174Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "That's probably my design: the logic is opt-in, so running `python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt` with no flags behaves exactly like your original. I'll make it on by default and add a visible status summary so you can see whether it's firing.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:40:49.426189Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:40:57.679321Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01729QfkaBucVk6sFZeVJNRc", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/build && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='algorithm_logic.py'\ns=open(p).read()\n\n# stats in controller\ns=s.replace('''        self.evaluate = evaluator\n        self.last = Decision()\n''','''        self.evaluate = evaluator\n        self.last = Decision()\n        self.stats: Counter = Counter()\n        self.steps = 0\n''')\ns=s.replace('''        self.last = Decision(label, facts, applied, relaxed, step, len(region))\n        return region''','''        self.last = Decision(label, facts, applied, relaxed, step, len(region))\n        self.steps += 1\n        self.stats.update(f\"rule:{n}\" for n in applied)\n        self.stats.update(f\"relaxed:{n}\" for n in relaxed)\n        self.stats[f\"gate:{label}\"] += 1\n        return region\n\n    def summary(self) -> str:\n        fired = {k[5:]: v for k, v in self.stats.items() if k.startswith(\"rule:\")}\n        gates = {k[5:]: v for k, v in self.stats.items() if k.startswith(\"gate:\")}\n        silent = [r.name for r in self.rules.rules if r.name not in fired and r.is_constraint]\n        lines = [f\"[logic] {self.steps} gated steps | gates: \" + \", \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in gates.items()),\n                 \"[logic] constraints applied: \" + (\", \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in sorted(fired.items())) or \"none\")]\n        if self.tracker:\n            lines.append(f\"[logic] plan cycles completed: {self.tracker.cycles}; current plan: \"\n                         f\"{' -> '.join(self.tracker.plan_names()) or '(none)'}\")\n        if silent:\n            lines.append(\"[logic] rules that never fired: \" + \", \".join(silent))\n        return \"\\\\n\".join(lines)''')\n\n# CLI: on by default\ns=s.replace('''    g.add_argument(\"--logic\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Enable perception + rule-based reasoning gate.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--plan\", metavar=\"GOAL\", help=\"Enable STRIPS planning toward GOAL \"\n                                                  \"(default spec: sentence, compound, quoted).\")''','''    g.add_argument(\"--logic\", action=\"store_true\", help=argparse.SUPPRESS)  # kept for compatibility (now default)\n    g.add_argument(\"--no-logic\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Disable the rule-based reasoning gate.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--plan\", metavar=\"GOAL\", default=\"sentence\",\n                   help=\"STRIPS planning goal: sentence (default), compound, quoted, or 'none'.\")''')\ns=s.replace('''        if args.logic or args.plan or args.explain:\n            logic = build_logic(spec, space, named, args.plan, use_rules=args.logic or args.explain)''','''        goal = None if args.plan.lower() == \"none\" else args.plan\n        if not (args.no_logic and goal is None):\n            logic = build_logic(spec, space, named, goal, use_rules=not args.no_logic)''')\ns=s.replace('''        result = run(args.prompt)\n        print(\"\\\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\\\n\")\n        print(result, \"\\\\n\")\n''','''        result = run(args.prompt)\n        print(\"\\\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\\\n\")\n        print(result, \"\\\\n\")\n        if logic:\n            print(logic.summary())\n''')\ns=s.replace('''  python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --logic --explain --tokens 80\n  python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --logic --plan compound --tokens 400\n  python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --logic --plan quoted --prompt 'He said \"we\\'''','''  python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --explain --tokens 80      # logic is ON by default\n  python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --no-logic                  # original behaviour\n  python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --plan compound --tokens 400\n  python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --plan quoted --prompt 'He said \"we\\'''')\ns=s.replace(\"--spec my_spec.json --logic --plan sentence\",\"--spec my_spec.json --plan sentence\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 -m py_compile algorithm_logic.py && echo \"== default run ==\" && python3 algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --tokens 200 && echo \"== --no-logic ==\" && python3 algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --tokens 200 --no-logic | tail -n +3 && grep -n \"logic --plan\\|--logic \" algorithm_logic.py | head", "description": "Make logic default-on, add status summary, verify both modes"}, "message": "Make logic default-on, add status summary, verify both modes", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/build && python3 - <<'EOF'\\np='algorithm_logic.py'\\ns=open(p).read()\\n\\n# stats in controller\\ns=s.replace('''        self.evaluate = evaluator\\n        self.last = Decision()\\n''','''        self.evaluate = evaluator\\n        self.last = Decision()\\n        self.stats: Counter = Counter()\\n        self.steps = 0\\n''')\\ns=s.replace('''        self.last = Decision(label, facts, applied, relaxed, step, len(region))\\n        return region''','''        self.last = Decision(label, facts, applied, relaxed, step, len(region))\\n        self.steps += 1\\n        self.stats.update(f\\\"rule:{n}\\\" for n in applied)\\n        self.stats.update(f\\\"relaxed:{n}\\\" for n in relaxed)\\n        self.stats[f\\\"gate:{label}\\\"] += 1\\n        return region\\n\\n    def summary(self) -> str:\\n        fired = {k[5:]: v for k, v in self.stats.items() if k.startswith(\\\"rule:\\\")}\\n        gates = {k[5:]: v for k, v in self.stats.items() if k.startswith(\\\"gate:\\\")}\\n        silent = [r.name for r in self.rules.rules if r.name not in fired and r.is_constraint]\\n        lines = [f\\\"[logic] {self.steps} gated steps | gates: \\\" + \\\", \\\".join(f\\\"{k}={v}\\\" for k, v in gates.items()),\\n                 \\\"[logic] constraints applied: \\\" + (\\\", \\\".join(f\\\"{k}={v}\\\" for k, v in sorted(fired.items())) or \\\"none\\\")]\\n        if self.tracker:\\n            lines.append(f\\\"[logic] plan cycles completed: {self.tracker.cycles}; current plan: \\\"\\n                         f\\\"{' -> '.join(self.tracker.plan_names()) or '(none)'}\\\")\\n        if silent:\\n            lines.append(\\\"[logic] rules that never fired: \\\" + \\\", \\\".join(silent))\\n        return \\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\".join(lines)''')\\n\\n# CLI: on by default\\ns=s.replace('''    g.add_argument(\\\"--logic\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Enable perception + rule-based reasoning gate.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--plan\\\", metavar=\\\"GOAL\\\", help=\\\"Enable STRIPS planning toward GOAL \\\"\\n                                                  \\\"(default spec: sentence, compound, quoted).\\\")''','''    g.add_argument(\\\"--logic\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=argparse.SUPPRESS)  # kept for compatibility (now default)\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--no-logic\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Disable the rule-based reasoning gate.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--plan\\\", metavar=\\\"GOAL\\\", default=\\\"sentence\\\",\\n                   help=\\\"STRIPS planning goal: sentence (default), compound, quoted, or 'none'.\\\")''')\\ns=s.replace('''        if args.logic or args.plan or args.explain:\\n            logic = build_logic(spec, space, named, args.plan, use_rules=args.logic or args.explain)''','''        goal = None if args.plan.lower() == \\\"none\\\" else args.plan\\n        if not (args.no_logic and goal is None):\\n            logic = build_logic(spec, space, named, goal, use_rules=not args.no_logic)''')\\ns=s.replace('''        result = run(args.prompt)\\n        print(\\\"\\\\\\\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\\\\\\\n\\\")\\n        print(result, \\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\")\\n''','''        result = run(args.prompt)\\n        print(\\\"\\\\\\\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\\\\\\\n\\\")\\n        print(result, \\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\")\\n        if logic:\\n            print(logic.summary())\\n''')\\ns=s.replace('''  python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --logic --explain --tokens 80\\n  python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --logic --plan compound --tokens 400\\n  python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --logic --plan quoted --prompt 'He said \\\"we\\\\'''','''  python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --explain --tokens 80      # logic is ON by default\\n  python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --no-logic                  # original behaviour\\n  python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --plan compound --tokens 400\\n  python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --plan quoted --prompt 'He said \\\"we\\\\'''')\\ns=s.replace(\\\"--spec my_spec.json --logic --plan sentence\\\",\\\"--spec my_spec.json --plan sentence\\\")\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nEOF\\npython3 -m py_compile algorithm_logic.py && echo \\\"== default run ==\\\" && python3 algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --tokens 200 && echo \\\"== --no-logic ==\\\" && python3 algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --tokens 200 --no-logic | tail -n +3 && grep -n \\\"logic --plan\\\\|--logic \\\" algorithm_logic.py | head\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:40:59.135497Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:40:59.135561Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01729QfkaBucVk6sFZeVJNRc", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"== default run ==\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\nOnce upon and again and nobody asket up the story again and again and the village walked slowly along. A tired the boats goats go?\\nMara's grandfather over the stars one by one by one, because keeper the storm ga \\n\\n[logic] 200 gated steps | gates: rules+plan=200\\n[logic] constraints applied: capital_opens_sentence=2, no_double_punct=1, no_double_space=37, no_early_end=64, no_space_before_punct=37, space_after_end=2\\n[logic] plan cycles completed: 2; current plan: gap -> capitalise -> write_words -> terminate\\n[logic] rules that never fired: close_open_quote, space_after_close_quote, break_long_word, no_run_on\\n== --no-logic ==\\n\\nOnce upon and again and nobody asket up the story again and again and the village walked slowly along. A tired the boats go?\\nEvery child in the stars one. The old the nets before the village baker told the every \\n\\n[logic] 200 gated steps | gates: rules+plan=200\\n[logic] constraints applied: none\\n[logic] plan cycles completed: 3; current plan: gap -> capitalise -> write_words -> terminate\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"== default run ==\\n\\n--- GENERATED TEXT ---\\n\\nOnce upon and again and nobody asket up the story again and again and the village walked slowly along. A tired the boats goats go?\\nMara's grandfather over the stars one by one by one, because keeper the storm ga \\n\\n[logic] 200 gated steps | gates: rules+plan=200\\n[logic] constraints applied: capital_opens_sentence=2, no_double_punct=1, no_double_space=37, no_early_end=64, no_space_before_punct=37, space_after_end=2\\n[logic] plan cycles completed: 2; current plan: gap -> capitalise -> write_words -> terminate\\n[logic] rules that never fired: close_open_quote, space_after_close_quote, break_long_word, no_run_on\\n== --no-logic ==\\n\\nOnce upon and again and nobody asket up the story again and again and the village walked slowly along. A tired the boats go?\\nEvery child in the stars one. The old the nets before the village baker told the every \\n\\n[logic] 200 gated steps | gates: rules+plan=200\\n[logic] constraints applied: none\\n[logic] plan cycles completed: 3; current plan: gap -> capitalise -> write_words -> terminate\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:41:00.524131Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:41:02.457252Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Fixing the no-logic flag to disable all defaults."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:41:02.457423Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:41:02.457611Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "`--no-logic` still ran the planner because the plan now defaults to `sentence`. It should restore the original behaviour exactly, so I'll fix that.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:41:02.457619Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:41:04.783401Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_019no8kk6mPYg9eYd6NgZ3Fe", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/build && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='algorithm_logic.py'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''g.add_argument(\"--plan\", metavar=\"GOAL\", default=\"sentence\",\n                   help=\"STRIPS planning goal: sentence (default), compound, quoted, or 'none'.\")''','''g.add_argument(\"--plan\", metavar=\"GOAL\", default=None,\n                   help=\"STRIPS planning goal: sentence (default unless --no-logic), compound, quoted, or 'none'.\")''')\ns=s.replace('''goal = None if args.plan.lower() == \"none\" else args.plan''','''plan_arg = args.plan or (\"none\" if args.no_logic else \"sentence\")\n        goal = None if plan_arg.lower() == \"none\" else plan_arg''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 -m py_compile algorithm_logic.py\necho \"== --no-logic (should have no [logic] lines, same as original engine) ==\"; python3 algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --tokens 120 --no-logic | tail -n +3\necho \"== default ==\"; python3 algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --tokens 300 | tail -n +3\npython3 check.py 2>&1 | tail -3\ncp algorithm_logic.py /mnt/user-data/outputs/algorithm_logic.py", "description": "Fix --no-logic to disable planner; rerun benchmark; update output file"}, "message": "Fix --no-logic to disable planner; rerun benchmark; update output file", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/build && python3 - <<'EOF'\\np='algorithm_logic.py'\\ns=open(p).read()\\ns=s.replace('''g.add_argument(\\\"--plan\\\", metavar=\\\"GOAL\\\", default=\\\"sentence\\\",\\n                   help=\\\"STRIPS planning goal: sentence (default), compound, quoted, or 'none'.\\\")''','''g.add_argument(\\\"--plan\\\", metavar=\\\"GOAL\\\", default=None,\\n                   help=\\\"STRIPS planning goal: sentence (default unless --no-logic), compound, quoted, or 'none'.\\\")''')\\ns=s.replace('''goal = None if args.plan.lower() == \\\"none\\\" else args.plan''','''plan_arg = args.plan or (\\\"none\\\" if args.no_logic else \\\"sentence\\\")\\n        goal = None if plan_arg.lower() == \\\"none\\\" else plan_arg''')\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nEOF\\npython3 -m py_compile algorithm_logic.py\\necho \\\"== --no-logic (should have no [logic] lines, same as original engine) ==\\\"; python3 algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --tokens 120 --no-logic | tail -n +3\\necho \\\"== default ==\\\"; python3 algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --tokens 300 | tail -n +3\\npython3 check.py 2>&1 | tail -3\\ncp algorithm_logic.py /mnt/user-data/outputs/algorithm_logic.py\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:41:13.039460Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:41:13.039506Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_019no8kk6mPYg9eYd6NgZ3Fe", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"== --no-logic (should have no [logic] lines, same as original engine) ==\\n\\nOnce upon and again and nobody asket up the story again and again and the wandering musician mended the boats as the storm gather c \\n\\n== default ==\\n\\nOnce upon and again and nobody asket up the story again and again and the village walked slowly along. A tired the village minded. The old the storm gather over the boats go? The old lighthouse the roofs. The village baker water, while the waited the story again and again and again and the nets b? A small brow \\n\\n[logic] 300 gated steps | gates: rules+plan=299, rules (plan yields)=1\\n[logic] constraints applied: capital_opens_sentence=5, no_double_punct=1, no_double_space=56, no_early_end=127, no_space_before_punct=56, space_after_end=5\\n[logic] plan cycles completed: 5; current plan: gap -> capitalise -> write_words -> terminate\\n[logic] rules that never fired: close_open_quote, space_after_close_quote, break_long_word, no_run_on\\nrules+plan sentence    double_space=0 space_before_punct=0 double_punct=0 no_space_after_end=0 lower_after_end=0 unbalanced_quotes=0 | sentence len min/mean=25/70\\nrules+plan compound    double_space=0 space_before_punct=0 double_punct=0 no_space_after_end=0 lower_after_end=0 unbalanced_quotes=0 | sentence len min/mean=43/105\\nrules+plan quoted      double_space=0 space_before_punct=0 double_punct=0 no_space_after_end=0 lower_after_end=0 unbalanced_quotes=39 | sentence len min/mean=24/60\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"== --no-logic (should have no [logic] lines, same as original engine) ==\\n\\nOnce upon and again and nobody asket up the story again and again and the wandering musician mended the boats as the storm gather c \\n\\n== default ==\\n\\nOnce upon and again and nobody asket up the story again and again and the village walked slowly along. A tired the village minded. The old the storm gather over the boats go? The old lighthouse the roofs. The village baker water, while the waited the story again and again and again and the nets b? A small brow \\n\\n[logic] 300 gated steps | gates: rules+plan=299, rules (plan yields)=1\\n[logic] constraints applied: capital_opens_sentence=5, no_double_punct=1, no_double_space=56, no_early_end=127, no_space_before_punct=56, space_after_end=5\\n[logic] plan cycles completed: 5; current plan: gap -> capitalise -> write_words -> terminate\\n[logic] rules that never fired: close_open_quote, space_after_close_quote, break_long_word, no_run_on\\nrules+plan sentence    double_space=0 space_before_punct=0 double_punct=0 no_space_after_end=0 lower_after_end=0 unbalanced_quotes=0 | sentence len min/mean=25/70\\nrules+plan compound    double_space=0 space_before_punct=0 double_punct=0 no_space_after_end=0 lower_after_end=0 unbalanced_quotes=0 | sentence len min/mean=43/105\\nrules+plan quoted      double_space=0 space_before_punct=0 double_punct=0 no_space_after_end=0 lower_after_end=0 unbalanced_quotes=39 | sentence len min/mean=24/60\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:41:17.379261Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:41:17.390773Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "The logic now runs by default, and I've updated `algorithm_logic.py`. Before, you had to pass `--logic` or `--plan`, so a plain `python algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt` behaved exactly like your original.\n\n- **Default:** rules and a `sentence` plan are on.\n- **Status lines:** after each run you get a `[logic]` summary showing how many steps were gated, which rules fired, how many plan cycles completed, and which rules never fired. If those lines are missing, you're running a different file (e.g. the original `algorithm.py`).\n- **Switches:** `--no-logic` gives the original engine, `--plan compound` or `--plan quoted` changes the goal, and `--plan none` keeps the rules but drops the planner.\n- **Check it live:** `--explain` prints one line per symbol showing the gate size, plan step and rules applied.\n\nIf you're still not seeing it, tell me the exact command you ran and what the `[logic]` lines say. Some rules (`close_open_quote`, `break_long_word`) only fire when the text has quotes or very long words. A corpus without uppercase letters or sentence punctuation will also leave most rules silent.", "citations": []}], "sender": "assistant", "created_at": "2026-10-20T01:41:17.467830Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-20T01:41:17.467830Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a156f7-c0be-7394-91a1-b10d4cf082e9"}, {"uuid": "01a156fa-ea86-762f-ab0e-46618880ec3c", "text": "make it phenomenal where the rules use other symbol sets to maintain logical composure", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:44:10.330763Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:44:10.330763Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "make it phenomenal where the rules use other symbol sets to maintain logical composure", "citations": []}], "sender": "human", "created_at": "2026-10-20T01:44:10.331121Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-20T01:44:10.331121Z", "attachments": [], "files": [], "parent_message_uuid": "01a156f7-c0be-7151-beb5-2aef80ba5c59"}, {"uuid": "01a156fa-ea86-7b9a-a387-e584c5113f07", "text": "Understood: the rules so far only use character classes (`LOWER`, `END`, \u2026). I'll give them richer, dynamic symbol sets computed from the corpus at every step: legal word continuations, the symbols that follow the current word, the next-letter set licensed by the previous word, the matching bracket closer. Rules can then compose these with set logic, e.g. `deny: ALNUM - CONT_AFTER`.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\nThat's a real bug: `windowhile` glues two words together, which the lexicon rules should make impossible. Tracing the exact step.\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n\n```\nThis block is not supported on your current device yet.\n```\n\n", "content": [{"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:44:10.330537Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:46:44.516002Z", "flags": null, "type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "summaries": [{"summary": "Exploring richer symbol sets for expression rules."}, {"summary": "Designing lexicon-based sets to curb repeated or invalid words."}, {"summary": "Balancing corpus fidelity against invented vocabulary and bracket pairing."}, {"summary": "Refining bracket-closing logic and avoiding redundant rule noise."}, {"summary": "Handling capitalization and word-boundary rules for lexicon matching."}, {"summary": "Deriving word-ending symbols directly from corpus data."}, {"summary": "Building bigram-aware licensing rules for word continuations and endings."}, {"summary": "Preventing repeated words with stutter-detection rules."}, {"summary": "Avoiding repeated phrases and closing brackets correctly."}, {"summary": "Mapping prefix-to-character lookups for word continuations."}, {"summary": "Determining word boundaries and prefix context from trailing text."}, {"summary": "Defining boundary-only versus continuation licensing rules precisely."}, {"summary": "Tracking follow-up character sets for word extensions."}, {"summary": "Adding follow-character sets and planning metrics for evaluation."}, {"summary": "Caching perception results to avoid redundant computation."}, {"summary": "Building a lexicon from corpus word and bigram statistics."}, {"summary": "Optimizing prefix scanning and extracting trailing-word context efficiently."}, {"summary": "Assembling continuation, stutter, and fallback rules for word endings."}, {"summary": "Planning precise code replacements for perceiver and lexicon logic."}, {"summary": "Writing prefix detection and completion checks for word matching."}, {"summary": "Caching percept lookups to skip recomputation."}, {"summary": "Evaluating expression caching and simplifying no-op rule reporting."}, {"summary": "Finalizing default rule ordering and bracket-matching edge cases."}, {"summary": "Wiring lexicon construction and patch scripts into the main build."}, {"summary": "Defining percept data structure for lexicon-based perception."}, {"summary": "Replacing controller, logic-building, and lint code with new rules."}], "cut_off": false, "truncated": true, "hidden": false, "thinking_hidden": true, "alternative_display_type": null, "signature": null}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:46:44.516054Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:46:45.648636Z", "flags": null, "type": "text", "text": "Understood: the rules so far only use character classes (`LOWER`, `END`, \u2026). I'll give them richer, dynamic symbol sets computed from the corpus at every step: legal word continuations, the symbols that follow the current word, the next-letter set licensed by the previous word, the matching bracket closer. Rules can then compose these with set logic, e.g. `deny: ALNUM - CONT_AFTER`.", "citations": []}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:46:45.648662Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:47:29.212690Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01RBjkoXpHi1KTvT5YDDjxKP", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/build && cp algorithm_logic.py algorithm_logic.v2.bak && cat > patch3.py <<'PYEOF'\nimport re\np='algorithm_logic.py'\ns=open(p).read()\n\ndef sep(title):\n    i=s.index(title)\n    return s.rfind(\"\\n# ----\",0,i)+1\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- imports\ns=s.replace(\"import json\\nimport math\\n\",\"import json\\nimport math\\nimport re\\n\",1)\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- spec rules\na=s.index('    \"rules\": [')\nb=s.index('    # STRIPS operators.')\nnew_rules='''    \"rules\": [\n        # -- spacing and punctuation (character-class sets) ------------------\n        {\"name\": \"no_double_space\",       \"if\": [\"last:SPACE\"], \"then\": \"deny:SPACE\"},\n        {\"name\": \"no_space_before_punct\", \"if\": [\"last:SPACE\"], \"then\": \"deny:END | PAUSE\"},\n        {\"name\": \"no_double_punct\",       \"if\": [\"last:PAUSE\"], \"then\": \"deny:PAUSE | END\"},\n        {\"name\": \"space_after_end\",       \"if\": [\"last:END\"], \"if_not\": [\"dq_open\"],\n         \"then\": \"allow:SPACE | END | QUOTE\"},\n        {\"name\": \"close_open_quote\",      \"if\": [\"last:END\", \"dq_open\"],\n         \"then\": \"allow:chars('\\\\\"') | END\"},\n        {\"name\": \"space_after_close_quote\", \"if\": [\"last:QUOTE\", \"sentence_start\"], \"if_not\": [\"dq_open\"],\n         \"then\": \"allow:SPACE\"},\n        {\"name\": \"fresh_sentence\",        \"if\": [\"sentence_start\", \"last:SPACE\"], \"then\": \"fresh\"},\n        {\"name\": \"capital_opens_sentence\", \"if\": [\"fresh\", \"has:UPPER\"],\n         \"then\": \"deny:LOWER | PAUSE | END | chars(\\\\\"'\\\\\")\"},\n        {\"name\": \"no_early_end\",          \"if\": [\"sentence_short\"], \"then\": \"deny:END\"},\n        {\"name\": \"break_long_word\",       \"if\": [\"word_long\"], \"then\": \"allow:SPACE | PAUSE | END\"},\n        {\"name\": \"no_run_on\",             \"if\": [\"sentence_long\"], \"then\": \"deny:PAUSE\"},\n\n        # -- bracket discipline (dynamic set CLOSER = closer of the innermost opener)\n        {\"name\": \"no_stray_closer\",       \"if\": [], \"if_not\": [\"bracket_open\"], \"then\": \"deny:chars(')]}')\"},\n        {\"name\": \"match_closer\",          \"if\": [\"bracket_open\"], \"then\": \"deny:chars(')]}') - CLOSER\"},\n        {\"name\": \"close_before_end\",      \"if\": [\"bracket_open\"], \"then\": \"deny:END\"},\n\n        # -- lexical logic (dynamic sets learned from the corpus) ------------\n        #   CONT        letters that keep the current prefix a real word\n        #   CONT_AFTER  ...restricted to words that followed the previous word in the corpus\n        #   TERM        symbols that ended this exact word in the corpus\n        {\"name\": \"bigram_word\",           \"if\": [\"word_known\", \"bigram_support\"],\n         \"then\": \"allow:CONT_AFTER | TERM\"},\n        {\"name\": \"lexical_word\",          \"if\": [\"word_known\"], \"then\": \"allow:CONT | TERM\"},\n        {\"name\": \"bigram_initials\",       \"if\": [\"at_boundary\", \"bigram_support\"],\n         \"then\": \"deny:ALNUM - CONT_AFTER\"},\n        {\"name\": \"lexical_initials\",      \"if\": [\"at_boundary\"], \"then\": \"deny:ALNUM - CONT\"},\n\n        # -- anti-loop composure ---------------------------------------------\n        {\"name\": \"no_stutter\",            \"if\": [\"stutter\"], \"then\": \"deny:TERM\"},\n        {\"name\": \"no_echo\",               \"if\": [\"repeat_recent\"], \"then\": \"deny:TERM\"},\n    ],\n\n'''\ns=s[:a]+new_rules+s[b:]\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Perceiver block\na=s.index(\"class Perceiver:\")\nb=sep(\"# REASONING: Horn rules\")\nnew_percept=r'''_WORD = re.compile(r\"[^\\W_]+(?:['\\u2019\\-][^\\W_]+)*\")\n_TAIL = re.compile(r\"[^\\W_]+(?:['\\u2019\\-][^\\W_]+)*['\\u2019\\-]?$\")\n_PAIRS = {\"(\": \")\", \"[\": \"]\", \"{\": \"}\"}\n\n# Symbol sets that change every step. Rules may use them like any named set.\nDYNAMIC_SETS = (\"CONT\", \"CONT_AFTER\", \"TERM\", \"CLOSER\", \"FOLLOW\", \"RECENT\")\n\n\nclass Lexicon:\n    \"\"\"Word-level knowledge distilled from the corpus; answers come back as symbol sets.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, text: str):\n        self.complete: Counter = Counter()\n        self.nxt: Dict[str, Set[str]] = defaultdict(set)      # prefix -> next letters\n        self.term: Dict[str, Set[str]] = defaultdict(set)     # word   -> symbols that followed it\n        self.after: Dict[str, Set[str]] = defaultdict(set)    # prev word (lower) -> words that followed\n        self._cache: Dict[Tuple[str, str], Set[str]] = {}\n        prev: Optional[str] = None\n        for m in _WORD.finditer(text):\n            w = m.group()\n            if w not in self.complete:\n                for k in range(len(w)):\n                    self.nxt[w[:k]].add(w[k])\n            self.complete[w] += 1\n            if m.end() < len(text):\n                self.term[w].add(text[m.end()])\n            if prev is not None:\n                self.after[prev].add(w)\n            prev = w.lower()\n\n    def known(self, prefix: str) -> bool:\n        return prefix in self.nxt or prefix in self.complete\n\n    def cont(self, prefix: str) -> Set[str]:\n        return self.nxt.get(prefix, set())\n\n    def terminators(self, word: str) -> Set[str]:\n        return self.term.get(word, set())\n\n    def cont_after(self, prev: str, prefix: str) -> Set[str]:\n        key = (prev.lower(), prefix)\n        if key not in self._cache:\n            n = len(prefix)\n            self._cache[key] = {w[n] for w in self.after.get(key[0], ()) if len(w) > n and w.startswith(prefix)}\n        return self._cache[key]\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Percept:\n    facts: FrozenSet[str]\n    sets: Dict[str, SymbolSet]\n    prefix: str = \"\"\n    prev: str = \"\"\n\n\nclass Perceiver:\n    \"\"\"Maps a context to ground atoms (working memory) plus dynamic symbol sets.\"\"\"\n\n    WATCH = [\"LOWER\", \"UPPER\", \"LETTER\", \"VOWEL\", \"CONSONANT\", \"DIGIT\",\n             \"SPACE\", \"END\", \"PAUSE\", \"QUOTE\", \"BRACKET\", \"OTHER\"]\n\n    def __init__(self, named: Dict[str, SymbolSet], lexicon: Optional[Lexicon] = None,\n                 follow: Optional[Dict[str, SymbolSet]] = None, max_word: int = 14,\n                 min_sentence: int = 25, long_sentence: int = 160, window: int = 8):\n        self.named, self.lex, self.follow = named, lexicon, follow or {}\n        self.space = named[\"ALL\"].space\n        self.empty = self.space.empty()\n        self.max_word, self.min_sentence, self.long_sentence, self.window = max_word, min_sentence, long_sentence, window\n        self.ends = named[\"END\"].members()\n        self.skip = named[\"SPACE\"] | named[\"QUOTE\"]\n        self.static = frozenset(f\"has:{n}\" for n in self.WATCH if named[n])\n\n    def atoms(self) -> Set[str]:\n        out = {f\"last:{n}\" for n in self.WATCH} | set(self.static)\n        out |= {\"empty\", \"word_start\", \"in_word\", \"word_long\", \"sentence_start\", \"sentence_short\",\n                \"sentence_long\", \"dq_open\", \"bracket_open\", \"gap_pending\", \"at_boundary\", \"word_known\",\n                \"word_complete\", \"bigram_support\", \"stutter\", \"repeat_recent\"}\n        return out\n\n    def __call__(self, context) -> FrozenSet[str]:\n        return self.percept(context).facts\n\n    def percept(self, context) -> Percept:\n        text = context if isinstance(context, str) else \"\".join(context)\n        nm, sp = self.named, self.space\n        facts: Set[str] = set(self.static)\n        sets: Dict[str, SymbolSet] = {n: self.empty for n in DYNAMIC_SETS}\n        if not text:\n            facts |= {\"empty\", \"word_start\", \"sentence_start\", \"sentence_short\"}\n        else:\n            last = text[-1]\n            for name in self.WATCH:\n                if last in nm[name]:\n                    facts.add(f\"last:{name}\")\n            if last in nm[\"SPACE\"]:\n                facts.add(\"word_start\")\n\n            i = len(text)                   # sentence boundary: END, then optional spaces/quotes\n            while i > 0 and text[i - 1] in self.skip:\n                i -= 1\n            if i == 0 or text[i - 1] in nm[\"END\"]:\n                facts.add(\"sentence_start\")\n\n            k = len(text)                   # trailing alphanumeric run = current word\n            while k > 0 and text[k - 1] in nm[\"ALNUM\"]:\n                k -= 1\n            wl = len(text) - k\n            if wl > 0:\n                facts.add(\"in_word\")\n            if wl >= self.max_word:\n                facts.add(\"word_long\")\n\n            j = max((text.rfind(c) for c in self.ends), default=-1)\n            sl = len(text) - j - 1\n            if sl < self.min_sentence:\n                facts.add(\"sentence_short\")\n            if sl >= self.long_sentence:\n                facts.add(\"sentence_long\")\n\n            dq = text.count('\"') % 2 == 1\n            if dq:\n                facts.add(\"dq_open\")\n            if \"sentence_start\" in facts and last not in nm[\"SPACE\"] and not dq:\n                facts.add(\"gap_pending\")    # a new sentence needs a separator first\n\n            if any(o in text for o in _PAIRS):   # bracket stack -> innermost closer\n                stack: List[str] = []\n                for c in text:\n                    if c in _PAIRS:\n                        stack.append(c)\n                    elif stack and c == _PAIRS[stack[-1]]:\n                        stack.pop()\n                if stack:\n                    facts.add(\"bracket_open\")\n                    sets[\"CLOSER\"] = sp.chars(_PAIRS[stack[-1]])\n\n            sets[\"RECENT\"] = sp.chars(text[-self.window:])\n            sets[\"FOLLOW\"] = self.follow.get(last, self.empty)\n\n        prefix, prev = self._lexical(text, facts, sets)\n        return Percept(frozenset(facts), sets, prefix, prev)\n\n    def _lexical(self, text: str, facts: Set[str], sets: Dict[str, SymbolSet]) -> Tuple[str, str]:\n        lex = self.lex\n        if lex is None:\n            return \"\", \"\"\n        tail = text[-400:]\n        if len(text) > 400:                  # drop a possibly truncated first word\n            parts = tail.split(None, 1)\n            tail = parts[1] if len(parts) == 2 else tail\n        words = _WORD.findall(tail)\n        m = _TAIL.search(tail[-80:])\n        prefix = m.group() if m else \"\"\n        if prefix:\n            prev = words[-2] if len(words) > 1 else \"\"\n        else:\n            prev = words[-1] if words else \"\"\n        sp = self.space\n        sets[\"CONT\"] = sp.chars(lex.cont(prefix))\n        sets[\"CONT_AFTER\"] = sp.chars(lex.cont_after(prev, prefix))\n        if sets[\"CONT_AFTER\"]:\n            facts.add(\"bigram_support\")\n        if not prefix:\n            facts.add(\"at_boundary\")\n            return prefix, prev\n        if lex.known(prefix):\n            facts.add(\"word_known\")\n        if prefix in lex.complete:\n            facts.add(\"word_complete\")\n            term = lex.terminators(prefix) or set(\" .,;:!?\")\n            sets[\"TERM\"] = sp.chars(term)\n            if prev and prefix.lower() == prev.lower():\n                facts.add(\"stutter\")\n            if len(prefix) >= 5 and prefix.lower() in {w.lower() for w in words[:-1][-6:]}:\n                facts.add(\"repeat_recent\")\n        return prefix, prev\n\n\n'''\ns=s[:a]+new_percept+s[b:]\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- RuleBase.region: ignore no-ops\nold='''            if new:                       # never let a rule empty the gate\n                region = new\n                applied.append(r.name)\n            else:\n                relaxed.append(r.name)'''\nnew='''            if not new:                   # never let a rule empty the gate\n                relaxed.append(r.name)\n            elif new.mask != region.mask:  # only record rules that actually shaped the gate\n                region = new\n                applied.append(r.name)'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Controller / builder / lint block\na=sep(\"Controller: ties perception\")\nb=sep(\"# Generation\")\nnew_ctrl=r'''# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Controller: ties perception, rules and plan into one gate per step\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n@dataclass\nclass Decision:\n    label: str = \"\"\n    facts: FrozenSet[str] = frozenset()\n    applied: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n    relaxed: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n    plan_step: str = \"-\"\n    size: int = 0\n    ctx: str = \"\"\n\n\nclass LogicController:\n    def __init__(self, space: SymbolSpace, named: Dict[str, SymbolSet], perceiver: Perceiver,\n                 rulebase: RuleBase, tracker: Optional[PlanTracker] = None, evaluator=None,\n                 lexicon: Optional[Lexicon] = None):\n        self.space, self.named, self.perceiver = space, named, perceiver\n        self.rules, self.tracker, self.evaluate, self.lexicon = rulebase, tracker, evaluator, lexicon\n        self.last = Decision()\n        self.stats: Counter = Counter()\n        self.steps = 0\n        self._memo: Optional[Tuple[str, Percept]] = None\n\n    def _percept(self, context: Sequence[str]) -> Percept:\n        text = \"\".join(context)\n        if self._memo is None or self._memo[0] != text:\n            self._memo = (text, self.perceiver.percept(text))\n        return self._memo[1]\n\n    def start(self, context: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n        if self.tracker:\n            self.tracker.start(self._percept(context).facts)\n\n    def gate(self, context: Sequence[str], user_allowed: Optional[SymbolSet]) -> SymbolSet:\n        p = self._percept(context)\n        _, fired = self.rules.infer(p.facts)\n        base = user_allowed if user_allowed else self.space.universe()\n        region, applied, relaxed = self.rules.region(fired, base, lambda e: self.evaluate(e, p.sets))\n        label, step = \"rules\", \"-\"\n        if self.tracker:\n            step = self.tracker.describe()\n            pr = self.tracker.region()\n            if pr is not None:\n                joint = region & pr\n                if joint:\n                    region, label = joint, \"rules+plan\"\n                else:\n                    label = \"rules (plan yields)\"\n        self.last = Decision(label, p.facts, applied, relaxed, step, len(region), f\"{p.prev}|{p.prefix}\")\n        self.steps += 1\n        self.stats.update(f\"rule:{n}\" for n in applied)\n        self.stats.update(f\"relaxed:{n}\" for n in relaxed)\n        self.stats[f\"gate:{label}\"] += 1\n        return region\n\n    def observe(self, token: str, context_after: Sequence[str]) -> None:\n        if self.tracker:\n            self.tracker.observe(token, self._percept(context_after).facts)\n\n    def summary(self) -> str:\n        shaped = {k[5:]: v for k, v in self.stats.items() if k.startswith(\"rule:\")}\n        relaxed = {k[8:]: v for k, v in self.stats.items() if k.startswith(\"relaxed:\")}\n        gates = {k[5:]: v for k, v in self.stats.items() if k.startswith(\"gate:\")}\n        idle = [r.name for r in self.rules.rules if r.is_constraint and r.name not in shaped]\n        lines = [f\"[logic] {self.steps} gated steps | gates: \" + \", \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in gates.items())]\n        if self.lexicon:\n            lines.append(f\"[logic] lexicon: {len(self.lexicon.complete)} word types, \"\n                         f\"{len(self.lexicon.after)} bigram contexts\")\n        lines.append(\"[logic] rules that shaped the gate: \" + (\", \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in sorted(shaped.items())) or \"none\"))\n        if relaxed:\n            lines.append(\"[logic] relaxed (would have emptied the gate): \" + \", \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in sorted(relaxed.items())))\n        if self.tracker:\n            lines.append(f\"[logic] plan cycles completed: {self.tracker.cycles}; current plan: \"\n                         f\"{' -> '.join(self.tracker.plan_names()) or '(none)'}\")\n        if idle:\n            lines.append(\"[logic] rules that never changed the gate: \" + \", \".join(idle))\n        return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Building from a spec, and static verification\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef load_spec(path: Optional[str]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    spec = dict(DEFAULT_SPEC)\n    if path:\n        spec.update(json.loads(Path(path).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")))\n    return spec\n\n\ndef make_evaluator(space: SymbolSpace, named: Dict[str, SymbolSet]):\n    \"\"\"evaluate(expr) uses static sets; evaluate(expr, dyn) also sees this step's dynamic sets.\"\"\"\n    trees: Dict[str, ast.AST] = {}\n    static: Dict[str, SymbolSet] = {}\n\n    def evaluate(expr: str, extra: Optional[Dict[str, SymbolSet]] = None) -> SymbolSet:\n        if extra is None and expr in static:\n            return static[expr]\n        try:\n            if expr not in trees:\n                trees[expr] = ast.parse(expr.strip(), mode=\"eval\").body\n            env = named if extra is None else {**named, **extra}\n            result = _eval_node(trees[expr], space, env)\n        except (SyntaxError, ValueError) as exc:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Bad set expression {expr!r}: {exc}\")\n        if extra is None:\n            static[expr] = result\n        return result\n    return evaluate\n\n\ndef _uses_dynamic(expr: str) -> bool:\n    return any(re.search(rf\"\\b{n}\\b\", expr) for n in DYNAMIC_SETS)\n\n\ndef build_logic(spec: Dict[str, Any], space: SymbolSpace, named: Dict[str, SymbolSet],\n                goal_name: Optional[str], use_rules: bool = True,\n                lexicon: Optional[Lexicon] = None,\n                follow: Optional[Dict[str, SymbolSet]] = None) -> LogicController:\n    evaluate = make_evaluator(space, named)\n    dummy = {n: space.empty() for n in DYNAMIC_SETS}\n    perceiver = Perceiver(named, lexicon, follow, **spec.get(\"perceiver\", {}))\n    rulebase = RuleBase([Rule.from_dict(r) for r in spec[\"rules\"]] if use_rules else [])\n    for r in rulebase.rules:                       # fail early on bad expressions\n        if r.is_constraint:\n            evaluate(r.then.split(\":\", 1)[1], dummy)\n    tracker = None\n    if goal_name:\n        if goal_name not in spec[\"goals\"]:\n            raise ValueError(f\"unknown goal {goal_name!r}; choose from {sorted(spec['goals'])}\")\n        g = spec[\"goals\"][goal_name]\n        tracker = PlanTracker([Operator.from_dict(o) for o in spec[\"operators\"]],\n                              Goal(frozenset(g[\"pos\"]), frozenset(g.get(\"neg\", []))),\n                              spec[\"grounding\"], evaluate)\n    return LogicController(space, named, perceiver, rulebase, tracker, evaluate, lexicon)\n\n\ndef lint(spec: Dict[str, Any], space: SymbolSpace, named: Dict[str, SymbolSet]) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Static checks: dead atoms, empty sets, rule conflicts, unreachable goals.\"\"\"\n    out: List[str] = []\n    ev = make_evaluator(space, named)\n    dummy = {n: space.empty() for n in DYNAMIC_SETS}\n    perceiver = Perceiver(named, **spec.get(\"perceiver\", {}))\n    rules = [Rule.from_dict(r) for r in spec[\"rules\"]]\n    RuleBase(rules)                                   # structural validation\n    known = perceiver.atoms() | {r.then for r in rules}\n    cons: List[Tuple[Rule, str, SymbolSet]] = []\n    for r in rules:\n        for a in sorted((r.if_all | r.if_none) - known):\n            out.append(f\"rule {r.name}: atom {a!r} is never perceived or derived\")\n        if r.is_constraint:\n            kind, expr = r.then.split(\":\", 1)\n            ev(expr, dummy)                           # raises on unknown names / bad syntax\n            if _uses_dynamic(expr):\n                continue                              # value only known at run time\n            s = ev(expr)\n            if kind == \"allow\" and not s:\n                out.append(f\"rule {r.name}: {r.then!r} denotes the empty set in this alphabet\")\n            cons.append((r, kind, s))\n    for i, (ra, ka, sa) in enumerate(cons):\n        for rb, kb, sb in cons[i + 1:]:\n            body = ra.if_all | rb.if_all\n            if body & (ra.if_none | rb.if_none):\n                continue                              # bodies can never hold together\n            lasts = sorted(a[5:] for a in body if a.startswith(\"last:\") and a[5:] in named)\n            if any(not (named[x] & named[y]) for x, y in zip(lasts, lasts[1:] + lasts[:1]) if x != y):\n                continue                              # last symbol cannot be in two disjoint classes\n            if ka == kb == \"allow\" and not consistent(sa, sb):\n                out.append(f\"{ra.name} / {rb.name}: allow sets are disjoint; the earlier rule wins\")\n            elif {ka, kb} == {\"allow\", \"deny\"}:\n                (al, a_s), (dn, d_s) = ((ra, sa), (rb, sb)) if ka == \"allow\" else ((rb, sb), (ra, sa))\n                if entails(a_s, d_s):\n                    out.append(f\"{al.name} / {dn.name}: every allowed symbol is denied; the earlier rule wins\")\n    ops = [Operator.from_dict(o) for o in spec[\"operators\"]]\n    live = [o for o in ops if ev(o.region)]\n    for o in ops:\n        if o not in live:\n            out.append(f\"operator {o.name}: region is empty in this alphabet (dropped)\")\n    sync = spec[\"grounding\"]\n    for name, g in spec[\"goals\"].items():\n        goal = Goal(frozenset(g[\"pos\"]), frozenset(g.get(\"neg\", [])))\n        bad = []\n        for mask in range(2 ** len(sync)):\n            init = frozenset(e[\"present\"] if (mask >> k) & 1 else e.get(\"absent\")\n                             for k, e in enumerate(sync)) - {None}\n            if plan(live, init, goal) is None:\n                bad.append(sorted(init))\n        if bad:\n            out.append(f\"goal {name}: unreachable from {len(bad)} of {2 ** len(sync)} perceivable \"\n                       f\"initial states (tracker idles until a reachable one is perceived), e.g. {bad[0]}\")\n    return out or [\"no problems found\"]\n\n\n'''\ns=s[:a]+new_ctrl+s[b:]\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- explain line\nold='''f\"plan={d.plan_step:<18} rules={','.join(d.applied) or '-'}\"'''\nnew='''f\"plan={d.plan_step:<18} ctx={d.ctx!r:<22} rules={','.join(d.applied) or '-'}\"'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- main\ns=s.replace('''    g.add_argument(\"--no-logic\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Disable the rule-based reasoning gate.\")''','''    g.add_argument(\"--no-logic\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Disable the rule-based reasoning gate.\")\n    g.add_argument(\"--no-lexicon\", action=\"store_true\",\n                   help=\"Do not learn word-level symbol sets (CONT, CONT_AFTER, TERM); open vocabulary.\")''')\nold='''    space = SpaceHolder'''\ns=s.replace('''    named = build_named_sets(space)\n\n    if args.sets:''','''    named = build_named_sets(space)\n    fragments = SetFragments(space, named, model, window=args.window)\n    lexicon = None if args.no_lexicon else Lexicon(corpus)\n\n    if args.sets:''',1)\ns=s.replace('''            logic = build_logic(spec, space, named, goal, use_rules=not args.no_logic)''','''            logic = build_logic(spec, space, named, goal, use_rules=not args.no_logic,\n                                lexicon=lexicon, follow=fragments.follow)''')\ns=s.replace('''    fragments = SetFragments(space, named, model, window=args.window)\n    tau = float''','''    tau = float''')\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- docstring\ns=s.replace('''Everything is data (DEFAULT_SPEC below''','''Dynamic symbol sets (recomputed every step, usable in any rule expression):\n  CONT        next symbols that keep the current word prefix a real corpus word\n  CONT_AFTER  ...restricted to words that followed the previous word in the corpus\n  TERM        symbols that followed this exact word in the corpus\n  CLOSER      closing bracket matching the innermost open bracket\n  FOLLOW      Follow(last symbol) from the n-gram (the g1 fragment)\n  RECENT      symbols in the last few positions\nSo a rule such as  deny:ALNUM - CONT_AFTER  (\"no letter that can't start a word\nlicensed by the previous word\") composes learned sets with the Boolean algebra.\n\nEverything is data (DEFAULT_SPEC below''',1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPYEOF\npython3 patch3.py && python3 -m py_compile algorithm_logic.py && echo compiled && python3 algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --lint", "description": "Patch in lexicon-derived dynamic symbol sets, bracket logic, anti-loop rules; compile and lint"}, "message": "Patch in lexicon-derived dynamic symbol sets, bracket logic, anti-loop rules; compile and lint", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/build && cp algorithm_logic.py algorithm_logic.v2.bak && cat > patch3.py <<'PYEOF'\\nimport re\\np='algorithm_logic.py'\\ns=open(p).read()\\n\\ndef sep(title):\\n    i=s.index(title)\\n    return s.rfind(\\\"\\\\n# ----\\\",0,i)+1\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- imports\\ns=s.replace(\\\"import json\\\\nimport math\\\\n\\\",\\\"import json\\\\nimport math\\\\nimport re\\\\n\\\",1)\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- spec rules\\na=s.index('    \\\"rules\\\": [')\\nb=s.index('    # STRIPS operators.')\\nnew_rules='''    \\\"rules\\\": [\\n        # -- spacing and punctuation (character-class sets) ------------------\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"no_double_space\\\",       \\\"if\\\": [\\\"last:SPACE\\\"], \\\"then\\\": \\\"deny:SPACE\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"no_space_before_punct\\\", \\\"if\\\": [\\\"last:SPACE\\\"], \\\"then\\\": \\\"deny:END | PAUSE\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"no_double_punct\\\",       \\\"if\\\": [\\\"last:PAUSE\\\"], \\\"then\\\": \\\"deny:PAUSE | END\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"space_after_end\\\",       \\\"if\\\": [\\\"last:END\\\"], \\\"if_not\\\": [\\\"dq_open\\\"],\\n         \\\"then\\\": \\\"allow:SPACE | END | QUOTE\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"close_open_quote\\\",      \\\"if\\\": [\\\"last:END\\\", \\\"dq_open\\\"],\\n         \\\"then\\\": \\\"allow:chars('\\\\\\\\\\\"') | END\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"space_after_close_quote\\\", \\\"if\\\": [\\\"last:QUOTE\\\", \\\"sentence_start\\\"], \\\"if_not\\\": [\\\"dq_open\\\"],\\n         \\\"then\\\": \\\"allow:SPACE\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"fresh_sentence\\\",        \\\"if\\\": [\\\"sentence_start\\\", \\\"last:SPACE\\\"], \\\"then\\\": \\\"fresh\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"capital_opens_sentence\\\", \\\"if\\\": [\\\"fresh\\\", \\\"has:UPPER\\\"],\\n         \\\"then\\\": \\\"deny:LOWER | PAUSE | END | chars(\\\\\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"no_early_end\\\",          \\\"if\\\": [\\\"sentence_short\\\"], \\\"then\\\": \\\"deny:END\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"break_long_word\\\",       \\\"if\\\": [\\\"word_long\\\"], \\\"then\\\": \\\"allow:SPACE | PAUSE | END\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"no_run_on\\\",             \\\"if\\\": [\\\"sentence_long\\\"], \\\"then\\\": \\\"deny:PAUSE\\\"},\\n\\n        # -- bracket discipline (dynamic set CLOSER = closer of the innermost opener)\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"no_stray_closer\\\",       \\\"if\\\": [], \\\"if_not\\\": [\\\"bracket_open\\\"], \\\"then\\\": \\\"deny:chars(')]}')\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"match_closer\\\",          \\\"if\\\": [\\\"bracket_open\\\"], \\\"then\\\": \\\"deny:chars(')]}') - CLOSER\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"close_before_end\\\",      \\\"if\\\": [\\\"bracket_open\\\"], \\\"then\\\": \\\"deny:END\\\"},\\n\\n        # -- lexical logic (dynamic sets learned from the corpus) ------------\\n        #   CONT        letters that keep the current prefix a real word\\n        #   CONT_AFTER  ...restricted to words that followed the previous word in the corpus\\n        #   TERM        symbols that ended this exact word in the corpus\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"bigram_word\\\",           \\\"if\\\": [\\\"word_known\\\", \\\"bigram_support\\\"],\\n         \\\"then\\\": \\\"allow:CONT_AFTER | TERM\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"lexical_word\\\",          \\\"if\\\": [\\\"word_known\\\"], \\\"then\\\": \\\"allow:CONT | TERM\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"bigram_initials\\\",       \\\"if\\\": [\\\"at_boundary\\\", \\\"bigram_support\\\"],\\n         \\\"then\\\": \\\"deny:ALNUM - CONT_AFTER\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"lexical_initials\\\",      \\\"if\\\": [\\\"at_boundary\\\"], \\\"then\\\": \\\"deny:ALNUM - CONT\\\"},\\n\\n        # -- anti-loop composure ---------------------------------------------\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"no_stutter\\\",            \\\"if\\\": [\\\"stutter\\\"], \\\"then\\\": \\\"deny:TERM\\\"},\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"no_echo\\\",               \\\"if\\\": [\\\"repeat_recent\\\"], \\\"then\\\": \\\"deny:TERM\\\"},\\n    ],\\n\\n'''\\ns=s[:a]+new_rules+s[b:]\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Perceiver block\\na=s.index(\\\"class Perceiver:\\\")\\nb=sep(\\\"# REASONING: Horn rules\\\")\\nnew_percept=r'''_WORD = re.compile(r\\\"[^\\\\W_]+(?:['\\\\u2019\\\\-][^\\\\W_]+)*\\\")\\n_TAIL = re.compile(r\\\"[^\\\\W_]+(?:['\\\\u2019\\\\-][^\\\\W_]+)*['\\\\u2019\\\\-]?$\\\")\\n_PAIRS = {\\\"(\\\": \\\")\\\", \\\"[\\\": \\\"]\\\", \\\"{\\\": \\\"}\\\"}\\n\\n# Symbol sets that change every step. Rules may use them like any named set.\\nDYNAMIC_SETS = (\\\"CONT\\\", \\\"CONT_AFTER\\\", \\\"TERM\\\", \\\"CLOSER\\\", \\\"FOLLOW\\\", \\\"RECENT\\\")\\n\\n\\nclass Lexicon:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Word-level knowledge distilled from the corpus; answers come back as symbol sets.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self, text: str):\\n        self.complete: Counter = Counter()\\n        self.nxt: Dict[str, Set[str]] = defaultdict(set)      # prefix -> next letters\\n        self.term: Dict[str, Set[str]] = defaultdict(set)     # word   -> symbols that followed it\\n        self.after: Dict[str, Set[str]] = defaultdict(set)    # prev word (lower) -> words that followed\\n        self._cache: Dict[Tuple[str, str], Set[str]] = {}\\n        prev: Optional[str] = None\\n        for m in _WORD.finditer(text):\\n            w = m.group()\\n            if w not in self.complete:\\n                for k in range(len(w)):\\n                    self.nxt[w[:k]].add(w[k])\\n            self.complete[w] += 1\\n            if m.end() < len(text):\\n                self.term[w].add(text[m.end()])\\n            if prev is not None:\\n                self.after[prev].add(w)\\n            prev = w.lower()\\n\\n    def known(self, prefix: str) -> bool:\\n        return prefix in self.nxt or prefix in self.complete\\n\\n    def cont(self, prefix: str) -> Set[str]:\\n        return self.nxt.get(prefix, set())\\n\\n    def terminators(self, word: str) -> Set[str]:\\n        return self.term.get(word, set())\\n\\n    def cont_after(self, prev: str, prefix: str) -> Set[str]:\\n        key = (prev.lower(), prefix)\\n        if key not in self._cache:\\n            n = len(prefix)\\n            self._cache[key] = {w[n] for w in self.after.get(key[0], ()) if len(w) > n and w.startswith(prefix)}\\n        return self._cache[key]\\n\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass Percept:\\n    facts: FrozenSet[str]\\n    sets: Dict[str, SymbolSet]\\n    prefix: str = \\\"\\\"\\n    prev: str = \\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass Perceiver:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Maps a context to ground atoms (working memory) plus dynamic symbol sets.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    WATCH = [\\\"LOWER\\\", \\\"UPPER\\\", \\\"LETTER\\\", \\\"VOWEL\\\", \\\"CONSONANT\\\", \\\"DIGIT\\\",\\n             \\\"SPACE\\\", \\\"END\\\", \\\"PAUSE\\\", \\\"QUOTE\\\", \\\"BRACKET\\\", \\\"OTHER\\\"]\\n\\n    def __init__(self, named: Dict[str, SymbolSet], lexicon: Optional[Lexicon] = None,\\n                 follow: Optional[Dict[str, SymbolSet]] = None, max_word: int = 14,\\n                 min_sentence: int = 25, long_sentence: int = 160, window: int = 8):\\n        self.named, self.lex, self.follow = named, lexicon, follow or {}\\n        self.space = named[\\\"ALL\\\"].space\\n        self.empty = self.space.empty()\\n        self.max_word, self.min_sentence, self.long_sentence, self.window = max_word, min_sentence, long_sentence, window\\n        self.ends = named[\\\"END\\\"].members()\\n        self.skip = named[\\\"SPACE\\\"] | named[\\\"QUOTE\\\"]\\n        self.static = frozenset(f\\\"has:{n}\\\" for n in self.WATCH if named[n])\\n\\n    def atoms(self) -> Set[str]:\\n        out = {f\\\"last:{n}\\\" for n in self.WATCH} | set(self.static)\\n        out |= {\\\"empty\\\", \\\"word_start\\\", \\\"in_word\\\", \\\"word_long\\\", \\\"sentence_start\\\", \\\"sentence_short\\\",\\n                \\\"sentence_long\\\", \\\"dq_open\\\", \\\"bracket_open\\\", \\\"gap_pending\\\", \\\"at_boundary\\\", \\\"word_known\\\",\\n                \\\"word_complete\\\", \\\"bigram_support\\\", \\\"stutter\\\", \\\"repeat_recent\\\"}\\n        return out\\n\\n    def __call__(self, context) -> FrozenSet[str]:\\n        return self.percept(context).facts\\n\\n    def percept(self, context) -> Percept:\\n        text = context if isinstance(context, str) else \\\"\\\".join(context)\\n        nm, sp = self.named, self.space\\n        facts: Set[str] = set(self.static)\\n        sets: Dict[str, SymbolSet] = {n: self.empty for n in DYNAMIC_SETS}\\n        if not text:\\n            facts |= {\\\"empty\\\", \\\"word_start\\\", \\\"sentence_start\\\", \\\"sentence_short\\\"}\\n        else:\\n            last = text[-1]\\n            for name in self.WATCH:\\n                if last in nm[name]:\\n                    facts.add(f\\\"last:{name}\\\")\\n            if last in nm[\\\"SPACE\\\"]:\\n                facts.add(\\\"word_start\\\")\\n\\n            i = len(text)                   # sentence boundary: END, then optional spaces/quotes\\n            while i > 0 and text[i - 1] in self.skip:\\n                i -= 1\\n            if i == 0 or text[i - 1] in nm[\\\"END\\\"]:\\n                facts.add(\\\"sentence_start\\\")\\n\\n            k = len(text)                   # trailing alphanumeric run = current word\\n            while k > 0 and text[k - 1] in nm[\\\"ALNUM\\\"]:\\n                k -= 1\\n            wl = len(text) - k\\n            if wl > 0:\\n                facts.add(\\\"in_word\\\")\\n            if wl >= self.max_word:\\n                facts.add(\\\"word_long\\\")\\n\\n            j = max((text.rfind(c) for c in self.ends), default=-1)\\n            sl = len(text) - j - 1\\n            if sl < self.min_sentence:\\n                facts.add(\\\"sentence_short\\\")\\n            if sl >= self.long_sentence:\\n                facts.add(\\\"sentence_long\\\")\\n\\n            dq = text.count('\\\"') % 2 == 1\\n            if dq:\\n                facts.add(\\\"dq_open\\\")\\n            if \\\"sentence_start\\\" in facts and last not in nm[\\\"SPACE\\\"] and not dq:\\n                facts.add(\\\"gap_pending\\\")    # a new sentence needs a separator first\\n\\n            if any(o in text for o in _PAIRS):   # bracket stack -> innermost closer\\n                stack: List[str] = []\\n                for c in text:\\n                    if c in _PAIRS:\\n                        stack.append(c)\\n                    elif stack and c == _PAIRS[stack[-1]]:\\n                        stack.pop()\\n                if stack:\\n                    facts.add(\\\"bracket_open\\\")\\n                    sets[\\\"CLOSER\\\"] = sp.chars(_PAIRS[stack[-1]])\\n\\n            sets[\\\"RECENT\\\"] = sp.chars(text[-self.window:])\\n            sets[\\\"FOLLOW\\\"] = self.follow.get(last, self.empty)\\n\\n        prefix, prev = self._lexical(text, facts, sets)\\n        return Percept(frozenset(facts), sets, prefix, prev)\\n\\n    def _lexical(self, text: str, facts: Set[str], sets: Dict[str, SymbolSet]) -> Tuple[str, str]:\\n        lex = self.lex\\n        if lex is None:\\n            return \\\"\\\", \\\"\\\"\\n        tail = text[-400:]\\n        if len(text) > 400:                  # drop a possibly truncated first word\\n            parts = tail.split(None, 1)\\n            tail = parts[1] if len(parts) == 2 else tail\\n        words = _WORD.findall(tail)\\n        m = _TAIL.search(tail[-80:])\\n        prefix = m.group() if m else \\\"\\\"\\n        if prefix:\\n            prev = words[-2] if len(words) > 1 else \\\"\\\"\\n        else:\\n            prev = words[-1] if words else \\\"\\\"\\n        sp = self.space\\n        sets[\\\"CONT\\\"] = sp.chars(lex.cont(prefix))\\n        sets[\\\"CONT_AFTER\\\"] = sp.chars(lex.cont_after(prev, prefix))\\n        if sets[\\\"CONT_AFTER\\\"]:\\n            facts.add(\\\"bigram_support\\\")\\n        if not prefix:\\n            facts.add(\\\"at_boundary\\\")\\n            return prefix, prev\\n        if lex.known(prefix):\\n            facts.add(\\\"word_known\\\")\\n        if prefix in lex.complete:\\n            facts.add(\\\"word_complete\\\")\\n            term = lex.terminators(prefix) or set(\\\" .,;:!?\\\")\\n            sets[\\\"TERM\\\"] = sp.chars(term)\\n            if prev and prefix.lower() == prev.lower():\\n                facts.add(\\\"stutter\\\")\\n            if len(prefix) >= 5 and prefix.lower() in {w.lower() for w in words[:-1][-6:]}:\\n                facts.add(\\\"repeat_recent\\\")\\n        return prefix, prev\\n\\n\\n'''\\ns=s[:a]+new_percept+s[b:]\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- RuleBase.region: ignore no-ops\\nold='''            if new:                       # never let a rule empty the gate\\n                region = new\\n                applied.append(r.name)\\n            else:\\n                relaxed.append(r.name)'''\\nnew='''            if not new:                   # never let a rule empty the gate\\n                relaxed.append(r.name)\\n            elif new.mask != region.mask:  # only record rules that actually shaped the gate\\n                region = new\\n                applied.append(r.name)'''\\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Controller / builder / lint block\\na=sep(\\\"Controller: ties perception\\\")\\nb=sep(\\\"# Generation\\\")\\nnew_ctrl=r'''# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Controller: ties perception, rules and plan into one gate per step\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass Decision:\\n    label: str = \\\"\\\"\\n    facts: FrozenSet[str] = frozenset()\\n    applied: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\\n    relaxed: List[str] = field(default_factory=list)\\n    plan_step: str = \\\"-\\\"\\n    size: int = 0\\n    ctx: str = \\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass LogicController:\\n    def __init__(self, space: SymbolSpace, named: Dict[str, SymbolSet], perceiver: Perceiver,\\n                 rulebase: RuleBase, tracker: Optional[PlanTracker] = None, evaluator=None,\\n                 lexicon: Optional[Lexicon] = None):\\n        self.space, self.named, self.perceiver = space, named, perceiver\\n        self.rules, self.tracker, self.evaluate, self.lexicon = rulebase, tracker, evaluator, lexicon\\n        self.last = Decision()\\n        self.stats: Counter = Counter()\\n        self.steps = 0\\n        self._memo: Optional[Tuple[str, Percept]] = None\\n\\n    def _percept(self, context: Sequence[str]) -> Percept:\\n        text = \\\"\\\".join(context)\\n        if self._memo is None or self._memo[0] != text:\\n            self._memo = (text, self.perceiver.percept(text))\\n        return self._memo[1]\\n\\n    def start(self, context: Sequence[str]) -> None:\\n        if self.tracker:\\n            self.tracker.start(self._percept(context).facts)\\n\\n    def gate(self, context: Sequence[str], user_allowed: Optional[SymbolSet]) -> SymbolSet:\\n        p = self._percept(context)\\n        _, fired = self.rules.infer(p.facts)\\n        base = user_allowed if user_allowed else self.space.universe()\\n        region, applied, relaxed = self.rules.region(fired, base, lambda e: self.evaluate(e, p.sets))\\n        label, step = \\\"rules\\\", \\\"-\\\"\\n        if self.tracker:\\n            step = self.tracker.describe()\\n            pr = self.tracker.region()\\n            if pr is not None:\\n                joint = region & pr\\n                if joint:\\n                    region, label = joint, \\\"rules+plan\\\"\\n                else:\\n                    label = \\\"rules (plan yields)\\\"\\n        self.last = Decision(label, p.facts, applied, relaxed, step, len(region), f\\\"{p.prev}|{p.prefix}\\\")\\n        self.steps += 1\\n        self.stats.update(f\\\"rule:{n}\\\" for n in applied)\\n        self.stats.update(f\\\"relaxed:{n}\\\" for n in relaxed)\\n        self.stats[f\\\"gate:{label}\\\"] += 1\\n        return region\\n\\n    def observe(self, token: str, context_after: Sequence[str]) -> None:\\n        if self.tracker:\\n            self.tracker.observe(token, self._percept(context_after).facts)\\n\\n    def summary(self) -> str:\\n        shaped = {k[5:]: v for k, v in self.stats.items() if k.startswith(\\\"rule:\\\")}\\n        relaxed = {k[8:]: v for k, v in self.stats.items() if k.startswith(\\\"relaxed:\\\")}\\n        gates = {k[5:]: v for k, v in self.stats.items() if k.startswith(\\\"gate:\\\")}\\n        idle = [r.name for r in self.rules.rules if r.is_constraint and r.name not in shaped]\\n        lines = [f\\\"[logic] {self.steps} gated steps | gates: \\\" + \\\", \\\".join(f\\\"{k}={v}\\\" for k, v in gates.items())]\\n        if self.lexicon:\\n            lines.append(f\\\"[logic] lexicon: {len(self.lexicon.complete)} word types, \\\"\\n                         f\\\"{len(self.lexicon.after)} bigram contexts\\\")\\n        lines.append(\\\"[logic] rules that shaped the gate: \\\" + (\\\", \\\".join(f\\\"{k}={v}\\\" for k, v in sorted(shaped.items())) or \\\"none\\\"))\\n        if relaxed:\\n            lines.append(\\\"[logic] relaxed (would have emptied the gate): \\\" + \\\", \\\".join(f\\\"{k}={v}\\\" for k, v in sorted(relaxed.items())))\\n        if self.tracker:\\n            lines.append(f\\\"[logic] plan cycles completed: {self.tracker.cycles}; current plan: \\\"\\n                         f\\\"{' -> '.join(self.tracker.plan_names()) or '(none)'}\\\")\\n        if idle:\\n            lines.append(\\\"[logic] rules that never changed the gate: \\\" + \\\", \\\".join(idle))\\n        return \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines)\\n\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Building from a spec, and static verification\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndef load_spec(path: Optional[str]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\\n    spec = dict(DEFAULT_SPEC)\\n    if path:\\n        spec.update(json.loads(Path(path).read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")))\\n    return spec\\n\\n\\ndef make_evaluator(space: SymbolSpace, named: Dict[str, SymbolSet]):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"evaluate(expr) uses static sets; evaluate(expr, dyn) also sees this step's dynamic sets.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    trees: Dict[str, ast.AST] = {}\\n    static: Dict[str, SymbolSet] = {}\\n\\n    def evaluate(expr: str, extra: Optional[Dict[str, SymbolSet]] = None) -> SymbolSet:\\n        if extra is None and expr in static:\\n            return static[expr]\\n        try:\\n            if expr not in trees:\\n                trees[expr] = ast.parse(expr.strip(), mode=\\\"eval\\\").body\\n            env = named if extra is None else {**named, **extra}\\n            result = _eval_node(trees[expr], space, env)\\n        except (SyntaxError, ValueError) as exc:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Bad set expression {expr!r}: {exc}\\\")\\n        if extra is None:\\n            static[expr] = result\\n        return result\\n    return evaluate\\n\\n\\ndef _uses_dynamic(expr: str) -> bool:\\n    return any(re.search(rf\\\"\\\\b{n}\\\\b\\\", expr) for n in DYNAMIC_SETS)\\n\\n\\ndef build_logic(spec: Dict[str, Any], space: SymbolSpace, named: Dict[str, SymbolSet],\\n                goal_name: Optional[str], use_rules: bool = True,\\n                lexicon: Optional[Lexicon] = None,\\n                follow: Optional[Dict[str, SymbolSet]] = None) -> LogicController:\\n    evaluate = make_evaluator(space, named)\\n    dummy = {n: space.empty() for n in DYNAMIC_SETS}\\n    perceiver = Perceiver(named, lexicon, follow, **spec.get(\\\"perceiver\\\", {}))\\n    rulebase = RuleBase([Rule.from_dict(r) for r in spec[\\\"rules\\\"]] if use_rules else [])\\n    for r in rulebase.rules:                       # fail early on bad expressions\\n        if r.is_constraint:\\n            evaluate(r.then.split(\\\":\\\", 1)[1], dummy)\\n    tracker = None\\n    if goal_name:\\n        if goal_name not in spec[\\\"goals\\\"]:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"unknown goal {goal_name!r}; choose from {sorted(spec['goals'])}\\\")\\n        g = spec[\\\"goals\\\"][goal_name]\\n        tracker = PlanTracker([Operator.from_dict(o) for o in spec[\\\"operators\\\"]],\\n                              Goal(frozenset(g[\\\"pos\\\"]), frozenset(g.get(\\\"neg\\\", []))),\\n                              spec[\\\"grounding\\\"], evaluate)\\n    return LogicController(space, named, perceiver, rulebase, tracker, evaluate, lexicon)\\n\\n\\ndef lint(spec: Dict[str, Any], space: SymbolSpace, named: Dict[str, SymbolSet]) -> List[str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Static checks: dead atoms, empty sets, rule conflicts, unreachable goals.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    out: List[str] = []\\n    ev = make_evaluator(space, named)\\n    dummy = {n: space.empty() for n in DYNAMIC_SETS}\\n    perceiver = Perceiver(named, **spec.get(\\\"perceiver\\\", {}))\\n    rules = [Rule.from_dict(r) for r in spec[\\\"rules\\\"]]\\n    RuleBase(rules)                                   # structural validation\\n    known = perceiver.atoms() | {r.then for r in rules}\\n    cons: List[Tuple[Rule, str, SymbolSet]] = []\\n    for r in rules:\\n        for a in sorted((r.if_all | r.if_none) - known):\\n            out.append(f\\\"rule {r.name}: atom {a!r} is never perceived or derived\\\")\\n        if r.is_constraint:\\n            kind, expr = r.then.split(\\\":\\\", 1)\\n            ev(expr, dummy)                           # raises on unknown names / bad syntax\\n            if _uses_dynamic(expr):\\n                continue                              # value only known at run time\\n            s = ev(expr)\\n            if kind == \\\"allow\\\" and not s:\\n                out.append(f\\\"rule {r.name}: {r.then!r} denotes the empty set in this alphabet\\\")\\n            cons.append((r, kind, s))\\n    for i, (ra, ka, sa) in enumerate(cons):\\n        for rb, kb, sb in cons[i + 1:]:\\n            body = ra.if_all | rb.if_all\\n            if body & (ra.if_none | rb.if_none):\\n                continue                              # bodies can never hold together\\n            lasts = sorted(a[5:] for a in body if a.startswith(\\\"last:\\\") and a[5:] in named)\\n            if any(not (named[x] & named[y]) for x, y in zip(lasts, lasts[1:] + lasts[:1]) if x != y):\\n                continue                              # last symbol cannot be in two disjoint classes\\n            if ka == kb == \\\"allow\\\" and not consistent(sa, sb):\\n                out.append(f\\\"{ra.name} / {rb.name}: allow sets are disjoint; the earlier rule wins\\\")\\n            elif {ka, kb} == {\\\"allow\\\", \\\"deny\\\"}:\\n                (al, a_s), (dn, d_s) = ((ra, sa), (rb, sb)) if ka == \\\"allow\\\" else ((rb, sb), (ra, sa))\\n                if entails(a_s, d_s):\\n                    out.append(f\\\"{al.name} / {dn.name}: every allowed symbol is denied; the earlier rule wins\\\")\\n    ops = [Operator.from_dict(o) for o in spec[\\\"operators\\\"]]\\n    live = [o for o in ops if ev(o.region)]\\n    for o in ops:\\n        if o not in live:\\n            out.append(f\\\"operator {o.name}: region is empty in this alphabet (dropped)\\\")\\n    sync = spec[\\\"grounding\\\"]\\n    for name, g in spec[\\\"goals\\\"].items():\\n        goal = Goal(frozenset(g[\\\"pos\\\"]), frozenset(g.get(\\\"neg\\\", [])))\\n        bad = []\\n        for mask in range(2 ** len(sync)):\\n            init = frozenset(e[\\\"present\\\"] if (mask >> k) & 1 else e.get(\\\"absent\\\")\\n                             for k, e in enumerate(sync)) - {None}\\n            if plan(live, init, goal) is None:\\n                bad.append(sorted(init))\\n        if bad:\\n            out.append(f\\\"goal {name}: unreachable from {len(bad)} of {2 ** len(sync)} perceivable \\\"\\n                       f\\\"initial states (tracker idles until a reachable one is perceived), e.g. {bad[0]}\\\")\\n    return out or [\\\"no problems found\\\"]\\n\\n\\n'''\\ns=s[:a]+new_ctrl+s[b:]\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- explain line\\nold='''f\\\"plan={d.plan_step:<18} rules={','.join(d.applied) or '-'}\\\"'''\\nnew='''f\\\"plan={d.plan_step:<18} ctx={d.ctx!r:<22} rules={','.join(d.applied) or '-'}\\\"'''\\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- main\\ns=s.replace('''    g.add_argument(\\\"--no-logic\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Disable the rule-based reasoning gate.\\\")''','''    g.add_argument(\\\"--no-logic\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\", help=\\\"Disable the rule-based reasoning gate.\\\")\\n    g.add_argument(\\\"--no-lexicon\\\", action=\\\"store_true\\\",\\n                   help=\\\"Do not learn word-level symbol sets (CONT, CONT_AFTER, TERM); open vocabulary.\\\")''')\\nold='''    space = SpaceHolder'''\\ns=s.replace('''    named = build_named_sets(space)\\n\\n    if args.sets:''','''    named = build_named_sets(space)\\n    fragments = SetFragments(space, named, model, window=args.window)\\n    lexicon = None if args.no_lexicon else Lexicon(corpus)\\n\\n    if args.sets:''',1)\\ns=s.replace('''            logic = build_logic(spec, space, named, goal, use_rules=not args.no_logic)''','''            logic = build_logic(spec, space, named, goal, use_rules=not args.no_logic,\\n                                lexicon=lexicon, follow=fragments.follow)''')\\ns=s.replace('''    fragments = SetFragments(space, named, model, window=args.window)\\n    tau = float''','''    tau = float''')\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- docstring\\ns=s.replace('''Everything is data (DEFAULT_SPEC below''','''Dynamic symbol sets (recomputed every step, usable in any rule expression):\\n  CONT        next symbols that keep the current word prefix a real corpus word\\n  CONT_AFTER  ...restricted to words that followed the previous word in the corpus\\n  TERM        symbols that followed this exact word in the corpus\\n  CLOSER      closing bracket matching the innermost open bracket\\n  FOLLOW      Follow(last symbol) from the n-gram (the g1 fragment)\\n  RECENT      symbols in the last few positions\\nSo a rule such as  deny:ALNUM - CONT_AFTER  (\\\"no letter that can't start a word\\nlicensed by the previous word\\\") composes learned sets with the Boolean algebra.\\n\\nEverything is data (DEFAULT_SPEC below''',1)\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nPYEOF\\npython3 patch3.py && python3 -m py_compile algorithm_logic.py && echo compiled && python3 algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --lint\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:47:30.589231Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:47:30.589271Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_result", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01RBjkoXpHi1KTvT5YDDjxKP", "name": "bash_tool", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"compiled\\ngoal quoted: unreachable from 6 of 8 perceivable initial states (tracker idles until a reachable one is perceived), e.g. ['capitalised']\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}], "is_error": false, "structured_content": null, "meta": {"output_format_category": "none"}, "message": null, "integration_name": "File Creation", "mcp_server_url": null, "integration_icon_url": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"returncode\":0,\"stdout\":\"compiled\\ngoal quoted: unreachable from 6 of 8 perceivable initial states (tracker idles until a reachable one is perceived), e.g. ['capitalised']\\n\",\"stderr\":\"\"}"}, "hidden_in_chat": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:47:32.668909Z", "stop_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:47:33.506615Z", "flags": null, "type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01AAFpw7xyzgCFS2xMgwrm2i", "name": "bash_tool", "input": {"command": "cd /home/claude/build && python3 algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --tokens 400 && echo ---- && python3 algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --tokens 30 --explain | sed -n '1,22p'", "description": "Run default generation and explain trace with the new lexical rules"}, "message": "Run default generation and explain trace with the new lexical rules", "integration_name": "File Creation", "integration_icon_url": null, "tool_identifier": null, "icon_name": "commandLine", "context": null, "display_content": {"type": "json_block", "json_block": "{\"language\": \"bash\", \"code\": \"cd /home/claude/build && python3 algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --tokens 400 && echo ---- && python3 algorithm_logic.py corpus.txt --tokens 30 --explain | sed -n '1,22p'\"}"}, "approval_options": null, "approval_key": null, "approval_key_legacy": null, "is_mcp_app": null, "hidden_in_chat": null, "mcp_server_url": null, "tool_origin": "first_party"}, {"start_timestamp": "2026-10-20T01:47:34.099564Z",